{"columns":["comment_id","issue_key","issue_project_key","comment_author_email","comment_author_name","comment_body","comment_created_at_ts"],"row_count":10000,"rows":[["3811014","RDXENG-4661","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Hey *@user-UKNQVK26B* & *@user-U048HD7HRHP*!\n\n[TECH-150211|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-150211]: CI.216.0: External reporter states:\n\n{quote}User sent two screenshots of the same ride. In the first one there is a name of the driver who cancelled the ride but app shows it as finalised order. \nOn the second one there is a correct driver for this order.{quote}\n\nLooking at the orders I can see that during [this order attempt|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2340049044/1?orderTryId=3008511086] the driver called Ahmed rejected the trip and the final trip was completed by Roman ([here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2340049044/1?orderTryId=3008509036]), however, the app history shows Ahmed as the driver.\n\nWe can see this on log line 745 under {{/mobility/history/getDetails}} where it states:\n\n{noformat}\"title\":\"Ride with Ahmed Mrzoog Musa Mohammed\"{noformat}\n\nCould you ptal, the invoice has the correct driver, but the app history does not. :eyes:","2026-01-15T05:10:37.041Z"],["3811015","RDXENG-4661","RDXENG",null,"Slack","[Ankit Goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1768392139186189?thread_ts=1768392139.186189&cid=CSFF3R571|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1768392139186189?thread_ts=1768392139.186189&cid=CSFF3R571|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T05:10:38.221Z"],["3811016","RDXENG-4661","RDXENG","anastasiya.sviatokha@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Sviatokha","[@ankit.goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] Could you please take a look? Seems like BE issue.","2026-01-15T05:10:38.779Z"],["3811017","RDXENG-4661","RDXENG","germo.rikk@bolt.eu","Germo Rikk","Hey, another report [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-150403] ([order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2339534452/159?orderTryId=3007576531]) in Poland, so it's not a once off FYI - let me know if you also would like logs for this user. :eyes:\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8SK9G5B6/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8SK9G5B6/image.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8SKA6MFW/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8SKA6MFW/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-15T05:10:39.821Z"],["3811019","RS-1950","RS","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","[^DRF 137 12 2025.docx (1).docx] _(28 kB)_\n\n[^Old DRF.pdf (1).pdf] _(1.48 MB)_","2026-01-15T05:27:44.837Z"],["3811028","LSS-58462","LSS","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Is there any advise on this [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] ?","2026-01-15T05:49:02.880Z"],["3811056","LSS-60735","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","[^Project Diamond - EY Advisory Support vF.pdf]\n\nHey [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] can you please help us get this signed by Ahto? All changes/reviews/etc. have been approved by Corporate Legal and the business Peter/Simon. ","2026-01-15T06:08:22.285Z"],["3811057","PFI-833577","PFI","tochi.adimachukwu@bolt-outsource.eu","Tochi Adimachukwu","!{EBBF3B60-B1C2-4E91-A255-42A5AB7079CD}-20260115-061058.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T06:11:18.229Z"],["3811058","PAW-14879","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-15T06:14:59.573Z"],["3811059","PIF-3283","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-alter-automation, pint-product-data-management, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-15T06:15:05.149Z"],["3811060","PIF-4150","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-product-data-management, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-15T06:15:09.908Z"],["3811062","PIF-3283","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Review Results:\n• Severity: 7\n• Reproducibility: 4\n• Priority: N/A\n• Accept: 1\n• Suggested improvements: Providing more details on any commonalities between the two cases and environment specifics where the issue occurs would be helpful.","2026-01-15T06:17:26.213Z"],["3811063","PFI-833583","PFI","regina.agada@bolt-outsource.eu","Regina Agada","[^PaymentNotification (3) 1.pdf]","2026-01-15T06:17:38.075Z"],["3811065","WFM-9915","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:a4969d25-8e58-49a1-a0b4-179bb77e9ff8],\n\nAs we haven’t received a response from you, we’ll consider this case resolved. Please feel free to reach out if you need any further assistance.","2026-01-15T06:19:33.829Z"],["3811069","IOTTEAM-289","IOTTEAM","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] what do you think if we made this initiative as general “Vehicle unlock improvements” or something like that. We could then also add stuff like [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/G3IOT-1205|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/G3IOT-1205|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T06:22:34.824Z"],["3811070","WFM-10000","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:a4db27c0-87f6-4a6d-ace2-ec23e6b8f1aa], could you please check this request? User is asking for Safety queues assignments. ","2026-01-15T06:22:49.095Z"],["3811074","G3IOT-1205","G3IOT","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","realistic impact most likely higher than €3…5k per month due to search tasks etc","2026-01-15T06:29:54.844Z"],["3811076","DSR-3755","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-15T06:31:22.954Z"],["3811083","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - regarding section 11 of KPIs - are you sure we don’t want to say that some of the metrics they have requested cannot be shared?  I mean like system logs and the like.  Requesting you to also give access to contract with your comments to [~accountid:5b0fdc5182e05b22cc7d4cf3] - [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] is there someone else from operations you can loop in to comment on the what KPIs are we actually allowed to share and whether they are possible or available? ","2026-01-15T06:35:24.495Z"],["3811085","WD-22477","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi there, the sabbatical has been added from 01/01/2027 to 31/12/2027 ","2026-01-15T06:38:56.317Z"],["3811087","WFM-9998","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Requested [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C068PG9935Y/p1768458941433699?thread_ts=1768456806.585439&cid=C068PG9935Y] the reason or recommendation for the above agents on why they need UA market access, since it is a very sensitive market. ","2026-01-15T06:41:15.840Z"],["3811088","WD-22477","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","approved my \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 08.41.44.png|width=373,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 08.41.44.png\"!","2026-01-15T06:41:52.922Z"],["3811089","WFM-9992","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:6171356e58006300691b9686],\n\nRole granted. Have a great day.","2026-01-15T06:43:07.063Z"],["3811091","WFM-9996","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:b2d15fe0-4ac2-48c5-9e25-34268c88fe65] ,\n\nCould you please provide screenshots of the mentioned error? Agents already have the role assigned.","2026-01-15T06:44:38.932Z"],["3811092","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14], thank you for sharing the documents! \n\nBefore I start reviewing them, I wanted to check whether Bolt has the possibility to propose amendments or additions to these documents - i.e. to negotiate certain terms so they better reflect Bolt’s interests - or whether the documents are strictly non-negotiable and, if we want to participate in the tender, must be accepted entirely on an “as-is” basis?\n\nThanks! ","2026-01-15T06:44:48.930Z"],["3811093","LSS-61192","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[~accountid:712020:f8c30920-765a-42dd-bbe7-058336c97a0c] KPIs are a commercial terms, not legal, therefore I require your instructions. \n\nPlease advise whether Bolt can deliver on these KPIs or specifiy which requirements are not supported. Once you have provided this feedback I can assist to update the clause accordingly - I would rather we remove the ones causing any concern to be on the safe side. \n\nConfirming that the draft has been shared to [~accountid:5b0fdc5182e05b22cc7d4cf3] ","2026-01-15T06:47:23.991Z"],["3811096","BLTF-116","BLTF","omar.quiroga@bolt.eu","Omar Quiroga","!image-20260115-065018.png|width=590,alt=\"image-20260115-065018.png\"!","2026-01-15T06:50:28.188Z"],["3811099","PFI-833606","PFI","torfun.aemong@bolt.eu","Torfun Aemong","[^TH6525-2016.pdf]","2026-01-15T06:52:26.053Z"],["3811100","PFI-833606","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T06:52:28.259Z"],["3811101","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - yes, they may be commercial terms, but as they also touch on our operations, I have reached out to the business data request slack channel for additional guidance. But I will also align with [~accountid:5b0fdc5182e05b22cc7d4cf3] for more guidance on those deemed commercial terms. I will advise you accordingly. ","2026-01-15T06:56:00.642Z"],["3811108","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","germo.rikk@bolt.eu","Germo Rikk","Hey, smallest to largest so  {{€ 3.8 - 7.2}} ([source|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02CUF8CFCZ/p1755007969876119])","2026-01-15T07:00:15.136Z"],["3811110","LSS-58347","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Mateusz Ryska,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-15T07:00:50.920Z"],["3811111","LSS-60211","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Andrew Simiyu Mwibanda,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-15T07:00:51.474Z"],["3811112","PFI-831280","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Patrycja Matus,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:05.425Z"],["3811113","PFI-831323","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Patryk Flakowski,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:06.257Z"],["3811114","PFI-830963","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Elijah Ojeamien,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:06.293Z"],["3811115","PFI-830957","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Andrei Grecu,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:06.440Z"],["3811116","PFI-831513","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Yusuf Juma,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:06.621Z"],["3811117","PFI-830876","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Mwanamu Hemed,\n\nWe haven't heard from