 it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:11.333Z"],["3811132","PFI-827376","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Parvin Alirrzayeva,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:11.770Z"],["3811135","PFI-814652","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Timofey Shapovalov,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:13.617Z"],["3811136","PFI-813786","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Külli Tuka,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:13.977Z"],["3811140","PFI-823715","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Anastasiya Nikolayeva,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:01:28.487Z"],["3811141","LSS-60461","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T07:01:43.677Z"],["3811142","LSS-58904","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T07:01:44.019Z"],["3811144","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Are you sure? It is RTL language.","2026-01-15T07:03:05.092Z"],["3811145","WFM-10001","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","*CS Support Specialist*: [_Deprecated. Soon to be removed. Please do NOT request this role._|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/permissions/edit/412?tab=roles]\n\nChecking with the team.","2026-01-15T07:03:23.001Z"],["3811148","BD-1979","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160805|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160805|smart-link] \n\nDev. notes:\n\n* added dynamic config for cron limit and interval","2026-01-15T07:04:00.311Z"],["3811150","PFI-833234","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-15T07:05:16.031Z"],["3811151","PFI-833304","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-15T07:05:18.314Z"],["3811152","PFI-833353","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-15T07:05:20.666Z"],["3811153","PFI-833384","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-15T07:05:23.034Z"],["3811155","PFI-817272","PFI","natalie.kolinova@bolt-outsource.eu","Natalie Kolínova","Hello. Can you please send the money to the driver so we could delete his account? Thank you!","2026-01-15T07:06:24.251Z"],["3811157","RDXENG-4652","RDXENG","germo.rikk@bolt.eu","Germo Rikk","Not a 100% sure but as they still read numbers from left to right & universally values are min to max (afaik) then I think it'd be a safe bet :eyes:\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8TBWUKML/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_09.06.47.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8TBWUKML/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_09.06.47.png|smart-link]","2026-01-15T07:07:44.336Z"],["3811158","LSS-61606","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nBeatričė Krašenko has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T07:08:38.727Z"],["3811159","PIF-3283","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 *Auto-set WSJF Opportunity Enablement*\n- Component: `pint-component-alter-automation`\n- Tier: 1\n- Opportunity Enablement: 13\n\nReason: Opportunity Enablement is derived from component tier.","2026-01-15T07:08:47.215Z"],["3811160","LSS-61606","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","[^2026-01-15 Pretenzija dėl nuostolių atlyginimo (Bolt Operations OÜ).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T07:08:52.590Z"],["3811161","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Good morning, Beatrice. I would suggest that we include the necessary amendments and additions to this tender to ensure that, if successful, the terms align with the way Bolt conducts business.","2026-01-15T07:09:18.847Z"],["3811164","RIDE-658","RIDE","fatmakhanim.mammadova@bolt.eu","Fatya Mammadova","Hi! Updated scope of project is:\n*Version 0:*\n\n* Create a partner specific space in Confluence\n* Create a partner-specific Confluence role with:\n** Read-only permissions\n** Strict space-level access control\n* Ensure access is:\n** Managed by IT / Atlassian admins\n** Visible to InfoSec\n** Protected against accidental over-permissioning\n\n*Confluence Setup*\n\n* Space is separated from internal spaces.\n* Access limited only to explicitly approved partner content.\n\n*Content (version 0)*\n\n* Manually duplicate selected pages into the partner space.\n* Initial content focus:\n** To be prepared \n* Exclude by default:\n** Internal-only or confidential data\n\nh3. Version 1:\n\n* Automatic synchronization of internal Confluence pages, so partners would get up to date data \n\n[~accountid:6012aafadc29b4006a59453e] [~accountid:6053147e4a91ad0068c082df] [~accountid:615ea2fec5388b0069924c5e] [~accountid:5f6d8701ed55c7006af1700e]\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:d4126fc0-85ff-45d4-af88-bc851d5b32bc] ","2026-01-15T07:11:17.706Z"],["3811166","PFI-833092","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank; the provider returned a generic UPI-related error code and did not supply a clear reason. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again. To help prevent another rejection, please ask the partner to double-check their beneficiary details (UPI ID or bank account details are correct and the account is active/unblocked).\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-15T07:11:22.267Z"],["3811167","PFI-833099","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending (last update on 11 Jan) due to payment validation in progress at the payment provider, which typically indicates a compliance review or technical check. Please inform the partner that no action is required on their side; we are monitoring and will handle any provider requests so the payout can be released as soon as validation completes. The status will update automatically once processed and the funds should reflect shortly after. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; feedback is welcome.","2026-01-15T07:11:56.999Z"],["3811168","PFI-833103","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is still in pending status with the provider since 2025-12-16, which is unusually long and likely due to an ongoing compliance review or a technical issue on their side. Please inform the partner that we are actively monitoring such pending payouts and respond to any provider compliance requests as soon as they come; no action is required from the partner at the moment. We will proceed as soon as the provider clears it and update once the status changes.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-15T07:12:25.243Z"],["3811169","PFI-833148","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the payment provider, and they did not share a specific reason for the failure. Please inform the partner that the payout will be automatically retried during the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting it again. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-15T07:13:02.649Z"],["3811170","PFI-833180","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout has been successfully processed and marked completed by the provider. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still do not see the funds, ask them to check with their beneficiary bank using the proof. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-15T07:13:32.294Z"],["3811171","PFI-833282","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed (value date 2026-01-12). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still do not see the funds, they should contact their beneficiary bank. If the complaint is about only a part of the payout being missing, please open a Service Desk ticket for the Billing team, as they calculate the amounts. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; feel free to share any feedback.","2026-01-15T07:14:08.886Z"],["3811172","HS-28925","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Perfect! The confirmation letter will be forwarded to you via BoxSign to your personal email.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-15T07:14:42.795Z"],["3811173","PFI-833309","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending; payment validation is in progress with the provider, which indicates an ongoing compliance review and can cause delays. It has been pending since 05 Jan 2026, so please inform the partner that we are monitoring this and responding to any compliance requests promptly. No action is required from the partner right now; once the review completes, the payout will be processed and should reach their bank account soon after.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-15T07:14:46.548Z"],["3811176","PFI-833323","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is currently in pending status; the latest log from today shows the bank file was accepted and processing is underway. Please inform the partner that funds should reflect within 1–2 business days, and the app status will update once the bank completes processing. If the funds are not received within 2 business days, please ask the partner to contact their (beneficiary) bank and update this ticket. P.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—thanks for your feedback.","2026-01-15T07:15:18.021Z"],["3811178","PFI-833354","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed; the account statement date is 01.12.2025 (last status on 2025-12-01). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner, and ask them to check their bank statement for that date; if they still cannot locate the funds, they should contact their beneficiary bank to trace it. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-15T07:15:51.839Z"],["3811180","PFI-833389","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected because the bank details on file don’t pass the bank’s routing checks (likely an incorrect/missing account number or clearing/routing code). Please ask the partner to update their payout details to the exact values issued by their bank (account number/IBAN and the correct clearing/routing code, with the proper format/length). After the details are corrected, the payout will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can submit the request again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-15T07:16:19.855Z"],["3811181","LSS-61606","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T07:16:34.334Z"],["3811182","PFI-833419","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout was successfully processed; bank value date is 2026-01-12. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the courier; if funds are still not visible, ask them to contact their bank with the value date to trace the transfer. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase; feedback is welcome.","2026-01-15T07:16:50.118Z"],["3811183","PFI-833459","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed (value date 2026-01-05), and the last log shows it finished on 2026-01-06. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner. If the partner still doesn’t see the funds, ask them to contact their beneficiary bank using the proof for tracing. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-15T07:17:03.747Z"],["3811186","PFI-833528","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout has been pending since 05 Jan because a payment validation (compliance review) is in progress at the payment provider, which can take longer than usual. No action is required from the partner at this time; we are monitoring these cases and responding to any requests so it can be released as soon as possible. Please inform the partner that once the review is completed, the payout will be processed in the next available cycle and the status will update accordingly. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-15T07:17:46.285Z"],["3811187","CORA-387","CORA","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","[~accountid:712020:0d04167f-dce4-443a-8156-8acc576e7815] Thank you fo the reports but it is not enough. We would need to have a Looker on this since this information changes constantly and we need to have updated data on this matter. ","2026-01-15T07:18:15.583Z"],["3811188","WD-22513","WD","mathis.bogens@bolt.eu","Mathis Bogens","Hey! Thank you so much for this, George! \n\nWe’ll take it from there and reach out if there’s anything we need additional support with.\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\nMathis Bogens\n\n\n\n","2026-01-15T07:19:18.276Z"],["3811189","HS-28957","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Integration error/duplicate ticket, no action needed. ","2026-01-15T07:20:08.444Z"],["3811190","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] thanks! \n\n\nBut before starting work on reviewing the documents and preparing proposed amendments, it is important for me to understand whether there is a real possibility to negotiate the content of the documents.\n\nWe have encountered situations more than once where we carefully review, comment on, and suggest changes to tender documents, only to find that the tender organizer is not willing to engage in any negotiations at all. In such cases, a significant amount of time and Bolt’s resources are wasted, which is neither economical nor efficient.\n\nTherefore, before proceeding with this work, we would appreciate confirmation that the tender organiser is open to negotiating the terms and that Bolt will have the opportunity to propose additions or amendments to the document conditions.\n\nThanks a lot! ","2026-01-15T07:20:37.535Z"],["3811191","DSR-3757","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-15T07:21:06.177Z"],["3811192","TAXP-2011","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Filed and paid. Details are in the below folder.\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zEoqU9lb8kIWMHEx5-UyxF39-MbB6CEW|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1zEoqU9lb8kIWMHEx5-UyxF39-MbB6CEW|smart-card]","2026-01-15T07:24:16.205Z"],["3811193","WD-22577","WD","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Please assign this ticket to PT [~accountid:712020:176612de-64ab-442f-84ee-ed63bbac2b50] 🙏 ","2026-01-15T07:25:16.852Z"],["3811196","HS-28959","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Mattis Rahnel?","2026-01-15T07:26:58.505Z"],["3811197","HS-28963","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Paula! Unfortunately, it’s not possible to change your health benefit from Confido to Stebby at this time. As was mentioned in the initial form, once you have chosen the Confido Health Insurance, you cannot change this selection until the current insurance policy ends on 31st May 2026, as it is locked for that duration. So, currently I can't change it to Stebby, so sorry!\n\nYou can change it from June - sometime in May, everyone will be asked to fill out a new questionnaire to choose a benefit, so you can make your new choice then.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-15T07:27:15.901Z"],["3811198","PFI-833616","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T07:27:33.426Z"],["3811199","PFI-833616","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:bc7bca9c-4d13-42b6-9684-04014a47f7aa, 63a00ef0f3e7004f77fadf98] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T07:27:35.150Z"],["3811200","HS-28959","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Integration error/duplicate ticket, no action needed. ","2026-01-15T07:27:55.686Z"],["3811203","HS-28965","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in eesti.ee yet.","2026-01-15T07:30:25.111Z"],["3811204","PFI-833323","PFI","edvin.hansson@bolt-outsource.eu","Edvin Hans Wilhelm Hansson","Asked partner to await 1-2 businiess days, and contact their bank if it is not reflected in their bank account. ","2026-01-15T07:30:37.062Z"],["3811206","HS-28969","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-15T07:31:29.207Z"],["3811209","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768462301312649]*{color}:\nCreate the ticket [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-833616?created=true], apparently there is no option to chose under issue type anymore, so I had to chose a random one.\n\nWill you approve the ticket as well <@U04FV4Z0GQ4>?\n\nI am requesting the creation of 3 new temporary compensation subtypes to cover the three cases we currently have and that are a blocker due to transparency:\n\n1. Legacy balance transfers (Viggo → Bolt)\n\n2. Equipment deposit refunds (Fleet Owner offboarding)\n\n3. Charging equipment deposits for new Fleet Owners\n{quote}","2026-01-15T07:31:57.643Z"],["3811210","PFI-832687","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hi [~accountid:712020:92e1ef86-c3f2-44dc-9919-605e500b8161],\n\nThanks for the update!\n\nThe device UID suspension has now been lifted.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:33:50.598Z"],["3811211","PFI-833220","PFI","innaaime.kalju@bolt.eu","Inna Aime Kalju","Thank you, Marten\ni will create a reply for police, i will let you know, if they come back\nkeep the ticket open until next week, please","2026-01-15T07:35:01.531Z"],["3811212","PFI-833620","PFI","nikita.laar@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikita Laar","[^Anna-Mariya Davydkina 1336888207.pdf]","2026-01-15T07:35:28.024Z"],["3811213","WD-22372","WD","keidi.helm@bolt.eu","Keidi Helm","Hi!\n\nI received PY primary payroll report on 14th of January morning. Please see screenshot:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 09.26.38.png|width=1305,height=131,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 09.26.38.png\"!\n\nBut the schedule Mo shared with you states 14.01.2026 evening 23:00+1 GMT.\nPlease keep Mo schedule, but correct the time, so that cut-off date is in the evening, info inserted in WD on date 14.01.2026, 13.02.2026…. etc would reflect in the primary report.\n\nThank you!\nKeidi","2026-01-15T07:35:54.090Z"],["3811215","PFI-832262","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f7a5b04d-b48e-4f8c-a4a0-34159bbb7f81],\n\nSeems like now all the blocks have been removed, thank you for the update.\n\nWe have also proceeded from our side and have removed all the device UID suspensions.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:36:39.798Z"],["3811216","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768462645270689]*{color}:\nOn another note <@U04FV4Z0GQ4>, we will proceed with returning the deposit off all FOs that are under offboarding via Viggo's Console Legacy tool until we have the above fixed, let me know if there are any remarks or concerns with that.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T07:37:38.535Z"],["3811217","DO-5792","DO","tanel.joala@bolt.eu","Tanel Joala","[~accountid:712020:35c6db0e-ea69-4585-b18c-0e29c17e126d] , I approve. Thanks","2026-01-15T07:37:42.840Z"],["3811225","LSS-56917","LSS","katrin.anier@bolt.eu","Katrin Anier","Hello!\nLooping in [~accountid:63dba2fb1b13d42998e22e00] from the Controlling team regarding this question.\n\n","2026-01-15T07:42:06.617Z"],["3811228","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Working on fixing rundeck error:\n\n{noformat}TASK [db_alter_automation_deploy : Copy deploy.cgi] ****************************\n--- before\n+++ after: /var/lib/rundeck/bolt/dbre/139331/ansible/roles/db_alter_automation_deploy/files/deploy.cgi\n@@ -0,0 +1,323 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/perl\n+#\n+# AUTHOR: Kain Kalju (kain@taxify.eu)\n+# LICENSE: The \"Artistic License\" - http://dev.perl.org/licenses/artistic.html\n+\n+use CGI;\n+use Encode;\n+use JSON::XS;\n+use NetAddr::IP;\n+\n+$APT_BIN = '/usr/bin/apt-get';\n+$MARK_BIN = '/usr/bin/apt-mark';\n+$SUDO_BIN = '/usr/bin/sudo';\n+$SYSTEMCTL_BIN = '/bin/systemctl';\n+$RESTART_EXPORTER_CMD = 'service taxify-process-exporter restart';\n+$NOTIFY_NODE_MONITOR = '/bin/touch /var/log/apt/history.log';\n+\n+%rc = ( # responseCodes\n+ 'OK' => 0,\n+ 'PACKAGE_ERROR' => 10,\n+ 'DEPLOY_ERROR' => 20,\n+ 'ALREADY_INSTALLED' => 30,\n+ 'PURGE_ERROR' => 40,\n+ 'RESTART_ERROR' => 50,\n+ 'HEALTH_ERROR' => 60,\n+ 'VERSION_ERROR' => 70,\n+ 'STOP_ERROR' => 80,\n+ 'START_ERROR' => 90,\n+ 'ACCESS_DENY' => 666,\n+ 'SERVER_ERROR' => 999,\n+);\n+\n+# Process an HTTP request\n+my $q = CGI->new;\n+our $user = $q->param('user');\n+our $pkg_name = $q->param('pkg');\n+our $pkg_ver = $q->param('ver');\n+our $action = $q->param('action');\n+our $service_names = $q->param('services');\n+\n+my @allow_ip_ranges = (\n+ '127.0.0.1/32', # local\n+ '172.31.6.252/32', # builder\n+ '52.28.83.184/32', # builder\n+ '217.159.229.88/32', # bolt HQ\n+ '172.29.32.32/32', # jenkins\n+ '3.126.191.40/32', # jenkins\n+ '172.17.0.0/18', # prelive-eks\n+ '172.17.128.0/18', # prelive-eks\n+ '172.17.64.0/18', # prelive-eks\n+ '172.18.0.0/16', # live-eks\n+ '172.19.0.0/16', # live-eks\n+ '172.20.0.0/16', # live-kes\n+);\n+\n+# examples:\n+# ?pkg=taxify-htdocs-dispatcher&ver=20141121-1332-943973f&user=Oliver\n+\n+our $remote_ip = $ENV{'HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR'};\n+$remote_ip = $ENV{'REMOTE_ADDR'} unless ($remote_ip);\n+\n+if (!whitelist_ips($remote_ip, @allow_ip_ranges)) {\n+ &send_response('ACCESS_DENY', 'Access denied', {});\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+unless (&isExecutable($APT_BIN)) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'SERVER_ERROR'},'Apt-Get binary not found',{});\n+ exit;\n+}\n+unless (&isExecutable($MARK_BIN)) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'SERVER_ERROR'},'Apt-Mark binary not found',{});\n+ exit;\n+}\n+unless (&isExecutable($SUDO_BIN)) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'SERVER_ERROR'},'Sudo binary not found',{});\n+ exit;\n+}\n+unless ($pkg_name =~ m,^(taxify|bolt)-,) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'PACKAGE_ERROR'},'Unknown package',{});\n+ exit;\n+}\n+if ($action eq 'purge' && $pkg_name) {\n+ &do_purgepackage();\n+}\n+if ($action eq 'restart' && $pkg_name) {\n+ &do_restartpackage();\n+}\n+if ($action eq 'stop' && $pkg_name && $service_names) {\n+ &do_stopservices();\n+}\n+if ($action eq 'start' && $pkg_name) {\n+ &do_startservices();\n+}\n+if ($action eq 'health' && $pkg_name) {\n+ &do_healthpackage();\n+}\n+if ($action eq 'version' && $pkg_name) {\n+ &do_versionpackage();\n+}\n+if ($pkg_name && $pkg_ver) {\n+ &do_installpackage();\n+}\n+\n+&send_response($rc{'SERVER_ERROR'},'Bad action',{});\n+exit;\n+\n+#### funktsioonid ####\n+\n+sub do_installpackage {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my %data = ();\n+ my $aptUpdateFailed = 0;\n+ for (1..2) { # retry if first time fails\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $APT_BIN update -o Dir::Etc::sourcelist=sources.list.d/taxify.list -o Dir::Etc::sourceparts=- -o APT::Get::List-Cleanup=0\");\n+ $data{'repo-update'} = $stdout;\n+ if ($?) {\n+ $aptUpdateFailed = 1;\n+ sleep 1;\n+ } else {\n+ $aptUpdateFailed = 0;\n+ last;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($aptUpdateFailed) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'DEPLOY_ERROR'},'Deploy failed',\\%data);\n+ exit;\n+ }\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $APT_BIN -y --force-yes -o 'Dpkg::Options::=--force-confmiss' -o 'Dpkg::Options::=--force-confnew' install $pkg_name=$pkg_ver\");\n+ $data{'install'} = $stdout;\n+ my $isSuccess = 0;\n+ for (split(/\\n/,$stdout)) {\n+ if (/Setting up $pkg_name/) {\n+ $isSuccess = 1;\n+ }\n+ elsif (/$pkg_name is already the newest version/) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'ALREADY_INSTALLED'},'Package is already installed',\\%data);\n+ exit;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($isSuccess) {\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $MARK_BIN hold $pkg_name\");\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $RESTART_EXPORTER_CMD\");\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'},'OK',\\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'DEPLOY_ERROR'},'Deploy failed',\\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub do_purgepackage {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $APT_BIN -y --force-yes purge $pkg_name\");\n+ my %data = ('purge' => $stdout);\n+ my $isSuccess = 0;\n+ for (split(/\\n/,$stdout)) {\n+ if (/Purging configuration files for $pkg_name/) {\n+ $isSuccess = 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($isSuccess) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'},'OK',\\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'PURGE_ERROR'},'Purge failed',\\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub do_restartpackage {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $NOTIFY_NODE_MONITOR\");\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN $SYSTEMCTL_BIN restart $pkg_name\");\n+ my $exit_code = $? >> 8; # Extracting the exit code from the $? variable\n+ my %data = ('restart' => $stdout);\n+\n+ if ($exit_code == 0) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'}, 'OK', \\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'RESTART_ERROR'}, 'Restart failed', \\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub do_stopservices {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN /etc/init.d/$pkg_name stop-services $service_names\");\n+ my %data = ('stop' => $stdout);\n+ my $isSuccess = 0;\n+ for (split(/\\n/, $stdout)) {\n+ if (/Stopping services $pkg_name/) {\n+ $isSuccess = 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($isSuccess) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'}, 'OK', \\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'STOP_ERROR'}, 'Stop failed', \\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub do_startservices {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN /etc/init.d/$pkg_name start-all\");\n+ my %data = ('start' => $stdout);\n+ my $isSuccess = 0;\n+ for (split(/\\n/, $stdout)) {\n+ if (/Starting all services $pkg_name/) {\n+ $isSuccess = 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($isSuccess) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'}, 'OK', \\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'START_ERROR'}, 'Start failed', \\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub do_healthpackage {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN /etc/init.d/$pkg_name health\");\n+ my %data = ('health' => $stdout);\n+ my $isSuccess = 0;\n+ for (split(/\\n/,$stdout)) {\n+ if (/Starting health check of $pkg_name/) {\n+ $isSuccess = 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($isSuccess) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'},'OK',\\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'HEALTH_ERROR'},'Health failed',\\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub do_versionpackage {\n+ $ENV{'USER'} = $user;\n+ my $stdout = &exec_program(\"$SUDO_BIN /etc/init.d/$pkg_name version\");\n+ my %data = ('version' => $stdout);\n+ my $isSuccess = 0;\n+ for (split(/\\n/,$stdout)) {\n+ if (/Querying version information of $pkg_name/) {\n+ $isSuccess = 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ if ($isSuccess) {\n+ &send_response($rc{'OK'},'OK',\\%data);\n+ } else {\n+ &send_response($rc{'VERSION_ERROR'},'Version failed',\\%data);\n+ }\n+ exit;\n+}\n+\n+sub send_response {\n+ my ($status, $message, $data) = @_;\n+\n+ my %result = (\n+ 'code' => $status,\n+ 'message' => $message,\n+ 'data' => $data,\n+ );\n+\n+ # Prepare various HTTP responses\n+ print $q->header(-type=>'application/json',-charset=>'utf-8');\n+ $json_coder = JSON::XS->new->utf8->pretty->allow_nonref;\n+ print $json_coder->encode(\\%result);\n+}\n+\n+sub isExecutable {\n+ my $cmdline = shift;\n+ return unless ($cmdline);\n+ my $cmd = $cmdline;\n+\n+ if ($cmdline =~ /\\s/) {\n+ ($cmd) = split(/\\s/,$cmdline);\n+ }\n+ if ( -x $cmd ) {\n+ return 1;\n+ }\n+ for (split(/:/, $ENV{'PATH'})) {\n+ if ( -x \"$_/$cmd\" ) {\n+ return 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+}\n+\n+sub esc_chars {\n+ # will change, for example, a!!a to a\\!\\!a\n+ $_[0] =~ s/([;<>\\*\\|`&\\$!#\\(\\)\\[\\]\\{\\}\"])/\\\\$1/g; #`:'\n+ return $_[0];\n+}\n+\n+sub whitelist_ips {\n+ my ($remote_ip, @allow_ip_ranges) = @_;\n+\n+ my $remote_ip_obj = NetAddr::IP->new($remote_ip);\n+\n+ foreach my $allow_ip_range (@allow_ip_ranges) {\n+ my $allow_ip_range_obj = NetAddr::IP->new($allow_ip_range);\n+\n+ if ($remote_ip_obj->within($allow_ip_range_obj)) {\n+ return 1;\n+ }\n+ }\n+ return 0;\n+}\n+\n+sub exec_program {\n+ my $cmdline = shift;\n+ &esc_chars($cmdline);\n+ system (\"/usr/bin/renice +19 $$ >/dev/null\") if (-x '/usr/bin/renice');\n+ system (\"/usr/bin/ionice -c 3 -p $$\") if (-x '/usr/bin/ionice');\n+ my $output;\n+ open PROG, \"$cmdline 2>&1 |\";\n+ while (<PROG>) {\n+ next if (/GPG error/); # hack. need better solution!\n+ $output .= decode('utf-8',$_);\n+ }\n+ close PROG;\n+ return $output;\n+}\nchanged: [cs-db-4]\nRUNNING HANDLER [db_vector : vector.restart] ***********************************\nfatal: [cs-db-4]: FAILED! =>\nchanged: false\nmsg: |-\nUnable to restart service vector: Job for vector.service failed because the control process exited with error code.\nSee \"systemctl status vector.service\" and \"journalctl -xeu vector.service\" for details.\nPLAY RECAP *********************************************************************\ncs-db-4 : ok=313 changed=121 unreachable=0 failed=1 skipped=52 rescued=0 ignored=1{noformat}","2026-01-15T07:43:01.719Z"],["3811231","PFI-833621","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","[^wise_transfer_confirmation__transfer__1917297120__7243160339__en.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-15T07:43:22.205Z"],["3811232","PFI-833622","PFI","pareena.klinkaewpa@bolt-outsource.eu","Pareena Klinkaewpa","!image-20260115-074047.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-074329.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-074337.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T07:43:43.740Z"],["3811233","PFI-833595","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers payment has failed due to an error message Rejected due to high risk and received the status PAYMENT_ERROR_FRAUD (327). \n\nCould you please ask the user to check with their bank if there are any restrictions placed on their card. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n","2026-01-15T07:44:16.003Z"],["3811237","PFI-833354","PFI","fahmin.mikayilov@bolt.eu","Fahmin Mikayilov","Hey, [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b]. here the statement. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.47.44.png|width=828,height=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.47.44.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T07:45:22.918Z"],["3811238","HS-28918","HS","valentina.nicolosi@bolt.eu","Valentina Nicolosi","hi!\n\nI didnt seem to receive just yet can you try again please?\n\nRegards,\n\nValentina","2026-01-15T07:45:49.644Z"],["3811239","HS-28918","HS","valentina.nicolosi@bolt.eu","Valentina Nicolosi","Found it!","2026-01-15T07:46:18.455Z"],["3811240","PFI-833623","PFI","nikita.kasparovics@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikita Kasparovics","!IMG_8017.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T07:46:22.951Z"],["3811241","WFM-10001","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:5da9601913c16d0c35b93523] ,\n\nSince you already have CS - Rides role, it will not be necessary to extend the permission - it is already in this role.","2026-01-15T07:46:41.215Z"],["3811242","PFI-813484","PFI","fahmin.mikayilov@bolt.eu","Fahmin Mikayilov","hey, [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b]. here the statement.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.47.44.png|width=828,height=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.47.44.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T07:46:55.837Z"],["3811243","DSR-3759","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-15T07:47:04.167Z"],["3811244","EBIKE1-369","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","We will do vibration test on EB1.2 frame where we will add these Nord lock washers and apply 60Nm. Only motor will be assembled without wheel parts. ","2026-01-15T07:47:22.044Z"],["3811245","EBIKE1-390","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Next week [~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec]  will go to LY to test them out. \n\nLet’s try to test Okai crank arm as well as we have a good feedback from the market.","2026-01-15T07:48:59.181Z"],["3811246","WD-22575","WD","lysette.ranne@bolt.eu","Lysette Ranne","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 09.48.34.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 09.48.43.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Telema.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T07:49:10.611Z"],["3811247","DRX-28206","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DA.126.0 (1507) Firebase build on Google Pixel 8 Pro, OS:16\n\n!screen-20260115-092449.mp4|width=320,alt=\"screen-20260115-092449.mp4\"!","2026-01-15T07:50:47.284Z"],["3811250","PFI-833625","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","[^Receipt-2026-01-09 161753.172258.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-15T07:51:49.092Z"],["3811252","PFI-833566","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 270.00 ZAR was issued on 01/01/2026, 09:12:43UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 31st of December to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:52:22.957Z"],["3811254","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Rundeck for the below fix\n* [https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139422|https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139422]","2026-01-15T07:53:01.464Z"],["3811255","LSS-60142","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:712020:57b36b99-7144-476f-a96e-ee6e8296217c], thanks! \nI have reviewed and updated [the document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kQPrSsfOK4o-1x3egg-YRJr7g3EHFv5-/edit].\n\nPlease see the comments, thanks! ","2026-01-15T07:53:21.288Z"],["3811256","SCM-1112","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","[~accountid:712020:a39b930f-52b0-4732-9cfa-d8a1b4a18ccd] let me check with insurance team if they need anything else. ","2026-01-15T07:53:22.409Z"],["3811257","LSS-51065","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:61b9ef0e9e8a370068af893c], should this ticket still be open or can I close it ? Thank you ! ","2026-01-15T07:53:37.720Z"],["3811258","PFI-833553","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-15T07:53:59.983Z"],["3811261","CNT-431","CNT","adam.cherry@bolt.eu","Adam Cherry","[~accountid:712020:c9a5e707-0d6d-488a-bafd-1418ebf8e556] Thanks for this! We’ll send the copy back to you to check once it’s ready.","2026-01-15T07:54:27.747Z"],["3811262","SCM-1113","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","[~accountid:712020:a39b930f-52b0-4732-9cfa-d8a1b4a18ccd] We need the date we moved from the warehouse, so it should be end of contract date.","2026-01-15T07:55:00.445Z"],["3811263","PFI-833539","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 10.80 on Dec 19, 2025, 23:13:20 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505353004877637095  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 19th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_WD6ZTK7ZJ6FN26Z3_H967943JH9RC7CZ3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:55:07.612Z"],["3811265","PFI-833536","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for GBP 54.08 on Dec 29, 2025, 16:21:07 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 17979675363001459343223  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 29th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_TTZWM8HK6F25DWG6_MWTZGBZ46DQBCBZ3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:56:07.736Z"],["3811267","PFI-833531","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:56:53.884Z"],["3811268","PFI-833626","PFI","leyla.mammadova@bolt.eu","Leyla Mammadova","Rider may be blocked, need to know what to do with the negative balance.","2026-01-15T07:57:04.051Z"],["3811269","LSS-61288","LSS","stephanie.oreoluwa@bolt.eu","Stephanie Oreoluwa","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Can I share the SLA that highlighted your concerns with the client, so they can address it?","2026-01-15T07:57:13.020Z"],["3811271","PFI-833419","PFI","laura.grota@bolt-outsource.eu","Laura Grota","Cashout was sent to wrong bank account, is it possible to return the cashout to the original bank account?","2026-01-15T07:57:57.462Z"],["3811272","PFI-833524","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 14.00 GBP on 10/10/2025, 08:24:01UTC\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 75184895283136649593285  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 10th of October until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Proof of Refund 10-10-2025.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T07:58:18.200Z"],["3811275","HS-28749","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-15T07:59:23.653Z"],["3811276","MVRT-1446","MVRT","evamaria.ots@bolt.eu","Eva Maria Ots","[~accountid:712020:a68bad68-4d18-4aca-aaf7-10e00df84534] the current prices are: \n\n* Local: €0.6 unlock + €0.23\n* Tourist: €0.75 unlock + €0.23\n\nBut they might change in 1-2 weeks. ","2026-01-15T07:59:40.472Z"],["3811279","PFI-833627","PFI","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","!Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 08.59.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T08:00:02.686Z"],["3811280","LSS-61477","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] As the new contracts have not been uploaded online, the drivers would be signing the conditions for the old compensation (8% + 100€) the new tiered offer could be seen as misleading: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-51060|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-51060|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:00:13.518Z"],["3811281","PFI-833627","PFI","tomasz.symonowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Symonowicz","cc [~accountid:62b9a75a37780d89a3507d57] ","2026-01-15T08:00:22.738Z"],["3811282","PRODSEC-576","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Download works. Improvement plan is to move it from my ownership to the team.","2026-01-15T08:00:42.493Z"],["3811284","LSS-59216","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:7709bc17-997f-4b44-90ce-cd544e26178c] hey, please see below the draft with the comments and revisions that you can share with the partner. Please discuss with them the points they raised regarding the equipment provision, restriction on audit of the performance of the services, agreement term, etc., to be aligned on commercial terms before we proceed with further revisions.\n\nPlease also ask them to check Appendix 1 in Annex 2 and fill in their details. cc [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/147pMLDeLmzT1O99xSN3TN9o4Q7TbLPntPPm1qUmieu0/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/147pMLDeLmzT1O99xSN3TN9o4Q7TbLPntPPm1qUmieu0/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:01:15.822Z"],["3811286","LSS-61255","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hi there [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] Yes you are correct. \n\nBolt will move from 14&15th floors, to 15th&16th floors under this lease. \n\nTo answer your question, myself, [~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3] & [~accountid:641c083b2cee496759ec3ff2] are looking through the contract now and aim to have it checked completely by Monday morning. I hope to have a meeting with Brannicks early next week to start further negotiations. |\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T08:01:26.816Z"],["3811287","SCM-1113","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] okay, all clear, I will discuss it with Marko to have it added in WD","2026-01-15T08:01:50.111Z"],["3811290","PFI-833521","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Fraud team, \n\nWould you be able to whitelist the user so they could delete their account. \nThey have a negative balance of 8.33 EUR, but unable to pay it because they are located in Hungary. ","2026-01-15T08:02:11.507Z"],["3811291","LSS-61430","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Confirmation: no legal recommendation was given last year, only a general guidance from compliance understanding that there was a reclassification risk.","2026-01-15T08:02:20.618Z"],["3811293","HS-28493","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Sent documents to PP","2026-01-15T08:03:08.428Z"],["3811296","BDB-1461","BDB","alexsandra.kruusberg@bolt.eu","Alexsandra Kruusberg","Hello! \n\nHopp Plus logos are here: [https://www.figma.com/design/5BTLqdnPbNJG8x14TLitbA/Logos?node-id=1834-16&t=r75OY2f3zH7fjhrg-1|https://www.figma.com/design/5BTLqdnPbNJG8x14TLitbA/Logos?node-id=1834-16&t=r75OY2f3zH7fjhrg-1|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:03:43.207Z"],["3811297","BDB-1482","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] hey! They told me that there is still something wrong with the dimensions. I asked once again about dimensions and they said: Dimensions: 6,20 m x 2,90 m and shared once again the template. I don’t understand what is wrong, as the template is completely different from the dimensions they are sharing. Do you understand? ","2026-01-15T08:03:53.770Z"],["3811299","CAMLE-9415","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","Status update:\nDiscussion was held around the scope and agreement was reached that we do not want to add support for 1 campaign : N periods usecase. more context can be found in the design document [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7384498666/Rejected+-+Design+Doc+-+Driver+conditional+campaigns+multiple+periods]","2026-01-15T08:04:42.886Z"],["3811302","LSS-61248","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi team,\n\nwe have an update regarding the complimentary gifts and prizes. All participants will receive a coffee voucher for circle k and 20 drivers will receive earphones worth 49 Eur. Earphone winners will be chosen randomly.\n\nThanks","2026-01-15T08:04:59.443Z"],["3811305","MVRT-1446","MVRT","lorrayne.oliveira@bolt.eu","Lorrayne Corais","[~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3] Thank you!","2026-01-15T08:05:51.353Z"],["3811306","CAMLE-9414","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","[discussion|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7QN72NG2/p1768398934447429?thread_ts=1768396082.952809&cid=C0A7QN72NG2] held and decided not required on our path to migration to driver conditional campaigns from driver campaigns.","2026-01-15T08:05:53.323Z"],["3811308","CAMLE-9414","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","sticking with 1:1 campaign/period mapping and 1:N cases will be handling by using bundle instead","2026-01-15T08:06:28.126Z"],["3811309","GRN-106","GRN","irina.nedelcu@bolt.eu","Irina Nedelcu","Implemented and merged: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160703|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160703|smart-link], the error log is not at [notice level|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/zCbM4]. Once a long term fix is applied we’ll consider putting back the error log level","2026-01-15T08:06:37.767Z"],["3811310","RS-1950","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] , due to the nature of the crime, I think we can proceed with the disclosure. The amount of the data is not large as well","2026-01-15T08:07:28.500Z"],["3811314","CEBF-1828","CEBF","oleg.demkiv@bolt.eu","Oleh Demkiv","[~accountid:712020:ed2533e0-41fa-49c6-9812-aa965d995be0] [~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] need estimation for this ticket","2026-01-15T08:07:55.636Z"],["3811315","PFI-833629","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked all of the payments and I can confirm that everything looks fine on Bolt’s end. \n\nPlease note that according to financial regulations no merchant is able to keep the reserved funds for more than 30 days. It means that the pre-authorized funds have been released to the customer. \n\nIt’s in Bolt’s interest to release the authorized amount as soon as possible. We release it as soon as the payment reaches it’s final state (Captured in this case) \n\nThe users bank should be able to locate the authorizations with the date and the amount. \nYou can also provide the user the ARN references to locate the authorizations. \nThese can be found in the payment logs. \n\nPayment > Attempts > Authorisation > Authorize > ctrl + F “ARN”\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T08:08:37.870Z"],["3811317","LSS-61607","LSS","domantas.dabrukas@bolt.eu","Domantas Dabrukas","[^Vilniaus vandenys UAB. Specialiosios sąlygos. Bolt Business  (2) (1).adoc]\n\n","2026-01-15T08:09:58.153Z"],["3811318","PRIV-547","PRIV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Legal research from Rides launch: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aPbphuMeMc7f9AgUGpFtYkfJEmOqBNnP/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aPbphuMeMc7f9AgUGpFtYkfJEmOqBNnP/edit|smart-link] \n\n\n\n||Data Localization||:white_x_pink_background: (Data transfers to EU permitted :green-check: )||\n|Legitimate Interest Legal Basis|:white_x_pink_background:|\n|Registration Requirements|:white_x_pink_background:|\n|Use Bolt’s Group DPO|:green-check:|\n|Special processes / permits to process ID docs|:white_x_pink_background:|\n|Biometric processing|Apparently there may be special requirements once the Executive Regulations are published.|\n|ADM reporting to Authority|:white_x_pink_background:|\n\n\n\n* Governing law: *Federal Law No. 45 of 2021* (the UAE Data Protection Law → applies extraterritorially similarly as GDPR – similar to GDPR\n* DFIC Data Protection Law (The Data Protection Law DIFC Law No. 5 of 2020) → Applies only to controller or processor incorporated in the DFIC.\n\n\n\nInternational data transfers to EU should be OK – to clarify once we have better understanding of the setup\n\n* According to Article 26 of the DIFC Data Protection Law, transferring Personal Data outside the DIFC is only allowed if the receiving jurisdiction ensures an adequate level of protection\n\n\n\n*Legal Bases:*\n\n# consent of the data subject.\n# necessity of the processing for the performance of a contract, the fulfilment of legal obligations, the protection of public interest, the protection of the data subject's interests, or the exercise of rights in the field of employment, social security or social protection.\n# availability of proper protection level in the state or province to which the personal data is transferred, or the existence of a bilateral or multilateral agreement on personal data protection.\n# explicit consent of the data subject, or the necessity of the processing for certain purposes, such as judicial cooperation, public health, or claiming or defending rights, in case of transferring personal data to a state or province that does not have proper protection level.\n\n\n\n*Sensitive data category:* any data which directly or indirectly reveals a natural person's family, ethnic origin, political or philosophical opinions, religious beliefs, criminal record, biometric data, or any data relating to such person's health and physical, psychological, mental, genetic or sexual condition, including information related to the provision of healthcare services to him/her which reveals his/her health status. Sensitive Personal Data can only be processed with the explicit consent of the Data Subject, unless one of the exceptions listed in Article 4 applies.\n\n\n\n*Marketing:* hard opt in required\n\n\n\nNo mandatory registration requirements → double check if still applicable\n\n\n\n*Data Breach Reporting:* The controller must notify the Bureau of any breach or violation of personal data that would prejudice the privacy, confidentiality, and security of data, within the period and in accordance with the measures and requirements set by the Executive Regulations.\n\n\n\n*DSR:* access, erasure, transparency, object to ADM, contact controller, withdraw consent, rectify\n\n\n\n*Penalties:* monetary & criminal liability","2026-01-15T08:10:12.320Z"],["3811321","FDBT-4793","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_data_integration_processout fails on 2026-01-14 03:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_data_integration_processout/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-14T03%3A00%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=processout_settlements_raw_task&base_date=2026-01-14T03%3A00%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-15T08:11:31.302Z"],["3811323","PFI-833427","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the previous SD ticket that was raised. \n\nWe can confirm the refund was not applied. Could you retry sending the refund again?\n\nPlease note that customer payments team does not have any accesses to issue refund to the Bolt balance. This refund needs to be issued by the CS team. If you need any assistance with the refund then you can reach out to your team lead. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T08:13:27.706Z"],["3811324","LSS-61608","LSS","domantas.dabrukas@bolt.eu","Domantas Dabrukas","[^Vyriausybės atstovų įstaiga. Specialiosios sąlygos. Bolt Business  (1).adoc]\n\n","2026-01-15T08:13:48.285Z"],["3811325","MVRT-1446","MVRT","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","[~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3] thanks for sharing! But just to clarify - how do we define tourists? 🤨 We can’t really show 2 different prices in comms, so just trying to understand which one should be shown. Probably local ones?","2026-01-15T08:13:54.969Z"],["3811327","DO-5797","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Hey [~accountid:631aec119796033b256e3421] 👋 \n\nWe will proceed after approval from Aleksei.","2026-01-15T08:14:19.520Z"],["3811329","BDO-3157","BDO","mattias.moisto@bolt.eu","Mattias Moisto","Hello!\nParking has been restricted in front of Lauliku 57. We will not restrict it more, the land belongs to the city and our cars are allowed to park there. Snow clearing is a problem everywhere, if needed the user can re-park the car and we can refund it to them. ","2026-01-15T08:15:02.852Z"],["3811330","BDB-1525","BDB",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Lars-Erik Lunden 👋. This is a reminder, that the task is due today or it's resolved but hasn't been moved to \"Done\" status yet.\n\n- If the task is resolved, move it to the \"Done\" status. Or if the task is canceled, move it to \"Canceled\" status\n\n- If the task can't be resolved in the initial timeframe, then make sure that the Project Manager(Team Lead, in case PM is not available), and Customer are notified. And change the new due date accordingly.","2026-01-15T08:15:13.971Z"],["3811331","DBRE-8615","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","By the [dashboard|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/dbre-s3-cost-optimization/dbre-s3-backup-cost-optimization?orgId=1] we dont have any recommendations for using Glacier. Standard S3 is valid on current setup. My assumption is that  we doing daily basis backup restores ","2026-01-15T08:15:25.043Z"],["3811332","SUPX-2320","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Duplicate of  [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2323?actionerId=631f27278738d3ca32254937&sourceType=assign|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2323?actionerId=631f27278738d3ca32254937&sourceType=assign|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:15:38.310Z"],["3811334","PFI-833168","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Correct value imported now https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/77178001 ","2026-01-15T08:16:54.849Z"],["3811335","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] do we also need to review the terms in the order form ? Is it renewal or we are adding a new service from Zendesk ? ","2026-01-15T08:17:06.301Z"],["3811336","FDBT-4795","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-15T08:17:15.883Z"],["3811337","CEBF-1832","CEBF","oleg.demkiv@bolt.eu","Oleh Demkiv","[~accountid:6218cbe4468c2e007170c08b] will inform Merchant Success about need to update triggers","2026-01-15T08:17:45.628Z"],["3811345","LSS-56128","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Please collect the signature of Ahto on this letter: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1k6SlZMYS5VhZyaJry8ydxhT9c3t1wRFL/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1k6SlZMYS5VhZyaJry8ydxhT9c3t1wRFL/edit|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T08:20:25.872Z"],["3811348","LSS-60984","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] , I agree with your approach. [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] , please continue pushing the authority to resend the correct version of the request with a clear explanation. I think Gabriele’s message explains the situation very detailly, you can follow the same approach ","2026-01-15T08:20:46.168Z"],["3811349","SCM-1087","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","Initial information is collected [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/167vCLMxgn_iDm-JsM9bquS9a7vbZa_dWdhcyEA9XGjM/edit?gid=0#gid=0]. \nHowever, due to delayed responses caused by Christmas/New Year time, I will postpone the deadline for this task by one week, as I still wait for quotes and more information from some companies.","2026-01-15T08:20:55.866Z"],["3811350","PFI-833426","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T08:21:08.204Z"],["3811351","RDS-1257","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] I assume it is not often, but it is a critical issue when it appears. \n\nWe are also working on improving Delivery visibility and expanding to new markets (the goal is to double GMV% here), which will make the issue more common. IMO, we should prioritize it and treat it as a part of the delivery expansion. ","2026-01-15T08:21:11.760Z"],["3811355","GEORM-445","GEORM","akos.nagy@bolt.eu","Akos Nagy","Was this item created from my comment on Slack or something else? [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NS2H0C48/p1768304132683729?thread_ts=1768301589.309579&cid=C09NS2H0C48|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09NS2H0C48/p1768304132683729?thread_ts=1768301589.309579&cid=C09NS2H0C48|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:23:32.201Z"],["3811356","BD-1979","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","Released on {{2026-01-15}}","2026-01-15T08:23:42.574Z"],["3811357","WD-22576","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Henelin, hope you are well. Please can you let me know which tickets you are referring to?","2026-01-15T08:23:50.481Z"],["3811358","LSS-60707","LSS","oldrich.plechacek@bolt.eu","Oldřich Plecháček","Thank you very much! For a followup reaciton:\n\n1) It is doable for fleets and drivers to terminate the agreement on short notice. In practice, it just means they lose the bonus eligibility. Despite it being in the T&Cs, we don’t normally enforce the requirement for the drivers to de-brand the vehicle and provide us with proof, only in very rare cases. So please, go through with the change to 7 days notice.\n\n2) Regarding this\n\n{color:#36b37e}*If greater flexibility is required, the clause would need to be amended to:*{color}\n\n* {color:#36b37e}*carve out exceptions (e.g. for incentive mechanics), or*{color}\n* {color:#36b37e}*allow certain changes to apply during an ongoing Incentive Period with appropriate notice.*{color}\n\nCould it maybe be solved by just changing the T&C listed incentive period to 7 days, always going Mon-Sun? I think this would make more sense, as the bonus campaigns are always set up for this period anyways.\n\n3) Changes to bonus requirements - thank you for the info. We never change the conditions retroactively or for an ongoing campaign. Generally we inform the drivers that a change will take place starting from next week’s campaign.\n\nNoted about the translations, we will be counting on checking them once the draft is ready. Thank you ","2026-01-15T08:23:51.805Z"],["3811359","HS-28971","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Ann! To get access to your chosen benefit, please fill out this form [+here+|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfuToPY0MitacbQkG7ID1_uYOnRaZbkew4_0gu9juDLwOtCJg/viewform].\n\nWe’ll be registering employees to benefits on the 23rd, so if you could make your choice by that time then that would be perfect.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-15T08:23:55.939Z"],["3811360","LSS-59711","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2], I spoke to the Office of the Data Protection Officer (ODPO) and the Risk & Compliance teams, and confirmed that we do not have visibility into or control over the operational handling of CCTV systems, including technical capabilities, access setup, incident workflows, or on-site processes.\n\nExtending CCTV retention to 14 days can be assessed and supported from a *privacy compliance perspective*, but implementation and justification based on operational needs (e.g. fire investigations, insurance) must be owned by *Physical Security team*. \n\nThe process for immediate download and preservation of footage after incidents is an operational control and must be defined and executed by Physical Security to prevent loss of evidence.\n\nQuestions around access management, centralization, avoidance of single-person dependency, and contingency plans fall entirely under Physical Security ownership, as system owner.\n\nPrivacy’s role is to set compliance guardrails and provide recommendations, not to design or implement CCTV operating procedures. \n\n*Next steps and implementation* should be driven by the Physical Security team, with Privacy supporting as needed on compliance input. Tagging [~accountid:712020:6ea61242-681c-4fee-9add-2547487ff931] for visibility.\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d0c8f1621a5d30bc4e096a8] ","2026-01-15T08:24:10.064Z"],["3811361","PFI-833639","PFI","patrycja.florczuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Patrycja Florczuk","!SD.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T08:24:26.818Z"],["3811363","PRODSEC-715","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Potential improvement, need to switch from log to block/challange in some domains (some already have block)","2026-01-15T08:24:41.720Z"],["3811364","LSS-58717","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Hi [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab]! We are finally advancing with this campaign.\n\nCan you please help fill this additional form and confirm that the Agreement is ready to share back with partner?\n\nAlso can you confirm what are our two MIDs in the UK, for London & outside London. \n\nThanks in advance!\n\n[^Reward - New Starter Form1.docx]\n\n","2026-01-15T08:24:50.171Z"],["3811365","PFI-833424","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T08:25:01.971Z"],["3811366","DPLC-692","DPLC","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Morning,\nFYI: You're running some batch stuff in dataeng account({{451613234044}}) on ECS using legacy AL2 AMIs.\nThey'll be deprecated in June, please switch them to AL2023.\nExample: {{arn:aws:ecs:eu-central-1:451613234044:container-instance/default20240619092155073100000004_Batch_1eeba07d-f9ee-350c-be58-265d941bc957/021ef95543a543b79e6247cce399b102}}\n\n{quote} Key Points:\n* Amazon ECS-optimized AL2 AMI will reach EOL on June 30, 2026.\n* Customers should migrate their workloads from Amazon ECS-optimized AL2 AMI to Amazon ECS-optimized Amazon Linux 2023 (AL2023) AMI to continue receiving security updates and benefit from performance improvements.\n* The AL2023 based ECS-optimized AMIs are not guaranteed to be backward compatible with your existing application.{quote}","2026-01-15T08:25:13.449Z"],["3811367","DPLC-692","DPLC",null,"Slack","[Gazandi Cahyadarma|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:061a9010-0948-45f3-81ba-d6d4ba88b4bf] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01UMLG885S/p1768462245693199?thread_ts=1768462245.693199&cid=C01UMLG885S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01UMLG885S/p1768462245693199?thread_ts=1768462245.693199&cid=C01UMLG885S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T08:25:14.990Z"],["3811368","DPLC-692","DPLC","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Thanks. Looks like this is on *group-S06EESBBYSY*.","2026-01-15T08:25:15.341Z"],["3811369","DPLC-692","DPLC","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Thank you! We will create the ticket and do it before June 30, 2026 :bowing:","2026-01-15T08:25:16.147Z"],["3811371","LSS-60112","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Thank you [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] \n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] could you kindly assist with the signing please? Thanks a lot! ","2026-01-15T08:25:30.376Z"],["3811372","DPLC-692","DPLC","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Remove the workload if possible","2026-01-15T08:26:56.809Z"],["3811373","HS-28873","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Henelin is checking with PP regarding JT","2026-01-15T08:27:12.142Z"],["3811375","WD-22372","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","!image-20260115-082700.png|width=657,alt=\"image-20260115-082700.png\"!\n\n\nThanks, [~accountid:6390559a2acfad92d7b59f11] , this is updated. Plz review. \n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-15T08:27:24.261Z"],["3811376","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","H Beatrice\nI have reached out to the contact person from PWC regarding this request.\nDuring our supplier briefing, we were informed that we should present our proposed solution to this RFP, including our business approach, even if it were to deviate from their stated requirements.","2026-01-15T08:27:24.225Z"],["3811382","LSS-56334","LSS","patrick.frei@bolt.eu","Patrick Frei","Hey [~accountid:5d1b218591943f0d2ac52db0] AON reached out to me and asked if we are still interested to pursue this? Any update? Any critical blocker, otherwise let’s move forward?","2026-01-15T08:28:52.096Z"],["3811384","PFI-833639","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the payment and could not see any evidence that would suggest a double charge. \n\nPlease note that this payment consists of two transactions. \n\nAuthorization for 10.82 PLN\nCapture for 10.82 PLN \n\nThe user might see the authorization and the capture as separate transactions in their mobile banking app. \nI can confirm that the authorization has been released from Bolt as soon as the payment was captured. \n\nYou can instruct the user to confirm this with their bank. If they are still insisting on the double charge then please ask them to provide their bank statement and the payment operations team will investigate further. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n\n\n","2026-01-15T08:29:15.062Z"],["3811385","WD-22569","WD","annamaria.marist@bolt.eu","Anna-Maria Marist","Hi, its okay now, please deactivate them again. Thanks!","2026-01-15T08:29:25.696Z"],["3811386","RDS-423","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] [~accountid:627b6b8f19b1290068296d3b] I added a description from the team delivery ticket for clarity.","2026-01-15T08:29:56.898Z"],["3811388","HS-28892","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-15T08:30:20.933Z"],["3811390","RCE-84","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sudipto Das [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768465825552869]*{color}:\nThanks <@U01NNTGRXD0> for the broader context and thank you for sharing the regulation.\n\nAs per the regulation, this is what I get as per Art 23 &amp; 24 mentioned for _hoja de ruta_\n• Present before the service begins;\n• Carried on board the vehicle during the service; and\n• Stored by the fleet company for at least one year for inspection by transport authorities.\nEach _hoja de ruta_ must, at a minimum, include:\n• Name and national identity number or tax identification code of the provider (fleet/company).\n• Name and ID number(optional) of the customer \n• Place, date and time at which the service is to begin\n• Place, date and time at which the service is scheduled to end\n• Vehicle registration number (matrícula) used for the service.\nSo waybills and fleets to have the ability to download and retain for a year are key considerations for ES as per this regulation.\n\n&gt; • A rough estimate of how many  waybills we weren’t able to provide in time, and potential cost to us\n&gt; • % of time drawn from CS\n<@U01NNTGRXD0> even with the original ask of bulk download by Ops, this issue will remain and will be a cost we bear as a biz. Any rough estimates here would be helpful. :pray::skin-tone-3:\n\n<@U9T7W8KUP> Lets review with the above OPEX values and discuss this.\n\ncc <@U09D62DKH9P> For your visibility as well. :pray::skin-tone-3:\n{quote}","2026-01-15T08:30:41.980Z"],["3811391","LSS-61598","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","SD: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343113|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343113|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:30:46.486Z"],["3811393","LSS-58070","LSS","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Thanks for the update Gabriele.","2026-01-15T08:31:28.465Z"],["3811394","LSS-61584","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:5cf40694-0837-4f72-b92a-c4936529065f]! Thanks for reaching out. I reviewed the draft and added it here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1K20M5jGsBZZjkEtQKEFil5K6RC3AWvZO/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=107030908950286443607&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1K20M5jGsBZZjkEtQKEFil5K6RC3AWvZO/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=107030908950286443607&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link].\n\nI changed a few small things in the details of the partner and our signatory from Ahto to Nikolai. One important change that I made was that I removed clause 4 about lower agency fee and added Agency Fee for delivery by Delivery Partner below “date of conclusion” to be 10%. This is because you were not offering lower agency fee and the text related to standard delivery and not ROD. This does not hurt if Partner will be offering only ROD and just provide some clarity.\n\nI have sent the agreement for signing, you can track the progress here: [https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343112|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343112|smart-link].","2026-01-15T08:31:57.089Z"],["3811395","RS-1945","RS","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Hey [~accountid:5da0457bea65c10c3fdc180f] \n\nWe have a similar setup in other markets as well, where we have tenured Tier 1 agents supporting Tier 2. However,  Law Enforcement Requests are still out of scope, as our policy around such requests is that they are fully handled in-house. I’m fine for this new team to support with ANPC requests (consumer protection) as the KB anyway suggests discussing such cases with the Legal Counsel through Service Desk. If ANPC requests data about a user, then the in-house team would need to take over. \n\n*To further elaborate on the why:*\n\n# Recently, we have seen an increase in data breaches, many of which were directly linked to CS human errors (specifically outsourced). These incidents have forced us to report violations to data protection authorities, exposing us to potential fines. Given this growing risk profile, we cannot afford additional vulnerabilities.\n# Authority requests involve data of individuals suspected of crimes. Any mishandling, such as unauthorised disclosure or procedural errors, exposes Bolt to legal claims for user distress and comes with significant reputational damage.\n# Authority requests are not standard CS tickets; they are legal documents. Interactions with the police and judicial bodies are high-stakes. They expect us to process these requests with the highest level of confidentiality. Keeping this in-house allows us to limit data access/processing to a small, vetted group. Moving this to an outsourced supplier would also require granting additional system access to facilitate data gathering.\n# While outsourcing might offer operational relief, a single mishandled request could result in GDPR violations, penalties or lawsuits that would far outweigh any savings gained from shifting the workload.\n\n*We recommend:*\n\n* Maintaining the current process, where such requests are handled by a specialised, trained in-house team with controlled access and oversight.\n* Ensuring that only designated and trained employees within our internal CS, CS Privacy Compliance, Risk and Privacy teams process these requests, in line with our GDPR and security obligations.\n\n","2026-01-15T08:32:00.244Z"],["3811396","PFI-833550","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","hi team, any update?\n\n","2026-01-15T08:32:47.490Z"],["3811397","LSS-60028","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] - do we have a new notary time in place for this? 🙏 ","2026-01-15T08:33:17.956Z"],["3811398","DSR-2285","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] - another ping on this. Could you please advise on a draft answer to the lawyer?\n\n\nRecap:\n\n* The driver does not agree with the suspension decision concerning his account. \n* The driver’s legal representative, as per the driver’s request, is planning on bringing this matter before the court. They are asking whether Bolt can agree to deviate from NL TnC clause 15.1 (see below for convenience) by bringing the claim to the Amsterdam court:\n_15.1. The Terms and Conditions and the Agreement shall be governed by, construed, and enforced in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Estonia. If any dispute arising from the Agreement (including these Terms and Conditions) cannot be resolved through negotiations, the dispute shall be settled by the Harju County District Court._","2026-01-15T08:34:01.062Z"],["3811399","LSS-55043","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","This will come through DocuSign, need to check Ahto inbox.","2026-01-15T08:34:16.336Z"],["3811401","LSS-55043","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:5e3bcefc-e2ed-4de9-8197-663f375263bd] - any status updates here? 🙂 ","2026-01-15T08:34:51.448Z"],["3811402","LSS-60028","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi, not yet - I will revert to this topic starting from next week. Thanks!","2026-01-15T08:35:13.910Z"],["3811403","CSDA-294","CSDA",null,"Viola Nzyimi","Hi [~accountid:6419ad769d6383e32a32888a] , \n\nYes, The reason we had the ow usage was the person manning that domain in KE moved to a different venture. Right now [~accountid:712020:fb945a5a-397e-4997-bf7d-469ff91b31a0] is owning that KPI, and she would like to receive personalised feedback on bolt send from a support perspective and see how the product can be improved. . ","2026-01-15T08:35:16.295Z"],["3811404","LSS-60545","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:62c696a740923988ba0ae796],\n\nAttached you will find the adendum signed by Bolt’s legal representative. \n\nNow you can proceed with the signature by Prosegur. Once they sign it, I kindly ask you to include in this ticket the signed copy of the adendum. \n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nBest,\n\nAngela ","2026-01-15T08:35:50.210Z"],["3811408","LSS-50764","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] note: once Ahto signs the agreements, please upload them here in the ticket. [~accountid:5cd9daa0bc70090d6ce26227] will send them back to the counterparties to sign 🙂 Thank you! 😇 ","2026-01-15T08:36:07.066Z"],["3811410","LSS-60076","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Jan 09_Certinal Order Form_Bolt.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T08:36:18.545Z"],["3811412","LSS-57405","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] - may we please ask for the signed doc for archiving purposes? Thank you! 🙂","2026-01-15T08:36:29.339Z"],["3811413","LSS-60545","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","[^Adenda-BOLT Prosegur 2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T08:36:52.382Z"],["3811415","WFM-9996","WFM","ana.radmilo@bolt.eu","Ana Radmilo","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 09.36.26.png|width=1121,height=463,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 09.36.26.png\"!\n\nHere is the screenshot.","2026-01-15T08:36:57.997Z"],["3811417","LSS-60974","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Hi [~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c], I reviewed the documents and can confirm that we can sign vendor’s DPA given the limited scope of personal data processing. \n\nPlease make sure that the Zero Data Retention functionality is enabled within the Service during the trial. \n\nHave you opened a ticket for Legal review as well? ","2026-01-15T08:37:52.177Z"],["3811420","LSS-57973","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","Likely done by Legal Ops side - pinging Thiago for confirmation to close the ticket.","2026-01-15T08:37:56.440Z"],["3811425","LSS-61589","LSS","klaudia.bochenko@bolt.eu","Klaudia Bochenko","!Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 09.36.34.png|width=1453,height=869,alt=\"Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 09.36.34.png\"!\n\n\n\n!Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 09.37.05.png|width=1495,height=958,alt=\"Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 09.37.05.png\"!\n\n\n\n!Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 09.37.29.png|width=1577,height=404,alt=\"Zrzut ekranu 2026-01-15 o 09.37.29.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-15T08:39:01.269Z"],["3811427","LSS-58403","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","Kirsika checking today if we can link with the device.","2026-01-15T08:39:11.837Z"],["3811428","RDS-618","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] [~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] should we split this ticket? With the current form, it feels like a big effort topic with multiple different issues inside. On the other hand, for example “Card expired” case feels like a clear case with a fairly limited scope and effort. ","2026-01-15T08:39:34.698Z"],["3811429","PFI-833646","PFI","ezinne.njoku@bolt-outsource.eu","Ezinne Njoku","[^transaction-confirmation-report_en_e423bb-1-1.pdf]","2026-01-15T08:40:03.545Z"],["3811430","LSS-59741","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:622f05a61c09d2007012deff] - any updates here? thanks! 🙂 ","2026-01-15T08:40:05.738Z"],["3811432","LSS-60715","LSS","silvia.plochanbenova@bolt.eu","Silvia Plocháň Beňová","[~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] with you","2026-01-15T08:40:34.493Z"],["3811433","DSR-2608","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] - no response needed on our end. \n\nI understand that the driver disagrees with the outcome of the suspension, but the block was placed and reviewed multiple times by the Safety team. We have provided the relevant data as per the driver’s request. At this point, there is nothing more we can do from our end.","2026-01-15T08:40:50.929Z"],["3811434","LSS-61332","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] - friendly ping, may we ask for access for [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]? Thanks!","2026-01-15T08:41:02.739Z"],["3811435","WEBSD-1476","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nThis is an article so the ticket should be created [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/4] . They should be able to help you with the changes need it.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-15T08:41:51.931Z"],["3811438","LSS-61500","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] - may we ask for your approval to proceed? thanks!","2026-01-15T08:42:01.779Z"],["3811439","PAI-922","PAI","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Currently discussing with [~accountid:5fbb62502730d800768e5f8c] ","2026-01-15T08:42:57.439Z"],["3811441","PFI-833647","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","[^SupplierRemittance.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-15T08:43:18.148Z"],["3811442","RDS-1207","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] [~accountid:712020:13244152-55c1-46c5-a6f1-86ca2de2c01c] IMO P1 Prio as it might a big impact (Sign-up flow is probably the only part of our product that have 100% reach).","2026-01-15T08:43:20.815Z"],["3811443","HS-28961","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:6360e1d41cc605b1fd17a60b], \n\nWe are required to include your ID card or passport information in the Visa Letter. I noticed that the copy of your ID card currently on file expires on 22.02.2026. Could you please send us a scanned copy of your new identification document so that I can include the updated details in the letter?\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-15T08:43:22.678Z"],["3811444","LSS-61606","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:60acb13f1155bb006fce252c] , please assess the validity of the claim from the business perspective first - it is valid, or you disagree. Please provide your arguments accordingly. Legal cannot assess it since we are not in charge of the commission. ","2026-01-15T08:43:56.575Z"],["3811446","LSS-59632","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","[~accountid:62567ec6a872710069210b83] just an update regarding this - we have provided all the documents to our external legal counsel and now waiting for the official registration of the new share capital to be completed. The process of registration is quite long and will take approx. 2-3 weeks.","2026-01-15T08:44:16.417Z"],["3811450","CSDA-296","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hi, Iuliia! Thank you for reaching out. We will create a dashboard that covers all Food Delivery delivery types (including Dine Out) and share here when ready. ETA: end of next week. ","2026-01-15T08:45:36.444Z"],["3811451","PFI-833641","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the payment and could not see any evidence that would suggest a double charge. \n\nPlease note that this payment consists of two transactions. \n\nAuthorization for 14.64 PLN \nCapture for 14.64 PLN \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4032144138|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4032144138]\n\nAuthorization for 12.90 PLN \nCapture for 12.90 PLN \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4032230298|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4032230298]\n\n\nThe user might see the authorization and the capture as separate transactions in their mobile banking app. \nI can confirm that the authorization has been released from Bolt as soon as the payment was captured. \n\nYou can instruct the user to confirm this with their bank. If they are still insisting on the double charge then please ask them to provide their bank statement and the payment operations team will investigate further. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T08:46:17.643Z"],["3811452","WFM-9960","WFM","jana.mariakova@bolt.eu","Jana Marjakova-Līdeka","Hello [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95], \r\n\r\nPlease clear the cookies and try to log in again. It should now work well. \r\n\r\nPlease come back if any issues with that? ","2026-01-15T08:46:44.140Z"],["3811453","HS-28918","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:8d1ed1b3-4c3e-44ca-814f-5d126cf277b8] all good. We have received your filled form 🙂 Thank you!","2026-01-15T08:46:47.953Z"],["3811455","RDS-1320","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] [~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] IMO prio P1: based on what I learned so far, driver's availability is clearly one of the most crucial problems to tackle, not only from UX but generally from a company’s success perspective. Therefore, any initiatives to reduce it may have a great impact. ","2026-01-15T08:48:47.530Z"],["3811456","IOTTEAM-219","IOTTEAM","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","[~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] BB charging test with CHG_EN HIGH. The max charging current of the charging controller is 500mA.\n\n!image-20260115-084816.png|width=250,alt=\"image-20260115-084816.png\"!\n\nTurning off the main supply didn’t create any glitches in MCU operation. ESP didn’t report BROWNOUTS or anything at 3.5V BB voltage","2026-01-15T08:48:50.151Z"],["3811458","PAW-14903","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-15T08:50:05.900Z"],["3811459","WFM-9995","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello,\n\nBL is available until the queue calms down.","2026-01-15T08:50:18.309Z"],["3811463","PFI-830547","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Hey [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \nIt’s weird cause these clients always receive…\nI asked in business tech support and they said the same thing as you so told me to ask billing…","2026-01-15T08:51:06.294Z"],["3811466","HS-28964","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Kevin, thank you for the request. I have prepared the letter and sent it for signing. It should come to your personal email. ","2026-01-15T08:52:06.547Z"],["3811467","WD-22576","WD","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","We would like to request access to all Bulgaria employee information and future tasks in Workday, as [~accountid:712020:7f339fc8-1d2a-4500-903a-50ef7065e24d]  and [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] will be managing People Operations side for this country.","2026-01-15T08:52:19.414Z"],["3811471","MM-938","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|The issue describes the problem and desired outcome but lacks detailed requirements, acceptance criteria, and edge cases.|\n|Clarity|🟢|The language is clear and the intent is understandable, though more structure would help.|\n|Auditability|🟡|There is an attached screenshot, but no links to specs or related documentation.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add acceptance criteria and edge cases to the description.\n* Provide a time estimate.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs if available.","2026-01-15T08:53:04.318Z"],["3811473","PC-4940","PC","roman.zavodskikh@bolt.eu","Roman Zavodskikh","Depends on [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-4939|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PC-4939|smart-link] .","2026-01-15T08:53:25.621Z"],["3811474","WFM-9996","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hey [~accountid:712020:ddf1e045-1184-4210-9e73-da3ce949a13b] could you please check what can be happening in this case? The agents already have the necessary roles, would it be something linked to their certificate? ","2026-01-15T08:53:32.310Z"],["3811475","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hello [~accountid:712020:ee1c1af8-636c-441c-be5b-0948c0dfac08],\n\nThank you. I’ve checked that I can now see the ticket for the map.\n\nI do not have acces to the other tickets (tickets a, b, and c mentioned by Alexia). Can you please grant me access? Thanks! ","2026-01-15T08:53:34.755Z"],["3811477","FX-3640","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768467215324369]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3640 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T08:53:47.605Z"],["3811479","LSS-61612","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^LT20260115-001 Vo-Link - Bolt Drive LT.docx.pdf] _(340 kB)_","2026-01-15T08:54:42.956Z"],["3811480","HS-28968","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Waiting for document from UHY ","2026-01-15T08:54:56.352Z"],["3811481","CCM-22278","CCM","natthaphong.buarawong@bolt-outsource.eu","Natthaphong Buarawong","[^CNX Onboarding Training Request.xlsx]","2026-01-15T08:54:56.827Z"],["3811482","LSS-61592","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","I believe this is a renewal","2026-01-15T08:55:00.213Z"],["3811483","HS-28967","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Waiting for document from UHY ","2026-01-15T08:55:06.107Z"],["3811489","RDXENG-4653","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested on CA.193.0 (*🍒*) and unable to reproduce* (/) ","2026-01-15T08:55:46.550Z"],["3811491","DRX-27934","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Verified as fixed on DI.127.0 (194894103) Firebase build","2026-01-15T08:55:50.239Z"],["3811496","HS-28148","HS","maciej.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Maciej Bednarczyk","Hi! I'm sending Work Certificate in the attachment.\n\n[^Świadectwo Pracy Pwc.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T08:57:08.243Z"],["3811499","TAXP-2045","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","This has been completed on time. There were no invoices in the month [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/124iMIzer4ZNHYe7NsG9S6N5JOJlVe9Kh|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/124iMIzer4ZNHYe7NsG9S6N5JOJlVe9Kh|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T08:57:46.429Z"],["3811500","LSS-61613","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","[^Bolt - Notice of Bill Rate Increase - January 2026.pdf] _(230 kB)_","2026-01-15T08:58:00.205Z"],["3811501","LSS-61614","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^_LV20260115-001 Vo-Link - Bolt Drive LV.docx.pdf] _(341 kB)_","2026-01-15T08:58:03.972Z"],["3811502","MM-939","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided. The issue lacks sufficient information for a developer to start.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is somewhat clear but lacks context and details. No sections or acceptance criteria are present.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are included.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-15T08:58:08.494Z"],["3811503","LSS-59741","LSS","kaidi.erisalu@bolt.eu","Kaidi Erisalu","Hi!\n\nData is checked and I confirm. \n\n\n\nThanks!\nKaidi","2026-01-15T08:58:18.923Z"],["3811504","RDS-1360","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] +1 to the context and finding the way to integrate past drives with Search. Based on my own experience, it works well for the destination (as we show you locations from the latest trips), but not for pickup. Also, it feels we could be generally more clever/efficient in setting up the pickup spot.  ","2026-01-15T08:58:22.658Z"],["3811505","LSS-58717","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8]  thanks for letting me know.\n\nAs discussed previously, we’ll need to sign two agreements rather than one to reflect the fact that we have two operating entities in the UK. Would you be able to track when services are provided for the benefit of Bolt Flex rather than Bolt Standard? I recall this was an issue the last time we looked at it.\n\nAs for the form, please fill in the form as far as you can using the information available on Companies House UK. The two entities are:\n\n* Bolt Services UK Limited\n* Bolt Operations UK Limited\n\nI expect each entity will need a separate form since we're signing two agreements. \n\nOnce you’ve done that, I’ll review and flag anything that’s missing, and confirm whether it’s something legal or finance needs to weigh in on.","2026-01-15T08:58:37.454Z"],["3811512","PRODSEC-588","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","{quote}[~accountid:642aa1eb7e859baa54f54b06] \nAlthough there is reasoning to have all requested dependencies visible company wide (or at least ENG wide) to avoid duplication and to allow endorsement of requests with larger number of beneficiaries.{quote}\n\nAlternatively, we dont need to agree right now. Another option is to convert this to a task and place it under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRODSEC-694|smart-link]  then we take it into a Sprint.","2026-01-15T09:01:19.042Z"],["3811515","RS-1951","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","[^ORI_827937054.pdf en-US.pdf] _(120 kB)_\n\n[^ESCRITO BOLT.pdf en-US.pdf] _(326 kB)_\n\n[^ESCRITO BOLT.pdf.pdf] _(358 kB)_\n\n[^ORI_827937054.pdf.pdf] _(163 kB)_","2026-01-15T09:01:40.993Z"],["3811516","CLOUDSEC-451","CLOUDSEC","iuliia.laaneots@bolt.eu","Iuliia Laaneots","Link to postmortem which needs to be finilized: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~633889565/pages/edit-v2/6369542883?draftShareId=5731eecd-3b3e-4366-8793-a474b3b36f32|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~633889565/pages/edit-v2/6369542883?draftShareId=5731eecd-3b3e-4366-8793-a474b3b36f32|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:01:51.811Z"],["3811520","TAXP-2044","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","Done [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1PGAgU8tFX37yV-dgOn3zCnaMXbywMK4r|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1PGAgU8tFX37yV-dgOn3zCnaMXbywMK4r|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T09:03:00.676Z"],["3811522","CAMLE-9621","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","*Analysis update*:\nDived deeper and investigated this further and found that the timeouts were related to {{fleet-driver}} endpoint {{/internal/driver/campaign/getSelectedCarId}}\n\nthis aligns with other use-cases as-well mentioned [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02H52XUKPG/p1767775417117049?thread_ts=1764942308.742629&cid=C02H52XUKPG] and likely adds to the culprit being event loop lags in the {{fleet-driver}} service\n\nalthough the randomly [high|https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/d/000000004/internalrequestclient3a-requests-per-node-path?orgId=1&var-team=All&var-type=All&var-host=All&var-shard=All&var-service=All&var-to_service_id=car-branding-periods&var-path=%2Finternal%2FgetCarBrandingVerificationStatus&var-node_release_track=Canary&var-node_release_track=Release&from=1752566250147&to=1768467450147] timeout spikes have subsided from {{fleet-driver}} service will just need to monitor this in future.\nas can be seen from kibana logs aswell the errors rate has dropped\nthe relevant team has informed us that the service will be split in the near future.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.00.25.png|width=654,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.00.25.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 10.57.09.png|width=654,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 10.57.09.png\"!\n\n*Action items:*\n\n* no action, just keep monitoring further and incase spikes reappear reach out to [#dev-driver-growth-conversion-support|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C02H52XUKPG] in [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02H52XUKPG/p1767775417117049?thread_ts=1764942308.742629&cid=C02H52XUKPG] thread\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:b8094c97-c94f-4f57-ace0-b8f45753b3d6] [~accountid:6305dd67cf3340e8737f8f66] \n","2026-01-15T09:03:11.898Z"],["3811526","LSS-61615","LSS","georgiana.ciobanca@bolt.eu","Georgiana Ciobancă","[^Contract furnizare produse & servicii, UtilDeco.docx] _(188 kB)_\n\n[^Acord de parteneriat UtilDeco_unitate protejata .docx] _(171 kB)_","2026-01-15T09:04:25.854Z"],["3811529","FRAUDOPS-1117","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","{noformat}(\nCASE\n    WHEN (lower(get_json_object(i_sel.input,'$.user.first_name')) LIKE '%juden%' \n    OR lower(get_json_object(i_sel.input,'$.user.last_name')) LIKE '%juden%' \n    OR lower(get_json_object(i_sel.input,'$.user.email')) LIKE '%juden%')\n    THEN 1 ELSE 0 \n  END AS juden_check\n\n  OR \n\n  CASE\n    WHEN (lower(get_json_object(i_sel.input,'$.user.first_name')) LIKE '%dildo%' \n    OR lower(get_json_object(i_sel.input,'$.user.last_name')) LIKE '%dildo%' \n    OR lower(get_json_object(i_sel.input,'$.user.email')) LIKE '%dildo%')\n    THEN 1 ELSE 0 \n  END AS dildo_check\n  )\n\n  AND profile_features__user__net_spending_rate = 0\n  AND user__language = 'de'{noformat}\n\n\n\njuden:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.04.51.png|width=879,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.04.51.png\"!\n\n\n\ndildo:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.04.35.png|width=871,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.04.35.png\"!","2026-01-15T09:04:57.103Z"],["3811530","TAXP-2047","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1uTdVEHfUACybymRi-h4AtDr6CGSkpKco|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1uTdVEHfUACybymRi-h4AtDr6CGSkpKco|smart-link] Done","2026-01-15T09:05:08.295Z"],["3811531","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] If we want to add 0.5-1.5mm extra material, do we need to open a new mold? ","2026-01-15T09:05:33.203Z"],["3811532","SREP-1107","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","etcd sts is also spamming with the same messages time by time, but we have a placeholder here, so nothing critical yet","2026-01-15T09:05:39.281Z"],["3811533","LSS-61500","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","approved!","2026-01-15T09:05:46.318Z"],["3811534","DBRE-7545","DBRE","akhmad.islami@bolt.eu","Akhmad Mukhson Islami","[campaign]\r\n- campaign_automation_testing (LIVE - 13/01/2026 13:24:49) | (PRELIVE - 13/01/2026 14:59:55)\r\n\r\n[fleet]\r\n- fleet_automation_test (LIVE - 13/01/2026 13:50:15) | (PRELIVE - 13/01/2026 15:00:41)\r\n\r\n[fraud]\r\n- test_fraud_automation (22/09/2025)\r\n\r\n*[central]*\r\n- taxify_alter_orchestrator (n/a)\r\n- taxify_testbox (PRELIVE - 15/01/2026 11:01:58) | (LIVE - 15/01/2026 10:59:38)\r\n\r\n*[invoicing]*\r\n- percona (PRELIVE - 14/01/2026 11:33:33) | (LIVE - 14/01/2026 11:34:51)\r\n\r\n*[rental-central]*\r\n- dbtest (PRELIVE - 14/01/2026 11:54:36) | (LIVE - 14/01/2026 11:55:20)\r\n- taxify_rental_car_simulator (*PRELIVE - used for iot test*) | (LIVE - 14/01/2026 13:47:33)\r\n- taxify_stories (PRELIVE - 14/01/2026 13:36:17) | (LIVE - 15/01/2026 10:40:04)\r\n\r\n*[order]*\r\n- test_automation (09/2025)\r\n\r\n*[n/a]*\r\ntaxify_invoicing_refund (n/a)\r\ntaxify_subscription_billing (n/a)\r\npricing_automation_test (n/a)\r\ntaxify_oidc_provider (n/a)\r\ntaxify_partner_payments_citi_sftp (n/a)\r\ntaxify_backend_credentials (n/a)","2026-01-15T09:06:13.807Z"],["3811537","SUPX-2323","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1768467673809499|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1768467673809499]","2026-01-15T09:06:44.242Z"],["3811539","SREDESK-7417","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Jevgeni,\n\nThanks for sharing the records via Google Sheets. It made translating them into Terraform code much easier.\n\nCopying records directly from Jira tickets is a bit challenging, and the formatting sometimes changes the characters.\n\nI’ve prepared all the records in [*this PR*|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15395] and will start applying them shortly. Applying everything should take around 30–40 minutes.","2026-01-15T09:07:09.934Z"],["3811540","SREDESK-7421","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Editor access has been granted to your account.","2026-01-15T09:07:23.664Z"],["3811541","PFI-833402","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:a86e3f5d-8ff8-4fd2-bac0-2e4712e56a68],\n\nThank you for escalating this.\nAll the users and their related payment methods/devices have been Fraud-blocked. I can see that the business account was already de-activated.\n\nRegarding the drivers, then related to the fees, the only driver that should be affected is Arkadi Sidorov, and only the trips that were taken by Rider *Hill*, these orders have the fraud tag attached which resulted in the full refunds.\n\nIf I am not mistaken, then the situation regarding Arkadi Sidorov was already raised, and I also suggested compensating the driver.\n\nOther drivers do not seem to have the fraud tag attached and I do not see that there would’ve been full refunds issued, therefore there should be no issues.\nFor example one of the drivers and their orders that you have linked: [Example1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2335068366/1?orderTryId=3000335945] \n*Final driver income (on ride finish)*\n\n*Total income after commission:*\n\n*9.68€*\nThis means that all is good with this driver and their order, no issues here (seems to be the case for most of the drivers besides the one mentioned)\n\nPlease manually check if Arkadi Sidorov has not already been manually compensated/has ongoing process for it, and if he does not, please proceed with manually compensating them.\n\nWe will be manually checking further if we can find any patterns to avoid this in the future, but for now all the related users, their devices and payment methods have been completely disabled, which will also affect all the future devices/methods they may add.\n\nThank you again for escalating the case and providing such detailed information about the incident.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:07:36.270Z"],["3811542","CAMLE-9621","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","have also conveyed the same to fleet-driver owner team to support the case of splitting their service","2026-01-15T09:07:42.555Z"],["3811548","FIS-4201","FIS","pavel.permenov@bolt.eu","Pavel Permenov","The issue [was raised again|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GLECZC8G3/p1768413550228689] by the local Ops rep","2026-01-15T09:08:29.405Z"],["3811549","PAW-14901","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160811\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 09:08:34 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T09:08:35.081Z"],["3811550","FINDATA-4175","FINDATA","ismayil.aghahasanli@bolt.eu","Ismayil Aghahasanli","IT ticket- [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349537?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349537?created=true|smart-link]  -shared drive has been created.\ndir -[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AKRJx6DqYihaUk9PVA|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0AKRJx6DqYihaUk9PVA|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:08:37.570Z"],["3811553","L10N-27867","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27862](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27862)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T09:09:02.223Z"],["3811554","L10N-27871","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, a