e main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27862](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27862)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T09:09:30.043Z"],["3811567","L10N-27893","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27862](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27862)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T09:09:30.948Z"],["3811568","RS-1951","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","⚠️ Also asked for assistance due to an *URGENT* *DEADLINE* in Slack in channel [_#cs-privacy-compliance-support_|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1768468091538749]","2026-01-15T09:09:40.124Z"],["3811569","RDS-618","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Yes makes sense, some issues there make more sense to solve than others, then we can at least start from somewhere. Most of the effort comes from connecting/building the trigger logic as they are vastly different.","2026-01-15T09:09:46.866Z"],["3811572","PFI-830972","PFI","sheraton.donbosco@bolt.eu","Sheraton Donbosco","? ","2026-01-15T09:10:00.981Z"],["3811574","PFI-792039","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Please provide account details !","2026-01-15T09:11:00.594Z"],["3811580","LSS-59711","LSS","martin.tomberg@bolt.eu","Martin Tomberg","First of all in what document we have less than 30 days retention? We have policy [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/3489661435/Policy+on+using+video+surveillance+on+the+premises+of+Bolt|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/3489661435/Policy+on+using+video+surveillance+on+the+premises+of+Bolt|smart-link]  \nLimitation is coming from local laws. And most important is regarding GDPR  in EU and local laws are - what is camera purposes?\nAll camera installations in Warehouses is done and organized by vertical - Physical security is not include here in any steps. \nPhysical security does not have any information where, what system warehouses and other vertical has or even who has access to them and how. I have heard that lot of cheap Chinese systems are in use.\nPhysical security controls Offices, hubs  and some DECs.\n\nFYI Physical Security team is one man show, who is designated mainly for offices. I can support vertical with knowledge and suggestions. If also needed to control all verticals then this discussion needed to be agreed with [~accountid:5cf7cf76840f290e75625425] ","2026-01-15T09:12:14.420Z"],["3811581","PFI-833004","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Reissued: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"created_from\"%3A1768428000%2C\"created_to\"%3A1768514400%2C\"to_agent_id\"%3A173136%2C\"to_agent_type\"%3A\"delivery_provider\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22created_from%22%3A1768428000%2C%22created_to%22%3A1768514400%2C%22to_agent_id%22%3A173136%2C%22to_agent_type%22%3A%22delivery_provider%22%7D%7D]","2026-01-15T09:12:23.269Z"],["3811583","PFI-833656","PFI","darren.seruwagi@bolt.eu","Darren Mbigiridde Seruwagi","[^Faktura DK1525-227.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-15T09:12:34.858Z"],["3811584","PFI-833521","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello there,\n\nWe have made some changes from our side.\nIt is estimated that it may take roughly 2-3 hours before the changes go live, after that the user should be capable of deleting their account.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:12:37.108Z"],["3811585","HS-28974","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting for PQ.","2026-01-15T09:12:41.660Z"],["3811591","RDXENG-3916","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested on CA.193.0* {{develop}} *and unable to reproduce* (/) \n\n!expected.mp4|width=320,alt=\"expected.mp4\"!","2026-01-15T09:13:36.756Z"],["3811593","PFI-833657","PFI","marija.jasiskyte@bolt-outsource.eu","Marija Jasiškytė","!IMG_5659.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T09:14:19.238Z"],["3811596","PFI-833579","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:2aa43d8c-ac5b-4bae-91a2-e3ed433a5c3e],\n\nThe PR is now completed.\nPlease note that it may take up to 72h for the PR to be reviewed.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:14:57.421Z"],["3811597","WEBSD-1428","WEBSD","marit.ausmees@bolt.eu","Marit Ausmees","Hey! Do you know when you could help me with this? 🙏 ","2026-01-15T09:15:00.884Z"],["3811599","PFI-833211","PFI","vanazwan.riannamwong@bolt.eu","Vanazwan Riannamwong","Hi, I have added another company ID which is 253957, Name: Bangkok Fleet บริษัท เค.พี.เอ็น. มอเตอร์ กรุ๊ป จำกัด into the spreadsheet [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1KWcYlb1KFfo_9Ld9dwDA97tfU0_OrXMxyJ3mvicdzF0/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1KWcYlb1KFfo_9Ld9dwDA97tfU0_OrXMxyJ3mvicdzF0/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] . Please kindly change both company invoice strategy into Company. Thank you.\n\n","2026-01-15T09:15:03.483Z"],["3811602","LSS-61615","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T09:16:33.994Z"],["3811608","CAMLE-7389","CAMLE","mateja.sela@bolt.eu","Mateja Sela","Haven’t seen this in one year, going to close it.","2026-01-15T09:17:16.246Z"],["3811615","PFI-833262","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hihi! All done! ","2026-01-15T09:19:01.027Z"],["3811620","LSS-58216","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","Solidgate sent their feedback with these comments:\n\n{quote}We accepted almost all suggestions and have three clarifications/amendments remaining:\n\n* clause 10.7 on marketing, please advise on whether that is acceptable (former clause 10.5 has been deleted); \n* clause 11.7 clarification that the liability cap will not apply to compliance, risk, warranties, and data protections sections; and\n* clause 9.2 of DSA regarding reciprocal indemnity.\n\nWill also appreciate if you provide the contact email (page 1, alternatively we can use [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu]) and the details of a data exporter contact person (page 36, Annex 1).{quote}\n\nFile itself: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zIHe6ii8zb1fKtirn2LNsL_CWDbyCo1w/edit?usp=drive_web&ouid=118032114846122975551&rtpof=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zIHe6ii8zb1fKtirn2LNsL_CWDbyCo1w/edit?usp=drive_web&ouid=118032114846122975551&rtpof=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:19:33.404Z"],["3811627","LSS-59751","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Given that the scope of data processing does not involve customer data, the low liability limit for data breach is not considered a blocker from privacy perspective. We are satisfied with Pipedrive responses.","2026-01-15T09:20:38.449Z"],["3811635","WFM-9961","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","assigned T1 and LM queues of Nigeria and Uganda","2026-01-15T09:22:59.225Z"],["3811638","LSS-61617","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","[^index_delayed_ui.pdf] _(268 kB)_","2026-01-15T09:23:25.881Z"],["3811641","LSS-61616","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] \n\n\n\nShould we assign this ticket to you - regarding improvements to the LERR process?\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] just fyi, no actions","2026-01-15T09:23:31.763Z"],["3811642","WFM-10003","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:6023caa8f6e6c5006906bb11] ,\n\nKindly make this request directly to the TL. Thank you.","2026-01-15T09:23:33.421Z"],["3811643","OKAI-179","OKAI","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","We want to start collecting errors one by one to avoid triggering too many collections at once, since we do not yet have SOPs for each error. We will create SOPs for each error and pilot them first in Berlin, as it has the largest OKAI fleet.\n\nh3. Next steps:\n\n* Lets start collecting E49 and GTULF(E9999) in Berlin.\n* Make a SOP/Flowchart for E49 and GTULF.\n* Lets ask Berlin ops to send 2 scooters with E478 to Tallinn for further investigation, since we do not know exactly what is the root cause.\n\nh3. SOP/Flowchart E49 GTULF\n\n# Remove battery\n# Test battery with OKAI battery tester\n# Measure CAN resistance form the battery terminal when IOT is connected (120+-10 ohm)\n# Measure CAN resistance form the battery terminal when IOT is disconnected  (10+-3 kohm)\n\n*More detailed outcomes will be described in the SOP*","2026-01-15T09:23:34.033Z"],["3811647","PAW-14894","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160796\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 09:24:20 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T09:24:20.309Z"],["3811648","WD-22569","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Locations inactivated!","2026-01-15T09:24:27.470Z"],["3811649","WFM-9998","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello team,\nAs this is a very sensitive market, we kindly ask you to share the reason or recommendations for this request.","2026-01-15T09:24:37.862Z"],["3811651","LSS-61618","LSS","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","[^TPEQ Bolt Australia_Engagement Letter_15Jan26.pdf] _(130 kB)_","2026-01-15T09:25:22.715Z"],["3811656","PFI-833609","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:8887b456-dfb7-4bd7-a17a-50103025b031],\n\nThis user is fine, at least for now. While they do have slightly suspicious and expensive orders, then they are still currently providing us with positive GMV. We do not really have 100% information for now to say that this user is absolutely doing fraud, therefore we can not take any actions against them either, however, the Fraud rules are working, therefore, even if they are trying something, then most likely they will get stopped beforehand.\n\nPlease do not take any actions against this user for now.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:25:46.600Z"],["3811658","DELIVERY-1425","DELIVERY","mihai.burlaciuc@bolt.eu","Mihai Burlăciuc","[~accountid:712020:66bb9418-0d92-46e7-811e-6ba68a304999] \nRegarding Option 2\n\n\n{quote}how much development effort and time would it require to implement a sound-switching feature in the Merchant app? _Note_: That also considers:\n\n# The notification sound that was changed in the past and received negative feedback\n# The current sound that is live today{quote}\n\nI’d say around 5-6 days extra, that would include the settings in the app, Mixpanel events when when the sound was changed, and a persistent way of knowing what is the current sound they are using.\n\nRegarding the UI, we can go with a pretty raw version in the Sound settings tab of the Marchant app - i.e. a Section title and a list with radio buttons to pick between the 2 sounds - like “Select new order sound” and the the radio buttons list. Although, we’d have to come up with some names for the sounds that we, since the only way I know we can differentiate between the 2 now are: “Old sound” and “Current sound”, so maybe come up with some flashy names here? ","2026-01-15T09:25:53.575Z"],["3811662","HS-28971","HS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","Thank you [~accountid:712020:6bc77170-e958-4b44-90fe-43a2fc30553a] - submitted it.","2026-01-15T09:26:34.633Z"],["3811663","PFI-833659","PFI","juliet.imeze@bolt-outsource.eu","Juliet Imeze","[^DEBT PAYMENT.pdf]","2026-01-15T09:26:48.573Z"],["3811667","HS-28976","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Rabeez! Your employment confirmation letter will be forwarded to you via BoxSign to your personal email.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-15T09:27:24.788Z"],["3811669","MM-940","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided. The issue lacks details for a developer to start work.|\n|Clarity|🔴|The summary is vague and there are no clear sections or explanations.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the summary and break down the work into clear steps.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-15T09:27:52.406Z"],["3811670","WFM-9980","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","added the queues to advised emails [~accountid:712020:2540f48c-18fa-40a9-91cf-5d7340c3750b]","2026-01-15T09:28:00.241Z"],["3811678","PFI-833614","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:9bca79a2-cc3f-4867-abd0-e93af8fd629a],\n\nThe device UID suspension has been lifted.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:29:14.341Z"],["3811679","WEBSD-1428","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","Hi Marit\n\nI have created the triggers for the individual steps for the new DCP courier portal within GTM. You will need to create the tags for meta here and then use the triggers for each step. Poland is a unique case and is the only one on a different platform for now. I am hoping they switch to the new platform soon 🤞 \n\nIs there any reason why you are not sending users to the landing page? [https://bolt.eu/en/food/courier/|https://bolt.eu/en/food/courier/|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:29:20.723Z"],["3811680","RDS-1061","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] what is the status of this ticket? Is it something we plan to explore further in the future?","2026-01-15T09:29:22.592Z"],["3811684","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* ProxySQL monitor\n* [https://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000036/proxysql3a-overview?orgId=1&refresh=1m&var-group=.*live-proxysql-.*&var-proxysql=All&var-hostgroup=55&var-hostgroup=56|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/000000036/proxysql3a-overview?orgId=1&refresh=1m&var-group=.%2Alive-proxysql-.%2A&var-proxysql=All&var-hostgroup=55&var-hostgroup=56]\n* cs-db-4 online at 2026-01-15 11:30 EET","2026-01-15T09:30:15.766Z"],["3811686","LSS-61617","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T09:31:08.079Z"],["3811690","LSS-61619","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","[^18_09_2013-947_2013-83374 (1).pdf] _(102 kB)_\n\n[^Government Gazette - 29th July.pdf] _(1.44 MB)_","2026-01-15T09:32:24.149Z"],["3811691","PFI-833615","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:ce514ac3-7ca9-4bbc-978d-90297ad242e1],\n\nThe device UID suspensions have been lifted.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:32:29.726Z"],["3811692","CLOUDSEC-679","CLOUDSEC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Looks like these days we should create a single IT request.  [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/4747821317/Guide+to+installing+third+party+software+and+services#Software-tools-and-systems-purchase-workflow|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/4747821317/Guide+to+installing+third+party+software+and+services#Software-tools-and-systems-purchase-workflow|smart-link]  \n\nFollowing the new flow","2026-01-15T09:32:34.492Z"],["3811693","WD-22544","WD","anton.suhov@bolt.eu","Anton Sukhov","[~accountid:605ee2ff2f7d900070c2e481] Hey hey! A bit more context. Boris was in my team as a *Staff Software Engineer*.\nAfter he moved to a new team, I now see the position in my team as *Site Reliability Engineer*.\n\nCan you please update it to the correct role: *Staff Software Engineer*?\nI only want to fix the information. I am not hiring now.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T09:32:45.751Z"],["3811695","LSS-61404","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343139|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343139|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:33:01.209Z"],["3811696","PFI-819866","PFI","szymon.barabasz@bolt.eu","Szymon Barabasz","Hi, can I get a confirmation of that refund - payment?","2026-01-15T09:33:16.714Z"],["3811699","FDBT-4796","FDBT","rainer.kana@bolt.eu","Rainer Kana","Added it to [~accountid:6001a70e4d2179006e1b4fee] \n\nBut maybe [~accountid:62ce7d1f8afb5805e5d441ae] you want to check it also (part of handover)?","2026-01-15T09:34:08.052Z"],["3811701","MM-941","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🟡|Basic tasks listed, but requirements are vague and reference further interviews for details. Edge cases and acceptance criteria are missing.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The language is mostly clear, but the description is brief and references people for more info instead of documenting it.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to supporting documentation or specs; relies on interviewing team members for details.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate provided in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add detailed requirements and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.\n* Summarize key points from interviews directly in the issue.","2026-01-15T09:34:32.103Z"],["3811703","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","[@marek.pagel|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5fedc5a9a9d03001079cb077] Based on this [testing|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C018LH51RRV/p1768465537572079?thread_ts=1768399360.981049&cid=C018LH51RRV], do you think we can proceed with the deployment for now?","2026-01-15T09:35:37.685Z"],["3811705","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","cc: [@fahad.khan|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/60f2a71d2f97d5006920d615]","2026-01-15T09:36:01.584Z"],["3811706","CSDA-297","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-15T09:36:06.239Z"],["3811707","TAXP-1076","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","All in order","2026-01-15T09:36:35.882Z"],["3811708","FDBT-4796","FDBT","rainer.kana@bolt.eu","Rainer Kana","{{select * from commerce_finance_tests_spark.uniqueness_pl_finance_model_pl_bolt_plus_subscription_revenue_}}","2026-01-15T09:37:10.399Z"],["3811714","PFI-833666","PFI","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","!IMG_5129.png.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_5186.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T09:38:50.002Z"],["3811715","DRX-28147","DRX","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nFollow ticket description","2026-01-15T09:39:30.355Z"],["3811716","HS-28874","HS","ala.mohamed@bolt.eu","Ala Mohamed","!Capture d’écran 2026-01-15 à 10.34.16.png|thumbnail!\n{color:#172B4D}Hello Marilin,{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}I hope you are doing well 🙂{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Thank you for your reply.{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Unfortunately, I am still unable to make the change. When I click on “Change My Preferred Name”, a message appears indicating that I have already submitted a request, and I cannot proceed further, as shown in the attached document.{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Would you be able to update it directly on your side?{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Thank you very much for your help.{color}\n\n\n{color:#172B4D}Have a great day,{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Ala{color}","2026-01-15T09:39:49.533Z"],["3811717","LSS-61602","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - sent out for signatures 🙂 ","2026-01-15T09:40:12.198Z"],["3811718","RDS-1061","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Yes, something potentially for the future.","2026-01-15T09:40:15.867Z"],["3811719","LSS-61602","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343142|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343142|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T09:40:16.157Z"],["3811720","WFM-10000","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:3cca891b-969f-4571-8d99-3e90479e630c] this isn’t about your profile, it’s on the agent’s profile.\nSafety queues have match restrictions enabled. Meaning that when this setting is enabled on a queue, if a task has that restricted queue among its matching queues and an agent does not have any of the same queues in their assigned list, the task will be automatically unassigned or declined to be assigned to that agent. \n\nIn other words, if you’re trying to assign a Safety queue to an agent who doesn’t have a Safety queue assigned at all, it will reject it. So if you need to assign certain agents, you’ll need to raise this request to be added by Bolt WFM. ","2026-01-15T09:40:22.575Z"],["3811722","WFM-10000","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Let us know if you have other questions or feel free to ask [~accountid:625c10eb9506d6006fd7cf91] for further details.","2026-01-15T09:40:56.693Z"],["3811723","LSS-61381","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","[^PoA (Bolt) (Luminor Agreements) (EE) - update 15.01.2026.docx]\n[^PoA (Bolt Operations) (Luminor Agreements) (EE) - 15.01.2026.docx]\n[^PoA (Bolt) (Swedbank Agreements) (EE) - 15.01.2026.docx]\n\nHi [~accountid:61b1d141b0b630006a9698e1] clear, thanks! Please find the drafts attached - please confirm whether I can forward them for signing.","2026-01-15T09:41:04.441Z"],["3811726","PFI-833667","PFI","klaudia.bochenko@bolt.eu","Klaudia Bochenko","[^TEMPLATE FINANCE BPP.xlsx]","2026-01-15T09:41:32.642Z"],["3811728","LSS-58510","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] ! The documents will be signed today","2026-01-15T09:42:07.728Z"],["3811730","WD-22572","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:61c07bf9a54af90069a42e2f] , please help me out with providing an example from a recent transaction in Workday, is it Accounting Journal, Supplier Invoice, something else? \nThat will enable me to more easily find where the issue is.","2026-01-15T09:42:55.934Z"],["3811733","LSS-61573","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:22f1d9b5-1599-49ef-8ecd-0c67511d3425],\n\nThanks for reaching out.\n\nCould you please confirm whether the Abogacía del Estado is our direct client -that is, whether they have accepted our Terms & Conditions and signed our Special Conditions- so that the contractual relationship is directly with us and not through a third party?\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-15T09:43:20.926Z"],["3811734","LSS-61101","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.[^aneks czynsz 2026 bolt (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T09:43:26.574Z"],["3811739","MLC-3891","MLC","mariaadelina.stana@bolt.eu","Maria Adelina Stana","Localization [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101154?created=true] has been requested for the first batch of confirmed markets","2026-01-15T09:44:46.960Z"],["3811741","DSR-3133","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, thanks for this. I reviewed the letter and the extracted data (added Device + Blocks plugins). Please share it with the driver by OED (/) ","2026-01-15T09:44:51.227Z"],["3811744","DELIVERY-1699","DELIVERY","ali.zeynalov@bolt.eu","Ali Zeynalov","26W02:\n- mainly busy with support tickets that required debugging and checking SFTP files.\n- [MerchantApp Issue|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06RL5RQX5L/p1766395875236129] - claim of problem in item availability management, resolved by config update\n- New Validation for Selling Price Length added across all services (PR is relatively big, is in review as of now)\n- picking items to be sorted by categories enabled back again and the config setup updated to work always only for 3P regions, to avoid potential issues in future.\n- [WMS-UI new Transformation Utility|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/STOC-945] added to clean the non-existent SKUs, to unblock user\n","2026-01-15T09:45:31.302Z"],["3811748","DLSP-1594","DLSP","habib.fikri@bolt.eu","Fikri Sundayana","Done in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLSP-2013|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLSP-2013|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:45:46.626Z"],["3811749","PFI-833626","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:5d6baa754e654c0db0af2fc7],\n\nI have Fraud-blocked the rider. This order was indeed most likely fraudulent, however, we can not connect them to the driver and frankly this is money that we will not further see as it has already been paid out to the driver.\nThe negative balance will remain on the user, however, it does not really matter as they will not have any further access to their account nor devices via Bolt. The user also had fraudulent relations which have already been shut down.\n\nNo further action is required from your side, however, if you’d like to reply to the user, then you would need to do so via e-mail.\nWhen and if providing an answer to the user, then simply say that their account has been terminated due to the irregular activities associated with their account.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:46:03.923Z"],["3811752","LSS-61619","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T09:46:33.702Z"],["3811753","WFM-9966","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:49794f0b-50af-405d-9c8d-0892508b103a]","2026-01-15T09:46:48.600Z"],["3811754","PFI-830309","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Dear Bolt,\n\n\nThe chargeback was processed to close the dispute. \n|  *{color:white} *#*{color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Merchant*{color}*{color:white}{color} | {color:white} *{color}[{color:white} {color}{color:white} *Invoice No.*{color}{color:white} {color}|https://adm.2c2p.com/pgwadmin/Home/SortTransactionListData?sortBy=invoice]{color:white} {color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Approval Code*{color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Credit Card No*{color}*{color:white}{color} | {color:white} *{color}[{color:white} {color}{color:white} *Date / Time*{color}{color:white} {color}|https://adm.2c2p.com/pgwadmin/Home/SortTransactionListData?sortBy=date]{color:white} {color}*{color:white}{color} | {color:white} *{color}[{color:white} {color}{color:white} *Trans Amount*{color}{color:white} {color}|https://adm.2c2p.com/pgwadmin/Home/SortTransactionListData?sortBy=amount]{color:white} {color}*{color:white}{color} |  *{color:white} *Status*{color}*{color:white}{color} | | \n| {color:#172B4D}1{color} | {color:#172B4D}Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited{color} | {color:#172B4D}7YoAmVum1PUhGrcAY7Mq{color} | {color:#172B4D}NA{color} | {color:#172B4D}494312XXXXXX5665{color} | {color:#172B4D}15/01/2026 10:43:12{color} | {color:#172B4D}THB 222.00{color} | {color:#172B4D}Chargeback{color} | | \n| {color:#172B4D}2{color} | {color:#172B4D}Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited{color} | {color:#172B4D}7YoAmVum1PUhGrcAY7Mq{color} | {color:#172B4D}132980{color} | {color:#172B4D}494312XXXXXX5665{color} | {color:#172B4D}30/12/2025 23:44:23{color} | {color:#172B4D}THB 222.00{color} | {color:#172B4D}Settled{color} | |","2026-01-15T09:46:51.707Z"],["3811758","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","To improve the bike's stability when supported by the kickstand, the kickstand legs must exceed *220mm* in width compared to the Okai EB100.\n\nThe EB1 and Cruiser were estimated at approximately *250mm*.\n\nHowever, 250mm poses a risk on the EB1, as the heels touch the kickstand tips.\n\nAccording to the test in [the comment|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-392?focusedCommentId=3810197], the kickstand leg width for the EB1 cannot be 250mm.\n\nThe new target width for the kickstand legs is *207mm*, which aligns with the Q-factor of the EB1 cranks.\n\n|207mm|!9e4e1cb9068aecee05ff47ee5fa3af8f-20260115-094504.jpg|width=177,alt=\"9e4e1cb9068aecee05ff47ee5fa3af8f-20260115-094504.jpg\"!|!3c69ba412747288d6e6d3c4a795c6e69-20260115-094237.jpg|width=226,alt=\"3c69ba412747288d6e6d3c4a795c6e69-20260115-094237.jpg\"!|!7b05c4e4d9b8ebf49e6ce6b870c61fa1-20260115-094259.jpg|width=226,alt=\"7b05c4e4d9b8ebf49e6ce6b870c61fa1-20260115-094259.jpg\"!|(Test to be added)|\n|250mm|!417b8bbae2c363e6032f8f6a95214921-20260115-094429.jpg|width=177,alt=\"417b8bbae2c363e6032f8f6a95214921-20260115-094429.jpg\"!|!dc6459ac4b0dae7e3abd19e6ecf0b84b-20260115-094610.jpg|width=177,alt=\"dc6459ac4b0dae7e3abd19e6ecf0b84b-20260115-094610.jpg\"!|!39396a1f86debc003330d4b491f2b206-20260115-094546.jpg|width=177,alt=\"39396a1f86debc003330d4b491f2b206-20260115-094546.jpg\"!|!9af07f111f4e1a69d8f0ff4076d89e25 (6f4a7b41-44fb-4e1e-bf74-ad25af8b2f96).mp4|width=320,alt=\"9af07f111f4e1a69d8f0ff4076d89e25.mp4\"!|","2026-01-15T09:47:33.828Z"],["3811759","LSS-61604","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] \n\nKindly share the details of the project - what kind of tender is this and what is the value? The cost centre is indicated as Public Policy Rentals - is this a rentals tender?\n\nAdditionally, kindly grant permission to access and edit the document you added in the description.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-15T09:47:33.419Z"],["3811761","CCM-22278","CCM","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","Hi [~accountid:712020:d92e20dc-92b8-47fd-920c-26e5630a941a] \n\nThe training has been assigned to the learners 🙂 \n\nBest, Taisiia ","2026-01-15T09:47:47.539Z"],["3811764","TAXP-683","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","We did not make this payment as we were in a refund position. We have received the refund [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1B2HAS59gjpk-g_HL1AKwW7NDH2IvJS6C|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1B2HAS59gjpk-g_HL1AKwW7NDH2IvJS6C|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:48:22.716Z"],["3811766","WD-21984","WD","linton.chikwenengere@bolt.eu","Linton Chikwenengere","{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nHi [~accountid:63fca2bdf00d095406f1fda7] , found additional suppliers planned for migration that are missing the entity supplier group (currently, WD shows only numeric or alphabetical classifications). I’ve added them to the list in red. Could you please help with the correct entity classification? Thanks!\n{panel}\n\n[^EIB file for supplier groups v2.xlsx]\n\n","2026-01-15T09:48:36.479Z"],["3811771","PFI-792039","PFI","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Hello!\n\nHere are the account details. ","2026-01-15T09:49:37.325Z"],["3811772","PFI-792039","PFI","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","!Skärmbild 2026-01-15 104456.png.png|width=346,height=171,alt=\"Skärmbild 2026-01-15 104456.png.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T09:49:47.389Z"],["3811775","CRC-2375","CRC","linnet.puskar@bolt.eu","Linnet Puskar","Scope:\n\n* Currency clearing models\n* ABB rejection model\n* Terrapay integration updates + modelling + reconciliation\n* Pawapay modelling + reconciliation\n* Intercompany logic for African market allocations (currently accounting is doing it manually)\n* Business allocations","2026-01-15T09:50:16.036Z"],["3811778","WFM-9981","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","[~accountid:712020:f8777cd9-bbc1-420a-93df-3ef14e315717]T1 and LM Taiwan RH queues assigned. If Safety queues need to be added, please raise a new ticket and tag [~accountid:625c10eb9506d6006fd7cf91]. Thanks!","2026-01-15T09:50:44.673Z"],["3811780","PFI-833660","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f370e2a2-c96b-43e0-a40e-ca32196cca7d],\n\nThank you for the detailed case report.\nSeems to be a false-positive.\nPlease manually compensate the Driver for the loss of their earnings for this incident.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-15T09:51:19.005Z"],["3811781","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Downscaling cs-db-2:\n* [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15401|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15401|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T09:51:42.902Z"],["3811782","LSS-56363","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:712020:78a05f99-3674-4d15-8f97-f78c85ca9826] ! Thanks for raising this - can you please clarify the final decision regarding the entity from which we will be paying the fees and hence I will be able to use such entity for contract details? Would we contract with GerOrder and pay them from *Bolt Operations Ukraine LLC* or *Bolt Operations OU?* Then we will use one of the respective drafts provided by GetOrder.","2026-01-15T09:51:46.015Z"],["3811783","LSS-58105","LSS","emils.mamedovs@bolt.eu","Emīls Mamedovs","Hi [~accountid:5cca9996e494c810153b1b03] any update on this topic ? ","2026-01-15T09:51:47.424Z"],["3811784","PFI-830972","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nThis is a PM matter and not Ops 😞 \n\nwe will direct it to our PMs and when they have availability they will look into it.\n\n[~accountid:712020:fb07882f-e7b7-4ccc-a944-5b44db14f802] [~accountid:712020:28f1a8fb-1d02-4f0c-b69a-61a5b33fc8de] - fyi, here is a good example of what invoice could/should/may look like.","2026-01-15T09:52:05.206Z"],["3811785","LSS-61573","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ,\n\nThat's correct; however, as a public entity, it has the specific requirement that invoices must be uploaded to this state platform.","2026-01-15T09:52:34.447Z"],["3811786","LSS-61604","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e], this is RH. I already tagged [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] in the relevant slack channel with all the relevant info.","2026-01-15T09:52:40.091Z"],["3811791","L10N-27900","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where yo