pdates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27937](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27937)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T10:24:33.216Z"],["3811968","L10N-27996","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27937](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27937)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T10:24:33.568Z"],["3811970","LSS-58414","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:71a7cd9a-50a4-4498-a9e0-da88ed773162] ! Any updates from the Counterparty side?","2026-01-15T10:24:52.215Z"],["3811971","LSS-58158","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^NEW Supply Chain Code of Conduct June 2023 -FSN Capital Partners FSNC 16 june 23 (1) (2) (2).pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:25:25.327Z"],["3811973","PFI-819162","PFI","viktorija.valinskaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktorija Valinskaitė","Any update?\n\n","2026-01-15T10:26:24.300Z"],["3811974","LSS-61519","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] can you please help me review this? \n\nPrevious ticket for ESG as mentioned in the description: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-34083|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-34083|smart-link] \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-7249|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-7249|smart-link] \n\nIf questions regarding ESG → please refer to [+Liisa Aavik+|mailto:liisa.aavik@bolt.eu] (we do not answer such questions ourselves). \n\nWhen I’m OoO, please consult Beatrice if any questions, she’s experienced in working with Bolt Business questions. \n\nThanks!","2026-01-15T10:26:34.268Z"],["3811977","MTE-1230","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","[~accountid:712020:cd383b4c-dce2-4e04-98a6-4398af29ffc2] just in case, please check with {{dev-rides-campaigns-support}} team as well as it might overlap with their code I believe","2026-01-15T10:26:44.684Z"],["3811979","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - this is the feedback I got from the business data slack channel: Hello Mehdi, our team does not expose reports to be consumed by a business client directly. But I am aware of some AMs who provide some data reports to businesses on an adhoc basis using [+this dash+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/2627?] and others.As far as the metrics themselves, the first three are fine and are available at company level if someone will report them to the business. As for the vehicle compliance metric, I am not aware of any BA clients being given such information. Our team doesn't have a dash or a datasource built to access this information readily. And honestly I am not too sure if we can share this data externally. For customer support, please ask in [#cs-looker|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/CFN1NTKB5]Also I am not sure if these targets set by the clients are realistic. That would need to be validated.  \n\n[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - Please see my comments on section 11.  I am just waiting for CS to confirm their complaint resolution benchmark in 48 hours.  Requesting your assistance to word the comments appropriately (legally) within the document, may be include an extra column with our remarks. ","2026-01-15T10:27:23.542Z"],["3811983","LSS-61321","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:2bd6b1d7-fd05-480e-8362-30ae2b3fc776] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club German Driver GmbH Jan2026 (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:28:20.446Z"],["3811984","SREDESK-7417","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi [~accountid:712020:f0f7cc2d-5968-45e9-91ec-ea445d725066] \n\nUnfornately, I can’t add these TXT records for some of the domains.\n\nSome of the TXT records have corresponding CNAME records and the [RFC prohibits this|https://stackoverflow.com/a/20230670].\n\n!image-20260115-102741.png|width=1083,alt=\"image-20260115-102741.png\"!\n\n{noformat} A CNAME record is not allowed to coexist with any other data.  In\n other words, if suzy.podunk.xx is an alias for sue.podunk.xx, you\n can't also have an MX record for suzy.podunk.edu, or an A record, or\n even a TXT record.  Especially do not try to combine CNAMEs and NS \n records like this!:\n\n           podunk.xx.      IN      NS      ns1\n                           IN      NS      ns2\n                           IN      CNAME   mary\n           mary            IN      A{noformat}","2026-01-15T10:28:22.387Z"],["3811985","WD-21923","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] *Could someone please remove the randomized check for Spain, Germany and Sweden currently?* \nIt turned out there are issues with the payment type and employees are not always aware what will be paid with salary (manual payment type) and what directly to bank account (direct deposit) and some things have been paid out incorrectly. So here would also help the process that you are working on for UA, but before these risks are maintained, we have to revert the randomized check and have everything come to AP table so we could check the payment types. ","2026-01-15T10:28:25.929Z"],["3811986","PFI-833653","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThat’s a difficult request to fulfill as the ApplePay payment method tokenizes the card details and it does not match the actual card registered in the ApplePay wallet. We don’t know what is the actual card used by the customer. \n\nThis is all of the information that we have available. As you can see the card numbers are not matching. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3865912139|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3865912139]\n\n!image-20260115-102716.png|width=1092,height=386!\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3909863173|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3909863173]\n\n\n!image-20260115-102732.png|width=1163,height=374!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T10:28:45.076Z"],["3811987","LSS-61325","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:847e5892-e286-4a70-a463-8a646733a72d] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^AUTO1 Remarketing GmbH Bolt Drive Sales Agreement.docx (3) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:28:48.562Z"],["3811990","DRX-26235","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the ticket on DA.126.0 (1507) - App tester build on Android 16\n\nVerified the following screens in the scope of this task:\n\n*Transactions history*\n\n* Main list view (No Internet connection banner is present for OLD TRANSACTION history but is not present for the new one)\n* Transaction details view (No Internet connection banner is present)\n\n*Old Transaction History:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-114245.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-114245.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Transaction details view:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-111532.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-111532.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n*Earnings (Main landing screen):*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-103839.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-103839.png\"!\n\n*Permission onboarding:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-112040.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-112040.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-112059.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-112059.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-112102.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-112102.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-112104.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-112104.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Full screen driver preferences* {{dev_is_full_screen_driver_preferences_enabled=true}}\n\n* *Main preferences view*\n* *Vehicle list*\n* *Vehicle categories*\n* *Pricing methods*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-122125.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-122125.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-103305.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-103305.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-103558.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-103558.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-122029.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-122029.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Lead became driver screen (It’s the main Home Screen of the App):*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-122501.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-122501.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-122522.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-122522.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n*Terminal connection screen (boltdriverapp://posTerminal/connect):*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-122717.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-122717.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Driver profile screens (I was able to trigger most of them with deeplinks but not sure where they would appear in the app)*\n\n* *Add driver profile list*\n* *Driver profile list*\n* *Activate driver profile*\n* *Driver profile explanatory screen*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-120126.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-120126.png\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-120153.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-120153.png\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-120516.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-120516.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Offers screen:*\n\n* *Feedback usage (appears after like/dislike)*\n* *Feedback reasons screen*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-113538.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-113538.png\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-113632.png|width=673,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-113632.png\"!\n\n\n\nVerified","2026-01-15T10:29:48.230Z"],["3811992","WD-22570","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi,\n\nI kindly request the cancellation of all draft reports, as the system is unable to determine the appropriate reference date, which is preventing submission due to the monthly limit.\n\nSubsequently, please create and submit a new report, and proceed with the next one only after the first one was submitted. This method proved effective during our testing phase. However, [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c]  can provide confirmation regarding the behavior of the expense reports and lines, as I currently lack access to the expense module in Workday.\n\nThank you\n\nOana","2026-01-15T10:29:51.005Z"],["3811993","PFI-833648","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T10:29:58.267Z"],["3811994","LSS-61342","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342317?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FCONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6InNhaW50Y29kZSIsIm9wZXJhdG9yIjoiZXEifV19%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/342317?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FCONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6InNhaW50Y29kZSIsIm9wZXJhdG9yIjoiZXEifV19%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T10:29:58.530Z"],["3811995","DO-5798","DO","nathan.valencia@bolt.eu","Nathan Ruiz Valencia","Hi Gazandi,\n\nyes it is for the notebook you have here \n\nand regarding the PII to clarify I did have the access, but somehow my cluster got cancelled and i recreated one. here is the ticket for the PII access [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/3335619|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/3335619]\n\nlet me know if anything else is required  \n","2026-01-15T10:30:27.641Z"],["3811996","LSS-59488","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Glad we could assist, [~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669]! Thank you for letting us know.","2026-01-15T10:30:39.019Z"],["3811998","PFI-833408","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 128.84 ZAR  was issued on 22/10/2025, 10:13:47UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 21st of October to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-15T10:30:43.614Z"],["3811999","WD-22512","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi Demetri,\n\nI kindly request the cancellation of all draft reports, as the system is unable to determine the appropriate reference date, which is preventing submission due to the monthly limit.\n\nSubsequently, please create and submit a new report, and proceed with the next one only after the first one was submitted. This method proved effective during our testing phase. However, [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] can provide confirmation regarding the behavior of the expense reports and lines, as I currently lack access to the expense module in Workday.\n\nthank you\n\nOana","2026-01-15T10:30:52.371Z"],["3812003","WFM-10005","WFM","nutcha.numsri@bolt-outsource.eu","Nutcha Numsri","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 173026.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T10:31:20.551Z"],["3812004","HS-28939","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Task cancelled on Workday by People Tech - new ticket made. ","2026-01-15T10:31:22.342Z"],["3812005","MLC-657","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Dubai* \n\n*Status:*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n* *BU:* Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn, Promo Codes, HVO *LIVE*\n* *BA:* *Acquisition - needs translation and proofreading - ticket raised*\n* *BA:* Onboarding, Product Education, 0 Orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo Codes, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*Angola*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*Moldova*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*New Zeland*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*Taiwan*\n\n* *WP:* Translations ready, setting up Figma for proofreading ","2026-01-15T10:31:52.963Z"],["3812007","SREDESK-7417","SREDESK","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Hi [~accountid:712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef] noted, for bolt subdomains, thank you. I want to check in with you regarding gethopp subdomains, those were successfully added, right?\n\nIf it’s success for [gethopp.com|http://gethopp.com] subdomains, I know just what we need to change in setup with Braze for Bolt, so that those CNAME records that currently are present would disappear.","2026-01-15T10:32:05.587Z"],["3812008","HS-28979","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting for confirmation about the start date.","2026-01-15T10:32:14.845Z"],["3812009","PFI-805373","PFI","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","Hey, a bit of a late update, but development was completed and rolled out at the end of November. [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] we can close the ticket. ","2026-01-15T10:32:43.301Z"],["3812010","CRC-2333","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Putting together business case to implement direct connection with dLocal","2026-01-15T10:32:43.652Z"],["3812011","LSS-61338","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Fleet Agreement_Alcance Jubilante Unipessoal LDA (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:32:45.780Z"],["3812013","MLC-3171","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Finland*\n\n*Status:*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n* *BU:* Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n* *BU:* Promo Codes, HVO need proofreading \n* *BA:* Onboarding & Churn: *LIVE*\n* *BA:* Product Education, 0 Orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo Codes, *need proofreading*","2026-01-15T10:32:56.229Z"],["3812016","LSS-61623","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","[^Fleet BK XWay s.r.o. SLAs contract, 2025.docx] _(478 kB)_","2026-01-15T10:33:31.757Z"],["3812017","CRC-2376","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Researching bank connectivity capabilities","2026-01-15T10:33:35.036Z"],["3812018","LSS-61598","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Updated and dated document attached!\n\n[^Sole director's resolutions - Bolt Operations UK Limited - resignation of Nick Walker_15.01.26 (b82f1ab9-0158-41a2-a52f-1f71e7379b99).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T10:33:51.656Z"],["3812019","PFI-831450","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hello! Reissued! ","2026-01-15T10:34:08.482Z"],["3812020","LSS-61622","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:523b0039-eb47-4ccc-aca3-88d82c0c880a] thanks, please give me access to the main contract.","2026-01-15T10:34:16.970Z"],["3812021","PFI-833385","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer had a negative balance of 2.04 PLN from 10 Jan 2026, 07:39:57 (UTC+01:00) as Bolt was not able to capture the full amount from the customer. There was a refund issued to the OPM, but the negative balance remained. If you wanted to get rid of the negative balance then you should have issued a BB refund. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4023273463|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4023273463]\n\nThe users can eliminate their debt by topping up their Bolt balance or covering the debt with their next order. \n\nIn this case the user covered their debt of 2.04 PLN with a new order. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4030112642|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4030112642]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T10:34:21.789Z"],["3812022","GRWA-1510","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","[+Confluence+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CAM/pages/7403667597/GMV+UC+CUPED+Bootstrap+-+Aggregation+Logic]","2026-01-15T10:34:28.245Z"],["3812023","SUPX-2291","SUPX","michal.rapinczuk@bolt.eu","Michał Rapińczuk","Refinement notes:\n\n* let’s try to get access to data around legitimate cases (particular API partners for which we are hitting limits already)\n* short-term solution\n** white-list email addresses for which limiting will be lifted → although we need to be mindful of OOO emails that could cause issue when we start sending web forms without limits\n** introduce observability around number of cases that hit the limit and particular partners\n* long-term solution\n** rely on classifying emails around spam, OOO replies to be used to configure whenever the case should be created","2026-01-15T10:35:06.001Z"],["3812024","PFI-830972","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","feedback from PMs:\n\n----\n\nThis is very interesting feedback and very much aligned with what we are currently working on (Tax Report feature in FOP) - where Fleets would be able to see breakdowns for their earnings/ taxes/ deductions.\n\nFrom initial read, we will address a lot of concerns with new version we aim to release, where fleets would be able to have more granular reconciliation of their earnings/dedutions/taxes for the month.\n\nOur plan is to have a phased roll-out, and currently we are busy with preparing roll-out for 4 markets. I suggest to pick it up again after February, to see how it might help Denmark.","2026-01-15T10:35:10.666Z"],["3812025","SREDESK-7424","SREDESK","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","My username - [mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu|mailto:mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu]","2026-01-15T10:35:21.589Z"],["3812026","LSS-61598","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85]! 🙏 ","2026-01-15T10:35:32.536Z"],["3812027","PFI-820068","PFI","akisa.mathenge@bolt.eu","Akisa Mathenge","Called driver and he has confirmed that he received the refund. Cased closed.","2026-01-15T10:35:40.184Z"],["3812028","LSS-61358","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] ! \n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.[^SO FOR Modification order_ Bolt Operations OU - Carbon - 122325-62712 20260109 V0 (1) (1).pdf] [^Bolt Operations OU Amendment Contract 052924-22741 Price Guarantee 20260109 V0 (1).pdf] \n\n\n\nAs the Counterparty signs, please send the executed version to [*contracts@bolt.eu*|mailto:contracts@bolt.eu] for archiving purposes.","2026-01-15T10:35:56.316Z"],["3812029","DO-5800","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Hey [~accountid:712020:5d2c94f7-18bd-42ce-8b94-1f8b12d120df] \n\nThese are customer support looker specific views and not tables.\nCould you please mention the one who provide this information and ask them which tables that under these views?\n\n\n{noformat}fact_support_case.average_csat_weighted_score_utc\nprice_review_price_review_extended\netl_data_api_support_case_extended\nagent_info\nagent_utilisation\nnew_handling_time_event{noformat}","2026-01-15T10:36:19.069Z"],["3812030","LSS-61104","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:289d7ba0-a9c0-4cbb-82d4-a9ed8c05aeab] and [~accountid:712020:1e9398f2-efcd-4dcd-8ece-28e6f8578e37] , gentle reminder here, since we are supposed to send a reply today.\n\nThank you!\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:6273b7d8e51c620070bea596] ","2026-01-15T10:37:13.128Z"],["3812032","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - please see additional clarification from business data team: I would recommend having a discussion with the privacy team of what data is ok to share, I know of finish rate, ETA/ATA and cancellation rate +at BA account level+ is being communicated now. As for the other metrics, I am not aware of a case where we share them, and can't make a recommendation on whether they are ok to share - could you loop in a privacy team resource or do you think the other data falls under that?  I mean do we need to consult the privacy team? ","2026-01-15T10:37:26.679Z"],["3812035","LSS-61622","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:523b0039-eb47-4ccc-aca3-88d82c0c880a] please see my comments below:\n\n# The referenced number of the main contract needs to be amended as now it is incorrect.\n# We need bilingual version (ENG-ru) as the English version of the main contract prevails.\n# Please clarify why the start period of the rent is updated to 1 January 2026. ","2026-01-15T10:37:51.009Z"],["3812036","SOBB-1026","SOBB","luca.cardoso@bolt.eu","Luca Cardoso de Gouvea","[~accountid:712020:c28ac319-83e4-4d10-926a-3e90f309e781][~accountid:712020:55f8d571-60a5-4faf-bb90-1d80d8fad9e3] please follow this Jira Task for tracking progress","2026-01-15T10:37:57.891Z"],["3812037","DRX-26235","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Ticket is tested by [~accountId:628dd714269a9a0068f2a783].","2026-01-15T10:38:03.827Z"],["3812038","DRX-27835","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-26235 has been resolved","2026-01-15T10:38:04.187Z"],["3812039","SREDESK-7424","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Hey,\nGranted to you editor access.","2026-01-15T10:38:04.504Z"],["3812042","L10N-28000","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27998](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27998)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T10:38:36.664Z"],["3812043","L10N-28003","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27998](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27998)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T10:38:38.374Z"],["3812044","L10N-28004","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27998](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27998)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T10:38:39.640Z"],["3812045","L10N-28007","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\