fset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768473522900?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-15T10:38:57.933Z"],["3812051","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","[^RfP taxaudbud.pdf]\n\nHi Beatrice, here is the RFP. Can’t remember if this has been shared with you also","2026-01-15T10:39:11.088Z"],["3812052","L10N-28021","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-27937](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-27937)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T10:39:32.911Z"],["3812054","PFI-833407","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 11.00 on Dec 28, 2025, 02:50:58 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 15265675362000412443029  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 28th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_B487Q6NQ38R32XW3_TL3HHBHTVKXGFTX3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T10:40:00.062Z"],["3812055","TAXP-999","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1uTdVEHfUACybymRi-h4AtDr6CGSkpKco|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1uTdVEHfUACybymRi-h4AtDr6CGSkpKco|smart-link]  Done","2026-01-15T10:40:03.688Z"],["3812056","SREDESK-7424","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","It appears that it was not configured correctly.","2026-01-15T10:40:07.381Z"],["3812057","PFI-833007","PFI","tumininu.oguntifa@bolt-outsource.eu","Tumininu Oguntifa","Hello team user was refunded and the account is still showing minus what can we do to this situation.   [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/721727860|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/721727860]","2026-01-15T10:40:09.897Z"],["3812061","DSR-2555","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[andreiadrian5@yahoo.ro|mailto:andreiadrian5@yahoo.ro] is his email address per people team.\n\nPlease mark this DSAR as completed [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] !","2026-01-15T10:41:10.404Z"],["3812062","DSR-3761","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-15T10:41:17.687Z"],["3812065","LSS-61096","LSS","himanshu.narvekar@bolt.eu","Himanshu Narvekar","Yes, this is good to go from CS side. ","2026-01-15T10:42:17.170Z"],["3812066","LSS-55593","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:641aac4f9d6383e32a32c047] and [~accountid:60918c062c2f6c0068da0d43] ,\n\nI’m attaching draft version of Whistleblower policy for Sweden with the comments and some clarifying questions from DLA that needs decision:\n\n* Should we keep anonymous reporting or delete as suggested by DLA? We have this option under Global Policy.\n* To which Bolt entity this policy should be applicable - Bolt Services AB, Bolt Support Sweden AB or both?\n* Fill in first-line reporting channels under section 2.4.1.\n** Decide who will be the designated “internal person or body” in Sweden?\n** Do we need call and physical meeting option\n* Do we want to keep appeals part under 2.5.4. - this is not necessary but it is in line with our Global Policy.\n\n[^Bolt - Whistleblowing policy (Sweden).docx]\n\n","2026-01-15T10:42:50.248Z"],["3812067","LSS-61541","LSS","christos.hadjistylianou@bolt.eu","Christos Hadjistylianou","Hey [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] \n\nThe older tickets had to do with the addition of the rider’s correct address. \n\nThe issue that he (and we) face now is in this [ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/720899397]. Unfortunately we cannot grant access to beehive and the message is too long. \n\nHow can we send you the content?","2026-01-15T10:43:10.707Z"],["3812068","LSS-61418","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt Poland - IC loans notice and acknowledgement - 12.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:43:34.745Z"],["3812069","SREDESK-7417","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Adding the TXT records for [*these domains*|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15395/changes] was successful.\nThe rest had conflicting CNAME records and I couldn’t add them.\n\n\n!image-20260115-104200.png|width=1083,alt=\"image-20260115-104200.png\"!\n\n!image-20260115-104218.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260115-104218.png\"!\n\n!image-20260115-104238.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260115-104238.png\"!\n\n!image-20260115-104301.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260115-104301.png\"!\n\n!image-20260115-104318.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260115-104318.png\"!\n\n!image-20260115-104334.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260115-104334.png\"!","2026-01-15T10:43:39.499Z"],["3812070","LSS-61619","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] !\n\nI believe this should be treated as a high-severity safety allegation, but the facts we have (or at least the ones you presented to me) are too unclear to assume there was an actual physical fight (the rider uses “physically assaulted” but provides no detail; driver denies). We should run a structured fact-gathering first and apply a proportionate precautionary measure while we clarify.\n\nOn the “criminal history” angle: a “clean” Maltese conduct certificate does not necessarily mean the driver never had issues. Older convictions can stop appearing on the conduct certificate after certain periods (“non-registration/expiry”), and civil matters (e.g., debt / non-payment of bills) would not typically appear as a criminal record. So the mismatch is not proof the driver lied or that onboarding failed.\n\nCould you please paste here prints of the Rider & Driver messages regarding this?\n\nIn the meantime, my recommended actions - for now - are the following:\n\n# *Preserve evidence* \n#* Trip ID, GPS trace, timestamps, pick-up/drop-off points, any in-app messages/calls, driver/rider prior safety history.\n# *Apply a proportionate precautionary measure*\n#* Because the allegation is potentially violent but ambiguous, it might make sense to apply a short “safety hold” (e.g., 12–24h) or temporary restriction re the Driver while we collect basic facts. The rationale behind this is risk-control pending initial assessment, not a finding of guilt.\n# *Clarify what “physically assaulted” means (fact-gathering)*\nSend both rider and driver a structured set of questions with a 24–48h deadline:\n#* What exactly happened? (threats only vs physical contact; if physical, what type: shove/hit/grab/blocking exit/property damage)\n#* Where did it happen (in-car vs after stopping) + exact location/time\n#* Any injuries and evidence (photos/medical notes/witnesses/etc)\n#* Request police report copy or number/station/date.\n# *Regarding the “criminal record” claims: handle them carefully*\n#* *Externally:* do not confirm/deny any criminal history with the rider/lawyer. Keep response process-based.\n#* *Internally:* request the driver to *re-submit a freshly issued conduct certificate* as a neutral verification step.\n# *Compensation/media threat handling*\n#* Route to claims/legal workflow: ask rider/lawyer for police ref + evidence + heads of loss.\n# *Decision after initial assessment (24–48h)*\n#* If evidence suggests credible violence risk or police confirm active investigation → maintain precautionary measure and evaluate offboarding per policy.\n#* If unsupported/inconsistent with objective data → lift precautionary measure, document rationale, keep rider/driver unmatched.\n\nIf you can paste here the conversations with the Driver and Rider and their exact description of what happened, I can then draft a tailored message for you to send to both of them, in case the team agrees with my suggested approach.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T10:44:19.757Z"],["3812071","SREDESK-7424","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Please verify the labels in the query as well, as there may be incorrect labels that were filtered out.","2026-01-15T10:44:30.503Z"],["3812073","TAXP-2076","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","Done [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1OwfxAsNrlXc5xZflcYo91g6IOQ89Xur_|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1OwfxAsNrlXc5xZflcYo91g6IOQ89Xur_|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T10:44:52.350Z"],["3812074","LSS-61050","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hello [~accountid:712020:979961a6-5216-4ee0-aa85-a7302993f5e6] any updates? Thank you! ","2026-01-15T10:44:52.511Z"],["3812076","TAXP-2077","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","Done [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/11baAnHVzOvDuPB7_kC0xpuMIJcnA0-0H|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/11baAnHVzOvDuPB7_kC0xpuMIJcnA0-0H|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T10:45:18.411Z"],["3812078","TAXP-2078","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1js9gM5qhsThsS9eT7Hf-CDnQxswVan7Y|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1js9gM5qhsThsS9eT7Hf-CDnQxswVan7Y|smart-link]  Done","2026-01-15T10:45:45.200Z"],["3812079","LSS-60246","LSS","nisley.ciacareli@bolt.eu","Nisley Ciacareli","HI [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] \n\nAll clear! Thanks for bringing us more details.\n\nCc: [~accountid:5b7be9e6b8e3cb589585eb47] \n","2026-01-15T10:46:05.228Z"],["3812080","TAXP-2079","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1Q2X5Fra-xT8Xqdg_5Kfxee1eNZ0-69Em|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1Q2X5Fra-xT8Xqdg_5Kfxee1eNZ0-69Em|smart-link]  Done","2026-01-15T10:46:10.944Z"],["3812081","DO-5798","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","If you have already requested the access, you can use your personal instance profile from your cluster [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation#Databricks|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation#Databricks|smart-link]","2026-01-15T10:46:19.650Z"],["3812082","PFI-816181","PFI","patricie.cholevova@bolt-outsource.eu","Patricie Cholevova","The driver is mentioning that he will contact his lawyer about this, can we get an update? ","2026-01-15T10:46:20.406Z"],["3812083","GRWA-1511","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Added \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.45.44.png|width=915,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.45.44.png\"!","2026-01-15T10:46:23.140Z"],["3812084","LSS-61435","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, document has been swapped. Please let the partner know.","2026-01-15T10:46:26.033Z"],["3812085","HS-28984","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","Hey Borys,\n\nI just sent you a new PIT-2 form via Box Sign to your personal email. Please fill and sign this. I will notify Payroll once it’s signed.\n\nKind regards,\n\nKristin - People Ops","2026-01-15T10:46:28.184Z"],["3812086","DO-5800","DO","asma.muzaffar@bolt.eu","Asma Muzaffar","Ok let us ask CX team for this information.\nJust for clarification, the first table i shared the complete name is f_leet_campaign_bonus_","2026-01-15T10:46:31.602Z"],["3812087","PC-4942","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","For reference: enhanced getPayment API doc: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/coLsJgE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/coLsJgE|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T10:46:35.800Z"],["3812088","LSS-60246","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","No problem - I will close the ticket for now, but let me know if there is anything else you need 🙂 ","2026-01-15T10:46:54.232Z"],["3812090","SREDESK-7417","SREDESK","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Thank you!\nWe can close the ticket for now then. I’ll start a thread with Braze so that we swap out CNAME bolt subdomain records of Sparkpost to a combination of A, MX and TXT records. Then we can pick up these google TXT records again. 🙏","2026-01-15T10:47:11.874Z"],["3812092","EBIKE1-423","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1csMTvGYBYQKLse192CkOOXhAAwoHebTI/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=103870233518445107680&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1csMTvGYBYQKLse192CkOOXhAAwoHebTI/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=103870233518445107680&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T10:47:29.978Z"],["3812093","LSS-60866","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Terms of engagement_Bolt Support KE Limited_Anne Babu & Co. Advocates_14.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T10:47:34.126Z"],["3812094","LSS-61579","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Annex 3 Bolt_VLM_Court rep (0333a961-8aef-49a2-ad17-9312539afb97).pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:47:39.388Z"],["3812095","WFM-9988","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","role approved","2026-01-15T10:47:48.553Z"],["3812097","WFM-9987","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","role approved","2026-01-15T10:48:02.788Z"],["3812098","PFI-833695","PFI","monika.jurcik@bolt-outsource.eu","Monika Jurčík","!IMG_2612.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T10:48:11.740Z"],["3812100","DO-5800","DO","dinithi.dulmini@bolt.eu","Dinithi Dulmini","Hi [~accountid:712020:061a9010-0948-45f3-81ba-d6d4ba88b4bf] Please help to grant access for “f_leet_campaign_bonus”_ table meanwhile. \n\n","2026-01-15T10:48:18.364Z"],["3812103","HS-28977","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Dudu, will do it today. ","2026-01-15T10:48:45.826Z"],["3812104","DO-5798","DO","nathan.valencia@bolt.eu","Nathan Ruiz Valencia","Yes i’m trying to use is but my problem is that it doesn’t work I still have error while I use the personal instance \n\n!image-20260115-104838.png|width=1782,height=149,alt=\"image-20260115-104838.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T10:48:59.888Z"],["3812105","PFI-833696","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-15T10:49:06.376Z"],["3812106","HS-28964","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Kevin, the letter should be in your personal inbox now. I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-15T10:49:10.921Z"],["3812108","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Thanks, [~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf].\n\nI still have no access to the ticket. Is it maybe possible for you to “copy-paste” it in a Google doc? I think it is important to have access to those communications to have visibility on how to prepare a response to the client.\n\nIf copy-paste is not an option, we can arrange a Google meeting and you share your screen so I can read the content…\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T10:49:14.034Z"],["3812110","TAXP-2037","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1ch7JzIO8I3WB3ys8Zm_L5_tYdG4pvyR4|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1ch7JzIO8I3WB3ys8Zm_L5_tYdG4pvyR4|smart-link]  done","2026-01-15T10:49:40.548Z"],["3812112","LSS-47933","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Alright, I’ll pencil in some time on our calendars.\n\nIt seems we have limited leverage at the moment. I would suggest we focus on the highest priorities with high likelihood to be accepted by the dealers for now. If we open topics for negotiation, we’ll again end up with non-standard processes agreed upon in a hurry for each individual dealer and bank, therefore, leaving room for further issues in the future.","2026-01-15T10:50:11.619Z"],["3812114","LSS-61484","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi, hope you’re doing fine too!\n\nHere are my findings about this invoice [Rider|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/61149706] - [Order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1499321128/18?orderTryId=2849448155] - [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7999918]\n\nFrom the order page, we can see that the driver did not take the suggested route and finished the order far from destination, which matches with the rider’s comment on the order : \n\n{quote}The driver took wrong route, went to the closed road, cancelled the ride in a less than middle of the way at night (2am), promised to cancel the trip totally, but didn’t, so we paid full fare of 61 euro. Bolt was totally uncooperative and proposed first 5 euro, and then 20 euro. What a shame{quote}\n\nAbout the price rising, it’s due to the date the ride took place on : on the night of the 1st of january. A surge of 3x was applied to this order.\n\nThe rider contacted us in this [case|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/715255890]. Support proposed a 5€ then a 21.40€ refund, both declined by the rider.\nFinal message from the rider was : \n\n{quote}I don’t accept any refund lower than 50 eur out of 61 paid. If this is your final decision, i pass this dispute to external mediation according to Bolt rules{quote}\n\nFollowing our processes for cases like this (Rider: I wasn’t dropped off at my destination, Rider compensation guidelines & Rider: Small compensation values), and since more than half of the trip was completed, only a compensation of 3€ should have been issued.\n\nThat being said, due to the high surge of this order, the fact that the recalculation was disabled and that the driver ended the trip 2.24km from destination, I would advise a full refund.\n\nKindly give me your thoughts about it and I can issue a full refund immediatly if you agree.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-15T10:50:32.935Z"],["3812115","SREDESK-7423","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi Gajane,\nBoth of them were in the suppression list.\n\nI removed them and emptied the suppression list.\n\nSo the suppression list is empty now and doesn’t include any email addresses.\n\n\n{noformat}Thu Jan 15 12:47:37 EET 2026\n{\n    \"SuppressedDestination\": {\n        \"EmailAddress\": \"kalpana.kattamanchi@ruralshores.com\",\n        \"Reason\": \"BOUNCE\",\n        \"LastUpdateTime\": \"2026-01-07T15:37:40.463000+02:00\",\n        \"Attributes\": {\n            \"MessageId\": \"0107019b98ad5e00-68eb0092-6be7-4e23-ad87-fa7ae7b90974-000000\",\n            \"FeedbackId\": \"0107019b98ad6a4e-4297ea37-452b-4249-8057-54b3c9828423-000000\"\n        }\n    }\n}{noformat}\n\n-\n\n{noformat}{\n    \"SuppressedDestination\": {\n        \"EmailAddress\": \"divya.gorrala@ruralshores.com\",\n        \"Reason\": \"BOUNCE\",\n        \"LastUpdateTime\": \"2026-01-07T15:39:22.490000+02:00\",\n        \"Attributes\": {\n            \"MessageId\": \"0107019b98aef1cd-ac26fc5b-cccb-44e5-a0d7-4c8b41c5bdfe-000000\",\n            \"FeedbackId\": \"0107019b98aef8d0-49ee2e00-b416-42eb-96d2-1c6387481a69-000000\"\n        }\n    }\n}{noformat}","2026-01-15T10:50:36.069Z"],["3812117","LSS-58158","LSS","jimmy.pavesi@bolt.eu","Jimmy Pavesi","Awesome!!! thanks all!","2026-01-15T10:51:14.383Z"],["3812118","LSS-61381","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","looks fine! please proceed with the signatures","2026-01-15T10:51:21.698Z"],["3812121","DO-5798","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","You are not using your personal instance profile, you need to use {{dap-hu-nathan-valencia}} instead\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.18.png|width=556,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.18.png\"!","2026-01-15T10:52:11.876Z"],["3812122","SREDESK-7417","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Sounds good.\n\nPlease refer to this ticket later so the SREC on-call engineer will have more context.\n\nHave a nice day.","2026-01-15T10:52:19.873Z"],["3812123","PAW-14909","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160833\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 10:52:29 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T10:52:29.944Z"],["3812124","MM-942","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided. Developers lack information to start work.|\n|Clarity|🔴|The summary is vague (\"Adjust data replication\") with no further context or explanation.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting materials are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the scope and expected outcome.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-15T10:52:35.774Z"],["3812125","CSDA-281","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Got it. I will prep the query and the notebook by January 19. And then I will adjust from there based on the available data points and needs. So I will share the first export next Tuesday, January 20.\n\nLet me know if you have any further questions or comments ✨","2026-01-15T10:52:40.007Z"],["3812126","SREDESK-7424","SREDESK","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","Thank you!","2026-01-15T10:52:57.315Z"],["3812129","LSS-61620","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] !\n\nAfter taking a look at this contract, I believe that this is something that did not involved regional legal.\n\nCan you please let me know who and how the original contract was handled?\n\nAnd can you provide the original contract it here, please?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T10:53:10.343Z"],["3812131","LSS-61096","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] then we are ready to move with signing of the order, please proceed \n\ncan we sign and share pdf with supplier ?","2026-01-15T10:53:27.163Z"],["3812134","WDFT-3529","WDFT","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] the agreement has not been signed yet, but I have shared the list of fixed assets with local team and tax team who are dealing with the finalisation. Also our External legal advisor as marked this as part of the business transfer (I’ll share the file with you in slack as I can’t add any screenshots or attachment here).","2026-01-15T10:55:17.710Z"],["3812135","WFM-9997","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","Rux will request Beehive Rides OPS Agent\n\n[+08 RH_France_OPS+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/queues/edit/450009?tab=manage_agents] added","2026-01-15T10:55:32.758Z"],["3812136","GRWA-1481","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15336|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15336|smart-link] \n\nBackfilling the data to test in prod now.","2026-01-15T10:55:38.573Z"],["3812137","BSKT-4533","BSKT","yauheni.zara@bolt.eu","Yauheni Zara","Hello [~accountid:5f524fe6fcaf93003b5c6930] 👋 \n\nThis is an error code we are going to additionally throw if Card deletion requires {{force_delete}} flag to be passed - [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/ad37a9d690d825b8d0b61bb678e7ced005888eec/src/platform/payment/payment_instrument/main/constants/ResponseCodes.ts#L14|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/ad37a9d690d825b8d0b61bb678e7ced005888eec/src/platform/payment/payment_instrument/main/constants/ResponseCodes.ts#L14] ","2026-01-15T10:56:32.981Z"],["3812142","WFM-9969","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","role approed","2026-01-15T10:57:20.843Z"],["3812143","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] no, unfortunately this was not added in the ticket before. Thanks for sharing! \nAre there any other documents that were submitted with the tender but are not included with this ticket?\nThanks!","2026-01-15T10:57:21.254Z"],["3812144","LSS-60541","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:62c696a740923988ba0ae796], \n\nPlease find below the link to the bilingual version of the LOI (Spanish and English).\n\nFeel free to share it with the partners, and if they are comfortable with the terms, please let me know so we can proceed with the signing process.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n[EN - ES (bilingual) LOI|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QqlDzGVrLgNK-CZzfrC_fUzvixZnwGjz/edit]","2026-01-15T10:57:23.687Z"],["3812145","LSS-61626","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","[^Chesterfield - Business Rates Refund Claim Form .pdf] _(3.64 MB)_","2026-01-15T10:57:31.299Z"],["3812146","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","h2. Call notes – Voi / Bolt alignment on Unit 9 Phoenix Park\n\nh3. Date and time: 15 January 2026, 10am.\n\nh3. Attendees\n\n*Bolt:*\n\n* John Buckley (JB)\n* Rachel Sallnow (RS)\n* Sasha Dornan (SD)\n\n*Voi:*\n\n* Isaac Cole (IC) – Legal\n* James Timmins (JT) – Operations\n\n----\n\nh2. Background / context\n\n* JB confirmed he met with the landlord in January and the landlord is *comfortable with Bolt occupying the premises as soon as possible*.\n\n----\n\nh2. Discussion\n\nh3. Voi’s preferred position\n\n* *IC:* Voi is currently the tenant. Their lease includes a *break option in July*, which requires *notice to be served by April*.\n* Voi’s *ideal scenario* is:\n** Bolt agrees a *new lease directly with the landlord*, and\n** Voi *surrenders its existing lease*, removing its ongoing liability.\n* To achieve this, Voi would need to *serve its break notice imminently*, so Bolt needs to progress landlord negotiations as soon as possible.\n* Voi’s position is that there is *no commercial interest for Voi in assigning the lease*.\n\n----\n\nh3. Timing and occupation\n\n* *JB:* Bolt wants access to the warehouse *as soon as possible* and is open to any structure that allows early occupation.\n* *JT:* Voi will *stop using the warehouse after 8 February* and is comfortable for Bolt to take over occupation from around that date.\n* *IC:* 8 February is a *theoretical date*. Bolt can occupy earlier, but legally this depends on structure.\n* IC noted it is *unlikely that a new lease with the landlord will be agreed by 8 February*.\n\n----\n\nh3. Interim solution – sub-lease\n\n* *IC:* Given timing constraints, the likely interim solution is for Bolt to *enter as a sub-tenant* while Voi remains the head tenant.\n* *IC:* Nothing in Voi’s existing lease *prevents sub-letting*.\n* *JT:* Voi is happy to pursue:\n** sub-letting to Bolt as a temporary measure, followed by\n** surrender of Voi’s lease once Bolt’s new lease is agreed with the landlord.\n* This structure has been used successfully by Voi previously (e.g. Bristol warehouse with Tier / DOT).\n\n----\n\nh3. Landlord engagement\n\n* *IC:* Voi has already proposed *surrender + new lease* to the landlord via Bee (Brabners), but has *not yet received a response*.\n* *IC / JT:* At this stage, Bolt (as the incoming tenant) needs to *push landlord negotiations forward*, as there is a limit to what Voi can do.\n* *IC:* If Bolt does *not* secure a new lease by July, Bolt will *not have warehouse access beyond that point*.\n\n----\n\nh3. Next steps and responsibilities\n\n* *SD:* Bolt will reply to Bee confirming that Bolt and Voi have discussed and aligned on the position.\n* *IC:* Voi will:\n** instruct external counsel to prepare a *sub-lease*, and\n** share a draft with Bolt for review.\n* *IC:* Voi expects *Bolt to cover Voi’s legal fees* in relation to the sub-lease (quote to follow).\n* *IC:* Requested that Bolt keeps Voi updated on progress with the landlord.\n* *IC:* Voi intends to *serve its break notice within the next week*.","2026-01-15T10:57:31.938Z"],["3812147","LSS-54291","LSS","viktor.skalivskyi@bolt.eu","Viktor Skalivskyi","Hello colleagues. As I wrote in Slack our document with the approval of the internal services of ATB - but there are still comments from the partner.\n\nI am copying the text from the email here without translation so as not to be ambiguous.\n\nThank you.\n\n_(egarding point 1, I have already clarified - they need our documents for the LLC >_ [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1AvfhVN0pX7IyzIFcT64SGXwxV27PVXhD?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1AvfhVN0pX7IyzIFcT64SGXwxV27PVXhD?usp=drive_link|smart-link] \n\n----\n\nЗауваження до проекту договору б/н\nпро надання посередницьких послуг між ТОВ «АТБ – МАРКЕТ» та ТОВ «Болт Оперейшнз Україна»\n\n# Відсутні правовстановлюючі документи щодо контрагента.\n# П. 3.3.4 – рекомендуємо доповнити і вказати, що належним підтвердженням факту настання форс-мажорної події буде сертифікат, виданий Торгово-промисловою палатою та бґрунтоване письмове повідомлення про це іншої Сторони.\n# П. 3.13 та п. 4.1 – вказано, що Партнер уповноважує Bolt приймати платежі від Користувачів від імені Партнера за допомогою вбудованих алгоритмів Додатку. А в п. 3.2 зазначено, що Партнер зобов’язується надати Кур’єрові фіскальний чек із зазначенням виду оплати “післяплата” для надання її Користувачу. Рекомендуємо чітко прописати форму оплати товару Користувачами.\n# П. 4.2 – сума винагороди «4% від Бази нарахування, без урахування ПДВ» - зона відповідальності профільної служби.\n# П 5.4.1 – звернути увагу на строк прийняття замовлення ТОВ «АТБ – МАРКЕТ» (5 хвилин).\n# Розділ 9 – доповнити умовами, згідно яких належним підтвердженням виникнення форс-мажорних обставин є сертифікат Торгово-промислової палати України або її територіальних органів.\n# Додаток № 3 – виправити назву з «Звіту агента» на «Звіт агента».\n# В Договорі відсутня відповідальність Bolt перед Партнером за несвоєчасну оплату товару, не врегульовані обставини щодо відповідальності кур’єрів або Bolt у випадку несвоєчасної доставки замовлення.\n# Умови щодо податкових ризиків рекомендуємо погодити з бухгалтерією.\n\n\n10. Даний договір повинен бути погоджений усіма відповідальними службами.\n11. Рішення про укладення договору, з урахуванням зауважень ЮС, є управлінським.\n\nТакож немає жодних змін з попередньої версії, ви просто надали коментар – коментар це не договір.\nБудь ласка, зазначте всі зауваження (в тому числі і попередні) в самому договорі.\n\nТакож прошу врахувати:\nРекомендуємо додати у пункт 3.13 Договору, назву і реквізити Договору з банківською установою,\n\nщо уповноважена на збір коштів від Замовників та їх передачу на БОЛТ.\nВідсутність пунктів про податкові ризики, у Виконавця скорочується відповідальність за нарахування контролюючими органами\n\nподаткових донарахувань, штрафних санкцій, за коректність відображення показників у податковій звітності,\n\nта можливість проведення оперативних заходів щодо усунення негативних/ризикових ситуацій, пов'язаних з претензіями контролюючих та правоохоронних органів.\n\n\n----\n\nThis is the last version of the contract.\n\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jF8KMMYZYMVTKYf9O_dEvr-F0b2OOSWa/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jF8KMMYZYMVTKYf9O_dEvr-F0b2OOSWa/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\n----\n\nThank you! \n\n[~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95] [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] [~accountid:619628e6b0b630006a6d2919] \ncc: [~accountid:712020:d6cadc67-55ba-4993-9498-9fb9531798c5] ","2026-01-15T10:57:35.090Z"],["3812148","LSS-61625","LSS","fernando.berzosa@bolt.eu","Fernando Berzosa","please find here the notification: [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MZDOP3o89VLNh_gBGYRjo4UhbC-mB0K2/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MZDOP3o89VLNh_gBGYRjo4UhbC-mB0K2/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T10:57:36.131Z"],["3812149","FX-3640","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768474647666499]*{color}:\nPR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160818]\n{quote}","2026-01-15T10:57:39.806Z"],["3812150","SREDESK-7419","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Hey [~accountid:712020:82a49ddb-c340-4f47-963d-7acca442cb8b] ,\n\nCan you confirm whether it is it related to ITGC or any other team?","2026-01-15T10:57:42.833Z"],["3812153","LSS-61618","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached. [^TPEQ Bolt Australia_Engagement Letter_15Jan26 (5782dff8-0387-4836-92bc-08cda018603d).pdf] ","2026-01-15T10:58:24.513Z"],["3812154","LSS-61421","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Template - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G27H_-uHkHMmTlSfvs-K4Rj4siDOyPRb/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G27H_-uHkHMmTlSfvs-K4Rj4siDOyPRb/edit]","2026-01-15T10:58:24.373Z"],["3812156","LSS-60637","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - should we go ahead and cancel this flow?","2026-01-15T10:59:14.472Z"],["3812157","CSXDL-148","CSXDL","kristiina.himma@bolt.eu","Kristiina Himma","Met with [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] who wil get us a Legal perspective on ROD across all markets.","2026-01-15T10:59:25.418Z"],["3812159","PFI-833703","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^NBC STATEMENT EXTRACT.pdf]\n\n[^SWIFT COPY BOLT (1).pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.40.36.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^payment BOLT NBC.pdf]","2026-01-15T11:00:00.444Z"],["3812162","LSS-59379","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","The letter template is fine and can be sent to the mall. Thank you! ","2026-01-15T11:00:50.818Z"],["3812163","LSS-61626","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T11:01:11.882Z"],["3812164","DO-5800","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","I need approval from Yash and get the whole list since the access grant needs to be added programmatically","2026-01-15T11:01:19.639Z"],["3812165","LSS-61421","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:5e835f0f9b6a000c1a324a3f] can you please provide the signed agreement with the previous fleet (CF Somda) along with all of the amendments, if any?\n\nBelow is the draft template for assignment, please check and fill in all missing details (both fleets and sureties' details, details of the original agreement, etc.) that are highlighted in yellow.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1__2REgQp_D-_Ssq1dKW_g07P2RGk1dvZ/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1__2REgQp_D-_Ssq1dKW_g07P2RGk1dvZ/edit|smart-link] \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:76b6df07-e71d-429f-a069-ee3c132ee915] ","2026-01-15T11:01:25.843Z"],["3812167","LSS-55096","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:5e6b55b518039c0cf3f19c12] [~accountid:712020:e001fc10-7a16-4f85-8b97-61c45aa27669] - please find the signed document attached 🙂 \n\n[^Provision of Services Agreement_Bolt Support Services PT_CBRE GWS_22.12.25.pdf] ","2026-01-15T11:02:25.579Z"],["3812169","TA-11","TA","paulo.morna@bolt.eu","Paulo Morna","Meeting with People tech (January 15th)\n\nh2. Overall Status\n\nThe offer standardization and automation project in Greenhouse is *largely built and nearing pilot readiness*. Core functionality (salary, grades, stocks, templates, and country logic) is in place, with final data refreshes and validation pending before pilot launch.\n\n----\n\nh2. What’s Completed\n\n* *Automated offer generation in Greenhouse*\n** Offers generated directly in Greenhouse with PDF and editable Word versions.\n** Default template selection largely automated (with limited manual override if needed).\n* *Compensation automation*\n** Salary ranges, grades, and role-based logic integrated.\n** Stock calculations (grant amount and annualized value) implemented and auto-calculated based on salary.\n** Stock one-pager explanations dynamically included in the offer PDF based on location and stock type.\n* *Custom fields & data setup*\n** Significant work completed to configure custom fields (manager, probation period, compensation details, etc.).\n** Manager now auto-populates correctly.\n** Blue-collar vs white-collar logic supported and tied to job profiles.\n* *Templates & usability*\n** Offer templates are functional and already shared internally.\n** Editing flow supported (download Word → edit → re-upload).\n** Early demo completed and positively received by TA.\n\n----\n\nh2. What’s Still Pending / In Progress\n\n* *Final data refresh for 2026*\n** Update salary ranges and stock data using the latest inputs from Getter.\n** Mihood to complete this upon return from vacation.\n* *Validation & testing*\n** Thorough testing of stock grant and annualized value calculations to ensure 100% accuracy.\n** Additional testing across countries before broader rollout.\n* *Stock documentation*\n** Some stock one-pagers from Getter are still outstanding or need confirmation they are finalized.\n* *Design & branding*\n** Branding/design improvements pending.\n** Existing branded offer template has now been shared and will be reviewed for integration.\n** Brand team ticket may be raised if needed.\n* *Offer email configuration*\n** Email subject line and body for sending offers via Greenhouse not yet finalized.\n** TA team to share proposed email copy for configuration.\n* *E-signature*\n** Greenhouse e-signature functionality acknowledged but planned as a later enhancement, not blocking pilot.\n\n----\n\nh2. Pilot Plan & Timelines\n\n* *Week of Jan 19*\n** Refresh 2026 salary and stock data.\n** Final internal checks and preparation.\n* *Week of Jan 26*\n** *Start pilot testing* with TA team.\n** Testing kickoff session to be scheduled (targeting sometime between *Jan 26–30*).\n** Pilot group: Commercial Team (maybe High Volume team too)\n* *End of January*\n** Live demo / walkthrough session with TA and project team.\n** Feedback collection and issue fixing.","2026-01-15T11:02:29.466Z"],["3812170","LSS-61533","LSS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e], \n\nWe are the ones asking her to send us their criminal record from the Criminal Record registry of all countries you have been living in the past 3 years, which should include the archived/expired records. \n\nFrom my knowledge, it is internal procedure and we are not sharing those documents with a third party. \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin ","2026-01-15T11:02:55.945Z"],["3812171","RDXENG-4661","RDXENG","germo.rikk@bolt.eu","Germo Rikk","Thanks!\n\nSadly this was never reproducible for me (I had trips on live & prelive and for me the correct driver was always shown), however, I'll keep an eye out for any new reports! :salute:","2026-01-15T11:03:28.759Z"],["3812172","FX-3640","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768475005498329]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3640 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T11:03:39.371Z"],["3812175","INSUR-175","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","* Sent Carlo all the details needed to get quotes.\n* Today, I am following up with the local team and asking them to contact Alianza/our broker about it. \n* Consider self-insurance, although it may not seem like a viable solution at this time.\n** High claim-loss %\n** Structure not in place \n** Exposure risks  ","2026-01-15T11:04:17.448Z"],["3812176","DO-5800","DO","dinithi.dulmini@bolt.eu","Dinithi Dulmini","It will take time for us to connect with the respective POCs for the CX tables. Appreciate if we can have above only for now as it’s urgent. \n\n[~accountid:712020:1ad69740-fd8b-4546-a0ef-3ea66f0f19bf] Please help to approve","2026-01-15T11:04:34.355Z"],["3812177","LSS-61627","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Qamar Ahmad.pdf] _(126 kB)_","2026-01-15T11:04:35.152Z"],["3812180","WD-22581","WD","luigi.de.rosa@bolt.eu","Luigi De Rosa","!1000000893.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image (1).png|thumbnail!\n\n!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T11:04:58.870Z"],["3812181","LSS-60250","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] this ticket can be closed we have now added all cars into one contract under a different ticket so all is done. ","2026-01-15T11:05:18.709Z"],["3812182","LSS-61049","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","Hi [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad] any updates? Thank you! ","2026-01-15T11:05:25.187Z"],["3812184","LSS-61183","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pvW8Jiuz4et5o-N3SLWz1PTP6DgchO9E/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pvW8Jiuz4et5o-N3SLWz1PTP6DgchO9E/edit]","2026-01-15T11:05:32.491Z"],["3812186","LSS-60774","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","[~accountid:712020:d8161849-388c-4312-84ee-638c0b0ece4f]  this ticket can be closed we have now added all cars into one contract under a different ticket so all is done. ","2026-01-15T11:06:00.373Z"],["3812189","LSS-61421","LSS","bayram.khalilzade@bolt.eu","Bayram Khalilzade","Here are the links for the signed agreements [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] \n[{color:#4c9aff}*CF Somda*{color}|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1y8ldKlKsmfo84cdYvrWEsD3cO-BK9pmi/view?usp=sharing]{color:#4c9aff} {color}\n[{color:#4c9aff}*CF Somda Amend_1*{color}|https://drive.google.com/file/d/156N-MmYwtry6WhW5BeG2-XPkHBHwaUXe/view?usp=sharing]{color:#4c9aff} {color}\n\n\n","2026-01-15T11:06:38.396Z"],["3812192","LSS-61408","LSS","lavinia-georgiana.ene@bolt.eu","Lavinia-Georgiana Ene","Hi, team! Any updates? It’s pretty urgent.🙏 ","2026-01-15T11:07:17.138Z"],["3812193","WD-22372","WD","keidi.helm@bolt.eu","Keidi Helm","Hi\n\nWe discussed it additionally in our team. Could I please ask to change the schedule to the one I shared:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.01.04.png|width=873,height=203,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.01.04.png\"!\n\nSince we have time difference with Paraguay 5h, this would ensure the ability to have the  cut-off late evening at 23:00 PY time, meaning any info completed before the 23:00 PY time would reach the primary report. Otherwise the cut-off would be the the end of working hours for them.\n\nThank you for your support!\nKeidi\n\n","2026-01-15T11:07:58.533Z"],["3812195","PFI-833708","PFI","vania.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Vania Silva","[^Bolt Oficial.pdf (2).pdf]","2026-01-15T11:08:05.036Z"],["3812196","PFI-833708","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T11:08:07.110Z"],["3812199","LSS-61421","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] hey, please check that all details of the parties and the main contract along with its amendment are added to the assignment correctly, thanks! \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:76b6df07-e71d-429f-a069-ee3c132ee915] ","2026-01-15T11:08:33.922Z"],["3812203","PAW-14893","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-15T11:10:11.378Z"],["3812205","LSS-61123","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5b7bea7195627d2a5723efff] ! This document will be ready shortly","2026-01-15T11:10:41.533Z"],["3812207","DBRE-8701","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","*@user-U01AH7VKNHY*, are you checking it?  They have fullscans from [archiver|http://ti-user-pd-3.sqldb:2379/dashboard/#/statement/detail?query=%7B%22digest%22%3A%2281986b70facef8bc15f774a01436056bc5e041147ef63256202fdeec74085314%22%2C%22schema%22%3A%22taxify_gdpr_data_deletion%22%2C%22beginTime%22%3A1768471377%2C%22endTime%22%3A1768473178%7D] (i guess they assume limit 10 will help) and [gdpr deletion|http://ti-user-pd-3.sqldb:2379/dashboard/#/statement/detail?query=%7B%22digest%22%3A%225e189db1aa67e2153737870bed736ebb9f4b479eb0d3785bdf79886f283bcd0b%22%2C%22schema%22%3A%22taxify_gdpr_data_deletion%22%2C%22beginTime%22%3A1768471377%2C%22endTime%22%3A1768473178%7D] (properly bad query with shitty cardinality)","2026-01-15T11:11:34.017Z"],["3812208","DBRE-8701","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Leandro Morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1768473391436859?thread_ts=1768473169.910209&cid=C03055EHHPS|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03055EHHPS/p1768473391436859?thread_ts=1768473169.910209&cid=C03055EHHPS|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T11:11:34.831Z"],["3812209","DRX-8347","DRX","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","prelive is done: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C5SQB8V6G/p1768386905751619|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C5SQB8V6G/p1768386905751619|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T11:11:44.928Z"],["3812212","DBRE-8701","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* First GPDR query now has plan binding to force it to use index over full table scan\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.05.17.png|width=735,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.05.17.png\"!\n{noformat}root@ti-user-dba.sqldb:taxify_gdpr_data_deletion>EXPLAIN ANALYZE /* gdpr-data-deletion-86bc85564d-kwr75|@privacy-backend|gdpr-data-deletion|cron_process|DeletionRetryingCron|live-gdprdatadeletion */\n                                             ->  SELECT\n                                             ->    /*+ MAX_EXECUTION_TIME(60000)