uild_task_duration: 32.5µs, max_distsql_concurrency: 1, max_extra_concurrency: 1}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:2, total_time:1.77ms}, rpc_errors:{region_not_found:1}}, backoff{regionMiss: 2ms}, tikv_task:{time:0s, loops:1}, scan_detail: {total_process_keys: 1, total_process_keys_size: 81, total_keys: 4, get_snapshot_time: 13.7µs, rocksdb: {key_skipped_count: 3, block: {cache_hit_count: 9, read_count: 1, read_byte: 9.94 KB, read_time: 8.85µs}}}, time_detail: {total_process_time: 146.9µs, total_wait_time: 31.7µs, tikv_wall_time: 253.3µs}\noperator info  | keep order:false\nmemory         | N/A\ndisk           | N/A\n5 rows in set\nTime: 0.011s{noformat}","2026-01-15T11:12:59.637Z"],["3812217","PFI-833712","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T11:13:37.800Z"],["3812218","PFI-833712","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5ad49d416f41620ce1adf1ee] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T11:13:39.160Z"],["3812220","LSS-61123","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343206|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343206|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T11:14:06.627Z"],["3812222","LSS-60589","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f4038db4-c597-4af7-9604-402e9f17edd5] and [~accountid:712020:54af1c3b-f46c-435b-b870-e013cd29eada], \n\nScenario 1 (11k) + Scenario (13k) → in both cases, but for different reasons, payment was made to the wrong fleet entity. \n\n* Scenario 1 - correct me if I am wrong, full payment was not made to correct fleet entity because was partially due to the fleet owner providing an inccorect RIB + wrong fleet beneficiary is refusing or uncooperative to refund the payment received in error;\n* Scenario 2 - full payment was made to correct fleet because error was on Bolt (TP)'s fault as the IBAN was incorrectly inputted + wrong fleet beneficiary is refusing or uncooperative to refund the payment received in error. \n\n\n\nThe internal process of who to contact in order to ask the bank to request the funds back due to a mistaken payment is one topic. \n\nThis ticket is to analyse our options in respect of TP’s fault. \n\n* In light of this, we could claim contractual penalties from TP (most likely more applicable in Scenario 2) → to be noted that a claim should be made within 60 days of discovering the breach. Can we verify whether we have documents supporting this and evidencing the date we discovered the breach?\n* In parallel, could you confirm whether any discussions have been held with TP to share discontent of the error or to address these mistakes going forward? [~accountid:712020:af076e83-bb33-4eb6-8634-6e435217c5e4] I think you mentioned a “penalty document” ? Please could you share it here?\n\n\nThank you !\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ","2026-01-15T11:14:27.685Z"],["3812225","LSS-61573","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","Hi Beatriz,\n\nAnswering your questions:\n\n\n# Invoice submission period:\n\n* Once a month\n\n# Approximate number of invoices involved:\n\n* 2 invoices\n\n# Who is ultimately responsible for submitting invoices on behalf of Bolt Business?\n\n* Initially, during the client's setup, it will be me; later, it will be someone from the After-Sales team.\n\n[~accountid:712020:793bd952-a372-4264-98c5-05f34ecedce8] , could you tell us who will be responsible? Perhaps Catarina?","2026-01-15T11:15:42.239Z"],["3812231","DO-5800","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Granted for “f_leet_campaign_bonus_”. Could you please check?","2026-01-15T11:16:56.398Z"],["3812232","DO-5800","DO","dinithi.dulmini@bolt.eu","Dinithi Dulmini","Thanks. Got it","2026-01-15T11:17:22.448Z"],["3812233","PFI-833717","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T11:17:22.793Z"],["3812234","LSS-58833","LSS","pawel.orfin@bolt.eu","Paweł Orfin","Hey team, Zabka Jush! confirmed our changes and asked us to adjust PL version and initiate signing. Can we do it?\n\nFrom their side it’s two people signing: \n\n* Zuzanna Dębowska, CCO, zuzanna@lite.tech\n* Maciej Nowakowski, CEO Lite E-commerce, maciej@lite.tech\n\n","2026-01-15T11:17:36.170Z"],["3812235","LSS-61381","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi Legal Ops! Please sign by the signature of Ahto with DigiDoc asice signature. Thanks!","2026-01-15T11:18:09.690Z"],["3812236","LSS-61620","LSS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] ,\n\nPlease let me know if the original contract for Malta payroll provider was handled through you/your dep and if we can answer to the above request. \n\nAppreciate the support, \n\nLore","2026-01-15T11:18:44.802Z"],["3812238","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team! \n\nAlthough we still do not know whether the contractual terms will be open for negotiation, I am sharing my initial review and comments on the NDA, the Code of Conduct, and the Supply Agreement.\n\n*Key points:*\n\n# [*Code of Conduct*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1102pFPl8QSnU9Ns-MHizao9ZZ9NUerwt/edit]\nI do not see any major risks in signing the CoC in its current form. However, if there is room to negotiate, I have proposed alternative CoC wording that is more closely aligned with Bolt’s standard contractual approach.\n# *Separate NDA vs. confidentiality provisions in the Supply Agreement*\nIt is unclear why a standalone NDA is required, given that the Supply Agreement already contains a dedicated confidentiality section, including breach penalties and other safeguards.\n\nFrom Bolt’s perspective, this needs to be clearly communicated to PwC: *we cannot sign both agreements covering the same subject matter.* Accordingly, either:\n\n* a separate NDA is signed and the confidentiality section is removed from the Supply Agreement, *or*\n* no separate NDA is signed and the parties rely solely on the confidentiality provisions set out in the Supply Agreement.\n\n\n\n# [*NDA* |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xAHmpM5TkVgPEOWgq5_yOl0Fn8BX4Si6/edit]\nThe NDA is drafted with an unlimited duration and very high penalties for each breach. I have suggested amendments aimed at making these provisions more balanced.\n\n\n\n# [*Supply Agreement* |https://docs.google.com/document/d/10ciLA6CYrJNAsA7RCgJSk4aYQx0xjaPDOJ0yRo6riPw/edit?tab=t.0]\nThe Supply Agreement is not tailored to Ride-Hailing or Taxi services *at all*. Ideally, and with more time, it would require a substantial rewrite.\n\nFor now, I have focused on amending the most critical provisions from a Bolt perspective. *That said, the agreement as a whole must also be thoroughly reviewed from an Ops standpoint (*[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14]). *In particular, what we can realistically commit to, what we cannot, and where the contractual assumptions do not reflect operational reality.*\nWhere a clause does not match how things work in practice, or where we cannot genuinely ensure compliance, please tag me so that appropriate wording can be suggested.","2026-01-15T11:19:39.938Z"],["3812239","FX-3601","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768476002405979]*{color}:\nHey! I didn't have time to take a look.\n<@U099AALFKFH> do you have time to look at this task as part of your duties? If not, I can come back to it by the end of next week.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T11:20:15.630Z"],["3812240","LSS-61541","LSS","christos.hadjistylianou@bolt.eu","Christos Hadjistylianou","[~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] \n\nDo you have access to [this|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17yfl_d85YtTXgArAew4AqkkK27Qp6-FQ2m9TK60pHFg/edit?tab=t.0]?","2026-01-15T11:21:27.057Z"],["3812245","SCM-1080","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Data export by inventory team:\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/11qU0fBJgNprTmKVbXZOlRapfixcGaqwhZF1QV1Xdcyc/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/11qU0fBJgNprTmKVbXZOlRapfixcGaqwhZF1QV1Xdcyc/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-15T11:22:46.377Z"],["3812247","PFI-833722","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T11:22:55.281Z"],["3812248","L10N-28033","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:23:40.609Z"],["3812249","L10N-28037","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:23:40.721Z"],["3812250","L10N-28036","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide 