7.656Z"],["3812270","PFI-822324","PFI","karla.blekte@bolt-outsource.eu","Karla Blekte","Hi! Any updates? ","2026-01-15T11:25:55.594Z"],["3812271","RF-156","RF","siddhant.saxena@bolt.eu","Siddhant Saxena","Targets\nRatio level first\nThen Non Ratio - how to come to weekly\nHow do we get to country and region ","2026-01-15T11:25:56.547Z"],["3812274","LSS-59624","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey team,\n\nDo you have anything to add here?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T11:26:15.618Z"],["3812276","DSR-2905","DSR","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] we are awaiting feedback from local ops.","2026-01-15T11:27:04.122Z"],["3812279","FX-3601","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768476457551719]*{color}:\nHey <@U05A7SK0P8B> I will be able to look at it, but it will take time as I need to make proper investigation for that, so <@UCVT712UR> please note there can be a delay here\n{quote}","2026-01-15T11:27:51.295Z"],["3812281","PC-4941","PC","alexander.blinov@bolt.eu","Alexander Blinov","Billing calls capture as fast as possible already","2026-01-15T11:28:05.491Z"],["3812284","LSS-61469","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6], in addition to those provided by [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] please kindly find attached the [repository|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WXbFr0kkO_TIDEHS25zjdf9Vi_6TM6CVeFw1T4gbOJ0/edit?gid=0#gid=0] containing all resolutions adopted at HQ. I have shared access with you. The repository includes the date of each resolution, the drafting status, links to the resolutions, and a brief summary of what has been resolved or decided.\n\nFor your convenience, I am also attaching the resolutions as separate files (starting from Sept 2025). Please let me know if you need anything else.\n\n[^MB resolution - conversion 29.12.2025 (2).asice] [^Board Meeting Minutes 09.09.2025 .docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T11:28:31.758Z"],["3812286","WD-22372","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Update in progress: \n\n!image-20260115-112935.png|width=1102,alt=\"image-20260115-112935.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-15T11:29:41.193Z"],["3812287","DO-5800","DO","dinithi.dulmini@bolt.eu","Dinithi Dulmini","[~accountid:712020:061a9010-0948-45f3-81ba-d6d4ba88b4bf] Apologies, we were able to find the table names faster than expected 🙂 . Below are the CX tables. Please help to grant access 🙏 \n\n{{core_models_spark.fact_support_case}}\n\n{{core_models_spark.fact_support_price_review}}\n\n{{core_models_spark.dim_support_agent_snapshot}}\n\n{{core_models_spark.fact_support_case_handling_time_event}}","2026-01-15T11:29:52.025Z"],["3812289","SREP-1107","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","[https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/issues/2777|https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/issues/2777]","2026-01-15T11:30:33.120Z"],["3812290","WD-22581","WD","sami.elchami@bolt.eu","Sami El-Chami","Approved ","2026-01-15T11:30:33.737Z"],["3812293","HS-28985","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:82f745be-d9fb-4c21-a96d-23ad0cbc7e2f] , the from was sent to your personal e-mail ([lecomte.clement0996@gmail.com|mailto:lecomte.clement0996@gmail.com]). I sent a reminder to better find it. Please check your spam box, as it might’ve gone there. ","2026-01-15T11:30:45.191Z"],["3812295","LSS-61629","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T11:31:27.972Z"],["3812298","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:712020:23b54a2f-1913-42e1-9019-8b2c32303d27] \n\nTested in newer CA.193.0 {{develop}} 21028310058 build and it’s format has broken (x) \n\n!capture-20260115-113205.png|width=198,alt=\"capture-20260115-113205.png\"!","2026-01-15T11:32:37.932Z"],["3812300","LSS-61421","LSS","ramil.maharramov@bolt.eu","Ramil Maharramov","Thanks Anna. It would be great if we could sign this assignment agreement by  mid next week latest. Thanks a lot. ","2026-01-15T11:32:41.371Z"],["3812303","LSS-60959","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Cognito: [https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyoü/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries/287|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/personaldatabreachriskassessment/1-all-entries/287]","2026-01-15T11:33:03.702Z"],["3812305","LSS-61620","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Hey [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac],\n\nI was not involved in these discussions back then, so I do not know who from local/regional reviewed the contract as it is since 2022. \n\nMaybe Regional legal can search / try searching through Jira records and see if there was a ticket back then.\n\nBut nevertheless, I managed to do some digging and found the agreement that is being extended in Spotdraft, see it attached here. \n\nOne note, though, when checking the amendment attached there is a typo in the extension and it says “parties wish to extend until the 30th of June 2025” and I think it should be “2026”. (screenshot attached)\n\nAlso as a side note, as this is an operational extension most likely to allow for Payroll Processing continuity until Papaya will be implemented ([~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] to confirm), from Procurement side this is good to go. So a short term extension of 6 months of existing service. \n\n*! Only one thing to be kept in mind is when we terminate UHY for payroll (if/when that will be the case) , that we clearly make it clear that we only want to terminate payroll related services of this agreement and not agreement entirely as based on the contract I see they also due some CIT/accounting/other services for us not just payroll.* \n\nThank you both!\n\n[^Service agreement_Bolt Support Services MT Ltd_UHY BASL_27.04.2022.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.22.41.png|width=661,height=59,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.22.41.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T11:33:52.428Z"],["3812307","DBRE-8701","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","High read rate is gone:\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.33.56.png|width=759,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.33.56.png\"!","2026-01-15T11:34:19.846Z"],["3812311","DELIVERY-1425","DELIVERY","mihai.burlaciuc@bolt.eu","Mihai Burlăciuc","Screenshot with the Sound Settings page in Marchant app for context \n\n!IMG_5642.png|width=1170,height=2532,alt=\"IMG_5642.png\"!","2026-01-15T11:35:00.460Z"],["3812312","RNTL-29682","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","[AB Scorecard|https://ab-scorecard.data.boltint.net/abtests/targeting?mode=hypothesis&k=targeting&n=MM%20-%20Dual%20Pricing%20-%20Brussels%20(14518)&e=2025-12-19&cg=Control&tg=Treatment%201&tg=Treatment%202&f=&min=500&sep=] show DBP has lower GMV by 5%, while DBP price also [setup lower|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10F5-kTMrF4D7QsncaKPYehkkIUGUNf_M13MBpLGzgT8/edit?gid=1965673943#gid=1965673943] than TBP by 8%.","2026-01-15T11:36:11.591Z"],["3812313","LSS-61460","LSS","joshua.okeleke@bolt.eu","Josh Okeleke","Hi Thomas,\n\nQuick update, our sync with Finmid has been moved up to the 20th PM - so\nthe hard deadline would be the 19th please.\n\nThank you 🙏","2026-01-15T11:36:16.921Z"],["3812314","PFI-822079","PFI","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Hello, [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b], could you please have a look at the above? 🙏 ","2026-01-15T11:37:26.368Z"],["3812316","WAVE-230","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","Initiated talks with [~accountid:61a72da7ebce4700677d174f] , created new react-native-platform team in the SaaS instance, so they can have alerts, projects etc","2026-01-15T11:37:56.492Z"],["3812317","PFI-833710","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f28ada62-b0db-47a0-93bc-12a25ae2b2d6],\n\nCould you please explain further on how you have reached the conclusion of our rules working incorrectly and that the users should be getting the discounts?\n\nFrom what we can see, these are essentially fake accounts created at the very same location, detected by the location GPS that is within the profiling rule that you have mentioned. This means that there already is a legit user who has received the discount/promotion and they are no longer eligible for another one.\nFrom the example that you have shared, everything seems to be working correctly.\n\nPlease keep in mind, that the fraudsters will do whatever it takes to receive an additional promotional code/discounts.\n\nWe will not be loosening our rules based on this example.\n\n*Please keep in mind that the information above is strictly internal and should not be shared with the user, we do not want to educate our users on how to perform fraud on our platform and not get caught.*\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-15T11:38:24.824Z"],["3812318","WAVE-229","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","+ helped to setup alerting to their alerts channel","2026-01-15T11:38:25.350Z"],["3812319","LSS-61105","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:5acb1f48d8b95a2b34f150a8] and [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446],\n\nQuick update on this driver escalation (cc: [~accountid:60c7025b5c64b10071aef787]).\n\n*Background:* the driver has sent a Letter Before Action claiming *loss of earnings* following two temporary suspensions of his account. Bolt’s investigation confirmed that the second suspension should not have occurred and was the result of *human error*. The driver is now reinstated but is threatening a small-claims action for compensation.\n\nWe’ve reviewed the claim against the *standard driver T&Cs* and, on that basis, I’ve drafted a *defensive response letter* (attached) setting out why Bolt does not accept liability for loss of earnings, while explaining the contractual basis for temporary suspension and reinstatement.\n\nBefore we send this, could you please let me know:\n\n# *Goodwill gesture* – would you like to include a small goodwill gesture (e.g. a discretionary credit) alongside the letter, or would you prefer to keep the response strictly contractual? As you know, a goodwill gesture can help de-escalate the situation, reduce the likelihood of a small-claims filing, and show good faith without admitting liability, but it’s entirely optional.\n# *Service details* – [~accountid:60c7025b5c64b10071aef787], please could you confirm the driver’s *current postal address and email address*, so we can send the letter directly once agreed?\n\n*Timing:* the deadline to respond to the driver is {color:#ff5630}+*tomorrow*+{color}, so we’d appreciate a quick steer on the above if possible, please.\n\n[^Letter to Mr Sau Wa Wong - Bolt Services UK Limited.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T11:38:30.274Z"],["3812320","L10N-28066","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28064](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28064)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:38:35.936Z"],["3812321","L10N-28068","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28064](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28064)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:38:39.312Z"],["3812322","L10N-28070","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28064](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28064)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:38:40.133Z"],["3812323","L10N-28074","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks