 note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28064](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28064)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:38:45.661Z"],["3812327","L10N-28080","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28064](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28064)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T11:38:45.891Z"],["3812329","CAMLE-9822","CAMLE","uladzislau.tolkach@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tolkach","thread with details: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C051F6RN1RP/p1768394866179469|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C051F6RN1RP/p1768394866179469|smart-link] \n\n{quote}I've looked into /internal/getCampaignDiscountsForHomeScreen from RCC which has increased timeouts.\nTBH I don't thinkg that it's related to refactoring I've done:\n\n* these changes were merged Nov 26, 2025 (W5) while degradation was noticed 1-2 weeks before\n* another endpoint /internal/getActiveCampaignBannersForUser that doest literally the same and shows no signs of degradation\n* moreover, processing duration of these endpoints actually noticeable went down\n\nSeems like root cause is more complicated, will continue to investigate.\n\n\n\nIMO bad performance of RCC's {{getCampaignDiscountsForHomeScreen}} is related to degraded performance of {{/internal/getCampaignsWithProgressForTarget}} as it's called under the hood.\nUnfortunately {{getCampaignsWithProgressForTarget}} was removed and replaced with another one, so I suggest to take a pause and wait for new API report to check if anything was changed.{quote}","2026-01-15T11:38:55.374Z"],["3812330","XP-3061","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","{quote}*= 0.5*{quote}\n\n:redalert: *ERROR :: targeting-admin :: [RC] responses* Triggered with value *0.56*  The ratio of *non-OK responses* endpoint returns to users has exceeded the threshold.","2026-01-15T11:39:11.725Z"],["3812331","XP-3061","XP",null,"Slack","[Andrey Kuzmin|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/61b0698cc75da800725c5dce] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0384T4FU1H/p1768465738800789|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0384T4FU1H/p1768465738800789|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T11:39:12.731Z"],["3812334","WEB-9703","WEB","orkhan.yusubov@bolt.eu","Orkhan Yusubov","To be implemented using this tool [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08BGG4696J/p1767816182386299|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08BGG4696J/p1767816182386299|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T11:39:44.964Z"],["3812335","PLUS-77","PLUS","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","Was redirected to martech [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05PUMKN4C8/p1768472987399429|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05PUMKN4C8/p1768472987399429|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T11:39:57.240Z"],["3812336","LSS-61534","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - thanks for this. Question: was the TECNO device historically associated with the account? If so, I do agree with your assessment - although it still doesn’t make sense how this ride was ordered. Perhaps we can ask CS to validate if those devices belong to the Rider before we close this reported incident out? ","2026-01-15T11:40:50.963Z"],["3812338","LSS-61629","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi all, copy-pasting the relevant information and timeline below:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nContext:\n{panel}\n\n* On *7.06.25,* the Driver ([+Katarzyna Szałowicz+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-root/partners/edit/9543033]) verification selfie check failed ([here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity-trust/verifications/56c2a998-a6e8-4276-9766-7767cbb30075?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]). The verification attempt was marked as SUSPICIOUS_MULTIPLE_DEVICES_DISTANT_LOCATIONS and SUSPICIOUS_MULTIPLE_DEVICES, which is also known as the ‘Superman is not real” flag. This flag is applied to accounts where the verification flow is started from a device in a set point A, and the selfie was uploaded from another device in point B. These locations are (too) distant from each other, in a way that the verification flow ends up being completed in less time than it would realistically take for the Driver to cover said distance. \n* On *4.12.25,* the Driver submitted a DSAR ([here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/698291890]) where they requested access to the personal data relative to the suspension decision. As per our processes, our specialised CS team for all privacy matters [reached out|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06BQ7T6L4F/p1765191467897689] to the responsible team to enquire about the suspension and whether it was correctly applied to the account on *8.12.25*. The team reverted with the following information: “The verification failed due to a Superman issue. It was completed with two devices at distant locations within 8 minutes. However, it seems the driver was moving on a motorway at the time of verification. So it looks like a mistake. I’ve scheduled a new selfie check for the driver and once she passes it, she should be unblocked.”\n* As a result, on *8 Dec 2025*, the suspension was lifted.\n* On *10.12.25*, CS informed the Driver that the account was wrongly suspended due to a system error, and invited them to go through the verification process again in order to re-gain access to the account ([here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/702351440]).\n* Finally, on *27.12.25*, the Driver messaged Bolt and is claiming compensation based on the wrongful suspension ([+here+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/712473840]). The full message is as follows:\n\n*Compensation claim from Driver - click to expand*\n\nSzanowni Państwo,\nniniejszym składam formalną reklamację oraz wnoszę o wypłatę odszkodowania w kwocie 17 000 zł w związku z bezpodstawnym zawieszeniem mojego konta w aplikacji Bolt.\nJak wynika z wiadomości otrzymanej od Zespołu Wsparcia Bolt, zawieszenie mojego konta nastąpiło na skutek błędu systemowego leżącego po stronie Bolt, co zostało przez Państwa jednoznacznie potwierdzone wraz z przeprosinami. Tym samym doszło do nieuzasadnionego pozbawienia mnie dostępu do usługi bez jakiejkolwiek winy z mojej strony.\nOkres bezpodstawnego zawieszenia konta wynosił około pięciu miesięcy. W tym czasie zostałam pozbawiona możliwości korzystania z aplikacji oraz osiągania dochodów, co spowodowało wymierne straty finansowe. Wysokość szkody, obejmującej utracone korzyści, została przeze mnie oszacowana na kwotę 17 000 zł.\nW związku z powyższym wzywam do zapłaty kwoty 17 000 zł w terminie 14 dni od dnia otrzymania niniejszego pisma, poprzez przelew na\n68 1160 2202 0000 0004 7037 5763 ]\nBrak zapłaty w powyższym terminie lub brak merytorycznej odpowiedzi będzie skutkować podjęciem dalszych kroków prawnych.\nNa potwierdzenie zasadności niniejszego roszczenia dysponuję dowodem w postaci wiadomości od Zespołu Wsparcia Bolt, w której przyznano wystąpienie błędu systemowego oraz bezpodstawność zawieszenia konta.\nZ poważaniem\nKatarzyna Szałowicz\n\n* Since then, the driver has followed up on their compensation claim on 03.01.26 and 11.01.26 in the same [BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/698291890] ticket.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nWhat support is needed from Regional Legal:\n{panel}\n\nThe Driver’s account was suspended in June 2025 following a failure in the identity verification flow. The restriction was triggered automatically by the system during the selfie verification process. At the time of the suspension, there was no contemporaneous human review.\n\nThe Driver challenged the suspension on multiple occasions via Customer Support. However, based on the information currently available, we have no evidence that the suspension was escalated for review or substantively re assessed by the responsible team at that time. Relevant links:\n\n* 9.06.25 - [+here+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/589105802]: Driver used Personal Data Form to ask more information about suspension and requested to stop by the Hub. CS simply replied that the suspension cannot be lifted.\n* 9.06.25 - [+here+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/586921813]: Driver follows-up, asks more information. CS redirected to previous ticket.\n\nThe first confirmed human review took place in December 2025 following the submission of a DSAR. This review confirmed that the restriction had been applied incorrectly due to a system error. The outcome was communicated to the Driver on 10 December 2025, together with an apology and instructions to complete the verification process again.\n\n➡️ In light of the above, the Driver’s compensation claim may have some legal standing. Given the fully system triggered nature of the suspension, the absence of contemporaneous human review despite repeated challenges by the Driver, and the length of time before the error was identified, our position may be difficult to defend in the event of scrutiny by a data protection authority or other regulator. There is therefore a material risk of regulatory escalation.\n\nCould you please support with guidance on the appropriate response strategy to the compensation claim (eg rejection, partial acceptance, goodwill payment, settlement) and any legal, litigation, or regulatory risk considerations that should be taken into account?\n\n----\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nWhy the claim for compensation is legitimate and why there is a risk of regulatory escalation:\n{panel}\n\n# *Risk of negative consequences from a privacy perspective*\n\nYes. From a GDPR perspective, this case presents a material risk, particularly in relation to Article 22.\n\nThe current suspension flow works as follows in EU:\n\n# the account is flagged by the system,\n# the account is automatically suspended without prior human review,\n# when the driver requests a review, Customer Support often rejects the request without escalating it to the responsible team for a substantive check.\n\nSteps 1 and 2 are not necessarily unlawful on their own. However, where a decision is based solely on automated processing and produces legal or similarly significant effects, the data subject must have the ability to obtain meaningful human intervention, express their point of view, and contest the decision.\n\nThe issue here is step 3. In practice, there is no evidence that Customer Support ensured a genuine human review took place before repeatedly confirming to the driver that the suspension could not be lifted. In this case, we have not identified any escalation from CS to the responsible team prior to Privacy getting involved.\n\nIf this were escalated to a regulator, Bolt would struggle to defend its position. The lack of documented human intervention is not a one-off error but appears to be a process-level gap. This significantly increases the risk of regulatory scrutiny, particularly if framed as a systemic failure to comply with Article 22 safeguards.\n\n# *Considerations when deciding whether to compensate or litigate*\n\nFrom a privacy and regulatory risk standpoint, settling is the safer option.\n\nAllowing this to escalate to court or a supervisory authority would likely expose:\n\n* the absence of effective human review,\n* inconsistencies between the theoretical safeguards and how the process operates in practice,\n* the fact that the driver remained suspended for months due to process failures rather than substantive grounds.\n\nThe likelihood of a negative outcome for Bolt is high, either in the form of regulatory criticism, formal enforcement, or reputational damage. An amicable settlement would significantly reduce the risk of this case becoming a test case for our suspension and review practices.\n\n# *Why the error was detected only after six months*\n\nThe error was identified essentially by chance.\n\nWhen a driver submits a DSAR relating to a suspension, Privacy follows a different process than Customer Support. As part of that process, we contact the team responsible for the suspension and explicitly ask them to re-check whether the block was correctly applied.\n\nIn this case, that DSAR-triggered review appears to have been the first real human assessment of the suspension. Once reviewed, the responsible team concluded that the suspension was incorrect and lifted it.\n\nIn other words, had the driver not submitted a DSAR at that point, the suspension could have continued indefinitely. Despite the driver requesting a review multiple times, CS appears to have declined those requests by default, without meaningful escalation. If challenged by a regulator, we would likely have to characterise this as human error and process failure rather than an isolated mistake. This is not a position Bolt would want to be in. Defending this case and the underlying suspension process in front of a regulator would be highly undesirable, particularly given the indications that the issue is systemic rather than exceptional. From a risk management perspective, the clear preference should be to avoid regulatory scrutiny altogether rather than attempt to justify the current process after the fact.","2026-01-15T11:41:19.174Z"],["3812339","LSS-61631","LSS","tomas.calado@bolt.eu","Tomás Figueira Calado","[^Adenda ao contrato Bolt Food - Unilever FIMA, Lda 2026pdf.pdf] _(117 kB)_\n\n[^CONTRATO BOLT 2021.pdf] _(319 kB)_","2026-01-15T11:41:26.238Z"],["3812341","MLC-3777","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*W3*: Activation & Incentives are proofread. The email builder tool was also updated, so we can start building the content blocks next week.\n\nFrequency Flow is still being proofread.","2026-01-15T11:41:37.631Z"],["3812344","LSS-61460","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:49ec724a-806f-42f1-86dc-bf9f93671a23] - noted. \n\nThat is quite a tight timeline indeed, particularly if any privacy issues are identified here. To save on my review time, can I just check - did anyone from the Privacy Team review / input into the agreement that was signed in December? \n\nIf not, then going forward please ensure that we are looped in at _that_ stage (rather than just before launch), as otherwise we are limiting our own ability to deal with any issues that we identify in the process 🙂 ","2026-01-15T11:42:00.972Z"],["3812346","LSS-61573","LSS","alexandre.lancastre@bolt.eu","Alexandre Lancastre","Hey team,\n\nYes, it should be Catarina. [~accountid:712020:22f1d9b5-1599-49ef-8ecd-0c67511d3425] , let’s schedule a handover meeting with her next week and explain her the specifc nuances of this client so that she is aware once it’s handovered.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex","2026-01-15T11:42:18.429Z"],["3812347","MLC-3769","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*W3:* Shared audit results with Helina - waiting for feedback.","2026-01-15T11:42:25.315Z"],["3812348","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Hi Beatrice, there is 3 other excel files for us to fill out; assumptions, Q&A and pricing. But since they are empty, I do not assume they are relevant in this conversation.","2026-01-15T11:42:42.915Z"],["3812349","RDXENG-4561","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested on CA.193.0* {{develop}} *build and OK* (/) ","2026-01-15T11:42:48.810Z"],["3812350","MLC-3621","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*W3*: Agreed with the Product team that we should postpone the other groups to Spring 26 since all cities are closed now in LV.","2026-01-15T11:43:33.361Z"],["3812354","LSS-61619","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Hi @Catarina Faria, the driver has been blocked since yesterday.\n\nThe [trip |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2343543005/324?orderTryId=3014362737]ID is *2343543005*. I will attach GPS trace, timestamps, pick-up and drop-off points, and the driver’s and rider’s prior safety history.\n\nRegarding reaching out to the [{color:#0747a6}driver {color}|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723113151]and [{color:#4c9aff}rider {color}|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723586392]for further clarification, I believe we already have most of the relevant information in the Beehive ticket from both sides. Do you have access to Beehive? If not i will paste here the conversations\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.43.40.png|width=843,height=667,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.43.40.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.43.27.png|width=1232,height=615,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.43.27.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.43.48.png|width=818,height=409,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.43.48.png\"!\n\nThank you\n\n","2026-01-15T11:44:35.291Z"],["3812356","UXA-2148","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","I’ve created a doc: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7385251958/2026-01+Rider+app+-+Food+cross+pollination|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7385251958/2026-01+Rider+app+-+Food+cross+pollination|smart-link] \n\nMeeting notes: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08LRJUAU5P/p1768304366539839|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08LRJUAU5P/p1768304366539839|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T11:44:46.786Z"],["3812357","WD-22071","WD","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","Hello, sorry for the long wait for an answer! \nno worries, i built my own tracker with a workday monthly download 🙂 \nwe can mark this ticket closed","2026-01-15T11:45:00.771Z"],["3812360","LSS-61619","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] !\nI don’t have access to Beehive, so it would be amazing if you could provide the prints.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T11:46:33.773Z"],["3812363","LSS-55593","LSS","lillian.martin@bolt.eu","Lillian Martin","New RPP for Sweden will be joining on Monday 19th. I’ll make sure she’s aware of the topic but I think it makes sense to have an initial meeting with her when you’re back first week of February to align and then she can look into things further from a local perspective. Would suggest I already pop in the meeting today, fine for your [~accountid:641aac4f9d6383e32a32c047] ?","2026-01-15T11:47:35.813Z"],["3812364","LSS-58216","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] I went through the comments for me and I have answered. About SolidGate feedback:\n\n\n* Clause 10.5 removal, I am ok with it. Its replaced by 10.7. They just want to do marketing with us. We have added guardrails. \n* Clause 10.7: As above, I just added that we need to respect each other brand guidelines. \n* Clause 11.7: Ok. \n* Clause 9.2: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] will help there. \n\nThe two additional requests for POCs are also resolved. We will use payment ops team email for notices and we have added data exporter contact accordingly. Final draft is [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zIHe6ii8zb1fKtirn2LNsL_CWDbyCo1w/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=116714997278541814965&rtpof=true&sd=true]. \n\nI thin k we can ask SolidGate to start the signing process. Just ask to send it to Ahto Kink, Director of Bolt Operations OU and cc [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu]. \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e]  ","2026-01-15T11:47:51.525Z"],["3812365","MTE-1230","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","[~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] Not really, we need to change only our inbox message service\n\nDo we really need {{test_name}}? It is not exposed by default, and implementation can take more time","2026-01-15T11:47:54.285Z"],["3812366","WFM-9996","WFM","ana.radmilo@bolt.eu","Ana Radmilo","The agents let me know that everything is okay now. Thank you!","2026-01-15T11:47:56.597Z"],["3812367","WD-22550","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] Thank you, it worked now and i was able to submit IC invoice to Bolt Ops in sandbox.\n\n[~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] layout is still an issue, please see attached. Now i also discovered that we are  missing bank details etc from the bottom..\n\n[^0000000012 2026-01-15.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T11:47:59.053Z"],["3812369","DSR-3721","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Requested extraction from engineers: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768477657963939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768477657963939|smart-link] \n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wwWBXnsMCNfDUSJbxshg1NbTqJs-Ds4d|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wwWBXnsMCNfDUSJbxshg1NbTqJs-Ds4d|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T11:48:19.394Z"],["3812372","MTE-1230","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","@sander.nommik could you please check if test name is necessary \n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-15T11:48:36.125Z"],["3812373","WEBSD-1475","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hello! 👋 \n\nFew comments here [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \n\n1.- We do not have *global files* for TnC but we have the section EU (Europe) where we have some specific files for some countries in Europe.\n\n 2.- We need the *confirmation from legal team* (I do not know who will be the person) to know *where this should be uploaded*. Maybe we can decide the markets or Sam can create some global page.\n\n3.- Please provide the *PDF’s and .docx (I think this is the one for the link)* with the content need it because currently I see only confluence.\n\nLet me know your comments please.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-15T11:49:04.278Z"],["3812374","PAW-14908","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160839\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 11:49:04 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T11:49:05.068Z"],["3812375","CLOUDSEC-654","CLOUDSEC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Appears like as of Jan 8 my part is done","2026-01-15T11:49:06.321Z"],["3812376","LSS-60399","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:9851d3e6-ea86-42ec-8adc-7b241151ad4a] any update?","2026-01-15T11:49:09.078Z"],["3812377","RS-1875","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:60f2a71843c956007065f2ad] ,\n\n[~accountid:5f1538051c682d00295dbb61] , prepared the data based on the example provided by MP. Please have a look and share your comments. Hope that will satisfy their expectations🙏  [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/12Hr5-GUHLT53-P4gl6qavK7oVdDSCNsWgFn9nxrwFvI/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-15T11:49:27.430Z"],["3812379","WFM-9996","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","done","2026-01-15T11:49:59.079Z"],["3812381","HS-28991","HS","mariano.dangelo@bolt.eu","Mariano D'Angelo","Could this be send to [mariano.dangelo2000@gmail.com|mailto:mariano.dangelo2000@gmail.com] ?","2026-01-15T11:50:00.833Z"],["3812382","PFI-833735","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T11:50:02.044Z"],["3812383","LSS-61631","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T11:50:27.948Z"],["3812385","LSS-61541","LSS","christos.hadjistylianou@bolt.eu","Christos Hadjistylianou","[^Issue with a cancellation fee - Customer Support - Beehive.html]\n\n[~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] check this please","2026-01-15T11:50:36.237Z"],["3812388","WEB-9578","WEB","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","{noformat}export enum FormEvents {\n  FormStarted = \"Form Started\",\n  StepCompleted = \"Form Step Completed\",\n  FormSubmissionCompleted = \"Form Submission Completed\",\n}{noformat}","2026-01-15T11:51:58.989Z"],["3812389","MTE-1230","MTE","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","[~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] [~accountid:712020:cd383b4c-dce2-4e04-98a6-4398af29ffc2] Asked the team and I’m waiting for a response now.","2026-01-15T11:52:06.147Z"],["3812390","WEBSD-1480","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi! 👋 \n\nDo you need access for Blog?\n\nRegards,","2026-01-15T11:52:18.118Z"],["3812391","BDB-1482","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] we got this feedback\nThe *visible size of the lightbox is 620 × 290 cm*, however the *print data must be prepared in the size of 650 × 320 cm*.\nThe reason is as follows:\n\n* Approximately *15 cm on each side is folded inside the lightbox construction*\n* This folded area *will not be visible* and is used only for fixing the fabric\n* If the graphic were prepared exactly at 620 × 290 cm and left with white margins, even a *small shift during installation could result in visible white strips*\n* Therefore, the graphic must be *printed with bleed / safety margin*, so that even with minor movement, the visible area remains fully covered by the design\n\nSummary:\n\n* *Final visible size:* 620 × 290 cm\n* *Print data size:* 650 × 320 cm\n* *The graphic must cover the entire print area, with no white borders*\n* *Important elements (texts, logos)* should be placed at least *10 cm inside from the visible edge*\n\nCan you help me adjust the backlight design? ","2026-01-15T11:52:22.606Z"],["3812392","RNTL-30220","RNTL","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","[~accountid:61b06988d5986c006a9a8fda] I have done some analysis: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Jyy2QRK_oM_n4Cbej00H-0bYeT-42x7_yYW722syT0A/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Jyy2QRK_oM_n4Cbej00H-0bYeT-42x7_yYW722syT0A/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link]  I think the picture is clear for me now, and no actions needed from you. However, if you want to look into this / discuss, happy to do it. ","2026-01-15T11:52:48.625Z"],["3812393","LSS-61573","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","ok! I will Schedule a handover meeting with her.","2026-01-15T11:53:01.877Z"],["3812395","CNT-457","CNT","kyrylo.matiupatenko@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Matiupatenko","Hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd]!\n\nI’ve assembled [all the edits in this doc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Na2WIc85PT22Y_QG0JVnJdwemaaWSKgzLvgiECH6UeI/edit?usp=sharing] 🙂 ","2026-01-15T11:53:24.078Z"],["3812396","LSS-61632","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","[^Bolt_Citibank_confirmation.pdf] _(225 kB)_\n\n!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T11:53:45.039Z"],["3812397","UXA-2219","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","Started thread on Food channel: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02SWJK1ADU/p1768478007248759|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02SWJK1ADU/p1768478007248759]","2026-01-15T11:53:50.786Z"],["3812398","PAW-14914","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-15T11:53:58.462Z"],["3812399","LSS-61619","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Rider \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.52.03.png|width=587,height=214,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.52.03.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.58.png|width=590,height=324,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.58.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.53.png|width=606,height=363,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.53.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.48.png|width=604,height=351,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.48.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.43.png|width=603,height=357,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.43.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.29.png|width=601,height=362,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.29.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.24.png|width=614,height=359,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.24.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.18.png|width=593,height=364,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.18.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.09.png|width=621,height=354,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.09.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.01.png|width=616,height=364,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.51.01.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.55.png|width=614,height=362,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.55.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.49.png|width=592,height=361,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.49.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.39.png|width=610,height=360,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.39.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.33.png|width=610,height=353,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.33.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.26.png|width=578,height=340,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.26.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.21.png|width=614,height=360,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.21.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.13.png|width=589,height=352,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.13.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.08.png|width=582,height=360,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.08.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.02.png|width=602,height=348,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.50.02.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.53.png|width=594,height=358,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.53.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.47.png|width=599,height=374,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.47.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.37.png|width=619,height=366,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.37.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.31.png|width=586,height=351,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.49.31.png\"!\n\nIt starts from the bottom ","2026-01-15T11:54:08.950Z"],["3812400","LSS-61408","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:932dcda3-b9db-4c1f-8de8-254211945ea6] , thanks for the ping! \nIn order for me to get the full context of this incident, could you please share the BH with the rider (if any) as well? I assume that this happened in the context of a lost item case (? ) - please confirm.\n\n\nUnfortunately there isn’t much that can be done from Bolt’s side - once I have an overview of the full context, I will share adapted templates for both the driver and the rider. ","2026-01-15T11:54:12.160Z"],["3812402","LSS-60696","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","Hey [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] \n\nThe client has accepted the modifications.\n\nFor the signature, they tell me they use DocuSign, and they're asking for an email address to send the contract to for Bolt to sign.\n\nWhat email address should I give them to send the contract to?","2026-01-15T11:54:45.100Z"],["3812403","DSR-3721","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey CSPC – the Courier has a Courier profile opened: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/couriers/823298?tab=COURIER&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/couriers/823298?tab=COURIER&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\n\n\nPlease proceed as usual with extraction.","2026-01-15T11:55:02.072Z"],["3812404","PFI-833007","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:be4ac75c-3276-40e8-be21-fc6be1b4bc6a] \n\nThanks for letting me know! \n\nJust to clarify what happened. \n\nThe user paid the fine of 900 NOK to the municipality. \n\n2 Dec 2025, 19:44:56 (UTC+01:00). User had a fine payment which failed due to insufficient funds on \nSince the payment failed it caused a negative balance for the customer. This means that the customer did not actually pay off the fine yet and received a negative balance. \n\n5 Dec 2025, 20:25:03 (UTC+01:00) the user had a ride hailing order and since they had a negative balance of 900 NOK it was added to their order price. The user paid off their debt created by the failed fine payment. \n\n14/01/2026, 17:31 we have issued a OPM refund to the customer for 900 NOK to cover the overcharge. \nHowever, the payment was done to cover the negative balance. Since the payment is refunded to the OPM the negative balance is no longer covered. \n\nI think the best option to solve the issue for the customer is to issue a BB refund for the fine payment. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3908356688|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3908356688]\n\nWould you be able to do it? If not then you can check with your team lead as they might have higher permissions to issue the BB refund? \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n\n\n\n","2026-01-15T11:55:29.507Z"],["3812405","PFI-833740","PFI","nutsa.shevardenidze@bolt.eu","Nutsa Shevardenidze","!1.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!2.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T11:56:14.439Z"],["3812406","PFI-833711","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-15T11:56:28.066Z"],["3812407","PFI-833741","PFI","gabija.kantaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Gabija Kantaitė","!IMG_7049.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T11:56:39.779Z"],["3812408","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","[^Bilag C. Antagelser taxaudbud.xlsx]\n\nHi Beatrice, I have received following answer from PWC right now (attached is the file for this action): Please kindly list all reservations, prerequisites, and assumptions in Appendix C. We look forward to receiving your offer no later than 19 January at 12:00, and we will review the contents thereafter.","2026-01-15T11:56:49.956Z"],["3812410","PFI-833742","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-15T11:57:18.028Z"],["3812411","WD-22574","WD","rada.tibar@bolt.eu","Rada Tibar","hey! could please put this: Tallinn - Veerenni 24 (HQ Hub, Local Office)","2026-01-15T11:57:24.250Z"],["3812412","WD-22506","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:62bd9335018dea0d40751f4b] !\n\nCreated reverse one \n\n!image-20260115-115722.png|width=1088,alt=\"image-20260115-115722.png\"!","2026-01-15T11:57:32.202Z"],["3812413","LSS-61619","LSS","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","Driver \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.56.03.png|width=571,height=287,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.56.03.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.51.png|width=577,height=276,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.51.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.47.png|width=580,height=166,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.47.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.36.png|width=592,height=291,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.36.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.42.png|width=578,height=207,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.42.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.29.png|width=598,height=236,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.29.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.12.png|width=576,height=263,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.55.12.png\"!\n\nIts strats from the bottom as well","2026-01-15T11:57:48.642Z"],["3812414","HS-28991","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Mariano! Your employment contract and the associated amendment have been sent to your personal email.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-15T11:58:35.379Z"],["3812415","LSS-57332","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:5d81df0e9581710c30328f3a], [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a], below is the first draft of the T&Cs for the ambulance service. \n\nFor my side it looks fine, but I will also request the advisor to expand on the role of intermediary agency in connecting the users with the ambulances.\n\nMeanwhile, please check the terms from your side along with the comments I tagged you in and let me know if you have any additional noted to be addressed in the T&Cs.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/196m5lLH9dlYP6_C9GwMBsEelSOgqiP-o/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/196m5lLH9dlYP6_C9GwMBsEelSOgqiP-o/edit|smart-link] \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:76b6df07-e71d-429f-a069-ee3c132ee915] ","2026-01-15T11:58:43.705Z"],["3812416","WD-22506","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","HI [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] please add new tax codes to Telema. Thank you!","2026-01-15T11:58:45.815Z"],["3812418","WD-22372","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:6390559a2acfad92d7b59f11] , i have updated the schedule based on your feedback. Please review.\n\n\n\n!image-20260115-115958.png|width=769,alt=\"image-20260115-115958.png\"!","2026-01-15T12:00:02.830Z"],["3812420","BP-13445","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Test cases:\n\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T230|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T230]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T231|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T231]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T232|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T232]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T233|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T233]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T234|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T234]","2026-01-15T12:00:44.979Z"],["3812421","LSS-61633","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","[^Commercial Questionnaire - SICPA.pdf] _(3.63 MB)_","2026-01-15T12:00:47.962Z"],["3812422","LSS-61633","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMehdi Hameer has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T12:01:09.646Z"],["3812424","PFI-833623","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:ebc35d95-9563-46b2-a110-5f27dd0318c8],\n\nThank you for letting us know.\nI would like to confirm that we have received your escalation and that we are on it.\nWe aim to get back to you as soon as possible!\n\nMarten","2026-01-15T12:01:38.450Z"],["3812429","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1]  - so I can proceed and share the contract with your comments with client? ","2026-01-15T12:02:07.018Z"],["3812430","PFI-833623","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Confirming the situation with Felix","2026-01-15T12:02:08.992Z"],["3812432","PFI-833732","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 20.99 AZN on 24/12/2025, 22:30:12UTC\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 24th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T12:02:21.383Z"],["3812433","LSS-61634","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","[^Bolt_Baker&McKenzie law firm_confirmatoin.pdf] _(169 kB)_\n\n!image.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^FY25 Bolt_Engagement Letter(final signed).pdf] _(6.88 MB)_\n\n[^FY25_Bolt(Taiwan)_lawyer's letter.pdf] _(186 kB)_","2026-01-15T12:02:25.377Z"],["3812435","PFI-833747","PFI","wojciech.nawracala@bolt-outsource.eu","Wojciech Nawracala","!image-20260115-120250.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T12:03:00.704Z"],["3812439","LSS-58436","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:3af8f992-95ee-44bb-8d3c-9998350e5e42]. Apologies for the delay in my response.\n\nI reviewed the documents and the amendments proposed by the client can be accepted. However, they need to be written/reflected in the Special Terms document, which the client did not do. So, I will prepare the document.\n\nI just need one clarification:\n\n* The client mentions that a credit limit was agreed, but does not mention the amount. Could you inform what is the amount?\n* Also, the client mentions that it was agreed that the deadline for invoice payment would be 45 days, instead of the standard 30 days. Could you confirm if this was agreed/authorized from the commercial side?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T12:04:14.090Z"],["3812440","PFI-833425","PFI","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","Hi team - the intent is to have the option to send individual ride invoices to certain business customers instead of the single monthly invoice. \n\n","2026-01-15T12:04:55.375Z"],["3812441","BD-1978","BD","ave.tarend@bolt.eu","Ave Tarend","There were new cases with orders 282145705 and 281927512. Ops asked them to be solved.","2026-01-15T12:05:08.566Z"],["3812443","DO-5800","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Granted all tables!","2026-01-15T12:06:36.247Z"],["3812444","PFI-833747","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:632d60b5748d1bfcb857fc3c],\n\nThe user is related to a hard-blocked [user|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/174100405/overview] which has been assigned by the Safety team.\nDue to this relation they are not able to make any further orders.\nIf you would like to receive any further information about the suspension, then I would recommend reaching out to the Safety team.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T12:06:45.687Z"],["3812446","DELIVERY-1425","DELIVERY","song.luo@bolt.eu","Song Luo","[~accountid:61cc1c8d326554006ca9925c] I’d like to proceed with the first approach in Q1 first \n\nbut I’ll consider second approach in Q2 depends on other tasks on my hand ","2026-01-15T12:07:35.796Z"],["3812447","ROPSC-486","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Done on the {{2026-01-15}}","2026-01-15T12:07:40.141Z"],["3812449","WD-22581","WD","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi [~accountid:712020:176612de-64ab-442f-84ee-ed63bbac2b50], can you please move it to People Tech 🙏  Thanks!","2026-01-15T12:08:46.824Z"],["3812450","HS-28882","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi Jessica.\n\nI reopened the ticket as it still needs to be completed and sent for signatures.\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\nKadri","2026-01-15T12:08:47.415Z"],["3812452","LSS-61238","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:44e59489-5db2-4488-8537-588bccee709b], could you please clarify the list of personal data that will be processed BV?\n\nIf it is strictly limited to contact information for commercial and invoicing purposes, then I don’t see the need for a proper DPA. However, if they will have access to customer data, we would like to sign our DPA template.","2026-01-15T12:08:58.507Z"],["3812453","PFI-829532","PFI","andrezza.demarchi@bolt.eu","Andrezza Perfetto Demarchi","It seems like an issue with FONOA - I will reach out to the fleet in the meantime.","2026-01-15T12:09:07.817Z"],["3812456","DO-5798","DO","nathan.valencia@bolt.eu","Nathan Ruiz Valencia","I see my mistake thanks a lot for your support it’s working !","2026-01-15T12:10:40.035Z"],["3812457","PFI-833741","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThis is a reuse booking case. \nWe have used the customers payment for a different order. \nOrignial cancelled order: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2344188355/9?orderTryId=3015533352|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2344188355/9?orderTryId=3015533352]\n\nPayment was used to pay for this order instead. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2344208042/9?orderTryId=3015566499|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2344208042/9?orderTryId=3015566499]\n\nReused booking \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory/user/156918251/booking/3796819527|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory/user/156918251/booking/3796819527]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T12:11:01.843Z"],["3812458","SREP-1098","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","During the scan, increased DNS requests to some external records happen from web apps, as a result of ndot5, such requests are relatively slower than usual, and as a result, p99 is higher at this time. We can identify what records are requested during increased load by enabling logging for nodelocaldns and then collaborating with the web team to mitigate potential misconfiguration or align optimization, or at least ask them to use the full FQDN with a dot at the end. records to avoid ndots search in locals.","2026-01-15T12:11:09.684Z"],["3812459","DSR-3621","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768479064735469|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1768479064735469|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T12:11:20.282Z"],["3812460","LSS-61105","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","[~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] Hi, \n\nThe driver’s address is:\n12 Lawrie Avenue\nRamsbottom\nBury\nBL0 9NW\n\nEmail address:\n[seamaster@me.com|mailto:seamaster@me.com]","2026-01-15T12:11:54.534Z"],["3812461","MTE-1230","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","[~accountid:712020:0b749a8a-fe6a-4f53-837a-a79e10d19db5] update, there is testName, I can use it ","2026-01-15T12:12:01.261Z"],["3812463","SRED-1072","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","So far +2Tb, +$2,285/month\n\nWill see how much more will be required over a week.","2026-01-15T12:12:12.612Z"],["3812464","WD-21923","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","[~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a] 🙏 ","2026-01-15T12:12:37.183Z"],["3812468","FX-3557","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768479200868469]*{color}:\nQueries to get possible duplicate active cars with same reg number in 1 company which are created within 2 hour timeframe (so might come from the same application being accepted):\n{code}WITH duplicated_reg_numbers AS (\n  SELECT\n    company_id,\n    reg_number,\n    COUNT(1) AS cnt\n  FROM ng_public_spark.fleet_car\n  WHERE status = \"active\"\n  GROUP BY company_id, reg_number\n  HAVING COUNT(1) &gt; 1\n),\n\ncandidates AS (\n  SELECT\n    car.id,\n    car.company_id,\n    car.reg_number,\n    car.status,\n    car.created AS ingested_at\n  FROM ng_public_spark.fleet_car car\n  INNER JOIN duplicated_reg_numbers d\n    ON d.company_id = car.company_id\n   AND d.reg_number  = car.reg_number\n  WHERE car.status = \"active\"\n),\n\nrides_per_car AS (\n  SELECT\n    driver_car_id,\n    COUNT(*) AS finished_rides_count\n  FROM core_models_spark.fact_rides_order_try\n  WHERE order_state = 'finished'\n  GROUP BY driver_car_id\n)\n\nSELECT DISTINCT \n  c1.id, \n  c1.company_id, \n  c1.reg_number, \n  c1.status, \n  c1.ingested_at,\n  COALESCE(r.finished_rides_count, 0) AS finished_rides_count\nFROM candidates c1\nINNER JOIN candidates c2\n  ON c1.company_id = c2.company_id\n AND c1.reg_number = c2.reg_number\n AND c1.id != c2.id\n AND ABS(UNIX_TIMESTAMP(c1.ingested_at) - UNIX_TIMESTAMP(c2.ingested_at)) &lt; 3600 * 2\nLEFT JOIN rides_per_car r\n  ON c1.id = r.driver_car_id\nORDER BY 2, 3, 1\n;{code}\nFetches 283k of possible duplicate cars and 168k of those cars have 0 rides :exploding_head:\n{quote}","2026-01-15T12:13:37.517Z"],["3812473","DAEN-1301","DAEN","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","Tagging [~accountid:641af323b05b4e3e7daa9a67] and [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ","2026-01-15T12:14:38.888Z"],["3812475","WFM-9997","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","Beehive Rides OPS Agent role granted\r\n08 RH_France_OPS queue added","2026-01-15T12:14:45.243Z"],["3812476","SREDESK-7419","SREDESK","sander.arnus@bolt.eu","Sander Arnus","Hey [~accountid:712020:ae0f284e-839d-45dd-9814-2a13629b7be1] ,\n\nThis is not related to ITGC. It will be used for delivering some security alerts and we would like to use Rootly to make sure the alerts are not missed and are all resolved by our team (internal security).\n\nAlternative is to send the alerts from Elastic directly to Slack, without Rootly, but then the alert resolution is not tracked.\nSecond reason for this integration is for us to learn how the alerts are handled in Rootly. We have set up ITGC alerts for other teams, but are currently not handling any alerts in Rootly ourselves.\n\nI guess it should be similar to the existing PCI service: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/blob/main/rootly/security/service.tf|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/blob/main/rootly/security/service.tf|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T12:14:46.532Z"],["3812477","LSS-61631","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:62c6861d9763a5e6027057ca] ,\n\nCould you kindly provide Gdoc version of both documents, please?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T12:15:49.860Z"],["3812480","LSS-61546","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343232|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343232|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T12:15:56.153Z"],["3812481","LSS-57372","LSS","dominik.lopuch@bolt.eu","Dominik Lopuch","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] could you please send a remider to the client? I just sat with him and he assuer me he will sign it today. Thanks.","2026-01-15T12:15:58.298Z"],["3812485","PFI-833717","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* if you see _to_execute →_ it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-15T12:18:24.038Z"],["3812487","PFI-833722","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* if you see _to_execute →_ it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-15T12:18:29.568Z"],["3812488","HS-28749","HS","patryk.wojtowicz@bolt.eu","Patryk Wojtowicz","[^Świadectwo Ukończenia Technikum.pdf]\n[^Świadectwo Pracy ProPoint od 2019-03-04 do 2019-10-05.pdf]\n[^Świadectwo Pracy Multikino od 2017-04-01 do 2018-09-20.pdf]\n[^Świadectwo Pracy Goodrich od 2018-12-10 do 2019-02-22.pdf]\n\nI'm uploading 4 files:\n\n* Certificate of completion of a 4-year technical school\n\n* 3 employment certificates, totaling over 2 years of service.\n\nAdding to this over 4 years at our company, I have a total of over 10 years of service.","2026-01-15T12:18:33.453Z"],["3812489","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] , thank you for testing, I think this is becuase the layout for BG002 was not configured in sandbox. I updated it, can you please test it now?","2026-01-15T12:18:46.298Z"],["3812490","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","The changes are deployed on live.","2026-01-15T12:18:56.213Z"],["3812492","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","marek.pagel@bolt.eu","Marek Pagel","thank you! this went way faster than I expected :bowing:","2026-01-15T12:19:41.512Z"],["3812494","LSS-60607","LSS","kaarel.kook@bolt.eu","Kaarel Kook","Heyyy!\n\nCould I get some feedback on this please? 🙏\n\n","2026-01-15T12:20:15.137Z"],["3812495","DRX-28147","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the ticket on DA.127.0 (Release build) on Android 16, after a fix is made\n\nVerified the UI on side bar and Profile screen, no visual issues are present\n\nAttaching the screenshot for reference\n\n*Light Theme mode:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-141055.png|width=812,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-141055.png\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-141058.png|width=812,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-141058.png\"!\n\n\n\n*Dark Theme mode:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-141111.png|width=812,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-141111.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot_20260115-141115.png|width=812,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115-141115.png\"!\n\nFixed","2026-01-15T12:20:30.223Z"],["3812497","DRX-28149","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28147 has been resolved","2026-01-15T12:20:37.207Z"],["3812498","DRX-28083","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28147 has been resolved","2026-01-15T12:20:37.225Z"],["3812502","PFI-833708","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T12:21:27.623Z"],["3812503","PFI-833708","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","please raise with partner payment team.","2026-01-15T12:21:38.376Z"],["3812504","PRODSEC-696","PRODSEC","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","Permissions received for me and Amy","2026-01-15T12:21:40.844Z"],["3812505","PFI-833708","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T12:21:42.244Z"],["3812507","LSS-60915","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] ! Please check both Spotdraft and wet ink versions\n\n[^Prijevod.docx (2).pdf] \n\n[^Prijevod.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T12:22:26.842Z"],["3812510","HS-28867","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","[^Yousef Moungad MT-E009189 FS4 2026 SIGNED.pdf]\n\nDear [~accountid:712020:0b9924ff-04d9-493a-9bc0-d3ae48359ea8] , forwarding the signed document.","2026-01-15T12:23:07.256Z"],["3812512","BDB-1461","BDB","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","[~accountid:60ab71565dc18500701cae80] Thank you! 🙌 ","2026-01-15T12:23:43.210Z"],["3812513","PFI-833342","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have refunded the card payment.\nRefund issued for 478.68 EUR on Jan 15, 2026, 14:23:11 GMT+2\t\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4008150197|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4008150197]\n\nPlease find the proof of refund attached. \n\n\n[^Refund_Letter_RXMCD746RTVHKWZ3_GQV2MQM5LSMFZSH6.pdf]\n\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-15T12:24:16.038Z"],["3812514","LSS-60604","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:72d9f759-4292-4662-bbdb-0a2843291aff] hey, as the counterparty in this agreement is the International Bank of Azerbaijan, do I understand correctly that the purpose of the agreement then is for us to partner with the Bank and agree on the promotional discounts that Bolt will provide to the users? Do you have more details on this project that we need to take into account?\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:76b6df07-e71d-429f-a069-ee3c132ee915] ","2026-01-15T12:24:23.390Z"],["3812515","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","fahad.khan@bolt.eu","Fahad Ahmed Khan","amazing!\n\n[@ankit.goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] just to get an understanding of the effort required for next steps, do you know how easy it would be to:\n1. enable push notifications\n2. enable chat with driver\n3. disable stops editing","2026-01-15T12:24:49.114Z"],["3812516","LSS-61635","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nSalvador de Almeida Campos Furtado has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T12:25:03.761Z"],["3812519","LSS-61591","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343238|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343238|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T12:25:25.865Z"],["3812520","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","No idea! Need to investigate it further.","2026-01-15T12:25:29.688Z"],["3812524","LSS-61534","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey[~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \nYes, the TECNO device is historically associated with the account. It appears consistently in the login history going back to 2021 and was the device used to place the disputed ride. There’s no indication of a new device, credential change, or third-party access around that time.\n\nFrom my side this looks fairly straightforward based on the logs. The user also seems happy with the mitigation that was taken (devices logged out, account secured), so I’m not sure an additional clarification is strictly needed at this stage.\nBut I agree we can ask CS to do a quick validation with the rider about the TECNO device before closing, *if* you think that’s safer.","2026-01-15T12:25:56.454Z"],["3812525","PFI-832864","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nif you apply it as manual adjustment → it will be a compensation.\n\nCompensation in Ukraine is charged with 0% VAT.\n\nAlso it is netted.\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 14.25.12@2x-20260115-122514.png|width=1114,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 14.25.12@2x-20260115-122514.png\"!","2026-01-15T12:26:11.367Z"],["3812526","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","I see that its taking the older gapless invoice number format: \n\n!image-20260115-122401.png|width=447,alt=\"image-20260115-122401.png\"!\n\n\n\neven after the gapless doc number updated:\n\n\n\n\n!image-20260115-122543.png|width=816,alt=\"image-20260115-122543.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260115-122618.png|width=816,alt=\"image-20260115-122618.png\"!\n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15] \n\n\n\n\n\n[~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] , [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] , any idea why the gapless number is not reflecting on the invoice ? Does a the period need to be closed for it to show? ","2026-01-15T12:26:23.991Z"],["3812528","PFI-833710","PFI","ivaylo.georgiev@bolt.eu","Ivaylo Georgiev","An example of this are student dorms - there’s hundreds of people in the same building, what are the chances of new ones creating their first profile and receiving the error?","2026-01-15T12:26:25.557Z"],["3812530","RS-1944","RS","mariia.nedosekova@bolt.eu","Mariia Nedosekova","Hi,[~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c]! Does anything need to be set up on your side?","2026-01-15T12:26:33.805Z"],["3812531","LSS-61619","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:712020:cb7d1436-9800-43db-821c-db7028a6ff03] !\n\nEven though the Beehive thread you provided contains most of the narrative from both sides, I recommend we still take two targeted follow-ups / actions (and document them):\n\n*Identity / account integrity check (priority):* \n\nThe Rider claims the driver was not the same as the person shown in-app (police photo mismatch + physical description discrepancy). To be honest this worries me more that the “he went to prison” allegations, since what the court decision you attached says is _“imprisonment of six (6) months but orders that, in terms of Article 28A of Chapter 9 of the Laws of Malta, t_+_his sentence does not take effect unless, during the period of eighteen (18) months from today, the offender commits another offence punishable with imprisonment_+_.” ._ Plus what I wrote previously on the fact that none of this necessarily means that the criminal record is false (unless you tell me there are other reasons why we believe it is fake).\n\nHaving this said, I would run an internal verification to: \n\n* Confirm driver account identity (selfie/profile/ID on file, onboarding docs).\n* Check for any recent re-verification events / selfie checks.\n* Review device/account anomalies (device changes, unusual logins, etc.).\n* Confirm the vehicle/plate used on trip 2343543005 matches what is registered.\n\nIf identity mismatch/account sharing is confirmed, this is a standalone basis for termination.\n\n*Interim measure:* given this is flagged as the driver’s 2nd report in the same “physical assault/attempt” category, I support keeping the driver blocked pending outcome and proceeding with the termination review once the identity check is completed and trip telemetry is reviewed.\n\n\n\n*Re the Rider:*\n\nThe rider provided a police reference (NPS 7/POL/342/2026, Fgura Police Station) and alleges injury + laptop damage, while also threatening media exposure.\n\nWe should:\n\n* Avoid any discussion of alleged criminal history or onboarding checks (we cannot confirm/deny third-party personal data).\n* Confirm we are cooperating with the police upon valid request.\n* Make clear we are taking the report seriously and have blocked the driver pending investigation.\n* Not offer compensation simply because of media threats (we should not set that precedent). As long as we show prompt action + cooperation with authorities + appropriate measures on the driver, our position is defensible.\n\nI propose sending the following message to the rider:\n\n_“Hello Javier,_\n\n_Thank you for the information provided, including the police reference (NPS 7/POL/342/2026, Fgura Police Station). We are treating your report as a priority. The driver has been blocked while we investigate, and we will cooperate with the police investigation and provide relevant trip information to the authorities upon a valid request._\n\n_With regard to your request for compensation, please note that Bolt operates a platform that connects passengers with independent service providers. The transportation service is provided by the driver (or their fleet/operator, if applicable), who is an independent service provider and not an employee of Bolt. As such, any claim for compensation relating to alleged injury or property damage arising from a ride is, as a matter of principle, a claim to be pursued against the relevant service provider (and/or through the appropriate legal channels), rather than against Bolt._\n\n_We will continue our internal review and take appropriate action in line with our policies based on the outcome of our investigation and any official findings._\n\n_Please note we are not able to discuss another person’s personal data (including any alleged criminal history)._\n\n_Kind regards,”_\n\n\n\nLMK if you agree with this or if the team believes we should take a different approach.\n\nThank you!\n\ncc: [~accountid:60bd1baef650540069f28c36]  ","2026-01-15T12:26:35.177Z"],["3812532","PFI-832857","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Did local ops say that driver is correctly onboarded now?","2026-01-15T12:26:54.733Z"],["3812534","RDXENG-4677","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","It is expected. Discussion [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09SBKYAN1L/p1767357864356389]. BE will ignore the sent preferences if the category is not eligible","2026-01-15T12:27:26.059Z"],["3812537","LSS-61626","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5] , can you please fill in the document (as you have the original version) and then scan it again signed. \n\nPerson signing this document will be Ahto Kink, director. \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T12:28:19.097Z"],["3812539","PFI-830577","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","At the moment, we’re not able to amend or reissue the invoices. Please note that drivers are expected to report VAT based on their actual tax status when submitting their tax returns.\nIf the tax authority reviews these invoices and asks for clarification or correction from Bolt, please let us know and we’ll review the situation further. In this case, you can contact your country’s tax manager to raise the issue with us by defining the impact.","2026-01-15T12:29:27.657Z"],["3812540","PFI-832467","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","thank you.\n\nfor now it is best if driver uses only invoices for accounting.\n\nregarding why commission on invoice is lower → because of commission netting (described below)","2026-01-15T12:29:31.615Z"],["3812541","CNT-377","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] , I addressed all comments, feel free to take a look and then we can finalise everything and move forward with design","2026-01-15T12:29:39.815Z"],["3812542","LSS-61421","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:5e835f0f9b6a000c1a324a3f] Can you please fill in the agreement the marked yellow parts per Anna’s last comment? ","2026-01-15T12:29:42.667Z"],["3812543","RISK2-3231","RISK2","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Initially, we gathered 2024 Oct-Nov LER cases and recent cases to analyze","2026-01-15T12:29:43.510Z"],["3812549","LSS-61636","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","[^Lawyers_Younity SCRL 31.12.2025.pdf] _(85 kB)_\n\n[^Lawyers_Claeys and Engels SRL 31.12.2025.pdf] _(85 kB)_\n\n[^Supplier confirmation_BV Moby Green 31.12.2025.pdf] _(94 kB)_\n\n[^Lawyers_Eubelius 31.12.2025.pdf] _(86 kB)_\n\n[^Lawyers_Osborne Clarke CVBA_SCRL 31.12.2025.pdf] _(87 kB)_","2026-01-15T12:30:22.814Z"],["3812550","LSS-61631","LSS","tomas.calado@bolt.eu","Tomás Figueira Calado","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ,\n\nI only have it for the addendum [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iB2QLVDp6Qf7QoVLzTVsEozU2-PxTiVO69ag_nABl5I/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iB2QLVDp6Qf7QoVLzTVsEozU2-PxTiVO69ag_nABl5I/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nPlease let me know if you need additional detail from my side.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T12:30:24.378Z"],["3812551","MLC-3423","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Context of the project/initiative:* Multiple initiatives to support the expansion and growth of the Bolt Plus membership.\n* *Status / Milestone:*\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n* *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n** [+Confluence page+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7018905601/2025-11+Bolt+Plus+Plus-ready+modal+experiment]\n** *Status:* {color:#36B37E}*[ EXPERIMENT RUNNING ]*{color}\n** *Tentative ETA for results:* January 2026, but it also depends on the enrolments\n** *Monitoring the enrolments*: more time is needed to draw conclusions. Currently, the enrolments numbers are on the lower side due to exposing the modals mostly only to new enrolments as suggested by MarTech.\n* *Hopp Plus launch*\n** *Technical preparations:* Discussions with the Bolt Plus Engineering and MarTech teams to pass the necessary events and Custom Attributes with the correct brand value to the Hopp workspace in Braze.\n*** *Custom Attributes:* in the Hopp space (/) \n**** As Custom Attributes don’t include brand property, it came out that they were already passed there by default.\n*** *Events:* WIP :yellow_circle: \n** *Hopp Plus logo:* delivered (/) \n*** [Link|https://www.figma.com/design/5BTLqdnPbNJG8x14TLitbA/Logos?node-id=1834-16&p=f&t=wxCMBtOJ2NwqKZm6-0]\n*** [Jira ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BDB-1461]\n* *2026 planning*\n** Rider 26Q1 planning: call with Cristina and Spencer\n** Bolt Plus spring planning: sync with Anette and Spencer\n*** We’ll be joining the cross-pollination spring-planning every Monday for 15 minutes.\n** New Bolt Plus Jira Epic to be created on {{2026-01-16}}\n** Coordinator support for setting up LCM ad-hoc canvases: Quick effort calculations based on previous quarters.\n*** Estimation: 0.1 w/w needed\n*** Workflow: Everything else remains the same, Vertical Marketing owns and coordinates the ad-hocs.\n* *Rides Marketing Overview*\n** Assisting with the Bolt Plus updates for the LCM section\n** Assisting with the Bolt Plus updates for the general section\n* *Bi-weekly sync with Vertical Marketing*\n* *Comms audit*\n** Reviewing Bolt Plus auto comms to ensure everything’s good → in Q4, there were so many changes and launches, so I’d like to ensure nothing slipped through the cracks (and if it did, we’re now on top of it).\n* *Next steps:*\n** *26Q1 items:* Getting started with the first items for Q1 (prioritisation TBC).\n** *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n*** Monitoring the enrolments.\n** *Hopp Plus launch*\n*** Ensuring we have the necessary events in the Hopp workspace\n*** Getting started with the first template setups.","2026-01-15T12:30:59.288Z"],["3812552","LSS-61635","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T12:31:05.657Z"],["3812555","SRED-1070","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Status after (last 3 nodes removed as well):\n\n{noformat}'targeting' status from targeting1.redis.boltint.net:6379 (init node):\n\ncluster_state cluster_known_nodes cluster_size cluster_slots_assigned cluster_slots_ok cluster_slots_fail cluster_slots_pfail cluster_current_epoch maxmemory_human redis_version\n           ok                  18            6                  16384            16384                  0                   0                   142           1.27G         7.4.6\n\n                                                                    node_id          flags                                 master_id                                                                 slots connected master_connection\ntargeting1.redis.boltint.net:6378  2810a70f56abcb404fdd4aafb33500e3d26ec968          slave  aaa630484e3a37976ddb72edca27f68845f826b6                                                                    []      True               n/a\ntargeting1.redis.boltint.net:6379  602982441ad8192580617d1a8194da49b108c5f9         master                                         -                   [[455, 1819], [3641], [9102, 9556], [10926, 11835]]      True               n/a\ntargeting2.redis.boltint.net:6378  1a06be99c2cb3921c688b73229ac03fc7cf91271          slave  602982441ad8192580617d1a8194da49b108c5f9                                                                    []      True         connected\ntargeting2.redis.boltint.net:6379  6ff31ecc87111016549690eb84e0db533b1034e4  myself,mas