ntargeting7.redis.boltint.net:6378  f3a0ea7754544dcf6b01c5e6d623743d0cbfa5a4          slave  5a1620d2c7bb6f71174b22a081fb8656ee70502f                                                                    []      True         connected\ntargeting7.redis.boltint.net:6379  ad473035dc224563d50ca4651b7dac4f730f32ea         master                                         -                                                                    []      True               n/a\ntargeting8.redis.boltint.net:6378  b3a974c204bd4888d82961a53091a531ef157dba          slave  ad473035dc224563d50ca4651b7dac4f730f32ea                                                                    []      True               n/a\ntargeting8.redis.boltint.net:6379  ac674afc886cc22b1d1211bd162bf2322cfcbcbf         master                                         -                                                                    []      True               n/a\ntargeting9.redis.boltint.net:6378  a83b8870ae372ae2d394415dcb5b6d773df3b6f1          slave  ac674afc886cc22b1d1211bd162bf2322cfcbcbf                                                                    []      True               n/a\ntargeting9.redis.boltint.net:6379  aaa630484e3a37976ddb72edca27f68845f826b6         master                                         -                                                                    []      True               n/a{noformat}","2026-01-15T12:31:39.816Z"],["3812558","CNT-377","CNT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945] will do! Wil also get Product to review parallely, thank you! ","2026-01-15T12:32:06.796Z"],["3812559","LSS-61623","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5ece16662490cf0c09d78cae] ! only one contract is currently visible. Are there some more?","2026-01-15T12:32:18.678Z"],["3812560","LSS-61617","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5] , as this is a pdf version (non editable), can you please fill in all the required information and then send us the document for signing. \n\nBolt Operations UK Limited \n\nLeather Market, Unit J, Taper Studios, 175 Long Lane, London, SE1 4GT\n\nReg number: 12683400\n\nDirector: Alex Wong","2026-01-15T12:32:27.935Z"],["3812561","DRX-28139","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the ticket on DA.127.0 (Release Build) on Android 16, after an update is made\n\nFor testing, turned off the {{dev_is_auto_acceptance_filters_enabled}} from tweaks and checked the behaviour. App is now displaying the correct message to user in snack-bar\n\nAttaching the screen recording for reference:\n\n!screen-20260115-162747-1768487246577.mp4|width=794,alt=\"screen-20260115-162747-1768487246577.mp4\"!\n\nFixed","2026-01-15T12:32:29.236Z"],["3812562","PFI-830822","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Hello, are you referring to how to determine and mark VAT-liable fleets in the admin, or to how the VAT process will work?\nCould you please specify the case so I can assist accordingly","2026-01-15T12:32:44.621Z"],["3812563","SRED-1070","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, -$201/month","2026-01-15T12:33:00.768Z"],["3812564","RCE-352","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768480413744459]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@sandra.figari>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-352] `Investigate document upload failure for drivers` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T12:33:47.225Z"],["3812566","PFI-832945","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","At the moment, we’re not able to amend or reissue the invoices. Please note that drivers are expected to report VAT based on their actual tax status when submitting their tax returns.\nIf the tax authority reviews these invoices and asks for clarification or correction from Bolt, please let us know and we’ll review the situation further. In this case, you can contact your country’s tax manager to raise the issue with us by defining the impact.","2026-01-15T12:34:50.588Z"],["3812567","LSS-61630","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^UMOWA O WSPÓŁPRACY.pdf] ","2026-01-15T12:35:11.299Z"],["3812569","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email sent to Brabners, attaching requested DD documents and setting out Voi’s proposal. \n\n*Next steps:* await confirmation that landlord is happy with proposal ➡️ update Isaac (Voi legal) ➡️ review and negotiate sub-lease with Voi and new lease with landlord.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Bolt - Liverpool Scooter Operations Unit 9 Phoenix Park [IMAN-WSLIVE.FID4687096].pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T12:35:26.325Z"],["3812571","PAR-3860","PAR","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","[^BOLT_TH7018_CAMT54_202601121443]\n[^BOLT_TH7018_CAMT54_202601120043]\n\n","2026-01-15T12:35:54.621Z"],["3812572","RS-1944","RS","mariia.nedosekova@bolt.eu","Mariia Nedosekova","Waiting for Beehive engineers to add Morocco slack channel code to mapping for the integration.","2026-01-15T12:35:59.458Z"],["3812575","MKP-9825","MKP","daniil.popov@bolt.eu","Daniil Popov","*@user-U02FQDRB35H* correct me if I’m wrong, since you already did this. The process should be something like this:\n1. I give you new credentials for your services\n2. You add these credentials to bolt-vault alongside your old credentials with a new name \n3. You upgrade your Kafka client configuration to point to the new credentials\n4. You redeploy the service with new configs\nFor live environment I’ll help with both steps 1 and 2, since there are plenty of shards and they use different credentials. I can pre-create secrets directly in bolt-vault, so for live I’ll need your help only with steps 3 and 4.","2026-01-15T12:36:24.698Z"],["3812576","MKP-9825","MKP",null,"Slack","[Daniil Popov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f4905b29aa9650046196c33] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01U0PMTU69/p1768401793298619?thread_ts=1762871865.949249&cid=C01U0PMTU69|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01U0PMTU69/p1768401793298619?thread_ts=1762871865.949249&cid=C01U0PMTU69|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T12:36:26.031Z"],["3812577","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","I drafted a [Confluence page|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/bYBWuQE] to explain the goals, limitations, and summarize the kickstand design for EB1.","2026-01-15T12:36:36.991Z"],["3812578","WD-22550","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask","[~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] it is reflected only on printed invoice atrer invoice is in approved status 🙂  i think it’s good now \n\n[^Bolt Operations OÜ 0000000014 2026-01-15.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T12:37:08.037Z"],["3812579","RS-1944","RS","mariia.nedosekova@bolt.eu","Mariia Nedosekova","Hi [~accountid:5f1a9692b385da00156b98be]! \n\nMorocco and Marrakesh should be available in the tool now. I have added you to ma-ridersafety and ma-rides-crisis-escalations channels too, the workflows should be up and running.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions! ","2026-01-15T12:37:17.488Z"],["3812582","LSS-61105","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you very much [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a]! 🙏 ","2026-01-15T12:37:35.508Z"],["3812584","DO-5799","DO","aleksandr.leontev@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Leontev","[~accountid:61cc1c85ce3652006a6822c7] \n\n# this example is not a very good one for adding Spark:\n[https://github.com/bolteu/spark/pull/1910|https://github.com/bolteu/spark/pull/1910|smart-link] \nIn addition, it’s a strikethrough text, which means it should not be used. \n# Debugging section is not possible to use - there’s no template to debug Spark jobs.\n# {{databricks.yml}} does not have {{dbx_deployment_conf}} section.\n# Usage of the bucket in the code should be updated - seems like now we can just use {{AwsS3Factory.createLegacy}} with the {{bolt-scheduled-reports}} bucket name.\n\n","2026-01-15T12:38:15.036Z"],["3812585","WD-22550","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask","aah got it now, you meant why it’s not taking the new number 0000000024 😅 ","2026-01-15T12:38:20.424Z"],["3812587","PFI-833766","PFI","aderinsola.brown@bolt-outsource.eu","Aderinsola Brown","!Payment invoice 1.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T12:38:42.104Z"],["3812590","LSS-42337","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Thank you [~accountid:5e835f0f9b6a000c1a324a3f] - as discussed today, [~accountid:712020:4270191e-b006-439e-a800-5b8e06cf2c60] please confirm we still want to proceed with the court case against the fleet, or whether we would use the assignment agreement to transfer the liability to another partner.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:76b6df07-e71d-429f-a069-ee3c132ee915] ","2026-01-15T12:39:33.032Z"],["3812594","PFI-832983","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Hi, all invoices have been sent","2026-01-15T12:40:48.250Z"],["3812597","PFI-832945","PFI","artem.raievskyi@bolt.eu","Artem Raievskyi","Hey Nazrin, the issue is not on the fleet side but on the rider side. We cant add the invoice to their accounting as there is no VAT on it. \nThank you.\nPlease assist.","2026-01-15T12:41:18.898Z"],["3812599","PFI-830822","PFI","mariam.maghalashvili@bolt.eu","Mariam Maghalashvili","Hi, [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] thank you for your response.\n\nCould you please explain how the VAT process will work?\n\nI have attached profiles for two fleet owners, both of which are LTD companies.\n\nRegarding the commission, my understanding is that we should *not* deduct the full 23.6%. Since 3.6% of that amount represents VAT, we should not be deducting the VAT portion.\n\n[+Profile1+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/135285?tab=profile]\n\n[+Profile2+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-company/companies/edit/102801?tab=profile]\n\n","2026-01-15T12:41:44.208Z"],["3812601","LSS-61622","LSS","rustem.aidarkhanov@bolt.eu","Rustem Aidarkhanov","# They messed up before with re-signing multiple time due to errors in contracts if you remember, so they uploaded to the system the contract with the number written in the amendment. I requested to send me the contract that they uploaded to the system and will share with you soon. \n# They will provide billingual version too.\n# Because VAT increase is effective from 1st January 2026\n\n","2026-01-15T12:41:50.060Z"],["3812606","FDBT-4778","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_dimensions_modelling fails on 2026-01-14 21:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_dimensions_modelling/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-14T21%3A00%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=custom_report_loading.commerce_finance_workday_finance_reports_custom_fx_rates&base_date=2026-01-14T21%3A00%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-15T12:43:35.187Z"],["3812607","DO-5804","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Granted!","2026-01-15T12:43:35.349Z"],["3812608","LSS-61533","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] - thank you for clarifying this.\n\nI suggest using the following wording to obtain consent:\n\n{quote}_I,_ *_[full name]_*_, passport/ID number_ *_[ID]_*_, hereby give my voluntary and informed consent to_ *_[full name - Bolt entity processing background check]_* _to collect, process, store, and use my personal data for conducting a background check related to my employment, including verification of employment-related information for the last three (3) years._\n\n_I confirm that I have been informed of my rights under the Law of Ukraine “On Personal Data Protection” and that detailed information regarding the processing of my personal data is available in Bolt’s Candidate Privacy Notice:_ [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-recruitment/?category=other|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-recruitment/?category=other|smart-link]\n\n_Date:_  \n_Signature:_{quote}\n\nSince this is for Ukraine, I’ve prepared the following translation:\n\n{quote}_Я,_ *_[ПІБ повністю]_*_, паспорт / ідентифікаційний код_ *_[ID]_*_, надаю свою добровільну та поінформовану згоду_ *_[full name - Bolt entity processing background check]_* _на збір, обробку, зберігання та використання моїх персональних даних з метою проведення перевірки (background check) у зв’язку з моїм працевлаштуванням, у тому числі перевірки відомостей, пов’язаних із трудовою діяльністю, за останні три (3) роки._\n\n_Підтверджую, що мені повідомлено про мої права відповідно до Закону України «Про захист персональних даних», а також що детальна інформація щодо обробки моїх персональних даних викладена в Повідомленні про конфіденційність для кандидатів Bolt за посиланням:_ [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-recruitment/?category=other|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-recruitment/?category=other|smart-link]\n\n_Дата:_  \n_Підпис:_{quote}\n\nI recommend signing this digitally with the employee and retaining a copy of the consent in the employee file. Please ensure this document is not accidentally deleted; we need it for accountability and to demonstrate the record of consent, even after the employee's termination.\n\nThe Privacy Team will address the retention period for employee records, including consent forms, as a separate topic.\n\n----\n\nPlease let me know if you have further questions - I am preparing to close the ticket😌 ","2026-01-15T12:43:46.594Z"],["3812611","DSR-3585","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Response prepared: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G263o83_NOx4uLFsGJ89zXnfu17RH_tucgZ1rHXAXaw/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G263o83_NOx4uLFsGJ89zXnfu17RH_tucgZ1rHXAXaw/edit?tab=t.0] ","2026-01-15T12:44:21.675Z"],["3812612","VERIFY-4062","VERIFY",null,"Automation for Jira","*Aleksandr Zhigulich* has updated the *Epic Link* on VERIFY-3470 so the total Story Points on this Epic has been adjusted to *29.0*.\n","2026-01-15T12:44:26.187Z"],["3812616","LSS-61632","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Scan_Bolt TW.pdf] ","2026-01-15T12:44:40.819Z"],["3812617","MLC-186","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* Dropping email Open Rates\n* *Status update:*\n** *Updating the HTML builder tool*\n*** *Changes made:* Optimisation of the HTML code based on learnings from our testing.\n*** *Status:* Done (/) \n*** *Owner:* Web team\n*** *Update to the team:* [Slack post|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GDSPNFU22/p1768469585547729]\n** *Storytelling planning for 2026*\n*** Sync with Cristina on the approach, timelines, goals.\n**** [Meeting notes|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1k7lasNNZ7SnRHr9umR85VWbSK3DO9TDf99aTEuAXaAM/edit?tab=t.0]\n*** Working on effort estimation for Q1 and mapping out all of the communications for 2026.\n*** Working on testing Poe with some communications and mapping out the quality of the output.\n**** *Next step:* Sharing this with the Content team so they can understand how much effort needs to be planned on their side to support storytelling.\n** *Replicating the storytelling template in drag-and-drop*\n*** *Owner:* [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327]\n*** *Status:* Close to being ready; Roman is reviewing the final feedback regarding paddings.\n**** However, this isn’t the highest priority item anymore, considering we can proceed with testing the HTML builder again.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Finalising mapping the next communications for storytelling*\n** *Implementation handover to* [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327]*:* sync on what’s planned, how to proceed, workflow, etc.","2026-01-15T12:45:16.320Z"],["3812618","LSS-60727","LSS","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^PEL_ZUS PUE_Aleksandra Kusiak (579a17e4-9013-4c08-88be-acde335c0554).pdf]\n\nHi Team, please proceed with signing the attached PoA with Ahto’s wet-ink signature (only a scan is needed). Please note that the signature should be above the sign “Podpis osoby, która udziela pełnomocnictwa”. Thank you! ","2026-01-15T12:45:35.240Z"],["3812620","PAW-14916","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160860\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 12:46:05 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T12:46:05.842Z"],["3812621","LSS-61533","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Internal [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] - it would be interesting to understand if we have any data retention rules established for employee records, including the consent forms that they need to sign. I would assume this is a separate topic that should be addressed centrally. Recruitment PN is not very clear in that regard🙂 \n\nHappy to assist if you are planning any developments re/ this.","2026-01-15T12:46:29.700Z"],["3812622","GRWA-1491","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Updates:\n\n* [+Adhoc - Cuped Bootstrap Policy Tag Good/Bad Validation+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dkEj5FJ8jOkGOLFfvOjAKOOSvPafP6ILomtkYVe7uVU/edit?gid=1799249710#gid=1799249710]\n* [+Slack_post+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09V5AY4EAE/p1767947319294569?thread_ts=1767797411.183919&cid=C09V5AY4EAE]\n* Final Confluence page: [+Page: Policy Tag Logic – Good/Bad Pivot Alignment with Campaigns Setup Warnings+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CAM/pages/7404585423/Policy+Tag+Logic+Good+Bad+Pivot+Alignment+with+Campaigns+Setup+Warnings]","2026-01-15T12:46:39.616Z"],["3812625","LSS-61533","LSS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e],\n\nCan we modify the wording so she could wet sign it? \n\nWe don’t sign anything digitally in Ukraine (atleast regarding employment documents), so we would prefer if this document would also be wet signed and then scanned and saved in employee digital file (original in the paper document file) \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin ","2026-01-15T12:47:04.495Z"],["3812626","CSDT-960","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Agreed with JZ that bucket names should be: \n\n* 0-3 months -> New Hire\n* 3-6 months -> Ramp-up\n* 6-12 months -> Proficient\n* 12+ months -> Experienced","2026-01-15T12:47:21.331Z"],["3812629","LSS-61533","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Thank you for clarifying your standard practice for Ukraine. Feel free to use the same text, including keeping the link to the privacy notice [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] .","2026-01-15T12:47:57.729Z"],["3812630","PFI-830577","PFI","vit.sztogryn@bolt.eu","Vít Sztogrýn","Okay, thank you!","2026-01-15T12:48:16.170Z"],["3812633","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","marek.pagel@bolt.eu","Marek Pagel","enabling chat seems very useful. Would you prefer to start a new thread? I can also investigate myself, if you point me towards the right direction","2026-01-15T12:48:55.039Z"],["3812634","LSS-61638","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","[^0417 - REIGATE, Regus London Road - UK Pricing Plan - 20230518 (7).pdf.pdf] _(9.39 MB)_\n\n[^OSA_PRT13098128_150120261242.pdf] _(499 kB)_","2026-01-15T12:48:57.239Z"],["3812636","LSS-61638","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:62ff8d58b582d07a14a96588] can you please confirm if you are happy to proceed\n\nHey [~accountid:60528926695c3900706cc79e] can you please confirm if the floor plan is all good","2026-01-15T12:49:01.131Z"],["3812637","LSS-60941","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343250|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343250|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T12:49:38.288Z"],["3812640","PFI-833771","PFI","bostina.mielcioiu@bolt-outsource.eu","Bostina Mielcioiu","[^invoice.pdf]","2026-01-15T12:49:59.204Z"],["3812641","PFI-833771","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T12:50:01.203Z"],["3812643","PFI-833772","PFI","elena.popa@bolt.eu","Elena Popa","!Captură de ecran din 2026-01-13 la 14.46.57.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image002 (1).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T12:50:10.845Z"],["3812644","PFI-833449","PFI","adriana.baranowska@bolt-outsource.eu","Adriana Baranowska","# Payout from 06.01.2025\nOrders: [GZWQ7|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280521065?cityId=449], [O5WU9|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280526232?cityId=449], [WW1ZF|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280532860?cityId=449], [J104D|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280535860?cityId=449], [7JB3L|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280541855?cityId=449], [4IJHC|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280544830?cityId=449], [VWW88|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280552801?cityId=449], [HNS1X|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280559705?cityId=449], [20P3C|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280563474?cityId=449], [Q8KO5|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280570660?cityId=449], [4M4IA|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280578720?cityId=449], [HLLZT|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280584412?cityId=449], [46E34|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280588535?cityId=449], [K8UFX|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280599498?cityId=449], [7YRFW|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280606492?cityId=449], [0OSBV|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280615657?cityId=449], [JA1ID|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280623185?cityId=449], [31SKK|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/280625278?cityId=449]\nExpected amount and why: 277.83 PLN is shown as the sum in the app\nWhy it’s incorrect: courier received 252.15 PLN from his fleet, his fleet informed him that Bolt takes 25 zloty VAT for the order\n# Payout from 14.01.2025\nOrders: [BVAHO|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282031253?cityId=449], [34S6W|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282036588?cityId=449], [EZWSS|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282054154?cityId=449], [2KNXA|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282059576?cityId=449], [KPYEL|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282070524?cityId=449], [NXRMB|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282101758?cityId=449], [RP9N7|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282102345?cityId=449], [C4PRX|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282107902?cityId=449], [VY2I7|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282116331?cityId=449], [VM4YC|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282129252?cityId=449], [48GVF|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282131634?cityId=449]\nExpected amount and why: 203.46 PLN is shown as the sum in the app\nWhy it’s incorrect: courier received 191.73 PLN from his fleet\n\n","2026-01-15T12:50:17.150Z"],["3812646","LSS-61533","LSS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Did you mean use the same wording on paper including the link? \n\n","2026-01-15T12:50:39.440Z"],["3812647","MLC-2609","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:*\n** *Home_city_ID rollout:* The Identity team has finalised rolling out the new home city ID for Rider profiles (/) \n** *Check with MarTech:* How can we validate that everything is updated in Braze as well.\n*** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNH34A2BY/p1768377493149939]\n*** Suggestion to check with the Identity team → For MarTech, this is something that is hard to check, as the Custom Attribute name didn't change, which makes it hard to distinguish these changes in Kibana and Braze (because Identify calls containing city_id are very frequent). In addition, we don't store data from Braze so we can't do any before/after comparisons either.\n** *Check with the Identity team:* How can we validate that everything is updated in Braze as well\n*** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0669RP1EMS/p1768470092832159?thread_ts=1767706310.641039&cid=C0669RP1EMS]\n*** They did a small sanity check → all good (/) \n*** Not reasonable in terms of effort to build a process for a larger-scale validation check. On their side, everything went as expected. If we spot any odd use cases, we need to report to them.\n** *Working on* *actual’/current location tagging*\n*** [Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0669RP1EMS/p1765871835519259]\n*** Get back to the Identity team on the question they had. \n**** The quick answer is that we need real-time data from the backend.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Update with the whole department:* Share an update with the department that Rider profiles have been updated.","2026-01-15T12:50:43.138Z"],["3812650","RDXENG-4655","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","Yes, it's better to start a new thread.","2026-01-15T12:51:14.447Z"],["3812654","LSS-61533","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","[~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] correct","2026-01-15T12:52:28.511Z"],["3812658","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] , If I remember correctly, the gapless number can be updated only at the beginning of the year yearly and 2026 already started …. would it be the reason its not picking the new format? can you please advice here > [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22550?focusedCommentId=3812526|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22550?focusedCommentId=3812526|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T12:53:15.332Z"],["3812659","L10N-28082","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28081](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28081)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T12:53:49.965Z"],["3812660","L10N-28083","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28081](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28081)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T12:53:52.665Z"],["3812661","L10N-28086","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28081](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28081)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T12:53:52.958Z"],["3812662","L10N-28088","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28081](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28081)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T12:53:53.289Z"],["3812663","L10N-28087","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The 