ng Ops and revert with info, once we have it we will kick it off.","2026-01-15T12:54:23.867Z"],["3812678","DSR-3585","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] \nCSPC dont have access to the prepared response so please give us that :than: ","2026-01-15T12:54:33.802Z"],["3812679","WEBSD-1480","WEBSD","tekla.chikhradze@bolt.eu","Tekla Chikhradze","Hi, yes, I need to publish a blog. ","2026-01-15T12:54:36.850Z"],["3812680","CNT-432","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","Hey, [~accountid:62472b362e101c006a8f50e6] , once you’re back, let’s agree on the name of the campaign and the tagline. Here are some options for you:\n\n# *Bolt Plus Weekly Deals* \n\n_Editorial framing (copy ):_\n\n* “This week’s Bolt Plus deals”\n* “Better menu deals, every week”\n* “Bolt Plus members get more off the menu”\n\n# *Bolt Plus Weekly Picks* \n\nEasier sell to top merchants: They’re _featured_, not _discounted as in Deals_\n\nTagline can be something like “Better menu deals, every week” for both\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] ","2026-01-15T12:54:53.228Z"],["3812682","TAX2-554","TAX2","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","+Update 14 Jan 26+\n\nProject will be resumed in Feb, waiting on Billing ops availability. Next countries KE, GH, CZ as per discussions.","2026-01-15T12:56:08.062Z"],["3812683","WD-22582","WD","maile.nittim@bolt.eu","Maile Nittim","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.55.15.png|width=1004,height=866,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.55.15.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T12:56:19.792Z"],["3812684","WD-22582","WD","maile.nittim@bolt.eu","Maile Nittim","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.55.28.png|width=1530,height=864,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.55.28.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T12:56:24.690Z"],["3812685","PFI-792039","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment return processed !","2026-01-15T12:56:25.349Z"],["3812688","LSS-61636","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hello, please also sign this bank confirmation, page 1. Thank you, Karoli\n\n[^Banks_Papaya.31.12.2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T12:57:31.715Z"],["3812689","PFI-830438","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","!CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 14.45.48@2x-20260115-124553.png|width=958,height=151!\n\nthe commission for dec was about ~4000.\n\nsee that in december the number decreased from 7300 by ~4000.\n\nso they did not owe us 7300, now they do not owe us 3249.\n\nnext month if they do commission ~4000 → they will owe us about ~750 - and would need to pay a commission of 750.\n\n\n\n\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768481718073589|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768481718073589]","2026-01-15T12:57:32.439Z"],["3812690","RS-1941","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab] ,\n\nCapturing questions from Slack on here for visibility and providing the answers.\n\n# [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab]: Do we have any update here for 2026? Or should I leave the way it is for now?\n\n_100% renewable electricity by 2025 across Bolt-controlled offices, warehouses, charging docks, and Bolt Market premises. / We're working to transition all Bolt-controlled offices, warehouses and Bolt Market stores to renewable electricity by the end of 2025._\n\n[~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] : Let’s consistently use: ‘_Bolt uses_ _100% renewable electricity from 2025 across Bolt-controlled offices, warehouses, charging docks, and Bolt Market premises.’_ \n\n# I previously described it as “eco-friendly commutes”, would the description below work, or do you have any other suggestions?\n\n{quote}*_→ Micromobility:_* _On-demand scooters and e-bikes for short, more sustainable commutes._{quote}\n\n[~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] : Your proposed wording is good! 😎 \n\n# [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab]: And btw about the “Bolt Business or Bolt for Business”comment -> From now on it's going to be Bolt for Business (B4B).\n\n[~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] : Thank you, noted! ","2026-01-15T12:57:59.554Z"],["3812691","LSS-61442","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed agreement attached.\n\n[^Agreement on mandatory protective equipment_Bolt Operations OÜ_Nueva Era Prime Services_13.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T12:58:02.810Z"],["3812693","PFI-833722","PFI","patricie.cholevova@bolt-outsource.eu","Patricie Cholevova","Hello,\n\nthank you for the detailed help. I have taken a look and the status for December says done, therefore I assume the driver should have it there. I will ask the driver for a screenshot to see, why he does not see it there or what he sees on his side. ","2026-01-15T12:58:27.209Z"],["3812694","LSS-61514","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi Aleksei,\n\nWhile we’re still waiting for your input on the questions below, here’s a preliminary assessment:\n\n\nI checked our agreements with Google and couldn’t find any Google Maps–specific agreement that specifically addresses logo handling. That means we have to rely on the [Google Maps Policy|https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/policies], which requires that attribution (including the Google logo) be clearly visible, legible, and unobstructed whenever Google Maps content is visible on screen:\n\n{quote}*“Don't remove included attribution regardless of where it is displayed. Don't alter, hide, or obscure the attribution and make sure it is clearly visible against the background.*”{quote}\n\nBased on this, I see we have the following available options:\n\n# *Option A -* Fully compliant\n#* Keep logo visible in all map-visible states\n# *Option B* - Fully compliant\n#* Fully hide the map in the vehicle selection state\n#* If the map is completely hidden or replaced, attribution is no longer required.\n# *Option C* - gray area\n#* Partial visibility (e.g. a small visible map area) or visual treatments such as blurring may still be technically considered hiding, altering, or obscuring attribution and therefore remain non-compliant. \n#** Penalty: Enforcement of Maps Platform Terms violation is discretionary but AUP violations are typically handled via remediation and later by suspension if the violation is not corrected within 24h. In spite of this, Google also reserves the right to immediate suspension when certain conditions are present. Based on this, it is difficult to say with a 100% certainty what consequences we’d be facing should we decide to keep up with or increase non-compliance. ([https://cloud.google.com/terms/maps-platform/eea|https://cloud.google.com/terms/maps-platform/eea|smart-link] Section 5)\n#** In theory, the requirement could be avoided if the map is altered to the point it is no longer recognisable as Google Maps content, but this requires more research, and would be a grey area carrying compliance risk and would need an explicit sign-off.\n# *Option D* - Seek written approval/exception from Google. But this implies a longer timeline and uncertain outcome. \n\nBased on my discussions with other lawyers in the department, our assessment can be summarised as follows:\n\nNot displaying the Google Maps logo when only a small portion of the map is visible is likely low likelihood from an enforcement perspective, but potentially high impact if challenged. On balance, we should aim to display the Google Maps logo whenever the map is being meaningfully used to convey information to users, as this is likely aligned with Google’s expectations.\n\nWe do not have clear visibility on how aggressively Google enforces this in practice. In a best-case scenario, Google would simply request a fix; in a worst-case scenario, the issue could escalate further. If this can be addressed with relatively modest effort, it would be preferable to resolve it proactively rather than wait for a potential issue to be raised. Separately, we should ensure we are alert and prepared to respond quickly in the event Google does raise any questions or concerns.\n\nPlease let me know your thoughts. Thank you! ","2026-01-15T12:58:39.525Z"],["3812696","PFI-833425","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo [~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c] [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] \n\nCould you please provide the invoice issuer template for intermediary model, thank you","2026-01-15T12:59:08.140Z"],["3812698","LSS-61533","LSS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi again[~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] , \n\nCan you recommend a subject line for this in English and Ukrainian? \n\nBest,\n\nKerilin\n\n","2026-01-15T12:59:35.818Z"],["3812699","LSS-57372","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi [~accountid:63d0eccfa197e05f9dadc837] - Reminder has been sent","2026-01-15T12:59:36.139Z"],["3812700","LSS-50124","LSS","rinaldi.yudakusumah@bolt.eu","Rinaldi Yudakusumah","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] \nWe won’t move forward with this partnership.\nPlease close the ticket.","2026-01-15T12:59:36.420Z"],["3812702","PFI-796956","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment return processed","2026-01-15T12:59:59.645Z"],["3812705","MLC-3830","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W3 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] assisted with creating stories and Crowdin strings (🌟 as usual)\n** Added story setup and logic for CA to the vertical banner, plus created a template for in-app stories that can be duplicated [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/modal/modalPollCampaigns/edit/3871557] (frequency caps also need to be added during the actual setup, I’ve left them out atm as it seems up to local teams to decide how long the stories will run for).\n** Set up email templates and canvas template in Braze for Bolt + Hopp and shared with local teams in the channel. Also let local managers with approval rights know that they can approve the comms themselves, since chances are very low for them to break something 😄\n* *Next steps:*\n** Processing tickets for the campaign ([~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff], pls assist here once they start coming in)","2026-01-15T13:00:49.559Z"],["3812706","MTE-1230","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","Unfortunately not, I was wrong, question is still valid, do we need test_name?","2026-01-15T13:01:02.155Z"],["3812707","WD-22573","WD","maile.nittim@bolt.eu","Maile Nittim","This Bolt Ops - PT is a random example I just made.\n\nEORI number is needed for export invoices.\nWith this current request I’m just checking if adding EORI to this field is even possible.\n\n\n\nWe have EORI numbers for Bolt Ops, PT, IT, UK. Would like to have EORI numbers added to all these entities.\n\n","2026-01-15T13:01:11.162Z"],["3812708","LSS-61638","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T13:01:24.901Z"],["3812709","PFI-831038","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","CSPC does not need to edit invoices - they need to give you existing invoices (if that is what you need) \n\nthey can give you existing invoices.","2026-01-15T13:01:28.272Z"],["3812711","PFI-832337","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi [~accountid:712020:4c535860-58d9-423b-bb8f-a379254d4af3]  \n\nTo be more compliant with tax rules, we do not reissue the rider invoices.\n\nPlease ask the user to make sure that their Personal Profile and/or Work profile have correct information. And make sure they pick the right Billing profile before the ride. \n\nIt is as essential as picking the right payment method before the ride.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,\n\nNikolay Roll  ","2026-01-15T13:01:55.044Z"],["3812713","LSS-61626","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf], can you let me know which section needs to be filled out? Thought it was just the account details that needed filling","2026-01-15T13:02:29.256Z"],["3812715","WEBSD-1480","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi 👋 \n\nIt says you already have access to CMS.\n\n[https://cms.bolt.eu/admin|https://cms.bolt.eu/admin]\n\nIs it related to your credentials or could you please try to logged in?\n\nRegards,","2026-01-15T13:02:49.747Z"],["3812716","HS-28913","HS","mykhailo.brynchak@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Brynchak","Hi [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0],\nThanks a lot for your help. It works now and I’ve completed the document signing.\n\nHave a nice day,\nMykhailo","2026-01-15T13:03:18.646Z"],["3812717","MLC-3416","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W3 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Joined marketing sync with the local team today. Nothing super relevant for LCM (discussion was focused mainly on ads), but shared additional notes on how the team can get Braze access/send out ad-hocs; also shared city launch comms template with them to start preparing.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Finish setting up comms and share previews with the local team to review.","2026-01-15T13:03:27.451Z"],["3812719","LSS-61622","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:523b0039-eb47-4ccc-aca3-88d82c0c880a] thanks - in such case please ask them to provide the editable bilingual version with the correct reference to the lease agreement number.\n\nRe the lease period - my point is that even if the tax changes from 1 Jan, the lease period remains unchanged as it is defined under the main agreement. In order to specify that the tax is calculated differently due to the change in the law, we need to address it in the amendment in this specific manner instead of changing the lease term - I will revise it once we get the editable version.","2026-01-15T13:04:19.589Z"],["3812721","C2-461","C2","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] One suggestion would be to not limit this process to only repair shipments, but all received shipments regardless of the origins (scope extended to include battery relocations).","2026-01-15T13:04:31.586Z"],["3812722","LSS-58614","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Closed and now tracked in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LEG-1358|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LEG-1358|smart-link] .","2026-01-15T13:04:38.720Z"],["3812723","CSDT-962","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15347|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15347|smart-link] & [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15373|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15373|smart-link] & [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15448|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15448|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:04:51.816Z"],["3812724","SREDESK-7422","SREDESK","jake.murphy@bolt.eu","Jake Murphy","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.59.30.png|width=325,height=424,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 12.59.30.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T13:05:11.616Z"],["3812726","LSS-61636","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hello, apologies, also this one. Thanks! Karoli\n\n[^Insurance confirmation_Cachet Insurance Broker OÜ 31.12.2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T13:05:15.408Z"],["3812727","LSS-61640","LSS","rinaldi.yudakusumah@bolt.eu","Rinaldi Yudakusumah","[^Transsion x Bolt partnership agreement 2025 - ESG.docx] _(1.45 MB)_","2026-01-15T13:05:26.127Z"],["3812728","LSS-61640","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nRinaldi Yudakusumah has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T13:05:27.993Z"],["3812729","LSS-61638","LSS","karolina.wolanska@bolt.eu","Karolina Wolańska","In [~accountid:62ff8d58b582d07a14a96588]'s absence- confirmed.","2026-01-15T13:05:35.021Z"],["3812731","PFI-833722","PFI","patricie.cholevova@bolt-outsource.eu","Patricie Cholevova","!Screenshot_20260115_140111_Chrome.jpg|width=2340,height=1080,alt=\"Screenshot_20260115_140111_Chrome.jpg\"!\n\nThe driver has provided this screenshot, he does not see it there. ","2026-01-15T13:05:50.677Z"],["3812733","DSR-3763","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-15T13:06:33.837Z"],["3812735","PFI-832350","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","If trip did not take place and amount for fare is 0 → invoice can’t be issued by the system (we do not issue invoices manually).\n\nThe status of the ride needs to be changed and the amount user actually paid needs to be reflected.\n\nif user did not pay anything for the ride - there is nothing to issue an invoice for.","2026-01-15T13:06:50.343Z"],["3812736","DRX-28138","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the ticket on DA.127.0 (Release Build) on Android 16, after a fix is made\n\nChecked that Swipe action is not resetting when the user drag the swipe arrow\n\nChecked in the following cases:\n\n* E2E order flow (Arrived, Waiting, Driving towards destination, End Trip, Confirm Price)\n* Multiple Destination (Next stop & Start Driving)\n\nAttaching the screen recording for reference:\n\n!screen-20260115-144716-1768481171446.mp4|width=812,alt=\"screen-20260115-144716-1768481171446.mp4\"!\n\n\n\n!screen-20260115-145122-1768481462783.mp4|width=812,alt=\"screen-20260115-145122-1768481462783.mp4\"!\n\n!screen-20260115-145541-1768481723811.mp4|width=812,alt=\"screen-20260115-145541-1768481723811.mp4\"!\n\n\n\nFixed","2026-01-15T13:07:22.485Z"],["3812737","SRED-833","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","All tasks in epic done.","2026-01-15T13:07:26.205Z"],["3812738","PFI-832794","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Tip is a voluntary addition to the service - it’s not a part of the service, which is why it’s not documented as part of the invoice. And we are not able to modify the invoice amounts. ","2026-01-15T13:07:50.914Z"],["3812740","PFI-832443","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","I see that driver is not liable to VAT.\n\nplease raise with local ops to update the driver’s profile.","2026-01-15T13:08:12.100Z"],["3812741","CSDA-293","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-15T13:08:18.335Z"],["3812742","GRWA-1481","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Currently we only incorporate SR countrywide campaigns in {{core_models_spark.fact_scheduled_rides_campaign_test_treatment}} table (campaign setup details).\n\nFor AB Scorecard tables (test_performance), it requires a quite big change in the scripts. We will create another ticket for that.","2026-01-15T13:08:30.194Z"],["3812743","SAI-1408","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Hello team,\nAn agent just [*reported*|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768480755671219] that, although the refund appears as _expired_ in the Beehive [*ticket*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723919830], it seems to have been [*correctly issued*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory/user/116836581/booking/3797697552] to the user’s Bolt Balance. I understand this is not a major issue, but could this indicate some kind of bug in the system?\nThanks for taking a look. :meow_bow:","2026-01-15T13:08:46.658Z"],["3812744","SAI-1408","SAI",null,"Slack","[Grzegorz Brotoń|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768481258111809?thread_ts=1768481258.111809&cid=C064FCFAT0S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768481258111809?thread_ts=1768481258.111809&cid=C064FCFAT0S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T13:08:47.520Z"],["3812745","SAI-1408","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Thanks for the report! We will take a look into it, seems like an edge case, but still should not work that way.","2026-01-15T13:08:47.981Z"],["3812746","LSS-57344","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026: \n\n* *Airwallex topics*: Product legal has aligned with commerce legal regarding the updates to internal CS guidances. To share final input for CS (Lisanna Lomp) we need to get confirmations on some questions from Airwallex. [Commerce legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57383] has been updated accordingly and relevant stakeholders contacted. \n* *Escalation from CS to merchant team:* sync with Kshitij from merchant tops has been agreed on for 19.01.2026 so he could explain what are the plans with Cognizant and whether merchant team want to outsource some CS support for merchant accounts from them. Important so that CS would know where and to whom escalate P2B or DSA complaints related to merchant accounts and writ it in to their processes. \n* After above has been cleared out we can:\n** finalise new CS processes for DSA complaints (P2B related will be updated next)\n** upload [new complaint rules|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KyffcN_OQYJ_RbEJfAFPSGh2AHvOIS1YGqzjx_md_Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xeajywah5w4] on Bolt webpage","2026-01-15T13:08:55.080Z"],["3812749","WAVE-232","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","*Severity:* :ladybug: Bugs\n\n*Category:* Admin Panel Modules\n\n*From:* *@user-U027N9G59KP*\n\n*Summary:* hot reload does not work\n\n*Details:* whenever I did changes to {{modules/unsafe-driving/src/components/UnsafeDrivingReportsTable.tsx}} the running app did not catch them,  i had to restart the app manually:\n\n{{pnpm start -m fleet }}","2026-01-15T13:09:19.577Z"],["3812750","WAVE-232","WAVE",null,"Slack","[Artur Luik|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1768471046264479?thread_ts=1768471046.264479&cid=C049U1GKWQN|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1768471046264479?thread_ts=1768471046.264479&cid=C049U1GKWQN|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T13:09:20.409Z"],["3812751","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","Hmm, cannot reproduce\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8QC8JNH1/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_13.02.23.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8QC8JNH1/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_13.02.23.png|smart-link]","2026-01-15T13:09:21.241Z"],["3812752","WAVE-232","WAVE","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","here is the recording. current develop branch\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8UPD751U/no-hot-reload.mov|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8UPD751U/no-hot-reload.mov|smart-link]","2026-01-15T13:09:22.186Z"],["3812753","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","Aha, I gave up after I saw “started incremental compilation” upon save and figured it works fine. Let me dig in!","2026-01-15T13:09:22.748Z"],["3812754","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo",":aha:","2026-01-15T13:09:23.337Z"],["3812755","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","It’s not much of a module, this unsafe-driving, is it? It just exposes a component :slightly_smiling_face:","2026-01-15T13:09:23.911Z"],["3812756","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A90RL8UVA/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_14.30.07.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A90RL8UVA/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_14.30.07.png|smart-link]","2026-01-15T13:09:24.497Z"],["3812757","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","So yep, this works:\n\n{{pnpm start -m fleet,unsafe-driving}}\n\nSmall cave-at, it’s not inplace replacement, still need to refresh","2026-01-15T13:09:25.133Z"],["3812758","WAVE-232","WAVE","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","ok, thanks","2026-01-15T13:09:25.754Z"],["3812759","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","[https://github.com/bolteu/lattice/blob/main/packages/lattice/scripts/commands/start.js#L92|https://github.com/bolteu/lattice/blob/main/packages/lattice/scripts/commands/start.js#L92]\n\n:point_up: *group-S090TQ845QS*","2026-01-15T13:09:26.465Z"],["3812760","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8QTWRAMR/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8QTWRAMR/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-15T13:09:27.080Z"],["3812761","WAVE-232","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik",":bandit:  Fix it - refers to the idea that refresh is not happening OR the colour of the message in the console makes people not see it?","2026-01-15T13:09:27.859Z"],["3812762","WAVE-232","WAVE","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","tbh i did not see the message it is opaque and there are too many texts anyways","2026-01-15T13:09:28.430Z"],["3812763","WAVE-232","WAVE","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","i would rather like {{pnpm start -m fleet}} to take into account its own dependencies without explicit command","2026-01-15T13:09:29.186Z"],["3812764","WAVE-232","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","There are cases where it could start ~ 20 modules :slightly_smiling_face: 20x 500MB per module 10G of your RAM goes boom right away + CPU resources. I am not sure you actually want this. I see the problematic behaviour here tho - if you miss the message, is not obvious that hot reload and refresh won’t work for remote components that you haven’t started. Maybe something lines of\n\n• Stop user, wait for confirmation that he/she understand what this log line means and interactively choose more modules to watch\n• Allow “hot” starts of watching during the development cycle, when user touches other modules\n• UI level toolbars that give you the context you are operating in - what files are watched, what are ignored etc","2026-01-15T13:09:30.809Z"],["3812765","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","{quote}message it is opaque{quote}\n\nThat I can fix, I can even make it blink :slightly_smiling_face:\n\n{quote}there are too many texts anyways{quote}\n\nThat has a little bit to do with your fleet module, as it pulls in a lot of things, as Artur said","2026-01-15T13:09:31.735Z"],["3812766","WAVE-232","WAVE","helmer.aaviksoo@bolt.eu","Helmer Aaviksoo","I played with RsPack/Devserver settings a bit, trying to reduce the output, but it’s not that simple or I dunno how. Well, I do, but it would be so ugly that you wouldn’t merge my PR :slightly_smiling_face:\n\nBut simplest thing we can do, after making the purple blink (and not purple), is to delay the message until after build is finished (or even after devserver is started). Then it’s in your face.","2026-01-15T13:09:32.678Z"],["3812767","LSS-61534","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] great work with the assessment! You’re picking everything super fast – keep it up :mechanical_arm: \n\n\n\nI’d recommend you start from the order that is linked to the BH ticket to save yourself time.\n\n\n\nAs we can see, [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2148331573/54?orderTryId=3362804793] was made using device dMaAtBvuRnWAUPVAZGlBnp (TECNO MOBILE LIMITEDTECNO KF6j). \n\nAlways check the device UID rather than device name. To add a layer of complication to this, sometimes devices have the same or similar names.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.54.01.png|width=781,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.54.01.png\"!\n\n\n\nAccording to login sessions data in Admin, this device was first logged in on 9 September 2022 using phone number (OTP to SMS) and then logged out on 23 October 2022. Then this device logged in again on the same day 23 October 2022 with the same method and stayed logged in – as we see it was last used on 13 Jan 2026 before the allegedly unauthorized order occured.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.55.32.png|width=831,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.55.32.png\"!\n\n\n\nThere are 2 possible explanations, from my experience:\n\n# User passed on their old device to someone else and didn’t log out of their Bolt account\n# User is trying to get refund for ride they took\n\n* if you’d like to confirm this, then [#dev-user-auth-support|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS] are your PoCs\n\n\n\nIn this case, we can see that CS logged user out of all devices, so if scenario 1 is correct – the new device owner should no longer have access. If there was a breach we managed to take protective measures. \n\n\n\nPlease check if CS communicated the necessary details to the user – that we logged all devices out and recommended switching on 2FA for the future. We don’t need to know exactly what happened, Users often don’t tell us. Please ask Martin if he filled out Cognito assessment for this. Also explain to him what likelky happened. \n\n\n\nIf all done, you made it and close your privacy ticket!!!! YAY! Cheers to first of many 💚 ","2026-01-15T13:09:35.107Z"],["3812769","HS-28892","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hei! Assignin selle sulle (ma vaatasin Smartsheetist, et see on sinu Hire) 😄 ","2026-01-15T13:10:48.509Z"],["3812770","LSS-61561","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:613a01a1e2a0d60069d29ca1] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.[^SBH - GHSTNBOFF102 - BOLT HOLDINGS OU (1) copy (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T13:11:04.648Z"],["3812771","DRX-28017","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please do regression for map, double check lights / dark mode, order and home flows, and maps on scheduled rides, past order history details, surge heat map on main screen","2026-01-15T13:11:06.105Z"],["3812772","CLIENTAPP-38775","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please do regression for map, double check lights / dark mode, order and home flows, and maps on scheduled rides, past order history details, surge heat map on main screen","2026-01-15T13:11:06.747Z"],["3812773","RISK2-3127","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","Training for Aviv on 21.01. when we’re in Tallinn.","2026-01-15T13:11:20.667Z"],["3812774","PFI-833486","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please reach out to customer payments for this. Thanks! ","2026-01-15T13:11:25.926Z"],["3812775","PFI-833486","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T13:11:31.694Z"],["3812776","MLC-3612","MLC","nida.altug@bolt.eu","Nida Altuğ","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* In Progress\n* *Blockers: N/A*\n* *Status update:*\n** Data showed it didnt neccesarily performed worse than general rider performance.\n** We can provide generic holiday comms again but we need to make sure we dont spend too much work force on it as local teams also ha their own plans and usage was limited.\n** Final sheet will be uploaded to google drive and will update here as well.","2026-01-15T13:12:19.946Z"],["3812777","LSS-60941","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^POGODBA O UPORABI SKLADIŠČNEGA PROSTORA BOLT (signed) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T13:12:47.914Z"],["3812778","WEBSD-1475","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] \n\nThanks a lot for the explanation! Following up on your bullets below: \n\n# and 2. [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c]  could you please confirm whether it would be appropriate to upload the above-mentioned documents under the EU region on the web?\n\n\n3.[~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] could you please help us with the confirmed PDF and DOCX files? Alternatively, if these files currently exist only on Confluence, would that be sufficient to move them to the CMS, [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f] ?\n\nThanks a lot in advance! ","2026-01-15T13:12:49.607Z"],["3812779","PFI-833780","PFI","jorge.veiga@bolt-outsource.eu","Jorge Veiga","!IMG_4578.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T13:13:05.881Z"],["3812780","DSR-3585","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] Heyyy! I’ll finalize the response and once it’s done I’ll share it with you and change the ticket to in progress CSPC 💚 ","2026-01-15T13:13:27.010Z"],["3812782","HS-28977","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Dudu, I have sent both letters for signing. ","2026-01-15T13:13:59.043Z"],["3812783","PFI-832546","PFI","bohdan.hanulych@bolt-outsource.eu","Bohdan Hanulych","Hello, team. Any news?","2026-01-15T13:14:07.929Z"],["3812784","LSS-56235","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:5b8517da332df52a5d9460cc] [~accountid:712020:4270191e-b006-439e-a800-5b8e06cf2c60] since as I understand we do not currently have information on whether we will proceed with the involvement of the debt collector company, I will close this ticket until we have the clarity on this. \n\nPlease let me know if we have a decision to proceed.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:76b6df07-e71d-429f-a069-ee3c132ee915] ","2026-01-15T13:14:09.320Z"],["3812787","MLC-3729","MLC","nida.altug@bolt.eu","Nida Altuğ","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone: 5%*\n* *Blockers: N/A*\n* *Status update:* \n** Re-aligned w [~accountid:5fb225a6f2df6c00762b994d] for the project this week we went over the processes and what might be missing\n** Re-requested access for figma edit as acceses were chaged and got the access back.\n** Working on listing exact missing comms to start replacing will add the final list here as well.","2026-01-15T13:14:44.401Z"],["3812788","PFI-833782","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T13:14:59.265Z"],["3812789","LSS-57346","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026:\n\n* *Airwallex topics*: Product legal has aligned with commerce legal regarding the updates to internal CS guidances. To share final input for CS (Lisanna Lomp) we need to get confirmations on some questions from Airwallex. [Commerce legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57383] has been updated accordingly and relevant stakeholders contacted.\n* *Escalation from CS to merchant team:* sync with Kshitij from merchant tops has been agreed on for 19.01.2026 so he could explain what are the plans with Cognizant and whether merchant team want to outsource some CS support for merchant accounts from them. Important so that CS would know where and to whom escalate P2B or DSA complaints related to merchant accounts and writ it in to their processes.\n* *After above has been cleared out we can:*\n** finalise new CS processes for DSA complaints (P2B related will be updated next)\n** upload [new complaint rules|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KyffcN_OQYJ_RbEJfAFPSGh2AHvOIS1YGqzjx_md_Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xeajywah5w4] on Bolt webpage","2026-01-15T13:15:01.065Z"],["3812790","MTE-1230","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","[~accountid:712020:cd383b4c-dce2-4e04-98a6-4398af29ffc2] lets proceed without a test name.\n\nTest ID is doable, correct?","2026-01-15T13:15:08.850Z"],["3812791","LSS-61048","LSS","karina.kochanovskaya@bolt.eu","Karina Kochanovskaya","hey! what’s the ETA here? ","2026-01-15T13:15:14.081Z"],["3812792","LSS-60727","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^PEL_ZUS PUE_Aleksandra Kusiak (8c0330bc-2e6d-468e-9def-3e5c54144d07).pdf] ","2026-01-15T13:15:23.295Z"],["3812793","LSS-57345","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026:\n\n* *Airwallex topics*: Product legal has aligned with commerce legal regarding the updates to internal CS guidances. To share final input for CS (Lisanna Lomp) we need to get confirmations on some questions from Airwallex. [Commerce legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57383] has been updated accordingly and relevant stakeholders contacted.\n* *Escalation from CS to merchant team:* sync with Kshitij from merchant tops has been agreed on for 19.01.2026 so he could explain what are the plans with Cognizant and whether merchant team want to outsource some CS support for merchant accounts from them. Important so that CS would know where and to whom escalate P2B or DSA complaints related to merchant accounts and writ it in to their processes.\n* After above has been cleared out we can:\n** finalise new CS processes for DSA complaints (P2B related will be updated next)\n** upload [new complaint rules|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KyffcN_OQYJ_RbEJfAFPSGh2AHvOIS1YGqzjx_md_Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xeajywah5w4] on Bolt webpage","2026-01-15T13:15:23.486Z"],["3812797","LSS-61641","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T13:16:34.714Z"],["3812798","LSS-57348","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026:\n\n* *Airwallex topics*: Product legal has aligned with commerce legal regarding the updates to internal CS guidances. To share final input for CS (Lisanna Lomp) we need to get confirmations on some questions from Airwallex. [Commerce legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57383] has been updated accordingly and relevant stakeholders contacted.\n* *Escalation from CS to merchant team:* sync with Kshitij from merchant tops has been agreed on for 19.01.2026 so he could explain what are the plans with Cognizant and whether merchant team want to outsource some CS support for merchant accounts from them. Important so that CS would know where and to whom escalate P2B or DSA complaints related to merchant accounts and writ it in to their processes.\n* After above has been cleared out we can:\n** finalise new CS processes for DSA complaints (P2B related will be updated next) with Lisanna Lomp (covers also rides)\n** upload [new complaint rules|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KyffcN_OQYJ_RbEJfAFPSGh2AHvOIS1YGqzjx_md_Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xeajywah5w4] on Bolt webpage\n\nfyi: [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] ","2026-01-15T13:16:40.446Z"],["3812800","MTE-1230","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","[~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] yes, we have testId, partner_uuid, treatment_id and modal name","2026-01-15T13:17:09.850Z"],["3812802","MTE-1230","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","[~accountid:712020:cd383b4c-dce2-4e04-98a6-4398af29ffc2] What about {{InboxMessageTitle}}? Is it possible to add as well?","2026-01-15T13:17:44.426Z"],["3812803","EBIKE1-423","EBIKE1","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","Reviewed, very good SOP. Released to LOPS.","2026-01-15T13:18:09.446Z"],["3812804","MLC-2769","MLC","nida.altug@bolt.eu","Nida Altuğ","*Week 3:*\n\n* *Status / Milestone: 25%*\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:* \n* [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] prepped the new comms sheet to share with the local team also for them to go over and make sure we have everything we need.\n* Had written introduction with local team will schedule a call for next week for general introduction and progress alignment.\n* Communicated with local team for detecting missing comms and coordinated with localisation team for next steps after local teams list is ready.","2026-01-15T13:18:33.403Z"],["3812806","LSS-60183","LSS","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\nGiving initial insights to answer your questions:\n\n\n{quote}when the vulnerability was introduced (and fixed, if not on Jan 7);{quote}\n\nWe don’t know for sure yet, might have been there for a while.\n\n\n{quote}were there any other types of docs accessible other than driver’s license;{quote}\n\nI have been observing the incoming docs for a few days, and we still get approximately 50 events per day. Most of the remaining links appear to be email attachments sent to Bolt CS (which would be accessible to engineers through Beehive in any case).\n\nWe will probably close the current vulnerability ticket and open up a new, less severe one to resolve the remaining links (as we have found no PII there).\n\n\n{quote}confirm if the vulnerability could not be exploited by parties outside Bolt.{quote}\n\nConfirming, accessing these URLs via this channel is only possible for Bolt employees with Bolt B2-B1 VPN access level (software engineers, site reliability engineers, and security engineers).","2026-01-15T13:18:59.656Z"],["3812807","DSR-3057","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Hi,\nCan you please check if all good to go, all in the folder you created :than: ","2026-01-15T13:19:24.818Z"],["3812808","LSS-44904","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026:\n\nBelow update is related to updating global complaint handling rules - [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57331]: \n\n* *Airwallex topics*: Product legal has aligned with commerce legal regarding the updates to internal CS guidances. To share final input for CS (Lisanna Lomp) we need to get confirmations on some questions from Airwallex. [Commerce legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57383] has been updated accordingly and relevant stakeholders contacted.\n* *Escalation from CS to merchant team:* sync with Kshitij from merchant tops has been agreed on for 19.01.2026 so he could explain what are the plans with Cognizant and whether merchant team want to outsource some CS support for merchant accounts from them. Important so that CS would know where and to whom escalate P2B or DSA complaints related to merchant accounts and writ it in to their processes.\n* After above has been cleared out we can:\n** finalise new CS processes for DSA complaints (P2B related will be updated next)\n** upload [new complaint rules|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KyffcN_OQYJ_RbEJfAFPSGh2AHvOIS1YGqzjx_md_Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xeajywah5w4] on Bolt webpage","2026-01-15T13:19:24.849Z"],["3812809","PFI-812195","PFI","viktorija.valinskaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktorija Valinskaitė","waiting for an update. ","2026-01-15T13:19:32.854Z"],["3812810","LSS-61421","LSS","bayram.khalilzade@bolt.eu","Bayram Khalilzade","[~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] done. Could you please check? ","2026-01-15T13:19:48.082Z"],["3812813","HS-28908","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-15T13:20:15.140Z"],["3812814","LSS-57331","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026:\n\n* *Airwallex topics*: Product legal has aligned with commerce legal regarding the updates to internal CS guidances. To share final input for CS (Lisanna Lomp) we need to get confirmations on some questions from Airwallex. [Commerce legal ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57383] has been updated accordingly and relevant stakeholders contacted.\n* *Escalation from CS to merchant team:* sync with Kshitij from merchant tops has been agreed on for 19.01.2026 so he could explain what are the plans with Cognizant and whether merchant team want to outsource some CS support for merchant accounts from them. Important so that CS would know where and to whom escalate P2B or DSA complaints related to merchant accounts and writ it in to their processes.\n* After above has been cleared out we can:\n** finalise new CS processes for DSA complaints (P2B related will be updated next)\n** upload [new complaint rules|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11KyffcN_OQYJ_RbEJfAFPSGh2AHvOIS1YGqzjx_md_Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xeajywah5w4] on Bolt webpage","2026-01-15T13:20:30.506Z"],["3812816","HS-28935","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi!\n\nThank You, document received!\n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-15T13:21:13.151Z"],["3812817","DELIVERY-754","DELIVERY","ankit.gupta@bolt.eu","Ankit Gupta","26W02: card payment option, a few things need to be polished on the UI dev side, and the analytical setup is done for A/B test. \nTest launch date:  {{2026-02-03}}","2026-01-15T13:21:13.621Z"],["3812819","WD-22372","WD","keidi.helm@bolt.eu","Keidi Helm","Hi\n\nI confirm.\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T13:21:25.528Z"],["3812820","BRE-1063","BRE","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","Done:\n\n* added new table to CDC\n* notified Tauri\n* checked fleet-related and commission records","2026-01-15T13:21:39.894Z"],["3812824","CSDA-298","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-15T13:22:15.988Z"],["3812825","PFI-804990","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Clearing backlog if issue still exists please reach out partner payments slack channel or comment on this ticket !","2026-01-15T13:22:27.157Z"],["3812830","LSS-61382","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","I will close the ticket since legal advise was provided 🙂 ","2026-01-15T13:23:07.627Z"],["3812831","MLC-3472","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W3 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** Started prepping [results summary|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gbaur2SK9jBzTRgMkNFWtsyVr-aTZ4LRzKEHGciW-cI/edit?tab=t.i808357h8xpf] for the experiment, Cristina to review\n* *Next steps:*\n** Finalize the results summary on Tuesday (20/01).","2026-01-15T13:23:12.979Z"],["3812832","PFI-832794","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T13:23:24.168Z"],["3812836","L10N-28122","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28118](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28118)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T13:24:15.590Z"],["3812837","L10N-28126","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28118](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28118)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T13:24:18.376Z"],["3812838","L10N-28128","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic h