cessed ","2026-01-15T13:25:17.266Z"],["3812851","PFI-832864","PFI","volodymyr.gonchar@bolt.eu","Volodymyr Gonchar","I’ll clarify, so I understand your point correctly.\n\nIf we apply bonus as manual adjustment then it’s compensation. Even despite the fact it is not set up in admin the amount of compensation is deducted from our commission (as any other bonuses from automated campaigns) > VAT is lower?","2026-01-15T13:25:30.371Z"],["3812852","LSS-60735","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Project Diamond - EY Advisory Support_Bolt Operations OÜ_Ernst & Young LLP_14.01.26.pdf] ","2026-01-15T13:25:40.088Z"],["3812853","RNTL-27071","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","Migrated metrics:\n\n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_orders_in_finished_state.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_orders_in_finished_state.yml|smart-link] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_orders_in_cancelled_state.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_orders_in_cancelled_state.yml|smart-link] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_gmv_before_discounts.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_gmv_before_discounts.yml|smart-link] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_gmv_pay_as_you_go_before_discounts.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_gmv_pay_as_you_go_before_discounts.yml|smart-link] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_gmv_subscription.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_gmv_subscription.yml|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:25:45.829Z"],["3812854","PFI-805068","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","clearing backlog if issue still exists please drop a comment !","2026-01-15T13:25:47.031Z"],["3812855","WEBSD-1481","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","Data: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oHLRpyjdXRHIs4gJtex8FKDyQHqLAJ4O-B6dsI_EpT0/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oHLRpyjdXRHIs4gJtex8FKDyQHqLAJ4O-B6dsI_EpT0/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:26:04.830Z"],["3812856","HS-28874","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi!\n\nThank You for reaching out! \n\nThis is a task that every new employee receives to their mailbox in Workday. This is to confirm Your legal name. You would need to go to Your WorkDay inbox what is located on Workday on the right top corner and confirm Your legal name change task. Once this is confirmed You can proceed with the previously shared guidance on how to change Your preferred name. \n\nPlease let me know if You have any questions.\n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-15T13:26:15.940Z"],["3812857","LSS-55755","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed documents attached!\n\n[^Amendment agreement no. 1_Bolt Operations OÜ_Stella Energy Norway AS_14.01.26.pdf]\n[^Annex 1 of the Appendix 1 - Bolt Operator Reward Scheme to the Partnership Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_Stella Energy Norway AS_14.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T13:26:25.841Z"],["3812858","LSS-60541","LSS","sandra.figari@bolt.eu","Sandra Figari","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897]! Thank you very much 💚 \n\nI’ll let you know as soon we can proceed with the signing process.\n\n","2026-01-15T13:26:33.071Z"],["3812859","CLOUDSEC-723","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-15T13:26:43.673Z"],["3812861","PFI-833791","PFI","ludovit.filatov@bolt.eu","Ľudovít Filatov","[^2025-12-22 -- 2025-12-29 La Pizza King Weekly Report (1).pdf]","2026-01-15T13:27:05.116Z"],["3812862","MLC-2742","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W3 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** Working on final small padding adjustments for the DND template, should be fully finalized by EOW. \n* *Next steps:*\n** Sync with Mariann on next steps re: fixing the already live HTMLs and rolling out the rest of the comms that were initially planned.","2026-01-15T13:27:06.223Z"],["3812864","SREDESK-7425","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_delivery_courier_activity;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.517s\n\nroot@ti-delivery-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_delivery_courier_activity;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 1.012s{noformat}","2026-01-15T13:27:29.217Z"],["3812865","PFI-833790","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T13:27:29.968Z"],["3812866","LSS-56585","LSS","emmanuel.lewis@bolt.eu","Emmanuel Lewis","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] & [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a], please find the attached MOU from the Vodacom team. Despite mentioning that we have no leeway for further negotiation,s they have made their final recommendations on the MOU and the DSA annexure. \n\nIf you have concerns regarding their recommendations, and in order to streamline this process, can we please set up a quick meeting with the Vodacom legal team so that we can finalise any final amendments? \n\n\n\n[^Bolt Rewards ZA_MOU - VODACOM BOLT 14Jan2026.docx]\n\n","2026-01-15T13:27:41.819Z"],["3812872","UXA-2219","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","Food ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BSKT-4598|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BSKT-4598|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:28:10.885Z"],["3812878","LSS-58216","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] - thanks for sharing!\n\nI’ve added our contact details to page 36.\n\n----\n\nRe/ clause 9.2 - essentially, Solidgate changed our usual indemnity setup so that liability works *both ways*, instead of mainly protecting Bolt.\n\nAs written, this could make Bolt financially responsible for data or security issues even considering that Solidgate runs the payment systems and controls the technical setup. There is also *no liability cap applicable to the DSA*, meaning Bolt’s exposure could be much higher than the value of the deal.\n\nTo mitigate the risk, I suggested small, standard changes to:\n\n* make sure each party is only responsible for issues *they actually cause*,\n* avoid Bolt paying for problems inside Solidgate’s systems,\n* cap Bolt’s liability at *EUR 100,000 under the DSA*, while Solidgate remains uncapped & comment clarifying why this is still balanced for Solidgate.\n* and ensure the procedure of how claims are handled under the DSA are more clearly clarified.\n\nPlease kindly inform Solidgate of this update. I will be ready to respond to any new questions, but I believe this is a proportionate and clear update.\n\n----\n\nOtherwise, everything else from privacy side seems to be clear and no issues arose, which is very good news🙌 ","2026-01-15T13:28:38.972Z"],["3812879","PFI-833791","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-15T13:28:40.417Z"],["3812880","FIS-4201","FIS","pavel.permenov@bolt.eu","Pavel Permenov","The courier fleets are not able to provide their credentials to us, because the Formaloo form in [the guide|https://bolt.eu/pt-pt/support/articles/9163624171666/] that local Ops share with courier fleets shared was disabled by Infosec.","2026-01-15T13:29:35.609Z"],["3812881","PFI-805566","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment return was processed ","2026-01-15T13:29:36.846Z"],["3812882","HS-28911","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-15T13:29:59.640Z"],["3812883","PFI-805571","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Clearing Backlog if issue still exists please drop a comment or reach out via slack !","2026-01-15T13:30:03.798Z"],["3812884","LSS-61620","LSS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Thank you, Alex!\nI confirm the reason of extension is the business continuity until we implement the new payroll provider. \n\n[~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] - please let me know if anything else is needed.\n\n","2026-01-15T13:30:22.978Z"],["3812889","WEBSD-1475","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd]  👋 \n\nDirectly we can't. \n\n# We cannot use *confluence* files for our CMS related to *PDF’s* \n#  .*docx* we can copy and paste from confluence. I haven’t tried from Confluence to be honest but I guess it’s possible.\n\nUsually we get the files.\n\nif something please let me know.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-15T13:30:48.032Z"],["3812891","LSS-61192","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:f8c30920-765a-42dd-bbe7-058336c97a0c] yes you can share the [this draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IEjdoYYTjAWl4XBDqHZwO3uechDnr11M6jgVg11-a9E/edit?tab=t.0] with the client. \n\nPlease delete your comment responding to my comment addressed to SICPA on Annex 2, clause 11 KPIs. ","2026-01-15T13:30:52.988Z"],["3812892","LSS-59793","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update re/ Solidgate - copying developments from the main ticket:*\n\n----\n\nRe/ clause 9.2 - essentially, Solidgate changed our usual indemnity setup so that liability works *both ways*, instead of mainly protecting Bolt.\n\nAs written, this could make Bolt financially responsible for data or security issues even considering that Solidgate runs the payment systems and controls the technical setup. There is also *no liability cap applicable to the DSA*, meaning Bolt’s exposure could be much higher than the value of the deal.\n\nTo mitigate the risk, I suggested small, standard changes to:\n\n* make sure each party is only responsible for issues *they actually cause*,\n* avoid Bolt paying for problems inside Solidgate’s systems,\n* cap Bolt’s liability at *EUR 100,000 under the DSA*, while Solidgate remains uncapped & comment clarifying why this is still balanced for Solidgate.\n* and ensure the procedure of how claims are handled under the DSA are more clearly clarified.\n\nPlease kindly inform Solidgate of this update. I will be ready to respond to any new questions, but I believe this is a proportionate and clear update.\n\n----\n\nOtherwise, everything else from privacy side seems to be clear and no issues arose.","2026-01-15T13:30:53.817Z"],["3812896","BP-12602","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:0559a7fa-2c87-497d-957a-02b7de3945e1] I have this old ticket for updating the visuals, it is up to you whenever you will implement the desing as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-12849|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-12849|smart-link]  or seperating them and using this task for the design/copy update that is not related just to the “Trust this device” checkbox","2026-01-15T13:31:32.519Z"],["3812897","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] Thank you, however, *the table provided is intended and suitable for completing only information related to this file, “Bilag A. Kravsspecifikation taxaudbud,” and not to other documents.*\n\nCould you please clarify with PwC *whether they would accept our proposed changes to the NDA, CoC, and Supply agreement if those changes are made directly in the draft* documents themselves, using track changes?\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T13:32:04.673Z"],["3812901","LSS-61238","LSS","aivo.toots@bolt.eu","Aivo Toots","* Hello [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] . My understanding is that DPA is not usually required and signed with ISO27001 external auditors.\n\n\nWhat the auditors usually do:\n\n* *Evidence Review:* Auditors review documented evidence, observe processes, conduct staff interviews, and check system configurations and audit logs. They may ask to see records that confirm policies are being followed (e.g., a log of user access reviews) but often do not need to view the specific underlying personal or customer information. Auditors often visually verify that some records exist, but the contents are not recorded, just the fact of verification.\n* *Read-Only or Assisted Access:* If auditors require access to systems to verify a control, access is typically limited to *read-only*. Alternatively, a system administrator with the necessary permissions may access the system on the auditor's behalf and present the requested evidence. \n\nWhat they usually get access to:\n\n* *Employee and personnel information:* This is often the most common type of personal data encountered, as auditors need to verify controls related to human resource security and access management. Examples include:\n** Names and job roles\n** Contact information (e.g., email addresses)\n** Access rights and permissions data (logs, access reviews)\n** Training and awareness records\n** Disciplinary actions and termination records (to check processes for revoking access)\n* *Audit-related operational data:* The process of the audit itself generates some personal data related to the audit process. This might include:\n** Auditor names and credentials\n** Interview notes with key personnel\n** Documentation of assigned roles and responsibilities\n* *Accessing customers data is being avoided.*\n* The personal data of *suppliers* processed is generally limited to contact and contractual information of relevant personnel (e.g., names, job titles, contact details) if even that.\n\n","2026-01-15T13:32:42.414Z"],["3812903","HS-28989","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:c6aafe58-3b3b-42c5-b22d-76a1d553b53c] , the start date is changed. Closing this ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-15T13:33:30.224Z"],["3812905","LSS-60941","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] !","2026-01-15T13:33:46.020Z"],["3812906","MLC-3755","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*W3 updates:*\n\n* *Blockers:* N/A\n* *Status update:*\n** TBA, will finish and launch first setups tomorrow\n** Localisations are in progress, some languages still waiting for support even though ticket deadlines are tomorrow - will ping the localisation team Monday for an updated ETA \n* *Next steps:*\n** Monitoring the results of A/B testing + continue with creating test setups as localisations come in  ","2026-01-15T13:33:59.385Z"],["3812907","LSS-58344","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Thanks [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] \n\n[~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] Kindly see above recommendations and assist \n\nOn the last point regarding bearing of Withholding tax - we are waiting for feedback from the providers. ","2026-01-15T13:34:00.182Z"],["3812910","RDXENG-4668","RDXENG","grigorii.dzhanelidze@bolt.eu","Greg Dzhanelidze","Tested on prelive, not worth QAing on top of that","2026-01-15T13:34:30.331Z"],["3812911","MLC-3297","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:*\n** *Data collection*\n*** *Sync with Roman:* workflow, what we’ll report, deadlines\n*** *Rewind 2025 report:* finalised (/) \n**** Updating the Jira with the report: 90% done → unifying the language + adding a stakeholder summary\n*** Sharing a summary with the Brand team tomorrow, on {{2026-01-16}}\n* *Next steps:*\n** N/A","2026-01-15T13:34:45.236Z"],["3812913","LSS-61192","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - ok will do, not sending contract yet to client because cs-looker channel on slack said we need to have a more indepth discussion around my query for the CS response time of 90% within 48 hours.   I will revert once I hear from them in case anything needs to be modified before I share with client the final comments. ","2026-01-15T13:35:03.847Z"],["3812914","BP-12602","BP","uladzislau.tsyrkunou@bolt.eu","Uladzislau Tsyrkunou","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] thanks for highlighting it. \nI’ll create a technical implementation doc as a part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-12849|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-12849|smart-link] and the  implementation itself can be a part of BP-12602 ticket.","2026-01-15T13:35:57.183Z"],["3812915","LSS-61238","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:712020:44e59489-5db2-4488-8537-588bccee709b], thanks for this clear confirmation.","2026-01-15T13:36:05.779Z"],["3812916","FX-3644","FX","carlo.fanton@bolt.eu","Carlo Leone Fanton","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160306|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160306]","2026-01-15T13:36:16.331Z"],["3812917","LSS-61294","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Replied in the main ticket.","2026-01-15T13:36:25.135Z"],["3812918","PFI-805974","PFI","jakub.kavina@bolt.eu","Jakub Kavina","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] Hey there, would you be able to provide a PoP please? The courier contacted us that he still did not receive the payment. Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-15T13:36:30.340Z"],["3812921","LSS-60735","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Thank you! [~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] this can be marked as Done, thank you all for your support.","2026-01-15T13:37:00.813Z"],["3812923","MLC-3683","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:*\n* *Status update:*\n** *Sending out an ad-hoc to dormant users in FR*\n** Owned by [~accountid:712020:5ee0b1d5-3b9b-4a48-826c-fce4ef2d1492] while I was OOO.\n** Investigating the low OR (0.71%) → didn’t spot anything unusual in the setup.\n*** Hypothesis: low OR came from targeting sunset users.\n** *Next steps:*\n*** *Planning the next steps for Q1:* Aligning on the experiment we planned for Q1.\n*** *Updating Jira:* Updating this Jira epic with more context around the project.","2026-01-15T13:37:11.223Z"],["3812924","LSS-61123","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5b7bea7195627d2a5723efff] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt_ Izjava o partnerskoj suradnji_ VELIKI IGRAČ j.d.o.o. (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T13:37:16.213Z"],["3812927","RDXENG-4680","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","Looks like same icon is sent from BE for both light and dark variant cc: [~accountid:712020:32ff1b8a-e85e-4b94-8a79-56484670e212] [~accountid:5c66c5ba58edf75c2b8e458b] \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.33.26-20260115-133710.png|width=371,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.33.26-20260115-133710.png\"!","2026-01-15T13:38:04.287Z"],["3812928","FRAUDOPS-562","FRAUDOPS","guilherme.franciulli@bolt.eu","Guilherme Franciulli","rules for *driver_destination_update*:\n\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_ADJUST_AUTH?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_ADJUST_AUTH?tab=approval_requests]\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/user_destination_update/DESTINATION_CHANGE_RIDER_ADJUST_AUTH?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/user_destination_update/DESTINATION_CHANGE_RIDER_ADJUST_AUTH?tab=approval_requests]\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_DISTANCE_TO_PICKUP?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_DISTANCE_TO_PICKUP?tab=approval_requests]\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_FRAUD?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_FRAUD?tab=approval_requests]\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_NEW_USERS?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_NEW_USERS?tab=approval_requests]\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_STOP_IS_FAR?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_STOP_IS_FAR?tab=approval_requests]\n* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_NUMBER_LIMIT?tab=approval_requests|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/driver_destination_update/DRIVER_DESTINATION_CHANGE_NUMBER_LIMIT?tab=approval_requests]","2026-01-15T13:38:06.575Z"],["3812929","MTE-1230","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","[~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] There is a problem, because I assume this title should be translated in user language? It is doable, but it can be slow, because we need to make a lot of request to fetch language per user, translations for these languages and send right title.\n\nI suggest to send event without it and if it will be good to have title we can add. I can also add title but not translated right now.","2026-01-15T13:38:07.476Z"],["3812930","LSS-58830","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] Bolt Ops OU will share data with *EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH,* who will then transfer the cases through their Cross Border platform to their relevant local entities (EOS companies or partners depending on country).","2026-01-15T13:38:13.499Z"],["3812931","LSS-61533","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0] - if I understand you correctly, I can suggest the following:\n\n* CONSENT FORM - PERSONAL DATA PROCESSING FOR BACKGROUND CHECK\n* ЗГОДА НА ОБРОБКУ ПЕРСОНАЛЬНИХ ДАНИХ ДЛЯ ПРОВЕДЕННЯ ПЕРЕВІРКИ КАНДИДАТА","2026-01-15T13:38:22.881Z"],["3812934","LSS-61643","LSS","kristjan.jalakas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Jalakas","[^Bolt Services DE GmbH Account Confirmation.docx] _(233 kB)_","2026-01-15T13:38:24.717Z"],["3812937","FX-3645","FX","carlo.fanton@bolt.eu","Carlo Leone Fanton","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160884|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160884|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:38:57.080Z"],["3812939","L10N-28154","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28118](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28118)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T13:39:16.178Z"],["3812941","MTE-1230","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","[~accountid:712020:cd383b4c-dce2-4e04-98a6-4398af29ffc2] Makes total sense, thanks for the info. I’ll share it with the revelant team.","2026-01-15T13:39:33.184Z"],["3812946","LSS-60949","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343301|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343301|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T13:40:36.970Z"],["3812947","LSS-61433","LSS","andrea.rietmeijer@bolt.eu","Andrea Rietmeijer","[^Rückforderung der Vorauszahlung gemäß Kooperationsvereinbarung_Yusuf_v3.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T13:40:56.390Z"],["3812949","SRED-1072","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-15T13:41:07.194Z"],["3812950","GS-144","GS","gabriel.munteanu@bolt.eu","Gabriel Munteanu","We know about flaky test and will approach them soon,","2026-01-15T13:41:12.365Z"],["3812951","MLC-185","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*Week 3 updates*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* progress 92%\n* *Blockers:* None\n* *Status update:* \n** 100% rollout was postponed until 20.01 ([thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08EY6QA98E/p1766405563839789]).\n\n* *Next steps:*\n** [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] create setups for remaining planned use cases (Bolt XL, Bolt Comfort, Scheduled Rides, Bolt Drive, Family Profile) and release to internal test group for feedback.\n** If needed, will also revive the discussion on control groups for next week","2026-01-15T13:41:18.662Z"],["3812953","LSS-61644","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","’ve reviewed the App Store age ratings [guidance|https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/age-ratings-values-and-definitions/] and don’t see a strong reason to change our current rating (4+). Our app fits the 4+ criteria, as we have messaging/chat features, ads, and some age-assurance tools, all of which are allowed in that category.\nThe only potential grey area is the “mature themes” indicator, since Bolt Food lists alcohol/tobacco for sale. Under Apple’s definitions, this could push us into 13+. But the way the guidance is written, “mature themes” seems aimed at _depictions of alcohol consumption_ (e.g., showing people drinking), rather than simply offering alcohol for purchase with legal age checks. I see that some food delivery apps have adopted a more cautious approach - Wolt, Uber Eats. Deliveroo have 12+ (will be changed to 13+ in the new rating system). That said, our rating has been 4+ for a while now, so I don’t see any immediate need to change it based on the new rating system.\nOn that basis, I think our current 4+ rating is ok for all apps!","2026-01-15T13:41:38.031Z"],["3812955","LSS-61534","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] \nThank you for a super-detailed overview - REALLY appreciate it 💚 \n\nI can confirm that CS has communicated the necessary details to the user. I’ll proceed by asking Martin about the Cognito assessment and explaining to him what likely happened. 🙂 ","2026-01-15T13:41:52.770Z"],["3812957","SRED-927","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-15T13:42:14.995Z"],["3812960","PFI-833796","PFI","augustas.baublys@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustas Baublys","!IMG_4038.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_4039.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T13:42:59.030Z"],["3812961","LSS-61644","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.35.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.35.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.56.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.56.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.40.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.40.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.53.01.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.53.01.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.44.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.44.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.52.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.52.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.28.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.28.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.48.png|width=1115,alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-13 at 11.52.48.png\"!\n\nSome have not been answered, but the answers are: \n\n\n# arental Controls - no\n# Age Assurance - yes (I think ID check falls under here..)\n# User-generated content-  no\n# Messaging and chat - no (there’s no chat for courier-courier chats)\n# Advertising - No\n# Health or Wellness - no\n# Weapons - no\n# Loot boxes - no","2026-01-15T13:43:06.192Z"],["3812962","WD-22573","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","This EORI number will first need to be added to the Workday entity, each of them, ATM I don't think there is a field for that. \n\n\n\n[~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] , can you please advise if there is a placeholder for such a field on the company? or maybe it goes under the tax id types?\n\n\n\nIf not, then we can hard code it to the layout, in that case, [~accountid:712020:ff293eea-e5af-4325-9057-8f1a09bd3aa3] , please provide the numbers for each EORI code, and we can only hard code say form company ee003, or any other one company, otherwise its going to be very manual and tough to create and maintain mappings for each of these companies. \n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-15T13:43:05.006Z"],["3812964","LSS-58897","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] \n\nRe/ personal data processing, for my information, what T&Cs are we planning to advise using for this campaign?\n\nI believe, considering this is CA, I would need to review our standard section on data protection to double check if its adequate for this jurisdiction.","2026-01-15T13:43:46.145Z"],["3812966","RDXENG-4680","RDXENG","pavel.panarad@bolt.eu","Pavel Panarad","[~accountid:60fbd5ec9f975e0069eec7a1] iOS is doing client side tinting then as it looks ok there","2026-01-15T13:44:12.990Z"],["3812967","LSS-61346","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343305|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343305|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:44:33.057Z"],["3812969","LSS-58897","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:6ca2307e-6766-4d7e-a7b5-7f3b9a6cb0b6] \n\nTo assist the privacy team, can you kindly clarify the following:\n\n# What personal data will you require from participants and winners;\n# For what purpose will each category of personal data will need to be collected;\n# How are you planning to collect the data;\n# How long do you need to retain the personal data.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-15T13:45:15.209Z"],["3812970","LSS-61101","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","Thank you, I will share it with landlord! 🙂 ","2026-01-15T13:45:25.395Z"],["3812973","PFI-833340","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Asking the devs to take a look\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1768484710429139?thread_ts=1768484668.856719&cid=CNV6QPRFT|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1768484710429139?thread_ts=1768484668.856719&cid=CNV6QPRFT]","2026-01-15T13:45:53.485Z"],["3812974","PFI-823577","PFI","natalie.kolinova@bolt-outsource.eu","Natalie Kolínova","Hello [~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] . \nWe have already contacted the fraud team ([ticket here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-830354]), and they told us to contact you. Could you please look into this together, or is there anyone else we need to contact? \n\nThank you.\n\n","2026-01-15T13:45:56.672Z"],["3812977","RDXENG-4680","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","[~accountid:5d036d01618d7b0bcdf10340] why do we need client side tint when we have {{url_variant}} for different themes?","2026-01-15T13:46:41.709Z"],["3812978","PFI-830354","PFI","natalie.kolinova@bolt-outsource.eu","Natalie Kolínova","Hello [~accountid:5d96f0fd7a6d950c289dfeea] . \nWe have already contacted the commerce billing team ([ticket here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-823577?created=true&isEligibleForUserSurvey=true]), and they told us to contact you. Could you please look into this together, or is there anyone else we need to contact? \nThank you.\n\n","2026-01-15T13:46:45.083Z"],["3812979","BDB-1482","BDB","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] will you be able to support this today? Thank you!","2026-01-15T13:46:45.915Z"],["3812980","RNTL-27071","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","Another metrics migrated:\n\n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_finished_order_ride_distance.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/sum_micromobility_finished_order_ride_distance.yml|smart-link] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_orders_with_subscription_in_finished_state.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_orders_with_subscription_in_finished_state.yml|smart-link] \n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_subscriptions_created.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/rentals/models/metrics/count_micromobility_subscriptions_created.yml|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:47:08.152Z"],["3812984","CLOUDSEC-724","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-15T13:48:11.855Z"],["3812985","MLC-3471","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","*Week 3*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* 90%\n* *Blockers:* none\n* *Status update:* \n** Feature full roll-out [expected 19.01|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09D09ULB9R/p1768469007185549?thread_ts=1767609564.821389&cid=C09D09ULB9R] (Monday).\n* *Next steps*\n** [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] to set up and launch comms.","2026-01-15T13:48:44.153Z"],["3812987","RS-1952","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey, \n\n*Entity*\n\nWe will pursue this assessment for Technology OÜ not Operations OÜ. This is because the certification is best held by the parent company of the group. The activities of Operations overlap with Technology, as well, so the risk is covered. And we will be able to share the result with the customer.\n\n*Timing*\n\nSustainability team has planned assessing Bolt through EcoVadis no earlier than Q2 2026. \n\nInternal context not to be shared with the client: The reason for the timing is that Sustainability team resources are currently focussed on getting our own suppliers assessed through EcoVadis as part of all supplier management being rehauled by the Procurement team. Taking on the self-assessment for Bolt would divert our limited resources away from the more impactful wider effect task. \n\nUnfortunately, it is not possible to start the assessment now to show goodwill and then return to it in Q2 because the assessment input expires in 90 days. Nonetheless, Bolt Technology OÜ does have an assessment ‘on hold’ until we reopen it in Q2. \n\nTo soften the later than hoped assessment completion, I recommend to leverage the sales materials on Sustainability that Dominika Kozub from B4B is putting together to show that Bolt’s sustainability efforts are mature for going through the EcoVadis assessment. \n\nPlease let me know if there is any other way I can support right now. \n\nThanks,\n\nKadi","2026-01-15T13:49:29.216Z"],["3812988","WEB-7803","WEB","vishal.kapoor@bolt.eu","Vishal Kapoor","Translations [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101164|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101164|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:49:46.990Z"],["3812990","MTE-1312","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","If we are adding character count and SMS calculator, we should also take into account if possible – when displaying translations to check the count of SMS for a particular language.\n\n ","2026-01-15T13:49:55.405Z"],["3812993","LSS-55755","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85], thank you very much! \n[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f], please find the signed documents below.\n\nThank you, everyone! ","2026-01-15T13:50:07.763Z"],["3812999","RDXENG-4594","RDXENG","sergei.emelianov@bolt.eu","Sergey Emeliyanov","[~accountid:623340b966b6de0068883243] Thx, additional edge case discovered, opened a PR with fix","2026-01-15T13:51:35.795Z"],["3813000","CLOUDSEC-724","CLOUDSEC","iuliia.laaneots@bolt.eu","Iuliia Laaneots","Confluence page about the usage of the Jira: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/7396851756/Jira+usage+for+task+tracking+activity|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/7396851756/Jira+usage+for+task+tracking+activity|smart-link] \n\n\n\nRules that are created:\n\n* Notify user, if he created the task in the open sprint without epic and label. \n* Send email to me every friday on the list of the tasks in the current sprint that are without epic and/or label.\n* Notify it you are moving the task from the backlog to the current sprint and it is without epic and/or label.","2026-01-15T13:51:36.339Z"],["3813003","CLOUDSEC-724","CLOUDSEC","iuliia.laaneots@bolt.eu","Iuliia Laaneots","Need to find the way to limit the list of Epic that should be in drop down for the user to choose.","2026-01-15T13:52:20.876Z"],["3813005","HS-28881","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Integration error/duplicate ticket, no action needed. ","2026-01-15T13:53:16.418Z"],["3813010","WD-22572","WD","kristiina.vaik@bolt.eu","Kristiina Vaik","Ad Hoc Bank Transaction: EE003 CIT EUR 276 06/08/2025. \n\n* [Journal Sequence Number EE003-2025-8445618|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$17/963$75079319.htmld]\n\n","2026-01-15T13:54:01.476Z"],["3813015","LSS-60637","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","Yes, you can cancel it. Thank you!","2026-01-15T13:54:59.964Z"],["3813018","WEBSD-1470","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ,\n\nI cannot duplicate the table. I see you are using automated numbered list and it is broken the layout adding only 1 as a number.\n\nWe have 2 options here:\n\nRemove the automated numbered list or doing it manually.\n\nPlease let me know.\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.54.23.png|width=654,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.54.23.png\"!","2026-01-15T13:56:21.299Z"],["3813020","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","[~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf] , thanks!\n\nI do have access to the doc “paisios” that you includen in the link.\n\nOn the contrary, the doc “issues with a cancellation fee - customer suport” that you attached is unreadable, I only see lines of coding. ","2026-01-15T13:56:23.402Z"],["3813022","LSS-61364","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343315|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343315|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:56:32.583Z"],["3813023","PFI-833811","PFI","darja.borkina@bolt-outsource.eu","Darja Borkina","!Screenshot_2026-01-15-13-07-34-183_com.bolt.deliverycourier.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_2026-01-15-15-44-50-214_org.telegram.messenger.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T13:56:37.080Z"],["3813024","PFI-833811","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-15T13:56:39.416Z"],["3813028","DRX-26535","DRX","dmitry.lazarev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Lazarev","Linking the PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159225|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/159225|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T13:57:22.132Z"],["3813029","WD-22583","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Task reassigned to Caroline, please ping her to get it approved ASAP as requested.","2026-01-15T13:57:43.187Z"],["3813030","HS-28914","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-15T13:57:50.825Z"],["3813031","DELIVERY-1425","DELIVERY","mihai.burlaciuc@bolt.eu","Mihai Burlăciuc","As per previous comments, in Q1 we will do an A/B test without the possibility of changing the sound back for providers. \n\nWhat we need to decide before Development is ready:\n\n* Global or Localized A/B test: should we consider a Full Global A/B test were the Treatment group represents 50% of all providers or should be more conservative and only run the A/B tests in major cities such as Tallinn, Riga, Warsaw and Bucharest. I’d say that a localized version may be safer while achieving a similar Discovery impact\n\n* Need to sync with Data Analyst team to monitor for the Order Acceptance Rate as we cannot monitor this metric from the Admin-Panel A/B Test experimentation section since this is not available for Providers (Providers don’t have scorecards), thus, this needs to be monitored manually ","2026-01-15T13:57:51.508Z"],["3813035","LSS-60674","LSS","rayko.chakarov@bolt.eu","Rayko Chakarov","Hello again , Aladin sent me back only the T&C , they are marked with yellow this point which are without comments from us, meanwhile everything else is okey for them. \n\nSo can we look over this ? \n\n\n\n[^Bolt_Partner_General_Terms_BG_ENG_BG_09_2025 (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-15T13:59:15.318Z"],["3813037","PFI-830438","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","!CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 14.45.48@2x-20260115-124553 (677ebfe4-098c-4779-9426-d98fe89007da).png|width=50%!\n\nthe commission for dec was about ~4000.\n\nsee that in december the number decreased from 7300 by ~4000.\n\nso they did not owe us 7300, now they do not owe us 3249.\n\nnext month if they do commission ~4000 → they will owe us about ~750 - and would need to pay a commission of 750.\n\n\n\n\n\nHow is invoice sum has got to be -8000 - we paid them a campaign bonus which made invoice sum negative because of commission netting.\n\nBelow is a deeper desceription of commission netting:\n\nHey,\n\nIn Czech Republic we have commission netting.\n\n_Through commission netting, your campaigns/bonuses/compensations are reflected as a discount from your commission, instead of each having their individual invoices. Simply, your commission is reduced in the amount of your campaigns/bonuses/compensations - ensuring a more clear invoicing process, and less invoicing noise._\n\n_For example, previously you would see a commission of 416.91€ and separate bonus lines of 11€ on your invoice, which totaled up to 361.92€. Now, you would only see a single row of commission in the amount of 361.92€, meaning the calculation is already done in the background._\n\n\n\nExample for some [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3318350?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]:\n\nTaking November 2025 example from [Balance history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A3318350%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22month%22%3A11%2C%22year%22%3A2025%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22monthly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1762725600000%2C%22end%22%3A1763330399999%7D%7D]. \n\nCommission that driver had to pay is\n\n{quote}*Commission = expense_cash_commission* + *expense_commission* (48.50 EUR + 190.83 EUR) = €239.33 EUR{quote}\n\nthis commission is ±20% of the amount driver had in Ride fees\n\n{quote}Fees = *earning_in_app_ride_fee* + *earning_cash_ride_fee* (947.70 EUR + 242.50 EUR) = €1,190.20 EUR\n\nCommission % = commission / fees = €239.33 EUR / 1,190.20 EUR = 0.20 = 20%{quote}\n\nthe [invoice|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5649895597?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was issued for 132.94 euro, which is less than 239.33 because we do *commission netting* in Estonia.\n\n{quote}*What is Commission Netting?*\n\n*Commission netting* is a process used to simplify how drivers are invoiced for commissions, especially when there are bonuses, campaigns, or compensations involved.\n\n*Without Netting:*\n\nNormally, a driver would receive separate invoices:\n\nOne for the commission they owe (e.g., 20% of ride fees)\n\nSeparate invoices for any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations they receive\n\n*With Netting (as done in Estonia):*\n\nInstead of issuing multiple invoices, the system *reduces the commission amount* by the total value of any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations the driver earned.\n\nThe driver receives a *single, lower commission invoice* that already accounts for these discounts.{quote}\n\nYou can see discounts earned via cash and app rides in *earning_cash_discount_netted* and *earning_in_app_discount_netted.*\n\nSo we can calculate the final netted commission like this:\n\n{quote}Netted Commission = Commission - *earning_cash_discount_netted - earning_in_app_discount_netted* = €239.33 - 26.70 EUR - 79.70 EUR = €132.93{quote}\n\n132.93 is the same amount you can see on Monthly invoice (take invoice from November from [+here+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients/128179276?tab=partner_invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn])\n\n✨ That’s how you can calculate Commission Netting in Balance history.\n\nNikolay Roll   ","2026-01-15T13:59:58.048Z"],["3813038","FX-3646","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768485585868449]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@sergei.toroshchin>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3646] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T13:59:59.816Z"],["3813039","WEBSD-1470","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","I will add for now only a PDF but we need the proper .docx .\n\nRegards,","2026-01-15T14:00:00.338Z"],["3813040","MLC-1662","MLC","gerardo.gomez@bolt.eu","Gerardo Gomez","week 1 2026Q1\n\n\n* Blockers: none\n* Status update:\n** Included the reservation confirmation landing page to the email. I’m double checking translations and will launch either this week or monday 19th the latest. \n* Next steps:\n** Push emails live. and finito. ","2026-01-15T14:00:13.901Z"],["3813041","PAW-14921","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-15T14:00:25.667Z"],["3813042","LSS-61638","LSS","saiful.islam@bolt.eu","Saiful Islam","[~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5] Floor plan is fine, let’s see if we can get a higher quality image/plan just in case","2026-01-15T14:00:36.800Z"],["3813043","LSS-58436","LSS","martin.barrail@bolt.eu","Martín Nicolas Barrail Baez","Hi [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] tks a lot in advance! Let me go below with both points:\n\n\n* The client mentions that a credit limit was agreed, but does not mention the amount. Could you inform what is the amount? Gs. 20.000.000 (This should be reflected in the terms?)\n* Also, the client mentions that it was agreed that the deadline for invoice payment would be 45 days, instead of the standard 30 days. Could you confirm if this was agreed/authorized from the commercial side? Yes, confirmed, it’s a special condition/exception cause they managed all providers (Actually 60 days with others providers).\n\nTks!\n\n","2026-01-15T14:00:42.384Z"],["3813044","LSS-61439","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343321|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343321|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T14:01:18.849Z"],["3813045","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], thank you very much for your detailed response! I am looking into this and will come back to you shortly 🙂 ","2026-01-15T14:01:31.408Z"],["3813046","SREDESK-7426","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Thanks for the ticket.\n\nI will add the context notes here and come back to the ticket later.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CN6SFK4SW/p1740653775992529|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CN6SFK4SW/p1740653775992529|smart-link] \n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CN6SFK4SW/p1768480736307069|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CN6SFK4SW/p1768480736307069|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:01:46.020Z"],["3813049","LSS-59846","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:5d7b698997d8980d8ead4b01], it is my understanding that Sentry does not require any personal data to operate. Bolt will be in complete control of what data is sent from Bolt applications to Sentry. \n\nCould you please clarify if the described use cases involve sending any personal, confidential or sensitive data from our applications to Sentry? If not, we don’t need to sign any DPA with Sentry. ","2026-01-15T14:02:45.913Z"],["3813051","BDB-1482","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2] \nNew backlit printfile is here: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/raq4inlmn1bcw48atw086/Bolt_Bratislava-airport_wall-backlit_6500x3200mm.pdf?rlkey=012oom55ge4cunc8n8geagifs&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/raq4inlmn1bcw48atw086/Bolt_Bratislava-airport_wall-backlit_6500x3200mm.pdf?rlkey=012oom55ge4cunc8n8geagifs&dl=0|smart-link] \n\nPlease let me know if everything works for you.\nThank you!","2026-01-15T14:03:23.040Z"],["3813052","BPPA-71","BPPA","yuliia.hakkinen@bolt.eu","Yuliia Häkkinen","*Write up on the retention topic:* [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jVAyapzZA34gAoMBrSsGfqCgJTVTEQ48tPAddYYILm4/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jVAyapzZA34gAoMBrSsGfqCgJTVTEQ48tPAddYYILm4/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nNotebook: [https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1281178220169832?o=2472566184436351|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1281178220169832?o=2472566184436351]","2026-01-15T14:03:23.114Z"],["3813055","PFI-833778","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-15T14:04:08.671Z"],["3813056","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768485847437659]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@joel.palgi>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-353] `Add lcm event triggering for car blocks` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T14:04:20.924Z"],["3813057","CEBF-1805","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Check Eligibility button is no longer needed. We use Refresh button instead\n\n!2026-01-15_16-03-47.mp4|width=555,alt=\"2026-01-15_16-03-47.mp4\"!","2026-01-15T14:04:25.309Z"],["3813058","CSDA-291","CSDA","lilian.nguyo@bolt.eu","Lilian Nguyo","Hi [~accountid:5bdc567ddabb7e15b08738ec] , the reason we need this report is to support us with detecting patterns from riders/drivers who are continuously abusing card and business client accounts for ‘Ghost Trips’ and no action is being taken since we do not have a way of picking these under Fraud. We’re losing business clients and spending so much time CS Ops time investigating and refunding these cases whilst the drivers continue to operate as usual. There’s not Fraud feature that has been built yet to detect this and we do not have a feature to equip riders to stop this abuse. We’re looking at this jointly with the COPs safety team to remedy the situation.","2026-01-15T14:04:35.937Z"],["3813060","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a], just a quick follow-up question on some of the data you’ve provided in relation to the driver’s absence - please can you clarify the following entries that do not clearly indicate what document was at issue:\n\n* *21 Dec 2023 – 21 Dec 2023*\n** Reason: Expired document (undefined system document type)\n** Document: Document type ID 2772 (system-defined)\n* *21 Dec 2026 – 10 Mar 2025*\n** Reason: Expired document (undefined system document type)\n** Document: Document type ID 2772 (system-defined)\n\nWe just want to try and avoid follow-up questions by the court on those points - thank you! 🙂 ","2026-01-15T14:05:17.697Z"],["3813061","MLC-2438","MLC","gerardo.gomez@bolt.eu","Gerardo Gomez","w2 2026Q1 updates:\n\n* Blockers: none.\n* Status update:\n** Provided summary of the auto-comms [performance|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hrad0uSJUzlljqjC-b4nw-NDi7wk5y-9RTOQ37xOBhY/edit?gid=1126307330#gid=1126307330] to the Chauffeur team.\n** Created documentation for the Chauffeur team so they can start launching ad hocs by themselves. \n** Created template for Chauffeur Ad hocs.\n** Had training session with Chauffer team member Francisco to guide him on what to do in Braze. \n* Next steps:\n** Nothing so far. Yet they might request help with a Valentines Campaign for this year. ","2026-01-15T14:05:26.633Z"],["3813062","LSS-61642","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","h1. Use in tickets where a user reports having logged in another user’s account \n\n→ This is where the *_new_* phone number owner reports accidentally logging in an existing account. Your investigation should reveal that the account was previously owned by a different user, because the phone number associated to said account used to be owned by that “OG” phone number owner. \n\n{color:#bf2600}*⚠️ Please FILL IN and REMOVE red text before posting this comment! ⚠️*{color}\n\n{color:#bf2600}*NOTE TO PRIVACY:* {color}{color:#bf2600}+*only*+{color}{color:#bf2600} *use the templates below once it has been confirmed that the issue at hand is a phone number recycling case. If this is not 100% confirmed, engage*{color}[{color:#bf2600} {color}|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS][{color:#bf2600}+*#dev-user-auth-support*+{color}|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS]{color:#bf2600} *and ask them to double-check on the case.*{color}\n\n----\n\nHi @{color:#bf2600}NAME{color} {color:#bf2600}[this will be filled in automatically when you get access to the template] {color}- This appears to be a phone recycling case, where the reporting user got access to another user’s Bolt account +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: add account link+{color}+]+ via their new phone number [{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: add phone number+{color}+]+ which was initially associated with the account through another user.\n\nPlease proceed as follows:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nIf there is an outstanding debt from the *original account owner* on the account \n{panel}\n\nPlease reach out to the fraud team, explain the situation, and ask them if the debt can be forgiven in order to archive the account. \n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nMessage the user who reported logging in the account with the recycled phone number +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: clarify if message needs to be sent in-app/same BH thread/by email (based on specific situation) - add link to desired comms channel+{color}+]+:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nThank you for your patience while we investigated your case.\n\nThe Bolt account you are currently using was originally registered by another individual with the phone number ending with {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add 4 last digits of the phone number]*{color} that has since been reassigned to you by your mobile operator. Please note that, in accordance with our policies, we will now archive this account.\n\nOnce this account is archived, you will be able to create a new account using your phone number. To continue using our services, we kindly request that you create a new account. This will give you a secure and personalized experience, without any of the previous account owner’s data linked to it.\n\nTo help protect your account going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication by clicking to _“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_.\n\nIf you have any questions or need assistance during the process, please contact our Support Team.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt Customer Support\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nMessage the original account owner +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: clarify if message needs to be sent in-app/same BH thread/by email (based on specific situation) - add link to desired comms channel+{color}+]+:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nWe hope this message finds you well. \n\nOur records show that your Bolt account associated with the phone number ending with {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add 4 last digits of the phone number]*{color} was recently accessed by another user. This happened because your account was still linked to that phone number, which has since been reassigned by your mobile operator. This can sometimes occur when operators recycle numbers that are no longer in use. Bolt users may log into their account via their phone number. If a user does not enable two-factor authentication (‘2FA’) in the Bolt App nor updates their phone number in the Bolt App after changing it, and their old phone number is later reassigned by the mobile provider to a new customer, that new customer may inadvertently gain access to the existing Bolt account linked to it. This situation may occur if the new customer attempts to register a new account or requests a one-time password (‘OTP’) to a phone number previously owned by an account holder.\n\nPlease note that, in accordance with our terms and conditions available at: [Terms and Conditions|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/] , you must inform us of any update in your contact details, including phone number changes, at the earliest opportunity. This ensures the continued security of your Bolt account and prevents similar situations from occurring. If you’d like to continue using Bolt, please create a new account using your current phone number.\n\nTo protect your data and ensure proper access control, the account in question will now be permanently archived. Once archived, neither you nor the new number owner will be able to access its details, data, or history.\n\nTo help keep your new account secure going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication via_“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_;\n* You never share your passkey, or OTP codes received via SMS with anyone.\n\nIf you notice any suspicious activity in your account in the future, or receive an email about a new device login, please contact our Customer Support Team immediately.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n+*Archive*+ *the disputed account -* +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: add account link+{color}+]+\n{panel}\n\nPlease *archive* the account (do not _delete_ or _schedule for deletion_ ⚠️). If you do not have the necessary access rights to *archive* (in contrast to _delete_) an account, please escalate this case to the CSPC team. This is important for audit trails.","2026-01-15T14:05:27.686Z"],["3813063","C2-461","C2","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] totally agreed on this!","2026-01-15T14:05:50.511Z"],["3813067","LSS-61646","LSS","rita.agnilleri@bolt.eu","Rita Agnilleri","[^Service_Agreement_(Mechanics)_Bolt_Support_Services_IT_MY_PLUS_SRL_20.02.2025.pdf] _(1.07 MB)_\n\n[^Service_Agreement_Regarding_E-Vehicles_Bolt_Support_Services_IT_Myplus_SRL_18.02.2025.pdf] _(830 kB)_","2026-01-15T14:06:28.480Z"],["3813068","LSS-61646","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nRita Agnilleri has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:06:29.914Z"],["3813070","PFI-833722","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","but what is the pdf that you see on the screenshot?","2026-01-15T14:06:38.858Z"],["3813071","WFM-10011","WFM","gaurav.singh@bolt-outsource.eu","Gaurav Singh","Hi Team, Kindly add the below agents in *Assembled* under the team name - *“Belgium & France”* and add the below queues only rest other queues should remove from the agents.\n\n[essowedeou.ana@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:essowedeou.ana@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[yannick.weka@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:yannick.weka@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[adjo.hodji@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:adjo.hodji@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[akou.donyo@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:akou.donyo@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n+*Queues details:-*+\n01 RH_France_T1,\n01 RH_France_T1_Low/Moderate,\n01 RH_Belgium_T1,\n01 RH_Belgium_T1_Low/Moderate\n\n","2026-01-15T14:07:18.334Z"],["3813072","FRAUDOPS-1014","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","h2. Refunds\n\nSo, we also have actions that read the profilings. For BAD_PAYMENT profiling, it seems we don’t have a direct refund action. ✅ \n\nHOWEVER, noticed that we have another profiling called *fraud_driver_failed_payment* that does refunds based on the flag is_failed_payment → [https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/blob/main/order_fraud/get_order_fraud_driver_failed_payment.sql|https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/blob/main/order_fraud/get_order_fraud_driver_failed_payment.sql]  This profiling will have the same issue for failed payment vs actual uncovered cases where we make.\n\nHENCE: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUDOPS-1122|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUDOPS-1122|smart-link] \n\nOverall, for profilings, we make auto-refunds for 6 strategies.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.32.54.png|width=520,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.32.54.png\"!\n\nInterestingly, we seem to do a lot of actions for cases that do not fall under any issue: \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.41.44.png|width=816,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.41.44.png\"!\n\n\n*approx 23K eur of refunds on average monthly:* \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.52.37.png|width=607,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 13.52.37.png\"!\n\nIn general, for profilings this means: \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.49.12.png|width=1254,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 14.49.12.png\"!\n\nSo luckily we can say that majority of profilings end up refunding actual problematic sums. ","2026-01-15T14:07:51.267Z"],["3813074","PFI-832350","PFI","andrea.caceres@bolt-outsource.eu","Andrea Luján Chávez Cáceres","Thanks for the answer, team.","2026-01-15T14:08:17.591Z"],["3813075","DELIVERY-781","DELIVERY","tudor.suruceanu@bolt.eu","Tudor Suruceanu","26W03: Fixed support for Vehicle Types in Batch Routing.\n\nThe epic is ready for A/B testing.","2026-01-15T14:08:20.435Z"],["3813076","RDXENG-4680","RDXENG","anastasiya.sviatokha@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Sviatokha","[~accountid:60fbd5ec9f975e0069eec7a1] Icons should have {{content/secondary}} color in both light and dark modes, not only in dark mode. I apply tint to both icons","2026-01-15T14:08:34.434Z"],["3813077","LSS-57487","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hey [~accountid:712020:5863bdf0-2fd8-4e92-aa72-f46da22e78cc] [~accountid:712020:4270191e-b006-439e-a800-5b8e06cf2c60] please confirm if there are currently any further details on this initiative, and whether this was discussed and approved by the Business development team cc [~accountid:622852f26a4c4c0070b16e66] [~accountid:712020:dcaeeaea-b979-4efa-93e7-594a518b6eb5] \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:c9e0b423-51d9-40ce-a9ef-b4c651b92973] ","2026-01-15T14:08:34.608Z"],["3813078","L10N-27923","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.422Z"],["3813079","L10N-27927","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.649Z"],["3813080","L10N-27932","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.633Z"],["3813081","L10N-27926","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.663Z"],["3813082","L10N-27922","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.684Z"],["3813083","L10N-27920","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.749Z"],["3813084","L10N-27928","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.767Z"],["3813085","L10N-27918","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.780Z"],["3813086","L10N-27917","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.796Z"],["3813087","L10N-27924","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.797Z"],["3813088","L10N-27934","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.815Z"],["3813089","L10N-27925","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.847Z"],["3813090","L10N-27930","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.893Z"],["3813091","L10N-27919","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.936Z"],["3813092","L10N-27931","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:36.914Z"],["3813093","L10N-27929","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:37.056Z"],["3813094","L10N-27933","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:37.117Z"],["3813095","L10N-27921","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:37.331Z"],["3813096","L10N-27935","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:37.569Z"],["3813097","L10N-27916","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:39.619Z"],["3813098","L10N-27914","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:41.580Z"],["3813099","L10N-27911","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:41.759Z"],["3813100","L10N-27908","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:41.753Z"],["3813101","L10N-27912","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:41.818Z"],["3813102","L10N-27915","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:41.839Z"],["3813103","L10N-27913","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:41.865Z"],["3813104","L10N-27905","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.006Z"],["3813105","L10N-27900","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.147Z"],["3813106","L10N-27903","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.407Z"],["3813107","L10N-27910","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.418Z"],["3813108","L10N-27909","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.421Z"],["3813109","L10N-27907","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.540Z"],["3813110","L10N-27904","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.616Z"],["3813111","L10N-27901","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.661Z"],["3813112","L10N-27906","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.654Z"],["3813113","L10N-27902","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:08:42.844Z"],["3813115","WD-22581","WD","arina.vorozhtsova@bolt.eu","Arina Vorozhtsova","Hey hey, \nIn the position P013460, where you are trying to move Rahul, there is no open job requisition. \nPlease create it first, and then you will be able to promote. \n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.56.02.png|width=642,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 15.56.02.png\"!","2026-01-15T14:09:44.872Z"],["3813116","LSS-61647","LSS","yolandah.chinyani@bolt.eu","Yolandah Chido Chinyani","[^BOLT Technology_Daily-21-Nov-2023.pdf] _(294 kB)_","2026-01-15T14:09:44.942Z"],["3813118","LSS-61647","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nYolandah Chido Chinyani has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:09:48.295Z"],["3813119","CSDT-956","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR Approved, Marts re-generated, in review","2026-01-15T14:10:02.943Z"],["3813120","CSDT-950","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","PR Approved, Marts re-generated, in review","2026-01-15T14:10:10.352Z"],["3813121","PFI-833812","PFI","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","[^Arts Club - December report.xlsx]\n\n[^GB1125-29177121.pdf]\n\n[^GB6526-40.pdf]","2026-01-15T14:10:12.942Z"],["3813122","PFI-833812","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T14:10:15.437Z"],["3813123","LSS-59846","LSS","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","> Sentry does not require any personal data to operate.\n\nCorrect.\n\n> Bolt will be in complete control of what data is sent from Bolt applications to Sentry.\n\nCorrect.\n\nHowever, I would like to emphasise that Sentry will be part of an application that handles potentially sensitive information. It’s not required to submit any PII to Sentry; however, due to a developer mistake or mishandling of PII, some information may end up in Sentry.\n\nI have taken the necessary precautions to partially mitigate this situation, even if such a risk materialises, as[ Sentry|https://sentry.io/trust/privacy/]’s[ provided PII Scrubbing tools|https://sentry.io/trust/privacy/] can hide the PII information from end users.\n\n!image-20260115-140819.png|width=1482,height=444,alt=\"image-20260115-140819.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-15T14:10:27.981Z"],["3813125","LSS-61642","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","h1. Use in tickets where a user reports activity on their account that they do not recognise → someone else is logged in and used the “OG account owner” 's account \n\n→ This is where the OG account owner (and OG phone number owner) reports that there’s been activity on their account that they do not recognise. The activity in question (rides) can be traced back to a device that logged in via the phone number (originally) associated with the account, where it is clear that the _new_ phone number owner logged in the account, because the phone number associated to said account used to be owned by the “OG” account owner.\n\nNote: this situation can be reported a) via one same account (where both the OG and new phone number owner are still logged in) OR b) via two different accounts, where the OG phone number owner does not have access to the account anymore but their payment method is still linked to that account → the OG phone number owner then creates a *new* account to report the issue concerning their *old* account.\n\n{color:#bf2600}*⚠️ Please FILL IN and REMOVE red text before posting this comment! ⚠️*{color}\n\n{color:#bf2600}*NOTE TO PRIVACY:* {color}{color:#bf2600}+*only*+{color}{color:#bf2600} *use the templates below once it has been confirmed that the issue at hand is a phone number recycling case. If this is not 100% confirmed, engage*{color}[{color:#bf2600} +*#dev-user-auth-support*+{color}|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS]{color:#bf2600} *and ask them to double-check on the case.*{color}\n\n----\n\nHi @{color:#bf2600}NAME{color} {color:#bf2600}[this will be filled in automatically when you get access to the template]{color} - This appears to be a phone recycling case, where a new user got access to the reporting user’s Bolt account +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: add account link+{color}+]+ via their old phone number [{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: add phone number+{color}+]+.\n\nPlease proceed as follows:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n# Message the reporting user +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: clarify if message needs to be sent in-app/same BH thread/by email (based on specific situation) - add link to desired comms channel+{color}+]+:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nThank you for your patience while we investigated your case.\n\nOur records show that your Bolt account associated with the phone number ending with {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add 4 last digits of the phone number]*{color} was recently accessed by another user. This happened because your old account was still linked to that phone number, which has since been reassigned by your mobile operator. This can sometimes occur when operators recycle numbers that are no longer in use. Bolt users may log into their account via their phone number. If a user does not enable two-factor authentication (‘2FA’) in the Bolt App nor updates their phone number in the Bolt App after changing it, and their old phone number is later reassigned by the mobile provider to a new customer, that new customer may inadvertently gain access to the existing Bolt account linked to it. This situation may occur if the new customer attempts to register a new account or requests a one-time password (‘OTP’) to a phone number previously owned by an account holder.\n\nPlease note that, in accordance with our terms and conditions available at: [Terms and Conditions|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/] , you must inform us of any update in your contact details, including phone number changes, at the earliest opportunity. This ensures the continued security of your Bolt account and prevents similar situations from occurring. If you’d like to continue using Bolt, please create a new account using your current phone number.\n\n{color:#ff5630}*IF ACCOUNT ARCHIVAL NEEDED:* {color} To protect your data and ensure proper access control, the account in question will now be permanently archived. Once archived, neither you nor the new number owner will be able to access its details, data, or history.\n\n{color:#ff5630}*IF ACCOUNT SAFE TO USE:* {color}We confirm that your account is now secure and safe to use. The person who briefly gained access through your old phone number has been logged out by our team, and all active sessions linked to that number have been terminated. Your updated phone number is now correctly linked to your account, ensuring that only you can receive verification codes or log in. Our system shows no signs of any further unauthorised activity.\n\nTo help keep your {color:#bf2600}*new [Privacy*{color}{color:#bf2600}: remove “new” if account doesn’t need to be archived]{color} account secure going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication via_“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_;\n* You never share your passkey, or OTP codes received via SMS with anyone.\n\nIf you notice any suspicious activity in your account in the future, or receive an email about a new device login, please contact our Customer Support Team immediately.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt Customer Support\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n{color:#4c9aff}*NOTE TO PRIVACY*{color}{color:#bf2600}*: INCLUDE THIS ONLY IF ACCOUNT ARCHIVAL NEEDED*{color}\n\n*2. Message* the user who logged in the account with the recycled phone number +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: clarify if message needs to be sent in-app/same BH thread/by email (based on specific situation) - add link to desired comms channel+{color}+]+:\n{panel}\n\nDear {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add user’s name]*{color},\n\nWe hope this message finds you well. \n\nThe Bolt account you are currently using was originally registered by another individual with the phone number ending with {color:#ff5630}*[CS: add 4 last digits of the phone number]*{color}  that has since been reassigned to you by your mobile operator. Please note that, in accordance with our policies, we will now archive this account.\n\n Once this account is archived, you will be able to create a new account using your phone number. To continue using our services, we kindly request that you create a new account. This will give you a secure and personalized experience, without any of the previous account owner’s data linked to it.\n\nTo help protect your account going forward, please ensure that:\n\n* Your phone number linked to the account is up to date;\n* Your email address linked to the account is verified; and\n* You enable multi-factor authentication by clicking to _“My account > Log in and security > Turn on Two-Step Verification”_.\n\nIf you have any questions or need assistance during the process, please contact our Support Team.\n\nBest regards,\n\nBolt\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*3.* +*Archive*+ *the disputed account -* +[+{color:#ff5630}+*Privacy*+{color}{color:#ff5630}+: add disputed account link+{color}+]+\n{panel}\n\nPlease *archive* the account (do not _delete_ / _schedule for deletion_ ⚠️). If you do not have the necessary access rights to *archive* (in contrast to _delete_) an account, please escalate this case to the CSPC team. This is important for audit trails.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n4. If the user requests a refund \n{panel}\n\nPlease note that the Privacy team does not advise on refund requests stemming from phone number recycling cases. If the reporting user requests a refund for rides taken by individual who logged in their account, please discuss with your Team Lead on this matter.","2026-01-15T14:10:50.238Z"],["3813127","SREDESK-7427","SREDESK","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","From the k8s github runner pod, the DNS of MySQL/TiDB is resolvable:\n\n{noformat}Testing DNS resolution for ti-incentives-datalake.sqldb.internal\n✓ DNS resolution successful\nResult: 172.30.2.82     ti-incentives-datalake.sqldb.internal\nResolved IP: 172.30.2.82\n\nTesting DNS resolution for weu-debezium.sqldb.internal\n✓ DNS resolution successful\nResult: 172.30.4.4      weu-debezium.sqldb.internal\nResolved IP: 172.30.4.4{noformat}\n\n","2026-01-15T14:11:16.025Z"],["3813128","LSS-61534","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] 👋 \nQuick question - have you already completed the Cognito assessment for this case?\n\nFrom what I can see on our side, the order was placed from a device that’s been linked to the account for a long time, so this looks more like an old device not being logged out of or a disputed ride rather than an account takeover.\nI can also see CS logged the user out of all devices and advised enabling 2FA, so mitigation is already in place.\n\nLet me know once you’ve confirmed the Cognito step and I’ll close this from Privacy. Thanks!","2026-01-15T14:11:21.394Z"],["3813129","PFI-831423","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\ni do not see any bonus in that period.\n\nWe do not know why there is no bonus - might have not applied to the user.\n\nSince we do not work with campaign bonuses - I can’t help you with it 😞\n\nonly point of contact would be campaign team to find out if the campaign even applied and if they see any logs, traces or anything.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe only thing I see is this campaign bonus - but it is for 04.01.2026: \n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 16.10.12@2x-20260115-141015.png|width=1106,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 16.10.12@2x-20260115-141015.png\"!\n\n\n\nNot much we can help with.","2026-01-15T14:11:30.072Z"],["3813130","RDXENG-4680","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","{quote}I apply tint to both icons{quote}\n\nBut why? can’t we ask BE to send the correct icons with {{content/secondary}}?","2026-01-15T14:11:35.942Z"],["3813131","PAW-14907","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-jenkins, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-15T14:12:06.487Z"],["3813132","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Some existing product examples from retail.\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"cd24cb60-ad25-4fcc-b585-028180f23152\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"link\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"https://www.rivbike.com/products/sks-fender-mudflap-long-each\"}},{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Link\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"https://artedimano.com/shop_view/?idx=600\"}},{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":306,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-140048.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-140048.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":140,\"width\":200}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":306,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-140156.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-140156.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":140,\"width\":200}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":226,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-140548.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-140548.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":667,\"width\":667}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":177,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-140652.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-140652.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":667,\"width\":667}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":221,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-140339.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-140339.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":225,\"width\":225}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":145,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-140829.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-140829.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":225,\"width\":225}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":122,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260115-141119.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260115-141119.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":675,\"width\":1200}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-15T14:12:14.659Z"],["3813133","PIF-3284","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-15T14:12:14.441Z"],["3813137","LSS-61642","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] just adding you for visibility - [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] is currently facing difficulties with accessing our team’s canned responses so I am sharing the content with him here for convenience so that he can already push his own cases forward. \n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] for any questions on the below templates or on phone number incidents handling, feel free to raise them here or at the office! ","2026-01-15T14:13:11.791Z"],["3813140","LSS-61494","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] Can you please update us here on the progress?","2026-01-15T14:13:35.703Z"],["3813141","LSS-58216","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","Saving changes that went back to Solidgate","2026-01-15T14:13:43.338Z"],["3813142","LSS-58216","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","[^MSA-2026-01-15-Solidgate_Bolt--Bolt-responses.docx]\n\n","2026-01-15T14:13:54.862Z"],["3813143","PFI-809183","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi,\n\nplease raise with technical team regarding incorrect info in the app.","2026-01-15T14:14:05.075Z"],["3813144","BP-13446","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Test cases:\n\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T235|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T235]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T236|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T236]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T237|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T237]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T238|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T238]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T239|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T239]\n# [https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T240|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/BP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/BP-T240]","2026-01-15T14:14:08.367Z"],["3813145","PFI-816693","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hey,\n\nIn France we have commission netting.\n\n_Through commission netting, your campaigns/bonuses/compensations are reflected as a discount from your commission, instead of each having their individual invoices. Simply, your commission is reduced in the amount of your campaigns/bonuses/compensations - ensuring a more clear invoicing process, and less invoicing noise._\n\n_For example, previously you would see a commission of 416.91€ and separate bonus lines of 11€ on your invoice, which totaled up to 361.92€. Now, you would only see a single row of commission in the amount of 361.92€, meaning the calculation is already done in the background._\n\n\n\nExample for some [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3318350?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]:\n\nTaking November 2025 example from [Balance history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A3318350%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22month%22%3A11%2C%22year%22%3A2025%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22monthly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1762725600000%2C%22end%22%3A1763330399999%7D%7D]. \n\nCommission that driver had to pay is\n\n{quote}*Commission = expense_cash_commission* + *expense_commission* (48.50 EUR + 190.83 EUR) = €239.33 EUR{quote}\n\nthis commission is ±20% of the amount driver had in Ride fees\n\n{quote}Fees = *earning_in_app_ride_fee* + *earning_cash_ride_fee* (947.70 EUR + 242.50 EUR) = €1,190.20 EUR\n\nCommission % = commission / fees = €239.33 EUR / 1,190.20 EUR = 0.20 = 20%{quote}\n\nthe [invoice|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5649895597?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was issued for 132.94 euro, which is less than 239.33 because we do *commission netting* in Estonia.\n\n{quote}*What is Commission Netting?*\n\n*Commission netting* is a process used to simplify how drivers are invoiced for commissions, especially when there are bonuses, campaigns, or compensations involved.\n\n*Without Netting:*\n\nNormally, a driver would receive separate invoices:\n\nOne for the commission they owe (e.g., 20% of ride fees)\n\nSeparate invoices for any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations they receive\n\n*With Netting (as done in Estonia):*\n\nInstead of issuing multiple invoices, the system *reduces the commission amount* by the total value of any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations the driver earned.\n\nThe driver receives a *single, lower commission invoice* that already accounts for these discounts.{quote}\n\nYou can see discounts earned via cash and app rides in *earning_cash_discount_netted* and *earning_in_app_discount_netted.*\n\nSo we can calculate the final netted commission like this:\n\n{quote}Netted Commission = Commission - *earning_cash_discount_netted - earning_in_app_discount_netted* = €239.33 - 26.70 EUR - 79.70 EUR = €132.93{quote}\n\n132.93 is the same amount you can see on Monthly invoice (take invoice from November from [+here+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients/128179276?tab=partner_invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn])\n\n✨ That’s how you can calculate Commission Netting in Balance history.\n\nNikolay Roll   ","2026-01-15T14:14:32.070Z"],["3813146","LSS-56917","LSS","katrin.anier@bolt.eu","Katrin Anier","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] \nI hope you saw the comment in the agreement left by Tatjana. As mentioned there, the question under point 3.3 should be addressed with the Billing department, as this is not something the Finance team can approve. Finance does not generate account statements and is therefore unable to adjust or change the currency rates set in the system. ","2026-01-15T14:14:48.842Z"],["3813147","DELIVERY-1164","DELIVERY","mohamed.abdel-kader@bolt.eu","Mohamed Abdelkader","Adjusted name to “new user orders”","2026-01-15T14:14:51.589Z"],["3813149","PFI-833813","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T14:15:04.107Z"],["3813150","SRED-1073","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, added ' as valid character in name.","2026-01-15T14:15:14.576Z"],["3813152","PFI-833814","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^B00M5WU8T.pdf]","2026-01-15T14:16:16.057Z"],["3813153","PFI-826248","PFI","uche.ohaji@bolt-outsource.eu","Uche Ohaji","Hi Team, \n\nDriver’s payment is yet to reflect since 21st of December, 2025. \n\nPlease review.","2026-01-15T14:17:13.007Z"],["3813154","LSS-61619","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], thanks for the quick reply! \n\nI agree with your wording that you have proposed above. \n\nHowever before sending this out - given that the rider is also threatening to take this public - [~accountid:60bd1baef650540069f28c36] is there any other consideration you believe we should take or can we proceed with sending this communication and keep you in the loop with any updates / social media posts?\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-15T14:17:26.417Z"],["3813155","HS-28972","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hi, the document has been sent to your People Advisor for signing. Once signed, a copy will reach your *personal* email. Let me know in case of any questions.\n\n\n\nFeel better soon!","2026-01-15T14:17:47.868Z"],["3813156","OKAI-179","OKAI","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","Scooters I propose that we ask Berlin to send to HQ:\n\n[613-619|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/list/edit/germany/560161?tab=details] - In WH\n[942-992|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-micromobility/vehicles/list/edit/germany/563453?tab=details] - Operational\n\nThese scooters have recently triggered E478 and no other errors.","2026-01-15T14:17:58.116Z"],["3813157","WFM-10004","WFM","valeria.tiilikainen@bolt.eu","Valeria Tiilikainen","Hello [~accountid:712020:d68d8892-e046-430d-b677-2436ad1bdae7]\r\nDone, agent was unassigned from ZA T1 queue (/)","2026-01-15T14:18:00.665Z"],["3813158","PFI-820503","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hey,\n\nIn Romania we have commission netting.\n\n_Through commission netting, your campaigns/bonuses/compensations are reflected as a discount from your commission, instead of each having their individual invoices. Simply, your commission is reduced in the amount of your campaigns/bonuses/compensations - ensuring a more clear invoicing process, and less invoicing noise._\n\n_For example, previously you would see a commission of 416.91€ and separate bonus lines of 11€ on your invoice, which totaled up to 361.92€. Now, you would only see a single row of commission in the amount of 361.92€, meaning the calculation is already done in the background._\n\n\n\nExample for some [Driver|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3318350?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]:\n\nTaking November 2025 example from [Balance history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A3318350%2C%22type%22%3A%22Driver%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22month%22%3A11%2C%22year%22%3A2025%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22monthly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1762725600000%2C%22end%22%3A1763330399999%7D%7D]. \n\nCommission that driver had to pay is\n\n{quote}*Commission = expense_cash_commission* + *expense_commission* (48.50 EUR + 190.83 EUR) = €239.33 EUR{quote}\n\nthis commission is ±20% of the amount driver had in Ride fees\n\n{quote}Fees = *earning_in_app_ride_fee* + *earning_cash_ride_fee* (947.70 EUR + 242.50 EUR) = €1,190.20 EUR\n\nCommission % = commission / fees = €239.33 EUR / 1,190.20 EUR = 0.20 = 20%{quote}\n\nthe [invoice|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5649895597?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] was issued for 132.94 euro, which is less than 239.33 because we do *commission netting* in Estonia.\n\n{quote}*What is Commission Netting?*\n\n*Commission netting* is a process used to simplify how drivers are invoiced for commissions, especially when there are bonuses, campaigns, or compensations involved.\n\n*Without Netting:*\n\nNormally, a driver would receive separate invoices:\n\nOne for the commission they owe (e.g., 20% of ride fees)\n\nSeparate invoices for any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations they receive\n\n*With Netting (as done in Estonia):*\n\nInstead of issuing multiple invoices, the system *reduces the commission amount* by the total value of any bonuses, campaigns, or compensations the driver earned.\n\nThe driver receives a *single, lower commission invoice* that already accounts for these discounts.{quote}\n\nYou can see discounts earned via cash and app rides in *earning_cash_discount_netted* and *earning_in_app_discount_netted.*\n\nSo we can calculate the final netted commission like this:\n\n{quote}Netted Commission = Commission - *earning_cash_discount_netted - earning_in_app_discount_netted* = €239.33 - 26.70 EUR - 79.70 EUR = €132.93{quote}\n\n132.93 is the same amount you can see on Monthly invoice (take invoice from November from [+here+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients/128179276?tab=partner_invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn])\n\n✨ That’s how you can calculate Commission Netting in Balance history.\n\nNikolay Roll   \n\n","2026-01-15T14:18:15.104Z"],["3813159","LSS-61486","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","*BACKGROUND*\n\nOn 27 December 2025, [a user contacted Bolt in-app|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/712713162] stating that when attempting to create a Bolt account, they were automatically logged into another person’s existing account. The user explicitly clarified that they are *not the original account holder* and that they have been assigned a phone number previously used by someone else.\n\nThe user’s stated intention throughout the conversation was to create their own account, not to access or use the existing one.\n\nThis incident was reported in Germany and concerns a Scooter Rider account.\n\n*FINDINGS*\n\nAdmin logs and Beehive correspondence indicate a *phone number recycling scenario*:\n\n* The phone number used by the reporting user had previously been linked to an existing Bolt account belonging to a different individual (original account holder).\n* The reporting user gained access to the existing account due to the phone number being reassigned by the mobile operator while still linked to the Bolt account.\n* Login session data confirms two distinct devices:\n** Original account holder: iPhone 12 (historical usage).\n** New phone number holder: iPhone 16e (new device).\n* No indicators of credential compromise, phishing, or deliberate account takeover were identified.\n* The reporting user immediately contacted CS upon noticing access to another person’s account and did not attempt to use the account.\n\n*ACTIONS TAKEN*\n\n* CS followed the updated KB for “access to someone else’s account due to phone number recycling”.\n* Both the new phone number holder and the original account holder were contacted using the appropriate comms templates.\n* The original account holder was notified and instructed to update their contact details.\n* The affected account was archived to prevent any further access.\n* The reporting user was instructed to create a new account using their current phone number.\n* No further activity has been observed on the archived account.\n\n*THOUGHTS*\n\nThis is a *straightforward phone number recycling case*, not a malicious account takeover or voluntary account sharing scenario. Access occurred due to telecom number reassignment, and the reporting user acted promptly and transparently.\n\nThere is no evidence of:\n\n* third-party compromise,\n* misuse of Bolt systems,\n* intentional access or use of another user’s personal data beyond initial login.\n\nWhile personal data was briefly exposed to the new phone number holder, the incident was contained quickly and handled in line with the KB and mitigation guidance.","2026-01-15T14:18:26.149Z"],["3813160","PFI-824140","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Billing does not handle price reviews → please contact the local IH cs team to see if they can review this manually or compensate the driver if necessary. ","2026-01-15T14:18:43.179Z"],["3813161","PFI-824140","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T14:18:50.014Z"],["3813162","CEBF-1832","CEBF","oleg.demkiv@bolt.eu","Oleh Demkiv","[~accountid:712020:fc274657-f7b5-4366-9f2d-5ec68865cf48] I aligned with business [*here*|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03MNK9JWSV/p1768469100524489]\n\nSolution:\n\n{quote}*Proposed solution*\n\n* Create ELC Intro & Study *on activation / reactivation regardless of Parent Account owner*\n* If no AM is assigned yet, the opportunity is created without an AM and reassigned once segmentation runs\n* *Increase SLA from 14 to 21 days* to account for the segmentation delay (instead of recalculating SLA on AM assignment){quote}","2026-01-15T14:18:50.359Z"],["3813166","RDXENG-4680","RDXENG","anastasiya.sviatokha@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Sviatokha","[~accountid:60fbd5ec9f975e0069eec7a1] We could ask BE. Honestly, I just did it together with other SR review design review changes, didn’t think about asking BE back then.","2026-01-15T14:20:22.916Z"],["3813167","GRWA-1505","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6399a588abc764d2ca5f3706/pages/7394263339/Cohort+Plus-Ready+Frequency+Reporting+Migration+to+Fact+Mart|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6399a588abc764d2ca5f3706/pages/7394263339/Cohort+Plus-Ready+Frequency+Reporting+Migration+to+Fact+Mart|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:20:30.669Z"],["3813168","LSS-61512","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","what contract you have with Medicina del lavoro?\n\nthanks\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-15T14:20:35.032Z"],["3813171","CSXRT-192","CSXRT","tanya.kravchuk@bolt.eu","Tanya Kravchuk","Clarified all KPIs here [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C037F41MPSR/p1767777378541929|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C037F41MPSR/p1767777378541929|smart-link] , so we have the main dashboard to use [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/28142?Time+Grain=Month&Time+Period=3+month+ago+for+3+month&Geography+Grain=Global&Geography+Value=|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/28142?Time+Grain=Month&Time+Period=3+month+ago+for+3+month&Geography+Grain=Global&Geography+Value=]","2026-01-15T14:21:24.506Z"],["3813173","GRWA-1496","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Market share issues has been \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 16.21.38.png|width=789,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 16.21.38.png\"!\n\n for cities.","2026-01-15T14:21:46.417Z"],["3813174","HS-28996","HS","anita.kasprzyk@bolt.eu","Anita Kasprzyk","!image (10).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T14:21:50.754Z"],["3813175","LSS-61292","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026: Reviewed LOI was shared with stakeholders in slack channel [HERE|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08PTDELW6L/p1768486658528869] where it was asked for them to review it once more before  [~accountid:60feb11575ad960069b6163f] send it to Cognizant for approval. ","2026-01-15T14:21:51.083Z"],["3813178","LSS-58389","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","*Safety gate account information for the company phone:*\n\nFirst name: Bolt\n\nLast name: Bolt\n\nEmail address: [registry.notices@bolt.eu|mailto:registry.notices@bolt.eu]\n\nusername: *n00ldgg9*\n\npassword*: SafetyGateAccount1.1*\n\n*Device name: Bolt*\n\n*4 digit pin code: 5918 (Company phone linked and logged in in the app)*","2026-01-15T14:22:45.974Z"],["3813179","LSS-61617","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] , the details have now been filled\n\n[^index_delayed_ui (1e93a2e3-dfc1-495f-b555-0f36e144d6a1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T14:22:48.345Z"],["3813180","L10N-28160","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-281