 where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28155](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28155)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-15T14:24:01.994Z"],["3813196","PAW-14923","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160882\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 14:24:50 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T14:24:50.533Z"],["3813197","PFI-833818","PFI","monica.acevedo@bolt.eu","Mónica Acevedo","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 11.23.56 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T14:24:52.273Z"],["3813198","RNTL-30443","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/looker-rental/pull/2109|https://github.com/bolteu/looker-rental/pull/2109|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:24:57.269Z"],["3813199","CSXRT-194","CSXRT","tanya.kravchuk@bolt.eu","Tanya Kravchuk","Schedule a call with the Head of Drive, Andrei, on the {{2026-01-21}} to discuss the new template and receive feedback. ","2026-01-15T14:25:19.404Z"],["3813203","HS-28148","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey, I have made the change in Workday!\n\nYou now have 26 days of annual leave from 2026 and onwards. Additionally, I also added 3 days of annual leave to 2025 in retrospect, as you had reached seniority already when you joined Bolt in July. These are reflected in your carryover balance.\n\nLet me know in case of additional questions, \n\nBest!","2026-01-15T14:25:58.098Z"],["3813204","PFI-826753","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! What is the amount of the adjustment and when was it applied? ","2026-01-15T14:25:59.081Z"],["3813205","WAVE-233","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","First result in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7403144101/Onboarding+to+Sentry|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7403144101/Onboarding+to+Sentry|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:26:06.645Z"],["3813206","LSS-59846","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","Thanks for clarifying! In this case, there is no need for separate DPA.","2026-01-15T14:26:28.360Z"],["3813207","WFM-9984","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! I will close this ticket, if anything else is needed please let me know; Wish you a great day!","2026-01-15T14:26:46.293Z"],["3813209","DISC-3752","DISC","lucas.colucci@bolt.eu","Lucas Rodrigues Colucci","[~accountid:61ddb0e268926d0068b689c5] I guess that is fine 🙂 ","2026-01-15T14:27:29.362Z"],["3813210","HS-28790","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey! Pinging again just in case, do you have the possibility to submit proof of employment from Ukraine as well?\n\nBest!","2026-01-15T14:27:31.774Z"],["3813213","DRX-28209","DRX","ajinkya.deshmukh@bolt.eu","Ajinkya Suhas Deshmukh","Test Scenarios - [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VQ9YUuRNF5nhMGRJxPNXZE8ifCDCdTFktKQ5dAGIEIM/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VQ9YUuRNF5nhMGRJxPNXZE8ifCDCdTFktKQ5dAGIEIM/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:28:19.961Z"],["3813214","PAW-14690","PAW","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-15T14:29:25.262Z"],["3813215","PAW-14690","PAW","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. Build: http://mock-jenkins/queue/12345","2026-01-15T14:29:29.512Z"],["3813216","WEB-9598","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","Feedback covered [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \n\nDesign file [here|https://www.figma.com/design/EA6o5cVzolpDBewnCZ3BOd/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Supply?node-id=1761-16078&t=UURoD686Tg97ua6t-1].\n\nMedia for the page [here|https://drive.google.com/open?id=1WogwGm5QhvO8g3s0G2oHKMIpEGSXhyNs&usp=drive_fs]","2026-01-15T14:29:45.055Z"],["3813218","PFI-812939","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","I see that the ticket was resolved.\n\nclosing it.","2026-01-15T14:30:06.003Z"],["3813220","LSS-61648","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nJuozas Masteika has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:31:16.269Z"],["3813221","PFI-808333","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi,\n\nwe no longer support weekly reports - so they were depricated for incorrect numbers.\n\ndrivers/fleet owners should use monthly commission invoices for paying commissions.","2026-01-15T14:31:17.770Z"],["3813222","LSS-61648","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T14:31:32.106Z"],["3813223","LSS-61646","LSS","rita.agnilleri@bolt.eu","Rita Agnilleri","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] the agreements termination conditions are more longer than 15 days, below the terms, please double check: \n \n*Mechanic and WH agreement:* \npoint 6.7 \nThe Company is entitled to terminate\nthis Agreement at any time by giving 90\n(ninety) days' prior notice to the\nContractor.\nAt the moment we are keeping 50 operational vehicles on the street, so the \n\npoint 6.3  could be mentioned:\nThe Company may reduce the Services\nat any time, at its sole discretion, by\ngiving the Contractor a 15 (fifteen) days'\nprior notice (the \"Reduced Service\nPeriod\") and terminate the Reduced\nService Period by giving to the\nContractor a 15 (fifteen) days' prior\nnotice.\n\n*3PL service logistics:*\n9.5 Bolt may terminate this Agreement for convenience at any time without liability by notifying the Contractor sixty\n(60) days in advance or without notice should Bolt lose the rights to operate the rental services .\n\n\nthanks in advance\n","2026-01-15T14:31:33.645Z"],["3813224","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hey [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a], apologies for the second message, but upon collating the CSVs into one document, I have noticed that they only cover the driver’s earnings for the months April-July 2024. We have been asked to show the driver’s earnings from *6 February 2024 - 4 August 2024*. Please could you provide the same data for the months February, March, and August?","2026-01-15T14:31:39.100Z"],["3813225","PAW-14925","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-15T14:31:45.920Z"],["3813226","LSS-61648","LSS","juozas.masteika@bolt.eu","Juozas Masteika","[^VKI 2026-01-15 raštas UAB „Bolt Services LT“.docx.docx.pdf]\n\nUploading official request","2026-01-15T14:31:54.110Z"],["3813227","HS-28997","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-15T14:31:56.836Z"],["3813228","HS-28993","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-15T14:32:15.590Z"],["3813230","LSS-60122","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","HI [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7], \n\nPlease see feedback from landlord below and also updated in the agreement draft. \n\nLandlord: _early termination of the lease requires the participation of both parties. In other words, termination does not occur automatically - the parties must sign an additional termination agreement. The key condition for such termination is that, as of the termination date, there are no outstanding debts or unpaid obligations_.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1QEJDiMvc8AV4R-QSeGrw9qQx05USS6/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1QEJDiMvc8AV4R-QSeGrw9qQx05USS6/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:33:18.384Z"],["3813231","LSS-61649","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:33:22.144Z"],["3813233","PFI-811574","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Hey [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \nyes, but the client in the end considered the March invoice alone…\nBut the Feb we need to re-issue with the a new date 😕 ","2026-01-15T14:34:25.411Z"],["3813235","PFI-792464","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Updated the netting settings.\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 16.34.17@2x.png|width=1106,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 16.34.17@2x.png\"!\n\n!CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 16.34.34@2x-20260115-143436.png|width=1106,alt=\"CleanShot 2026-01-15 at 16.34.34@2x-20260115-143436.png\"!","2026-01-15T14:34:53.343Z"],["3813236","HS-28790","HS","anna.tiurina@bolt.eu","Anna Tiurina","Hey-hey [~accountid:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\nYes, I’ll submit it till the end of the week ☺️ \n\nKind regards,","2026-01-15T14:34:54.654Z"],["3813237","CLOUDSEC-728","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-15T14:35:09.659Z"],["3813238","LSS-58869","LSS","vlad-gabriel.ene@bolt.eu","Vlad-Gabriel Ene","Hey [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] ! Unfortunately, the partner completely dropped the deal and we can close this case as we will not sign them any time soon. Thank you for the help and I am sorry for this sudden change but sadly it was something outside my control.","2026-01-15T14:35:10.831Z"],["3813239","CLOUDSEC-728","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-15T14:35:18.312Z"],["3813240","HS-28790","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Great, thanks!","2026-01-15T14:35:18.984Z"],["3813242","FIS-4211","FIS","pavel.permenov@bolt.eu","Pavel Permenov","Rejected, too many security implications","2026-01-15T14:35:44.333Z"],["3813244","PRF-1848","PRF","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Hi [~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] 😊\n\nFeedback for RO:\n\n*V1 (Portrait formats):* Could we keep only _„Economii la curse și livrare”_ on Row 1 and move _„luna aceasta, de până la”_ to Row 2? It would be easier to read—right now it feels a bit fragmented. It’s not mandatory, but I would recommend it.\n\n*V2:* OK\n\n*V3:* _„Cu programul Bolt Plus”_ — “Program” isn’t the term we usually use for Bolt Plus; we typically say _Subscription (Abonament)_. So the correct phrasing would be _„Cu abonamentul Bolt Plus”_.\n\n*V4:* OK","2026-01-15T14:35:52.870Z"],["3813246","HS-28950","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey, apologies - I am not sure what correction you have in mind, as it seems from your profile everything is in order. Could you elaborate who asked for this correction? Thanks a lot!","2026-01-15T14:36:32.792Z"],["3813248","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Hi Beatrice, changes must be tracked in the latest excel fil shared. ","2026-01-15T14:37:29.260Z"],["3813249","LSS-60983","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey team,\n\nAny news here?\n\nShould I keep this ticket open, or can I close it for now (and then if something comes up, you can write here and I reopen it)?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T14:37:33.609Z"],["3813250","LSS-61650","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:37:42.918Z"],["3813251","DO-5806","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","Hey! Can you ask Jaanus to quickly comment “Approve” here, I think it won’t send approval request that is needed..","2026-01-15T14:38:08.223Z"],["3813253","FX-3365","FX","dmitry.andrienko@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Andryienka","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] Sorry for late reply, yes it was done and by default sorted by Request data DESC, the indication was not added as there was already default sorting logic with no indication, it was just updated.","2026-01-15T14:38:51.443Z"],["3813255","PFI-816791","PFI","ivan.farkasovsky@bolt-outsource.eu","Ivan Farkasovsky","Hello guys! It has been more than a month. Any update please?","2026-01-15T14:39:21.166Z"],["3813260","PFI-827828","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! The balance is correct - the 1043.38 is the in-app balance that eligible for payout. The rest (65) is the cash in hand the driver already has. ","2026-01-15T14:40:11.106Z"],["3813265","LSS-60983","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \nNo, nothing for now. You can close it, and I will reopen it if anything comes up","2026-01-15T14:41:06.826Z"],["3813266","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] please see the above comment. Thank you","2026-01-15T14:41:08.952Z"],["3813267","LSS-61651","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:41:24.473Z"],["3813268","LSS-61623","LSS","petr.kratky@bolt.eu","Petr Krátký","Great!Thank you","2026-01-15T14:41:25.161Z"],["3813269","DSR-3625","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9] [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] [~accountid:712020:da839b78-87fc-4471-947b-3aae59c6030b] - now that Eliise is gone, could you please advise as to who is currently in charge of People DSRs?\n\nCould you also please post an update on this topic in both [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q|smart-link]  and [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0623C123AP|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0623C123AP|smart-link] so that all relevant POCs and stakeholders are aware of who is in charge of this process going forward? Thank you in advance.","2026-01-15T14:41:25.745Z"],["3813273","LSS-58869","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:c6064cb8-f931-41fd-8f2e-10e1e45b14e7]! No worries, always happy to help 🙂 Good luck with your new deals!","2026-01-15T14:42:21.986Z"],["3813274","WEBSD-1485","WEBSD","giulia.zanotto@bolt.eu","Giulia Zanotto","[^SK Global Template_ Customer Terms (Rides) CONFIDENTIAL AND SUBJECT TO LEGAL PRIVILEGE FINAL.docx.pdf]","2026-01-15T14:42:29.876Z"],["3813278","LSS-61652","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:43:25.120Z"],["3813279","WFM-10012","WFM","maykl.grigoryan@bolt.eu","Maykl Grigoryan","!Bolt_logo (4382be75-a298-49ac-9d23-b260270bcf42).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T14:43:53.958Z"],["3813281","DSR-3625","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] hello - I’m currently responsible for managing employee DSRs - I cannot access [this link|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q] but my details have been shared with the members in the second slack channel.","2026-01-15T14:44:19.916Z"],["3813283","CLOUDSEC-728","CLOUDSEC","iuliia.laaneots@bolt.eu","Iuliia Laaneots","Created under admin user in Elastic. Only write permissions. \nShared with Dadash. ","2026-01-15T14:44:59.587Z"],["3813288","LSS-61649","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T14:46:07.883Z"],["3813291","VULN-1459","VULN","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04N7D3CGNA/p1768469056941559|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04N7D3CGNA/p1768469056941559|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:46:38.270Z"],["3813293","DSR-3625","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","[~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9] Thanks - I have reached out to Juan to align on an announcement in the relevant channel so that CSPC knows who to escalate People-DSRs in the future. I will reassign this ticket to you :)","2026-01-15T14:46:45.753Z"],["3813294","CSDT-965","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Doing it together with Looker sync for this task: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CSDT/boards/2029?selectedIssue=CSDT-956|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CSDT/boards/2029?selectedIssue=CSDT-956|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T14:47:04.091Z"],["3813296","LSS-61653","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:47:27.437Z"],["3813298","PFI-833827","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T14:47:38.108Z"],["3813299","LSS-61654","LSS","bryan.seixas@bolt.eu","Bryan de Jesus Seixas","[^Benfica Store Contract Signed Scanned.pdf] _(3.30 MB)_","2026-01-15T14:47:46.590Z"],["3813300","LSS-61654","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nBryan de Jesus Seixas has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:47:48.338Z"],["3813320","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","+*Internal note to self / update:*+\n\nI’ve had a call with Ramone to query some discrepancies in the data provided. Ramone is looking into this and will provide updated data asap. \n\nAttached is my draft letter, as it stands. I need to merge several PDF documents once the letter is finalised (e.g., data from privacy, converted CSV files, copy of order, etc). The highlighted dates are ones I have queried for either being the wrong way around or not within the relevant period (all discussed with Ramone).\n\n[^DRAFT Response Letter to Thorntons Court Order - Bolt Services UK Limited.docx (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T14:49:10.334Z"],["3813321","LSS-61248","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8],  thank you for your ticket. \nI have updated [the T&Cs |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zBd8TjKk4oqe2CVwrQDe0C0oQhSt9KU_mNcR8uikXjs/edit?tab=t.0]accordingly, please review. \nWe also need to wait for approval from Privacy’s side 😉 I have already created a sub-ticket for them. \nIf you have any additional questions, let me know, thanks! ","2026-01-15T14:49:11.149Z"],["3813322","DRX-27790","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27819 has been resolved","2026-01-15T14:49:29.646Z"],["3813332","DBRE-8310","DBRE","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","The biggest consumers of inodes on the ti-manager are:\n\n# {{tiup cluster}} command logs\n# {{tiup dm}} command logs\n# Also, tiup has a bug, it is described here [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1763040909454079?thread_ts=1762932052.734379&cid=GFGTF111A|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1763040909454079?thread_ts=1762932052.734379&cid=GFGTF111A|smart-link] \n\n\n\nFor the 1st and 2nd points, I’ve adjusted tiup cleanup parameters in [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5563|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5563|smart-link] and in [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5542|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5542|smart-link]. You can check if it works by running {{systemctl status}} {{tiup-clean-audit.service‎}}\n\nThe 3rd one has ben resolved with [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8334|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8334|smart-link]. ","2026-01-15T14:50:05.238Z"],["3813333","LSS-58389","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Logging into account: [https://ec.europa.eu/safety-gate/Online-Marketplace-Registration/screen/home|https://ec.europa.eu/safety-gate/Online-Marketplace-Registration/screen/home|smart-link]\n\nSubmitting reports: [https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/safety-business-gateway/screen/public/home|https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/safety-business-gateway/screen/public/home|smart-link]\n\n* Account on company phone and Liisa have been both added as local admins. \n* New users can be invited from both accounts, this requires an account for the user to be created first, device linked and after that only can admins invite users.\n* Each new marketplace needs to be created separately, unique emails are required. Same email cannot be used for all accounts unfortunately.\n* Users most likely need to be linked under all marketplaces separately as well.","2026-01-15T14:50:08.031Z"],["3813334","HS-28924","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-15T14:50:16.720Z"],["3813335","LSS-61655","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:50:21.702Z"],["3813337","PFI-833833","PFI","seema.matli@bolt.eu","Seema Matli","!IMG_0484.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_0485.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_0487.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T14:50:34.453Z"],["3813338","CLOUDSEC-424","CLOUDSEC","iuliia.laaneots@bolt.eu","Iuliia Laaneots","[~accountid:60c8cb62b2156100696dc765] is it still relevant? or as Farshid already revised, we can close it?","2026-01-15T14:50:37.861Z"],["3813341","FX-3646","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Meruzhan Kerobyan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768488663047679]*{color}:\nHi, it is beeing used by us (FleetX team), driver portal (driver-earnings team) and ride booker for lux (lux team).\n\nThe overall monorepo is maintained by fleetx.\n\nWhy?\n{quote}","2026-01-15T14:51:45.320Z"],["3813342","FX-3649","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768488715958619]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3649] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T14:52:08.419Z"],["3813346","PFI-833722","PFI","patricie.cholevova@bolt-outsource.eu","Patricie Cholevova","I will ask him to screenshot me that as well, and then send it here, apologies for not thinking of that initially. ","2026-01-15T14:52:55.136Z"],["3813349","PAW-14922","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17171\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 14:53:05 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T14:53:05.773Z"],["3813350","LSS-61656","LSS","diana.morkunaite@bolt.eu","Diana Morkūnaitė","[^Teisiniu paslaugu sutarties Priedas 12 (1).pdf] _(395 kB)_","2026-01-15T14:53:19.844Z"],["3813351","LSS-61656","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDiana Morkūnaitė has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:53:21.728Z"],["3813352","L10N-28013","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.560Z"],["3813353","L10N-28001","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.590Z"],["3813354","L10N-28014","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.603Z"],["3813355","L10N-28006","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.672Z"],["3813356","L10N-27999","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.713Z"],["3813357","L10N-28008","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.713Z"],["3813358","L10N-28007","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.783Z"],["3813359","L10N-28000","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.810Z"],["3813360","L10N-28009","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.841Z"],["3813361","L10N-28004","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.912Z"],["3813362","L10N-28012","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.891Z"],["3813363","L10N-28003","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.946Z"],["3813364","L10N-28011","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.982Z"],["3813365","L10N-28010","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.987Z"],["3813366","L10N-28002","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:30.982Z"],["3813367","L10N-28005","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T14:53:31.119Z"],["3813369","PFI-833827","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","please raise with campaign team.","2026-01-15T14:53:34.770Z"],["3813370","PFI-833827","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-15T14:53:41.047Z"],["3813373","MARTECH3-1506","MARTECH3","anirudhan.anbuchezhian@bolt.eu","Ani rudhan","*Update 15.01.2026*\n\n* Completed the comms coverage query and had a call with Tomasz to confirm all requirements are met for creating the ETL using this query.\n* [Link to the query.|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2487055656175998?o=3829506390716583#command/8747707579407460]\n* [Link to the Jira ticket |https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MARTECH3-1511]created for Tomasz to build the ETL.","2026-01-15T14:54:21.946Z"],["3813374","DBRE-8310","DBRE","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","Currently, tiup is the main consumer of inodes. However, it may change given the nature of ti-manager, i.e. how we use it.\n\nLimiting disk (and not only disk) resources for each user may not help, as a lot of stuff is happening under root.\n\nI’ve added a long term fix for issues we have been experiencing lately, but it does not guarantee that new issues won’t pop up later, at some point of time.\n\nIn my opinion, the long term solution is to have a better solution, than machine like ti-manager where a lot of things happen and all the team do different operations. Kubernetes is the best fit for these purposes, in my opinion. But I understand that team is not familiar with it and development will take some time.","2026-01-15T14:54:26.419Z"],["3813377","LSS-58389","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","@Narmin Ahmadova will be POC instead of Galina for safety side. ","2026-01-15T14:54:39.379Z"],["3813379","LSS-58403","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Account has been created for the company phone. Device has been linked and is currently logged in as well (EU Login Mobile). Instructions and credentials have been left in the main ticket as an internal comment. \n\n+Current status:+ new emails need to be created by IT for each country separately. Each marketplace needs to be created with a unique email address. Account for EE has been created, but is currently marked as a test account.","2026-01-15T14:55:11.616Z"],["3813382","DBRE-8310","DBRE","yehor.naumenko@bolt.eu","Yehor Naumenko","Closing this ticket for now, as the issue was mitigated and the long term fix was rolled out.\r\nHowever, the issue may reoccur with new kind of inode consumers. Further discussion is needed. My vote goes for k8s.","2026-01-15T14:55:41.667Z"],["3813383","LSS-61658","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T14:55:52.803Z"],["3813385","LSS-59252","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Requested clarifications re/ the applicable T&Cs to the Campaign from Legal; privacy will review the T&Cs standard section on data protection to double check if its adequate for this jurisdiction.\n# Requested more details from the business stakeholders re/ how personal data will be processed.","2026-01-15T14:56:42.907Z"],["3813386","LSS-58700","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","15.01.2026: To-do-list:\n\n* -ask IT to create emails for all Bolt Market entities since Safety gate doesn’t allow to use same email and credentials for several stores. -\n* together with Legal OPs/Safety create accounts for all Bolt Market stores in Safety Gate. ","2026-01-15T14:57:02.130Z"],["3813387","CLOUDSEC-679","CLOUDSEC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Ticket made, waiting for Guido to confirm we can proceed. \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349549|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349549|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T14:57:06.580Z"],["3813388","BR-4006","BR","arsen.ali@bolt.eu","Arsen Ali","Created the subtpyes, mapped them.\nToDo: Backfill record_compensation where the compensation_fee_type is missing.","2026-01-15T14:57:22.010Z"],["3813391","LSS-55858","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hey [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1] ,\n\nYes - we’ve now received the external advice. That said, we need a bit more time to digest it and discuss internally with Tax and FinReg before we can land on a clear position. [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] is leading that internal review.\n\nI’ll come back to you with a more concrete steer once those discussions have taken place and I’ll keep you posted on timing.","2026-01-15T14:57:41.080Z"],["3813397","CLOUDSEC-726","CLOUDSEC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15419|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15419] ","2026-01-15T15:00:04.519Z"],["3813398","MARTECH3-1499","MARTECH3","anirudhan.anbuchezhian@bolt.eu","Ani rudhan","*Update 15.01.2025*\n\n* Tomasz helped with data ingestion to store the raw experiment results from Braze for use in this incentive experiment.\n* Anette created a test experiment to confirm the results are being stored correctly, and they are.\n* All future incentive experiments will be conducted in the Admin Panel, as agreed in [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04J0MNQC5R/p1768387354165019?thread_ts=1768302747.905099&cid=C04J0MNQC5R]  conversation.","2026-01-15T15:00:23.759Z"],["3813399","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* [https://www.githubstatus.com/incidents/5ccghcfrkv39|https://www.githubstatus.com/incidents/5ccghcfrkv39|smart-link] \n\n!image-20260115-150108.png|width=942,alt=\"image-20260115-150108.png\"!","2026-01-15T15:00:50.951Z"],["3813401","LSS-61541","LSS","alexia.matsangou@bolt.eu","Alexia Matsangou","Hello [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] I have shared you a link to the document that [~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf] originally send. \n\nCan you check if you have access to [this now?|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17yfl_d85YtTXgArAew4AqkkK27Qp6-FQ2m9TK60pHFg/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-15T15:01:12.212Z"],["3813402","CLOUDSEC-729","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-15T15:01:16.713Z"],["3813403","CLOUDSEC-729","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-15T15:01:21.080Z"],["3813404","LSS-61659","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T15:01:30.349Z"],["3813405","LSS-61656","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T15:01:30.387Z"],["3813406","LSS-61655","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T15:01:30.388Z"],["3813407","LSS-61654","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T15:01:30.452Z"],["3813408","PAI-922","PAI","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Pushed a fix [here|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9714]. Changed pipelines to run every 4th of month.","2026-01-15T15:01:41.207Z"],["3813410","LSS-61660","LSS","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","*Order vs Ticket Data (Restaurant Own Delivery)* 3 complete months – October, November, December\n\n|Market|[+Delivery orders ROD+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46529]|[+ROD ticket %+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46532] (Eater)|\n|Romania|24,622 (0.65%)|1.1% (1,932)|\n|Lithuania|0|0|\n|Estonia|7591 (0.61%)|2% (627)|\n|CzechR|13,836 (0.94%)|1.4% (1,003)|\n|Malta|0|0|\n|Latvia|552 (0.05%)|7 tickets|\n|Ukraine|33,118 (2.01%)|5.4% (3,464)|\n|Slovakia|52,965 (4.83%)|9% (3,621)|\n|Portugal|9759 (1.02%)|2.1% (1,667)|\n|Cyprus|18,641 (2.83%)|4.7% (947)|\n|Poland|44,546 (7.03%)|12% (4,370)|\n|Ghana|2,001 (0.19%)|0.7% (179)|\n|Azerbaijan|22 (0.01%)|2 tickets|\n|Kenya|9839 (3.85%)|7.6% (601 tickets)|\n|Bulgaria|6,147 (8.82%)|21,6% (622 tickets)|\n\nThe data shows Restaurant Own Delivery is widely used and CS receives significant queries in relation to these orders","2026-01-15T15:02:15.427Z"],["3813412","LSS-61660","LSS","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","[~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] Perhaps you can assist 🙏 ","2026-01-15T15:02:42.106Z"],["3813414","WFM-10010","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, he is assigned ","2026-01-15T15:03:05.162Z"],["3813422","BP-13321","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] pls check [design and copy|https://www.figma.com/design/LIBdd7OhjHd0wQSlMThTSt/Dashboard?node-id=9352-4279&t=nzQChfWY9a97tKBK-4]\nThere is Got it button - next week, I want to check whenever we can tie the banner for the admin, not for the company. If only for the company, then we surely remove it from the warning version. Feel free to comment directly in Figma","2026-01-15T15:04:42.656Z"],["3813425","RS-1953","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","[^Vorderingsbrief Bolt (02-12-2025) en-US.pdf] _(150 kB)_\n\n[^Vorderingsbrief Bolt (02-12-2025).pdf] _(347 kB)_","2026-01-15T15:05:49.640Z"],["3813429","RCE-354","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768489603625179]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-354] `Investigate document date upload issue` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:06:55.327Z"],["3813454","FX-3646","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Sergei Toroshchin [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768489746021069]*{color}:\nAt some point, I was discussing with Max Shashkov an opportunity to join it as well with our projects (courier/courier fleet portals), and wanted to discuss how it can be done right now, how long it would take for the previous team, etc. Also curious about reusability and tech future of fleet portal. We can make a meeting or discuss async\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:09:19.564Z"],["3813456","SAI-1408","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","User posted two comments and one provided solution and second caused bot to unassign.\n\nThis is support-bot service, when unhandled exception happens (here it was time out), we call unassign\n\nWhen firing two requests concurrently, and both are successful, we call submit agent comment, and then the one which is referring to not most recent user message is discarded in customer-support submit comment handler. Here we just called unassign, which doesn't check anything like that.","2026-01-15T15:10:25.847Z"],["3813457","LSS-61460","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:49ec724a-806f-42f1-86dc-bf9f93671a23] - I have now taken a closer look at this - I assume that the ask here is to flag whether we are ok to proceed with this pilot from a privacy POV, correct? If that is the case, then in order to properly advise on this I need a bit more visibility on the following topics - could you please answer these questions as soon as you can? \n\nI would be happy to have a call to discuss if that would be easier / quicker - feel free to find some time in my calendar if so.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n{color:#4c9aff}*QUESTIONS*{color} (i) \n\n*Stage 1 Sharing:*\n\n* Why have we assumed that the data sharing here is “anonymised”? Is this because we are taking specific steps to anonymise the data before we share it, r because of the nature of the data itself?\n* Are any of the fleets whose information we are sharing here natural persons / sole traders (rather than businesses)?\n* Is the list of categories of data in Schedule 3 of the agreement (i.e., categories of data being shared as part of Stage 1) complete? \n* On the understanding that fleets have not yet expressed an interest in any financing options at this stage, are we sharing information about *_all_* German fleets with the third-party lender, or only certain fleets (if the latter, which ones)?\n\n*Stage 2 Sharing:*\n\n* Am I correct in understanding that Stage 2 data sharing is not covered in Schedule 3 of the agreement? If so, do we know why not?\n* How will the fleets be ‘expressing interest’ and ‘consenting’ to data sharing, in practical terms (i.e., what will this look like in practice? Will it be by clicking a link, checking a tickbox, emailing Bolt, or something else)?\n\n*Promoting the Finmid Project:*\n\n* I see from the agreement that Bolt will be promoting the lender’s financing options to German fleets. Do we know what mediums Bolt will be using to do so? (e.g., will we just be posting this on a general fleet page on the platform, or will we be specifically emailing fleets encouraging them to consider the financing options?)\n{panel}\n\n----\n\n+_Subject to the above_+ (please confirm first), it sounds like we have already signed a binding agreement on this in December and will be going ahead in any event - as such, in practical terms, I am limited to advising on the main risks to make sure that we are doing this _sensibly,_ rather than implementing any major changes - just to manage expectations on this 🙏 \n\nSuch advice is likely to look like the following:\n\n{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\nh3. *General Note - “Anonymised” Data* 💡 \n{panel}\n\nI see from the ticket description (and the agreement) that we consider Stage 1 data sharing to be “_anonymised_” fleet data only. If this is on the basis that we consider the data categories listed to be “_anonymous_”, then this is not technically correct - if these datapoints relate to natural persons (e.g., sole traders), then even though it is difficult to link them to those specific individuals on the lender side, the *Stage 1 datapoints could still count as personal data* under German data protection law. \n\n*Why this matters*: We likely need to consider privacy requirements for both Stage 1 and Stage 2 (not just the latter).\n\n{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\nh3. *Sharing Fleet Data* ♻️ \n{panel}\n\nGenerally, the data sharing under this program is not high risk, and so is something that we can do ✅ \n\n*_However_*, this is subject to the following flags 🚩 \n\n* *Stage 1 data sharing*: Based on the ticket description, it sounds as though we could be sharing personal data about many / all German fleets with the lender, without those fleets necessarily being aware of this. Our preference from a privacy POV would be to implement an opt-out mechanism and include some sort of disclaimer language - however, on the assumption that we will not have time to implement this (since the data is being transferred in a few days' time), our focus should instead be on *only sharing* *_strictly necessary_* *data with the lender as part of Stage 1*. In practical terms, this means: (a) making sure that the categories of information we are sharing are proportionate (if anything is unnecessary, then remove it); and (b) if there is an option of sharing data of certain fleets rather than all of them, then this would lower the risk profile.\n* *Stage 2 data sharing*: It is helpful that we are seeking fleet permission to share data as part of Stage 2, although we should *make sure that we have obtained permission properly*. In practical terms, what this means is: (a) the fleet should be fully informed at the time they give permission of what information will be shared and why (we can assist with transparency language here, if there is time to do so); and (b) we have an effective means of recording such permission on our systems (this is why I am asking about how exactly permission is given here - currently this is unclear).\n\n*Why this matters*: Without taking the above steps, there is a risk that we could receive complaints about sharing fleet data with third parties in a non-transparent manner, which could result in operational strain and (in extreme cases) potential interest from the German regulator.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\nh3. *Agreement Review* :Google_Doc: \n{panel}\n\nThe data protection provisions in the agreement attached to this ticket are much more in favour of the third party (rather than Bolt) than we would ordinarily agree to, which is not in our interests ⚠️ For example:\n\n* Bolt is required to notify the lender of data subject requests and personal data breaches, but this does not apply the other way around; and\n* Bolt has given a pro-lender indemnity for any breaches of data protection obligations, but the lender has not given the same to Bolt.\n\n*Why this matters*: This: (i) places a disproportionate amount of operational effort on us, despite us being the ones who have more to lose (as the data exporter); and (ii) places most of the commercial risk on us, if something went wrong here from a privacy POV.\n\nUltimately, the agreement has already been signed (and the data sharing is not high risk and for a 6-month period), and so assuming that there is no time to sign anything else/suggest amendments, the business can decide to accept the risk and proceed. Instead, my recommendation would be that *after the 6-month pilot period, we should renegotiate the data sharing terms* to make sure that Bolt’s position is properly protected. I would be happy to help with this when the time comes.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}\nh3. *Direct Marketing* ✉️ \n{panel}\n\nI see from the agreement that Bolt is required to “promote” this opportunity to fleets. Where we are promoting this to fleets (whether individuals or businesses) via *_targeted / direct means_* (e.g., emails, SMS messages, push notifications), EU / German law requires us to: (i) only do so where we have first obtained the recipient’s *_opt-in consent_*; and (ii) offer the recipient the ability to *_unsubscribe_* from such comms at any time.\n\nAs such, it is important to check precisely how we are marketing this offering to fleets, as if we are not compliant with the above then this approach carriers regulatory risks.\n\n----\n\nHappy to discuss if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-15T15:10:57.106Z"],["3813459","PIF-3284","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-njsc-db, pint-product-backend-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-15T15:11:35.989Z"],["3813461","HS-28994","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Kristiina! There’s an error happening when these dates are being added to Workday. I have escalated this problem to People Tech who are looking into it. \n\nI’ll let you know as soon as it’s resolved and the dates have been added successfully.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-15T15:12:12.193Z"],["3813476","LSS-61661","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T15:16:35.566Z"],["3813477","LSS-61048","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] we will aim to provide the reviewed agreement this week ","2026-01-15T15:16:41.538Z"],["3813480","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768490210097969]*{color}:\n&gt; But also you removed the FleetCarBlocked and FleetCarUnblocked LCM event triggering\nWas this related to car's hard block or scheduled blocks?\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:17:06.162Z"],["3813482","LSS-61662","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","[^Engagement letter - Bolt Operations UK.pdf] _(249 kB)_\n\n[^Engagement letter - Bolt Services UK.pdf] _(249 kB)_\n\n[^Terms and privacy notice (current)_4129-7702-3011.pdf] _(121 kB)_","2026-01-15T15:17:41.554Z"],["3813483","PFI-823402","PFI","mihai.raucea@bolt.eu","Mihai Răucea","Hi [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] , do you have any news abou this?","2026-01-15T15:18:14.415Z"],["3813484","PFI-833841","PFI","janek.jappinen@bolt-outsource.eu","Janek Jäppinen","[^ProofOfPayment-9cf9c795-bf8c-4eb4-9a1a-81a2c1357b89.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-15T15:18:24.097Z"],["3813485","PFI-826753","PFI","sylwia.siwek@bolt-outsource.eu","Sylwia Siwek","hi\n\n2025-08-01 expense_adjustment -30.75 PLN [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/620408189|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/620408189] 25 pln bonus (25 zł + 23% VAT = 30.75 pln)","2026-01-15T15:18:49.780Z"],["3813486","LSS-57341","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Carried over to Q1 2026. Has been deprioritised, but will be worked on together with product counsel.","2026-01-15T15:18:55.651Z"],["3813487","HS-28950","HS","aleksandra.menio@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Menio","Hello, no worries, I’ll try to provide a bit more context.\n\nI received a lower salary for December than I expected. After sending an inquiry to the appropriate team, I received the following information:\n\n”Hi Aleksandra,\n\nThank you for contacting us.\nWe have check the payroll and as per our report you were on sick leave 24/11/2025 - 28/11/2025,\nhowever we have not received your work certificate (swiadectwo pracy) from the previous employer, and our payroll provider automatically calculated this as unpaid.\nCould you please provide us with your last work certificate so we could correct with next payroll accordingly?”\n\nAnd then I was instructed by the Regional Payroll Advisor to reach People Operations Team and provide the documentation. \n\n\n","2026-01-15T15:19:31.394Z"],["3813491","WEBSD-1475","WEBSD","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:9e668ce4-0877-43c6-bae9-52f1ecbc753f]  can you please share exact link of the section EU (Europe) where these documents is planned to be uploaded so I can check? \n\nWhistleblower and Code of Conduct are global policies so I am not sure if uploading only under EU region is sufficient enough.\n\nPlease see PDF and Word export from Confluence pages attached. Is this ok? Also I have attached PDF of the Directive thus cannot find how to get Word file of the directive.\n\n[^BILP-Code of Conduct-150126-150441.pdf]\n[^CELEX_32019L1937_EN_TXT.pdf]\n[^IMS-Bolt Whistleblower Policy - RCMS-POL-01.04.07.03-150126-150331.pdf]\n[^Bolt+Whistleblower+Policy+-+RCMS-POL-01.04.07.03.doc]\n[^Code+of+Conduct.doc]\n\n","2026-01-15T15:20:14.991Z"],["3813496","LSS-61640","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hey [~accountid:712020:2765baba-2b31-484f-8570-0cc671e879cb] what are Transion devices? Are we talking about Android phones ? ","2026-01-15T15:21:02.458Z"],["3813498","SAI-1408","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768483749160779|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768483749160779|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T15:21:14.463Z"],["3813500","LSS-61664","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmelie Dufva has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T15:22:16.289Z"],["3813511","LSS-59742","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:712020:ca818823-efac-45fe-ba7d-a6686a5e08b5], thank you for your patience once again! \n\n\nI have reviewed the agreement, please see my comments in[ the document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1avRLiPaT6XngOQhTFNnTZ3zyO_bk53Kh/edit]. \nOnce we clear those open questions, we will be able to share this agreement with our partner for their review, and after that we’ll be able to collect the signatures. \n\nAlso, for the next time for [service agreement in Sweden please use this template|https://docs.google.com/document/d/19l8AZAed75CuUvSngMmDg-MrR5Pl32MI/edit#bookmark=id.1v1yuxt], I think it is the newest one (please make a copy first), thanks a lot!\n\nLet me know if you have any additional questions 🙏 ","2026-01-15T15:23:32.370Z"],["3813512","LSS-61486","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] \nPlease advice - do we need to take any further action on this ticket?\nFrom what I can see, CS has already handled everything:\n\n* CS followed the updated KB for “access to someone else’s account due to phone number recycling”.\n* Both the new phone number holder and the original account holder were contacted using the appropriate comms templates.\n* The original account holder was notified and instructed to update their contact details.\n* The affected account was archived to prevent any further access.\n* The reporting user was instructed to create a new account using their current phone number.","2026-01-15T15:23:37.484Z"],["3813517","CSXRD-143","CSXRD","justus.debruin@bolt.eu","Justus de Bruin","Updated the processes and announced the changes","2026-01-15T15:24:42.829Z"],["3813518","PFI-819191","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","<\\!--[endif]-->    \n\n *email:*6202635  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +andrus.treiberg@bolt.eu+{color}|mailto:andrus.treiberg@bolt.eu]{color:blue} {color}++{color:blue} +,+{color}+  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +antifraud@fondy.eu+{color}|mailto:antifraud@fondy.eu]{color:blue} {color}++{color:blue} +,+{color}+  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +chargeback_reports@bolt.eu+{color}|mailto:chargeback_reports@bolt.eu]{color:blue} {color}+ BOLT.EU \n| !/img/aval_white.png! |  *{color:gray} *Публічне акціонерне товариство «Райффайзен Банк»  \\\\ Public Joint Stock Company «Raiffeisen Bank»*{color}* | \n|  *АТ Райффайзен Банк* |  *ТОВ БОЛТ ОПЕРЕЙШНЗ УКРАЇНА* | \n|  *Телефон 0-800-500-738, 044-495-91-91* | | \n|  *E-mail:*  *[rb.acq@raiffeisen.ua|mailto:rb.acq@raiffeisen.ua]* | | \n| | | \n|  *15/01/2026* |  *№ 81-19-1-00/26/KK_559286_15012026_EM* |\n \n\n  \n\n *Повідомлення про утримання коштів* \n|  *{color:#172B4D} *Кліше*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Місце проведення транзакції*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Номер карти*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Дата трансакції*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Код авторизації*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Сума трансакції, грн.*{color}* | \n| 6202635 | bolt.eu; Volodymyrska ST. 79a; Kyiv; UKR | 4149 5110 **** 5988 | 2025-12-08 13:41:29 | 597415 | 3170.00 UAH |\n \n\n  \n\nІнформуємо, що суми, згідно зазначених трансакцій, будуть утримані з подальших надходжень Вашої Компанії по еквайрингу.\n Причина утримання: ненадання / невчасне надання документів або підтвердження можливості утримання з боку Компанії \n\n  \n\n *Коментар:* Торговець не надав документи у встановлені терміни  \n\n  \n\n  \n \n\n{color:#172B4D} Classification: GENERAL{color}\n   \n\n *From:* Kateryna KHARCHENKO <kateryna.kharchenko@raiffeisen.ua>  *On Behalf Of*  Rb ACQ RBUA","2026-01-15T15:24:46.393Z"],["3813519","LSS-56022","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","*Document Expiry / Missing Documents*\n\n# *Created 24 Oct 2023, 16:24:43, Start 15 Feb 2024, 23:30:00 – End 3 Feb 2024, 10:22:07*\n*Reason*: Expired documents – Certificate of Compliance (MOT document)\n# *Created 3 Feb 2024, 10:22:07, Start 15 Feb 2024, 23:30:00 – End 10 Feb 2024, 11:26:01*\n# *Reason*: Expired documents – Certificate of Compliance (MOT document)\n# *Created 24 Oct 2023, 16:24:42, Start 15 Feb 2024, 23:30:00 – End 10 Feb 2024, 11:25:25*\n*Reason*: Expired documents – Private Hire Vehicle Licence\n(Suspension for both above, set for the 15th, was cancelled after the driver uploaded the required document on 2 and 9 Feb 2024)\n\n*Incorrect or Pending Document Uploads*\n\n# *Created: 3 Feb 2024, 10:22:34, Start: 15 Feb 2024, 23:30:00 – End: 3 Feb 2024, 11:45:05*\n*Reason*: Pending document review\n(Suspension cancelled on 3 Feb 2024 due to document review)\n\n*Customer Safety Support / High Priority Case*\n\n# *Created 7 May 2024, 10:00:19, Start 7 May 2024, 10:00:19 – End 31 May 2024, 13:07:52*\n*Reason*: Customer Safety Support - Vehicle accident\n# *Created 5 May 2024, 08:35:27, Start 5 May 2024, 08:35:27 – End 7 May 2024, 10:00:28*\n*Reason*: Customer Safety Support - Vehicle accident\n# *Created 15 Apr 2024, 04:06:04, Start 15 Apr 2024, 04:06:04 – End 18 Apr 2024, 12:57:09*\n*Reason*: Customer Safety Support - Damaged vehicle\n\n\n\nCSV for earnings from Feb - Aug\n\n[^Aug.csv]\n[^Jul.csv]\n[^Jun.csv]\n[^May.csv]\n[^Apr.csv]\n[^Mar.csv]\n[^Feb.csv]\n\n","2026-01-15T15:24:51.443Z"],["3813521","LSS-61512","LSS","bruna.miguel@bolt.eu","Bruna Miguel","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ,\n\nAt the moment we don’t have a copy of the contract, and I truly don’t know what was agreed at the time. I have requested a copy directly to Medicina del lavoro, and once I have it, I will share with you.\n\nThis way we can check how to proceed.\n\nThank you. ","2026-01-15T15:25:14.155Z"],["3813522","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768490711397879]*{color}:\nThey were triggered for hard blocks. But they were not migrated for scheduled blocks\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:25:24.408Z"],["3813524","LSS-59827","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Thanks for your query [~accountid:5d9c300987dd6f0dcb4d2b58] .  I will take a look at this next week. ","2026-01-15T15:25:39.615Z"],["3813528","LSS-61369","LSS","jan.huk@bolt.eu","Jan Huk","Hello [~accountid:5bb7726959e46d7be31aad4c], should we continue forward with legal action only? To sum things up - Taxi driver association created a fake AI generated image of Bolt and Uber cars crashing in snow. It is a clear defamation can. How should we proceed with this? It did not spread in regular media, it only spread on SoMe. It is now a week old case. Can we take legal action against the association, or at least threaten the association with such steps? Or can it backfire? We have already reported the case to Facebook.","2026-01-15T15:26:09.751Z"],["3813529","FX-3650","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768490760675869]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3650] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:26:14.412Z"],["3813532","LSS-61430","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] to discuss with Emily on Monday","2026-01-15T15:27:19.581Z"],["3813533","LSS-61495","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:8a574999-84e1-4c69-ba7b-46d08c4cff29] 👋 If we only want to share number of fleets (for example, something like: _“We have 120 Fleets in Poland, 3 Fleets in Spain, 18 Fleets in Hungary“_ - then this is not personal data and we can share it without any additional constraints. \n\nLet me know if this is what you’re intending to do or if I misunderstood 🙂 ","2026-01-15T15:27:25.536Z"],["3813535","FX-3650","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768490866397049]*{color}:\nAtm we only have whitelists for country, city and company id. So with the current setup its not possible\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:27:58.591Z"],["3813536","WFM-9999","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-15T15:27:59.592Z"],["3813537","LSS-61664","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","+Finance input+:\n\n* [@emelie.dufva|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U06T67GD6CU] can you ask advisors for option 2, do we need to do incorporation process first via the bank (similar to Germany, open temp. account, transfer share capital, then open final account), or is this company registration done in full without needing the account live?Asking as if it needs formal incorporating via bank this delays things by several weeks in my experience compared to option 1 (edited) \n* *Borenius response*: the advisor has informed the following:\n** The account would be needed prior to and as a condition for registration of the entity in the Trade Register, *if the new entity has a share capital* (as the share capital has to be paid into the company’s account for it to be registered, and the payment has to be demonstrated to the Trade Register by an auditor certificate or otherwise).\n** *If the company has no share capital, it can be registered without a bank account*.\n** In practise the bank account would be open to the entity “under formation”, but it would typically be a regular account (i.e. not a temporary one). The account does not necessarily have to be opened in a Finnish bank, but foreign banks have, in our experience, not been willing to open accounts for Finnish companies under formation. \n* Finance: \n** okay then if we go for option 2, then I propose we register the company without share capital, as to speed up account opening. Then we can remit equity to the entity once account is opened. If that works for others too,\n** We do have relations with Citi Finland branch so also opening for company under formation we can get done, it just takes such a long time in my experience\n\n+Tax input+: \n\n* The Key risks described should not affect deciding between the options. If Bolt Holdings will be the shareholder, then group contributions will not be available anyway; and secondly, as you mention then the shelf company has no tax losses to begin with.\n* However, I believe it should be possible to opt for VAT registration when incorporating the entity, so some convenience in Option 2","2026-01-15T15:28:03.586Z"],["3813539","FPD-1414","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","*Update:*\n\n* Changed the model logic fetching to be more concurrency-friendly, which significantly reduced the number of errors\n* There are still quite a few failures remaining; I inspected several of them and created a [Jira ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1537] to address the root causes (I will work on this on my next extra task day)\n* Relaunched backtests for 15, 30, 50, and 100 hyperparameter tuning trials\n* Launched backtesting accuracy jobs\n* Gathered all results in a Google Sheet ([link|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IQ975aObNKR89MUUu98YZCaHRzlfjbrPG0eSy6ObpBg/edit?usp=sharing])","2026-01-15T15:28:31.937Z"],["3813540","SREC-375","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","I think we should refactor [InfoSec AWS roles|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/blob/main/iam/eu-central-1/iam-identity-center/okta-groups/terraform.tfvars#L135-L163].\nIt's getting out of hand. :smile:\n\nAWS roles are based on Workday teams.\n\n{{SUP5.95}} is [Tarmo and his direct reports' team|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$2500/2500$115.htmld#TABTASKID=2998%249867].\n\n[OktaENGCloudSec|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$2500/2500$2419.htmld#TABTASKID=2998%249867] ({{SUP1600}}) has the [correct role|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/blob/main/iam/eu-central-1/iam-identity-center/okta-groups/terraform.tfvars#L153-L158].\nI don't understand the difference between this role and {{OktaENGInfoSecAdmin}}\nWhy does the same team have two roles? :smile:\n\nAlso, I think we should create new roles for InternalSec and ProductSec and use {{OktaENGInformationSec}} only for Tarmo and InfoSec EM permissions.\n\nHaving 17 people in one role is against the least privilege policy.\nExample of [refactoring Geo teams|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/14684/changes].","2026-01-15T15:28:50.637Z"],["3813541","SREC-375","SREC",null,"Slack","[Amin Khoshnood|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03GMLEA664/p1768485315485879?thread_ts=1768485315.485879&cid=C03GMLEA664|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03GMLEA664/p1768485315485879?thread_ts=1768485315.485879&cid=C03GMLEA664|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T15:28:51.767Z"],["3813542","SREC-375","SREC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Sounds reasonable to me :smile:","2026-01-15T15:28:52.330Z"],["3813543","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","agreed","2026-01-15T15:28:53.170Z"],["3813544","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","{quote}OktaENGInformationSec{quote}\n\nwe should probably have {{OktaENGInformationSecManagers}}  and {{OktaENGComplianceSec}}  or something","2026-01-15T15:28:54.511Z"],["3813545","SREC-375","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Compliance is not a separate Workday team.\nI would rather keep AWS roles as close as possible to Workday to have room for automating this in the future.","2026-01-15T15:28:55.672Z"],["3813546","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","That's fine of course","2026-01-15T15:28:56.260Z"],["3813547","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Do you know why the group memberships are not synced from Okta?","2026-01-15T15:28:56.807Z"],["3813548","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","i.e. for n8n, we are adding folks to an Okta group x-y-z","2026-01-15T15:28:57.407Z"],["3813556","LSS-61080","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Aligned - to check with EFJ if unsure about drafting of letter of response","2026-01-15T15:30:33.812Z"],["3813558","LSS-61512","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:49595943-fb9f-4151-8a74-b00c57b18f30] \n\nin that case, lets wait for the contract - I’ll be able to answer once received.\n\nthanks,\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-15T15:30:52.961Z"],["3813561","LSS-61369","LSS","karin.kase@bolt.eu","Karin Kase","We should: \n1) Tell the taxi association to take the fake posts down and if they disagree, threaten them with legal action\n\n2) Respond in the social media threads where this is spreading that this photo is fake. Why didn’t we do it a week ago when it started?\n\n","2026-01-15T15:31:48.587Z"],["3813562","COP-1936","COP","zhenyu.wang@bolt.eu","Zhenyu Wang","Experiment design is documented here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Ince/pages/7375421443/Churned+Model+Experiment|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Ince/pages/7375421443/Churned+Model+Experiment|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T15:31:50.480Z"],["3813565","LSS-61660","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","hey [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] - I can take this!","2026-01-15T15:32:14.799Z"],["3813567","BPPA-104","BPPA","yuliia.hakkinen@bolt.eu","Yuliia Häkkinen","Results are shared with PMs: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07NRK0KLAW/p1768403728505959|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07NRK0KLAW/p1768403728505959|smart-link]\n\nExperiment design doc: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/18r2uk8w2XsRyjtBkQwKG200HeWa2eO5lHeKj26KSI70/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.z89rs1j00al6|https://docs.google.com/document/d/18r2uk8w2XsRyjtBkQwKG200HeWa2eO5lHeKj26KSI70/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.z89rs1j00al6|smart-link]","2026-01-15T15:32:54.689Z"],["3813569","PFI-822307","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","*email:*6202635  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +andrus.treiberg@bolt.eu+{color}|mailto:andrus.treiberg@bolt.eu]{color:blue} {color}++{color:blue} +,+{color}+  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +antifraud@fondy.eu+{color}|mailto:antifraud@fondy.eu]{color:blue} {color}++{color:blue} +,+{color}+  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +chargeback_reports@bolt.eu+{color}|mailto:chargeback_reports@bolt.eu]{color:blue} {color}+ BOLT.EU \n| !/img/aval_white.png! |  *{color:gray} *Публічне акціонерне товариство «Райффайзен Банк»  \\\\ Public Joint Stock Company «Raiffeisen Bank»*{color}* | \n|  *АТ Райффайзен Банк* |  *ТОВ БОЛТ ОПЕРЕЙШНЗ УКРАЇНА* | \n|  *Телефон 0-800-500-738, 044-495-91-91* | | \n|  *E-mail:*  *[rb.acq@raiffeisen.ua|mailto:rb.acq@raiffeisen.ua]* | | \n| | | \n|  *15/01/2026* |  *№ 81-19-1-00/26/KK_559600_15012026_EM* |\n \n\n  \n\n *Повідомлення про утримання коштів* \n| |\n \n\n  \n\nІнформуємо, що суми, згідно зазначених трансакцій, будуть утримані з подальших надходжень Вашої Компанії по еквайрингу.\n Причина утримання: ненадання / невчасне надання документів або підтвердження можливості утримання з боку Компанії \n\n  \n\n *Коментар:* Торговець не надав документи у встановлені терміни  \n\n  \n\n  \n \n\n{color:#172B4D} Classification: PUBLIC{color}\n   \n\n *From:* Kateryna KHARCHENKO <kateryna.kharchenko@raiffeisen.ua>  *On Behalf Of*  Rb ACQ RBUA","2026-01-15T15:33:46.515Z"],["3813572","PFI-833848","PFI","andrei.neagu@bolt-outsource.eu","Andrei Neagu","!IMG_0816.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T15:34:29.634Z"],["3813573","PFI-833848","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T15:34:31.832Z"],["3813574","MLC-3893","MLC","mariaadelina.stana@bolt.eu","Maria Adelina Stana","All comms are now stopped. No need for an informing message at the moment. \n\nSigned off by local ops and expansion team, ","2026-01-15T15:34:51.426Z"],["3813575","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768491290215859]*{color}:\nThere are existing lcm triggers on car scheduled blocks in driverx-events service ([source|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/22d1122eb95398878c7c93c181152c7bab8194d4/src/rides/driver/driverx_events/main/service/DriverEventService.ts#L1182]). Are these not sufficient?\n\nLinked messages:\n[DriverEventService.ts|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/22d1122eb95398878c7c93c181152c7bab8194d4/src/rides/driver/driverx_events/main/service/DriverEventService.ts]\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:35:04.395Z"],["3813576","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768491302860479]*{color}:\nlooks like they are for driver level though.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:35:16.186Z"],["3813577","EBIKE1-366","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","There is a slight issue with the 24V output as the short circuit protection does not work properly.\n\nThe schematic needs to be improved but we have some ways to mitigate this problem in current hardware.\n\nHere is the [testing document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HixjeZbpO0DTW63-rmF2F2D4tuuFqMWYtGlBzzSZgFk/edit?tab=t.0], which described the issue in more detail. \n\n[~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] FYI","2026-01-15T15:35:24.610Z"],["3813578","LSS-58813","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Thanks [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] , this clarification is helpful 🙏 Based on the targeting logic you’ve outlined, I don’t see privacy blockers, subject to a few clear guardrails.\n\n* *Targeting based on home city ID / country code*\n\nUsing the home city ID logic (activity across Bolt products in the past 12 months, falling back to phone prefix where there is no activity) is acceptable from a privacy standpoint. This relies on existing account and usage data and does not involve sensitive data or live location. Reaching users assigned an Italian country code on this basis for Italy launch communications is fine.\n\n* *Former micromobility users in Italy*\n\nWhere users have been most active in Italy (e.g. micromobility), engaging them about the Rides launch is permissible. The services are closely related and there is a clear existing customer relationship in Italy. Soft opt-in can be relied on for launch communications, including promotional content, provided opt-outs are respected.\n\n* *“Travellers”  (Italian users active abroad)*\n\nThe proposed approach for the second group (Italian phone prefix + recent activity abroad, e.g. last 30 days) is also acceptable from a privacy perspective. Informing Italian users that a Bolt service they already use is now available in Italy/Milan is reasonable and proportionate. Limiting this segment to _recently active_ users is an important safeguard and I would recommend keeping this recency constraint. [~accountid:6203a0ea1fec260068c20327] so let’s make sure we’re not engaging a user who took a trip 10 years ago, and instead make it truly recent.\n\n* *Channels and data usage*\n** Email, push, and in-app messages are acceptable, assuming users have not opted out of marketing in those channels and each message includes a clear opt-out\n** SMS should only be included if we can confirm applicable consent/soft opt-in coverage.\n** Data points used should remain limited to country code/home city assignment, product usage, and general app usage data. Live location or inferred travel history based on location data should not be used for marketing.\n\n\nIf you are comfortable operationally with engaging the “traveller” segment, the targeting logic you described is defensible under GDPR and ePrivacy. \n\nHappy to review the final audience definition or message framing once LCM confirms the final setup 🙇‍♀️ ","2026-01-15T15:35:29.585Z"],["3813579","PFI-824487","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","*email:*6202635  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +andrus.treiberg@bolt.eu+{color}|mailto:andrus.treiberg@bolt.eu]{color:blue} {color}++{color:blue} +,+{color}+  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +antifraud@fondy.eu+{color}|mailto:antifraud@fondy.eu]{color:blue} {color}++{color:blue} +,+{color}+  {color:blue} +{color}[{color:blue} +chargeback_reports@bolt.eu+{color}|mailto:chargeback_reports@bolt.eu]{color:blue} {color}+ BOLT.EU \n| !/img/aval_white.png! |  *{color:gray} *Публічне акціонерне товариство «Райффайзен Банк»  \\\\ Public Joint Stock Company «Raiffeisen Bank»*{color}* | \n|  *АТ Райффайзен Банк* |  *ТОВ БОЛТ ОПЕРЕЙШНЗ УКРАЇНА* | \n|  *Телефон 0-800-500-738, 044-495-91-91* | | \n|  *E-mail:*  *[rb.acq@raiffeisen.ua|mailto:rb.acq@raiffeisen.ua]* | | \n| | | \n|  *15/01/2026* |  *№ 81-19-1-00/26/KK_560552_15012026_EM* |\n \n\n  \n\n *Повідомлення про утримання коштів* \n|  *{color:#172B4D} *Кліше*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Місце проведення транзакції*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Номер карти*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Дата трансакції*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Код авторизації*{color}* |  *{color:#172B4D} *Сума трансакції, грн.*{color}* | \n| 6202635 | bolt.eu; Volodymyrska ST. 79a; Kyiv; UKR | 4149 5110 **** 5000 | 2025-12-16 16:26:16 | 954923 | 2835.75 UAH |\n \n\n  \n\nІнформуємо, що суми, згідно зазначених трансакцій, будуть утримані з подальших надходжень Вашої Компанії по еквайрингу.\n Причина утримання: ненадання / невчасне надання документів або підтвердження можливості утримання з боку Компанії \n\n  \n\n *Коментар:* Торговець не надав документи у встановлені терміни  \n\n  \n\n  \n \n\n{color:#172B4D} Classification: PUBLIC{color}\n   \n\n *From:* Kateryna KHARCHENKO <kateryna.kharchenko@raiffeisen.ua>  *On Behalf Of*  Rb ACQ RBUA","2026-01-15T15:37:17.608Z"],["3813582","LSS-59572","LSS","alistair.blaza@bolt.eu","Alistair Blaza","Please find attached the countersigned NDA for archiving purposes. \n\n\n\nThanks,\n\n[^NDA FIRMADO.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T15:37:45.096Z"],["3813585","LSS-61436","LSS","sorina.mihai@bolt.eu","Sorina Mihai","Hey Alex,\n\nAre we ok with Omega comments? Can we agree and send it to signature? Thanks a lot!\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uVU5634Kd3iMWRMKWhIyWQfPtx6WH-ac/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uVU5634Kd3iMWRMKWhIyWQfPtx6WH-ac/edit|smart-link] \n\nSorina ","2026-01-15T15:38:07.614Z"],["3813587","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768491481179709]*{color}:\nYes those are driver based. We would need `CompanyManagerEventType.CAR_BLOCKED` and `CompanyManagerEventType.CAR_UNBLOCKED`\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:38:14.450Z"],["3813588","PFI-833810","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:07746941-2eee-430d-a2cf-f3aa307d9a17],\n\nThank you for escalating.\nSeems like they have a lot of failed payments and chargebacks at the same time, therefore yes, these users will be removed from the platform.\nThanks again for the heads up!\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T15:38:50.660Z"],["3813589","WFM-10002","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-15T15:39:26.558Z"],["3813592","PAW-14924","PAW","mihai.casandra@bolt.eu","Mihai Casandra","New confluence space for architecture: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7404519780/Architecture+Hub|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7404519780/Architecture+Hub|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T15:40:08.159Z"],["3813595","PAW-14768","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @udankobolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17086\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 15:41:27 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T15:41:28.021Z"],["3813597","WFM-10006","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-15T15:41:38.937Z"],["3813598","WD-22582","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff293eea-e5af-4325-9057-8f1a09bd3aa3] , it should be solved right now! I have excluded the item by removing the value and reached out to the Rentals Hardware team regarding the incorrect value. ","2026-01-15T15:41:48.981Z"],["3813599","DO-5805","DO","aleksandr.leontev@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Leontev","And this one too:\n[https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9715|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9715|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T15:42:14.551Z"],["3813601","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768491730348359]*{color}:\nI could not find any other fleet related comms on car scheduled suspensions. Can you please bring it up with your team. I believe you'd also want to review the different comms issued for different reasons, the pre-existing templates are less likely to be reusable here\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:42:22.785Z"],["3813602","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] thank you!\nI understand, that we have already asked them once about submitting proposals. However, the provided sheet is not suitable for sharing this type of information — namely proposed changes to the NDA, Code of Conduct, and supply agreement terms.\n\nSince the sheet is not designed to be completed with such information, even if we were to provide it in that format, *I cannot guarantee that our proposals would be accepted by the tender organizer*. Therefore, I wanted to flag this here in the ticket.\n\nNevertheless, tomorrow I will, to the best of my understanding, transfer our proposal from the drafts into the provided sheet.\n\nI would also like to note that *the documents submitted to the tender organizer must be in Danish*. I will therefore translate the document using DeepL, and a review by Danish-speaking colleagues will be needed. [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] would you be able to help with this? Thanks! ","2026-01-15T15:42:31.258Z"],["3813604","WD-22586","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:5da01f361027a00dc508e189] ! AS far as I understand, [~accountid:712020:ed089f76-267b-4dd0-9cc5-614d4e2b8e14]  should have the same permissions in WD as all other DWH team members, correct? Do you approve adding [~accountid:712020:ed089f76-267b-4dd0-9cc5-614d4e2b8e14] to WD Security group Bolt Financial Data Warehouse? ","2026-01-15T15:42:52.514Z"],["3813611","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768491792795849]*{color}:\nExactly there isnt any :smile: Just thought to write here, as you made the migration from hard blocks to scheduled blocks but missed the migration of these events to the scheduled blocks from hard blocks.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:43:26.381Z"],["3813612","MLC-3727","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","h3. Segments Testing\n\n* [Takeaway Checkout Completed +2 in the last 60 days|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/martech/warehouse/segment/delivery/edit/1470002?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n* Feedback\n** Generally, easy to work with and has logical steps.\n** Had a bug that when I add a new property rule, then the event’s timeframe moves immediately back to “Date range”. Although this wasn’t my chosen timeframe.\n** !Screen Recording 2026-01-15 at 16.28.01.mov|width=813,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-15 at 16.28.01.mov\"!\n Would be nice to have user properties as a rule as well. That’s what we can do in Braze, for example. Although in the Segment Ext part. \n** Would be nice to have options in the Comparison rule – {{exactly or more than}}. So it takes the added value into account also.\n** It would be nice to choose All Countries for the calculation. It’s a bit annoying to have to calculate each separately. ","2026-01-15T15:43:30.958Z"],["3813613","PFI-833710","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","[~accountid:712020:f28ada62-b0db-47a0-93bc-12a25ae2b2d6],\n\nIP address GPS location is one of the examples. Our Fraud engine takes different complex decisions and makes decisions based upon it. If it gets caught by the profiling rule, then the user is generally always considered bad.\n\nIf you would make a case on it, then please create a new ticket including all the users affected by it.\n\nKindly note that if the amount of users affected is below 5, then most likely there will not be a review as it is difficult to include Analysts and their resources for a case which barely affects the GMV on the larger scale.\n\nThank you for your understanding,\nMarten","2026-01-15T15:44:13.370Z"],["3813617","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] I am happy to help as much as possible. ","2026-01-15T15:46:03.429Z"],["3813618","WD-22556","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi Yuvi! Reassigning this ticket to you since it is related to BIRT layout. ","2026-01-15T15:46:27.281Z"],["3813619","WD-21923","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","!image-20260115-154628.png|width=487,alt=\"image-20260115-154628.png\"!\n\nPrevious:\n\n!image-20260115-154642.png|width=801,alt=\"image-20260115-154642.png\"!\n\nNew Conditional Rule Every 5th Expense Report on CZ,UK,ES,DE,SE. 3rd on CH,TH,NL,CN\n\n!image-20260115-154759.png|width=833,alt=\"image-20260115-154759.png\"!\n\nRemoved 3 values from the first and second company fields.","2026-01-15T15:48:29.703Z"],["3813620","BEE-1059","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Fixed by establishing fixed set of types and parsing strings into numbers when Number freeSolo autocomplete is used","2026-01-15T15:48:30.235Z"],["3813621","PFI-830354","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:d94524c3-94e8-4fa9-95f2-5afd20cbd32c],\n\nIf you’re able to compensate them the owed sum and approach it that way, then that is something that you should do.\nUser’s fraud calculation will be affected either way, unfortunately there is no way around it.\nThe user will not be whitelisted from our side.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T15:49:01.762Z"],["3813622","WD-21923","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:637f26822acfad92d7b13ddb] , \nthe following companies have been removed from the rule:\nBolt Services AB\nBolt Services DE GmbH\nBOLTEST TXFY SL\nas requested. Everything should work normally now. Please confirm.","2026-01-15T15:49:29.428Z"],["3813626","PFI-827602","PFI","joseph.kamange@bolt-outsource.eu","Joseph Kamange","Please assist with payment issue. ","2026-01-15T15:51:06.209Z"],["3813627","LSS-61369","LSS","jan.huk@bolt.eu","Jan Huk","Hello Karin,\nit was Friday late afternoon. Setting aside alerting PP dept as well as raising the ticket with legal, *I have also discussed the issue with rides GM* and he mentioned that this *Association in the process of liquidation anyway*, so in order for the thing not to get too much traction, and association does not play victim threatened by a big corporation, it would be better only to report it and threaten with legal action directly towards the association with out engaging in the discussion.\n\nI have *reported it to facebook as did some of the ops colleagues*. I have also raised the issue with legal dept - hence here. \n\nThere is *a new marketing specialist for Czechia and Slovakia* so I will allign with him on steps to take in such case. \n\nAgain, *it did not get traction in regular media* and people took it as AI generated thing, not a real case. But still it is defamation. \n\n\n----\n\nI am happy to raise and discuss cases like these (and they will get more and more common with AI) during Friday or Monday call to align on steps to take in such cases. ","2026-01-15T15:51:08.574Z"],["3813632","FX-3646","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Meruzhan Kerobyan [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768492307801279]*{color}:\nSure, we can have a call if needed.\nLast time was added there. <@U01HUBX6934> can you please answer the above questions?\n{quote}","2026-01-15T15:52:28.858Z"],["3813633","LSS-59281","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\ncan you kindly start having a first review of this? \n\nI guess this can wait beginning of next week.\n\nthanks a lot\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-15T15:52:31.578Z"],["3813638","L10N-27920","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:33.847Z"],["3813639","L10N-27934","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:33.860Z"],["3813640","L10N-27921","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:33.859Z"],["3813641","L10N-27919","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:33.921Z"],["3813642","L10N-27933","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:33.961Z"],["3813643","L10N-27930","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:33.982Z"],["3813644","L10N-27935","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.000Z"],["3813645","L10N-27924","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.032Z"],["3813646","L10N-27925","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.069Z"],["3813647","L10N-27932","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.100Z"],["3813648","L10N-27927","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.094Z"],["3813649","L10N-27923","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.101Z"],["3813650","L10N-27928","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.139Z"],["3813651","L10N-27918","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.181Z"],["3813652","L10N-27926","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.172Z"],["3813653","L10N-27931","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.194Z"],["3813654","L10N-27929","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.220Z"],["3813655","L10N-27922","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.230Z"],["3813656","L10N-27917","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:34.597Z"],["3813657","L10N-27915","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.682Z"],["3813658","L10N-27913","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.728Z"],["3813659","L10N-27901","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.858Z"],["3813660","L10N-27902","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.909Z"],["3813661","L10N-27906","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.877Z"],["3813662","L10N-27908","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.881Z"],["3813663","L10N-27910","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.892Z"],["3813664","L10N-27905","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.925Z"],["3813665","L10N-27914","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.941Z"],["3813666","L10N-27911","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:38.942Z"],["3813667","L10N-27909","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.046Z"],["3813668","L10N-27903","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.044Z"],["3813669","L10N-27912","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.060Z"],["3813670","L10N-27916","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.061Z"],["3813671","L10N-27907","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.094Z"],["3813672","L10N-27904","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.103Z"],["3813673","L10N-27900","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-15T15:53:39.191Z"],["3813679","LSS-61581","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Partner reached out in regards of IBAN being incorrect on the Deutch side. Has been replaced with the correct one from the English side. ","2026-01-15T15:55:22.737Z"],["3813680","PFI-833822","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:a65fbd35-40e8-465a-b00a-02c5c115eff0],\n\nDevice UID suspension lifted for *C263AAB5-9F18-4B6E-866E-337AE7572714.*\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-15T15:56:26.914Z"],["3813681","LSS-61460","LSS","joshua.okeleke@bolt.eu","Josh Okeleke","Hi Thomas,\n\nThanks for Getting back to me. Happy to hop on a quick call this PM to talk\nit through.\n\nTo confirm the above, we've already signed the partnership agreement and\nthe ask is to clarify if there will be any privacy issues from our side\nonce we start sharing data wit the pilot\n\nJosh","2026-01-15T15:56:41.031Z"],["3813683","LSS-61441","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343457|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343457|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T15:57:43.436Z"],["3813686","BP-13450","BP","fahad.khan@bolt.eu","Fahad Ahmed Khan","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] [~accountid:712020:3c6bcc42-4172-4c4d-b924-e17fb5f0a336] I updated acceptance criteria","2026-01-15T15:58:56.816Z"],["3813689","PFI-823399","PFI","israel.kizito@bolt-outsource.eu","Israel Kizito","We are yet to receive an update on this case. Kindly review.","2026-01-15T15:59:41.290Z"],["3813690","PFI-833857","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:00:18.210Z"],["3813692","LSS-61591","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:0dcccdab-40ef-4e81-988a-67af3ae07691] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt Confirm Request_Jan 7th 2026_ Filled (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T16:00:55.312Z"],["3813694","LSS-61591","LSS","paolo.catani@bolt.eu","Paolo Catani","Legend!","2026-01-15T16:01:49.190Z"],["3813695","PFI-833858","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:02:01.398Z"],["3813696","FX-3646","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Marek Pagel [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768492914618249]*{color}:\nI believe when we added Driver Portal, the effort was about 1mw. The lux one was already smoother thanks to the previous one, but when rounded up, I would still say 1mw. But both of these were done by people familiar with the repo for projects somewhat similar to each other.\nI know Max was very bullish on the idea and maybe I’m too modest, but I’m still not sure our repo should be the base of the monorepo. There might be other repos with better or more generic/reusable tooling and setup (e.g. web, some delivery teams) maintained by developers with more FE expertise.\nSaying that, I’m not against adding more projects to ours and I’m sure it is going to be faster for you than starting from the scratch (unless setting up FE projects is second nature for you)\n{quote}","2026-01-15T16:02:31.447Z"],["3813697","PFI-830013","PFI","israel.kizito@bolt-outsource.eu","Israel Kizito","Hello Team,\nWe are yet to receive a resolution on this issue. Kindly review.","2026-01-15T16:02:43.594Z"],["3813701","PFI-833861","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:03:21.365Z"],["3813703","PFI-833862","PFI","natia.balamtsarashvili@bolt.eu","Natia Balamtsarashvili","[^Receipt_1768491658783.pdf]","2026-01-15T16:04:06.660Z"],["3813704","PFI-833862","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T16:04:09.009Z"],["3813706","PFI-833863","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:04:59.310Z"],["3813707","PFI-833864","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:06:25.325Z"],["3813710","PFI-833775","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:5e4e4eadab90210c8de19b32],\n\nThank you for escalating, we have also suspended some additional accounts that were in relation to these accounts in order to further restrict their devices.\n\nIn these cases there is not very much for us to do besides suspending the users, mainly because at the end of the day, this is internal business fraud from their own side, they must be accepting the users in order for them to have access, there is no real other way for the users to  get in.\n\nFor now, the users and the ones related are now suspended.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-15T16:06:41.429Z"],["3813711","SREDESK-7426","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","For the record and future reference by SREs, in the AWS main account →  AWS Systems Manager → Parameter Store → {{/atlantis/databricks/profiles}} path, profiles are defined base64 coded.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02NYDW87CN/p1740655489714079?thread_ts=1740655467.204799&cid=C02NYDW87CN|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02NYDW87CN/p1740655489714079?thread_ts=1740655467.204799&cid=C02NYDW87CN|smart-link] \n\n!image-20260115-160557.png|width=1083,alt=\"image-20260115-160557.png\"!","2026-01-15T16:06:59.972Z"],["3813713","LSS-61460","LSS","joshua.okeleke@bolt.eu","Josh Okeleke","In response to this question: I believe the team got input from: Dawit\nVillarzu","2026-01-15T16:07:46.283Z"],["3813718","PFI-833865","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:08:10.926Z"],["3813721","PFI-833866","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:09:19.603Z"],["3813723","SREDESK-7427","SREDESK","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","After the PR ([https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15413|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15413|smart-link] ) has been applied by DBRE, we have network connectivity between k8s runner pod and mysql/tidb, we can close this ticket now 🙂 ","2026-01-15T16:09:30.219Z"],["3813724","PFI-833710","PFI","ivaylo.georgiev@bolt.eu","Ivaylo Georgiev","Yeah, I suppose so, but I thought IP address would be related to “CUDDO_PROFILING_CREATION_IP” and not the destination location. Also, the GPS location wouldn’t usually consider height, so if people would make an account from the 1st, 2nd, 3rd floor, I assume the person on the 5th will receive the error, hence why, I’m enquiring about its accuracy. \n\n","2026-01-15T16:09:33.992Z"],["3813726","LSS-58567","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey team!\n\nOn the second tab of the document previously provided, we added:\n\n* Summary of external counsel advise;\n* Proposed next steps;\n* Full legal advice provided by external counsel.\n\nYou can find it [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R3aocNewCd_EURV-QkisK7xny1bXQYSN8xUlHu3yIhI/edit?tab=t.dvdr79xfx6hx].\n\nWe are happy to arrange a call if you want to discuss this.\n\nOtherwise, please let us know your thoughts so we can start drafting the agreement.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T16:09:55.096Z"],["3813727","UXA-2208","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","TODO: clarify if oidc-provider is called by external clients and if we can detect if internal service is calling oidc-provider.","2026-01-15T16:10:08.468Z"],["3813728","PFI-833867","PFI","marcela.castillo@bolt-outsource.eu","Marcela Soledad Filizzola Castillo","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 13.09.13.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 13.09.18.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:10:18.687Z"],["3813729","PFI-833868","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T16:10:35.883Z"],["3813730","LOC-4878","LOC","ariana.saplana@bolt.eu","Ariana Saplana","When you receive and sign the quote, you can store it here [~accountid:63abfbf46f068efec8f6b8f8] > [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1FY-2lljGY0eotUcCQ4xoNVgE_oNWptys|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1FY-2lljGY0eotUcCQ4xoNVgE_oNWptys|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T16:10:54.669Z"],["3813737","LSS-48620","LSS","emilie.chesse@bolt.eu","Emilie Chesse","Thanks and understood [~accountid:61cc1c959ee70a00680edd89] , we’ll discuss this among the team and see which approach we adopt","2026-01-15T16:15:04.109Z"],["3813738","PFI-833823","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:628b90a588ebba006f94b43c],\n\nWe already have rules in place for this, that is also evident from the order that you have linked, our rules are already working and flagging the orders as required.\n\nThese flags are not notified to the Driver, main reason is that we do not want them to know that we are on their suspicious activities. Their bonuses get removed/orders get fully refunded, this is generally enough for the drivers to stop the fraudulent activities, as they see that their schemes are not working, meaning that we keep the driver without losing GMV, even though they attempted.\n\nFor us to provide you with the data requested, we would need a case for it first, otherwise it is hard to justify including Analysts and their resources.\nI can however confirm, that this pattern is already known to us and rules are in place to protect us.\n\nIf you would still like to receive the data mentioned, then please submit a new ticket with at least over 5 cases within the same timeframe.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-15T16:15:07.537Z"],["3813741","LSS-61447","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343466|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343466|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T16:15:44.659Z"],["3813747","FX-3436","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768493756143259]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3436 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T16:16:40.357Z"],["3813749","LSS-61285","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:2bd6b1d7-fd05-480e-8362-30ae2b3fc776] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Branding Contract - Bolt Club Fleet BSH Fahrdienst GmbH (1).pdf] ","2026-01-15T16:17:08.526Z"],["3813750","WD-22572","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:61c07bf9a54af90069a42e2f] , thank you for helping out. \nI have set up a conditional rule that now allows Ad Hoc Bank Transactions involving LA 1070 to only happen with Spend Category Bank Deposits up to 3M (BS). \n\nI have tested the previous transaction done by Karin in SBX and got this error:\n\n!image-20260115-161618.png|width=773,alt=\"image-20260115-161618.png\"!\n\n\n\nWhen I change Spend category to Bank Deposits up to 3m (BS): \n\n!image-20260115-161729.png|width=757,alt=\"image-20260115-161729.png\"!\n\nNow this rule works only with account 1070 so no other Ad Hoc Bank Transactions (with other Ledger Accounts ) should be affected. \nI kindly ask you to communicate this change to the Payments team (Janeli and her team) in a public channel so everyone is aware of the change that was done here. \nThank you! Let me know if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-15T16:19:20.216Z"],["3813751","LSS-58436","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hey [~accountid:712020:3af8f992-95ee-44bb-8d3c-9998350e5e42]. Thank you for the clarification.\n\nHere are the [Special Terms|https://docs.google.com/document/d/10Zjt0przlPqpZweIgjD6IRnsPjhhpe6E/edit] with the amendments proposed by the client, for their review.\n\nResponding to your question - Yes, anytime there is a credit limit agreed with the client, this should be reflected in the Special Terms.","2026-01-15T16:19:22.079Z"],["3813752","LSS-57822","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi Team,\n\nThanks for clarifying that the goal.\n\nI wanted to share a few thoughts from the Legal side, after discussing this with Central Legal:\n\n*Selfie checks as a fraud prevention tool:*\nFrom a legal perspective, there’s no issue with using selfie verification in cases of suspected fraud - for example, where we believe a courier profile may be transferred or accessed by an unauthorized individual. In fact, this kind of check helps us mitigate legal and compliance risks, and ensures that only properly verified individuals operate on the platform.\n\nThis is especially relevant in contexts such as:\n\n* Immigration/work permit compliance,\n* Ensuring fleets do not bypass our onboarding procedures,\n* Minimizing risks of impersonation or unauthorized access.\n\nOn a *reclassification risk perspective,* we believe that the reclassification risk remains low when selfie checks are used in response to fraud suspicion, because this provides a clear, legitimate justification for the verification. In such cases, the check is not about controlling the courier’s work, but rather about verifying the identity of the individual accessing the platform, which is a basic compliance requirement.\n\nHowever, if selfie checks were to be triggered routinely for all contact detail changes, regardless of any fraud indicators, this could be seen as a broader control mechanism and might carry higher reclassification sensitivity. That’s why we see the fraud-linked use as safer and more legally defensible.\n\nFrom a Privacy standpoint, we believe our current Privacy Policy already allows for identity verification in cases of “unusual activity,” which should cover situations involving suspected fraud.\n[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] - could you please confirm if you agree that this is already covered, or if a broader use case would require any updates?\n\n*Recommendation:*\nFor the reasons enhanced above, we believe it is OK  to use the selfie check verification, but we would recommend using it only in cases where there is suspicion of fraud. This approach is:\n\n* Legally proportionate and (in principle) covered under our Privacy Policy,\n* Backed by a clear legitimate interest (identity security, immigration compliance, fraud prevention),\n* Defensible from a reclassification perspective, as it avoids suggesting control over how the work is performed, and focuses solely on _who_ is accessing the account.\n\nIf you’re concerned that many fraud cases are going undetected, we suggest exploring additional risk signals or flags (e.g. frequent number changes, fleet behavior patterns) to trigger selfie checks more often — but still tied to an identifiable risk, rather than applying it blanketly.\n\nLet me know if this is something you’d be open to discussing further, or if there’s a strong operational reason for broader implementation.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T16:19:56.977Z"],["3813753","MKP-9517","MKP","alexandr.kuldin@bolt.eu","Alexandr Kuldin","{noformat}select\n  lg.created,\n  lg.`id`,\n  lg.created_date,\n  lg.state,\n  lc.created,\n  lg.driver_destination_location_id,\n  lc.created_date,\n  d.created,\n  lc.driver_destination_id,\n  d.created_date,\n  d.`type`,\n  d.address\nfrom ng_public_spark.dispatch_pref_driver_destination_log lg\nleft join ng_public_spark.dispatch_pref_driver_destination_location lc\n  on lc.`id` = lg.driver_destination_location_id and lc.driver_city_id = lg.driver_city_id\nleft join ng_public_spark.dispatch_pref_driver_destination d\n  on d.`id` = lc.driver_destination_id and d.driver_city_id = lc.driver_city_id\nwhere lg.driver_id = 8208603\norder by lg.created desc{noformat}\n\n[^driver_destination_logs.csv]\n\n{noformat}select d.created, d.`id`, d.created_date, d.`type`, d.address, d.lat, d.lng  from ng_public_spark.dispatch_pref_driver_destination d\nwhere d.driver_id = 8208603 and d.driver_city_id = 1\norder by d.created desc{noformat}\n\n[^driver_destinations.csv]\n\n","2026-01-15T16:20:22.048Z"],["3813754","LSS-61431","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:622b6eb2302c6b006af70509], I’ve now reviewed the Driver Giveaway T&Cs and suggested a small number of targeted amendments directly in the document, which are clearly marked so you can see exactly what has changed.\n\nI’ve also added *comments in the document where certain links do not appear to work*, so these can be checked and corrected before launch.\n\nOne point to clarify before we finalise: you mentioned that the giveaway is open to *all drivers, mainly around the Manchester area*. However, the definition of *“Winner(s)”* currently states that “_one winner will be selected from each of the following geographical areas: London, Birmingham, and the Rest of the UK”_. Can you please confirm whether this is accurate? Once confirmed, we can make sure the *correct driver terms and geographic framing* are applied consistently.\n\nHappy to discuss or adjust once we have confirmation 🙂 ","2026-01-15T16:20:31.722Z"],["3813755","WD-22572","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","!image-20260115-162047.png|width=623,alt=\"image-20260115-162047.png\"!\n\n!image-20260115-162140.png|width=709,alt=\"image-20260115-162140.png\"!","2026-01-15T16:21:48.496Z"],["3813756","LSS-61528","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:dc012e17-7e04-4ad8-8750-81fc7f7c6047] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached. [^Xerox Scan 2026-01-12 03.54.55 PM (d827ca09-3464-4a3b-8f37-671d747ed9c4).pdf] ","2026-01-15T16:22:00.995Z"],["3813757","PFI-833710","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:f28ada62-b0db-47a0-93bc-12a25ae2b2d6],\n\nPlease make an official case via a new SD ticket.\n\nAdditionally, kindly include roughly around 10 users within similar timeframe (for example 10 users within a week), below that we can not really justify including our Analysts and their resources.\n\nKind regards,\nMarten","2026-01-15T16:22:25.419Z"],["3813759","LSS-61665","LSS","vladislav.kochetov@bolt.eu","Vladislav Kochetov","[^Contract Aliaksei Charankevich Signed.pdf] _(10.65 MB)_","2026-01-15T16:22:32.555Z"],["3813760","PFI-833871","PFI","oluchi.akor@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluchi Akor","[^transaction-confirmation-report_en_602c1b.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-15T16:23:19.319Z"],["3813768","LSS-61666","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","[^UPL-1(6) SENAGO MF.pdf] _(1.85 MB)_\n\n[^UPL-1(6) Senago RB.pdf] _(1.85 MB)_\n\n[^Senago_ZAW-FA (KSEF)_Ahto Kink_read only.pdf] _(236 kB)_\n\n[^E-Urzad Skarbowy Senago.pdf] _(83 kB)_","2026-01-15T16:27:08.748Z"],["3813769","LSS-61666","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","cc [~accountid:62bd9335018dea0d40751f4b] ","2026-01-15T16:27:29.039Z"],["3813771","SREDESK-7426","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","I added the new profile.\nNow I will redeploy Atlantis:\n\n!image-20260115-162820.png|width=1083,alt=\"image-20260115-162820.png\"!","2026-01-15T16:28:29.450Z"],["3813773","PFI-832832","PFI","kati.pruel@bolt.eu","Kati Pruel","Hi,\nI am looping in [~accountid:63ec99ebaf665dfde890c2e3] because local entity is providing support service and not receiving the funds that are currently needed to be refunded. ","2026-01-15T16:29:02.505Z"],["3813778","PFI-825462","PFI","raimot.abdullahi@bolt-outsource.eu","Raimot Abdullahi","Hi team, Payment is yet to reflect, please assist.","2026-01-15T16:32:30.307Z"],["3813781","PFI-833875","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^transaction-confirmation-report_en_258bf4 (2).pdf]","2026-01-15T16:33:50.778Z"],["3813786","CEBF-1835","CEBF","oleg.demkiv@bolt.eu","Oleh Demkiv","[~accountid:712020:0fcc8631-9d3d-40f3-be4c-5d72a07f50fa] [~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] team, would appreciate if you take a look at this one. Maybe I forgot something","2026-01-15T16:36:40.923Z"],["3813789","CEBF-1835","CEBF","oleg.demkiv@bolt.eu","Oleh Demkiv","[~accountid:6218cbe4468c2e007170c08b] to update tomorrow with:\n\n{quote}Call = Call, Email = Email, Booked meeting = Event, Walkin = Task (Meet in person), Action Item = Task, LinkedIn = Task{quote}","2026-01-15T16:37:35.665Z"],["3813791","RLONE-501","RLONE","niklas.svegeboe@bolt.eu","Niklas Svegeboe","FYI [~accountid:712020:7905b35a-ac36-42a0-a1c2-1b9fbcc2a4bb] , since we also had an existing tickets on reviewing pricing on other categories, I linked them. We could also delete one to only keep one ticket - up to you!","2026-01-15T16:38:26.356Z"],["3813793","LSS-61453","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343471|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343471|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T16:38:33.193Z"],["3813799","RLONE-501","RLONE","niklas.svegeboe@bolt.eu","Niklas Svegeboe","AY: Here are my [suggestions|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09TZ23589M/p1768487281906269?thread_ts=1768318793.537219&cid=C09TZ23589M] for comfort and premium:\n\nIncrease min price to 129 and 149 (uber min price 139 and 159)\nIncrease multiplier for start rate, distance and time rates to 1.3 and 1.42 (8.3% and 15.4% increase)\nAdd long distance multiplier of 1.4 and 1.5 to close the increasing price gap in longer distance trips\n\nWe would expect to be ~10% below but with a higher surge coefficient it should make up for it\n\nAll [calc here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1uN2ZE9EiPzw3npOC1JABAj19pw5oXS4XtxqQvS6UrNo/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-15T16:39:05.368Z"],["3813800","MP-3480","MP","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nHorizontal scrolling views (especially BDUI elements if any) snap behaviour","2026-01-15T16:40:44.135Z"],["3813802","CEBF-1835","CEBF","martin.stefanec@bolt.eu","Jimmy Štefanec","[~accountid:6218cbe4468c2e007170c08b] Its perfect! Only 1 note. Values - Successful / Unsuccessful were hidden from users. They exist for the filtering purposes, e.g. if call is unaswered => unsuccessful and than in reporting you can filter out only successfull call dispositions (as maybe only those should be counted as proper sales activity)","2026-01-15T16:41:38.476Z"],["3813803","LSS-61477","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hello [~accountid:61b9ef0e9e8a370068af893c], as confirmed by Elisabetta, no red flag on launching a pilot of this tiered offer test. In addition to Elisabetta’s question, please could you also share for review the communication you would like to send and confirm how you will collect driver’s acknowledgment to this communication? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-15T16:41:44.052Z"],["3813804","LSS-61606","LSS","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","Hi [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] [~accountid:60acb13f1155bb006fce252c] ,\n\nIf I read the claim correctly, the provider is claiming that they should not bear the marketing costs on food and delivery, pursuant to Clause 4.8 of the Partner Agreement for the Use of the Bolt Food Platform (the Agreement) and its Annex 1 \"Service Level Requirements\" - the prices of the Goods indicated on the Bolt Food platform cannot be higher than the price of the same Goods at the Partner’s establishment.\n\nFor example, \n\n* Order value per Bolt Food App = $10\n* Discount to eater = $2\n* Cost-sharing on discount to eater between Bolt and provider = 50:50\n** Provider funded discount = $1 \n* Order value from provider pov = $9 (below the Bolt Food App $10)\n* Now, the provider is asking for the $1 back.  \n\nWould you please revisit and share the Agreement and Annex 1 for further discussion?  \n\nPlease correct me if I am wrong. \n\nThank you.","2026-01-15T16:42:23.012Z"],["3813805","WD-22573","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska"," it goes under the tax id type, so they can be easily added to Tax ID table and connected to countries","2026-01-15T16:43:30.250Z"],["3813806","RCE-355","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768495439203439]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@azza.ltifi>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-355] `Test selfie check feature in Malta for select drivers` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T16:44:13.887Z"],["3813807","LSS-61031","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] I went over the document and I have no major concerns overall. I only edited the name of Bolt company correctly: It should be Bolt Operation*S* OU, not Bolt Operation OU, and changed Republic of Estland for Estonia. Also, added Ahto Kink, Director in page 2 as signer. \n\nMoreover, we need to add Client (Bolt) email address in Schedule A for DocuSign signer ([ahto.kink@bolt.eu|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] is added) and the respective email for e-invoices. We also need to select Group Billing if we want to have it.   \n\nThis is only a *Service Order* between Bolt (Ops OU) and Silverflow that adds to the agreement we already have (signed last year on December). This will let Bolt to use Silverflow's payment processing services with an +additional acquirer+ (Solidgate in this case), in addition to Deutsche Bank.\n\nNote:\n\n* Has a *3-year initial term.* Confirm this is ok. \n* Covers multiple payment schemes: VISA, Mastercard, Bancontact, Diners, and Amex\n* Services include authorization, clearing, settlement, 3DS authentication, chargeback processing, tokenization, and others not selected. Please confirm the selection in the Order Form is accurate. \n* *Silverflow is waiving EUR 20,000 in one-off fees* for adding the additional acquirer. \n* \"Top Tier Pricing\": all transactions are charged based on total monthly volume. Confirm this is ok. \n\nIf you have no concerns, we can ask Silverflow if they want to start the signing process or how do they prefer to move forward. Here is the edited document: [^20251215KK_Bolt_Silverflow SO - Direct Merchant & Solid_Bot review.docx] \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-15T16:44:15.912Z"],["3813808","LSS-61494","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] ! Currently the document is pending on both parties.","2026-01-15T16:44:16.583Z"],["3813809","PAW-14929","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17174\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-15 16:44:38 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-15T16:44:38.224Z"],["3813811","LSS-61581","LSS","dennis.hennemann@bolt.eu","Dennis Hennemann","Hey, yeah he just sent me a message as well. did you already replace it?","2026-01-15T16:45:54.504Z"],["3813812","LSS-61581","LSS","dennis.hennemann@bolt.eu","Dennis Hennemann","so nothing to do from my side?","2026-01-15T16:46:00.259Z"],["3813813","WD-22550","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] [~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a]  🙏 ","2026-01-15T16:46:22.390Z"],["3813816","RSE-8","RSE","mykola.mozghovyi@bolt.eu","Mykola Mozghovyi","this is definetly not 1 estimate anymore","2026-01-15T16:47:48.543Z"],["3813817","LSS-61494","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343472|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343472|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T16:48:00.120Z"],["3813821","HS-28961","HS","natavan.gasimzade@bolt.eu","Natavan Gasimzade","Hi [~accountid:712020:233a6d49-7634-40c9-bf6d-95ce9d2980e0], \nI have recently renewed my national ID card, as the previous one was nearing its expiration date. The ID number remains the same, and I received the new card today.\n\nFor your reference, my passport number is: C04008091\n\nGovernment ID: 6VRAUQ0 \nI have uploaded scanned copies of both documents below for your visibility. \n\n\n[^passport.pdf]\n[^shexsiyyet vesiqesi.pdf]\n\nThank you in advance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nNatavan","2026-01-15T16:49:05.719Z"],["3813822","SUPX-2317","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","*Grzegorz Brotoń* [Jan 15, 2026 6:45 PM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768495514304659?thread_ts=1768308504.508939&cid=C064FCFAT0S] in Slack channel [#dev-support-automation-support|https://slack.com/app_redirect?channel=C064FCFAT0S]\n\n{quote}Yea, seems like this is fix:\n```if (eventRow.event_data.attempt_automatic_solution === false) {{quote}\n\n    snapshot.automationData = {\n        ...snapshot.automationData,\n        automation_requested: null,\n    };```","2026-01-15T16:49:14.579Z"],["3813823","WD-22580","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Hi [~accountid:712020:c8f6d6ec-ae4a-4cf3-9078-0632b32a5d28] Could you provide the example (invoice number).","2026-01-15T16:49:34.990Z"],["3813826","LSS-60696","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:22f1d9b5-1599-49ef-8ecd-0c67511d3425],\n\nUnfortunately, we’re unable to follow the signing process proposed by the client.\n\nCould you please ask them to sign the document and return it to us duly executed? We will then arrange the signature on our side and send them back the fully executed version.\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-15T16:50:59.910Z"],["3813828","LSS-61513","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343473|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343473|smart-link]  ","2026-01-15T16:52:46.726Z"],["3813829","LSS-61668","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","[^410-22.2PELSB_BOLT_23-05-2024.pdf] _(684 kB)_\n\n[^oficio (1).pdf] _(6.40 MB)_","2026-01-15T16:52:49.594Z"],["3813832","CEBF-1833","CEBF","pavlo.savenko@bolt.eu","Pavlo Savenko","[~accountid:712020:fc274657-f7b5-4366-9f2d-5ec68865cf48] its calculating correctly, scroll the table down and you will see more values)","2026-01-15T16:54:17.995Z"],["3813833","LSS-61668","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","similar case: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57999?search_id=9793bda6-f84e-4764-8b31-e64f1b0d411a|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57999?search_id=9793bda6-f84e-4764-8b31-e64f1b0d411a]","2026-01-15T16:54:24.353Z"],["3813835","LSS-61372","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","*Analysis:*\n\n* User reached out via [malmqvistjohan499@gmail.com|mailto:malmqvistjohan499@gmail.com] on [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/720657633] and [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722994749] - this is the email address that was associated with the account at the time of creation.\n* 20 Sept 2025 - Account appears to have been created with device 85B956B3-CB7F-48BF-88C9-909EE11BCF9F - OG details on account are name: Johan Malmqvist, email: [malmqvistjohan499@gmail.com|mailto:malmqvistjohan499@gmail.com], phone number: +46760292154\n* 21 Sept 2025 - account details are changed to name: “Abdullahi Fidow”. Those changes were made with the same device used to create the account - 85B956B3-CB7F-48BF-88C9-909EE11BCF9F.\n* On 24 Sept 2025, 1 Oct 2025, and 11 Jan 2026, one (same) new device logs in the account via the phone number associated with the account + cross-app: 152E2A9B-53A3-427F-A3D8-1429B4B3DA17\n* The rides ([1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2336773944/574?orderTryId=3003007115], [2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2342425974/574?orderTryId=3012499884])disputed by the alleged OG account owner were booked by device 152E2A9B-53A3-427F-A3D8-1429B4B3DA17\n\nTo me, this doesn’t seem to be a phone number recycling case as the same phone number used to create the account was used to log into the account with another device 3 days after the creation of the account. The timeline seems too short for a phone number recycling case to materialise.\n\n*Current suspicion:*\n\n* OTP sharing back in Sept? This does not explain the name change one day after creating the account.\n\n*Reaching out to Identity team:* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS/p1768496062089229|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06R63EQ6CS/p1768496062089229|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T16:55:16.877Z"],["3813836","LSS-61496","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343476|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343476|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T16:55:35.694Z"],["3813837","LSS-61668","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hello [~accountid:5f7aaad6021acf0076d55a90] . Could you please provide the information that is being requested?\nThank you!","2026-01-15T16:55:40.974Z"],["3813839","CNT-459","CNT","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","Hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] as result we have 3 page templates. They are still quite similar. Unfortunately, I had very limited time to make a deeper research. But I think Page 3 (City-specific template) should be slightly different in terms of copy. Because my vacation starts tomorrow, I have to give you quite raw version. \n\nHere are all 3 page templates for Driver/earn section: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YGeY9uYsz0HuiPB8_mdaqTSplxSA_XyoXtoUhGkcR6Y/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YGeY9uYsz0HuiPB8_mdaqTSplxSA_XyoXtoUhGkcR6Y/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nIdeally, I would spend a bit more time to provide final layout. Maybe Robert will have additional recommendations. Let’s see. ","2026-01-15T16:56:28.089Z"],["3813841","PFI-823399","PFI","marvellous.paul@bolt-outsource.eu","Marvellous Paul","Hi Team,\n\nWe are still expecting a response as regarding the SD raised.","2026-01-15T16:57:41.889Z"],["3813842","LSS-61372","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d27c06d8-7953-45bd-a52f-766a72d84de8] - thanks for escalating this issue. I am looking into it with the Identity team. I suggest refraining from giving further refunds to the user at this time - it is not yet clear whether the user is actually at the source of the issue himself (i.e., shared his credentials/OTP with another person) or if the issue happened on Bolt’s side (very unlikely from the data I can see so far). In cases where Bolt is not at fault, refunds are typically not issued.\n\nI will update this ticket as soon as I hear back from the Identity team - please hang tight 🙏 ","2026-01-15T16:57:50.820Z"],["3813845","BZNS-129","BZNS","fahad.khan@bolt.eu","Fahad Ahmed Khan","Done in [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/155507|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/155507|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T16:58:53.128Z"],["3813847","WD-22575","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] , \nam I understanding this correctly that some functionality in Telema which should be working is not working?\nDo you have an example of the invoice? \nPlease do screenshots from Telema (with invoice number). Also in Workday and point out where the issue is as from the provided data I’m unable to understand it 🙂 \n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T16:59:19.671Z"],["3813848","PFI-833886","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T17:00:29.717Z"],["3813849","PFI-833862","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-15T17:00:50.793Z"],["3813850","LSS-58897","LSS","britt.doll@bolt.eu","Britt Doll","# Won't need any personal data from riders as the mechanism will be if they take any qualifying Hopp ride during the promo they will automatically be entered into the campaign\n# Again, no personal data needed as we will simply pull who has completed the highest amount of qualifying rides to be declared the winner\n# No personal data needed. Again, we run a query to see has completed the most amount of qualifying rides\n# Once determined, we will reach out to the winner with the email address associated on their existing Hopp account\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-15T17:00:51.220Z"],["3813853","LSS-61638","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], can I please check if you tried to use the [Custom ChatGPT|https://chatgpt.com/g/g-6942c8f6e7c0819190a172cf405a8970-bolt-unmanned-office-licence-assistant] that I created before raising this ticket to the Legal team?\n\nI have ran this review through the GPT and [here are the results|https://chatgpt.com/share/e/69691df1-c7c8-8001-bb17-c272032ad130]. There’s no longer any need to raise a legal ticket when the results are like this, unless of course you have any specific queries or believe the custom GPT is incorrect. For example, if another entity needed to be added (in this case, Bolt Services UK Limited as an additional licensee alongside Bolt Operations UK Limited if you were not happy with the office space only permitting use solely in connection with the Bolt Flex Private Hire Operator licence).\n\nPlease do let me know if anything is unclear and I’ll be happy to help! 🙂 \n\nFor the sake of the ticket, this is approved by legal (/) \n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T17:05:49.698Z"],["3813856","LSS-60746","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] Please let me know if you checked my comments and if there is anything else that should be amended or clarified. Thank you!","2026-01-15T17:08:29.317Z"],["3813857","SREDESK-7426","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Related Slack thread:\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01UZQN086B/p1733752635515779|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01UZQN086B/p1733752635515779|smart-link] \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15405/changes#diff-846a97c198bf54d2129389567b39fa4dd0ed8af4017832950118740b085aa77b|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15405/changes#diff-846a97c198bf54d2129389567b39fa4dd0ed8af4017832950118740b085aa77b] \n\n{noformat}running 'sh -c' 'inv plan -e '-no-color -input=false -out=$PLANFILE' > /dev/null' in '/home/atlantis/.atlantis/repos/bolteu/terraform-main/15405/default/dataeng/eu-central-1/databricks/ext-hub/workspace': exit status 1: running \"inv plan -e '-no-color -input=false -out=$PLANFILE' > /dev/null\" in \"/home/atlantis/.atlantis/repos/bolteu/terraform-main/15405/default/dataeng/eu-central-1/databricks/ext-hub/workspace\": \n\nError: validate: more than one authorization method configured: google and pat. Config: host=https://bolt-ext-hub.cloud.databricks.com, token=***, profile=ext-hub, google_credentials=***. Env: GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS\n\n  with provider[\"registry.terraform.io/databricks/databricks\"],\n  on main.tf line 13, in provider \"databricks\":\n  13: provider \"databricks\" {{noformat}","2026-01-15T17:10:03.935Z"],["3813858","DRAG101-463","DRAG101","tom.evans@bolt.eu","Tom Evans","[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] Ok, thanks for explanation. Please let me know ETA! For sample and arrival in HQ. Thanks! \nCan they also confirm whether a bigger chip has bigger range? Feedback form SW questioned the range of first sample.\nAlso, what’s the ETA to find other suppliers. Thanks! \n","2026-01-15T17:10:26.778Z"],["3813862","PFI-832686","PFI","yuliia.nenasheva@bolt.eu","Yuliia Nenasheva","payout rejected","2026-01-15T17:12:14.671Z"],["3813864","LSS-61374","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:e08f01ef-2849-432e-9ba1-dd2eb3b1ff44] - thanks for escalating this. I can see from the [BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/721379316] that the driver already shared a [link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Zx-SzuEdXDKGtmONrblGwY8zC6aMJprp/view?usp=drivesdk] to a recording, the timestamps of which seem to correspond to the ride reported to the passenger: \n\n* Reported [ride|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1505173483/387?orderTryId=2879081485]: start 15:29, end 16:05\n* Timestamp on shared video: 15:36 to 15:39\n\nAre you able to work with this, or do you still need further guidance from my side? \n\nIf you need a timeframe that covers the entire ride in question, then I suggest to provide a larger time period to the driver in order to lower the chances of passenger re-identification, for example 15:00 to 18:00 (the latter is the end of the next ride he handled). Since the driver was inactive for long periods before and after those two rides back to back, this is the best we can do while following a data minimisation approach.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 7.12.53 PM.png|width=639,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 7.12.53 PM.png\"!","2026-01-15T17:14:07.710Z"],["3813865","PFI-833888","PFI","chanita.saengprapacharoen@bolt-outsource.eu","Chanita Saengprapacharoen","!image-20260115-170937.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-170952.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-171008.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:14:16.315Z"],["3813869","LSS-61638","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] , I tried to open the link from your previous message but it wasn’t opening and still isn’t. Is there a different link?","2026-01-15T17:16:37.902Z"],["3813870","IOTTEAM-289","IOTTEAM","tom.evans@bolt.eu","Tom Evans","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] sure! as long as we have the NFC unlock as an epic I think it’s fine","2026-01-15T17:17:34.126Z"],["3813871","DSR-2071","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] This matter can be closed per correspondence with external counsel ([Samir Buhl|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cx5skDCcX2dhJKhgAtI8b8zI426e7jBu/view?usp=sharing]) dated 22 December 2025, as a contingent of a settlement agreement, both data subjects waived request to completed DSAR although only one data subject formally withdrew via notification. External counsel advised that they would engage with Bolt only if required.","2026-01-15T17:18:44.441Z"],["3813872","LSS-60495","LSS","toomas.parts@bolt.eu","Toomas-Hendrik Parts","Hi! Auditors came back with the following:\n\n\n\n_Thank you for sharing the documents. Our AML team had a look at the ID,  it doesn't show who certified it? The signature looks like the name of the individual in the ID, but we can't accept individuals certifying their own ID. Only reason that they feel this is the case, there is no name of the independent certifier on the document. Please would it be possible to get the ID certified again?_\n\n_Please find below guidance for independent certification and the process to be followed:_\n\n* _\"Independent certification of documents can be undertaken by a PwC employee; an independent lawyer, accountant or public notary; or Consulate or Embassy staff. Alternatively, a document can be certified by an employee/representative of the Client, provided that PwC can evidence the individual who has certified the document performs a legal or accountancy role within the client, e.g Legal Counsel or equivalent, client accountant; and that PwC can evidence the individual’s membership of a legal or accountancy professional body which provides anti-money laundering supervision._\n\n* _The certification should state: \"_*_I hereby certify that this is a true copy of the original document provided to me_*_.\"_\n\n* _The certifying individual should use the official stamp of the organisation which they represent; clearly print their name; and sign and date the document with the date of certification.\"_\n\nCould we try to fix this?","2026-01-15T17:19:57.127Z"],["3813873","PFI-830726","PFI","naomi.agyeman@bolt.eu","Naomi Amponfi Agyeman","hello team, this payment is still pending ","2026-01-15T17:20:49.185Z"],["3813875","LSS-61638","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], apologies, I’m not sure why that is as I set the access to people in Bolt with the link. I’ve just set it to anyone at Bolt - does [this link|https://chatgpt.com/g/g-6942c8f6e7c0819190a172cf405a8970-bolt-unmanned-office-licence-assistant] work for you now? ","2026-01-15T17:22:44.680Z"],["3813878","LSS-61140","LSS","xavier.bendavid@bolt.eu","Xavier Bendavid","[^CONVENTION ARPE - partage et traitement de donneģes _ réponses ARPE pour BOLT.docx]\n\nNew contract sent by ARPE to be approved prior sending the data \n\n","2026-01-15T17:23:22.057Z"],["3813882","DSR-2654","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] please mark this DSAR as complete. The partial response was sent to data subject on [23 December 2025|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Lt5M_JyaBsfAsf5cTX46eLPBPuJQELDg]. ","2026-01-15T17:26:43.974Z"],["3813883","LSS-60495","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9], thank you for flagging. I will aim to arrange the certification when I am in the office next week with Alex.\n\nOne quick question please: we do not have a company stamp at the London office - will this be a problem?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-15T17:28:56.870Z"],["3813884","LSS-61140","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a], please allow me to loop you in a second time to get your final green light on these privacy-related changes. \n\nIn my opinion, I think that the changes are acceptable - I believe that they have realised that these are indeed personal data and they are including additional guarantees that they will only use the data for the agreed statistical purposes and that they prohibit themselves the use of this data to identify any drivers. \n\nSee FR version here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1534qpbd9fyqVV8Blo48vIYXC57mDucJK/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1534qpbd9fyqVV8Blo48vIYXC57mDucJK/edit|smart-link] \nENG translation here (deepl): [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q_k_lX3leU-VYPP12Wx3gJVPk1Ky7TfP/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q_k_lX3leU-VYPP12Wx3gJVPk1Ky7TfP/edit|smart-link] - if some of the wording seems weird, please don’t hesitate to let me know if I can help\n\nThank you in advance for your review 🙏 ","2026-01-15T17:32:59.073Z"],["3813890","PFI-833894","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:38:38.900Z"],["3813891","PFI-833895","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:40:27.949Z"],["3813893","LSS-56022","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","[~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] Just to confirm the only dates the driver was absent were: \n\n*Customer Safety Support / High Priority Case*\n\n# *Created 7 May 2024, 10:00:19, Start 7 May 2024, 10:00:19 – End 31 May 2024, 13:07:52*\n*Reason*: Customer Safety Support - Vehicle accident\n# *Created 5 May 2024, 08:35:27, Start 5 May 2024, 08:35:27 – End 7 May 2024, 10:00:28*\n*Reason*: Customer Safety Support - Vehicle accident\n# *Created 15 Apr 2024, 04:06:04, Start 15 Apr 2024, 04:06:04 – End 18 Apr 2024, 12:57:09*\n*Reason*: Customer Safety Support - Damaged vehicle\n\n\n\nPlease ignore the document blocks, the driver would still have access as the documents did not expire. \n\n","2026-01-15T17:42:07.196Z"],["3813894","PFI-833896","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:42:24.005Z"],["3813896","PFI-833897","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:43:47.111Z"],["3813897","PFI-833898","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:45:04.873Z"],["3813899","PFI-833899","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:46:32.503Z"],["3813901","PFI-833900","PFI","wannapat.huang@bolt-outsource.eu","Wannapat Huang","!image-20260115-174038.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-174050.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-174058.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:47:14.653Z"],["3813902","PFI-833902","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:47:47.191Z"],["3813903","RLONE-367","RLONE","niklas.svegeboe@bolt.eu","Niklas Svegeboe","[~accountid:712020:9e46e650-47e3-4e6a-bf6b-631f3326ab58] this is an “old” task, that has gotten stuck in the backlog. I think it would be good to review this flow again, and I suggest that you have a go at it","2026-01-15T17:48:35.899Z"],["3813904","PFI-833903","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:49:04.217Z"],["3813905","PFI-833905","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:50:22.812Z"],["3813907","WD-22551","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","All PDFs uploaded to [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1L4RMzXYWFN8wX2PKqBvzvaXEiXKphAad|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1L4RMzXYWFN8wX2PKqBvzvaXEiXKphAad]\n\nGoogle sheets in use - [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15_Nd6dUySUocCpBfg_xr0CSwbrpiX4ZewNUIY8bab5o/edit?gid=1035743011#gid=1035743011|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15_Nd6dUySUocCpBfg_xr0CSwbrpiX4ZewNUIY8bab5o/edit?gid=1035743011#gid=1035743011|smart-link]  shared with Kadi","2026-01-15T17:50:51.789Z"],["3813908","PFI-833906","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:51:38.887Z"],["3813909","PFI-830756","PFI","rui.freitas@bolt-outsource.eu","Rui Freitas","Hello Team, any update on this situation?","2026-01-15T17:52:37.004Z"],["3813910","PFI-833907","PFI","janisata.haekna@bolt-outsource.eu","Janisata Haekna","!IMG_3765.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!att.koMhGQXhH5AqAWBpzHyFqSz37wQTdh0tiOwE4B_Tmak.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260115-175044.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:52:50.436Z"],["3813911","PFI-833908","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:52:57.764Z"],["3813913","PFI-833909","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T17:54:10.500Z"],["3813915","WD-22565","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:b73d65c1-8791-4157-9850-c426365a190b] , \nseems like Steven doesn’t have a Workday Account yet.\n\n!image-20260115-175534.png|width=517,alt=\"image-20260115-175534.png\"!","2026-01-15T17:55:58.302Z"],["3813920","PFI-833910","PFI","natalia.mucha@bolt-outsource.eu","Natalia Mucha","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 190506.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T18:05:41.424Z"],["3813921","PFI-833910","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T18:05:43.816Z"],["3813922","LSS-57822","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] - please liaise with [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] , as I don’t support Bolt Food 🙈 CC [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] ","2026-01-15T18:09:00.950Z"],["3813923","PFI-833911","PFI","vasil.slavov@bolt.eu","Vasil Slavov","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 17.57.52.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T18:09:31.553Z"],["3813926","LSS-58347","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:dbba722b-dffd-49d5-81b0-4867668b3d06] may I suggest having a sync to discuss this further? Or alternatively, I’d really appreciate your thoughts here 🙏 [~accountid:712020:00e9e170-53d8-46af-aaee-51ab33faf145] perhaps you could help out as well?","2026-01-15T18:11:26.401Z"],["3813927","WD-21965","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","!image-20260115-181325.png|width=1202,alt=\"image-20260115-181325.png\"!","2026-01-15T18:13:28.194Z"],["3813928","LSS-60847","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - The contract is pending the counterparty's signature. Please remind them to sign it.\n\nThank you.","2026-01-15T18:14:34.476Z"],["3813929","LSS-60847","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/336614?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FCONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6IkJhcmVremFpIiwib3BlcmF0b3IiOiJlcSJ9XX0%253D%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/336614?blocked=true&returnTo=%2Fcontracts%2Fv2%3FCONTRACTSV3_SEARCH%3DeyJxdWVyeSI6W3siZmllbGROYW1lIjoicXVlcnkiLCJ2YWx1ZSI6IkJhcmVremFpIiwib3BlcmF0b3IiOiJlcSJ9XX0%253D%26clusterId%3DEU%26workspaceId%3D31839&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T18:14:39.065Z"],["3813931","LSS-60746","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] - checked your comments and I have no further remarks. I’ll document this accordingly.\n\nRegarding the declaration notice:\n\n* I made the assumption that we’ll be reaching out to existing drivers to encourage them submit the videos, explaining the purpose, actions they need to take. If that’s the case - when you’ll have these comms prepared - can you share that with me so I can add some privacy disclaimers there (don’t worry - I’m not planning to add lengthy disclaimers, but rather a link to privacy notice). Or are you not communicating anything to existing drivers?\n* For new drivers, if this is a field in the onboarding flow and if we won’t be doing any outreach, then we don’t need any disclaimers 🙂 \n\nApologies that this caused confusion, but hope this clarifies it.","2026-01-15T18:28:45.418Z"],["3813933","PFI-833917","PFI","jane.dike@bolt-outsource.eu","Jane Dike","[^BOLT HOLDINGS OU._202611415512416.pdf]","2026-01-15T18:31:53.217Z"],["3813937","LSS-61542","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:8a574999-84e1-4c69-ba7b-46d08c4cff29] , thanks for submitting this! \n\nYou are absolutely correct to refer to the process (this one: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/33697?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/33697?country=global&language=en]), and even if we rolled out the feature where drivers can mark whether they have a camera in their car, *the rollout of the feature does not affect the usage of this process.* \n\nHowever, there seems to be a bit of a misunderstanding - according to the global process, which also applies to Estonia, the only action we need to take is inform the driver of their obligations, however, as they act absolutely independently when using cameras, we don’t need to advise them to remove the camera. I appreciate that the ticket you linked is from 2023, and the process was updated since then, hence the confusion 🙏 \n\nSo, in short, in case of questions:\n\n* From drivers, we follow this response guide: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/33697?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/33697?country=global&language=en]\n* For riders, we follow this response guide: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/23948?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/23948?country=global&language=en]\n\nI know you didn’t specifically ask this, but just for sake of completeness in case of doubt: this new feature neither legitimizes the use of cameras, nor prohibits it. We’re simply following the market standard and collecting information on which drivers have cameras in cars, so we could see the trends and later establish what product enhancements we can make to enhace user privacy/transparency.\n\n\n\nHope that clarifies things but in case you have more questions - happy to help! 🙂 ","2026-01-15T18:36:34.727Z"],["3813947","LSS-61670","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 20.48.10.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 20.48.22.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T18:50:02.341Z"],["3813948","LSS-61670","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T18:50:04.565Z"],["3813950","LSS-60580","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Thanks [~accountid:5fb227c70d2f61006ff6cce2] 🙏 Just for clarity - User ID is also personal data, and therefore all other details/metrics related to the ID become personal data as well (the reason being - we can internally link the user ID to a specific user). Do we need to share the user ID or can it be hashed/anonymized?\n\n*_Regarding the contract (opt-out clause):_*\n\nI have amended the clause in question to remove any explicit reference to opt-out rights.\n\nInstead, we have broadened the language to cover data subject rights (DSRs) generally, positioning Bolt, as Controller, as solely responsible for managing all user rights requests (they are not explicitly mentioned in the contract but are set in the law), including access, deletion, objection, and opt-out, in line with GDPR.\n\nWe’ve preserved legal compliance by:\n\n* Ensuring the clause still reflects Bolt's responsibility for the lawful basis and data subject transparency;\n* Avoiding any language that could contractually commit Bolt to provide an opt-out that doesn't exist;\n\n❗ +*_Important note:_*+ This is a contractual risk mitigation step and not a compliance fix. The absence of opt-out may still be problematic, so want to make sure that the risk is there and subject to user complaints/regulatory scrutiny but the contractual risk is lowered.\n\nCC [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] ","2026-01-15T18:51:45.635Z"],["3813954","LSS-60580","LSS","anastassia.tsarenko@bolt.eu","Anastassia Tsarenko","Asked the team about user ID being hashed on or not, will confirm shortly! ","2026-01-15T18:54:39.446Z"],["3813955","LSS-61671","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","[^BOLT-GUILLAUME William (1).pdf] _(217 kB)_\n\n!Confirmation - Formulaire .png|thumbnail!\n\n!GUILLAUME William - Bolt .png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 20.54.32.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 20.54.48.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T18:55:35.956Z"],["3813956","LSS-61671","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T18:55:37.439Z"],["3813957","LSS-61672","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 20.57.00.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 20.57.11.png|thumbnail!\n\n!BAE Abdou-El-Azize - Bolt.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Confirmation - Formulaire .png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T18:58:27.787Z"],["3813958","LSS-61672","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T18:58:30.200Z"],["3813962","LSS-61671","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:01:07.703Z"],["3813963","LSS-61670","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:01:07.778Z"],["3813964","LSS-61672","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:01:07.793Z"],["3813965","LSS-61673","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","[^BOLT-TALEB Abdelmonaim (1).pdf] _(215 kB)_\n\n!Confirmation - Formulaire .png|thumbnail!\n\n!TALEB Abdelmonaim - Bolt.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.01.05.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.01.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T19:01:31.982Z"],["3813966","LSS-61673","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T19:01:33.572Z"],["3813967","LSS-61674","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.02.40.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.02.52.png|thumbnail!\n\n!SLIMANI Hicham - Bolt .png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T19:04:06.065Z"],["3813968","LSS-61674","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T19:04:07.979Z"],["3813970","LSS-61675","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.04.59.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.05.09.png|thumbnail!\n\n!BARRY Oumar - Bolt .png|thumbnail!\n\n!Confirmation - Formulaire .png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T19:06:33.531Z"],["3813971","LSS-61675","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T19:06:35.108Z"],["3813972","LSS-61676","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Confirmation - Formulaire .png|thumbnail!\n\n!KOK Pascal - Bolt.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.07.26.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.07.37.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T19:08:57.792Z"],["3813973","LSS-61676","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T19:08:58.843Z"],["3813975","LSS-61677","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.09.47.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-15 at 21.09.57.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^BOLT- KERFOUH Karim (1).pdf] _(218 kB)_\n\n!Confirmation - Formulaire .png|thumbnail!\n\n!KERFOUH Karim - Bolt .png|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T19:11:38.706Z"],["3813976","LSS-61677","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-15T19:11:40.299Z"],["3813978","LSS-61673","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:16:35.656Z"],["3813979","LSS-61676","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:16:35.697Z"],["3813980","LSS-61675","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:16:35.701Z"],["3813981","LSS-61674","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:16:35.730Z"],["3813982","LSS-61677","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-15T19:16:35.792Z"],["3813990","FX-3649","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768505316746089]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3649 successfully transitioned to state 'To Do'.\n{quote}","2026-01-15T19:28:51.958Z"],["3813992","DAEN-1330","DAEN","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","The supply metrics that we mostly need are listed in this document [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xLZvuhQ6WSaM_-v-mzJhJpr1u_nSGZ9QmHoclDYTdT0/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xLZvuhQ6WSaM_-v-mzJhJpr1u_nSGZ9QmHoclDYTdT0/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T19:32:44.324Z"],["3813993","LSS-61678","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^DE20260114-001 Exleasing cars - Bolt Drive DE.docx.pdf] _(334 kB)_","2026-01-15T19:40:30.815Z"],["3813995","SRED-1064","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","All nodes recreated.","2026-01-15T19:44:02.093Z"],["3813996","SRED-1065","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Fixed","2026-01-15T19:44:11.354Z"],["3813997","SREDESK-7402","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Only prelive cluster created.","2026-01-15T19:44:48.141Z"],["3813999","PFI-833929","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^reporte - 2026-01-15T144533.425.pdf]","2026-01-15T19:51:38.538Z"],["3814002","PFI-833930","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^reporte - 2026-01-15T145047.815.pdf]","2026-01-15T19:54:31.820Z"],["3814003","PFI-833931","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^reporte - 2026-01-15T144918.764.pdf]","2026-01-15T19:57:38.964Z"],["3814004","LSS-61031","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","Comment somewhat unclear, followed up on slack 1:1 first.","2026-01-15T19:58:09.862Z"],["3814005","DRX-28163","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: according to the ticket","2026-01-15T19:59:44.632Z"],["3814006","PFI-833933","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^reporte - 2026-01-15T145246.398.pdf]","2026-01-15T20:00:14.287Z"],["3814007","LSS-58216","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","{quote}The swift response is very much appreciated.{quote}\n\n{quote}The amendments were accepted, and the final versions are attached. Please confirm we can circulate the Docusign.{quote}\n\n[^MSA-2026-01-16-Solidgate_Bolt_f.pdf]\n[^MSA-2026-01-16-Solidgate_Bolt_f.docx]\n\n[~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] : do you do one last scan-through / compare docs? or what’s the next step before signing.","2026-01-15T20:00:59.952Z"],["3814008","PFI-833775","PFI","anastacia.njunge@bolt.eu","Anastacia Njunge","Hi Marten,\n\nWell noted, Thank you. ","2026-01-15T20:01:48.112Z"],["3814009","PFI-833935","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^reporte - 2026-01-15T150116.071.pdf]","2026-01-15T20:04:51.402Z"],["3814010","PFI-833936","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^reporte - 2026-01-15T152838.144.pdf]","2026-01-15T20:07:32.218Z"],["3814015","LSS-61587","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:60528926695c3900706cc79e] Please find below our response: \n\n\nEarnings comms are generally allowed; competitor comparisons are higher risk and must be tightly controlled.\n\n# Comms 1 – Earnings Information\n\n*a) Activated Bolt Flex drivers (in-app / email)*\n\nAllowed, provided communications are factual and qualified.\n\nOK to share\n\n* Historical average earnings (day / week / month / weekend).\n* Top 5% / top 1% earnings, only if clearly labelled as exceptional.\n* Earnings linked to specific hours worked (e.g. “45 hours/week”).\n\nRequired safeguards\n\n* Must be historical data (not projections).\n* State time period, location, and assumptions.\n* Clearly say earnings are not guaranteed and vary by driver.\n* Distinguish gross fares vs net earnings (commission, costs, tax not included).\n\n*Avoid*\n\n* “You can earn £X” (use “drivers earned…”).\n* Any suggestion of guaranteed, stable, or minimum income.\n\n\n\n*b) Prospective drivers* \n\n* Higher risk but still possible.\n\n*Only allowed if*\n\n* Framed as historical averages, not promises.\n* Disclaimers are prominent (same visibility as headline claim).\n* No personalised or predictive earnings claims.\n\n*Avoid*\n\n* “Earn up to £X” without clear context.\n* Using top-earner figures as implied typical outcomes.\n\n\n\n# Comms 2 – Comparisons with Uber / competitors \n\n*a) Commission / fare split examples (e.g. £10 fare)*\n\n*High-risk area* \n\nPermissible only if\n\n* Data is accurate, current, and like-for-like (same city, product, timing).\n* Assumptions are stated (excludes incentives, tips, taxes, promos).\n* Clearly labelled as illustrative examples, not universal truth.\n* No suggestion competitors are acting unlawfully or unfairly.\n\n*Key risk*\n\n* Competitor commission structures vary which leads to  misleading comparisons and  legal exposure.\n\n*b) Distance-based comparisons (e.g. 5-mile trip)*\n\n*Strongly discouraged.*\n\nReason: Distance alone ignores time, surge, waiting, and incentives and very likely misleading unless supported by robust, current datasets for all competitors.\n\nh2. \n\nh2. \n\nh3. ","2026-01-15T20:29:00.285Z"],["3814017","DSR-3765","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-15T20:31:06.934Z"],["3814019","BRE-1229","BRE","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","most likely blocker for RH: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LEB128QP/p1768303734502829|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LEB128QP/p1768303734502829|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T20:38:36.692Z"],["3814020","C2-461","C2","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Google Form for responders: [https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfsmhLu-XjclxRS5xSEEaXJIBUQjLhcXG7r1TrZQJ_5oXeP5w/viewform|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfsmhLu-XjclxRS5xSEEaXJIBUQjLhcXG7r1TrZQJ_5oXeP5w/viewform|smart-link] \nGoogle Form for edit:[https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1nC64gWXv09U2NiGyRMnFR7N-3TqBZmfzcr8RZTdlLJg/edit|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1nC64gWXv09U2NiGyRMnFR7N-3TqBZmfzcr8RZTdlLJg/edit|smart-link] \nResponses sheet: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1JS6zUpbyQWH1UtCLtvBIIhdafETaEN0Pz1GdL3DqQH4/edit?resourcekey=&gid=226577103#gid=226577103|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1JS6zUpbyQWH1UtCLtvBIIhdafETaEN0Pz1GdL3DqQH4/edit?resourcekey=&gid=226577103#gid=226577103|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T20:41:45.734Z"],["3814021","LSS-61438","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] \n\nWe have reviewed the agreement in full. The contract has a 12-month minimum term ending in April 2026. After that, it automatically continues on a rolling basis at the same monthly price unless we give 30 days’ written notice.\n\nKey points for planning:\n\n* There is no obligation to renew or purchase the booths at the end of the term.\n* We can legally keep the booths beyond April 2026 (e.g. until June 2026) under the automatic rollover, paying only the additional months used.\n* Once the office move date is confirmed, we simply need to give 30 days’ written notice to terminate.\n* There are no exit fees or collection costs when terminating after the minimum term.\n\nWhat we should avoid:\n\n* Terminating before April 2026 (this would trigger payment of all remaining rent).\n* Agreeing to any “renewal” or new fixed term, the existing rollover already gives us the flexibility we need.\n\n*Recommended approach:*\nLet the contract roll over after April 2026, retain the booths as needed, and serve 30 days’ notice once the relocation date is fixed. ","2026-01-15T20:43:09.471Z"],["3814022","LSS-61524","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:622b6eb2302c6b006af70509] we are reviewing this request and will get back to you as soon as possible. ","2026-01-15T20:44:10.216Z"],["3814023","C2-461","C2","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","ADR packaging SOP for reference: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fowfOmBxjc-sJLQLdUkLcMuCfKJPX5OWqlS29W6B2I/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-fowfOmBxjc-sJLQLdUkLcMuCfKJPX5OWqlS29W6B2I/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-15T20:44:10.716Z"],["3814026","PFI-810251","PFI","monika.roszig@bolt-outsource.eu","Monika Roszig","hello, i’ve contacted my TL and he was able to download only report for november. Fleet owner needs reports for october and november, but for october there is such error: There is an unhandled exception. Details: BillingProfileData not found for externalId: 227150, type: Company and date: 2025-10-01","2026-01-15T20:49:19.262Z"],["3814030","WD-22512","WD","demetri.manias@bolt.eu","Demetri Manias","Thanks Oana!","2026-01-15T20:56:58.752Z"],["3814031","RS-1954","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","[^BOLT pomoc prwana dla Wydziału Dochodzeniowo-Śledczego KMP Ostrołęka en-US.pdf]\n[^BOLT pomoc prwana dla Wydziału Dochodzeniowo-Śledczego KMP Ostrołęka.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-15T20:59:53.696Z"],["3814032","PFI-833910","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-15T21:00:49.127Z"],["3814042","INT-668","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","Yes, indeed.\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-15T22:08:12.579Z"],["3814043","XVER-310","XVER","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:61d554bb68926d00685d5727] I assume it should be cross-vertical, right?","2026-01-15T22:08:41.603Z"],["3814044","DRX-28024","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: - check that `eng_is_cs_webview_custom_header_enabled` feature flag is not more presented in debug menu and custom headers for CS webviews still enabled","2026-01-15T22:15:36.865Z"],["3814049","WFM-9998","WFM","iga.glowinska@bolt-outsource.eu","Iga Głowińska","Hi, since we cooperate with this market in case of high backlog and agents are delegated to help each other, without access to this market, we are unable to enable queues from Ukraine for them","2026-01-15T22:52:38.798Z"],["3814053","PFI-833959","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-15T23:14:53.556Z"],["3814054","PFI-833961","PFI","phattana.ratsamee@bolt-outsource.eu","Phattana Ratsamee","!016015064213AOR06897.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-15T23:31:41.983Z"],["3814055","PFI-814990","PFI","stanislav.vladicescu@bolt-outsource.eu","Stanislav Vladicescu","Can we get an answer?","2026-01-15T23:43:45.038Z"],["3814056","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado",":hellooo: Hello again *group-S06DTJJN2HK*\n\nHave a backfill request. One of the Ti-CDC got stuck:\n\n{{ti-payments --id=cdc-taxify-payment-data}} \nTime line below:\n\n[http://ti-payments-monitor.sqldb:3000/goto/U9qRQMIDk|http://ti-payments-monitor.sqldb:3000/goto/U9qRQMIDk]\n\nFROM: “checkpoint_time”: “2026-01-15 21:59:28.363\",\nTO:    “create_time”: “2026-01-15 22:37:12.704\",","2026-01-15T23:46:09.594Z"],["3814057","DBRE-8705","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Leandro Morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1768517045100809?thread_ts=1768517045.100809&cid=GMBRX6L8M|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1768517045100809?thread_ts=1768517045.100809&cid=GMBRX6L8M|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-15T23:46:11.059Z"],["3814058","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9F0EJQPK/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_23.45.12.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9F0EJQPK/screenshot_2026-01-15_at_23.45.12.png|smart-link]","2026-01-15T23:46:11.293Z"],["3814059","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* Tried to pause/resume changefeed => lag did not decrease\n* Removed and started the changefeed from “now”\n* Requested backfill from DAP","2026-01-15T23:47:07.808Z"],["3814060","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","{noformat} lmorgado@lmbolt-m1  ~/github/terraform-cdc/scripts   main  cat /Users/lmorgado/github/terraform-cdc/scripts/cdc-taxify-payment-data.json\n{\n  \"version\": \"2.3.7\",\n  \"created\": \"2026-01-15T22:35:38.076Z\",\n  \"filters\": [\n    \"--id=cdc-taxify-payment-data\"\n  ],\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"upstream_id\": 7329501166194665616,\n      \"namespace\": \"default\",\n      \"id\": \"cdc-taxify-payment-data\",\n      \"sink_uri\": {},\n      \"create_time\": \"2025-12-01T02:59:55.38611405Z\",\n      \"start_ts\": 462568291097116701,\n      \"config\": {\n        \"memory_quota\": 1073741824,\n        \"case_sensitive\": false,\n        \"force_replicate\": false,\n        \"ignore_ineligible_table\": false,\n        \"check_gc_safe_point\": false,\n        \"filter\": {\n          \"rules\": [\n            \"taxify_payment.notification\",\n            \"taxify_payment.payment\",\n            \"taxify_payment.payment_order\",\n            \"taxify_payment.payment_request_log\",\n            \"taxify_payment.payment_row\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"mounter\": {\n          \"worker_num\": 16\n        },\n        \"sink\": {\n          \"protocol\": \"avro\",\n          \"schema_registry\": \"http://schema-registry.data.internal:8081\",\n          \"dispatchers\": [\n            {\n              \"matcher\": [\n                \"*.*\"\n              ],\n              \"partition\": \"index-value\",\n              \"topic\": \"cdc_tidb_avro__ti-payments__{schema}__{table}\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"terminator\": \"\\r\\n\",\n          \"delete_only_output_handle_key_columns\": null,\n          \"content_compatible\": null,\n          \"advance_timeout\": 150\n        },\n  