or customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-16T07:00:24.046Z"],["3814248","LSS-58999","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Mihaela Vatamanu,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-16T07:00:24.121Z"],["3814249","LSS-60103","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Samuel Dubnický,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-16T07:00:24.214Z"],["3814250","LSS-59079","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Papa Omar Diouf,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-16T07:00:24.345Z"],["3814251","LSS-58550","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Denys Miroshnychenko,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-16T07:00:25.085Z"],["3814252","LSS-57013","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Ilya Rybin,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-16T07:00:28.472Z"],["3814257","LSS-51678","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Viktoriia Voskolup,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T07:01:30.752Z"],["3814258","LSS-52203","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Viktoriia Voskolup,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T07:01:30.789Z"],["3814259","EBIKE1-376","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Problem with one of the simulation, I can get it working as it should. And deformation difference is around 5x.","2026-01-16T07:03:32.726Z"],["3814260","PFI-826496","PFI","yawovi.segbe@bolt-outsource.eu","Yawovi Mawunyo Jean-Baptiste Segbe","Hello Team, any update please ?","2026-01-16T07:04:19.450Z"],["3814261","PFI-826494","PFI","yawovi.segbe@bolt-outsource.eu","Yawovi Mawunyo Jean-Baptiste Segbe","Hello Team, any update please ?","2026-01-16T07:05:00.059Z"],["3814263","G3IOT-1206","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","I have tried different wi-fi settings, protocols (bgn) but wasn't able to find any reliable configuration when IOT is inside the case. Sometimes Wi-Fi does connect though the speed is not that high comparing to IOT Wi-Fi speed without the case.\n\nThe antenna tuning is probably required","2026-01-16T07:05:37.998Z"],["3814264","PFI-833607","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-16T07:06:51.586Z"],["3814266","WD-22506","WD","lysette.ranne@bolt.eu","Lysette Ranne","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec], I can’t find the Transaction Tax IDs. Have these been created?","2026-01-16T07:09:03.744Z"],["3814268","PFI-828094","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Our engineers are aware of this and investigating. Will keep you updated 🙂 ","2026-01-16T07:09:31.849Z"],["3814269","PFI-828094","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768214106524969?thread_ts=1767692312.280399&cid=C02C2SY0MHT|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768214106524969?thread_ts=1767692312.280399&cid=C02C2SY0MHT]","2026-01-16T07:09:34.819Z"],["3814270","PFI-828094","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! \n\nLooks like this issue needs input from our developers. The issue has been flagged to them & they are investigating. We will keep you posted with any updates! \n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T07:09:41.295Z"],["3814271","GROWTH-138","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 16.01.26*\n\n* Variant Resolution Engine has been made available in CMS.\n* New test tasks have been created and shared with the Lifecycle Testing Workgroup.\n** For future tests, more thorough approach will be taken for the existing functionality testing (in addition to improvement ideas).\n* Issues with the Journey Manager have been fixed. Delivery use cases with the issue have been taken live (Bolt Market Cart Abandoned). Also Restaurant Cart Abandoned flows have been taken live (a new use case).\n* Feedback sync sessions with the Design and Engineering team.\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Work on CMS<>Journey module integration, which takes us closer to using CMS while building comms flows.","2026-01-16T07:09:45.378Z"],["3814272","WD-22506","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","IDs of Tax codes \n\n!image-20260116-071100.png|width=1423,alt=\"image-20260116-071100.png\"!","2026-01-16T07:11:07.786Z"],["3814273","HS-29009","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-16T07:11:19.417Z"],["3814276","DO-5806","DO","jaanus.uudmae@bolt.eu","Jaanus Uudmäe","Approve","2026-01-16T07:12:00.440Z"],["3814277","RNTL-30385","RNTL","nurhidayat.thalib@bolt.eu","Nurhidayat Thalib","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7404388444/2026-01+Mark+Store+Risky+Users|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RNTL/pages/7404388444/2026-01+Mark+Store+Risky+Users|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:12:30.669Z"],["3814279","PFI-833552","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout (Payout ID 233063214) is still pending since 2026-01-11 with payment validation in progress, which indicates an ongoing compliance/processing review on the provider side. Please inform the partner that no action is required from their side; we are monitoring and will handle any checks so it can be processed as soon as possible, after which the status will update and the funds will reach their bank account. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:12:53.361Z"],["3814281","PFI-833572","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still in pending status (last update on 11 Jan 2026) with payment validation in progress, which indicates an ongoing compliance/validation review on the provider side and can take longer than usual. As it has been pending for several days, please inform the partner that the payout may be delayed; our team is monitoring it and responding to any checks so it can be released as soon as possible. No action is required from the partner at this time; the payout will proceed once validation is completed.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:13:12.973Z"],["3814283","PFI-833574","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected, and the bank only returned a technical code without a clear explanation. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try requesting it again. As a precaution, ask the partner to double-check their bank details (account name/number and required bank codes) to prevent further rejections. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:13:44.526Z"],["3814284","PFI-833642","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is still in pending status; the last update in our logs was on 2026-01-05, which is longer than usual. It may be delayed due to an ongoing compliance review or technical issues on the payment provider’s side; the Partner Payments team is monitoring it and responding to any checks, so please inform the partner that no action is needed from their side and to wait until it clears (the status will update automatically once processed). \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-16T07:14:10.814Z"],["3814285","PFI-833643","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with value date 2025-12-23. If the partner reports non-receipt, please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with them; they can then contact their bank to trace the funds using the value date. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:14:31.744Z"],["3814286","PFI-833652","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot see the funds, ask them to check with their bank using the proof as reference. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:14:57.523Z"],["3814287","BDB-1535","BDB","karolis.simkus@bolt.eu","Karolis Šimkus","Hello,\n\nCould we please ask for assistance with the mockup for Vilnius Airport on how we could use the pillars in Vilnius Airport?\n\nWe want to use 4 pillars (they are different sizes) to capture all the possible traffic.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.25.28.png|width=903,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.25.28.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.26.13.png|width=903,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.26.13.png\"!\n\nAs you can see they are in very different shapes and forms. But this would be perfect for us since we could capture 85-90% of traffic. Adding a scheme of how traffic flows and I marked the places where these pillars are.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.28.49.png|width=903,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-13 at 11.28.49.png\"!\n\nInitially we wanted to make a square lightbox, and put our messages there facing in 4 different locations and potentially catching more eyeballs with the Ad. Our manufacturing partners created this mockup:\n\n!image (23).png|width=903,alt=\"image (23).png\"!\n\nBut Airports don’t agree with that, since people are getting close to that place, kids are running around and someone could get hurt in those sharp edges. They added a picture like this just to show how close people passing by these pillars.\n\n!image (24).png|width=903,alt=\"image (24).png\"!","2026-01-16T07:15:02.230Z"],["3814289","PFI-833664","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The last payout attempt was rejected by the bank due to an issue with the beneficiary’s payment details (the bank did not accept the provided account/UPI information). Please ask the partner to review and correct their banking/UPI details (account/UPI ID, name as per bank records, IFSC/routing code, and ensure the account is active). Once corrected, the payout will be retried in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to cash out again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-16T07:15:21.351Z"],["3814290","PFI-833666","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with value date 2025-12-16 (status finished on 2025-12-17). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot locate the funds, advise them to contact their beneficiary bank to trace the credit using the value date. \n\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:15:37.110Z"],["3814293","PFI-833740","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout shows status Finished (successfully processed) with the last update on 2026-01-13. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still don’t see the funds, advise them to check with their bank. If multiple payouts are involved, please add their payout IDs in this ticket so we can confirm each one.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:16:00.276Z"],["3814295","RISK2-3232","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*14.01.2026 Internal team call*\n\n* Operational Risk Instance Setup in terms of Product Risks and EFR\n** Affects whether we inherit the description from OR to OR-Instance. For example, if the Operational Risk is Driver Safety (user-based approach, not grouping based), then it does not make sense for the Instance to inherit the description, as the Instances will be different events from various groupings, therefore they will have different descriptions.\n** {color:#bf2600}*Pending Sujit to get back to us whether inheriting the description from OR to OR-Instance is possible.*{color}\n** We will have a grouping-based solution for [+Product Risks+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oAhKT6_oQo8MwLucW1W3go5LP6O-qQvFOfbr24sOdWA/edit#gid=751001539] and EFR\n*** Enterprise Risk - Safety\n*** Operational Risk - Driver Commits Criminal Activity\n*** Operational Risk Instance - Driver Threatens Terrorist Activity\n*** Key Risk Indicators -\n**** Driver Threatens Terrorist Activity EFR 2025 Q4\n**** Driver Threatens Terrorist Activity  - Number of Crises 2025 Q4\n**** Driver Threatens Terrorist Activity - Number of Events 2025 Q4\n** Central Operations - Safety will manage this going forward, we will upload the categories based on their input.\n* We want to track multiple countries under one instance, by using the Key Risk Indicator (KRI) section. This way we are able to log the data for each country and showcase it, but we’ll still only have one Instance (we will also then have one assessment, but we can have an overarching assessment, so this shouldn’t be an issue. I.e we do an assessment of this one risk event overall).\n* When creating an {{Assessment}} to an {{Instance}}, it doesn’t allow you to fill out an assessment immediately, instead it directs you to create an assessment and then assign it. We discussed having two options immediately available for the user to choose from, either to:\n** Create an assessment (to assign to smb)\n** Fill out an assessment (yourself, immediately)\n** Please advise how this could be added to LogicGate for the ease of flow and better user experience, since we may foresee that an Accountable Manager might want to fill out the assessment themselves immediately, not create it, assign it and only then start filling it out.\n** _This also means that we’ll have different approaches to the following enterprise risks:_\n*** _Reclassification - we have an OR Instance for each country_\n*** _Safety/Product Risks - we have a KRI for each country_\n* Could we also get an updated Compliance permissions file, considering we adjusted the namings?","2026-01-16T07:16:26.716Z"],["3814297","PFI-833748","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout is still in pending status; the last update was on 2026-01-09, so the delay is longer than usual. It may be held due to an ongoing compliance review or provider-side technical checks; we are monitoring these and will respond promptly—no action is needed from the partner right now. Once processed, the funds should reach their bank shortly after.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-16T07:16:42.340Z"],["3814298","PFI-833807","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed; the provider confirms completion on 29 Dec 2025. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot see the funds, advise them to contact their bank with the proof for tracing. P.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-16T07:17:02.742Z"],["3814300","DRAG101-417","DRAG101","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Estimated Time of Arrival 02-Feb-2026, according to the [tracking|https://www.zimchina.com/tools/track-a-shipment?consnumber=ZIMUSNH7763524]","2026-01-16T07:17:36.134Z"],["3814301","PFI-833880","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank because the beneficiary account details are invalid (the account number or the bank code/routing is incorrect). Please ask the partner to correct their payout details in the app; once updated, the transfer will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle, or they can retry an Early Cashout after fixing the details. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; if you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:17:38.327Z"],["3814302","PFI-833921","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank because the beneficiary details don’t match what the bank has on file (account holder name and/or account number). Please ask the partner to update their payout details to the exact bank-registered name and correct account/IBAN (and any required bank codes); once fixed, it will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle, or they can request Early Cashout again after updating. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; feel free to share feedback.","2026-01-16T07:18:06.214Z"],["3814303","RISK2-3249","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","Copying over comments:\n\n{{Incidents}}*:* LogicGate highlighted that setting up {{Incidents}} is likely not in scope of the SOW.\n\nDiscussed with Gregory that we might tie this with Key Indicators/or we might want to set it up separately ourselves after implementation. So let’s see how they set up {{Key Indicators}} for us and we can then go from there, no immediate action points here.\n\nUnder {{Incidents}}, we’d like to log:\n\n# quarterly reports for high-volume safety events\n# lawsuits/consequences of lawsuits\n\nShared an example of safety risks with LogicGate [+here+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1767020641863229]","2026-01-16T07:18:31.938Z"],["3814304","PFI-833954","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected because the beneficiary details don’t match the bank’s records — the account name or account number is incorrect. Please ask the partner to update their payout details to exactly match their bank account (full legal account holder name and correct account number/IBAN; also check routing/sort/BSB if applicable) and save the changes. Once fixed, the payout will be retried automatically in the next regular payout cycle; for Early Cashout, they can request it again after updating the details. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:18:41.058Z"],["3814305","LSS-61648","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Hi, just reminding about this response we’ve sent to the authority [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-54571?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6ImY2MWYwMDk1ZjY3ZWFkNWM0NGU5MGE3MmEwNjVjNWJmY2RjNzUxOTc0ODgyNDFlNGMxZjM3ZGM3OWExMzkxYWMiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiMTMwODIiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IkxTUy01NDU3MSJ9LCJleHAiOjE3NTg3MDIxOTYsImlhdCI6MTc1NjI4Mjk5Nn0.Jc4wR-0J6C-N5zCbAj974hLLxSpPrSkW-rd18TxitVg]. They have never came back with official request.\n\nIt is the first language law related inquiry which mentions drivers we receive.\n\nIf all the inquiries will look like this we will need the templated response about us being the app which connects passenger and driver, and not the company with employed workers (drivers). \n\nThe inquiry looks like “the first” so we have to explain what and how we are going to provide to them in the future, so both Legal and Privacy look is required. \n\nLet me know if you need any additional input or help from Operations end on this. Thanks. ","2026-01-16T07:18:44.187Z"],["3814307","PFI-833689","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. Our logs show this payout was successfully processed on 2026-01-15; please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the courier, and if the funds still aren’t visible, ask them to contact their bank to trace the incoming transfer. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-16T07:19:14.709Z"],["3814308","PFI-833877","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending (last update on 12 Jan), which is longer than usual and likely due to a provider-side compliance review or a temporary technical delay; we are monitoring it and responding to any requests promptly. Please inform the courier that no action is needed from their side and the funds will be processed once cleared. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-16T07:19:55.929Z"],["3814310","PFI-828455","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Your calculation is absolutely correct, but the driver has a negative balance from June. So if you deduct the previous negative balance of -188.45 from 3775.97 you will get the amount that was paid out 🙂 \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 09.19.23.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 09.19.23.png\"!","2026-01-16T07:20:23.803Z"],["3814311","EBIKE1-314","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Full test is done connectors and battery was okay. But no difference in the force for closing hatch. Also handle strap left an notable mark on the dampeners which also shows that spring back is not that good. \nKevin will measure if the thickness is changed.\n\n\nBut for now we don’t see any difference between current and new dampener.\nI will discuss with supplier again to check for different material.\n\n\n\n[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076]  ","2026-01-16T07:21:02.938Z"],["3814313","WD-22506","WD","lysette.ranne@bolt.eu","Lysette Ranne","Thank you! Telema has been updated.\nFYI [~accountid:712020:5a4edf94-bd1c-4ae3-85a1-442242d02a49] ","2026-01-16T07:21:12.282Z"],["3814314","EBIOT-220","EBIOT","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Parts are 3D printed, I will assemble them by {{2026-01-23}} ","2026-01-16T07:22:13.614Z"],["3814315","GROWTH-555","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 16.01.26*\n\n* New test tasks have been created and shared with the Lifecycle Testing Workgroup. Focus is on the following:\n** [CMS, Push Builder] Functionalities necessary for Push Builder\n** [CMS, Content Preview] Image loading issue - has been fixed now\n** [CMS] Testing And Debugging Tools\n** [CMS] Variant Resolution Engine logic\n** [CMS] Render Engine logic\n* For future tests, more thorough approach will be taken for the existing functionality testing (in addition to improvement ideas).\n** The feedback can be split into two: \n*** Actionable feedback on bugs/errors/issues with the current developed functionalities\n*** Improvement ideas added to the backlog and that will be worked on as separate functionalities.\n* Feedback sync sessions with the Design and Engineering team.\n** All the current topics (Journey Manager, CMS, Segments) were thoroughly analysed with the focus on achievability, priority and whether design team’s input is necessary as well.\n** We’ll go forward with the process of having similar syncs once per sprint (every 2 weeks).\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Create missing backlog tasks based on the syncs with the Engineering and Design team.\n* Sync with LCM PM regarding the current sprint results, next sprint, tasks and more focused approach.","2026-01-16T07:22:25.680Z"],["3814319","PFI-777012","PFI","urszula.albrecht@bolt-outsource.eu","Urszula Albrecht","[~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] bonus is attached in the desription: Bonus for new drivers +500 PLN for the first 3 weeks!\nComplete at least 200 rides during the specified period and get a bonus of 500 PLN! Bonus is applied only to rides in Szczecin.\n3887077 21/07/2025 00:00:00 - 10/08/2025 23:59:59","2026-01-16T07:24:05.014Z"],["3814320","BDB-1535","BDB","karolis.simkus@bolt.eu","Karolis Šimkus","Additional limitations and why we are asking for a help with something not traditional:\n\n* We already used digital screens (DOOH) last year, and they performed pretty low. We are not getting 100% of attention by being 1/6th amount of the time on the screen. So in this case we want to add static ads.\n* A few times we got a suggestion to make some sort of “wrap” around pillar. We had them in the past and they did not performed enough. In Lithuania by the law ads must have either just Lithuanian text, or it should be bi-lingual. So usually pillars ar not readable.\n\nFrom the other hand - pillars themselves are pretty huge, so it’s possible to do some sort of full wraps in a few cases (if we would get this approved).\n\n\nWe were thinking to use this copy:\n{{Catch a ride to an early morning conference.}}\n{{Or late night TV Tower panorama.}}","2026-01-16T07:24:22.750Z"],["3814323","HS-28994","HS","kristiina.kuutok@bolt.eu","Kristiina Kuutok","Thank you, let me know🙏","2026-01-16T07:24:55.109Z"],["3814325","FX-3646","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768548297483199]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3646 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T07:25:10.316Z"],["3814326","FX-3650","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768548310352459]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3650 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T07:25:22.945Z"],["3814329","PFI-833879","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:31026123-addd-49f6-a43f-800f7149925d],\n\nThis is a feature from the Identity team to block any device (identified by Device ID) that has logged into at least 5 accounts in the last 24h via SMS OTP.\n\nThis is not Fraud related, I’d advise reaching out to [Privacy|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47] for more info on this.\n\nAll the best,\nMarten","2026-01-16T07:26:45.307Z"],["3814330","PFI-808708","PFI","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","Hi there. Did somebody have time to take a look at this case?","2026-01-16T07:26:45.757Z"],["3814334","HS-27884","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","sent to signing 15.01","2026-01-16T07:27:21.717Z"],["3814335","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Summary of the week\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"ecec38ce-f107-4f89-a529-62c2d3153c2f\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":6},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Long term solution\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Additional features to stop rotation.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It stops rotation when riding over a bump.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The clip is not securely fixed.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Add 0.4mm thickness under the clip as shown on the right side.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"+0.4mm thickness\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The clip fixes the phone holder more tightly.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Only this modification possibly is enough to stop rotation.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Customised clip\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Mold cost: 15000RMB\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"it works the same way as glue \"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":191,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-070742.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-070742.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"357a9997a7098054d9b0fba3489cc55e.mp4\",\"alt\":\"357a9997a7098054d9b0fba3489cc55e.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":139,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-071424.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-071424.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":622,\"width\":622}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":139,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"ac6ab7335d63e776e6ee48b3993b6696-20260116-070936.jpg\",\"alt\":\"ac6ab7335d63e776e6ee48b3993b6696-20260116-070936.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":108,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-072308.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-072308.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":756,\"width\":756}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":87,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-072620.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-072620.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":489,\"width\":489}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"985fa620-5afb-4687-85c0-1303fb5ec85c\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Ad hoc solution\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Ethyl-2-cyanoacrylate\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" (Wuerth super glue)\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"to be used to fix the clip to the holder.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Clean up glue residues.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Glue fixes the clip and phone holder properly.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":250,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260114-073837 (1385cc6f-bf18-420a-828f-32e79fda5966).png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260114-073837.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":250,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"1207bd5f6e31a1e403e717b80d52fe34-20260114-084144 (249e787f-019d-4e82-bd60-f5f300c44ed8).jpg\",\"alt\":\"1207bd5f6e31a1e403e717b80d52fe34-20260114-084144.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"4b70fa0e07826a92614fe3a0c5c1b260 (a6d17670-3de7-4636-a2f2-64eacbb52519).mp4\",\"alt\":\"4b70fa0e07826a92614fe3a0c5c1b260.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-16T07:27:29.393Z"],["3814336","PFI-834016","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","!Screenshot_20260114-140209_OPay.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T07:27:34.085Z"],["3814340","EBIOT-243","EBIOT","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","I made 3 iterations, and now the 3D printed model works well. \n\n* After the tool is pressed on the bottom plastic, snaps are holding the tool in position. \n* Then, with a knife, the plastics can be separated from each other. \n\n!image-20260116-072713.png|width=758,alt=\"image-20260116-072713.png\"!","2026-01-16T07:28:48.652Z"],["3814343","PFI-834005","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:ce4d8f92-7ade-427d-80c0-fe788eba2f72],\n\nThe user tried to add their card multiple times but did not follow through with the necessary verification process. After that, it was not possible to add the card anymore.\n\nThe user account itself is not blocked.\n\nPlease advise the user to wait 24h before trying to add their card again, and after adding the card follow the necessary verification steps to verify their card.\n\nThe user can consult with their bank on how they can pass the verification.\n\nBest,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T07:29:36.250Z"],["3814345","PFI-834017","PFI","chaiyachat.sabphaso@bolt-outsource.eu","Chaiyachat Sabphaso","CC [~accountid:712020:5ea96d2b-7eeb-4f19-87f7-7df3b5c1a3f9] [~accountid:712020:416b6365-4efe-4eac-b8c7-461f58da07c8]  [~accountid:712020:d92e20dc-92b8-47fd-920c-26e5630a941a] [~accountid:712020:47686407-95f4-4c43-8b07-5984e2a65bea] [~accountid:712020:851cedd4-4822-4cdf-a347-5952153442e4]  [~accountid:712020:7680dc10-5752-4f40-af73-45011c358020] [~accountid:712020:bfc62aa9-8d70-4b0c-a849-a9eecb0b0301] [~accountid:712020:3bc601f0-57aa-466e-88e1-de084c7ce10f] [~accountid:712020:3cca891b-969f-4571-8d99-3e90479e630c]","2026-01-16T07:29:45.820Z"],["3814348","HS-28519","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:a335a5ec-2969-45be-8f2f-6561cf7e7d62],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-16T07:30:20.313Z"],["3814349","LSS-61495","LSS","therese.ilves@bolt.eu","Therese Ilves","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] You’re right — this is exactly the kind of information I intended to share 🙂 \n\nThank you for your support! ","2026-01-16T07:30:27.510Z"],["3814351","PFI-834017","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello there!\n\nThe user tried to add their card multiple times but did not follow through with the necessary verification process. After that, it was not possible to add the card anymore.\n\nThe user account itself is not blocked.\n\nPlease advise the user to wait 24h before trying to add their card again, and after adding the card follow the necessary verification steps to verify their card.\n\nThe user can consult with their bank on how they can pass the verification.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-16T07:31:15.380Z"],["3814353","LSS-61671","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] cancelling this ticket because a ticket exists for this request: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-59848|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-59848|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:32:16.056Z"],["3814358","PFI-829394","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi![ Bonus 1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/supply-campaign/checklog?filter=%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A3910373979%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw] was for  31.12.2024 to 01.01.2025, so that probably sin’t applicable here 🙂 \n\nFor [Bonus 2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/supply-campaign/checklog?filter=%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A5138792621%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw] it is the 137.53 that’s visible, it’s just with VAT included. \n\nSeems to be all good 🙂 \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 09.33.46.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 09.33.46.png\"!","2026-01-16T07:33:57.358Z"],["3814359","LSS-59848","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f989ec0f-bf00-4c9b-be89-cc44499bb288] please allow me to loop you in here - please could you check if this driver has compliantly received an email when blocked?\n\nDriver name: William Guillaume\nPartner ID: 3099299","2026-01-16T07:33:58.107Z"],["3814365","RS-1955","RS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[^20260115112212.pdf en-GB.pdf] _(193 kB)_\n\n[^20260115112212.pdf.pdf] _(202 kB)_","2026-01-16T07:34:32.169Z"],["3814369","PFI-833780","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:58c40afb-9015-4b5b-a3c9-579602dc28ea],\n\nWe do not see any restrictions nor error codes from our side.\nPlease escalate the user and their number towards the Tech team as the problem seems to be somewhere else.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-16T07:36:23.655Z"],["3814370","HS-29001","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-16T07:37:30.456Z"],["3814373","RF-64","RF","siddhant.saxena@bolt.eu","Siddhant Saxena","Noticed there was significant difference when I tried to reconcile ( 15% bw order level data and mart data)\n\nI am waiting for Andrus for his changes.\n\nImp : I need to confirm the exact column mapping between the 4 accounts and the column names","2026-01-16T07:38:01.936Z"],["3814374","HS-28961","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:60bf5e79b1f93b0069640a64],\n\nCan you please print, stamp, sign and give [*this document*|https://bolt.box.com/s/5nram7jhj3g7q84kmhew46gn61cx761r] to Natavan?\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-16T07:38:28.031Z"],["3814376","LSS-61606","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","Their main issue from the beginning was that being on V1 means that we are charging commission from full price, not after discount and amount which eater actually paid. I am not sure what they are trying to prove with clause of 4.8. Once they found out how the commission is charged and how their sales are displayed in our invoices they raised concerns for overcharging commission and showing inflated sales from which they pay the VAT (before discounts rather than actual payed amount). They fixed overpayments of VAT with tax authorities themselves for the last two years and now commission overpayment is left as an issue. ","2026-01-16T07:39:23.535Z"],["3814377","LSS-61508","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Thank you, Stefano! How urgent is this topic? Then we know how to prioritize it. \n\nBest regards, \nKaija","2026-01-16T07:40:00.334Z"],["3814378","LSS-61516","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \n[~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] thank you for sharing all of the communications with the driver. \nI see that the deadline for submitting this response is 12 February, right? \n\nCould you please prepare a response to this driver from the factual side of his request (_an explanation of why such a situation occurs and how to avoid it in the future and a detailed report of all cancellations I have made during my 4 years of work with the Bolt platform and of all cases where customers received a refund of compensation_) so then Legal and Privacy could add any necessary legal information to this response. \n\nWould you be able to do that until 26 January? That would be great 😊 \n\nIf you have any additional questions, please let me know! \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-16T07:40:23.675Z"],["3814380","LSS-61672","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Previous ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-58596|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-58596|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:41:16.544Z"],["3814381","LSS-61248","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] , checked the T&C wording and have no issues - it’s consistent with what you said (that the survey is not anonymous). \n\nHowever, if we need to publish survey results, under T&C we are allowed to publish aggregated/anonymous information about winners, i.e. not include any names or other personal details. If that is fine from your POV, then I have no more comments 🙂 ","2026-01-16T07:41:43.673Z"],["3814383","RISK2-3249","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","[15.01 ask to LogicGate:|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1768484058338729]\n\nMultiple countries under one OR-Instance\n\n# We would like to track multiple countries under a single instance using the {{Key Risk Indicator}} section. This would allow us to log and display country level data while maintaining one Instance overall. We would still have a single assessment, potentially an overarching one, which should be sufficient as the risk event itself is assessed holistically. [@Sujith|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQBS230B] Please advise us how this could be best set up in LogicGate?\n\n* Team, As a result of this, we would have different configurations across enterprise risks for managing {{country}} data:\n** Reclassification: one OR instance per country\n** Safety: one instance with KRIs per country","2026-01-16T07:42:10.089Z"],["3814384","LSS-61670","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Previous ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-53421|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-53421|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:42:43.942Z"],["3814385","LSS-60578","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","Hi [~accountid:5bc9c3edbc49ac2bb1553bd2] - closing this ticket for now, Slack me for any follow-ups!","2026-01-16T07:43:07.634Z"],["3814386","RISK2-3248","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","[15.01. ask to LogicGate:|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09RH0NTS8J/p1768484058338729]\n\n*Risk Assessment creation and user flow*\nWhen creating an assessment for an OR-Instance, the system currently requires the user to create the assessment first and then assign it before it can be completed. We discussed enabling two immediate options for the user:\n\n* Create an assessment to assign to responsible user\n* Fill out an assessment immediately themselves\n\nFrom a user experience perspective, an Accountable Manager may want to complete the assessment straight away rather than create, assign, and then return to it. Please advise how this could be supported within LogicGate so we don’t have these extra steps.","2026-01-16T07:43:39.285Z"],["3814390","LSS-61248","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team,\n[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], thank you for your quick assistance 🙏\n[~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8], I also don’t have any additional questions, so you can proceed with this survey.\n\nThanks, everyone!","2026-01-16T07:44:49.014Z"],["3814391","LSS-60604","LSS","sakina.balayeva@bolt.eu","Sakina Balayeva","Hey [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] !\n\nABB (International Bank of Azerbaijan) plays a purely operational role in this setup. Its main function is to automatically allocate an agreed percentage (x%) from each transaction directly to the Ministry’s account.\n\nSince the Ministry provides broad marketing support for partners (in our case, Bolt) to promote cashless payments, they are willing to receive, for example, 1% per transaction. This percentage is agreed with us in advance.\n\nThis approach eliminates the need for us to collect the amount manually and transfer it at the end of each period (e.g., monthly). ABB is involved solely to ensure automated and transparent money flow.","2026-01-16T07:46:05.486Z"],["3814392","LSS-61682","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T07:46:06.974Z"],["3814393","HS-29011","HS","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[^Visa Letter (3).docx]","2026-01-16T07:46:16.795Z"],["3814395","DPM-2320","DPM","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] Please let me know if new Filter Reset button looks fine to you. Now when it’s pressed it will clean up text search and reset filters to default ones\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 09.44.04.png|width=755,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 09.44.04.png\"!","2026-01-16T07:46:20.109Z"],["3814397","LSS-61311","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Hei Fredi!\n\nHere is the updated POA - please review and let me know if I can move it to signing stage. Do you need it to be signed with Estonian e-signature?. \n[^Fredi Sepp PoA - Circle K_16.01.2026.docx] \n\nBest regards, \nKaija","2026-01-16T07:46:47.856Z"],["3814398","PFI-833666","PFI","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Hello! The above reply did not solve the issue. ","2026-01-16T07:46:50.271Z"],["3814401","LSS-61656","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Sveiki, [~accountid:712020:205d4738-bfe4-4519-9265-ae39ab3e2aed], dėkoju už ticketą.\nDokumente reikėtų pakeisti Sajūną Aliukonį į direktorių Beną Jurlovą.\n\nAtlikus pakeitimus, pasidalinkite dokumentu komentaruose ir galėsime surinkti reikiamus parašus, dėkui. ","2026-01-16T07:47:35.073Z"],["3814402","MARTECH3-1406","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Progress:\n\n# Built the [comms coverage logic|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/933909924553618?o=3829506390716583#command/4667848251610972], delivered the numbers, and shared to Business LCM team: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1V31VhV2ylgW23HAGCtpJ3LPdVY-2oLvsveQcxmtYplY/edit?gid=375664452#gid=375664452|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1V31VhV2ylgW23HAGCtpJ3LPdVY-2oLvsveQcxmtYplY/edit?gid=375664452#gid=375664452|smart-link] \n\nAction Item:\n\n# Waiting for review from Business LCM team for the sense checking\n# Replicate for other snapshot period to get patterns\n# [Build Documentation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7343702411/WIP+Lifecycle+Comms+Coverage+Calculation+-+Business+Admin]\n# If needed, build dashboard %comms coverage by lifecycle stage","2026-01-16T07:48:16.420Z"],["3814406","LSS-61674","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] I have nothing in our files regarding this case. Please can you share the previous ticket ? Thank you","2026-01-16T07:49:22.658Z"],["3814409","SCM-1125","SCM","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SCM-978?focusedCommentId=3791279|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SCM-978?focusedCommentId=3791279|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:49:55.766Z"],["3814410","FDBT-4796","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics fails on 2026-01-15 05:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 41554726607879, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-15T05%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=bolt_plus_subscription_revenue.bolt_plus_subscription_revenue&base_date=2026-01-15T05%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-16T07:50:14.568Z"],["3814411","LSS-61676","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] I have nothing in our files regarding this case. Can you share the previous ticket please?","2026-01-16T07:50:15.612Z"],["3814412","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Thanks, will handle that today.","2026-01-16T07:50:25.633Z"],["3814413","LSS-61675","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Previous ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-55224?search_id=27923e59-c6ee-43a3-9942-5e82dec75b51|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-55224?search_id=27923e59-c6ee-43a3-9942-5e82dec75b51|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:51:16.563Z"],["3814416","PFI-830905","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Looking into this","2026-01-16T07:52:19.509Z"],["3814417","PFI-834036","PFI","emmanuel.ojeikhodion@bolt-outsource.eu","Emmanuel Ojeikhodion","!Screenshot_20260116-083324.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T07:52:23.486Z"],["3814418","LSS-61673","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] I cannot find this case in our files, please can you share the previous ticket?","2026-01-16T07:52:25.605Z"],["3814419","PFI-830905","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A2M1UL9L5/p1768549641875879|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A2M1UL9L5/p1768549641875879|smart-card]","2026-01-16T07:52:38.461Z"],["3814420","LSS-61677","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Previous ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-58486|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-58486|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:52:54.917Z"],["3814421","LSS-61311","LSS","fredi.sepp@bolt.eu","Fredi Sepp","Hey!\nReviewed and the PoA can be signed. Should be signed with Estonian e-signature in .asice format. Thank you!","2026-01-16T07:53:01.568Z"],["3814422","TS-4662","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","Stage 1 - Drive workshop :done: \n\nStage 2 - Refreshment course on Micromobility - :loading: ","2026-01-16T07:53:26.270Z"],["3814425","DRX-28074","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DI.127.0 (195020870) Firebase build on iPhone 14 Pro, OS:18\n\nNew order pushes appear:\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 09-42-03_1.MP4]","2026-01-16T07:55:22.047Z"],["3814426","DRX-27566","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28074 has been resolved","2026-01-16T07:55:28.580Z"],["3814427","CSP-277","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W03: Feature flag has been cleaned up and feature is exposed to all permitted admin users. Project complete.","2026-01-16T07:55:32.154Z"],["3814429","LSS-61642","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Thank you very much[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] 🙂 \n\nI’ve raised an IT ticket, as Greg and Annet were unable to resolve the canned responses issue 😞 \nIf IT is also unable to help, I will create the canned templates myself.","2026-01-16T07:55:50.905Z"],["3814430","WD-22575","WD","lysette.ranne@bolt.eu","Lysette Ranne","Hi,\n\nWe tested it with Telema prelive invoice 9050708434-TEST(PL001), but it seems to be missing in Telema now, IN-PL001-26-000279 in sandbox. \n\n","2026-01-16T07:55:58.338Z"],["3814431","WFM-9998","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","done","2026-01-16T07:56:03.022Z"],["3814432","LSS-60324","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Thank you.","2026-01-16T07:56:27.401Z"],["3814434","WEBSD-1480","WEBSD","tekla.chikhradze@bolt.eu","Tekla Chikhradze","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.55.54.png|width=369,height=250,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.55.54.png\"!\n\nHey, I am still unable to log in. ","2026-01-16T07:56:31.620Z"],["3814435","LSS-59597","LSS","ann.koljalg@bolt.eu","Ann Kõljalg","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] Thank you! The lease agreement is quite long and understandably  will take some time! Could you provide some estimate when would you be able to finish the review so I can notify the landlord who is eagerly waiting the agreement.\n\nI have added in all my responses and will try to get response to deposit question!\n\nRegards the alternation works, Over the meeting and email LL stated they cant start with any alternation works before the agreement is signed. The lease start date will be the date the premises are delivered. Could you update the sentence based on that?","2026-01-16T07:56:36.894Z"],["3814436","CSP-344","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W03: Implementation of the fix blocking the release in progress. Expected to be completed early next week. Canary testing will continue afterwards.","2026-01-16T07:56:59.115Z"],["3814437","LSS-59641","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - please check if support is still required and if not, you can close the ticket.","2026-01-16T07:57:10.011Z"],["3814438","PFI-834018","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T07:57:20.217Z"],["3814439","RCE-345","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768550234194019]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-345 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T07:57:26.259Z"],["3814441","LSS-59421","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - please check if support is still required and if not, we can close the ticket.","2026-01-16T07:57:33.765Z"],["3814442","LSS-61534","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] \nThanks for confirming.\nI’ll go ahead and close this ticket from the Privacy side.\n\nThank you 🙂 ","2026-01-16T07:57:34.025Z"],["3814443","RCE-345","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768550240874549]*{color}:\nLocal ops to follow up with Halda. details in the main main thread\n{quote}","2026-01-16T07:57:34.613Z"],["3814445","LSS-60708","LSS","anita.kasprzyk@bolt.eu","Anita Kasprzyk","hi, thank you! sent it to the partner! 🙂 ","2026-01-16T07:57:59.723Z"],["3814446","BEE-3397","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Closing as won’t do.","2026-01-16T07:58:01.947Z"],["3814447","LSS-59165","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - reassigning to you. Keep me updated on this one as it isn’t as straight forward as some other incidents.","2026-01-16T07:58:02.037Z"],["3814448","PFI-834015","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T07:58:05.355Z"],["3814449","BEE-3398","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Closing as won’t do.","2026-01-16T07:58:10.002Z"],["3814450","BEE-3399","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Closing as won’t do.","2026-01-16T07:58:19.230Z"],["3814451","BEE-3400","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Closing as won’t do.","2026-01-16T07:58:26.463Z"],["3814452","LSS-58771","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:66cd78a4-d39f-4bba-8287-1d4b2ace432b] - closing this ticket due to inactivity. If you need help again, please reach out.","2026-01-16T07:58:26.930Z"],["3814453","BEE-3396","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Closing as won’t do.","2026-01-16T07:58:36.414Z"],["3814455","LSS-58251","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Support is ongoing, being provided to [~accountid:712020:b75759f0-ea50-4319-bfe5-48b28f4cab21] in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-60600?focusedCommentId=3770681&sourceType=mention|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-60600?focusedCommentId=3770681&sourceType=mention|smart-link]  - closing this ticket.","2026-01-16T07:59:00.564Z"],["3814457","LSS-61681","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Already handled here [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1768313361352219|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1768313361352219|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T07:59:59.159Z"],["3814458","PFI-834001","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 47.00 ZAR was issued on 17/12/2025, 01:17:48UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 16th of December to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:00:32.724Z"],["3814459","CSP-401","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W03: Workshop with PEX team held last week. PEX team is to build a first proposal for the first routine covering a full process description (including steps for agents).","2026-01-16T08:01:31.834Z"],["3814462","PFI-831167","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Well, ride receipt emails are not marketing emails and follow different rules - they are emails that contain the invoice for the ride that was taken. That said, I couldn’t find an option in my own app to switch off receiving those emails, but I know this may differ by country. Can you please reach out to [#dev-comms-and-privacy-support|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY] channel and confirm? ","2026-01-16T08:01:57.468Z"],["3814463","XP-3044","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:641d5e7c9796ea0a8718ca5e], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-16T08:02:32.257Z"],["3814464","XP-3040","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:641d5e7c9796ea0a8718ca5e], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-16T08:02:32.269Z"],["3814465","CSDT-967","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Only pending item left: get back to the user when Fleet ID is available in refunds & compensations explore","2026-01-16T08:03:05.147Z"],["3814466","LSS-61464","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","customer can’t sign as he is getting error, can reupload it. ","2026-01-16T08:03:14.011Z"],["3814467","LSS-61593","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you for the ticket. I will review and get back to you by early next week. ","2026-01-16T08:03:29.611Z"],["3814468","HS-28977","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Dudu, both letters went out. I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-16T08:03:33.360Z"],["3814469","MARTECH3-1420","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Progress:\n\n# The 1 year GMV estimated evaluation from both existing methods is here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7329972262/WIP+Evaluating+LTV+Estimation+Methods+for+Business+Ads|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7329972262/WIP+Evaluating+LTV+Estimation+Methods+for+Business+Ads|smart-link]  which we find quite big average percentage errors in the initial month of GMV actuals. \n# I’m going to build simple forecasting model for getting 1st year GMV predicted using listed tables below for building feature tables first:\n## etl_business_business_company\n## etl_business_business_daily_metrics\n## etl_business_company_churn_log\n## etl_business_company_daily_orders","2026-01-16T08:03:45.659Z"],["3814471","PFI-831803","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Our engineers are aware of this and investigating. Will keep you updated. ","2026-01-16T08:03:47.402Z"],["3814472","PFI-831803","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768214132820559?thread_ts=1767597721.342579&cid=C02C2SY0MHT|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768214132820559?thread_ts=1767597721.342579&cid=C02C2SY0MHT]","2026-01-16T08:03:50.370Z"],["3814474","LSS-61555","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you for the ticket. I will review and get back to you next week. ","2026-01-16T08:03:58.313Z"],["3814475","PFI-831803","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! \n\nLooks like this issue needs input from our developers. The issue has been flagged to them & they are investigating. We will keep you posted with any updates! \n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:03:58.318Z"],["3814477","PFI-834038","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","[^2025-11-30_2025-12-31_rides (2).csv]\n\n[^52213068-LV1125-1545.pdf]","2026-01-16T08:04:07.055Z"],["3814478","PFI-834038","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T08:04:09.475Z"],["3814481","LSS-61531","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] have we uploaded contract to sign? ","2026-01-16T08:04:41.976Z"],["3814482","RDXENG-4563","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:625fb496efc8a5006a5557e5] Let’s update both *Send* and *Receive* flow screen +titles+ and +input placeholders+ based on *final* [*design*|https://www.figma.com/design/jw4rVWHtuGnZ2RaMYIAGjH/Bolt-Parcel?node-id=327-25640&m=dev].\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09N41TTA78/p1768502817091769|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09N41TTA78/p1768502817091769|smart-card]","2026-01-16T08:04:53.115Z"],["3814483","LSS-55520","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Hi everyone!  \n\nPlease comment if this ticket can be closed? I see there is an agreement signed with Disainiosakond, but Kristjan is referring that something is still missing. Please comment if there is anything else needed. \n\nBest regards, \nKaija","2026-01-16T08:05:03.032Z"],["3814484","PFI-833987","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user was issued a 1.26 EUR refund to the Bolt balance on 14/09/2025, 17:14. \nThe balance was used on 21/09/2025, 01:55 to partially pay for their next scooter ride. \n\n\n!image-20260116-080441.png|width=1353,height=257!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T08:05:06.725Z"],["3814485","MARTECH3-1445","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","key takeaways from the discussion 2026-01-14:\n\n# After [@mostafa.mahmoud|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U077V1K7B4P] checking using logic above, we got 36% missed attribution from GA4 compared to rudderstack.\n# There is an impact of cookie consent on unique identifiers like the Google Analytics cookie, so If the users don't accept the cookie, GA4 couldn't track the event.\n# Web Team ([@orkhan.yusubov|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U017MF4BGHM]/[@tom.gander|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03LND9C54K] team) and Dev Team ([@anton.lyubarskiy|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UR3LX2Z0D] / [@mammad.imanov|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/UPV7NJW14]) to investigate the GA issue (why GA cookie created on the first step is not visible until the ID is sent) before implementing the hash identifier solution. ETA: Next week.\n# Once we go to the hash identifier solution, it requires legal involvement due to PII concern.\n# Tracking attribution is a high priority due to needs proper planning for €4.1 million marketing budget and everyone aligned as the high priority.\n# At this stage, rudderstack attribution may be used as interim attribution approach, with the notes that we'd discuss with business team on the naming convention (channel level or campaign level) we should use.","2026-01-16T08:05:10.963Z"],["3814488","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:712020:23b54a2f-1913-42e1-9019-8b2c32303d27] Let’s update both *Send* and *Receive* flow screen +titles+ and +input placeholders+ based on *final* [+*design*+|https://www.figma.com/design/jw4rVWHtuGnZ2RaMYIAGjH/Bolt-Parcel?node-id=327-25640&m=dev].\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09N41TTA78/p1768502817091769|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09N41TTA78/p1768502817091769|smart-card]","2026-01-16T08:06:13.339Z"],["3814489","LSS-61486","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] 👋 \n\nFrom what I can see, CS has already taken all the appropriate steps in line with the KB for cases involving access due to phone number recycling:\n\n* The updated KB for “access to someone else’s account due to phone number recycling” was followed.\n* Both the new phone number holder and the original account holder were contacted using the correct communication templates.\n* The original account holder was advised to update their contact details.\n* The affected account was archived to prevent any further access.\n* The reporting user was instructed to create a new account using their current phone number.\n\nFrom a privacy perspective, everything appears to be handled appropriately.\nPlease let me know if there’s anything further you’d like me to look into.","2026-01-16T08:06:14.897Z"],["3814490","LSS-61427","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:aa9604d8-cd49-4f98-bc6e-9c46af871b6b] thank you! If this was already reviewed and approved by me (I remember it was so for LV), feel free to proceed based on the same terms. ","2026-01-16T08:06:37.537Z"],["3814491","MARTECH3-1373","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","Planned for February","2026-01-16T08:07:23.675Z"],["3814492","LSS-59694","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","+Attachment from email received by Dolinda+:\n\n\n\n[^Mise_en_demeure CONTESTATION_Ben_Sik_Ali_Ameur_bolt.pdf]\n[^Copie de Engagement_sur_l_honneur_Chauffeur_Ben_Sik_Ali_Ameur.pdf]\n[^pre assignation tribunal de commerce mr ben sik.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:07:29.115Z"],["3814493","BLTF-100","BLTF","omar.quiroga@bolt.eu","Omar Quiroga","need further investigation, at the moment we cannot identify if the user just finished the onboarding","2026-01-16T08:07:35.728Z"],["3814496","MARTECH3-1354","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","hey [~accountid:712020:568b827f-68b5-432a-8f63-d9bca8543886]  could you please confirm final shape of the conversion event? I’m ooo starting mid next week so this will be implemented when I’m back on Feb","2026-01-16T08:08:43.732Z"],["3814497","GRWA-1474","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Cluster has been increased, next run test is on {{2026-02-05}}","2026-01-16T08:08:45.368Z"],["3814499","PFI-833985","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe refund was issued to the OPM instead of the Bolt Balance. \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 2.24 on Jan 9, 2026, 10:31:22 GMT+2\t\n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 9th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:10:00.520Z"],["3814500","MARTECH3-1524","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Progress:\n\nFivetran created a schema and tables, but nobody has ownership on that since Data Platform no longer own models and maintain the privileges on them, so Tomasz raised a ticket to claim ownership, then I’ll request ticket to get the access to the tables.","2026-01-16T08:10:05.179Z"],["3814502","EBIKE1-424","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","QC will check if battery swapping is OK or NOT then there will be rework either by the assembly factory or in local WHs. ","2026-01-16T08:10:10.367Z"],["3814503","LSS-59467","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:642aa1eb7e859baa54f54b06], my apologies for the delayed response.\n\nGiven that the overall risk level is assessed as medium, you may proceed with the implementation of the security feature. The ODPO team will review the DPIA in parallel so as not to delay your timelines.\n\nPlease let us know if any material changes arise during implementation that may impact the risk assessment.","2026-01-16T08:10:16.994Z"],["3814506","LSS-61412","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:aa9604d8-cd49-4f98-bc6e-9c46af871b6b] , to review the terms more effectively, please always ask clients to reflect the changes they want directly in the Special Terms, instead of sending comments by email.\n\nThis time, let’s keep the comments as they are - I will reply next week. Thank you! 🙂 ","2026-01-16T08:11:30.593Z"],["3814508","INT-425","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","added 0 additional effort for eng as development is done, only need alignment w growth on timing and then configuration help from [~accountid:63184a4556010c40d44804e6]  next.","2026-01-16T08:11:55.622Z"],["3814510","INT-425","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: will align next week with Food vertical growth team on countries and timing to rollout to rest of markets, and then configuration help from Guru.","2026-01-16T08:12:14.698Z"],["3814512","MLC-3895","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W3:\n\n* Follow up emails for the Pilot went out on 09.01\n* Follow up SMS went out on 12.01\n* Coordinating with Klāvs on content for full launch in Feb\n* In December, Sponsored Listings generated ~144,000 € in revenue across all markets. Pilot list we’ve been sending comms to contains around 23k IDs ","2026-01-16T08:12:45.383Z"],["3814513","LSS-61659","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hello [~accountid:60c88e6e8f2cc1006909fcf6] , thank you! Please specify the deadline for this task. ","2026-01-16T08:12:54.317Z"],["3814516","BP-13415","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] I selected location for the banner in emails\n[https://www.figma.com/design/l2rr94ixcSA5XLK1WffT35/BB-Emails?node-id=1010-424&t=OjbRMjiJ6si0oG45-4|https://www.figma.com/design/l2rr94ixcSA5XLK1WffT35/BB-Emails?node-id=1010-424&t=OjbRMjiJ6si0oG45-4|smart-link] \nThis can be scaled across them all, no need for each design, between heading and body\nLet me know what you think","2026-01-16T08:14:06.888Z"],["3814517","PFI-832667","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Billing does not handle pricing. Please reach out to the pricing team to have them advise. ","2026-01-16T08:14:16.062Z"],["3814518","LSS-61101","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","Just to confirm, sending there signed agreement by the second part. Thanks a lot for solving this 🙏 \n\n[^aneks czynsz 2026 bolt podpisany .pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:14:17.565Z"],["3814519","PFI-831167","PFI","kornelia.chrustowska@bolt-outsource.eu","Kornelia Chrustowska","[~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] unfortunately agents RH don’t have access to these channels.","2026-01-16T08:14:20.296Z"],["3814520","PFI-832667","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:14:22.210Z"],["3814521","HS-28996","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:1a447c27-5947-4ed5-b674-3b465dfa89ac],\n\nI have contacted the Workday Team, as People Ops is unable to edit this field.\n\nAll the best,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-16T08:14:23.038Z"],["3814522","PFI-831167","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:14:24.125Z"],["3814523","PFI-834039","PFI","marten.koger@bolt.eu","Marten Koger","Hello [~accountid:712020:2a2780a7-8f76-45e2-8861-75ee162bf2c9],\n\nGenerally we do not really deal with this part, as this is mostly considered as a behavioural issue and not exactly fraud, however, this specific user is generating negative GMV to us, therefore, we will be suspending them for failed payments and refunds.\n\nIn the future, please consider similar cases where users attempt to get more money/refunds a behavioural case. These should be considered to be escalated towards OPS/Safety.\n\nFor this specific user we already took action and permanently suspended them from the platform. If you still need to contact the user, then kindly note that they have no further access to the app, therefore, messages can only be sent via the e-mail.\n\nBest,\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:14:34.314Z"],["3814525","BDB-1546","BDB",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Jevgeni Trombovetski 👋. This is a reminder, that the task is due today or it's resolved but hasn't been moved to \"Done\" status yet.\n\n- If the task is resolved, move it to the \"Done\" status. Or if the task is canceled, move it to \"Canceled\" status\n\n- If the task can't be resolved in the initial timeframe, then make sure that the Project Manager(Team Lead, in case PM is not available), and Customer are notified. And change the new due date accordingly.","2026-01-16T08:15:14.308Z"],["3814527","BLTF-100","BLTF","reinis.paulins@bolt.eu","Reinis Paulins","A skeleton screen is a temporary, content-shaped placeholder that appears while data is loading.  Instead of showing a blank screen or a spinner, the app displays a simplified version of the layout with gray blocks or lines where text, images, or cards will eventually appear.\n\nSkeletons make the app feel faster by showing progress immediately, even if content still needs a few seconds to load.","2026-01-16T08:15:41.617Z"],["3814529","RCE-355","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768551357046279]*{color}:\nHey! A clarification please, is this an internal initiative or a regulatory request?\n<@U02JFD5KMUH> could you please help assess this and with setting up the gradual rollout, if it is needed?\n\n&gt; Can we set the frequency at *multiple times a day*?\nTechnically, we can. how many times per day are we looking at?\n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:16:11.490Z"],["3814533","LSS-61656","LSS","diana.morkunaite@bolt.eu","Diana Morkūnaitė","[^Teisiniu paslaugu sutarties Priedas 12 (3).pdf]\n\natsiprašau, ne tą failą prisegiau, šitas sutvarkytas.","2026-01-16T08:16:23.666Z"],["3814536","PFI-832920","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","👋 Hey there,\n\nPlease try:\n\n* Open the [Client page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] in Admin \n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open  {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ - The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see another _error_ → let us know.\n* if you see _to_execute →_ it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the tab (or under {{Partner Invoices}})\n\nBest regards\n\nKetlin Peldes ","2026-01-16T08:16:43.482Z"],["3814538","PFI-834042","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T08:16:54.131Z"],["3814539","INT-753","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: getting internal team feedback on doc, once edited, will share with designer (dependency) for design work. ","2026-01-16T08:17:21.502Z"],["3814541","WD-22580","WD","sofja.pomazan@bolt.eu","Sofja Pomazan","Hi [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82], I do not have new invoices in draft status now. But I added the tax code and tax applicability for IN-EE003-26-001207 and IN-EE003-26-001183","2026-01-16T08:17:45.926Z"],["3814543","WFM-9992","WFM","tomas.lu@bolt.eu","Tomáš Lu","Hello [~accountid:712020:9c0690de-08a9-41cf-93b1-9184ed368330],\n\nI’ve checked the permissions with the agent, and he still does not have the role in the admin. Could you please double-check if the role was granted to [~accountid:712020:f004d9ba-8f6a-434f-b0e4-94977446c91d] ?\n\n","2026-01-16T08:19:22.925Z"],["3814544","PFI-833045","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please summarize the issue. What is the issue with balance exactly, for what period, what’s the expected amount and why? Thanks! ","2026-01-16T08:19:33.501Z"],["3814545","LSS-61684","LSS","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","Here is the request from our supplier  Incap Electronics Estonia OÜ:\n\n“2025 financial audit of Incap Electronics Estonia OÜ is done by Audiitorteenuse OÜ. In this connection we kindly ask you to compare balances as of *31.12.2025*.\n\nPlease send your confirmation to [kinnituskirjad@audiitorteenused.ee|mailto:kinnituskirjad@audiitorteenused.ee] as presented in the file attached, signed by a member of the Management Board or by a person properly authorized*.* We would be grateful if you could respond by *16.01.2026*. As this is at very short notice, we would appreciate it if you could respond as soon as possible.”\n\n\n\n[^INCAP Confirmation Request 2025_Bolt Operations OÜ.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:19:36.881Z"],["3814547","LSS-59404","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Ongoing ","2026-01-16T08:19:59.521Z"],["3814548","CSXRT-154","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Will be discussed with the Process team regarding new issue titles & tagging as it’s connected to their initiatives ","2026-01-16T08:20:00.288Z"],["3814549","LSS-61581","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","I have already changed it and sent it out again, so no action for You 🙂 ","2026-01-16T08:20:17.070Z"],["3814550","LSS-61148","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","What about we ask Product Legal to answer this ticket?","2026-01-16T08:20:39.750Z"],["3814553","LSS-59339","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Is that something where [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] can help you?","2026-01-16T08:22:04.530Z"],["3814554","LSS-61516","LSS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] Hi! \nWe already shared the full order history with the driver, where it’s shown how ma many cancelled orders he had. We agreed with the Privacy Legal team that we should not share information as to which rider requested and successfully obtained refunds - this isn't personal data about the driver.\nThe driver is not happy with this response and is still requesting to know if he received all the compensations, or whether some were withheld from his balance.\ncc: [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] \n\n","2026-01-16T08:22:05.093Z"],["3814557","PFI-833254","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please reach out to the campaigns team to have them look into this, as afaik we receive this data from them. Thanks! ","2026-01-16T08:22:21.667Z"],["3814558","PFI-833254","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:22:29.219Z"],["3814560","GRWA-1482","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","rider lpct cohort lifetime value view in looker was using internal schema, it has been replaced with mart","2026-01-16T08:22:39.105Z"],["3814561","LSS-60403","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","*Internal Note – IBAN Disclosure (France)*\n\n* Bolt can disclose IBANs if legally required (e.g. _droit de communication_ under Labour/Transport Code).\n* Doesn’t trigger requalification risk alone if response is limited, justified, and Bolt reaffirms its role as booking platform (not employer).\n* IBAN use is allowed under commercial agent exemption (no payment license needed) – funds are routed via PSPs.\n* Always check legal basis, log disclosure, send securely. Avoid voluntary DPAE/vigilance checks unless legally required.","2026-01-16T08:22:41.419Z"],["3814562","LSS-58302","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:23:06.913Z"],["3814563","RCE-355","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768551747249639]*{color}:\n<@U01FT85U92N> let's take it to the safety request channel \n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:23:12.749Z"],["3814568","RCE-355","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Shreya Bhandari [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768551806234499]*{color}:\n<@U02GQDXF7KJ> create a request on <#C07TWR3FL0P|> and we will discuss there \n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:23:38.384Z"],["3814569","LSS-59076","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:23:49.191Z"],["3814571","L10N-28198","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28192](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28192)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:23:57.382Z"],["3814572","L10N-28200","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28192](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28192)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:23:59.033Z"],["3814573","L10N-28202","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communicati