he latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28193](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28193)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:24:48.676Z"],["3814603","L10N-28255","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28193](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28193)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:24:50.809Z"],["3814604","LSS-59745","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:24:53.911Z"],["3814605","L10N-28265","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28193](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28193)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:24:55.166Z"],["3814606","CSXRT-163","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Under discussion topics for 29.01 MBR","2026-01-16T08:25:00.356Z"],["3814607","LSS-59835","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:25:07.553Z"],["3814608","LSS-59882","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:25:21.689Z"],["3814609","PRODSEC-658","PRODSEC","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","Follow-up (less severe) vuln: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/VULN-1460?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiZTM4NDdjMTEwNzQzNDM1NzhkMjllZGE0YTFiNjYwYjEiLCJwIjoiaiJ9|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/VULN-1460?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiZTM4NDdjMTEwNzQzNDM1NzhkMjllZGE0YTFiNjYwYjEiLCJwIjoiaiJ9|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T08:25:22.082Z"],["3814612","LSS-59914","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:25:55.593Z"],["3814613","PFI-833982","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 119.00 ZAR was issued on 22/12/2025, 11:01:49UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 19th of December to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:25:56.506Z"],["3814614","LSS-59922","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:26:10.494Z"],["3814615","SCM-837","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] do you approve this process? Can I mark the task as done?","2026-01-16T08:26:15.066Z"],["3814617","LSS-60382","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:26:41.491Z"],["3814618","SCM-839","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] do you approve this process? Can I mark the task as done?","2026-01-16T08:26:42.286Z"],["3814619","CSXRT-196","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","[~accountid:712020:5b21df93-85a4-4d9e-9f87-9708ebfe5439] Will perform analysis as per priority during Q1","2026-01-16T08:26:46.051Z"],["3814620","LSS-60386","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:26:54.524Z"],["3814623","LSS-60638","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:27:32.075Z"],["3814628","PFI-833965","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 52.90 ZAR was issued on 01/01/2026, 12:46:14UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 31st of December to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:28:02.897Z"],["3814629","SREDESK-7419","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","I have set up the on-call schedules for the team; however, some of your team members do not have an on-call role assigned in Rootly. I recommend asking within your team to identify who can request this role.\n\nAdditionally, you'll need to finish configuring the webhooks.\n\n\n*Basic Alert Workflow:*\n\n# An alert arrives and is received by the webhook.\n# A routing rule sends it to the \"Intsec Alerts\" service.\n# The service triggers the \"InfoSec - Internal Security\" escalation policy.\n# Notifications are sent:\n#* *Schedule:* Alerts the on-call person for the week.\n#* *Slack:* Posts to the #alerts-security-tooling channel.","2026-01-16T08:28:05.862Z"],["3814630","PFI-833963","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T08:28:26.717Z"],["3814632","LSS-60071","LSS","mahmoud.iskandarani@bolt.eu","Mahmoud Iskandarani","[~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] DB just emailed you the docs. Waiting on Citi ","2026-01-16T08:28:36.788Z"],["3814633","PFI-833958","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T08:28:44.318Z"],["3814636","PFI-833953","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T08:29:25.854Z"],["3814637","LSS-60701","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, attaching here the document signed by the partner. Igne’s signature is missing currently. As today will be my last day then kindly obtain the duly signed version from the system once it has been signed by Igne as well. In the meantime attaching here the version with only partner’s signature.\n\n[^ANNEX 2 to LT251043-LT251060_AT agreement_18 cars.adoc]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:29:45.971Z"],["3814638","LSS-60997","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:30:04.364Z"],["3814641","LSS-60999","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, closing the ticket due to inactivity. In cases of any issues or questions regarding this please reach out to [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-16T08:30:16.258Z"],["3814642","DO-5767","DO","kostiantyn.tsykulenko@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Tsykulenko","details communicated on Slack","2026-01-16T08:30:18.157Z"],["3814643","LSS-58270","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:feba077c-0585-4e5b-8e4d-2cdc0e19ecf8] , can you take a look at my latest comment please? 🙏 ","2026-01-16T08:30:23.120Z"],["3814644","DLSP-1993","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-16T08:30:27.617Z"],["3814645","LSS-58698","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:07746941-2eee-430d-a2cf-f3aa307d9a17] - could you please confirm whether you need any further support on this ticket?","2026-01-16T08:30:35.278Z"],["3814647","PFI-833949","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for sharing the bank statement. \nThe refund is displayed to the user in the Pending Card Transactions section. \nPlease instruct the user to check with their bank why the refund is still pending. \n\n!image-20260116-083049.png|width=738,height=102!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T08:31:12.407Z"],["3814648","WEBSD-1480","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Ok I will get back to you directly with few steps to follow.","2026-01-16T08:31:14.051Z"],["3814651","DLSP-1961","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","Not clear how to fix this test and what is the rootcause, so we marked the test with {{xctest}}","2026-01-16T08:32:00.557Z"],["3814653","CSXRT-197","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","New global dashboard created by the data team - [Refunds & Compensations|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/28188?Time+Period=3+week&Is+Partner+market+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=&Is+Bolt+Business+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=&Geography+Grain=Country&Time+Grain=Week&Geography+Value=&Is+Rental+Fine+Refund+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=No&Vertical=delivery&Is+Refund+Initiated+by+User+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=No&Is+Refund+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=&Is+Solved+by+Automation+Refund+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=&Actor+at+Fault=&Refund+Target=&Is+Legacy+Automation+Refund+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=&Is+AI+Refund+%28Yes+%2F+No%29=]","2026-01-16T08:32:09.516Z"],["3814654","SCM-1059","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Data Analytics team request for adding Motor controller serial numbers.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030MJW96CA/p1768552190944939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030MJW96CA/p1768552190944939|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T08:32:13.882Z"],["3814655","PFI-833405","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! That’s because there’s also cash toll road (which the driver already has as cash in hand), that’s where the difference is coming from. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.31.38.png|width=630,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.31.38.png\"!","2026-01-16T08:32:15.306Z"],["3814656","LSS-61435","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Assigning this to You [~accountid:5f0436f3b545e20015573888] as it’s in Dokobit and You have been added as a viewer.","2026-01-16T08:32:26.465Z"],["3814657","PFI-827943","PFI","ngoc.nguyen@bolt-outsource.eu","Ngoc Thien Nguyen","Hi!, the driver is asking about the balance on the following week from 29/12/2025 to 04/01/2026\n\n!image-20260116-083235.png|width=1145,height=168,alt=\"image-20260116-083235.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-16T08:33:07.726Z"],["3814658","LSS-60604","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Hi [~accountid:712020:72d9f759-4292-4662-bbdb-0a2843291aff], thank you, the draft contract has the following provision:\n\n_The Bank provides acquiring services to the Partner for arranging payments_ *_under the POS Terminal Installation and Operation/E-commerce Through Electronic Trading Platforms Contract, most recently concluded and currently in force between the Bank and the Partner (hereinafter – the Contract)._* \n\nCan you please confirm that there is a mentioned contract for arranging payments between us and the bank?","2026-01-16T08:33:12.251Z"],["3814660","LSS-60403","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] agreed - invoices contain sensitive information (rider details). \n\nI would suggest the following response - please could you review and confirm that you are aligned so that we can confirm to Dolinda?\n\n\n+ENG+:\nDear Madam,\n\nRegarding your request for invoices issued by Bolt Operations OÜ “in the name and on behalf of” each listed EVTC, we wish to draw your attention to the fact that these invoices contain passengers’ personal data (in particular, pick-up/drop-off addresses, and potentially identifying information), which are protected under the GDPR and French consumer protection law.\n\nTo ensure that any transmission is compliant with applicable data protection regulations, we would be grateful if you could clarify:\n\n* Which specific elements of the invoices are required;\n\n* The purpose of this request, so that we may assess whether a partial or anonymised transmission would meet your needs.\n\nWe of course remain fully available to cooperate in good faith and in accordance with our legal obligations.\n\n+FR+:\n\nMadame,\n\nConcernant votre demande relative à la facturation émise par la société Bolt Operations OÜ « au nom et pour le compte » de chaque EVTC mentionné, nous souhaitons attirer votre attention sur le fait que ces factures contiennent des données à caractère personnel de passagers (notamment adresses de départ/arrivée, potentiellement des noms ou éléments identifiants), protégées par le RGPD et le Code de la consommation.\n\nAfin de garantir une transmission conforme aux exigences de la réglementation en matière de protection des données personnelles, nous vous serions reconnaissants de bien vouloir préciser :\n\n* Quels éléments spécifiques de ces factures vous souhaitez obtenir ;\n\n* L’objectif poursuivi par cette demande, afin d’évaluer si une transmission partielle ou anonymisée pourrait répondre à vos besoins.\n\nNous restons bien entendu pleinement disponibles pour coopérer dans le respect des obligations légales qui nous incombent.","2026-01-16T08:33:22.870Z"],["3814662","PRODSEC-562","PRODSEC","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","Rejecting task for now:\n* Not doable with current access\n* rootly not considered secure enough for storing sensitive security incidents ","2026-01-16T08:33:42.273Z"],["3814663","LSS-61529","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached.\n\n[^Motor vehicle sale agreement_Bolt Services LT UAB_Fleetcom UAB_14.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:33:43.262Z"],["3814664","LSS-58698","LSS","juozas.masteika@bolt.eu","Juozas Masteika","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] the answer was sent. I don’t need further support. We can close the ticket. Thank you! 🙂 ","2026-01-16T08:33:50.181Z"],["3814665","PFI-833790","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi, indeed there is a BFC missing - fleet should NEVER be created without attaching a fee calculator. Please create a ticket to our configurations changes queue so we could look into this. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T08:34:12.238Z"],["3814666","PFI-833790","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:34:17.881Z"],["3814667","PFI-833910","PFI","filip.kieronczyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Filip Kieronczyk","please let a human agent analyse this case, AI responses are inaccurate","2026-01-16T08:34:58.968Z"],["3814668","LSS-58596","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Good day [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nI sent another ticket yesterday, the Lawyer reverted.\n\nI attached the new documents and info, on yesterday’s ticket that got cancelled\n\n\n\nThank you\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-16T08:35:22.180Z"],["3814669","DRX-28234","DRX","maxim.nikulin@bolt.eu","Maxim Nikulin","4QA:\n- check that phone numbers sent to `partnerDriver/startAuthentication` don't have spaces and always have `plus` sign before \"372 5367 9185\" -> +\"37253679185\" for all auth options with phone number: manual entering, autofill suggestions, saved phone number from previous successful login","2026-01-16T08:35:55.169Z"],["3814671","LSS-58698","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Many thanks for confirming. Have a good day! 🙏 ","2026-01-16T08:36:49.474Z"],["3814674","CMO-12980","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Stores course updates regarding the Picker app are anticipated. [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QMGQqycoC1sEFBy-9eHkJLCAe9wmAlp0wr-wFfmQlSI/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.kop3d7anhy9p|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QMGQqycoC1sEFBy-9eHkJLCAe9wmAlp0wr-wFfmQlSI/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.kop3d7anhy9p|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T08:37:03.689Z"],["3814676","SRED-1062","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, costs diff hard to calculate as some nodepools got more redises in the middle.\n\nIn general, some nodepool got costs decrease by ~50$, some increase by similar amount.","2026-01-16T08:37:16.916Z"],["3814678","LSS-61670","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742]\n\nI am unable to access the link sent for the previous ticket.\n\nI sent another ticket yesterday, and the Lawyer reverted.\n\nI attached the new documents and info, to yesterday’s ticket that got cancelled\n\n \n\nThank you\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n","2026-01-16T08:37:40.040Z"],["3814679","LSS-59597","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7], thank you for this information! \nI’ll do my best to finish the review of this agreement no later that Tuesday EOD, thank you very much for your understanding 🙏 ","2026-01-16T08:37:44.848Z"],["3814680","L10N-28274","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28272](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28272)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:38:37.034Z"],["3814681","L10N-28279","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28272](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28272)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:38:39.398Z"],["3814682","L10N-28276","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28272](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28272)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T08:38:39.556Z"],["3814683","L10N-28278","L10N",null,"Automat