ohhalev","Hi [~accountid:712020:717fab88-dfd9-4711-a062-2c115084414e] !\n\nIt seems that you have selected incorrect queue in SD, since Customer support doesn’t own Looks about courier data, as well as this specific one - “_Courier Info_”\n\nPlease contact [#food-analytics|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/CNBHSTPAN] in Slack for additional assistance.","2026-01-16T08:38:52.007Z"],["3814692","LSS-61315","LSS","jelena.glavas@bolt.eu","Jelena Glavaš","Hi team, \nwe are still missing signed contract [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf]  [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] \nWhen can we expect it? \n\nThank you","2026-01-16T08:39:31.931Z"],["3814693","CAMLE-9826","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","Feature Channel [#feature-dynamic-holdout-labels|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0A9YH07XCG]","2026-01-16T08:39:35.068Z"],["3814694","PFI-833886","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi - the business doesn’t have any rides though? [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/262667?tab=invoices&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/262667?tab=invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]","2026-01-16T08:39:56.567Z"],["3814695","PFI-833904","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:40:19.159Z"],["3814697","PFI-833959","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please create this to our tax tech queue so we can better support: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T08:41:01.454Z"],["3814698","PFI-833890","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T08:41:03.121Z"],["3814699","HS-29000","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi Marja,\n\nThanks for letting us know!\nI uploaded the NDA for signing between you and Christopher.\nHave a nice end of the week!\n\nKind regards,\nAike-Maris ","2026-01-16T08:41:09.329Z"],["3814700","PFI-833959","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:41:11.713Z"],["3814703","HS-28966","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi, task is already submitted, so just assigning to you to put Closed Complete :heart_hands: ","2026-01-16T08:41:31.641Z"],["3814704","PFI-833878","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 13.46 on Dec 10, 2025, 13:06:34 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505344002308153064 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 10th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_MCBDGLW5CH3TT5Q9_HRGZ6L5GS2QSPNQ9.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:42:18.814Z"],["3814705","LSS-61656","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:205d4738-bfe4-4519-9265-ae39ab3e2aed] puiku, dėkui! \n \nTo the Legal Ops team,\n\nCould we please obtain the signatures for this document?\n\nOn Bolt’s side, the signatory is *Benas Jurlovas*, and on the law firm’s side, *Rūta Goliančik* (email: [ruta.goliancik@advocorg.eu|mailto:ruta.goliancik@advocorg.eu]).\n\nThank you very much — much appreciated 🙏\n\n\n[^Teisiniu paslaugu sutarties Priedas 12 (3) (72ee6d6a-1f66-4071-8938-6ae9d1507119).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:42:33.547Z"],["3814706","LSS-61674","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","[^BOLT- SLIMANI Hicham (1).pdf]\n\n[~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nShould we treat this as a new request?\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.42.16.png|width=1023,height=357,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.42.16.png\"!\n\n\n\nDriver (7329987)  [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7329987?tab=profile&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FParis|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7329987?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FParis]","2026-01-16T08:42:34.416Z"],["3814707","CEBF-1700","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] AC8, AC9\nSo I validate that in one year for the country and group can be only one active plan (AC9).\nTo avoid related duplicates, we can check duplicates between related accounts for each plan. Right? (AC8)","2026-01-16T08:43:06.600Z"],["3814708","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768552978079809]*{color}:\nSo who is going to pick this up? You as missing part of the migration or us?\n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:43:10.963Z"],["3814709","DELIVERY-751","DELIVERY","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","26W3\n\n*Backend*\n\n* Logistic planning started working on the found problem. ETA of delivery is EOW or BOW\n\n*Front*\n\n* Continue addressing review notes","2026-01-16T08:43:31.112Z"],["3814710","PFI-834042","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Yes, I can see that there were some updates to the cash block threshold. I recommend reaching out to the local ops team to see what the reasoning behind this was if further reasoning is needed.","2026-01-16T08:43:33.352Z"],["3814713","HS-29015","HS","lilian.nguyo@bolt.eu","Lilian Nguyo","[^_Visa Letter Lilian.docx]","2026-01-16T08:44:20.522Z"],["3814715","WFM-10019","WFM","cheryl.annum@bolt.eu","Cheryl Odofoley Annum","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 8.41.21 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T08:44:37.408Z"],["3814716","GWSP-6","GWSP","martin.tomberg@bolt.eu","Martin Tomberg","Waitng Infosec access","2026-01-16T08:44:50.644Z"],["3814720","PFI-833849","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking with pawaPay \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06S6M3J6RY/p1768553132898369|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06S6M3J6RY/p1768553132898369]","2026-01-16T08:45:44.678Z"],["3814723","WFM-9472","WFM","karine.puls@bolt.eu","Karine Kersting Puls","Hello [~accountid:712020:ddf1e045-1184-4210-9e73-da3ce949a13b]! \n\nI joined the safety team last week, and I also can’t assign the tickets. Could you please give me the same access you gave to my colleagues to Global T2 and safety? \n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T08:46:47.831Z"],["3814726","CEBF-1700","CEBF","pradeep.yadav@bolt.eu","Pradeep Kumar Yadav","[~accountid:712020:c573470a-712d-474e-a9e6-b0635a9decb9] No not related accounts.\n\nOne active JBP for Year+Group+Country","2026-01-16T08:47:23.101Z"],["3814728","LSS-57822","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] I’ll take a look next week!","2026-01-16T08:47:32.603Z"],["3814730","DO-5802","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Please approve this rna to get the access. [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/4200176|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/4200176] \nI will let you know when the sync succeeded. ","2026-01-16T08:47:51.210Z"],["3814731","LSS-59339","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n[~accountid:5f0ea3c39d9a1200294cef2c], if necessary, I can order a translation of these T&Cs. However, as you’ve seen the quality, it would still require the same review as this DeepL translation.\nBut please let me know how I can help. ","2026-01-16T08:47:53.129Z"],["3814734","LOC-3813","LOC","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Hi [~accountid:62472b362e101c006a8f50e6] \n\nSorry for the late message — it’s been a very heavy workload, and I’m only now able to take care of this.\n\nWould it be okay to set up the campaign and send it on Monday, 19 January? 😃 \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T08:48:41.528Z"],["3814738","LSS-61676","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Morning [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nI re double-checked, and this Driver is only blocked for failed selfies.\n\nI will respond to the lawyer, send him the reactivation link, and ask him to give it to the driver so he can send the request.\n\nHope it is okay \n\n\n\nDolinda","2026-01-16T08:49:07.056Z"],["3814739","PAW-14938","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T08:49:45.063Z"],["3814742","LSS-61676","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Or would you like to draft a text to accompany the reactivation link that I will send?\n\nMaybe that would be better, to have a text drafted by Legal to explain that it was a failed selfie check back in nov 2025.","2026-01-16T08:50:13.967Z"],["3814743","AIOT-509","AIOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Results: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1j0QiIAv49HU46xeiD9QcGjnsuoFrJQVzwPI-Mzo-awc/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1j0QiIAv49HU46xeiD9QcGjnsuoFrJQVzwPI-Mzo-awc/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-16T08:50:14.810Z"],["3814745","HS-29011","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Celia, than you for the request. I have sent the letter for signing. It should come to your personal email. ","2026-01-16T08:50:53.596Z"],["3814748","INT-452","INT","marina.pai@bolt.eu","Marina Pai","let’s break this into two initiatives (enter promo code and require specific payment method) [~accountid:712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] ","2026-01-16T08:51:01.945Z"],["3814749","PFI-834073","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-16T08:51:31.478Z"],["3814750","PFI-834073","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:712020:cd367b4f-9ca2-4acd-bd4a-af6de2c8976a, 61f3e7cd632452006b8c120b] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T08:51:33.089Z"],["3814751","LSS-55224","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","[~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nI attached new documents and info written by the lawyer to the ticket sent yesterday about this driver\n\nThanks\n\nDolinda","2026-01-16T08:51:56.290Z"],["3814752","LOC-4683","LOC","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Hey [~accountid:712020:b88aff9e-121c-4a18-aa7f-eafdec68f35a] [~accountid:61a72da5d5986c006a3673d4] [~accountid:712020:e87531cf-1339-41a0-abb7-aa4f7f3ef984] [~accountid:712020:0810e688-9019-4b45-a466-a274a885f3f9] [~accountid:712020:eeb243a0-2dca-4f48-84e6-fb2758545a65] \n\nSee above campaigns for Q1. The team is in the process of adding all necessary documentation for these initiatives.","2026-01-16T08:51:59.928Z"],["3814753","LSS-61516","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949], thanks for sharing this!\nCould you please add the response you’ve already shared with the driver to this ticket?\nAlso, could you please clarify what kind of legal support is needed here?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T08:51:59.939Z"],["3814755","WDFT-3607","WDFT","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] ! Please now add BG002 and PL002 to the hierarchy. Thank you! 🙂 \nIs there a way we could maintain the list ourselves? 🤔 \n\n","2026-01-16T08:52:06.843Z"],["3814759","PFI-833838","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 101.00 ZAR was issued on 02/12/2025, 11:53:05UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 30th of November to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:53:27.116Z"],["3814765","PART-575","PART","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Note: If budget is not 100% consume in incentives we need to execute a backup media plan. \n","2026-01-16T08:54:35.883Z"],["3814766","FX-3587","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768553676045549]*{color}:\nDiscussed in the main thread - changes will be made by the rider team. I'll close this issue\n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:54:50.721Z"],["3814767","PFI-833849","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe have received a confirmation from pawaPay the payment has been now refunded. Please see the proof of refund attached. \nI will work to fix the payment state in Admin as well. \n\n\n[^payout_73172754904.pdf]\n\nCheers, \nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T08:54:56.452Z"],["3814769","HS-29017","HS","mohammad.rahil@bolt.eu","Shaikh Mohd Rahil","!Rahil's Medical certificate.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T08:55:00.794Z"],["3814772","INT-85","INT","zhenyu.wang@bolt.eu","Zhenyu Wang","26W3 Experimentation design for comparing churned uplift model and LPCT churned part is finalised. Experiment is set to be launched next week.","2026-01-16T08:55:12.235Z"],["3814773","FX-3587","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768553702250379]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3587 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:55:14.964Z"],["3814774","LSS-61616","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Team,\n\nCould you please confirm whether it is possible to share data simultaneously while a ride is taking place?\n\nIf so, we would appreciate clarification on any limitations or constraints associated with this process. As mentioned during the call, there is interest in accessing data in real time, i.e. while the ride is ongoing.\n\nAdditionally, as discussed, one of the objectives of this exercise is, as a second step, to establish a clear framework outlining:\n\n* what data can be requested,\n* under which legal basis, and\n* within which timeframe.\n\nThank you in advance for your support.\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-16T08:55:20.162Z"],["3814775","LSS-61673","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nThis driver seems to have multiple accounts that have all been blocked. \n\nBelow is the most recent one: Abdelmonaim Taleb, blocked 28 Aug 2025\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.54.53.png|width=978,height=268,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.54.53.png\"!\n\n\n\nDriver - 6441306 -  [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/6441306?tab=profile&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FParis|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/6441306?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FParis]\n\n","2026-01-16T08:55:29.108Z"],["3814777","PAW-14933","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160933\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 08:55:33 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T08:55:33.850Z"],["3814778","HS-29015","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Lilian, thank you for the request. I have sent the letter for singing. It should come to your personal email, once signed. ","2026-01-16T08:55:38.702Z"],["3814779","PFI-834076","PFI","jeff.irikefe@bolt-outsource.eu","Jeff Irikefe","!JPEG_1768552071820_8381175894359934559.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T08:55:43.619Z"],["3814780","PFI-833837","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T08:55:51.246Z"],["3814782","DSR-3777","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T08:56:06.487Z"],["3814783","PAW-14821","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/pull/3078\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 08:56:14 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T08:56:15.161Z"],["3814784","LSS-58930","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:d77c5e6c-f92f-4d79-955d-9f88e6d0a883] ,\n\nDo you have any information on the scope of coverage of Advantage Saúde?\n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T08:56:30.549Z"],["3814785","MVRT-1446","MVRT","evamaria.ots@bolt.eu","Eva Maria Ots","[~accountid:5fa51169b38e61007151d47e] Just use local pricing yes, the comms are targeting based on city_ID anyway, yeah? ","2026-01-16T08:56:37.755Z"],["3814786","WEBSD-1475","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c]  👋 \n\nI hope you are doing great.\n\nTo move forward, I need to confirm the correct upload path for these documents. Should these be handled by your side or the Legal team? . I do not know where they should go.\n\n*TnC Section* - Doesn't have global section and it was requested by legal time that way e.g [https://bolt.eu/en/legal/|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/|smart-link] \n\n*Privacy Section* *Policy*- It has global section and maybe it should be there under *Other* section e.g  [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|smart-link]  but still all legal files that we upload need approval from legal and for this case it should be Privacy team (Maybe you can talk with [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] )\n\n*EU section is under all European countries* e.g [https://bolt.eu/en-at/legal/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/en-at/legal/?category=rides|smart-link]  . I do not think it should be here.\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.42.28.png|width=654,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.42.28.png\"!\n\n*My proposal would be Privacy Policy but as I mentioned it has to be confirmed by privacy team.* \n\nLet me know your comments and I hope this info can help.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \n","2026-01-16T08:56:39.422Z"],["3814787","MM-943","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description, requirements, or acceptance criteria provided.|\n|Clarity|🟡|Summary is understandable, but lacks detail and context.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-16T08:56:40.032Z"],["3814788","LSS-58486","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nThe lawyer reverted after receiving the above\n\nI attached the new documents and info to the ticket sent yesterday.\n\n\n\n\n\nDolinda","2026-01-16T08:56:47.311Z"],["3814791","FX-3440","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Emiwodew Nigussie Gizaw [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768553826390479]*{color}:\nIs this discussion still active or can I close the ticket?\n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:57:18.840Z"],["3814794","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* cs-d1 downscale: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15426|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15426]","2026-01-16T08:57:35.454Z"],["3814799","LSS-59864","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:61b6f8b2599f18006a270ae2] ,\n\nPlease let me know when you hear back from the agency handling this agreement with the influencer.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T08:58:22.370Z"],["3814800","CSP-451","CSP","quentin.legrand@bolt.eu","Quentin Émile N. Legrand","26W3: continued EDA, plan to create doc around it. Next week will be dedicated to prototyping","2026-01-16T08:58:44.725Z"],["3814801","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768553938965259]*{color}:\nI'd still suggest for you to pick it up, and have the comms reviewed before they are implemented\n{quote}","2026-01-16T08:59:13.187Z"],["3814803","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n\nI’m sharing the completed[ sheet with our suggestions.|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/17hM-A7LNsFiMe8VxSKwP_8gI32zfeHJT/edit?gid=1751506711#gid=1751506711]\n\nI’ve left the CoC suggestions out of this file, as including them would make it extremely messy. As mentioned earlier, there aren’t many major risks in signing the document as it stands.\n\nI’m also [sharing the DeepL-translated Danish version|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VZQmdBiY8KhCNh6-LYWSlRBCJ6bt3ftE/edit?gid=1844353644#gid=1844353644] —  [~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] please review the accuracy of the translation.\n\n\nWe’re still waiting for the Privacy team’s input on the Supplier Agreement privacy section.\nCC [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \n\nThanks, everyone!","2026-01-16T08:59:55.199Z"],["3814804","MVRT-1446","MVRT","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","[~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3] clear, thanks 👌 We can target only based on city_id, yeah.","2026-01-16T09:00:52.049Z"],["3814805","LSS-61315","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:459f4dab-1b84-4b5a-8aec-5b1cfceef16b] !\n\nI have attached the signed contract in the message from January 13, 2026 at 5:42 PM. May you kindly tell me if something is wrong with the signature. \n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T09:01:04.296Z"],["3814806","DSR-3779","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T09:01:14.261Z"],["3814807","TAXP-1647","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","[https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AjK___-AzvUev0R5alWYIMbaWuaTJ28k/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AjK___-AzvUev0R5alWYIMbaWuaTJ28k/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] \nNote: the entity was liquidated and this was its last CIT return. It was submitted without TP review and it should have said that it did have the obligation to prepare local file documentation. ","2026-01-16T09:01:19.712Z"],["3814808","HS-29016","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Dudu, I have sent the letter for signing. ","2026-01-16T09:01:22.059Z"],["3814809","BB-2162","BB","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] [~accountid:62fc9aa82e3849d137774ba7] , seems one invoice hasn’t been reissued and is still  with 22% VAT for the Service Fee *(EE1525-21018):* [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5487985149|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5487985149]\n\nCan you, please, reissue this one too with 24% VAT","2026-01-16T09:01:49.823Z"],["3814810","XVER-314","XVER","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","reassigned to [~accountid:712020:6f095333-c438-429c-9660-a9de5d845fe7] as prod owner!","2026-01-16T09:01:52.311Z"],["3814814","PFI-833833","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe charge for 13.12 GBP is related to a  76.37 GBP claim on 1 Jan 2026, 07:40:22 (UTC+02:00). \nThe business topped it up in two parts. \n\n1 Jan 2026, 07:41:18 (UTC+02:00) 63.25 GBP \n1 Jan 2026, 14:43:08 (UTC+02:00) 13.12 GBP \n\n\n\n!image-20260116-090136.png|width=1352,height=161!\n\nThe claim 12.44 GBP comes from 7 Jan 2026, 21:54:14 (UTC+02:00)\nThe claim 14.1 GBP comes from  7 Jan 2026, 19:50:51 (UTC+02:00)\n\nUnfortunately, I don’t have accesses to check what are the claims related to. \n\nI would suggest checking the balance entries page for more detailed information. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/799974?tab=balance_entries&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"limit\"%3A50%2C\"business_company_id\"%3A799974}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/799974?tab=balance_entries&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22business_company_id%22%3A799974%7D%7D]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T09:03:29.509Z"],["3814815","LSS-61686","LSS","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","[^Poslovne vožnje d.o.o. - PoA - bank mandate.pdf]\n[^Poslovne vožnje d.o.o. - LHV onboarding application.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T09:03:41.220Z"],["3814818","LSS-61686","LSS","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","For some unknown technical issue, I couldn’t attached the documents to the ticket and attached them to the comment above","2026-01-16T09:04:16.960Z"],["3814819","LSS-58216","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] no concerns. The final version is as agreed. We can move on to sign. As always: Please send the invitation to sign to the Director, Ahto Kink to [ahto.kink@bolt.eu|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] otherwise it will not be signed.","2026-01-16T09:04:24.286Z"],["3814820","INT-485","INT","priit.tiganik@bolt.eu","Priit Tiganik","26W3 had an alignment call with Growth team to discuss solutions and potential problems using just pure trendline for classifying true CPs. Also discussed ideas how to start using the feature: either to replace current classification entirely or append it. More analysis will be needed to propose a solution for further alignment","2026-01-16T09:04:30.662Z"],["3814822","PFI-833828","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nUnfortunately, we are not able to provide an authorization letter or any other documentation about the pre-authorization release. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T09:04:43.838Z"],["3814823","PFI-833796","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user is reporting a double-charge because of incremental authorization.\nIncremental authorization in card payments refers to the process of requesting an additional authorization on a customer’s card when the original authorized amount is insufficient to cover the final transaction cost. This typically happens in scenarios where the final amount of the transaction is not known upfront or may change.\n\nI have checked the case and everything looks good on Bolt’s end. The pre-authorization has been released to the customer. \nYou can ask the customer to reach out to their bank in order to confirm the authorized funds have been released. Their bank can locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions.\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T09:05:36.554Z"],["3814824","LSS-60123","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","[~accountid:712020:8af2b159-71c0-448a-80ba-ff5059bb02f6] Marking this ticket as “Done”. We can always revisit this in case any further assistance is required from our end. \n\nThank you. \n\ncc: [~accountid:62722e092db308007024a425] [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] ","2026-01-16T09:05:41.070Z"],["3814829","LSS-61315","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] just FYI the business does not see anything posted in the sub tickets. Please always attach the signed agreements to main ticket. Thank you! \n\nSharing the signed agreement here. \n\n[^111 Ugovor o certificiranju (1) (1) copy.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T09:06:01.091Z"],["3814830","LSS-61683","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:2845c580-6c2a-4373-b0ec-b66ddb6e8c48] I’ve dealt with the Privacy sections of the case here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DSR-3557|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DSR-3557|smart-link] the rest of the claim is more of a Consumer Claim that should be escalated to Regional Legal here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/2450|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/2450|smart-link] as Privacy team does not handle T&Cs-related transparency issues.","2026-01-16T09:06:05.014Z"],["3814833","PAW-14889","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160785\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 09:07:10 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T09:07:10.991Z"],["3814834","LSS-60899","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you [~accountid:5b7beb37eb18d0589b9b1c63] for a very clear and structured response ! This all makes sense and we are reviewing in order to revert back to you shortly.\n\n\nTo verify if i have understood correctly, please could you confirm whether the below is correct?\n\nCentral → block drivers under 4.66 after several warnings\nFrance → block drivers under 4.0 after several warnings + introduce blocking of drivers between 4.0 - 4.5\n\nI would like to clarify my understanding of how France is deviating from central’s approach.","2026-01-16T09:07:57.194Z"],["3814835","PFI-832630","PFI","temidayo.akinduyo@bolt-outsource.eu","Temidayo Akinduyo","wrong SD","2026-01-16T09:08:05.512Z"],["3814837","LSS-61494","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9fd45c83-380e-410c-83d8-9f700c4718bd] ! Yes, I have sent it to the email you provide. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.06.06.png|width=543,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.06.06.png\"!\n\n\n\nThere is how emails looks like:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.07.25.png|width=431,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.07.25.png\"!","2026-01-16T09:08:09.370Z"],["3814838","CSENP-419","CSENP","bashir.ibrahim@bolt.eu","Bashir Ibrahim","{{2026-01-13}}\n\nh3. Meeting outcome & ownership\n\n* *Projects Groups confirmed* by VP CS (5).\n* *Ownership change:* [~accountid:712020:10681b8a-d4f0-4c4b-a35a-ac65104846c2] Bashir to handover transition project. execution [~accountid:712020:7501407c-7b36-4916-b6bc-43e3ed6c3e3c] \n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Schedule Directors’ *calibration session* in next LT. Owner: Bashir. *Due:* {{2026-01-20}}\n* Track licence procurement (78 users) as Risk R1 with IT Service Desk. ETA: 3–5 weeks.","2026-01-16T09:08:15.449Z"],["3814839","LSS-61315","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Thank you, Iva!","2026-01-16T09:09:20.406Z"],["3814840","PFI-833319","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Refunded in Tingg portal. \nAsking for a double approval to correct the payment state \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768554505805?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768554505805?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-16T09:09:22.192Z"],["3814842","INT-516","INT","priit.tiganik@bolt.eu","Priit Tiganik","26W3 mapping spend differences to billing data and subsequent bugfixes to the model are largely done. As a result it was realised that logically some of the supply spend cannot be mapped to order since no orders happened during mapping periods. New type of fleet campaign mapping was added to the system that’ll map legacy branding bonuses from fleet campaigns. Bugfixes and developments here [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15165|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15165|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T09:09:49.255Z"],["3814843","LSS-60899","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] , this concerns the launch of the low-rated driver warning program we had reviewed in June last year for France and Belgium. Since then, the T&Cs have been amended to support this initiative, and all proposed communications from central have been reviewed and validated locally.\n\n\n\n+*Request for Input:*+\n\nThey would like to apply blocking measures to drivers listed on the Prevention List (i.e., those with average ratings between 4.0 and 4.5). Specifically:\n\n* Blocking would apply only to drivers who have received more than three warnings.\n* This concerns approximately 500 drivers.\n\n\n\nI have asked a final question to Jacqueline to get further context, but here below is my recommendation:\n\n+*My recommendation :*+\n\nThere are no major legal blockers to raise against rolling this out, particularly if the aim is to drive greater impact through this program. +However+, I would advise against applying the same suspension scale to drivers in the Prevention List as we do to those with lower ratings (<4.0).\n\nTo preserve proportionality—and limit potential friction with drivers or regulators—I recommend capping suspensions for Prevention List drivers to a maximum of 3 days. This would still allow us to send a strong signal while giving drivers a fair opportunity to adjust their performance without disproportionate penalties.\n\nWhat do you think?","2026-01-16T09:09:49.404Z"],["3814844","LSS-61486","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] – amazing work! \n\nNothing from my side to add. As discussed yesterday, CSPC should fill out Cognito form and then ticket can be closed.","2026-01-16T09:10:09.185Z"],["3814846","CSXRT-200","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Brought up with both [~accountid:712020:248d279a-85db-4438-8af9-d236e6e661d5] & [~accountid:6268ef941a4eb30069d0a75c] (who was responsible for pushing it at the time), he shared that it was de-prioritised while he was still in the team. Will check with [~accountid:5cf61a4c3fc4980fa4f07998] when he is back","2026-01-16T09:10:21.634Z"],["3814848","CSXRT-201","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Now available to check -  Can check it by filtering in the aggregated changelog of the vehicle for Initiator type \"Admin\" and then look for any entry like \"Vehicle State Change        marker_mask        ADMIN_REPORTED_PROBLEM,VEHICLE_SAFETY_CHECK_REQUIRED\"","2026-01-16T09:11:03.552Z"],["3814850","CSXRT-202","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Similar to MM specific block - will bring up with [~accountid:5cf61a4c3fc4980fa4f07998] when he is back mid-feb","2026-01-16T09:11:36.032Z"],["3814851","CSENP-419","CSENP","bashir.ibrahim@bolt.eu","Bashir Ibrahim","{{2026-01-15}}\n\nh3. Project Charter update\n\n*Summary*\n\n* [Charter|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/Q4DauAE] updated to reflect:\n** Final Projects Groups terminology and definitions\n** Roles: Programme Lead (Bashir), Delivery Lead (Ana)\n** Phases & Milestones (Phase 1: Planning & Setup)\n** Metrics & Reporting (with *Frequency* column)","2026-01-16T09:12:21.058Z"],["3814852","PFI-834080","PFI","temidayo.akinduyo@bolt-outsource.eu","Temidayo Akinduyo","[^ProofOfPayment (2).pdf]","2026-01-16T09:12:30.035Z"],["3814853","RNTL-29361","RNTL","arnaud.lafeuillade@bolt.eu","Arnaud Lafeuillade","Duplicate, report missing vehicle topic","2026-01-16T09:12:42.945Z"],["3814856","LSS-61311","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Thank you! I will initiate the signature collection now. ","2026-01-16T09:12:53.704Z"],["3814858","IOTTEAM-315","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Modem USB and command interface worked\nModem was able to register into network\nSignal strength: RSRP -87, RSRQ -13, SINR 7, RSSI -74 (good to average)","2026-01-16T09:13:14.885Z"],["3814860","FX-3217","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768554802054129]*{color}:\n<@U090E7WNXUG> this should all be fixed now - let me know if you have any further issues.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T09:13:34.999Z"],["3814861","PFI-834081","PFI","emmanuel.ojeikhodion@bolt-outsource.eu","Emmanuel Ojeikhodion","!Screenshot_20260116-093045.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T09:13:39.799Z"],["3814865","LSS-60696","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","Hi Beatriz,\n\nI just asked the client if it's possible for them to send us the signed contract directly.\n\nI'll keep you updated.","2026-01-16T09:13:58.651Z"],["3814867","RNTL-24272","RNTL","arnaud.lafeuillade@bolt.eu","Arnaud Lafeuillade","No updates","2026-01-16T09:14:05.300Z"],["3814868","LSS-57822","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Sorry [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ! And thank you for pointing me the right person! 🙏 \n\nHey [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] , thank you!","2026-01-16T09:14:11.138Z"],["3814869","PFI-833886","PFI","kokou.bakpa@bolt-outsource.eu","Kokou Avoulété Bakpa","We can see the  business profile completed some orders. Can we provide the user the invoice as requested?","2026-01-16T09:14:27.106Z"],["3814870","BLTF-122","BLTF","omar.quiroga@bolt.eu","Omar Quiroga","[~accountid:611cb51f41ff95006a8c5b74] [~accountid:6068291c8a0f7c006ff22858] Lets check cause I am able to do pull to refresh on iOS","2026-01-16T09:14:41.102Z"],["3814872","RNTL-28296","RNTL","arnaud.lafeuillade@bolt.eu","Arnaud Lafeuillade","Duplicated","2026-01-16T09:14:52.829Z"],["3814873","DPX-3539","DPX","giacomo.giorgianni@bolt.eu","Giacomo Giorgianni","We don’t have this values in the backend so we would first need to understand how to propagate them from the dataset. \nEstimation doesn’t take into account the work needed to make these value available in the backend and the task will be blocked until we get them. ","2026-01-16T09:15:12.727Z"],["3814879","FX-3217","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768554951932419]*{color}:\nThanks once again, really appreciate all the work done\n{quote}","2026-01-16T09:16:06.047Z"],["3814881","PFI-829976","PFI","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] ! This case looks a lot like [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-801006|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-801006|smart-link]. Should we act the same, just asking the driver not to use this document as it is not an official one and contains discrepancies? Thanks!","2026-01-16T09:16:20.726Z"],["3814883","SUPX-2317","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","Handing over after RCA, as agreed","2026-01-16T09:16:33.685Z"],["3814884","DPX-3539","DPX","markus.velt@bolt.eu","Markus Velt","Effort estimation for backend: \n\n* Edit Spark files to include the new metric and start a backfill.\n* Write some code in the merchant-insights service to make it available in the API after backfill has finished. Also add passthrough to delivery-provider-portal. \n\n(2d effort, +1 day if someone is onboarding to this)\n\nFrontend likely ~1 day, since you have to add a new API call for the new metric and then draw it inside an existing card.\nTotal effort estimate: 3-4 days.","2026-01-16T09:16:34.753Z"],["3814885","GRWA-1463","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","There was an error in the formula which was causing problems in data, both tiles have been fixed.\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.16.31.png|width=689,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.16.31.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.16.19.png|width=777,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.16.19.png\"!","2026-01-16T09:16:39.145Z"],["3814886","WEB-9250","WEB","krister.looga@bolt.eu","Krister Looga","Synced with Orkhan, for now we will close this ticket and create a new one during form-builder epic","2026-01-16T09:17:01.408Z"],["3814887","WFM-10008","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","Dear [~accountid:61ea6e9084311c0069465f61] ,\n\nThanks for reaching out. We checked on our end that the above mentioned user already has a role that provides him with the access you mentioned. Please double check if they can access the link. \n\nIf there’s still any access required, please specify what task this user needs to perform so that we can see what permission he’s lacking in the system. If you have any agents that have the access to the page you mentioned, please kindly provide their usernames so that we can see if we can mirror the sets. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T09:17:04.872Z"],["3814888","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","I’ve been slowly asking my team if they’re :green: for end of March and so far all is positive","2026-01-16T09:17:12.283Z"],["3814889","PFI-834077","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI could not see a negative balance for the customer. Their current balance is PLN 0.00\nThe payment that you are referencing to has failed, but it was created before Bolt Balance existed so it did not create a negative balance. \n\nI read through the Beehive ticket and it seems the user is asking about the parking fine not the negative balance.  \n\nUnfortunately, I don’t have any visibility over the parking fine and would not be able to advise on it. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T09:17:18.129Z"],["3814891","LSS-28626","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","You may close this ticket. ","2026-01-16T09:17:36.552Z"],["3814892","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Master switch notification: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768555035118419|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768555035118419|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T09:17:55.146Z"],["3814898","LSS-61162","LSS","ahto.kink@bolt.eu","Ahto Kink","Hi!\n\nAccesses granted to both platforms as from 16.01.2026.\n\nBest regards,\n\nAhto","2026-01-16T09:19:38.481Z"],["3814900","RDXENG-4690","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal",":wave_hi: We just enabled showing of active orders in rider app that are created from ride booker (VIP orders only). Currently it looks like driver-rider chat is not enable for such rides. Can we enable it?","2026-01-16T09:20:17.303Z"],["3814901","RDXENG-4690","RDXENG",null,"Slack","[Ankit Goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L9EMP4TE/p1768482605041909?thread_ts=1768482605.041909&cid=C02L9EMP4TE|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L9EMP4TE/p1768482605041909?thread_ts=1768482605.041909&cid=C02L9EMP4TE|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T09:20:18.210Z"],["3814902","RDXENG-4690","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","[Context|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C018LH51RRV/p1768465537572079?thread_ts=1768399360.981049&cid=C018LH51RRV]","2026-01-16T09:20:18.722Z"],["3814903","PFI-834091","PFI","success.igbinosa@bolt-outsource.eu","Success Igbinosa","!500.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T09:20:39.395Z"],["3814904","PFI-819935","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi [~accountid:619628e6b0b630006a6d2919] - apologies for missing your response! I understand that if we do the adjustment, you will need to inform the accounting partner again to only reflect the actual agency fee amount? \n\n[~accountid:712020:1ac9e18d-07ba-4c40-99d7-7b2cc972055e] - is it acceptable from your side if finance team excludes this adjustment and order from their model? ","2026-01-16T09:20:51.560Z"],["3814905","PFI-834092","PFI","punyawee.kangwanwongs@bolt-outsource.eu","Punyawee Kangwanwongs","[^Manual payouts requested, January 2026, Week 3..csv]","2026-01-16T09:20:59.589Z"],["3814908","LSS-61031","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","Asked to fix the formalities and send to signing.","2026-01-16T09:22:00.701Z"],["3814912","FX-3440","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768555362007529]*{color}:\nwill come back to you today with a decision.....\n{quote}","2026-01-16T09:22:56.794Z"],["3814914","DSR-3777","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","[~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] - as I am not familiar with non-EU/UK markets, could you please confirm with the relevant stakeholders (T2/Ops) whether BH is the only platform used to communicate with Drivers in Kenya? The block refers to “multiple warnings” sent to the driver - we need to make sure that those are reflected in the responsive data. \n\nShould any comms related to the suspension have been sent from a different place (e.g. Infobip or similar), please extract those as well. Please also double-check whether any call recordings are available and relevant to this case, if not done already.","2026-01-16T09:23:48.591Z"],["3814916","PFI-801465","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Indeed, this report has an error in it. These fleet reports have since been depreciated because of this exact reason. As this is not a tax document, but merely an overview, we do not need to reissue this, but just inform the driver that it’s indeed correct and to please rely on the official invoices for their reporting purposes. Thanks! ","2026-01-16T09:24:43.934Z"],["3814917","PFI-833291","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 8.08 and EUR 6.78 on Jan 11, 2026, 21:50:20 GMT+2, Jan 14, 2026, 16:47:20 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 15265676011002430147221, 15265676014002728527222 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 11th of Jan until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_VGSSLNNB6VCTRXF3_TG42B99FGV6X3VG6.pdf]\n[^Refund_Letter_VGSSLNNB6VCTRXF3_V7MSKTTH47BSGTP9.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T09:24:59.336Z"],["3814921","DSR-3777","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","I have added the suspension note (profile comment) to the responsive data (/) - *redacted* as per our processes: removed name of admin who placed the block.","2026-01-16T09:26:14.240Z"],["3814924","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","{quote} was reason again oversized poison message like last time?{quote}\n\nI checked the CDC logs yesterday but couldn’t find anything regarding size:\n\n{noformat}[root@ti-payments-cdc-1 log]# grep \"Single message is too large for avro\" cdc.log\n[root@ti-payments-cdc-1 log]#\n\n[root@ti-payments-cdc-2 log]# grep \"Single message is too large for avro\" cdc.log\n[root@ti-payments-cdc-2 log]#{noformat}\n\nIn fact, around time it happened nothing particular stood out in logs. Just the usual sarama disconnects:\n\n{noformat}[2026/01/15 21:57:34.981 +00:00] [WARN] [sarama.go:129] [\"client/metadata fetching metadata for all topics from broker kafka-6.data.internal:9093\"] [component=sarama]\n[2026/01/15 21:57:34.981 +00:00] [WARN] [client.go:1066] [\"client/metadata got error from broker 6 while fetching metadata: write tcp 172.30.2.132:56408->172.29.120.244:9093: write: broken pipe\"] [component=sarama]\n[2026/01/15 21:57:34.981 +00:00] [WARN] [sarama.go:129] [\"Closed connection to broker kafka-6.data.internal:9093\"] [component=sarama]\n[2026/01/15 21:57:34.981 +00:00] [WARN] [client.go:774] [\"client/brokers deregistered broker #6 at kafka-6.data.internal:9093\"] [component=sarama]\n[2026/01/15 21:57:34.981 +00:00] [WARN] [sarama.go:129] [\"client/metadata fetching metadata for all topics from broker kafka-1.data.internal:9093\"] [component=sarama]\n[2026/01/15 21:57:35.026 +00:00] [WARN] [sarama.go:129] [\"client/brokers registered new broker #6 at kafka-6.data.internal:9093\"] [component=sarama]{noformat}","2026-01-16T09:27:15.382Z"],["3814926","BP-13415","BP","daria.zaichykova@bolt.eu","Daria Zaichykova","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] looks great!","2026-01-16T09:27:23.634Z"],["3814929","WDFT-3529","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] ,\n\nI just wanted to summarize the approach we discussed yesterday regarding *deferred costs*:\n\n* January error-related operational journals cannot be canceled.\n* To “close” the schedules, you can cancel them, ensuring that the *December 2025* period is closed beforehand.\n* Canceling the schedules will create postings *DR 1302 / CR 5151* for the full amount of expenses recognized from the first installment.\n* To reverse these operational journals, you will need to post a *manual correction journal in January 2026*.\n* To prepare the reversal journal, you can use the EIB *“2025_correction_Bolt Accounting Journals EIB.”*\nThis EIB is similar to the commonly used *“Bolt Accounting Journals EIB,”* but it includes two additional columns for *Tax Applicability* and *Tax Code* worktags, which are required to reverse operational journals for schedule cancellation. \n* This EIB does not support data extraction. However, to populate the template, you can use the report *“TEMPORARY Find Journal Lines – Detailed – w RefIDs.”*\nThis report contains most of the required IDs. You can run it with appropriate prompts to identify all journals created by the schedule cancellation.\n\n!image-20260116-092407.png|width=585,alt=\"image-20260116-092407.png\"!\n\n\n\nI tested the EIB in the *sandbox* environment. I attached to this ticket  an example of the template I used, along with the Excel version of the report and the pivot table I used to populate the template. Btw, unfortunately , you can not use journal source “ Prepaid Spend Authorization” in EIB ( EIB does not allow use workday-delivered journal sources, only Accounting Journal sources are allowed that is why I put “Manual_Journal” in template). Here is Journal created by EIB \n\n!image-20260116-092632.png|width=1392,alt=\"image-20260116-092632.png\"!\n\n* In PL002 you will have to create recurring journals to have periodic recognition of Deferred cost transferred from PL003 to PL002, because WD allowed to  create schedules only for supplier invoices. ","2026-01-16T09:28:11.217Z"],["3814935","LSS-61464","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]  i am attaching contract with customer signature as he sent me. Provide this contract to be signed by our side. \n\n[^signed contract Bolt 50x yaris cross.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T09:28:37.235Z"],["3814936","CSXRT-204","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Discussions with the UK Policy manager done - phone number for Authorities needed (police, mostly for accidents). \n\nCurrent phone number with low response rate - feedback with CS OPS shared on to improve agent performance & to add additional agents to the queue by the launch. Additional guidelines for dealing with UK authorities needed for the TP Lagos team by 1st of Feb.\n\nBackup solution - using RH safety/authority specific phone number > additional trainings needed for MM in that case.\n\nTo improve response rate - possibility to add slack notifications for phone calls specifically.","2026-01-16T09:28:36.880Z"],["3814937","PFI-833550","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hi team can you give me some update. Thank you.","2026-01-16T09:28:51.865Z"],["3814939","PFI-833274","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nCould you please clarify if the refund should be done to the Bolt Balance or to the OPM? \n\nPlease note that the refunding process is owned by the CS teams. You might want to check with your team lead as they have higher permissions to issue refunds. \n\nThe customer payments team does have access to issue the OPM refund from the CheckOut portal. However, we would issue the refund only as a last resort. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T09:29:05.868Z"],["3814940","DCOR-428","DCOR","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","Officially not part of DAC7 but local gov wants a similar report. Not a law yet. No need to make any changes as of now until commerce/tax let’s us know anything different.","2026-01-16T09:29:13.269Z"],["3814941","WDFT-3529","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","And Regarding transfer of assets, let me know when you are about to do it , so I can set up transfer with historical cost and accumulated depreciation ","2026-01-16T09:29:13.332Z"],["3814942","LSS-61419","LSS","kati.pruel@bolt.eu","Kati Pruel","Hi, \nFirst payment done.","2026-01-16T09:29:17.453Z"],["3814943","INT-752","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] deleted the following tasks as redundant: Proper AB test set up per benefit and moving discount from billing to us ","2026-01-16T09:29:23.248Z"],["3814944","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Guys, but actually, you can create the backfills on your own, [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-ingestion/ingestion/backfills?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22status%22%3A%5B%22active%22%2C%22completed%22%5D%7D%7D]. Can you?","2026-01-16T09:29:24.435Z"],["3814948","LSS-61419","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Amazing. Thank you [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552]!","2026-01-16T09:29:55.609Z"],["3814949","HS-29017","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.29.44.png|width=200,height=200!","2026-01-16T09:30:04.078Z"],["3814950","LSS-61419","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Is it possible to have a payment proof, so I can send an email to LESA?","2026-01-16T09:30:06.409Z"],["3814951","HS-29017","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Waiting for another certificate.","2026-01-16T09:30:12.723Z"],["3814954","HS-28936","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-16T09:30:17.700Z"],["3814955","INT-752","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] copied over comments from redundant task: \n\nCurrently we have a hacky solution around A/B testing  for service fee discounts where we send a blacklist of campaigns to delivery campaigns. We want to have a proper solution for menu, service discounts and other benefits, that is scalable and doesn’t need delivery campaigns team to iterate through “blacklisted” campaigns list.\n\n*Note:* this could be related to country-wide offers and going from global to enrollment-based setup, where we need to wait for the next billing period.\n\nAC:\n\n* Remove the existing blacklist approach to A/B testing a single benefit\n* Decouple our setup from billing (for the sake of A/B testing and enrolling users in the middle of a billing period to a test).\n* Add a proper testing setup, where we can just roll users into a test group based on their benefit.","2026-01-16T09:30:25.100Z"],["3814957","DBRE-8505","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","Implemented, working on QA/verification on local env","2026-01-16T09:31:01.335Z"],["3814959","LSS-51524","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Airwallex have shared their feedback. Saved [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iO7udXgIxmR1YpTyvk8kDxq5pwZYt2oE/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=116714997278541814965&rtpof=true&sd=true] (External - Airwallex has access). \n\nInternal copy is [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uCODQUp9Vp-rv6nlzYnpo7-7EPab7BqC/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=116714997278541814965&rtpof=true&sd=true].  ","2026-01-16T09:31:04.307Z"],["3814961","DSR-3777","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Note: we usually do *not* share ratings with Drivers. [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] should you believe that this case should be an exception (given the context, I assume it may be the case), please clarify this so that the data can be sourced accordingly. CSPC has never had to deal with extracting ratings AFAIK - I can support.","2026-01-16T09:31:17.489Z"],["3814962","LSS-61612","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] can you send this contract for signing? Customer is waiting. ","2026-01-16T09:31:17.948Z"],["3814963","LSS-61614","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] can you send this contract for signing? Customer is waiting. ","2026-01-16T09:31:32.363Z"],["3814964","WEBSD-1487","WEBSD","zoe.johnson@bolt.eu","Zoë Johnson","[^Website Updates_ CH .pdf]","2026-01-16T09:31:54.552Z"],["3814965","DBRE-8505","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","[https://github.com/bolteu/tidb-tools/pull/62|https://github.com/bolteu/tidb-tools/pull/62]","2026-01-16T09:32:10.497Z"],["3814966","WD-22588","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] \n\nUnfortunately People Tech will not be able to provide you with needed access. \nI will reassign the ticket to Finance Tech. \n\n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-16T09:32:27.178Z"],["3814967","INT-580","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] will discuss with [~accountid:61386b180016a700697b9436] and update","2026-01-16T09:32:56.618Z"],["3814968","HS-28977","HS","duduzile.langa@bolt.eu","Duduzile Langa","Hi Berit, i rejected Given letter because the termination date was incorrect","2026-01-16T09:32:57.937Z"],["3814969","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","ETK sounds good to me, it’s right in Telliskivi too, so we can theoretically just order whatever we want from there :thumbsup::skin-tone-2: \n\nRegarding activities - what does ETK have? Maybe we can organize something there? I’m not sure it’ll be easy to organize an activity like we’re used to for 20+ people 🤔 \n\nCross-domain team also (/) for end of March.","2026-01-16T09:33:00.269Z"],["3814971","PFI-833272","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe refund has been issued to the business not the user who placed the order. \n\nRefund can be found from here: \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/802968?tab=refunds&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/802968?tab=refunds&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\n\n\n!image-20260116-093300.png|width=1391,height=456!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T09:33:10.308Z"],["3814975","FDBT-4800","FDBT","rainer.kana@bolt.eu","Rainer Kana","[~accountid:618265cc3e3753006f82d870] there are 3000+ rows with\n\n* line_of_business = 'UNKNOWN'\n* business_subline = 'UNKNOWN'\n\n{code:sql}%sql\nselect \nline_of_business, business_subline,\n*\nFROM commerce_finance_spark.finance_model_payment_payment_transaction\nWHERE \n    payment_row_created_date BETWEEN DATE('2026-01-11') AND DATE('2026-01-15')\n    AND \n    (\n        line_of_business = 'UNKNOWN'\n        OR allocated_line_of_business = 'UNKNOWN'\n        OR line_of_business IS NULL\n        OR allocated_line_of_business IS NULL\n    ){code}","2026-01-16T09:34:54.660Z"],["3814976","PFI-831668","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 112.00 ZAR was issued on 13/12/2025, 17:07:26UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 13th of December to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T09:35:20.301Z"],["3814978","PC-906","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-1094 has been resolved","2026-01-16T09:35:23.584Z"],["3814980","LSS-61619","LSS","sugandha.bhandari@bolt.eu","Sugandha Bhandari","is this on social media? [~accountid:712020:289d7ba0-a9c0-4cbb-82d4-a9ed8c05aeab] \n\nJust keep me in the loop if anything is in public and/or social media. thanks ","2026-01-16T09:35:49.860Z"],["3814982","CSXRT-156","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","On-hold due to more urgent priorities","2026-01-16T09:36:04.895Z"],["3814985","PFI-834113","PFI","evelyn.obi@bolt-outsource.eu","Evelyn Obi","!image-20260116-093603.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T09:36:14.655Z"],["3814986","PFI-822382","PFI","filip.kieronczyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Filip Kieronczyk","any updates?","2026-01-16T09:36:44.769Z"],["3814987","PFI-831612","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe users payment has failed with an error message Rejected due to high risk. This is a fraud related error. \nThe user should reach out to their bank to clarify if there are any restrictions on their payment method. \n\nAlternatively, the user could try a different payment method. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T09:37:04.087Z"],["3814988","PFI-810251","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Thank you for the information, it has been escalated to the engineering team for further review","2026-01-16T09:37:14.888Z"],["3814990","CSXRT-155","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Analysis currently on-hold due to other priorities.","2026-01-16T09:37:26.330Z"],["3814991","DSR-3777","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","I didn’t find any *Call* *Recordings* that would be relevant to this case.\n\nAsked if BH is the only communication platform in the Slack incident channel [+_here_+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7DAJ0A8M/p1768555718498669?thread_ts=1768476810.005019&cid=C0A7DAJ0A8M] ⏳","2026-01-16T09:37:27.142Z"],["3814994","PFI-832832","PFI","kristinliis.ratto@bolt.eu","Kristin-Liis Rätto","Hey \nAll admin related transaction should go through commerce team as our accounting system and admin is not connected this way and all the balance in admin remain open. As I know they are making refunds as well. ","2026-01-16T09:38:15.270Z"],["3814999","LSS-58999","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:f50af85a-3d8b-4b5c-b19d-ad552b86d158] - hope you’re well! Is support still required on the DPA? I don’t recall us ever hearing back from the Providers.","2026-01-16T09:39:07.992Z"],["3815000","LSS-51678","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:2765baba-2b31-484f-8570-0cc671e879cb] could you please let us know the latest status here ? thanks ! ","2026-01-16T09:39:12.731Z"],["3815001","RDXENG-4690","RDXENG",null,"Slack","This conversation thread has been automatically unsynced from the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L9EMP4TE/p1768482605041909|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L9EMP4TE/p1768482605041909|smart-link] because [@Ankit Goyal|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6358f09ab0b6ef03564955ba] removed the connected work item unfurl on Slack.\n\nFuture replies will no longer sync or update across Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T09:39:15.755Z"],["3815003","PFI-831607","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Payment captured in EveryPay portal. \nAsking for double approval to mark as captured \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768556341498?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768556341498?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-16T09:39:22.940Z"],["3815005","PC-3316","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","Replaced with new epics PI-*","2026-01-16T09:40:06.852Z"],["3815007","PFI-832651","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi [~accountid:712020:4c978950-b03c-4d90-9c92-c0a5d373f33a] , this is not an invoice, this seems to be a printout from the fiscalization system. [~accountid:712020:783602a6-282a-4f15-930c-066bdff8e5c5] you have more experience with what are the possibilities, is this some type of new report that fleets/drivers get from Novitus?","2026-01-16T09:40:25.082Z"],["3815008","PFI-833045","PFI","emmy.abok@bolt-outsource.eu","Emmy Abok","D wants an explanation of a $562.19 discrepancy in his balance from December. Wants a detailed description of the deductions made ","2026-01-16T09:40:36.666Z"],["3815009","DRX-28237","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","For comparison, on iOS, the Rider profile picture is visible when the new internal navigation is enabled: \n\n!20260116_111707 (1).jpg|width=228,alt=\"20260116_111707 (1).jpg\"!","2026-01-16T09:40:44.245Z"],["3815012","LSS-61691","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","[^Bolt Operations OU-Teleperformance Europe Middle-East and Africa SAS-SOW Client IC-34077-Effective December 1, 2024.pdf] _(7.66 MB)_","2026-01-16T09:41:34.395Z"],["3815013","LSS-61690","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^DEMERGE (THAILAND) CO., LTD. Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited 2025.pdf] _(42 kB)_\n\n[^Adyen NV Bolt Rides PL sp. z o.o. 2025.pdf] _(42 kB)_\n\n[^AMEX Bolt Operations UK Limited 2025.pdf] _(71 kB)_\n\n[^Adyen NV Bolt Services CA Inc. 2025.pdf] _(41 kB)_\n\n[^Adyen NV Bolt Operations UK Limited 2025.pdf] _(75 kB)_\n\n[^Worldpay UK Limited Bolt Services UK Ltd 2025.pdf] _(42 kB)_\n\n[^Checkout Ltd Bolt Services UK Limited 2025.pdf] _(43 kB)_\n\n[^Adyen N.V.Bolt Services UK Limited 2025.pdf] _(43 kB)_\n\n[^Worldpay BV Bolt Operations OU 2025.pdf] _(44 kB)_\n\n[^Deutsche Bank AG Bolt Operations OU 025.pdf] _(44 kB)_\n\n[^PayU SA Bolt Operations OU 2025.pdf] _(44 kB)_\n\n[^Checkout SAS Bolt Operations OU 2025.pdf] _(76 kB)_\n\n[^AMEX Bolt Operations OU 2025.pdf] _(42 kB)_\n\n[^Dlocal LLP Bolt Operations OU 2025.pdf] _(43 kB)_\n\n[^Adyen Bolt Operations OU 2025 .pdf] _(42 kB)_","2026-01-16T09:41:36.723Z"],["3815014","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","[@marat.saddarov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3] would you mind that the DBRE team creates a SEV 4 incident in Rootly? I see the following tables ingestion are affected:\n\n{noformat}        \"taxify_payment.notification\",\n        \"taxify_payment.payment\",\n        \"taxify_payment.payment_order\",\n        \"taxify_payment.payment_request_log\",\n        \"taxify_payment.payment_row\"{noformat}\n\nUntil backfill is done, there is a gap of missing data during the ticdc feed downtime I imagine.","2026-01-16T09:41:40.348Z"],["3815015","LSS-61692","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^LV20260116-001 Vo-Link - Bolt Drive LV.docx.pdf] _(361 kB)_","2026-01-16T09:41:52.908Z"],["3815016","LSS-61691","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","[^MSA_Bolt_Operations_OÜ_Teleperformance_Europe_Middle_East_and_Africa_SAS_12.12.2022.pdf]\n\nExpired MSA attached\n\n","2026-01-16T09:42:03.342Z"],["3815017","PRF-1323","PRF","anna.oliinyk@bolt.eu","Anna Oliinyk","Waiting for the Hopp for Business page be finalized. On the performance side, creatives and resizes are ready to be launched.","2026-01-16T09:42:21.339Z"],["3815018","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Which is already noticed by the data team.","2026-01-16T09:42:31.582Z"],["3815019","LSS-56585","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] the majority of changes are to the DSA. \n\nIn the circumstances (Vodacom having launched early), please can you review these as a priority. Thanks \n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/125o395bpmCwcIyETink5Eb72-twZ0SvE/edit?pli=1|https://docs.google.com/document/d/125o395bpmCwcIyETink5Eb72-twZ0SvE/edit?pli=1]","2026-01-16T09:43:29.022Z"],["3815023","PFI-815946","PFI","denis.janco@bolt-outsource.eu","Denis Jančo","Hello team, any update please ? ","2026-01-16T09:44:06.836Z"],["3815028","DBRE-8705","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","Which Tier-3 or Tier-4 services were impacted?","2026-01-16T09:44:43.879Z"],["3815030","PFI-834118","PFI","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.41.40.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T09:44:48.234Z"],["3815032","PFI-833833","PFI","seema.matli@bolt.eu","Seema Matli","Hey [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] \nThe claims are related to [*order 1* |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/608908054/25?orderTryId=1512837762]and [*order 2*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/608921464/25?orderTryId=1512917748], respectively*.* The payment links for each order are [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4016675760] and [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4017104475]. As you can see the final price is 11.75 and 10.37, but for some reason we captured more than that. In one instance, the payment type states that the payment is an overcapture. Do you have any idea why this could happen? And could it be the case that we mistakenly charged the client more than the ride price?","2026-01-16T09:44:56.799Z"],["3815033","WFM-9992","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Resent the request [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541758]","2026-01-16T09:45:40.647Z"],["3815034","GRWA-1514","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","here is the post in [growth tools|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C1JQJKT5/p1768556705840819]","2026-01-16T09:45:49.335Z"],["3815045","VERIFY-1456","VERIFY","aliaksei.tuzik@bolt.eu","Aliaksei Tuzik","This could be already fixed by [~accountid:6256f19413c2c8006a365659] .","2026-01-16T09:47:46.365Z"],["3815046","LSS-61692","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","sorry, correct contract uploaded: with correct pricing\n\n\n[^LV20260116-001 Vo-Link - Bolt Drive LV.docx (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T09:47:51.517Z"],["3815047","PFI-832832","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi @Kristin-Liis Rätto,\n\nUnfortunately, this request cannot be supported by the Customer Payments team for several reasons.\n\nFirst, this was a cash payment and was not processed through the app. As such, it falls outside the scope of Customer Payments, as we do not handle cash transactions.\n\nSecond, the Customer Payments team does not have the required access to issue refunds. The refund process is fully owned by the Customer Support teams. While there are limited edge cases where we can initiate a refund to the original payment method directly via our payment service providers’ portals, this is considered a last-resort option and is not applicable here.\n\nAdditionally, we do not have any capability to initiate payments or transfers to bank accounts.\n\nI agree that issuing a refund directly to the user’s bank account is outside of standard operating procedures. If a refund is to be considered in this case, it would need to be handled by the accounting team.\n\nPlease let me know if any further clarification is needed.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T09:48:02.084Z"],["3815049","SCM-839","SCM","zuzanna.antoniewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Izabela Antoniewska","[~accountid:712020:a39b930f-52b0-4732-9cfa-d8a1b4a18ccd] Process looks good, please instead of writing on slack, but to have regular meetings with new warehouses, to check documentation, progress form the checklist and bottlenecks. Please add this process explanation to Lifecycle playbook to LOPS are aware. ","2026-01-16T09:48:22.944Z"],["3815052","PAW-14940","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T09:48:42.688Z"],["3815053","LSS-58960","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","*UPDATE*: “_Bolt Ops OU will share data with_ *_EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH,_* _who will then transfer the cases through their Cross Border platform to their relevant local entities (EOS companies or partners depending on country)_.”\n\n* These are the two parties to the agreement, and so they are caught by the data sharing obligations. \n* The agreement also contains an ‘onward transfers’ obligation (to comply with applicable laws).\n* As such, no further comments on the Special Terms for now ✅ ","2026-01-16T09:48:49.168Z"],["3815054","WFM-10018","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","Hello, Faith, \n\nI can see that this agent has OPS roles& permissions assigned right now. Please confirm if we can remove the OPS roles and assign new support roles. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T09:48:49.392Z"],["3815056","BB-2162","BB","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] ⁣Only one? That's awesome 😄 I’ll take a look right now, thanks for bringing this up!","2026-01-16T09:48:51.583Z"],["3815058","PFI-834121","PFI","chatrawee.saenwerm@bolt-outsource.eu","Chatrawee Saenwerm","!image-20260116-094802.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-094809.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T09:48:53.790Z"],["3815059","DRAG-679","DRAG","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","Waiting for input from TWS and LG. Currently they are asking us to store the batteries until further notice. They were supposed to have a meeting on {{2026-01-16}}, but it was pushed to next week. ","2026-01-16T09:49:07.922Z"],["3815060","DSR-3777","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","In addition to BH, Kenya Local OPS use the following:\n\n* _We also communicate with drivers via_ *_Braze_* _(email and push),_ *_Infobip_*_, and_ *_in-app messages_*_._\n\n*I asked Brian Kamau to extract the warnings that were sent to the driver* ⏳","2026-01-16T09:49:10.970Z"],["3815062","LSS-61635","LSS","afonso.freitasecosta@bolt.eu","Afonso Freitas e Costa","[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] sorry for the push, but this one is critical if you’re able to prioritize. thanks","2026-01-16T09:49:17.819Z"],["3815063","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","I saw they have a pingpong table there 😄 I was thinking of “Väike Saal”, it fits max 40 people, so there’s room to roam and has a bar. When writing email, we can ask if they have other games etc so people can roam around. Or we can potentially borrow from office games and poker chips 💰 \n\nWhat we should figure next is structure - meaning, how are we planning days out. Do we want:\n\n* Arrival Day\n* Seminar Day + ETK\n* Next Day after main responsibilities whole team activity + Dinner together (Or per domain) / Or skip activity+dinner alltogether\n* _Depending on situation either travel back or one more day of Main responsibilities, after free roam and then next day travel back_\n\nFor activity over 20 people, the easiest would be Megazone 😄 then difficulty wise next would be Hill Hill and then Kuulsaal (I even have a fun idea how to make it super competitive _tehehe_) - other activities would work better in smaller groups. Restaurant-wise we can find that’d fit all of us (the same F-hoone or for extra flare Texas Cantina 🤠 )","2026-01-16T09:49:25.612Z"],["3815064","LSS-61421","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Thank you [~accountid:5e835f0f9b6a000c1a324a3f] \n\nAs I can see from the last amendment, the original fleet should have 115 cars, but my understanding is that only 70 will be transferred. What will happen with the remaining 45 cars?","2026-01-16T09:49:52.072Z"],["3815065","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","Our users have reported data issue [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CF65PRL0N/p1768555181857879]. Most of data analytics incident should be [Tier-4|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/19NUp_sklsMy7iOLCDmcTmdTJfkinr0p7o0VqZxTm3Zc/edit?gid=844196354#gid=844196354].","2026-01-16T09:49:53.835Z"],["3815068","LSS-61554","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","{color:#36b37e}+*Signing process:*+{color} \n\nHi, team! Please find attached the PoA for [~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e] from Bolt Rides for P4 (Play) agreement. [^PoA Karolina Jędrzejczak Bolt Rides PL 2026.docx.pdf] \n\n*A wet ink* is required as before - [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] to sign off the PoA (a new member of the company board).\n\nto the attention of [~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e], Bolt Office Warsaw, Prosta 67 Street, 00-838 Warsaw, Poland. Please send her the original version of PoA. 😉\n\nThank you! \n\n=====\n\n{color:#6554c0}+*FYI*+ {color}[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d]{color:#6554c0} +*below:*+ {color}\n\n*As to enterprise transfer between Bolt Rides and Bolt Poland:*\n\n* this contract involves some telephone numbers and Internet cards for Bolt Rides employees but in fact they are not used by anybody. As a rule the company which is responsible for such telecommunication matters is Bolt Services but this is quite an old case and that’s why Bolt Rides keeps this contract so far. \n* As these numbers are inactive. +Karolina is going to terminate this contract as soon as possible.+ \n* So, my conclusion is that w*e don’t need to transfer this agreement from Bolt Rides to Bolt Poland* as we are aiming to terminate this contract asap. \n\nBest, Jola 😊  ","2026-01-16T09:50:16.263Z"],["3815070","CSDA-300","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review all new project requests every Monday morning. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-16T09:51:03.385Z"],["3815071","LSS-61694","LSS","marcin.klimkiewicz@bolt.eu","Marcin Klimkiewicz","[^OŚWIADCZENIE CBAM 09.02.20-20260116092056.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T09:51:59.729Z"],["3815073","CSP-79","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","26W03: Enabled 90/10 for TAXI and 50/50 for MM and carsharing. Enabling for delivery needs copy adjustments (in review). ","2026-01-16T09:52:15.361Z"],["3815074","PFI-834123","PFI","emelda.eze@bolt-outsource.eu","Emelda Eze","!Screenshot_20260116-103213.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T09:52:17.791Z"],["3815078","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","To me even the {{predicate: \"TRUE\"}} can be used for the backfill if it shows :green: in the admin panel.","2026-01-16T09:52:56.866Z"],["3815079","HS-28229","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","pinged Michal 16.01","2026-01-16T09:52:57.510Z"],["3815080","LSS-60282","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Given that tender deadline has passed and no further update from the business, I will now close this ticket. ","2026-01-16T09:53:07.729Z"],["3815081","DBRE-8705","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","sev4 definition requires tier3/4 services to have partial degradation or minor impact.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9Z3145PA/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9Z3145PA/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T09:53:15.222Z"],["3815085","CSP-63","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","25W41: Feature disabled as requested by ops, no longer needed.","2026-01-16T09:53:45.830Z"],["3815086","LSS-58103","LSS","elnara.nabiyeva@bolt.eu","Elnara Nabiyeva","[^Сканирование 16 янв. 2026 г..pdf]\n\nHI, [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] , here is the signed pdf, thank you!","2026-01-16T09:54:01.038Z"],["3815088","LSS-61406","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hey [~accountid:61c2e90fe67ea2006b1c96a7]. Thanks for the ticket.  I am reviewing the amendment and have a few questions:\n\n1. Are any of the credit-based services (polygons, clean room analysis, customer-level computations) expected to involve data that could be personal, granular location-based, or re-identifiable - beyond the anonymised data covered in the main agreement?\n2. Do we expect to freely reuse all outputs created under the Credit System (SQL queries, dashboards, new fields, polygon logic) across teams and countries, or are any of these intended to be one-off or restricted to this engagement?\n3. Is the business comfortable with the risk that prepaid credits may expire or lose value if priorities change, countries close, or usage is lower than expected?\n4. Who internally is authorised to approve and track credit usage (including via email/Slack), and how do we ensure spend control and auditability?\n","2026-01-16T09:54:27.591Z"],["3815089","LSS-57372","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hey! Please find the signed document attached!\n\n[^Agreement for use of Bolt Food Platform for partner_Bolt Operations OÜ_Remy, s.r.o._24.10.25.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T09:54:31.430Z"],["3815090","HS-29015","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi again Lilian, the letter should be in your personal inbox now. Let me know if you need anything else. For now I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-16T09:54:53.956Z"],["3815091","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","{quote}Guys, but actually, you can create the backfills on your own, <https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-ingestion/ingestion/backfills?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22status%22%3A%5B%22active%22%2C%22completed%22%5D%7D%7D|here{quote}\n\n>. Can you?\nI don’t see a way to give it a changefeed and time range.. it only has tables. Does that mean one has to:\n1. Look at all the tables in the changefeed\n2. create one backfill per table?\nSeems somewhat cumbersome, especially if you have lots of tables.","2026-01-16T09:54:56.850Z"],["3815092","HS-29011","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi again Celia, the letter should be in your personal inbox now. Let me know if you need anything else. For now I’ll close the ticket. ","2026-01-16T09:55:09.459Z"],["3815093","HS-28305","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:e1427b30-bc75-43cd-9e45-85c863998272],\n\nI don’t see a clause in the contract which states, that this new contract will overwrite the previous contract. Will the other one be terminated?\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-16T09:55:19.976Z"],["3815094","LSS-53880","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:5f52461dfdc3f5003f51865e] but we are talking about injury damages not disability. Is this rider disabled because of this accident?\n\nCan I close this ticket? It seems like it did not progress further, correct?","2026-01-16T09:55:23.112Z"],["3815096","CSP-56","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","25W11: Feature rolled out globally, old CSAT logic cleaned up.","2026-01-16T09:55:33.392Z"],["3815101","WEB-7610","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi\n\n[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852], could you please review and confirm whether this request is still needed?\n\n[~accountid:5f23e43bef11df0025a6a7a0] in one of your comments you mentioned a technical complication. Is this now resolved, or is there anything we should consider?","2026-01-16T09:56:00.324Z"],["3815102","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","You can find the affected configurations [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-ingestion/ingestion/configs?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] and create backfills for all of them with a single click in the top-right corner.","2026-01-16T09:56:50.267Z"],["3815104","PFI-832651","PFI","izabela.adamiec@bolt.eu","Izabela Rosińska","Hi,\n\nThis is a monthly report generated directly from the fiscal cash register - it is generated by the Fleet Owners from their own devices.\n\nUnfortunately, I think we’re not able to support FO with this report on our side. Only Novitus can help investigate why the report shows zero values for the entire December, even though over 300 trips were completed during that period.\n\nBest regards,\nIza","2026-01-16T09:57:01.492Z"],["3815106","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","The affected tables were already listed by Kewei. And I guess he took it from the {{terraform-cdc}} repo.","2026-01-16T09:58:20.322Z"],["3815107","CSP-62","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","25W14: Proactive & reactive comms enabled globally for riders, drivers, eaters, providers and couriers.","2026-01-16T09:58:20.672Z"],["3815108","LSS-57841","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] The court decision would still need to be enforced by any authority, so we should only share data if requested by the relevant authority directly. Court orders are not necessarily directly enforeceable!","2026-01-16T09:58:39.558Z"],["3815110","LSS-58103","LSS","liisa.puu@bolt.eu","Liisa Puu","Thank you [~accountid:712020:3aab0dff-7ae2-461e-b7c7-c61be1f47a3c] those are signed API terms. \n\nWhat about Partner Special Terms which were last shared [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-58103?focusedCommentId=3736236] with you. Can you add signed copy for tracking purposes also here. Since I didn’t find anything from AZ folder in [Partner Files Directory folder|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ISE7vNmn6u_-yJhWO1YJ6tb9h3FIeYp0?usp=share_link]\n\nLiisa","2026-01-16T09:58:52.822Z"],["3815112","HS-28994","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Kristiina, the tentative maternity leave dates have now been added to Workday. All done!","2026-01-16T09:59:28.748Z"],["3815115","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","hey, I have a question here:\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768548802609809|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768548802609809|smart-link]\n\nI've already asked [Automations|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768556298529379?thread_ts=1768556027.889139&cid=C064FCFAT0S] but Grzegorz reflected it to you :smile:","2026-01-16T09:59:34.331Z"],["3815116","SUPX-2325","SUPX",null,"Slack","[Christian Kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768556398754439?thread_ts=1768556398.754439&cid=C064CEL9FKP|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768556398754439?thread_ts=1768556398.754439&cid=C064CEL9FKP|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T09:59:35.238Z"],["3815118","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Interesting :thinking_face:\n\n[@artem.kudlaienko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/630e0b9a9796033b256bd3a5] have you noticed similar cases after changing auto close timeframe?","2026-01-16T09:59:36.280Z"],["3815119","SUPX-2325","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","{quote}the refund has been pending since 08.01.{quote}\n\nThis interaction was invalidated. What I see in the UI ({{Pending}}) only suggests that we cannot properly render an invalidated interaction, right?","2026-01-16T09:59:37.172Z"],["3815120","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","It’s not invalidated","2026-01-16T09:59:37.995Z"],["3815121","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","UI shows as expired when it’s invalidated","2026-01-16T09:59:38.907Z"],["3815122","SUPX-2325","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","Is this its invalidation?\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A94P8P4TC/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A94P8P4TC/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T09:59:39.671Z"],["3815123","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","that should be for csat","2026-01-16T09:59:40.333Z"],["3815124","SUPX-2325","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","no, this is ssat","2026-01-16T09:59:41.134Z"],["3815125","SUPX-2325","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8YCGEJEP/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8YCGEJEP/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T09:59:41.726Z"],["3815126","SUPX-2325","SUPX","artem.kudlaienko@bolt.eu","Artem Kudlaienko","csat expired a bit later\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9HMGQDGR/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9HMGQDGR/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T09:59:42.236Z"],["3815127","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Hmm, interesting. The interaction is expired, but users_choice_refund_action_state state is still pending :thinking_face:","2026-01-16T09:59:43.015Z"],["3815128","SUPX-2325","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9HN47SKB/screenshot_2026-01-16_at_11.57.48.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9HN47SKB/screenshot_2026-01-16_at_11.57.48.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T09:59:43.828Z"],["3815129","LSS-58830","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] - in which case I have no additional comments on the agreement from the privacy side for now ✅ Let me know if EOS reverts with any comments / edits.\n\nOtherwise, my previous advice on [+LSS-53566+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-53566] with respect to EOS, namely:\n\n* We should be confident from an InfoSec POV that EOS’s security measures are sufficiently robust when exchanging personal data with them, particularly given the broader international scope of this arrangement. If that has already been reviewed, then that is fine.\n* We should ensure that we have sufficient internal controls in place to make sure that we are are transferring ‘special category’ or 'criminal data ' to EOS, given that this is prohibited under Clause 5(5). We should not be doing this anyway, but making sure that the relevant stakeholders are appropriately briefed and implementing internal escalation procedures to handle edge cases would be sensible.\n* We should try to avoid sharing personal / tax ID numbers unless this is strictly necessary, as the laws of some of the in-scope countries may place restrictions on processing such data.\n\nI hope this helps - let me know if you have any Qs 🙂 ","2026-01-16T10:00:02.046Z"],["3815130","LSS-61638","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f], no, it’s not ","2026-01-16T10:00:23.819Z"],["3815136","LSS-60229","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:604b91443ab18c0068f95304] has this been signed? Can I close the ticket?","2026-01-16T10:01:03.636Z"],["3815137","PFI-832832","PFI","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:63ec99ebaf665dfde890c2e3] and [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] thank you for sharing your feedback on this question. \n\nFrom what I understand, there are technical limitations that would enable us to make this transfer directly to the rider’s bank account. \n\nAccounting team could handle this, however - so [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552] does this come back to you?\n\nThank you in advance for your help and support on this !","2026-01-16T10:01:22.674Z"],["3815138","PFI-829509","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Apologies for missing the response. Setting these rates is in the local team domain, so please ask them to update the VAT rate here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-city/cities/326?tab=general|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-city/cities/326?tab=general]\n\n\n\nand here you can set the rates for VAT tags if some items should have a different VAT rate. I’m not sure if this is something that providers need to apply to products themselves or if it can be done from our side as well: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-provider/menuVatTags?tz=Europe%2FLondon&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"country_code\"%3A\"ee\"}%2C\"country_code\"%3A\"sk\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-provider/menuVatTags?tz=Europe%2FLondon&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22country_code%22%3A%22ee%22%7D%2C%22country_code%22%3A%22sk%22%7D%7D]\n\n\n\nBut yes, overall it doesn’t impact us, although I do agree that just for appearances sake it may be worth to update those. ","2026-01-16T10:02:00.751Z"],["3815142","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","I do think {{Non-urgent reports}} is an example of {{Tier-4 low-impact services}}. In Data Platform, the services are in terms of the data quality of tables.\n\nIn this case, user even [reported|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CF65PRL0N/p1768555181857879] data quality issue. Sometimes reports also suffer \"silently\" from data quality issue. So I think missing data is an incident even regardless of whether users have reported it or not. The ingested data is the first layer that cause this issue, if there is a gap of data of table A, and table B derives from table A, then table B will also be affected by the gap from table A.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A94Q4C6KU/screenshot_2026-01-16_at_11.57.39.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A94Q4C6KU/screenshot_2026-01-16_at_11.57.39.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T10:03:00.678Z"],["3815145","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","TBH, I’m having trouble figuring out how to do it .. do you have any docs or are you able to guide me how to create backfill?","2026-01-16T10:03:15.224Z"],["3815147","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","But let's focus on solve the backfill for now, we could always create a retro incident later if necessary","2026-01-16T10:03:49.079Z"],["3815148","WFM-10016","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","The role request has been submitted here: \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601694|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601694]","2026-01-16T10:03:57.770Z"],["3815150","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","I can look at terraform cdc and find changefeeds and corresponding datalake tables, but translating that to Admin panel backfill request is blocking me","2026-01-16T10:04:15.871Z"],["3815151","LSS-61191","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","@ legal ops please collect signatures by [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] thank you!\n\n\nApproved under the following conditions: \n\nAs neither the contract nor the TnCs are very specific most of the relationship will be governed by statutory law (not necessarily a bad thing as Swiss law is quite balanced and evidence based). \n\nCommercially and risk approved by [~accountid:712020:9481de22-c025-4852-aaae-b8144230d5fa] ","2026-01-16T10:04:46.705Z"],["3815152","LSS-61369","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:712020:fde8e40a-0c43-479b-a07d-dd05334dd10a] ! to be 100% sure, I understand that for now you don’t need a legal letter to the association and you are going to threaten them in informal way (message/mail etc.) with a legal proceedings if they fail to take the post down. Please confirm 😉 \n\nThanks 😉 ","2026-01-16T10:05:14.659Z"],["3815153","LSS-58103","LSS","elnara.nabiyeva@bolt.eu","Elnara Nabiyeva","Special Terms, \n\n[^Сканирование 16 янв. 2026 г. (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:05:16.182Z"],["3815154","DBRE-7645","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Put this ticket into backlog","2026-01-16T10:05:43.957Z"],["3815155","LSS-61431","LSS","ivan.falco@bolt.eu","Ivan Falco","Thanks [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] we can remove that bit“_one winner will be selected from each of the following geographical areas: London, Birmingham, and the Rest of the UK”_\n\nI also provided to close all your suggestions after fixing them.  ","2026-01-16T10:05:48.420Z"],["3815156","LSS-39534","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","approved, I dont see specific risks that are not already existing","2026-01-16T10:05:49.891Z"],["3815159","HS-29020","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-16T10:06:23.647Z"],["3815164","WFM-10016","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","Hello Tiago, \n\nThe permission has been granted. \n\nHave a great day!","2026-01-16T10:06:54.256Z"],["3815166","LSS-53897","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:c9719acb-78c4-4bbc-b93d-e656e1839010] [~accountid:712020:1d600e3f-d3ca-4f4e-b8af-f6c7510bb923] das Thema hier wurde außerhalb von Jira schon finalized oder?","2026-01-16T10:07:25.769Z"],["3815167","BR-3857","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","The endpoint for fetching authorization amount:\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/d2e0a633b961850c24fac377881595f94562a667/gen/asyncApi/commerce_gateway/CommerceGatewayInternalAsyncApi.ts#L747-L752|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/d2e0a633b961850c24fac377881595f94562a667/gen/asyncApi/commerce_gateway/CommerceGatewayInternalAsyncApi.ts#L747-L752] \n\n[*CommerceGatewayInternalAsyncApi.ts*|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/d2e0a633b961850c24fac377881595f94562a667/gen/asyncApi/commerce_gateway/CommerceGatewayInternalAsyncApi.ts]\n\n{noformat}        public getPayment(ctx: Context, body: GetPaymentRequestV5, requestConfig?: InternalRequestPerRequestConfig): PromiseGetPaymentResponseV5;\n        public getPaymentFB(ctx: Context, body: GetPaymentRequestV5, requestConfig?: InternalRequestPerRequestConfigWithFallbackFB): PromiseFB;\n        public getPaymentFB = never(ctx: Context, body: GetPaymentRequestV5, requestConfig?: InternalRequestPerRequestConfig | InternalRequestPerRequestConfigWithFallbackFB): PromiseFB {\n            this.checkFallbackType(ctx, requestConfig);\n            return this.orFallback(ctx, \"/internal/getPayment\", this.sendAsyncPost(ctx, \"/internal/getPayment\", body, null, requestConfig), requestConfig !== undefined && \"fallback\" in requestCon…{noformat}","2026-01-16T10:07:40.081Z"],["3815169","LSS-61698","LSS","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","[^1000833292.heic] _(835 kB)_","2026-01-16T10:08:39.881Z"],["3815170","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Ok, I will get back to this in an hour.","2026-01-16T10:08:41.255Z"],["3815173","LSS-61699","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^EE20260116-001 Fleetbrains - Bolt Drive EE.docx.pdf] _(344 kB)_","2026-01-16T10:09:46.174Z"],["3815174","PFI-834127","PFI","anastasiia.vynohradova@bolt.eu","Anastasiia Vynohradova","[^заповненаУгода_щодо_виконання_доручення (1).pdf]","2026-01-16T10:10:05.329Z"],["3815175","LSS-60002","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] please give regular updates about this project here, thanks!","2026-01-16T10:10:08.163Z"],["3815177","LSS-61431","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you [~accountid:622b6eb2302c6b006af70509]. I have now removed that phrase and inserted a link to the main T&Cs page for drivers.","2026-01-16T10:10:11.212Z"],["3815179","LSS-60647","LSS","yuliya.shulayeva@bolt.eu","Yuliya Shulayeva","[~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] , the eater came back with this. Please let me know what we should respond.\n\nHello, Thank you for your final response. After carefully reviewing Bolt’s statements throughout this correspondence, I must point out that your position contains clear internal contradictions that undermine your conclusion that no GDPR infringement has occurred.\n\nLazarus Davidsson\n\nOn the one hand, Bolt states that my phone number was lawfully shared with the courier under a Data Sharing Agreement and that appropriate safeguards are in place. On the other hand, Bolt explicitly admits that it is “not in a position to fully control how individual couriers use the phone number during the delivery process.\n\nThese two positions cannot logically coexist.\n\nUnder Articles 5(2) and 24 GDPR, Bolt is required not only to define safeguards contractually, but to ensure and demonstrate that personal data is processed in compliance with GDPR in practice. If Bolt cannot ensure that couriers follow the prescribed safeguards, then those safeguards are, by definition, ineffective.\n\nFurthermore, Bolt has confirmed that the courier contacted me using a private phone number via WhatsApp, rather than Bolt’s official communication channel. This fact alone demonstrates that the safeguards Bolt claims to rely on failed in real-world operation, resulting in my personal data being used outside the controlled environment described in your own policies.\n\nDespite this, Bolt maintains that:\n\nno personal data breach occurred,\n\nno improper processing took place,\n\nand no compensation is warranted.\n\nThis raises several fundamental questions:\n\nHow can Bolt claim GDPR compliance while simultaneously stating that it cannot fully control how personal data is used by couriers?\n\nHow can Bolt assert that safeguards are sufficient when it admits they were not followed in this case?\n\nHow can Bolt conclude that processing was secure and compliant when personal data was used through an unofficial private channel?\n\nIf contractual clauses alone are sufficient, why were “corrective measures” required after the incident?\n\nAnd finally, how is a data subject expected to trust that their personal data is handled securely when Bolt itself acknowledges a lack of practical control?\n\nGDPR compliance is not satisfied by intent, contractual language, or post-incident remediation. It requires effective, enforceable safeguards at the time of processing.\n\nGiven these unresolved contradictions, I do not accept Bolt’s conclusion that this matter falls outside GDPR liability. This correspondence will therefore be submitted as part of a formal complaint to the competent data protection authority for independent assessment.\n\nPlease confirm that this message is retained as part of Bolt’s GDPR compliance documentation.\n\nFYI [~accountid:712020:54af1c3b-f46c-435b-b870-e013cd29eada] ","2026-01-16T10:10:50.035Z"],["3815181","PFI-834038","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Thank you for the escalation. Will escalate this with engineering to fix going forward. Seems we apply the % VAT, rather that sum of VAT Records on Rides level.\n\nCan you, please, share what are the implications of the wrong values in the report? I.e. is it just bad UX or the Clients needs Reports to pay for invoices? This would help with prioritization of the request. \n\nIn the meantime I will gather the corrected list for December","2026-01-16T10:11:06.491Z"],["3815183","DSR-3777","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","* Extracted the [ratings|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/17_NCBvCkYtueaSm7HUjI6Nqa95mFd5Wg?usp=drive_link] → taught [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] how to redact the data. [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] as agreed please check with Brian what *timeframe* relevant to orders (and associated ratings) was used to place the suspension. Based on this, please carry on with amending the responsive data both from a timeframe and redaction POV.\n* Added the [document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LLJuqfhevxpa0rdgUZjMf_V-8wRPqrzccF_1d15ps78/edit?usp=drive_link] with all relevant templates for suspensions → [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] as discussed, review and pick the most appropriate wording for the suspension at hand. Considering that we do not have a template for this specific type of suspension, you will need to leverage the existing templates and draft something that is most appropriate to your case.\n* Reviewed the responsive data - all identified relevant data is [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sPI5bXIqt8SI2-KbkDI_l5lX6YnLUsGz?usp=drive_link] (I moved the relevant folders from the PDE folders to this Responsive Data folder as well). [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] please add the comms data to that folder once you have them 🙏 \n","2026-01-16T10:11:11.999Z"],["3815184","HS-29022","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-16T10:11:13.820Z"],["3815185","LSS-61215","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (16.01)*+\n\n* APRE reverted with some changes to the agreement: [LINK|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q_k_lX3leU-VYPP12Wx3gJVPk1Ky7TfP/edit]\n* Changes and thoughts are below:\n** Recital D / Clause 3.2 (Classification as personal data): No comments ✅ \n*** APRE seems amenable to the nuance here (although they are aware of the 2025 judgement meaning it may not be personal data for _them_ - this does not change things on our side).\n** Indemnity / PDB requirements: No comments ✅ \n*** As expected, APRE has removed these wholesale. We can take a risk-based approach and allow this, as it is very low risk.\n* Parent ticket has been updated ✅ ","2026-01-16T10:11:17.998Z"],["3815188","BR-3857","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","Once we fetch the preauthorization amount, we can pass it as a parameter to email. The ride_receipt and ride_receipt_hopp templates do not need an update, but every single translation for *preauth_disclaimer* must be updated in each email translation like here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/edit/1541|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/edit/1541]\n\nAnother option is to move email translations to crowdin before this change.","2026-01-16T10:11:37.811Z"],["3815189","RNTL-29429","RNTL","karolina.epifantseva@bolt.eu","Karolina Epifantseva","Tested ✅ ","2026-01-16T10:11:45.661Z"],["3815191","LSS-54620","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","!image-20260116-101110.png|width=1202,height=302,alt=\"image-20260116-101110.png\"!\n\nHey Team,\nS&P has acknowledged the termination.\nThanks, and we can now close this ticket.\n\n","2026-01-16T10:12:02.011Z"],["3815192","HS-29021","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-16T10:12:01.624Z"],["3815193","HS-28749","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:619e65173618cd006f8b68c9],\n\nThank you for providing these documents. \n\nAs you reached 10 years of experience last year, you were entitled to 26 annual leave days starting from last year.  I have made changes in Workday.\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-16T10:12:11.913Z"],["3815194","LSS-61641","LSS","olanrewaju.soyinka@bolt.eu","Olanrewaju Soyinka","Attached is the [Incident Report|https://docs.google.com/document/d/16EC7VcFfPSHy-LbBqKEJ12N6F4K1-qGHEgeZc09hHDM/edit?tab=t.0].\n\n","2026-01-16T10:12:24.035Z"],["3815195","PFI-829509","PFI","adam.ruman@bolt.eu","Adam Ruman","Hey Ketlin, thank you for all this info.\n[~accountid:5fbf9493f8b0120069af2a45] I don’t have permissions for the provided pages and I’m not sure whether I’ll be granted these. Could you please have a look at what Ketlin posted? Thank you.","2026-01-16T10:12:43.062Z"],["3815197","LSS-61105","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* Slack chaser message to Jason and Britta.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.12.55 AM.png|width=1049,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 10.12.55 AM.png\"!","2026-01-16T10:13:24.925Z"],["3815199","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], we had aligned on our response to draft → refund the rider the difference directly in his bank account. \n\nThis is proving to be more difficult than expected because the ride was paid in cash, which makes the refund impossible; this needs to be a bank transfer: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-832832?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6ImUyNDE4NmRiYTUxZThkNjE5NDBiYTE1ODI5ZGM4NWUzNjkxYjRhNWZjNWIxYTViNTI4YzI0MWMyN2EyZTk3MDAiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNDAwMzEiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IlBGSS04MzI4MzIifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcwOTc2MTQ5LCJpYXQiOjE3Njg1NTY5NDl9.ABEljfHcGoAzZmMGGbdcGKKIRR7TWhNpLHJE0gQWVhQ|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-832832?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6ImUyNDE4NmRiYTUxZThkNjE5NDBiYTE1ODI5ZGM4NWUzNjkxYjRhNWZjNWIxYTViNTI4YzI0MWMyN2EyZTk3MDAiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNDAwMzEiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IlBGSS04MzI4MzIifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcwOTc2MTQ5LCJpYXQiOjE3Njg1NTY5NDl9.ABEljfHcGoAzZmMGGbdcGKKIRR7TWhNpLHJE0gQWVhQ|smart-link] \n\n\n\nI have been pushing that this needs to be a bank transfer and not promo codes because to be compliant with consumer laws, the ride was misleading and the compensation should not be in a form where the rider needs to use our platform in order to benefit from it.\n\nAs a plan B in case it is not possible to make the bank transfer, should we accept the rider’s request of 100€ on his Bolt Balance ?\n\nThank you for sharing your thoughts on this 🙏 ","2026-01-16T10:13:40.629Z"],["3815200","LSS-61140","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] - we are ok with these changes from the privacy side - no further comments ✅ \n\nAs a flag - APRE has removed the personal data breach / data protection indemnity clauses. This exposes us to a small amount of risk (i.e., APRE suffers a data breach involving the data we share, and the affected drivers come after us instead), *_but_* this is unlikely to materialise, particularly given that the data is pseudonymised. As such, we can take a risk-based approach and proceed :green: \n\nLet me know if you need anything else from me, otherwise I will consider this as closed on my end 🙂 ","2026-01-16T10:13:46.942Z"],["3815202","HS-28874","HS","ala.mohamed@bolt.eu","Ala Mohamed","!Capture d’écran 2026-01-16 à 11.11.12.png|thumbnail!\n\n{color:#172B4D}Hi Marilin,{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}I hope you are doing well.{color} \n\n{color:#172B4D}Thank you for your reply.{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Perfect, noted. I have confirmed my legal name, and now it needs to be validated by the People Service, right? Because I can’t start another request if this one hasn’t been confirmed.{color}\n\n{color:#172B4D}Thank you again for your help.\nHave a great day,{color}\n{color:#333333}Ala{color}","2026-01-16T10:14:00.124Z"],["3815205","HS-29017","HS","mohammad.rahil@bolt.eu","Shaikh Mohd Rahil","Hi, updated the date and attested with the doc 🙌 \n\n!Rahil's Updated Medical Certificate.jpeg|width=960,height=1280,alt=\"Rahil's Updated Medical Certificate.jpeg\"!\n\n","2026-01-16T10:14:32.155Z"],["3815206","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","[@leandro.morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] let's have a call and I'll show you how to do the backfill?","2026-01-16T10:14:33.030Z"],["3815207","FX-3662","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Akash Yadav [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768558428299469]*{color}:\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1768558290692259?thread_ts=1768301694.564939&amp;cid=C02C2SY0MHT]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 16th, 2026 2:11 AM] akash.yadav: this is the DC for enabling monthly summary report.\n[prelive|https://admin-panel.prelive.bolt.eu/dynamic-config/entity/edit/ZmxlZXQtb3duZXItcG9ydGFsL3RheF9yZXBvcnRfaW52b2ljZXNfZW5hYmxlZF93aGl0ZWxpc3Q=/:shard] and [live|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/dynamic-config/entity/edit/ZmxlZXQtb3duZXItcG9ydGFsL3RheF9yZXBvcnRfaW52b2ljZXNfZW5hYmxlZF93aGl0ZWxpc3Q=/:shard] . I see on live, norway is also launched.  it's controlled by fleet-owner\n\nneed to check with them why it's still coming despite not enabled in DC\n{quote}","2026-01-16T10:14:35.697Z"],["3815208","FX-3662","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768558433073529]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@akash.yadav>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3662] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T10:14:38.081Z"],["3815209","LSS-61625","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:6299f17a9582b8006fc6b6c8],\n\nThanks for reaching out.\n\nWe have not received the original claim nor the notification to attend the conciliation hearing referred to in the attached document. For this reason, we were unable to attend the hearing or prepare a defense response.\n\nI have already contacted *SEDECO* (see attached), informing them of these circumstances and formally requesting that they provide us with the original claim and any other relevant documentation on file so that we can properly exercise our right of defense.\n\nOnce we receive the claim, we will prepare our response accordingly. Given the low material relevance of this type of matter, my current inclination is to request that the proceeding be resolved in writing and that we be exempted from attending any in-person hearing, in order to minimise time and costs.\n\nI will keep you updated as soon as we hear back from SEDECO or once we receive the documentation.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Solicitud de remisión de reclamación original – Expediente N° 5064_2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:14:40.536Z"],["3815213","WD-22670","WD","andrzej.lipson@bolt.eu","Andrzej Lipson","Approved","2026-01-16T10:15:07.594Z"],["3815214","HS-28994","HS","kristiina.kuutok@bolt.eu","Kristiina Kuutok","Thank you so much!","2026-01-16T10:15:26.446Z"],["3815216","LSS-61435","LSS","kirsika.liiva@bolt.eu","Kirsika Liiva","Hi, please find the signed document attached!\n\n[^Motor vehicle sale agreement_Bolt Services EE OÜ_Exleasingcar UAB_12.01.26.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:15:33.890Z"],["3815217","FX-3662","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768558530524249]*{color}:\nThey are talking about driver portal, not fleet portal\n{quote}","2026-01-16T10:15:44.774Z"],["3815218","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","{quote}<@U01AH7VKNHY{quote}\n\n> let’s have a call and I’ll show you how to do the backfill?\nI’m in a meeting for next ~45min … is it ok to do it right after meeting finishes?","2026-01-16T10:15:56.729Z"],["3815220","FX-3662","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768558547492389]*{color}:\ni believe this the channel for that: <#C0A86SXNFDH|>\n{quote}","2026-01-16T10:16:05.488Z"],["3815221","WFM-10014","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","This is an ops request.","2026-01-16T10:16:06.105Z"],["3815222","LSS-61698","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T10:16:06.776Z"],["3815225","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","We should check [last year’s feedback|https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1CILyTGzKgunOJZ6bVh_Z-lb3Cupkbv8WnBuk9rkSYtw/edit#responses] and see what we should improve on 🤔 \n\nI can see ETK being the activity AND the dinner, but in a more free form. If they have a TV there, I can bring a steam deck and we can play jackbox again, we can take a bunch of tabletop games from the office, I have What do you meme?, we can order a ton of food from different places and share it, we still have alcohol bottles left from last year’s seminar too.\n\nNext day would be team-specific activities and then after that we’d have to figure out if people wanna stay longer or go back.\n\nThat’s how I see it at least 😄 ","2026-01-16T10:16:20.743Z"],["3815226","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","Sure, let's do that :slightly_smiling_face:","2026-01-16T10:17:09.044Z"],["3815227","HS-28999","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Waiting for settlement agreement","2026-01-16T10:17:31.140Z"],["3815228","RDS-1053","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5f23e70bb7a35e002a73ef5d] What is the status of this initiative? I assume Planned it Q3 2024 is not accurate 😉 ","2026-01-16T10:17:32.681Z"],["3815229","PFI-834131","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-16T10:17:36.066Z"],["3815230","PFI-822328","PFI","seema.matli@bolt.eu","Seema Matli","Hey [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] please could you take a look at the above and advise accordingly, TY🙏🏾","2026-01-16T10:17:41.267Z"],["3815232","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Thanks [@kewei.shang|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5dfb984e9a14250cb69f1697], I’ll ping you when meeting is finished.","2026-01-16T10:18:28.154Z"],["3815234","PFI-834132","PFI","norbert.kato@bolt.eu","Norbert Kato","!Képernyőfotó 2026-01-09 - 14.19.08.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Képernyőfotó 2026-01-16 - 11.17.47.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260109-135952.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T10:18:35.930Z"],["3815235","PFI-834132","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T10:18:38.119Z"],["3815240","CSXRT-200","CSXRT","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","In order to move forward with this case, we’d need to understand the use-case better:\n\n# What is the volume of cases in which micromobility users should be blocked?\n# What are the main reasons for blocking micromobility users? \n# In what cases are we blocking users from all Bolt vs only from a certain vertical? ","2026-01-16T10:19:59.223Z"],["3815241","PFI-834077","PFI","urszula.albrecht@bolt-outsource.eu","Urszula Albrecht","[~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] the user asked for a failed payment, it’s not about BB - is there a chance it will be charged in the future or we won’t charge him?","2026-01-16T10:20:14.005Z"],["3815242","LSS-61499","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:0b391d02-6c8a-4494-99fd-3d2ff0d7ef37] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Szczególne warunki Bolt Business PL 16.12_zwer. (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T10:20:22.579Z"],["3815243","RDS-1053","RDS","pedro.araujo@bolt.eu","Pedro Araújo","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] , [~accountid:5f23e70bb7a35e002a73ef5d] moved to Ads Platform\nI will move this initiative to AB testing as there is an ongoing AB","2026-01-16T10:20:30.506Z"],["3815245","BP-13343","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on Prelive via Bolt rider prelive app\n\n# Country selector dropdown - use {{GET /business/workProfile/countries}} endpoint to populate the dropdown (/) \n# Input validation errors (/) \n!IMG_0165.PNG|width=300,alt=\"IMG_0165.PNG\"!\n!IMG_0172.PNG|width=297,alt=\"IMG_0172.PNG\"!\n\n#* VAT format validation check failure (/) \n!IMG_0163.PNG|width=289,alt=\"IMG_0163.PNG\"!\n\n*Acceptance Criteria check:*\n\nAC-1: A new back-end driven WP company details form has been implemented in work-profile-frontend that can be displayed in a webview inside Rider app (/) \n\nNew work profile - add company details:\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 12-02-47_1.MP4]\n\nExisting work profile - details edit:\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 11-54-29_1.MP4]\n\nAC-2: the form has country dropdown selector and can display text and radio button form fields (/) \n\n!IMG_0168.PNG|width=269,alt=\"IMG_0168.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_0169.PNG|width=280,alt=\"IMG_0169.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_0170.PNG|width=281,alt=\"IMG_0170.PNG\"!\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 12-18-10_1.MP4]","2026-01-16T10:20:58.191Z"],["3815246","FX-3662","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Akash Yadav [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768558851449129]*{color}:\nyeah, i found out. thanks\n{quote}","2026-01-16T10:21:05.654Z"],["3815247","PFI-822328","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo [~accountid:5f01e8651c682d0029d6ea82] , [~accountid:6155b82fa70710006958c85b] \n\nI’ve replied here, you can inform the rider accordingly:\n\n{quote}It depends on the driver’s VAT liability. If the driver is VAT-liable, the rider invoice will reflect this accordingly, if not, VAT will be 0%.{quote}","2026-01-16T10:21:08.270Z"],["3815248","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:628b3e951a437e0070414307] ,\n\nJust to update you on the response we’ve now had from Bee / the landlord’s solicitors (attached):\n\n* Bee has passed our proposal to the landlord for consideration.\n* If the landlord does agree to a surrender and new lease, Bee expects the landlord will require Bolt to cover the landlord’s *legal costs for negotiating the new lease* and the *surrender with Voi*.\n* In addition, the landlord *may require a surrender premium* (amount TBC at this stage).\n* On the sub-letting option, Bee confirms it is permitted under the lease, but would still require landlord consent and a formal licence to underlet.\n\nBee has also suggested that, *if Bolt has a direct relationship with the landlord*, that may be the quickest way to move the commercial negotiations forward.\n\nIt would be helpful to get your view on:\n\n# Whether you’re happy to reach out to the landlord directly to discuss the commercial position; and\n# At a high level, *what Bolt is prepared to pay* (if anything) in terms of:\n#* landlord legal costs, and\n#* a potential surrender premium, so we can align our legal position with the commercial one.\n\nI’ll send Bee a short holding / placeholder response now to keep things moving, but let me know how you’d like to approach the landlord engagement and I’m very happy to support or join any conversations if helpful.\n\nThank you!\n\n\n[^Bolt Mail - REBolt - Liverpool Scooter Operations Unit 9 Phoenix Park [IMAN-WSLIVE.FID5498717].pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:21:11.346Z"],["3815249","PFI-834133","PFI","success.igbinosa@bolt-outsource.eu","Success Igbinosa","!3000.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T10:21:13.864Z"],["3815250","LSS-60899","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","aligned with you!\n\nThank you.\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-16T10:21:45.787Z"],["3815251","FX-3662","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768558896219879]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3662 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T10:21:49.330Z"],["3815252","WD-22670","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","the access was granted","2026-01-16T10:21:53.266Z"],["3815253","FIS-4211","FIS","pavel.permenov@bolt.eu","Pavel Permenov","Back to “In progress” after [a discussion|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C036X55150A/p1768557825931039?thread_ts=1768551310.781549&cid=C036X55150A] with the team","2026-01-16T10:22:16.906Z"],["3815259","LSS-58999","LSS","mihaela.vatamanu@bolt.eu","Mihaela Vatamanu","Hi Alon, your memory is on point. They haven’t come back to us, but I just reminded them and emphasized the need to move faster here. Will keep you posted. Thanks! \n\n","2026-01-16T10:23:07.485Z"],["3815260","PFI-834134","PFI","danylo.udovytskyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Danylo Udovytskyi","[^d827efa7-ff62-49f3-a68c-c4902ef52837.pdf]","2026-01-16T10:23:19.277Z"],["3815261","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* holding response sent to Bee / landlord’s solicitor.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - RE_Bolt - Liverpool Scooter Operations Unit 9 Phoenix Park [IMAN-WSLIVE.FID5498717].pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:23:22.384Z"],["3815263","LSS-61228","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nthanks for looking at this, if we dont have any other choice yes, please proceed with  rider’s request of 100€ on his Bolt Balance.\n\nthank you\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-16T10:23:35.689Z"],["3815264","SREDESK-7420","SREDESK","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hi,\n\nA change on your Okta account is needed.\n\nI asked the IT team.\n\nAfter that, I will grant the Zero Trust permission.\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349568|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349568|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T10:24:09.963Z"],["3815265","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","Alrighty, I’ve emailed ETK to get quote (just in case asked about corkage fee if we bring our own booze), and it’s fair being activity+dinner. Then next day domains plan their own.\nIf we’re doing seminar in auditorium, we can ask from EA to supply us with Fork cards for lunches 👀 ","2026-01-16T10:24:19.491Z"],["3815266","LSS-61604","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] the answer to both questions is yes :done: \n\nWe can use the document we used for West Midlands, it is accurate.\n\nRegarding the second question (technical part) - I want to understand what the expectations there - it also seems like Information Security team might be better equipped to support with providing technical descriptions, could you loop them in?","2026-01-16T10:24:34.330Z"],["3815268","RDXENG-3979","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:5cca8c2d8869dd0e78a063b8] \n\n(x) Tested 4 digit CVV - network name should not be included to the tooltip text.\n\n!IMG_1800-20260116-102140.PNG|width=281,alt=\"IMG_1800-20260116-102140.PNG\"!","2026-01-16T10:25:06.917Z"],["3815269","RDS-1313","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] IMO this feels like a bug that should be easy to fix. Wdyt? ","2026-01-16T10:25:12.084Z"],["3815270","DBRE-8705","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","retro incident is ok, question is still the same - which exactly business services were impacted and how exactly? So far i see payments lifecycle team reporting issue on behalf of payments analysts being part of product management org, so was impact on PM analytics only/mostly?","2026-01-16T10:25:21.198Z"],["3815271","LSS-61638","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], as discussed on Slack, if you log into ChatGPT through your *Bolt account*, then you should be able to access 🙂 ","2026-01-16T10:25:37.864Z"],["3815272","PFI-832488","PFI","aiga.gegere@bolt-outsource.eu","Aiga Gegere","Hello, again! The issue is solved. Please close the ticket.","2026-01-16T10:25:51.189Z"],["3815274","MVRT-1492","MVRT","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","Localization Request : [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101321|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101321|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T10:26:17.382Z"],["3815278","DBRE-8705","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","asking mostly to understand if it was proper full fledged incident or Near-Miss Incident","2026-01-16T10:27:36.654Z"],["3815279","LSS-61599","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5], just to confirm that I will be picking this one up and will message Alex now re a suitable witness for his signature.","2026-01-16T10:27:46.906Z"],["3815282","RDS-1315","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:34206d98-4d0d-43ac-93e3-4a910bc0fe7e] Out of curiosity, how does it work on Android now? Is entering past data just blocked?","2026-01-16T10:28:06.380Z"],["3815283","CNT-339","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","Hey [~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] do you have an ETA in mind for the article and carousel? I’m planning for next week and wanted to check whether it could be ready to share then.","2026-01-16T10:28:14.156Z"],["3815284","GS-71","GS","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nWorking on Admin-panel page for editing: Pickup Directions per search_category_group\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\nADR:https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7053639713/2025+Oct+-+Airport+meet+greet+instructions+for+Lux+riders+-+Bolt+Chauffeur+-+ADR ( )https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7053639713/2025+Oct+-+Airport+meet+greet+instructions+for+Lux+riders+-+Bolt+Chauffeur+-+ADR (2025 Oct - Airport meet &amp;amp;amp;amp; greet instructions for Lux riders - Bolt Chauffeur - ADR)\n\n- :done: done implementation \"Alternative #2: Pickup directions per search_category_group\" . Released.\n- :loading: working in progress on: integration with admin-panel: new UI fields to support editing of directions with search_category_group","2026-01-16T10:28:24.806Z"],["3815285","PFI-832470","PFI","folashade.akinsola@bolt.eu","Folashade Dolapo Akinsola","Thank you. We will make the necessary updates accordingly. However, we would need visibility into the change trail, including the employee who made the edits.\n\nPlease also confirm that once the changes are made, the invoices will be updated to reflect the correct name.","2026-01-16T10:28:51.161Z"],["3815286","LSS-61701","LSS","kaija.riismaa@bolt.eu","Kaija Riismaa","Hi Maksim! \n\nThis does not seem to be a question that can be answered by  the legal team (it is not related to any legal matter), but rather by  Product Team or Local Operations team. In the light of that this request should be submitted via some other Service Desk, but I do not know which one. \n\nBest regards, \nKaija","2026-01-16T10:28:52.263Z"],["3815287","WFM-10014","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","hey, upon your previous request it was added to the beehove rides ops agent role which both of them have. if something is not working please follow the usual troubleshooting steps below. if still not success please come back with screenshots so we can investigate further.\r\n• refresh\r\n• hard refresh\r\n• connect to another network (ideally fast wired internet)\r\n• disable all browser extensions (incl ad-blocks), then refresh the page\r\n• clear cache and cookies\r\n• another browser (ideally Chrome, and needs to be updated to latest version)\r\n• restart browser\r\n• restart laptop","2026-01-16T10:29:27.251Z"],["3815289","LSS-56585","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[~accountid:5b7d5435b57ed25933f64464] the review from my side is completed, unfortunately [the draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/125o395bpmCwcIyETink5Eb72-twZ0SvE/edit?pli=1] will need to go back to Vodacom for review before finalising. \n\n* Our material amendments have mostly been accepted. \n* Defined Effective Date of 1 December 2025 at clause 1.2. \n* As you will note from clause 7.1 we are not imposing any further obligations on Bolt until such time that the MOU is signed. ","2026-01-16T10:30:08.967Z"],["3815293","GC-3171","GC","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nMinor progress, due to working with priority on \"Bolt Chauffeur - Lux Category - Pickup Directions\":\n\n- :loading: Analysing BUG: TollRoad detection at large distance (few km away): causes EdgeDetection to estimate too many tolls. Analysis & testing in progress\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\n- :done: implementation complete, last PR was merged this week.\n- :done: Run silent-live test for comparing EdgeDetection vs TollGuru,  in Thailand.\n- :done: Extract silent-live results\n- :done: Map OPs team found some bugs while analysing the last silent-live test: EdgeDetection vs TollGuru in  Thailand).\n- :loading: BUG: TollRoad detection at large distance (few km away): causes EdgeDetection to estimate too many tolls. Analysis & testing in progress\n- :done: Tooling: working on Admin-panel page for testing our internal solution: Route-Tolls","2026-01-16T10:31:29.652Z"],["3815294","LSS-61701","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T10:31:36.076Z"],["3815296","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Consulting databricks for the records created in 2026 in Bulgaria give the following result for subtype of the records:\n\n{noformat}+----------------+------+\n|                |count |\n|subtype         |      |\n+----------------+------+\n|food            |324   |\n|serviceFee      |43    |\n|delivery        |21    |\n|deliveryCampaign|12    |\n|foodCampaign    |11    |\n|smallOrderFee   |9     |\n+----------------+------+\n{noformat}\n\nFor an example order 279235364, we can verify the billing trail [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-delivery/invoicing/delivery/billingTrails/279235364|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-delivery/invoicing/delivery/billingTrails/279235364] and see that this received a partial refund for custom amount and delivery fee, and both the custom amount and delivery fee were refunded.\n\nThe records were created, but the invoices apparently were not. For the order above, the task to create the courier invoice failed with error “30008 INVALID_DATA: Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals.”\n\nInvestigating whether this is a common problem or if this is an isolated case. If an isolated case, why.","2026-01-16T10:31:45.337Z"],["3815299","PFI-833383","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Reissued: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6037949123?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6037949123?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-16T10:32:22.411Z"],["3815300","DSR-3777","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","The comm hat was sent is called “Global, Drivers, Email, Adhoc, Low rated drivers warning”.\nIt was sent on Sep 2, 2025 at 16:12.\nBasis of the warning and later termination is his low rated trips.\n\n_EDIT: I added this screenshot to the_ [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sPI5bXIqt8SI2-KbkDI_l5lX6YnLUsGz?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sPI5bXIqt8SI2-KbkDI_l5lX6YnLUsGz?usp=drive_link|smart-link] _folder in G Drive_\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.30.16.png|width=539,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.30.16.png\"!","2026-01-16T10:32:40.278Z"],["3815301","PFI-834077","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:637b7db18fd2d2d5f12d48c0] \n\nSince all of the payment logs have expired I don’t see any triggers that would charge the customer for the failed payment. \nBolt has accepted the loss. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T10:32:55.074Z"],["3815303","WD-22584","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Access granted!","2026-01-16T10:34:03.087Z"],["3815304","PFI-834137","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T10:34:56.542Z"],["3815305","RDS-1313","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Isn’t a bug as far as I understood, just pieces of legacy design. It’s a simple fix and planned to take anytime we might need to fill a short window. We have couple of other such tickets as well ready to take whenever we can","2026-01-16T10:35:15.336Z"],["3815308","LSS-61702","LSS","aviansarah.abraham@bolt.eu","Avian Abraham","[^BOLT BUSINESS IMAGINE (1).pdf] _(621 kB)_","2026-01-16T10:36:10.221Z"],["3815311","PFI-834134","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","asking for a double approval to mark the payment as cancelled. \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768559720403?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768559720403?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-16T10:37:23.283Z"],["3815312","PFI-834138","PFI","oluwayemisi.jamgbadi@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwayemisi Jamgbadi","!Screenshot_20260116-102001 payment.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260116-102705.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T10:37:39.012Z"],["3815314","RDS-1320","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] agree – and actually it’s planned for this quarter. see ticket I linked (only now) for more context. ","2026-01-16T10:37:48.502Z"],["3815317","PFI-831605","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 10.27 EUR on 26/12/2025, 19:44:10UTC\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 72700925360172991658478  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 26th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Proof of Refund 26-12-2025.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T10:39:10.262Z"],["3815318","PFI-833791","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! What do you mean it’s lower than it should be? What’s the expected amount and why? ","2026-01-16T10:39:21.996Z"],["3815320","PFI-833383","PFI","patrik.kupco@bolt.eu","Patrik Kupčo","Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-16T10:39:27.958Z"],["3815321","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","Thanks [@marat.saddarov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3], I'm clarifying with the user on the impact in this separate [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CF65PRL0N/p1768559731854379?thread_ts=1768555181.857879&cid=CF65PRL0N].","2026-01-16T10:39:32.829Z"],["3815322","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Consulting databricks for the records created in 2026 in Bulgaria give the following result for subtype of the records:\n\n{noformat}+----------------+------+\n|                |count |\n|subtype         |      |\n+----------------+------+\n|food            |324   |\n|serviceFee      |43    |\n|delivery        |21    |\n|deliveryCampaign|12    |\n|foodCampaign    |11    |\n|smallOrderFee   |9     |\n+----------------+------+\n{noformat}\n\nFor an example order 279235364, we can verify the billing trail [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-delivery/invoicing/delivery/billingTrails/279235364|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-delivery/invoicing/delivery/billingTrails/279235364] and see that this received a partial refund for custom amount and delivery fee, and both the custom amount and delivery fee were refunded.\n\nThe records were created, but the invoices apparently were not. For the order above, the task to create the courier invoice failed with error “30008 INVALID_DATA: Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals.”","2026-01-16T10:39:42.718Z"],["3815323","RDS-618","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] FYI – I think you should consider / discuss with [~accountid:712020:28ec7636-10da-43ee-a95c-be32cdfb7744]/Kasper if this should be handed over to Commerce. As most triggers would come from them, and I think they got their FE resources confirmed, they might be able to execute it better. ","2026-01-16T10:40:07.693Z"],["3815324","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","It seems it was an isolated case:\n\n{code:sql}select reference_data, reference_id, reference_type, state, error_message\nfrom ng_delivery_spark.delivery_invoicing_task\nwhere entity_type='order_refund_invoice_uds'\nand reference_id IN (576