                                                    |\n|f-328-421119497-0-delivery_provider-570240269|570240269   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-421119497-0-bolt_issuer-570240269      |570240269   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-421034582-0-bolt_issuer-570067436      |570067436   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-421034582-0-delivery_provider-570067436|570067436   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424716944-0-delivery_provider-576315728|576315728   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424746199-0-bolt_issuer-576395557      |576395557   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424716944-0-bolt_issuer-576315728      |576315728   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424746199-0-delivery_provider-576395557|576395557   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424648596-0-bolt_issuer-576337793      |576337793   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424648596-0-delivery_provider-576337793|576337793   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424596575-0-bolt_issuer-576023791      |576023791   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424596575-0-delivery_provider-576023791|576023791   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424205210-0-delivery_provider-575280817|575280817   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424205210-0-bolt_issuer-575280817      |575280817   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424149708-0-bolt_issuer-575279488      |575279488   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-424172811-0-bolt_issuer-575134597      |575134597   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424149708-0-delivery_provider-575279488|575279488   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-424172811-0-delivery_provider-575134597|575134597   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-423273067-0-delivery_provider-575383382|575383382   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-423273067-0-bolt_issuer-575383382      |575383382   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-423752139-0-delivery_provider-575068896|575068896   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-423752139-0-bolt_issuer-575068896      |575068896   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-420784451-0-delivery_provider-569768046|569768046   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-420784451-0-bolt_issuer-569768046      |569768046   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-420692301-0-bolt_issuer-569623069      |569623069   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-420692301-0-delivery_provider-569623069|569623069   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-420670462-0-delivery_provider-569446235|569446235   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-420670462-0-bolt_issuer-569446235      |569446235   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-420530779-0-bolt_issuer-569405438      |569405438   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-420530779-0-delivery_provider-569405438|569405438   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-422130758-0-bolt_issuer-572856559      |572856559   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-422130758-0-delivery_provider-572856559|572856559   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-420237972-0-bolt_issuer-572561118      |572561118   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-420237972-0-delivery_provider-572561118|572561118   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-423929212-0-delivery_provider-574676233|574676233   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-423929212-0-bolt_issuer-574676233      |574676233   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-421548464-0-delivery_provider-571040718|571040718   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-421548464-0-bolt_issuer-571040718      |571040718   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer-571110677      |571110677   |event         |fail |30008 INVALID_DATA: Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals|\n|f-328-419611207-0-delivery_provider-571110677|571110677   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|f-328-422533381-0-delivery_provider-573109097|573109097   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n|d-328-422533381-0-bolt_issuer-573109097      |573109097   |event         |done |null                                                                       |\n+---------------------------------------------+------------+--------------+-----+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n{noformat}\n\nAll the other partial events were processed correctly, as the table demonstrates.","2026-01-16T10:40:18.001Z"],["3815326","WFM-10020","WFM","panagiotis.kabolis@bolt-outsource.eu","Panagiotis Kabolis","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 123802.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T10:40:58.698Z"],["3815330","PFI-831598","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nThe refund has failed. Our partner does not store refund details. We can ask our partner to issue the refund again, however we need the customers refund details. \nCould you please ask the customer to provide the following.\n\n*Bank name:* \n*Account name:* \n*Account number:*\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T10:41:06.349Z"],["3815331","DSR-3781","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T10:41:06.525Z"],["3815332","RDS-1320","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] , Yes, I remember from the document you shared 🙂 Therefore, I was surprised by the priority. Thx for adjusting!","2026-01-16T10:41:10.211Z"],["3815334","PFI-830801","PFI","nantawat.boonchu@bolt-outsource.eu","Nantawat Boonchu","Dear payment team,\n\nKindly follow up on updating driver commission on 8 Jan 2026.\n\nThank you in advance.","2026-01-16T10:41:26.977Z"],["3815337","HS-28874","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hey Ala!\n\nYes, I received the task, but it came to with Your name change. In this task please don’t change Your name, legal name should stay as it is in Your Government documents. Firstly please just check if the Legal name is correct and submit it (I have sent the task back to You). After that please fallow the instructions attached earlier. \n\nPlease let me know if You have any questions 🙂 \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-16T10:42:06.031Z"],["3815338","PFI-834013","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Reconciliation in progress ","2026-01-16T10:42:08.953Z"],["3815342","WD-22588","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] , \nI have checked your access since January last year and you didn’t had it then, nor did Enelys or Carmen. Which means you haven’t had access to the report for the whole year. \n\nThe access you lost is actual Workday report or something more like workbook, google sheet, something else? Do your colleagues still have access? ","2026-01-16T10:43:15.859Z"],["3815343","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Error:\n\n{code:json}{\n  \"error\": \"BoltError: INVALID_DATA(30008)\\nerror_data: {\\\"text\\\":\\\"Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals\\\",\\\"invoice_totals\\\":{\\\"sum\\\":0.1917,\\\"vat_sum\\\":0.0384,\\\"sum_with_vat\\\":0.2301,\\\"vat_percentage\\\":0},\\\"record_totals\\\":{\\\"sum\\\":0.19,\\\"vat_percentage\\\":0,\\\"vat_sum\\\":0.04,\\\"sum_with_vat\\\":0.2301},\\\"task\\\":{\\\"id\\\":2973630841,\\\"state\\\":\\\"to_execute\\\",\\\"error_message\\\":\\\"30008 INVALID_DATA: Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals\\\",\\\"retry_left\\\":5,\\\"entity_type\\\":\\\"order_refund_invoice_uds\\\",\\\"payload_json\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"billing_document_migration_config\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"is_billing_document_integration_enabled\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"is_billing_document_source_of_truth\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"is_invoicing_document_deprecated\\\\\\\": false}, \\\\\\\"original_invoice_external_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"reference_data\\\":\\\"d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer-571110677\\\",\\\"reference_id\\\":571110677,\\\"reference_type\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"city_id\\\":0,\\\"dependencies_list\\\":\\\"[{\\\\\\\"e\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"eater_payment_refund\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ri\\\\\\\":571110677,\\\\\\\"rd\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"e\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"eater_delivery_bolt_instant_invoice_uds\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ri\\\\\\\":567941160,\\\\\\\"rd\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\"}]\\\",\\\"ignore_until\\\":1768550400}}\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"code\": 30008,\n    \"error_data\": {\n      \"invoice_totals\": {\n        \"sum\": 0.1917,\n        \"sum_with_vat\": 0.2301,\n        \"vat_percentage\": 0,\n        \"vat_sum\": 0.0384\n      },\n      \"record_totals\": {\n        \"sum\": 0.19,\n        \"sum_with_vat\": 0.2301,\n        \"vat_percentage\": 0,\n        \"vat_sum\": 0.04\n      },\n      \"task\": {\n        \"city_id\": 0,\n        \"dependencies_list\": \"[{\\\"e\\\":\\\"eater_payment_refund\\\",\\\"rt\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"ri\\\":571110677,\\\"rd\\\":\\\"0\\\"},{\\\"e\\\":\\\"eater_delivery_bolt_instant_invoice_uds\\\",\\\"rt\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"ri\\\":567941160,\\\"rd\\\":\\\"0\\\"}]\",\n        \"entity_type\": \"order_refund_invoice_uds\",\n        \"error_message\": \"30008 INVALID_DATA: Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals\",\n        \"id\": 2973630841,\n        \"ignore_until\": 1768550400,\n        \"payload_json\": \"{\\\"billing_document_migration_config\\\": {\\\"is_billing_document_integration_enabled\\\": true, \\\"is_billing_document_source_of_truth\\\": true, \\\"is_invoicing_document_deprecated\\\": false}, \\\"original_invoice_external_id\\\": \\\"d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer\\\"}\",\n        \"reference_data\": \"d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer-571110677\",\n        \"reference_id\": 571110677,\n        \"reference_type\": \"event\",\n        \"retry_left\": 5,\n        \"state\": \"to_execute\"\n      },\n      \"text\": \"Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals\"\n    },\n    \"message\": \"INVALID_DATA\"\n  },\n  \"row\": {\n    \"city_id\": 0,\n    \"dependencies_list\": \"[{\\\"e\\\":\\\"eater_payment_refund\\\",\\\"rt\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"ri\\\":571110677,\\\"rd\\\":\\\"0\\\"},{\\\"e\\\":\\\"eater_delivery_bolt_instant_invoice_uds\\\",\\\"rt\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"ri\\\":567941160,\\\"rd\\\":\\\"0\\\"}]\",\n    \"entity_type\": \"order_refund_invoice_uds\",\n    \"error_message\": \"30008 INVALID_DATA: Refund invoice totals do not match refund record totals\",\n    \"id\": 2973630841,\n    \"ignore_until\": 1768550400,\n    \"payload_json\": \"{\\\"billing_document_migration_config\\\": {\\\"is_billing_document_integration_enabled\\\": true, \\\"is_billing_document_source_of_truth\\\": true, \\\"is_invoicing_document_deprecated\\\": false}, \\\"original_invoice_external_id\\\": \\\"d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer\\\"}\",\n    \"reference_data\": \"d-328-419611207-0-bolt_issuer-571110677\",\n    \"reference_id\": 571110677,\n    \"reference_type\": \"event\",\n    \"retry_left\": 5,\n    \"state\": \"to_execute\"\n  }\n}{code}","2026-01-16T10:43:26.497Z"],["3815345","PFI-831009","PFI","norbert.kato@bolt.eu","Norbert Kato","HI [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] Do we have any updates on this one? ","2026-01-16T10:44:24.910Z"],["3815346","PFI-774192","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e]This payment is still missing, need to import missing wema payments","2026-01-16T10:44:39.141Z"],["3815347","LSS-61669","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:13ae7353-697f-46e7-99dd-8fc938931751],\n\nThanks for reaching out.\n\nCould you kindly upload the agreement to the ticket?\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-16T10:44:40.485Z"],["3815348","WD-22588","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","CC [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] did you guys do any role changes related to Lysette or domain security policies updates related to Set Up: Adaptive Planning? \n\nI didn’t find anything in audit trail so I’m reaching out like this.","2026-01-16T10:44:59.661Z"],["3815349","LSS-61614","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343656|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343656|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T10:45:01.274Z"],["3815353","RDS-1313","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] thx, makes sense.","2026-01-16T10:45:26.527Z"],["3815354","LSS-61616","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] ,\n\nI can take ownership of the ticket, but it seems that we'll both need to contribute to some extent to ensure it’s handled effectively.","2026-01-16T10:45:48.443Z"],["3815357","PFI-834144","PFI","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","[^bolt 6.11 outgoing transfer 2nd page highlited.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-16T10:46:14.932Z"],["3815358","WD-22588","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","I did not change anything in regards neither Lysette nor domain security","2026-01-16T10:47:18.086Z"],["3815359","PFI-834144","PFI","joao.nunes@bolt.eu","João Nunes","[^Notes_260114_192102 fees highlited.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:47:21.578Z"],["3815360","LSS-57841","LSS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","So, should we reject it? 🙂","2026-01-16T10:47:27.242Z"],["3815362","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","The sum_with_vat is the same, but the sum to be refunded from the records is 0.19, while from the invoice_totals is 0.1917 (*Note:* there is something weird going on with vat_percent).\n\nThe original order was made before the end of the year and the refund processed after the end of the year, so this is very likely a rounding error caused by currency conversion.","2026-01-16T10:47:36.800Z"],["3815363","WEB-7610","WEB","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] Hey! This seems like an older request and I don’t have full historical context on it. From what I can see now, the multi-location setup is working, and roles are displayed as “Various locations”, which seems to address the main issue around avoiding multiple duplicate postings. Am I correct? \n\nIf any limitations around titles or locations come up in practice, I’ll reach out again and we can revisit this.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T10:47:46.533Z"],["3815365","LSS-61140","LSS","xavier.bendavid@bolt.eu","Xavier Bendavid","thank you Thomas for your help here, then we are going to send the data and the signed contract. Merci","2026-01-16T10:48:07.550Z"],["3815366","PFI-834150","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T10:48:34.407Z"],["3815367","PFI-832954","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Driver made a mistake in account number, payment has been reallocated https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75636809\r\n\r\nOnce again reminder to use the admin search to add the payment link to yours tickets as well would help us a lot and you can already see why the payment is not in the driver balance. ","2026-01-16T10:48:38.829Z"],["3815368","LSS-61298","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","hello [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], thank you for the comments and the amendments suggested. \n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else or we are good to move forward with initiating this. \n\nThank you","2026-01-16T10:48:45.119Z"],["3815369","RS-1944","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5f1538051c682d00295dbb61] ,\n\nWhen is the launch date?","2026-01-16T10:48:52.106Z"],["3815372","LSS-61612","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343662|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343662|smart-link]  ","2026-01-16T10:49:05.622Z"],["3815375","MLC-3","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","*W3:*\n\n* Updates:\n** Engineering team picked up fleet owner comms event as part of their team duty (Currently we cannot differentiate between suspension and termination). They created a new event Courier Behaviour Action that has a property for action_type that we were missing before.\n* Next steps:\n** I will work on comms updates for fleet owners starting Monday.\n** I will catch up with Anna-Lota on fraud reasons specific content will be needed sometime in the future.","2026-01-16T10:49:46.442Z"],["3815376","WEBSD-1474","WEBSD","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","Hi team, do you have any updates here? Thank you, ","2026-01-16T10:50:03.278Z"],["3815379","PFI-832957","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Re-allocated to the owner [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75772246|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75772246]","2026-01-16T10:50:19.737Z"],["3815380","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","Record indicate that the vat_percent is 20%. \n\n0.2301 / 1.2 should have given a vat_sum of 0.1918, which is wrong in both cases, but the invoice is closer to what it should be.\n\n* *Follow-up question:* Why was the converted sum for the delivery record 0.19 intead of 0.1917?","2026-01-16T10:50:32.594Z"],["3815381","PFI-834151","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-16T10:50:35.089Z"],["3815382","BP-13343","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Known issues:\n\n# *[fixed in* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13224|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13224|smart-link] *]*Changing country clears all fields of the form\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 12-41-43_1.MP4]\n# *[fixed in* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13224|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13224|smart-link] *]* Country selection → going back after save\n# *[under design review]* Exclamation mark under “Is your company VAT registered?” from design is not present in the webview\n!IMG_0172 (c4cbb86a-5bcc-4a48-9c14-e316dd3ea23b).PNG|width=204,alt=\"IMG_0172.PNG\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.25.29.png|width=285,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.25.29.png\"!\n# *[to be fixed in* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13224|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13224|smart-link] *]* Currently the “Review your company information” banner is shown all the time (needs to be displayed only when a *required field is not filed)","2026-01-16T10:50:37.591Z"],["3815383","PFI-834151","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:63e3ef2dbf837c6893db58e3, 712020:555b4857-4677-4c34-84b6-3a64431574dd, 712020:876960aa-09c5-44ff-9c52-2cb24c637062] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T10:50:37.253Z"],["3815384","LSS-60335","LSS","juozas.masteika@bolt.eu","Juozas Masteika","Adding the final answer document from VDI \n\n[^O. Z. - Bolt Operations OU.pdf.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:50:47.192Z"],["3815385","SCM-839","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] added [note|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hRsxJvSeplONaUQozo-jXSx_lB9FTWc-1hiqg-b6PjM/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.lrzt4gfaqvy2] to the playbook and also shared a reminder about opening a warehouse process on Slack. From now on the process willo be tracked through regular meetings with LOPS. I mark the task as done.","2026-01-16T10:50:52.997Z"],["3815386","LSS-60403","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] , Looks good to me! Thanks🙏 ","2026-01-16T10:50:56.262Z"],["3815387","RLONE-839","RLONE","robin.wersall@bolt.eu","Robin Wersäll","I’ve [raised|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CLG9WR600/p1745925845046229] this in tech support last year as we have seen multiple examples of drivers solely active in add-on categories such as “Pet” which makes no sense. Back then we did not have any solution for it, but should definitely be revisited. ","2026-01-16T10:51:14.543Z"],["3815389","CRC-2036","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Engaging in discussion with aircash as well.","2026-01-16T10:51:21.755Z"],["3815391","LSS-61140","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you very much [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] for your quick and clear feedback throughout! All clear for us. \n\n[~accountid:712020:cf457436-e17c-4575-8d48-f2b9135ccc82] you can confirm that we accept their changes, and you can share the signatory details for the e-signature process: \n\nName: Ahto Kink\nEmail: [ahto.kink@bolt.eu|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu]\n\nplease put [signing@bolt.eu|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] in cc. (important, otherwise Ahto will not sign)\n\nThank you ","2026-01-16T10:51:32.472Z"],["3815392","LSS-61698","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] please assist ","2026-01-16T10:51:44.815Z"],["3815393","PFI-833833","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:5f01e8651c682d0029d6ea82] \n\nOh, I see what you mean now. \nUnfortunately, I’m unable to advise on any pricing related questions. The price is decided by the ride hailing vertical and sent to payments via API. The customer payments team doesn’t have any impact on the pricing. \n\nOvercapture can happen where the final order price increases. We are using this feature in countries where authorization adjustments are not enabled. Overcapture can be triggered by the order being more expensive than initially estimated or could be tip related. I did not see any destination changes or tipping for these orders though. \n\nI would suggest checking with the ride hailing technical support team to see how the pricing was calculated. \nIf the the ride hailing tech support team is not able to assist you then I think it’s also worth checking with the Business Billing team to see if the invoices match the payment or the order. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T10:51:59.597Z"],["3815399","LSS-54100","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] \n\nWe prepared review of the website terms and highlighted these  risks \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-768xZEMlnMwS16vqxDOMKP9m-k-jCTI/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-768xZEMlnMwS16vqxDOMKP9m-k-jCTI/edit|smart-link] \n\n[https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/terms/jetbrains-ai-service/|https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/terms/jetbrains-ai-service/|smart-link]  and [https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/company/useterms/|https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/company/useterms/|smart-link] \n\n*Most important points:* \n\n* No liability in case of damages (liability is capped at the greater of 100 USD or fees paid in 12 months \n* No liability for data loss \n* Exclusion from the warranties that Bolt’s content will be secure \n* Automatic renewal unless opted out in the account settings \n\n\n\nPlease let me know if InfoSec reviewed the tool, as well ","2026-01-16T10:53:10.943Z"],["3815400","PFI-832960","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment reallocated https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75636983","2026-01-16T10:53:11.301Z"],["3815402","RLONE-844","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","[~accountid:712020:4f32d8aa-fb3b-41d6-8660-25925fc53773] please remember to input details on task-level aslo. Minimum requirements is deadline, team and assignee","2026-01-16T10:53:49.056Z"],["3815403","LSS-61403","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*BACKGROUND*+\n\n* Bolt has upcoming partner visits to its premises in France (19 and 20 Jan). \n** Apparently “no personal data will be processed or transferred” here. There will be no access to systems or tools; just an on-site visit.\n* We have an existing NDA and DPA in place, issued by Central Ops and covering data sharing.\n** We entered our standard DPA with the partner (Rounded).\n* *Request*: Are the above docs enough, or are additional agreements required?\n\n+*THOUGHTS*+\n\n* We do not review NDAs - Local counsel (Philippine) should review this.\n* Re the DPA, this only covers data processing in the context of providing the services (or responding to technical problems). Also, categories are limited to name, account ID, contact info, driver compliance data, and call-related data. As such, +*the DPA is unlikely to fully cover personal data sharing in the context of a premises visit*+.\n** This is not necessarily an issue, particularly if no systems access takes place - DSAs are more standard for structured / ongoing disclosures. The focus should be more on sensible practices rather than agreements. The NDA should do most of the heavy lifting from an agreement POV.\n* Overall, IMO we do not need an additional DSA/DPA here - the visits are short, limited to a few persons, and no access to our systems will be granted. However, I would still recommend the following:\n** *Minimise unintended disclosure*: Do not take the partner anywhere with visible screens / whiteboards / loud calls discussing confidential matters. Do not allow the taking of photos or videos. Do not let them see documents that are not strictly part of the visit.\n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* QUESTIONS:\n** So to be clear - Rounded is visiting our premises, and you want to know fit the NDA and DPA entered last November covers this? This does not relate to other partners?\n** What is the purpose of the visit? What will you be doing / discussing / showing them? Where will you be going (anywhere with screens)? Any photos? Any docs shared?\n* ADVICE:\n** Per the above.","2026-01-16T10:53:50.678Z"],["3815404","RS-1956","RS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[^_大安分局來函 01_15 .pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:54:02.601Z"],["3815405","LSS-60609","LSS","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","*FYI:* This is the official response that CVKeskus sent to the Language Inspectorate (Keeleamet).\n\nThey confirm active work on automated translations for compliance, while also clearly stating that English-language job ads are a justified and intentional choice when the working environment and role require strong English skills, emphasising proportionality and target audience context.\n\n\n[^Vastus_Keeleametile_CV Keskus.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T10:54:03.562Z"],["3815406","PFI-831596","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T10:54:07.744Z"],["3815407","LSS-61464","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343666|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343666|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T10:54:15.748Z"],["3815408","RLONE-844","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","It enbales us to view the tasks across all views ","2026-01-16T10:54:28.255Z"],["3815409","PFI-834156","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T10:54:31.929Z"],["3815410","RLONE-837","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","[~accountid:712020:4f32d8aa-fb3b-41d6-8660-25925fc53773] please remember to input project details on the project. Minimum requirements is deadline, team and assignee","2026-01-16T10:54:55.637Z"],["3815411","PFI-831592","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team,\n\nI can confirm that a refund of 45.00 ZAR was issued on 10/12/2025, 15:57:32UTC.\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to provide refund confirmation documents or reference numbers that can be used by the customer to independently locate the transaction.\n\nIn some cases, the refund may not appear directly in the main transaction list of the user’s bank statement. The user should be advised to also check the “Scheduled payments” or “Pending transactions” sections of their statement.\n\nPlease note that partial refunds may be reflected as an adjusted transaction amount rather than a separate refund entry. For example, if a ride cost 100 ZAR and a 19 ZAR refund was issued, the transaction may appear as 81 ZAR on the bank statement.\n\nIf the user still reports that the refund has not been received, please ask them to provide a bank statement covering the period from 9th of December to the present. The statement must clearly show the account holder’s name, account details, and the bank name or logo.\n\nOnce this information is received, the Customer Payments team will be able to investigate further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nMarten","2026-01-16T10:55:04.636Z"],["3815412","PFI-832963","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment allocated https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75602972 ","2026-01-16T10:55:04.880Z"],["3815414","PAW-14943","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T10:55:48.200Z"],["3815416","WEB-8063","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] \n\nCould you please check my last comment here below before I go ahead and close the ticket. Thanks! ","2026-01-16T10:56:09.742Z"],["3815417","PFI-829700","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Closing this as it’s expected to continue in the tech ticket. I’ll likely get notified of their reply. In case I don’t, and it’s still somehow a fraud issue, please ping me here 🙂 ","2026-01-16T10:56:20.129Z"],["3815419","LSS-59952","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hey Team! Could you confirm if the reply below was sent? Thank you!","2026-01-16T10:56:26.625Z"],["3815422","LSS-60403","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], apologies for the delayed response.\n\nTo respond to your question: can we send the following information: {color:#ff5630}Invoices issued by Bolt Operations OU, in the name and on behalf of each EVTC number, for the period from 1 to 30 September 2025.{color}\n\n\nWithout additional information from the requesting authority on why they want this information, it would be disproportionate to share invoices that contain rider personal data. If we can get clarity on why they need the invoices or what information they are seeking from it, we may be able to help without divulging rider data. \n\nKindly could you respond to the requestor with the following response?\n\n\n\n{quote}Bonjour Madame,\n\nConcernant votre demande relative à la facturation émise par la société Bolt Operations OÜ « au nom et pour le compte » de chaque EVTC mentionné, nous souhaitons attirer votre attention sur le fait que ces factures contiennent des données à caractère personnel de passagers (notamment noms, adresses de départ/arrivée), protégées par le RGPD.\n\nAfin de garantir une transmission conforme aux exigences de la réglementation en matière de protection des données personnelles, nous vous serions reconnaissants de bien vouloir préciser :\n\n* Quels éléments spécifiques de ces factures vous souhaitez obtenir ;\n\n* L’objectif poursuivi par cette demande, afin d’évaluer si une transmission partielle ou anonymisée pourrait répondre à vos besoins.\n\nNous restons bien entendu pleinement disponibles pour coopérer dans le respect des obligations légales qui nous incombent.{quote}\n\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions before sending and can you confirm once this has been sent? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-16T10:57:11.964Z"],["3815425","WEB-7610","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] Thanks for the prompt reply! I’ll close the ticket then, thanks! ","2026-01-16T10:57:22.343Z"],["3815426","HS-29017","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.57.15.png|width=200,height=200!","2026-01-16T10:57:25.157Z"],["3815428","CNT-339","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:610a6c97ec92ab0070d4d852] The carousel is ready, the deadline for copy review is Monday. 🙂  [^bolt-hq_carousel.pdf] ","2026-01-16T10:58:18.113Z"],["3815430","DELIVERY-1159","DELIVERY","sergey.lapin@bolt.eu","Sergey Lapin","26W3: created an A/B test doc draft for already existing implementation based on priority assignment bucket for already prepared orders. Finalizing final details of the launch.\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BF/pages/7375650817/WIP+EXP+-+2026.01+Introduce+priority+bucket+for+prepared+orders+in+Matrix+Dispatch+to+tackle+starvation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BF/pages/7375650817/WIP+EXP+-+2026.01+Introduce+priority+bucket+for+prepared+orders+in+Matrix+Dispatch+to+tackle+starvation|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T10:58:30.463Z"],["3815432","RLONE-93","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","[~accountid:712020:6615e403-65ac-4a5f-8afe-afb4d81cac6c] When youre back, please revise the project deadline","2026-01-16T10:58:45.962Z"],["3815433","CEBF-1700","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] ready to code review\n[https://github.com/bolteu/sf-bolt-food/pull/631|https://github.com/bolteu/sf-bolt-food/pull/631]","2026-01-16T10:58:46.895Z"],["3815434","LSS-61526","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343669|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343669|smart-link]  ","2026-01-16T10:58:47.567Z"],["3815438","CNT-339","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] woohoo, thanks! ","2026-01-16T10:59:43.719Z"],["3815439","LSS-61695","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:7257ab62-a7ae-4da0-8457-6957af214bd5] hey do you need this for both of our companies or only one? And it is only for Ukrpost?\n\nAlso do you have a previous ticket for PoA or previous draft PoA for this person?","2026-01-16T11:00:19.778Z"],["3815440","DELIVERY-343","DELIVERY","mihai.jugariu@bolt.eu","Mihai Jugariu","26W03: Added the possibility to use configure different batch allowed delays in control vs treatment when running an AB test","2026-01-16T11:00:47.530Z"],["3815441","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[@kewei.shang|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5dfb984e9a14250cb69f1697] my meeting has just finished.. are you free now?","2026-01-16T11:00:53.079Z"],["3815442","LSS-61403","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:6052892160d39e006f72f166] - so just to be clear on the request here - representatives specifically of *_Rounded_* will be visiting Bolt’s French premises? If so, then what is the purpose of the visit? What will you be discussing / showing them / sharing with them? Just so that I am fully aware of the context.\n\nSubject to the above, here are my thoughts:\n\n* Please note that I will not be able to review the NDA, as I only cover privacy topics (i.e. sharing of personal data and not company data). So for NDA review, please liaise with Regional Legal.\n* The DPA that we entered with Round will *not* cover the on-site visits, although this is not necessarily a major issue. We push for data processing/sharing agreements where there is systematic/ongoing sharing of personal data - if the present scenarios is limited to a few one-off visits with no systems access, then *we will not need to enter into any additional privacy agreements for the on-site visits* (particularly given that the visits are early next week).\n* Instead, the focus from a privacy POV should *minimising the risk of unauthorised disclosures of personal data* to the partner while they are visiting. In practical terms, this means:\n** Avoid taking the partner anywhere where computer screens / whiteboards are clearly visible, or where loud calls can clearly be heard (if possible).\n** Do not allow the partner to take photos or videos, and limit any documents that the partner sees to what is strictly necessary.\n** As you have already mentioned, do not grant the partner access to any Bolt systems.\n\nIf you have any questions then let me know 🙂 ","2026-01-16T11:01:06.121Z"],["3815443","PFI-832857","PFI","jakub.pekar@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Pekar","local ops changed vat registration","2026-01-16T11:01:25.641Z"],["3815444","CNT-459","CNT","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","cc: [~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] ","2026-01-16T11:01:37.691Z"],["3815449","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","I will join too.","2026-01-16T11:02:41.725Z"],["3815451","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","Yes","2026-01-16T11:03:09.556Z"],["3815453","PFI-831583","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Asking for a double refund to reverse the payment. \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768561381864?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768561381864?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-16T11:03:14.385Z"],["3815456","FPD-1534","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","This week findings:\n\n* ingestion into data lake from s3 seems to be possible\n* for testing it out, I’ve decided to reuse the s3 bucket {{presto-ingestion}} that has already been configured previously for the ingestion of sensitive data from v3\n* I created a PR that configures the ingestion for 3 types of tables as a starting point (cycle metadata, city dataset metadata, forecast metrics): [https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/pull/4687|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/pull/4687|smart-link] \n* and I’ve put some sample data into the respective s3 bucket folders to see whether the ingestion would be successful\n* hive partitioning does not seem to be a feature, so we will need to write the metadata that we want to have ourselves\n\nNext steps:\n\n* check whether the ingestion is successful\n* change our code so that we could write the data to be ingested to s3 easily ","2026-01-16T11:03:48.713Z"],["3815459","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","[@kewei.shang|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5dfb984e9a14250cb69f1697] will you start the meeting?","2026-01-16T11:04:05.347Z"],["3815460","PAW-14942","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-alex-somai\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160977\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 11:04:11 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T11:04:11.948Z"],["3815461","LSS-60229","LSS","dustin.williams@bolt.eu","Dustin Williams","yes thanks","2026-01-16T11:04:20.222Z"],["3815462","RLONE-799","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","[~accountid:712020:228a835c-834d-4ca5-b7c2-ebedb4eb0356] remember to fill in the project details. Minimum requirement is: Team, duedate and start date and assignee (done).\n\nSuggestion to add the KAM meetings with specific fleets and assignee as a task. Assignees will receive notifications of this to ensure that they follow up on the task. \n\nSame thing applies: need project details. Should we create a “KAM” swimlane in Kanban? ","2026-01-16T11:04:28.985Z"],["3815463","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","[https://bolt.zoom.us/j/97750862833?pwd=5TRjEaol3GQof9UOxnqrO0aFv8Teda.1|https://bolt.zoom.us/j/97750862833?pwd=5TRjEaol3GQof9UOxnqrO0aFv8Teda.1]","2026-01-16T11:04:46.525Z"],["3815468","PFI-834038","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Quick note on the company Tier. Based on the, [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/9181?qid=cpDejHCKKaaKBr93BG4dMn&toggle=fil|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/9181?qid=cpDejHCKKaaKBr93BG4dMn&toggle=fil], the company is T3. Please, try to select the correct Tier going forward.","2026-01-16T11:05:35.309Z"],["3815470","PFI-832832","PFI","kati.pruel@bolt.eu","Kati Pruel","Ok, let’s do it. Please send bank details.","2026-01-16T11:06:08.696Z"],["3815471","LSS-61669","LSS","manuel.ortiz@bolt.eu","Manuel Ortiz","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] \n\nHere you can find the agreement.\n\nThanks for your help! M\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FSqUTEP6E9p0lfeLJk9pYGenSHj_dnysJV6LM3cI2zU/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FSqUTEP6E9p0lfeLJk9pYGenSHj_dnysJV6LM3cI2zU/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\n","2026-01-16T11:06:11.569Z"],["3815472","PFI-822496","PFI","darja.rojenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Darja Rojenko","issue solved ","2026-01-16T11:06:26.918Z"],["3815474","PFI-834166","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","[^UA_Manual payout template - 16.01.26.csv]","2026-01-16T11:06:40.982Z"],["3815477","LSS-61406","LSS","andrei.ivanov@bolt.eu","Andrei Ivanov","Hey Ankita, \nThanks for looking into it:\n1. No, the same type of data will be used\n2. We will have the same limitations as now (e.g we currently don’t provide access to country data for ppl from another country local team, central teams have global access) \n3. Yes, we assess 20 credits to be spend in 2026, however to be safe we agreed with Fox on the 2 year time period \n4. This will be done by my team and agreed directly with FoxInt ","2026-01-16T11:07:00.207Z"],["3815478","RLONE-809","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","[~accountid:712020:f4c2d3fc-5a3b-493c-a126-72ab71bb7717] Terningkast 6 på input i epic og tasks! \nKeep it up 😄 ","2026-01-16T11:07:04.698Z"],["3815480","WD-22415","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] , closing as per our conversation. 🙂 ","2026-01-16T11:08:02.636Z"],["3815481","PFI-831576","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nSorry for the late reply! \n\nThe negative balance of 17.42 EUR is coming from these two payments. Bolt was not able to capture the full amount for the Micromobility orders. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/2351321779|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/2351321779] 21 Apr 2024, 16:27:42 (UTC+01:00)\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/2351350933|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/2351350933] 21 Apr 2024, 16:27:59 (UTC+01:00)\n\n\n!image-20260116-110737.png|width=1354,height=267!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T11:08:38.661Z"],["3815482","CNT-459","CNT","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] I will check next week and finalise everything in one doc leaving the content examples for each page as well. \n\nThank you, Aleks!","2026-01-16T11:09:14.374Z"],["3815485","WEB-7675","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] [~accountid:64009ca94307e46ad144aee7] \n\nI asked the Content team to review the Driver page content for reclassification risk, to avoid a repeat of what happened with the Safety page redesign. Kyrylo put together [this file|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Na2WIc85PT22Y_QG0JVnJdwemaaWSKgzLvgiECH6UeI/edit?tab=t.ludliv7n23vu], and since all comments are purely editorial, would it be possible to still factor them in? Hoping this won’t significantly impact the localisation timeline.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:f0f7cc2d-5968-45e9-91ec-ea445d725066] ","2026-01-16T11:09:34.131Z"],["3815486","BRE-1225","BRE","mariia.bukhanska@bolt.eu","Mariia Bukhanska","payment_instrument_id was manually updated. The initial cause will be investigated shortly","2026-01-16T11:09:43.468Z"],["3815487","RLONE-790","RLONE","christian.johannessen@bolt.eu","Christian Ingdal Johannessen","[~accountid:5f689921f0d401007029c6b0] *For the sake of learning and activation:* Could you please add one or two tasks for quarterly business review? \nRemember to input the task details required: \n- Team\n- Duedate\n- Start date\n- Assignee \n- Priority\n- labels (optional) \n","2026-01-16T11:10:04.357Z"],["3815489","PFI-832470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Regarding the Change Trail, please, use the Admin Change Log: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start_time\"%3A1768428000}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_time%22%3A1768428000%7D%7D]\n\nOn the reissue side, please, provide a list of invoices to reissue, and I will create a task to engineering with that. The future invoices are gonna be issued correctly","2026-01-16T11:10:55.583Z"],["3815492","MTE-929","MTE","sergei.drondin@bolt.eu","Sergei Drondin","Removed deprecated Clevertap and Segment secrets","2026-01-16T11:11:20.291Z"],["3815493","RS-1948","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hi [~accountid:712020:88708e1d-c334-4279-9692-ef3f2432966b] ,\n\nCan you please assist with determining whether we have an obligation to report such statistics? The official letter is attached to the ticket🙏 ","2026-01-16T11:11:34.725Z"],["3815494","WEB-9824","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] ! \n\nHere are the editorial comments for the Merchant page, in case it’s possible to factor them into the current phase. They also cover the Couriers page, but I couldn’t find the Phase 1 ticket for that if Elina is working on that already. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Na2WIc85PT22Y_QG0JVnJdwemaaWSKgzLvgiECH6UeI/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Na2WIc85PT22Y_QG0JVnJdwemaaWSKgzLvgiECH6UeI/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T11:11:46.945Z"],["3815497","DELIVERY-1154","DELIVERY","andrei.pit-rada@bolt.eu","Ioan-Andrei Piț-Rada","26W03: Started implementation the Courier App UI. Finishing up the components behaviour and then the backend integration for a new ABTest to control the feature.","2026-01-16T11:12:56.464Z"],["3815498","WEB-7675","WEB","krister.looga@bolt.eu","Krister Looga","I will update it in CMS and push it to translation [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] ","2026-01-16T11:14:03.597Z"],["3815499","PFI-831545","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI have checked the refund status and I could not locate any refunds to the Bolt Balance. \nCould you please issue the refund again? \n\nIf you are having any issues with the BB refund then could you please escalate to the technical support teams. \n\nUnfortunately, I’m not able to advise further as the customer payments team doesn’t have access to issue refunds to BB. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T11:14:09.053Z"],["3815506","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:c94f2cba-c25e-4b00-8ef4-2cad9045ee22] ,\n\nJust a gentle reminder regarding this.\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-16T11:15:46.352Z"],["3815508","FPD-1546","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Started a deck of slides:\n\n [https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1vXWOdxm73Xw_AvG2muLm0nTegWk22VYpnpgkdJFKlJE/edit?slide=id.g3b814e2c4e5_0_137#slide=id.g3b814e2c4e5_0_137|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1vXWOdxm73Xw_AvG2muLm0nTegWk22VYpnpgkdJFKlJE/edit?slide=id.g3b814e2c4e5_0_137#slide=id.g3b814e2c4e5_0_137|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T11:16:40.438Z"],["3815509","PFI-831470","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for RON 60.88 on Nov 17, 2025, 21:53:06 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505321004779902224 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 17th of November until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n\n[^Refund_Letter_PNX2HSDHMS43XVW3_VJZBWQMDVBCH44Z3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T11:16:46.148Z"],["3815513","PFI-831464","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for NOK 99.01 on Dec 10, 2025, 22:08:58 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505344001469819059 to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 10th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_XDNZ9QZM2LZ6NXG6_WDZDBPSNZ3VRPDX3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T11:18:24.272Z"],["3815515","PFI-831504","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Closing the ticket now. Once we receive confirmation or unblock from Safety, please ping me here and I’ll assist further if needed.","2026-01-16T11:19:12.987Z"],["3815516","LSS-61635","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:5fa511639e35e50068b366f0] and [~accountid:712020:4e0187e4-1d10-4ecf-a2d9-b182190f90fd]. Apologies, but I don’t see any document attached to this ticket.\n\nAnyway, if this is a template from the client, before sending this for legal review, the first option should always try to push back on client templates and use [our own Bolt template|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VAlZh7RAF6J3-9OjhIOOJ8xrdaCLw_xBHcnx8rZNaU0/template/preview]. ","2026-01-16T11:19:21.985Z"],["3815518","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","{noformat}Immutable tables:\n\"taxify_payment.notification\": 16TB, `created` column only, it is indexed\n\"taxify_payment.payment_request_log\": 7TB, `created` column only, it is indexed\n\nMutable tables:\n\"taxify_payment.payment\": 1TB, `last_update` column only, it is indexed\n\"taxify_payment.payment_order\": 505GB, `last_update` column only, it is indexed\n\"taxify_payment.payment_row\": 1TB, `last_update` column only, it is indexed{noformat}","2026-01-16T11:19:55.344Z"],["3815520","PFI-832459","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, please ping me here once this is done, and we’ll assist further. Closing the ticket now 🙂 ","2026-01-16T11:21:33.852Z"],["3815524","CEBF-1590","CEBF","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","[~accountid:712020:fc274657-f7b5-4366-9f2d-5ec68865cf48] please see the attached.\n\nSIM card section is corret.\n\nDevice section, to remove the following: “/device / Συσκευή”\n\n!image-20260102-083855 (dce1504d-2528-4420-834b-70b3b86c1d5e).png|width=790,alt=\"image-20260102-083855.png\"!","2026-01-16T11:22:25.716Z"],["3815525","BP-5430","BP","abhishek.gupta@bolt.eu","Abhishek Gupta","Check with PINT, why do we get this for business-portal as it seems like valid use-case. ","2026-01-16T11:22:33.684Z"],["3815526","PFI-831462","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T11:22:42.861Z"],["3815527","PFI-831451","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T11:23:07.456Z"],["3815528","PFI-832881","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","161941.50 TZS [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/74220358|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/74220358]\nCould not locate payment 1,169,428.00 TZS [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] would you be able to check on this. ","2026-01-16T11:23:22.685Z"],["3815531","LSS-61635","LSS","salvador.furtado@bolt.eu","Salvador de Almeida Campos Furtado","Hey [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] I included the [link |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NyR5rm9L7rZ4bos9SRuMzB_BtiVuv4Pg/edit]to the document, since it was giving an error every time I tried to upload it. I tried to push the client to use our NDA, but on their side I encountered a lot of resistance.\n\n","2026-01-16T11:24:14.536Z"],["3815532","FRAUD-5400","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","*DB access requested*\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/backend-credentials/authorizations/edit/342561|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/backend-credentials/authorizations/edit/342561]","2026-01-16T11:24:35.981Z"],["3815534","HS-29024","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No action from People Ops.","2026-01-16T11:25:07.246Z"],["3815537","CLOUDSEC-730","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-16T11:25:30.776Z"],["3815538","CLOUDSEC-730","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-16T11:25:31.954Z"],["3815539","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Preliminary estimation of the flap length is 180 mm.\n\nNext steps:\n\n# Create a rapid prototype to test a sheet rubber stamped version.\n# Conduct a splash test to check if it stops splashes.\n# Perform a riding test to:\n## Ensure safety:\n##* Too flexible material may get stuck between the tire and the upper part of the flap.\n## Check for noise:\n##* Too flexible material may touch the tire and produce noise.\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"bbd2a93d-dbdf-4a89-b968-d1abafb6561b\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Identical length in fornt and rear\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Flap L: \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"127mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Tip clearence from the ground: \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"100mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Identical length in fornt and rear\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Flap L: \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"179mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Clearence from the ground: \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"50mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":223,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-110919.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-110919.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":711,\"width\":711}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":297,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-110309.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-110309.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":711,\"width\":711}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":223,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-111312.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-111312.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":711,\"width\":711}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":218,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260116-112458.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260116-112458.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":711,\"width\":711}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-16T11:25:35.170Z"],["3815542","PFI-831441","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for providing the users bank statement. \n\nThe refund is reflecting in the bank statement. The users bank has subtracted the refund from the captured amount. \nCaptured 308 ZAR\nRefund 180.23 ZAR\n\nBank statement shows 308 ZAR - 180.23 ZAR = 127.77 ZAR\n\n\n!image-20260116-112505.png|width=993,height=68!\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T11:26:07.940Z"],["3815545","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","You can track the progress of the backfill [here|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/ed32d69b-37d0-487d-9c19-e6012161161c/datalake-backfilling?orgId=1].","2026-01-16T11:26:13.383Z"],["3815546","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","I will keep an eye on this.","2026-01-16T11:26:21.906Z"],["3815547","BRE-1212","BRE","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","Presently, the task doesn’t make sense to me and is not worth investing time in it. However, I still sparked the discussion [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C091T5BQHPU/p1768562731477949] to confirm my understanding","2026-01-16T11:26:29.250Z"],["3815549","DELIVERY-614","DELIVERY","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","26W2: [Experiment|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GBM/pages/6833111045/Delivery+Parking+Detection+at+Provider+AB+Test+with+Annotated+Parking+Locations] finished.  Metrics went down a bit, no statsig \n\nSharing an update on the results of our parking at provider with annotated parking locations test, which are available [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GBM/pages/6833111045/Delivery+Parking+Detection+at+Provider+AB+Test+with+Annotated+Parking+Locations]. As a refresher, we tested explicit parking guidance (routing couriers to suggested parking + UI changes in courier app telling couriers they are being guided to a parking spot) to reduce last-mile pickup time for car couriers. *Even with manually curated parking spots*, the experiment showed *no* *statsig* *improvement*; in fact, most last-mile metrics *slightly worsened* in treatment. Quick sanity checks suggest couriers did follow the parking guidance, so it looks like the feature had adoption.*Key takeaway:* parking suitability is highly contextual, and “better” parking often increases walking distance (which has a negative impact on last-mile efficiency metrics). Future iterations should focus on collecting courier/provider input for parking suggestions, or other metrics beyond last-mile duration to assess courier last-mile experience.","2026-01-16T11:26:46.735Z"],["3815552","CEBF-1590","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] Thank you. FYA: [~accountid:712020:ed2533e0-41fa-49c6-9812-aa965d995be0] ","2026-01-16T11:27:16.741Z"],["3815553","PFI-834130","PFI","nuno.fontoura@bolt.eu","Nuno Fontoura","To provide further context: Our Frankfurt operations are limited to a single fleet with only one active Mercedes S-Class which is the only eligible vehicle to operate on 'Chauffeur First Class' category. Furthermore, this vehicle is driven exclusively by only two drivers.\n\nBecause this is our premium and most expensive offering, transaction volume is naturally low. Given these highly specific operational constraints, we believe the current activity may be triggering false positives. Is it possible to adjust Chauffeur profiles or whitelist these specific Chauffeurs to prevent future automatic blocks?","2026-01-16T11:27:21.886Z"],["3815555","PFI-834118","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] These errors should display a “Fraud:…“ when it’s fraud-related. Please follow the KB [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003841794?country=global&language=en].\n\n*_account_has_active_restrictions_*\n_An active restriction is a 48-hour restriction placed on the user’s account to prevent account phishing when a login via a new device is detected. This restriction temporarily prevents the user from deleting their account._","2026-01-16T11:27:34.919Z"],["3815556","HS-29025","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No action, fixed term.","2026-01-16T11:27:36.448Z"],["3815557","LSS-50863","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] \nMany thanks for your patience herein! \nI’ve requested access to the meeting notes you shared. \n\nIn the meantime, since a lot of time has passed since the ticket was created, could you please confirm if we have proceeded with the partner on any basis (e.g. without a contract)? Or did we put this on hold until the agreement could get signed? \n\nMany thanks.\nVeera ","2026-01-16T11:27:44.900Z"],["3815558","RDS-1313","RDS","karina.gorodnitskaia@bolt.eu","Karina Gorodnitskaia","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Yes, as Andreas said, is’t not a bug, just a copy update","2026-01-16T11:27:56.969Z"],["3815559","DPX-3560","DPX","mihai.burlaciuc@bolt.eu","Mihai Burlăciuc","Question about how to get A/B test provider ids after rollout: [slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CMET7BK2S/p1768562827836719]","2026-01-16T11:28:08.321Z"],["3815560","LSS-54977","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[https://www.kmu.gov.ua/news/uriad-zaprovadzhuie-reiestr-saitiv-prodavtsiv-pidaktsyznykh-tovariv-krok-do-prozoroho-rynku-ta-zakhystu-spozhyvachiv|https://www.kmu.gov.ua/news/uriad-zaprovadzhuie-reiestr-saitiv-prodavtsiv-pidaktsyznykh-tovariv-krok-do-prozoroho-rynku-ta-zakhystu-spozhyvachiv|smart-link] \n\n[https://thepharma.media/uk/business/36936-novi-pravila-e-torgivli-likarskimi-zasobami-yakix-zmin-cekati-06012025|https://thepharma.media/uk/business/36936-novi-pravila-e-torgivli-likarskimi-zasobami-yakix-zmin-cekati-06012025|smart-link] \n\n[https://forbes.ua/news/kabmin-dopratsyue-postanovu-yaka-dozvolyae-prodavati-liki-onlayn-lishe-cherez-vebsayti-diyuchikh-aptek-30052024-21477?utm_source=chatgpt.com|https://forbes.ua/news/kabmin-dopratsyue-postanovu-yaka-dozvolyae-prodavati-liki-onlayn-lishe-cherez-vebsayti-diyuchikh-aptek-30052024-21477?utm_source=chatgpt.com]","2026-01-16T11:28:27.582Z"],["3815564","LSS-61704","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^Bank confirmation letter Citibank Inc (Bolt Operations Ukraine).docx] _(2.79 MB)_","2026-01-16T11:29:06.718Z"],["3815565","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Thank you both for lesson on creating backfills. I will pass on this to rest of DBRE team. :thank_you:","2026-01-16T11:29:08.785Z"],["3815566","LSS-53880","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] Yes, close the ticket, because there was no follow up from the user.\n\n{quote}but we are talking about injury damages not disability. Is this rider disabled because of this accident?{quote}\n\nInjury damages are not covered by our insurance, unless the user is at least 15% permanently disabled due to the accident. User was not permanently disabled as previously mentioned.","2026-01-16T11:29:16.497Z"],["3815568","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* (1) email from John to Bee, (2) email from myself to Isaac (Voi legal).\n\n[^Bolt Mail -Voi Liverpool Warehouse.pdf]\n[^Bolt Mail - Bolt - Liverpool Scooter Operations Unit 9 Phoenix Park [IMAN-WSLIVE.FID5498717].pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T11:29:40.181Z"],["3815569","LSS-61705","LSS","sian.dvorkin@bolt.eu","Sian Dvorkin","[^Steer Bolt-Hopp BC Regulatory Approval Analysis_Terms_17Dec2025_HHsigned v2.pdf] _(1.21 MB)_","2026-01-16T11:29:40.860Z"],["3815570","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* Meeting with DAP to learn how to create backfills\n* Backfill requests created\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.28.21.png|width=1096,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 11.28.21.png\"!","2026-01-16T11:29:49.999Z"],["3815572","LSS-61421","LSS","bayram.khalilzade@bolt.eu","Bayram Khalilzade","The remaining 45 cars will stay on the CF Somda fleet and be operated by the fleet owner. [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] \n\n","2026-01-16T11:30:13.637Z"],["3815574","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","The status in admin panel will switch to {{Completed}} once the backfill of the data lake is done.\n\nAlso, some TiDB/MySQL tables are ingested into 2 data lake tables. E.g. {{ng_pii.payment_notification}} and {{ng_public.payment_notification}}, this is because PII columns need to be isolated into a separate physical PII table. In such case, you see 2 items in the backfill list in the admin panel.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8PSGM31V/screenshot_2026-01-16_at_13.29.14.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8PSGM31V/screenshot_2026-01-16_at_13.29.14.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T11:31:02.479Z"],["3815577","DPLC-696","DPLC","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","We want to try the easiest immediate solution first.\n\nWrite a script that periodically tries to load based on history, with a load time longer than 60 seconds. This immediate solution determines whether the cache can improve query performance.\n\n[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/system__activity/history?qid=KC5UUnnZcHZamJVBYjMlLE&toggle=fil|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/system__activity/history?qid=KC5UUnnZcHZamJVBYjMlLE&toggle=fil]\n\nIf it succeeds, we can separate the warehouse for p0 dashboards and warm it up regularly based on history. It needs a dashboard change, LookML change, and query history, so I need help from *group-S05FGH5B82W*","2026-01-16T11:31:27.841Z"],["3815580","DPLC-696","DPLC",null,"Slack","[Gazandi Cahyadarma|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:061a9010-0948-45f3-81ba-d6d4ba88b4bf] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05HAD1SLDD/p1768493847531919?thread_ts=1768476067.547609&cid=C05HAD1SLDD|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05HAD1SLDD/p1768493847531919?thread_ts=1768476067.547609&cid=C05HAD1SLDD|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T11:31:30.201Z"],["3815581","LSS-61706","LSS","anais.jourdain@bolt.eu","Anaïs Jourdain","[^Memento Fiscal BOUDIER MARTIN.pdf] _(652 kB)_","2026-01-16T11:31:30.450Z"],["3815583","RDS-1315","RDS","karina.gorodnitskaia@bolt.eu","Karina Gorodnitskaia","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Yes, as far as I remember. [~accountid:5d428c9176cb3e0d9d3200df] We’ve discussed that before, could you please confirm?","2026-01-16T11:31:32.650Z"],["3815585","LSS-61706","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nAnaïs Jourdain has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-16T11:31:33.390Z"],["3815586","LSS-61706","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T11:31:41.007Z"],["3815588","PFI-833811","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please reach out to the campaigns team for this. Thanks! ","2026-01-16T11:32:17.136Z"],["3815589","PFI-833811","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team!  🍔\n\n- Provider/Courier payment didn't reflect in their balance: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/503\n- Provider/Courier didn't receive payout: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/319\n- Eater had issues with the payment: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/316\n- Early cashout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/556\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/317\n- App and backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76\n- Balance and Invoices issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/318\n- Invoice Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T11:32:23.761Z"],["3815595","LSS-61707","LSS","bruno.pereira@bolt.eu","Bruno dos Reis Pereira","[^processo 147 2026 BOLT.docx.docx] _(116 kB)_\n\n[^BoltFood_Complain2.pdf.pdf] _(79 kB)_\n\n[^BoltFood_Complain.pdf.pdf] _(37 kB)_\n\n[^Translation.pdf] _(70 kB)_","2026-01-16T11:33:35.304Z"],["3815596","LSS-61707","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nBruno dos Reis Pereira has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-16T11:33:36.908Z"],["3815597","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","BTW, maybe DBRE team can get approval access, in case of emergency backfill during the night. Then we don’t need to wait on DAP to approve during regular biz hours.","2026-01-16T11:34:26.488Z"],["3815599","BP-8368","BP","abhishek.gupta@bolt.eu","Abhishek Gupta","TODO: Check what is required (if anything) to completely move to the new openapi based client generators.","2026-01-16T11:34:44.527Z"],["3815600","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","To me it makes sense, we will discuss it internally.","2026-01-16T11:34:51.444Z"],["3815605","PFI-834125","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, did a quick check, the driver seems to be doing legitimate orders with good payments. I’ll ping the respective analyst to have a look as to why this is over-triggering. You may compensate the lost amounts.\nThanks!","2026-01-16T11:35:23.270Z"],["3815606","PFI-834132","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hey, the sum seems to be matching this [service fee invoice |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5989403477?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]. Unfortunately billing is not able to help with the card error, for this you should reach out to customer payments team.","2026-01-16T11:35:31.044Z"],["3815608","BD-1960","BD","rafael.barros@bolt.eu","Rafael Adson Barbosa Barros","The problem is that in this [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/2646c38917945ccc0024cdc32219d925e1dc9176/src/delivery/commerce/delivery_invoicing/main/handler/service/processor/RecordPostProcessor.ts#L17-L52|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/2646c38917945ccc0024cdc32219d925e1dc9176/src/delivery/commerce/delivery_invoicing/main/handler/service/processor/RecordPostProcessor.ts#L17-L52] \n\nWe use {{DEFAULT_PAYMENT_ROUNDING_PRECISION}} instead of {{DEFAULT_RECORD_ROUNDING_PRECISION}} to calculate the precision of the vat_sums of the record.\n\nBecause this is precision 2, the vat sums are being generated in the wrong manner.\n\nWill confirm why we made this decision, but either way, the record will have to be credited & reissued.","2026-01-16T11:36:14.526Z"],["3815609","SREDESK-7429","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_delivery_basket_replacement;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.530s\n\n\nroot@ti-delivery-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_delivery_basket_replacement;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.512s{noformat}","2026-01-16T11:36:24.003Z"],["3815616","HS-29017","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi Shaikh,\n\nThank you for the updated certificate!\nI forwarded the information to the Health Insurance Fund. I will approve your sick leave request in Workday once they will open the leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee].\nHave a great weekend!\n\nKind regards,\nAike-Maris","2026-01-16T11:38:25.638Z"],["3815617","SREDESK-7428","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_beehive_queue_statistics;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.519s\n\n\nroot@gamma-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_beehive_queue_statistics;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.069s{noformat}","2026-01-16T11:38:31.705Z"],["3815618","L10N-28290","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28289](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28289)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T11:38:39.411Z"],["3815619","L10N-28294","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28289](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28289)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T11:38:40.186Z"],["3815620","L10N-28292","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28289](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28289)\n\nThanks for co