01-16T11:38:53.537Z"],["3815626","L10N-28308","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28289](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28289)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T11:38:53.590Z"],["3815627","L10N-28313","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28289](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28289)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T11:38:55.931Z"],["3815628","L10N-28311","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28289](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28289)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T11:38:55.945Z"],["3815629","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","I've created a follow jira ticket for DAP [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ING-646|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ING-646|smart-link]","2026-01-16T11:38:56.546Z"],["3815630","PFI-833282","PFI","wisdom.salaou@bolt-outsource.eu","Wisdom Delphine Salaou","Hello, the payment has been made, but it is incomplete. We would therefore like to have more details please\n\n","2026-01-16T11:39:11.022Z"],["3815631","FPD-1508","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Had a discussion with [~accountid:6274fd88d7fd480068da636a]  -  would need some extra developments by Engineering so that it would be possible to generate both ranges +/- 3pp and +/-25%","2026-01-16T11:39:16.790Z"],["3815632","LSS-61625","LSS","fernando.berzosa@bolt.eu","Fernando Berzosa","thanks [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] , they just sent me an email with the details of the Audiencia Telemática.\n\n[~accountid:712020:bd27ea39-912c-4d98-9fd7-247ac2e54ec6] do you know anything about this case/person?  \n\n!image-20260116-113849.png|width=889,height=439,alt=\"image-20260116-113849.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-16T11:39:39.896Z"],["3815634","FPD-1509","FPD","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Had a discussion with [~accountid:6274fd88d7fd480068da636a]  -  would need some extra developments by Engineering so that it would be possible to generate both few markets and all the market","2026-01-16T11:39:56.741Z"],["3815636","PFI-834039","PFI","sandra.davidsson@bolt.eu","Sandra Davidsson","Hello! 🙂 \n\nSorry for reopening this SD, but we have received additional reports of related accounts. After thoroughly checking the user relations, several connected accounts appear highly suspicious, even if they haven't all attempted to request refunds yet. Through the [*account reported here*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/294897516/overview], it’s connected to [*this other account*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/userRelations/176743336?] who have even more fraud connections, is it possible to proactively block all these linked accounts to prevent further abuse, rather than waiting for them to contact us? \n\n\n\nThis issue is not only incurring costs through fraudulent refunds and operational handling, but it is also negatively impacting our drivers. They are facing financial losses and unfair reports based on false accusations, leading to a loss of trust in the platform, [example here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/724461988].\n\n\n\nOn a more general note, if these cases should be escalated to OPS/Safety instead of Fraud, can we establish a process with them to decide on hardblocks? Since most of these cases end up with Tier 2, we want to know if we should bypass Fraud and go directly to OPS for future blocking decisions? \n\nLooking forward to your thoughts on this! ","2026-01-16T11:40:19.425Z"],["3815637","RS-1951","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] ,\n\nAs far as I understand, they want to obtain data because of the communication happend between the CS agent and a specific ride. I would suggest offering to support as an organization rather than an individual. CS represents Bolt and responds to everything as a face of the organization. This is not a individual level interaction.\n\nI’ll involve Regional Legal to get their POV. ","2026-01-16T11:40:27.785Z"],["3815638","PFI-832651","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Iza is correct, Novitus has also confirmed that this should be reported to their helpdesk by the fleet owner 🙂 ","2026-01-16T11:40:27.848Z"],["3815639","CEBF-1837","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:5da9bc599aebed0c29c2acb8] Please verify, task is completed.","2026-01-16T11:40:41.737Z"],["3815640","LSS-61625","LSS","fernando.berzosa@bolt.eu","Fernando Berzosa","just fyi, they send me the email from a gmail email.\n\n!image-20260116-114046.png|width=1247,height=404,alt=\"image-20260116-114046.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-16T11:40:49.428Z"],["3815641","CSXPR-70","CSXPR","justus.debruin@bolt.eu","Justus de Bruin","Competitor analysis: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FWZ79POD7daFUfE0GJ0QF6mX9piO2Fl-Ke1Yyh0HLMA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FWZ79POD7daFUfE0GJ0QF6mX9piO2Fl-Ke1Yyh0HLMA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T11:41:34.908Z"],["3815642","LSS-59671","LSS","klaudia.bochenko@bolt.eu","Klaudia Bochenko","Hi [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] is the current version of the draft is final and can be sent?","2026-01-16T11:41:37.020Z"],["3815644","PFI-831412","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T11:42:28.500Z"],["3815648","BR-4104","BR","temirlan.tursunov@bolt.eu","Temirlan Tursunov","\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160991|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160991|smart-card]","2026-01-16T11:43:17.375Z"],["3815650","LSS-61625","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","*Audiencia telemática en fecha 05/02/2026 a las 08:30hs*\n\nTema: EXP N°5064\nÚnase a la reunión de Zoom\n[https://us06web.zoom.us/j/83053218041?pwd=5DkAxpFJ2j0Z7sYbwaTR9vvo2DB5ah.1|https://us06web.zoom.us/j/83053218041?pwd=5DkAxpFJ2j0Z7sYbwaTR9vvo2DB5ah.1|smart-link] \n\nID de reunión: 830 5321 8041\nCódigo de acceso: 341640","2026-01-16T11:43:30.147Z"],["3815652","PFI-834165","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for 11.00 EUR on 03/11/2025, 17:31:27UTC\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 72700925307147551900623  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 3rd of November until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n[^Proof of Refund 03-11-2025.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T11:44:24.585Z"],["3815654","PFI-831411","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customers' order was cancelled before we managed to capture the payment. Since the there was no payment we are not able to refund them. \nThe customer might mean the authorization has not been released instead. \n\nI have checked the case and can confirm everything looks line on Bolts end. The authorization has been released. \nYou can advise the customer to confirm with their bank if the authorized funds have been released. The customers bank is able to locate the funds with the authorization date and amount. \n\nPlease also refer to this KB article \n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T11:44:54.718Z"],["3815656","RDS-1313","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:34206d98-4d0d-43ac-93e3-4a910bc0fe7e] This specific ticket is about the purple tooltip color, they should be black","2026-01-16T11:45:09.532Z"],["3815657","VULN-1459","VULN","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","Issue is verified to be true and is waiting for Development\n\n\n\nAccording to the [Remediation guidelines|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/3987112061/Application+Vulnerability+Management], a “High” priority finding timeline is as follows, by latest date:\n\n* *29.01.2026 -* Develop a remediation plan\n* *27.03.2026 -* Have the final fix ready\n* *30.03.2026 -* Fix is tested","2026-01-16T11:45:52.388Z"],["3815659","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c]  The following was not accepted by the airport “*_baggage takes a while, dinner does not.”_*\n\nCan you please provide an alternative?\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] ","2026-01-16T11:46:33.332Z"],["3815660","LSS-61707","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:5bf2989995a1f935f7db9e66] !\nCan you give me context and more details of this case? If the allegations are confirmed, what actually happened, if there are any interactions with CS, if we already took any measurements to compensate the client, etc.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T11:46:36.065Z"],["3815673","DSR-3783","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T11:49:00.084Z"],["3815675","PAW-14931","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @not-much-io\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160756\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 11:49:14 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T11:49:14.537Z"],["3815676","LSS-61288","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbef963c-e707-4042-8024-5afb4c08aa16] you may share with the Client for their comment and consideration\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wmpNaDf1zl0a2QPtRw4x9LlvdfzWUqvc4F4sf8pNuVQ/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wmpNaDf1zl0a2QPtRw4x9LlvdfzWUqvc4F4sf8pNuVQ/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T11:49:32.666Z"],["3815677","LSS-61708","LSS","robert.buzukasvili@bolt.eu","Robert Buzukašvili","[^Zmluva s BOLT_15.01.2026.pdf] _(62 kB)_","2026-01-16T11:49:41.229Z"],["3815678","LSS-61288","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Added to NG market late 2025: \n*Bolt Rentals – Category Overview*\n*Bolt Rentals* is a flexible mobility solution that allows individuals and businesses to book a vehicle with a driver for extended periods, rather than for single trips. This service is ideal for organizations that require reliable transportation for daily operations, meetings, inspections, or staff movement.\n*Key Features of Bolt Rentals*\n\n* *Hourly or Daily Bookings*\n Vehicles can be rented for a specified number of hours or for a full day, depending on operational needs.\n* *Dedicated Driver*\n Each rental comes with a professional Bolt driver assigned for the duration of the booking.\n* *Multiple Stops Allowed*\n Users can make several stops within the rental period without ending the trip.\n* *Cost Transparency*\n Pricing is based on time and distance, providing better cost control compared to multiple individual trips.\n* *Real-Time Tracking & Reporting*\n All trips are monitored via the Bolt platform, with access to detailed usage and expense reports.","2026-01-16T11:50:22.935Z"],["3815679","DO-5808","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Hi!\n\nAt Bolt, we use fivetran.com for 3rd party data ingestions - access is granted via Okta. I had a quick look, and it looks like there’s a Typeform source, so an ingestion can be set up. Please ask the IT team to get access, and you can experiment on your own. The “DeltaLake” is a destination of your interest. A guide can be found [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/2784234692/Fivetran+at+Bolt].\n\nIf, for any reason, the above does not work, you can maybe export the data to the CSV format? If so, then we can utilize the S3 ingestion to ingest it into the datalake. Another [guide|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4191224039/Data+Lake+S3+Ingestion+User+Manual].","2026-01-16T11:50:30.374Z"],["3815680","DO-5808","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Have a good day!","2026-01-16T11:50:39.938Z"],["3815681","CEBF-1833","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Cancelling, not a bug","2026-01-16T11:50:55.032Z"],["3815682","WFM-10021","WFM","nikita.bogomazovs@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikita Bogomazovs","Hey! Could you please set-up those queues permanently as a fallback? Thank you! ","2026-01-16T11:51:22.589Z"],["3815684","PFI-834187","PFI","pareena.klinkaewpa@bolt-outsource.eu","Pareena Klinkaewpa","!image-20260116-114823.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-115055.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-115106.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T11:52:29.820Z"],["3815685","HS-29028","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting on info on why shift work was removed.","2026-01-16T11:52:42.444Z"],["3815688","PFI-834189","PFI","filip.kieronczyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Filip Kieronczyk","[^Potwierdzenie realizacji.pdf]","2026-01-16T11:53:33.578Z"],["3815689","L10N-28317","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28314](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28314)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T11:53:40.798Z"],["3815690","L10N-28322","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language t