nt dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T11:56:07.128Z"],["3815710","HS-29030","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Background check consents sent out. ","2026-01-16T11:57:34.001Z"],["3815713","PFI-830905","PFI","wisdom.salaou@bolt-outsource.eu","Wisdom Delphine Salaou","Thank you, we look forward to hearing from you.","2026-01-16T11:57:59.684Z"],["3815714","RS-1951","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hi [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] , Can you please review the request and provide your POV","2026-01-16T11:58:05.212Z"],["3815715","CLOUDSEC-727","CLOUDSEC","iuliia.laaneots@bolt.eu","Iuliia Laaneots","Tested in the testing deployment on the Hive logs. \n\nThe manual can be found here:\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/7410352631/Troubleshooting+Mapping+Conflicts+Reindexing+Data|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/7410352631/Troubleshooting+Mapping+Conflicts+Reindexing+Data|smart-link] \n\nLast steps should be added. \n","2026-01-16T11:58:23.435Z"],["3815719","PFI-831400","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nMy apologies for a delayed response! \n\nI have checked the RRN codes the user provided and they are both related to the same payment. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4013748862|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4013748862]\n\nUnfortunately, we don’t see and charges for 3.48 AZN nor 3.62 AZN in our system. \nCould you please advise the user to reach out to their bank INTERNATIONAL BANK OF AZERBAIJAN to clarify why they were changed for an additional amount. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T11:59:11.718Z"],["3815720","FX-3651","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768564748159819]*{color}:\nYesterday I fixed these tests.\nPR: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160818]\n{quote}","2026-01-16T11:59:22.918Z"],["3815722","FX-3651","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768564774024789]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3651 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T11:59:45.665Z"],["3815724","PFI-834192","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260116-115556.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-115606.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T11:59:58.008Z"],["3815725","PFI-834038","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","I've checked in with the team to understand the implications and will get back to you straight away once I hear back! \n\nI selected the highest tier because they have a large collaboration on a country level, and this would need to be the top priorty to resolve.[ *Slack post* |https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02CUF8CFCZ/p1765990040743369]","2026-01-16T12:01:15.304Z"],["3815728","RDS-126","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* ios hopefully ready next week","2026-01-16T12:01:33.755Z"],["3815729","LSS-61709","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T12:01:54.163Z"],["3815730","RDS-128","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* a/b test saw no issues. small .5% gmv increase. not going to research further. will ship next week","2026-01-16T12:02:13.569Z"],["3815731","PFI-834193","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260116-120206.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-120216.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:03:08.628Z"],["3815733","CSXRT-101","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","Rides is planning to pick up the same idea, project lead Shady El Waziry, spoke with him and he would be happy to cooperate on this & push from both Verticals","2026-01-16T12:03:55.108Z"],["3815734","RDS-1107","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* [~accountid:712020:eb64fa24-b70d-49d6-b62c-e4560e7e1457] \n\n* b2g issue resolved. doing regression testing. some bugs discovered. fixing next week","2026-01-16T12:04:05.253Z"],["3815735","LSS-51524","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi guys! [~accountid:712020:f5c52198-9bb5-40b8-865d-70e96f6ccf5a] [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] you can find the outstanding issues in the EEA/UK Amendment listed [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1c7EassSzgrZcODFRS5A_pmJaddd06jWjv9o5BubXFxs/edit?usp=sharing]. I have tagged you in each relevant row so you can see what needs your attention and then write a note in this same table accordingly. Please check it. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T12:04:06.358Z"],["3815737","RDS-1223","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* In David’s hands. will take it after driver ratings work finished","2026-01-16T12:04:44.189Z"],["3815738","PFI-831399","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe user has not received the promised refund because it cannot be applied. \n\nThe refund cannot exceed the captured amount. \nUser paid 79.71 RON from their card and 2.67 RON from their Bolt balance. \nThe maximum you are able to issue to the OPM is 79.71 RON. \n\nIf you would like to issue a full refund then please issue a 79.71 RON refund to the OPM and 2.67 RON refund to the Bolt Balance. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T12:04:47.518Z"],["3815739","WD-22565","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] , can you please support with creating a Auditor Workday Account.\n[~accountid:712020:b73d65c1-8791-4157-9850-c426365a190b] reached out to the PeopleTech team and they said we can do it. I haven’t created an Auditor Account before. \n\n!image-20260116-120424.png|width=1021,alt=\"image-20260116-120424.png\"!","2026-01-16T12:04:55.703Z"],["3815740","WFM-10018","WFM","faith.ndinda@bolt-outsource.eu","Faith Ndinda","Hello [~accountid:712020:73528ba9-f129-4b0c-b65d-38a479119ccc],\n\nShe is a trainer, and she is being cross-utilized. Kindly don’t restrict access to other markets that she has been assigned. Kindly add just the DE Global English and DE Global Translation Queue for her to have access to the tickets and admin. ","2026-01-16T12:04:55.175Z"],["3815741","LSS-61493","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] - do you need any support with the ticket?\n\nThis was urgently escalated to me by [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] , but it appears you are working on this and is the assignee for the sub-ticket\n\nI am glad to help with any part where my specific competence is needed.\n\nCC [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] ","2026-01-16T12:05:02.322Z"],["3815744","WD-22565","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","!image-20260116-120510.png|width=602,alt=\"image-20260116-120510.png\"!","2026-01-16T12:05:13.164Z"],["3815748","PFI-834194","PFI","denisa.stepanova@bolt-outsource.eu","Denisa Stepanova","!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:06:05.470Z"],["3815749","RDS-636","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","[~accountid:712020:eb64fa24-b70d-49d6-b62c-e4560e7e1457] \n\n* some riderx bugs before going forward with a/b test\n* nothing needed from driverx side\n* not fixing price modification unless needed\n* employee testing ongoing","2026-01-16T12:06:25.895Z"],["3815751","PFI-834195","PFI","success.igbinosa@bolt-outsource.eu","Success Igbinosa","!2000.png|thumbnail!\n\n!5200.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:06:38.925Z"],["3815752","LSS-61526","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b63472c3-a177-45a8-b81f-2269d17e33ac], Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n [^MWG Drive GmbH - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T12:06:46.881Z"],["3815756","RDS-1248","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* don’t actually see any rider complaints yet\n* maybe some in Poland","2026-01-16T12:07:34.246Z"],["3815758","RDS-1332","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* no updates. still in discovery","2026-01-16T12:07:53.626Z"],["3815760","LSS-61695","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:7257ab62-a7ae-4da0-8457-6957af214bd5] I see the second [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/issue/LSS-61696] for TY Services LLC, will provide both PoAs here, but please revert on my other questions.","2026-01-16T12:08:25.366Z"],["3815763","PFI-834197","PFI","vania.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Vania Silva","[^Bolt Oficial.pdf (2).pdf]","2026-01-16T12:09:15.744Z"],["3815764","LSS-61408","LSS","lavinia-georgiana.ene@bolt.eu","Lavinia-Georgiana Ene","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], thank you! \nThis is the rider’s [ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/716800559], and yes, it was a lost item case. \n\n","2026-01-16T12:09:22.094Z"],["3815765","PFI-834198","PFI","linda.ragause@bolt-outsource.eu","Linda Ragause","!IMG_0096.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:09:50.071Z"],["3815766","PFI-834038","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Thanks for clarification; brought the priority back","2026-01-16T12:09:55.094Z"],["3815768","PIF-3285","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the User Story!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-16T12:10:03.039Z"],["3815769","LSS-59952","LSS","nisley.ciacareli@bolt.eu","Nisley Ciacareli","[~accountid:63dcee0028cddcc70772479d] [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] ","2026-01-16T12:10:13.224Z"],["3815770","PFI-833336","PFI","vania.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Vania Silva","Wrong team","2026-01-16T12:10:14.360Z"],["3815772","GRWA-1495","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Value Prop Dashboard has been [updated|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C1JQJKT5/p1768495258410139]","2026-01-16T12:10:35.223Z"],["3815773","PFI-829509","PFI","roman.igaz@bolt.eu","Roman Igaz","I only have access to the first link, but there is nothing to change - it is the default VAT setup, which is correct. So we either create new VAT tag or we simply hide the VAT column on the invoice for eater. [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] do you know who might have the superpower to do the latter? If not, you can close the ticket and we will keep digging. Thank you! 🙂 ","2026-01-16T12:10:36.572Z"],["3815774","DBRE-8706","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","Hey! I need some help with Alter Automation related logs (alter-agent, alter-supervisor, gh-ost - [https://monitor.boltint.net/dashboards/f/f4dbb039-adf0-45e1-8d73-540d0841a0f0/alter-automation|https://monitor.boltint.net/dashboards/f/f4dbb039-adf0-45e1-8d73-540d0841a0f0/alter-automation]).\n\nI noticed that logs don't work anymore, I haven't checked these dashboards in a few months, so I'm not sure when this stopped working.\n\n*@user-U036TM43CUV* as far as I know you've [set these up|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-4936], could you help here?","2026-01-16T12:10:55.241Z"],["3815775","DBRE-8706","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Andres Kepler|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6215e9ed2d1a9d0069952697] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02UNAPUCL9/p1768481370682089|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02UNAPUCL9/p1768481370682089|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T12:10:56.146Z"],["3815776","SCM-1116","SCM","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","[~accountid:712020:16f9a1bd-630a-44fc-acfd-57a270c13c42] The EB1 IOT repair ticket and List of items to order based on [~accountid:5fc10e1e2730d80076c1d3a4] 's list that we just discussed.\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bemO9iJfEklS9VzF1kaAwpjG_ShgGxT376bKGAXtB70/edit?pli=1&gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1bemO9iJfEklS9VzF1kaAwpjG_ShgGxT376bKGAXtB70/edit?pli=1&gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T12:11:07.905Z"],["3815777","RDS-129","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* still waiting on new a/b test of 50 to 30m\n* ongoing discussions on whether benefits outweigh extreme edge case negatives\n** → may make feature optional for drivers","2026-01-16T12:11:10.810Z"],["3815778","PFI-834039","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Example rule: \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/rides_cs_issue/CS_RIDES_PROFILING_CREATION_IP?tab=script&scriptTab=script_view|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/rules/edit/rides_cs_issue/CS_RIDES_PROFILING_CREATION_IP?tab=script&scriptTab=script_view]\nExample profiling? \n[https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/blob/main/fraud_rides_cs_creation_ip/get_fraud_rides_profile_by_creation_ip.sql|https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/blob/main/fraud_rides_cs_creation_ip/get_fraud_rides_profile_by_creation_ip.sql]\n\nHAVING SUM(x.sum_of_net_spending_eur) - SUM(x.amount_eur) < -500 (net spend - comp)\n   AND COUNT(DISTINCT x.user_id) >= 10\n\nDon’t see any profiling inputs in the calculations, other than additional.profiling.user\n\nOld profilings, Sumran will do an overhaul at some point?","2026-01-16T12:12:05.755Z"],["3815780","PFI-822328","PFI","seema.matli@bolt.eu","Seema Matli","Hey [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] As advised by [~accountid:6155b82fa70710006958c85b] , the user is a rider, and we were hoping you could help us with what we should say to the rider in relation to their query. \n\nAm I correct to assume that invoices that show 0% VAT indicate that the driver is not liable for VAT?","2026-01-16T12:12:10.450Z"],["3815781","RDS-1345","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* ready for design","2026-01-16T12:12:18.707Z"],["3815785","HS-29032","HS","joanna.stachowicz@bolt.eu","Joanna Stachowicz","[^Bolt Mail - Proposal for cooperation with Bolt.pdf]","2026-01-16T12:13:08.565Z"],["3815787","RDS-1389","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* android and BE in progress\n* ios dev bottleneck\n* expect QA readiness (android) by end of next week","2026-01-16T12:13:14.083Z"],["3815788","LSS-61493","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","FYi - I had a look and suggested to remove the N/A wording in the [supplier agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/10ciLA6CYrJNAsA7RCgJSk4aYQx0xjaPDOJ0yRo6riPw/edit?tab=t.0] - commented in the doc.We want to be engaged as an independent and separate data controller.","2026-01-16T12:13:59.203Z"],["3815789","RDS-1049","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* possibly optional tag improvements\n* and look at epic leftovers","2026-01-16T12:14:04.876Z"],["3815798","MAB-227","MAB","balaji.senthilkumar@bolt.eu","Balaji Senthilkumar","Made all the changes to reflect the timestamps for respective stages with Onboarding funnel to measure SLA calculations in a more accurate way. So, for this I have added all the timestamps column from the onbaording funnel for each stage and made a change in logic for SLA. \n\nShared the PR with engineering team, waiting for approval. \n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15205|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15205|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T12:15:32.304Z"],["3815799","PTWS-2117","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Findings from Darja: only the time off process has a rule for the payroll cutoff dates; no action for Jan as the Payroll cutoff date is aligned in Workday","2026-01-16T12:16:01.089Z"],["3815800","DSR-3787","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T12:16:07.028Z"],["3815801","DSR-3789","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T12:16:07.119Z"],["3815803","RDS-1178","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* starting BE dev next week\n* and android once resources available (if Progression team doesn’t need android)","2026-01-16T12:16:15.790Z"],["3815804","PAW-14924","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-16T12:16:48.272Z"],["3815805","PIF-3285","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-review-and-approval-system, pint-product-identity-and-communication-management, pint-capability-itgc\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-16T12:16:54.884Z"],["3815806","FPD-1533","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Still to do:\n\n* fix the ingestion\n* change the code to transform the data into the necessary format and write to a specific location in s3","2026-01-16T12:17:05.827Z"],["3815812","WD-22567","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hello  [~accountid:61c07bf9a54af90069a42e2f] !\n\nValidation for Customer Invoice is created. I assumed that intercompany entities should be excluded from the rule ( same works for supplier invoices validation), but if needed to include all companies, let me know. \n\nAdditionally, this validation should work only for customer invoices? or should I also enable it for customer invoice adjustments? \n\n!image-20260116-121712.png|width=1442,alt=\"image-20260116-121712.png\"!","2026-01-16T12:19:08.805Z"],["3815813","LSS-61711","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^LOA_Bolt_Operations_OU_Hungary_PwC_Estonia.docx] _(32 kB)_","2026-01-16T12:19:09.700Z"],["3815814","RDS-1179","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* having issues with being able to disable b2b ride requests while in a ride\n* a/b test removing break mode","2026-01-16T12:19:11.522Z"],["3815817","PC-4935","PC","rushang.chauhan@bolt.eu","Rushang Chauhan","The preliminary investigation indicates that there are numerous instances where the {{getPayment}} endpoint returns zero amounts for the Bolt Balance Instrument, as detailed in the [Kibana Logs|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/iytJz].","2026-01-16T12:19:22.467Z"],["3815819","DRX-28248","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Andrii Pustovoit, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-16T12:19:26.446Z"],["3815820","DSR-3195","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], can we reply as below. This is a previously used template:\n\n*Template*\n\nDear [NAME],\nThank you for contacting us regarding the processing of your personal data, and in particular to ask whether Bolt sells users' information.\nWe would like to clarify that Bolt does not sell users' personal data in exchange for financial consideration or other forms of direct commercial gain. This has always been our approach to user data.\nAs part of providing and optimising our services, we process your personal data. Data protection law permits this processing for legitimate operational purposes. This processing may involve the sharing or transfer of data with certain categories of recipients. These recipients include other companies within the Bolt group, as well as trusted third‑party partners who help us perform the essential functions necessary to provide and improve our services.\nAll processing activities, including any necessary sharing or transfer of personal data, are carried out in strict compliance with applicable data protection laws. We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures designed to protect your personal data during these processes.\nFor more information about how we process relevant personal data, please refer to our privacy statement available at [Privacy|https://bolt.eu/fr-fr/privacy/], which includes information on:\n* The categories of personal data we process (please also note that you have the right to request a copy of your personal data processed by Bolt at any time);\n* The purposes for which we process personal data;\n* The sources of personal data;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom personal data have been or will be disclosed;\n* The applicable retention periods for the personal data we process, including the criteria we use to determine retention periods for personal data; and\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision‑making/profiling.\nYour rights\nIn addition to your right to access all personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request that we rectify or erase your personal data, to restrict the processing of your personal data, or to object to such processing. Any request of this type submitted to us will be considered in accordance with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws.\nIf you are not satisfied with this response to your request or with any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve it. You also have the right to lodge a complaint directly with your data protection authority/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek judicial remedy.\nIf you have any further questions, please contact our customer support by replying to this email.\nKind regards,\nBolt","2026-01-16T12:20:07.611Z"],["3815821","C2-458","C2","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","h2. Ilvestments recycled batteries\n\nThree main reasons why batteries are recycled at the repair facility. \n\n* 54% cell imbalance\n* 36% water damage\n* 8% failed BMS\n\n!image-20260116-084932.png|width=278,alt=\"image-20260116-084932.png\"!\n\nh3. “Water damage” incoming reasons\n\nCurrently water damage is the most likely cause for battery fires. In the recycling data we can see that \n\n* 25% of recycled water damage batteries also have a cell error,\n** There were 20 cell error water damaged C2 batteries in the last two years of repair sent to Ilvestments. That’s around 1 fire hazard battery per month. \n* 22% were sent to repair because of broken female connector,\n* 12% go to repair because of “not charging”,\n* 12% “led indicator issue”.\n* 3pcs C2.5 batteries that gave water ingress error were sent to repair. \n** This risk should now be mitigated with the new firmware where the water ingress error is set permanent and error is indicated with LEDs. LOPS were instructed to recycle batteries with water ingress error.\n\n!image-20260116-085511.png|width=379,alt=\"image-20260116-085511.png\"!\n\nh3. “Cell imbalance” incoming reasons\n\nMain incoming reasons are \n\n* 27% cell error\n* 19% not charging\n* 13% female connector\n\n!image-20260116-085216.png|width=375,alt=\"image-20260116-085216.png\"!","2026-01-16T12:20:26.539Z"],["3815822","WD-22516","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hello [~accountid:712020:0df7300f-0bb9-493c-9e9c-7aea366c53e6] ! do you still need any help? ","2026-01-16T12:20:35.204Z"],["3815824","LSS-61634","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, Karoli! May you please clarify: this type of signature won’t work for the engagement letter?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.20.17.png|width=166,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.20.17.png\"!","2026-01-16T12:20:52.792Z"],["3815825","LSS-60730","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Hey. last amend from Cogs, can someone review this and advice if you re ok with the amendment:\n\n\"Further to our conversations on the liability cap proposed in Clause 15.6 of the MSA earlier today, where the Client’s maximum aggregate liability is limited to the lower of (i) the fees paid in the previous 12 months or (ii) EUR 1,000,000, please see below an example where Cognizant might incur losses significantly above EUR1M which due to faults by Bolt.*GDPR Article 82 Exposure* Under Article 82 of the GDPR, controllers and processors can be held _jointly and severally liable_ for damage suffered by data subjects. This liability arises regardless of which party is primarily at fault, and processors are explicitly exposed if they have in any way contributed to the processing activity—even if the root cause of the breach is the controller’s failure.\n*Example scenario:*\nA client provides the supplier with a corrupted or improperly vetted dataset containing personal data. The client later instructs processing that results in a large‑scale personal‑data breach, leading to a coordinated claims campaign by affected data subjects risking claims where processors is required to compensate data subjects first, and only subsequently seek recourse from the controller.\nIn such circumstances:\n\n* The supplier may face significant damages in data‑subject compensation claims.\n* Article 82(5) allows the supplier to seek recourse from the controller.\n* Clause 15.6 would effectively cap that recourse at EUR 1 million, even though the liability originated from the Bolt’s failure and even though Cognizant has been made to compensate the data subjects in [full.In|http://full.In] light of the above, we request that losses incurred due to Bolt’s failure to comply with regulatory requirements are not limited to the EUR 1 million. Please see suggested edits in the below:\"_The maximum aggregate liability of the Client for any and all Losses, damages, claims, or expenses arising out of or in connection with this Agreement, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty, or otherwise, shall be limited to an amount equal to the (i) total Fees paid by the Client under this Agreement in the 12 (twelve) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim or (ii) 1 000 000 (one million) EUR, whichever is lower. If the Losses, damages, claims, or expenses arise of out the Client’s failure to comply with regulatory requirements such as the GDPR, the liability shall be limited to an amount equal to the (i) total Fees paid by the Client under this Agreement in the 12 (twelve) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim._\"\n\n","2026-01-16T12:20:59.414Z"],["3815827","DSR-3791","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T12:21:20.279Z"],["3815828","WD-22540","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hello [~accountid:712020:4031005b-be5e-413a-b7da-919304795012] ! do still any help? or should I close the ticket? ","2026-01-16T12:21:21.145Z"],["3815829","DRX-27886","DRX","vishalkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vishal Singh","Issue reported [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04J4MF8X8U/p1766997812097439]","2026-01-16T12:21:26.328Z"],["3815831","HS-29028","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Added shift work back as agreed with Kristiina Kuutok.","2026-01-16T12:21:34.040Z"],["3815832","HS-29028","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","No other action needed - manager change.","2026-01-16T12:22:02.810Z"],["3815836","LSS-57822","LSS","alijan.dias@bolt.eu","Alijan Keval","Hey Catarina, thank you for the detailed response.\n\nFrom field work, in discussion with couriers and “courier profile shops” we have gathered that Bolt is the best app for courier fraud in Portugal and that our profiles are currently being sold in Hourly slots, due to insufficient verification. Meaning that we need to start fraud prevention in any way possible.\n\nWhat happens is that many couriers rent a complete package of Equipment (Bike + Bag) & Device. This is a direct bypass of a guardrail we have of checking the number of devices used by a single account.\n\nRegarding the selfie check for all information change requests, from what we understand, once a courier profile is approved and active, it can be sold or rented perpetually, for that you simply need to change the login data email or phone, and anyone can start using the courier app. That why we need the selfie checks for every change to stop the fraud selling/renting market. \n\nWe’ve learnt that for example Uber Eats requires a selfie check every time the account initiates (every day or every other day), hence couriers mention that they cannot rent UE accounts.  \n\n\n","2026-01-16T12:22:47.093Z"],["3815837","PFI-834210","PFI","hira.hassan@bolt.eu","Hira Hassan","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.50.49.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:23:07.616Z"],["3815838","LSS-59846","LSS","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Hey!\n\nWe often consider telemetry systems to be part of PII processing, because it is very common to send PII to these systems.\n\nI think with data scrubbing, we will be fine - however, don’t we need a DPA for the Bolt employee data we share with Sentry, when creating Bolt employee accounts in Sentry?","2026-01-16T12:23:18.740Z"],["3815839","CEBF-1702","CEBF","serhii.kostyhin@bolt.eu","Serhii Kostyhin","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] \nFor AC1: we check by Active Status. Should I add additional checking by Approval Status?","2026-01-16T12:23:20.844Z"],["3815841","L10N-28339","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28337](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28337)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T12:23:42.264Z"],["3815842","L10N-28338","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28337](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28337)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T12:23:42.497Z"],["3815843","L10N-28341","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28337](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28337)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T12:23:43.037Z"],["3815844","L10N-28342","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28337](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28337)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T12:23:45.063Z"],["3815845","L10N-28344","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28337](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28337)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T12:23:45.112Z"],["3815846","L10N-28346","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one)