 can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28337](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28337)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T12:23:47.602Z"],["3815849","RS-1954","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] it’s not valid, please request a new valid legal basis","2026-01-16T12:23:51.921Z"],["3815852","LSS-61695","LSS","valentina.pavlova@bolt.eu","Valentyna Pavlova","Hi, yes, this is for Ukrpost. The girls at the reception of our official address receive it. There have been no cases of receiving mail from other postal companies yet.\nNo, I don’t have a previous ticket or PoA for this person.\n","2026-01-16T12:24:48.380Z"],["3815854","DSR-3135","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9], deadline is on January 16, 2026. This date was the one mentioned to the user. Let me know if there’s any update.","2026-01-16T12:24:52.804Z"],["3815857","DSR-3793","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T12:26:06.908Z"],["3815858","WD-22573","WD","maile.nittim@bolt.eu","Maile Nittim","Currently we have EORI numbers for four entities:\n\nBolt Support Services IT S.R.L - IT11860660965\nBolt Operations UK Limited - GB459053772000\nBolt Support Services PT, Unipessoal Lda - PT514858168\nBolt Operations OÜ - EE14532901\n\nPT and Bolt Ops already have EORI numbers on seller side.\n\nIt would be great if these EORI numbers would appear always whether the entity is seller or buyer.","2026-01-16T12:26:09.805Z"],["3815859","WDFT-3424","WDFT","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Split Template Mapping\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m2vuadGFg_SsXbwF5y6ZZ5i5awWGNkPLpDwA-K5zR2k/edit?gid=1919168334#gid=1919168334|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1m2vuadGFg_SsXbwF5y6ZZ5i5awWGNkPLpDwA-K5zR2k/edit?gid=1919168334#gid=1919168334|smart-card]","2026-01-16T12:26:26.382Z"],["3815860","WDFT-3424","WDFT","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1uvvkIH-YEdm3i4ItoSg4GUis3albFnasTecmKzmMrX0/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1uvvkIH-YEdm3i4ItoSg4GUis3albFnasTecmKzmMrX0/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-16T12:27:06.573Z"],["3815861","HS-29031","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","No action needed from People Ops","2026-01-16T12:27:16.648Z"],["3815862","PFI-834213","PFI","darja.borkina@bolt-outsource.eu","Darja Borkina","!Screenshot_20260104_193718_Bolt Food.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:27:42.722Z"],["3815863","DRX-27886","DRX","joonas.lomps@bolt.eu","Joonas Lõmps","Expected behaviour if we have both UI and dynamic config set up.\r\nhttps://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-25246\r\n","2026-01-16T12:27:43.886Z"],["3815865","RDS-1179","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* why is there a ‘break’ button and ‘pause’ button?","2026-01-16T12:27:54.347Z"],["3815866","FPD-1488","FPD","andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu","Andrei Kuchev","Update - we’re incorporating changes and planning to run pipeline today by EOD","2026-01-16T12:27:59.278Z"],["3815869","LSS-60730","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] \n\nWe will share the questions with our Privacy team for the review ","2026-01-16T12:29:41.950Z"],["3815870","DO-5811","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Hey Anton 👋 \n\nPlease create PR to airflow-main [https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/blob/main/dags/common/driverx/etl_config.yml|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/blob/main/dags/common/driverx/etl_config.yml|smart-link]  and you can run the DBT from airflow instead from databricks.\n\nIf you need further help, please contact the other team {{@insight_support}} in `#dev-data-platform-support`","2026-01-16T12:30:04.776Z"],["3815872","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4], the Accounting team have confirmed that they can send the bank transfer. \n\nPlease could you confirm the bank details for this purpose?\n\nThank you ! ","2026-01-16T12:30:28.473Z"],["3815874","WD-22587","WD","steve.white@bolt.eu","Steve White","yes this was updated at the request of Reward team to have no decimals.","2026-01-16T12:30:45.077Z"],["3815875","LSS-61620","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] and [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] !\n\nThe addendum looks fine to me.\n\nIn order for Local Ops to arranje signatures, we also need the email address of the person who will sign on UHY behalf (Pierre Galea Musu’ FIA CPA).\n\nCan you obtain it?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T12:30:52.159Z"],["3815879","RDS-1303","RDS","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","* price breakdown having issues\n* UK regs\n** special components like holiday pay and tolls\n** but not full fare breakdown, which became expectation\n* Only enabled in UK now, maybe in Kenya because of regs","2026-01-16T12:31:24.458Z"],["3815881","WDFT-3607","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:637f26822acfad92d7b13ddb] ! BG002 & PL002 are added","2026-01-16T12:31:29.667Z"],["3815882","CCM-22279","CCM","toyosi.olusesi@bolt-outsource.eu","Toyosi Olusesi","[^New Training Request form _ Teleperformance.xlsx]","2026-01-16T12:31:38.972Z"],["3815883","DSR-3777","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Added the rest of the comms from the Slack incident channel [+_thread_+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7DAJ0A8M/p1768565777347429?thread_ts=1768476810.005019&cid=C0A7DAJ0A8M] to the Google Drive folder [+_here_+|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1qD2wohipjGhwUx-vCX5tTkv_xDb7pa7s?usp=drive_link] ✅","2026-01-16T12:31:39.040Z"],["3815885","WDFT-3607","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","[~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82]  can we give Janeli permissions to change companies' hierarchy? ","2026-01-16T12:32:26.391Z"],["3815887","LSS-61712","LSS","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","[^Bolt TH_Dlocal TH_Second Amendment.docx] _(24 kB)_","2026-01-16T12:32:34.955Z"],["3815889","LSS-51490","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:da839b78-87fc-4471-947b-3aae59c6030b] - can you please kindly check if the update was completed by our local DPO in Zimbabwe? \n\nContext is in Eliise’s message below - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-51490?focusedCommentId=3772126|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-51490?focusedCommentId=3772126|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T12:33:34.233Z"],["3815894","LSS-61620","LSS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi Catarina, \n\nYes, I already have it: [pgm@uhymalta.com|mailto:pgm@uhymalta.com] \n\nWhat are the next steps?\n\nThank you, \n\nLore","2026-01-16T12:34:18.552Z"],["3815895","LSS-61589","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","⏳ *Deadline to respond to the letter:* {{2026-01-23}}(Friday, next week). \n\n{color:#0747a6}*The background of the case (TBC):*{color}\n\n# {color:#ff5630}+*The waiting fee was not charged in August 2025;*+{color}{color:#ff5630} {color}it was only recorded as a negative amount on the *Bolt Balance Account* (-7.85 PLN).\n# Bolt determined that this negative balance was applied incorrectly. Two solutions were proposed for the user: either *resetting the Bolt Balance Account to zero*, or *refunding the amount of 7.85 PLN to the original payment method* (which would effectively mean that the bank account holder who paid via BLIK would receive an extra 7.85 PLN).\n# Because Bolt has no control over which bank account the ride payment is made from (i.e. it does not have to belong to the same person as the holder of the Bolt Balance Account), from both the user’s perspective (the person ordering the ride) and Bolt’s perspective, *the situation balances out to zero:* the account shows a negative balance, but at the same time 7.85 PLN was refunded to the original payment method (BLIK).\n# If a Bolt user wants to recover the money that was actually lost, they should contact the passengers directly; Bolt’s role ends at this point. This is the most logic solution of this problem.\n\nBut in practice we want to minimize an escalation of this case as much as possible, especially that the claim’s amount is very low (7.85  PLN ~1.86 EUR). So here are two options:\n\n# :orange_circle: *(The most logical and financially advantageous solution for Bolt)*\nWe can stand by our position, as described above, and refer the user to the passengers to whom we actually transferred the amount of 7.85 PLN (in line with the user’s request), as Bolt’s role ends at this point.\n\nor\n\n# :green_circle: *(The most reasonable solution to avoid escalation of the issue and potential proceedings before the Office of Competition and Consumer Protection – UOKIK)*\nWe waive the amount of 7.85 PLN and refund the user 7.85 PLN as an unjustifiably charged amount for the last ride (from October 2025). As in October 2025, this amount was already charged, we should refund this payment in a way the user wish for.\n\n{color:#36b37e}*Why the option 2 is most recommended by Legal?*{color} [In the current T&Cs for the Bolt Balance Account, PL|file:///Users/jolantaprystupa/Downloads/bolt_balance_terms_pl_pl_58419ba324.pdf] we do not explicitly specify how refunds relating to the Bolt Balance are processed or what consequences they have for the balance (which weakens our position before the users).\n\nAdditionally, as a follow-up, in order to prevent UOKIK from challenging our practice, I would amend the Polish T&Cs relating to the *Bolt Balance Account* so that in situations like this (i.e. an unjustified charge to the Bolt Balance Account where the amount was not actually charged by Bolt), the only permissible action is to cancel the negative amount (i.e. remove it) from the balance, rather than issuing a refund via the original payment method. This approach would allow us to avoid similar situations in the future and keep the flow of funds within the Bolt app.\n\n\n\nPlease [~accountid:712020:783602a6-282a-4f15-930c-066bdff8e5c5] and [~accountid:712020:38ef5817-1c12-4bf5-b0d1-116b99b69ddf] let me know what you think about this and which option we can follow next week 😉 \n\nMany thanks, Jola 🙏 ","2026-01-16T12:34:19.610Z"],["3815896","LSS-61710","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n [^AuthorisationletterBoltOperationsOUCitibank171225 (1).pdf]\n\n [^AuthorisationletterBoltTechnologyOUCitibank171225 (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T12:34:22.692Z"],["3815897","CNT-460","CNT","marit.ausmees@bolt.eu","Marit Ausmees","Hey, [~accountid:624c636af40798007059caa8] Could someone please double-check the visuals? Why are there 2 variations for GH, no percentage for RO, wrong language for LV etc. I already corrected some, but there are still many mistakes left.","2026-01-16T12:34:27.201Z"],["3815898","LSS-59377","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team, \n[~accountid:62bdcba29e6ba34c99375ad9] sorry for the delay 🙏 \n\nHere’s the key information related to this matter:\n\n*_1) Does BF have to collect / verify alcohol licenses?_*\n\n*Legal baseline:*\n\n* The obligation to hold a valid *retail alcohol licence* sits with the *merchant (trader)* — i.e., the entity that actually sells alcohol to the consumer and releases it for delivery / collection.\n\n*Why BF should still collect and do at least a light verification (practical / regulatory rationale):*\n\n* *Remote sale of alcohol requires a retail alcohol licence.* If BF enables alcohol sales by merchants without a licence (or from a location not covered by the licence), this creates a structural risk of unlawful trade.\n* If BF operates as a platform enabling consumers to conclude distance contracts with traders, the *business standard* in practice requires collecting trader identification information, making *best efforts* to assess whether it is reliable/complete, and *suspending* traders (at least from alcohol sales) if key information is missing or clearly inaccurate.\n* *Risk management:* even if liability for licence breaches sits with the merchant, BF remains a high-exposure target for *regulatory scrutiny and reputational damage* if the platform knowingly enables a model without safeguards.\n\n*Recommended BF minimum standard:*\n\n* Enable alcohol selling only after collecting *licence details* (licence number, issuing authority/municipality, validity, licensed address/premises, permitted categories) plus a document copy/screenshot.\n* Hard-code a contractual and operational right to *disable alcohol selling* for non-compliance or repeated incidents.\n\nh3. *_2) If an under-20 user orders or receives alcohol - who is at fault?_*\n\n*Primary liability:*\n\n* *Merchant:* as the selling entity, the merchant is the primary party responsible for ensuring alcohol is not sold/handed over to anyone under 20 (including refusing the sale where age cannot be verified).\n* *Courier:* separate administrative risk arises for the person who *physically hands over / delivers* alcohol to a person under 20 (the “handover point”).\n\n*BF exposure in practice (even if BF is not the “seller”):*\n\n* BF may argue it *does not assume the seller’s role*, however:\n** if BF’s platform design makes it easy to bypass age checks (e.g., “contactless”, no mandatory ID-check flow, no refusal flow), BF will face heightened *regulatory and reputational* exposure;\n** in incidents, BF is often treated publicly as the “channel operator”, especially where the system is not designed to reduce infringements (“compliance-by-design”).\n\n*Practical standards to support a strong BF position (though I believe these steps are already in place):*\n\n* Mandatory *ID-check* flow for couriers + a clear *refusal-to-deliver* process (refusal flow) with recorded reason (no ID / underage / intoxicated / after hours).\n* Automatic blocking of *contactless / leave-at-door* options for orders containing alcohol.\n\nh3. *_3) If alcohol is delivered during restricted hours or on 1 September — who is at fault?_*\n\n*Primary liability:*\n\n* *Merchant:* responsible for breaches of time-based restrictions. For distance sales, this effectively means the sale/hand-over must not occur during prohibited periods.\n\n*Courier exposure (practical):*\n\n* *Courier:* while enforcement typically targets the merchant for time restrictions, a courier may still face exposure in practice if they knowingly deliver alcohol during prohibited hours / on 1 September, depending on how authorities frame the breach and the courier’s role in execution.\n\n*BF risk:*\n\n* If BF accepts orders in a way that makes compliant handover predictably impossible (e.g., no buffer, no hard blocks, no “alcohol after-hours” gating), *BF can be viewed as the enabling factor that created conditions for non-compliance (regulatory + PR risk)*.\n\n*Recommended controls (though I believe these steps are already in place):* \n\n* Hard blocks + time buffers + “do not dispatch if risk of after-hours handover” logic; refusal flow for couriers when handover would occur during restricted periods.\n\nh3. \n_4) Recommended position:_ \n\n*Assessment:*\n\n* Full self-serve (all merchants can add alcohol items without BF controls) is a *high-risk* model. It increases the likelihood of (i) *unlicensed alcohol sales*, (ii) i*ncorrect age/time settings*, and (iii) *incidents that quickly become PR/regulator issues*.\n\n*Recommended compromise (safest implementation):*\n\nLet merchants manage alcohol listings themselves, *while making it hard to sell alcohol unlawfully or in the wrong way*, and keeping BF’s risk exposure under control.\n\nh4. 1) First: “unlock” alcohol only for licensed merchants\n\n* The merchant submits licence details (number, validity, licensed address/premises) and uploads a document/screenshot.\n* BF performs a light verification (at minimum: confirm a licence exists and matches the merchant).\n* Only then the merchant gets the capability to sell alcohol on BF.\n\nh4. 2) Second: alcohol items can only be created via a dedicated “Add Alcohol” flow\n\nNot via generic free-text menu editing.\n\nMerchants still do everything themselves (products, pricing, assortment), but the system forces compliance by default:\n\n* the item must be classified as alcohol (mandatory flag/category),\n* *20+* restriction is applied automatically,\n* ordering/delivery is automatically blocked during restricted hours and on *1 September*,\n* *no contactless / leave-at-door* is enforced automatically,\n* courier app automatically triggers mandatory *ID-check* steps + a clear *refusal flow*.\n\nh4. 3) Third: the courier is the final “gatekeeper” at handover\n\nIf an order contains alcohol:\n\n* the courier must check ID,\n* if no ID / customer is under 20 / handover would occur in restricted hours → the courier must refuse delivery and select the reason in-app. \n\n*This approach makes the risk low*:\n\n* Merchants remain largely self-serve (they manage items, prices, assortment).\n* BF ensures the product design *prevents non-compliance by default* (compliance-by-design).\n* If an incident occurs, BF can demonstrate: licence gated + time blocks + mandatory ID check → reasonable and proportionate controls were in place.\n\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please let me know! \n\nThanks! ☺️ ","2026-01-16T12:34:28.982Z"],["3815900","CCM-22280","CCM","peace.anumia@bolt-outsource.eu","Peace Anumia","[^New Training Request form _ Teleperformance (160126).xlsx]","2026-01-16T12:35:10.654Z"],["3815901","LSS-61634","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]  nope - as it provides the timestamp under the name. \n\n[~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] could you please advise which program to use that does not give a timestamp underneath the name? \n\n\nThank you and best wishes, Karoli","2026-01-16T12:35:12.507Z"],["3815902","PFI-834219","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","!16848.png.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:35:20.691Z"],["3815903","RS-1954","RS","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Will do. Thank you very much 🙌","2026-01-16T12:35:36.573Z"],["3815905","DSR-3795","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T12:36:33.639Z"],["3815909","DBRE-8607","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Duplicate of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-7659|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-7659|smart-link].","2026-01-16T12:36:52.033Z"],["3815911","PFI-834221","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","[^List of wrongly matched payments - Sheet2.csv]","2026-01-16T12:37:10.904Z"],["3815912","PFI-833848","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi Andrei. I've put the invoice to ignore state on tax tech side. If the customer now downloads the invoice, the ID will be there.\n\nAdded the example in the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|smart-link] guide as well, please make sure that you have always done all that can be done before escalating to billing 🙂 ","2026-01-16T12:37:37.262Z"],["3815915","PAR-3847","PAR","kateryna.oliferchuk@bolt.eu","Kateryna Oliferchuk","The majority of the errors are caused by admin actions: \n1. Payout is marked as finished after being rejected:  admin rejects unprocessed (stuck) payouts and reimports them via payouts import tool. \nExamples: [payout 1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/231756998?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FBerlin], [payout 2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/231832055?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FBerlin]\nRelated to an incident on the Jan 2nd: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G011LPT6DC6/p1768567730604819?thread_ts=1768567056.047319&cid=G011LPT6DC6|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G011LPT6DC6/p1768567730604819?thread_ts=1768567056.047319&cid=G011LPT6DC6|smart-link] \n2. Payout is rejected twice: already rejected payout (by CAMT.53) is rejected again via payouts import. \nExamples: [payout 1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233404722?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FBerlin], [payout 2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233404509?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FBerlin]","2026-01-16T12:37:44.095Z"],["3815916","LSS-61634","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Alright, Karoli!  Thank you for clarification. ","2026-01-16T12:37:52.914Z"],["3815917","WFM-10022","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","!Iveta Griskeviciute adherence.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:38:14.694Z"],["3815918","CNT-377","CNT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945] will Brand need the exact copy for working on design guidelines? Can we ship this draft so they can kickoff their work stream while I gather feedback from Product as well?","2026-01-16T12:38:20.144Z"],["3815919","LSS-61638","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","Hey [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f], the floor plan is fine to accept, can the agreement be sent for signing? All new Regus tickets i’ll submit after using custom chatgpt ","2026-01-16T12:38:29.908Z"],["3815920","PFI-834039","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","[~accountid:5e4fb3b04d2a000c9114bc04] \nHey hey, our original approach here wasn’t proactive blocking as such, but rather removing the CS escalation/refund function for these users. A more comprehensive overhaul of this profiling is already in our new analyst’s backlog. That said, these cases are currently relatively low priority for Fraud, so the ETA for a full solution is unfortunately unclear at the moment.\n\nFor the time being, I do support OPS taking action to block rider accounts as soon as this type of coordinated or related-account behaviour is detected. Rider blocking is a relatively light measure, and if a user does turn out to be legitimate, they still have the option to create a new account. But if you wish to create an SOP for all of this, it can take some longer planning i think. @ me in this ticket if you wish to discuss this further or if you have any more questions.\n\nI’ve blocked the related accounts for now, and I’ll ping the analyst as well just in case 🙂 \n","2026-01-16T12:38:39.523Z"],["3815923","LSS-61619","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","Hi [~accountid:60bd1baef650540069f28c36], nothing yet that we have noticed - will ping you the second we come across anything","2026-01-16T12:38:54.169Z"],["3815924","LSS-61038","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* confirmation and copy of our response submitted - +*rejected claim in full*+.\n\n[^response_sealed_form_763MC252.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.37.57 PM.png|width=680,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 12.37.57 PM.png\"!","2026-01-16T12:39:25.937Z"],["3815925","LSS-58949","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] \n\n*Cognizant came back with feedback, please add  changes to MSA in comments mode if needed* \n\n\"Further to our conversations on the liability cap proposed in Clause 15.6 of the MSA earlier today, where the Client’s maximum aggregate liability is limited to the lower of (i) the fees paid in the previous 12 months or (ii) EUR 1,000,000, please see below an example where Cognizant might incur losses significantly above EUR1M which due to faults by Bolt.*GDPR Article 82 Exposure* Under Article 82 of the GDPR, controllers and processors can be held _jointly and severally liable_ for damage suffered by data subjects. This liability arises regardless of which party is primarily at fault, and processors are explicitly exposed if they have in any way contributed to the processing activity—even if the root cause of the breach is the controller’s failure.\n*Example scenario:*\nA client provides the supplier with a corrupted or improperly vetted dataset containing personal data. The client later instructs processing that results in a large‑scale personal‑data breach, leading to a coordinated claims campaign by affected data subjects risking claims where processors is required to compensate data subjects first, and only subsequently seek recourse from the controller.\nIn such circumstances:\n\n* The supplier may face significant damages in data‑subject compensation claims.\n* Article 82(5) allows the supplier to seek recourse from the controller.\n* Clause 15.6 would effectively cap that recourse at EUR 1 million, even though the liability originated from the Bolt’s failure and even though Cognizant has been made to compensate the data subjects in [full.In|http://full.In] light of the above, we request that losses incurred due to Bolt’s failure to comply with regulatory requirements are not limited to the EUR 1 million. Please see suggested edits in the below:\"_The maximum aggregate liability of the Client for any and all Losses, damages, claims, or expenses arising out of or in connection with this Agreement, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty, or otherwise, shall be limited to an amount equal to the (i) total Fees paid by the Client under this Agreement in the 12 (twelve) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim or (ii) 1 000 000 (one million) EUR, whichever is lower. If the Losses, damages, claims, or expenses arise of out the Client’s failure to comply with regulatory requirements such as the GDPR, the liability shall be limited to an amount equal to the (i) total Fees paid by the Client under this Agreement in the 12 (twelve) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim._\"\n\n *MSA draft version with Cognizant:*  \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gZbbJzM7gGPTA63gNDbguRwbEBi_MhAK/edit#heading=h.cgpkt78xuciz|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gZbbJzM7gGPTA63gNDbguRwbEBi_MhAK/edit#heading=h.cgpkt78xuciz|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T12:39:48.416Z"],["3815927","DSR-3795","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Provided template to driver app for download. ","2026-01-16T12:40:10.806Z"],["3815928","LSS-61038","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Closing this ticket since we have received no response from the claimant and our response has now been submitted via the Government portal.","2026-01-16T12:40:34.450Z"],["3815929","LSS-61634","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please use DocuSign - that should provide the timestamp in a separate sheet, that then can be excluded. \n\nPlease let me know if it works. Thank you and best wishes, Karoli","2026-01-16T12:42:23.402Z"],["3815931","SOBB-1026","SOBB","lucas.santossilva@bolt.eu","Lucas Oliveira dos Santos Silva","[~accountid:712020:7d95934d-5639-4088-90fe-77e85828226f], tested in Staging and looks fine, I did some tests sending single/multiple callouts and it’s working as expected. Lead information, requests and response from N8N can be found here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1mCfae89Tz-LaonNMEMQnOTJ8SWEBeIToWf8KZmtr6Mc/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1mCfae89Tz-LaonNMEMQnOTJ8SWEBeIToWf8KZmtr6Mc/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T12:43:01.316Z"],["3815932","GRWA-1501","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Seems like a PDT missing data for past days. I have rebuild the pdt and numbers have been increased.","2026-01-16T12:43:13.296Z"],["3815934","LSS-61638","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Thank you for confirming [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5]!\n\n*Legal Ops:* please can you kindly arrange the signing of the attached by *Alex Wong* on behalf of *Bolt Operations UK Limited*? Please can you also append the attached floorplan to the agreement.\n\nThank you in advance! 🙏 \n\n[^OSA_PRT13098128_150120261242 (1).pdf]\n[^0417 - REIGATE, Regus London Road - UK Pricing Plan - 20230518 (7).pdf (8be68228-8558-4e98-8e4f-44237522c044).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T12:44:07.015Z"],["3815935","PFI-832470","PFI","folashade.akinsola@bolt.eu","Folashade Dolapo Akinsola","On the reissue side, please reissue invoices covering *September 2025 through December 2025*. Thanks","2026-01-16T12:44:17.556Z"],["3815936","DELIVERY-828","DELIVERY","ashish.puri@bolt.eu","Ashish Puri","26W3: Product Discovery Doc shared. Had discussion with Max related to leveraging the work he has done in pressure metric. Further narrowing down of the scope is expected in the upcoming week.","2026-01-16T12:44:24.133Z"],["3815937","DSR-3135","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] Thanks - I was just responding to your previous message which indicated deadline as {{2026-01-19}}! Thanks for changing it as I too was working on the date communicated to the user.\n\nThe request has been completed but I am waiting on language to update the email address momentarily.","2026-01-16T12:44:37.969Z"],["3815940","DSR-3195","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Great first draft [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - I amended lightly:\n\n{quote}Dear *[NAME]*,\n\nThank you for contacting us regarding the processing of your personal data, including your question as to whether Bolt sells users’ personal information.\n\nWe would like to clarify that Bolt does not sell users’ personal data in exchange for financial consideration or other forms of direct commercial gain. As part of providing and operating the Bolt services, we process personal data where this is necessary to perform our contract with you, to comply with legal obligations, or where we have a legitimate interest to do so. This processing is not optional where it is required to deliver the service.\nIn practice, this means that personal data may be shared with limited categories of recipients, including other companies within the Bolt group and carefully selected third-party service providers that support core functions such as payments, customer support, safety, fraud prevention, and regulatory compliance.\n\nAll processing activities, including any sharing or transfer of personal data, are carried out in compliance with applicable data protection laws. We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard personal data and limit access strictly to what is necessary for the relevant purpose.\n\nFor more information about how we process personal data, please refer to our Passenger Privacy Notice, available in the Bolt app and on our website, which explains in detail:\n\n* the categories of personal data we process;\n* the purposes and legal bases for processing;\n* the sources of the personal data;\n* the recipients or categories of recipients with whom personal data may be shared;\n* applicable retention periods and the criteria used to determine them.\n\n*Your rights*\n\nIn addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this message.\n\nSincerely,\n*Bolt*{quote}","2026-01-16T12:45:26.352Z"],["3815942","CEBF-1702","CEBF","pradeep.yadav@bolt.eu","Pradeep Kumar Yadav","[~accountid:712020:c573470a-712d-474e-a9e6-b0635a9decb9] Yes both","2026-01-16T12:45:55.716Z"],["3815943","PFI-798762","PFI","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","No, not yet. We are validating the path forward. This is a very old balance and there is no easy way to tackle. Will provide next answer before {{2026-01-21}}. May not be a final resolution.","2026-01-16T12:45:58.686Z"],["3815944","LSS-61713","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T12:46:07.344Z"],["3815945","DSR-3797","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T12:46:07.446Z"],["3815946","LSS-61714","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:d30129ff-7d6f-4bbd-82d3-3c1cbd5e1d77] - I will copy the results of our discussion in #*tmp-work-profile-billing-issues* here for the audit trail:\n\n# *TLDR Context*: The Work Profile (WP) was created to help users separate business and personal rides while ensuring they receive employer-ready invoices. However, WP currently allows unvalidated, free-form company information, leading to incomplete, non-compliant invoices that are not fiscally acceptable. In Poland, only 32% of users have fully correct or partially filled WP details according to current norms, which require full compliance from the [regulators|https://ksef.podatki.gov.pl/pytania-i-odpowiedzi-ksef-20?lid=oh6lu7m71y9d]. Due to these compliance requirements, WP will need to be disabled in Poland if validation is not achieved by the end of January 2026.\n# *Task*: Review the LCM copy and confirm it can be sent to users who opted out of marketing.\n\n----\n\n*Result of the privacy team’s review:* This message can reach all users, including those who opted out, as it is a service notification. I reviewed the content of the messages you shared and I agree with this assessment.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nAs a general note for future cases: if a communication is a clear compliance notification or required due to compliance, we can include users who opted out of marketing.\n{panel}","2026-01-16T12:46:11.126Z"],["3815953","LSS-56363","LSS","mykhailo.boiko@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Boiko","Hey [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] \nWe will pay from *Bolt Operations Ukraine LLC*\nThank you!","2026-01-16T12:48:29.855Z"],["3815954","DRX-27729","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DI.127.0 (194761070) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.3\n\n* Screen displayed is correct\n\n\n\n\n\n!IMG_5979.PNG|width=414,alt=\"IMG_5979.PNG\"!","2026-01-16T12:48:54.445Z"],["3815956","DELIVERY-1173","DELIVERY","tudor.suruceanu@bolt.eu","Tudor Suruceanu","26W03: There is a working experimental Rust module that we can now use for running the Matrix Dispatch algorithm. I am currently benchmarking it against the TypeScript version, and applying various tweaks.\n\nThe code is not production-ready yet.","2026-01-16T12:49:36.526Z"],["3815957","RDS-1409","RDS","andres.tack@bolt.eu","Andres Jaan Tack","Looks like we won’t actually do this?! In our last meeting with Herman from Noot, head of development, he thinks we’re good to go on all fronts. They will use GPS coordinates (already available) to approximate wait time, which is good enough for the use-case.\n\nTheir use-cases for timing the stops is customer support: if the taxi arrives to school late because the car waited too long for various students, they need to be able to say this confidently and turn the question back on the district/parents.","2026-01-16T12:50:29.624Z"],["3815960","RDS-1352","RDS","andres.tack@bolt.eu","Andres Jaan Tack","Got further evidence from Johan (SE) that this isn’t ever going to be a priority. Withdrawing.","2026-01-16T12:51:07.261Z"],["3815961","PFI-834226","PFI","omobolaji.okanrende@bolt-outsource.eu","Omobolaji Oluwatofarati Okanrende","!JPEG_1768558751406_1914333491918277377 x.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:51:36.259Z"],["3815963","INT-730","INT","dzmitry.kasakouski@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Kasakouski","26W3:\n\n* working on adding payment plans on green banner on the offer landing page, benefits list","2026-01-16T12:51:45.003Z"],["3815965","LSS-60562","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Hi Viktoriia!\nIn order to complete the registration process with Lloyds Bank I need the following data, can you please share it with me?+*Why This Matters*+Lloyds Banking Group uses the Ariba Network to manage sourcing, procurement, and supplier collaboration. Registration is required in order to:\n\n* Onboard your business as the agreed supplier type for procurement or sourcing activity\n* Receive payment(s) for goods and services supplied to Lloyds Banking Group\n* Maintain your company profile and compliance documentation\n\n+*What You’ll Need*+Before starting, please have the following information ready for submission:\n\n* Your *national business registration number* (e.g. Companies House number for UK-based suppliers)\n* *DUNS number* (Dun & Bradstreet)\n* *VAT registration number* or country equivalent\n* *Legal entity classification* (e.g. Parent Undertaking, Subsidiary of an Institution, Payment Institution)\n* *Legal entity type* (e.g. Public Limited Company, Private Company Limited by Shares, Company Limited by Guarantee)\n* *Declaration of any government ownership percentage*, if applicable\n* *Registered withholding tax schemes*\n* *Banking details* and *preferred currency*\n\n*Why This Information Is Required*To comply with regulatory requirements and internal policies, we require this information to complete our Supplier Onboarding process and conduct the necessary verification and due diligence checks.","2026-01-16T12:51:53.605Z"],["3815966","DSR-3191","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - I added a few relevant data points and edited the answer to reflect the question on ADM. You may share with the driver (/) ","2026-01-16T12:52:07.331Z"],["3815970","RDS-1345","RDS","andres.tack@bolt.eu","Andres Jaan Tack","[~accountid:712020:81377b7a-4a7f-417a-a4aa-7306f122b309] I learned something (the address) that may contribute to design and implementation. There’s an {{address}} field that we can pass in the RideBooker API – if it matches nearly-enough with the lat/lon coordinates, then it’s transmitted directly to the frontend.\n\nI’ve yet to verify this. Perhaps you can help me do that.","2026-01-16T12:53:05.342Z"],["3815971","CCM-22281","CCM","bianka.broczka@bolt-outsource.eu","Bianka Broczka","[^New TalentLMS Training Request Form (5).xlsx]","2026-01-16T12:53:05.418Z"],["3815972","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Hello team,\nCould you please take a look at [*this*|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C021M19NET1/p1768470489288979] case? The [*ticket*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/705016155] was being hold by Alfred for almost a month and was found accidentally by one of the TLs while checking the “All” tab for Eaters. What could be the reason? According to the OS TL, he was not able to assign the case, as it appeared to still be assigned to Alfred. When the in-house specialist opened the ticket, she was able to assign it to herself as usual.","2026-01-16T12:53:06.969Z"],["3815973","SAI-1412","SAI",null,"Slack","[Grzegorz Brotoń|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768470932685849?thread_ts=1768470932.685849&cid=C064FCFAT0S|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064FCFAT0S/p1768470932685849?thread_ts=1768470932.685849&cid=C064FCFAT0S|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T12:53:07.882Z"],["3815974","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","{quote}The *<https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/705016155|ticket{quote}\n\n>* was being hold by Alfred for almost a month\nThat's not true.\n\nIssue submitted: 12/15/2025, 1:41:51 PM\nAlfred assigned: 12/15/2025, 1:54:54 PM\nAlfred unassigned: 12/15/2025, 1:54:54 PM\n\nPlease go to <#C032D4ZGZR6|>, they manage queues and will be able to resolve why ticket didn't reach the queue. From automations side, everything was good.","2026-01-16T12:53:08.908Z"],["3815975","SAI-1412","SAI","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","Hey [@grzegorz.broton|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:f79c0085-d2cb-444c-a121-d9c86bb2bfca], it seems that something went wrong with this unassignment - it was never synced with Beehive, and in Beehive task Alfred was there for entire month\n\n{noformat}SELECT * FROM sel_beehive_spark.task_changed WHERE external_id = '705016155' AND created_date >= date '2025-11-01' ORDER BY version ASC;{noformat}\n\n{noformat}SELECT * FROM ng_beehive_spark.beehive_task_task_event WHERE task_id = 168354424 AND created_date >= date '2025-11-01' ORDER BY id ASC;{noformat}\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8STEV01Z/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8STEV01Z/image.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8HRM9NNT/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8HRM9NNT/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T12:53:09.891Z"],["3815976","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","I will look tomorrow","2026-01-16T12:53:10.819Z"],["3815977","SAI-1412","SAI","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł",":thank_you:","2026-01-16T12:53:11.429Z"],["3815978","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","can you help me [@piotr.musiol|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/6017bc27a41ea5006a86f73b] undrstand what I should look at the screens you attached?","2026-01-16T12:53:12.421Z"],["3815979","SAI-1412","SAI","piotr.musiol@bolt.eu","Piotr Musioł","so this shows, that from the beehive task perspective, the task was being created while beeing assigned to 19039 (Alfred).  At 15.12.2025.\n\nAnd the task was unassigned only at 15.01.2026","2026-01-16T12:53:13.361Z"],["3815980","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","From our side, and case events Alfred was unassigned at 15.12.2025. I have no knowledge how that converts to Beehive tasks, it is beyond scope of automations.","2026-01-16T12:53:13.981Z"],["3815981","SAI-1412","SAI","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","{quote}I have no knowledge how that converts to Beehive tasks{quote}\n\nSo far the agreement was that post escalation, the source of truth of assignments is the BeehiveTask entity.\nOnce BeehiveTask is created (this happens on escalation), assignment data is only synced back to SupportCase entity as read-only.\nAny arbitrary modifications to assignments of SupportCase do not change the state of the assignment in the system.\nI believe that in this case the assignment was not cleaned up prior to escalation. New assignment to a bot seemed to have happened after escalation, which is not supported by our system.\nI believe it should be in scope of the automations to keep the invariants as agreed - or discuss how the system can be extended if you require different behaviours.","2026-01-16T12:53:14.773Z"],["3815982","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","{quote}New assignment to a bot seemed to have happened after escalation, which is not supported by our system.{quote}\n\nWhich one are you referring to?","2026-01-16T12:53:15.630Z"],["3815983","SAI-1412","SAI","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","This might have been a temporary bug, race condition etc.\nLet's check if there are more cases like this and plan actions accordingly to the volume of the problem.","2026-01-16T12:53:16.389Z"],["3815984","SAI-1412","SAI","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","{quote}Which one are you referring to?{quote}\n\nAfter escalation on 13:54:56\nThere was a bot assignment at 13:54:57\nBot was later quickly unassigned, but at this point the case was already escalated and assignment modifications on SupportCase entity are not propagated anywhere.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8Q7STT4P/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A8Q7STT4P/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-16T12:53:16.986Z"],["3815985","SAI-1412","SAI","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","{quote}entity are not propagated anywhere{quote}\n\nOr maybe - are not ensured to be propagated\n\nIt would be a race condition if escalation and assignment + unassignment happen roughly at the same time.\n\nOn case escalation BeehiveTask does take the initial assignment as an input - and it got the bot assignee (this is a one time propagation of assignment from SupportCase to BeehiveTask).\n\nSo escalation event must have been processed somewhere between bot being assigned and bot being unassigned.","2026-01-16T12:53:17.507Z"],["3815986","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","yea, keep us posted in this case about future such cases. Let's see if it is more common","2026-01-16T12:53:18.127Z"],["3815987","SAI-1412","SAI","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","I'd recommend checking if there are any existing cases like this by exploring data-api","2026-01-16T12:53:18.680Z"],["3815988","SAI-1412","SAI","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Agents spotted one after a month. There may be more which weren't noticed","2026-01-16T12:53:19.280Z"],["3815989","LSS-59952","LSS","gabriel.souza@bolt.eu","Gabriel Gonçalo","Hello team!\n\nSince João is out of office and the case was being handled via his email, we sent the response and documents to the PSP agent email address: [vrpinheiral@psp.pt|mailto:vrpinheiral@psp.pt] [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/724380840]. (/) \n\n\n\n","2026-01-16T12:53:21.656Z"],["3815993","PFI-834227","PFI","dennis.abet@bolt-outsource.eu","Dennis Abet","!Screenshot_20260116-143327.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:53:59.093Z"],["3815995","HS-27969","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hey [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] !\n\nI will currently close this ticket, as the process may take time and currently no more action is needed. \n[~accountid:6390559a2acfad92d7b59f11] can keep You posted on DPAE via slack as well or You can reach out again via this closed ticket or payroll Jira. \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-16T12:54:14.655Z"],["3815998","LSS-61531","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343731?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343731?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T12:54:38.277Z"],["3816003","LSS-61716","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","[^Brokers' Appointment in WORD ( Not Sole).docx] _(13 kB)_\n\n[^MIB_CTOBA_PRIV_PLY_V13_2025_03_13.docx.pdf] _(684 kB)_","2026-01-16T12:55:49.497Z"],["3816004","LSS-61716","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nTriin Soon-Köster has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-16T12:55:51.227Z"],["3816006","WD-22570","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi Prajwal, \n\ndid it work?\n\nthanks\n\noana ","2026-01-16T12:56:29.028Z"],["3816007","PFI-834156","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi, what do you mean by “has not received”? if the documents are generated in admin (the link you provided), they will also be available in the fleet owner protal. Is it possible that he had logged in to the driver portal and this is why he didn’t notice the invoices? ","2026-01-16T12:56:34.444Z"],["3816008","DRX-27727","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27729 has been resolved","2026-01-16T12:56:40.854Z"],["3816009","DSR-3777","DSR","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] thank you for looping me in. \nFYI, I’ve asked Brian to clarify the relevant timeframe [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A7DAJ0A8M/p1768565499071359?thread_ts=1768554887.066709&cid=C0A7DAJ0A8M] and followed up via DM to speed things up. I’m still waiting for his response, and as soon as I receive it, I’ll proceed with amending the responsive data.\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ","2026-01-16T12:57:06.358Z"],["3816011","WD-22512","WD","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Hi Demetri,\n\ndid it work?\n\nthanks\n\noana","2026-01-16T12:57:41.505Z"],["3816014","PFI-834232","PFI","otis.wella@bolt-outsource.eu","Otis Wella","!{180EE17D-1171-4706-BEFC-86800C88E087}-20260116-125740.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T12:58:01.435Z"],["3816015","CSP-453","CSP","olga.kuchina@bolt.eu","Olga Kuchina","26W3: finished development of model configuration files and logic, now working on developing query and preprocessing steps for version 2 of the model","2026-01-16T12:58:01.455Z"],["3816032","SRED-1075","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-16T12:58:33.578Z"],["3816037","PFI-833208","PFI","sasha.maletskaya@bolt.eu","Aliaksandra Maletskaya","Hi, any updates?","2026-01-16T12:59:34.024Z"],["3816038","CNT-377","CNT","aleksandra.onutsina@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Onutšina","[~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] They don’t need an exact copy, so they can kickoff their work 🙂 ","2026-01-16T12:59:34.358Z"],["3816041","WD-22594","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","This will be changed in this promotion, still in progress\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.58.57.png|width=899,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.58.57.png\"!","2026-01-16T13:00:13.151Z"],["3816044","FPD-1414","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","Hello everyone 👋\n\nResults for the last round of hyperparameter tuning backtest are done. The results are [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IQ975aObNKR89MUUu98YZCaHRzlfjbrPG0eSy6ObpBg/edit?usp=sharing].The most interesting part, in my opinion, is the portfolio-level performance for finished orders and GMV local (below).Overall, the results mostly confirm what we saw in the previous backtest: 50 trials often perform worse than 15 trials.\n\nFurther insights are:\n\n* 100 trials is never the best\n* Around 30 trials seems to be the sweet spot and is often the best-performing {{n_trials}}\n\nThat said, the numbers are quite close, so some of the differences could just be noise.One thing does seem clear though: changing the number of hyperparameter trials is not really a low-hanging fruit for improving accuracy. The impact on performance is smaller than we hoped.Based on these numbers, I would propose reducing the number of hyperparameter tuning trials to 30. It is much faster than 50 and appears to perform slightly better overall.Btw, I used the new backtesting accuracy job and it worked really well. Great job [@rodrigo.ponzetto|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U084MB0E867] 👏","2026-01-16T13:00:24.321Z"],["3816045","LSS-61718","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","[^Nova Mobility UG - Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (2).pdf] _(133 kB)_","2026-01-16T13:01:09.574Z"],["3816046","PFI-834131","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! There’s no invoicing records nor invoice, so we don’t really have anything to refund to them. Afaik we don’t even charge them - we may book the amount, but if there’s no successful order, we don’t charge it and release the amount. However, we do not deal with charges on billing side. Please reach out to customer payments 🙂 ","2026-01-16T13:01:10.665Z"],["3816047","LSS-61140","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] I hope that you are well ! \n\nPlease find attached the Convention to be signed by Ahto Kink for Bolt Operations OÜ. We should partially sign it and the Authority for Social Relations on Employment Platforms (ARPE) will countersign it and send us back the duly signed version. \n\nThank you !\n\n[^CONVENTION ARPE - partage et traitement de données _BOLT.VFIN.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:01:13.336Z"],["3816048","PFI-834131","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team!  🍔\n\n- Provider/Courier payment didn't reflect in their balance: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/503\n- Provider/Courier didn't receive payout: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/319\n- Eater had issues with the payment: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/316\n- Early cashout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/556\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/317\n- App and backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76\n- Balance and Invoices issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/318\n- Invoice Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-16T13:01:31.104Z"],["3816049","LSS-57722","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:62e0e5a93257defaf50d1e34].\n\nThey have made the following amendment regarding payment, in the contract. \n\n“_1115,92€, o montante total corresponde a 12 meses de assinatura, porém a forma de pagamento poderá ser flexível, podendo ser à vista, 30-60 dias, em 3 meses, ou mensal._”\n\nCould you please clarify what were exactly the terms of payment agreed? This clauses results very unclear, as it does not specify wether they expect the payment to be made in totality, in the beginning of the service, or if the payment is expected in installments and, if yes, what is the periodicity.\n\nThe commercial proposal (it says “_Total a vista (pronto pagamento), Condições de faturamento: Após assinatura do aceite desta proposta_”) suggests that the full payment is to be made after the signature.\n\nAlso, I’m assuming the amount is excluding VAT, but this is not specified anywhere.\n\nTherefore, I would recommend this aspects to be clarified before moving forward with signature.\n\n[^Proposta Comercial Bolt & Bizneo HR (2).pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:02:15.578Z"],["3816050","CSDA-301","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-16T13:02:18.835Z"],["3816051","SREC-376","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","Hey, Happy New Year! {{atlantis plan}} is failing with\n\n{noformat}creating new workspace: mkdir /home/atlantis/.atlantis/repos/bolteu/terraform-main/15182/default: no space left on device{noformat}","2026-01-16T13:02:31.384Z"],["3816052","SREC-376","SREC",null,"Slack","[Amin Khoshnood|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01UZQN086B/p1767601758681939?thread_ts=1767601758.681939&cid=C01UZQN086B|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01UZQN086B/p1767601758681939?thread_ts=1767601758.681939&cid=C01UZQN086B|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T13:02:32.615Z"],["3816053","SREC-376","SREC","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","All green now.","2026-01-16T13:02:32.790Z"],["3816054","WD-22570","WD","prajwal.neupane@bolt.eu","Prajwal Neupane","HI [~accountid:712020:80f31809-0e9d-4c0f-8939-db5dd3d77922] ,\n\nThis one worked at least for now.\n\nThank you.\n\nBest regards,\n\nPrajwal","2026-01-16T13:03:27.672Z"],["3816056","DELIVERY-1237","DELIVERY","ali.zeynalov@bolt.eu","Ali Zeynalov","26W03\n- Options & Option groups UI merge released\n- Started to plan & a bit of of coding on Merging UI for Product Forms. Will be continuing so, next week.\n","2026-01-16T13:03:35.156Z"],["3816057","LSS-61584","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:5cf40694-0837-4f72-b92a-c4936529065f]! The special terms were signed, please see attached. You can share them with the Partner. Let me know if you have any questions.\n\n\n\n[^2026.01 Bolt Support Services BG Sombrero 2 Bolt Food Special Terms (signed).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T13:03:36.530Z"],["3816059","LSS-61700","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","Hi Ruska!\n\nCould you describe the commercial side of the planned partnership? I.e. what is the partnership about, what do we have to do, what do they have to do etc. ","2026-01-16T13:04:17.279Z"],["3816063","PFI-831038","PFI","lawrancetshepo.motsepe@bolt.eu","Lawrance Tshepo Motsepe","Hi Team,\n\nI am handling a query from a customer requesting VAT tax invoices for their December rides. They are using a work profile with a business payment method and require these documents for tax reclaiming purposes.\n\nWe currently have access to their standard invoices, but these reflect 0% VAT.\n\n*Could you please advise on the following:*\n\n# *Can we provide a VAT invoice?* (My understanding is that we cannot if the partner-driver is not VAT registered).\n# *Approved Messaging:* If we cannot provide a VAT invoice, are we permitted to explain the reason using South African SARS regulations?\n\n*Proposed Explanation to the Customer:* I would like to clarify to the customer that under South African law, VAT registration is only mandatory if taxable turnover exceeds R1 million per annum. As individual drivers generally do not meet this threshold, they are not VAT registered and are legally prohibited from charging VAT. Therefore, the invoice provided is a valid document reflecting 0% VAT.\n\nIs it acceptable to share this explanation regarding the R1 million threshold to resolve their query?\n\nThanks,","2026-01-16T13:05:22.522Z"],["3816064","MLC-3877","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W3*\n\nI’ve created the [document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FYB4jhw7TY8VVpZN_AXBnnjAxEoSBE0cQfCVoyTllG4/edit?tab=t.jj4dk1cjt4hm] that contains the copies that I ran through Poe. \nSo far, Poe is more efficient in rewriting courier comms. Ticket is also created for the content team to review. Just waiting for the feedback on the content and will move on with HTML template. ","2026-01-16T13:05:39.489Z"],["3816067","MLC-3725","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W3*\n\nI’ve created the [document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FYB4jhw7TY8VVpZN_AXBnnjAxEoSBE0cQfCVoyTllG4/edit?tab=t.jj4dk1cjt4hm] that contains the copies that I ran through Poe. \nSo far, Poe is more efficient in rewriting courier comms. Ticket is also created for the content team to review. Just waiting for the feedback on the content and will move on with HTML template. ","2026-01-16T13:06:13.724Z"],["3816068","FX-3648","FX","adam.sokolowski@bolt.eu","Adam Sokołowski","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] can we make the Lock-in level field visible in the table all the time?\nIf I understood correctly I will only be able to see the lock-in level field when I click the edit button (pencil icon).\nOr did I misunderstand that?","2026-01-16T13:06:23.007Z"],["3816070","MLC-3884","MLC","robert.pirnuta@bolt.eu","Robert-Mihai Pîrnuță","*Update:*\n\n* Email template done\n* In-app stories Crowdin strings sent to localization\n\n*Next steps:*\n\n* Setting up in app stories once localization is done\n* Setting up Braze email","2026-01-16T13:06:37.558Z"],["3816074","FPD-1509","FPD","andrei.kuchev@bolt.eu","Andrei Kuchev","[~accountid:5df3830edfde6b0e555bc5c1] Just to clarify:\n\n# Including / excluding markets is easy - this is already supported and can be configured\n# The engineering work I mentioned was mostly related to the switch from SB+-3 to SB+-25, specifically the ability to support both versions, so we can estimate how it affects optimization.","2026-01-16T13:06:50.720Z"],["3816075","WD-22594","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","This has already been changed and it’s under review","2026-01-16T13:07:05.166Z"],["3816076","INT-803","INT","artem.markov@bolt.eu","Artem Markov","26W3:\n\nMore translation strings on transaction history side\n\nMerged bolt logic cleanups","2026-01-16T13:07:13.508Z"],["3816077","RNTL-30051","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","New event {{Finish Ride Browse Passes Tap}}\n\n[https://mixpanel.com/project/1165336/view/32804/app/insights#oxrJAg1RNFJ9|https://mixpanel.com/project/1165336/view/32804/app/insights#oxrJAg1RNFJ9|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:07:43.412Z"],["3816078","DELIVERY-690","DELIVERY","mark.bogdanov@bolt.eu","Mark Bogdanov","26W03:\nWe started QA for the 1.50 release on this week. It includes multiple features, so it takes a while. \n\nFor now no critical issues were found for the {{strict}} replacement mode, but {{strict_with_no_additional_items}} has some issues.\n\nMost of the non breaking issues are already fixed and ready for the review for the next patch version. ","2026-01-16T13:07:45.250Z"],["3816079","WD-22595","WD","kristinliis.ratto@bolt.eu","Kristin-Liis Rätto","Bolt Operations OÜ as well","2026-01-16T13:07:50.199Z"],["3816080","LSS-60674","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:5cf40694-0837-4f72-b92a-c4936529065f]! I checked the document you shared and there are no comments that we added at all. Perhaps there was a misunderstanding? We replied to all their questions and responded to every suggestion. Can you please double check with them? Could it be that they don’t speak English?","2026-01-16T13:07:52.497Z"],["3816081","LSS-61132","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","[~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] Please note that this is not a Fleet Deal Agreement. ","2026-01-16T13:07:59.252Z"],["3816083","INCIDENT-175","INCIDENT","kostiantyn.tsykulenko@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Tsykulenko","Was not needed, the problems was the cluster shut down due to lack of activity cause the token was inactive, but we do want to keep the auto-shutdown behaviour, there’s not easy workaround here, just a good to know point for updating Looker connections","2026-01-16T13:08:19.270Z"],["3816084","DELIVERY-1355","DELIVERY","mark.bogdanov@bolt.eu","Mark Bogdanov","26W03:\nWe started QA for the 1.50 release on this week.\n\nCurrently in review. ","2026-01-16T13:08:26.410Z"],["3816085","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] \n\n# *A3:* I used shorter copy because people’s attention span in bars is quite short. It should therefore be as straightforward as possible.\n# *Table talker:* Same comment regarding the copy. I would use the same visual on all three sides because it’s very straightforward and avoids unnecessary information noise.\n# *Bar coaster:* Same comment regarding the copy.\n\nPlease take a look [here|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/vb7ilkqvm66wpsfb78q09/ACYlV4ofjCXDuRRTbKLe5wQ?rlkey=3pt9gtjvzyflq4cti6ms8ggds&dl=0] and let me know if everything works for you. \n\nAlso please update me regarding cutline for bar coasters and promo codes when you have more information. 🙏 \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T13:08:37.526Z"],["3816086","DELIVERY-1699","DELIVERY","nursultan.yerezhepov@bolt.eu","Nursultan Yerezhepov","26W03:\n- Many support requests from the picker app, integrations that were fixed with the help from domain teams. \n- There’s an [issue|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C026LFZ44SJ/p1768232559317009] with purchasing prices in inventory. There’s a discussion with possible solutions but still no solution was created.\n- exposed fields for CDC in groc selling price\n","2026-01-16T13:08:52.513Z"],["3816088","LSS-47933","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hey, in preparation for our call on Monday I put together the attached table summarising the changes x priority level x likelihood of acceptance by the dealer. Feel free to have a look ahead of the call. Thanks!\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VBDlTaVcHipzHnd8Y7yun6_8Dmxo1YHByy5Rjnl87ZU/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VBDlTaVcHipzHnd8Y7yun6_8Dmxo1YHByy5Rjnl87ZU/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:08:58.319Z"],["3816089","CCM-22279","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hey Toyosi, \n\nWe have enrolled the listed agents in the requested course and updated their profile information. The course should appear in their LMS now. \n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS Training team ","2026-01-16T13:09:00.988Z"],["3816091","FX-3657","FX","adam.sokolowski@bolt.eu","Adam Sokołowski","[~accountid:712020:d3fd53e6-f124-4770-a577-b09d6688566f] please review the ticket","2026-01-16T13:09:03.302Z"],["3816092","PFI-834234","PFI","ramon.pagliarini@bolt-outsource.eu","Ramón Giménez Pagliarini","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 10.08.29.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:09:05.137Z"],["3816093","PFI-834234","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T13:09:07.478Z"],["3816094","LSS-61486","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] Since there’s no further action needed from the Privacy side here, could you please fill out the Cognito form and share it in this ticket?\n\nOnce that’s done, please share the link to the form and then we can go ahead and close it. Thanks!","2026-01-16T13:09:11.261Z"],["3816097","LSS-61646","LSS","rita.agnilleri@bolt.eu","Rita Agnilleri","HI [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] the 3PL refused to collect the vehicles without notice at the moment, so.\n\n* Yesterday I’ve already sent an email as notice regarding point 6.3:\n_\"The Company may reduce the Services at any time, at its sole discretion, by giving the Contractor fifteen (15) days' prior notice (the \"Reduced Service Period\") and may terminate the Reduced Service Period by giving the Contractor fifteen (15) days' prior notice.\"_\n* Both agreements will expire on February 18, so please prepare a legal notice stating that we do not intend to renew our current agreements.\n\nI’ll share FYI the 3PL email via Gmail.\n\nThanks\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-16T13:09:54.055Z"],["3816098","CCM-22280","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hey Peace, \n\nWe have enrolled the listed agents in the requested course and updated their profile information. The course should appear in their LMS now. \n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS Training team ","2026-01-16T13:09:57.412Z"],["3816099","DO-5799","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Hi!\n\nThanks, I’ve added this to our backlog 🙂 ","2026-01-16T13:10:01.961Z"],["3816100","DO-5799","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Have a good day!","2026-01-16T13:10:15.146Z"],["3816105","WD-22595","WD","dagmar.olesk@bolt.eu","Dagmar Olesk","Approved for the following entities:\n* Bolt Operations OÜ\n* Bolt Technology OÜ\n* Bolt Holdings OÜ","2026-01-16T13:11:30.056Z"],["3816108","LSS-60580","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nI hope you are doing well.\n\nMay you please advise if you have any feedback on this contract?\n\nThank you.","2026-01-16T13:12:02.249Z"],["3816109","DELIVERY-1706","DELIVERY","mark.bogdanov@bolt.eu","Mark Bogdanov","26W03:\nWe started QA for the 1.50 release on this week. It includes multiple features, including total order price.\n\nFor now we implemented basic version of it, which calculates using user’s price for items in order, and for any basket adjustments we use basic price. \n\nWe also implemented this featured under the picker region config, so it would be shown only primary for 3P partners. \n\nWe also decided to use 2 digit precision instead of 6 digits. ","2026-01-16T13:12:07.773Z"],["3816110","XP-3060","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","When trying to fix issue by aggregating to user level, there was still a sizeable difference between CUPED and default metrics on the group average, which are expected to match with proper implementation.\n\nAfter investigation, found that it was being caused by the {{AVG}} statements in the CUPED CTEs. These ignore {{NULL}} , which are common in v3 metrics, even for metrics which should have none (those that count all users in the {{count_expression}}, e.g. user spend has nulls in [table|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/blob/93258eff5bb48037872a8e304b4dfa5ceeff60d5/experimentation/experimentation/ab_processor/v3/tables/targeting_user/rh/targeting_user_test_rh_table.sql#L192] but counts all users in v3 [definition|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/blob/master/experimentation/experimentation/ab_processor/v3/metrics/targeting_user/rh/kpi/avg_user_gmv.yaml].\n\n[~accountid:712020:53be219b-8d47-4ba0-8cd1-a8b886503164] in v4 do we have guarantees that metrics that include all users will have no nulls?\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:40cb7816-0b3b-4f87-ae87-8ac607ccf2c0] ","2026-01-16T13:12:09.850Z"],["3816112","PFI-834235","PFI","victoria.akinfenwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Akinfenwa","!Screenshot_20260116-135741 101.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:12:10.601Z"],["3816113","PIF-3287","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the User Story!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-16T13:12:29.798Z"],["3816116","RNTL-30460","RNTL","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","According to the [+Remediation guidelines+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEC/pages/3987112061/Application+Vulnerability+Management], a “High” priority finding timeline is as follows, by latest date:\n\n* *29.01.2026 -* Develop a remediation plan\n* *27.03.2026 -* Have the final fix ready\n* *30.03.2026 -* Fix is tested","2026-01-16T13:13:28.965Z"],["3816118","MQA-4248","MQA","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","[DRIVERAPP-T3728 (1.0) |https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/262296722] - Location permission ​request is displayed after I tap \"let's go\" on the step 3\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 15-07-48_1.MP4]","2026-01-16T13:13:46.743Z"],["3816126","LSS-60863","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:605e0642039f310071424017] !\nWe believe this can be signed.\nHowever, we note that, even though the dates of performance and payments are in the past, the signature date will be current, which could raise confusion or create interpretive ambiguities in the future. \nI would suggest, then, maybe adding a simple clarifying clause, that can eliminate any doubt about the retrospective nature of the contract.\n\nSomething like the following:\n\n_“_*_Cláusula de Formalização Retroativa_*\n_As Partes reconhecem que o presente Contrato visa formalizar, por escrito, uma relação contratual anteriormente acordada entre elas por via de comunicações eletrónicas e ordens de publicidade, cuja execução material e financeira já foi integralmente realizada. Assim, para todos os efeitos legais, este Contrato tem natureza meramente formalizadora e aplica-se exclusivamente à campanha publicitária veiculada nos termos constantes do Quadro Resumo, durante os períodos ali indicados.”_\n\nCan you ask JCDecaux if they agree?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T13:15:31.585Z"],["3816127","VULN-1459","VULN","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","Mixpanel events to see how frequently it’s abused [https://mixpanel.com/project/1165336/view/32804/app/events#SLv4j1646KGG|https://mixpanel.com/project/1165336/view/32804/app/events#SLv4j1646KGG|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:15:33.538Z"],["3816136","RLONE-589","RLONE","anton.berggren@bolt.eu","Anton Berggren","* [Current NPS Survey|https://rideswithbolt.eu.typeform.com/to/zpY0xSr3#token=xxxxx&cohort=xxxxx]\n** Survey frequency is weekly every Tuesday limited to 200 drivers each week and the same driver wont receive it until 90 days are complete.\n** [Survey responses |https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1oV-1MC8w2zijo1_70oHqMigFYEpyfzocb-_nOuynitU/edit?gid=0#gid=0]since April 2025.","2026-01-16T13:19:44.613Z"],["3816139","CNT-460","CNT","birgit.jurivete@bolt.eu","Birgit Jürivete","[~accountid:614ad8fe47a8b5006f846ec4] SUPER odd, all of them were fine yesterday. Could it be something didn’t end up saving automatically? Fixed RO, KE, LV","2026-01-16T13:20:06.449Z"],["3816141","CNT-460","CNT","birgit.jurivete@bolt.eu","Birgit Jürivete","[~accountid:624c636af40798007059caa8] But KE can be skipped then since we don’t have ads","2026-01-16T13:20:29.108Z"],["3816144","PFI-832470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Apologies, but that not enough information. \n\nThe company is under Intermediary model: do you want reissue of all Ride invoice; only SF invoices? Statements?\n\nSeptember - December? From which date/invoice to which date/invoice exactly.","2026-01-16T13:21:08.286Z"],["3816145","LSS-61132","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] , can you be more specific/clear? what do you mean? \n\nthanks\n\nElisabeta ","2026-01-16T13:21:08.426Z"],["3816147","PAW-14941","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-16T13:21:30.023Z"],["3816148","HS-28950","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-16T13:21:32.130Z"],["3816149","LSS-61708","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b6a69643-6b58-4e2d-bb7f-26d32c94aff9] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.[^Zmluva s BOLT_15.01.2026 (1c27c1dc-34c2-42ce-98b1-a8a80eef483a).pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:21:34.131Z"],["3816150","PIF-3287","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-builder, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-16T13:21:36.103Z"],["3816152","MLC-663","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","+*W3:*+\n\n*Updates:* \n\n* Created new template for comms according to Dale’s and Joana’s comments.\n* Got correct thresholds from Joana\n* Agreed with Dale and Joana to send this comm only to Mid-market and SMB merchants. We can use custom attribute _provider_traits_ does not contain _segmentation-enterprise-all_ to exclude enterprise accounts. \n\n*Next steps:*\n\n* Get a green light for the template for merchants with one and with multiple locations. Send comms to localisation.","2026-01-16T13:21:44.722Z"],["3816153","RDS-1247","RDS","julia.mitzinneck@bolt.eu","Julia Mitzinneck","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] also worth considering if we should include price info more explicitly [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L23PNYKZ/p1768569552143139?thread_ts=1768316340.962099&cid=C02L23PNYKZ|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L23PNYKZ/p1768569552143139?thread_ts=1768316340.962099&cid=C02L23PNYKZ|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:21:48.133Z"],["3816154","LSS-61421","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Do we have the exact list of cars that will be transferred?","2026-01-16T13:21:51.766Z"],["3816156","PFI-834241","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-16T13:22:13.719Z"],["3816158","LSS-60580","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] my feedback was highlighted in the ticket below \n\nReviewed order [Bolt Singular Order .docx|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R0V3ubJzLL92aIT8cjy8kpEdHSwF1hCC/edit]\n\nPlease check my comments.\n\nOpen question about liability limit, currently it’s 12 months fees. How much potentially will we pay to Singular ? ","2026-01-16T13:22:30.459Z"],["3816159","LSS-59641","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:712020:26721b53-6340-4f94-beff-a16789e04516] \nJust checking in on this. Could you please confirm whether the steps previously outlined by Alon were followed?\n\nLet me know if support is still needed from our side.","2026-01-16T13:22:44.890Z"],["3816160","PFI-834199","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, can you fill out the data manually? \n\nSeems like some bug with Fetch WP button, would be okay to just manually type out data and Reissue as usual; ","2026-01-16T13:23:10.912Z"],["3816161","MLC-3847","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","*W3:* \n\n* Project kick-off: reached out to Roberts to confirm new reasons that we need to add ([thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02HG4Z5DC7/p1768460403112149])","2026-01-16T13:23:17.863Z"],["3816163","PFI-834229","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T13:24:06.411Z"],["3816164","LSS-61702","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:db8c9f27-fadf-4c29-98f8-4024f9ce6c19] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^BOLT BUSINESS IMAGINE (1) (be0f3a83-73f9-4ec3-8ed9-e84412f9195b).pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:24:11.394Z"],["3816165","MLC-2749","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 16th - No Updates*+\n\n* +*Status*+\n** *Current* [*performance*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ijbpEjqRFQ5y0B8ptFT_S4BitRAfjWEiPzWD1QkHTAw/edit?gid=195435210#gid=195435210] *of what is currently live:*\n*** RO and SK showed the strongest improvements, with higher open rates (+8% RO, +34% SK) and solid conversion uplift (+33% RO, +67% SK), indicating better message relevance.\n*** CZ saw a major open-rate lift (+48%) and conversion growth (+33%), with also growth of CTR from 0.00% to 1.98%, but also an increase in unsubscribe rate from 0.00% to 1.40% (17 usubscribes)\n*** AZ underperformed across the funnel, with declines in opens (-1%), conversions (-6%), and a complete drop in clicks and unsubscribes.\n** We worked with data ream to analyse order frequency by tier (T2/T3/T4) to replace the current blanket “30 days since last order” rule with tier-specific thresholds that better reflect actual behaviour.\n** We measured days between consecutive orders, split by tier, for 2025 and priority markets. Used the 80th percentile to benchmark “typical” reorder timing and excluded the first 3 months of company lifetime to reduce early-life bias. This shows 80% of T4s reorder with 23 days, while T3 sits at 3 days and T2 at 1 day.\n** We will test new entry points, depending on tier: T4 - 24 days, T3/T2: ~7 days (to catch outliers, avoid noise)\n* +*Next steps*+\n** Adjust segments with the new definitions - on Tuesday\n** Clone out for the rest of the markets and push live - Next week (allowing one week of testing new approach on a set of markets)\n** 2026: Redo templates after confirmation on working template.\n** Dummy templates in translations\n** Implement for CEE markets - then move of to rest of markets","2026-01-16T13:24:15.800Z"],["3816166","FRAUDOPS-1014","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","h3. *Blocked partners*\n\nSo, in general we block around 30 partners per month for the bad_pay scenarios: \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.18.46.png|width=769,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.18.46.png\"!\n\nComparing patterns for the bad payment suspension and reverting to logic on uncovered amount picks up about 2 block cases and 1.5K eur of GMV weekly that would not have been suspended if we had a different logic. \n\nAnnually this makes a difference: \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.59.08.png|width=408,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 14.59.08.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 15.16.06.png|width=407,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 15.16.06.png\"!\n\n*In comparison to total blocking rate, this suggest a rough 30% false positive rate due to the faulty input.*\n\nAnnually we are blocking 49K€ of GMV for 75 partners making it cost around 650€ per each block/driver action. ","2026-01-16T13:24:25.349Z"],["3816167","PFI-834213","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team is unfortunately not able to assist with pricing, discount or promo code related questions. \nPricing is decided by the vertical and the customer payments team does not have any impact on it. \nCould you please raise a ticket with the verticals technical support team instead. \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2]\n\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T13:24:24.832Z"],["3816169","LSS-61689","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60a37337391e56006e62277c] ! Please give me an access to the doc.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T13:25:24.410Z"],["3816171","FRAUD-5500","FRAUD","liisi.laasik@bolt.eu","Liisi Dovbnja","Compared checks:\nfamily member order: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_order_request/9594124689|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_order_request/9594124689]\nfamily owner order: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_order_request/9580365118|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_order_request/9580365118]\n\nfamily member order: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_rental_request/686015254|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_rental_request/686015254]\nfamily owner oder: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_rental_request/685348598|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_rental_request/685348598]\n\nQuestions: \n\n* why does the family owner order have an owner data block? \n* why family.owner_related.users.unpaid_booking_stats is null","2026-01-16T13:25:28.833Z"],["3816172","MLC-2350","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 16th*+\n\n* Deepdives completed\n* Noticed an overall drop across Business Account, which in turn affected some Business User comms. Root cause seems to be seasonality.\n* Work Profile in an overall healthy state.","2026-01-16T13:25:35.613Z"],["3816173","PAW-14959","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T13:25:49.261Z"],["3816174","PAW-14958","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T13:25:51.282Z"],["3816175","PAW-14956","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T13:26:02.052Z"],["3816179","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742]! Can I send an email to the rider to ask for an IBAN? Do you want to draft one or can I keep it free form? At the moment we only have a card linked to the rider’s account -card/798cb14c-ae36-40f8-b7e0-e715e2e0a351-, but I don’t think accounting will be able to send a payment on it.","2026-01-16T13:26:43.869Z"],["3816180","DSR-3191","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]! I’ve sent the response and the data prepared [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/705908280]. Thank you!","2026-01-16T13:26:50.148Z"],["3816181","LSS-61666","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] ! will be done on Moday, since Ahto is working remotely today🙏 ","2026-01-16T13:26:53.870Z"],["3816182","PFI-834244","PFI","bernice.bediako@bolt.eu","Bernice Asiedua Bediako","!IMG_2933.PNG|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:26:58.535Z"],["3816183","DELIVERY-910","DELIVERY","francesco.cherubini@bolt.eu","Francesco Cherubini","26W02\nDevelopment is moved to integration of the demand forecast with multipliers:\n- Validation is done\n- Agreed on process and template for pilot start next week","2026-01-16T13:27:52.806Z"],["3816187","PFI-834198","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI’m not seeing any restrictions from commerce side. The users is not being blocked by any fraud rules either. \n\nThe user was able to place a cash order 16/01/2026, 14:56. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282417695?cityId=1965|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282417695?cityId=1965]\n\nMaybe the merchant the user was trying to order from did not support cash order? \nProbably better to ask the delivery technical support team for assistance if the user is still having this issue. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T13:28:24.199Z"],["3816190","MLC-2962","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 16th*+\n\n* *Company VAT* - Decided to drop it for now until we get more insights on how Growth team is handling this. Current volumes do not warrant an automation\n* *Relaunch of Card BINs / Geofencing* - Templates to be rebuilt and tested next week. Will start with Card BINs and test Signal sequentially to avoid noise - will need a grace period of 1-2 week to ascertain that everything is running as expected and results signal towards an uplift.","2026-01-16T13:28:50.128Z"],["3816191","WFM-10018","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","Roles assigned. Please proceed with the queue assignment","2026-01-16T13:29:08.657Z"],["3816193","WD-20008","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:6285ef56bd640f0068aeb51b] ! Is this ticket still relevant? if yes- how urgent is it? ","2026-01-16T13:29:49.753Z"],["3816194","LSS-61666","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","noted, thank you Aleksandra! I would appreciate if it could be arranged in a way that it will be sent out still on Monday, if this is possible. Time is tight unfortunately..","2026-01-16T13:30:06.738Z"],["3816195","RCE-357","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768570194214469]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-357] `Investigate auto block on verified car documents` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T13:30:09.036Z"],["3816198","PFI-834190","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can confirm the refund was issued for EUR 8.21 on Dec 18, 2025, 02:19:09 GMT+2\t\n\nYou can provide the customer the refund reference 74987505352000012743088  to locate the payment. \n\nIf the user still claims non-receipt then please ask them to provide their bank statement as proof. It should be dated from 18th of December until present. Please make sure the account details, account name and bank name/logo are visible. \n\nOnce received the customer payments team would be able to investigate further. \n\n\n[^Refund_Letter_HHTSRBK29HRBDSQ9_CKVXR6654NK74MG3.pdf]\n\nCheers,\nMarten","2026-01-16T13:30:52.866Z"],["3816199","PFI-833449","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Indeed, these are the correct amounts without VAT. For understanding why this specific amount was paid out, the courier needs to contact their FO as they are responsible for the payout. ","2026-01-16T13:31:04.179Z"],["3816200","LSS-61719","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T13:31:07.282Z"],["3816201","LSS-60674","LSS","rayko.chakarov@bolt.eu","Rayko Chakarov","What i understood form the email is that , those with the yellow , they want to be changed or deleted from the document","2026-01-16T13:31:12.264Z"],["3816204","DSR-3195","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Thank you for your help, [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]! I’ve sent the response [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/706685946].","2026-01-16T13:31:26.362Z"],["3816206","WD-22593","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","He should be able to do it now.","2026-01-16T13:31:40.113Z"],["3816212","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[~accountid:712020:dbc22d70-1983-4414-80b3-27f087787ae4] Yes, please ask them for their bank details. You can mention that the Legal team is still evaluating the request, but obtaining their bank details would expedite the process.\n\n\n\nInternally (not to be discussed with the rider), we will draft a letter to acknowledge receipt of the mediation request and offer a refund of the difference via bank transfer.\n\nWhile the rider’s request for 100€ on their Bolt balance is disproportionate and unjustified, we need to refund the difference directly to their account rather than through a promo code to ensure compliance and support our position regarding the 100€.","2026-01-16T13:32:25.054Z"],["3816215","IOTTEAM-316","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","DTR pin works fine. \nCan’t test RI ping since there seems to be a problem with SMS reception (SMS reception toggles RI pin). Maybe toggle the pin directly by an external source [~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] \nAlso if to compare the signal connection to eBike IOT then on eBike IOT there are also pullups on MCU side.","2026-01-16T13:32:41.091Z"],["3816219","BR-3857","BR","triinu.tasa@bolt.eu","Triinu Tasa","*Daniil Musienko*  [Today at 1:51 PM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1768564271773759?thread_ts=1768489041.717409&cid=CNV6QPRFT]\n\n\nPlease, discuss the project requirements with [@marija.skiljevic|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U07BYED6E9E] and the Payments team.\nI don't know the context of your project, but I see potential issues:\n\n* what will you show in case of cash payments\n* what will you show in case of APMs, when we actually do a charge in one go before the ride, because APMs don't support preauth\n* What will you show when we cancel the original pre-authorisation and do a new one to capture a bigger amount after the ride\n* What will you show in case of Pay After The Ride\n* ...","2026-01-16T13:33:09.620Z"],["3816222","LSS-60879","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:33e8acff-2d71-4964-b18f-c5e64f82b97d] \nJust checking in on this ticket. Could you please confirm whether the steps outlined earlier by Alon have been completed (token revocation, password reset, and confirmation that no earnings were withdrawn)?","2026-01-16T13:33:53.185Z"],["3816223","RDXENG-4586","RDXENG","veronika.gainetdinova@bolt.eu","Veronika Gainetdinova","Updated in scope of this task:\n\n* Cancellation reasons design\n* Color of inactive “Live location” icon\n\n“Live location” active state is lottie animation, we don’t have a new lottie right now, will be updated later.\n\nDriver avatar accessory and Get directions banner are BE tasks.","2026-01-16T13:34:00.042Z"],["3816224","DSR-3157","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Aligning with Jelena in DM as to:\n\n* _Why_ no termination email was sent? Is there an issue that we should be aware of?\n* Whether you could prepare a termination email to the driver, preferably and if possible still today - if not, I will tweak our response to indicate that the exact suspension reason will be communicated in a separate email shortly.","2026-01-16T13:34:01.597Z"],["3816227","HS-29014","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","hey [~accountid:712020:740c6298-2781-402d-b09b-daba42f340a2]!\n\nI have document available with info as of Dec 1st 2025 but nothing newer yet. I have requested the file and will let you know once we have it. \n\nBest\nAlice, People Ops ","2026-01-16T13:34:55.890Z"],["3816228","PRF-1848","PRF","kristine.jansone@bolt.eu","Kristīne Jansone","Hey, [~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c]! Upon reviewing the assets we started wondering if the original copy was correct - it states “up to” everywhere, but shouldn’t it be “on average” instead? I recall such copies in the past and also what made me wonder regarding this more — during december I was a happy camper with ordering a lot and potential savings banner showed me 24 eur, whereas we mention for Latvia “up to 13”. ","2026-01-16T13:34:59.858Z"],["3816229","SUPX-2326","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","*[Safety Ex | CS Video Upload Process/tooling]* \n\nHey.  I am new and wanted to ask some Qs around this case regarding the video uploads segment.\n1. _[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723576823|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723576823]_\n2. _[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723492040|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/723492040]_\nQs for submission flows (chat, email, web form):\nQ1:  Does our systems tell the cst if a file is too large or incorrect type?  Below is the error they saw.  I understand this could be on the user end as well, just trying to learn what we have in place.\nQ2: Do we keep any audit trails that identify failed upload reasons?  If so, how can I check the failure reasons?\nQ3: Is there any work planned around this topic?  Just asking in general.\nQ4: Is there a look/dash to see failed upload volumes for the different means?\n\nIf easier to chat f2f or on a call, happy to do so when you have time.","2026-01-16T13:35:00.151Z"],["3816230","SUPX-2326","SUPX",null,"Slack","[Christian Kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768570103763919?thread_ts=1768570103.763919&cid=C064CEL9FKP|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768570103763919?thread_ts=1768570103.763919&cid=C064CEL9FKP|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-16T13:35:01.552Z"],["3816231","SUPX-2326","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Hey,\n\nUnfortunately on portals where we use the widget, it seems we don’t show specific errors when file is too large. I’ll create a task for it.\n\nThere are trails, but they are within internal tools that’s currently only accessible by engineers.\n\nWe have some ideas on improving the overall UX on widget users, but nothing concrete yet.","2026-01-16T13:35:01.933Z"],["3816232","PFI-834126","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, this user has multiple related accounts and devices linked to them. The rule you’re seeing was specifically set up to limit campaign abuse via new account creation. Given this risk, we won’t be making any changes to the rule.\n\nHowever, the rule should not to block usage when the discount does not cover 100% of the price for a single available category. In this scenario, I’d recommend the user try applying the promo to a slightly longer ride so that the discount doesn’t fully cover the order value.","2026-01-16T13:35:02.103Z"],["3816233","SREDESK-7373","SREDESK","alvar.hansen@bolt.eu","Alvar Hansen","Cost center: {{ENG-MOBILE-PLATFORM}}","2026-01-16T13:35:19.359Z"],["3816234","DRX-28038","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: nothing to test yet","2026-01-16T13:35:40.761Z"],["3816235","LSS-61720","LSS","roman.balakirsky@bolt.eu","Roman Balakirsky","[^POEM3_EMEA_490002.pdf] _(146 kB)_","2026-01-16T13:35:51.541Z"],["3816236","DSR-3799","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T13:36:10.525Z"],["3816237","WD-22571","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a] [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82]! Need your advise … I see that [Data Audit - Tax Codes report|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/task/1422$4871.htmld] report is done with Plan Dimension as a Business object , and Tax code is just defined as prompt value.  For that reason I can not add Tax code country to [Data Audit - Tax Codes report|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/task/1422$4871.htmld], right? ","2026-01-16T13:36:51.870Z"],["3816241","WD-19452","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:63ec99ebaf665dfde890c2e3] ! Do you still need help? or should I close the ticket? ","2026-01-16T13:38:02.968Z"],["3816242","PRF-1848","PRF","karina.kochanovskaya@bolt.eu","Karina Kochanovskaya","[~accountid:5c0697b59439134c517c3f90] hey! “up to” is legal-approved so let’s stick to that 🙂 ","2026-01-16T13:38:22.608Z"],["3816243","LSS-60674","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","We agreed to change most of them and the changes are in the Special Terms. There is no need to amend the General Terms file because it is “fixed” on our website, so we cannot change it. But legally we will agree to apply different terms to Aladin in Special Terms. Clause 13.3 states which documents prevail and Special Terms prevail over General Terms. This means that if we stated something in the Special Terms and it conflicts with wording in the General Terms, then what is stated in the Special Terms will take precedence. Those proposals that are not reflected in the Special Terms are not amended and we explained why in the comments.\nCan you please clarify this to them?","2026-01-16T13:38:38.923Z"],["3816245","DRX-28163","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified on DI.127.0 (195054040) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.3\n\n* element is no longer displayed in full width when header has only one header value\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 3.38.18 PM.png|width=414,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 3.38.18 PM.png\"!","2026-01-16T13:38:40.968Z"],["3816246","L10N-28351","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28349](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28349)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T13:38:40.061Z"],["3816248","L10N-28357","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The 