38:53.820Z"],["3816256","L10N-28373","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28349](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28349)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T13:38:54.176Z"],["3816257","L10N-28374","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28349](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28349)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T13:38:54.625Z"],["3816258","L10N-28376","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28349](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28349)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T13:38:55.455Z"],["3816259","BDB-1513","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Hi Polina - should we try adding a QR code to the table talkers and posters?\n\nThere appears to be quite a lot of blank space under the promo code - would this be suitable?","2026-01-16T13:39:09.299Z"],["3816260","PFI-834130","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Already discussed → [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C068KFNAVHD/p1768557856795199|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C068KFNAVHD/p1768557856795199|smart-link] \nClosing the ticket, thanks","2026-01-16T13:39:33.941Z"],["3816261","PFI-829509","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","We can’t hide the VAT column somehow easily and right now the impact doesn’t really warrant doing any manual changes by engineering (if that’s even possible/allowed), especially considering tax manager has already also evaluated this current case. \n\nI think local ops may have access to the VAT tags, so they may be able to help. But I’ll close the ticket for now, since I don’t think I can really provide anything further valuable from billing side. But if you request any other support or have questions, please do not hesitate to create a ticket! ","2026-01-16T13:39:41.202Z"],["3816262","LSS-61666","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] sure! Would be my first priority Monday morning","2026-01-16T13:39:42.524Z"],["3816263","PFI-834189","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","HI team, \n\nI have checked the payment and I can confirm the users payment and the invoice are not matching because the user partially paid for the order with the Bolt Balance. \n\nThe invoice has been created for the order price which is 75.64 PLN. \nHowever, the customer reported they were charged only 71.46 PLN.\n\nPlease note the customer paid 4.18 PLN from their Bolt balance. \n\n71.46 PLN + 4.18 PLN = 75.64 PLN \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3963850961|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3963850961]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T13:39:46.385Z"],["3816264","FRAUD-5576","FRAUD","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Updating impact numbers for cases in _driver_period_check_:\n\nThe failed payment/uncovered mismatch in period_check is causing us to perform 30% more blocks on undeserving partners for this issue type, making it around 75 affected partners annually and halting estimated 49K€ GMV annually from the action of block on these partners. Source([https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUDOPS-1014?focusedCommentId=3816166|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FRAUDOPS-1014?focusedCommentId=3816166|smart-link])","2026-01-16T13:39:54.800Z"],["3816265","WD-22571","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Yes, also the Data Audit reports are used by Data Warehouse team, so I suggest not to change anything in them without consultation with Nataliia and DW team. \n\nAdditionally each Tax Code has the same logic, and we use the ISO country codes in them. Tauno can just pull all the data, build a filter based on the codes in the tax code to get the country he needs. \n\nBut Nataliia has the final say.","2026-01-16T13:40:09.606Z"],["3816266","INT-86","INT","mate.varadi@bolt.eu","Máté Váradi","26W3\n\n* investigated and fixed a bug in the conversion rate GLM, which contributed to overestimating hit-rates \n* validated playbook output together with [~accountid:712020:6f950347-7487-41a9-aafd-80ed0f9290ba] \n* put V2 playbook into “production” (i.e. updated shared copy of budget tool, missed rides estimation job, conversion model training job, etc.)\n* started re-writing campaign selection optimization ([ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1937])","2026-01-16T13:40:09.953Z"],["3816268","WFM-9472","WFM","oleh.pater@bolt.eu","Oleh Pater","Hello, all the queues were assigned","2026-01-16T13:40:15.014Z"],["3816269","LSS-61620","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:63934c5900cb2fc3f98c7e44] \n\nI can send the contract for Signature and legal Ops will arrange it through an electronic signature request that they will send to both parties.\n\nUnless you are used to / want to do it another way, which is totally fine.\n\nLet me know if it is OK to proceed like this. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T13:40:39.110Z"],["3816273","RNTL-30502","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","Manually calculate to decide LU rebalance in Namur\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0950FKMP4J/p1768316854587759?thread_ts=1764677586.453249&cid=C0950FKMP4J|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0950FKMP4J/p1768316854587759?thread_ts=1764677586.453249&cid=C0950FKMP4J|smart-link]","2026-01-16T13:42:05.857Z"],["3816274","XP-2876","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","Ideas by [~accountid:712020:40cb7816-0b3b-4f87-ae87-8ac607ccf2c0] and [~accountid:712020:53be219b-8d47-4ba0-8cd1-a8b886503164]:\n\n{code:python}definition:\n    type: dbt-derived\n    metric:\n        expr: sum_gmv_eur_utc / ...\n    inclusion:\n        expr: COUNT_IF(sum_orders_finished_utc > 0)\n\n\ndefinition:\n    type: dbt-report\n    metric:\n        numerator_expr: sum_gmv_eur_utc\n        denominator_expr: sum_orders_finished_utc\n    inclusion:\n        expr: COUNT_IF(sum_orders_finished_utc > 0)\n\n# sum_gmv_eur_utc / sum_orders_finished_utc per user\n\nSUM(sum_gmv_eur_utc)\nSUM_SQ(sum_gmv_eur_utc)\nSUM(sum_orders_finished_utc)\nSUM_SQ(sum_orders_finished_utc)\nCOVAR(sum_gmv_eur_utc, sum_orders_finished_utc) AS cov\nCOUNT(analysis_unit/user_id)\n\n-> sum(gmv) / sum(order) {code}","2026-01-16T13:42:26.731Z"],["3816275","LSS-58105","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","Hi [~accountid:5fc110f331795a006f947e12]! The risks don’t materially differ for Latvia and Lithuania. The same recommendations should be followed for both. ","2026-01-16T13:42:33.612Z"],["3816276","MLC-650","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 3:\n\n* [Documentation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7403602591/Braze+Guide+-+Ad-hoc+Comms+for+Chauffeur] and training for Chauffeur Ad Hocs done.\n** Pending a post with all the details - done by EOD Monday - need to specify all the details (content, localisation, etc.)","2026-01-16T13:42:48.636Z"],["3816281","PFI-809817","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \nI can see the Beehive ticket has been solved. I will close this ticket. \nPlease let me know if you still need any assistance. ","2026-01-16T13:43:51.531Z"],["3816282","MLC-657","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 3:\n\n* *Canada*\n** Pushing to X Ride cloned and live.","2026-01-16T13:43:53.191Z"],["3816284","SAI-1412","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","Some quick thing with llm\n\nThe Bug\nIn PartnerBotAssignmentRunner.hasWork() (cs/customer_support/main/automations/runners/PartnerBotAssignmentRunner.ts:18-20):\npublic hasWork(ctx: Context, supportCase: SupportCase): boolean {\n    if (\n        !supportCase.isOngoing() ||\n        !supportCase.shouldAssignPartnerBot ||\n        (supportCase.assigneeHandle && isPartnerBot(supportCase.assigneeHandle))\n    ) {\n        return false;\n    }\n    return true;  // ❌ BUG: Should check escalatedToAgent here!\n}\nThe runner does NOT check if the case has been escalated! After escalation, bot assignments should be prohibited, but this automation doesn't enforce that invariant.\nWhy This Happens\n\n# The support_automations service calls SolutionService.tryAutomateSupportCase() asynchronously\n# This service runs LLM issue detection and calls customerSupportApi.updateIssues() with IssueKeySource.LLM_ISSUE_DETECTION\n# This creates an issue_labels_update event which triggers automation runners via Kafka\n# The PartnerBotAssignmentRunner runs without checking supportCase.escalatedToAgent\n# The bot gets assigned even though the case was already escalated\nSolution\nFix: Add escalatedToAgent check to PartnerBotAssignmentRunner.hasWork()\npublic hasWork(ctx: Context, supportCase: SupportCase): boolean {\n if (\n     !supportCase.isOngoing() ||\n     !supportCase.shouldAssignPartnerBot ||\n     supportCase.escalatedToAgent ||  // ✅ ADD THIS CHECK\n     (supportCase.assigneeHandle && isPartnerBot(supportCase.assigneeHandle))\n ) {\n     return false;\n }\n return true;\n}\nThis ensures that bot assignments are never attempted after escalation, maintaining the invariant that BeehiveTask is the source of truth for assignments post-escalation.\nWould you like me to implement this fix?","2026-01-16T13:44:55.422Z"],["3816287","IOTTEAM-316","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Directly connecting RI pin to GND also drives signal low on MCU side, but having 1.8V on modem side doesn’t translate to 3.3V on MCU side. (because of missing pullup)","2026-01-16T13:45:29.430Z"],["3816288","C2-457","C2","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","h2. Error query\n\nThe shipment from Bielefeld contained 95 batteries, C1 - 47pcs, C2 - 48pcs.\n\nh3. C1\n\nh4. Voltage errors\n\n27/47 batteries had reported voltage errors. There were no “suspicious” voltages, voltage errors showed “open nickle” or cases where one cell voltage was lower than others.\n\nh4. Water ingress \n\nNo water ingress errors were triggered. 4 batteries had a water sensor.\n\nh4. Other errors\n\n19/47 batteries reported E3 communication issues, this is not considered a dangerous error.\n\nh3. C2\n\nh4. Voltage errors\n\n2/48 batteries had cases where IoT reported cell voltage 0.2V, today this is not considered a dangerous error. \nThere were no E523 - cell errors. \n\nh4. Water ingress\n\nNo water ingress errors were triggered. Unknown how many batteries have a water sensor (can be checked).\n\nh4. Other errors\n\n16/48 batteries reported E3 communication issues, this is not considered a dangerous error. \n\nh2. Issues\n\n* TWS batteries do not trigger IoT voltage errors E24591, E24593, E24602. [~accountid:5f7722e1a2909600750e0434] \n* TWS batteries don’t have a cell error - E523 [~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] \n\nh2. Summary\n\nBatteries in the shipment STK-EE003-26-000011 didn’t show any signs of fire hazard or water ingress in the logs. \n\nThere were no C2 batteries with E523 - cell error.","2026-01-16T13:46:02.039Z"],["3816289","PFI-834248","PFI","shahnaz.huseynova@bolt-outsource.eu","Shahnaz Huseynova","[^149231281 (1).pdf (2).pdf]","2026-01-16T13:46:03.029Z"],["3816291","LSS-61323","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:6241b7de247a4b00691b57bb] \n\nPlease attend to the comments in clause 2 of the addendum before sharing with the Contractor. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/14sYPLa-xIWf1YVOK_vecZH_FXmaE7zUGo4psNuGcZGI/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14sYPLa-xIWf1YVOK_vecZH_FXmaE7zUGo4psNuGcZGI/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:46:21.618Z"],["3816293","FRAUDOPS-1014","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","[https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/212286361579139?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/212286361579139?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-16T13:46:39.344Z"],["3816296","MTE-929","MTE","sergei.drondin@bolt.eu","Sergei Drondin","Removed old unused secrets","2026-01-16T13:47:27.658Z"],["3816297","PFI-834255","PFI","otis.wella@bolt-outsource.eu","Otis Wella","!{AB9D0547-93C7-49A5-96BB-01414C69AFC4}-20260116-134347.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:47:34.859Z"],["3816298","PFI-834256","PFI","otis.wella@bolt-outsource.eu","Otis Wella","!{E29689BE-BEDE-4C5C-B545-985D7DD685FA}-20260116-134304.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:47:43.340Z"],["3816299","MLC-795","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 3:\n\nDone:\n\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LM-21308|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LM-21308|smart-link] \n\nIn progress:\n\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-21333|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-21333|smart-link]\n\nPending - all these 3 are pending the correct frequency from the requester. Localisations are ready.\n\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-20201|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-20201|smart-link] \n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-20749|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-20749|smart-link] \n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-20300|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LM/queues/custom/175/LM-20300|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:47:43.811Z"],["3816302","WD-16950","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","In Nov 2025 there were two similar cases \n\n!image-20260116-134423.png|width=1423,alt=\"image-20260116-134423.png\"!\n\n!image-20260116-134606.png|width=1404,alt=\"image-20260116-134606.png\"!\n\n\n\nAfter implementation of new revaluation rules based on book codes  the issue is fixed. Details here - > [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/7120585034/Currency+Rate+Types+and+Revaluation+Rules|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/7120585034/Currency+Rate+Types+and+Revaluation+Rules|smart-link]\n\n\n\n\n\n!image-20260116-134720.png|width=1150,alt=\"image-20260116-134720.png\"!\n\n \n\n!image-20260116-134754.png|width=1150,alt=\"image-20260116-134754.png\"!","2026-01-16T13:48:12.861Z"],["3816303","MLC-3869","MLC","yulia.nikitina@bolt.eu","Yulia Nikitina","W3: \n\n*Updates:* \n\n* Project kick-off: reviewed current retention and churn stage comms. \n* Added ideas for segmented flows in these stages:\n** [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7374799446/WIP+Retention+flow+optimisation+and+segmentation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7374799446/WIP+Retention+flow+optimisation+and+segmentation|smart-link] \n** [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7390855353/WIP+Churn+stage+segmentation+and+optimisation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7390855353/WIP+Churn+stage+segmentation+and+optimisation|smart-link] \n\n*Next steps:*\n\n* Discuss the project with Jason\n* Review comms ideas with COPS","2026-01-16T13:48:23.387Z"],["3816305","DELIVERY-1532","DELIVERY","antero.leedu@bolt.eu","Antero Leedu","26W3: *We’ve ended the Cuisine Shortcuts test as of today.*The results will be analyzed by [@ansh.jain|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U0456R63KC3] next week, and decision on next steps will be made once I’m back from vacation on 05.02. Based on the data so far, conversion metrics have been declining week over week, with no positive impact observed on our primary hypothesis or key metrics, so no roll-out is expected.","2026-01-16T13:48:36.705Z"],["3816306","SUPX-2326","SUPX",null,"Slack","[@christian.kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16]  One last Q...Do we have data viz on upload fails?  Meaning can we see how small or large volumes are for failed uploads are?","2026-01-16T13:48:50.156Z"],["3816307","LSS-61711","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^LOA_Bolt_Operations_OU_Hungary_PwC_Estonia.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:48:55.819Z"],["3816308","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] \n\n*Regarding the QR code:* we can add it to the table talkers, it makes sense there. \nHowever, I wouldn’t add it to the poster, as it would make it look crowded and wouldn’t add up much.We usually use CTA instead of QR code, since it already communicates downloading the app.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T13:49:07.542Z"],["3816312","MLC-3104","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 3:\n\n* Web builder is updated - started setting up emals.\n** Master emails are set up in Braze, needs a sync to Crowdin, translations applied and then setups. Will launch Tuesday.\n** Karl to run a GPT check on the HTML","2026-01-16T13:49:28.489Z"],["3816315","LSS-61705","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:638f45c0f6c85b343c0cdf90] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Steer_Bolt-Hopp_BC_Regulatory_Approval_Analysis_Terms_17Dec2025_HHsigned_v2.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:49:50.811Z"],["3816317","PFI-834258","PFI","kokou.bakpa@bolt-outsource.eu","Kokou Avoulété Bakpa","!IMG_8715.png|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_8716.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:50:15.949Z"],["3816318","CCM-22281","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Bianka,\n\nI have enrolled Pavel in the requested onboarding course. \n\nHave a lovely rest of your day and the upcoming weekend ahead! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-16T13:50:16.689Z"],["3816320","PRF-1848","PRF","laura.suveika@bolt.eu","Laura Suveika","[~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] Thanks, [~accountid:5c0697b59439134c517c3f90]! If we stick to “up to” this time, then everything is good with LV assets.","2026-01-16T13:50:24.998Z"],["3816321","LSS-61665","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:00149b52-b55e-4ada-ae80-bc0691ab9a37] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Contract_Aliaksei_Charankevich_Signed.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:50:34.789Z"],["3816323","XP-2368","XP","denys.kovalenko@bolt.eu","Denys Kovalenko","is this within test page, or actually new scorecard? ","2026-01-16T13:50:41.983Z"],["3816325","HS-29035","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","With global mobility.","2026-01-16T13:50:55.128Z"],["3816326","TS-4661","TS","paulina.borkowska@bolt.eu","Paulina Borkowska","Conclusions:\n\n* Pricing - based on pricing comparison there is a room for Bolt to win at pricing, especially in scooter passes options - will be further discussed with pricing\n* User statistics can be added under Good Rider score\n* Pricing details/scooter pass info can be added on scan screen\n* Currency consistency","2026-01-16T13:51:06.866Z"],["3816331","BB-2162","BB","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] Done, here is your [document|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6060941208?filter=%7B%22limit%22:25,%22offset%22:0,%22filter%22:%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe/Berlin] 🙂 \n\nSo you checked everything, and there was only one incorrect invoice left, right?","2026-01-16T13:51:21.209Z"],["3816334","LSS-61643","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:63934c5700cb2fc3f98c7e42] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt_Services_DE_GmbH_Account_Confirmation.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:51:35.307Z"],["3816335","SUPX-2326","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Unfortunately no","2026-01-16T13:51:35.198Z"],["3816336","PFI-811415","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe apologize for a very delayed response. \n\nWe have investigated with the payment service provider and they have confirmed the payment was processed. \nDue to technical issues Bolt received a response the payment had failed. \n\nWe are unfortunately, not able to correctly display the captured payment state in Admin. \n\nCould you please assist with issuing compensation for the customer. The user should receive 50 ZAR refund on their Bolt balance. \n\nBest regards, \nMarten","2026-01-16T13:51:38.572Z"],["3816337","WD-20008","WD","marleen.parmakson@bolt.eu","Marleen Parmakson","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] This could be done after we figure out the double asset book question and we can use the Group level movements in the PPE schedule.","2026-01-16T13:51:39.235Z"],["3816338","SUPX-2326","SUPX",null,"Slack","Thanks","2026-01-16T13:51:48.217Z"],["3816339","PFI-811415","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Double approval to finish the payment. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768571423359?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/operations/batchUpdate/1768571423359?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-16T13:51:51.938Z"],["3816343","LSS-61613","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] !\n\nPlease find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt_-_Notice_of_Bill_Rate_Increase_-_January_2026.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:52:19.197Z"],["3816344","LSS-61588","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt_Minutes (549069ab-d65e-4648-8c58-15f6ac69f867).pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:52:56.343Z"],["3816347","CSDA-281","CSDA","polina.fateeva@bolt.eu","Polina Fateeva","Brilliant, thanks so much!","2026-01-16T13:53:31.307Z"],["3816348","L10N-28385","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28349](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28349)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T13:53:50.297Z"],["3816349","LSS-61554","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] ! Will be ready on Monday","2026-01-16T13:54:02.133Z"],["3816350","LSS-61722","LSS","lili.kirikal@bolt.eu","Lili Kirikal","[^IPOready_Participant_agreement_2026_Bolt.pdf] _(328 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt Mail - IPOready Participant agreement 2026 Bolt.pdf] _(217 kB)_","2026-01-16T13:54:03.921Z"],["3816351","SUPX-2326","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","We are however migrating to a new error capturing tool. There may be some possibilities to build some dashboards in the future, but can’t promise anything yet","2026-01-16T13:54:09.473Z"],["3816352","MLC-1724","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W3*\n\nMade the announcement to country channels regarding these comms. Letting them know that these are just ad-hoc comms templates that are prepared in case local OPs need it. \n\nI also found out the events we have requested is still pending. \n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1751011816435819|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1751011816435819|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T13:54:32.061Z"],["3816354","PAW-14946","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @BoltCristianLupu\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161001\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 13:54:57 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T13:54:57.623Z"],["3816358","PFI-834259","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T13:55:09.146Z"],["3816360","LSS-61569","LSS","maria.paraschiv@bolt.eu","Maria-Speranta Paraschiv","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95], please find below the doc updated with comments from IDrive: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDuCsh2Zy4wfljXTdk1_T3uILUneacikPTWrzyGt1Wc/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDuCsh2Zy4wfljXTdk1_T3uILUneacikPTWrzyGt1Wc/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\n\n\nWe will review the Ops side and revert. \nThank you!","2026-01-16T13:55:25.091Z"],["3816361","MLC-1370","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 3:\n\n* January incentives were launched - all good, enrollments are happening across the board.\n\n* -Karl to check open rates.-","2026-01-16T13:55:30.333Z"],["3816362","PFI-811635","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nSorry for the delayed response. \n\nI can confirm the customers payment failed and Bolt did not charge any funds from the customer. \nThe payment failed with an error message PAYMENT_EXPIRED (448) which means the user did not complete the payment authentication and the payment expired. \n\nPlease let us know if the user is still having any issues. \n\nCheers, \nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T13:55:32.932Z"],["3816366","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf], [~accountid:712020:ed0860b7-47ec-4834-8e13-d50d5463df29] ,\n\nI confirm I am able to access and read the document with the entire thread on the ticket opened (and re-opened) on January 10th until {{2026-01-14}}.\n\nI will proceed to prepare a formal response to the customer.\n\n\n\nIn the meantime, however, *I would like to confirm with you if it is possible from your side to:*\n\n# Re-open the ticket or open a new ticket with *maps*, to tackle the issue still pending on the location of the rider. As he is not able to see the car coming, he will just stand in the pick-up spot and the driver won’t find him, generating more and more inaccurate “no-shows” and cancellations. \n# If necessary, please open a specific investigation or escalate it, in order to fix it. \n# Please keep me updated in this ticket, as the information on this issue has to be included in the response to the user.\n\n\n\nFinally, I am inquiring on the initiatives we have in Bolt for improving accessibility to visually-impaired users.\n\n\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-16T13:55:39.356Z"],["3816369","PFI-834260","PFI","carlos.segovia@bolt.eu","Carlos Segovia","[^Comprobante-700100003125976.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-16T13:55:58.609Z"],["3816370","LSS-61492","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:613a01a1e2a0d60069d29ca1] has the renewal of the original term to 2027 already been attended to and confirmed? \n\nIf so, and all the commercials are in order and as agreed, this can be signed. ","2026-01-16T13:56:00.412Z"],["3816371","LSS-60422","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , I see that the agreement is very basic and cannot be accepted, as already correctly commented by Liisa. Instead of redrafting it, it seems much more efficient to use Bolt’s standard vehicle purchase agreement template.\n\nIs there any reason why Bolt’s template is not being used here? Has Adam Auto refused to accept our template, or has it not yet been shared with them?\n\n[~accountid:61cc1c959ee70a00680edd89] could you please share the latest vehicle purchase agreement template here?\n\nMany thanks! ","2026-01-16T13:56:06.927Z"],["3816372","LSS-61554","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Thanks, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] 😉 ","2026-01-16T13:56:24.828Z"],["3816375","MLC-1527","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 3:\n\n* 2 additional templates converted\n** business_portal_manual_verification_rejected\n** business_portal_postpaid_application_rejected\n\n9/21 done","2026-01-16T13:57:04.852Z"],["3816379","MLC-3181","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 16th*+\n\n* *Updates:*\n** [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Ea_q9uOFfQRQUidat63MGALZ1NdpMP6W7XpWUh1_xY0/edit?gid=1836943145#gid=1836943145|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Ea_q9uOFfQRQUidat63MGALZ1NdpMP6W7XpWUh1_xY0/edit?gid=1836943145#gid=1836943145|smart-link] \n** Ran a report after 22 days of new strategy and results are mixed in terms of Conversion Rate. Total Markets considered: 36.\n*** 4 markets have had a clear positive uplift (between 8% and 11%)\n*** 5 Markets had a slight or flat uplift (between 0% - 3%)\n*** 3 Markets had a minor negative uplift (between -1% and -5%)\n*** 24 Markets had a significant negative uplift (between -5% and -33%)\n** As of now, all signals point towards outliers which performed better. Keeping seasonality in consideration, we will monitor for 1 more week to see if numbers pick back up. Otherwise we need to revert to previous user flow (removing story from link).","2026-01-16T13:57:51.330Z"],["3816381","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\nAfter the Privacy comments and other clarifications (in the supplier agreement in the comments), I have updated the information in the sheets (both English and Danish).\n\n[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14], could you please review it and check whether we have missed anything and whether everything in the sheet reflects our actual requests and proposals?\n\n[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] I would also like to clarify whether our legal proposals will be provided only in the sheet, or whether drafts of the CoC, NDA, and supplier agreement with proposed changes will also be shared? If so, I need to update them, so please share this information with me as soon as possible. \n\n[English sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/17hM-A7LNsFiMe8VxSKwP_8gI32zfeHJT/edit?gid=1751506711#gid=1751506711]\n[Danish sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VZQmdBiY8KhCNh6-LYWSlRBCJ6bt3ftE/edit?gid=1844353644#gid=1844353644]\n\nThank you.","2026-01-16T13:58:08.327Z"],["3816382","FPD-1414","FPD","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","From the results:\n\n|Forecast Horizon (Months)|Metric|15 Trials|30 Trials|\n|1|asp_local|4.56%|4.67%|\n|1|finished_orders|6.89%|6.68%|\n|1|gmv_local|7.82%|7.26%|\n|3|asp_local|4.57%|4.99%|\n|3|finished_orders|7.13%|6.25%|\n|3|gmv_local|8.31%|8.53%|","2026-01-16T13:58:09.027Z"],["3816383","LSS-61690","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] ! There are the ones, signed by Ahto. Benas and Alex have not signed yet, so I will attach their letters later[^Adyen_Bolt_Operations_OU_2025_.pdf] [^Adyen_N.V.Bolt_Services_UK_Limited_2025.pdf] [^Adyen_NV_Bolt_Rides_PL_sp._z_o.o._2025.pdf] [^Adyen_NV_Bolt_Services_CA_Inc._2025.pdf] [^AMEX_Bolt_Operations_OU_2025.pdf] [^Checkout_Ltd_Bolt_Services_UK_Limited_2025.pdf] [^Checkout_SAS_Bolt_Operations_OU_2025.pdf] [^Contract_Aliaksei_Charankevich_Signed.pdf] [^Deutsche_Bank_AG_Bolt_Operations_OU_025.pdf] [^Dlocal_LLP_Bolt_Operations_OU_2025.pdf]  [^PayU_SA_Bolt_Operations_OU_2025.pdf] [^Worldpay_BV_Bolt_Operations_OU_2025.pdf] [^Worldpay_UK_Limited_Bolt_Services_UK_Ltd_2025.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:58:14.202Z"],["3816384","LSS-61625","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:6299f17a9582b8006fc6b6c8],\n\nSEDECO has just responded and provided the original claim filed by the user. Please find below a brief summary:\n\nThe claim was filed by *Rosa Benedicta Destefano Admen* against *Bolt Service Paraguay S.A.* before *SEDECO* (Secretaría de Defensa del Consumidor y el Usuario) for *alleged poor service* in connection with a *Bolt delivery order*.\n\nThe claimant alleges that on *Sunday, 7 December 2025*, she used the Bolt platform to send a *bag containing colostomy supplies* to a third person. According to her statement, the courier collected the item but *the delivery was never completed*, and the goods were not received by the intended recipient. She claims that despite waiting several days, the item was never delivered.\n\nAs a result, the claimant requested:\n\n* *Refund of the cost of the product*, and\n* Consideration of the matter as a consumer protection violation, invoking *Law No. 1.334/98 on Consumer Protection*.\n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:bd27ea39-912c-4d98-9fd7-247ac2e54ec6] - did this user reach out to Customer Support? If so, could you please share screenshots of any communications with the user? This would be very helpful for [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] and me when preparing our response to the claim.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n[^EXP N° 5064-2025 COMPLETO.pdf] ","2026-01-16T13:58:11.138Z"],["3816385","PFI-811637","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nSorry for the delayed response! \n\nThe payment had failed with an error message PAYMENT_EXPIRED (448). This means the user did not complete the payment 3DS authentication and the payment failed. \n\nPlease let us know if the user is still having any issues. \n\nCheers,\nMarten\n\n","2026-01-16T13:58:21.522Z"],["3816386","LSS-61604","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Re/ p. 2 [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] - *I am aligned with Gabrielle’s suggestions below.*\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*On the topic of technical measures to ensure compliance with UK data protection law* -as a quick measure, I suggest clarifying that Bolt’s data security standards are outlined here: [https://bolt.eu/en/security/|https://bolt.eu/en/security/|smart-link] , and that Bolt undertakes to provide sufficient protection of personal data in accordance with its obligations under UK data protection law.\n{panel}\n\nCC [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ","2026-01-16T13:58:33.574Z"],["3816387","HS-28685","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","contract and medical signed, waiting for tax form","2026-01-16T13:58:35.697Z"],["3816388","LSS-61048","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] \n\nplease find MSA  and SOW reviewed [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hcuxzy3idapkvtZByoLRzWHIisReSOoA/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hcuxzy3idapkvtZByoLRzWHIisReSOoA/edit|smart-link]   \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EYkprfwYJnvEXKoMQ-83yORGAMNMDURQ/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EYkprfwYJnvEXKoMQ-83yORGAMNMDURQ/edit|smart-link] \n\nFor what term do we want to have the agreement ? ","2026-01-16T13:58:37.935Z"],["3816390","WFM-10017","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:f0c170c5-3f64-4ef4-b4c1-6a66ba6464ba]\r\n\r\nConfirming, that I have unassigned both agents from *01 RH_South Africa_T1_Low/Moderate* queue. Have a great day!","2026-01-16T13:58:59.438Z"],["3816392","PFI-834259","PFI","melanija.pticek@bolt.eu","Melanija Ptiček","Hey, here is the .csv mentioned above. \n\n[^PERPERA, Obrt za autotaksi prijevoz, vl. Marko Petričić - ono što su nam poslali - Sheet1.csv]\n\n","2026-01-16T13:59:19.566Z"],["3816393","PFI-829714","PFI","marvellous.paul@bolt-outsource.eu","Marvellous Paul","Hi Team,\n\nWe are still expecting a response from you","2026-01-16T13:59:19.992Z"],["3816395","PFI-834261","PFI","carlos.segovia@bolt.eu","Carlos Segovia","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-16 at 09.14.58.jpeg.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T13:59:55.487Z"],["3816396","MLC-3791","MLC","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","*Update W3*\n\nAdding a note here to include these [issues|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0798V5TJBS/p1768387533750459] [~accountid:712020:d6329bde-8ac9-46e0-8c20-8ca2102c07a3] found recently that need to be fixed. ","2026-01-16T13:59:57.680Z"],["3816398","MLC-1378","MLC","durrah.abdullah@bolt.eu","Durrah Abdullah","*Update*:  Following comms live, status updated in tracker [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OoH-LkotL6kpINRbnLd-ChzUdiHAITumcZB9LUbYEZQ/edit?gid=0#gid=0]\n\n* Churn with Debt live for SA\n* Churn Without Debt live for TW, MD, PL, CH, UA & ZW\n* Full churn live for SA & FI\n\n*Next Steps*:\n\n* Only Dubai, MY & DK Churn without Debt pending\n* Complete post analysis of comms for markets completing 30 days since being live","2026-01-16T14:00:19.087Z"],["3816399","RCE-358","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768572004783589]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-358] `Change dynamic config for flanders search category` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-16T14:00:37.387Z"],["3816400","CSDA-258","CSDA","polina.fateeva@bolt.eu","Polina Fateeva","Nope, still no access unfortunately - can’t open either link","2026-01-16T14:00:45.333Z"],["3816401","PFI-834263","PFI","babajide.bamidele@bolt-outsource.eu","Babajide Bamidele","!IMG_26.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T14:00:47.337Z"],["3816402","DELIVERY-1639","DELIVERY","oleksandr.stelmakh@bolt.eu","Oleksandr Stelmakh","26W3: Rolled out ML based [pricing|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/J4CerQE] in *Accra* (*+0.36% Absolute contribution profit (+60K EUR)*) and *Bratislava (+3.16% Absolute contribution profit (+327K EUR)).*","2026-01-16T14:00:47.904Z"],["3816403","HS-28664","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-16T14:00:53.288Z"],["3816404","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Hi Beatrice, thank you for the great work. I would suggest, that we also share  the CoC, NDA and supplier agreement for them to have and move on with, if they choose us. ","2026-01-16T14:00:56.167Z"],["3816410","LSS-61048","LSS","karina.kochanovskaya@bolt.eu","Karina Kochanovskaya","thank you! preferred option would be one month with a possibility to easily prolong by signing an additional SOW - we’re also still working out what deliverables we’d like, so we might end up changing that part ","2026-01-16T14:02:34.803Z"],["3816411","DO-5803","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Hi there!\n\nThere’s been a ticket created for that,  already WIP.","2026-01-16T14:02:41.490Z"],["3816412","CSDA-302","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review all new project requests every Monday morning. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-16T14:02:56.597Z"],["3816413","LSS-61493","LSS","malene.stojberg-olsen@bolt.eu","Malene Støjberg-Olsen","Will you fill in answers to the legal part in this sheet also? \n\n!https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1QR4GVc2_ZWuJIXFuzm25HBI-TdmM7Njx/edit?gid=420706529#gid=420706529|thumbnail!\n\n","2026-01-16T14:03:08.953Z"],["3816414","WD-22592","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Hello! Do you have an org or do we need to create one? If we need to create one, please give me the details of the org (org name, location, superior organization)","2026-01-16T14:03:21.692Z"],["3816417","INS-895","INS","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7405011515/RFC+Insights+Classifying+Incidents+Types+and+Severity|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7405011515/RFC+Insights+Classifying+Incidents+Types+and+Severity|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T14:04:33.229Z"],["3816418","CSDA-300","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Hi [~accountid:712020:126c4f20-cb89-48c3-84d1-3cd27b0eefcd],\n\nThank you for the request, we will review it with the team next week.","2026-01-16T14:04:55.283Z"],["3816419","LSS-61383","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:93a83d4d-5005-4a53-ad96-dc0c8205bf70], I got a little bit swamped by the end of the week with other high priority tasks. My apologies for not getting to you this week, I will aim to complete the review on Monday 🙏  ","2026-01-16T14:05:13.640Z"],["3816420","RDXENG-4671","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","*Tested and OK* (/) \n\nApplies to only send flow. Sanity check on default RH ordering and SR.\n\n||*Device name*||Google Pixel 8a||iPhone 15||\n|OS Version|16|18.0.1|\n|Client build|CA.193.0|CI.219.0|\n|Comment|physical|physical|\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 15-58-02_1.MP4]","2026-01-16T14:05:16.489Z"],["3816423","MLC-3854","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W3:\n\n* Launched LT on 13.01 and sent next batch for LV\n* 12,000 € for LT so far, additional 33,000 € for LV in acceptances this week. Total since LV launch is ~223,000 €\n* Waiting for offers from Youlend for PL\n* Should be sending follow-up send for LV and LT in W4\n* Onboarded Annie to go over the process of ad-hoc sends","2026-01-16T14:06:11.629Z"],["3816424","INT-622","INT","evgeniy.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Evgeniy Kuznetsov","26W03:\n\n* Had a demo with GAs\n* Did testing\n* Fixing small issues\n* On Monday GAs planning to experiment with the feature\n* Overall development here is done","2026-01-16T14:06:32.418Z"],["3816425","INT-558","INT","kristjan.praks@bolt.eu","Kristjan Praks","26W03\n\nWorked on campaign automation tooling planning with the team (MM-811).","2026-01-16T14:06:51.241Z"],["3816429","MLC-3779","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W3:\n\n* Supported EE and LV for ad-hoc sends\n* Submitted emails to content to prep for AZ and PL launches\n* Coordinating with Klāvs on new country launches and next batch of enrollments for current countries","2026-01-16T14:07:46.289Z"],["3816433","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","[~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nHere is the email sent to [h.mssq2010@gmail.com|mailto:h.mssq2010@gmail.com] at the moment.\n\n{quote}*Subject :* Bolt : Votre demande de remboursement\nBonjour,\n\nJe me permets de faire suite à votre demande de support (n° 710550573) effectuée via l'application Bolt.\n\nJe souhaiterais vous inviter à nous transmettre votre relevé d'identité bancaire (IBAN). Cela nous permettra d'étudier la possibilité d'un remboursement par ce biais.\n\nJe vous remercie par avance de votre réponse à cet e-mail et reste à votre disposition.\n\nExcellente journée à vous,\nMael, Bolt{quote}\n\nI will keep you updated! Have a great week-end.","2026-01-16T14:08:20.200Z"],["3816434","CCM-22282","CCM","olufemi.oluwale@bolt-outsource.eu","Olufemi Oluwale","[^LMS REQUEST.xlsx]","2026-01-16T14:08:31.518Z"],["3816435","LSS-61104","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], as discussed:\n\nA holding has email has been sent my [~accountid:6273b7d8e51c620070bea596] and the authorities answered saying the following:\n\n”_Dear Mr Mahoney,_\n_Good afternoon_\n_Your response and action are noted. This action will strengthen bolts reputation; hence I hope this office doesn’t receive any such cases._\n_Thanks, and regards_”\n\nShould they have any further follow-up, we will include them in this ticket and keep you in the loop.\n\nThanks!\n\n\n","2026-01-16T14:08:47.490Z"],["3816436","LSS-61724","LSS","nina.paragoso@bolt.eu","Nina Paragoso","[^[EXTERNAL] Kebab water_ Services agreement Vinkymon OÜ.asice]","2026-01-16T14:09:47.216Z"],["3816437","LSS-61228","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Just in case, this is the [BH outgoing |https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/724499911] 😉 cc [~accountid:5d15dd8c0d64020c403ae98c] ","2026-01-16T14:09:54.290Z"],["3816439","WD-22571","WD","tauno.tagel@bolt.eu","Tauno Tagel","Discussed with dwh team and we’re trying to include country to this report in order to use them in dwh dimension tables. I could of course join this to some iso country code table and extract this way but it makes our code very messy and need to replicate for each time I need it.","2026-01-16T14:10:10.683Z"],["3816440","RDS-1315","RDS","denis.komissarov@bolt.eu","Denis Komissarov","[~accountid:712020:34206d98-4d0d-43ac-93e3-4a910bc0fe7e] yes, past date is blocked on Android now.","2026-01-16T14:10:44.660Z"],["3816441","PAW-14911","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-16T14:11:27.869Z"],["3816443","WD-22597","WD","martin.schmidt@bolt.eu","Martin Schmidt","!Bild 15.01.26 um 13.36.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!Bild 15.01.26 um 13.39 (40944a06-9ce1-40db-85b1-6930ad4508ff).jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!Bild 15.01.26 um 13.39.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T14:11:37.848Z"],["3816444","PFI-814506","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] \n\nKind reminder","2026-01-16T14:11:57.802Z"],["3816445","MLC-3821","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","* In-app notifications in admin panel are set up.\n* Setting up email and pushes in Braze - will be done by 16Jan.\n* Waiting for engineering team - preview is done. Hoping to launching 20.Jan. ","2026-01-16T14:12:22.698Z"],["3816447","PFI-817505","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Checking for updates ","2026-01-16T14:12:39.473Z"],["3816448","DGD-171","DGD","friedrich.vogt@bolt.eu","Friedrich Vogt","[Notebook|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3719541956434570?o=2472566184436351#command/6341914115808689]\n\n* Current status: Modeling is done and currently writing up a summary doc. The models only slightly outperform the current targeting on average. It seems the main issue we need to fix is the holdout data, due to massive violations. Additionally, the current sorting metric (gmv uplift to cost uplift) is extremely noisy\n* Created GMV and cost uplift models using ULC holdout data in Bucharest\n* Built cost-aware cumulative gain curves to evaluate the model","2026-01-16T14:13:02.965Z"],["3816449","BP-13455","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101359?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101359?created=true|smart-link]  ","2026-01-16T14:13:10.285Z"],["3816450","BB-2162","BB","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Thanks! \n\nThat was the only one that was escalated and got to my desk;","2026-01-16T14:13:47.689Z"],["3816451","MLC-3835","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W3:\n\n* Continued ad-hoc support and approved EE W3 comms and RO W4 comms\n* Building exclusion list to reduce users receiving too many messages even after converting, etc. Drafting proposal to reduce total number of sends per week due to lack of results tied to comms","2026-01-16T14:14:40.640Z"],["3816453","PFI-817617","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:6012aaf8a41ea5006a613a63] \n\nI can see that the issue has been closed. I will be closing the ticket. \n\nPlease let me know once you get an update and I will re-open the ticket. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T14:14:57.983Z"],["3816456","RDS-890","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:52a73231-4dc8-4054-82a3-d741603d65af] should we split this ticket into smaller pieces? It can help in making it more actionable.","2026-01-16T14:15:08.926Z"],["3816457","LSS-61280","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you [~accountid:712020:95922f19-94a5-49f1-b3c6-43a9c9ddd746] , looks good to me. ","2026-01-16T14:15:15.328Z"],["3816458","LSS-61562","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:5e6b55b2c54d0a0d044302f1] 👋  As I understand, you need this information to respond to a user.\n\nHave you followed the BH KB guidance when handling and escalating requests about Audio Trip Recording? [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/57409?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/57409?country=global&language=en]\n\n\n\nThe feature has been reviewed by privacy, and we have relevant processes in place. Can you please check out the guidance I shared and let me know if it resolves your question?","2026-01-16T14:15:24.220Z"],["3816459","PFI-834184","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, our profilings marked the orders suspecting driver bonus abuse. Checked the orders/riders, all looks legitimate. If there was any monetary loss to the driver due to these orders, then this may be compensated.\nThanks","2026-01-16T14:15:39.286Z"],["3816460","LSS-61542","LSS","katrin.voloditsev@bolt.eu","Katrin Voloditšev","Hey! Thank you for replying! Could you please specify when was the process changed and was there an update in Slack or somewhere else?","2026-01-16T14:15:40.167Z"],["3816461","WD-22571","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","!image-20260116-141438.png|width=362,alt=\"image-20260116-141438.png\"!\n\n[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] you do have country inside the dimensation field. Technically you could extract attempt to extract it with a calculated field. But try in SBX first so the report isn’t broken in production","2026-01-16T14:15:42.538Z"],["3816462","RDS-904","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","Also need a description/link 🙂 ","2026-01-16T14:16:01.926Z"],["3816466","LSS-61726","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","[^BOLT (55).pdf] _(68 kB)_","2026-01-16T14:17:55.350Z"],["3816467","HS-29032","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:9dcaf049-08b3-4db3-8347-9b88531a3941] \n\nI see that there are WD tasks regarding him waiting for your action. Can you please complete them? They should be in your Workday inbox .\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 16.17.09.png|width=838,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 16.17.09.png\"!","2026-01-16T14:18:03.893Z"],["3816469","DSR-1585","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - you can send the following message:\n\n{quote}Dear Ciprian,\n\nThank you for your message.\n\nAt the time you submitted your deletion request, your account was subject to an internal review relating to refund activity. To complete that review, Bolt needed to retain the relevant account data. This temporary retention was based on Bolt’s legitimate interests in preventing and detecting potential misuse of the platform and ensuring the accuracy of refunds (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Deletion could also not proceed where the data remained necessary for assessing potential legal claims arising from the review, as permitted under Article 17(3)(e) GDPR.\n\nCommunication regarding the expected handling timeframe for your request should have been clearer. Bolt acknowledges that this was not done correctly in your case and regrets the inconvenience caused. This omission resulted from human error and does not affect the underlying legal basis for the temporary retention described above.\n\nThe internal review required Bolt to retain specific account data until the assessment was completed. For this reason, the deletion request could not be actioned at the time of your initial request. Once the review concluded and no irregularities were identified, the deletion should have proceeded. This final step did not occur due to human error.\n\nBased on the above clarifications and the previous correspondence exchanged with you, Bolt considers that your data subject request has been addressed in full. Bolt does not intend to engage in further correspondence on this matter unless you provide materially new and relevant information that has not already been assessed.\n\nKind regards,{quote}","2026-01-16T14:18:13.583Z"],["3816470","MLC-3733","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W3:\n\n* Scheduled meeting with Ruslanas on 20.01 to go over guidelines and templates","2026-01-16T14:18:20.902Z"],["3816471","PFI-817922","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe could see the ticket has been solved. Closing the SD request. \nPlease let me know if you still need any assistance and I will reopen the case. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T14:18:32.744Z"],["3816472","LSS-58216","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] we should have received this agreement from Solidgate for Ahto to sign. Please help me with it. It should be the document Martin posted here in his comment from yesterday. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T14:18:33.538Z"],["3816473","DRX-27955","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27710 has been resolved","2026-01-16T14:18:40.996Z"],["3816475","RSE-8","RSE",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27955 has been resolved","2026-01-16T14:19:28.690Z"],["3816476","DRX-27957","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27955 has been resolved","2026-01-16T14:19:28.950Z"],["3816478","DAEN-1301","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","the surge metric seems to be the one that is missing here is [where it’s defined|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/yuriy-t-metricflow-revamp-playground/rides/models/metrics/marketplace/search/rides_search_avg_selected_surge_multiplier.yml#L24]\n\n[here’s|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09BSV4UVD3/p1768572967702629?thread_ts=1765447789.215149&cid=C09BSV4UVD3] why I’m saying only surge is missing ","2026-01-16T14:19:49.708Z"],["3816481","LSS-61562","LSS","katrin.voloditsev@bolt.eu","Katrin Voloditšev","Hey!\nNo, my questions were a bit different: \n\n* Is the user (driver or rider) who starts the recording required to notify the other participant that the interaction is being saved?\n* The voice recording should be used in emergency situations, but who is to judge what is an emergency situation for the user? Do we have a list of situations where the user is allowed to use this toolkit?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T14:20:07.028Z"],["3816483","WFM-10013","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b]\r\n\r\nSouth Africa market access for both agents granted. Have a nice day!","2026-01-16T14:20:31.513Z"],["3816484","PFI-834194","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, we don’t reject any login OTPs from our side, and the app itself looks valid from our inputs. I’d recommend you reach out to tech support with this 🙂 \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 16.18.58.png|width=751,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 16.18.58.png\"!","2026-01-16T14:20:39.792Z"],["3816485","WFM-10023","WFM","gerda.morkvenaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Gerda Morkvenaite","[^list of agents.xlsx]","2026-01-16T14:20:50.345Z"],["3816486","RNTL-29734","RNTL","aytan.gurbanova@bolt.eu","Aytan Gurbanova","* -Drive Marker Tap [is_recommended: Boolean]-\n* -Drive Recommended Option Banner Tap-\n* -Drive Recommended Option Modal-","2026-01-16T14:21:04.799Z"],["3816487","DSR-1585","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Thank you for your help, [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]! ","2026-01-16T14:21:09.374Z"],["3816489","MLC-3932","MLC","jimmy.soldatos@bolt.eu","Jimmy Soldatos","W3:\n\n* Confirmed that experiment will roll out on the 19th, scheduling emails to go out 16.01","2026-01-16T14:21:47.162Z"],["3816491","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Agreed, thank you for picking it up.\n\nAt this time, we have the following team structure:\n\n* Head of Infosec (Tarmo)\n** Sec-Compliance (Aivo, Gaya)\n** InternalSec (manager: Martin Jaan)\n** CloudSec (manager: Iuliia)\n** ProductSec (manager: Amefon)\n\nNot sure if the Supervisory Orgs in Workday align with the structure. ","2026-01-16T14:22:20.289Z"],["3816492","BZNS-101","BZNS","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/BZNS/ideas/view/6748432?selectedIssue=BZNS-101&issueViewLayout=sidebar&issueViewSection=capture&focusedInsightId=7560501|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/BZNS/ideas/view/6748432?selectedIssue=BZNS-101&issueViewLayout=sidebar&issueViewSection=capture&focusedInsightId=7560501|smart-link] \nDesign stand on Shubham idea\nNoticication center next to logo was implemented only as an MVP which means:\n\n* only in ENG, no other language is supported\n* no action button\n* no animation to bring attention to it (only red badge)\n\nWe have quality task improvement, but it wasn't prioritized. Changes to current state needs to be done to roll it out fully.\n\nIn your [document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cBt4R32mYechGeS5RwXivw6rJEGoiTNYlsJdo9U578s/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.osf4txvfwlu5], I see pop-up (in design we call them dialogues), and these have specifications and rules\n\n* They are invasive and should be used sparingly\n* Disable all app functionality when they appear, and remain on screen until confirmed, dismissed, or a required action has been taken.\n* *Should be user-initiated*\n* The number of interactions in a dialog should be minimal and support the task at hand.\n* Avoid complex decision-making that requires additional sources of information unavailable in the dialog.\n\nI agree there is potential, and the communication about news and features is poor atm. Improvement of the notification center and possibly the creation of a product walkthrough, and some other options would be great.\nPop-up dialogues are not favored from a UX perspective","2026-01-16T14:22:37.528Z"],["3816494","RLONE-479","RLONE","niklas.svegeboe@bolt.eu","Niklas Svegeboe","[~accountid:712020:64b64810-17ee-4eae-a1d9-0887a9baa408] I believe we concluded this one in Q4, correct?\nIt may have gotten duplicated, as I’ve been updating the Epics 🙂 ","2026-01-16T14:22:57.896Z"],["3816495","DAEN-1301","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","Both come from {{fact_rides_search}} \n\n\n\nconsists of these 2 metrics \n\n!image-20260116-142039.png|width=662,alt=\"image-20260116-142039.png\"!\n\nwhich are in turn \n\n[1|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/yuriy-t-metricflow-revamp-playground/rides/models/metrics/marketplace/search/rides_search_sum_selected_surge_multiplier.yml#L4]\n\n!image-20260116-142205.png|width=764,alt=\"image-20260116-142205.png\"!\n\n[rides_search_sum_selected_surge_multiplier_local|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/yuriy-t-metricflow-revamp-playground/rides/models/semantic_models/semantic_fact_rides_search.yml#L229]\n\n----\n\n[2|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/yuriy-t-metricflow-revamp-playground/rides/models/metrics/marketplace/search/count_rides_sessions_converted_to_order.yml#L4]\n\n!image-20260116-142304.png|width=743,alt=\"image-20260116-142304.png\"!\n\n[count_rides_sessions_local|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/yuriy-t-metricflow-revamp-playground/rides/models/semantic_models/semantic_fact_rides_search.yml#L50]","2026-01-16T14:23:08.139Z"],["3816496","PFI-819991","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can see the Beehive ticket has been closed. Let us know if you need further assistance and we will reopen this ticket. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T14:23:15.290Z"],["3816497","XVER-310","XVER","jaskaran.saluja@bolt.eu","Jaskaran Singh Saluja","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd] Let’s keep the final domain coverage contingent on our 22nd Jan meeting with the platform and privacy team. wdyt?","2026-01-16T14:23:19.030Z"],["3816498","LSS-60647","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\nPlease analyse the eater’s response and prepare the answers to it. We need to ensure we finally explain we are in violation and no compensation is granted. ","2026-01-16T14:23:53.942Z"],["3816499","BZNS-101","BZNS","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","Ideally, data should be checked first for potential, and then small user research to get insights on the best approach for users and what their current problem space is related to information and new feature knowledge.","2026-01-16T14:24:24.797Z"],["3816500","PFI-821449","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nI can see the Beehive ticket has been closed. Please let us know if you need any further assistance and will reopen the ticket. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T14:24:35.216Z"],["3816502","PFI-834244","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Bernice, user’s device unblocked. Thanks!","2026-01-16T14:26:55.272Z"],["3816503","PFI-834272","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T14:26:56.893Z"],["3816505","LSS-58216","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^MSA-2026-01-16-Solidgate_Bolt_f (72bf7bc9-d293-4243-8455-b44693b16ace).pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:27:04.535Z"],["3816506","LSS-61728","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","[^Ista Hybridlimouisenservice UG Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (2).pdf] _(131 kB)_","2026-01-16T14:27:40.312Z"],["3816507","PFI-822409","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nWe have not hear back from you in 3 weeks. Please let us know if you need any assistance and we will reopen the ticket. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T14:28:14.548Z"],["3816510","CSDA-298","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey!\n\nHere are 2 data exports:\n\n* [^csda_298_call_data.csv] - data on each call attempt (data period - October - December 2025)\n* [^csda_298_call_data_aggregated_by_support_case_id.csv] - data on call attempts made by agents aggregated on a support case level (data period - October - December 2025).\n\nA few notes on the dimensions available:\n\n* {{caller_user_id}} - Admin ID of the user who initiated the call (here - Admin agent ID)\n\n* {{caller_user_type}} - type of the user who initiated the call (here - admin_user)\n* {{agent_email}} - email associated with the Admin agent ID\n** Please note that we don’t have any admin user with the email {{munthanicha.wonglert1@bolt-outsource.eu}}, but rather {{munthanicha.wonglert@bolt-outsource.eu}}. The latter was used for filtering the data.\n* {{call_created_date_utc}} - date when the call was created (UTC)\n* {{call_created_ts_utc}} - timestamp when the call was created (UTC)\n* {{call_direction}} - direction of the call (here - outbound)\n* {{callee_joined}} - whether a callee (user who was called) joined the call, i.e. answered the call\n* {{call_status}} - status based on the {{callee_joined}}: either {{call_missed_time_out}} (call was ended due to time out), {{call_cancelled}} (call was cancelled by caller), or {{call_answered}}.\n** Please note that for {{call_missed_time_out}}, we don’t have {{support_case_call_duration_seconds}}, unfortunately.\n* {{callee_user_id}} - ID of the callee (here is the voip event client)\n* {{callee_user_type}} - user type of the callee (here - phone)\n* {{support_case_id}}\n* {{call_id}}\n* {{beehive_task_id}}\n* {{support_case_call_duration_seconds}} - total call duration in seconds (if calculated)\n* {{support_case_call_duration_seconds_edited}} - total call duration in seconds, but only for answered calls\n* {{outbound_duration_seconds}} - total duration of the call when the callee joined in seconds.\n\nIt is also possible to get the driver lead ID for each call, but it will require additional efforts - I can take it if this is really necessary.\n\nLet me know if you have any further questions or comments. Have a nice week ✨ ","2026-01-16T14:29:56.313Z"],["3816511","HS-28960","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-16T14:30:05.913Z"],["3816512","PFI-834273","PFI","samuel.maghanga@bolt-outsource.eu","Samuel Maghanga","!IMG 2.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG1.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG3.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T14:30:07.426Z"],["3816513","CSDA-298","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","[notebook|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3854228640576543?o=3598988355446810#command/6996872918544817]","2026-01-16T14:30:13.188Z"],["3816514","DO-5802","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Granted for Databricks and Common SQL. Please let me know if you want to give access to Common SQL.\r\n\r\nThe schema uses dbfs and will not be synced to Common SQL at the moment.","2026-01-16T14:30:22.107Z"],["3816515","PFI-832806","PFI","sophie.chavaregi@bolt-outsource.eu","Sophie Chavaregi","any update team?\n\n","2026-01-16T14:30:23.584Z"],["3816516","PFI-822592","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThank you for escalating! \n\nThe customer payments team has escalated the case to our payment service provider. \nWe have received some feedback that the issue is most likely coming from the customers bank. \nCheckOut the payment service provider has reached out to the users bank to avoid this from happening in the future. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-16T14:31:05.479Z"],["3816518","PFI-834194","PFI","denisa.stepanova@bolt-outsource.eu","Denisa Stepanova","Thank you😊 ","2026-01-16T14:31:08.975Z"],["3816519","LSS-61559","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:a729743a-fea5-401d-a417-a7025bd4ee5a] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Cooperation agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_Urban Drive_01.01.26.pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:31:13.445Z"],["3816520","LSS-60630","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hello [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \nJust checking in. Any update on the assessment?","2026-01-16T14:31:15.890Z"],["3816523","PFI-834273","PFI","samuel.maghanga@bolt-outsource.eu","Samuel Maghanga","Kindly assist","2026-01-16T14:31:56.585Z"],["3816524","LSS-61723","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:1d0a34aa-e1ae-4c55-bae7-010cdaef89e3] ! Google says that the link is invalid. Maybe you can add it once more?","2026-01-16T14:33:28.603Z"],["3816525","CEBF-1834","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","bug is fixed\n\n!2026-01-16_16-31-53.mp4|width=607,alt=\"2026-01-16_16-31-53.mp4\"!","2026-01-16T14:33:29.697Z"],["3816526","BR-4108","BR","svetlova.katerina@bolt.eu","Katsiaryna Kasakouskaya","[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/46305de6d2f3fb37262e3f3a03f21a5a99a981ff/src/platform/commerce/invoicing_user/main/service/UserInvoiceDataProvider.ts#L41|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/46305de6d2f3fb37262e3f3a03f21a5a99a981ff/src/platform/commerce/invoicing_user/main/service/UserInvoiceDataProvider.ts#L41] \ngetOrder only works for new orders","2026-01-16T14:33:32.764Z"],["3816527","GRWA-1512","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Currently only one city Encarnacion is added. rest are yet to be added in CI data source by CI team","2026-01-16T14:33:43.627Z"],["3816532","LSS-61729","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","[^Engel Drive Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (1).pdf] _(133 kB)_","2026-01-16T14:34:54.475Z"],["3816534","LSS-61728","LSS","anton.schoeps@bolt.eu","Anton Schöps","[^Ista Hybridlimouisenservice UG Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (2) (2d9620f5-bb77-4ae6-a3c3-c81acc1e09d1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T14:35:13.937Z"],["3816535","IOTTEAM-317","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Ibeacon is detected with a phone app. Estimated distance in the app is about correct.","2026-01-16T14:35:16.289Z"],["3816536","PFI-834275","PFI","olena.kuzmych@bolt-outsource.eu","Olena Kuzmych","!IMG_20260116_143103_941.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260116-152503.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T14:35:17.023Z"],["3816538","PFI-834276","PFI","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","!unnamed (2).png|thumbnail!\n\n!unnamed (3).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T14:35:27.711Z"],["3816539","LSS-61614","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^_LV20260115-001 Vo-Link - Bolt Drive LV.docx (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:35:41.906Z"],["3816540","LSS-61493","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:f567ef89-de0b-45fd-b2bf-1e8358323a14] as you indicated, these are draft translations of the documents, which reflect our proposals:\n[NDA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fcYleDLrM7mYQ31AqOk8_ihvSu_CW7gT/edit]\n[CoC|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rbOj_150IeZGqssuxk3hfABmZ__TXJqr/edit]\n[Supply agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BoWGXhamWE-icddwK4_309Aoqw7OHCfj/edit] \n\nSince the translations were done using DeepL, before sending them to PwC it is necessary to make sure that the translation has been done properly and that it accurately reflects our proposals in English.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T14:35:45.462Z"],["3816541","BR-4108","BR","svetlova.katerina@bolt.eu","Katsiaryna Kasakouskaya","was broken in [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/134839|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/134839|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T14:35:47.142Z"],["3816542","LSS-61612","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^LT20260115-001 Vo-Link - Bolt Drive LT.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:36:17.545Z"],["3816543","CEBF-1828","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed. \n\n!2026-01-16_16-36-05.mp4|width=560,alt=\"2026-01-16_16-36-05.mp4\"!","2026-01-16T14:36:31.630Z"],["3816544","LSS-61464","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n [^signed contract Bolt 50x yaris cross (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:37:17.502Z"],["3816545","LSS-60746","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","Thank you [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd]. Well explained. \n\nWe are not planning to reach out to drivers. But rather, continue the same current process that any driver can request to have the Rikba Category on their profile. \n\nWe can have the disclaimer shared by CS through Beehive they they confirm that the tag  is added. ","2026-01-16T14:37:42.576Z"],["3816546","LSS-61723","LSS","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Sure, here it is: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/14GRXrFBiIzZEefgOqXLiAsJqjthXvDI7/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14GRXrFBiIzZEefgOqXLiAsJqjthXvDI7/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T14:37:48.398Z"],["3816547","LSS-59413","LSS","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","Hey! Sorry, I started to reply but forgot to send it in time :melting_face: First, thank you for the answers. While I fully understand legal POV on these points, there are several important things to consider also from operations side.\n\n\n\n* *Fake GPS fraud – Blocking/Suspension based on GPS use*\n\nI agree that solving this fully with a product solution would be the best option, instead of having speed and distance anomalies as indicators. As part of our team just had a market visit, I’m sure this will be a topic we, together with product, will be focusing on more.\nI would also like to highlight that actioning fake GPS fraud according to the criteria above, wouldn’t be something new we would start doing - it’s something that has already been done since late 2024. It’s also important to know that automatic 72h suspension is only triggered to give us time to confirm the fraud really happened _(action previously aligned with relevant people)_ after which we are able to take further action.\nFinally, on fake GPS, as I previously mentioned, after our team’s market visiti there is definitely a plan to tackle this topic more aggressively with an aligned and clear strategy. More to follow on this from Dhurv & others.\n\n* *Multiapping during active deliveries*\n\nMultiapping is allowed under [Portugese fleet T&C point 2.7|https://bolt.eu/en-pt/legal/tnc-bolt-food-fleet/?category=delivery] however, this doesn’t include during delivery aka active multiapping. We don’t have anything against multiapping as such, but if it happens during delivery, it hurts user experience and creates mistrust towards our platform and brand. I also read point 4.11 - would it help if we were to follow goe criteria (below) + connect lateness & courier not moving complaints to the accused courier and take action according to this? Would this mean we have a clear T&C violation (against point 4.11)?\n\n{quote}Criteria:\n\n* GPS path deviations that can't be explained by traffic-related detours\n* distance discrepancies vs. OSRM routes\n** _GPS tracking data to compare the actual route distance and compare it with estimated OSRM route distance_\n* unusual delivery delays{quote}\n\n","2026-01-16T14:38:02.908Z"],["3816548","LSS-61593","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:6fe32059-7a68-4aa8-ba31-68f6c2731793] , please see short analyses of the cases, hope it helps to decide how to proceed: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zlZFhe875fVuaJAKGBjHwAz82B5ZBML1-D6ofJtptXY/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zlZFhe875fVuaJAKGBjHwAz82B5ZBML1-D6ofJtptXY/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  🙂 ","2026-01-16T14:38:10.256Z"],["3816549","MLC-3605","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","*Dubai* \n\n*Status:*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n* *BU:* Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn, Promo Codes, HVO *LIVE*\n* *BA:* *Acquisition - needs translation and proofreading - ticket raised*\n* *BA:* Onboarding, Product Education, 0 Orders, Awareness, HVO, Promo Codes, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*Angola*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*Moldova*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*New Zeland*\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition, Activation, Pushing to X Ride, Retention, Churn *LIVE*\n\n*Taiwan*\n\n* *WP:* Translations DONE, setting up for proofreading ","2026-01-16T14:38:12.830Z"],["3816550","LSS-61531","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^LT20260114-002 United Motors - Bolt Drive LT.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:38:16.635Z"],["3816551","LSS-61730","LSS","teun.esveld@bolt.eu","Teun Esveld","[^Breeze Social B.V. Trademark consent Bolt.docx] _(240 kB)_","2026-01-16T14:38:19.562Z"],["3816552","DRAG101-405","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Dekra is finalizing the paperwork for submitting to KBA (/) \n\nThey also confirmed to finish the speedometer test in the first half of next week. When that is done and no issues arise, the documentation can be handed over to KBA for confirmation :loading: \n\n\n\nI feel like we can actually get it done in time 🤞 ","2026-01-16T14:38:57.742Z"],["3816555","LSS-59403","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","[~accountid:632d88e0748d1bfcb858128d] please see a comment in your agreement, otherwise almost finalized!\n\n[~accountid:712020:9aeb03eb-e5d1-4baa-9187-537295012ac9] I left multiple questions in your agreement before Christmas and I see that all has been marked as done, although no changes made. Should this be understood as no change was needed/no deviation at all from the template as is? \n\nThanks!","2026-01-16T14:39:14.686Z"],["3816556","PFI-823014","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Asking Paystack to issue the refunds. ","2026-01-16T14:39:18.766Z"],["3816557","DPM-2313","DPM","pawel.dabrowski@bolt.eu","Paweł Dąbrowski","[~accountid:712020:ddfe83d1-e2c1-4238-8459-1dfffb836745] changed to High as per Cognziant Feedback on OCR enabling incremental average handling time decrease compared even to Airtable ","2026-01-16T14:39:20.975Z"],["3816560","TA-157","TA","paulo.morna@bolt.eu","Paulo Morna","[Rollout plan |https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1oFsi9DoWmS6BC3GVnhSpcZKIk_aOs-jvpVNrs9jstZE/edit?slide=id.g3b879b9a104_0_3#slide=id.g3b879b9a104_0_3]completed.","2026-01-16T14:39:59.530Z"],["3816561","PAW-14949","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160924\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-16 14:40:02 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-16T14:40:02.676Z"],["3816562","BRE-1126","BRE","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","split to 3 separate epics","2026-01-16T14:40:38.970Z"],["3816563","INT-653","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: Rolled out efficiency channel measurements 8 cities, will continue gradual rollout next week (including uplift retention measurements). Found some violations in  control groups, identifying root cause. Working on productionising efficiency measurement pipeline.","2026-01-16T14:40:46.350Z"],["3816564","GS-385","GS","gabriel.munteanu@bolt.eu","Gabriel Munteanu","This is happening because offline-trip-detector was the only creator of geofecences and was designed with this in mind. Now there is another services that create geofences and when an unknown geofence arrives in offline-trips-detector it ‘panics’ and throws an exception which means that the event is put back in the queue. Because of this there were moments with around 4M events in the queue. We need to fix this by adding a new field on the createGeofence API: requested_by_service , stored in Redis and also sent on the events so the consumer services can filter out unwanted events. We can first use this new field only in offline-trips-detector and ask the other team to enhance their service.","2026-01-16T14:40:49.660Z"],["3816566","INT-656","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: ENG work ongoing, will be finished next week.","2026-01-16T14:41:16.583Z"],["3816570","INT-657","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: Continued exploratory analysis on simple uplift modeling. First results will be shared next week. ENG work (trigger based enrolment) on apology vouchers in progress, once ready, we will design experiment plan.","2026-01-16T14:41:48.571Z"],["3816571","LSS-50764","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^Bolt-Superpharm Special Terms DROGERIA 22.09.2025 CLEAN FINAL (66d0b991-50e8-47e3-86b6-1a28eae4ce2f).pdf]\n[^Bolt-EUFA (Superpharm) Special Terms DROGERIA 22.09.2025 CLEAN FINAL (88bc1b3e-3502-4b59-987b-af6228bce1cf).pdf]\n\n[~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] Please find the signed document(s) attached.","2026-01-16T14:41:51.870Z"],["3816575","BNDGFT-14","BNDGFT","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","The State has decided to again pursue an objection that the case should be dismissed as “_abstract_” (this was raised earlier but not followed up by the State). The District Court will decide this *before the main hearing* and will give us 1-week response deadline, i.e. {color:#bf2600}*January 23*{color}. \n\nOC thinks it’s *unlikely* that the court will refuse to hear the case, but there is some uncertainty. OC has started drafting a procedural submission responding to this.\n\nPleading from the State:\n\n* [NO version|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZF8s3rXMv0KxVUp6tVbD4MkcWeFFQe1i/view?usp=drive_link]\n* [ENG AI version|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mIDF2YnrHIqMYZHSFI1PleCuG2bERrbA/view?usp=drive_link]\n\nOC will circulate a draft beginning of next week, aiming at Tuesday. We should then review this as swift as possible, to ensure we can meet the deadline. Comments should be made to Wiersholm no later than Thursday January 22, but even better if Wednesday EoD. Lets decide when we know how the pleading looks like.OC agrees that we need to push back strongly on this and is fairly confident that the court will be on our side!As for the uncertainty, OC has informed the following. Including in full for visibility as I'm soon off for vacation:\n\n* _The reason for the slim uncertainty relates to the conditions for admissibility under the Disputes Act. In short, the issue is that purely abstract questions cannot be put before the courts (like – is this provision legal?), an actual and specific interest in the outcome is required. Based on this, one will typically have to wait for a negative decision by a public authority before a case can be brought before the courts, as opposed to filing a case on the basis of the expected outcome. This has created some uncertainty in cases where the action in question does not directly necessitate or will imply a formal decision by a public authority._ *_In later years, the case law from the Supreme Court has ensured that such cases are not thrown out – as this would render the aggrieved party without any access to justice_*_._\n* _The position of the Government is as a_ *_matter of principle to try to limit these types of claims_* _– as they will typically touch on more political decisions like the one at hand. We had expected them to focus on this from the start, but as you note they did not follow up on their initial comments at the time._","2026-01-16T14:42:09.396Z"],["3816577","DAEN-1301","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","it seems that the data might be missing fom {{fact_rides_search}} before 2022 \n\n!image-20260116-144013.png|width=777,alt=\"image-20260116-144013.png\"!","2026-01-16T14:42:16.350Z"],["3816582","LSS-60647","LSS","lev.goffert@bolt.eu","Lev Goffert","[~accountid:5f06c5841a26ad0014019484], please respond with:\n\nThank you for your message.\n\nWe understand that being contacted from an unexpected phone number may have caused concern, and we appreciate you taking the time to raise this.\n\nAfter a careful review, we confirm the following:\n\n* Your phone number was lawfully shared with the courier solely for the purpose of completing your delivery.\n* The courier already had authorised access to your contact details as part of that delivery.\n* Your personal data was not disclosed to any third party, misused, or processed for any purpose unrelated to the delivery.\n\nWhile the courier should have used the communication tools and phone number registered with Bolt, their failure to do so does not represent a personal data breach under the GDPR. Importantly, there was no loss of control, unauthorised disclosure, or compromise of your personal data.\n\nWe have addressed this matter with the courier to prevent a recurrence. However, based on the circumstances and applicable data protection law, this incident does not give rise to a right to compensation.\n\nIf you remain dissatisfied, you are of course entitled to raise your concerns with the relevant data protection authority, who can independently assess the matter.\n\nSincerely,\nBolt Support","2026-01-16T14:42:58.774Z"],["3816583","GS-385","GS","gabriel.munteanu@bolt.eu","Gabriel Munteanu","For now I have done a hotfix to ignore unknown events but those changes are only in production and not in the codebase so if we do some changes to that code and deploy it we will reactivate the issue.","2026-01-16T14:43:05.244Z"],["3816584","INT-553","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: Implementation of provider targeting improvements in progress (scoped exclusion filter improvement with GA & PA). Holdout labels automation work aligned with ENG teams, will begin next week.","2026-01-16T14:43:43.687Z"],["3816585","PFI-834247","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Darja, the driver either forgot to finish the trip on time, or knowingly tried to overcharge the client. Since the order also resulted in a failed payment, by process, we refund the suspected overcharge amount. In this case, the PR was closed incorrectly 😄  and the full amount was refunded.\nFrom our side, you may compensate the final commission amount 7.64€ + predicted net income 9.84€ + tips 3.00€, although please do double-check the logic here.\n\nAs to the question of _why_ this specific commission amount was applied, this is not a Fraud issue. I’d recommend reaching out to Pricing or local OPS for this.\n","2026-01-16T14:43:52.287Z"],["3816588","INT-647","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: Development will start next week.","2026-01-16T14:44:03.081Z"],["3816591","LSS-61541","LSS","christos.hadjistylianou@bolt.eu","Christos Hadjistylianou","Hey [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] \n\nRegarding this comment “The central and recurring issue is a technical failure whereby the address I enter appears correctly on my side of the application (Nicosia), but on the driver-side application the destination appears as a different city (Paphos).”, I checked the orders of the last 2 months and none of them are shown to have a destination or pick-up in Paphos. \n\nIt’s probably something a driver said as an excuse not to pick him up. Something we cannot confirm though as all the communication is through in-app calls. \n\nHis home address had an issue in the past that was forwarded to the maps team that confirmed that the issue was fixed. ([Ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/49/MAPPROD-19741])","2026-01-16T14:44:22.257Z"],["3816592","LSS-61381","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:66939b2f-e5c1-42e2-8cbe-244458fd12f9] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^PoA (Bolt) (Luminor Agreements) (EE) - update 15.01.2026.asice] ","2026-01-16T14:44:39.315Z"],["3816593","XP-2368","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","[~accountid:5b8cea0ad0b4022bdc51a8a2] not fully decided, but since scorecard will be in AP likely both","2026-01-16T14:45:03.121Z"],["3816594","WD-22571","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","[~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a]  The report is build based on Plan Dimension as business object, which is not liked to Tax code business object, so i can not look up country from Tax code ((… so I need kind of build new Data audit report but based on Tax rate as primary business object (tax rate and tax code are related) \n\n!image-20260116-144356.png|width=1150,alt=\"image-20260116-144356.png\"!","2026-01-16T14:45:14.193Z"],["3816595","INT-652","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: Aligned to define playbook per spend channel as per  growth framework v2 (Churned, New+Reactivated, Occasional, Plus Ready, Plus). There will be campaign packages per channel, managed by Growth, that define the variable and fixed campaign parameters for each budget point. Starting with New+Reactivated, came up with playbook template - will now populate with all possible campaign parameters and align with GA on fixed & variable (by budget) parameters.","2026-01-16T14:45:27.783Z"],["3816598","INT-650","INT","mikk.tonissoo@bolt.eu","Mikk Tõnissoo","26W3: Initial development finished, will start testing once playbook is defined.","2026-01-16T14:45:57.534Z"],["3816599","BP-13443","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","Result of spike:\n\n* Overall, no blockers for Tailwind upgrade. Can be easily done, was successfully attempted with Kalep Ember and Business Portal.\n\n* Removing the prefix tw- also led to no issues, making it viable to remove it.\n* The amount of time necessary for upgrade is a few hours max.","2026-01-16T14:46:30.110Z"],["3816601","LSS-61423","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","hei, [~accountid:61979e9e977c5b007273d99d] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached. [^VOLIKIRI.asice] ","2026-01-16T14:46:48.584Z"],["3816604","WD-22592","WD","vladislav.kochetov@bolt.eu","Vladislav Kochetov","I need to create one, to be used in future for contractors:\n\nOrg name: Drive - Marketplace - Contractors\nPrimary location: Dubai, UAE - remote\nSuperior organization: Drive - Marketplace (Vladislav Kochetov)\n\n\n\n","2026-01-16T14:47:29.652Z"],["3816606","LSS-61607","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:618d20acfba4d0006ae30dd3] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Vilniaus vandenys UAB. Specialiosios sąlygos. Bolt Business (2) (1).adoc]\n[^REH_2025_2307_Ignitis renewables UAB. Specialiosios sąlygos. Bolt Business 2026.adoc]\n\n","2026-01-16T14:47:46.082Z"],["3816607","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768574834856869]*{color}:\nCreated a task for us to be picked up :bowing:\n{quote}","2026-01-16T14:48:02.194Z"],["3816608","BP-13415","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","need Dev to check for final solution","2026-01-16T14:48:07.940Z"],["3816609","BP-13321","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","need Dev to check for final solution","2026-01-16T14:48:17.933Z"],["3816610","L10N-28387","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26169](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26169)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T14:48:33.692Z"],["3816611","L10N-28388","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-26169](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-26169)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-16T14:48:34.578Z"],["3816612","LSS-61575","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60c88e6e8f2cc1006909fcf6] ! Please find the signed document(s) a