miankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","Not needed. We are setting both ext_id/public_id for records now (in new refund flow handling)","2026-01-16T14:54:58.312Z"],["3816686","WDFT-3506","WDFT","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","[^Submit_Supplier_v44.1 (12) (c3510c23-9ae1-437c-bf91-972275416cb0).zip]\n\n","2026-01-16T14:55:32.621Z"],["3816687","WFM-10023","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","role request: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601700","2026-01-16T14:55:51.991Z"],["3816688","BDB-1461","BDB","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:60ab71565dc18500701cae80] Pls find [here|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5422-44775&p=f&t=ig8RMYnEqDM0Zzvn-0] the copy draft for CA launch comms. Let us know if you need anything else to kickstart HoppPlus design toolkit, thanks! \n\n[~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] I’m on standby for OOH media plan (deciding on our vs comp’s offering).","2026-01-16T14:56:01.647Z"],["3816689","PFI-834289","PFI","akram.abubaker@bolt.eu","Akram Abubaker","!dedu.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T14:56:12.277Z"],["3816690","MVRT-1446","MVRT","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","Hey [~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3]\n\nWe’re technically ready with launch comms✨ This is not urgent as it’s regarding the 5th push in the flow, and we can edit it later, but:\n\nI noticed that the body copy says “{{Ride the new e-bike for as little as €x.xx}}“ - I assume it should say “€x.xx per minute”? The localisations also need an update in that case :smiling_face_with_tear: ","2026-01-16T14:56:44.391Z"],["3816691","LSS-61704","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bank conf (2).pdf] ","2026-01-16T14:57:08.461Z"],["3816693","EBIKE1-195","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Feedback from SATE-LITE:\n\nFor M16, 2 ways to be changed; change the internal cable gluing to outside cable gluing; change silicone glue to UV glue(as we find that it's still the micelle was \"seperated\" by the pressure under water in 1m during IPX7 test.\n\nFor the new proposal, we are testing now as well.\n\nshall come back to you soon on the testing results.\n\n|!889b4a17718b5542fde0086927ea9eac-20260116-145524.jpg|width=305,alt=\"889b4a17718b5542fde0086927ea9eac-20260116-145524.jpg\"!|!daa1f4f892bd659b180df3f92838a211-20260116-145537.jpg|width=226,alt=\"daa1f4f892bd659b180df3f92838a211-20260116-145537.jpg\"!|\n|!dd2538b270e46d94100c23c72c0026be-20260116-145542.png|width=226,alt=\"dd2538b270e46d94100c23c72c0026be-20260116-145542.png\"!|!2c784a88a5286552bd875c2d98cecca2-20260116-145551.png|width=226,alt=\"2c784a88a5286552bd875c2d98cecca2-20260116-145551.png\"!|","2026-01-16T14:57:48.796Z"],["3816694","WD-22524","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:10a49e8d-5a58-427c-a3ca-ddcab256a5d5] ! \n\nIn order to add  book code prompt to your matrix report, you firs need to add such prompt to your sub-reports, based on which *BOLT Management Reporting – Balance Sheet* is build, \n\nTo add book code as prompt to sub-report, first add it to filters of sub report and then to prompts of sub report. \n\n!image-20260116-145722.png|width=1423,alt=\"image-20260116-145722.png\"!\n\n!image-20260116-145734.png|width=1404,alt=\"image-20260116-145734.png\"!\n\n after that Book code will appear as a prompt to matrix report \n\n!image-20260116-145811.png|width=1404,alt=\"image-20260116-145811.png\"!","2026-01-16T14:58:18.458Z"],["3816695","EBIKE1-196","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Feedback from SATE-LITE:\n\nC10, the direction to add the glue outside the heat sink is totally right; also, we need to change the welding machine with more excision/controlling; the samples are in test.","2026-01-16T14:58:20.848Z"],["3816698","WFM-10022","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","WW-SHIFT has been added while the overtime has already been there all along [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95] \n\n!image-20260116-145814.png|width=745,alt=\"image-20260116-145814.png\"!\n\n!image-20260116-145857.png|width=748,alt=\"image-20260116-145857.png\"!","2026-01-16T14:59:45.319Z"],["3816700","DSR-3637","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - the answer letter and responsive data in the GDrive can be shared with the user (/) ","2026-01-16T15:00:55.850Z"],["3816701","BP-13456","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on Prelive rider app.\n\nAdd {{Review your company information}} banner (/) \n\n* banner should only be displayed for partially filled work profiles (/) \n\n!IMG_0178.PNG|width=310,alt=\"IMG_0178.PNG\"!\n\n\n\nIssues found:\n\n# [fixed] Currently the “Review your company information” banner is shown all the time (needs to be displayed only when a *required field is not filled)","2026-01-16T15:01:03.894Z"],["3816702","WFM-10007","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Ireland RH T1 queue moved to primary","2026-01-16T15:01:09.273Z"],["3816704","BDB-1494","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] lets go with the “*Food that’s at the door when you are*” then.","2026-01-16T15:01:34.347Z"],["3816705","SCM-1116","SCM","omar.masum@bolt.eu","Omar Faruk Masum","[~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] thanks for the list.\n\nHi [~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390], As discussed please help us to add these list of items in WD for further order process via WD.\nThank you!","2026-01-16T15:01:42.115Z"],["3816707","WFM-10009","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","removed queues [~accountid:63627a607d4645af4f03d008]","2026-01-16T15:02:09.684Z"],["3816708","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] for the schengen wall, can you kindly replace: *-_baggage takes a while, dinner does not._-*\nwith:\n*Food that’s at the door when you are*\n\nthanks!","2026-01-16T15:02:19.594Z"],["3816710","LSS-59467","LSS","andres.jogi@bolt.eu","Andres Jõgi","Thank you, we will proceed with the implementation.","2026-01-16T15:02:57.474Z"],["3816711","WFM-10012","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","They should now have Germany/Switzerland queue accesses reinstated [~accountid:5f8fc365950f8c0076328d3a] ","2026-01-16T15:04:09.404Z"],["3816712","SREDESK-7369","SREDESK","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","This week, the TTL was implemented on the {{taxify_subscription_marketplace.campaign_target}} table [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7345|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7345|smart-link], along with service-side caching. It seems the query has improved, as it no longer appears in the slow query rankings.\n\n[~accountid:712020:fc56290c-479e-4c00-8dd2-84e9af4473b0] shared [this|http://ti-incentives-pd-1.sqldb:2379/dashboard/#/slow_query/detail?digest=c1315ade24cfb22d343061b75c1481a2ae82a72ce07d309e55d4a9b9325defca&connection_id=2474686002&timestamp=1767176829.295785] other query with abnormal execution times during New Year's Eve. The avg execution time for this is 4.2ms\n\n\n","2026-01-16T15:04:53.425Z"],["3816714","PFI-834294","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T15:05:33.876Z"],["3816715","WFM-10019","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","queue access reinstated [~accountid:6127af434f2923006951af57] ","2026-01-16T15:05:37.690Z"],["3816721","WFM-10020","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Edit access reinstated [~accountid:712020:f1ed1d5f-b5cc-4b1c-99bc-943be4c483d4]","2026-01-16T15:07:09.629Z"],["3816722","DAEN-1301","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","[trying this|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/658191735195492/runs/932728801279916?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-16T15:07:30.818Z"],["3816723","LSS-60080","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi [~accountid:712020:da5adcfc-e0e5-4c21-a4df-4e108cffc244] \nJust following up on Alon’s question above - could you please confirm whether the rider’s account has now been secured and the password changed?","2026-01-16T15:08:16.604Z"],["3816724","LSS-61436","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:60f2a71843c956007065f2ad] , verified alterations made, and we can sign as is to avoid further delays related to this matter. In the future, we should consider revisiting extending the scope of work of the agreement.\n\nThanks so much,\n\nAlex ","2026-01-16T15:08:30.443Z"],["3816727","DSR-3157","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Jelena’s answer:\n\n{quote}Regarding two of your questions:\n\n* I may ask BPO TLs for reasoning, but I can bet it will be \"lack of attention\"\n* The response that BPO usually sent out. If this sounds OK, I will contact BPOs TL and ask to send it out:\n\n{{Hello XXX,  After a thorough investigation, we regrettably discovered that you received a significant amount of reports related to safety rule violation. According to our terms of service, which you agreed to upon registration, any activities that put clients safety at risk are strictly prohibited on our platform. Violation of these terms results in immediate termination of the user account.  Because we received numerous reports about safety related incidents for this reason your account will be suspended indefinitely.  This measure serves to protect our users and the integrity of our platform. We regret that it had to come to this.}}{quote}\n\n→ Confirmed further that the email is in line with the usual comms sent out to drivers in similar cases. Email will be send on their end. I have adapted the answer on our end.","2026-01-16T15:09:26.653Z"],["3816728","PFI-834296","PFI","shahnaz.huseynova@bolt-outsource.eu","Shahnaz Huseynova","[^149345221 (1).pdf]\n\n[^149345224 (1).pdf]\n\n[^149345228 (1).pdf]","2026-01-16T15:09:57.793Z"],["3816729","DSR-3157","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - the responsive data and answer in the Gdrive can be shared with the driver (/) ","2026-01-16T15:10:07.586Z"],["3816730","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi all,\n\nThank you very much for your help in collating the information in response to the court order – much appreciated by everyone involved.\n\nI’ve now been able to produce the *attached draft response letter and appendices* to the court order.\n\nBy way of update against [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]’s previous points:\n\n* Confirmed – thank you.\n* Thank you for this additional data – I’ve included it in our response.\n* I’ve applied redactions as suggested and clarified the periods of absence with Ramone. We have also included timestamps where appropriate.\n* Thank you for the further data; however, I’ve decided not to include this, as we’ve now removed the “Automated Online Time Restrictions” section. The dates provided fall outside the relevant period covered by the order.\n\n[~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a] – could you please review the attached document and confirm that you’re happy with its contents? Once confirmed, I’ll arrange for it to be sent to you for signature of the certificate.\n\nIn the interests of time, once the document is signed, I’ll email a copy to Thorntons Law LLP, and will also print and post a physical copy when I’m back in the office next week.\n\nThanks again everyone for your support on this! 🙂 \n\nCc: [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab] \n\n[^Response Letter to Court Order Ref. No PIC-PN3178-25 - Bolt Services UK Limited - 16 January 2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T15:10:19.546Z"],["3816733","LSS-59421","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:1f6c1fe9-0a65-49ae-b40f-fa69270b3167]\nCould you please clarify if the privacy support is still needed for this incident?\nThank you!\n","2026-01-16T15:10:58.955Z"],["3816734","DRX-28210","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","Tested and verified DI.127.0 (195054040) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.3\n\n* Badge is present when driver has two profiles\n** Private driver and Substitute\n\n\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 5-02-21 PM_1.MP4]","2026-01-16T15:11:02.187Z"],["3816735","DRX-26884","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28210 has been resolved","2026-01-16T15:11:07.873Z"],["3816740","LSS-61189","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nI think that the problem today is that currently, we don’t have a clear or consistent process in place for handling such cases — including who should prepare the report, sign it, and submit it.\nTo address this gap, I propose we implement a *simple, structured process* that ensures:\n\n* Proper legal framing of the complaint,\n* Internal clarity on ownership and responsibilities,\n* Consistency across teams (Safety, Legal, CS).\n\nProposed Process:\n\n# *Safety or CS completes a standard incident report template* (drafted below),\n# *Legal signs a formal cover letter* to accompany the report,\n# *Safety sends the complete file by email* to the relevant local police authority (via email)\n\nDraft Documents:\n\n* *Threat Incident Report Template* (for CS/Safety to complete)\n* *Cover Letter Template* (for Legal to sign)\n\nThe idea is to keep the process lightweight but structured, so we can act quickly when a threat is made, and reduce legal and reputational risk.\nCould you please review the two draft templates and let me know if you’re aligned with this approach? Once confirmed, we can finalise the materials and share them with the Safety and CS teams.\nThanks,\n\nTEMPLATE: *Threat Incident Report – Bolt France*\n\n{quote}To be completed by Customer Support or Safety{quote}\n\nFieldInput\n\n*Date of Report*[DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n*Rider Full Name (if known)*\n\n*Rider Bolt ID /* \n\n*PhoneDriver* \n\n*NameDriver* \n\n*Bolt ID*\n\n*Date and Time of IncidentCity /* \n\n*RegionType of Threat*Verbal / Physical / via App / Other (specify)\n\n*Description of Threat*[Describe what was said, done, or sent. Be precise. Include how driver or platform was threatened.]\n\n*Screenshots / Evidence Attached*Yes / No\n\n*Reported to Customer Support*[Date]\n\n*Internal Reference (ticket # or Slack thread)Any Prior Incidents Linked to Rider?*Yes / No / Unknown\n\n*Action Taken by CS or Safety*Rider blocked / warning issued / driver supported / etc.\n\nCOVER LETTER TEMPLATE (to be signed by Legal)\n\n{quote}*To be printed, signed, and attached to the Threat Report for police filing*{quote}\n\n*[BoltOps]*\n [Registered address]\n SIRET: [SIRET Number]\n [Date]\n*À l'attention de :* Station de Police \n\n*Objet : Dépôt de plainte*\nMadame, Monsieur,\nNotre société souhaite porter plainte contre un utilisateur de notre plateforme {color:#bf2600}ayant proféré des menaces graves à l'encontre d’un de nos chauffeurs partenaires et de la société elle-même(to be adapted).{color}\nLes faits se sont déroulés le [date], à [lieu], impliquant le compte client [nom ou identifiant du rider] et le chauffeur [nom ou identifiant du chauffeur]. Les menaces, telles que décrites dans le rapport joint, sont constitutives d’un délit prévu aux articles 222-17 et suivants du Code pénal.\nVous trouverez ci-joint :\n\n* Le rapport d’incident détaillé,\n* Les éléments de preuve disponibles (captures d’écran, messages, échanges),\n* Les informations d’identification pertinentes.\n\nNous vous remercions de bien vouloir donner suite à ce signalement et restons à votre disposition pour toute information complémentaire.\nVeuillez agréer, Madame, Monsieur, l’expression de nos salutations distinguées.\n\n *Bolt– Department Legal*\nWDYT? if we are aligned, we should recap this process for Emilie and likely put the above in a google doc.\n\nthanks a lot\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-16T15:13:52.143Z"],["3816741","LSS-55769","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] \n\nWe approved an extension of the campaign till the 31 of March.\nAn additional IO for 95k will be sent by Paylead to Ahto Kink, please support us in signing asap.","2026-01-16T15:14:08.414Z"],["3816742","LSS-60630","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:5de3bf86-6cba-4bd9-b71a-087b2b4da2eb] \n\nI’ve updated the [document|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1w7CDmbtYbCSjK5f1schDBDApPXXREBw-ieanzUBQXAU/edit?gid=0#gid=0].\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nI must note that some responses were already in the guidelines. I kindly ask you to please pay closer attention when completing this, rather than relying on the privacy team, as the guidelines are designed for self-service and to protect privacy resources.\n{panel}\n\nFor the remaining AI-related questions, I recommend:\n\n# Consulting the AI Compliance FAQ - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/6879281810/Bolt+Business+AI+Compliance+Questions+FAQ|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/6879281810/Bolt+Business+AI+Compliance+Questions+FAQ]\n# If you cannot find a response, consult the Legal Team and submit a ticket in the Help Centre. Please add [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] to the ticket for visibility, as it relates to Bolt Business.","2026-01-16T15:14:27.411Z"],["3816743","DSR-3637","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Data and response sent! Thanks! 👑","2026-01-16T15:14:59.198Z"],["3816745","LSS-60630","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","I will be closing the ticket but please let me know if you have further privacy-related questions - in this case, we can re-open the ticket🙂 \n\nI will also make sure that the questions that were not addressed in our existing guidelines will be added so next time you can proceed without involving the privacy team😌 ","2026-01-16T15:15:37.546Z"],["3816746","LSS-61512","LSS","bruna.miguel@bolt.eu","Bruna Miguel","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ,\n\nWe’ve received the following email from Medicina del lavoro and the contracts attached.\n\n_“Buongiorno,_\n\n_confermiamo il contratto in essere tra la nostra Società Medicina del Lavoro S.r.l. e BOLT (allegato Contratto Bolt)._\n\n_L’offerta per i servizi riguardanti la sorveglianza sanitaria era stata inviata dalla Società Sigmaelle della quale facciamo parte come “Gruppo” ma era stato specificato che la fatturazione relativa ai servizi del medico competente sarebbero stati gestiti/fatturati direttamente da Medicina del Lavoro._\n\n_Lo stesso contratto, a seguito della vostra richiesta, vi è già stato inviato dalla collega in data 28/11/2025 (allegato 5571-Bolt SL 108-22).”_\n\nDoes this mean we do not need to terminate a contract with them, because it was with Sigmaelle? Could you let us know? \n\nThank you! \n\n[^Sigmaelle Contract - Termination Document 2026 H&S.pdf]\n[^Contratto Bolt.pdf]\n\n ","2026-01-16T15:15:40.700Z"],["3816747","BDB-1494","BDB","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] Aligned, thank you!","2026-01-16T15:15:46.170Z"],["3816749","PFI-742818","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] you have the discounts project, right? ","2026-01-16T15:16:19.711Z"],["3816752","LSS-55769","LSS","mauricio.oropeza@bolt.eu","Mauricio Oropeza","New IO: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1x3eelrJzgnN69y2qb-juAa_kpgI3TW8s/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1x3eelrJzgnN69y2qb-juAa_kpgI3TW8s/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T15:16:38.255Z"],["3816753","FPD-1534","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Update regarding hive partitioning:\n\n* we can organize our data in folders like `{{/city=X/file1.parquet  and `/city=Y/file2.parquet`}}and have it ingested into a single table from there, but the city column wouldn’t appear in the table automatically and would need to be present in the source files from the beginning (so basically whether we use the folder structure or not depends on what is more convenient)","2026-01-16T15:16:41.225Z"],["3816755","RDS-1351","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] [~accountid:712020:73f630c1-899f-4b5d-ac71-8a7e5c89eb30] agree it is not discoverable, probably, an (i) icon (or an equivalent) next to it would make it clearer. \n\nBut the bigger question is, should we generally make the Rider Rating concept more visible and detailed, as building reputation and trust over time is often an integral part of two sided marketplace. Something to think about.","2026-01-16T15:16:42.973Z"],["3816756","LSS-61082","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* email chain confirming landlord agreeable position:\n\n# Landlord agrees licence to underlet (landlord’s legal costs of £2,250 plus VAT payable by Voi/Bolt)\n# Voi breaks on 26^th^ July per terms of lease\n# Bolt enters new lease from 27^th^ July, the terms of which the parties will start negotiating now and landlord’s legal costs of £3,500 plus VAT payable by Bolt.\n\n[^Bolt Mail - RE_Bolt - Liverpool Scooter Operations Unit 9 Phoenix Park [IMAN-WSLIVE.FID5498717].pdf .pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T15:16:48.156Z"],["3816757","LSS-60630","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","[~accountid:712020:5de3bf86-6cba-4bd9-b71a-087b2b4da2eb] I also noticed the link permissions are open to the internet - this is not allowed per our internal policy and is a security risk.\n\nPlease kindly change the permissions only to Bolt organisation.🤫 ","2026-01-16T15:17:01.350Z"],["3816758","LSS-61732","LSS","andrea.rietmeijer@bolt.eu","Andrea Rietmeijer","[^Branding Contract - Durali Özmen (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T15:17:55.078Z"],["3816759","WFM-10023","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:5c75f61c-3531-4b91-8943-2ee3c355f252]","2026-01-16T15:17:59.861Z"],["3816773","LSS-46781","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* further Slack message sent to Daniel Severin, chasing for an update.\n\n!image-20260116-152038.png|width=1165,alt=\"image-20260116-152038.png\"!","2026-01-16T15:20:41.816Z"],["3816774","LSS-61172","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Internal update: I haven’t been able to locate a driver profile matching the information provided just yet","2026-01-16T15:21:10.431Z"],["3816775","DO-5809","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","Please ask on #analytics-engineering-support","2026-01-16T15:21:10.922Z"],["3816780","DO-5801","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","Hey! Where did you get this link and are you sure you need access to an Explore, not to the Look/Dashboard?","2026-01-16T15:22:13.494Z"],["3816781","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] sent ! thanks","2026-01-16T15:22:55.958Z"],["3816783","PFI-831958","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","Dear team, driver payment is yet to reflect. Please assist.","2026-01-16T15:23:05.710Z"],["3816785","WFM-10011","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:61d2a784e763790068e85541]changes have been applied both in assembled and admin queue assignments. However, please be cautioned that I just received the request to assign them to safety queues a few days earlier. If changes need to be made, raise a new ticket.","2026-01-16T15:23:12.781Z"],["3816786","BP-13405","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","It was decided to be unnecessary to upgrade.\n\nWe still need it for font files, but everything else is not needed and doesn’t get used either way, so we can keep it as-is.","2026-01-16T15:23:14.611Z"],["3816787","MLC-3936","MLC","dovainis.kaleda@bolt.eu","Dovainis Kalėda","Previous week progress:\nDeprecated after alignment / ownership changed:\n\n# [+Page: Request for Additional Rider User Properties in Braze for Content Personalisation+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/5282005495/Request+for+Additional+Rider+User+Properties+in+Braze+for+Content+Personalisation?search_id=2b1af7ee-e552-4747-8abe-80b5e5f4757f]\n# [+Page: [How-To] Send Push Notification via CleverTap (if you don't receive them normally)+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/4626252603/How-To+Send+Push+Notification+via+CleverTap+if+you+don+t+receive+them+normally?search_id=2b1af7ee-e552-4747-8abe-80b5e5f4757f]\n# [+Page: Rider Activation Journey Revamp+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/4728946694/Rider+Activation+Journey+Revamp?search_id=2b1af7ee-e552-4747-8abe-80b5e5f4757f]\n# [+Page: [WIP] Rider Airport Initiatives+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/4555505811/WIP+Rider+Airport+Initiatives?search_id=2b1af7ee-e552-4747-8abe-80b5e5f4757f]","2026-01-16T15:23:37.979Z"],["3816788","CRC-1980","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Mombasa pilot scheduled for JAN 21. ","2026-01-16T15:23:49.089Z"],["3816790","MQA-4248","MQA","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","[DRIVERAPP-T3791 (1.0)|https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin:com.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/v2/testCase/274562076/testScript] On the step 2 the error banner is shown instead of the screen when a lead where documents were declined was used\n\n!IMG_4407.PNG|width=173,alt=\"IMG_4407.PNG\"!","2026-01-16T15:24:14.625Z"],["3816791","RDS-1066","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e74df6f3c90030cce2deedb] Love the idea, but I would question some descriptions. \n\n”Accessibility” is not wrong, but in the digital word is so connected with just following WCAG guidelines, the title feels misleading. I would rather rename it something like: “Ride options for people with disabilities”. Regarding the theme, I also suggest changing from Usability to Reliability.","2026-01-16T15:24:19.926Z"],["3816792","CRC-2321","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Mombasa pilot scheduled for JAN 21.","2026-01-16T15:24:31.102Z"],["3816793","CRC-2322","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Scheduled work for scoping implementation estimation in January 2026.","2026-01-16T15:24:40.418Z"],["3816794","LSS-60984","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","I’ve sent the suggested message to the Authority [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/713188559] (/) ","2026-01-16T15:24:43.055Z"],["3816795","CRC-2308","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Confirmed as queued task at ProcessOut for February 2026.","2026-01-16T15:24:48.857Z"],["3816797","CRC-1768","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Ready for implementing when Pay After Ride is ready / Attempting to test wallets UX and flow with drivers before that.","2026-01-16T15:25:46.468Z"],["3816799","CRC-1988","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Re-engaging with local branch after confirming legal entity payment operator is Bolt Operations OU","2026-01-16T15:26:31.971Z"],["3816800","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Vibration test\n\nThe added features on the side prevent the phone from rotating.\n\n|!image-20260116-151447.png|width=302,alt=\"image-20260116-151447.png\"!|!2d1170c4498dbd29add724687fe26013-20260116-151621.jpg|width=302,alt=\"2d1170c4498dbd29add724687fe26013-20260116-151621.jpg\"!|!4ecbd50a6785ea524899257af76080c1.mp4|width=320,alt=\"4ecbd50a6785ea524899257af76080c1.mp4\"!|!152b8ba3-85ea-4a1d-bad1-2e17dc12c58c.png|width=175,alt=\"152b8ba3-85ea-4a1d-bad1-2e17dc12c58c.png\"!\nPhone holder dind`t change its vertical alignment.|!f74a3036db69d5200ff5d51928084a19.mp4|width=320,alt=\"f74a3036db69d5200ff5d51928084a19.mp4\"!|","2026-01-16T15:26:37.648Z"],["3816802","DIO-528","DIO","mihai.esanu@bolt.eu","Mihai Eșanu","W2: Switched system to 1way as per their request. Still waiting for them.","2026-01-16T15:26:44.855Z"],["3816807","MLC-3710","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 16th*+\n\n* Worked with Martech to define methodology to calculate Business Admin Coverage\n* We agreed to standardize based Rider methodology for time-window stages, with one exception (Onboarding)\n*  We will adopt the Rider full-month lifecycle overlap approach (stage counts if active at any point during the month, eligibility checked at month-end, comms counted if sent within the stage window and month) for Acquisition, Activation, and Churn\n* Onboarding will be documented as an exception because it’s event-triggered at signup and can be measured as a simpler event-based stage.\n* Queries after changes need to be reviewed - early next week\n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:d30129ff-7d6f-4bbd-82d3-3c1cbd5e1d77] FYI some of the challenges and back and forth:\n\n* *Main challenge:* mismatched methodology created misleading coverage. Early queries mixed a *12-month addressable base* with *only one month of comms sent (Dec)*, which produced artificially low coverage (e.g., onboarding+activation ~18%). Once aligned to like-for-like periods, onboarding jumped to ~97%, proving the issue was the measurement approach, not necessarily comms performance.\n* *Second challenge: l*ifecycle “stage” definitions + data sources didn’t line up. There was confusion between the Working Doc stage naming vs Martech/Braze logic (e.g., onboarding vs activation definitions), plus cases where “unique users targeted” included IDs that *d*idn’t meet stage rules (activation example: users already had orders prior to the message), which overstated targeted counts and broke trust in the denominator/numerator.\n* *Third challenge:* snapshot logic undercounted eligibility for stages with long eligibility windows. Activation/Churn comms are sent over extended periods (e.g., activation day 6–105 until first order; churn beyond 30 days), so evaluating eligibility on a single as-of date (e.g., Dec 31) misses users who were eligible earlier in the month and makes coverage look too low.","2026-01-16T15:27:39.811Z"],["3816816","CSDA-286","CSDA","radek.peka@bolt.eu","Radek Peka","Hey Mariia,\n\nThank you for sharing the Looker dashboard. We have reviewed it and noticed a few issues that we wanted to flag.\n\nFirst, when filtering by Team Leader and then by vertical or country, the report shows only three agents, although there are four team members performing validations in Czech/Slovak delivery.\n\nSecond, the data of CZ/SK DE appears to include only Non-Safety and Low/Moderate Safety cases. High and Significant Safety cases are not reflected, even though we know that such cases were completed during the relevant month.\n\nAdditionally, the validation counts seem inconsistent. This may be related to having two BPOs (TP and Mplus) within the markets and two scorecards within the region. For example, for Nikola Spoustová, the report shows 105 validations for the month, while in Klaus, it shows 149 validations across all BPOs for the same period.\n\nWe also noticed some inconsistencies with date filtering. When filtering for three completed months, the report sometimes displays only October, and in other cases only December. Our OM manager experienced a similar issue and mentioned that October appears as the latest month in the report for her as well.\n\nLastly, after checking with other TLs in the region, we observed that for Romanian ride-hailing, the report indicates one agent completing eight validations per month, which does not seem accurate at all. I will also ask my colleagues to add their observations here, too.\n\nOverall, this feedback is shared constructively. The Looker dashboard is a great initiative and looks very promising. Thank you for putting this together. 💚\n\nBest regards,\nRadek Peka","2026-01-16T15:28:50.453Z"],["3816818","PFI-834308","PFI","moridiyat.olanrewaju@bolt-outsource.eu","Moridiyat Olanrewaju","!image-20260116-152613.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T15:29:06.010Z"],["3816819","DIO-429","DIO","mihai.esanu@bolt.eu","Mihai Eșanu","W2: Created 17 live integrations","2026-01-16T15:29:10.611Z"],["3816820","WD-22592","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","I’ve created the org for you. Let me know if I can help with anything else!","2026-01-16T15:29:20.576Z"],["3816822","LSS-61569","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:712020:ec09f884-709e-4d12-8b74-3045f0b19650] , I have review modifications made to the NDA by the counter-party and can confirm that we have agreed on all aspects, except for their proposal of amendment to clause 11. Warranties, on which I have previously requested your input as per the comment inserted, namely “_[OPS] - please let us know on whether during the Relationship covered by the NDA you envisage that the counter-party will communicate any confidential information to us (meaning any data, document, information etc. as described in the present agreement), and, in case positive, please consider if we can accept having, for eg, incomplete data, inaccurate data, etc. coming from them, as proposed.”._ As such, their proposal of having the clause mutual and our input on this is dependent on your feedback as per my request.\nAs such, I am waiting for your feedback on this.\n\nBest,\n\nAlex","2026-01-16T15:29:26.522Z"],["3816823","RDS-612","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5f770d66021acf0076bbaef1] Hi! What is the status of this initiative from a dev perspective?","2026-01-16T15:29:53.567Z"],["3816825","PFI-834309","PFI","diana.bernyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Diana Bernyk","[^statement_17685768794337231077606295360430.pdf]","2026-01-16T15:30:12.399Z"],["3816828","CRC-1877","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Agreed to meet again on week of 21 Jan ","2026-01-16T15:30:48.974Z"],["3816830","CSDA-303","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-16T15:31:01.264Z"],["3816831","PFI-834310","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^Tranzactie_30-12-2025_13-10-41 (3).pdf]","2026-01-16T15:31:14.502Z"],["3816833","CRC-1767","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] Pasha Legal requested a change of the document used to their template which also has the AZ language version. Submitted to legal team","2026-01-16T15:31:35.943Z"],["3816835","RDS-651","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] , it looks like slack link shows a different topic. ","2026-01-16T15:32:10.905Z"],["3816838","WD-22589","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:633be2c588ed2ebef97dd442] [~accountid:5da9bc599aebed0c29c2acb8] \nJust letting your know that I’m working on your request and will try to finish it latest by Monday.\n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-16T15:34:39.308Z"],["3816840","RDS-1222","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:52a73231-4dc8-4054-82a3-d741603d65af] [~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] for some strange reason, I see this topic in RiderX (Selected Domains looks fine though). ","2026-01-16T15:34:56.824Z"],["3816841","PFI-834314","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","[^plata f 407263.pdf]","2026-01-16T15:35:39.276Z"],["3816842","PFI-834315","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","[^plata f 221545.pdf]","2026-01-16T15:35:42.357Z"],["3816843","PFI-834316","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","[^plata f 179607.pdf]","2026-01-16T15:35:46.340Z"],["3816844","LSS-36510","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Closing this ticket considering legal advise has been provided","2026-01-16T15:36:15.964Z"],["3816845","LSS-61295","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] !\nWe can close this ticket, since I contacted the Inspector and sent him an email directly with the information required.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-16T15:37:05.344Z"],["3816848","FPD-1539","FPD","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","Conversion rates model accuracy with actual inputs are now integrated into accuracy reporting","2026-01-16T15:38:14.875Z"],["3816850","LSS-61172","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a] - I have not been able to locate a driver profile that matches the information provided by the law firm. Is this something you might be able to support with? \n\nShould there not be any driver profile matching, then we can check whether this individual was actually employed (full time or as a contractor) with Bolt. In case we still cannot locate anyone in our systems, then we will have to follow up with the requestor for some more information.","2026-01-16T15:39:41.552Z"],["3816851","LSS-59165","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] thanks for reassigning this one to me. Agreed, it’s not a straightforward incident.\n\nI’ve checked the BeeHive outreach to [claims@prime.co.za|mailto:claims@prime.co.za] and at the moment we only have their auto-reply (they indicated a response within 2 working days). I’ll wait for their reply before moving forward with the assessment.","2026-01-16T15:39:50.367Z"],["3816852","FPD-1521","FPD","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","h1. Investigation Summary\n\nThe team identified and resolved reporting discrepancies between Investment Modelling and Rides Finance teams across two key areas:\n\nh2. 1. Differences in Actuals (FPD-1524) - Completed\n\nThe team discovered that Rides Finance uses a different MAPE calculation formula than the standard definition. RF calculates MAPE as {{abs(actual - predicted)/predicted}}, while the team correctly uses {{abs(predicted - actual)/actual}}. After accounting for this formula difference and RF's weighting approach (MAPE weighted by adjusted planned finished orders per market), the data points matched exactly between both reporting systems.\n\nh2. 2. Differences in Accuracy Calculations (FPD-1522) - Completed\n\nThe investigation revealed market-specific patterns of discrepancies across multiple metrics:\n\n* *Tallinn & Riga*: Discrepancies in most metrics except \"online hours per active partner,\" with root cause traced to S2O conversion rate generation logic\n* *Zürich*: Partner churn percentage showed 31% in accuracy reporting vs 26.5% in model files; numbers aligned after adjustment\n* *Barcelona*: Issues with active riders, rider churn, and rider activation metrics\n* *Košice & Stockholm*: Discrepancies starting from S2O conversion rate and online hours, cascading to partner churn, partner activations, and active partners\n* *Phuket*: Issues with search sessions and online hours affecting downstream partner metrics\n\nBoth subtasks are now complete, with discrepancies explained and calculation alignment established with Rides Finance.","2026-01-16T15:39:59.384Z"],["3816853","CSDA-282","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hi again! Thank you for coming back and providing the details 🙌\n\nWe have also discussed this request with JZ: it was agreed that for now, we won’t be picking it up.\n\nWe do have a project planned later this year to migrate supplier reports to the new_gen sources (similar to the internal report transition started in November - [slack post|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CFN1NTKB5/p1761565639987449], but for external reports). As part of that project, we will also look into whether the supplier report format needs an update. The supplier view/report based on Sprout data would be considered then as part of this project, alongside other related views.\n\nFor now, I will close this Service Desk request. But once the project kicks off, we will ensure the announcement is shared with the CS teams and leads.\n\nLet me know if you have any further comments or questions. Have a nice week ✨ ","2026-01-16T15:40:06.355Z"],["3816855","WEBSD-1490","WEBSD","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","[^PDF -  12122025_ECIJA_BOLT_ENG  ESP_Service Provider Terms (Rides) CONFIDENTIAL AND SUBJECT TO LEGAL PRIVILEGE_VF.docx.pdf]\n\n[^Word. 12122025_ECIJA_BOLT_ENG  ESP_Service Provider Terms (Rides) CONFIDENTIAL AND SUBJECT TO LEGAL PRIVILEGE_VF.docx]","2026-01-16T15:43:25.922Z"],["3816857","RDS-849","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] Really cool idea! It may not be seen as a big impact, but hard to miss when seen and IMO can generate clear positive emotions.","2026-01-16T15:43:44.985Z"],["3816860","WFM-10015","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, it's done","2026-01-16T15:45:39.810Z"],["3816861","LSS-60420","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:3628e8e4-2c88-4d47-8c51-14aa1e98735c], do you need any additional information, or can we close this ticket?","2026-01-16T15:46:14.302Z"],["3816863","FDBT-4800","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-16T15:47:08.012Z"],["3816864","INT-775","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","26W3: _[Note: most of the DS team was either sick or on holiday for the full week, we only had 20% DS IC capacity this week]_\nThe team completed comprehensive hyperparameter tuning analysis across multiple trial configurations (15, 30, 50, and 100 trials) to determine optimal model performance. Results showed that 30 trials consistently delivered the best portfolio-level performance for both finished orders and GMV forecasting, while higher trial counts (50 and 100) often underperformed. Backtest results showed how simply increasing hyperparameter to 30 led to: \n\n* GMV local MAPE diminishing from 7.82% to 7.26%\n\n* Finished orders MAPE diminishing from 6.89% to 6.68%\n\nThe analysis revealed that increasing hyperparameter trials beyond 30 provides diminishing returns and is not a low-hanging fruit for accuracy improvements as originally hypothesized. The team is therefore moving forward with 30 trials as the standard configuration, which reduces training time while maintaining or slightly improving forecast accuracy. ","2026-01-16T15:47:26.547Z"],["3816866","RDS-951","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] [~accountid:712020:73f630c1-899f-4b5d-ac71-8a7e5c89eb30] [~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] honestly speaking, the experience is seriously bad here (no option to upload a photo, taking a photo automatically, etc.).\n\nDo we know how many Riders are using this option? If adoption is small, I would consider killing it entirely.","2026-01-16T15:48:56.009Z"],["3816867","RDS-1313","RDS","karina.gorodnitskaia@bolt.eu","Karina Gorodnitskaia","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] Oh yes, sorry about that. We’re also working on copy updates, so I mistakenly associated this ticket with that work as well. But yes, the purple color is a bug.","2026-01-16T15:49:08.687Z"],["3816884","PFI-834324","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^transaction-confirmation-report_ro-ro_70ad8c.pdf]","2026-01-16T15:49:44.176Z"],["3816892","INT-776","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","26W3: We have launched a new special events management sheet ([https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1b_DtmqObaoRhlNDV4iK5p8u3MNPjzAIpRd18bYPFXuc/edit?gid=71978825#gid=71978825|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1b_DtmqObaoRhlNDV4iK5p8u3MNPjzAIpRd18bYPFXuc/edit?gid=71978825#gid=71978825|smart-link] ) that allows country teams to flag events affecting their cities, both in the past and in the future. We are currently working on loading those new events in the model, while we’ve given country teams up to Feb 1st to provide their inputs.\n\nAs a bonus, the new special events table is now made available to all other teams at Bolt to enable them to build more robust forecasting solutions within their domain.","2026-01-16T15:51:58.199Z"],["3816893","LSS-61093","LSS","loredana.panait@bolt.eu","Loredana Panait","Hi [~accountid:622f787a1f014e0069cc0d85] , \n\nDo you know if Malta entity is registered with MBR? This is also requested for the above set up.\n\nThank you, \nLore\n\n","2026-01-16T15:52:09.506Z"],["3816895","LSS-59454","LSS","kristjan.jalakas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Jalakas","Hi, [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] & [~accountid:712020:0051a059-9c34-4c65-96bf-ddd219dfda7c] \n\n\n\nI agree with [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] that it would be rather impossible for LHV to sign a template that would be edited after they provide a signature. As already shared, the framework agreement allows for the vehicle to be used in other EU countries, therefore, cannot we just have some short document that reiterates the same point and have that signed by LHV and use it as appendix for the template [~accountid:712020:0051a059-9c34-4c65-96bf-ddd219dfda7c] shared above? In that case, necessary details have been covered via template + LHV’s go-ahead is formally recognised where they are the owner of the vehicle.","2026-01-16T15:52:43.426Z"],["3816896","LSS-60707","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Thanks, [~accountid:712020:6cd5c50c-08f0-4f10-98a4-ab7a39fef5d3] ! \n\nRe_: Could it maybe be solved by just_ *_changing the T&C listed incentive period to 7 days, always going Mon-Sun?_* _I think this would make more sense, as the bonus campaigns are always set up for this period anyways._\n\nDo you mean by this that the incentive period shall last 7 days counting from Monday until Sunday *(instead of current period of 3 months)?* If so, I would confirm if this change impacts automatic prolongation for 30 days since the day of the successful verification? Or this change makes the prolongation for 7 days though? \n\n_Incentive period - the standard procedure and practical timelines are as follows:_\n\n_a) A new car applies for branding via a form_\n\n_b) If their application is approved, they can set an appointment with a wrapping company_\n\n_c) Once the car is branded, the driver uploads a photo of it in their driver documents - this is the manual review/verification stage._\n\n_d) The incentive for said car starts the following Monday 00:00 after the photo was uploaded. There is a deadline for uploads at Friday noon. Any later submissions are considered the same as next week’s uploads._\n\n_e) On the first day of the incentive a new verification process is triggered for the car, in order for the driver to be able to perform automated verifications going forward. This means the driver needs to upload new pictures of the car directly through the app (not uploading a document in their document set as before). The driver has 7 days to perform the in-app verification._\n\n_If they fail, they lose the branding bonus (it will have effectively lasted only 7 days) and they need to go back to step c)_\n\n_If they succeed,_ {color:#ff5630}*_the incentive period is automatically prolonged for 30 days since the day of the successful verification_*{color}_. 7 days before this period ends, the in-app verification process is triggered again. This would then go on indefinitely as long as the driver successfully verifies and we don’t deactivate the bonus on the car manually._\n\n_Please let me know if you this needs any further clarification._","2026-01-16T15:52:46.803Z"],["3816897","LSS-61733","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Summary:*\n\n# High value BB tender in DK\n# Escalated to privacy team last minute.\n# Request - check the supplier agreement & RfP sheet - shared in the main ticket.\n\n*Status*: completed - input provided in Slack & the main ticket.","2026-01-16T15:53:19.096Z"],["3816900","LSS-50764","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","yeah, thanks, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] !\n\n[~accountid:5cd9daa0bc70090d6ce26227] do your thing 😊 ","2026-01-16T15:53:46.680Z"],["3816901","CSDA-258","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hi again!\n\nDouble-checked: you don’t have explore access to any of those models. Unfortunately, I can’t find what role should it be; but you can raise a SD request to the IT team to grant you explore access to [+https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/curated/fact_rides_order?qid=q6XKL3UWGEX4u1WJbk4ozq&toggle=fil+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/curated/fact_rides_order?qid=q6XKL3UWGEX4u1WJbk4ozq&toggle=fil] - they should be able to check and assign the needed role in Looker 🙌 \n\nAlso, I saved the query as a Look in my personal folder - you should be able to check it and copy it to your folder. Here is the link to the Look - [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46823|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/46823].\n\nHave a nice weekend ✨ ","2026-01-16T15:55:09.545Z"],["3816904","LSS-58216","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Thank you for confirming [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] - glad to hear this.","2026-01-16T15:56:51.389Z"],["3816907","LSS-45240","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Closing this ticket due to inactivity","2026-01-16T15:57:23.994Z"],["3816908","LSS-59793","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Solidgate accepted Bolt’s suggestions; negotiations completed.\n# Legal Ops is coordinating on signature.","2026-01-16T15:57:47.773Z"],["3816910","INT-352","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","26W3: The team progressed on the annual reforecasting cycle (Release 2026-01-01) by updating dataset generation infrastructure to support revised business scenario modeling. The methodology was adjusted to use relative percentage changes (±25%) rather than absolute percentage point adjustments (±3pp), enabling more realistic sensitivity analysis across markets with varying baseline metrics. This change ensures that scenario testing scales appropriately with market size and historical performance, improving the reliability of annual forecast ranges provided to finance and operations teams. Pipeline execution was completed to generate updated forecasts for the 2026 planning cycle. Ongoing support to GAs adjusting the models is provided","2026-01-16T15:58:15.970Z"],["3816918","LSS-61734","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T16:01:26.425Z"],["3816921","LSS-52247","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/11wqGR6OdtYiTgycai2RCmj6NY0TpGx5ksX3o0dE0a98/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/11wqGR6OdtYiTgycai2RCmj6NY0TpGx5ksX3o0dE0a98/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]","2026-01-16T16:04:24.008Z"],["3816922","INT-386","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","26W3:   The team integrated conversion rate model accuracy with actual inputs into the accuracy reporting pipeline, enabling more effective root cause analysis when model predictions diverge from outcomes. Reporting alignment was also established with Rides Finance, ensuring both teams work from consistent metrics when evaluating model performance and presenting incentives allocation recommendations to stakeholders.","2026-01-16T16:04:50.722Z"],["3816923","LSS-44070","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Closing this ticket considering there are no further action to be taken from Legal side.","2026-01-16T16:05:55.984Z"],["3816924","RDS-1066","RDS","reinis.paulins@bolt.eu","Reinis Paulins","Renaming the ticket is fine if it helps us move faster on this, and move ticket from “Parking lot” 🅿️  😀 \n\nThe core vision of the design is to give riders explicit control over what information they share and how the app adapts to their needs, rather than limiting the experience to predefined categories like WAV or Assist. \n\nThe aim is to offer a scalable preference control centre that will first address ride-related requirements but will eventually be  expanded into more general accessibility options, such as reduced motion or high contrast modes, which sort of touches on the WCAG area.","2026-01-16T16:06:21.319Z"],["3816925","CSDA-286","CSDA","radek.peka@bolt.eu","Radek Peka","I have now identified that we have specific CEE scorecards under the Scorecard Name type, which resolves the issue regarding the number of people displayed in my team. The issue with the month filtering also appears to be resolved. However, the validation counts still seem slightly inaccurate.","2026-01-16T16:06:32.913Z"],["3816927","AIOT-509","AIOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Short results: many issues found with optical image quality, otherwise fine.\nTotal: 48 pcs\nBarely usable: 2\nPoor: 18 (should not pass QC, but still usable)\nOK: 28","2026-01-16T16:08:00.877Z"],["3816928","LSS-58326","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Closing this ticket, since legal advise has been provided. If any further assistance is necessary, please post here and I will reopen.","2026-01-16T16:08:12.689Z"],["3816932","AIOT-509","AIOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Some examples of OK images\n\n!20260116_174728.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_174728.jpg\"!\n\n!20260116_175006.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_175006.jpg\"!\n\n!20260116_175244.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_175244.jpg\"!","2026-01-16T16:10:33.623Z"],["3816937","LSS-60422","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi, this is the template but we haven’t used many times: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/12E2DDYiIkmDV28GG9DHuxYnylmqBwId4MuvInjYi9vY/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12E2DDYiIkmDV28GG9DHuxYnylmqBwId4MuvInjYi9vY/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nYou can also find other templates, if useful, in this confluence page: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/5227577347/Bolt+Drive+-+templates+and+other+useful+files|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/5227577347/Bolt+Drive+-+templates+and+other+useful+files|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T16:12:06.620Z"],["3816938","PRV-1072","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Privacy reviewed the [*Fraud Management Procedure*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14cYuLE-pwd-Z_6-r8qNiNq0bLx7H06SP/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106326439712206242177&rtpof=true&sd=true] and added a few references and clarifications on data protection, in line with Ellex’s recommendations.\n# These changes do *not* *introduce any substantive updates* to the procedure; the aim is to essentially clarify that the *Personal Data Protection Policy* and *Personal Data Retention Policy* apply where personal data is processed under the fraud framework.","2026-01-16T16:12:10.845Z"],["3816939","LSS-61408","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks [~accountid:712020:932dcda3-b9db-4c1f-8de8-254211945ea6] - please send the following messages to the respective users:\n\n*To the Rider*:\n\n{quote}Dear [*name*],\n\nWe are contacting you regarding a recent interaction with our customer support team on [*date*].\n\nDue to an internal error, the phone number of a driver was shared with you. This disclosure should not have occurred.\n\nWe kindly ask you to please delete the driver’s phone number from your device and refrain from contacting the driver now or in the future. The driver’s personal data must not be used for any purpose.\n\nThe issue has been addressed internally, and measures have been taken to prevent a recurrence. No further action is required from you once the number has been deleted.\n\nIf you have any questions, please let us know.{quote}\n\n*To the Driver:*\n\n{quote}Dear [*name*],\n\nWe are contacting you regarding a recent interaction with our customer support team on [*date*]. Thanks for bringing this issue to our attention.\n\nWe have investigated and confirmed that your phone number was shared with a passenger due to an internal error. This disclosure should not have occurred and was not in line with our procedures.\n\nThe issue has been addressed, and measures have been taken to prevent a recurrence. We have also instructed the passenger to delete your phone number and to refrain from contacting you. If you receive any further contact or notice anything concerning, please let us know immediately so we can take appropriate action.\n\nWe understand this situation is frustrating and apologise for the inconvenience caused.\n\nSincerely, \n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-16T16:12:11.633Z"],["3816941","AIOT-509","AIOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Some examples of poor quality images which are still usable on vehicle.\n\n!20260116_173703.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_173703.jpg\"!\n\n!20260116_172717.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_172717.jpg\"!\n\n!20260116_172256.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_172256.jpg\"!\n\n!20260116_172005.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_172005.jpg\"!","2026-01-16T16:12:19.940Z"],["3816944","PRV-1071","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# To be addressed under the Personal Data Protection Procedure;\n# Preliminary deadline for completion - 26th of January 2026.","2026-01-16T16:13:25.400Z"],["3816945","PFI-826735","PFI","davi.santos@bolt-outsource.eu","Davi Julião Da Silva Santos","Thanks for the update. Please let me know as soon as possible.","2026-01-16T16:14:02.145Z"],["3816946","LSS-61634","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66] Please find the signed document(s) attached. [^FY25_Bolt_Engagement_Letter(final_signed).pdf] [^FY25_Bolt(Taiwan)_lawyer's letter (1).pdf] [^Bolt_Baker&McKenzie law firm_confirmatoin (1).pdf] ","2026-01-16T16:14:07.512Z"],["3816947","PFI-834334","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T16:14:15.992Z"],["3816949","MVRT-1495","MVRT","teele.vallimae@bolt.eu","Teele Vallimäe","How long should the awareness campaigns run or they don’t have an end date at all?","2026-01-16T16:14:34.459Z"],["3816950","LSS-61477","LSS","gaspard.pirmez@bolt.eu","Gaspard Pirmez","Hey [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nThank you for the response\n\nI’ll send you the coms once we’ve designed it\n\nWe were thinking to use a typeform to collect answers \n\n{quote}Can you confirm that the time limitation for car branding (max 12 months, ideally capped at 6 months with possible renewal) is respected for Branded Cars in general and also for this pilot?{quote}\n\nThe test will only run for 2 months so the priod will be respected\n\nI’m not sure I understand what you mean. My understanding was indeed in the contract, we have 3 months period that can be renewed 3 times, so max 12 months. However, it can keep going after no ?\n\n","2026-01-16T16:14:49.297Z"],["3816951","MVRT-1496","MVRT","teele.vallimae@bolt.eu","Teele Vallimäe","Will this ticket have any description? 🤔 ","2026-01-16T16:14:57.542Z"],["3816953","AIOT-509","AIOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Examples of un-usable images\n\n!20260116_163511.jpg|width=540,alt=\"20260116_163511.jpg\"!","2026-01-16T16:15:16.711Z"],["3816954","PFI-834335","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^transaction-confirmation-report_ro-ro_c8aca7-1 (1).pdf]","2026-01-16T16:15:23.670Z"],["3816955","PRV-1067","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n* [@samantha.sayers|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U049448SKTM] confirmed for me that [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60]  *will be appointed as the DPO for PayCo*\n\n* Privacy team will coordinate with the ODPO to complete the official appointment.","2026-01-16T16:15:25.409Z"],["3816957","LSS-61735","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T16:16:08.378Z"],["3816959","PRV-955","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Latest update:*\n\n# The project currently has low priority, as the main focus is on preparing and submitting the EU Payments License application in Q1 2026 and implementing PayCo privacy compliance before obtaining the preliminary license in 2027.\n# The consolidated internal summary outlining key operations in commerce is also a lower priority and *will be completed in H2 2026*, following progress on the EU Payments License project and submission for the license.","2026-01-16T16:18:56.308Z"],["3816961","LSS-60213","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:6215e9f4347c690072f6f91d] \n\n*Updated contractual assessment – clawback feasibility (RentaCab)*\n\nFollowing confirmation that RentaCab terminated the Agreement early, Clause 11.2 now applies. Under this clause, where the Contractor terminates before the end of the Term, all Fees received under the Agreement become repayable.\n\nAccordingly, Bolt has a clear contractual basis to recover the paid Fees, subject to legitimate deductions and set-off.\n\nIn addition, and without prejudice to Clause 11.2, Bolt is contractually entitled to recover amounts via penalties and set-off:\n\n* *Clause 3.5:* Monthly contractual penalties of €183.33 per car per month for failure to meet the 150h KPI.\n* *Clause 3.7:* KPI Penalties triggered by KPI failure and/or termination before the end of the Term, calculated as ¼ of the Fee per affected car per KPI Year.\n* *Clauses 5.10–5.11:* Express right for Bolt to set off any amounts owed by the Contractor against Fees and Branding Bonuses.\n\nOn this basis, we should be able to proceed with the clawback in the stated net amount.","2026-01-16T16:19:08.080Z"],["3816962","DSR-3135","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] [Confirmation of erasure|https://drive.google.com/file/d/12NfPuV8476rffyfH361iKnJkmtGUCdaS/view?usp=drive_link] has been sent to data subject (using both email addresses provided). Kindly mark as complete.","2026-01-16T16:21:29.375Z"],["3816963","PFI-834342","PFI","panisara.trakulkoolsri@bolt-outsource.eu","Panisara Trakulkoolsri","!image-20260116-161916.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-161925.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T16:22:04.333Z"],["3816964","PFI-834343","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^revolut_tranzactie.pdf]","2026-01-16T16:22:38.432Z"],["3816965","DPX-3275","DPX","dmitrii.orlov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Orlov","Created draft PR with backend cleanup\n\nNext:\n\n* cleanup Portal FE\n* deploy BE to Prelive + test in FE to see if everything is stable\n* deploy BE to Live","2026-01-16T16:22:41.454Z"],["3816966","DSR-3157","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","All data and response sent to the user","2026-01-16T16:23:21.201Z"],["3816968","DGD-42","DGD","elie.kawerk@bolt.eu","Elie Kawerk","* analyzed the 9 Dec 25 release (Limassol, Bucharest, Constanta): [https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1862101788801693?o=2472566184436351#command/5513974154507099|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/1862101788801693?o=2472566184436351#command/5513974154507099]\n* planned and released a scale up of holdouts in 8 cities (13 Jan 2026), planning code [here|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/browse/folders/1955119991389037?o=2472566184436351]\n* analyzed the holdouts' compliance of the 13 Jan 2026 release [here|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2869975772983548?o=2472566184436351#command/4723845875852851]","2026-01-16T16:24:29.077Z"],["3816971","PFI-834344","PFI","panisara.trakulkoolsri@bolt-outsource.eu","Panisara Trakulkoolsri","!image-20260116-162405.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260116-162414.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T16:26:15.041Z"],["3816973","PFI-834345","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T16:27:41.384Z"],["3816977","LSS-61662","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5],\n\nAs discussed, I’ve reviewed the terms of business and the letters of engagement. Overall, these appear to be standard for a law firm and *I do not see any material risk to Bolt*.\n\nOne point I wanted to double-check relates to fees. Clauses 5.5-5.8 of the engagement letters state that the fees are estimates only (not caps), with a relatively wide range (£25k–£60k) and scope for escalation. Is this acceptable from our perspective? You mentioned that the work has already commenced and that the fee was agreed, so I assume this point is covered, but it would be helpful to confirm.\n\nI would also note that tax advice is expressly excluded unless separately agreed, which is standard for law firm engagement letters. However, in the context of property break notices, VAT, SDLT or group structuring issues can arise, so it is worth flagging that responsibility for identifying these risks remains with Bolt unless we provide a specific instruction.\n\nOther than the above, I do not consider any of the clauses to present a material risk for Bolt in the circumstances. (/) \n\nPlease let me know if there is anything else you need from me - thank you!","2026-01-16T16:29:52.521Z"],["3816978","WDFT-3417","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","The following updated to dashboard are done:\n\n* added chart of nonrecoverable VAT by country ( country is by default is taken from field TAx Country, Supplier Primary Tax ID Contry is taken for following but for Tax Applicabilities: VAT IC Acquisitions of Goods Non Recoverable & VAT IC Import of Services Non-Recoverable - Reverse Charge)\n* !image-20260116-162835.png|width=941,alt=\"image-20260116-162835.png\"!\n* the list of all reports used for nonrecoverable VAT dashboard is added to the dashboard \n\n!image-20260116-162855.png|width=976,alt=\"image-20260116-162855.png\"!\n\n* prompt set updated: company is added as prompt with default value “Bolt Group” \n\n!image-20260116-162947.png|width=658,alt=\"image-20260116-162947.png\"!","2026-01-16T16:29:55.633Z"],["3816979","WFM-10018","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, permissions added. However there is no need to assign into queues as trainer can filter tickets and pick it up","2026-01-16T16:30:19.248Z"],["3816980","INT-721","INT","james.davies@bolt.eu","James Davies","26W3\n\n+*What we did?*+\n\nAB Scorecard now fully accounts for Cashback across all uplift metrics. \n\nPlanned for February AB test according to country cost restrictions (if still to go ahead). \n\nDiscussed rollout of existing Cashback vs Menu discount tests (started 7th Jan). \n\n+*Next Steps*+\n\nAlign on who will have ownership of the AB testing in this initiative (we are currently not working according to what was agreed [here |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Zb8C0tMK4eGf-s-FX9k7LYUEPSmPEAzbWjGl_ldwqlU/edit?tab=t.0])\n\nAlign on success metrics and test design for Cashback insights.","2026-01-16T16:31:15.988Z"],["3816981","LSS-54100","LSS","oleg.shimchik@bolt.eu","Aleh Shymchyk","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] \nThank you. Yes, here it is:\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ISS-1143|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ISS-1143|smart-link]","2026-01-16T16:31:29.945Z"],["3816982","PTWS-2095","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Feedback after latest solution review on Thursday {{2026-01-15}}\n\n* branding update\n* Q : qq - how is the offer letter impacted if the contract is a fixed term? will the benefits etc. be changed automatically?","2026-01-16T16:32:11.394Z"],["3816984","PAW-14965","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T16:32:35.260Z"],["3816985","MAB-232","MAB","balaji.senthilkumar@bolt.eu","Balaji Senthilkumar","Oleh/Balaji Discussion on Opportunites being created for Agents - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/13JmqIJHRZh0K5MNUhRJSo8OqW9ei-R4uwbg7qKpO_Uo/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/13JmqIJHRZh0K5MNUhRJSo8OqW9ei-R4uwbg7qKpO_Uo/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T16:32:49.292Z"],["3816986","WD-22516","WD","carla.arroyo@bolt.eu","Carla Arroyo Armendariz","no need, lets close it!","2026-01-16T16:33:25.758Z"],["3816987","INT-60","INT","james.davies@bolt.eu","James Davies","\n\n26W3\n\n+*What we did?*+\n\nDBT adjustments to persist cherry picker assignment until 26th Jan \n\nStarted planning for v2 test.\n\nAnalyse template for V1 Test started. \n\n+*Next Steps*+\n\nFollow up with delivery leadership on the specific goals from this initiative (23.1)","2026-01-16T16:33:50.662Z"],["3816988","INT-825","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","26W3: There has been high priority request by the Rides Finance an Growth teams for us to support the improvement of the Month-to-date tracker. This tracker is currently hacked together based on an old model used for the financial planning model, and so far had no ownership (no KPIs or accuracy reporting).\n\nWe have sit with RF and identified a series of issues in the current approach and we will draft a design document in the upcoming week. \n\nIt is important to note that this MTD tracking work is not aligned with any of our current goals. ","2026-01-16T16:34:08.822Z"],["3816992","INT-825","INT","andrea.rabinelli@bolt.eu","Andrea Rabinelli","[~accountid:712020:1153c9d5-fb49-4e02-ba70-729d45e900dd] I am adding this here as it was presented to us as a top priority request. Once I will have a design document, it would be great if we could find some time to discuss how it can fit within our team scope, targets, and your future plans. cc [~accountid:5e843e7bcb85aa0c145d4b86] ","2026-01-16T16:35:52.310Z"],["3816993","MVRT-1446","MVRT","evamaria.ots@bolt.eu","Eva Maria Ots","[~accountid:5fa51169b38e61007151d47e] Just let it be atm, the price might change, so let’s leave that push out. ","2026-01-16T16:36:13.730Z"],["3816995","PTWS-2095","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","* offer letter branding [here|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GStRWvli3ZqYX8hbxjSUmeYaYj3c-OSt/view] but waiting for an editable version from Michal Lindenberg; editable version ->[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QgIFdbNfb-Oqy_uhd5WH5uA0Auu4JSLWFyTiefFXDRw/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QgIFdbNfb-Oqy_uhd5WH5uA0Auu4JSLWFyTiefFXDRw/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] there are 2026 offer letter makers so please ask Paulo to provide the latest templates before the testing launch","2026-01-16T16:37:25.166Z"],["3817005","DGD-196","DGD","mikita.shapavalau@bolt.eu","Nick Shapavalau","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OaO51cL_bE9wygt8kQ50nHnvErDDMORJ3hO-wpy0w4g/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OaO51cL_bE9wygt8kQ50nHnvErDDMORJ3hO-wpy0w4g/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T16:45:06.740Z"],["3817008","XP-2876","XP","danil.kazakov@bolt.eu","Danil Kazakov","For additive {{COVAR}} we could use the following formula:\nCov(X, Y) = E[XY] - E[X]E[Y] (the same as for variance).","2026-01-16T16:47:21.061Z"],["3817010","LSS-61559","LSS","sandra.loewe@bolt.eu","Sandra Löwe","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] \nUnfortunately, the name of the company missed the “GmbH” so I had to adjust it. \nCan you send it again? I am very sorry. \n\n[^Urban Drive Co-Invest + Kick-Back - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.docx (2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T16:47:59.391Z"],["3817011","PAW-14966","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-16T16:50:21.614Z"],["3817012","WD-22512","WD","demetri.manias@bolt.eu","Demetri Manias","Haven’t put it through yet!","2026-01-16T16:51:09.563Z"],["3817013","LSS-61736","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","[^requiz BOLT.pdf] _(55 kB)_\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 18.48.48.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 18.50.34.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T16:51:39.405Z"],["3817014","LSS-61736","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-16T16:51:40.619Z"],["3817015","LSS-61172","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] I have not be able to locate the driver either, sorry! ","2026-01-16T16:54:04.052Z"],["3817017","DSR-3801","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-16T16:56:07.788Z"],["3817018","HS-27969","HS","keidi.helm@bolt.eu","Keidi Helm","Hi [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] \n\nThe DPAE is updated with correct birth country. Please find it in the attachment.\n\nKind regards\nKeidi\n\n[^BOLT_DPAE_NOGUERA.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T16:56:28.730Z"],["3817019","PTWS-2134","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Start working on it next week to assess feasibility - if it implies more work, can go over to the next week 😉","2026-01-16T16:57:09.206Z"],["3817021","LSS-56022","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","[~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] Hi, I’ve reviewed the document and I’m happy with the contents. Thanks.","2026-01-16T16:59:12.662Z"],["3817023","PFI-834294","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-16T17:00:54.179Z"],["3817025","LSS-61736","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-16T17:01:08.551Z"],["3817026","LSS-61403","LSS","anais.jourdain@bolt.eu","Anaïs Jourdain","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] ,\n\nThanks for your message. Happy to provide more context.\n\nExactly three representatives from Rounded will be present. They will be visiting us for a working session. We will not be sharing any data beyond what we already share with them remotely, namely the contact lists we have been using for testing the launch of automated calls, and strictly within the volume limits that were previously agreed.\n\nThese lists contain the following personal data only: first name, last name, phone number, and email address.\n\nDuring the session, we will review the initial test results that Rounded will present, plan the next testing waves, and observe how calls are initiated directly from their platform. In a second step, they will give a presentation to the rest of our local team to explain how their tool works, answer questions, and potentially exchange ideas. This will be our first in-person meeting.\n\nUnderstood regarding the NDA — I will follow up with our local legal team accordingly.\n\nFrom an organisational standpoint, everything is clear. The entire visit will take place in our main meeting room, and we do not expect to leave it, as the session should last no more than 1.5 hours. Our Workplace Experience Manager, [~accountid:712020:daffdd55-b79f-408e-9859-186aadb103a8] , informed me that the visitors should be accompanied at all times during their stay, and I have therefore shared with her the full list of names of all attendees.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any further details.\n\nBest regards,\nAnaïs Jourdain","2026-01-16T17:03:39.474Z"],["3817029","LSS-61172","LSS","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","FOUND HIM: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/2271215?tab=profile&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FLondon|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/2271215?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FLondon]\n\n\n\nAddress has changed a few times but the address match his old DVLA license \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 17.07.35.png|width=430,height=338,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 17.07.35.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-16T17:08:27.851Z"],["3817031","LSS-61234","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Hi [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] following up here - let me know if you’d like me to create another ticket ","2026-01-16T17:09:44.257Z"],["3817032","LSS-61738","LSS","khadeza.islam@bolt.eu","Khadeza Islam","!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 17.13.38.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^Bolt Services UK Ltd.  License Agreement Dec 2025.pdf] _(325 kB)_","2026-01-16T17:14:07.983Z"],["3817033","INT-639","INT","daria.ryazhskikh@bolt.eu","Daria Ryazhskikh","26W03: Auto-tagging is in progress.","2026-01-16T17:16:55.753Z"],["3817034","BDB-1513","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Hi [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] here are the final 10 promo codes which we’d need the venues.\n\nCould we add a code to each poster and table talker (10 of each)?\n\nBOLT16T\nBOLTVULT\nBOLTTED\nBOLTGRND\nBOLTLUMS\nBOLTALBERT\nBOLTCLARE\nBOLTLUCKY\nBOLTBOXER\nBOLTPORT\n\nOtherwise we are good to go! ","2026-01-16T17:17:01.903Z"],["3817035","LSS-56022","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi *Legal Ops:* please can you arrange for the attached to be sent to [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a] for signing. Ramone needs to sign the +*certificate at Appendix 2 (page 15)*+.\n\nPlease do not close the ticket after the document is signed as we still need to use this ticket to track this matter - thank you! \n\n[^Response Letter to Court Order Ref. No PIC-PN3178-25 - Bolt Services UK Limited - 16 January 2026 (538b984c-f5fb-4849-ae5a-8778e4cce842).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T17:18:55.400Z"],["3817036","LSS-61605","LSS","paul.bittan@bolt.eu","Paul Bittan","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] - these tender questions relate to electronic invoicing (specifically Tungsten and Ariba), information security, security controls, business continuity and disaster recovery and AI. As such they are not queries that we would answer in the Legal team. You should liaise with the InfoSec and IT teams on these questions. Also worth exploring with Thomas Harper and Gabriele Kaveckyte (in the privacy team) who should be able to point you in the right direction.","2026-01-16T17:21:02.642Z"],["3817039","HS-27969","HS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Thank you [~accountid:6390559a2acfad92d7b59f11] and [~accountid:712020:58704fb5-3b31-40a0-896f-1d862e6e1fd9] ! 🙏 \n\nI’ll reopen this ticket when I have reference of my SSN. \n\nBest,\n\nAngela","2026-01-16T17:27:52.497Z"],["3817040","LSS-61583","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Thank you for raising a ticket, Ivan.\n\nThe videos and blog content position Flex as commercially better than Standard, rather than simply different. That creates exposure from a legal perspective, particularly around pensions inducement risk.\n\nAny public content that presents Flex as offering better earnings or more control can be characterised as nudging drivers away from pension bearing work. My consistent advice has been to stick to factual descriptions of how the flex features works, rather than opinion based or outcome driven language such as suggesting drivers can earn more with Flex.\n\nWhile this doesn’t break the model, I’d strongly recommend rephrasing the content to avoid language that implies Flex is more commercially advantageous, more flexible, or otherwise better than the standard model.","2026-01-16T17:36:32.631Z"],["3817041","RDS-1248","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:81377b7a-4a7f-417a-a4aa-7306f122b309] Check here:\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1754898148804929|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1754898148804929|smart-link] \n\nGranted, just a single example, but I’m pretty sure it’s basically what started this whole topic.","2026-01-16T17:36:49.627Z"],["3817042","LSS-61588","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] !","2026-01-16T17:40:02.156Z"],["3817043","RDS-1247","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] strongly support this. My old ticket:\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1191|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/RDS/ideas/view/6301152?selectedIssue=RDS-1191|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T17:40:02.609Z"],["3817044","LSS-61105","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* confirmation from Jason to offer the claimant a goodwill gesture of *£200*.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 5.40.43 PM.png|width=1018,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 5.40.43 PM.png\"!","2026-01-16T17:41:26.750Z"],["3817045","RDS-1351","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] I believe the brand team has a big push around ratings planned. [~accountid:712020:bca00e26-f5bd-4a5b-9a82-68a8ff2fc37e] maybe can share the latest on plans to message/inform about ratings, why they matter, how to keep them high, etc. ","2026-01-16T17:41:34.870Z"],["3817047","RDS-612","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] Aleksei changed teams some months ago. This is now owned by [~accountid:712020:91471b9c-fa3a-4c52-9554-437a07687be2] and [~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] \n\nAfaik the core copy updates have already been handled by [~accountid:712020:32ff1b8a-e85e-4b94-8a79-56484670e212] (great work 👏) — confirmation here: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09CN99RMSB/p1763468191801159|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09CN99RMSB/p1763468191801159|smart-link] \n\nThe push notification updates were implemented by [~accountid:712020:ef010281-23f5-47a0-bc36-dce8f4c192ec], but I am still seeing old copy there for some reason (e.g. got the “Welcome to Gdansk” push yesterday and it was the old copy). Also we have not implemented any logic changes. The feature channel is [#tmp-rider-product-message-edit|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C07GNGJ9V5L] — I’ll add you. ","2026-01-16T17:47:41.140Z"],["3817049","RDS-1222","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] It was my bad, I had it under *RiderX* group. Thanks for flagging, I corrected it 👍\n\n!image-20260116-174906.png|width=230,height=57,alt=\"image-20260116-174906.png\"!","2026-01-16T17:49:15.583Z"],["3817051","RDS-951","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] I believe this will be fixed as part of [#feature-account-tab-v2|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0985RN2536]. After many detailed discussions with the safety and identity teams, they agreed to let us upload images via gallery. So this should be much improved soon. ","2026-01-16T17:52:52.354Z"],["3817052","RDS-951","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","Never mind, it’s been marked “out of scope” 🫠\n\n[https://www.figma.com/design/8hdatZ17MVcFxVSJtd48YS/Growth-2025?node-id=60517-18176&t=eXZFjI34Z7AVfC8W-1|https://www.figma.com/design/8hdatZ17MVcFxVSJtd48YS/Growth-2025?node-id=60517-18176&t=eXZFjI34Z7AVfC8W-1|smart-link] \n\n!image-20260116-175324.png|width=819,height=755,alt=\"image-20260116-175324.png\"!","2026-01-16T17:53:34.347Z"],["3817053","LSS-58592","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Final version - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fG4YcfEKpM7hDvTVX3g6fJh-Y_lSRaxt/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fG4YcfEKpM7hDvTVX3g6fJh-Y_lSRaxt/edit|smart-link] \n\nAnnexes - [^Anexo 6.pdf] [^Anexo_1_Zona Blackout.pdf] [^Anexo_2_Kiss and Fly.pdf] [^Anexo_3.pdf] [^Anexo_4.pdf] [^Anexo_5.pdf] ","2026-01-16T17:55:36.593Z"],["3817055","LSS-61105","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* letter and email sent to claimant, denying liability and offering £200 goodwill gesture.\n\n[~accountid:5acb1f48d8b95a2b34f150a8], I will keep you updated on any response we may receive.\n\n[^Letter to Mr Sau Wa Wong - Bolt Services UK Limited - 16 January 2026.docx.pdf]\n[^Bolt Mail - Response to your Letter Before Action dated 28 December 2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-16T17:56:42.513Z"],["3817065","BDB-1461","BDB","alexsandra.kruusberg@bolt.eu","Alexsandra Kruusberg","Thanks for sending this over. The link currently opens a Figma file with multiple email drafts and comments. Could you point me to the specific version I should be looking at? A screenshot of the draft assets (rather than the Figma comment) would be helpful.\n\nAlex","2026-01-16T18:01:21.835Z"],["3817067","PFI-826411","PFI","yusif.mehdiyev@bolt-outsource.eu","Yusif Mehdiyev","Hello,\n\nSince the IBAn is incorrect we need to bounce the payout back if it is possible.  No proof of payment is required. \n\n","2026-01-16T18:19:01.265Z"],["3817068","PFI-826411","PFI","yusif.mehdiyev@bolt-outsource.eu","Yusif Mehdiyev","[~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b] ","2026-01-16T18:19:14.511Z"],["3817069","LSS-56418","LSS","gustavo.arriola@bolt.eu","Gustavo Brítez Arriola","Hi [~accountid:6172754ef485cd006863a3a8] \n\nThanks for the update — please find below the additional information we have on the infringing party and clarifications from our side:\n\n* *Name used online:* Nort Texturados PY\n* *Telephone / WhatsApp:* *+595 983 895515*\n* *Email:* [*norttexturadospy@gmail.com*|mailto:norttexturadospy@gmail.com]\n* *Address provided by the party:* *Dionisio Comet y 6 de Enero, Ñemby, Paraguay*\n** While the area is predominantly residential, it is not a gated neighborhood and it is common in Paraguay for small businesses to operate from mixed residential/commercial zones. Based on our checks, *the address provided is the correct one as shared by the party*.\n* *Instagram:* [https://www.instagram.com/p/C8nAFCDpZra/|https://www.instagram.com/p/C8nAFCDpZra/|smart-link]\n* *Potential link to an Argentinian brand:*\n** We also identified what appears to be the official page of an Argentinian brand under a similar name: [https://www.facebook.com/nortrevestimientos.pagina.oficial/|https://www.facebook.com/nortrevestimientos.pagina.oficial/|smart-link] \n** Our assessment is that the Paraguayan account is part *of the same brand name*, but the infringing activity we are addressing is tied to the Paraguay-based contact details above. \n** You are correct that their core business appears to relate to paint/surface finishings. However, during our outreach we were able to confirm that they also *offer vehicle painting and/or vinyl wrapping (“ploteados”) services*, which aligns with the context in which the Bolt logos were used. This was confirmed through direct messaging with the account.\n\nLet me know how else we can do to support, thanks! ","2026-01-16T18:26:50.056Z"],["3817070","PFI-834390","PFI","monika.roszig@bolt-outsource.eu","Monika Roszig","!image-20260116-182628.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T18:28:09.364Z"],["3817072","MLC-3876","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*W3*+\n\n* Created a report for the monthly Eater tracking – [LCM / Delivery / Eaters / Communications Monthly Overview / Sent Volumes – Braze Data|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1c-q2V8o-Ui_BKEa0odGPQb6UH8lm1iSkCjj7txIMr40/edit?usp=sharing]\n* We can review it in Wednesday’s meeting and share feedback on how to adjust it and what may be missing.\n* I’ll fill in the last month’s report before the meeting.","2026-01-16T18:34:54.675Z"],["3817073","PFI-834393","PFI","blessing.otih@bolt-outsource.eu","Blessing Otih","!image-20260116-183449.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-16T18:35:08.517Z"],["3817074","MLC-3132","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*W3*+\n\n* Synced with Ilja that they would need the cashback comms for the rest of the markets in Feb.\n* Scheduled a meeting with Dasha to align on that and show the Cashback setups. I think the deadline is negotiable. They are usually reasonable about our effort and timelines.","2026-01-16T18:36:35.868Z"],["3817076","LSS-61512","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","well, TBH this is not so clear for me either, can you kindly ask them?\n\nthanks!\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-16T18:42:51.885Z"],["3817078","MLC-2458","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*W3*+\n\n* The Web team relaunched the CMS tool with the HTML fixes that were tested on the Rider side. After many fixes and tests, the Rider team finally got their ORs on the same level across control and treatment.\n* I also requested the changes again, which we needed for the restaurant highlight blocks. As these weren’t accounted for in the HTML changes. The Web team was able to launch the changes already this week. I tested the CMS tool, created some Storytelling templates, and shared feedback.\n** [Eaters, Canvas, Auto, Hard Churn, Email (1)|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/templates_and_media/email_templates/660bb19705810f0061db11b4/6968e0e41721880e703c69d1] (restaurant highlights)\n** [Eaters, Canvas, Auto, Hard Churn, Email (2)|https://dashboard-02.braze.eu/engagement/templates_and_media/email_templates/660bb19705810f0061db11b4/6968f1ec1d64f60f56003e05] (content blocks)\n** The CMS tool was easy to use, and I think we can start scaling it within the team for Storytelling templates. There are some steps to keep in mind. So I’ll schedule a meeting for next week for the team. \n** [Thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0900469E6N/p1765880500833889?thread_ts=1761228022.114759&cid=C0900469E6N] with the Web team.\n* However, I do think that we should scale the templates market by market and keep an eye on the metrics. Do not scale it all globally. Move stage by stage and market by market.\n* Reached out to Tiffany to get support on gathering info on which cities/countries we can show stores/grocery content blocks. She promised to work on it and get some input for our next bi-weekly. ","2026-01-16T18:44:21.571Z"],["3817079","LSS-61736","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] ,\n\nso what is your request? You should have a process in place for that? Do you have it?\n\nYou should proceed as requested by the Police and confirm them.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.\n\nthanks,\n\nElisabetta\n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] FYI","2026-01-16T18:45:54.968Z"],["3817080","FDBT-4797","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_psp_payments fails on 2026-01-15 08:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 363724628733943, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_psp_payments/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-15T08%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=psp_currency_clearing.psp_currency_clearing&base_date=2026-01-15T08%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-16T18:46:20.291Z"],["3817081","MLC-3860","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*W3*+\n\n* Tested out the Segment function in the Targeting Platform and gave feedback. Work item attached. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-3727|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-3727|smart-link] ","2026-01-16T18:49:18.653Z"],["3817083","MLC-3762","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*W3*+\n\n* Finalised the Braze experiment setups for all markets. They’re in a draft state.\n* I’ll launch the experiment from the {{2026-01-21}}\n* Had multiple syncs with MarTech people as there were questions about why we are not doing the experiment from the Targeting Platform. From a sync with Sander, I actually got to know that there’s a functionality available to support event trigger (and event property) usage from TP. I proposed that for now, we’d continue with Braze. Later, when I have time, I’ll test the TP enrolment option. And if it works correctly, then we can use that for later experiments. MarTech was ok with it.\n* Helped Ani to create dummy enrollments on Braze, so he could capture enrollments on the backend and confirm that we can extract users from Braze experiment paths. All is good, and the test was successful.","2026-01-16T18:54:12.123Z"],["3817085","MLC-3861","MLC","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","+*W3*+\n\n* During the week, it turned out that the Bolt Plus Week(s) had started in some markets. Offering menu discount deals for Bolt Plus members. We weren’t briefed about it.\n** Support was needed to launch the menu discount for the Food banners. Because Karl is still Out Sick.\n** Also, ad-hocs needed support, as they were sent quite last-minute. \n*** The main blocker was an issue with the deeplink. When testing, the Home Category deeplink didn’t work as expected on some devices. When clicking on the link, the app opens, an error is shown, and then the HC opens.\n*** There was a lot of going back-and-forth with engineers ([thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01L45AEDPB/p1768475588312339]). Eventually, I was able to get the provider trait IDs for the participating restaurants, and I created new links for the ad-hocs. Banner link is working fine, and that’s expected.","2026-01-16T19:01:11.303Z"],["3817089","PFI-825654","PFI","obehi.iruebafa@bolt-outsource.eu","Obehi Iruebafa","Hello Team,\nSD is still open","2026-01-16T19:15:24.950Z"],["3817094","FDBT-4801","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-16T19:26:27.193Z"],["3817097","PFI-829102","PFI","zainab.sanni@bolt-outsource.eu","Zainab Sanni","Hi team, please assist with payment matching","2026-01-16T19:32:13.609Z"],["3817098","PTWS-2098","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","[~accountid:712020:4c80c500-8466-444d-b13e-b2984ef3723c] Hi! this should work better, however I don’t understand how the process flows afterwards , it seems it’s going to the manager for approving the One time payment - that shouldn’t happen since the regional people partner controls those costs, but we can double check.\nlet’s resume work on it asap","2026-01-16T19:41:08.671Z"],["3817099","PTWS-2091","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","[~accountid:712020:a5535fc2-4c96-407b-864b-f673b781e58e] was this deployed?","2026-01-16T19:41:44.705Z"],["3817100","PFI-834408","PFI","carlos.segovia@bolt.eu","Carlos Segovia","[^reporte detalle del movimiento (51).pdf.pdf]","2026-01-16T19:42:27.751Z"],["3817101","PFI-834401","PFI","viktoriia.spanchak@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Spanchak","same here [ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/724846517] [order |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282516037?cityId=158][eater admin|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/26784685/overview] [payments|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4040824694]","2026-01-16T19:43:30.150Z"],["3817104","PFI-834416","PFI","daniel.covas@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniel Covas","[^SEBASTIAO_07.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SEBASTIAO_08.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SEBASTIAO_09.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SEBASTIAO_10.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SEBASTIAO_11.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SEBASTIAO_12.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SERGIO_07.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SERGIO_08.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SERGIO_09.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SERGIO_10.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SERGIO_11.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^SERGIO_12.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^bolt - calculo (1).pdf.pdf]","2026-01-16T19:49:36.987Z"],["3817105","PFI-834416","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-16T19:49:39.212Z"],["3817108","PTWS-2124","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","We need to map the final list as follows: \n\n# we currently have these ones \n\n!image-20260116-195216.png|width=333,alt=\"image-20260116-195216.png\"!\n\n# Assessment should be:\n\n* keep 3PL Mechanics and B2B as is\n* Consultant = new type Consultants\n* Contractor = new type Individual Contractors\n* add 2 new categories for Outcome based …and Agency Temp…me might just integrate 3PL under one of these categories, I asked Liis which one they fit in.\n\n!image-20260116-194538.png|width=654,alt=\"image-20260116-194538.png\"!\n\n# is there any way we could add the definition somewhere? for people to understand what each category means? if this can only be done as part of the actual processes that’s fine, we can consider this for the next steps of the project - integrating the new changes to the Workday processes.\n\nthank you","2026-01-16T19:57:16.017Z"],["3817109","INT-758","INT","simo.pahk@bolt.eu","Simo Pähk","26W3: Scoping + discussions + design doc. Solution details still being worked on.","2026-01-16T19:59:22.905Z"],["3817110","INT-757","INT","simo.pahk@bolt.eu","Simo Pähk","26W3: On hold currently, working on other stuff.","2026-01-16T20:00:00.971Z"],["3817111","DAEN-1301","DAEN","silja.mardla@bolt.eu","Silja Märdla","And, I'm pretty sure this was the case where backfilling further doesn't help. The logic we use in fact_rides_search uses something that was only created then.\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-16T20:09:01.620Z"],["3817116","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","{{notification}} struggles a bit:\n\n{noformat}Caused by: java.sql.SQLException: Your query has been cancelled due to exceeding the allowed memory limit for a single SQL query. Please try narrowing your query scope or increase the tidb_mem_quota_query limit and try again.[conn=2446412270]{noformat}\n\nother than that, all good. I’ve checked if the {{created}} column is indeed indexed, and it is. For now we can still wait.","2026-01-16T20:19:58.297Z"],["3817117","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","OK, let me know if I need to intervene. We can always reduce the time range, it was a fair bit wider then the actual gap.","2026-01-16T20:21:11.489Z"],["3817118","SREDESK-7430","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Schema has been created on prelive and LIVE:\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_google_audit;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.517s\n\n\nroot@internal-dba.sqldb:(none)>create schema taxify_google_audit;\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 1.015s {noformat}","2026-01-16T20:23:48.181Z"],["3817119","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Not that much wider, actually :hmmmmmm:","2026-01-16T20:23:48.843Z"],["3817120","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Almost 1h before and 20min after\n\n{noformat}FROM: \"checkpoint_time\": \"2026-01-15 21:59:28.363\",\nTO:    \"create_time\": \"2026-01-15 22:37:12.704\", (edited) {noformat}\n\nVS\n\n{noformat}created >= '2026-01-15 21:00:00' AND created < '2026-01-15 22:59:00'\nlast_update >= '2026-01-15 21:00:00' AND last_update < '2026-01-15 22:59:00'{noformat}","2026-01-16T20:26:26.983Z"],["3817122","PFI-834438","PFI","denis.janco@bolt-outsource.eu","Denis Jančo","wrong beehive link provided ","2026-01-16T20:33:53.511Z"],["3817123","PFI-834440","PFI","carlos.segovia@bolt.eu","Carlos Segovia","[^CITIBANK -BOLT SERVICES.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-16T20:39:05.976Z"],["3817124","PFI-834441","