,"2026-01-18T07:01:03.906Z"],["3817545","PFI-820892","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Lasse Duang Nørgaard,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-18T07:01:04.800Z"],["3817546","PFI-828243","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Elaf Adam,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-18T07:01:06.028Z"],["3817547","PFI-830557","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Saiful Islam,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-18T07:01:15.763Z"],["3817548","PFI-834718","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-18T07:05:12.604Z"],["3817549","PFI-834528","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The Early Cashout was rejected because the recipient’s bank returned the transfer, indicating the beneficiary was not expecting these funds. Please ask the courier to double‑check their bank account details and contact their bank to ensure they can accept payouts from us; after that, they can try the Early Cashout again. If they do not retry, the payout will be sent automatically during the next regular payout cycle. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-18T07:10:31.019Z"],["3817550","PFI-834556","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the payment provider, and no specific rejection reason was returned. It will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try to request it again. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-18T07:10:51.034Z"],["3817551","PFI-834883","PFI","peter.uyokei@bolt-outsource.eu","Peter Uyokei","!image-20260118-071505.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T07:16:42.112Z"],["3817553","FDBT-4807","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-18T07:21:44.099Z"],["3817555","HS-28433","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:9d22087b-9bd3-42c9-944c-2112fcfa004e],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-18T07:30:17.483Z"],["3817556","FDBT-4796","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics fails on 2026-01-17 05:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 366496883292667, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-17T05%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=bolt_plus_subscription_revenue.bolt_plus_subscription_revenue&base_date=2026-01-17T05%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-18T07:35:10.420Z"],["3817558","PFI-834897","PFI","chubiyojo.shaibu@bolt-outsource.eu","Chubiyojo Shaibu","!image-20260118-074516.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T07:45:33.177Z"],["3817559","FDBT-4808","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-18T07:49:48.244Z"],["3817562","FDBT-4806","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-18T07:54:28.856Z"],["3817564","FDBT-4809","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-18T08:12:03.590Z"],["3817569","PFI-833740","PFI","nutsa.shevardenidze@bolt.eu","Nutsa Shevardenidze","Hi. The IBAN was closed before the payouts were processed. Although the payouts are marked as finished in the system, the driver has checked with the bank and confirmed that the funds were *not received*.\n\nThe bank has provided a *3-month statement* as proof that the funds were not credited. \n\nPlease let us know the next steps. Thank you. ","2026-01-18T08:37:25.432Z"],["3817574","PFI-830389","PFI","alexia.matsangou@bolt.eu","Alexia Matsangou","Kind reminder!","2026-01-18T09:00:51.840Z"],["3817575","PFI-829165","PFI","radka.remenikova@bolt-outsource.eu","Radka Remenikova","Hello Team, any update please? ","2026-01-18T09:29:41.791Z"],["3817576","LSS-61408","LSS","ioana.ungurean@bolt.eu","Ioana Ungurean","Thank you, messages sent to both parties. 🙏 ","2026-01-18T09:34:43.207Z"],["3817578","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","Approved both requests","2026-01-18T09:44:09.047Z"],["3817580","PFI-833392","PFI","zipporah.njoroge@bolt-outsource.eu","Zipporah Njoroge","The driver wishes to block their account deletion. ","2026-01-18T09:54:00.403Z"],["3817589","PFI-832798","PFI","marvellous.paul@bolt-outsource.eu","Marvellous Paul","Hi Team,\n\nWe are still expecting a response from you as regarding the payout ","2026-01-18T10:44:23.085Z"],["3817592","PFI-834952","PFI","mark.bauer@bolt-outsource.eu","Mark Bauer","!image-20260118-110341.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T11:03:51.741Z"],["3817593","PFI-834952","PFI","mark.bauer@bolt-outsource.eu","Mark Bauer","Hi, I couldn’t find a payment link, but there’s a linked SD ticket where the money was promised to be returned. Could you please send any proof of this payout?","2026-01-18T11:05:30.084Z"],["3817597","PFI-832648","PFI","ziporah.oriri@bolt-outsource.eu","Ziporah Oriri","I noticed that everything is correct according to their Void check sent.","2026-01-18T11:32:52.701Z"],["3817598","DBRE-8716","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Backfill approved. ","2026-01-18T11:35:22.516Z"],["3817600","FDBT-4797","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_psp_payments fails on 2026-01-17 08:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 838043517177460, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_psp_payments/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-17T08%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=psp_currency_clearing.psp_currency_clearing&base_date=2026-01-17T08%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-18T11:45:15.320Z"],["3817601","PFI-834966","PFI","techapat.tangtheeraboriboon@bolt-outsource.eu","Techapat Tangtheeraboriboon","!image-20260118-114833.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T11:49:55.074Z"],["3817606","PFI-834971","PFI","jarawee.ongsa@bolt-outsource.eu","Jarawee Ongsa","!image-20260118-121235.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260118-121251.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T12:14:11.176Z"],["3817607","PFI-834972","PFI","jarawee.ongsa@bolt-outsource.eu","Jarawee Ongsa","!image-20260118-121601.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260118-121607.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T12:16:46.677Z"],["3817609","PFI-812577","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","Hi, \n\nplease updare was the payment returned to the client?\n\nThank you.","2026-01-18T12:30:27.535Z"],["3817611","FDBT-4811","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-18T12:34:06.931Z"],["3817613","PFI-834862","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-18T13:00:49.558Z"],["3817625","FDBT-4810","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-18T13:52:44.835Z"],["3817628","HS-28882","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:712020:35ab0788-e5e6-46d9-80f6-993e673d6472], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-18T14:00:41.688Z"],["3817629","HS-28825","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:5b24221e927da916aaaa859a], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-18T14:00:42.919Z"],["3817636","PFI-835015","PFI","chinedu.ukaegbu@bolt-outsource.eu","Chinedu Ukaegbu","!Screenshot_20260118-140317.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T14:15:01.586Z"],["3817637","PFI-835023","PFI","yvette.ntumy@bolt.eu","Yvette Ntumy","!Untitled.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T14:21:33.869Z"],["3817639","PFI-828759","PFI","marvellous.paul@bolt-outsource.eu","Marvellous Paul","Hi Team,\n\nWe are still expecting a feedback from you","2026-01-18T14:28:45.115Z"],["3817640","PFI-835027","PFI","ruslana.korniiko@bolt-outsource.eu","Ruslana Korniiko","!Screenshot_20260118-162514.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T14:32:22.745Z"],["3817648","DRX-27504","DRX","aleksandr.stegnienko@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Stegnienko","* [x] Rename existing_partner_id_for_fed to override_partner_id\n* [x] Propagate override_partner_id to /adminPanel/driver/getCreationFields in order to override Partner’s data","2026-01-18T15:05:05.853Z"],["3817658","PFI-835058","PFI","serafim.turcan@bolt-outsource.eu","Serafim Turcan","!Screenshot_20260118-165638.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T15:48:54.094Z"],["3817659","PFI-835060","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-18T15:50:45.751Z"],["3817660","PFI-835061","PFI","rodeeyah.maseh@bolt-outsource.eu","Rodeeyah Maseh","!image-20260118-154754.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260118-154807.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260118-154823.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T15:53:40.532Z"],["3817664","LSS-60837","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi Merve Yilmaz, your CustomGPT request has been approved ✅\n\n*If this ticket was for a new CustomGPT*\nYour CustomGPT is now approved for use and has been added to the Legal & Compliance [toolstack tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jj2Mm-dJmnP6W4dBdFQZwrm2FGM0YTyTt2nC9i8BFQE/edit?gid=261811728#gid=261811728]. Before broader use, please ensure the permissions and intended audience are set correctly.\n\n*If this ticket was for updating an existing CustomGPT*\nThe requested changes have been approved and the [toolstack tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jj2Mm-dJmnP6W4dBdFQZwrm2FGM0YTyTt2nC9i8BFQE/edit?gid=261811728#gid=261811728] has been updated accordingly. If the edits affect the intended audience or scope of use, please double-check that permissions still reflect this.\n\n*If this ticket was for deleting a CustomGPT*\nThe deletion has been approved and the CustomGPT has been removed from the Legal & Compliance [toolstack tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jj2Mm-dJmnP6W4dBdFQZwrm2FGM0YTyTt2nC9i8BFQE/edit?gid=261811728#gid=261811728].\n\n***\n\nIf, at any point, you make changes to the CustomGPT (including prompt, data sources, functionality, or audience), or if you wish to delete it, a new ticket is required for approval.\n\nIf anything changes or you’re unsure whether an update requires a new ticket, it’s always safest to submit one so we can keep approvals and the toolstack tracker accurate.\n\nThank you,\nLegal Ops","2026-01-18T16:17:38.956Z"],["3817665","PFI-828846","PFI","ireoluwa.obigbemi@bolt-outsource.eu","Ireoluwa Obigbemi","Hello Team,\n\nKind reminder","2026-01-18T16:23:02.989Z"],["3817667","PFI-835070","PFI","charity.emeka@bolt-outsource.eu","Charity Emeka","!image-20260118-162347.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T16:30:06.111Z"],["3817668","LSS-60844","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Philippine Huret, your CustomGPT request has been approved ✅\n\n*If this ticket was for a new CustomGPT*\nYour CustomGPT is now approved for use and has been added to the Legal & Compliance [toolstack tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jj2Mm-dJmnP6W4dBdFQZwrm2FGM0YTyTt2nC9i8BFQE/edit?gid=261811728#gid=261811728]. Before broader use, please ensure the permissions and intended audience are set correctly.\n\n*If this ticket was for updating an existing CustomGPT*\nThe requested changes have been approved and the [toolstack tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jj2Mm-dJmnP6W4dBdFQZwrm2FGM0YTyTt2nC9i8BFQE/edit?gid=261811728#gid=261811728] has been updated accordingly. If the edits affect the intended audience or scope of use, please double-check that permissions still reflect this.\n\n*If this ticket was for deleting a CustomGPT*\nThe deletion has been approved and the CustomGPT has been removed from the Legal & Compliance [toolstack tracker|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1jj2Mm-dJmnP6W4dBdFQZwrm2FGM0YTyTt2nC9i8BFQE/edit?gid=261811728#gid=261811728].\n\n***\n\nIf, at any point, you make changes to the CustomGPT (including prompt, data sources, functionality, or audience), or if you wish to delete it, a new ticket is required for approval.\n\nIf anything changes or you’re unsure whether an update requires a new ticket, it’s always safest to submit one so we can keep approvals and the toolstack tracker accurate.\n\nThank you,\nLegal Ops","2026-01-18T16:30:30.915Z"],["3817671","PFI-829144","PFI","nikoleta.mikusova@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikoleta Mikušova","Hello, pls, any update?","2026-01-18T16:47:53.485Z"],["3817672","PFI-830105","PFI","ireoluwa.obigbemi@bolt-outsource.eu","Ireoluwa Obigbemi","Hello Team,\n\nPlease any update","2026-01-18T16:54:37.753Z"],["3817674","PFI-814802","PFI","oleksandr.anikin@bolt-outsource.eu","Oleksandr Anikin","Hello. Please let me know if there is any news regarding the client's issue.","2026-01-18T16:56:04.035Z"],["3817675","PFI-835060","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-18T17:00:47.772Z"],["3817679","PFI-835060","PFI","daniel.novo@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniel Novo","still need help","2026-01-18T17:10:30.127Z"],["3817683","DBRE-8694","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Checked both queries and the related code.\n\nFindings:\n\n# Code [1] does lock {{order}} table ({{SELECT … FOR UPDATE}}) for {{order_state_condition}} update to avoid order change during the condition update; although locking mechanism seems a bit too aggressive, code overall logic is valid and does not cause deadlock on its own\n# Code tries to lock the same order record multiple times using the same {{SELECT … FOR UPDATE}} record, and MySQL can handle this correctly – if the lock is already there, the second request will not fail not create additional locks:\n#* [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/02847ad360b97f6f4a59fcb632cb05c8a96900d9/src/rides/marketplace/order/main/core/service/orderState/OrderStateConditionService.ts#L154|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/02847ad360b97f6f4a59fcb632cb05c8a96900d9/src/rides/marketplace/order/main/core/service/orderState/OrderStateConditionService.ts#L154]\n#* [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/02847ad360b97f6f4a59fcb632cb05c8a96900d9/src/rides/marketplace/order/main/core/service/orderState/OrderStateConditionService.ts#L51|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/02847ad360b97f6f4a59fcb632cb05c8a96900d9/src/rides/marketplace/order/main/core/service/orderState/OrderStateConditionService.ts#L51]\n# Deadlock is caused by query [1] waiting for {{order}} table lock while query [2] already holding the lock over {{order}}; as a result, transaction [1] is rolled back\n# MySQL will resolve deadlocks as soon as they’re detected, there is no significant/configurable delay\n# Amount of deadlocks is minimal (a few per day worst case, not even every day), so it’s rather a bad coincidence than a logical error in the code\n#* [https://pmm.boltint.net/graph/d/mysql-innodb/mysql-innodb-details?orgId=1&refresh=1m&var-interval=$__auto_interval_interval&var-node_name=eu-db-4&var-service_name=eu-db-4-mysql&var-version=5.7.28-31&var-environment=All&var-cluster=All&var-replication_set=All&var-database=All&var-node_type=All&var-service_type=All&var-username=All&var-schema=All&from=now-30d&to=now&viewPanel=47|https://pmm.boltint.net/graph/d/mysql-innodb/mysql-innodb-details?orgId=1&refresh=1m&var-interval=$__auto_interval_interval&var-node_name=eu-db-4&var-service_name=eu-db-4-mysql&var-version=5.7.28-31&var-environment=All&var-cluster=All&var-replication_set=All&var-database=All&var-node_type=All&var-service_type=All&var-username=All&var-schema=All&from=now-30d&to=now&viewPanel=47]\n\n!image-20260118-173053.png|width=767,alt=\"image-20260118-173053.png\"!\n\n\n\nRecommendations:\n\n* Move locking logic from MySQL ({{SELECT * FOR UPDATE}} to Redis or alike); this will\n** separate “expected” locks from unexpected ones in MySQL\n** reduce amount of deadlocks\n** potentially make locking/unlocking faster (needs testing)\n\nTL;DR: this particular deadlock does not explain the NYE issues in ORDER-EU. Will continue locking investigation in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8709|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8709|smart-link].","2026-01-18T17:32:19.261Z"],["3817687","PFI-835091","PFI","luis.goncalves@bolt-outsource.eu","Luis Oliveira","!2026-01-18 174959.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T17:51:51.443Z"],["3817690","PFI-828780","PFI","aydan.kazimova@bolt-outsource.eu","Aydan Kazimova"," hello?","2026-01-18T18:09:00.383Z"],["3817691","PFI-835097","PFI","yunis.imanov@bolt.eu","Yunis Imanov","!IMG-20260102-WA0025.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T18:11:13.313Z"],["3817693","DPX-3794","DPX","maryam.heravi@bolt.eu","Maryam Heravi","[~accountid:712020:59ef2988-275c-471b-8931-bfc08a0ab578] I think we need to activate the save btn when a picker enters the weight but let’s see what  [~accountid:60bd1bad00bdd900683be69c] POV is here","2026-01-18T18:15:57.672Z"],["3817695","WFM-10031","WFM","shivam.pal@bolt-outsource.eu","Shivam Pal","Request - \n\nAgent ID - 562844\n\nRequest - Above agents is part DE GEQ Team and supposed to have *03 DE Global English queue* and *03 DE Global translation* as primary permanently","2026-01-18T18:24:03.021Z"],["3817698","PFI-831033","PFI","iren.asatryan@bolt-outsource.eu","Iren Asatryan","Hello [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24], \n\nThank you for the information provided. The rider has come back to us stating that the ARN is 23 digits long and that they require the correct number. Could you please confirm or provide the accurate ARN so we can forward it to the rider?\n\nMany thanks for your support.","2026-01-18T18:44:55.269Z"],["3817700","RCE-359","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768762261365329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@maksim.shashkov>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-359] `Validate external_reporter_az order data discrepancy` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-18T18:51:12.961Z"],["3817702","MLC-3108","MLC","shubham.sureka@bolt.eu","Shubham Sureka","*Update:*\nLaunched on 16 Jan by [~accountid:614b06ac47a8b5006f86d538] on Active Order Page\n\n* *WP:* Acquisition (when a payment card is saved), Activation, Scheduled Rides\n* *BU:* Acquisition, Activation and Churn - On active order page","2026-01-18T18:58:29.578Z"],["3817703","RCE-359","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768762897620849]*{color}:\nThe error margin reported is 3 orders of magnitude different (`422,612`), based on a quick'n'dirty query:\n{code}SELECT ci.name, COUNT(1)\nFROM ng_public_spark.company_order co\nJOIN ng_public_spark.admin_system_city ci ON (ci.id = co.city_id AND co.created_date = '2025-10-16')\nWHERE ci.country_code = 'az'\nGROUP BY 1{code}\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A99DZ0ANP/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-18T19:01:53.303Z"],["3817704","DMC-356","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:620e7f2de41f76006a6ece70] Existing issue. unrelated to [DPM-2320|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2320]","2026-01-18T19:02:08.403Z"],["3817706","DMC-360","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:620e7f2de41f76006a6ece70] Existing issue. unrelated to [DPM-2320|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2320]","2026-01-18T19:02:40.423Z"],["3817707","DMC-349","DMC","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","[~accountid:620e7f2de41f76006a6ece70] Existing issue. unrelated to [DPM-2320|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2320]","2026-01-18T19:03:46.507Z"],["3817711","TS-4658","TS","laura.kaselaid@bolt.eu","Laura Kaselaid","[~accountid:5a66e16b7fffe81da4caf5d2] This is my simple math, it isn’t confirmed or anything, and we can estimate 1000eur hit or miss depending on what gives or goes.\nIf all of our people join - hotel for 19 people, (13 boys rest girls) meaning 10 rooms. lets say max cost 100 eur per person stay/room, 4 nights with such amount of people and nights = roughly 2100-2600 (as per previous year -+ from outdoors considering from last year)\nThen add in fix cost for room in ETK+bar credit = 1200 eur\nAdditionally food = catering would be roughly 1.5K, but we can just either order sushi+pizza for 500 eur and we gucc, additionally get snacks i.e chips and dips ourselves (50 eur give or take), fixed cost would be bar credit, they seem to be adamant on serving drinks rather than corkage fee.","2026-01-18T19:27:28.995Z"],["3817713","CRC-2339","CRC","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","[update] Billing development is ready. We’ll generate invoices for VAT liable partners; and statements for non-VAT partners.","2026-01-18T19:28:35.640Z"],["3817714","CRC-1581","CRC","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","[update] Waiting for dummy test accounts to test the fiscalization integration.","2026-01-18T19:29:37.154Z"],["3817717","PFI-833042","PFI","ireoluwa.obigbemi@bolt-outsource.eu","Ireoluwa Obigbemi","Hello Team,\n\nPlease any update","2026-01-18T20:12:28.914Z"],["3817720","PFI-835137","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-18T20:42:55.609Z"],["3817725","PFI-835137","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-18T21:00:49.062Z"],["3817726","LSS-58632","LSS","patrik.piscak@bolt.eu","Patrik Piščák","[~accountid:712020:8c2f8fc2-ffb6-40f7-a6a4-79ab79b5c05e] Can you please answer here. We discussed this before Christmas.","2026-01-18T21:03:36.640Z"],["3817727","LSS-60556","LSS","patrik.piscak@bolt.eu","Patrik Piščák","[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] To my information, purchase of this very old used car was related to a long-term marketing campaign. This car is being sold for a price that corresponds to the market price.\n\nNatalia, let us know if you want some specific numbers and [~accountid:712020:cc83342e-0406-4e66-8201-8b0cd5b64c98] will provide it.","2026-01-18T21:08:31.520Z"],["3817729","INT-484","INT","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","26W03: No much progress last week, This week we plan to kick off the project, deliver in separate milestones (starting with popular item deliverable first)","2026-01-18T21:15:46.917Z"],["3817730","INT-777","INT","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd] I added a task here, we will investigate deeper this week: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CAMLE-9835|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CAMLE-9835|smart-link] ","2026-01-18T21:21:13.632Z"],["3817731","INT-570","INT","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","26W03: Working on admin panel changes to rename the flag and show the true state correctly","2026-01-18T21:23:31.108Z"],["3817732","INT-470","INT","david.pirtskhalava@bolt.eu","David Pirtskhalava","26W03\n\n* Model API for the product analytics team ready and handed over\n* This week: investigating model’s performance in Paris and Johannesburg. Model seems to be doing better than LPCT on backtesting, which needs to be reconciled with the A/B test results where we observed worse performance. \n* This week: building model interpretability layer (feature importances) to understand what drives model’s decision making\n* The higher frequency budget management system deployed and tested on a small technical test. Results are encouraging (budget alignment to ~ 1% deviations from target)\n* Working on a single metric for comparing a challenger model to the status quo (we are comparing u/c at all budget levels, that is two curves -- good for eyeballing, but automated decision metric favours a single metric that can capture most of the information from the curve)","2026-01-18T21:24:00.928Z"],["3817734","LSS-50832","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","_Hi_ [~accountid:5c0101ebd3af3b1ccfec6598]\n\n_Just to let you know that the update is currently in progress per my latest update and should be completed by end of the month._\n\n_If you need to expedite, I suggest to coordinate directly with the DPO team -_ [~accountid:712020:da839b78-87fc-4471-947b-3aae59c6030b] _._\n\n_kind regards,_","2026-01-18T21:26:03.924Z"],["3817735","INT-385","INT","adil.ansar@bolt.eu","Mohammad Adil Ansar","26W03: Finished moving enrollment APIs to separate bootstrap.","2026-01-18T21:28:08.750Z"],["3817736","LSS-60119","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Dear [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - considering there were no follow up questions, privacy will be closing the ticket. Let me know if you need support with this again.","2026-01-18T21:28:50.835Z"],["3817738","LSS-60581","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Closing as business did not come back with new requests.","2026-01-18T21:31:33.283Z"],["3817739","LSS-60663","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:89bc2f4c-58af-4ff3-a74a-f6b290b436e9] \n\nGetting back to this. I would like to clarify if you still need support with the ticket.\n\nI was unable to access the link, so please, if this still needs support, share the flowchart via a screenshot or a file.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-18 at 23.31.07.png|width=640,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-18 at 23.31.07.png\"!","2026-01-18T21:33:24.822Z"],["3817741","PRIV-520","PRIV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Previous update (copied from Slack):*\n\n# Privacy reviewed and commented the draft questionnaire regarding the proposed *collaboration between our Partner in Morocco with Chari* ([_see here_|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TDTDERtvjUACJotrtKZ1RyZhNAIPy7WikzivnddbS4k/edit?tab=t.0]) on Dec 3rd. \n# The documented was shared with the partner who came back with further comments on the possible launch model.\n\nFollowing this, Privacy commenced on the preferred launch model below⤵️ ","2026-01-18T21:36:45.179Z"],["3817743","LSS-59208","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Infosec gave green light to the supplier\n# Privacy still awaits feedback on the remaining points in Section 15.","2026-01-18T21:39:26.342Z"],["3817744","LSS-60356","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:5f1fbb0eef11df002588080f] \n\nTo clarify a little bit further the suggestion from [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] : \n\n# The best and simplest path would be to rely on *Bolt’s standard Bolt Business Data Sharing Agreement* for data sharing. This is already included in our updated T&Cs as an annex automatically, but we can also suggest to sign it separately if the customer requires this. This document aligns with Bolt’s operating model, and POPIA/GDPR principles.\n# If the customer confirms that using Bolt’s standard documentation is *not possible*, we will need to:\n## understand *why* it is mandatory from their side, and\n## assess whether a *limited clarification or carve-out* (rather than signing this template wholesale) is feasible.","2026-01-18T21:43:29.708Z"],["3817745","LSS-60450","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Provided response in the main ticket with the review of the suggested DSA;\n# The DSA cannot be accepted as is; privacy suggested to sign the BB standard DSA instead.\n\nStatus: waiting for the customer.","2026-01-18T21:44:39.364Z"],["3817748","PFI-835137","PFI","ricardo.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu","Ricardo Fernandes","Hello. This trip happened in Portugal, I still need help.","2026-01-18T22:02:29.452Z"],["3817749","PFI-835150","PFI","olubunmi.bakre@bolt-outsource.eu","Olubunmi Bakre","!image-20260118-220947.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-18T22:12:59.673Z"],["3817750","PFI-812434","PFI","julia.lechwar@bolt-outsource.eu","Julia Lechwar","update?","2026-01-18T22:15:37.487Z"],["3817753","PFI-835137","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi [~accountid:712020:c51255ae-017c-491b-a8fd-a3cd9c095ba0]  \n\n*I reissued the invoice several times → But invoice still comes out with incorrect data?*\n\nIf you reissue an invoice several times and it gets fiscalised with a VAT code at least once (ie you get an invoice with a QR) → whatever newly reissued (with a different VAT code) invoices will not get fiscalised.\n\nTherefore invoices get stuck with incorrect (old fiscalised) data.\n\n*What is the solution?*\n\nWe investigate with the provider if there is a workaround for it. However, it is not a high priority change as of now.\n\n*What to do now?*\n\nFrom now on please make sure that you reissue invoices to the correct Data (correct VAT code).\n\nBest regards,\n\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-18T22:50:25.808Z"],["3817754","PFI-835060","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","You can share the invoice from here:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"order_id\"%3A1384727934%2C\"city_id\"%3A817%2C\"system_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing\"%2C\"created_from\"%3A1751029459}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22order_id%22%3A1384727934%2C%22city_id%22%3A817%2C%22system_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing%22%2C%22created_from%22%3A1751029459%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]","2026-01-18T22:52:12.800Z"],["3817755","PLUS-36","PLUS","prateek.gauba@bolt.eu","Prateek Gauba","[~accountid:712020:808091d9-08c2-44da-8efc-0500c3190aff] Have added events here. Subscription AllBenefits Tap & Subscription PaymentPlan Tapped are relevant for our design. [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1diWn6EWDVzM0PQZGB5bvUVikxUIjOl8UAPj72swqm0s/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1diWn6EWDVzM0PQZGB5bvUVikxUIjOl8UAPj72swqm0s/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-18T22:58:08.863Z"],["3817757","PFI-835137","PFI","ricardo.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu","Ricardo Fernandes","After several edits, this is the error message that appears.\n\n!image-20260118-232645.png|width=299,height=145,alt=\"image-20260118-232645.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-18T23:24:52.357Z"],["3817758","MARTECH3-1421","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Submitted the changes for adding the features for tracking changes:\n\n* repo databricks-profiling-queries: [https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/pull/839|https://github.com/bolteu/databricks-profiling-queries/pull/839|smart-link] \n* repo bolt-server: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160945|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160945|smart-link] ","2026-01-18T23:25:15.547Z"],["3817761","MARTECH3-1524","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","ingestion via fivetran is done. Data is available in our database in {{ng_fivetran_linkedin_ads_prelive_spark}}","2026-01-19T00:42:47.886Z"],["3817762","MARTECH3-1525","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","build:\n\n* {{int_dim_ads_linkedin}}\n* {{ads_bm_metrics__linkedin}}\n\nupdate:\n\n* {{dim_ads}}\n* {{etl_marketing_ads_bm_metrics}}","2026-01-19T00:44:39.475Z"],["3817764","MARTECH3-1482","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Research study:\n\n* [https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228819557_Recapturing_Lost_Customer|https://www.researchgate.net/publication/228819557_Recapturing_Lost_Customer]\n* [https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304802113_Customer_Value|https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304802113_Customer_Value]\n* [https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1509/jm.14.0107|https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1509/jm.14.0107]\n* [https://www.imanet.org/research-publications/white-paper/-using-customer-lifetime-value-for-acquiring-retaining-and-winning-back-profitable-customers|https://www.imanet.org/research-publications/white-paper/-using-customer-lifetime-value-for-acquiring-retaining-and-winning-back-profitable-customers]\n* [https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/s41270-022-00158-7|https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/s41270-022-00158-7]\n* [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0148296321000187?via%3Dihub|https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0148296321000187?via%3Dihub]\n\nNotes:\n\n* *LTV target = GMV per user in the first year of the reactivated users* (first order after *>45 days* of inactivity)\n* Predict LTV *right after reactivation happens*\n* We possibly will build on country-level.\n* Possible fields to use:\n** User table (user_id, created_date, channel, etc)\n** Order table (user_id, order_id, gmv_eur, category, pick_up, drop_off, etc)\n** Incentive table (order_id, user_id, promo_type, discount_amount, etc)\n** Payment table (payment_method, payment_failure_flag, etc)\n** Engagement table (user_id, event_ts, session)\n** *Core features (*Ride-hailing GMV is usually dominated by *frequency × average fare*)\n*** {{lifetime_gmv_before_t0}}\n*** {{lifetime_trip_count_before_t0}}\n*** {{avg_gmv_per_trip}}, {{median_gmv_per_trip}}, {{std_gmv_per_trip}}\n*** {{trips_last_active_30d}} (where “active” is before churn started)\n*** {{gmv_last_active_30d}}\n*** {{days_since_signup_to_t0}}\n*** {{days_since_last_trip_before_gap}} (recency right before they went inactive)\n** Inactivity gap features (Longer gaps often imply lower future frequency, except for seasonal riders)\n*** {{gap_days}} = days between last completed trip and reactivation trip (t0)\n*** {{gap_bucket}} (45–90, 90–120, 121–180, 180-365, 365+)\n*** number of prior inactivity: {{num_prior_gaps_45d_plus}}\n*** {{max_prior_gap_days}}, {{avg_gap_days}}\n*** “reactivation seasonality”: month/weekday of reactivation\n** We use concept of FLV and HLV as in the Rider 1 year LTV.","2026-01-19T01:11:50.306Z"],["3817799","PFI-832771","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hello, \r\n\r\nPlease note that partner does not have any available balance. Partner seems to be churned in AUG2025","2026-01-19T02:03:13.137Z"],["3817802","LSS-50863","LSS","lisha.ye@bolt.eu","Lisha Ye","Hey [~accountid:62a88aabd0132d0068800eba] I have shared the meeting notes to you, and I also keep the communication with the supplier. But we will proceed until we signed the agreement.","2026-01-19T02:33:18.102Z"],["3817803","PFI-833572","PFI","theeranart.seatia@bolt-outsource.eu","Theeranart Seatia","Hi any update on this?","2026-01-19T02:35:53.077Z"],["3817804","PFI-835166","PFI","chotika.jungajung@bolt-outsource.eu","Chotika Jungajung","!Messenger_creation_EEEEBA43-230D-46C6-AD49-00C0DA13BD67.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T02:39:55.295Z"],["3817805","GCAP-279","GCAP","hana.rotinsulu@bolt.eu","Hana Rotinsulu","[https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1TuMHEXMZkrJKLychomohkSPhIDkZhmDkS2NPwvf2w5s/edit?slide=id.g37bfb622d32_0_1530#slide=id.g37bfb622d32_0_1530|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1TuMHEXMZkrJKLychomohkSPhIDkZhmDkS2NPwvf2w5s/edit?slide=id.g37bfb622d32_0_1530#slide=id.g37bfb622d32_0_1530|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T02:54:38.311Z"],["3817806","PFI-835167","PFI","oleksandr.strielov@bolt-outsource.eu","Oleksandr Strielov","the driver changed his mind","2026-01-19T02:59:17.065Z"],["3817809","PFI-829981","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hi team, any update on this one?. Thank you.","2026-01-19T03:07:24.668Z"],["3817811","PFI-830313","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hello team, kindly update on this one, the ticket status is resolved but still no respond from you. Thank you.","2026-01-19T03:13:09.367Z"],["3817812","PFI-835172","PFI","chatrawee.saenwerm@bolt-outsource.eu","Chatrawee Saenwerm","!image-20260119-032540.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-032547.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T03:26:35.923Z"],["3817813","PFI-835173","PFI","saksith.puntarwong@bolt-outsource.eu","Saksith Puntarwong","!image-20260119-031951.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-032035.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-032109.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T03:28:38.654Z"],["3817816","PFI-835178","PFI","ifeoluwa.oyemaja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ifeoluwa Oyemaja","[^Support case_ 725966309 - Customer Support - Beehive RECEIPT.html]","2026-01-19T04:35:56.826Z"],["3817819","PFI-835183","PFI","paratthakon.ainchat@bolt-outsource.eu","Paratthakon Ainchat","!image_480.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image_720.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T04:52:58.285Z"],["3817820","DSR-1858","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]! Is there any update regarding this? Thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-19T04:54:15.120Z"],["3817821","DSR-2680","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]! Is there any update regarding this? Thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-19T04:55:18.917Z"],["3817822","DSR-3255","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], as the deadline is approaching, is there any update on this case? Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-19T04:57:30.004Z"],["3817823","DSR-2751","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], as the deadline of the extension provided is approaching, is there any update on this? Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-19T04:58:48.191Z"],["3817824","FDBT-4812","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-19T05:00:09.346Z"],["3817833","DSR-3135","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9], thank you! I’ve already closed the tickets.","2026-01-19T05:07:27.103Z"],["3817836","PFI-835186","PFI","paratthakon.ainchat@bolt-outsource.eu","Paratthakon Ainchat","!image_480.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image_720.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T05:11:58.242Z"],["3817837","PFI-833987","PFI","liana.mirakyan@bolt-outsource.eu","Liana Mirakyan","Dear Team, the refund was issued on 10/01/2026, 03:50 not 14.09","2026-01-19T05:17:40.492Z"],["3817838","DSR-3803","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T05:21:07.228Z"],["3817839","WFM-10032","WFM","prim.vadhanajin@bolt-outsource.eu","Prim Vadhanajin","*Bolt Email(s) of Agent(s):*\n\n[tadapong.pintakam@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:tadapong.pintakam@bolt-outsource.eu]","2026-01-19T05:23:29.605Z"],["3817842","PFI-835190","PFI","nadiya.yasee-ngo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nadiya Yasee-Ngo","!image-20260119-053054.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-053124.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T05:34:33.908Z"],["3817843","DSR-3805","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T05:37:01.891Z"],["3817853","LSS-61748","LSS","ronoh.kiprotich@bolt.eu","Evans Ronoh","[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual).pdf] _(143 kB)_","2026-01-19T05:47:33.251Z"],["3817963","PFI-835197","PFI","victor.oradare@bolt-outsource.eu","Victor Oradare","[^account_statement_1-Oct-2025_to_19-Jan-2026.pdf]","2026-01-19T06:05:47.680Z"],["3817965","FDBT-4813","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-19T06:13:20.176Z"],["3817968","PAW-14897","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-19T06:18:35.349Z"],["3817971","DSR-3609","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi team! As the driver is a private driver active, I’ve sent the template as per OP. On hold for 5 days, in case of any updates.","2026-01-19T06:21:57.191Z"],["3817974","DSR-3713","DSR","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Additional Download for hidden profile [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1200057/view]","2026-01-19T06:29:01.314Z"],["3817982","DSR-3807","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T06:36:07.084Z"],["3817983","HS-29044","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi Jabbar!\n\nRequested document has been uploaded for signing. Once it is signed by Bolt You will receive it to Your personal email. \nIf You have any questions, feel free to reach out to me. \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-19T06:37:48.891Z"],["3817984","DSR-2249","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] We received a new message from the user\nOn 14 November 2025 I submitted a formal request for rectification of inaccurate personal data under GDPR Article 16. To date, I have not received any response, nor any notice of deadline extension. This exceeds the one-month response period required under GDPR Article 12. I kindly request your formal response within 7 days. If I do not receive a reply, I will proceed with a complaint to the relevant Data Protection Authority.\nBH ticket [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/724414251]","2026-01-19T06:37:50.913Z"],["3817992","EBIKE1-372","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","129C will be used as a front reflector. Do we have samples in HQ [~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] ?\n\n!image-20260119-064541.png|width=1044,alt=\"image-20260119-064541.png\"!","2026-01-19T06:46:24.269Z"],["3817994","EBIKE1-384","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Waiting for DFM and costs from suppliers. ","2026-01-19T06:47:54.091Z"],["3817996","PFI-807245","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hello! Update: as agreed, since the engineering effort to fix this is big, impact is small and the currency change may cause additional issues, it was decided to not reissue those records. ","2026-01-19T06:49:32.274Z"],["3817997","EBIOT-219","EBIOT","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","The IoT top and bottom plastics and gaskets are in Tallinn, it will be delivered by the end of the day. \n\nI will continue with the IP tests and assembly tests. And finalise by {{2026-01-23}} ","2026-01-19T06:50:39.769Z"],["3817998","WD-22577","WD","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi! This is something People Tech can help with. We assigned this ticket to them and I am sure they will have a look at it soon. ","2026-01-19T06:50:56.022Z"],["3818000","EBIOT-243","EBIOT","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","I will print 10pcs and close the task by {{2026-01-23}} ","2026-01-19T06:51:20.505Z"],["3818003","CCM-22283","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hi Peace, \n\nWe have enrolled the agents in the requested course and updated their details accordingly. The course should appear in their LMS dashboard now. \n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS Training team","2026-01-19T06:52:25.437Z"],["3818004","TAXP-3153","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Instalment calculated and paid.\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ryq_mlHwpiZYIOKvw5ap4yO_oZQRhM8x|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ryq_mlHwpiZYIOKvw5ap4yO_oZQRhM8x|smart-card]","2026-01-19T06:52:33.559Z"],["3818005","CCM-22284","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hi Ademola, \n\nWe have enrolled the agents in the requested course and updated their details accordingly. The course should appear in their LMS dashboard now. \n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS Training team","2026-01-19T06:53:37.439Z"],["3818007","TAXP-3144","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Instalment calculations done and tax payment made\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cd6i8Ypxcx6WkK6_HkduVQU9aIKz_ign|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cd6i8Ypxcx6WkK6_HkduVQU9aIKz_ign|smart-card]","2026-01-19T06:54:44.093Z"],["3818008","PFI-833616","PFI","kerli.uibo@bolt.eu","Kerli Uibo","Hi!\n\nApproved from my end, but please add the same namings which we already agreed to the not netted manual adjustments types - then it would be easier to understand and no need to spend time again to describe and align between the not netted types (which can be used later hopefully).","2026-01-19T06:55:11.541Z"],["3818009","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Kerli Uibo [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768805744860679]*{color}:\nHi!\n\nI approved the ticket, but please add the same types names which we already agreed ans created for non-netted types.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T06:56:00.252Z"],["3818010","CCM-22282","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hey Olufemi, \n\nWe are not able to enrol the listed agents in the requested course as they do not have an active email address yet. Could you please confirm that the ticket to create their accounts has been resolved with the Internal IT team? \n\nWe’ll be able to assist from there. ","2026-01-19T06:56:34.325Z"],["3818011","XP-3069","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","{quote}*= 1*{quote}\n\n:warning: *WARNING :: targeting-external :: [Targeting] Randomisation unit ID is not provided for the service call.* Triggered with value *2.67* ","2026-01-19T06:57:04.921Z"],["3818012","XP-3069","XP",null,"Slack","[Pavel Kiper|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0384T4FU1H/p1768743086222609|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0384T4FU1H/p1768743086222609|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T06:57:06.336Z"],["3818013","PFI-835210","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-19T06:58:44.001Z"],["3818014","PFI-835210","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:627cf5040d1e73006f7d2aa9] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T06:58:45.402Z"],["3818015","LSS-61742","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] , can you redirect the stakeholder to the correct flow and flag this to Lisanna?","2026-01-19T06:58:52.122Z"],["3818016","TAXP-3145","TAXP","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","Instalment calculated and paid\n\n\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1XhahcyDJlXMwzfpq-VqehYjYcFzAsGNX|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1XhahcyDJlXMwzfpq-VqehYjYcFzAsGNX|smart-card]","2026-01-19T06:59:00.351Z"],["3818017","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Kerli Uibo [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768805940849479]*{color}:\nRegarding the depostis from old tool - how does it work techincally? You return the deposit from there, but how the payout then works? Directly from some back account? We need to understand this to be able to separate these from other payouts and book to the old viggo balances account in accounting.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T06:59:18.920Z"],["3818018","DSR-3079","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","No response, closing the case","2026-01-19T06:59:30.235Z"],["3818019","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Kerli Uibo [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768806001845319]*{color}:\nFYI <@U0786LYPCG5> :point_up_2::skin-tone-2:\n{quote}","2026-01-19T07:00:25.984Z"],["3818020","PFI-835211","PFI","anna.zhou@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Zhou","!IMG_3560.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T07:00:35.948Z"],["3818022","PFI-832727","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Sikarin Seepol,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T07:00:40.915Z"],["3818023","PFI-830609","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Agil Heydarli,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T07:00:40.906Z"],["3818024","PFI-824866","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Satenik Iskandaryan,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T07:00:40.945Z"],["3818025","PFI-820795","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Evghenii Leanca,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T07:00:40.936Z"],["3818026","PFI-832797","PFI",null,"Automation for Ji