 hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T07:01:46.747Z"],["3818085","RCE-360","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768806160557759]*{color}:\nThis duty week is recorded @ [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-360]\n<@kairi.hennoch>, please move the task to the `Progress` state, or reassign first.\n\nProgressing of the task is necessary to automate the further reports assignment.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T07:03:17.740Z"],["3818086","FX-3664","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768806186620559]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3664] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T07:03:28.917Z"],["3818087","CRC-2218","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update]\n\n[Customer Payments]\n\nOne of the queue marked for review still requires SNS hence the request was rejected. There is one very last SNS/SQS queue waiting for review. The CRC can be closed afterwards. ETA end of January.","2026-01-19T07:03:28.996Z"],["3818088","RCE-361","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768806207843559]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-361] `Update container sizes for rides-compliance services` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T07:03:41.989Z"],["3818089","CSDA-289","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hey! Since there was no follow up on the ticket for significant amount of time, I will close it. In case this is still relevant, please feel free to reply in the ticket. Thank you! ","2026-01-19T07:03:42.588Z"],["3818090","CSDT-955","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Link: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i9L0EiU8bNlN7o1BXduyWePaMhoJcosx8IPqfP8DFHk/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i9L0EiU8bNlN7o1BXduyWePaMhoJcosx8IPqfP8DFHk/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T07:03:59.205Z"],["3818091","PFI-828294","PFI","mariia.patrakova@bolt.eu","Masha Patrakov","Hi, the rider knows about the verification, you can mention it","2026-01-19T07:04:43.374Z"],["3818092","LSS-61500","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343979|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343979|smart-link]  ","2026-01-19T07:05:06.528Z"],["3818093","LSS-61500","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:1d600e3f-d3ca-4f4e-b8af-f6c7510bb923] - FYI, waiting upon signatures by both parties.","2026-01-19T07:05:35.724Z"],["3818096","PFI-834885","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-19T07:07:16.782Z"],["3818097","PFI-835103","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-19T07:07:19.329Z"],["3818098","CRC-2037","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update]\n\nPayments including Bolt Balance transactions ie Phase 1B in progress. Last week: Added feature flag to control 1B behavior. Next: implement Balance capture and refund for self-serve UI.","2026-01-19T07:07:55.942Z"],["3818100","CRC-1598","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update] \n\nPrice review flows for cash orders with positive and negative balance will be tested and reviewed in January. Support automation and beehive development starting the week of Monday, {{2026-01-19}}.","2026-01-19T07:08:15.911Z"],["3818101","PFI-835205","PFI","alia.aziz@bolt.eu","Alia Aziz","Can we also get the reason for why the payout has been rejected? ","2026-01-19T07:09:17.658Z"],["3818102","DSR-3687","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a], Sigrid has provided clear instructions on how to proceed, but T2 has de-escalated to T1 and at the end they had only asked the user if they want their account to be deleted. This ticket has not been replied by the user.\n\n* Should we proceed to contact the user again? Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-19T07:09:33.081Z"],["3818103","PFI-835217","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^Transfer-Advice-HZ1JERI4FLS4D81E-130126_173306 (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T07:09:43.433Z"],["3818104","CRC-1855","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update]\n\nLast week: Added refund functionality in backend and UI. Next: capture functionality. Clarification regarding test payments in ledger ongoing. ","2026-01-19T07:09:58.410Z"],["3818105","LSS-59741","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:622f05a61c09d2007012deff] - just so that I’m clear before proceeding (taking over as Kirsika is now off to new adventures!). The dates seem a bit off or are we actually signing those retrospectively? Namely the last doc for Lilian - is it meant to be retrospectively done in 2024 and then marked until 2025 or should we by default move this to 2026 as well (understanding that this is a multi-option date given that the employment agreement is still valid, but just want to confirm, this is indeed the preferred approach). Thanks!","2026-01-19T07:11:20.852Z"],["3818108","PFI-834854","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout is still in pending state (Accepted) since 2026-01-10, which is longer than usual. Such delays typically happen due to an ongoing compliance review or technical issues on the payment provider’s side; we are monitoring and will respond to any provider requests. Please inform the partner it’s still being processed and may reach their account later; if not received yet, they can also check with their bank for incoming transfers.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-19T07:13:10.229Z"],["3818110","PFI-834883","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cash out has already been processed (state: finished) as of 2026-01-19, so it cannot be canceled and the funds are on their way to the partner’s bank. If the partner claims non-receipt, please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with them for their bank’s investigation; the app status may update by the next business day. If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-19T07:13:32.589Z"],["3818111","CRC-2300","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update]\n\nProgress: Instruments and Lifecycle implementation in progress.\n\nNext: Implementation, no milestones to highlight.\n\nOngoing internal design discussion how to model Payment Instruments immutability and versioning. ","2026-01-19T07:13:55.071Z"],["3818112","PFI-835058","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout has been successfully processed (value date 2025-12-15). Please download and share the proof of payout (if available); if the partner still cannot see the funds, ask them to contact their bank to confirm the credit.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-19T07:13:56.330Z"],["3818113","PFI-835143","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with value date 2026-01-12 (provider confirmation logged on 2026-01-13). Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot see the funds, ask them to contact their bank to trace the incoming transfer. If the concern is about earnings allocation between fleets (not a bank transfer), please raise a ticket to the Billing team.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-19T07:14:14.640Z"],["3818114","PFI-834896","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still in pending status (last update on 2026-01-12), which is longer than usual and likely due to a compliance review or technical issues on the payment provider’s side. Our team is monitoring these pending payouts and responds to any provider requests as soon as they come in—no action is needed from you or the partner for now. If the funds reach the account before the app updates, the status should change by the next business day.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-19T07:14:33.710Z"],["3818115","CRC-2190","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update]\n\nProgress: functionality successfully tested with limited user group. Minor issue with Redis TTL logic identified and fixed. Next: 21.01. GA rollout for ~10% users.","2026-01-19T07:16:14.474Z"],["3818116","XP-3070","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper",":x: {{[experimentation] Persist-AB-Processor-Query-Plans}} — a run has failed. *Workspace*:\n\n[datascience (3829506390716583)|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/?o=3829506390716583&utm_source=SLACK&utm_content=job-run-error] *Job*:\n\n[[experimentation] Persist-AB-Processor-Query-Plans|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/?o=3829506390716583&utm_source=SLACK&utm_content=job-run-error#job/491276378561341] *Run*:\n\n[[experimentation] Persist-AB-Processor-Query-Plans|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/?o=3829506390716583&utm_source=SLACK&utm_content=job-run-error#job/491276378561341/run/745130235097230] *State*:\nFailed *Attempt*:\n1 *Duration*:\n20m 18s *Started at*:\n2026-01-18 16:00:51Z (UTC)\n\n2026-01-18T16:00:51.838Z[UTC] (local time) *Terminated at*:\n2026-01-18 16:21:10Z (UTC)\n\n2026-01-18T16:21:10.233Z[UTC] (local time) *Launched*:\nBy scheduler *Run as*:\naugust.hovland@bolt.eu *Message*: Task Persist-AB-Processor-Query-Plans failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. View run button","2026-01-19T07:16:58.622Z"],["3818117","XP-3070","XP",null,"Slack","[Pavel Kiper|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05NL4GMUFK/p1768753270539199|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05NL4GMUFK/p1768753270539199|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T07:16:59.980Z"],["3818120","CRC-2075","CRC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[update]\n\nProgress: Rolled out on 16.01 for all Cartes Bancaires BINs! Next: migrate existing instruments to the new logic. ETA end of January.","2026-01-19T07:18:50.295Z"],["3818121","PFI-809382","PFI","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Please, we need an update here\n\n","2026-01-19T07:19:45.566Z"],["3818123","HS-29015","HS","lilian.nguyo@bolt.eu","Lilian Nguyo","Thanks Berit, all good now.","2026-01-19T07:20:32.829Z"],["3818124","SREP-1107","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","[https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/pull/2743|https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/pull/2743]","2026-01-19T07:22:05.395Z"],["3818125","PFI-834478","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi [~accountid:712020:bf226b03-702f-4fb1-a7f0-208d83ba63aa]  \n\nTo be more compliant with tax rules, we do not reissue the rider invoices.\n\nPlease ask the user to make sure that their Personal Profile and/or Work profile have correct information. And make sure they pick the right Billing profile before the ride. \n\nIt is as essential as picking the right payment method before the ride.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,\n\nKetlin Peldes  ","2026-01-19T07:23:16.175Z"],["3818126","CCM-22282","CCM","olufemi.oluwale@bolt-outsource.eu","Olufemi Oluwale","Hello Edwina\n\nThey have all have active emails","2026-01-19T07:23:38.506Z"],["3818127","LSS-61742","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Done [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1768807397590369|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06GRMZDE4Q/p1768807397590369|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T07:23:42.353Z"],["3818128","EBIKE1-372","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] No. [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] did the test fit in CN office and we never sent them here. If you need it, we can ask Satelite to send some.","2026-01-19T07:23:51.624Z"],["3818129","SREP-1107","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","[https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/pull/2780|https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/pull/2780|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T07:24:55.132Z"],["3818131","DRX-28266","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey ios.ci robot, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-19T07:25:21.717Z"],["3818132","CCM-22282","CCM","olufemi.oluwale@bolt-outsource.eu","Olufemi Oluwale","[favour.ujor@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:favour.ujor@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[temilade.olubiyo@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:temilade.olubiyo@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[glory.makinde@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:glory.makinde@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[abisola.oladokun@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:abisola.oladokun@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[mercy.fakayode@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:mercy.fakayode@bolt-outsource.eu]","2026-01-19T07:26:17.855Z"],["3818134","DSR-3687","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] can you please revert back to T2 and ask them to re confirm with the user whether they want to only change their email address or delete the whole account? If user doesn’t respond, please leave the account as it is and leave instruction to the User on how to delete their account.","2026-01-19T07:27:27.070Z"],["3818135","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Goals for the week:\n\n# Create a Confluence page detailing the root cause of the rear mudguard splashing issue.\n# Source silicone sheet material for the rubber flap.\n# Create a rapid prototype using the new in-house laser machine, if the machine will be usable this week, or cut it by hand.","2026-01-19T07:29:04.341Z"],["3818138","HS-28736","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:9d22087b-9bd3-42c9-944c-2112fcfa004e],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close Complete*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Close Incomplete*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and move it to status close incomplete.","2026-01-19T07:30:41.401Z"],["3818139","HS-28363","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:5d5149bc92705e0c1c5e519a],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-19T07:30:42.081Z"],["3818140","HWMISC-776","HWMISC","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","The parts are packed and are waiting for collection in Oslo WH. Should arrive in Tallinn by end of this week {{2026-01-23}} ","2026-01-19T07:30:45.112Z"],["3818141","RNTL-29425","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] ETA → 23.01","2026-01-19T07:30:59.651Z"],["3818143","LSS-61749","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T07:31:20.996Z"],["3818144","RNTL-29748","RNTL","dmitry.zamaleev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Zamaleev","[~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] ETA Jan 15->Jan 23","2026-01-19T07:31:21.187Z"],["3818146","PC-4773","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","Hi [~accountid:5fc10e1ffacfd6007606bd5b] … what the latest on this one? Are you still dealing with it?","2026-01-19T07:31:27.499Z"],["3818148","PC-4927","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","Hi [~accountid:5fc10e1ffacfd6007606bd5b] …  Can you, please, add just a sentence that explains why do we need to do that? Is it just to be able to distinguish between the two cases ie. \"default\" and \"unknown\" in monitoring, or is there something more behind that?","2026-01-19T07:32:18.712Z"],["3818152","G3IOT-1201","G3IOT","aare.palm@bolt.eu","Aare Palm","Postponed this more two weeks due to lower priority.\n\nFYI [~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] ","2026-01-19T07:34:20.939Z"],["3818154","PC-4773","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","From Alexey: completed last item from acceptance criteria. Failing capture with special code still on me.","2026-01-19T07:34:41.022Z"],["3818155","LSS-60663","LSS","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","Hello[~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \nYes, the legal support is still needed on this ticket. Have a look at this picture to understand different components and how they are connected. \n\nThe data will be stored at common places/services which includes data from PayCo(s) and OpCo(s). \n\n\n!image-20260119-073321.png|width=1414,height=865,alt=\"image-20260119-073321.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-19T07:34:47.253Z"],["3818157","CRC-2258","CRC","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","[update] In general this past quarter we covered: Mapping solution generalisation, Control generalisation which means that Performance optimization will move out of this epic, will be covered by transactional append and stability topics in Q1","2026-01-19T07:34:47.618Z"],["3818159","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Master switch is completed at 2026-01-19 09:30 EET","2026-01-19T07:35:09.817Z"],["3818161","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Looks, like it’s still in progress. I will take a look.","2026-01-19T07:35:44.266Z"],["3818163","EBIKE1-392","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Goals for the week:\n\nAs indicated by the test [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/bYBWuQE], we should create two separate kickstands for better stability on tilted ground: one for the e-bike and another for the Cruiser.\n\n# Create a 3D model and specifications for the Cruiser kickstand.\n# Set up the Confluence page for the Cruiser kickstand.\n# Test the maximum tilt angle of the EB1 kickstand and compare it with Okai.\n#* *CNC metal tips* for the kickstand must be made like shown below, as plastic fails under testing.\n#* Nylon will be tested first because it can be printed in-house.\n#* !image-20260119-074817.png|width=176,alt=\"image-20260119-074817.png\"!\n","2026-01-19T07:36:30.004Z"],["3818166","DSR-3809","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T07:36:57.142Z"],["3818168","PFI-812940","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Thank you for the issued document - received, re issued and case can be closed. ","2026-01-19T07:37:14.210Z"],["3818169","CRC-2159","CRC","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","[update] investigation of differences on account and peripheral dimensions level. Based on tests, looking for incorrect parallel flow logic and mapping issues.","2026-01-19T07:37:25.801Z"],["3818170","CSDT-956","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","For tier transfers per case, need to create a dimension in Looker, same approach as for reopen count. \n\n\n\nPlan: \n\n* Do general Looker sync for new metric ✅ \n* Test ✅ \n* Add joins for the order attributes to other explores ✅ \n* Test ✅ \n* Add dimensions to refinements ✅ \n* Test ✅ \n* Push ✅ ","2026-01-19T07:37:32.299Z"],["3818173","CRC-1897","CRC","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","[update] Staging model re-executed, and forwarded to stakeholders for feedback.","2026-01-19T07:38:18.870Z"],["3818174","DSR-3393","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Asked Tier 2 again","2026-01-19T07:38:37.168Z"],["3818175","PFI-834465","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please ask the driver to confirm when exactly was the screenshot taken and for what period is this. Additionally, daily breakdown view would help us confirm. \n\nAs for the reason the balance is showing as 0 in admin, it’s because they’re a fleet driver so the balance is transferred to the fleet. this is expected. ","2026-01-19T07:39:05.998Z"],["3818178","CRC-2264","CRC","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","[update] agreed on action plan for this topic and refined expectations","2026-01-19T07:39:22.157Z"],["3818181","DSR-3349","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Follow up from the user:\nSubject: Final request for deletion of my driver account \nHello, I hereby formally point out that about 25 days ago I submitted a clear and explicit request for my driver account to be completely deleted, but despite this I have still not received any clear, written, or definitive response from you, which is unacceptable; I therefore demand immediate written confirmation as to whether my driver account has been deleted in its entirety, and if this has not happened, a clear account of the legal basis for why my request has not been complied with, as lack of feedback and unclear handling of my personal data cannot be accepted; if I do not receive a definitive response without delay I will take legal action and proceed with judicial review, including contacting counsel and, if necessary, the courts.\nClosed BH ticket [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/722228370]","2026-01-19T07:40:19.542Z"],["3818182","PFI-823577","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Unfortunately, we can’t help in clearing Bolt balance debt or sending a new payment request to pay for the debt. Kindly check with your team on how to help solve this case or refund the user’s latest orders in the same currency and debt amount to help clear the debt?","2026-01-19T07:40:21.727Z"],["3818183","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Goals for the week:\n\n# Update 2D drawings to include additional features that prevent phone rotation, as demonstrated in the test video below.\n# Revise the bracket from R00 to R01","2026-01-19T07:40:29.282Z"],["3818184","WD-22599","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi, \n\nI have your permission you still have them over Ghana, \n\nDo you have an example of a miss birthday notification? \n\nKind regards,\n\nOli","2026-01-19T07:40:44.968Z"],["3818187","DO-5801","DO","rehema.athumani@bolt.eu","Rehema Athumani","I received the link from @anshul.sethi, who is responsible for the BH Visit Hub, and he has enrolled us. I think I may need dashboard access as well.","2026-01-19T07:41:08.451Z"],["3818188","CEBF-1831","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","Task is completed. \n\n!2026-01-19_09-41-10.mp4|width=430,alt=\"2026-01-19_09-41-10.mp4\"!","2026-01-19T07:41:30.667Z"],["3818191","DSR-3777","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Good morning 🌅\n\nDo we have any updates here? [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] 🙏","2026-01-19T07:42:17.571Z"],["3818193","LSS-58352","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Review ongoing with supplier","2026-01-19T07:42:21.784Z"],["3818196","HS-29072","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","[https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$427/23305$9555.htmld|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$427/23305$9555.htmld]","2026-01-19T07:42:50.454Z"],["3818199","DSR-2905","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","User sent another message:\nHello,\n\nMore than 20 days have passed since I submitted my claim for compensation, and despite my reminders I have not yet received any specific information regarding the status of the case or the deadline for its resolution.\n\nI remind you that my account suspension lasted six months and was due to Bolt's fault, which caused me financial losses.\n\nIn view of the above, I demand:\n\n* a written statement on my case,\n* an indication of a specific date for the conclusion of the proceedings.\n\nPlease respond within 7 days of receiving this message.\n\nA lack of response or further vague communications will force me to take further formal steps.","2026-01-19T07:43:49.573Z"],["3818201","HS-29073","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/inst/1$427/23305$9579.htmld","2026-01-19T07:43:54.850Z"],["3818202","PFI-835239","PFI","belinda.asiedu@bolt.eu","Belinda Asiedu","!Screenshot_customer's bank statement_ Notes.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T07:43:58.115Z"],["3818203","HS-29040","HS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","Hi Lauri,\n\nDzmitry fully vested his award on 12th of December 2025. The grant was originally made for 307 units with units issue price €141, i.e. total value at grant €43,287. With him moving to B2B contract the original grant was terminated, he kept all vested 249 units and unvested 58 units were issued to him as a B2B contractor.\n\nHis outstanding awards:\n\n* OP-15319: 14 units issued, unit issue price €230, vested as of 19.01.26 7 units, i.e. 7 unvested\n* OP-15320: 109 units issued, unit issue price €230, vested as of 19.01.26 31 units, i.e. 78 unvested\n* OP-15321: 61 units issued, unit issue price €230, vested as of 19.01.26 11 units, i.e. 50 unvested\n\nRefresh equity range for that level is: 50% - 63% - 75%.\n\nAs B2B contractors compensation details cannot be kept in WD then doing equity calculations is somewhat more complex. With this in mind, please let me know if help is needed when calculating how many units he could be issued as a refresh grant.\n\nKind regards","2026-01-19T07:44:05.036Z"],["3818204","PFI-834345","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please create a ticket to our config changes queue. Thanks! ","2026-01-19T07:44:10.842Z"],["3818205","PFI-834345","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T07:44:16.981Z"],["3818206","CRC-2291","CRC","ott.jalakas@bolt.eu","Ott Jalakas","\n\n[update] No updates for now. Supporting if any questions.","2026-01-19T07:45:01.691Z"],["3818207","FDBT-4796","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics fails on 2026-01-18 05:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 1040321031423676, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-18T05%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=bolt_plus_subscription_revenue.bolt_plus_subscription_revenue&base_date=2026-01-18T05%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-19T07:45:06.983Z"],["3818208","WD-22580","WD","sofja.pomazan@bolt.eu","Sofja Pomazan","Hi [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82], could you please check it ASAP? Bolt Operations will receive January invoices this week. So, all changes should be applied asap.","2026-01-19T07:45:11.135Z"],["3818210","CRC-2374","CRC","ott.jalakas@bolt.eu","Ott Jalakas","[update] 3 meetings for delivery and 1 for balance done, ","2026-01-19T07:45:56.142Z"],["3818212","LSS-61752","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","[^NXT Nicosia__Bolt_ Term sheet  .pdf] _(135 kB)_","2026-01-19T07:47:18.038Z"],["3818214","LSS-61690","LSS","maarja-liis@bolt.eu","Maarja-Liis Reiman","[^AMEX Bolt Services UK Limited 2025.pdf]\n\nHi, I forgot to add one… this needs Ahto’s signature.","2026-01-19T07:47:49.008Z"],["3818215","LSS-61752","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Please note that attached is only a draft lease, non-binding, I expect that the binding offer will come this week. ","2026-01-19T07:47:51.756Z"],["3818219","DSR-3777","DSR","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Good morning [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] ☀️ \nYes, we have an update. Brian has just confirmed that the suspension decision was based on orders (and associated ratings) from *02/09/2025 to 30/10/2025* under the KE Low Rated Drivers Program.\n\nI’ve updated the responsive data to reflect this timeframe :done: \n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] ","2026-01-19T07:48:27.175Z"],["3818220","PFI-829960","PFI","agne.pozelaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Agnė Požėlaitė","Hello [~accountid:712020:fc661671-1d51-4372-9578-b46465bd51ac] , we would appreciate an update on this. Thank you.","2026-01-19T07:48:53.557Z"],["3818222","LSS-56077","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:f989ec0f-bf00-4c9b-be89-cc44499bb288] and [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca], \n\nPlease could you review the cleaned one-pager (tab 3) ? Is there anything that was forgotten before we submit the ticket to CS?\n\nDoc: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GDMRuzZqUlkNJlo8LFij-mmAKyVd7yyynPLwEaBJDYI/edit?tab=t.pc3ycuxedokm|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GDMRuzZqUlkNJlo8LFij-mmAKyVd7yyynPLwEaBJDYI/edit?tab=t.pc3ycuxedokm|smart-link] \n\nThank you!  ","2026-01-19T07:49:23.146Z"],["3818223","LSS-61753","LSS","alina.solomka@bolt.eu","Alina Solomka","[^09.2025 Bolt-Partner Special Terms (LV) ENG-LV - Benu_2026.docx] _(66 kB)_\n\n[^Benu Aptieka_Bolt-Pharmacy-Agreement_2025_LV-ENG (1).docx] _(1.31 MB)_","2026-01-19T07:49:25.179Z"],["3818224","DRX-27651","DRX","aleksandr.stegnienko@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Stegnienko","[~accountid:712020:1b217ca8-3651-4a52-a7ae-3ed448546283] , I figured out that there are Admin Panel changes also needed to finish this task.\nSo, I added them [here|https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17198]. Waiting for the review form owning team.","2026-01-19T07:49:28.970Z"],["3818225","C2-371","C2","norman.tamm@bolt.eu","Norman Tamm","{{2026-01-16}} Firmware Live\n\nCurrently, there has been no significant increase in the % of short rides.\n\n!image-20260119-075011.png|width=976,height=460!\n\n% of negative feedback has not changed significantly.\n\n!image-20260119-075108.png|width=975,height=507!\n\nIoT error collections have not increased significantly\n\n!image-20260119-075306.png|width=977,height=508!\n\nThe slight increase in these KPIs is likely due to snow and bad weather.\n\nI will check back in a week to see if these metrics have changed and if there has been an increase in Water Ingress errors.","2026-01-19T07:49:35.397Z"],["3818228","LSS-61207","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hi there [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] , I have been working on another project in Germany so I have not had eyes here. I hope that you are well!\n\nI see that in the last comment you wrote that the LOI expires Jan 16th, since that is now past, is there anything Bolt needs to follow up on?\n\nThanks for the effort here and happy to be working with you again!","2026-01-19T07:50:19.731Z"],["3818230","LSS-61742","LSS","ketter.ots@bolt.eu","Ketter Ots","Hey! I have added instructions to the Beehive ticket, and the SD ticket be closed. Thank you!","2026-01-19T07:50:29.763Z"],["3818231","DSR-3721","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] Hey, the partner ID 10866989 doesn’t give any results. When we open the partner [profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-root/partners/edit/10866989?tab=partner_profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FOslo] the courier profile status shows application. The application ID 823298 is related to a different. \nI also updated the slack thread ","2026-01-19T07:50:49.088Z"],["3818232","CCM-22282","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Trainer reached out via Slack. Additional request made for: [+samuel.lana@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:samuel.lana@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n\n* Account reactivation \n* Account information update \n* Course enrollment ","2026-01-19T07:51:09.006Z"],["3818233","PFI-813099","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\n\n\nThe Customer Payments Operations Team does not have the required tools/permissions to issue refunds. If you are not able to issue the refund then we kindly ask you to check with your Team Lead on how to solve this case. You may need to request the following accesses in Admin to be able to issue refund for orders if you previously do not have such: \n\n\n\n* *Rides*: refund_payments and customer_support_beehive_ridehailing_order_refund\n* *Delivery*:  delivery_order_refund\n* *Rentals*: rental_order_refund, rental_subscriptions_refund and rental_order_refund_city_fine\n* *Carsharing*: rental_car_order_refund\n* *Bolt+*: subscription_offer_customer_support\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}*Note: A failed card payment can’t be refunded to the card. Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.*{color}\n\nFor issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.\n\n{color:#ff5630}For older orders refund, kindly check with your team lead as they have the required accesses to perform such operations.{color}","2026-01-19T07:51:21.772Z"],["3818234","LSS-57242","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hey [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] thanks a lot for this, I will add [~accountid:712020:cd367b4f-9ca2-4acd-bd4a-af6de2c8976a] to this ticket as I think she will be able to more easily answer these questions. \n","2026-01-19T07:51:33.093Z"],["3818235","CEBF-1633","CEBF","svitlana.vereshchagina@bolt.eu","Svitlana Vereshchagina","canceled since it’s included into a new smb flow ","2026-01-19T07:51:37.500Z"],["3818236","PFI-834294","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Looks like the address is missing on the driver profile. Please contact local ops to have them fix it and then retry the invoice. If that doesn’t work, please create a new ticket so we could look into this further. ","2026-01-19T07:51:46.157Z"],["3818237","CEBF-1634","CEBF","svitlana.vereshchagina@bolt.eu","Svitlana Vereshchagina","canceled since it’s included into a new smb flow","2026-01-19T07:51:48.981Z"],["3818238","DSR-2883","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","-no response, closing-\n\nNOT DONE, OPENING THE TICKET. Waiting for data sharing update","2026-01-19T07:52:00.759Z"],["3818239","PFI-834294","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T07:52:02.368Z"],["3818240","TAXP-1753","TAXP","john.khambo@bolt.eu","John Khambo","confirmation on individual markets ongoing. ","2026-01-19T07:52:05.833Z"],["3818245","SCM-1125","SCM","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Goal:\n- Modify the controller lid to guide the cables more efficiently.","2026-01-19T07:52:59.651Z"],["3818247","WD-21923","WD","janeli.niinemaa@bolt.eu","Janeli Niinemaa","Hey [~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a]! Checked and yes, it seems to be working regularly again, thank you!","2026-01-19T07:53:05.165Z"],["3818248","RDXENG-4550","RDXENG","ankit.goyal@bolt.eu","Ankit Goyal","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e]Just to clarify that driver notification will deeplink to rider chat however, the rider message “Hi wanted to find out where are you“ will not be present.\n\nIs it okay?","2026-01-19T07:53:08.209Z"],["3818249","DSR-3777","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Super, thanks [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - if any help needed, don’t hesitate to ping me :shakeh: ","2026-01-19T07:53:10.479Z"],["3818251","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] Can we push the supplier and ask them to take the mold cost up?","2026-01-19T07:54:20.534Z"],["3818253","CCM-22282","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hey Olufemi, \n\nConfirming that course enrollments have been completed as per our chat in Slack. \n\nPlease let us know if you need anything else. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS training team ","2026-01-19T07:54:30.545Z"],["3818254","DRAG101-353","DRAG101","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Lets see how does EB1 cable support helps. Waiting for TWS to make the test, eta for test {{2026-01-26}} ","2026-01-19T07:54:32.693Z"],["3818257","CEBF-620","CEBF","svitlana.vereshchagina@bolt.eu","Svitlana Vereshchagina","[~accountid:712020:fc274657-f7b5-4366-9f2d-5ec68865cf48]  can you please confirm if we have now option to toggle the map on opportunity? ","2026-01-19T07:54:58.268Z"],["3818262","PFI-831239","PFI","joseph.kamange@bolt-outsource.eu","Joseph Kamange","Payment issue yet to be resolved. Please assist ","2026-01-19T07:56:07.247Z"],["3818263","EBIKE1-425","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] is discussing the new cable routing with [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] and it seems that Kevin has a different cable routing. ","2026-01-19T07:56:07.789Z"],["3818266","LSS-61678","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] have sent this contract for signing? ","2026-01-19T07:56:30.165Z"],["3818271","BPPA-74","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Delivered v1 answers but auditors came back with questions on financial performance [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07NRK0KLAW/p1768491838342539?thread_ts=1764768419.935449&cid=C07NRK0KLAW]. Pending input from [~accountid:712020:bba87790-3d07-4531-9af3-f5df86d0d56a] ","2026-01-19T07:56:45.486Z"],["3818273","EBIKE1-27","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","All the modifications are done and ready for manufacturing. \nCan we but this task done? [~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] [~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] ","2026-01-19T07:57:00.848Z"],["3818274","LSS-60422","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you very much [~accountid:61cc1c959ee70a00680edd89] ! \n[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] , please comment on my questions so we can decide how to proceed with the template.\n\nIf the template has not been shared with Adam Auto, please download [this template|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12E2DDYiIkmDV28GG9DHuxYnylmqBwId4MuvInjYi9vY/edit?tab=t.0] and share it with them for review, stating that their template is very basic and does not meet the minimum Bolt legal requirements (no warranty terms, no terms on non-conformity, defects, delay, no explicit right to terminate, etc.) for vehicle purchase. Thus, for the sake of efficiency (to avoid redrafting their template), we are sharing our standard purchase agreement template, which we enter into with vehicle dealers globally. They are welcome to review it and add missing details for this specific deal.","2026-01-19T07:57:01.799Z"],["3818275","WD-22579","WD","olivier.blazy@bolt.eu","Olivier Blazy","Hi,\n\nThe changes have been implemented, except for Jevgeni Šimanski, who is currently on leave. If we were to move him, we would need to rescind the offboarding, transfer him, and then re-offboard him. Given the timing, it may not be worth pursuing this at the moment.\n\nCan you please confirm if everything looks good?\n\nMany thanks,\n\nOli","2026-01-19T07:57:03.683Z"],["3818276","INT-51","INT","rain.kask@bolt.eu","Rain Kask","26W3: created provider failed order rate as a feature and released all requested features to profiling.","2026-01-19T07:57:20.173Z"],["3818278","DSR-3667","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Hey user response to the question please specify the dates you need the data for. Do you basically need the data for the full year of 2025: \n_No, from October 1, 2025 until now. That's what I said in a previous message. Date/Departure/Destination/ Km._","2026-01-19T07:57:37.637Z"],["3818279","BPPA-72","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Actually not blocked but “in review” from Delivery leadership (Jeremy, Bavya)","2026-01-19T07:57:39.156Z"],["3818280","RCE-359","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768809448814149]*{color}:\nAzerbaijan reporting has historically been owned by expansion team, I will forward it to their support.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T07:57:43.102Z"],["3818284","EBIKE1-379","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","I think we can call it done? [~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] ","2026-01-19T07:58:15.377Z"],["3818290","L10N-28452","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28445](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28445)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T07:59:03.931Z"],["3818291","L10N-28459","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28445](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28445)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T07:59:05.819Z"],["3818292","L10N-28456","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\