are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28445](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28445)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T07:59:26.578Z"],["3818304","CCM-22285","CCM","karina.kligina@bolt.eu","Karina Kligina","!image-20260119-075937.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T08:00:17.695Z"],["3818305","INT-601","INT","rain.kask@bolt.eu","Rain Kask","26W3: Made various adjustments to core models (requested by AE) and created an additional data-mart for operational reporting. Models waiting to be released by AEs.","2026-01-19T08:00:44.220Z"],["3818306","PFI-833910","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! It seems like it wasn’t added as a manual adjustment to their balance. Please ask local team to check and process it again vie the weekly adjustment file. ","2026-01-19T08:01:11.548Z"],["3818307","PFI-833910","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T08:01:24.068Z"],["3818308","LSS-60422","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","Hi, \nThis is standard order contract. Purchase will be via leasing (bank). It is more formality. We do not have any advance payments. ","2026-01-19T08:01:31.393Z"],["3818309","XP-3043","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey, [~accountId:6268ef8e429789006946b1ac], the \"Sprint\" field on this ticket is empty. Is this intentional?\n\nPlease add this ticket to the current sprint and/or update the status. \nThank you!","2026-01-19T08:01:32.529Z"],["3818310","XP-3067","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey, [~accountId:61b0698cc75da800725c5dce], the \"Sprint\" field on this ticket is empty. Is this intentional?\n\nPlease add this ticket to the current sprint and/or update the status. \nThank you!","2026-01-19T08:01:32.848Z"],["3818314","LSS-61753","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T08:02:17.893Z"],["3818318","BDB-1461","BDB","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:60ab71565dc18500701cae80] hope you’re doing great! Sharing SC and  [+here+|https://www.figma.com/design/U7wnv1Gz61rZREc4SMWg4c/LCM-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Storytelling-Emails?node-id=5422-44775&p=f&t=ig8RMYnEqDM0Zzvn-0] if you search for Hopp Plus CA launch👯‍♀️ \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 10.02.19 AM.png|width=679,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 10.02.19 AM.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:02:56.880Z"],["3818321","PFI-835248","PFI","fisayo.oladele@bolt-outsource.eu","Fisayo Oladele","[^Proof of payment (2).pdf]","2026-01-19T08:03:50.752Z"],["3818322","DSR-3667","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] - could you create the file _without_ the pick-up address? Typically we do not share this information, and I currently do not see a reason to depart from that rule. We can explain to the driver that we do not provide this data. \nPlease go ahead and put together a report that contains the date and mileage per trip for rides between October 1, 2025 and now. No need to provide the _total mileage_ for all rides put together - this wasn’t requested, as far as I can see.","2026-01-19T08:03:57.062Z"],["3818326","BPPA-73","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","CA in final review with growth\n\nPL missing team input\n\nAZ hasn’t been discussed","2026-01-19T08:04:35.303Z"],["3818331","LSS-61743","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] - FYI - we have requested this NDA to be submitted for review in light of the Autonomous Vehicles project for Tallinn, as we need to check whether our standard NDA sufficiently covers the security/confidentiality requirements, or does it need enhancement. ","2026-01-19T08:05:33.499Z"],["3818333","DRX-27879","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","\n\nTested and verified on DI.127.0 (195054040) using iPhone 11, iOS 26.3\n\n* verified messages from polling shows ff {{show_polling_messages_enabled}} is true and not shown when it’s false\n* verified app shows warnings when ff {{is_show_poor_internet_message_enabled}} is enabled and internet is very poor and warnings is removed when internet is better\n\n\n\n\n\n!IMG_5990.PNG|width=414,alt=\"IMG_5990.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_5991.PNG|width=414,alt=\"IMG_5991.PNG\"!\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-16-2026 6-23-44 PM_1.MP4]\n\n\n\n!gps signal.png|width=712,alt=\"gps signal.png\"!\n\n!receiving gps.png|width=712,alt=\"receiving gps.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:05:52.071Z"],["3818335","RCE-331","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768809946450959]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-331 successfully transitioned to state 'Feature Request'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:05:58.770Z"],["3818336","RCE-331","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768809948346319]*{color}:\n<!subteam^S04LH4ZUSBS> FYI, there's a feature request :arrow_up: to review its priority and consider planning\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:05:59.539Z"],["3818337","RCE-331","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768809947891549]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-331 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:06:00.633Z"],["3818338","PC-4954","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[~accountid:6001a70dd364960139286b71] to add descripotion what is to do and handover it to the next firefighter.","2026-01-19T08:06:04.068Z"],["3818339","DRX-27874","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27879 has been resolved","2026-01-19T08:06:04.202Z"],["3818340","PFI-830895","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","hi team, any update on this one?","2026-01-19T08:06:33.682Z"],["3818341","RCE-325","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768809994909929]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-325 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:06:48.078Z"],["3818342","LSS-61275","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:5fc110f70d2f61006f7604a9], thanks! \n\nCould you please share information about this claim? Is it substantiated or not? What is our position - do we want to refund this money to the customer?\n\nDo we have the documents saved that the authority shared with us together with this notification, since the link no longer works?\n\nThanks! ","2026-01-19T08:06:56.375Z"],["3818343","FX-3665","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768810010688039]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3665] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:07:01.714Z"],["3818345","BPPA-103","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","Update:\n\n* added missing subscription revenue for rides + delivery\n* updated part of rides data. rides order data [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1j1-cWt42aZHp3ka6h09uGLKRS780YSBFmnOKshTVjKk/edit?gid=2065989869#gid=2065989869] failed to update. Solving with counterpart [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08J2H4F8MN/p1768561652144789] ","2026-01-19T08:07:25.797Z"],["3818346","PTWS-2116","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","updated condition to exclude the amount for Estonia\n\n!image-20260119-075543.png|width=651,alt=\"image-20260119-075543.png\"!\n\n!image-20260119-075501.png|width=651,alt=\"image-20260119-075501.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:07:29.600Z"],["3818347","CEBF-620","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:712020:6baf746d-d9a0-4048-9925-cb17dc392b48] Yes, we do. cc: [~accountid:621f66f84160640069c66ff4] [~accountid:712020:5dff0d44-5b3c-4dff-b225-944ac9a06241] \n\n!image-20260119-080717.png|width=448,alt=\"image-20260119-080717.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:07:42.116Z"],["3818348","BPPA-103","BPPA","hanshendrik.karro@bolt.eu","Hans-Hendrik Karro","New ETA: {{2026-01-20}}","2026-01-19T08:07:47.015Z"],["3818349","FX-3665","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768810070724839]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3665 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:08:03.698Z"],["3818350","LSS-59845","LSS","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Hi!\n\nThanks for the ping - looking at it today","2026-01-19T08:08:11.111Z"],["3818356","LSS-60422","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] Thank you, it is just a formality, and there should be no issue for them to sign our standard agreement template. Also, agreements are just a formality unless things go wrong. Therefore, to protect us from any future risk, let’s enter into a proper agreement at this stage.","2026-01-19T08:09:43.065Z"],["3818358","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] Hi!\nNot sure what you mean by one more category. Kindly explain.\nWhen do we expect feedback from the motion designer. We have already lost one of the placement as another partner paid and submitted relevant designs.\nCan we have this by today kindly. \n\nAll the previews are approved\n\nKindly send the dropbox for the remaining OOH - The bus station one","2026-01-19T08:10:21.103Z"],["3818360","CRC-2337","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Citi account opening in progress for Rides collection","2026-01-19T08:11:35.111Z"],["3818361","PC-4955","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","Number of PO API calls involved, the first task is to investigate which one of them is causing this, describe the impact and suggest options for improvements.","2026-01-19T08:12:00.822Z"],["3818363","CRC-2313","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Waiting local team to share CFG bank formats for payment initiation","2026-01-19T08:12:14.659Z"],["3818364","LSS-61562","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:5e6b55b2c54d0a0d044302f1] , thanks for clarifying. See my responses below, but I must stress that this is internal information and is not to be shared with the rider or the driver.\n\n* In short, no, the user who starts the recording is not required to notify the other participant. This is because it’s a safety feature and notifying the other party of the recording would jeopardise the purpose. Please note that this is not a privacy question per-se, so in case you have further questions about the design of the feature or the intent behind it - please escalate to the safety team via [#feature-audio-trip-recording|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C03FAJUDKGE]. However, for full context, this is how users are informed about the feature:\n** Information about the ATR feature is made available to both Passengers and Drivers through in-app stories, banners, safety-related prompts, and references in the [Privacy Notice|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/?category=rides].\n** The feature's purpose is to allow a user to initiate an audio recording *\"in case they feel unsafe\"* to provide objective evidence for safety incident investigations.\n** The recording is entirely user-controlled and can only be started by the user during an active ride via the in-app Safety Toolkit.\n* I suggest directing any questions about “what is an emergency situation for the user” to the safety team via [#feature-audio-trip-recording|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C03FAJUDKGE]. \n\nI would appreciate more context about this request - have we been receiving complaints? Or is it just for your knowledge?","2026-01-19T08:12:17.817Z"],["3818366","PC-4955","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","Putting it on high prio for the investigation, we can lowe the prio once we undesaratnd the issue itself.","2026-01-19T08:12:49.184Z"],["3818367","LSS-59165","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Good morning [~accountid:627121e62db3080070241431] ☀️ \nPlease let me know once we have any updates.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T08:12:52.521Z"],["3818368","DPM-2289","DPM","pawel.dabrowski@bolt.eu","Paweł Dąbrowski","[~accountid:712020:a5a9bde0-6d51-468a-85a6-ee3e42b31f73] [~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] changed this to “high” as Cogznizant team raised examples on not being able to import CSVs due to default language locale","2026-01-19T08:12:53.933Z"],["3818369","BSKT-4614","BSKT","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","duplicated: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BSKT-4613|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BSKT-4613|smart-link]  reject this one","2026-01-19T08:12:55.544Z"],["3818370","RDXENG-4711","RDXENG","oleg.voitenko@bolt.eu","Oleg Voitenko","Yes, it’s currently {{Body Tabular L Compact Accent}}\nSince this is a stand-alone label, we should rather use {{Body L Compact Accent}}\n\n*@user-U01QADS2R6E* Could you update it please?","2026-01-19T08:13:00.935Z"],["3818371","RDXENG-4711","RDXENG",null,"Slack","[Oleg Voitenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/60420d6730320b00696dab69] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1768561906350679?thread_ts=1768519127.134489&cid=CKYJD8AC8|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CKYJD8AC8/p1768561906350679?thread_ts=1768519127.134489&cid=CKYJD8AC8|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T08:13:01.927Z"],["3818372","PFI-835058","PFI","bostina.mielcioiu@bolt-outsource.eu","Bostina Mielcioiu","The issue is that the driver can not see the winnings for the period 08.12.25-14.12.25, why would we sent the proof of payout if he is not a fleet owner? the proof of payout includes all the drivers, not only him. the issue is with the app., What to do next?","2026-01-19T08:13:10.148Z"],["3818377","INSUR-178","INSUR","alessandro@bolt.eu","Alessandro Milici","h2. Cyber Insurance Underwriting: Technical Requirements Checklist\n\nh3. 1. Identity & Access Management (The \"Non-Negotiables\")\n\n* [ ] *Full MFA Deployment:* Is MFA enforced for *all* employees for:\n** Remote VPN/Zero Trust access?\n** Cloud-based email (M365/Google Workspace)?\n** Administrator/Privileged accounts?\n* [ ] *Service Account Security:* Are non-human/service accounts monitored, and have default passwords been changed?\n* [ ] *End-of-Life (EOL) Systems:* Are there any legacy systems (e.g., Windows Server 2012) that are no longer receiving security updates? (If yes, are they air-gapped?)\n\nh3. 2. Data Resilience & Recovery\n\n* [ ] *Backup Immutability:* Are backups stored in a format that cannot be altered, encrypted, or deleted by ransomware (e.g., S3 Object Lock, offline tapes, or hardened Linux repositories)?\n* [ ] *Testing Frequency:* When was the last \"Full Restore\" test completed? (Insurers usually want to see this done at least annually).\n* [ ] *Segregation:* Are backups stored on a separate network/domain from the production environment?\n\nh3. 3. Endpoint & Network Security\n\n* [ ] *EDR/MDR Implementation:* Is an Endpoint Detection and Response tool (e.g., CrowdStrike, SentinelOne, Defender for Endpoint) deployed on *100%* of workstations and servers?\n* [ ] *24/7 Monitoring:* Do we have a Security Operations Center (SOC) or a managed provider monitoring alerts around the clock?\n* [ ] *Patching Cadence:* Do we have a documented \"Critical Patch\" policy requiring updates within 15–30 days of release?\n\nh3. 4. Human & Vendor Risk\n\n* [ ] *Phishing Simulations:* Do we run at least quarterly simulations? What is the current \"Click Rate\" (fail rate) for the organization?\n* [ ] *Supply Chain Audit:* Do we have a list of our \"Critical Class\" vendors (SaaS/IaaS providers) and have we reviewed their SOC 2 Type II reports in the last 12 months?\n* [ ] *Wire Transfer Verification:* (For Finance/Accounting) Is there a formal process requiring a *voice call/second-channel verification* before changing bank details for any vendor or employee?\n\nh3. 5. Incident Response & AI Governance\n\n* [ ] *Tabletop Exercises:* When was the last time the Incident Response Plan (IRP) was physically tested by leadership?\n* [ ] *AI Shadow IT:* Are we currently monitoring or blocking the unauthorized upload of corporate data to public AI LLMs?\n* [ ] *Logging Persistence:* Do we retain at least *90 days* of security logs for forensic purposes?\n\n----\n\nh3. Pro-Tip for the Team:\n\nInsurers now often perform an *External Perimeter Scan* (using tools like BitSight or SecurityScorecard) before even looking at the application. Ask the team to check for:\n\n# *Open RDP Ports:* Ensure Port 3389 is closed to the public internet.\n# *Unprotected Subdomains:* Clean up \"dangling\" DNS records that could be used for takeovers.\n# *SPF/DKIM/DMARC:* Ensure these email authentication protocols are set to \"Reject\" or \"Quarantine\" to prevent spoofing.","2026-01-19T08:13:35.760Z"],["3818378","DRX-28236","DRX","gert.vesterberg@bolt.eu","Gert Vesterberg","Check with [~accountid:6423f37357f0c028e2f75b72] if it should be applied","2026-01-19T08:13:42.140Z"],["3818380","L10N-28479","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28445](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28445)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T08:14:11.423Z"],["3818381","C3HW-92","C3HW","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","PCB manufacturers are confirmed. Brandner questions answered, initial component questions cleared up. \n\nETA requested.","2026-01-19T08:14:15.117Z"],["3818382","HS-28983","HS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hey, I would appreciate if you could send me a digital version of the letter with wet signature before posting the original. Many thanks!","2026-01-19T08:14:20.637Z"],["3818387","BDB-1513","BDB",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Polina Petuhhova 👋. This is a reminder, that the task is due today or it's resolved but hasn't been moved to \"Done\" status yet.\n\n- If the task is resolved, move it to the \"Done\" status. Or if the task is canceled, move it to \"Canceled\" status\n\n- If the task can't be resolved in the initial timeframe, then make sure that the Project Manager(Team Lead, in case PM is not available), and Customer are notified. And change the new due date accordingly.","2026-01-19T08:15:15.302Z"],["3818388","PFI-835252","PFI","faith.ndonye@bolt-outsource.eu","Faith Ndonye","[^Confirmare_plata_2026-01-14 (1) (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T08:15:40.187Z"],["3818389","CRC-2316","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Waiting partner to top up Abu Dhabi bank account to proceed with payout test","2026-01-19T08:15:46.954Z"],["3818391","LSS-60422","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","we always sign dealers order agreements. can you mark, which parts are dangerous for us from dealers agreement? ","2026-01-19T08:16:08.133Z"],["3818392","DBRE-8599","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Working on configuration drift\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032VGUKR3K/p1768809914193459|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032VGUKR3K/p1768809914193459|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T08:16:16.014Z"],["3818393","CSDA-281","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","[notebook|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832068116?o=3598988355446810#command/8920732282548360], Gsheet file - [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/152zp1DQX-T15A-ATDKmBd4Kf_iGMH0h3tu_SXym3zmk/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/152zp1DQX-T15A-ATDKmBd4Kf_iGMH0h3tu_SXym3zmk/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] \n\nupdate from T&W on how to filter such cases - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A0T3NATF1/p1769171496298149?thread_ts=1768297534.699429&cid=C0A0T3NATF1|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A0T3NATF1/p1769171496298149?thread_ts=1768297534.699429&cid=C0A0T3NATF1|smart-link] \n\nchecking in with Polina via DMs in Slack - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D05J6UVNHQ8/p1769436622317929|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D05J6UVNHQ8/p1769436622317929|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T08:16:26.390Z"],["3818394","CRC-2235","CRC","marija.skiljevic@bolt.eu","Marija Škiljević","[Update] Total problem size for order_not_delivered refund requests estimated at 960k EUR/month. Estimated savings from the PIN verification feature are 50% of the total refund cost for this issue key. ","2026-01-19T08:16:35.764Z"],["3818396","CCM-22277","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Emmanuel,\n\nany progress on this? I still don’t see Prisca’s account in the Bolt Learning Hub.","2026-01-19T08:16:43.512Z"],["3818399","PAW-18353","PAW",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-19T08:16:55.589Z"],["3818406","LSS-61699","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please send contract for signing to: [rutmar@fleetbrains.com|mailto:rutmar@fleetbrains.com], signing person will be: *Rutmar Silde*","2026-01-19T08:17:34.345Z"],["3818409","LSS-61742","LSS","ugne.guigaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Ugnė Guigaitė","[~accountid:615c8598a7071000699c8c93] thanks for your reply. Unfortunately, the user no longer has access to their account and wants to delete it, we are not able to follow KB to delete since it is missing email verification. Could you please review it further?\n","2026-01-19T08:18:10.013Z"],["3818410","PFI-834278","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-19T08:18:11.209Z"],["3818411","WD-22599","WD","olivia.abera@bolt.eu","Olivia Nyarkoa Abera","Hi Olivier,\n\nI usually receive notifications for upcoming birthdays, however, last week, I did not receive the notifications for [~accountid:712020:1c358f69-b1b6-46d7-96b7-c81037b0c0f8] and [~accountid:61558a79bfa2c1006b71955a]\n\nI think it has been resolved as today I have received the notification for upcoming birthdays.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T08:18:11.703Z"],["3818412","PFI-834642","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-19T08:18:12.515Z"],["3818413","PFI-834967","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-19T08:18:13.879Z"],["3818414","LSS-60753","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi[~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ,\nJust to clarify - do you also want me to prepare the LIA?","2026-01-19T08:18:44.849Z"],["3818415","PFI-833425","PFI","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","Hi [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] , I’ve added to the original invoice issuer the alternative of “intermediary” [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HqshWRwpneSgbQ0mnvlEAKx_EuyuHMdp0WGqCguH5MA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HqshWRwpneSgbQ0mnvlEAKx_EuyuHMdp0WGqCguH5MA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] - in essence we will just remove the single invoice as Bolt Rides DK is the principal in both B2C as well as B2B - let me know if you see any concerns with making this option available.\n\nThank you\n\nMaret","2026-01-19T08:19:17.433Z"],["3818417","PFI-835259","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T08:19:32.342Z"],["3818418","CRC-2334","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Payment flows migrated successfully (/) ","2026-01-19T08:19:33.434Z"],["3818419","PFI-833425","PFI","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","cc: [~accountid:712020:1eca79ab-231a-45b5-b53f-3471723b5176] for your visibility as well!","2026-01-19T08:19:38.289Z"],["3818420","PC-4953","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[1] confirm with PO whether:\n\nINTERNAL means INQUIRY\nEXTERNAL means CHARGEBACK\n\n[2] Could PO standardize the gateway data to be the same for all gateways and instrument types","2026-01-19T08:19:48.468Z"],["3818423","PFI-835259","PFI","anna.pentinen@bolt.eu","Anna Pentinen","duplicate here https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-833833","2026-01-19T08:20:08.204Z"],["3818424","PFI-835259","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T08:20:12.393Z"],["3818428","CCM-22277","CCM","emmanuel.aboagye@bolt.eu","Emmanuel Aboagye-Asante","She joining on 2nd Feb","2026-01-19T08:20:42.600Z"],["3818429","LSS-61516","LSS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] I was asked to create this ticket so you would be aware of the pre-trial threat 🙂 \n Please see below the message we sent to the driver with his order history: \nThank you for your request received on 11.01.26.\n\nWe have provided a copy of your trip history for the past four years, which includes all cancelled rides associated with your driver account.\n\nWe cannot provide information on whether a passenger requested a cancellation refund or whether they received one. Such information pertains to the passenger’s personal data and Bolt’s internal refund procedure, not your personal data as a driver. Therefore, it does not fall under the right of access provided by Article 15 of the GDPR.\n\nTo protect the privacy of other users, we do not disclose passengers’ refund requests, fare adjustments, or interactions between passengers and our customer support team.\n\nIf you have any further questions, please contact our customer support by replying to this message.","2026-01-19T08:20:45.799Z"],["3818430","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","I’ve cancelled the backfills. The problematic table is the {{notification}}.","2026-01-19T08:20:48.653Z"],["3818431","LSS-61380","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Summary of the 13 January 2026 call may be found [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C076GDSHQLE/p1768810812556979].","2026-01-19T08:20:49.701Z"],["3818432","LSS-61716","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:5e3bcefc-e2ed-4de9-8197-663f375263bd] , please see reviewed letter attached. Please share with the counterparty for their review. [^Brokers' Appointment in WORD ( Not Sole)_Bolt review.docx] ","2026-01-19T08:21:03.624Z"],["3818433","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] \nHere you are: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/26w5o137lzdi8c45ixph4/AIQEZbv1qRoFepJJKEmX_1Y?rlkey=li8wf96iqr4zu27n0sall5yjp&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/26w5o137lzdi8c45ixph4/AIQEZbv1qRoFepJJKEmX_1Y?rlkey=li8wf96iqr4zu27n0sall5yjp&dl=0|smart-link] \nPlease let me know if everything works for you. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T08:21:07.928Z"],["3818434","HS-29038","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Waiting a JD from the manager.","2026-01-19T08:21:09.869Z"],["3818440","PFI-825462","PFI","israel.kizito@bolt-outsource.eu","Israel Kizito","Hello team, Payment is yet to reflect, kindly assist.","2026-01-19T08:22:29.878Z"],["3818442","PFI-835264","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","[^BOLT NOV2025.PDF.PDF]","2026-01-19T08:22:59.480Z"],["3818443","LSS-61716","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Thank you! Will share it with partners for a review.","2026-01-19T08:23:08.841Z"],["3818444","DBRE-8705","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","[@maciej.opala|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/61cc1c85ce3652006a6822c7], problematic in what way? Canceled as not finished and some data gap still existing?","2026-01-19T08:23:09.092Z"],["3818445","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","It times out on the bounds query. It’s not finished yet.","2026-01-19T08:23:25.733Z"],["3818448","CCM-22285","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey Karina ☀️ \n\nThe test has been reset. \n\nWishing you a lovely day :))\n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-19T08:23:46.895Z"],["3818449","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","I will get back here, let me take a look.","2026-01-19T08:23:51.143Z"],["3818452","DSR-3205","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi team, thanks a lot. [Answer|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nwYyB_G7sbbGJoUERIPFEzhMa7PN_7rgVTsH4Dlb448/edit?usp=drive_link] letter and responsive [data|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1HdhHTbba00SICQ4hNiC-Z8LBvhrGvWXC?usp=drive_link] can be shared with the driver (/) ","2026-01-19T08:24:12.928Z"],["3818454","PFI-835267","PFI","szymon.barabasz@bolt.eu","Szymon Barabasz","[^PL1526-3286.pdf]","2026-01-19T08:24:43.221Z"],["3818455","PFI-835267","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T08:24:45.420Z"],["3818456","SFLEET-196","SFLEET","bohdan.humeniuk@bolt.eu","Bohdan Humeniuk","!image-20260119-082446.png|width=650,alt=\"image-20260119-082446.png\"!\n\n!image-20260119-082510.png|width=650,alt=\"image-20260119-082510.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:25:16.117Z"],["3818458","PC-4951","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","1st task is to investigate the impact.","2026-01-19T08:25:39.880Z"],["3818463","IOTTEAM-219","IOTTEAM","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","Add pull-ups to RI and DTR lines:\n\n!image-20260119-082613.png|width=471,alt=\"image-20260119-082613.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:26:18.116Z"],["3818465","CEBF-1793","CEBF","svitlana.vereshchagina@bolt.eu","Svitlana Vereshchagina","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d] to discuss this one with [~accountid:6218cbe4468c2e007170c08b] ","2026-01-19T08:26:17.125Z"],["3818467","INT-799","INT","vivekkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vivek Kumar Singh","26W03 Update: Topic picked up by DriverX, alignment on timelines (especially for designs first) scheduled for CW04","2026-01-19T08:26:26.480Z"],["3818469","CCM-22277","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Thanks, Emmanuel.\n\nIn that case, I will close this ticket. Please be sure to send a new ticket for the onboarding, once she joins and after her OKTA is activated.\n\nWishing you a lovely rest of the day. ☀️ \n\nBest,\n\nIrena\n","2026-01-19T08:27:13.730Z"],["3818470","PFI-777012","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I don’t see it on the balance - please reach out to campaigns team to verify they have sent the amount and the timestamp as well os we could check. ","2026-01-19T08:27:14.696Z"],["3818473","LSS-61756","LSS","evelyn.skytte@bolt.eu","Evelyn Skytte","[^VAT correction 2024 - Iceland.pdf] _(402 kB)_","2026-01-19T08:28:03.820Z"],["3818474","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","[@leandro.morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] I see there’re two predicates for the {{taxify_payment.notification}} table:\n\n{noformat}created >= '2026-01-15 21:00:00' AND created < '2026-01-15 22:59:00'{noformat}\n\nand:\n\n{noformat}created >= '2026-01-18 05:00:00' AND created < '2026-01-18 06:05:00'{noformat}\n\nwhat is the reason for that? Was there another outage over the weekend?","2026-01-19T08:28:09.776Z"],["3818475","MKP-9778","MKP","andre.tamm@bolt.eu","Andre Tamm","Rejected - This task was created due to a misunderstanding. There is an investigation being done to figure out shortcomings in cancellation fees and this was floated as one potential idea for solving them. However at this point there is no concrete task or use cases decided on yet. Instead we will wait for the result of the investigation and based on that decide what should be done, if anything.","2026-01-19T08:28:17.395Z"],["3818477","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","# Room & rent - alright, 600€ rent sounds good, and they have some options for activities :thumbsup::skin-tone-2: \n# Drinks - let’s agree on credit per person, that’s what I was thinking as well. Let’s adjust the credit after we finalize other costs\n# Food - can you confirm with them if we can just order-bring our own food?\n## Ordering a bunch of food via Bolt Food and expensing it would be the best way I think, or going to Telliskivi in groups and eating there during the evening\n## I’m confident most people would want a hot meal they choose themselves instead of cold snacks for 1K€ or an unknown quality buffet for 1,5K€ 🙃\n## This way everyone will be able to get what they want as well since food was part of the feedback for the last seminar\n## If we can order-bring our own food, I think we can safely assume 50€ per person would be enough → 1000€ \n# Accommodation - we’ll have to bunk people together, but from the calculations at 100€ / per room and 10 rooms, that’s 1000€ per night, 4 nights in total = ~4000€ total for accommodation.\n\n----\n\nSumming it all up, I see we’re at 600+1000+4000 = 5600€. We can safely give people 50€ bar credit → 6600€, which is in theory less than year 🤔","2026-01-19T08:28:47.952Z"],["3818479","PFI-826494","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Not sure what this payment was for, but we do not provide invoices for such payments. ","2026-01-19T08:29:31.591Z"],["3818482","CRC-2332","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Business: LHV Certificates and integration are being updated by our engineers to enable VAs for new entity account.","2026-01-19T08:29:45.847Z"],["3818484","INT-800","INT","vivekkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vivek Kumar Singh","26W03 Update: \n\n* Capability to target winback campaigns based on user cohort already available, analytics needs to add the segments to the Profile Service, expected to be done in the coming weeks.\n* Plan to set lower discount for champions and high preference riders, before scaling to more markets. Current campaigns extended by 2 weeks.","2026-01-19T08:30:25.208Z"],["3818486","BDB-1513","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Hi [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] - good morning,  just checking in to see if this one will be possible to finalise today?\n\n\n\nMany thanks.","2026-01-19T08:30:28.335Z"],["3818490","PFI-826496","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Again, not sure why the payment was made, but we do not provide invoices on request. ","2026-01-19T08:30:50.932Z"],["3818494","PFI-835210","PFI","dean.goulding@bolt.eu","Dean Goulding","Hi [~accountid:5b7beb36358c9f2a008eab43] \nSeems like you have made an error in your request, “Please update billing from driver to driver based”?","2026-01-19T08:31:03.503Z"],["3818495","CMO-12668","CMO","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","*19 January* \n\n* *Problem*: Discussed with Olwethu regarding the current communication guidelines and the autonomy agents now have when it comes to replies. In addition to this, the guidelines are still being adjusted as time goes on due to changes in quality. \n* *Solution*: Because of this, we should rely on the KB as the source of truth. We will not include specific examples in the slides anymore; instead, this will be replaced with a reading exercise followed by questions based on the passage ","2026-01-19T08:31:04.117Z"],["3818496","LSS-57933","LSS","marketa.hlavac@bolt.eu","Marketa Hlavacova","Hi [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] \n\nas discussed in slack DMs sharing it here as well, understand you will review it earliest on Wednesday, thank you\n\n[^2026.01 Bolt Services RO Pickitoo Marketing Service Agreement (reverted changes).docx]\n\n","2026-01-19T08:31:09.816Z"],["3818497","LSS-58990","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","hey, they signed LV contract, you can cancel request if it’s still pending in the system. ","2026-01-19T08:31:19.745Z"],["3818498","LSS-60422","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] please see below the message from Liisa Daniel-Dixon of December 22, 2025, where she listed at a high level which matters are not covered at all by the shared dealer agreement. Thus, I kindly ask to use our template. \n\nAccepting the dealer agreement would be an option if the agreement were properly drafted to address also the purchaser’s rights and interests; this is not the case here.","2026-01-19T08:31:23.598Z"],["3818500","PFI-825998","PFI","ihor.asaulenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Ihor Asaulenko","Last payout [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/234309484|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/234309484]","2026-01-19T08:31:27.876Z"],["3818502","LSS-58622","LSS","oliver.vahar@bolt.eu","Oliver Martyn Vahar","Hi Gabriele! Sorry! It was delayed from my side as I was on leave for 2w in December, and didn’t deal with it over then. Will revisit the topic to pick it up, but will probably use the same agreement that we then had previously ","2026-01-19T08:31:48.378Z"],["3818503","CEBF-110","CEBF","svitlana.vereshchagina@bolt.eu","Svitlana Vereshchagina","[~accountid:712020:7621878e-e68d-4cea-9df5-171c95c4c62d]  [~accountid:712020:bcd1b76c-7935-49eb-a9ce-d0998dbc8d43]  to estimate the ticket ","2026-01-19T08:31:52.158Z"],["3818504","PFI-835275","PFI","daumantas.butvila@bolt-outsource.eu","Daumantas Butvila","[^payment_order_1317020044.pdf]\n\nAdding the payment order","2026-01-19T08:32:10.582Z"],["3818505","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Also, the error is:\n\n{noformat}org.apache.spark.SparkException: Job aborted due to stage failure: Task 3 in stage 34931.0 failed 4 times, most recent failure: Lost task 3.3 in stage 34931.0 (TID 34988) (172.21.39.31 executor 12): java.sql.SQLException: Your query has been cancelled due to exceeding the allowed memory limit for a single SQL query. Please try narrowing your query scope or increase the tidb_mem_quota_query limit and try again.[conn=2446691650]{noformat}\n\nDoes this cluster have atypical memory settings?","2026-01-19T08:32:19.518Z"],["3818509","C3HW-87","C3HW","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Hi [~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] [~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] \nHere are the updated files. We need to ask the supplier to modify the current mold. Then Incap can order 100pcs. ","2026-01-19T08:32:50.934Z"],["3818511","PFI-835281","PFI","oluwatosin.akinbolasere@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwatosin Akinbolasere","[^payment BOLT NBC.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-19T08:33:17.960Z"],["3818515","PFI-808708","PFI","leticija.jurjevic@bolt.eu","Leticija Jurjević","Agent still needed.","2026-01-19T08:34:05.607Z"],["3818516","LSS-61757","LSS","loi.nguyen@bolt.eu","Loi Nguyen","[^Cartel Media Advertising Agreement omgM1173 - BOLT NZ.pdf] _(534 kB)_","2026-01-19T08:34:06.224Z"],["3818518","PC-4948","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","[~accountid:6096595a33a941007116501b] … please, clariify with [~accountid:712020:71558a29-6aa8-4ba9-a65c-35de451da5e6] what is to do here. Thank you.","2026-01-19T08:34:32.636Z"],["3818520","LEG-1322","LEG","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Call last week with the core team. Launch ETA between mid and end of April. L&C work stream already kicked off with T&Cs review but still awaiting formal kick off by business so that we can look into the proposed market features, eligibility and verification rules, charges pass-through onto users and other key aspects.","2026-01-19T08:34:50.766Z"],["3818521","CEBF-1840","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","*Eleni Kallousia* [Jan 16, 2026 12:55 PM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C05RK5Y3HQR/p1768560939745839?thread_ts=1768560939.745839&cid=C05RK5Y3HQR] in Slack channel [#salesforce-rollout-global|https://slack.com/app_redirect?channel=C05RK5Y3HQR]\n\n{quote}Hello Team, I would like your help with the following issue.\nIn the commercial terms, we select Free Tablet, and the same is shown in the onboarding instructions. However, when the contract is sent to the provider, they only see two options: Rent Machine or Bring Your Own Machine.{quote}\n\nWhen Bring Your Own Machine is selected in the contract, the onboarding instructions automatically change as well. Because of this, cognizant does not send the tablet.\nTo avoid this issue in the future, could we add a Free Tablet option (in the contract) that is automatically applied when Free Tablet is selected in the commercial terms? This would help keep everything aligned and prevent missing tablet shipments. cc: *@user-U09B111NF2M* *@user-U01QWR5RUBV*","2026-01-19T08:35:19.420Z"],["3818523","CRC-1980","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] RiderX releasing a bug fix until 26.JAN. Mombasa pilot expected after that date.","2026-01-19T08:36:27.927Z"],["3818524","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \n\n# Please let me know which visual is for the bus stop.\n# If it’s 14×6, please provide the information for the third category (screenshot attached).\n# I need your final approval before proceeding with the printing files and motion assets. If everything looks good in the previews I’ve shared, I’ll forward them to the motion designer. However, I can’t guarantee completion today. \n\nThank you!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 10.27.40.png|width=225,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 10.27.40.png\"!","2026-01-19T08:36:31.448Z"],["3818525","CRC-2321","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] RiderX releasing a bug fix until 26.JAN. Mombasa pilot expected after that date.","2026-01-19T08:36:34.816Z"],["3818529","PFI-825998","PFI","ihor.asaulenko@bolt-outsource.eu","Ihor Asaulenko","The driver has more than 30,000 UAH in his account, so the payment must be divided.","2026-01-19T08:37:10.212Z"],["3818530","PFI-827943","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Everything on the balance is looking correct, they indeed receive the 1 campaign compensation and -4.25 commission debt. The 0.1 difference comes from rounding, but please assure the driver that our system takes the rounding differences into account and in the long run it evens out. ","2026-01-19T08:37:13.735Z"],["3818532","XVER-310","XVER","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","Sure\n\n_This comment was left via Slack._","2026-01-19T08:37:23.653Z"],["3818534","LSS-61757","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","Hey!\n\nMarketing - does the agreement reflect everything you agreed on?","2026-01-19T08:38:02.569Z"],["3818537","PFI-801722","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hi team, regarding the questions in the thread:\n\n# All invoices with updated VAT codes have been fiscalized successfully. For example, PT5525-106, PT5525-107). While our fiscalization provider has done modifications to their logic, and we’re now able to process invoices with updated VAT codes. Worth mentioning, that the recommendation to create a new account when a new Entity is created is still valid for the Tax and Legal reasons.\n# Any other changes to the Billing Identity data, for example, Address Components can be processed without any concerns, providing that, those are in format required for the fiscalization system to process. Please, see more here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7069859934/Portugal+Fiscalisation+Escalations+and+troubleshooting#Agents|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7069859934/Portugal+Fiscalisation+Escalations+and+troubleshooting#Agents|smart-link] \n\nPlease, let me know, if there any further questions to address.","2026-01-19T08:38:19.115Z"],["3818539","LSS-61207","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669], great to work with you again 😊 \n\n[~accountid:712020:daffdd55-b79f-408e-9859-186aadb103a8] , please could you confirm that you have signed and sent the reviewed LOI to the partner? ","2026-01-19T08:38:26.365Z"],["3818540","PFI-835288","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-19 at 09.32.24.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T08:38:34.477Z"],["3818541","PFI-835289","PFI","daumantas.butvila@bolt-outsource.eu","Daumantas Butvila","[^Mokėjimas (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T08:38:36.612Z"],["3818542","WD-22577","WD","lars.speekenbrink@bolt.eu","Lars Speekenbrink","thank you, both!","2026-01-19T08:39:20.454Z"],["3818544","PC-4935","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","* investigate failing refund for failed payments\n* why do we return 0 when we pput user to debt to pay for an order (paid from balance)","2026-01-19T08:39:28.142Z"],["3818545","PFI-835290","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-19 at 09.32.23.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T08:39:44.726Z"],["3818546","DRX-28147","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28083 has been resolved","2026-01-19T08:39:54.565Z"],["3818547","DRX-28139","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28083 has been resolved","2026-01-19T08:39:54.570Z"],["3818548","DRX-28138","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-28083 has been resolved","2026-01-19T08:39:54.613Z"],["3818549","PFI-835291","PFI","silvester.peter@bolt-outsource.eu","Silvester Peter","[^PaymentNotification.pdf.pdf] _(275 kB)_","2026-01-19T08:39:56.558Z"],["3818550","FX-3666","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768812039449649]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3666] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:40:51.822Z"],["3818553","FX-3666","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768812068851339]*{color}:\nEnabling vehicle marketplace delisting feature as was agreed [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08MAKTGQV9/p1768572925412569?thread_ts=1758870159.792939&amp;cid=C08MAKTGQV9].\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:41:21.404Z"],["3818554","LSS-56917","LSS","davis.baltvilks@bolt.eu","Dāvis Baltvilks","Dear [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] - do we have any updates on the status? The client is getting very impatient. ","2026-01-19T08:41:22.126Z"],["3818558","FX-3666","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768812142804039]*{color}:\nts -&gt; today at 12:00 new listing applications will create a job for a company to be checked against deactivation and if notifying comms are needed\n{quote}","2026-01-19T08:42:34.909Z"],["3818559","WFM-10008","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi [~accountid:61ea6e9084311c0069465f61] , could you please update us on the following matter?","2026-01-19T08:42:35.359Z"],["3818561","FRAUD-5658","FRAUD","aleksei.loos@bolt.eu","Aleksei Loos","[~accountid:6333d09c07a27ebeff16855f] check if we have Commece backlog item as well","2026-01-19T08:42:36.498Z"],["3818562","LSS-61661","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","[~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] would be great if you could provide a short update → or link to Slack-thread where Business has updated post-workshop. I do not think it will be much legal topics but Business has requested that Legal participates. If any questions, please discuss with PP, Roger Björkbacka. \n\nFor background regarding Sthlm Appeal: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-36339|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-36339|smart-link] \n\nAnd: [#stockholm-scooters-appeal-2024|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C07BRSEEB8Q] ","2026-01-19T08:42:41.747Z"],["3818567","FRAUD-5746","FRAUD","aleksei.loos@bolt.eu","Aleksei Loos","[~accountid:712020:0ef4b6b0-5fb9-4a66-a66b-0a7c707a4f8f] please create Commerce level backlog as well","2026-01-19T08:43:35.386Z"],["3818569","L10N-28489","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28488](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28488)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T08:43:58.715Z"],["3818570","L10N-28490","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28488](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N