ee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-19T09:29:14.983Z"],["3818901","PFI-835321","PFI","tatjana.ainson@bolt.eu","Tatjana Ainson","!Screenshot 2025-11-13 at 12.20.23.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T09:29:15.195Z"],["3818902","PFI-835321","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:6001a70e4d2179006e1b4fee] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T09:29:17.020Z"],["3818903","BEE-3658","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hello *@user-UNGCT0DHD* when using the [Pipeline automation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BF/pages/4288414244/Admin+Panel+Automation+-+Overview] to assign queues, what's the number to use when assigning queues to Fallback priority?","2026-01-19T09:29:18.223Z"],["3818904","BEE-3658","BEE",null,"Slack","[Andri Jasinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d807af94f9cf00d60213212] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C065UJULRT5/p1768812177971769?thread_ts=1768812177.971769&cid=C065UJULRT5|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C065UJULRT5/p1768812177971769?thread_ts=1768812177.971769&cid=C065UJULRT5|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T09:29:19.076Z"],["3818905","BEE-3658","BEE",null,"Slack","for additional context, when we use [Add queues automation|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-panel-automation/pipeline/start/server/720002], we assign:\n1 - for Primary\n2 - for Secondary\n? - for Fallback","2026-01-19T09:29:20.038Z"],["3818906","BEE-3658","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hi Richard, setting fallback is not yet supported for automations, do you need it?","2026-01-19T09:29:20.806Z"],["3818907","BEE-3658","BEE",null,"Slack","Yes please, we're starting to get a long list of requests for fallback assignments :pleading_face:","2026-01-19T09:29:22.188Z"],["3818908","PFI-833987","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:65f62741-f70e-4b3b-a536-a46ba26971c5] \n\nThank you for clarifying! \n\nFor future reference, could you please include the refund amounts and dates in the ticket to avoid confusion if the user has had multiple refunds. \n\nI have checked for the refund on Jan 10, 2026, 04:51:10 GMT+2 for EUR 1.84. \nIt was not issued to the users Bolt balance, but to the original payment method instead. \n\nHere is the proof of refund. \n[^Refund_Letter_P62RK6CJ5JC46JZ3_HLDPDWLK3TV7KHQ9.pdf] ","2026-01-19T09:29:23.453Z"],["3818909","HS-28983","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:dc4824f4-a6bc-41f2-af89-59d155dc0cc8],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-19T09:29:25.614Z"],["3818910","LSS-51490","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","I’ve added [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9] as participant in the meantime.\n\n[~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9] - can you please have a look at the ticket and let me know what is the status of registration of the new processing activity in Zimbabwe? ","2026-01-19T09:29:30.757Z"],["3818911","WD-22540","WD","angelina.korol@bolt.eu","Angelina Korol","Hi Iryna, thank you for clarifying the underlying process. Now it’s clear, you can close the ticket. Thank you very much for the support!","2026-01-19T09:29:31.509Z"],["3818912","LSS-60566","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:da839b78-87fc-4471-947b-3aae59c6030b] , for some reason I can’t re-assign the ticket. Can you liaise on ODPO side?","2026-01-19T09:29:34.778Z"],["3818915","LSS-59055","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","The lawyer has reverted regarding the Driver: FERON\n\nThank you\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.28.26.png|width=942,height=469,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.28.26.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.28.35.png|width=949,height=313,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.28.35.png\"!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T09:29:50.448Z"],["3818917","BEE-3658","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hi [@przemyslaw.burczyk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/604aad65ceccdd006a3af17d], should be a matter of regenerating APA module and connecting dots in automation edit UI. Can you handle it as a part of team duty if it's not too busy this week?","2026-01-19T09:30:14.733Z"],["3818919","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","[*link*|https://airflow-common.data.boltint.net/dags/dbt__all_core_models__24h_03/grid?search=dbt__all_core_models__24h_03&dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-18T02%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=rides_core&tab=logs]","2026-01-19T09:30:31.828Z"],["3818922","PFI-834615","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey [~accountid:712020:f370e2a2-c96b-43e0-a40e-ca32196cca7d] \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2640205427/881?orderTryId=3571286742|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2640205427/881?orderTryId=3571286742] was a self order. [288312200|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/288312200] is directly related to driver’s own rider account. So there was an attempt to cheat the driver bonus system. Please *no not compensate* for this, and please *do not discuss the self-order logic with the driver*. You may note that one of the trips did not align with best practices under our T&Cs, and as a result, the bonus will not be compensated.\nThank you.","2026-01-19T09:30:40.384Z"],["3818923","INT-470","INT","vivekkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vivek Kumar Singh","[~accountid:6096595fb9ac3a007193a097] can you update the header to 26CW03","2026-01-19T09:30:46.572Z"],["3818927","LSS-59052","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi,\n\nThe lawyer has reverted.\n\nThanks\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.30.48.png|width=947,height=482,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.30.48.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.30.58.png|width=953,height=456,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.30.58.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T09:31:45.575Z"],["3818929","LSS-61766","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMikk Vachtmeister has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T09:32:27.377Z"],["3818931","PAW-14979","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-19T09:33:09.123Z"],["3818932","PAW-14978","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-19T09:33:11.422Z"],["3818933","PFI-831033","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:bc1bf56a-b485-4e3e-930b-b1c071855123] \n\nI was able to get the Acquirer reference number from our payment service provider. \nPlease provide the reference 02700925344165763262741 to the customer. ","2026-01-19T09:33:32.456Z"],["3818936","LSS-59351","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi,\n\nThe lawyer ahs reverted.\n\nThanks\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.32.31.png|width=930,height=461,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.32.31.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.32.47.png|width=961,height=431,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.32.47.png\"!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T09:33:42.640Z"],["3818937","PFI-835334","PFI","emelda.eze@bolt-outsource.eu","Emelda Eze","!Receipt_032yiufacc00a.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Transaction Receipt-260119020100360357239158.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T09:33:45.054Z"],["3818938","PFI-833712","PFI","oluwasegun.olatunbosun@bolt.eu","Oluwasegun Olatunbosun","Hi team,\n\nAre there any updates regarding this request?","2026-01-19T09:34:12.077Z"],["3818939","PFI-833712","PFI","oluwasegun.olatunbosun@bolt.eu","Oluwasegun Olatunbosun","Hi team,\n\nAre there any updates regarding this request?{color:#1f1f1f}{color}","2026-01-19T09:34:13.958Z"],["3818940","PFI-835335","PFI","elina.panayotova@bolt.eu","Elina Panayotova","[^Мед Гурме (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T09:34:23.363Z"],["3818941","DSR-3241","DSR","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] - hi thanks for looping me in here. Could you please share some details about this request? The driver has submitted a SAR request through what means? When did we receive the request? \n\nI may need to create a separate legal ticket to review this matter. Thank you!","2026-01-19T09:34:24.252Z"],["3818942","PFI-835335","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-19T09:34:25.587Z"],["3818943","DAEN-1346","DAEN","bartosz.janota@bolt.eu","Bartosz Janota","Sure, let me know or our on-duty team if we can assist and help","2026-01-19T09:34:30.088Z"],["3818944","SREC-375","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","I applied the changes.\nAWS Identity Center has some cache.\nPlease from Okta, choose AWS Identity Center again and you should not see the {{OktaENGInfoSecAdmin}} anymore.\nPlease use {{OktaENGCloudSec}} role from now on and if any permissions are missing, add it to this role.\nThanks. :pepelove:","2026-01-19T09:34:38.378Z"],["3818947","DSR-3393","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] - thanks! Please update me when T2 clarifies _what_ alleged misuse was identified. I am not seeing anything on the user’s profile that suggests fraudulent behaviour.","2026-01-19T09:35:11.716Z"],["3818948","BDB-1494","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:628e5c9d8026a10068b1e457] Let’s please not spend our time on it. I did it as a preview for you and planning to delete the file anyway. ","2026-01-19T09:35:18.904Z"],["3818949","LSS-59055","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi Dolinda,\nAs previously discussed, can you please create a ticket.\nThanks\n\nElisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy\nSenior Legal Counsel | West Europe \nelisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","2026-01-19T09:35:23.293Z"],["3818952","PFI-826735","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:712020:ec8b5b06-3261-411c-9744-3a4bfb28dfb7] \n\nWe have checked with Adyen and MB Way. \nUnfortunately, we were not able to find out why the refund was rejected by the acquirer. We are also not able to issue a refund for the customer. \n\nCould you please find an alternative way to issue a 41.95 EUR refund? \n\nIf the user still has any questions about the failed refund then they could reach out to their Bank or to MB Way. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-19T09:35:45.099Z"],["3818953","LSS-59054","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi,\n\nThe lawyer has reverted - BENALI\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.35.02.png|width=934,height=408,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.35.02.png\"!\n\nThanks\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T09:35:53.303Z"],["3818956","BDB-1535","BDB","fred.vulkan@bolt.eu","Fred Vulkan","Hi [~accountid:712020:57b36b99-7144-476f-a96e-ee6e8296217c], thank you for the detailed input. Could you also provide the measurements of the pillars, so it’s easier to understand the actual size of the pillars?\n\nThank you","2026-01-19T09:37:11.195Z"],["3818957","PFI-835337","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-19T09:37:15.544Z"],["3818958","PFI-834289","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nFrom the image attached, both amounts have the same value in GBP and taking into account that the card used by the customer was a foreign card, these two amount must have been the preauthorisation amount and final capture amount converted from GBP to AED at different time period where the difference was caused by the fluctuation of the exchange rates. \n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba","2026-01-19T09:37:21.458Z"],["3818959","LSS-59762","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi,\n\nThe lawyer has reverted. Driver - KARIM DIAKITE\n\nThanks\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.36.22.png|width=935,height=410,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.36.22.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.36.27.png|width=957,height=338,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.36.27.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T09:37:25.173Z"],["3818961","LSS-61767","LSS","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","[^New_GA360_GA4_Properties_Bolt_2026.docx] _(1.06 MB)_","2026-01-19T09:37:28.632Z"],["3818965","PFI-834210","PFI","anastasiya.ivanova@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Ivanova","Hey! [~accountid:712020:3e7f9978-5a3f-4456-b715-a7f31229ae90] can you filter this looker the way you show it on the screenshot and point me out what exactly is wrong. Also from your message i don’t get what subtypes are reported wrong.","2026-01-19T09:38:09.434Z"],["3818968","PFI-832470","PFI","folashade.akinsola@bolt.eu","Folashade Dolapo Akinsola","I have updated the account to reflect the correct value as advised. However, the statement required for settlement is still displaying the incorrect value (Rosetti Pivot).\n\nKindly reissue the statements for *November 2025 (2025-11-01 to 2025-11-30)* and *December 2025 (2025-12-01 to 2025-12-31)* with the updated value (KongaPay Technologies Limited).\n\nThe customer would appreciate if this could be treated as urgent, as it will enable them to proceed with settling their outstanding balance with us as soon as possible.\n\nThank you","2026-01-19T09:38:51.907Z"],["3818970","PFI-835338","PFI","ingtita.phetsanguan@bolt-outsource.eu","Ingtita Phetsanguan","!image-20260119-093811.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-093823.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-093829.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T09:38:59.211Z"],["3818971","SREDESK-7422","SREDESK","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","Hello [~accountid:712020:c28ac319-83e4-4d10-926a-3e90f309e781] \n\nBased on the error and the fact that we don’t see any related reports in the Cloudflare logs on our side, I’d suggest trying the following before taking any further steps:\n\nGo to Preferences → Connection, then click Reset Encryption Keys.\n\nIf the issue still persists after that, please contact your Internet Service Provider to help check your home network.","2026-01-19T09:39:00.641Z"],["3818972","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","I am having a bit of trouble interpreting why it failed to even start the core and only started tests, if you guys could jump on that in parallel, that would be super helpful :pray:","2026-01-19T09:39:12.799Z"],["3818973","PFI-808691","PFI","reinis.levanovics@bolt.eu","Reinis Levanovičs","Hii [~accountid:62ea2a695111209f4fde8265] 🤗 \n\n\n[^645a7800-5f3f-40a4-b3f4-da5413e77628.pdf]\n\n\nReceived question from this FO regards that we are not compliant with VAT law in Latvia, he is stating that Bonuses and Tips should be applicable with VAT. \n\nWanted to understand, if thats true, as if it is, that means with are issuing invoices wrong or just FO is doing they accounting wrongly 🙃 \n\nHere are one [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2349533804/3?orderTryId=3024415794] example from this company( invoice attached to comment 😉 ) as i see VAT for ride are taken, but invoice isn’t even mentioning Tip information at all. \n\n","2026-01-19T09:39:14.897Z"],["3818974","RCE-357","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815549196709]*{color}:\nHey, the document on the car belongs to [Germany's countrywide set|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-documents/fleetDocuments/collection/edit/115?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FTallinn] and not to the [Cologne's document set|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-documents/fleetDocuments/collection/edit/302?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FTallinn].\n\nThe [original document|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet-documents/documentInformation/186089131?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FTallinn] is from [car application|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/car-applications/9421014?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FTallinn], that also belongs to the country wide set, was uploaded via fleet owner portal. It'd appear that FOP is not getting the correct document set details for document uploads.\n\nI checked a [few other car applications|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/car-applications/?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&amp;filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22statuses%22%3A%5B%22accepted%22%5D%2C%22start%22%3A1766095200%2C%22country%22%3A%22de%22%2C%22city%22%3A712%2C%22showTotals%22%3Afalse%7D%7D] belonging to different companies in Cologne and this appears to be working fine for them. (document belongs to right set)\n\nCould you check with FleetX why this company's car applications are defaulting to country set and not resolving correct Cologne's document set?\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:39:22.982Z"],["3818975","ID-1063","ID","oleksandr.drozd@bolt.eu","Oleksandr Drozd","Notify[~accountid:61386b11a4f86e0069546dff]when the product is released as her team will be an early adopter. ","2026-01-19T09:39:29.158Z"],["3818978","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","but this is also work in progress kind of thing","2026-01-19T09:39:39.962Z"],["3818979","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","just thinking the more eyes the quicker the answer","2026-01-19T09:39:50.210Z"],["3818980","PFI-835339","PFI","yurii.hirak@bolt-outsource.eu","Yurii Hirak","!Screenshot_20260118-104526.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T09:40:24.305Z"],["3818981","PFI-835295","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","For card payments please reach out customer payments !","2026-01-19T09:40:30.639Z"],["3818982","LSS-61768","LSS","iryna.yatsyna@bolt.eu","Iryna Yatsyna","!image.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^NETTING ACT 31-12-2025 2.docx] _(20 kB)_\n\n[^Delivery liab 2.docx] _(195 kB)_","2026-01-19T09:40:31.928Z"],["3818984","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","mb this but doubt\n\n{noformat}[2026-01-19 02:30:05,738] DatabricksRunNowWithRetry.execute cannot be called outside TaskInstance!{noformat}","2026-01-19T09:40:46.741Z"],["3818985","DAEN-1346","DAEN","pedro.paiva@bolt.eu","Pedro Paiva","I think this might be related to the repair strategy…\n\nseems like it failed on the 17th and 18th on a uniqueneess test and then the repair run picked it up from the test onwards and passes somehow which leads me to think we have a rollback strategy in place and the original build didn't go trough due to the failure","2026-01-19T09:40:53.129Z"],["3818987","DAEN-1346","DAEN","oleh.mykhash@bolt.eu","Oleh Mykhash","Hey Yuriy\nThe first job {{dbt__rides__core_24h}} failed during the original execution and then there was repair run executed","2026-01-19T09:40:56.400Z"],["3818988","SRED-1067","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-19T09:40:59.110Z"],["3818989","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","Attaching Slack reference → [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09N41TTA78/p1768502817091769|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09N41TTA78/p1768502817091769|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T09:41:02.695Z"],["3818990","DSR-3813","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T09:41:05.950Z"],["3818992","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","ahmed.elhadad@bolt.eu","Ahmed Shaban Abdelaziz Mohamed Elhadad","[~accountid:712020:ef5f49c9-39d4-4c05-820b-dbad89f985a0] as i see in slack we update it to pickup address not pickup location ","2026-01-19T09:41:11.671Z"],["3818993","DAEN-1346","DAEN","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Do we want to try {{clear task}} to reset the run?","2026-01-19T09:41:12.433Z"],["3818994","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","[@oleh.mykhash|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:7339525d-fb60-466f-8abf-16088e41a658] what I'm having trouble finding is the original execution :smile:","2026-01-19T09:41:14.563Z"],["3818995","RCE-353","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815664357779]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-353 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:41:16.134Z"],["3818996","LSS-61769","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nAire Vaigu has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T09:41:20.862Z"],["3818997","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","[@gazandi.cahyadarma|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:061a9010-0948-45f3-81ba-d6d4ba88b4bf] we could, but I wanted to double check the reason first","2026-01-19T09:41:30.880Z"],["3819001","RCE-358","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815700732449]*{color}:\nRefer: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01SWCMTKUG/p1768571882891089?thread_ts=1760448978.857599&amp;cid=C01SWCMTKUG]\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:41:54.249Z"],["3819002","DAEN-1346","DAEN","oleh.mykhash@bolt.eu","Oleh Mykhash","Original one [here|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/610872075062256/runs/592175767212830?o=3598988355446810]\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A93FNKHT9/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A93FNKHT9/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-19T09:42:03.335Z"],["3819005","PFI-835289","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Checking with accounting !","2026-01-19T09:42:16.254Z"],["3819008","RCE-355","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815745619929]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-355 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:42:37.300Z"],["3819009","LSS-60899","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5b7beb37eb18d0589b9b1c63], \n\nThere are no major legal blockers to raise against rolling this out, particularly if the aim is to drive greater impact through this program. +However, I would advise against applying the same+ suspension scale to drivers in the Prevention List as we do to those with lower ratings (<4.0).\n\nTo preserve proportionality—and limit potential friction with drivers or regulators—I recommend capping suspensions for Prevention List drivers to a maximum of 3 days. This would still allow us to send a strong signal while giving drivers a fair opportunity to adjust their performance without disproportionate penalties. \n\n\n\nUsing what you have shared before, this would look like the following :\n\n+*For drivers under 4.0*+ - there are three blocking stages:\n\n* *Block 1 (3 days):* Applied to a driver who has received more than three warnings and has never been blocked before.\n* *Block 2 (7 days):* Applied if, after Block 1, the driver again accumulates more than three warnings.\n* *Block 3 (7 days):* Applied if, after Block 2, the driver once more exceeds three warnings.\n\n\n\n+*For drivers between 4.0 and 4.0*+ - there is one blocking stage\n\n* *Block 1 (3 days):* Applied to a driver who has received more than three warnings.\n\n\n\nFrom an operational perspective, what do you think? Can we enable it in this way and what would be the expected impact? \n\nThank you !","2026-01-19T09:42:39.510Z"],["3819010","DAEN-1346","DAEN","oleh.mykhash@bolt.eu","Oleh Mykhash","and this was the failure in original execution\n\n{noformat}02:51:34  69 of 144 FAIL 48 unique_fact_rides_order_order_key ............................ [FAIL 48 in 14.16s]{noformat}","2026-01-19T09:42:43.879Z"],["3819012","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","wait but these are the tests","2026-01-19T09:43:09.253Z"],["3819013","RCE-348","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815779486899]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-348 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:43:09.988Z"],["3819017","BD-1911","BD","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Agreed with finance to not reissue the records due to the effort and impact not being proportional. ","2026-01-19T09:43:24.315Z"],["3819018","RCE-359","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815799075029]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-359 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:43:30.627Z"],["3819019","DSR-3813","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","DM sent to Jelena because Maaike is on holiday. ","2026-01-19T09:43:31.939Z"],["3819020","BD-1966","BD","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Agreed with finance to not reissue the records due to the effort and impact not being proportional.","2026-01-19T09:43:37.891Z"],["3819021","DAEN-1346","DAEN","manohar.sharma@bolt.eu","Manohar Sharma","[@oleh.mykhash|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:7339525d-fb60-466f-8abf-16088e41a658] What is the reason of the failure infra or business?","2026-01-19T09:43:45.117Z"],["3819023","PFI-834297","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T09:43:50.086Z"],["3819024","LSS-59055","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi,\n\nThank you for your response [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \n\nLast week, I created several *new* SD tickets regarding this same lawyer who reverted regarding previously handled cases. I was told by [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] that I should continue in the existing SD tickets - hence I did today.\n\nNow you are asking me to create a new ticket: How should I coherently proceed with a contradicting request from the same department? \n\nUnless I am mistaken, when you wrote to me last week, it was because I had forwarded an email instead of contacting you via SD ticket - that’s totally different from this situation.\n\nIf you wish, I can even attach all the screenshots received from [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] last week, reminding me to always continue on existing SD tickets instead of constantly creating new ones for existing cases.\n\nDolinda\n\n","2026-01-19T09:43:55.875Z"],["3819026","LSS-58216","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] . please see the fully executed contract\n\n[^MSA-2026-01-16-Solidgate_Bolt_f (979ec9b0-7470-4e91-96f3-2d7ea0f5a7ce).pdf] ","2026-01-19T09:43:56.737Z"],["3819027","PFI-834618","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","New user, many relations, expensive. Good 3ds tho. \nChecked with Mash","2026-01-19T09:44:04.548Z"],["3819028","PFI-835340","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:61f3e7cd632452006b8c120b] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T09:44:16.411Z"],["3819029","PFI-835340","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-19T09:44:17.571Z"],["3819030","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","ok, then I'm pretty sure it's some join somewhere giving duplicates","2026-01-19T09:44:28.578Z"],["3819031","LSS-61713","LSS","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Hey,\nUnfortunately, I don’t have access to Flank in RO.\nCould you please help me with the contract verification?\n\nPS: If there’s already a template we can use for contracting local services (e.g. driver training), that would be super helpful.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T09:44:28.783Z"],["3819032","PAW-14976","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sage386\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161088\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 09:44:39 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T09:44:39.502Z"],["3819033","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","I thought our tests are non-blocking though","2026-01-19T09:44:45.555Z"],["3819034","PFI-835341","PFI","paula.pakina@bolt.eu","Paula Pakina","[^Data requests EE - Bailiff SD template for multiple parthers.pdf]","2026-01-19T09:45:11.002Z"],["3819036","PFI-823014","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nSorry for the delayed response! \n\nWe have received a confirmation from PayStack the refunds have been issued to the customer. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-19T09:45:32.891Z"],["3819037","RCE-365","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768815922497459]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-365] `Request dynamic config change for flanders search category` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T09:45:41.646Z"],["3819038","BPPA-56","BPPA","yuliia.hakkinen@bolt.eu","Yuliia Häkkinen","The majority of metrics are calculated, and we still have a few pending that can stay as-is unless we need them for Quarterly. ","2026-01-19T09:45:46.110Z"],["3819040","RDXENG-4562","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:712020:23b54a2f-1913-42e1-9019-8b2c32303d27] Input placeholders are fine and updated, screen *titles* are not what design displays.\n\nPlease check [design|https://www.figma.com/design/jw4rVWHtuGnZ2RaMYIAGjH/Bolt-Send?node-id=590-27077&m=dev], current implementation of _where to_ and _where from_ should be updated.","2026-01-19T09:46:02.432Z"],["3819041","L10N-28603","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28602](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28602)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T09:46:19.375Z"],["3819043","L10N-28606","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks fo