cut the copy. [~accountid:712020:53a155f1-18aa-4e4a-8223-b8edbf9dbdcf] ","2026-01-19T09:49:47.237Z"],["3819106","BDB-1500","BDB","tracy.watiri@bolt.eu","Peace Watiri","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] I get you now\n\n# Visual for the bus stop is the 10M (W) x 12M(H) - So it does not require info on the third category. \n# All is approved. Kindly provide me with the printing file for the bus stop at least. I need to flight that.","2026-01-19T09:50:07.640Z"],["3819108","PFI-834618","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Mash said 3ds good = all good","2026-01-19T09:50:15.081Z"],["3819112","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","so [@bartosz.janota|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5de0e6d708d48c0d13acbb53] [@oleh.mykhash|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:7339525d-fb60-466f-8abf-16088e41a658] I would say one way is probably the revert, but I think adding some dedupe window function would achieve the same result of unblocking the run","2026-01-19T09:50:33.189Z"],["3819113","PFI-801722","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Hey [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] \nThank you for your feedback!\n\nSo what you are saying is:\n\n* We can correct the “old invoices”\n* We still need to open new accounts for the new details?\n\nCan I add here all the invoices that need correction?\n\nThank you!\n\n","2026-01-19T09:50:37.532Z"],["3819114","DSR-3687","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a]! I’ve created an outgoing message [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/725948753]. ","2026-01-19T09:50:44.137Z"],["3819115","RNTL-30506","RNTL","aleksei.antonov@bolt.eu","Aleksei Antonov","[~accountid:712020:53a155f1-18aa-4e4a-8223-b8edbf9dbdcf] mb we can cut down to “Benefits for safe driving“","2026-01-19T09:50:47.543Z"],["3819117","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","and considering the rest of it works and it's pretty big PR I am more leaning towards adding quick dedupe","2026-01-19T09:51:09.837Z"],["3819119","PC-4773","PC","alexey.efimov@bolt.eu","Alexey Efimov","I did this one:\n\n{quote}* If cancel call failed with {{gateway.authorization-expired}}, then {{payment-provider-processout}} service return OK.{quote}\n\nFailing capture with special code is to go.","2026-01-19T09:51:30.464Z"],["3819123","DSR-3241","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742]!\n\n* The driver submitted their case and several complaints about their account HB via email - [nicolas-puissant@laposte.net|mailto:nicolas-puissant@laposte.net]. I was not made aware of the *other* tickets (emails) the driver opened until I saw them this morning.\n* !Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.38.22 AM.png|width=943,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.38.22 AM.png\"!\nThe driver was HB on 19 December 2025 and informed about it via email ([BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/707409747])\n\n*See conversation here*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.40.32 AM.png|width=651,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.40.32 AM.png\"!\n\n\n* 2 Jan 2026: Driver sent another email about the pre-litigation notice ([BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/716218073]) - there is a second thread ([BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/715985383]) with the same documents and messages, on the same date.\n\n*See conversation here*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.42.42 AM.png|width=619,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.42.42 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.42.52 AM.png|width=590,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.42.52 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.42.56 AM.png|width=586,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.42.56 AM.png\"!\n\n\n\n* Between 19 Dec 2025 and now ([BH|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/707477207]), the driver submitted their DSAR and their pre-litigation notice (same text and same document as all previous threads)\n\n*See conversation here*\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.04 AM.png|width=586,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.04 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.10 AM.png|width=581,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.10 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.18 AM.png|width=580,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.18 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.23 AM.png|width=586,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.23 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.29 AM.png|width=584,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.29 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.34 AM.png|width=608,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.34 AM.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.39 AM.png|width=582,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.46.39 AM.png\"!\n\n\n* Other relevant information (summary from this ticket):\n** Driver suspension reason: +driver not the same as in app+, also the driver was using their phone while driving→ communicated to Driver on 19 Dec 2025\n*** Based on a rider’s report. You can see it [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ztGYbGHzHrJgBWMgc-f9RwGFmxCw5DoD?usp=drive_link] along with the picture the rider shared \n** Final block decision was maintained by POCs\n** The prepared responsive data and template answer will be sent today from Privacy/CSPC side re GDPR request (/) ","2026-01-19T09:52:29.366Z"],["3819125","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","Right. It is a big PR that would cause complications, if reverted. I am working on a duplication fix right now.","2026-01-19T09:52:32.621Z"],["3819128","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","{quote}org.apache.spark.SparkException: Job aborted due to stage failure: Task 3 in stage 34931.0 failed 4 times, most recent failure: Lost task 3.3 in stage 34931.0 (TID 34988) (172.21.39.31 executor 12): java.sql.SQLException: Your query has been cancelled due to exceeding the allowed memory limit for a single SQL query. Please try narrowing your query scope or increase the tidb_mem_quota_query limit and try again.[conn=2446691650]{quote}\n\n[@maciej.opala|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/61cc1c85ce3652006a6822c7] I can try to bump up the limit from 80% to 90%. Want to try that?","2026-01-19T09:52:57.952Z"],["3819130","LSS-60758","LSS","polina.racheeva@bolt.eu","Polina Racheeva","Hello, is there anything else I should be going with the account?","2026-01-19T09:53:19.016Z"],["3819131","WEBSD-1477","WEBSD","jevgeni.komkin@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Komkin","P.S.\nIf there is/will be a new hardware announcement blogpost, it would be nice to feature it on the page. ","2026-01-19T09:53:27.768Z"],["3819132","LSS-61104","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:289d7ba0-a9c0-4cbb-82d4-a9ed8c05aeab] !","2026-01-19T09:53:30.235Z"],["3819134","PRODSEC-718","PRODSEC","allar.lauk@bolt.eu","Allar Lauk","* Team responsible: RiderX (Micromobility)\n* Comms dispatched to [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04N7D3CGNA/p1768469056941559|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04N7D3CGNA/p1768469056941559|smart-link] \n* Timeline for fixing given, accepted by MM","2026-01-19T09:53:48.110Z"],["3819135","DAEN-1346","DAEN","bartosz.janota@bolt.eu","Bartosz Janota","Thanks, when do you think you will be able to have a fix?","2026-01-19T09:53:54.499Z"],["3819137","PC-4927","PC","alexey.efimov@bolt.eu","Alexey Efimov","Added *Acceptance Criteria* section to explain idea.","2026-01-19T09:54:01.885Z"],["3819138","PFI-833286","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Please look into the issue - the company was charged again a 0.05€ top-up for unknown reasons. ","2026-01-19T09:54:14.693Z"],["3819139","FPD-1408","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","A few bug fixes and improvements are being implemented based on feedback from the PR review. Changes will be applied and tested throughout today.","2026-01-19T09:54:14.965Z"],["3819140","UXA-2098","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","Created follow up tasks for mobile teams. ","2026-01-19T09:54:15.632Z"],["3819142","PFI-833286","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","[^Mokėjimas (38).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T09:54:30.372Z"],["3819145","DAEN-1346","DAEN","bartosz.janota@bolt.eu","Bartosz Janota","{quote}It is a big PR that would cause complications, if reverted.{quote}\n\nCan you link this PR please?","2026-01-19T09:54:39.659Z"],["3819148","PFI-834363","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment has been forwarded to the payment service provider to complete the refund. We will notify you once the refund is done.","2026-01-19T09:55:00.464Z"],["3819150","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","Ill have a PR ready in an hour max.\n\nHere is the PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15262|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15262]","2026-01-19T09:55:20.211Z"],["3819151","DRX-27415","DRX","nurbol.chorobaev@bolt.eu","Nurbol Chorobaev","As it adds extra complexity with a little benefit I'm dropping the task until Shared Prefs are migrated to `DataStore`.","2026-01-19T09:55:24.708Z"],["3819152","LSS-55901","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Hello [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] and [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] .\nWould you be able to review two more agreements with language schools? Ive copied additional details from previous agreements, so it shouldn’t take much of your time.\nWould be extremely great if you could review this on the first half of the week. 🙏\n\n[Sutartis, Bolt / KSU|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GHTHkWcDZTLTsWl3yE31d5Xi4u0xAu-nuqh73o7Gc4s/edit?tab=t.0]\n[Sutartis, Bolt / Skrivanek|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NYkuWKE2DKEI4H2iP08qFYVj6zqE4f8__VdP7tstV5w/edit?tab=t.0]\n\n*Thank you!*","2026-01-19T09:55:24.753Z"],["3819153","DRX-27418","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27415 has been resolved","2026-01-19T09:55:28.108Z"],["3819155","DRX-27418","DRX","nurbol.chorobaev@bolt.eu","Nurbol Chorobaev","As it adds extra complexity with a little benefit I'm dropping the task until Shared Prefs are migrated to `DataStore`.","2026-01-19T09:55:47.277Z"],["3819156","DRX-27415","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27418 has been resolved","2026-01-19T09:55:51.510Z"],["3819157","PFI-833286","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.55.06.png|width=524,height=154,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.55.06.png\"!\n\nLast invoice clearly states only 344.37 was needed to be paid - they did this, but another 0.05€ as debt was charged. ","2026-01-19T09:55:57.983Z"],["3819159","DBRE-8587","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* AA failing\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-14966|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-14966|smart-link] \n* CDC stuck on ti-payments\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8705|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8705|smart-link] \n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1768517045100809|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1768517045100809|smart-link] \n* Lots of noise on Vector alerts\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8701|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8701|smart-link] \n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8691|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8691|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T09:56:18.149Z"],["3819161","LSS-61770","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","[^Mise_en_demeure_Bolt_Version_Longue_Precontentieuse_IncidentZero.pdf.pdf] _(6 kB)_","2026-01-19T09:56:36.504Z"],["3819162","BEE-3637","BEE","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","[@andri.jasinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d807af94f9cf00d60213212] Hey! Let me know if any additional context/data is needed to make the change :pray::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-19T09:56:38.624Z"],["3819163","SAI-1291","SAI","henadzi.baranau@bolt.eu","Henadzi Baranau","[~accountid:608d15b352a3d400693c45a5] how {{max_output_tokens}} can help?","2026-01-19T09:56:42.969Z"],["3819165","RNTL-30506","RNTL","rose.cooperfinger@bolt.eu","Rose Cooper-Finger","[~accountid:712020:e911170f-33e2-422b-9832-ac1208b65096] Yep, we definitely can. It’ll still truncate in many “longer” languages (like DE, HU, RU, UA, etc.)… but it’s a start.","2026-01-19T09:56:48.295Z"],["3819166","PFI-834385","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nPayment: Nov 30, 2025, 12:52:17 GMT+2\nMerchant reference: iv_36C9uv10kkMFQ65io8M4x0UCFcfUS9fI\nStatus: Cancelled\nAmount: UAH 352.00\nAcquirer reference: 533410080434\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T09:56:50.490Z"],["3819169","PFI-834707","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Hanna, the user was temporarily blocked due to bad order requests, so the rider/driver matching didn’t even happen. The order rejections were due to very suspicious combinations of data. Please advise them to either not use a VPN, or instead use local wifi to order their ride in AZ.\nThanks 🙂 \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.54.48.png|width=1278,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.54.48.png\"!","2026-01-19T09:57:32.650Z"],["3819170","PFI-834387","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T09:57:32.818Z"],["3819171","LSS-61771","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nManuel Maldonado Felices has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T09:57:35.173Z"],["3819173","BEE-3637","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Hi! We've groomed this task and it will be prioritized for one of the future sprints :ok_hand::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-19T09:57:52.986Z"],["3819176","PFI-834390","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nThanks for reaching out! The Customer Payments team doesn't handle promotion or discount codes. For assistance with those, please reach out to the *Campaigns and Incentives team* (technical support). They'll be able to assist you with any questions you have.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T09:57:58.990Z"],["3819177","DAEN-1346","DAEN","silja.mardla@bolt.eu","Silja Märdla","[@yuriy.trofymenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:ea34e25e-5aed-4ec5-8c46-0238dbead6e3], there's a reason to keep severe tests like unique key on error, not warning.  I don't think we should let duplicates slip through with warnings only.","2026-01-19T09:58:29.931Z"],["3819178","LSS-61771","LSS","manuel.maldonadofelices@bolt.eu","Manuel Maldonado Felices","Attached the link of the contract [(View link)|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Tgw1-XyUSKqG1TPgJv7UcbmtRZiGU5On/edit#heading=h.lwm9y7qqy6l9] [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Tgw1-XyUSKqG1TPgJv7UcbmtRZiGU5On/edit#heading=h.lwm9y7qqy6l9|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Tgw1-XyUSKqG1TPgJv7UcbmtRZiGU5On/edit#heading=h.lwm9y7qqy6l9|smart-link] \n\n","2026-01-19T09:58:35.647Z"],["3819180","LSS-59793","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Signed - update is in the main ticket.\n\nClosing.","2026-01-19T09:58:43.981Z"],["3819184","PFI-834391","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has now been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T09:59:06.373Z"],["3819185","PAW-14934","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160933\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 09:59:10 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T09:59:10.947Z"],["3819188","PFI-834210","PFI","hira.hassan@bolt.eu","Hira Hassan","Hi [~accountid:712020:50946a54-1804-46ea-90e0-3e9829fc57af] , here is the [looker|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/23126?qid=AwY846y0HWBPQWdUVvcTGp&toggle=fil] with the filters used for the screenshot.\n\nThe amounts for the 4 subtypes highlighted on Country (blank) are the amounts I expect to see for Czech Republic Country.  \nFirstly, we should not even have a blank country dimension included on the report. \nSecondly, taking up CZ for example, for those 4 subtypes the amounts are correct with blank country dimension but not correct for the Country CZ itself.\n\nPerhaps connecting on a call might help? I can go over the discrepancies ","2026-01-19T09:59:43.441Z"],["3819189","DRX-21743","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T09:59:46.698Z"],["3819190","DRX-21744","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T09:59:54.344Z"],["3819191","LSS-58481","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Hello [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e], were you able to check Patricia’s last message? What do you think about updating the document?","2026-01-19T10:00:00.580Z"],["3819192","DRX-21747","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:00:03.727Z"],["3819193","PFI-834399","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nPayment: Dec 17, 2025, 16:42:00 GMT+2\nMerchant reference: iv_36yd0v10kkEm1gK5al6BwH3GAANMnY2k\nStatus: Cancelled\nAmount: EUR 27.47\nAcquirer reference: 535114078267\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T10:00:07.139Z"],["3819195","DRX-21748","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:00:18.148Z"],["3819197","DAEN-1346","DAEN","bartosz.janota@bolt.eu","Bartosz Janota","[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15262|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15262] - I guess we shouldn't be merging such PRs on Fridays either.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AADBWH5CG/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AADBWH5CG/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-19T10:00:26.395Z"],["3819198","DRX-21749","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:00:27.350Z"],["3819200","DRX-21751","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:00:36.648Z"],["3819202","LSS-61383","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:93a83d4d-5005-4a53-ad96-dc0c8205bf70], thank you for your patience! There is indeed a price protection clause in the agreement, thank you for pointing that out!\n\nI am answering your questions below:\n\n# Can Bolt be treated as a true principal in any Business Resale scenarios, allowing markup to be bundled into a single transport price?\n\n*  Or should Business Resale be treated as intermediation across the board, requiring separation of Bolt charges from the ride fee?\n\n*Answer:* Bolt should be treated as intermediation across the board. This means that Bolt charges (commission) should be separated from the ride fare. To bring an example:\n\n* Driver / Fleet is charging Business Customer with ride fare (e.g. 10 Eur). We can’t say that Bolt is charging Business Customer with the ride fare (exception is the UK);\n* Bolt is charging Driver / Fleet with commission for platform use (e.g. 2 Eur).\n\n\n\n# If Bolt is an intermediary, is it legally required that Bolt’s surcharge is shown as a separate line item (or section) on the customer invoice?\n\n* Is a single monthly invoice with multiple line items (ride + Bolt surcharge) acceptable from a legal perspective?\n\n*Answer:* Legally, the surcharge is ‘Bolt’s discount to the services Bolt provides to the Business Customer’. This means that the discount should be reflected as such on the invoice issued from Bolt to Business Customer. From legal pov, I see no issues with reflecting such discount on a monthly invoice issued by Bolt to business customer (with multiple line items). [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] please chime in if also fine from Tax pov.\n\nExample:\n\n* Agreement between Bolt and Business Customer says Bolt will charge no more than 10 Eur from the Business Customer per trip.\n* Driver A charges Business Customer with 12 Eur as a Ride Fare;\n* Driver B charges Business Customer with 14 Eur as a Ride Fare;\n* Business Customer is issued a monthly invoice where the first trip costs 10 Eur and the rest 2 Eur are shown as a discount on a separate line and the second trip costs 10 Eur and the rest 4 Eur are shown as a discount on a separate line.\n\n\n\n# Are there markets where Bolt must charge via the driver/fleet, or cannot invoice the business customer directly?\n\n*Answer:* I am not aware of such markets. I believe this might only happen if the wording in the agreement with Business Customer for some reason implies so, but generally should not be the case. [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] please chime in if you see I might be missing something.\n\n\n\n# Does current Bolt Business contract language support presenting the surcharge as a Bolt service fee?\n\n* If not, would changes be required to enable a cleaner invoicing structure?\n\n*Answer:* the contract you shared with me simply says that there are fixed fees and nothing else than what is reflected in the agreement will be charged from the Business Customer (LT Airport). From legal perspective this should be fine but kindly asking [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] to chime in if not okay from Tax perspective.","2026-01-19T10:00:46.746Z"],["3819203","DRX-21752","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:00:46.702Z"],["3819204","DRX-21768","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:00:58.952Z"],["3819207","LSS-58363","LSS","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Hello! Is there any update here? ","2026-01-19T10:01:14.103Z"],["3819209","DRX-21770","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:01:17.173Z"],["3819210","LSS-61770","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T10:01:21.520Z"],["3819211","DAEN-1346","DAEN","bartosz.janota@bolt.eu","Bartosz Janota","We recently introduced a rule in DAP that no infra changes on Fridays at all. Should we do the same with DBT models?","2026-01-19T10:01:21.949Z"],["3819212","LSS-61771","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T10:01:24.893Z"],["3819213","DRX-21771","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:01:35.558Z"],["3819214","L10N-28616","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28602](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28602)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:01:43.746Z"],["3819215","L10N-28618","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28602](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28602)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:01:44.604Z"],["3819216","DRX-21772","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:01:45.758Z"],["3819249","DAEN-1346","DAEN","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","We do have a release freeze after 14:00 EE on dbt repo.","2026-01-19T10:04:11.085Z"],["3819250","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","we are trying to follow that too, this is a bit of an outlier thingy afaiu [@bartosz.janota|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5de0e6d708d48c0d13acbb53]","2026-01-19T10:04:35.936Z"],["3819251","PFI-834401","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:05:13.764Z"],["3819252","PFI-835354","PFI","victoria.akinfenwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Akinfenwa","!Screenshot_20260119-103826 me 2.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:05:19.163Z"],["3819254","DRX-21776","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:05:42.677Z"],["3819255","PFI-834702","PFI","monicah.mumina@bolt-outsource.eu","Monicah Mumina","Update","2026-01-19T10:05:45.268Z"],["3819257","PFI-834618","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Ana, while the order details and user relations look suspicious, the payment was successfully authenticated via 3DS. There’s little to no chargeback or financial risk, and it’s unlikely to be fraud. Thanks for reporting still 🙂 \n","2026-01-19T10:05:56.217Z"],["3819259","DRX-21787","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:06:16.924Z"],["3819260","DRX-21786","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:06:23.666Z"],["3819262","DRX-21785","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:06:31.726Z"],["3819263","DRX-21783","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:06:44.314Z"],["3819264","DRX-21780","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:06:52.294Z"],["3819265","DRX-21779","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:06:58.381Z"],["3819268","DRX-21774","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:07:07.210Z"],["3819270","DRX-21778","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Rejected due to new Mapbox based implementation","2026-01-19T10:07:17.279Z"],["3819272","BD-1992","BD","agnes.kuus@bolt.eu","Agnes Kuus","This issue seems to happen only when cash rounding is used.\n\nIn the case of cash rounding the total amount for capture is not taken from records (which has correct values),\n\nbut is taken from user basket (which for some reason does not include tips in the total_amount)\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.01.36.png|width=397,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.01.36.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.01.12.png|width=397,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.01.12.png\"!","2026-01-19T10:07:43.288Z"],["3819276","DSR-3393","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC ([~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f]) - since the user’s request _actually_ reached us on 26 December, the acknowledgement letter should have communicated a response deadline set for 26 Jan instead of 19 Jan. Since we still don’t have clarity on CS’s claim that the user behaved fraudulently, please send the following message:\n\n* It corrects the deadline for our response\n* It reassures the user that the responsible team is looking into their question\n* It provides an answer to the user’s first question (_which personal data related to my account is being processed_)\n\n{quote}Dear [Name]*,*\n\nThank you for your patience while we review your request. We are writing to provide you with an update.\n\nFirst, we would like to clarify that the deadline for our response previously communicated to you was incorrect. As your questions concerning your personal data were received on 26 December 2025, the correct deadline for our response is 26 January 2026. Please consider this the updated and accurate deadline.\n\nOur specialist team is currently reviewing the circumstances under which your account was flagged for irregular activity. We aim to provide you with further information on this point by the deadline indicated above.\n\nIn the meantime, we invite you to consult our Privacy Notice, available at [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|smart-link] , which provides detailed information on how we process personal data, including:\n\n* The categories of personal data we process;\n* The purposes for which personal data is processed;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom personal data may be disclosed;\n* The criteria used to determine data retention periods;\n* The sources from which personal data is obtained;\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making or profiling; and\n* Details of any transfers of personal data to third countries or international organisations, including the safeguards applied.\n\nWe will follow up shortly regarding the outstanding aspects of your request. Should you be dissatisfied with this response or have any concerns relating to the processing of your personal data, we encourage you to continue engaging with us so we may address them. If you have any additional questions in the meantime, please contact our Customer Support team by replying to this message.\n\nYours sincerely,{quote}","2026-01-19T10:08:05.447Z"],["3819280","LSS-57822","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hi [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] and [~accountid:712020:9cfda827-f644-48a1-9da8-aff3fd427bf9] privacy here! 👋 \n\n\n\nAs I understand, the issue is that Fleets are changing account details without Courier’s awareness/consent. I’d suggest we pick up voluntary Courier account sharing as a separate project. Apologies in advance for any stupid questions, I’ve only been looped in now so I need a bit more context 💚 \n\n\n\nI have a few questions:\n\n# Does Bolt do any selfie verification for Fleet Couriers when they start? I am trying to understand how would selfie verification when account details are changed help us. Is there a selfie we can compare the selfie with?\n# How would this selfie verification work? Would we use Bolt’s verification system or would CS manually ask for a selfie via BH?\n# Are you essentially proposing that each time fleet would like to change Courier details, we trigger a selfie check on the concerned Courier account? Why can’t we simply notify the Courier account concerned that there is an attempted phone number change? Or would a selfie check be triggered for the account after it’s being transferred on the another individual? In that case, what’s the process? We suspend the Courier account? Can we suspend the account if it’s a Courier under fleet? What would be the desired result?\n\n\n\nThanks a lot for the answers in advance!","2026-01-19T10:08:15.598Z"],["3819285","LSS-61773","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.49.12.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.49.07.png|thumbnail!\n\n[^BOLT -ADRAR.pdf] _(1.33 MB)_","2026-01-19T10:08:55.231Z"],["3819286","LSS-61773","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nDolinda Mbensa has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T10:08:56.525Z"],["3819288","PFI-812948","PFI","joel.suldre@bolt.eu","Joel Süldre","Sorry for the delay! Approved now 🙂 ","2026-01-19T10:09:03.125Z"],["3819290","PFI-835362","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T10:09:23.358Z"],["3819292","SAI-1291","SAI","anton.taranovskyi@bolt.eu","Anton Taranovskyi","[~accountid:634684f4b380bb46a0910d44] it seems that ‘max_output_tokens’ won’t ‘encourage’ LLM to produce smaller responses - it will just return incomplete response (based on the [documentation|https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/reasoning#allocating-space-for-reasoning]), so it won’t help\n\nlooks like the only way is to adjust prompt to be produce kind of concise response, but it can cause degradation on the quality side","2026-01-19T10:10:18.418Z"],["3819294","PFI-832818","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:10:34.819Z"],["3819295","CCM-22286","CCM","ilia.moroz@bolt-outsource.eu","Ilia Moroz","[^TalentLMS import sheet (4) (1).xlsx]","2026-01-19T10:10:38.319Z"],["3819296","PFI-834762","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:10:49.309Z"],["3819297","LSS-61677","LSS","dolinda.mbensa@bolt.eu","Dolinda Mbensa","Hi,\n\nThe lawyer has reverted - KERFOUH Abderrazek\n\nThank you\n\nDolinda\n\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.09.58.png|width=944,height=506,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.09.58.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.10.06.png|width=954,height=293,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.10.06.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T10:10:59.103Z"],["3819299","DSR-3815","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T10:11:06.590Z"],["3819300","DSR-3817","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T10:11:06.662Z"],["3819301","PFI-835365","PFI","victoria.akinfenwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Akinfenwa","!Screenshot_20260119-103810 MEEE.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:11:10.551Z"],["3819303","IOTTEAM-319","IOTTEAM","andrei.porovajev@bolt.eu","Andrei Porõvajev","worked on r00 [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/IOTTEAM-245|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/IOTTEAM-245|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T10:11:33.906Z"],["3819311","PAW-14975","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17203\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 10:12:45 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T10:12:45.328Z"],["3819313","LSS-60513","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:61110fca627b56006860d802] , independent drivers are individually responsible for meeting their legal and regulatory requirements for operating in the taxi category. If the driver does not agree with the fine and believes that he has not committed any violation, he shall challenge the decision in accordance with the administrative process. If he agrees that there is a violation, he shall pay on time. How to proceed is the responsibility of the driver; we, as a platform operator, are not providing legal advice on such matters. ","2026-01-19T10:12:54.669Z"],["3819317","LSS-28796","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:c6829626-18d0-4d73-9974-74d1569b4bdf] just letting you know that I’ve assigned this to our Legal Secondee [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] as I’m soon off for vacation. If any questions re the payment, please reach out to her!","2026-01-19T10:13:09.797Z"],["3819318","PFI-835366","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-19T10:13:10.914Z"],["3819319","PFI-835366","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5b7bea33409ab057771e428c] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T10:13:12.602Z"],["3819324","EBIKE1-87","EBIKE1","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","[~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] I confirmed with the supplier, they only have one set of mold for the seat clamp right now, offering  seat clamps mainly for two big domestic customers, DIDI and Hellobike, yearly order qty is about 200K.  Because these two customers also buy the same seat clamp from  other suppliers, YCX can’t make any design change by themselves. If they modify the mold only for us, they can’t produce for these customers any more. \nAs a result, we have to open a new mold for our design. ","2026-01-19T10:14:05.755Z"],["3819325","MARTECH3-1545","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Research study:\n\n* [+https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1057/s41270-023-00234-6.pdf+|https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1057/s41270-023-00234-6.pdf]\n* [+https://web.itu.edu.tr/~elmadaga/MKT/Principles of MKT-master articles/Venkatesan 2004.pdf+|https://web.itu.edu.tr/~elmadaga/MKT/Principles%20of%20MKT-master%20articles/Venkatesan%202004.pdf]\n* [+https://digitalcollection.zhaw.ch/server/api/core/bitstreams/7f3c820c-bcd1-40e5-8d29-78a9b51affb3/content+|https://digitalcollection.zhaw.ch/server/api/core/bitstreams/7f3c820c-bcd1-40e5-8d29-78a9b51affb3/content]\n* [https://www.emerald.com/jbim/article-abstract/28/3/221/194536/Customer-flow-evaluating-the-long-term-impact-of?redirectedFrom=fulltext|https://www.emerald.com/jbim/article-abstract/28/3/221/194536/Customer-flow-evaluating-the-long-term-impact-of?redirectedFrom=fulltext|smart-link]\n* [+https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1094996898702506+|https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1094996898702506]\n* [+https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/documents/areas/fac/marketing/JSR2006(0).pdf+|https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/documents/areas/fac/marketing/JSR2006%280%29.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com]\n* [+https://www.brucehardie.com/papers/rfm_clv_2005-02-16.pdf+|https://www.brucehardie.com/papers/rfm_clv_2005-02-16.pdf]\n* [+https://support.sas.com/resources/papers/proceedings/proceedings/sugi28/120-28.pdf?+|https://support.sas.com/resources/papers/proceedings/proceedings/sugi28/120-28.pdf?]\n* [https://research.google/pubs/a-deep-probabilistic-model-for-customer-lifetime-value-prediction/|https://research.google/pubs/a-deep-probabilistic-model-for-customer-lifetime-value-prediction/|smart-link]\n\n \n\nPossible tables to use for building features:\n\n* etl_business_business_company\n* etl_business_business_daily_metrics\n* etl_business_company_churn_log\n* etl_business_company_daily_orders\n\nNotes:\n\n* {{LTV_12m_gmv}} = sum of GMV (gross merchandise value) for each company over the 12 months after an *observation cut-off date / cohort date* (first order date).\n* We use concept FLV and HLV as in the rider 1 year LTV.\n* Use a _cohort date_ per company (first order date) and sum GMV for {{cohort_date}} < date ≤ {{cohort_date + 365 days}}.\n* Exclude companies without 12 months of possible follow-up from training.","2026-01-19T10:14:09.809Z"],["3819327","MLC-3776","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","Recommended split for sprints:\n\n*0 Rides Communications*\n\n* Set up subject lines and push notifications in Braze and request localisations for all langauges\n* Set up emails in Braze and request localisations for all languages\n* Map countries that should receive only Scooter comms, only e-bike comms, and both\n* Edit existing Canvases in Braze to include new content (we already have comms live, but content should be switched once it’s ready)\n* Proofread communications with local teams/Language Specialists in Slack\n* Set live approved communications in all countries\n\n*Churn Communications*\n\n* Set up subject lines and push notifications in Braze and request localisations for all langauges\n* Set up emails in Braze and request localisations for all languages\n* Map countries that should receive only Scooter comms, only e-bike comms, and both\n* Edit existing Canvases in Braze to include new content (we already have comms live, but content should be switched once it’s ready)\n* Proofread communications with local teams/Language Specialists in Slack\n* Set live approved communications in all countries\n\nFeel free to edit this as you need ⭐ ","2026-01-19T10:14:28.147Z"],["3819329","MLC-3770","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*Split for sprints*:\n\n* Map existing communications - check which ones we are using for other countries in Braze and collect CrowdIn links for the ones we need to localise.\n* Make a plan for the roll-out (name of communication, priority, status, links)\n* Request Polish localisations for all comms (max 1000 words per ticket is recommended)\n* Set up Canvases in Braze\n* Proofread the translated communications with the Language Specialist in Slack\n* Set live approved comms after the service is launched\n\nThe last 3 items on the list can be done based on priority. Feel free to edit this however you see fit 🌸","2026-01-19T10:14:44.267Z"],["3819334","CRC-2360","CRC","kristiina.taube@bolt.eu","Kristiina Taube","Update: Response to the DNB sent out 13 January 2026. ","2026-01-19T10:15:10.114Z"],["3819338","LSS-59587","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] Any updates? Can we close the case from our side?","2026-01-19T10:15:38.619Z"],["3819340","ITI-1168","ITI","marko.toomla@bolt.eu","Marko Toomla","[Email - Germany workplace ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/WPEXG/settings/automate#/rule/019bd20b-5ec9-7f5e-a054-ec862e4d48c4]","2026-01-19T10:15:50.519Z"],["3819341","LSS-58717","LSS","ieva.fowler@bolt.eu","Ieva Fowler","Hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] thanks for confirming and appreciate you pushing this forward.\n\nI just want to clarify one point so we are aligned. Unfortunately we cannot sign the existing agreement as is through a single UK entity. Even if the partner is comfortable with that approach, we need the contract to accurately reflect the fact that services are provided to two separate UK operating companies. That is a transfer pricing and accounting requirement on our side (as confirmed by[~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] [~accountid:5c8677321f6ea3234ddaa682]). \n\nThere are two workable options from a contracting perspective:\n\n* *Option 1* is two separate agreements, one per UK entity; or\n* *Option 2* is a single tripartite agreement, but this would take time as it would require redrafting so that both Bolt Services UK Limited and Bolt Operations UK Limited are separate contracting parties with clearly allocated responsibilities and financial flows.\n\nHappy to review whichever structure you or the partner prefers, but we would need one of the above before we can proceed.\n\nOn the company details, you can obtain the registered address, VAT and related information via *legal-agent-uk* slack channel. This is operated by our AI assistant and is intended exactly for questions of this nature. Please fill in the forms as far as you can using that information and I will then review and flag anything that needs correction. \n","2026-01-19T10:16:15.188Z"],["3819342","LSS-61197","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b5de1fd-6c52-410d-afb2-757ecf5f9da4] ,\n\nIs this ticket still needed?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T10:16:44.809Z"],["3819343","PFI-835367","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-19T10:16:50.531Z"],["3819345","LSS-61773","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T10:17:02.744Z"],["3819349","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","[@leandro.morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] it does not seem necessary :) I’ve paired with Kewei, and we altered the backfill settings. The Thursday one is about to finish in 20 minutes. Then I will start the Sunday.For now all looks ok.","2026-01-19T10:17:23.758Z"],["3819350","WFM-10024","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","req [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571770|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571770]\n\nassembled updated as well","2026-01-19T10:17:26.681Z"],["3819351","WFM-10024","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","ops roles requested, awaiting approval. the CS roles removed as no longer needed","2026-01-19T10:17:47.940Z"],["3819352","PFI-835373","PFI","otis.wella@bolt-outsource.eu","Otis Wella","!{8A5559EA-A784-48BC-9AA0-8EC242942A37}-20260119-101727.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:17:48.328Z"],["3819353","PFI-833120","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:17:49.552Z"],["3819354","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","OK. Thanks for fixing that! :bow:","2026-01-19T10:17:55.770Z"],["3819358","PFI-833139","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:18:26.089Z"],["3819359","WFM-10014","WFM","fatimatou.amadou@bolt.eu","Fatimatou Amadou","Hi [~accountid:712020:ddf1e045-1184-4210-9e73-da3ce949a13b] Sorry for the delayed response. I've checked and everything is fine with the agents.\n\nThank you\n\n","2026-01-19T10:18:27.861Z"],["3819360","MLC-3550","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","*Recommended split for sprints*:\n\n* Clone Canvases from other countries for priority 1 comms, edit targeting\n* Set up priority 1 communications, proofread them with the local team and set live - start with this one so we’re ready for launch\n* Clone Canvases from other countries for priority 2 comms, edit targeting\n* Set up priority 2 communications, proofread them with the local team and set live\n* Clone Canvases from other countries for priority 3 comms, edit targeting\n* Set up priority 3 communications, proofread them with the local team and set live","2026-01-19T10:18:32.457Z"],["3819361","DBRE-8705","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","{quote}The Thursday one is about to finish in 20 minutes{quote}\n\nSurprised it takes that long, it was less than 2h of data (and has an index)","2026-01-19T10:18:38.373Z"],["3819362","PFI-835374","PFI","aida.ghazaryan@bolt-outsource.eu","Aida Ghazaryan","!Screenshot_20260118_085602_PayPal.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:18:54.217Z"],["3819363","PFI-801722","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","{quote}We can correct the “old invoices”{quote}\n\nYes, that’s correct. The issue we had, specifically, in PT was due to a technical limitations by our fiscalization provider and it is now resolved. All affected invoices and credit notes should already be refiscalized, but let’s run one final check to verify if there’re still any that need attention. \n\n{quote}We still need to open new accounts for the new details?{quote}\n\nYes; A new VAT or registration code essentially means a new legal Entity. For audit purposes, we should open a new account to keep the new Entity separate from the old one. Technically, we now can credit and reissue on the old account, but, it’s better to avoid it.","2026-01-19T10:19:07.437Z"],["3819366","LSS-61668","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] !\n\nCould you kindly take a look at this? The deadline is today. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T10:19:51.124Z"],["3819367","PFI-833102","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:20:02.835Z"],["3819369","PFI-835375","PFI","evelyn.obi@bolt-outsource.eu","Evelyn Obi","!image-20260119-101952.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:20:06.829Z"],["3819370","DMC-735","DMC","pawel.dabrowski@bolt.eu","Paweł Dąbrowski","Cognizant team also shared last week as per below that they’d see important for the city / vendor information nect to provider (store) to be shared upon menu candidate & most importantly publishing section to ensure correct menu is published live to the relevant merchants:\n\n”“_Cases with restaurant chains where menus vary by city. Seeing the city or vendor at the publishing step will help identify which providers need to be updated, so we don't have to manually search for information about which provider belongs to which city.”_\n\nfyi: [~accountid:712020:a8e993c7-e089-4c7f-96d3-8d2e1ee4caa6] ","2026-01-19T10:20:09.380Z"],["3819372","PFI-833138","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:20:15.158Z"],["3819373","WD-22601","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:63fca2bdf00d095406f1fda7] roles updated","2026-01-19T10:20:18.520Z"],["3819375","PFI-834508","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:20:27.446Z"],["3819376","LSS-60071","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Thank you [~accountid:60b5deeb5fa6f1006f994b75] both banks got back with the respective documents and these are already saved in their folders in Drive ([here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1N0uxCJy4m_-_BbZWtXWkhtiM9XdcEtE-?usp=drive_link]). ","2026-01-19T10:20:46.455Z"],["3819377","PFI-832825","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:20:56.379Z"],["3819378","PFI-835376","PFI","augustina.oweh@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustina Oweh","!Payment 2.0.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:21:05.349Z"],["3819380","PFI-834648","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T10:21:09.430Z"],["3819383","RNTL-30506","RNTL","aleksei.antonov@bolt.eu","Aleksei Antonov","[~accountid:61027986ec92ab00707f6978] ","2026-01-19T10:21:59.381Z"],["3819384","PFI-835378","PFI","otis.wella@bolt-outsource.eu","Otis Wella","!{3BC6A873-8BE4-4786-A6B4-43E13D4A484B}-20260119-102110.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:22:05.572Z"],["3819387","WFM-10032","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601707|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601707]","2026-01-19T10:22:34.612Z"],["3819389","WFM-10032","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","role requested, awaiting approval","2026-01-19T10:22:44.035Z"],["3819391","HS-29091","HS","duniya.zankyang@bolt.eu","Zankyang Zingy Duniya","[^Final EVL - Bolt (1-15-26).docx]","2026-01-19T10:23:05.393Z"],["3819395","LSS-61775","LSS","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[^Malta International Airport - Extra Charge Form 2 BOLT FOOD SCHENGEN WALLS (2).pdf] _(245 kB)_","2026-01-19T10:23:54.777Z"],["3819397","SUPX-2326","SUPX",null,"Slack","When you have time, what is the ETA on the migration completion of the tool?  I will just note to followup no sooner.","2026-01-19T10:24:08.644Z"],["3819403","HS-29008","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi [~accountid:639703ee61aba8a6a32c5a30] \n\nWe would appreciate if you could share the 2024 report so we know what exactly is expected.\n\nThanks!\nKadri","2026-01-19T10:25:05.364Z"],["3819405","PFI-835366","PFI","sherifa.sumani@bolt.eu","Sherifa Sumani","Can you assist with a letter from the Bank to indicate a change in Banking Details for Ghana, as there has been a recent change in Banking details?","2026-01-19T10:25:26.842Z"],["3819406","WFM-10025","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601708|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601708]","2026-01-19T10:26:02.961Z"],["3819408","WFM-10025","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","roles requested, awaiting approval","2026-01-19T10:26:13.970Z"],["3819410","PFI-834790","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-19T10:26:27.032Z"],["3819411","PFI-835085","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-19T10:26:29.667Z"],["3819412","LSS-61200","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] Any updates? Can we close the ticket from our side, because the deadline to respond has already passed?","2026-01-19T10:26:32.097Z"],["3819413","PFI-834708","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a tem