ade.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-19T10:26:51.586Z"],["3819424","PFI-835322","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-19T10:26:53.361Z"],["3819425","PFI-834550","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-19T10:26:55.239Z"],["3819427","BD-1995","BD",null,"Vishal Arora","*@user-U01707QH9BP* the endpoint we are using right now to resolve provider_company by provider_id is this one: [/internal/business/getProviderInfo|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/delivery/commerce/delivery_invoicing/main/handler/Bootstrap.ts#L743] in delivery-invoicing service.\nInternally it goes to {{deliveryProviderApi.invoicingGetProviderFieldsById}} to find out if provider has provider_company_id. From quick checking of this API - there is another one {{deliveryProviderApi.invoicingGetProviderCompanyData}}, but it supports only search by ID, not by custom fields, but I guess this can be added on delivery-provider side?\n\nAs my knowledge in delivery domain is very small - can you please help with figuring out the valid way to solve it?","2026-01-19T10:27:09.596Z"],["3819428","BD-1995","BD",null,"Slack","[Vishal Arora|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f0d61fc5ee2c300236d55b3] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C097HPXNW1X/p1768814412790179?thread_ts=1768489403.400679&cid=C097HPXNW1X|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C097HPXNW1X/p1768814412790179?thread_ts=1768489403.400679&cid=C097HPXNW1X|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T10:27:10.561Z"],["3819429","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] \nOOH print file is here: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/uu07y812a9cdts2wesjhp/ALRBN7bPBMrJNpq8FosVoa0?rlkey=rf1c1dhzz9s27cn4l4ziktvfb&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/uu07y812a9cdts2wesjhp/ALRBN7bPBMrJNpq8FosVoa0?rlkey=rf1c1dhzz9s27cn4l4ziktvfb&dl=0|smart-link] \nThank you!","2026-01-19T10:27:23.816Z"],["3819432","FRAUD-5737","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","*Testing*\n\nRechecked with the help of this query:\n\n{noformat}SELECT\n    id, created, concat('https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/rides_payment_capture_authorized_amount/', cast(id as STRING)) AS link,\n    meta.business_company_id,\n    meta.city_id,\n    get_json_object(input, '$.data.vertical.order.city_id') AS order_city_id\nFROM\n    sel_fraud_checks_pii_spark.rides_payment_capture_authorized_amount\nWHERE\n    created_date >= date '2026-01-15'\n    AND meta.business_company_id IS NOT NULL\n    AND meta.city_id != get_json_object(input, '$.data.vertical.order.city_id')\nLIMIT 500;{noformat}\n\nLooks like it is fixed","2026-01-19T10:27:53.233Z"],["3819434","HS-29039","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi again Kevin, both letters should be with you now. Let me know if you need any other assistance. ","2026-01-19T10:28:03.774Z"],["3819437","RDXENG-1941","RDXENG","daniel.mititelu@bolt.eu","Daniel Mititelu","I updated to counter everywhere except schedule rides.","2026-01-19T10:28:37.454Z"],["3819438","BDB-1500","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] please add specs for motion assets to the media plan next time","2026-01-19T10:28:55.102Z"],["3819439","L10N-28627","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28619](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28619)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:29:02.382Z"],["3819440","L10N-28626","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28619](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28619)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:29:02.526Z"],["3819441","L10N-28628","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- A