s?","2026-01-19T10:29:24.112Z"],["3819454","CSENP-229","CSENP","warwie.sanjuan@bolt.eu","Warwie San Juan","Since this is linked to the creation of the forecast sheets review for CS EXP and WFM, I consider this complete.","2026-01-19T10:29:28.572Z"],["3819455","L10N-28643","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28619](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28619)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:29:28.635Z"],["3819458","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Yes, totally makes sense. But the settings were too offensive previously so now we picked the opposite approach - slowly but steadily :)","2026-01-19T10:29:49.576Z"],["3819462","RNTL-30518","RNTL","aleksei.antonov@bolt.eu","Aleksei Antonov","[~accountid:61027986ec92ab00707f6978] info block title is limited to 2 lines, you can just use info block item as you did in penalty details card\n\n!1000010138.png|width=223,alt=\"1000010138.png\"!","2026-01-19T10:30:35.311Z"],["3819464","CRC-2362","CRC","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","Technical scoping for Billing in progress. Work is planned for W4-W5. Initial scoping:[https://docs.google.com/document/d/100IIK0AamAyu4NsdPsGh_yBaSECB3cDGYMrMa_pRpbs/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/100IIK0AamAyu4NsdPsGh_yBaSECB3cDGYMrMa_pRpbs/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] \n\n cc: [~accountid:712020:36181da6-7f24-4254-aae6-dd8f636be99b] \n\n[~accountid:712020:8394b01a-e7b1-40fd-92bc-a16f9c1760b2] Is there an extra Payments scope? Balance top-up seems to be disabled, so we are good on that front. ","2026-01-19T10:30:42.718Z"],["3819465","DBRE-8706","DBRE","andres.kepler@bolt.eu","Andres Kepler","if I expand filter to 30day then its visible\n\n[https://monitor.boltint.net/d/b61e580e-4bf2-4b21-b6e8-c8ab401aa605/pipeline-logs?orgId=1&from=now-30d&to=now|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/b61e580e-4bf2-4b21-b6e8-c8ab401aa605/pipeline-logs?orgId=1&from=now-30d&to=now]","2026-01-19T10:30:43.752Z"],["3819467","PFI-835384","PFI","emelda.eze@bolt-outsource.eu","Emelda Eze","!49BC5EA9-0F98-4B48-844F-4353A5CE7738.png|thumbnail!\n\n!9003B9F8-0181-4692-8E1A-009544FC7021.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:30:54.086Z"],["3819469","BDB-1535","BDB","karolis.simkus@bolt.eu","Karolis Šimkus","[~accountid:621fa8978a4bb60068f1fe09] It’s a little bit difficult to say, since these pillars are in the old part of the airport and they are all a bit different.\n\nAnyway, I’ll reach out to our ads manufacturing company who took measurements and will try to get them asap.","2026-01-19T10:31:11.135Z"],["3819470","LSS-61774","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T10:31:13.370Z"],["3819471","LSS-61775","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T10:31:13.373Z"],["3819473","DSR-3815","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]  Could I double check this rider request with you. User is requesting *licensing authority for the driver*, is this part of the request privacy related? I assume they want to know that the driver is licensed by TFL because it’s a London rider but do we need to provide anything else? \n I have prepared the call transcripts and BH chat. \n","2026-01-19T10:31:51.914Z"],["3819476","PFI-835386","PFI","erere.eriri@bolt-outsource.eu","Erere Eriri","!image-20260119-103148.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:32:20.581Z"],["3819480","DPLC-701","DPLC","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","I suppose we need additional CI to ensure the bundle name and path have the same value.","2026-01-19T10:32:55.759Z"],["3819481","DPLC-701","DPLC",null,"Slack","[Gazandi Cahyadarma|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:061a9010-0948-45f3-81ba-d6d4ba88b4bf] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GAD2D4CRF/p1768818531648289?thread_ts=1768555722.357679&cid=GAD2D4CRF|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GAD2D4CRF/p1768818531648289?thread_ts=1768555722.357679&cid=GAD2D4CRF|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T10:32:56.821Z"],["3819485","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Ok, finished, the second one.","2026-01-19T10:34:38.633Z"],["3819489","DAEN-1346","DAEN","bartosz.janota@bolt.eu","Bartosz Janota","I guess it was 11 am Friday, but thos doesn't matter now. Let's have it fixed and we can discuss the process later.","2026-01-19T10:35:29.635Z"],["3819490","CCM-22286","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hi Ilia 👋 \n\nLiliia has been enrolled to all of the listed courses.\n\nWishing you a lovely rest of the day! 🌷 \n\nIrena","2026-01-19T10:35:41.343Z"],["3819492","DO-5783","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Access was granted for viewing SQL only which can be copy pasted to databricks workspace for further drill down.","2026-01-19T10:36:39.673Z"],["3819495","SUPX-2326","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Migration will happen most likely this week, but I can’t give any eta when we can expose this sort of data as we can’t give access to the tool itself :slightly_smiling_face: Most likely we need to find some alternative method like reporting it to mixpanel and then replicating that data to data warehouse so we can then “use” this data on Looker.\n\ncc [@michal.rapinczuk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:05337a38-da5a-4860-91ed-01ab7b7b6cca] (perhaps this is something you have already taken a look at while exploring our mixpanel/data capabilities)","2026-01-19T10:36:53.930Z"],["3819498","RS-1958","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:b397f1e8-d486-425c-bf2c-ce0f62f620df],\n\nWe are working on this document here [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EWZPfETaaGA4IC4Jketll1fAccNwPUBAXDrUVGjqX9c/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EWZPfETaaGA4IC4Jketll1fAccNwPUBAXDrUVGjqX9c/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] \n\nWe will be sure to complete by early Feb. \n\nThank you!\n\nKadi ","2026-01-19T10:37:14.084Z"],["3819501","PFI-834958","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Johanna-Maria, at this stage, this is not something Fraud can conclusively prove, as we don’t have the investigative authority or tooling to act on this information alone. The source of these receipts could easily be external to Bolt, which means we’re unable to identify a definitive origin or culprit. While the users in question may have attempted to use this method, it does not factually prove that they are the creators of the receipts themselves.\n\nThe most effective course of action we can recommend is to remain vigilant and block users who display similar behavioural patterns. It’s also advisable to leave internal profile comments and ensure our agents are aware of this tactic. Once it becomes clear that this approach is ineffective, the scheme typically diminishes on its own.\n\nUnfortunately, we’re unable to take further action here, as this activity occurs outside of Bolt systems (e.g. images submitted to CS), which limits our ability to prevent it directly.","2026-01-19T10:37:33.720Z"],["3819502","DO-5801","DO","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","[~accountid:5bae2f6db6a5385ea2748d30] we don’t manage permissions for looker. Can you please raise this with IT? ","2026-01-19T10:37:46.597Z"],["3819503","LSS-61777","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","[^Tjenesteavtale.pdf] _(448 kB)_","2026-01-19T10:37:48.139Z"],["3819504","PFI-835389","PFI","john.akpan@bolt-outsource.eu","John Akpan","!Screenshot_ payment for dbt.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:37:58.516Z"],["3819505","CSDT-971","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Need to\n\n# Add escalated bool to mart_support_case_metrics\n# Re-generate mart_support_case_metrics\n# Backfill mart\n# Add escalated condition for count_support_cases_without_tier_transfer_post_escalation_utc in mart_support_case_metrics semantic\n# Re-generate other marts\n# Backfill marts\n# Looker sync - if needed? ","2026-01-19T10:38:02.633Z"],["3819507","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] previews are here\nAlso, I’ll need information regarding cutlines for coasters. I can define the corner radius myself and if the printing agency would like to use their own, I can adjust that. \nThank you!","2026-01-19T10:38:06.002Z"],["3819508","LSS-61479","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] Any updates?","2026-01-19T10:38:07.114Z"],["3819510","WD-22595","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:63ec99ebaf665dfde890c2e3], Bolt Accountant access added to Kairi Martin","2026-01-19T10:38:24.011Z"],["3819511","HS-29077","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:60bf5e79b1f93b0069640a64],\n\nPlease print, sign and stamp [this document|https://bolt.box.com/s/8rbbtrcaf4kgk73ta98pbbli7hmrcidz] for Ayshan. If you want any support with this, please let me know. \n\nKind regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-19T10:39:07.711Z"],["3819512","RS-1952","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","From Slack thread,[~accountid:712020:da2330ef-b0ca-426f-adf2-a1f78a2b33e2] : The client was informed and responded that sent us a request for an EcoVadis evaluation to be made. Client is now aware of our timeline so they will need to wait for Q2.\n\nWith the above, I am closing the ticket.\n\nThanks! \n\nKadi ","2026-01-19T10:39:34.526Z"],["3819515","RS-1952","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","BB client has been informed that Bolt will be pursuing Ecovadis assessment in Q2 2026. ","2026-01-19T10:40:00.240Z"],["3819518","PFI-808691","PFI","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","Hi [~accountid:712020:e04282ea-9d2c-4f81-8507-cea4db4cd1b9], there are remarks for internal information:  \n\n* VAT applies on goods/services provided.  Tips are given +voluntarily+ by riders, it is not part of the consideration of the rides and falls out of scope of VAT. \n* Billing to address your comment below why tip is not included in the ride invoice:\n\n{quote}but invoice isn’t even mentioning Tip information at all{quote}\n\n* AFAIK, billing setup on bonus is already VAT inclusive (if applicable).  That said, for Bonus = 50 presented to partner, it means 41.3 + 8.7 VAT.  Since fleet bonus is deducted from commission in Latvia, the commission invoice shows the net amount and VAT.  \n\n","2026-01-19T10:40:29.621Z"],["3819519","LSS-61421","LSS","bayram.khalilzade@bolt.eu","Bayram Khalilzade","If I’m not mistaken, we don’t have it. Please correct me if I’m wrong [~accountid:712020:4270191e-b006-439e-a800-5b8e06cf2c60] ","2026-01-19T10:40:53.355Z"],["3819521","DBRE-8515","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","* test-poc-proxysql-1.testdb: [https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139730|https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139730]\n* test-poc-proxysql-2.testdb: [https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139728|https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139728]\n* test-poc-proxysql-3.testdb: [https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139726|https://r.db.boltint.net/project/dbre/execution/show/139726]","2026-01-19T10:41:05.495Z"],["3819522","DSR-3819","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T10:41:05.907Z"],["3819523","PRODSEC-684","PRODSEC","amefon.affia@bolt.eu","Abasi-amefon Obot Affia-Jomants","Completed SOW for ember app. [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-61424|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-61424|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T10:41:09.892Z"],["3819525","RNTL-30378","RNTL","giorgi.basiashvili@bolt.eu","Giorgi Basiashvili","Hardcoded icon urls are located in {{MarkerStyleConfigRepository.kt}}","2026-01-19T10:41:25.277Z"],["3819528","LSS-59055","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b] ,\n\nthat’s ok to continue under the previous tickets, just that’s not useful to forward via email.\n\nthank you.\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-19T10:41:41.765Z"],["3819531","PFI-810251","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hi, please, try to download report again, it’s now fixed in the Admin.","2026-01-19T10:42:08.161Z"],["3819533","BDB-1513","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Previews look good!\n\nTo clarify printing files will include the 10 variations of the same design with the unique promo codes?\n\nAny questions let me know. ","2026-01-19T10:42:12.642Z"],["3819536","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] yes, all good. \nPlease let me know about cutlines for the coasters, thank you! ","2026-01-19T10:43:31.958Z"],["3819539","RCE-365","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768819408907449]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-365 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T10:43:41.567Z"],["3819541","L10N-28658","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28656](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28656)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:44:01.185Z"],["3819542","BD-1999","BD",null,"Vishal Arora","*@user-U03T2CSM7FD* yes, but right now we do a simple exclusion (by only considering records) therefore debt is introduced automatically by design. \n\nSo we need to make the behaviour such that correct amount is refunded if rounding results in us charging more so that debt is not induced. \n\nFor case where rounding results in charging lower amount we can do the same so we don't over refund. ","2026-01-19T10:44:06.170Z"],["3819543","BD-1999","BD",null,"Slack","[Vishal Arora|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f0d61fc5ee2c300236d55b3] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02BZ67SKFG/p1768484404727649?thread_ts=1768476520.554059&cid=C02BZ67SKFG|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02BZ67SKFG/p1768484404727649?thread_ts=1768476520.554059&cid=C02BZ67SKFG|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T10:44:07.300Z"],["3819544","L10N-28663","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28656](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28656)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:44:08.035Z"],["3819547","L10N-28668","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication