collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:44:27.316Z"],["3819560","L10N-28692","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28656](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28656)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:44:29.301Z"],["3819562","BD-1999","BD",null,"Vishal Arora","To refine ","2026-01-19T10:44:31.740Z"],["3819565","RCE-358","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768819493379519]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-358 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T10:45:05.589Z"],["3819570","PFI-835393","PFI","success.igbinosa@bolt-outsource.eu","Success Igbinosa","!1k.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!7h.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:45:49.177Z"],["3819573","PFI-835394","PFI","anna.zhou@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Zhou","!Screenshot_20260119-120829_PUMB (1).jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:46:43.538Z"],["3819575","PFI-835399","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-19T10:47:36.516Z"],["3819576","WD-20519","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","I have found solution to have default Cost Center “Talent (HQ)” for Activity “Learning and Development” via related worktags. This set up would not only affect expense items, but also other transactions where this Activity will be used. This is not critical validation, but just having field automatically populated. [~accountid:63be776494d18cbf6772b360] can you please confirm so that we can start configuring whole flow? ","2026-01-19T10:47:41.732Z"],["3819578","LSS-61694","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, team!\n\nTo be on the same page: you need to sign the attached statement by [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] on behalf of Bolt Operations OU for Poland (no PoA required as the ticket description wrongly suggests it 😉).\n\n{color:#36b37e}*signing process:*{color}\n\n* wet ink - [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] on behalf of Bolt Operations OU (for Poland)\n* the document to be signed: [^POLAND_Bolt Operations OU_OŚWIADCZENIE CBAM 09.02.20-20260116092056.pdf] \n* Please fill in the gaps in the document as follows:\n\n!image-20260119-104228.png|width=630,alt=\"image-20260119-104228.png\"!\n\n*whereas*: \n\n* “miejscowość, data” means “city, date” → Warszawa/Warsaw and the current date of signing\n* “pieczątka firmy; imię, nazwisko i stanowisko oświadczającego” means “company’s stamp (TO BE PROVIDED IF WE HAVE IT. IF NOT, PLEASE FILL “BOLT OPERATIONS OU” DETAILS), the representative’s name, surname and position.\n\n📮 once the statement is signed, please send the original version to the Bolt Warsaw Office at Prosta 67 Street, 00-838 Warsaw, Poland (PL: ul. Prosta 67, 00-838 Warszawa, Polska) - to the attention of [~accountid:5f9aac6499b42e0069a4f456] \n\nThank you and best,\n\nJola 😊 ","2026-01-19T10:48:09.513Z"],["3819583","RS-1949","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","[~accountid:712020:81ed6d45-d7b2-45d4-89cd-030f00488538] [~accountid:712020:9771c4dd-8605-4d8a-98e5-f550f6c78ee7] \n\nMy proposed responses are YES to all of them. Do you agree?:\n\n*1.14.1*: Do you have measures in place that enable you to comply with the minimum standards of the BBC Sustainable Supply Chain Code of Conduct in your business and supply chain and are you willing to work with us to ensure these are upheld during the delivery of the products and/or services?\n\n*YES*\n\n *_1.14.2_*_: If you have answered no to the above question, please provide an explanation as to why you cannot meet the minimum standards._\n\n_In your response, you must clearly state which specific requirement(s) you cannot meet and the relevant reasons why._\n\n*1.14.3* Do you have measures in place that enable you to meet the requirements of the attached BBC Ethical Trading Policy *(attached)* in your business and supply chain and are you willing to work with us to ensure the ethical supply of products and services?\n\n*YES*\n\n*_1.14.4_* _If you have answered no to the above question, please provide an explanation as to why you cannot meet the requirements._\n\n*1.14.5* *** Do you have measures in place that enable you to support the BBC’s Environmental Sustainability Policy Statement:\n\n*YES*\n\n*_1.14.6_*_: If you have answered No to the above question, please provide an explanation as to why you cannot support the requirements._\n\n*ADDITIONAL SUSTAINABILITY QUESTIONS (COMPULSORY BUT ONLY FOR INFORMATION PURPOSES)*\n\n*1.14.8* As part of supporting the BBC's net zero strategy, the BBC encourages all suppliers to have science based targets or equivalent which limit global warming to 1.5 degrees aligned to climate science. Please confirm whether you currently have targets in place and provide details of how they were calculated and how they will be delivered.\n\nIf you do not have targets in place please provide details of your future ambitions in this space.\n\n*YES, Bolt has SBTi validated short-term and long-term emission reduction targets. See more here* [https://bolt.eu/en/blog/the-sbti-validates-bolts-net-zero-targets/|https://bolt.eu/en/blog/the-sbti-validates-bolts-net-zero-targets/|smart-link] *.* \n\n*1.14.9 ** As part of supporting the BBC's net zero strategy, would you be able to provide your environmental data to the Carbon Disclosure Project on an annual basis?\n\n*_1.14.10_* _If you have answered 'no' to the above question please provide an explanation as to why._","2026-01-19T10:49:00.148Z"],["3819585","LSS-61421","LSS","bayram.khalilzade@bolt.eu","Bayram Khalilzade","[~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] Can we sign the agreement?","2026-01-19T10:49:10.846Z"],["3819587","LSS-61780","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nKrystian Miciukiewicz has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T10:49:45.867Z"],["3819589","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] ,\n\nI added you as (temporary) participant in this ticket. As it deals with a blind user, I believe it is somewhat sensible.\n\nAfter receiving complete context from Christos, Alexia and others, as well as very useful information from Lisette Suik, I have prepared a response to the blind customer. I would really appreciate if you could take a look with the lenses of risk prevention. I want to give a clear and honest response to the client, but without in being “auto-incriminating” or without promising what we can not accomplish. [Here |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eeGCiihfCZbBoQ6rYJxNU1ga35gWwljp3Jua7zqwEds/edit?usp=sharing]is the document. \n\nPlease let me know if you want us to comment in a call.\n\nThank you 🙏 !\n\nAngela  ","2026-01-19T10:49:54.179Z"],["3819590","PFI-835412","PFI","erere.eriri@bolt-outsource.eu","Erere Eriri","!image-20260119-104902.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:50:05.983Z"],["3819591","CSDA-304","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review ad-hoc requests once a day. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-19T10:50:18.305Z"],["3819597","DSR-3205","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], thank you for your help! I’ve sent the data prepared with the answer.","2026-01-19T10:50:43.856Z"],["3819598","PFI-830905","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Can you please confirm that the information that’s required to be on these invoices is: \nName: *NOVTC19*\n\nReg code: 99187132800019\n\nVAT code: FR92991871328\n\nAddress: 3 impasse de joinville 75019 Paris","2026-01-19T10:50:44.310Z"],["3819603","PFI-835415","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^103_P260114C00001047_1330 260114EXTNTZTZXXX0114133108 (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T10:51:47.324Z"],["3819604","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","It’s all done.","2026-01-19T10:51:52.031Z"],["3819605","CRC-2196","CRC","ekaterina.matson@bolt.eu","Ekaterina Matson","[update] A/B test in Romania with couriers rescheduled to February 3rd due to unfinished interface changes. Live payment from driver successfully tested, next step: technical test in Morocco and South Africa.","2026-01-19T10:51:56.636Z"],["3819606","BDB-1513","BDB","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","[^95x95mm Bar Coaster Dieline.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T10:51:59.208Z"],["3819607","CRC-2301","CRC","dmitri.mihhailov@bolt.eu","Dmitri Mihhailov","[linked update from CRC-2196]: 2026-01-19 Ekaterina Kornilitsina:\nA/B test in Romania with couriers rescheduled to February 3rd due to unfinished interface changes. Live payment from driver successfully tested, next step: technical test in Morocco and South Africa.","2026-01-19T10:52:01.265Z"],["3819613","WD-22577","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi [~accountid:5e620d95ed743a0afe39736b] please can you share the contact info that you would like to change","2026-01-19T10:52:45.590Z"],["3819614","LSS-61606","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","sent, thank you ","2026-01-19T10:52:45.930Z"],["3819615","LSS-61504","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] \nBased on the information reviewed, this appears to involve unauthorised changes to core account identifiers (email and phone number), which the driver clearly denies making.\n\nAt this stage, it’s still unclear how the changes were made, and this needs to be clarified via logs. I don’t fully understand why this remained at T1 CS initially and wasn’t escalated to CSPC sooner, given the nature of the changes and the driver’s denial.","2026-01-19T10:53:10.836Z"],["3819621","PFI-819935","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","[~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] Hi! Our accounting partner has already booked the correct fee amount.\nSo at this stage, we need the data in local accounting, WD, and Admin to be fully aligned.\n\n[~accountid:712020:1ac9e18d-07ba-4c40-99d7-7b2cc972055e] [~accountid:6001a70e4d2179006e1b4fee] [~accountid:712020:b1a3aa39-56a5-492b-9453-5372da990388] Could we please align on the next steps? As mentioned earlier by Joel, if I upload an adjustment ({{refund_commission}}), you will need to exclude it from your P&L model. My understanding is that this should ideally be done within the same reporting period (week). Could you please let me know when it would be convenient for you to proceed with this on your side?\n\nIn addition, the thing is, we’ve just identified a new issue with this partner - please have a look at order [*ZQD2X*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/282363405?cityId=498&showUserTz=false]. I’d prefer to fix both cases (YVOGS and ZQD2X) in one go. ","2026-01-19T10:53:48.688Z"],["3819623","WEB-9813","WEB","vishal.kapoor@bolt.eu","Vishal Kapoor","Hi [~accountid:5f23e43bef11df0025a6a7a0] \nPlease help me understand which project is the old project referred in this ticket?\n{color:#0747a6}_Bolt Plus will be launched in CA. Let’s please copy the page from the old project._ {color}","2026-01-19T10:53:53.310Z"],["3819625","BDB-1500","BDB","jevgeni.trombovetski@bolt.eu","Jevgeni Trombovetski","[~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] motion is here:\n[https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/bai9hxabbspjul5a5z9um/ABMt1ctvnn-H5AXtZ9fTtDA?rlkey=a7ihbev8p2has5kgb46uzjppn&st=3fq3b4va&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/bai9hxabbspjul5a5z9um/ABMt1ctvnn-H5AXtZ9fTtDA?rlkey=a7ihbev8p2has5kgb46uzjppn&st=3fq3b4va&dl=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T10:54:34.320Z"],["3819626","SRED-937","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","All done.","2026-01-19T10:54:46.747Z"],["3819628","PAR-3841","PAR","alexander.fokau@bolt.eu","Alexander Fokau","Hey! Have you found solution together with [@volodymyr.hadomskyi|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:fc7ada41-3f9c-4d74-95f1-90300ecbe201]? Do you need help from our side?","2026-01-19T10:54:58.855Z"],["3819630","SRED-1078","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","+$1,142 (+7%)","2026-01-19T10:55:18.886Z"],["3819631","RCE-359","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768820166067569]*{color}:\n[x-link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07R7QXSGRX/p1768809561054389]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 18th, 2026 11:59 PM] divyansh.kumar: Hey, we received a report from Ayna last Friday in email. Historically, AZ reporting has been maintained by expansion team, I have forwarded that to Gert/Sander, can you please have a look?\n{quote}","2026-01-19T10:56:19.265Z"],["3819632","SREDESK-7373","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","I have created a repository in JFrog for the Swift platform, named \"swift-mobile-local.\" The CI user for GitHub Actions has been shared with you separately. Please download the credentials and save them securely before closing the window.\n\nAdditionally, I have granted full permissions to your cost center, ENG-MOBILE-PLATFORM, for this repository.","2026-01-19T10:56:28.216Z"],["3819633","DBRE-8706","DBRE","mateusz.olszewski@bolt.eu","Mateusz Olszewski","I should've put more info, sorry.\n\nThese look ok:\n• Pipeline logs  ([http://monitor.boltint.net/d/b61e580e-4bf2-4b21-b6e8-c8ab401aa605/pipeline-logs?orgId=1&from=now-10d&to=now|http://monitor.boltint.net/d/b61e580e-4bf2-4b21-b6e8-c8ab401aa605/pipeline-logs?orgId=1&from=now-10d&to=now])\n• Alter-agent logs ([https://monitor.boltint.net/d/adbb4ef7-12a3-4dde-bc18-a41b60782203/alter-agent-logs?orgId=1&refresh=1m&from=now-10d&to=now|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/adbb4ef7-12a3-4dde-bc18-a41b60782203/alter-agent-logs?orgId=1&refresh=1m&from=now-10d&to=now])\nHere I can't see logs:\n• Tidb-alter-agent logs ([https://monitor.boltint.net/d/eecda598-8061-44a8-86ec-5b09e16b5a14/tialter-agent-logs?orgId=1&from=now-10d&to=now|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/eecda598-8061-44a8-86ec-5b09e16b5a14/tialter-agent-logs?orgId=1&from=now-10d&to=now])\nWe're getting multiple errors from tidb agent today and there are no logs.\n\n• supervisor logs ([https://monitor.boltint.net/d/b6e2798b-ffd8-46a1-97fe-3e20a3ff582b/supervisor-logs?orgId=1&from=now-10d&to=now|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/b6e2798b-ffd8-46a1-97fe-3e20a3ff582b/supervisor-logs?orgId=1&from=now-10d&to=now])\nSupervisor should be spitting out a lot of info logs e.g. when it's starting migration but there's nothing there","2026-01-19T10:56:55.172Z"],["3819634","LSS-61504","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","*Update:*\nAdmin logs show that on *13 Jan 2026 at 14:24 (UTC+02)*, both the email and phone number on the driver account were changed in a single action (email changed from [*ahmedbenjah@yahoo.co.uk*|mailto:ahmedbenjah@yahoo.co.uk] to [*fimid19411@imfaya.com*|mailto:fimid19411@imfaya.com], phone changed from _+447943429349_ to _+447888379554_). The change is recorded under _driver-profile_ with IP *79.127.146.223*.\n\nThis confirms unauthorised modification of core account identifiers; the actor and channel used for this change still need to be clarified.","2026-01-19T10:56:55.888Z"],["3819635","PAW-14937","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @dshilonosov\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160926\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 10:56:56 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T10:56:56.613Z"],["3819637","LSS-61749","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Scan_RO SRL.pdf] ","2026-01-19T10:57:02.429Z"],["3819638","PAW-14936","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @dshilonosov\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160926\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 10:57:05 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T10:57:05.894Z"],["3819640","LSS-61075","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey Team!\n\nThomas Bugeja already confirmed that he will attend on Bolt’s behalf.\n\nDo we have the information requested ready?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T10:57:15.250Z"],["3819641","CRC-1957","CRC","ekaterina.matson@bolt.eu","Ekaterina Matson","[update] PSP for Debt Collection changed from dLocal to Chari Money. Waiting for final decision to start integration. ","2026-01-19T10:57:22.447Z"],["3819642","HS-29070","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T10:57:27.102Z"],["3819646","SREDESK-7434","SREDESK","artem.borisov@bolt.eu","Artem Borisov","Please reject this one","2026-01-19T10:58:02.698Z"],["3819647","HS-29062","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T10:58:10.183Z"],["3819650","L10N-28706","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28697](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28697)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:59:00.626Z"],["3819651","HS-29061","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T10:59:02.635Z"],["3819652","L10N-28703","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28697](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28697)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:59:02.785Z"],["3819653","L10N-28711","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28697](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28697)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:59:06.293Z"],["3819654","L10N-28710","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28697](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28697)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:59:06.925Z"],["3819655","L10N-28709","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28697](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28697)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:59:07.535Z"]