r the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28656](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28656)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T10:59:17.679Z"],["3819666","HS-29060","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T10:59:27.771Z"],["3819668","PFI-835419","PFI","evelyn.obi@bolt-outsource.eu","Evelyn Obi","!image-20260119-105814.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-105846.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-105915.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T10:59:43.527Z"],["3819669","LSS-61512","LSS","bruna.miguel@bolt.eu","Bruna Miguel","Hey,\n\nThanks for the feedback. We have asked this to them directly, once we have feedback, we’ll let you know.\nThanks! ","2026-01-19T10:59:46.692Z"],["3819671","PFI-835420","PFI","sirichanya.phookrabil@bolt-outsource.eu","Sirichanya Phookrabil","!image-20260119-105451.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-105531.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-105542.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:00:00.243Z"],["3819673","LSS-61775","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey Legal Ops team!\n\nCould you kindly obtain [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] 's signature in the document, please?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T11:00:16.175Z"],["3819675","LSS-61768","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^Scan_UA_stamp (84735de4-5b7e-4183-87fd-e67009534e56).pdf] [^Scan_UA_stamp copy.pdf] [~accountid:6426a5407222b08f3e7400d7] , hei! Please find the signed document(s) attached.","2026-01-19T11:00:40.685Z"],["3819676","SRED-1079","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Upscaled","2026-01-19T11:00:46.971Z"],["3819680","SRED-1078","SRED","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Upscaled","2026-01-19T11:01:03.138Z"],["3819681","LSS-61780","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T11:01:11.952Z"],["3819682","DSR-3241","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], I’ve already sent the data and answer prepared [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/707477207]. Thanks!","2026-01-19T11:01:25.745Z"],["3819684","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] thank you! ","2026-01-19T11:01:44.458Z"],["3819685","BB-2284","BB","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","[~accountid:6411726057f0c028e2f4a9b1] don’t start yet, Kaur will fix the sums per vat liable and non liable row per invoice","2026-01-19T11:01:43.835Z"],["3819687","LSS-61075","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] data is ready, I added file on the internal notes in the ticket ","2026-01-19T11:01:52.162Z"],["3819689","RS-1949","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba],\n\nWe will reply with Sustainability related answers shortly. But the following questions ⬇️ have been assigned to our team erroneously. \n\nI believe 1.14.11 and 1.14.12 should be directed at the Data Privacy team. Please raise a ticket to them here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/157|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/157|smart-link] \n\nAnd question 1.16.1 and 1.16.2 is either Product Legal [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/735|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/1310/create/735|smart-link]  or Diversity and Inclusion which is looked after by Mare Heinluht. \n\nKadi 🙏 \n\n----\n\n*1.14.11* *** Please confirm whether you can meet the all the minimum requirements of the BBC’s Third Party Information Security Requirements in your business and supply chain and that you are willing to work with us to ensure that products and services are secure by design.\n\nSuppliers must be able to evidence their response if requested by the BBC.\n\nBBC’s Third Party Information Security Requirements:[ |https://tinyurl.com/2m5ctmke][https://tinyurl.com/2m5ctmke|https://tinyurl.com/2m5ctmke|smart-link] \n\n *1.14.12* IF you have answered 'no' to the above question, please provide an explanation as to why you cannot meet the requirements\n\n*1.16.1 ** For technology including digital products, services or hardware, the tenderer must self-certify that they have met (or will commit to meeting, by contract award) the BBC’s Technology Accessibility Policy – Guide to Accessibility Requirements to be met by Vendors, which includes meeting a Level AA standard of the current Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) from the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) Web Accessibility Initiative (WAI) Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 and the tenderer is willing to work with the BBC to ensure that the standards are maintained for the duration of the contract.\n\nSuppliers must be able to evidence accessibility if requested by the BBC.\n\nBBC Technology Accessibility Policy:[ |https://tinyurl.com/ykcw6huk][https://tinyurl.com/ykcw6huk|https://tinyurl.com/ykcw6huk|smart-link] \n\nWeb Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG):[https://tinyurl.com/56zvfrxn|https://tinyurl.com/56zvfrxn|smart-link] \n\n*1.16.2* If you have answered 'no' to the above question, please provide an explanation as to why.","2026-01-19T11:02:06.057Z"],["3819690","LSS-61782","LSS","ivan.halapa@bolt.eu","Ivan Halapa","[^Zahtjev (1).pdf] _(484 kB)_\n\n[^Ugovor o obavljanju usluga certificiranja.pdf] _(320 kB)_","2026-01-19T11:02:14.816Z"],["3819691","HS-29050","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T11:02:17.857Z"],["3819694","HS-29059","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T11:02:48.562Z"],["3819696","LSS-61694","LSS","marcin.klimkiewicz@bolt.eu","Marcin Klimkiewicz","Hi, all correct, but we don’t need the original to be sent to the PL office.","2026-01-19T11:03:25.382Z"],["3819697","SRED-1074","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done.","2026-01-19T11:03:26.929Z"],["3819698","BEE-3658","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","Sure, will handle it","2026-01-19T11:03:27.096Z"],["3819702","BEE-3658","BEE","andri.jasinski@bolt.eu","Andri Jasinski","Thanks!","2026-01-19T11:03:57.988Z"],["3819704","PFI-830905","PFI","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Hi [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] \nConfirming that the correct legal entity is *SASU NOVTC19* (SIRET 99187132800019, VAT FR92991871328, address: 3 impasse de Joinville, 75019 Paris).\n\nAll required documents were submitted on *27/11/2025*.\nDue to an internal processing delay, the November and December 2025 invoices and reports were issued under the former auto-entrepreneur entity (NOVTC).\n\nThe driver is requesting that *Nov–Dec 2025 activity be attributed to SASU NOVTC19*, or alternatively an official attestation confirming this and the internal delay.","2026-01-19T11:04:08.069Z"],["3819706","LSS-61785","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nNatalia Frończuk has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T11:04:42.780Z"],["3819711","PFI-835426","PFI","oluwayemisi.jamgbadi@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwayemisi Jamgbadi","!Screenshot_20260119_104012 paYMNET.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:05:48.795Z"],["3819715","PFI-834409","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T11:06:20.945Z"],["3819716","HS-29080","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.05.57.png|width=600,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.05.57.png\"!","2026-01-19T11:06:24.912Z"],["3819719","LSS-61783","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","In addition to this - could you please help on the following?\n\n\n1) has the turnover of your organisation been more or equal than £14.2m per annum in each of the last 2 audited trading years?\n2) as the turnover of your organisation been more or equal than £6.8m per year in each of the last 2 audited trading years?\n\n*3) If your answer to the above question is no, please provide other clear and demonstrable evidence of financial capacity*\n\n","2026-01-19T11:06:45.672Z"],["3819721","FC-915","FC","mirjam.arrak@bolt.eu","Mirjam Arrak","Another potential issue: if region is on country level, costs won’t go through GMV based Country to City allocations because Autonomous Driving BL doesn’t have any GMV.","2026-01-19T11:06:49.991Z"],["3819722","GRWA-1516","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/looker/pull/6447]\nAdded to metrics for orders finished end of month (Weekly/Monthly)\n\n*Summary*\n\nThis PR fixes an issue in the mart_non_additive__region__rides Explore where the metric rides_users_with_orders_finished_90d_end_of_week_local and rides_users_with_orders_finished_90d_end_of_month_local caused errors when users selected Date (or other non-week/month) granularity. The metric is only available/valid at weekly/monthly grain, but the Explore can dynamically switch across multiple grains via timeframe_picker, which led to “column not found”/SQL errors when the underlying table didn’t contain the weekly/monthly-only column.\n\n*What changed*\n\nAdded a new “safe/guarded” measure:\n\nrides_users_with_orders_finished_90d_end_of_week_local\nrides_users_with_orders_finished_90d_end_of_month_local\n\nThe measure uses a Liquid {% case %} on timeframe_picker._parameter_value:\n\nWhen Time Frame = Week → returns ${TABLE}.RIDES_USERS_WITH_ORDERS_FINISHED_90D_END_OF_WEEK_LOCAL\nWhen Time Frame = Month → returns ${TABLE}.RIDES_USERS_WITH_ORDERS_FINISHED_90D_END_OF_MONTH_LOCAL\n\nFor all other granularities → returns 0","2026-01-19T11:06:53.548Z"],["3819723","MLC-3968","MLC","daria.burr@bolt.eu","Daria Burr","Had a discovery session with [~accountid:62567ec8410206006e96e2f8] on 15th Jan to discuss the current state of affairs, objectives, and success metrics, as well as future vision and aspirations. Working document [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zxuQjzfZLYPakyqtYYdBuJh321e9-yfs2ZHyzetW_Xk/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.428s0cy8skc5]. \n\n*Next steps:* Kick-off meeting with [~accountid:62567ec8410206006e96e2f8] and [~accountid:712020:d98a1599-2e3b-4bac-bd9d-3c7377960838] planned for {{2026-01-22}}to agree on the first use cases and immediate next steps. ","2026-01-19T11:07:01.254Z"],["3819725","LSS-61592","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Renewal date is this Friday, so please can I have an update?","2026-01-19T11:07:57.684Z"],["3819730","PFI-835430","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^Confirmare_Tranzactie_26462_19-01-26.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-19T11:10:21.625Z"],["3819732","PFI-834419","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T11:10:37.499Z"],["3819735","PAW-14871","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-builder, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-19T11:11:24.554Z"],["3819737","PFI-835337","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! As far as I know, this is already being looked into by the team. [~accountid:712020:8b906c76-e5e5-4982-a2e9-3b1fc964a2e7] can you please include this in the investigation, this seems to be related to [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GLECZC8G3/p1768413550228689] topic. Thanks! ","2026-01-19T11:11:43.232Z"],["3819738","BRE-1222","BRE","mariia.bukhanska@bolt.eu","Mariia Bukhanska","No need to explicitly add the service, it could be done automatically","2026-01-19T11:11:46.485Z"],["3819739","PFI-834363","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has now been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T11:11:56.295Z"],["3819740","DSR-3821","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T11:12:08.285Z"],["3819743","PFI-835431","PFI","naomi.agyeman@bolt.eu","Naomi Amponfi Agyeman","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 11.13.19 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:13:37.927Z"],["3819744","PFI-834420","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T11:13:56.847Z"],["3819745","L10N-28735","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28697](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28697)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T11:14:15.074Z"],["3819748","DSR-2883","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] - was the responsive data actually sent to the driver+WIE before closing this ticket? \n\nPlease see the comments below - the case was extended as [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] was supporting us with creating an external GDrive to share the data with WIE and the driver.","2026-01-19T11:14:33.361Z"],["3819749","DRX-28234","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","\n\n* verified phone number value sent on `partnerDriver/startAuthentication' is done adequately when\n** no + sign is present in front of country code\n** verified + sign is present in requests\n** Verified space is not sent in request when phone number with space is copied and pasted\n** manual input and also when phone number was saved after successful login\n\n\n\n!phone number sent.png|width=715,alt=\"phone number sent.png\"!\n\n\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-19-2026 1-08-12 PM_1.MP4]\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-19-2026 12-59-59 PM_1.MP4]\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-19-2026 1-01-41 PM_1.MP4]\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-19-2026 12-56-41 PM_1.MP4]","2026-01-19T11:14:43.140Z"],["3819752","LSS-61786","LSS","aleksejs.batenko@bolt.eu","Aleksejs Batenko","[^Wess 2025 cars returns 01.2026.docx] _(742 kB)_","2026-01-19T11:14:59.536Z"],["3819756","FC-884","FC","hira.hassan@bolt.eu","Hira Hassan","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yoJJUElp82n48kSm2qZZKp75fF021Z86td6UjBP2eds/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yoJJUElp82n48kSm2qZZKp75fF021Z86td6UjBP2eds/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T11:16:07.144Z"],["3819757","DSR-3823","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T11:16:08.190Z"],["3819758","LSS-61786","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T11:16:08.718Z"],["3819759","LSS-61783","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T11:16:08.735Z"],["3819760","LSS-61785","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T11:16:08.767Z"],["3819761","LSS-61784","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T11:16:08.753Z"],["3819762","DBRE-8716","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Backfills finished","2026-01-19T11:16:24.315Z"],["3819764","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","The issue is with the model: {{rides/models/intermediate/marketplace/int_matching_blast_rounds/int_matching_blast_rounds.sql}} .  The model is calculating the partition date using  MIN(order_try_created_date). The incremental logic is creating duplicates in case of orders with order_tries spanning over two days.\nI am investigating with [@yuriy.trofymenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:ea34e25e-5aed-4ec5-8c46-0238dbead6e3] why {{overlap hours}} logic was not affective here.","2026-01-19T11:16:34.653Z"],["3819765","PFI-834439","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n[^Refund_Letter_KSJ55KM5TQQZX4G6_CXC4MQWW8TC7CBZ3.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T11:16:50.137Z"],["3819766","PFI-835414","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Hello! You can see by the payouts that they were rejected due to invalid bank details. For today's payout, you can see the reason was: \t\r\n/00000035/INVALID CHECK DIGITINVALID CHECK DIGIT (IMPS_00000035). Please get in touch with the partner to add some valid bank details with SEK payments enabled and we can reprocess the transaction","2026-01-19T11:17:09.322Z"],["3819768","SREC-375","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","I will [remove engineers|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15451] from the {{OktaENGInformationSec}} and keep this group for Tarmo and his direct reports.\nIf any permissions are missing, please add them to {{OktaENGCloudSec}}.","2026-01-19T11:17:44.986Z"],["3819774","PFI-834461","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi team,\n\nThe refund has failed. Our partner does not store refund details. We can ask our partner to issue the refund again, however we need the customers refund details. \nCould you please ask the customer to provide the following.\n\n*Bank name:* \n*Account name:* \n*Account number:*\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T11:18:39.974Z"],["3819775","PFI-835437","PFI","evelyn.obi@bolt-outsource.eu","Evelyn Obi","!image-20260119-111824.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-111841.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:18:50.904Z"],["3819777","BEE-3659","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","*Logic of FRT calculation in the RTM dashboard*\n\nHi *@user-U05LKLP4LSF*! Could you please share whether for FRT calculation in RTM dashboard you take into account all {{resolution_reason}} values? There are three of them: {{comment}}, {{voice_call}} and {{state}}. While {{comment}} and {{voice_call}} are correct, because there was an actual first response provided from our side, {{state}} resolution reason is applied when a case is closed without a first reply.\n\nWithin analytics we had a discussion and agreed that we want to exclude all instances where SLO is resolved with {{state}} reason as from the business logic perspective it does not make sense to include them. We would like to align with you to understand whether you already make this exclusion, and if not, do you see any blockers from your side to proceed this way?\n\nCC: *group-SQ1N3VDPX* *group-S04EPL97M97*","2026-01-19T11:19:30.486Z"],["3819778","BEE-3659","BEE",null,"Slack","[Stanislau Binko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:9687d9a4-446e-4c1f-9bf8-68017b3676b1] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QVGBP73R/p1768819420233309?thread_ts=1768819420.233309&cid=C08QVGBP73R|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QVGBP73R/p1768819420233309?thread_ts=1768819420.233309&cid=C08QVGBP73R|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T11:19:31.549Z"],["3819779","BEE-3659","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","hi :wave: as far as I see - we do not have any logic based on {{resolution_reason}} for FRT\n\ni.e. no matter what was that reason - we produce FRT related metrics (internally it's {{FIRST_RESPONSE_TIME}} time and also {{FRT_SLO_ACHIEVED_COUNT}} counter if integration event has {{slo_achieved = true}})","2026-01-19T11:19:32.008Z"],["3819780","BEE-3659","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","{quote}do you see any blockers from your side to proceed this way?{quote}\n\nI think technically it's not hard to adjust the logic how we produce metrics - but any kind of backfill / adjusting \"past\" would likely not be feasible, so we'd end up in situation where metric is calculated with different logic before change release vs after change release","2026-01-19T11:19:32.567Z"],["3819781","BEE-3659","BEE","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Thank you, clear. Since from the business logic perspective I think it makes sense to proceed anyway, unless *group-SQ1N3VDPX* *group-S04EPL97M97* anyone has concerns?","2026-01-19T11:19:33.327Z"],["3819782","BEE-3659","BEE","kevin.sutanto@bolt.eu","Kevin Sutanto","No concern - I think excluding {{state}} resolution reason is the right movement.\n\nJust to add business context, this {{state}} resolution reason create a problem because FRT is calculated not because of agent responding through comment or voice call but because a state of case was moved to {{closed}} example [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/718881149] - we only have ~2% of cases with this behaviour. As a result, this skewed the FRT calculation.","2026-01-19T11:19:34.150Z"],["3819783","LSS-61569","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:712020:ec09f884-709e-4d12-8b74-3045f0b19650] , as per the discussions had today, namely not to accept to have clause 11 mutual, as this is the last point open for negotiations with the counter-party, please note that I have already added the following comm for supplier in the [NDA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDuCsh2Zy4wfljXTdk1_T3uILUneacikPTWrzyGt1Wc/edit?tab=t.0]:\n”_We understand your request to make the clause mutual._\n_However, after aligning internally with OPS, and given the purpose of this NDA and the nature of the information exchanged, we do not consider a mutual non-reliance clause appropriate in this case._\n\n_The NDA is intended to allow Bolt to facilitate your technical solution and API integration capabilities. The information flow is therefore predominantly from the supplier to Bolt, and Bolt is not providing heavy technical specifications or information on which the supplier would reasonably rely for delivery or implementation._\n\n_The exchange volume of confidential information is asymmetrical, meaning it burdens the supplier more rather than Bolt. Having the clause mutual is not aligned with market practice for vendor assessments and API integration discussions. Moreover, we rely on your solution and experience, thus it is upon the supplier to provide accurate  and complete data, by having business knowledge on the topic._\n\n_For these reasons, we would prefer to keep the clause non-mutual.”_\n\n\nIf you agree with its content, please share the NDA with the counter-party. Fingers crossed!\n\nBest,\n\nAlex","2026-01-19T11:19:35.534Z"],["3819785","WFM-10026","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, should agents be assigned also for 03 DE_Global_Translation\r\n queue?\r\n","2026-01-19T11:19:49.620Z"],["3819786","BEE-3659","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","thanks for confirming, I've created task to adjust it on our side","2026-01-19T11:20:04.176Z"],["3819787","LSS-56363","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kt0Pnd_KMO5i3CRiK4hS1Xw7PBOZ0dGW61NuouePcyw/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kt0Pnd_KMO5i3CRiK4hS1Xw7PBOZ0dGW61NuouePcyw/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-19T11:20:13.194Z"],["3819788","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] \n\nWe will sign the order before the renewal date. We’d like to check if there was a legal review of the terms previously, since Zendesk have been Bolt’s supplier for a long time. I will reach out today if there are any questions. ","2026-01-19T11:20:14.021Z"],["3819789","LSS-61694","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","[~accountid:5f9aac6499b42e0069a4f456] fine! so the scan will be sufficient here 😉","2026-01-19T11:20:24.890Z"],["3819790","PFI-835437","PFI","evelyn.obi@bolt-outsource.eu","Evelyn Obi","The session ID is stated respectively. N2,500 first then N1,000. ","2026-01-19T11:20:27.983Z"],["3819791","DSR-3557","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a], response was sent, and T1 created an SD ticket relating to the transparency of T&Cs. \n\n→ [SD|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-61701] (They advised to go to Local OPS or Product team).","2026-01-19T11:20:39.884Z"],["3819792","DRX-28020","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Retest test case from task description","2026-01-19T11:21:08.681Z"],["3819793","CRC-2212","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nNL and CH have been launched on 15.01.","2026-01-19T11:21:24.694Z"],["3819795","WFM-10032","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","granted","2026-01-19T11:21:37.537Z"],["3819799","CCM-22287","CCM","peace.anumia@bolt-outsource.eu","Peace Anumia","[^New Training Request form _ Teleperformance (19th of January 26).xlsx]","2026-01-19T11:21:59.015Z"],["3819800","SREDESK-7369","SREDESK","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","I am closing this request as it’s being covered by investigations in TI-INCENTIVEs cluster related to the Admin Panel overloading the cluster with heavy queries. All queries are affected when KV storage is overloaded.\n","2026-01-19T11:22:28.298Z"],["3819805","INS-910","INS","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","* Agreed to implement a per-project warehouse operations file for approval by code owners (code owners or AEs; AEs must review).\n* After approval, execute commands manually while being informed on how to:\n** Set up the cluster\n** Obtain permissions\n** Roll back if changes fail or tables become corrupted\n* Release the history (we can reuse our workflow to update history files).\n* History files will remain in the repository, which is beneficial for tracking table drop history.\n* The ideal solution is to establish an automated workflow running under the project Unified Auth instance profile.\n* We can reuse our workflow that submits the job.\n* Caveats\n** We want to use both SQL and Python (with functions provided by Insights).\n** This may complicate parsing table names to verify project ownership and ensure they are or were dbt tables.","2026-01-19T11:23:47.010Z"],["3819806","PFI-835438","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^NBC STATEMENT EXTRACT (2).pdf]\n[^payment BOLT NBC (2).pdf]\n[^SWIFT COPY BOLT (3).pdf]\n\nAttached POP’s","2026-01-19T11:23:49.875Z"],["3819807","CRC-2366","CRC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","[update]\n\nProgress: the onboarding to the “Bolt Flow” started for 3 drivers. It’s still pending due to some issues with the virtual card addition on the apple & google wallets.\n\nNext: no progress this week due to vacation","2026-01-19T11:23:49.845Z"],["3819808","WFM-10024","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","approved","2026-01-19T11:24:10.684Z"],["3819810","PFI-833607","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Payout reversed accordingly, ","2026-01-19T11:24:23.951Z"],["3819812","DRX-27847","DRX","oliver.meus@bolt.eu","Oliver Meus","Can be done after we implement screenshot tests.","2026-01-19T11:25:11.048Z"],["3819815","PFI-834480","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe are unable to explain why the customer’s bank App is showing a double charge as this view is entirely dependent on the customer’s bank. Kindly advise the customer to refer to their bank regarding this issue. We can confirm that only one charge was made for this payment.","2026-01-19T11:26:04.489Z"],["3819820","DRX-27847","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - DRX-27848 has been resolved","2026-01-19T11:26:21.431Z"],["3819822","LSS-61592","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Thank you","2026-01-19T11:26:27.556Z"],["3819823","PFI-834421","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T11:26:32.488Z"],["3819825","PFI-834427","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully 