 capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T11:31:25.945Z"],["3819860","PFI-835442","PFI","oluwayemisi.jamgbadi@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwayemisi Jamgbadi","!Screenshot_20260119-121117  paymmmt.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:31:29.025Z"],["3819861","PFI-834996","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-19T11:31:29.958Z"],["3819866","DBRE-8505","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","Remaining: 3p/d","2026-01-19T11:32:15.850Z"],["3819867","PFI-835445","PFI","jakub.seibert@bolt-outsource.eu","Jakub Seibert","!image-20260119-113136.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-113144.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-113154.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:32:23.285Z"],["3819869","DSR-3057","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d] - do I understand correctly that you added new data to the original “[responsive data|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fK5qYwFnfu6quSIswmHEnVfl05vM2klV?usp=drive_link]” folder which we used for the first part of the DSR (sent on Jan 12)? There’s also a completely empty “[BH tickets|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1KTdCsm5gNH1aUBp6p3UddMDkyYqt2abL?usp=drive_link]” folder.\nCould you please re-separate those into two different folders so that we don’t get it mixed up? Please add the responsive data for the DSAR that has not yet been addressed (the March 2025 one) to the folder created by Sigrid, named “[Case from 17.03.25|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QkNd4fmFRF8jWazYPXehlqc27kR4QQon?usp=drive_link]”.\n\nCould you also tell me where the prepared response letter is? This one [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tJP-tJwOxuc9MKdsbAGcIlZJ_7B_b0X-IfC1hkHMSwQ/edit?usp=drive_link] is the one I drafted for our Jan 12 answer. I don’t see any other prepared answer for my review - the one in [Case from 17.03.25|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QkNd4fmFRF8jWazYPXehlqc27kR4QQon?usp=drive_link] doesn’t seem to have been prepared by CSPC as it is still in template format. Please review and re-escalate to me.","2026-01-19T11:32:46.721Z"],["3819874","SREDESK-7435","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","\n\n* Resource group limits have been modified\n\n{noformat}root@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT user, host, User_attributes->>\"$.resource_group\" as Resource_group from mysql.user WHERE user LIKE 'v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker';\n+-------------------------------+------+-------------------------------+\n| user                          | host | Resource_group                |\n|-------------------------------+------+-------------------------------|\n| v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker | %    | v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker |\n+-------------------------------+------+-------------------------------+\n1 row in set\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.007s\n\nroot@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM information_schema.resource_groups WHERE NAME='v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker';\n+-------------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n| NAME                          | RU_PER_SEC | PRIORITY | BURSTABLE | QUERY_LIMIT | BACKGROUND |\n|-------------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------|\n| v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker | 5000       | MEDIUM   | YES       | <null>      | <null>     |\n+-------------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.006s\n\nroot@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>ALTER RESOURCE GROUP `v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker` RU_PER_SEC = 10000 BURSTABLE = FALSE;\nYou're about to run a destructive command.\nDo you want to proceed? (y/n): y\nYour call!\nQuery OK, 0 rows affected\nTime: 0.514s\n\nroot@ti-incentives-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM information_schema.resource_groups WHERE NAME='v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker';\n+-------------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n| NAME                          | RU_PER_SEC | PRIORITY | BURSTABLE | QUERY_LIMIT | BACKGROUND |\n|-------------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------|\n| v2-omnibus-item-price-tracker | 10000      | MEDIUM   | NO        | <null>      | <null>     |\n+-------------------------------+------------+----------+-----------+-------------+------------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.006s{noformat}","2026-01-19T11:33:12.451Z"],["3819876","PFI-834983","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment failed due to insufficient funds and there was no charge on the customer’s card. Kindly advise the user to check with their bank regarding this charge.","2026-01-19T11:33:45.160Z"],["3819877","CRC-2381","CRC","emre.cakmak@bolt.eu","Emre Can Çakmak","[update] Technical scope is in progress.","2026-01-19T11:34:03.912Z"],["3819884","PFI-801722","PFI","catarina.silva@bolt.eu","Catarina Caneira da Silva","Thank you [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] but the fiscalized invoices will come out in the old VAT or the New One?\n\nSorry, to be fully clear! Because I already saw a couple that are fiscalized but with the old VAT still.","2026-01-19T11:34:22.237Z"],["3819886","FC-408","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","seems ok now","2026-01-19T11:34:40.667Z"],["3819887","FC-409","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","seems ok now","2026-01-19T11:34:56.859Z"],["3819888","FC-401","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","cancelled","2026-01-19T11:35:17.840Z"],["3819889","LSS-61766","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] \n\nEven if we get services for free we need to enter into DPA (Data Processing Agreement), sign NDA and also sign service agreement with supplier. \n\nPlease reach out to Privacy about DPA, create a ticket to review service agreement for me (HQ Legal) and create a ticket to InfoSec to evaluate supplier. \n\nLet me know if there are other questions, I will proceed with NDA review ","2026-01-19T11:35:22.706Z"],["3819891","FC-400","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","cancelled","2026-01-19T11:35:27.275Z"],["3819897","FC-477","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","YtD collections moved to 1203 account.","2026-01-19T11:36:03.404Z"],["3819898","CSDT-971","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","# Change made in dim_support_case_tier_history → model needs to be backfilled with correct values → ask Kevin to do it. After that proceed with next steps, as dim_support_case_history is an upstream dependency for mart_support_case_metrics, which is going to be changed next. \n# ","2026-01-19T11:36:08.881Z"],["3819901","FC-478","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","will be fixed with treasury core rules","2026-01-19T11:36:36.663Z"],["3819902","FPD-1545","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","This looks like a generalized issue. Below is an example for Paris (see image).\n\n!image-20260119-113041.png|width=1006,alt=\"image-20260119-113041.png\"!\n\nWe’re still investigating the root cause, but the most likely explanation is a mismatch between data sources: partner activations and churns appear to come from a different source than active partners and as a result the historical calculations don’t match.\n\nThe forecast logic itself is correct as the forecast decomposition into churns and reactivations is internally consistent by construction (i.e. *AP(t) = AP(t-1) − churns(t) + activations(t)*).\n\nThe fix is therefore limited to correcting the historical actuals as the model is trained solely on active partners, which means the overall impact should be minimal.","2026-01-19T11:36:40.804Z"],["3819905","LSS-61784","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] have we received any supporting docs here? Tender docs or similar? And when is the tender submission-deadline? Thanks!","2026-01-19T11:36:56.758Z"],["3819908","FC-506","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","cancelled","2026-01-19T11:37:23.323Z"],["3819909","WD-22603","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Before edit \n\n!image-20260119-113735.png|width=1036,alt=\"image-20260119-113735.png\"!","2026-01-19T11:37:38.882Z"],["3819910","FC-546","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","done, total balance below TH","2026-01-19T11:37:41.981Z"],["3819911","LSS-52662","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Controller list updated. Closing the ticket","2026-01-19T11:37:51.684Z"],["3819913","FC-855","FC","ilona.kajak@bolt.eu","Ilona Kajak","done","2026-01-19T11:38:12.301Z"],["3819915","WD-22603","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi! updated bank details are as following \n\n!image-20260119-113836.png|width=1021,alt=\"image-20260119-113836.png\"!","2026-01-19T11:38:40.373Z"],["3819917","PFI-834197","PFI","vania.silva@bolt-outsource.eu","Vania Silva","Hello,\n\nThe fleet has not received the payment. It was at the bank, so they sent us the bank statement proving that the amount was not credited. Could you please check why the amount did not enter the bank account?","2026-01-19T11:39:39.924Z"],["3819918","LSS-55769","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please support with signing, this is urgent request we need to sign today ","2026-01-19T11:39:41.954Z"],["3819920","LSS-61604","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","Thanks [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] [~accountid:712020:3f3165cb-0c0c-447a-9e47-71699c1cb05e] could you please suggest directly on text [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BoDIT1vm9Z9ZNy-btNp0JMDisv8j-HY_KForMhwpC1Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.b0zx0fsxrkcc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BoDIT1vm9Z9ZNy-btNp0JMDisv8j-HY_KForMhwpC1Q/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.b0zx0fsxrkcc|smart-link]  how to integrate your suggestion? \n\n","2026-01-19T11:40:10.147Z"],["3819924","LSS-61604","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","Sorry [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] tagged the wrong Gabriele before :)","2026-01-19T11:40:46.179Z"],["3819925","PFI-798762","PFI","martin.paroll@bolt.eu","Martin Paroll","Hi [~accountid:613f55541370f00069029b71] \n\nThe driver has had a lot of cash orders in 2022-2023, this is where the balance comes from. Our engineering has found the free transactions still in debt like \n\n{quote}2022-12-31 :  fee 86.94. \n\n2023-01-01 : fee 56.52{quote}\n\nand there are more.\n\nIt does not feel feasible to allocate more engineering resource into this one case. I suggest summarizing the answer into “previous cash orders from 2022 are causing this balance”.\n\nBest,\n\nMartin","2026-01-19T11:40:51.256Z"],["3819926","LSS-61782","LSS","ivan.halapa@bolt.eu","Ivan Halapa","Hey [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] for visibility.","2026-01-19T11:41:00.110Z"],["3819933","PFI-834520","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe other two payment attempts failed due to insufficient funds. I would suggest the customer refers back to their bank to check if these charges where completed in the end and were not just “on hold” and if yes provide a bank statement that shows these debits. The bank App transaction notifications are not sufficient to prove the charges.","2026-01-19T11:42:58.701Z"],["3819937","LEG-1325","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Kick-off call taking place today (19 January).","2026-01-19T11:44:54.070Z"],["3819938","LO-139","LO","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","All contract uploaded to Zycuses Onedrive and shared in slack with Zycus [https://zycusitis.sharepoint.com/sites/Bolt-Customer-Site/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FBolt%2DCustomer%2DSite%2FShared%20Documents%2FExternal%2FBolt%20Contract%20Migration%202026%2FWarehouse%20Lease%20Agreement&viewid=f5543317%2De708%2D488a%2D98cd%2D22afeb43270e&ga=1|https://zycusitis.sharepoint.com/sites/Bolt-Customer-Site/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FBolt%2DCustomer%2DSite%2FShared%20Documents%2FExternal%2FBolt%20Contract%20Migration%202026%2FWarehouse%20Lease%20Agreement&viewid=f5543317%2De708%2D488a%2D98cd%2D22afeb43270e&ga=1|smart-link]  ","2026-01-19T11:44:54.659Z"],["3819939","PFI-835027","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Ruslana, this doesn’t seem like a Fraud issue to me 😕 I don’t see any blockers from our side. It’s likely that no “cash-enabled“ couriers were available in that region at that specific time, but if you want to confirm 100% then I’d suggest asking tech.\nExample setting on a courier profile 👇 so turns out it’s possible to simply toggle this per courier.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.42.44.png|width=390,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.42.44.png\"!","2026-01-19T11:44:55.671Z"],["3819941","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","I am testing solution in dev.","2026-01-19T11:46:00.542Z"],["3819942","LSS-54100","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] will we sign any agreement, order with Junie or we will accept website terms ? \n\nLegal recommendation is to request MSA, DPA from Junie and sign in writing rather than accepting website terms. ","2026-01-19T11:46:03.119Z"],["3819943","PFI-835414","PFI","jenny.jensen@bolt.eu","Jenny Jensen","Details already updated and confirmed before creating this ticket (and after previous failed payout) hence the request to retry","2026-01-19T11:46:08.974Z"],["3819946","LSS-54100","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:63e354e3010d35637974a02c] will we sign any agreement, order with Junie or we will accept website terms ? \n\nLegal recommendation is to request MSA, DPA from Junie and sign in writing rather than accepting website terms. ","2026-01-19T11:46:36.599Z"],["3819947","FX-3440","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Ernests Rudzītis [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768823183852029]*{color}:\nHi! Do you have any updates regarding this?\n{quote}","2026-01-19T11:46:38.776Z"],["3819953","BD-1993","BD","alexander.embacher@bolt.eu","Alexander Embacher","Query to get all tasks related to this error:\n\n{code:sql}SELECT /* ROUTE READONLY=1 */ * FROM task\nWHERE reference_id IN (\n    SELECT reference_id\n    FROM task\n    WHERE error_message = '702 INVALID_REQUEST: Delivery records sum doesn''t match payment amount'\n)\nAND state IN ('failed', 'failed_waiting_dependencies')\nAND created > '2025-01-01 00:00:00'; -- 543{code}","2026-01-19T11:47:52.048Z"],["3819954","SREDESK-7418","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Trying to do it via AA first (skipped prelive, it will be synced during night)\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/schema-change/pipelines/161793|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/schema-change/pipelines/161793]","2026-01-19T11:47:56.129Z"],["3819959","RS-1948","RS","zuzanna.janiszewska@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Janiszewska","Hi [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c], thank you for adding me to the ticket. I added [~accountid:712020:5c454c27-a98f-4408-979d-0831728f5d07] (PP, RH) and [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] and [~accountid:712020:7ebf1982-dd36-43fb-a386-42b4b1ee6b59]  to the ticket for visibility.\n\n\nFrom my perspective, the police intends to ask us about the drivers, but we do not have employment relationship with them, which is determined by the Road Transport Act. Bolt, based on the provisions in the Road Transport Act, is the intermediary in passenger transport, holds the appropriate license to do so, and cooperates only with licensed legal entities entitled to provide passenger transport. \nTherefore, the number is 0. \n[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] would you be able to confirm my suspicion - as I am not a lawyer, that if the police releases us from trade secret obligation, we would be legally required to do so?","2026-01-19T11:49:02.989Z"],["3819960","LO-178","LO","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Templates weren’t needed. Contract uploaded to Onedrive [https://zycusitis.sharepoint.com/sites/Bolt-Customer-Site/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FBolt%2DCustomer%2DSite%2FShared%20Documents%2FExternal%2FBolt%20Contract%20Migration%202026&viewid=f5543317%2De708%2D488a%2D98cd%2D22afeb43270e&ga=1|https://zycusitis.sharepoint.com/sites/Bolt-Customer-Site/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FBolt%2DCustomer%2DSite%2FShared%20Documents%2FExternal%2FBolt%20Contract%20Migration%202026&viewid=f5543317%2De708%2D488a%2D98cd%2D22afeb43270e&ga=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T11:49:15.853Z"],["3819961","LSS-60399","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","No update from CS team. Seems outside of Bolt’s systems. Closing the ticket.","2026-01-19T11:49:25.389Z"],["3819965","LO-180","LO","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Contract uploaded to Onedrive\n\n[https://zycusitis.sharepoint.com/sites/Bolt-Customer-Site/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FBolt%2DCustomer%2DSite%2FShared%20Documents%2FExternal%2FBolt%20Contract%20Migration%202026&viewid=f5543317%2De708%2D488a%2D98cd%2D22afeb43270e&ga=1|https://zycusitis.sharepoint.com/sites/Bolt-Customer-Site/Shared%20Documents/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FBolt%2DCustomer%2DSite%2FShared%20Documents%2FExternal%2FBolt%20Contract%20Migration%202026&viewid=f5543317%2De708%2D488a%2D98cd%2D22afeb43270e&ga=1|smart-card]","2026-01-19T11:50:08.643Z"],["3819969","LSS-58745","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:cdea2b9c-07f7-4a74-b147-0308181dd47e] - hoping you’re doing well! Any updates here or has the initiative been deprioritized? Please let me know if you’d like to proceed or if I can close this ticket.","2026-01-19T11:50:45.733Z"],["3819970","PFI-835050","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Olena, doesn’t look like we’re blocking anything from our side. It’s possible that there weren’t any _cash-enabled_ couriers available at that specific time and in that area. If you want to confirm this, I’d suggest turning to tech support.\nThanks!","2026-01-19T11:50:46.858Z"],["3819971","FRAUD-5736","FRAUD","liisi.laasik@bolt.eu","Liisi Dovbnja","Affected checkpoints:\n\n||*checkpoint*||*service*||*device-info endpoint*||\n|user_order_request|fraud-order|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid|\n|user_car_sharing_request|fraud-rental-car-order|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid|\n|user_rental_request|fraud-rental-order|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid|\n|subscription_user_order|fraud-subscription|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid|\n|user_payment_instrument_adding_check|fraud-user|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid\ngetActorLatestDeviceInfo\ngetDeviceInfoByDeviceUidAndActorTypes|\n|user_show_tips_screen|fraud-user|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid|\n|user_top_up_request|fraud-user|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid\ngetActorLatestDeviceInfo\ngetDeviceInfoByDeviceUidAndActorTypes|\n|DisputeDocumentCreatorCron|fraud-chargeback-dispute|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid\ngetActorLatestDeviceInfo\ngetDeviceInfoByDeviceUidAndActorTypes|\n|drive_capture_authorized_amount\nmicromobility_capture_authorized_amount\nrides_payment_capture_authorized_amount|fraud-payment|getActorDeviceInfoByDeviceUid\ngetDeviceInfoByDeviceUidAndActorTypes|","2026-01-19T11:50:51.556Z"],["3819972","FX-3670","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768823442206329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3670] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T11:50:55.956Z"],["3819974","CSDT-964","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Add vendor_id and vendor_name from dim_order_delivery to dim_support_case_order_delivery model. \n\n\n\n# Added to sql & config\n# Backfill\n# Generate views based on instructions above\n# Looker sync","2026-01-19T11:51:04.297Z"],["3819977","FX-3440","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Ernests Rudzītis [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768823183852029]*{color}:\nHi! Do you have any updates regarding this?\n{quote}","2026-01-19T11:52:12.911Z"],["3819980","XP-3069","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","[@pavel.kiper|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] This is actually correct alert as we are the client {{targeting-external}} calls {{targeiting}} .\n Real fix would be moving the external methods to the teams that own the functionality.","2026-01-19T11:53:58.557Z"],["3819985","PAW-14986","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-19T11:54:26.438Z"],["3819991","LSS-61108","LSS","lucian.andrei@bolt.eu","Lucian Andrei","Hello [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , any updates here please?","2026-01-19T11:55:13.312Z"],["3819992","DPX-3794","DPX","aleh.zibrou@bolt.eu","Aleh Zibrou","Hey friends [~accountid:624b0ac545ece00069cc6017] [~accountid:712020:59ef2988-275c-471b-8931-bfc08a0ab578]  , I think we shouldn’t have separate save button here\nIf we changed anything — changed should be applied with Confirm button\nOn other side we have back to cancel changes  ","2026-01-19T11:55:42.938Z"],["3819993","MVRT-1486","MVRT","marit.ausmees@bolt.eu","Marit Ausmees","Hey, [~accountid:632d4729fedc6169aed5c944] What exactly should I launch on Meta? Is this ticket meant for the UGC videos:\n\n* [+UGC visuals 1+|https://app.shook.digital/app/clewkib5o0000la08zf2fjtf4/projects/cm5zedp1w00lds601ifd8ucgk/productions/cm9sshej300zqs60123ofr1bj/videos?token=Fe26.2*1*8b34dbf6a62b174f52f0eadfc6dac517823d6e63b1c5a413849df68c461379c9*VfR-BL4ZzY9h3nL0HpaeKg*N7N33PwixdoCtjNEaHFl9ml710t7jJ_BXzPqofxFeB8C6TQ5_KTSKvGJjPMT8Nvk6doAuAvz0Zv08Qgs8ylan2K8lDKBTTXkHO76qI1-1HKLKyHJGSV8pE2nNGH5aRROJOltuJ3eXtCyga18ApeyXA*4165991363401*10a70c233d5d052285840b3c975abd441532516f19cf320c729e1cd1727ebe69*MUMrL7fGFJhdfZol6VE1xYrePfYi0VbSg7jW8V4j7dc%7E2]\n* [+UGC visuals 2+|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1AUjDk_neIwwnQ4MW_wSa8-icbv0fsswL]\n* [+UGC visuals 3+|https://drive.google.com/file/d/13zlzhOUOqegErFYFNGYicoqiUHEuThE-/view?usp=drive_link]\n* [+Copies+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1AVDVmpMU1ZY0fWphOFV3CyeuJY62xytbJAU_rKNS2WQ/edit?gid=2097314132#gid=2097314132&range=A95:B95]\n\nThanks!","2026-01-19T11:55:56.950Z"],["3819996","PFI-834521","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe Kč 165 was the preauthorisation amount which can differ from the predicted price of the ride. The preauthorisation amount is tailored to the customer’s fraud calculations and some dynamic rules set by the Fraud team. To better understand the final captured amount, kindly check with the technical support team, they might be able to explain what was the actual predicted price and what factors affected the final captured amount.","2026-01-19T11:56:30.475Z"],["3819997","DAEN-1346","DAEN","silja.mardla@bolt.eu","Silja Märdla","Regarding the release freeze, we have discussed it before. If the pipelines run on daily, having the freeze on Friday afternoon is too late, because the next run will already be inside the freeze period.\nThat said, delivery domain has solved the problem by having intraday runs to capture any issues before the next morning run. If we would have that run around midday, we'd still have time to correct before the weekend.\n\nThere's room for improvement, but we can be smart about how we improve.","2026-01-19T11:56:58.122Z"],["3819999","PFI-835466","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260119-115512.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-115521.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:57:44.637Z"],["3820000","DSR-3057","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], asked Jens regarding this. As I’m not fully sure which data needs to be re-separated. ","2026-01-19T11:57:49.680Z"],["3820004","XP-3069","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","What does {{2.67 >= 1}} mean? Do we get an alert if there is more than 1 bad (external) request?","2026-01-19T11:58:31.217Z"],["3820005","LSS-61413","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Thank you [~accountid:642b0757551f476a04685f2d] , our legal secondee [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] will help you out with this one. ","2026-01-19T11:58:34.172Z"],["3820006","FIS-4186","FIS","maryalfredkamel.abdelmalek@bolt.eu","Mary Abdelmalek","[~accountid:61e7c9c038041c00685c0c11] they have added a reply can you please check","2026-01-19T11:58:35.378Z"],["3820008","LSS-61784","LSS","elisabeth.gunnarsson@bolt.eu","Elisabeth Gunnarsson","Yes, but nothing I want Legal to put time on yet, documents will be sent as ticket once we know we passed phase one. \n\n\n\nBut if interested - [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1PMbvm0OsY3YnKFds_3tqkTOtYBBqXiSl?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1PMbvm0OsY3YnKFds_3tqkTOtYBBqXiSl?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T11:58:48.114Z"],["3820009","LSS-61075","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:60bf496ea01e11006ac62a66] ! Is it in this ticket? If that is the case, then I don’t have access to your internal notes 🙂 ","2026-01-19T11:58:57.193Z"],["3820012","PFI-835467","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","!Screenshot_20260119-120318.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260119-121117.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T11:59:10.817Z"],["3820013","PFI-832852","PFI","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","hi sorry I missed your questions.\n\nKey is this part:\n\n“Wszyscy przedsiębiorcy posiadający polski NIP będą zobligowani do przesyłania faktur za pośrednictwem KSEF. *Wiemy, że dla części z Państwa ten obowiązek został przesunięty na 1 kwietnia 2026 r.*, jednak zachęcamy do korzystania z KSEF od 1 lutego 2026 r., co powinno się przyczynić do bardziej sprawnego procesowania Państwa faktur.”\n\nWe will be falling into obligatory KSEF as of 1 April, not Feb and therefore up until this point we will not be issuing invoices in KSEF as we are not under obligation. The commerce team is still working on a solution to issue invoices in KSEF.\n\nWe should kindly let know that we will comply with the law and start issuing invoices in KSEF when this will be obligatory for us, which is as of 1 April 2026. \n\n\n\nThe message imposing other partner to complu with KSEF, regardless of their individual go-live date, is way out of the line and has not any reflection in laws governing KSEF\n\n","2026-01-19T11:59:12.262Z"],["3820014","RNTL-30357","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","Other cities result:\n\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Nr1ZWQfcCkx9WeKnMxCaVZtYjloBa_OTneTiJ_x6PEY/edit?gid=548466388#gid=548466388|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Nr1ZWQfcCkx9WeKnMxCaVZtYjloBa_OTneTiJ_x6PEY/edit?gid=548466388#gid=548466388|smart-link] \n\nComplete the rest of cities numbers on the sheet.","2026-01-19T11:59:17.510Z"],["3820015","LSS-60758","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] can you please look into this? Thanks! 🙏 ","2026-01-19T11:59:23.415Z"],["3820018","HS-29098","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Task sent back on Workday","2026-01-19T12:00:03.061Z"],["3820019","BIZ-239","BIZ","thiago.oliveira@bolt.eu","Thiago Ibrahim","Legal team waiting assesment from external counsel.\nThe company was off and only returned 14-Jan.\n\n","2026-01-19T12:00:13.477Z"],["3820021","PFI-832470","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Two statements in question have been reissued","2026-01-19T12:00:21.217Z"],["3820022","FDBT-4797","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_psp_payments fails on 2026-01-18 08:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 553349251317293, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_psp_payments/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-18T08%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=psp_currency_clearing.psp_currency_clearing&base_date=2026-01-18T08%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-19T12:00:22.787Z"],["3820023","LSS-61752","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hi there, Yes more than happy to do that. Please could I ask that you attach it here and I will set up meeting with location partner to sort through any questions they have. ","2026-01-19T12:00:34.879Z"],["3820028","CCM-22288","CCM","toyosi.olusesi@bolt-outsource.eu","Toyosi Olusesi","[^New Training Request form _ Teleperformance.xlsx]","2026-01-19T12:01:12.706Z"],["3820029","CSXDL-182","CSXDL","kristiina.himma@bolt.eu","Kristiina Himma","WIP [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ibhn6lBkYsnWvapAKB1-z8CxXRQAjoPj1wM0PVy_jWE/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ibhn6lBkYsnWvapAKB1-z8CxXRQAjoPj1wM0PVy_jWE/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:01:43.227Z"],["3820031","DAEN-1346","DAEN","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","We don't have to outsmart it and plan any midday run of everything. One post deployment manual run of changed models is good-enough in my opinion and does not bring any technical complexity.\n\nFor me regular thing is to deploy smaller Databricks jobs, which I'm not putting into airflow to have the ability to backfill only a specific subset of models, and it's a good way to run only changed things before the next scheduled run happens.","2026-01-19T12:02:18.496Z"],["3820032","RCE-357","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768824093852679]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-357 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T12:02:20.376Z"],["3820033","PFI-835474","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260119-120023.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-120123.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T12:02:31.438Z"],["3820037","PFI-832852","PFI","mateusz.zawadzki@bolt.eu","Mateusz Zawadzki","Great! Thank you :)","2026-01-19T12:03:08.242Z"],["3820040","LSS-61075","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","[~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] let me know if you have access to this [link|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XtQ277cXZbcmHUI4tzTlKiYTuFQFFPbwNOtVEpbrlEs/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-19T12:03:45.534Z"],["3820043","PGC-306","PGC","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","This ticket was automatically closed because all linked tickets are now closed/done. 🤖","2026-01-19T12:05:16.216Z"],["3820044","BIZ-308","BIZ","teresa.rodrigues@bolt.eu","Teresa Cipriano Rodrigues","[~accountid:641c083a67102fc717c1538e] [~accountid:641c083a67102fc717c1538e] this is the food project. Are you sure this is here","2026-01-19T12:05:25.611Z"],["3820046","XP-3069","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","Yes. There should be no calls without provided randomisation unit ID.","2026-01-19T12:05:56.829Z"],["3820051","PAW-14981","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @olshak\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161095\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 12:06:45 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T12:06:45.841Z"],["3820052","BIZ-308","BIZ","thiago.oliveira@bolt.eu","Thiago Ibrahim","[~accountid:614ad8f941af83007135337d] fixed.","2026-01-19T12:06:50.684Z"],["3820053","PFI-835374","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Tech Support] App related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/104\n- [Customer Payments] Payment related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/313\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/314\n[Billing] - Invoice and Balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/315\n[Billing/ Tax Tech]- Invoices not reported (Fiscalized): https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n[Billing/Configuration Changes]- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T12:07:03.486Z"],["3820054","WD-22550","WD","anett.suurkask@bolt.eu","Anett Suurkask"," Hey [~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] any update here regarding gapless doc number? 🙏  I would need to issue invoices under BG002 soon.. and i need to be sure that first invoice number in 2026 should be 0000000024 🤞 ","2026-01-19T12:07:11.523Z"],["3820055","PFI-834834","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Tech Support] App related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/104\n- [Customer Payments] Payment related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/313\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/314\n[Billing] - Invoice and Balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/60/create/315\n[Billing/ Tax Tech]- Invoices not reported (Fiscalized): https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n[Billing/Configuration Changes]- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T12:07:21.071Z"],["3820056","XP-3069","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","What is the action here? What should we do based on this alert?","2026-01-19T12:07:32.607Z"],["3820058","RNTL-30037","RNTL","risqi.berliandie@bolt.eu","Risqi Berliandie Rubiandini","Callout from RH team that mention net negative impact on GMV and Rides.","2026-01-19T12:07:37.344Z"],["3820059","PFI-835479","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","[^FACTURA PY1526 96.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T12:07:43.028Z"],["3820060","BIZ-203","BIZ","thiago.oliveira@bolt.eu","Thiago Ibrahim","First test rides done under the test account.\nInvoices attached.|\nLegal/Tax team is checking before approving it.\n\nIt needs to have VAT added. Passed to commerce to check.\n[^2087489-MD1126-1412.pdf] [^2175939-MD1126-142.pdf] [^2181859-MD1126-876.pdf] ","2026-01-19T12:07:56.866Z"],["3820061","LSS-61790","LSS","yuanhsin.lee@bolt.eu","Carolyn Lee","[^[Shared Fleet] Bolt - Fleet Partnership Agreement Taiwan - (CN trans)_FINAL [MPT Exclusive].docx.pdf] _(613 kB)_","2026-01-19T12:08:21.063Z"],["3820067","PFI-835100","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, thanks for letting us know, devices unblocked 🙂 ","2026-01-19T12:08:46.572Z"],["3820069","LSS-61791","LSS","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","[^EXTENSION LETTER - BOLT.pdf] _(349 kB)_\n\n[^ADDENDUM CONTRACT TRANSPORT SERVICES - BOLT reviewed.docx] _(25 kB)_","2026-01-19T12:09:27.137Z"],["3820070","MVRT-1495","MVRT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:623de187d32a94006a658c4a] Awareness runs indefinitely, I will manage them month over month. Same way as performance ones, with no end date.","2026-01-19T12:09:31.262Z"],["3820073","LSS-61075","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you [~accountid:60bf496ea01e11006ac62a66] , I now have access.\n\nWas this already sent to the authorities?","2026-01-19T12:10:20.100Z"],["3820074","LSS-60855","LSS","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Hi! Thank you for the provided amendment draft.\n\nPlease check the comments on it from the partner’s financial team\n\n{quote}“1)Підкажіть, будь ласка, чи можуть ваші юристи \"полагодити\" перекрут між англійською та українською частинами договору? бо текст важко читати і виглядає це дуже дивно коли частину українського текста потрібно шукати в англійському варіанті:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 14.07.31.png|width=519,height=381,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 14.07.31.png\"!\n\n2)Не можна підписувати таку ДУ, бо та переписка, на яку посилається ДУ - це  погодження математики і ухилення від оформлення послуг з просування товарів та сплати податкових зобов'язань з ПДВ. Таку переписку не можна підкласти під Акт і ,за вимогою, показувати податківцям. \n\nУ даному періоді сторони не оформлювали жодних послуг зі стимулювання збуту\n\nСаме тому я пропонувала вигадати щось  інше,\n\n\"Наприклад, з метою підвищення зацікавленості Партнера у просуванні Додатка BOLT та збільшенні кількості замовлень через Додаток\" , замість посилання на послуги, які не оформили документально.\n\n3)Погодження будь яких послуг шляхом обміну електронними повідомленнями має бути таким, щоб ці повідомлення можна було показати податківцям, такі повідомлення мають додаватись до Акту наданих послуг і виконувати функцію угоди (але без підписання сторонами у Вчасно). В повідомленнях має бути погоджено: умови акцій, термін і місце проведення. Не можна домовлятись про математичне зарахування зустрічних акцій і не оформлювати кожну з них.”{quote}\n\nDo we need to involve UHY into this discussion?\n\n","2026-01-19T12:10:27.128Z"],["3820075","DRX-28024","DRX","jemma.muradyan@bolt.eu","Jemma Muradyan","FF is removed from tweaks, the CS webview is enabled.\n\n!IMG_0781.PNG|width=350,alt=\"IMG_0781.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_0780.PNG|width=350,alt=\"IMG_0780.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_0782.PNG|width=350,alt=\"IMG_0782.PNG\"!","2026-01-19T12:10:28.348Z"],["3820076","LSS-61784","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Thanks [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] noticing that deadline for submission phase 1 was yesterday, has the deadline been pushed? \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.07.31.png|width=578,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.07.31.png\"!","2026-01-19T12:10:28.964Z"],["3820077","SREP-1107","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","Tried to rollback karpenter to 1.7.1, doesn’t help, event occurs more rarely, but still happens.\n\nUpgrade to the latest 1.8.5 also doesn’t help.","2026-01-19T12:10:46.533Z"],["3820078","MVRT-1496","MVRT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:623de187d32a94006a658c4a] Apologies. \n\nDescription added.","2026-01-19T12:10:50.353Z"],["3820079","SREP-1107","SREP","igor.ignatev@bolt.eu","Igor Ignatev","Issue created [https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/issues/2803|https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/issues/2803|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:10:55.382Z"],["3820082","XP-3069","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","Action here is to fix the call, so that targeting is not called in case auth ID is not provided.\nSince we do not own the calling side and only act as a proxy, the action is to find the team that is responsible for the app and persuade it to take ownership of the backend methods.\nSo far I found [this thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0384T4FU1H/p1738670432705629?thread_ts=1738403874.603259&cid=C0384T4FU1H] and currently want to ask for the leads in the <#C04DRCGE3F0|>","2026-01-19T12:11:20.726Z"],["3820084","SRED-1080","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Last week inventories were switched.\n\nNow will run removal of sre-shell-agent.","2026-01-19T12:11:37.787Z"],["3820086","WFM-10037","WFM","leon.ouma@bolt-outsource.eu","Leon Ouma","[^List of agents onboarding.xlsx]","2026-01-19T12:12:01.913Z"],["3820087","CCM-22288","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hi Toyosi,\n\nWe have enrolled the agents in the requested course and updated their details accordingly. The course should appear in their LMS dashboard now.\n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else.\n\nRegards,\n\nThe CS Training team","2026-01-19T12:12:04.961Z"],["3820089","LO-179","LO","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Test contracts sent to Maarja 18.11.2025  [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D083LQKUACT/p1763462657659679|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D083LQKUACT/p1763462657659679|smart-link]  [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/10rX5DAxc_VXsCQAZnjPf-0HG2qJTdpNB|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/10rX5DAxc_VXsCQAZnjPf-0HG2qJTdpNB|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:12:24.494Z"],["3820091","XP-3069","XP","pavel.kiper@bolt.eu","Pavel Kiper","Can we return 400 for such calls?","2026-01-19T12:12:46.599Z"],["3820092","LSS-61666","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","hi Aleksandra, just checking if you remember about the documents to be signed today 😉 Thank you!","2026-01-19T12:13:00.404Z"],["3820095","PAW-14987","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-19T12:13:14.513Z"],["3820097","L10N-28740","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest contex