sions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28736](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28736)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:14:17.554Z"],["3820112","L10N-28767","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28736](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28736)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:14:20.294Z"],["3820118","MKP-9841","MKP","daniil.popov@bolt.eu","Daniil Popov","Hey! One more thing from my side. Order Offer is now used in (_almost_) all Matching flows. This means that {{createInWaitingDriverConfirmationState}} endpoint is unused and can be safely removed from your codebase.","2026-01-19T12:15:10.165Z"],["3820119","LSS-61108","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:10daa261-d587-4bee-926d-af5c022abc8e] ! Thanks so much for your patience 😊 The document will be sent tomorrow.","2026-01-19T12:15:10.952Z"],["3820120","MKP-9841","MKP",null,"Slack","[Daniil Popov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f4905b29aa9650046196c33] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1768817996321279?thread_ts=1768817996.321279&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1768817996321279?thread_ts=1768817996.321279&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T12:15:11.300Z"],["3820121","MKP-9841","MKP","jan.stoltman@bolt.eu","Jan Stoltman","jfyi [@boris.yartsev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5b839377eb18d0589b9b30d4]","2026-01-19T12:15:11.990Z"],["3820122","MKP-9841","MKP","boris.yartsev@bolt.eu","Boris Iartcev","Awesome!!!!","2026-01-19T12:15:12.936Z"],["3820123","MKP-9841","MKP","boris.yartsev@bolt.eu","Boris Iartcev","Thank you!","2026-01-19T12:15:13.974Z"],["3820124","MKP-9841","MKP","daniil.popov@bolt.eu","Daniil Popov","Nice. I am creating a ticket to do so.","2026-01-19T12:15:14.858Z"],["3820127","XP-3069","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","What will this solve? We are already returning an error to the client.\nI think that this we should offload this to the whatever team is responsible for the app.\nAlso we can actually override the altert not to trigger as it is not actionable.","2026-01-19T12:15:48.917Z"],["3820128","LSS-61666","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] ! The documents have been sent I am currently waiting for the DHL number","2026-01-19T12:15:53.886Z"],["3820129","LSS-61604","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba],\n\nCould you clarify your question and provide access to the link?\n\nTo be clear, please involve the privacy team only when necessary to protect our limited resources. Let us know if you have specific questions about our suggestions to address the issue. Otherwise, please proceed with our recommendations when completing the questionnaire.","2026-01-19T12:16:09.786Z"],["3820133","LO-201","LO","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Toolstack framework conflu [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/7291863439/Legal+Compliance+Toolstack+Framework|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/7291863439/Legal+Compliance+Toolstack+Framework|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:16:39.167Z"],["3820136","LSS-61108","LSS","lucian.andrei@bolt.eu","Lucian Andrei","Thank you, Aleksandra!🎉 ","2026-01-19T12:17:07.959Z"],["3820138","LO-200","LO","paula.pihelgas@bolt.eu","Paula Joanna Pihelgas","Update: Will be done in Zycus, once all contracts have been migrated there. ","2026-01-19T12:17:19.162Z"],["3820139","INT-803","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","26W3: (from business/GTM sicussions) in discussion with Rides growth (growth strategy and growth analytics) and local teams for rides campaigns approach in CA and potentially updating approach in NZ.","2026-01-19T12:17:22.747Z"],["3820140","CCM-22287","CCM","edwina@bolt.eu","Edwina Thebe","Hi Peace, \n\nThe agent has been enrolled in the requested course and profile information has been updated accordingly. \n\nPlease let us know if there is anything else. \n\nRegards, \n\nThe CS Training team ","2026-01-19T12:17:44.931Z"],["3820141","XP-3069","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","Created an [override|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/backend-alerting/overrides/edit/184196] with silencing the alert","2026-01-19T12:17:45.399Z"],["3820143","WD-22605","WD","laura.cedazo@bolt.eu","Laura Cedazo","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 12.54.05.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T12:17:47.763Z"],["3820145","XP-3069","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","Created [Override|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/backend-alerting/overrides/edit/184196]","2026-01-19T12:18:09.733Z"],["3820146","RLONE-479","RLONE","anton.berggren@bolt.eu","Anton Berggren","Hmm, I was wondering if Majorel iniatives and/or NPS process was related to this. But I think not as we have them as separate initiatives, kind off.\n\nMarking this as Done! ","2026-01-19T12:18:36.654Z"],["3820152","DLSP-2022","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","according to *Łukasz Wołodkiewicz* it should have been fixed\n\n!image-20260119-121813.png|width=903,alt=\"image-20260119-121813.png\"!","2026-01-19T12:19:27.042Z"],["3820153","LSS-61604","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","We need to attach a document (This) to the questionnaire. Could you either approve it as it is or edit it if needed (I see you suggested clarifying info on Bolt’s data security standards)?\nThank you!","2026-01-19T12:19:28.559Z"],["3820154","LSS-61604","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BoDIT1vm9Z9ZNy-btNp0JMDisv8j-HY_KForMhwpC1Q/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BoDIT1vm9Z9ZNy-btNp0JMDisv8j-HY_KForMhwpC1Q/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:19:35.575Z"],["3820157","MP-3506","MP","mirkamal.gasimov@bolt.eu","Mirkamal Gasimov","!image-20260119-122031.png|width=364,alt=\"image-20260119-122031.png\"!","2026-01-19T12:20:37.032Z"],["3820158","BIZ-283","BIZ","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi everyone!\n\nOverall from legal side - *Launch is legally feasible*, but with the following requirements:\n\n\n*Must-haves:*\n\n* Must operate via *Bolt Taiwan* (local entity) — cross-border from Estonia would violate the Company Act (criminal penalties apply)\n* *Cannot use a \"resale\" model* for transportation — Bolt doesn't hold a TT License.\n* Continue partnership with a TCS-licensed Fleet (same as current B2C model)\n\n*Invoicing approach:*\n\n* Transportation fees: Pass-through, no GUI required from Bolt (E-Receipt issued per ride via Fleet)\n* Service fees to corporate customers: Bolt Taiwan issues GUI (can be monthly/periodic — single invoice ✓)\n\n*Low-risk items (confirmed):*\n\n* Ride Booker / RB API: Same legal framework as current rider model\n* Restricting business customers from re-intermediating rides: No antitrust issue\n* B2B2C scenarios (e.g., hotel booking for guests): Low risk of being classified as dispatching\n\nFor your reference, please find the external analysis attached:\n\n [^Bolt Mail - Legal Questionnaire for Bolt Business launch in Taiwan (3).pdf]\n [^Bolt Mail - Legal Questionnaire for Bolt Business launch in Taiwan (4).pdf] \n\nPlease let me know if there are any further questions!","2026-01-19T12:20:52.736Z"],["3820159","PFI-835492","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260119-121753.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T12:21:05.283Z"],["3820161","HS-29103","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T12:21:35.030Z"],["3820165","WFM-10038","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","hey [~accountid:6156a567c5388b00694080f3] please let me know which queues are needed for the agent. We have: \n\nh2. 11 REG_Spain_Driver_Onboarding Registrations \n\nh2. 11 REG_Spain_Driver Registrations (contains documents resubmitted and submitted ) \n\nRole request was raised, waiting for appprval","2026-01-19T12:22:06.015Z"],["3820166","PFI-834177","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, thank you for raising the ticket; We were contacted by the Partners on this issue; I believe this issue should be resolved for all invoices going forward; please, let us, know if complaints persist","2026-01-19T12:22:07.970Z"],["3820167","HS-29096","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-19T12:22:18.193Z"],["3820168","ESL-1445","ESL","dan.muntean@bolt.eu","Dan-Iulian Muntean","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7421264091/Ingredients+allergens+nutritional+data|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7421264091/Ingredients+allergens+nutritional+data|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:22:21.161Z"],["3820169","LSS-61582","LSS","cristian.suciu@bolt.eu","Cristian Suciu","Hello, \n\nWhat does the process of becoming a civil party consist of ? \n\nAt the end of the day, Bolt spend resources in order to find the scooter, repair it and we’ve lost money with it not being on the street for several days. \nIt’s clear from everyone’s POV that the person did not have good intentions with the scooter.","2026-01-19T12:22:32.896Z"],["3820172","LSS-60756","LSS","alexandre.lancastre@bolt.eu","Alexandre Lancastre","Hey team,\n\nStill have not received any answer from your side, I need this to move forward asap.\n\n[~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] can you also support here?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlexandre Lancastre","2026-01-19T12:22:44.341Z"],["3820173","PFI-834177","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","To verify the validity of the fiscalization, please, use the: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-fiscalization/fiscalization/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"create_time_from_timestamp\"%3A1766181600%2C\"create_time_to_timestamp\"%3A1768825364.288}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-fiscalization/fiscalization/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22create_time_from_timestamp%22%3A1766181600%2C%22create_time_to_timestamp%22%3A1768825364.288%7D%7D]","2026-01-19T12:22:48.193Z"],["3820175","HS-29038","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent for signatures.","2026-01-19T12:22:59.628Z"],["3820177","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","after we've fixed up the model we will still however need to delete duplicates from fact_rides_order, because those duplicates are already created and the table is incremental\n\nmy idea was to mb drop everything for the last 5 days and rebackfill again, what do you think?","2026-01-19T12:23:08.398Z"],["3820179","HS-29084","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Not a re-hire task, waiting for PT to fix it.","2026-01-19T12:23:29.538Z"],["3820180","LSS-58409","LSS","alexandre.lancastre@bolt.eu","Alexandre Lancastre","Hey team,\n\nDo you have any news on this one?\n\n[~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] , also adding here for support.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlexandre Lancastre","2026-01-19T12:23:40.914Z"],["3820181","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","the other table, we can just full refresh afaiu with custom build afaiu and we should be good, however, if I'm wrong we might have to delete that int model too\n\njust wanted to let everyone know in advance","2026-01-19T12:23:57.272Z"],["3820182","FPD-1516","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Tested code once again after PR was approved, it all seems to be working. PR is now merged.","2026-01-19T12:24:07.211Z"],["3820186","LSS-61703","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] , thanks for raising this.\n\nAs the EU GDPR applies in the EU, our global assessments/privacy notices already cover what’s needed under the EU privacy law (/) I’ve done some research and it didn’t show that Malta has any additional restrictions set by local law.\n\nSo, in short, there are no issues with launching the feature from a privacy law POV.\n\nHowever, I have one question that’ll be important from accountability perspective: is there a law that requires us to do these checks (I am referring to “discussion with the Maltese legislation who requested this to be enabled for drivers”)? Or is this pressure from the regulators due to safety issues in the market? \n\nI’ve also double-checked the [Safety Features Prioritization framework,|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1JZFhbbnGtmo6q-GtB8xnflw33hLhDIWGlcIT969B8y0/edit?gid=1566258971#gid=1566258971] and it seems that driver selfie checks are not enabled in Malta due to other reasons, so please check with the team to investigate what those reasons might be 🙂 ","2026-01-19T12:24:21.917Z"],["3820187","MVRT-1486","MVRT","anton.sljussarev@bolt.eu","Anton Sljussarev","[~accountid:614ad8fe47a8b5006f846ec4] My mistake here. I’ve changed the assignee to myself now. \n\nThis is just a parent ticket to group all Meta ads tickets for BG.","2026-01-19T12:24:41.635Z"],["3820190","PFI-829960","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","Hi [~accountid:712020:a2bf14e3-f78c-4ef1-bcac-261cd3cd9ca7]  ,\n\nPlease find attached reissued invoices. \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6076511203?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6076511203?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\nThank you for submitting a ticket. \n\nBR,\nNikolay Roll ","2026-01-19T12:25:06.618Z"],["3820191","DSR-3825","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T12:26:07.449Z"],["3820194","MARTECH3-1315","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","*Update 19/01*\n\nCompleted all inputs for the [review document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bGrgB-gub7kR-Inho9R4H3ez5nHVyb5UrNUa3cd5mxM/edit?tab=t.0]. ","2026-01-19T12:26:15.344Z"],["3820197","RDXENG-4641","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:712020:23b54a2f-1913-42e1-9019-8b2c32303d27] \n\n(x) *Looks like placement is* *still a bit off and overlaps with nav bar*, [logs here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-150851]. Please check screenshot below:\n\n!capture-20260119-121748.png|width=205,alt=\"capture-20260119-121748.png\"!\n\n_Here is a comparison of same snack bar logic → deleting family profile scenario:_\n\n!capture (1)-20260119-121755.png|width=211,alt=\"capture (1)-20260119-121755.png\"!\n\n||*Device name*||Google Pixel 8a||\n|OS Version|16|\n|Client build|CA.194.0|\n|Comment|physical|","2026-01-19T12:27:15.164Z"],["3820198","LSS-61794","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[^Explanation letter.pdf] _(296 kB)_","2026-01-19T12:27:21.087Z"],["3820203","LSS-61793","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","Adding [~accountid:641aac4f9d6383e32a32c047] to check whether you or product legal would be responsible for this question","2026-01-19T12:27:57.827Z"],["3820204","PAW-15285","PAW",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the User Story!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-19T12:28:04.228Z"],["3820205","PFI-835496","PFI","ricardo.dias@bolt-outsource.eu","Ricardo Vieira Dias","!image-20260119-122835.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T12:28:13.476Z"],["3820206","PFI-835496","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T12:28:15.313Z"],["3820207","DO-5797","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","I will close the ticket tomorrow if it’s not approved yet","2026-01-19T12:28:26.832Z"],["3820216","FIN2-802","FIN2","wenjing.zhang@bolt.eu","Grace Wenjing Zhang","[~accountid:63a00ef0f3e7004f77fadf98] Could you please check if you can close this ticket?","2026-01-19T12:30:02.511Z"],["3820221","LSS-61793","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T12:31:08.610Z"],["3820222","WD-22427","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Case was submitted to Workday Support . Case Detail - 3117633","2026-01-19T12:31:21.906Z"],["3820225","DSR-3057","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], Ive moved the data prepared by Jens into the [folder|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QkNd4fmFRF8jWazYPXehlqc27kR4QQon] indicated. The data moved was the folder “report” and the “response”. Is this good to go? or am I lacking something? Thank you 🙏 ","2026-01-19T12:31:37.548Z"],["3820226","FIN2-768","FIN2","wenjing.zhang@bolt.eu","Grace Wenjing Zhang","[~accountid:63a00ef0f3e7004f77fadf98] could you please check if you can close this ticket?","2026-01-19T12:31:40.598Z"],["3820229","MVRT-1315","MVRT","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","Hii [~accountid:6101032e0b454a0068b57bef] can you share the detail of influencer that we are using for this? (instagram handle, post date, and cost). Thank you!","2026-01-19T12:32:03.393Z"],["3820230","DLSP-1764","DLSP","habib.fikri@bolt.eu","Fikri Sundayana","Need to update Ankit’s test account wrong document type:\n\n\n{code:sql}UPDATE `document` SET `document_type_id` = 30002 WHERE id = 6606339;{code}\n\n\n\n\n\nCurrently causing this:\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/courierComplianceChecks/300007|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-courier/courierComplianceChecks/300007]\n\n!image-20260119-123333.png|width=622,alt=\"image-20260119-123333.png\"!\n\nCurrently, the document has type {{330002}}, whereas it should be {{30002}}","2026-01-19T12:32:05.720Z"],["3820232","BIZ-297","BIZ","thiago.oliveira@bolt.eu","Thiago Ibrahim","Latest Update:\n[~accountid:62b2cf39566f3e7b0a8fa9b5] and [~accountid:628dd71f40b157006f734818] have started high-level discussions to amend the partner agreement to allow international cross-border rides in the UAE and Out.\nStill too early in the process, no timeline yet set. Waiting for their feedback from partner negotiation discussions, as this change includes other RH elements, not just BB.\n","2026-01-19T12:32:23.443Z"],["3820233","PFI-819935","PFI","alexander.medvedjev@bolt.eu","Alexander Medvedjev","Apologies, missed the letters. Solution works for me. Agree that it has to be then removed in the same week to avoid confusion. That should be on Ott’s side\n\n","2026-01-19T12:32:58.614Z"],["3820234","LSS-61666","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","great thank you!","2026-01-19T12:33:15.062Z"],["3820253","CCM-22289","CCM","sasha.caltagirone@bolt.eu","Sasha Caltagirone","[^Training Request Form Lithuania DE.xlsx]","2026-01-19T12:33:53.470Z"],["3820255","DRX-27820","DRX","jemma.muradyan@bolt.eu","Jemma Muradyan","Changes are reverted from driver, nothing to test.","2026-01-19T12:34:05.588Z"],["3820260","CASH-581","CASH","ivan.edrennikov@bolt.eu","Ivan Edrennikov","In Bank Of Georgia we are not searching for accounts by {{statement_identifier}} field, so we don’t need to do anything here.","2026-01-19T12:35:14.195Z"],["3820263","CSDA-295","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey!\n\nI created a temporary report - [Temp - Driver Impersonation Safety Cases|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29634?Case+State=-draft%2C-duplicate&Case+Created+%28UTC%29+Date=1+year+ago+for+1+year&Time+Grain=Year&Vertical=rides&Country+Name=]. Please review it; it should cover the major points requested. However, note that data for 2024 is not available. How important is it to include 2024 data?\n\nLooking forward to your reply!","2026-01-19T12:35:35.026Z"],["3820264","PFI-835502","PFI","anna.betina@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Betina","[^Payouts draft(2025) - Sheet1 (5).csv]","2026-01-19T12:35:36.204Z"],["3820270","PFI-835377","PFI","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] the payment does not reflect in the account","2026-01-19T12:36:11.239Z"],["3820274","FX-3670","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768826181557399]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3670 successfully transitioned to state 'To Do'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T12:36:34.131Z"],["3820275","BDB-1461","BDB","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:63e4c769614cb4ba5303b3e3] hello! The depth of Cashbacks and Discounts are still under review. Critical for prepping ooh media plan. Let me get back to you as this progresses; and acknowledged Alex’s away time 🙏  \n\nPlease let’s move the design work for the rest of the assets tho. Thank you!","2026-01-19T12:36:37.114Z"],["3820276","LSS-61421","LSS","ramil.maharramov@bolt.eu","Ramil Maharramov","No we don’t have them all. I suggest we keep that list issue flexible and what we count is the equivalent number of cars, and even that lets leave empty and adjustable as all will depend on the successful transfer of taxi permits from current owner, which depends on the decision of the regulator and leasing provider. Thanks\n\n","2026-01-19T12:36:51.036Z"],["3820277","PFI-835385","PFI","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] the payment does not reflect in the account\n\n","2026-01-19T12:36:58.068Z"],["3820278","PFI-811574","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, based on my understanding, the initial requirements about the amounts are satisfied?\n\nCould you, please, elaborate about which date should be on the invoice?","2026-01-19T12:37:01.171Z"],["3820280","PFI-835503","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T12:37:02.389Z"],["3820281","LSS-61096","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] and [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ,\n\nPlease wait a bit, I will ask supplier to updated the dates.\n\nThanks","2026-01-19T12:37:14.717Z"],["3820282","WD-22580","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","!image-20260119-123805.png|width=758,alt=\"image-20260119-123805.png\"!","2026-01-19T12:37:27.943Z"],["3820284","PFI-835391","PFI","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] the payment does not reflect in the account","2026-01-19T12:37:39.223Z"],["3820290","RCE-306","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768826289885339]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-306 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T12:38:22.270Z"],["3820295","DRX-28031","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please re-check these cases -\n* Lead can access to Home screen after registration (DRIVERAPP-T3727)\n* Lead can logout when they become drivers when congratulatory screen is displayed (DRIVERAPP-T3783)\n* Logout successfully as a lead (DRIVERAPP-T3786)\n* Lead can become a driver ","2026-01-19T12:39:19.976Z"],["3820299","PC-4711","PC","daniil.musienko@bolt.eu","Daniil Musienko","We migrated PayPal accounts in NL and CH to new merchant accounts on 15.01.","2026-01-19T12:39:57.663Z"],["3820301","CSDT-969","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","List of metrics that can be automated:\n\n* Schedule Adherence - old explores ✅ \n* Process adherence - old explores ✅ \n* Reopen rate - new explores, mart ✅ \n* Utilisation - old explores ✅ \n* Occupancy - old explores ✅ \n* Cost per ticket - new explores, mart ✅ \n* CS Cost as % of GMV - new explores, mart ✅ \n* Average handled cases per hour - TBA ❌ blocked by agent mart\n* Average handling time per case - new explores, mart ✅ \n* CSAT (Global) - new explores, mart ✅ \n* CSAT (Chaffeur) - new explores, mart ✅ \n* SLO Conformity Live: Under 30 Seconds - old explores ✅ \n* SLO Conformity non-Live: Under 6 Hours - old explores ✅ \n* First contact resolution rate - manual calculation in the sheet ❌ automation blocked because of lack of alignment\n* Overall T1 resolution rate - new explores, mart, but needs a fix first ❌ \n* Refunds & Compensations - new explores, mart ✅ \n* Refunds & Compensations as % of GMV - new explores, mart ✅ \n* Support requests per order (CCPO) - new explores, mart ✅ \n* Safety cases per 10 k order - new explores, mart ✅ ","2026-01-19T12:40:26.009Z"],["3820302","FDBT-4814","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-19T12:40:29.424Z"],["3820306","TS-4658","TS","oscar.ramos@bolt.eu","Oscar Ramos","While 1.5k for random catering is overkill, only having the end of evening option to eat can also have the opposite problem of too little option. We should still get some snacks / drinks to have while at ETK for in between activities, people enjoyed the wide array of vegan / savory / sweet options to hold them over till the evening last go around. ","2026-01-19T12:40:44.512Z"],["3820308","WD-22296","WD","deepak.chaturvedi@bolt.eu","Deepak Chaturvedi","Hello [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] ,\n\nI got the answer from our local accounting partner on per diem rates for domestic and international travel. \n\nFor Domestic travel, we can set up two rates as per high and low cost approach but for international travel it is not possible and we have to follow the list published by U.S. Department of State. The State Department does not publish a formal “high” or “low” categorisation; instead, rates vary by location.\n\nHi [~accountid:712020:264d351d-8f80-47e2-9be9-7f2ecf158e55] ,\n\nCould you please review the attached proposal and confirm if it looks fine for you ? \n\n\n\n[^US meal allowance overview.docx]\n\nRegards,\n\nDeepak","2026-01-19T12:40:55.306Z"],["3820311","PFI-817505","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nUnfortunately, we are not able to issue the refund to the OPM. \nSince we don’t have any volumes on the Cellulant KES account, we don’t have any balance to issue the refund. \n\nWe would suggest to find an alternative way to compensate the user or issue the refund from a more recent order instead. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-19T12:41:40.615Z"],["3820314","LSS-61604","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] - thank you, clear.\n\nWould it be acceptable if we review & approve the content tomorrow?","2026-01-19T12:42:06.537Z"],["3820316","PFI-835508","PFI","surachet.chaiwongkhajorn@bolt-outsource.eu","Surachet Chaiwongkhajorn","!image-20260119-124113.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T12:43:07.743Z"],["3820318","IOTTEAM-320","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Drokni works:\n{{D (30861) st_impl_bolt_can.c: 1287: pwrprofile: soc 62 temp0 22 temp1 22 temp2 21 min 21 lim 0 D (30862) scooter_task.c: 938: set brake current: old:15 new:15 soc:62 temp_low:0 err:0 D (35288) scooter_can_service.c: 5738: IOT_BUS_VOLTAGE 12133 D (35900) st_impl_bolt_can.c: 1287: pwrprofile: soc 62 temp0 22 temp1 22 temp2 22 min 22 lim 0 D (35901) scooter_task.c: 938: set brake current: old:15 new:15 soc:62 temp_low:0 err:0 D (35918) scooter_can_service.c: 6477: BMS_OUTPUT_STATUS:49841,0,2}}","2026-01-19T12:43:10.452Z"],["3820319","CSDA-258","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hi again!\n\nAlso, we now have the {{Rides Order Attributes}} in the *CS Refund & Compensation - Explorer*; here is the query for the refunds related to support cases with taxi orders linked - [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/customer_support/support_refund_compensation_explorer?qid=SehCctaekjsPyyGUcy1FO3&toggle=fil|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/customer_support/support_refund_compensation_explorer?qid=SehCctaekjsPyyGUcy1FO3&toggle=fil].\n\nPlease feel free to use it and build new ad-hoc reports if needed. Meanwhile, I will close this request. Please let us know if you have any further questions or comments. Have a productive week ✨","2026-01-19T12:43:15.336Z"],["3820320","CSDA-294","CSDA","zaur.ayralov@bolt.eu","Zaur Ayralov","Hey! [~accountid:5b7e76a8ed4f842a6ddb4fdb] \nI have created [ad-hoc dashboard |https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29637?Vertical+Grain=By+Vertical&Time+Grain=Month&Case+Created+%28UTC%29+Date=2+month+ago+for+2+month&Case+State=-draft%2C-duplicate&Country+Name=]with available metrics. We do not have order info for issue key level now , however it is in development , will be added soon.","2026-01-19T12:43:36.882Z"],["3820321","MARTECH3-1546","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","*Update 19/09*\n\nHad an initial discussion with Tomasz to understand the process. We considered building a cube table across all dimensions, but the number of dimension/value combinations would explode into billions of rows, making it impractical from a performance standpoint.\n\n*Next Steps*\n\nExplore the possibility of creating a parameter for each explore, something already implemented in one of the [Delivery views|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/projects/delivery/files/databricks_curated_views/metric_marts/metric_views/fact_delivery_non_additive.view.lkml?line=1]. ","2026-01-19T12:43:41.796Z"],["3820323","L10N-28774","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28773](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28773)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:44:17.047Z"],["3820324","L10N-28775","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28773](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28773)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:44:17.719Z"],["3820325","L10N-28777","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working 