or collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:44:28.213Z"],["3820335","L10N-28796","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28773](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28773)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:44:28.728Z"],["3820336","L10N-28797","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28773](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28773)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:44:29.036Z"],["3820337","L10N-28803","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28773](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28773)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T12:44:32.043Z"],["3820338","SRED-506","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Prelive was switched 3 months ago, now time for live.","2026-01-19T12:44:46.085Z"],["3820339","FRAUDOPS-1127","FRAUDOPS","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","{code:sql}WITH rider_changes AS \n(\n  SELECT \n    a.id,\n    CONCAT(\n      'https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fraud/calculations/user_destination_update/', \n      CAST(a.id AS varchar(255))\n    ) AS link_to_dest_change,\n    a.created,\n    a.meta.country,\n    a.meta.city_id,\n    a.meta.user_id,\n    get_json_object(a.input, '$.data.order_id') AS order_id,\n    CAST(\n      get_json_object(\n        a.input,\n        '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.order.price_prediction'\n      ) AS double\n    ) AS first_price_prediction,\n    CAST(\n      get_json_object(\n        a.input,\n        '$.data.price_prediction.amount'\n      ) AS double\n    ) AS last_price_prediction,\n    CASE\n      WHEN\n        CAST(\n          get_json_object(\n            a.input,\n            '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.order.price_prediction'\n          ) AS double\n        ) IS NOT NULL\n        AND CAST(\n          get_json_object(\n            a.input,\n            '$.data.price_prediction.amount'\n          ) AS double\n        ) IS NOT NULL\n        AND CAST(\n          get_json_object(\n            a.input,\n            '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.order.price_prediction'\n          ) AS double\n        ) > 0\n      THEN\n        CAST(\n          get_json_object(\n            a.input,\n            '$.data.price_prediction.amount'\n          ) AS double\n        )\n        /\n        CAST(\n          get_json_object(\n            a.input,\n            '$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.order.price_prediction'\n          ) AS double\n        )\n      ELSE NULL\n    END AS ratio_predictions,\n    get_json_object(a.input, '$.data.search_category_id') AS category_id,\n    get_json_object(a.input,'$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.business_payments.company_captured_payments.months_3.amount_in_eur') AS amount_in_eur,\n    get_json_object(a.input,'$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.business_details.company_created_age_in_days') AS company_age,\n    get_json_object(a.input,'$.query.corresponding_calculations.user_order_request.input.business_details.payment_type') as business_type\n  FROM sel_fraud_checks_pii_spark.user_destination_update a\n  WHERE a.created_date >= CAST(date_add(MONTH, -2, current_date) AS date)\n    AND a.decision.decision IN ('pass','adjust_auth')\n  QUALIFY row_number() OVER (\n    PARTITION BY \n      CAST(get_json_object(a.input, '$.data.order_id') AS varchar(255)) ||\n      CAST(a.meta.city_id AS varchar(255)) \n    ORDER BY a.created DESC\n  ) = 1\n)\nSELECT\n  co.created,\n  co.order_id,\n  co.city_id,\n  co.driver_courier_id,\n  co.driver_courier_fraud_label,\n  co.user_id,\n  rc.*,\n  co.user_price,\n  co.partner_price,\n  (co.partner_price - rc.first_price_prediction)/co.eur_currency_rate AS price_diff_eur,\n  coalesce(co.refund_amount,0) AS refund,\n  round(\n    CASE\n      WHEN co.is_current_failed_payment = TRUE\n        THEN co.uncovered_amount/co.eur_currency_rate\n      WHEN co.is_initial_chargeback = TRUE\n        OR co.is_payment_problem = TRUE\n        THEN co.partner_price_eur\n      ELSE 0\n    END\n  ) AS pay_problem_eur,\n  CASE\n    WHEN co.is_current_failed_payment = TRUE\n      OR co.is_initial_chargeback = TRUE\n      OR co.is_payment_problem = TRUE\n      OR co.refund_amount > 0\n      OR co.driver_courier_fraud_label = TRUE\n    THEN 1 ELSE 0\n  END AS flag_issue,\n  CONCAT(\n    'https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/',\n    CAST(co.order_id AS varchar(255)),\n    '/',\n    CAST(co.city_id AS varchar(255))\n  ) AS order_link\nFROM ng_public_spark.etl_denormalized_commerce_orders co \nLEFT JOIN rider_changes rc\n  ON rc.city_id = co.city_id \n  AND rc.user_id = co.user_id\n  AND rc.order_id = co.order_id\nWHERE co.created_date >= CAST(date_add(MONTH, -2, current_date) AS date)\n  AND co.created >= CAST(date_add(MONTH, -2, current_date) AS date)\n  AND CAST(rc.amount_in_eur AS DECIMAL(18,2)) < 300\n  --AND co.country_code = 'gb'\n  AND co.payment_method_group = 'business'\n  AND rc.business_type = 'credit_card'\n  AND rc.ratio_predictions > 5\n  --AND rc.category_id = '3564'{code}","2026-01-19T12:44:46.840Z"],["3820340","LSS-61075","LSS","kristina.pugaca@bolt.eu","Kristina Pugaca","[~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] No, we did not share it with the authorities. If it is an invitation to the court, we don’t share the information with the authorities.Please let us know if we should ","2026-01-19T12:44:51.477Z"],["3820343","PFI-834507","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Ales, thanks for reaching out. There are certain risks involved with new cards like this, which is why we require a successful 3DS verified transaction before we allow this card to be added on the family account. Please advise the user to set their card config to something like “always require confirmation“ or “always enforce SCA“ in the bank -> in order to trigger a 3DS verification. Once a verified transaction has been made (or the card has been added with said verification), they’ll be able to add it to their family account too.\n\nOtherwise they have to wait 20 days before being able to add the card.","2026-01-19T12:45:10.576Z"],["3820346","DAEN-1346","DAEN","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","{quote}after we’ve fixed up the model we will still however need to delete duplicates from fact_rides_order, because those duplicates are already created and the table is incremental\n\nmy idea was to mb drop everything for the last 5 days and rebackfill again, what do you think?{quote}\n\nWe can delete these already, as the current entries are not helpful anyway. Do you have a script ready?","2026-01-19T12:45:29.264Z"],["3820349","HS-29100","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:853cbe25-4d18-40c3-8211-69c3936bf72f], \n\nTravelPerk pulls your Preferred Name from Workday for your main profile. However, you must add your full legal name under 'Travel Documents,' which can be found by navigating to Profile → Wallet.\n\n!image-20260119-124253.png|width=933,alt=\"image-20260119-124253.png\"!\n\nClosing this ticket as there is no further action needed from People Operations. If you have questions regarding Travelperk, you can read [Travelperk guidelines|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/cALs7Q] or [raise a ticket to the procurement team|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1064]. \n\n\n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin ","2026-01-19T12:45:41.909Z"],["3820350","LSS-61795","LSS","annika.helimets@bolt.eu","Annika Helimets","[^EE_Fleet portal access agreement Eesti Kiirtoit OÜ.docx (1).asice.asice]\n\n","2026-01-19T12:45:58.283Z"],["3820353","LSS-61589","LSS","klaudia.bochenko@bolt.eu","Klaudia Bochenko","The issue was reported and handled based on internal communication with [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] . After reviewing the case, Marten confirmed that the user had received an incorrect negative balance of 7.85 PLN as a result of a known system issue related to failed refunds. Marten also confirmed that this issue had already been fixed on the engineering side and that no new cases had been observed since 29 November.\n\nMarten proposed two possible solutions to resolve the issue for the customer:\n\n* issuing a refund to the Bolt Balance via the CS team, or\n* issuing a refund to the original payment method from the payment where the user paid off the debt.\n\nFollowing this, the case was escalated to the PL Customer Support team. The assigned CS agent contacted the user and asked them to confirm their preferred refund method.\n\nThe user confirmed via [{color:#eae6ff}*Beehive*{color}|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/725949884][{color:#eae6ff} {color}|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/725949884]that they wished to receive the refund to their Bolt Balance. After receiving this confirmation, Marten coordinated with the CS team and confirmed that the refund was successfully processed.\n\nAll steps were taken in continuous consultation with  [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] \n\nRefund confirmation and beehive communication attached.\n\n\n!image-20260119-124505.png|width=1262,height=768,alt=\"image-20260119-124505.png\"!\n\n!image-20260119-124545.png|width=596,height=275,alt=\"image-20260119-124545.png\"!\n\n!image-20260119-124558.png|width=1622,height=542,alt=\"image-20260119-124558.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-19T12:46:39.203Z"],["3820355","TAXP-682","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1B2HAS59gjpk-g_HL1AKwW7NDH2IvJS6C|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1B2HAS59gjpk-g_HL1AKwW7NDH2IvJS6C|smart-link]  Done","2026-01-19T12:47:02.937Z"],["3820358","LSS-61604","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","sure, it works for us. Thanks!","2026-01-19T12:47:19.197Z"],["3820370","TAXP-643","TAXP","celia.kuria@bolt.eu","Celia Kuria-Kwach","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1B2HAS59gjpk-g_HL1AKwW7NDH2IvJS6C|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1B2HAS59gjpk-g_HL1AKwW7NDH2IvJS6C|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:48:50.527Z"],["3820373","BP-13321","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] In the banners, I have a button “Got it”, if an admin clicks on it, it removes it from the Dashboard. Will it happen on the dashboard to the spec Admin or for the entire company?\nAlso, [~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] wants the banner to be also in Billing page. Will it removes it from both or will admin needs to click on both banners? \nThe banner should be there only till spec date so even for Admins that do nothing, it will be removed. \n[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] do we have spec date for the banners to be removed from our side?","2026-01-19T12:49:02.526Z"],["3820381","LSS-61796","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[^2026.01.19 - PoA Bolt Baker McKenzie - Schenker.pdf] _(73 kB)_","2026-01-19T12:49:54.493Z"],["3820382","PFI-835518","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T12:50:11.604Z"],["3820384","LSS-61625","LSS","adela.ojeda@bolt.eu","Adela Ojeda","Hi team, \n\nFrom what I can see, the user reached out via the webform ([ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/701547179]), and the ticket was automatically closed due to not receiving an answer from her. I didn’t find any other contacts to CS from the user related to this matter.\n\n[This|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/820800276/862?orderTryId=979326356] is the order and I see that the trip finished at the destination selected by the user, apparently with no issues since we weren’t contacted by the driver either.\n\nWe can reach out to the driver to double-check that there weren’t any issues with the trip to make sure.\n\n!image-20260119-124913.png|width=642,height=567,alt=\"image-20260119-124913.png\"!\n\n!image-20260119-124859.png|width=648,height=568,alt=\"image-20260119-124859.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-19T12:50:27.088Z"],["3820385","CSDA-297","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey! This topic was raised a few times before; sharing here what was shared previously in case it can help too:\n\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04D54E3W84/p1752070180460139?thread_ts=1751886999.542149&cid=C04D54E3W84|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04D54E3W84/p1752070180460139?thread_ts=1751886999.542149&cid=C04D54E3W84|smart-link] (in case you don’t have access to this channel, I added the screenshot and the attachment to this comment)\n** [^promo_code_generator_data.2025.csv] & \n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.20.10.png|width=1206,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.20.10.png\"!\n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1074/CSDA-42|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1074/CSDA-42|smart-link] (added you there too).\n\nMeanwhile, I will work on pulling the recent data - will share here the stats either later today or tomorrow 🙌 ","2026-01-19T12:50:51.870Z"],["3820390","DPM-2317","DPM","dmitri.gaisan@bolt.eu","Dmitri Gaisan","It seems like we forgot to set properly price_measure_unit argument when calling Selling Price Editing API on BE. \n\nFor restaurants we need to default to {{SellingMeasureUnit.PIECE}}","2026-01-19T12:51:27.822Z"],["3820392","PAR-484","PAR","volodymyr.hadomskyi@bolt.eu","Volodymyr Hadomskyi","Following a reassessment by the Expansion leadership team, the Vietnam market has been removed from the launch roadmap and this epic is being rejected/closed.\n\nDespite the business case approval in March 2024 and significant cross-functional progress, the launch decision has changed due to:\n\n* Ongoing regulatory uncertainty, with unclear and challenging processes at multiple stages\n* A materially shifted competitive landscape, including increased investment by local player GSM and regulatory changes impacting the original EV-based business case\n* A higher central bar for new market investments where efficiency, long-term security, and return on investment are less certain\n\nVietnam is now considered a no-go market unless there is a meaningful change in policy or market conditions. A structured wind-down and post-mortem will be conducted, with outcomes to be shared once completed.\n\nSlack: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07JHFT61MW/p1767610604580399|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07JHFT61MW/p1767610604580399|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:52:00.683Z"],["3820394","CCM-22289","CCM","refilwe@bolt.eu","Refilwe Masanabo","Hello Sasha. The agent is now enrolled to the Food Delivery onboarding.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-19T12:52:05.130Z"],["3820397","PFI-835522","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-19T12:52:34.500Z"],["3820399","LSS-61797","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","[^Bolt Bank Mandate South Africa.docx] _(17 kB)_","2026-01-19T12:52:37.974Z"],["3820400","DBRE-8642","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Master switch announcements:\n\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CH2LCDA69/p1768827102877569|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CH2LCDA69/p1768827102877569|smart-link]\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768827112386479|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768827112386479|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:52:42.777Z"],["3820402","BP-13415","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] this task is done, can you check if all is clear? I made only one design as an example. In the file you can find, the exact location where to put the banner for each email.\n [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UOCSjtpyJn3MFPPxphjO6GReVe73N-QlIqJVAyG3kwU/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UOCSjtpyJn3MFPPxphjO6GReVe73N-QlIqJVAyG3kwU/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link]","2026-01-19T12:52:48.999Z"],["3820404","CNT-339","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","Published: [https://bolt.eu/en/blog/bolt-engineering-estonia/|https://bolt.eu/en/blog/bolt-engineering-estonia/|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T12:53:31.345Z"],["3820407","LSS-55769","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] supplier already sent doc for singing to Ahto. Could you please find it and support with signing ? ","2026-01-19T12:53:33.466Z"],["3820410","PFI-830556","PFI","joana.duo@bolt.eu","Joana Duó","Any update on [~accountid:5fec8943d364960139859c11] question? ","2026-01-19T12:53:43.312Z"],["3820411","PFI-834210","PFI","anastasiya.ivanova@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Ivanova","Where do you see blank country? ","2026-01-19T12:53:44.320Z"],["3820412","HS-29114","HS","dijo.joseph@bolt.eu","Dijo Joseph","[^discharge summary.pdf]\n\n[^lab report.pdf]\n\n[^medical certificate.pdf]","2026-01-19T12:54:01.960Z"],["3820413","CMO-12950","CMO","nigel.janssen@bolt.eu","Nigel Janssen","[TTT framework WiP|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17dguaW3UIT_LsGaufs2f_Ug0fCMndoJpT8bH6cVLEfY/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-19T12:54:34.695Z"],["3820418","LSS-61767","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3033a882e2be49d95a] ,\n\nAll god from legal side and we can proceed with signatures. Please provide information regarding counterparty signatory (name & email).","2026-01-19T12:56:29.810Z"],["3820421","PFI-834549","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe are unable to complete the refund on this payment due to some technical issues with the payment service provider. Could you please help refund the customer on a different order or offer a different type of compensation to the user?","2026-01-19T12:57:05.514Z"],["3820424","RS-1906","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] ,\n\nWe agreed to rely on your analysis and accept the legal basis. Can you please confirm if all of them can be considered valid legal basis when cited individually?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T12:57:31.645Z"],["3820426","MARTECH3-1401","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","*Update 19/01*\n\nWorked on the initial version of the document: [+Page: [WIP] Meta CLS Experiment Creator - User Guide+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7421198826/WIP+Meta+CLS+Experiment+Creator+-+User+Guide]\n\n*Next Steps*\n\nComplete the documentation","2026-01-19T12:57:49.076Z"],["3820433","HS-29091","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hi Zankyang, thank you for the template. So Our PP will sign this letter, but to whom shall we send it? Can you share the email please. ","2026-01-19T12:58:16.704Z"],["3820434","PFI-834565","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T12:58:16.738Z"],["3820435","LSS-59767","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:5de3bf86-6cba-4bd9-b71a-087b2b4da2eb] alright, if no sensitive data is being handled this should be fine.\n\n\n\n* *_Section 18 notification carve-out:_*\n_could you request a change of clause 18: notification obligation should apply_ *_only to the extent legally permitted_*_, to avoid conflicts with laws or legal orders that prohibit notice (e.g. gag orders, regulatory secrecy obligations)._\n\nhas this been included now? If yes, please attach the new Agreement here and we can collect signatures!","2026-01-19T12:58:31.539Z"],["3820436","DAEN-1346","DAEN","siddhant.saxena@bolt.eu","Siddhant Saxena","[@yuriy.trofymenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:ea34e25e-5aed-4ec5-8c46-0238dbead6e3] , any ETA around when the marts will be ready after the fix is implemented?\nDoes today look unlikely?","2026-01-19T12:58:39.986Z"],["3820437","RCE-359","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Kairi Hennoch [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768827507006309]*{color}:\nI see nothing suspicious for that date on our end. The amount of generated external order id's for 2025-10-16 is less than 400k, and even if they count all the reported order events, there is still only slightly over 1 million of those. As far as I can tell, no modifications to that service or outages have happened in that timeframe either, so my current suspicion is that they are miscounting somehow on their end, especially if it's only for that one date. <@U9T7W8KUP> please let me know if Anya responds with additional details.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T12:58:41.717Z"],["3820443","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:dc8e54ad-0402-41f9-ba6e-9f25f8b451bf] , [~accountid:712020:ed0860b7-47ec-4834-8e13-d50d5463df29] ,\n\nThanks again for all the context information you provided. On my side, I also got information on our commitments to accessibility from central legal. \n\nWith all these inputs, I prepared a formal response to the customer, that you can find [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gIrN0cDDOUHNfQ5Nqoy0fD4sQSlK0Rc56oosIbltv_c/edit?usp=sharing].\n\nPlease let me know if you have any comments or questions.\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nAngela","2026-01-19T12:59:49.879Z"],["3820445","UKIGFT-101","UKIGFT","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","*Status / Background*\n\n* The break date under each of the three leases (2F, 3F and 4F) is *20 July 2026*.\n* Break notices were served on the landlord on *Friday, 16 January 2026*, confirming Bolt’s intention to exit on the break date. A process server was instructed to ensure certainty of service.\n* Copies of the notices were also provided to:\n** *Aviva Investors Global Services Ltd* (as required under the 2F lease and, for completeness, in respect of the 3F and 4F leases); and\n** The landlord’s managing agent, *JLL Limited*, to facilitate prompt handling.\n\n*KITT MSAs*\n\n* The KITT MSAs terminate automatically (without notice) on termination of the underlying lease agreements.\n* The business team is considering the appropriate timing for communicating this to KITT.\n\n*Next steps / Exit obligations*\n\n* A full review of the lease agreements to confirm all exit obligations will be carried out in due course.\n* Key break conditions identified at this stage include:\n** *Payment of rent:* The full quarterly rent due on *24 June 2026* (covering 24 June – 24 September 2026) for each floor must be paid in full, including VAT. Rent cannot be pro-rated. The landlord is required to refund the period from *21 July – 24 September 2026*, together with any overpaid insurance rent.\n** *Vacant possession:* Bolt must give up vacant possession of the premises on the break date.","2026-01-19T13:00:03.206Z"],["3820446","HS-29114","HS","dijo.joseph@bolt.eu","Dijo Joseph","Sorry, I made a typo in the above. The leave request if from 2 Jan 2026 to 16 Jan 2026 - both dates inclusive. I am working from home today. I have made the application on workday too.","2026-01-19T13:00:09.171Z"],["3820449","PFI-830556","PFI","rita.goncalves@bolt.eu","Rita Teles Gonçalves","Hi [~accountid:712020:9d55cde8-4889-4cc5-9d25-472a197c7697], I’ve made the change and the payments went through, so it’s better to check if this is a rule to be reviewed (maybe in a dedicated channel, as the ticket is closed).\nAnd please warn us if something changes.\nThank you","2026-01-19T13:00:20.540Z"],["3820451","PFI-835518","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-19T13:00:48.032Z"],["3820452","DBRE-8676","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Docs updated: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/6513590981/MySQL+custom+export|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/6513590981/MySQL+custom+export|smart-link].","2026-01-19T13:01:06.808Z"],["3820455","SREDESK-7425","SREDESK","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* DB schema was supposed to be shared [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1768567157014459|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1768567157014459|smart-link] \n* Adjusted meta for shared schema\n\n{noformat}root@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM taxify_delivery_courier_activity._meta;\n+----------------------------------+------------+--------+\n| schema_structure_name            | code_owner | shards |\n|----------------------------------+------------+--------|\n| taxify_delivery_courier_activity |            |        |\n+----------------------------------+------------+--------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.019s\nroot@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>UPDATE taxify_delivery_courier_activity._meta SET shards='deliveryglobal,deliveryafrica';\nYou're about to run a destructive command.\nDo you want to proceed? (y/n): y\nYour call!\nQuery OK, 1 row affected\nTime: 0.006s\nroot@ti-prelive-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM taxify_delivery_courier_activity._meta;\n+----------------------------------+------------+-------------------------------+\n| schema_structure_name            | code_owner | shards                        |\n|----------------------------------+------------+-------------------------------|\n| taxify_delivery_courier_activity |            | deliveryglobal,deliveryafrica |\n+----------------------------------+------------+-------------------------------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.007s\n\n---\n\nroot@ti-delivery-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM taxify_delivery_courier_activity._meta;\n+----------------------------------+------------+--------+\n| schema_structure_name            | code_owner | shards |\n|----------------------------------+------------+--------|\n| taxify_delivery_courier_activity |            |        |\n+----------------------------------+------------+--------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.010s\n\nroot@ti-delivery-dba.sqldb:(none)>UPDATE taxify_delivery_courier_activity._meta SET shards='deliveryglobal,deliveryafrica';\nYou're about to run a destructive command.\nDo you want to proceed? (y/n): y\nYour call!\nQuery OK, 1 row affected\nTime: 0.005s\n\nroot@ti-delivery-dba.sqldb:(none)>SELECT * FROM taxify_delivery_courier_activity._meta;\n+----------------------------------+------------+-------------------------------+\n| schema_structure_name            | code_owner | shards                        |\n|----------------------------------+------------+-------------------------------|\n| taxify_delivery_courier_activity |            | deliveryglobal,deliveryafrica |\n+----------------------------------+------------+-------------------------------+\n1 row in set\nTime: 0.006s{noformat}","2026-01-19T13:01:12.262Z"],["3820456","LSS-55769","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] , signed from Ahto’s side\n\n[^Bolt_x_Paylead_-_Insertion_order_additionnal_budget.pdf] ","2026-01-19T13:01:14.087Z"],["3820457","DSR-3827","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T13:01:16.472Z"],["3820458","DSR-3829","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T13:01:16.510Z"],["3820459","BP-13472","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101488?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101488?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:01:37.693Z"],["3820463","PAW-14989","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-19T13:01:59.837Z"],["3820466","WEBSD-1487","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:03b9dd47-a13b-4694-b2eb-fcd7e49b9c60] \n\nCould you tell me what is the update from that document?\n\n*We have removed a document requirement*\n\nRegards,\n\nHector","2026-01-19T13:03:05.762Z"],["3820469","PFI-835539","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T13:03:18.874Z"],["3820476","WD-22607","WD","maryna.bezuhla@bolt.eu","Maryna Bezuhla","*in Workday","2026-01-19T13:04:43.263Z"],["3820477","HS-28911","HS","miina.kutta@bolt.eu","Miina Kutta","Hey, attaching the documents here. \n\n[~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb] , please help out with signing and stamping the documents! Thank you!!\n\nLet me know if i can help out with anything else.\n\n\n\n[^Dariush Hossein Poursiami Zaświadczenie o zatrudnieniu.pdf]\n[^Dariush Hossein Poursiami PKO.pdf]\n[^Dariush Hossein Poursiami Employment Confirmation Letter 19.01.2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T13:04:47.007Z"],["3820482","LSS-61275","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[^2026-01-19 atsakymas P. Vazniokas (VVTAT) (1).pdf]\n[^Priedas Nr. 2 Nr. 7G-7754.pdf]\n[^Priedas Nr. 1 7G-7754 (Invoices).pdf]\n\nResponse was sent to the authority.","2026-01-19T13:05:38.247Z"],["3820483","FX-3384","FX","jana.lutus@bolt.eu","Jana Lutus","Thanks for the ping. I’ll provide the answer in the relevant ticket if that’s okay with you ","2026-01-19T13:05:37.619Z"],["3820485","DSR-3831","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T13:06:07.764Z"],["3820488","LSS-61794","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] , Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Explanation letter (a32bac1b-65db-43f4-88ea-5b27ec72a1b9).pdf] ","2026-01-19T13:06:22.216Z"],["3820493","WAVE-229","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","+ release version creation help to identify why commit hashes were pushed to Sentry","2026-01-19T13:07:10.375Z"],["3820496","DSR-3831","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Data sent","2026-01-19T13:07:20.520Z"],["3820497","PFI-834631","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe debt comes from the next order [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2342657233/307?orderTryId=3012923310|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2342657233/307?orderTryId=3012923310] which was partially charged from the user’s Blik payment method and the remaining amount charged as a negative Bolt balance.\n\nThe refund of the PLN 20.07 was successfully completed to the user’s payment method. \n\n[^Refund_Letter_C88BL2FJ2T7ZXQF3_FK75QHVVP29VSJF6.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T13:07:32.833Z"],["3820500","TS-4658","TS","aleksandr.bregin@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Bregin","Yes, we will definitely get a few bags from Selver or wherever, with some chips-sweets-veggies maybe.","2026-01-19T13:08:05.293Z"],["3820501","MVRT-1319","MVRT","kertu.vill@bolt.eu","Kertu Vill","Influencer: [https://www.instagram.com/liisvelsker/|https://www.instagram.com/liisvelsker/|smart-link] \nInfluencer post: [https://www.instagram.com/reel/DTQqTikgigH/|https://www.instagram.com/reel/DTQqTikgigH/|smart-link] \n\n- €1000\n- 32.2k impressions","2026-01-19T13:08:09.636Z"],["3820505","MVRT-1315","MVRT","kertu.vill@bolt.eu","Kertu Vill","[~accountid:712020:9c4c0927-aeb3-4a47-9ea9-68428dc00be8] Hey\n\nadded it here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MVRT-1319?focusedCommentId=3820501|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MVRT-1319?focusedCommentId=3820501|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:08:27.621Z"],["3820507","LSS-61799","LSS","anastasiia.mirovednikova@bolt.eu","Anastasiia Mirovednikova","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 14.56.58.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:08:41.831Z"],["3820509","DRX-28259","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: according to the ticket","2026-01-19T13:08:54.566Z"],["3820511","PFI-835546","PFI","tuukka.tammela@bolt.eu","Tuukka Tammela","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 15.09.15.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:09:30.901Z"],["3820515","PC-2334","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n- Same topic is planned as part of PI improvements in 2026 ","2026-01-19T13:10:13.770Z"],["3820516","PFI-835210","PFI","kutlwano.tsetsewa@bolt.eu","Kutlwano Tsetsewa","Sorry, the billing type is currently driver-based, and the fleet owner now needs it to be fleet based. ","2026-01-19T13:10:30.170Z"],["3820518","PFI-835210","PFI","kutlwano.tsetsewa@bolt.eu","Kutlwano Tsetsewa","[~accountid:627cf5040d1e73006f7d2aa9] ","2026-01-19T13:10:45.192Z"],["3820520","CMP-37","CMP","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-31\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nMobile Development for IOS finished. Finalizing backend API after changes brought by mobile infrastructure redesign.\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\nDesigns\n• :xp-done:https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C097HCK3CSG/p1760011090183869 ( V2 published)\nUser Insights & Privacy\n• :xp-done: Service initial setup\n• :xp-done: Admin Panel configuration APis\n• :xp-done: Admin Panel configuration views\n• :xp-done: CrowdIn sync setup\n• :loading: Mobile Apis - waiting for mobile app api to be finished\n• :next: Integration with MarTech In-Apps\nMobile Platform/Vertical mobile teams\n• :xp-done: Mobile requirements are documented https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/6832752299/In-App+Survey+Mobile+Requirements (here).\n• :xp-done: BEUI contract is available in the https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-rfc/pull/1223/files (Bolt-RFC) repo.\n• Mobile SDK status:\n• :white_check_mark: BoltSurvey SDK architecture skeleton (Identity)\n• :white_check_mark: BoltSurveyDevHost app (Identity)\n• :white_check_mark: Integrating main UI components (Identity)\n• :white_check_mark: Integrating FormConditionals & ViewBuilders (Mobile Platform, ETA W46 W49)\n• :white_check_mark: Implementing FormTextArea (Mobile Platform, ETA W46 W49)\n• :white_check_mark: Integrating new Mobile Platform components into Survey SDK (Identity, both BE + SDK work, ETA W48 W51)\n    ◦ :white_check_mark: Work on the rating component. It will be made custom to support RTL\n• :white_check_mark: Integrate deeplink\n• :next: IOS testing planned for end of January\n","2026-01-19T13:11:32.530Z"],["3820522","EBIKE1-376","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","I remade simulation from beginning test different contact and support options, also [~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] check and seemed that simualtion setup is good.  [~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] will also check what Simscale will show.\nMean while I also wrote to YiYou to make sure that they made the test according to our requirements. ","2026-01-19T13:11:43.007Z"],["3820523","LSS-61323","LSS","ab.moula@bolt.eu","AB Moula","Thanks Lisa. I raised 1 comment relating to a new suggestion. Please let me know if it’s unclear. Thanks ","2026-01-19T13:11:52.633Z"],["3820527","LEG-1325","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Internal comment as an insight from 19 Jan call: from Tax pov, the research will need to be run whether the coupons will be run as a payment method or not. The consequence: if it’s a payment method, then for EU tax authorities it is not considered vouchers, and then we don’t need to issue invoices.\n\n* VAT is not paid on coupons\n* VAT is paid on Rides","2026-01-19T13:12:21.362Z"],["3820528","RS-1949","RS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","Thanks for redirecting some of this questions [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] ! i will wait for the rest of the answers","2026-01-19T13:12:30.045Z"],["3820531","RDXENG-4721","RDXENG","pavel.panarad@bolt.eu","Pavel Panarad","This was seen during the demo, but I’m unable to reproduce","2026-01-19T13:12:59.181Z"],["3820533","RNTL-30527","RNTL","aleksei.antonov@bolt.eu","Aleksei Antonov","moved to duty, the issue with the component is not related to the driving score feature","2026-01-19T13:13:46.735Z"],["3820535","PFI-835549","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","!Transaction Receipt-260119020100360557268196.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:14:01.744Z"],["3820538","LSS-61798","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","I also need the copy of the articles of association / memorandum of association please","2026-01-19T13:14:44.454Z"],["3820540","DGD-171","DGD","friedrich.vogt@bolt.eu","Friedrich Vogt","The results are documented [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKH3tTmB5HSiFdAWjgisirlB9dzdyD_k-QYZAfo9PvY/edit?tab=t.0]. \n\nTLDR: This first iteration of uplift modeling proves little to no value over the current targeting. There are some minor gains we see for the churning cohort, although these only make up a smaller share of the spend (~10%). The holdout data that was used for this modeling task suffered from violations that likely affect modeling results. We should strive for a clean holdout setup, ideally with a DEX-like randomization at various discount depths to allow for user level sensitivity estimations, and revisit this task once the data is available.","2026-01-19T13:15:33.930Z"],["3820542","BP-13321","BP","daria.zaichykova@bolt.eu","Daria Zaichykova","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] no date yet. The preliminary estimations is 2 billing cycles (to remove mid-March), but we can circle back if we understand we need this to stay on longer.\n\n[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] can we exclude companies with first ride after {{2026-01-01}}? this wouldn’t make any sense for them","2026-01-19T13:15:39.742Z"],["3820543","WFM-10038","WFM","david.ramon@bolt.eu","David Ramon","The agent needs both of them to make driver leads through Beehive.","2026-01-19T13:15:48.392Z"],["3820545","PFI-835550","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","!Transaction Receipt-260119020100361203866799.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:16:09.204Z"],["3820546","DRAG101-428","DRAG101","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","* [2D of the bracket|https://drive.google.com/open?id=10KDXyz_B50FHlOroamdJmaXCW_qIfsnO&usp=drive_fs] has been updated\n* 2D and 3D have been revised from R00 to R01\n* New bracket has been added to the BOM","2026-01-19T13:16:18.154Z"],["3820548","PFI-835551","PFI","victory.odeh@bolt-outsource.eu","Victory Odeh","!image-20260119-131633.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:16:57.961Z"],["3820549","DCOR-244","DCOR","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","W2\n\nFirst batches of lists received from Geo. Will start with manual annotations to teach the model.\n\nThe initial plan was to launch a pilot in PT & RO however, we will have to get a final alignment with PT local legal. For RO, we will try to start with execution once the local team confirms.","2026-01-19T13:17:09.344Z"],["3820550","LSS-61698","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ,\n\nAs far as I see it, it’s an invitation to a hearing. Please correct me if I’m wrong. I think this should be redirected to OC (Faruq Abbas <[foa@abdu-salaamabbasandco.com|mailto:foa@abdu-salaamabbasandco.com]  or  George Ayanjompe <[george@abdu-salaamabbasandco.com|mailto:george@abdu-salaamabbasandco.com]). \n\nShould this be sent to both emails, or is one of them sufficient?\n\n [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] have we communicated the new process to CS?","2026-01-19T13:17:20.523Z"],["3820551","PFI-834634","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nCould you advise the user to provide a bank statement showing the charged amount with the first 8 and last 4 digits of the debited card as well as the bank name? This will help us investigate this case further.","2026-01-19T13:17:24.497Z"],["3820553","LSS-55769","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] , there is fully executed contract\n\n[^Bolt_x_Paylead_-_Insertion_order_additionnal_budget (1).pdf] ","2026-01-19T13:17:34.975Z"],["3820554","LSS-61602","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] - hey! Please find the signed doc attached. Have a great week!\n\n[^Branding Contract (Fleet)_Bolt Operations OÜ_Mietwagenunternehmen_15.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-19T13:17:55.400Z"],["3820555","PC-2642","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* Cleanup duplicate data from the notification\n* Update data in payment core table\n* An engineer will pick up ","2026-01-19T13:18:03.270Z"],["3820556","FRAUD-5400","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","*Remaining*\n\nConfigure an alert for user hard block action in “already_applied” state","2026-01-19T13:18:08.049Z"],["3820560","PFI-835559","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","!Transaction Receipt-260119020100356031424683.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:18:36.100Z"],["3820561","WFM-10042","WFM","gerda.morkvenaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Gerda Morkvenaite","[^list of agents (1).xlsx]","2026-01-19T13:18:46.614Z"],["3820563","LSS-61589","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Many thanks for this update [~accountid:712020:38ef5817-1c12-4bf5-b0d1-116b99b69ddf] ! I will draft a responding letter based on these facts until Friday, this week. As this issue has been resulted from an IT error, I would not change the T&C and keep them as they are.  \n\nStay tuned\n\nBest, Jola 😇 ","2026-01-19T13:19:16.620Z"],["3820565","LSS-61796","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^2026.01.19 - PoA Bolt Baker McKenzie - Schenker (c0bd845d-d5d5-471f-81ea-15ddadea1dec).pdf] ","2026-01-19T13:19:21.513Z"],["3820567","WD-22580","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:c8f6d6ec-ae4a-4cf3-9078-0632b32a5d28] ! Invoices are in draft status because of validations, which were introduced 2024. My understanding, that it is expected behavior. \n\n\n\n!image-20260119-131132.png|width=778,alt=\"image-20260119-131132.png\"!\n\nI see that previous invoices were also in draft status because of validations. For example this invoice was created on 30/05/2025 , then you manually updated it on 04/06/2025 \n\n!image-20260119-131728.png|width=1067,alt=\"image-20260119-131728.png\"!\n\n\n\nAnd validations are in place to make sure the correctness of tax details. \n\nCould you please give more details what is the issue about? So far I understand that WD works as expected. \n\nThank you in advance! ","2026-01-19T13:19:28.519Z"],["3820568","DPX-3539","DPX","wahaj.baig@bolt.eu","Wahaj Baig","Column names in Fact_provider_hourly/daily_v2\n\nNot Responded Order Value:\n\n{{total_provider_price_before_discounts_not_responded_orders}}\n\n{{total_provider_price_before_discounts_not_responded_orders_eur}}\n\nRejected Order Value\n\n{{total_provider_price_before_discounts_rejected_orders}}\n\n{{total_provider_price_before_discounts_rejected_orders_eur}}","2026-01-19T13:20:06.461Z"],["3820569","PFI-796115","PFI","janek.vassin@bolt.eu","Janek Vassin","[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] hey! any luck?","2026-01-19T13:20:18.561Z"],["3820573","DCOR-369","DCOR","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","Due to dependency from logistics eng ETA was pushed back. Should receive an update from LCM mid Feb & hopefully we will be ready by then.","2026-01-19T13:20:47.010Z"],["3820576","BP-13321","BP","daria.zaichykova@bolt.eu","Daria Zaichykova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] which info for the banner placement do you need for the Emails? If the info in the [Table|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UOCSjtpyJn3MFPPxphjO6GReVe73N-QlIqJVAyG3kwU/edit?gid=0#gid=0] is enough, let me know. I will update the info there","2026-01-19T13:21:07.361Z"],["3820583","LSS-61698","LSS","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Hey!\n\nNo we’ve not communicated the new process to CS. We’ve not even drafted guidelines for the Police and external counsel. Until the Police and External Counsel receive guidelines on the new approach to data requests, there’s no point for CS to redirect them. This can cause further confusion as the external counsel doesn’t know yet what’s expected of them. ","2026-01-19T13:21:55.899Z"],["3820585","PFI-796115","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, it is reissued with 24%. Please, find updated invoice in Admin","2026-01-19T13:21:58.147Z"],["3820590","LSS-61666","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","DHL: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=9941317816&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=9941317816&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:22:55.519Z"],["3820591","PFI-834635","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-19T13:23:00.411Z"],["3820592","GRACQ-405","GRACQ","dzmitry.ulezla@bolt.eu","Dzmitry Ulezla","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/PwDMuAE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/PwDMuAE|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:23:09.421Z"],["3820594","PFI-835560","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-19T13:23:27.328Z"],["3820595","LSS-60756","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:793bd952-a372-4264-98c5-05f34ecedce8] ,\n\nI’ll look into it, and I’ll try to get back to you ASAP.","2026-01-19T13:23:44.390Z"],["3820596","PFI-835561","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","!ICON_732270.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:23:52.497Z"],["3820602","PFI-835562","PFI","victory.odeh@bolt-outsource.eu","Victory Odeh","!image-20260119-132354.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:24:20.760Z"],["3820603","PAW-14944","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-19T13:24:31.611Z"],["3820604","LSS-61743","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] \n\n# Are we good to proceed with this NDA for private persons or we have something AV specific developed ? [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bAC6lEPpb8ULu7qnYWgInqIEpHmcx2UDCdB4qFwjAUo/template/preview|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bAC6lEPpb8ULu7qnYWgInqIEpHmcx2UDCdB4qFwjAUo/template/preview|smart-link] \n# Is there a need to enter into separate NDA or we can rely on employment agreement and that’s it? ","2026-01-19T13:24:34.252Z"],["3820605","PAW-15285","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-configless-other, pint-product-resource-provisioning, pint-capability-self-service-infrastructure\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-19T13:24:40.330Z"],["3820610","BP-13321","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] I believe it should be enough, thank you!","2026-01-19T13:24:53.048Z"],["3820611","LSS-61554","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:590a0677-fdbb-4c13-9916-d32af1588d3e] , please see the DHL number attached [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=9941295976&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=9941295976&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:24:57.751Z"],["3820613","LSS-61698","LSS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ,\n\nI would suggest following the same flow you have done before. That will give us time to prepare the guidelines and communicate them properly with CS and OC. Thanks!","2026-01-19T13:25:11.331Z"],["3820614","BDB-1461","BDB","sohniya.nair@bolt.eu","Sohniya Nair"," [~accountid:712020:f172cd28-e81b-4011-8942-5ec6b2912f37] Thanks for the update and noted, kindly tag [~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] and I in the comments when media plan is finalised 😀","2026-01-19T13:25:33.278Z"],["3820616","PFI-835563","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","!ICON_1671120.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:26:14.184Z"],["3820617","WFM-10036","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a] , could you please attach which issue or error you get when you try to assign these cases to yourself? ","2026-01-19T13:26:18.080Z"],["3820618","BP-13321","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] I think we should be able to do that, yes. I will look into it.\n\nDo we by chance have any precedent of implementing something similar? Could be useful for seeing if my approach aligns with existing precedent.","2026-01-19T13:26:23.518Z"],["3820619","BP-13321","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] the email task is [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13415|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13415|smart-link] with all info","2026-01-19T13:26:23.667Z"],["3820621","PC-3010","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* Should not happen, Alexey to check and adjust the status of the task.","2026-01-19T13:26:41.821Z"],["3820623","PFI-835565","PFI","serhii.moroz@bolt-outsource.eu","Serhii Moroz","!image-20260119-132559.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:27:01.200Z"],["3820624","DSR-3713","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Driver is missing invoices, started new downloads to double check [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1830005/view] and [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-bulk-invoice-download/item/1530021/view]","2026-01-19T13:27:05.768Z"],["3820630","PFI-835566","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T13:27:31.399Z"],["3820631","WFM-10036","WFM","ramone.edwards@bolt.eu","Ramone Edwards","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.27.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:27:32.950Z"],["3820641","WFM-10040","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Hi [~accountid:712020:36916c51-9ca8-40d6-aab0-f6adcbd99df9] ,\nMentioned agents already have Safety roles assigned to their accounts, do they experience any issues?","2026-01-19T13:28:21.851Z"],["3820645","RS-1875","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Waiting for review","2026-01-19T13:29:34.296Z"],["3820646","PFI-835567","PFI","njteh.grboyian@bolt-outsource.eu","Njteh Grboyian","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 5.29.18 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:29:38.516Z"],["3820647","PC-3424","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* Keep monitoring usage of old endpoint every 1-3 months, when usage is NILL then clean the code.\n* Keeping the task in backlog","2026-01-19T13:29:40.352Z"],["3820648","BP-13321","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] do you mean banners? We have when company has dept, it is both in dashboard page and billing page. Or you mean something else?","2026-01-19T13:29:59.114Z"],["3820657","PFI-834653","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has now been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T13:31:45.270Z"],["3820660","HS-29117","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi Alexsey,\n\nThanks for reaching out.\nI forwarded all relevant documents to you via you personal email [alexeyermolaev91@gmail.com|mailto:alexeyermolaev91@gmail.com].\n\nKind regards,\nAike-Maris","2026-01-19T13:32:13.255Z"],["3820661","PIF-3064","PIF","andrei.troskov@bolt.eu","Andrei Troškov","Boosted the risk reduction as we had another case that lead to the incident.","2026-01-19T13:32:15.435Z"],["3820662","LSS-61436","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60f2a71843c956007065f2ad] ! May you please dive me an access to the doc to proceed with signing process.\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-19T13:32:15.676Z"],["3820663","PFI-833353","PFI","sera.teng@bolt.eu","Sera Teng","Hi, there is no payout link as I am asking to find a specific payout that I am having trouble  finding myself. thanks!","2026-01-19T13:32:40.341Z"],["3820664","LSS-61802","LSS","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","[^Malta International Airport - Extra Charge Form 2 BOLT FOOD SCHENGEN WALLS.pdf] _(245 kB)_","2026-01-19T13:32:47.998Z"],["3820665","LSS-59929","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:51e35655-4871-4357-bfb7-9fca7157a290],\n\nHave you heard back from Caixa? \n\nPlease let us know the status of this, and if you need any further assistance from us with this NDA.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-19T13:33:00.554Z"],["3820667","WFM-10041","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","[req|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601715] submitted for a safety role ","2026-01-19T13:33:03.432Z"],["3820672","PFI-835572","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T13:34:02.684Z"],["3820678","LSS-59991","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hello [~accountid:712020:b467cd93-0037-45b9-9f33-992ba5f38b42] , [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] ,\n\nHope you’re doing well. \n\nJust wanted to know whether you heard back from Trojan Economics, and if you need any further assistance, or if we can proceed to close this ticket.\n\nThank you!\n\nAngela","2026-01-19T13:35:14.718Z"],["3820684","PFI-834684","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-19T13:36:11.099Z"],["3820687","LSS-61662","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Thanks for flagging [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] HP has confirmed on email that for the work of preparing and serving the notices we agreed a fixed fee.  I will add the confirmation emails to the ticket.  Noted also re your comments on tax advice. ","2026-01-19T13:37:07.747Z"],["3820688","PFI-835575","PFI","serhii.moroz@bolt-outsource.eu","Serhii Moroz","!image-20260119-133707.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:37:14.243Z"],["3820689","WD-22580","WD","sofja.pomazan@bolt.eu","Sofja Pomazan","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec], I always add the tax code and tax applicability manually. But it should be added automatically. I check the tax coding anyway before submitting, so there are no risks if tax coding added automatically. \nPart of the invoices are “in progress” status. I would like to get all IC invoices to the WD mailbox (this is only possible for invoices with “in progress” status)","2026-01-19T13:37:21.871Z"],["3820690","CSDA-301","CSDA","zaur.ayralov@bolt.eu","Zaur Ayralov","We have discussed it as it is safety tool related data , requestor will check with Safety/Risk team.","2026-01-19T13:37:27.378Z"],["3820694","LSS-61472","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] Any updates?","2026-01-19T13:38:01.315Z"],["3820698","LSS-56917","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n[~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b] thank you, I have added [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] from Billing team to the ticket for her input 😉 \n[~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] Could you please review [this document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u6gRNeQ2oVRbuugKTlxGDFYNQFuQ-njR/edit] (the comment where you are tagged), and confirm that from the Billing side we can agree to the requested changes?\n\nThanks a lot! ","2026-01-19T13:38:52.413Z"],["3820699","HS-29119","HS","weronika.ners@bolt.eu","Weronika Ners","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 14.31.39.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:39:10.315Z"],["3820700","PAR-113","PAR","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","There is already another ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3767|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3767|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:39:16.071Z"],["3820701","LSS-59845","LSS","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Hi, to make sure the redline is properly addressed, I scheduled a meeting with [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7]  tomorrow. Will let you know how it goes.","2026-01-19T13:39:21.449Z"],["3820704","PFI-835410","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Please provide business id !","2026-01-19T13:39:28.055Z"],["3820705","DSR-2533","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], we have received follow-up:\n\n*Driver message*\n\nI hereby confirm that I have received your latest response regarding the permanent deactivation of my driver account.\nI note that I continue to dispute the legality and proportionality of the decision made, as it is based solely on two subjective passenger reports, without any objective evidence or independent verification, and without any real possibility of an effective appeal.\nSince you have confirmed that your internal procedure is fully exhausted and that the decision remains in force, I hereby consider that all internal legal remedies against Bolt Operations OÜ are exhausted.\nThe competent regulatory authorities will be informed of further steps, including the bodies responsible for oversight of GDPR enforcement and the Digital Services Act.\nThis email does not require a further response, unless you are prepared to offer a lawful, proportionate and transparent solution.\n\nAs I see it there’s no further privacy issues. Just is letting us know that is gonna escalate this to the competent regulatory authority. Can we proceed to close the ticket? Thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-19T13:39:41.946Z"],["3820707","PAR-114","PAR","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","There is already another ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3764|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3764|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:40:02.576Z"],["3820713","PFI-834697","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T13:42:03.030Z"],["3820714","LSS-61636","LSS","karoli.kesner@bolt.eu","Karoli Kesner","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] is there any update on this ticket? Thank you and best wishes, Karoli","2026-01-19T13:42:05.076Z"],["3820716","HS-29114","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Need another certificate for Tervisekassa. Waiting for that.","2026-01-19T13:42:12.644Z"],["3820717","SRED-1084","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, switched and sre-shell-agent removed.","2026-01-19T13:42:13.383Z"],["3820721","WFM-10043","WFM","gerda.morkvenaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Gerda Morkvenaite","[^list of agents.xlsx]","2026-01-19T13:42:52.633Z"],["3820722","WFM-10036","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","Thanks for the screenshot, these cases are on Ireland market and you have only UK queues assigned to you. [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] could you confirm if Ramone is meant to support Safety Ireland queues as well?","2026-01-19T13:42:56.128Z"],["3820724","PFI-833228","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, if some of the Payments are not visible in the Payments tab for the Business Account, but the payment was done, please, raise it with the Payments Team.","2026-01-19T13:43:41.098Z"],["3820726","PFI-833228","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T13:43:47.066Z"],["3820728","PFI-834706","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T13:44:04.878Z"],["3820729","LSS-61758","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344258|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344258|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:44:05.192Z"],["3820730","PFI-835577","PFI","monica.acevedo@bolt.eu","Mónica Acevedo","[^transferencia-260108231101.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-19T13:44:06.832Z"],["3820732","PFI-835254","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment was matched !","2026-01-19T13:44:26.353Z"],["3820735","DSR-3825","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Communications file sent to the user","2026-01-19T13:44:36.847Z"],["3820738","PFI-835246","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payments were imported !","2026-01-19T13:45:00.408Z"],["3820740","PFI-834660","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment has now been successfully cancelled and the preauthorisation amount returned to the customer. The reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.","2026-01-19T13:45:21.431Z"],["3820741","PFI-835522","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Seems like they were blocked due to past bounce: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"start_date\"%3A1768225454.205%2C\"end_date\"%3A1768830254.205%2C\"type\"%3A\"all\"%2C\"status\"%3A\"all\"%2C\"search\"%3A\"kokusushiwaw%40op.pl\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/comms-email/emails/sent/?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_date%22%3A1768225454.205%2C%22end_date%22%3A1768830254.205%2C%22type%22%3A%22all%22%2C%22status%22%3A%22all%22%2C%22search%22%3A%22kokusushiwaw%40op.pl%22%7D%7D]\n\n\n\nSince we don’t control that part, please reach out to [#dev-comms-and-privacy-support|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY] to have them look into this 🙂 ","2026-01-19T13:45:29.343Z"],["3820743","PFI-835522","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team!  🍔\n\n- Provider/Courier payment didn't reflect in their balance: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/503\n- Provider/Courier didn't receive payout: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/319\n- Eater had issues with the payment: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/316\n- Early cashout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/556\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/317\n- App and backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/76\n- Balance and Invoices issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/58/create/318\n- Invoice Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T13:45:35.180Z"],["3820744","CRC-2350","CRC","romet.varts@bolt.eu","Romet Varts","[update] Test for Ismail","2026-01-19T13:45:44.380Z"],["3820745","LSS-57846","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","[~accountid:5f646caf42547c007138d9c2] informed me on 14th of January that the partner resumed its activity on the platform. We are currently waiting for operations to decide on whether termination is still of interest or if they would like to further proceed with the execution of the agreement.","2026-01-19T13:45:53.768Z"],["3820746","WD-22597","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hello,\n\nThe Finance Platform team is responsible for technical aspects of the financial systems. The request you have raised is related to an operational activity, therefore please use the following Service Desk: \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/28|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/28|smart-link]  ","2026-01-19T13:45:59.033Z"],["3820748","PFI-801722","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Should be with the new one. Please, provide few examples when invoices come out with the old VAT, I will investigate","2026-01-19T13:46:13.430Z"],["3820750","LSS-60427","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:3f296324-f752-4088-93de-c90d8654a2ee] Do we have any updates here?","2026-01-19T13:46:19.362Z"],["3820751","LSS-61636","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66] ! sorry for the delayed reply. Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Lawyers_Eubelius 31.12.2025 (81749203-5eb2-4637-90cc-d71e41cea82a).pdf] [^Lawyers_Osborne Clarke CVBA_SCRL 31.12.2025 (6db9f5dd-33bc-4ff7-b03c-d5bcd4bd7cea).pdf] [^Lawyers_Claeys and Engels SRL 31.12.2025 (08d1cc76-dde7-4b29-93a0-02424dfbc813).pdf] [^Insurance confirmation_Cachet Insurance Broker OÜ 31.12.2025 (d23b62c0-22b9-491f-8851-e7688b66598a).pdf] [^Banks_Papaya.31.12.2025 (b508b7e5-23ae-49cb-9453-be3cee420529).pdf] [^Supplier confirmation_BV Moby Green 31.12.2025 (1).pdf] [^Lawyers_Younity SCRL 31.12.2025 (1).pdf] ","2026-01-19T13:46:32.892Z"],["3820754","BIZ-283","BIZ","tung.lok@bolt.eu","Zip Lok","Hello!\n\nTax comment and memo were provided on 19 Nov 2025 ([Slack|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09L27AR5GS/p1763545477502249?thread_ts=1760353701.817529&cid=C09L27AR5GS] and  [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TAX2-536|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TAX2-536|smart-link]).\n\nFrom tax pov, both intermediary model and resale model (but higher VAT costs for business clients and forbidden as per Legal’s pov) are feasible for Taiwan.  \n\ncc. [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] [~accountid:625fb4941046bb0071ddf44a] ","2026-01-19T13:46:47.178Z"],["3820756","PFI-835578","PFI","chiamaka.okeke@bolt-outsource.eu","Chiamaka Okeke","!IMG_0571.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!Pre-auth 2.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T13:46:51.047Z"],["3820757","BP-13415","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] Yup, seems to be clear! We can close this task.","2026-01-19T13:46:55.810Z"],["3820758","SRED-506","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Announced in #dev-backend [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C609XD6MD/p1768827315986239|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C609XD6MD/p1768827315986239|smart-link] \n\nList of affected states:\n\n# redis/eu-central-1/fraud-graph/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/geo-rides-routing/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/place-id-stash/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/profiling-delivery/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/profiling-fraud/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/profiling-incentives/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/profiling-rider-incentives/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/profiling/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"] ✅ \n# redis/eu-central-1/rate-limiting/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/rental-search/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/rider-mqtt-connection/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/rides-geo-adapter-mq/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/rides-order/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/rides-search/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/route-prediction-mq/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/route-prediction/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/targeting/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]\n# redis/eu-central-1/user-auth/live/main.tf:    sg      = [\"redis-live\"]","2026-01-19T13:47:03.764Z"],["3820760","RS-1906","RS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] hey, there is no specific list of articles or information that the Agency has to refer to in order for their request for be valid, hence in accordance with my understanding these articles can be considered valid legal basis when cited individually.","2026-01-19T13:47:20.099Z"],["3820764","PFI-834725","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T13:48:00.463Z"],["3820765","LSS-61398","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:61e144f79ee70a0068ec7efd] , I will close this ticket for now. In case there is anything needed in the future in relation to it, I will reopen it.\nThanks,\n\nAlex","2026-01-19T13:48:07.176Z"],["3820766","PFI-835210","PFI","dean.goulding@bolt.eu","Dean Goulding","In this case, will you need to log a new ticket? I am worried that if I approve this the fleet will just remain on driver based.","2026-01-19T13:48:07.625Z"],["3820769","DSR-2533","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks for the update - can be closed (/) ","2026-01-19T13:48:48.658Z"],["3820770","SRED-1080","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, removal applied to all hosts.","2026-01-19T13:49:04.160Z"],["3820773","PFI-834743","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-19T13:49:55.981Z"],["3820776","CRC-2350","CRC","ismayil.aghahasanli@bolt.eu","Ismayil Aghahasanli","[update]-new external shared driver created and files started being transferred there","2026-01-19T13:50:15.740Z"],["3820777","PFI-813112","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","Hi [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] the payment was made on December 16th and has not been allocated yet. Could you please help me with this case?","2026-01-19T13:50:18.613Z"],["3820778","PFI-835584","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-19T13:50:37.348Z"],["3820781","PFI-834758","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n[^Refund_Letter_V7TFPHVZVH88CPG6_G9QLMZ4S2TVDX9Q9.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T13:50:53.941Z"],["3820784","PFI-834759","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T13:51:16.997Z"],["3820785","LSS-58409","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:712020:793bd952-a372-4264-98c5-05f34ecedce8],\n\nThanks for following up on this.\n\nWe’re working on it and will get back to you later this week.\n\nMany thanks!","2026-01-19T13:51:26.228Z"],["3820786","PRV-976","PRV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","To be completed by 31 March 2025:\n\n* -Understand the verification flow (Veritas)-\n* -Understand the Courier verification at Delivery-\n* -Understand the Roles – Courier becomes a sub-processor on behalf of Restaurant/Store; Bolt becomes a data processor for Restaurant/ Store.-\n* Figure out the structure of Data Protection Addendum for Store\n* Figure out the structure of Data Protection Addendum for Courier\n* Edit Data Protection Addendums\n* Send Data Protection Addendums for translations\n* Update Data Protection Addendums","2026-01-19T13:51:34.951Z"],["3820787","PFI-834763","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T13:51:37.006Z"],["3820789","LSS-59991","LSS","alexandros.lamprou@bolt.eu","Alexandros Lamprou","hi [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] no did not hear back from them yet. i think for now we can close the ticket and if anything comes up we will revisit it. ","2026-01-19T13:51:40.247Z"],["3820791","RDXENG-4657","RDXENG","ahmed.elhadad@bolt.eu","Ahmed Shaban Abdelaziz Mohamed Elhadad","Can’t reproduce it \nas descuss with [~accountid:6401d565314f508813822b2e]  will be closed and return back if it reproduce again\n\n ","2026-01-19T13:51:54.850Z"],["3820792","PFI-835194","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-19T13:51:55.163Z"],["3820794","LSS-61804","LSS","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","[^BOLT CONTRACT RENEW 2026_ (1).docx] _(98 kB)_","2026-01-19T13:52:06.249Z"],["3820796","PFI-835182","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-19T13:52:22.038Z"],["3820801","PFI-834765","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\n\n\nThe Customer Payments Operations Team does not have the required tools/permissions to issue refunds. If you are not able to issue the refund then we kindly ask you to check with your Team Lead on how to solve this case. You may need to request the following accesses in Admin to be able to issue refund for orders if you previously do not have such: \n\n\n\n* *Rides*: refund_payments and customer_support_beehive_ridehailing_order_refund\n* *Delivery*:  delivery_order_refund\n* *Rentals*: rental_order_refund, rental_subscriptions_refund and rental_order_refund_city_fine\n* *Carsharing*: rental_car_order_refund\n* *Bolt+*: subscription_offer_customer_support\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}*Note: A failed card payment can’t be refunded to the card. Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.*{color}\n\nFor issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.\n\n{color:#ff5630}For older orders refund, kindly check with your team lead as they have the required accesses to perform such operations.{color}\n\n","2026-01-19T13:52:53.380Z"],["3820805","LSS-59991","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Thanks for your response [~accountid:712020:b467cd93-0037-45b9-9f33-992ba5f38b42]. We will proceed to close the ticket then.  ","2026-01-19T13:53:37.524Z"],["3820813","PC-3829","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* Update the config and remove extra currencies which are same on Adyen and internally. ","2026-01-19T13:54:50.281Z"],["3820815","COP-1882","COP","kartikeya.sharma@bolt.eu","Kartikeya Sharma","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/19/DO-5815?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/19/DO-5815?created=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:55:19.646Z"],["3820816","PFI-835585","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-19T13:55:31.016Z"],["3820819","DLSP-2022","DLSP","sergei.toroshchin@bolt.eu","Sergei Toroshchin","Let’s ping Lukasz, if they are okay to support, good, if not, then we should use a workaround","2026-01-19T13:55:41.732Z"],["3820820","PFI-834778","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has now been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T13:55:43.826Z"],["3820821","C2-458","C2","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","Let’s understand the waterdamage rate per symptom. ","2026-01-19T13:55:45.439Z"],["3820822","PC-3834","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* We have started returning error type response for new endpoints. \n* closing the task","2026-01-19T13:55:54.032Z"],["3820823","PFI-835586","PFI","dominika.wozniak@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Woźniak","[^FV_BOLT_01.2026.pdf (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T13:56:00.613Z"],["3820828","PFI-834792","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n[^Proof of Refund 01-01-2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T13:57:01.047Z"],["3820829","PC-3837","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","PI Meeting Notes:\n\n* As there is no solution from PINT, so we need to adjust the endpoint names and fix the generated errors","2026-01-19T13:57:02.948Z"],["3820830","WFM-10044","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","[^Agent Bolt Emails.csv]","2026-01-19T13:57:12.470Z"],["3820831","LSS-61436","LSS","sorina.mihai@bolt.eu","Sorina Mihai","Done! Thank you!\n\n","2026-01-19T13:57:29.252Z"],["3820835","CSDT-969","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Exports for new scorecard created: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1-K6iszmPRLwBfDJiQVNIbxk0tKjSDXV9ll0PhmKrqgY/edit?gid=1561512235#gid=1561512235|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1-K6iszmPRLwBfDJiQVNIbxk0tKjSDXV9ll0PhmKrqgY/edit?gid=1561512235#gid=1561512235|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T13:58:01.047Z"],["3820836","HS-28960","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nEmployment confirmation letter has been sent for a signature and once signed you will receive it to your personal email.\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-19T13:58:02.714Z"],["3820840","WD-22575","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:712020:42c95fcc-665c-491a-9341-767b89230c32] ,\n\ncan you please redo the invoice again SBX and I haven’t managed to get to the ticket last week. ","2026-01-19T13:58:41.992Z"],["3820841","LSS-60988","LSS","sergey.zubov@bolt.eu","Sergey Zubov","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a], Sony’s Legal team requested some changes to our changes. Please see the doc attached.\n\n[^NDA Form for SSS-EU Automotive Semiconductor Business bolt technology oü (Sony 16.01.26).docx]\n\n","2026-01-19T13:58:54.409Z"],["3820847","HS-29123","HS","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","[^Scan 1.pdf]","2026-01-19T14:00:19.056Z"],["3820848","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","The PR for fix is under review.\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15393|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15393]","2026-01-19T14:00:39.258Z"],["3820849","HS-29014","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:712020:740c6298-2781-402d-b09b-daba42f340a2], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-19T14:00:49.673Z"],["3820850","HS-28996","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountid:712020:1a447c27-5947-4ed5-b674-3b465dfa89ac], we haven’t heard from you in a while. \n\nIf you’d like to keep this request open or have any additional information, please leave a comment, and we’ll get back to you as soon as possible.\n\nIf we don’t hear from you soon, we’ll proceed with closing the ticket, but feel free to reopen it anytime if needed.","2026-01-19T14:00:51.077Z"],["3820851","DSR-3813","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Suspension cases here: [1|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1506242956/79?orderTryId=2884577915], [2|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1486179979/79?orderTryId=2780842403], [+3+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1484583981/79?orderTryId=2771472920]\nMatrix suggested termination on the second report, but IH agents decided to give them a change, but for the 3rd report in this grouping it's a termination without exceptions. We are not unblocking the D for this reason and for the reason of them being violent and disobeying road rules","2026-01-19T14:00:54.304Z"],["3820854","HS-28983","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hi Thiago!\n\nI don’t quite understand if you need the digitally signed version (that we normally do for Employment Confirmation letters) or a paper version (will take some days longer to arrive)?\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-19T14:01:14.227Z"],["3820855","PFI-835367","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! As far as I know, we don’t provide this document. We have tooling to download the invoices for the year, but the FO should technically already have them as well. ","2026-01-19T14:01:17.820Z"],["3820861","PFI-834837","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T14:02:41.801Z"],["3820862","FX-3391","FX","dmitrii.bokovikov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Bokovikov","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 16.02.22.png|width=635,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 16.02.22.png\"!\n\nFixed","2026-01-19T14:02:48.093Z"],["3820866","LSS-61421","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi team,\n\nThanks for the update. From a legal certainty perspective, an assignment agreement should ideally identify exactly what is being transferred. That said, I understand the challenge.\n\n+Can we sign the current agreement as-is?+ \n\nNo. The current draft is written as a complete handover of everything from the Original Fleet to Citymap. It effectively says the Original Fleet is exiting the business entirely.\n\nRegarding the flexibility -  I understand that we shouldn’t prolong this until we get the final list. However, we do need _some_ mechanism in the agreement to define what's being transferred, otherwise we'll have ambiguity about who's responsible for what (and that could cause problems later, especially if something goes wrong with one of the cars).\n\nI propose we structure this as a rolling transfer. We sign the main agreement now to set the terms, but actual liability only moves when cars get their permits. Every time a batch of cars is approved (whether it’s 5 or 50), we sign a simple one-page confirmation for that specific group to officially move them.\n\n*Please note!* This solves the flexibility issue, but it does mean +ongoing admin work for you+. You will need to ensure a confirmation document is actually signed and collected for every batch of cars transferred.\n\nBefore I start redrafting, does this approach work for you?","2026-01-19T14:03:12.889Z"],["3820868","SREC-372","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Will reboot the instances outside of working hours. Seems like unattended-upgrades is waiting for a reboot to apply the kernel patch on all machines:\n\n{noformat}root@openvpn2:~# cat /var/run/reboot-required.pkgs\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1017-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1018-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1019-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1020-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1021-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1023-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1024-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1025-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1026-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1027-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1028-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1029-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1030-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1031-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1009-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1010-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1011-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1012-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1013-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1014-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1015-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1016-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1017-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1018-aws\nroot@openvpn2:~#{noformat}\n\n\n\n{noformat}root@pki-4:~# cat /var/run/reboot-required.pkgs\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1023-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1024-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1025-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1026-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1027-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1028-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1029-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1030-aws\nlinux-image-6.8.0-1031-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1009-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1010-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1011-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1012-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1013-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1014-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1015-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1016-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1017-aws\nlinux-image-6.14.0-1018-aws{noformat}\n\n\n\n!image-20260119-140327.png|width=568,alt=\"image-20260119-140327.png\"!","2026-01-19T14:03:31.276Z"],["3820869","LSS-61782","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:c4b40874-5082-43e8-bf03-940002fefe16] ! There is the DHL number for your letter: [https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=2599365775&submit=1|https://www.dhl.com/ee-en/home/tracking.html?tracking-id=2599365775&submit=1|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T14:03:30.712Z"],["3820871","LSS-61743","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] \n\n# I am not aware of AV specific NDA. I know that some time ago Kai was planing to create a project-specific NDA template intended for employees involved in particularly sensitive projects requiring additional protection. I would suggest to check with Kai if  there is project-specific NDA template that we could evaluate for AV case. Bolt general NDA is intended to cover low to medium risk cases.\n# Do you know in which Bolt entity these employees will be employed? We could check specific employment agreement template and see if there is a need for additional NDA or not.","2026-01-19T14:03:51.839Z"],["3820872","FDBT-4815","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-19T14:04:09.435Z"],["3820875","PFI-834796","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe refund on this transaction is being rejected by the acquirer. Could you please refund the customer on a different order or offer a different compensation to the user?","2026-01-19T14:04:18.691Z"],["3820878","CRC-2386","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Payout flow to be tested this week","2026-01-19T14:05:01.626Z"],["3820879","CAMLE-9792","CAMLE","mateja.sela@bolt.eu","Mateja Sela","[~accountid:6102799e8ad5b60070a153d1] this appeared on our board, what is it about? 🤔 ","2026-01-19T14:05:07.743Z"],["3820881","LSS-61703","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","hello [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd], \n\nThe is no law in place but it will be introduced as a new regulation soon. \n\nTo give you a bit of an overview of why this is requested: \n\n#  There was some road checks by regulators that drivers using the App are not matching the Driver tag\n# We noticed that some drivers are online for 24 hours, which is impossible to be done by 1 driver. \n\nPreviously, we opted out of this feature because it was very limited, as the verification is done in 48h and the local team do not have access to verify in case of any mistakes or delay happened. \n\nFor now, we are in and we would like to have this feature live. \n\nTherefore, if we have the greenlight from your end, we will proceed with the product team to enable it. \n\nThank you,\n\n","2026-01-19T14:05:27.970Z"],["3820882","PFI-835590","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^26781513_01072025 (1) (1).PDF]","2026-01-19T14:05:44.040Z"],["3820883","LSS-58339","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \nI am reopening this ticket, as on Friday I received a supplement to the claim. \n\n[~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] Could you please look at this from an ops perspective—what happened with this driver, and whether he could have been acting on behalf of another driver? \n\nIt appears that a woman ordered a Bolt ride and, at that time, an accident occurred. Based on the information provided, it appears that the driver was Zavki Ruziev (vehicle registration number MTN 275). Could you please confirm whether this individual has an account and whether this vehicle is in fact registered under his profile?\n\nIn addition, could you verify whether Paulauskas genuinely does not have his own account, or whether there is any account history or linkage associated with him?\n\nI am attaching all the information received:\n[^1. E. Paulauskas atstovavimo sutartis.pdf] [^3. G. Jagminaitės momentinės ekrano kopijos.pdf] [^PRETENZIJOS PAPILDYMAS-s0116.pdf] [^4. Eismo įvykio deklaracija.pdf] \n\n!2. Gerdos Jagminaitės laiškas-20260119-140045.png|width=413,alt=\"2. Gerdos Jagminaitės laiškas-20260119-140045.png\"!\n\n\nThanks! \n\n","2026-01-19T14:05:53.387Z"],["3820884","PFI-834839","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe order pricing is handled by the vertical technical support team. Kindly reach out to the Technical Support team to help understand the pricing of this order.","2026-01-19T14:06:04.599Z"],["3820885","LSS-61743","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:6177b596f6da6a006af89fc3] \n\nDo you know by which Bolt entity these employees will be employed? We could check specific employment agreement template and see if there is a need for the NDA or we can rely just on employment agreement ","2026-01-19T14:06:08.405Z"],["3820887","LSS-61541","LSS","eleni.mina@bolt.eu","Eleni Mina","Hey [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] , \n\nCould you please grant me access to view the file? ","2026-01-19T14:06:22.486Z"],["3820888","FPD-1414","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","* After discussion in team meeting, we decided to move from 50 to 30 hparams tuning trials.\n* The reason is that not really that we are confident it improves our metrics, but we are pretty certain at least it doesn't make them worse, and it would almost halve training time.","2026-01-19T14:06:32.815Z"],["3820890","RDXENG-3087","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","[~accountid:5e21ae91ac570b0caa8672c1] Hi, I think I found an edge case where this could happen. To confirm I need 2 things.\n\n* Multiple (2 or 3) user ids to whom this issue has happened with their orderId  - To compare Mixpanel events. \n* I see you’ve added a [fix|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160929] in BE side to handle this. Although it is fine, can you please revert it in prelive alone, so that I can test and confirm my steps for the issue? \n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:9433cebd-7f30-4ee0-8e35-866172295b02] ","2026-01-19T14:06:40.756Z"],["3820891","LSS-61799","LSS","anastasiia.mirovednikova@bolt.eu","Anastasiia Mirovednikova","As a follow-up, I wanted to outline an alternative implementation option and get your view on any potential privacy risks.\n\nIf we are not able to technically limit the search feature by market, another option would be to allow Ops agents to search by driver personal data across the entire Beehive backlog for Driver registrations. In this case:\n\n* Agents would still need to already know the driver’s personal data (email, phone number, or name) in order to perform the search.\n* Even if an agent finds a task in Beehive using this search, they would *not* be able to open or process the driver registration in Admin unless they have the appropriate Admin access for that market.\n* Admin access controls would remain the primary gate for viewing and processing full driver personal data.\n* This option would be significantly easier to implement from a technical perspective.\n\nCould you please advise whether either option (market-limited search vs. global backlog search with existing access controls) presents any privacy concerns?","2026-01-19T14:06:43.680Z"],["3820893","CLOUDSEC-731","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-19T14:06:45.796Z"],["3820894","CLOUDSEC-731","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-19T14:06:46.809Z"],["3820895","CLOUDSEC-732","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-19T14:06:57.710Z"],["3820896","CLOUDSEC-732","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-19T14:06:58.833Z"],["3820897","PFI-835467","PFI","emefiok.udoh@bolt-outsource.eu","Emefiok Udoh","Dear team, the driver has made another payment to the correct account number provided but mentioned he has not received it. Upon checking, I found that payment of #6350 has reflected. Please disregard this SD.","2026-01-19T14:07:06.794Z"],["3820898","CLOUDSEC-733","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-19T14:07:14.260Z"],["3820899","CAMLE-9792","CAMLE","davit.khechoyan@bolt.eu","Davit Khechoyan","[~accountid:712020:233144b7-8984-4e6b-922e-2ed0d6700d5f] ooops 😄 this shouldn’t be in your board. Is it because of {{Components}} field?","2026-01-19T14:07:14.990Z"],["3820900","CLOUDSEC-733","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-19T14:07:16.456Z"],["3820903","PFI-834841","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nFor cases where refund was issued but can’t be seen on the user’s card or Bolt balance.\n\n* Check where the refund was sent to and if it was successful on the [transaction history page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A%2225%22%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22target_account_id%22%3A%2265766018%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] with the correct user ID \n** If Bolt balance refund is successful, there is a green button after the refund “🟢 success”\n** If refund to card, 💳 success\n* Check if the payment method used to make the order is not a business account. In this case, the refund will be sent to the business account balance.\n* Check if the user did not spend their refund on a next order (or orders) for Bolt balance refunds\n* Check if the user did not have a previous debt or previous failed payment that was covered up with the refund\n* If refund was sent to Balance instead of card, check first if payment was made from card. Usually, if card payment fails, card refund also fails. Sometimes refund will be sent to balance in cases payment was charged from balance first as debt and the refund will clear the debt previously created by the balance charge. \n* Check [payment page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/1946767063], to ensure there are no errors on the refund and advise the user to check with their bank if card refund was successfully completed.\n** If there is an error, escalate to Commerce > Ride Hailing/Food/Rentals payments\n* Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.\n{color:#bf2600}For issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.{color}\n\nIn this case, the refund was made to the card.","2026-01-19T14:07:38.249Z"],["3820906","DO-5815","DO","gazandi.cahyadarma@bolt.eu","Gazandi Cahyadarma","Hey [~accountid:6305dd7403058426d64af3df] 👋 \n\nCould you please add me temporarily to the channel? I need to create the webhook to that channel.","2026-01-19T14:08:31.296Z"],["3820907","CLOUDSEC-732","CLOUDSEC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","GPT review:\n\nh1. Information Security Code of Practice: Key Differences\n\nh2. 1. Document Header\n\n* *Edited*: Adds \"Exhibit A\" at the beginning\n\nh2. 2. Section 1.7 (General Security - Legal Compliance)\n\n* *Original*: \"...services provided to Bolt and its systems used to provide such services...\"\n* *Edited*: \"...services provided to Bolt *by you* and the systems *owned or controlled by you* to provide such services...\"\n\nh2. 3. Section 2.2 (Audit - Vulnerability Reporting)\n\n* *Original*: \"You shall immediately report any critical vulnerabilities or findings to Bolt.\"\n* *Edited*: \"Your independent audit reports should include in summary any critical vulnerabilities or findings.\"\n\nh2. 4. Section 2.3 (Audit - Notice Period & Scope)\n\n* *Original*: \"...upon *three (3)* business days' notice...\"\n* *Edited*: \"...upon *ten (10)* business days' notice...\"\n* *Original*: \"You shall provide *unfettered and immediate* access to the information...\"\n* *Edited*: \"You shall provide access to the information and/or systems *reasonably required*...\"\n* *Original*: \"...may perform ad hoc *testing and* application security reviews...\"\n* *Edited*: \"...may perform ad hoc application security reviews... *no more than one time per year*\"\n* *Edited adds*: \"All requests for audit/review must be submitted by email to [legal@sentry.io|mailto:legal@sentry.io]. The parties will agree in advance upon the reasonable start date, scope and security and confidentiality controls applicable to such review. Audits will be conducted no more than one time per year unless the audit was necessary due to material noncompliance with this Code of Practice.\"\n\nh2. 5. Section 2.5 (Audit - Document Submission)\n\n* *Original*: \"All policies, guidelines, plans, systems, schema, assessment results, methodologies, and others outlined in this Code of Practice shall be submitted to Bolt within fourteen (14) calendar days at any time as requested by Bolt if no shorter period is prescribed. Additionally, you shall provide visibility...\"\n* *Edited*: Removes the first sentence entirely; keeps only \"Additionally, you shall provide visibility...\"\n\nh2. 6. Section 2.6 (Data Transfer Consent)\n\n* *Original*: \"...obtain Bolt's prior written consent for such transfer.\"\n* *Edited*: \"...obtain Bolt's prior written consent for such transfer *in accordance with the subprocessor change provisions of the DPA*.\"\n\nh2. 7. Section 3.2.3 (Incident Notification)\n\n* *Original*: \"of any other breach of this Code of Practice.\"\n* *Edited*: \"of any other breach of this Code of Practice *that has a material impact on Bolt data*.\"\n\nh2. 8. Section 10.1 (Effect on Cessation)\n\n* *Original*: \"...you shall *deliver or* destroy all Bolt data...\"\n* *Edited*: \"...you shall destroy all Bolt data...\"\n\nh2. 9. Footer\n\n* *Original*: Includes \"Last amended 15.03.2023\"\n* *Edited*: Removed\n\n----\n\nh2. Summary of Changes\n\nThe edited version (appearing to be Sentry's redline) generally:\n\n# *Extends notice periods* (3 → 10 business days for audits)\n# *Limits audit scope/frequency* (adds annual limits, removes \"unfettered\" access)\n# *Reduces immediate reporting obligations* (critical vulnerabilities in reports vs. immediate notification)\n# *Narrows breach notification* (only material breaches)\n# *Removes document submission obligation* (14-day turnaround requirement deleted)\n# *References external agreement* (DPA subprocessor provisions)\n# *Removes delivery option* at termination (destroy only, not deliver)","2026-01-19T14:08:33.380Z"],["3820908","WFM-10039","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:35da6094-ea8f-4f8b-8484-c74558803722]!\r\n\r\nDummy [accounts|https://app.assembledhq.com/people/v2?agent_staffable=all&agent_status=active&limit=50&offset=0&search=lagos] created.\r\n\r\nWith best wishes,\r\nArtur","2026-01-19T14:08:34.297Z"],["3820910","CSXRT-81","CSXRT","tanya.kravchuk@bolt.eu","Tanya Kravchuk","Routes in Drive are blocked because of missing data points. We will follow up on it with the Product team, but this topic will be moved to the routines Project, so closing this project for now. ","2026-01-19T14:08:50.259Z"],["3820915","LSS-61805","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","[^RI_INF0293_25.pdf] _(350 kB)_","2026-01-19T14:09:14.633Z"],["3820916","PFI-834991","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T14:09:39.079Z"],["3820918","LSS-60542","LSS","liam.james@bolt.eu","Liam James","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] \n\nThank you for this its been really helpful, \n\nIn answer to the questions, you shared above, \n\n*Did you have any luck accessing Tom’s old emails?*\nI raised this with IT and they were unable to locate any previously signed document.\n*Please confirm if a debt collection agency has already been engaged.*\nI have a working relationship with the debt collection agency we have used them previously in the past to successfully recover funds. \n*Is the fee a percentage commission on amounts recovered?*\nYes a 10% fee on the recovered amount, however the agency does attempt to charge this fee directly to the client in the first instance.\n*Does the fee apply if Bolt subsequently settles directly with AIK?*\nOnce we engage the debt collection agency the fee would be due regardless of if we then settle the debt ourselves, including if payment is made directly to ourselves rather than through the agency.\n*Does the agency conduct negotiations or only enforcement activity?*\nThere are various steps, the first step would be the agency chasing the debt through letters, emails and phone calls. They would present us any negotiation or payment plan from the client before accepting anything. If they are unable to engage the client or receive notification that payment will not be made then they can assist us going down the legal route of courts. \n\nWe have now tried on several occassions to engage AIK management in meaningful discussion and have had no response so we would like to move forward with the letter before action, \n\nCan you please let me know what the next steps for this would be, and the timeline for getting this sent out? \n\nMany thanks \nLiam\n\n","2026-01-19T14:09:49.897Z"],["3820919","PFI-835003","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T14:10:05.972Z"],["3820921","PFI-835104","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-19T14:10:33.555Z"],["3820923","WD-22596","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:61f7dc370d3777006a90157d] ,\ncan you please provide example where we have remit to added and where we do not?\nAdditionally have you checked with DE Account Payable specialist of they add remit-to connection always?","2026-01-19T14:10:47.235Z"],["3820925","WD-22608","WD","elchin.nabiyev@bolt.eu","Elchin Nabiyev","entity CA002","2026-01-19T14:10:59.046Z"],["3820926","LSS-61541","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:17967e02-2e48-4923-9677-3a14549be9ae] ,\n\nI just did. Please let me know if you have any trouble accessing the doc.","2026-01-19T14:11:02.204Z"],["3820927","PFI-835197","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-19T14:11:02.870Z"],["3820929","RDXENG-3087","RDXENG","mykhailo.pohoda@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Pohoda","[~accountid:60fbd5ec9f975e0069eec7a1] sorry, I don’t have a list of recent orders, just [one|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2340241049/307?orderTryId=3008829844].\nSure, I can add a simple “if prelive don’t fix” statement. Or alternatively, maybe it’ll be just fine for you to test the behaviour by looking at “create ride” endpoint and checking whether it contained same promo code that was supplied to {{/getRideOptions}}?\n\n\n\nAnd thanks for looking into it 🙇‍♂️ ","2026-01-19T14:11:19.222Z"],["3820932","HS-28983","HS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi Kadri, thank you for the reply.\n\nI can use a scan of the signed document for now, which hopefully should arrive sooner. I will submit then it online to the authorities.\n\nHowever, I will need the original in paper to present in person once they invite me for the final interview.\n\nI hope this clarifies things. Let me know if not.\n\nThanks again!\n\nThiago","2026-01-19T14:11:53.154Z"],["3820933","CSDA-295","CSDA","hazel.omune@bolt.eu","Hazel May Omune","{quote}Thanks for the quick TAT, Mariia.\n\nQuick question on the report setup -  I’m not currently able to filter by country. Is this by design? If so, would it be possible to enable country-level filtering? At the moment it shows “No value,” which makes it difficult to assess market-specific trends. \n\nWe’d need 2024 data to support a YoY comparison. Given that several impersonation-related interventions were implemented in 2025, we’d like to understand how the trends have shifted post-intervention versus the prior year. \n\nWould obtaining 2024 data be a heavy lift on your side? {quote}\n\n","2026-01-19T14:12:05.461Z"],["3820934","BP-13321","BP","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] I mean in emails\n\nBut overall something with banners filtering by first ride or something else after a certain date would be relevant too","2026-01-19T14:12:29.172Z"],["3820936","PFI-814481","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nIs the user still facing the same issue?","2026-01-19T14:12:41.066Z"],["3820938","WFM-10038","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","All good! Queues added, role added and also Country spain added, as agent was missing access; Wish you a great day!","2026-01-19T14:12:56.446Z"],["3820941","WFM-10036","WFM","britta.haal@bolt.eu","Britta Hääl","Hi, yes, the UK Case Managers team is responsible for regulatory reporting and Termination decisions.\nCould we make sure the following list is added to the IE Safety Beehive queues?\n[+jake.collinson@bolt.eu+|mailto:jake.collinson@bolt.eu]\n[+muhammadbin.khalid@bolt.eu+|mailto:muhammadbin.khalid@bolt.eu]\n[+ogunnike.adelakun@bolt.eu+|mailto:ogunnike.adelakun@bolt.eu]\n[+ramone.edwards@bolt.eu+|mailto:ramone.edwards@bolt.eu]\n[+vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu+|mailto:vivien.antoniou@bolt.eu]\n[+britta.haal@bolt.eu+|mailto:britta.haal@bolt.eu]\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T14:13:08.167Z"],["3820944","L10N-28465","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated, please revisit.","2026-01-19T14:13:55.214Z"],["3820945","L10N-28474","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated, please revisit.","2026-01-19T14:13:55.390Z"],["3820946","L10N-28484","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.600Z"],["3820947","L10N-28478","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.686Z"],["3820948","L10N-28483","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.685Z"],["3820949","L10N-28479","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.691Z"],["3820950","L10N-28487","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.754Z"],["3820951","L10N-28476","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.795Z"],["3820952","L10N-28472","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.802Z"],["3820953","L10N-28481","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T14:13:56.808Z"],["38209