fiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nDo need further assistance on this ticket or have any update regarding the last comment?","2026-01-19T14:30:17.685Z"],["3821101","CCM-22290","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","[^II Wave 3 Food Delivery LMS Request.xlsx]","2026-01-19T14:30:17.896Z"],["3821102","DRX-27947","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DI.127.0 (195303926) Firebase Release build","2026-01-19T14:30:18.577Z"],["3821107","PFI-833220","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nDo need further assistance on this ticket or have any update regarding the last comment?","2026-01-19T14:30:43.507Z"],["3821109","PFI-833274","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nDo need further assistance on this ticket or have any update regarding the last comment?","2026-01-19T14:30:58.097Z"],["3821110","PFI-833653","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nDo need further assistance on this ticket or have any update regarding the last comment?","2026-01-19T14:31:13.608Z"],["3821113","PFI-833657","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nDo need further assistance on this ticket or have any update regarding the last comment?","2026-01-19T14:31:29.432Z"],["3821120","LSS-59421","LSS","daniele.fondjeutagouang@bolt.eu","Daniele Fondjeu Tagouang","Hello [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] \nThe driver did not regain access to their account given that they failed the Identity verification process. I don't know if something can been done from your end about this, then please let us know.\n\nThank you!\n","2026-01-19T14:32:09.729Z"],["3821122","PFI-835608","PFI","oluchi.onochie@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluchi Onochie","!Screenshot_20260119_143212_OPay.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot_20260119_152232_OPay.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T14:32:54.838Z"],["3821123","DSR-3713","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Driver found the invoices,  no issue :done: ","2026-01-19T14:32:55.929Z"],["3821128","PFI-835609","PFI","mia.hartova@bolt.eu","Mia Hartová","[^wise_transfer_confirmation__transfer__1906373268__7191643123__en.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-19T14:33:48.623Z"],["3821130","DCOR-390","DCOR","anna.aalberg@bolt.eu","Anna-Lota Aalberg","Most fixes were done.\n\n* still some uncertainty about CZ TIN - need to realign with several stakeholders before the EE tax authorities come back with fix requests.\n* DOB pipeline still in progress, no ETA but aim to develop ASAP\n* slowly sending out emails in several markets, requesting missing info from partners","2026-01-19T14:34:19.688Z"],["3821131","LSS-56128","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Vastus Dad Solutions OÜ seisukohtadele (Bolt)(5123103.2).docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-19T14:34:29.527Z"],["3821132","PFI-833717","PFI","prince.obasi@bolt.eu","Prince Obasi","The state shows “fail” as can be seen in this screenshot.\n\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 3.33.04 PM.png|width=1201,height=424,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 3.33.04 PM.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-19T14:34:34.155Z"],["3821133","PFI-833717","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-19T14:34:37.906Z"],["3821134","CNT-479","CNT","birgit.jurivete@bolt.eu","Birgit Jürivete","Hi [~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945], this campaign start was postponed to March 2, so we’re not rushing as much, but I’d still like to finalise all assets before mid-Feb, so we would be ready to go live on time. I will be OOO Jan 22-27, please let me know if you have any qq’s before that. Thank you!","2026-01-19T14:34:50.141Z"],["3821143","CCM-22290","CCM","ademola.oloja@bolt-outsource.eu","Ademola Oloja","Please it's [*iyanuloluwa.daramola@bolt-outsource.eu*|mailto:iyanuloluwa.daramola@bolt-outsource.eu] not _iyanololuwa.daramola@bolt-outsource.eu_","2026-01-19T14:37:17.225Z"],["3821144","LSS-61807","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","[^(Ready to be signed) A.1.3 Advertising declaration.pdf] _(3.37 MB)_\n\n[^(Ready to be signed) Anlage_4_Antragsformular.pdf] _(220 kB)_","2026-01-19T14:37:18.726Z"],["3821145","HS-29091","HS","duniya.zankyang@bolt.eu","Zankyang Zingy Duniya","Hi Berit, kindly send the email to: [Temitope_Sowunmi@amat.com|mailto:Temitope_Sowunmi@amat.com], thank you.","2026-01-19T14:37:24.706Z"],["3821148","PFI-832832","PFI","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552] thank you very much for your support - I have asked CS to share the rider’s bank details to issue the refund. I can will tag you directly in the legal ticket so that this one can be closed. \n\n[~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] thank you, you may close this ticket !","2026-01-19T14:37:58.840Z"],["3821150","LSS-61808","LSS","dovile.ligeikaite@bolt.eu","Dovile Ligeikaite","[^Bolt Operations NDA Munich Airport.pdf] _(237 kB)_","2026-01-19T14:38:35.497Z"],["3821155","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552] as discussed, looping you in this ticket - we are waiting for the rider to share their bank details to issue the refund by bank transfer. Thank you !","2026-01-19T14:39:05.641Z"],["3821156","XP-3060","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","Validating fix (i.e. checks are on whether sums of default and CUPED metrics match):\n\n* V3 metrics (GMV, finished orders) in carsharing dashboard user test 14086 ✅ \n* V3 metrics (GMV, finished orders) and V4 metrics (GMV) in rh dashboard user test 14612 ✅ \n* V3 metrics (food GMV, food orders) and V4 metrics (food GMV after discounts, food placed orders) :red_cross: - it appears metrics with Inclusion conditions ([example|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/blob/8d8a7931cca742b7873f114438abcd18da5ab042/experimentation/experimentation/ab_processor/v4/metrics/targeting_user/food/eater_kpi/food_placed_orders_per_user_utc.yaml#L11]) are not suitable for the general CUPED implementation\n\n\nCSV files available for all of above. Below are examples from Rides and Delivery\n\n\n!Delivery.png|width=561,alt=\"Delivery.png\"!\n\n!Rides.png|width=527,alt=\"Rides.png\"!","2026-01-19T14:39:33.332Z"],["3821159","RDXENG-4469","RDXENG","veronika.gainetdinova@bolt.eu","Veronika Gainetdinova","!533913075-a4c65bb0-5882-4d9a-b8d3-b82689a20477.png|width=475,alt=\"533913075-a4c65bb0-5882-4d9a-b8d3-b82689a20477.png\"!","2026-01-19T14:40:17.653Z"],["3821163","LSS-51490","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Thanks [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9] - much appreciated.\n\n{quote}_Notify the regulator, POTRAZ, via a letter that references the DPIA and details the Driver Selfie Verification function, including its benefits and risk mitigators. If possible, please attach the previously mentioned DPIA._{quote}\n\nI thought the letter had already been sent. Thank you for clarifying.\n\nIs sharing the DPIA strictly necessary in this case? While we should have a DPIA for this feature, our overall strategy aims to minimise exposure to regulators where permitted.","2026-01-19T14:41:11.514Z"],["3821164","PRF-1860","PRF","ariana.saplana@bolt.eu","Ariana Saplana","Hi [~accountid:712020:620ea7c5-429f-4501-a245-4d283f9eb036], kindly take a look at Karina’s request. 🙏🏼 cc [~accountid:63abfbf46f068efec8f6b8f8] ","2026-01-19T14:41:13.503Z"],["3821165","LSS-58768","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ,\n\nCoachHub came back with the following feedback:\n\n{quote}Please see our legal comments below:\n\nThere is a problem with making changes to the word versions and I have decided to save the document as pdf( find attached). We have accepted those topics that have been resolved by the parties and the following are the main open points:\n\n\n* clause 4.4 : confirmation of AI system compliance with data protection laws\n* clause 6.3 (Infosec): decrease of security measures\n* clause 15: CoachHub liability cap.\n\nWe look forward to your Infosec position on clause 6.1 and 6.3 and your legal’s position on the other open points.{quote}\n\nPlease let me know your feedback.\n\nThank you!\n\n[^Partly clean_CoachHub Data Processing Agreement (Bolt Privacy Team Review 22.12.2025)_CH2026_01_15.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T14:41:23.418Z"],["3821166","LSS-61534","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi[~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] \nCould you please share the link to the assessment 🙏 \n","2026-01-19T14:41:53.672Z"],["3821167","CLOUDSEC-735","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.\n","2026-01-19T14:42:35.339Z"],["3821168","CLOUDSEC-735","CLOUDSEC",null,"Automation for Jira","You must select an Epic and a q-label (e.g., q1-2026) before saving.","2026-01-19T14:42:36.278Z"],["3821174","LSS-61690","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^DEMERGE (THAILAND) CO., LTD. Bolt Support Services (Thailand) Limited 2025 (37f676c3-2fd8-40cc-af8f-35998f2b98e7).pdf]\n\nThe one that you have added was just sent","2026-01-19T14:44:00.031Z"],["3821176","PFI-835173","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Saksith, thanks for reporting! \nFor cases like this, cash orders can be typically ignored. However 😄 91% of his orders with income, have been due to cancellation fees.\nHis cancellation fee / finished order income ratios are not horrible, therefore due to being a new driver, we’ll monitor him for some more time before penalising, so to verify whether this is malicious. This is also due to the pickup location, which is known for very bad rider/driver matching, typically due to riders not finding the driver.\n\nI’ll keep this ticket open for a couple more days, and we’ll be able to better assess this behaviour.","2026-01-19T14:45:18.235Z"],["3821179","RDXENG-4641","RDXENG","ahmed.elhadad@bolt.eu","Ahmed Shaban Abdelaziz Mohamed Elhadad","[~accountid:712020:ef5f49c9-39d4-4c05-820b-dbad89f985a0] it only appear when *window insets* is not applied in device but if exist it work fine \nwill handle it nice catch 🔥 \n\n!Screenshot_20260119_164345.png|width=842,alt=\"Screenshot_20260119_164345.png\"!","2026-01-19T14:45:31.645Z"],["3821181","LSS-61776","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] ! Please add the contract to the ticket.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-19T14:45:33.763Z"],["3821185","LSS-59448","LSS","christiana.akinlade@bolt.eu","Christiana Modupe Akinlade","[~accountid:5d1b218591943f0d2ac52db0] [~accountid:5b7d5435b57ed25933f64464] can you please give me update on this supplier ? Thanks!","2026-01-19T14:46:27.724Z"],["3821186","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Thank you [~accountid:712020:c94f2cba-c25e-4b00-8ef4-2cad9045ee22] . Appreciate!","2026-01-19T14:46:31.558Z"],["3821188","PFI-835173","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","91% of order w/ cancellation fees. 34% of total income.\n*Bad pickup location, new driver*\n\nIf this continues, consider removing in-app","2026-01-19T14:46:36.938Z"],["3821189","LSS-61776","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Oh, sorry! \n\n[^Sutartis, Ames _ Bolt, 2026.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T14:46:52.187Z"],["3821192","LSS-61772","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:618d20acfba4d0006ae30dd3] ! Pleasee attach the document to the ticket.\n\nThanks you!","2026-01-19T14:47:30.650Z"],["3821193","LSS-61642","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Thank you for sharing the templates! 🙏 \nI’m closing this ticket now, as I’ve received access to the team’s canned responses.","2026-01-19T14:47:50.237Z"],["3821197","PRV-436","PRV","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","* Align on the status of the 3rd party PN\n*  Validate whether Waiter user will be created\n* Re-validate the data with business stakeholders\n* Draft a PN\n* Translate the PN\n* Upload the PN","2026-01-19T14:49:35.396Z"],["3821199","WFM-10037","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello, [~accountid:712020:35da6094-ea8f-4f8b-8484-c74558803722]\r\n\r\nCould you please clarify the purpose of this ticket?\r\n\r\nI checked the Excel file and noticed two columns with identical queues per agent, but with different priorities, which is a bit confusing.\r\n\r\nCould you please review the file or clarify your requirements?","2026-01-19T14:50:02.353Z"],["3821200","PAW-14995","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-19T14:50:19.017Z"],["3821203","LSS-61581","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b63472c3-a177-45a8-b81f-2269d17e33ac] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Cooperation Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_MP Chauffeurservice GmbH_01.02.26.pdf] ","2026-01-19T14:51:37.851Z"],["3821204","LSS-61772","LSS","domantas.dabrukas@bolt.eu","Domantas Dabrukas","[^1S-26-18(3.1)_LKT_BOLT_PPPS (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T14:51:55.419Z"],["3821206","FX-3633","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pavel Grigorev [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768834270504899]*{color}:\nHey <@U024XMNUKNW>! Added Company ID:\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A9HDDMSJH/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-19T14:52:04.894Z"],["3821207","LSS-61590","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b63472c3-a177-45a8-b81f-2269d17e33ac] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Cooperation Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_DLI Mobility UG_01.02.26.pdf] ","2026-01-19T14:52:19.648Z"],["3821209","LSS-61454","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Agreement on mandatory protective equipment_Bolt Operations OÜ_LOMARI TRADING LIMITED_13.01.26.pdf] ","2026-01-19T14:53:51.591Z"],["3821211","RDXENG-3087","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","This is the case I noticed.\n\n# Add promo code action contains 2 API calls {{code/add}} and {{code/list/v2}}\n# In this sequence if {{code/add}} passed but {{code/list/v2}} fails, then user will see an error on tapping “Add promo code” button. \n# But in the home page, this campaign will be shown as applied in the form of an Inapp banner. \n# And when user navigates to category listing screen. The campaign would visually be shown as applied in the form of stick banner (served by BE). But {{/getRideOptions}} request won’t contain {{campaign_code}}\n# Now user selects a category and navigates to confirm pickup screen. Here {{/getPickupData}} contains {{campaign_code}} (please note that {{/getPickupData}} internally calls {{/getRideOptions}}).\n# Then user taps on create order button and {{/rides/order/create}} is called, but without {{campaign_code}}\n\n\nMy hypothesis is that this is the cause of the issue, i.e step *4* (search happens without campaign code), step *5* (search happened with campaign code), step *6* (create ride called without campaign code)\n\nThe case matches with the above [user|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2340241049/307?orderTryId=3008829844] [events|https://mixpanel.com/project/1165336/view/32804/app/profile#distinct_id=397cd3da-6f0c-4aa4-979d-1b42749bac34&~(dateRange~(type~'between~exclusionOffset~null~to~'2026-01-13T00*3a00*3a00~from~'2026-01-11T00*3a00*3a00))]. \n\n* Apply Promo Code Tap (but with error, so lets assume {{code/add}} but {{code/list/v2}} had failed)\n* Inapp banner Tap (contains campaign details deeplink, so our above assumption is correct. i.e {{code/add}} but {{code/list/v2}} had failed - point 2)\n\nCheck out the video recording below. In the video I mocked {{code/list/v2}}to fail when adding the promo\n\n!Screen Recording 2026-01-19 at 16.50.44.mov|width=990,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-19 at 16.50.44.mov\"!","2026-01-19T14:54:30.670Z"],["3821212","LSS-54291","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","Thank you [~accountid:5b8d306bfa38ae2c89608b95], will check and revert asap.","2026-01-19T14:54:45.817Z"],["3821213","LSS-60994","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! Any updates there?","2026-01-19T14:54:47.913Z"],["3821214","PFI-835620","PFI","oluchi.onochie@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluchi Onochie","!IMG_7879.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T14:54:49.425Z"],["3821215","BDB-1548","BDB","sohniya.nair@bolt.eu","Sohniya Nair","Hi [~accountid:712020:9c4c0927-aeb3-4a47-9ea9-68428dc00be8] \n\nAs confirmed on delivery design [thread |https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C075GMC738V/p1768827766235259]. Delivery team is still awaiting on more information to finalise media plan.Once the media plan is finalised please tag the link here and tag [~accountid:60a8d3053fae6f00681b708e] [~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] and I. ","2026-01-19T14:54:51.422Z"],["3821216","PAW-14990","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161055\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 14:55:03 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T14:55:04.012Z"],["3821217","LSS-60992","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! Any updates there?","2026-01-19T14:55:05.229Z"],["3821219","WEBSD-1484","WEBSD","tom.gander@bolt.eu","Tom Gander","hey [~accountid:712020:71310fbd-d0d5-4628-b0a1-6c289f4f5976] \nI can create a report that you can use to check these metrics. For the clicks on each button you can use this link to have a look at which parts of the page were being engaged with. {{https://clarity.microsoft.com/shared/heatmap/768f361c-6e7b-4fb9-ba3f-e84e724d3dc0?heatmapType=0&heatmapDeviceType=2&elementToShow=uxydd6j5&areaMap=0}}","2026-01-19T14:55:47.918Z"],["3821221","PFI-835621","PFI","alexandru.stavarache@bolt.eu","Alexandru Stavarache","[^RO1525-47951.pdf]\n\n[^RO1526-4289.pdf]","2026-01-19T14:56:03.215Z"],["3821222","LSS-29559","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] can you upload here the files of invoices for or RM GROUP SPOLKA z.o.o. invoices no [FA/19/03/2022|https://portal.telema.com/eflow2/?siteLanguage=en#/documents/226309544], [FA/28/02/2022|https://portal.telema.com/eflow2/?siteLanguage=en#/documents/227901031], [FA/24/03/2022|https://portal.telema.com/eflow2/?siteLanguage=en#/documents/227334660] and [FA/19/04/2022|https://portal.telema.com/eflow2/?siteLanguage=en#/documents/233576262] + FA/16/06/2022, please? 😉 Many thanks!","2026-01-19T14:56:03.498Z"],["3821223","PFI-835621","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T14:56:05.333Z"],["3821224","PFI-835414","PFI","joao.santana@bolt.eu","João Victor Santana","Payout now resent accordingly","2026-01-19T14:56:07.272Z"],["3821225","PFI-833316","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","hi [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] could you help us with this case? thank you!","2026-01-19T14:56:46.400Z"],["3821227","IOTTEAM-322","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Temperature measurement is ok, but can’t get the correct reading for BAT_DET, I’d check that R6 and R7 values are indeed both 470K [~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] ","2026-01-19T14:57:37.426Z"],["3821230","PFI-835622","PFI","oluwatosin.akinbolasere@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwatosin Akinbolasere","!image-20260119-145905.png|width=1920,height=1080,alt=\"image-20260119-145905.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-19T14:59:20.399Z"],["3821232","HS-29127","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Hire submitted to Papaya platform. ","2026-01-19T15:00:24.433Z"],["3821233","FX-3671","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768834806696869]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3671] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T15:00:32.173Z"],["3821234","LSS-61806","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - you can include this DSA template for the ticket: [^Controller-Controller DSA Template (Africa & RoW) - November 2025 Revision.docx]. As usual, please complete the relevant Jira ticket fields.","2026-01-19T15:00:49.428Z"],["3821235","BP-13457","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","how it looks now\n\n!image-20260119-150041.png|width=592,alt=\"image-20260119-150041.png\"!","2026-01-19T15:00:53.743Z"],["3821236","FX-3671","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Joel Palgi [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768834812236949]*{color}:\nWas asked to give more time before deactivation. From 7 days to 9 days. Notifying with the same days\n{quote}","2026-01-19T15:00:53.363Z"],["3821237","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","The test on the link below investigates the front and rear mudguards' inadequate protection of riders.\n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/EIJfugE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/EIJfugE|smart-link] \n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"40ce77e0-8317-4e59-b57a-9302d0240fb0\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[154,142,114,114,116,115],\"colspan\":6},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"There are 4 hypothesis that may cause misaligned rear fender form the tire\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[154]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Hypothesis\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[142]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Test method\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114,114,116],\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[115]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Result\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[154]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":1},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Unequal tightening of the bolts on the mudguard sides may deform the mudguard and misalign the tire and mudguard tip.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[142]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Use a bike with the rear wheel and mudguard perfectly aligned.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Loosen one bolt.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Apply high torque to the opposite side bolt.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"85e941cef89dcaec90cee54bb84656e8.mp4\",\"alt\":\"85e941cef89dcaec90cee54bb84656e8.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[116]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[115]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The tip of the fender didn`t change its position.\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[154],\"rowspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The rear wheel is misaligned with the bike's center after chain tensioning.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[142]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Use a bike with the rear wheel and mudguard perfectly aligned.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Tighten one chain tensioner to measure how much it misaligns the wheel from the fender.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"da60eb8d5a68aebabb173702feadd8ef.mp4\",\"alt\":\"da60eb8d5a68aebabb173702feadd8ef.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":250,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"7023d98dcdf24ed077c068cd23d93c04-20260119-144206.jpg\",\"alt\":\"7023d98dcdf24ed077c068cd23d93c04-20260119-144206.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[116]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":250,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"cd8c79e0d1571991cab73ba11baad385-20260119-140534.jpg\",\"alt\":\"cd8c79e0d1571991cab73ba11baad385-20260119-140534.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[115],\"rowspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Tensioning a chain tensioner misaligns the wheel from the fender.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This cannot be the sole cause, as misalignment at the rear likely causes contact with the frame in front. However,\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" this was not the case on the bike where the issue was discovered.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[142,114],\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This is the bike which the splashing issue was discovered from to compare with the test above.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":250,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"d192b775d90cb80abc161ff67eeeada4-20260119-135236.jpg\",\"alt\":\"d192b775d90cb80abc161ff67eeeada4-20260119-135236.jpg\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[116]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":250,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"center\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"ee37adcdfe4627c1cb151d83d72ba6b9-20260119-143445.jpg\",\"alt\":\"ee37adcdfe4627c1cb151d83d72ba6b9-20260119-143445.jpg\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The wheel is perfectly  centered with the bike but the rear mudguard tip is misaligned with the tire.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[154]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Would sliding the side of the mudguard upward help align the tip of the fender with the tire?\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[142]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Remove one bolt and pull or push the rear mudguard to see if it aligns with the tire.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"666221abb9bb1df1c5da438b839315f4.mp4\",\"alt\":\"666221abb9bb1df1c5da438b839315f4.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"863dacccb625fc4f56fb6431f06528b3.mp4\",\"alt\":\"863dacccb625fc4f56fb6431f06528b3.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[116]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[115]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"If it was possible to adjust the sides up or down it would be a potential solution for the issue. \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"},{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#36b37e\"}}]}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[154]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"orderedList\",\"attrs\":{\"order\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The rear fender is deformed due to production.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[142]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[114]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[116]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colwidth\":[115]},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\nMultiple factors may cause the tip of the fender to misalign with the rear tire.","2026-01-19T15:01:20.533Z"],["3821238","LSS-60998","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Fleet Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_Majestic Move, Unipessoal, Lda_16.01.2026.pdf] ","2026-01-19T15:01:26.183Z"],["3821244","DAEN-1355","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","Found the solution. More about it [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C067MB2E162/p1768490022707129?thread_ts=1768404217.238369&cid=C067MB2E162]","2026-01-19T15:03:02.697Z"],["3821245","CCM-22290","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hello [~accountid:64182443b05b4e3e7daa195b]  👋 \n\nThey have been enrolled in the onboarding.\n\nWishing you the lovely rest of the day. ☀️ \n\nIrena","2026-01-19T15:03:14.074Z"],["3821246","FX-3671","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768834984667079]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3671 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-19T15:03:35.395Z"],["3821247","LSS-61242","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] [~accountid:712020:140cd5da-13da-4a76-91d2-dc8a151f6472] \nJust letting you know that I’m on it and it will be done EOW 🙂 ","2026-01-19T15:03:37.870Z"],["3821249","PFI-835624","PFI","alexandru.stavarache@bolt.eu","Alexandru Stavarache","[^2026.01.12-4607_BOLT OPERATIONS OU - curse 01.12.2025 - 31.12.2025 - Natasa.pdf]","2026-01-19T15:04:30.947Z"],["3821252","LSS-61810","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^DE20260119-001 KT-Germany - Bolt Drive DE.docx.pdf] _(456 kB)_","2026-01-19T15:04:55.634Z"],["3821253","PFI-835625","PFI","chinedu.ukaegbu@bolt-outsource.eu","Chinedu Ukaegbu","!IMG_0450.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T15:05:00.098Z"],["3821258","DPM-2343","DPM","artur.spunei@bolt.eu","Artur Spunei","This task concluded with the following [documentation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/q4NCugE]. It can be closed now.","2026-01-19T15:06:02.533Z"],["3821259","WD-22606","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Hey [~accountid:712020:8a3969ff-a877-45c5-82e8-74d7260b03cb], you already have Recruiter access for all orgs under Ali Rana. Is there a specific org you are missing permissions for?","2026-01-19T15:06:03.978Z"],["3821260","RDXENG-3087","RDXENG","mykhailo.pohoda@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Pohoda","To me that analysis makes sense. It also kind of aligns with one thing I’ve noticed in logs for our case: initial search, before code added, triggered pricing prediction for all search categories, while follow-up search, after code was added, triggered only one search category.\n\nThere are two questions from me:\n\n* do you have any visibility in what kind of errors were there? Or just boolean “failed or not”? Because {{/code/list/v2}} from our [dashboards|https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/d/nIwkIOGWk/incoming-requests?orgId=1&var-team=All&var-type=All&var-host=All&var-shard=All&var-service=campaign&var-entity=All&var-path=%2Fcampaigns%2Fcode%2Flist%2Fv2&var-windowSize=1m&var-node_release_track=Canary&var-node_release_track=Release&from=now-7d&to=now&viewPanel=4] is quite stable endpoint: fails either with authorisation errors rarely, or hitting rate limiter which is configured at 1rps. So, unless there was some network disruption, I can see only case when {{/code/list/v2}} was somehow called multiple times within one second.\n* and why do you need {{/code/list/v2}} within that flow? to update {{default_campaigns}} or something? Because our expectation from {{/code/add}} was that it would return all the data you need to display to user.","2026-01-19T15:06:18.786Z"],["3821262","HS-29121","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb] and [~accountid:712020:049f9fae-264e-423f-bbfe-4d83a6862561], \n\nCan you please print, sign and deliver these documents to Rusudan: \n\n* [Employment contract|https://bolt.box.com/s/0nvkmy2q65grw37siwdoe7370kj0lsjl] (signed by Ewa)  \n* [Amendment 3|https://bolt.box.com/s/hudhpajhzv399z1b7uyh0zm4ch9gk064] (signed by Victoria) \n\nI am not attaching amendment 2 as it was terminated. I hope it is okay. Let me know if you need that as well. \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-19T15:06:30.700Z"],["3821267","PFI-835630","PFI","rebecca.ankomah@bolt.eu","Rebecca Obeng Ankomah","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 3.07.18 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T15:07:38.252Z"],["3821268","WFM-10031","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello, [~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b]!\r\n\r\nQueue updated.","2026-01-19T15:08:08.602Z"],["3821272","HS-29119","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:5c010fa68ce9b546efc49454],\n\nYou should initiate a Data Change task for her in Workday where you could change her employment type to fixed term and then add the end employment date. \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-19T15:08:55.084Z"],["3821273","LSS-56938","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - this will be your first DSA negotiation. Will discuss with you in-person.","2026-01-19T15:09:05.924Z"],["3821274","BDB-1513","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:5d5a47614aeeb80c2cc0d00a] \nPrinting files are here: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/zo3bqgyb1166tbklpflmx/AEMDurra9zTtyxwpHwq_c3E?rlkey=rekdzklkh1ghoun9ccgq072fu&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fo/zo3bqgyb1166tbklpflmx/AEMDurra9zTtyxwpHwq_c3E?rlkey=rekdzklkh1ghoun9ccgq072fu&dl=0|smart-link] \n\nPlease let me know if everything works for you. \nThank you!","2026-01-19T15:09:39.179Z"],["3821280","CCM-22291","CCM","martyna.zdunek@bolt-outsource.eu","Martyna Zdunek","[^OS - Simply Contact - RO Onboarding.xlsx]","2026-01-19T15:11:29.398Z"],["3821284","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","*Update: fix for duplicate order-level records*\n\n*Status*\n• PR is approved and queued to merge: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15393|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15393]\n• Validation notebook: [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832085190?o=3598988355446810#command/8920732282550935|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832085190?o=3598988355446810#command/8920732282550935]\n\n*Root cause*\n• Duplicates were introduced by incremental runs of:\n\n{{int_matching_blast_rounds}}\n\n{{int_rides_company_order_event}}\n• Both models ingest *order_try / order_event–level* data and aggregate to *order-level* grain.\n• For orders where tries/events *span across two calendar days* (e.g., activity after midnight), the incremental logic processed relevant source events on *multiple daily runs*.\n• Because we use insert_overwrite on partitions and the partitioning/date derivation didn’t fully align with the incremental filter window, some previously produced order-level rows were *re-inserted*, resulting in duplicate records for the same (order_id, city_id).\n\n*Fix*\n• The fix ensures that within the rolling incremental window, we *exclude rows that have already been processed and exist in the target*, preventing re-insertion of the same order-level grain and eliminating duplicates going forward.\n\n*Next steps (cleanup)*\n\n1. *Full refresh* {{int_matching_blast_rounds}} and {{int_rides_company_order_event}} to remove existing duplicates from these intermediate tables.\n2. For {{fact_rides_orders}}: the affected columns are *incorrect*, not just duplicated. So we need to *delete and rebuild* the affected date partitions (we can’t safely “drop duplicates” because neither record is guaranteed to contain the correct values across the impacted columns).\n3. *Re-run* fact_rides_orders for the affected dates to backfill correct data.\ncc: [@yuriy.trofymenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:ea34e25e-5aed-4ec5-8c46-0238dbead6e3] [@silja.mardla|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63dd0f6fa5d0c826306adb04]","2026-01-19T15:12:36.868Z"],["3821288","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","*Update: fix for duplicate order-level records*\n*Status*\n\n* PR is approved and queued to merge: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15393|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15393|smart-link] \n* Validation notebook: [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832085190?o=3598988355446810#command/8920732282550935|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832085190?o=3598988355446810#command/8920732282550935]\n\n*Root cause*\n\n* Duplicates were introduced by incremental runs of:\n\n\n{{int_matching_blast_rounds}}\n{{int_rides_company_order_event}}\n\n* Both models ingest *order_try / order_event–level* data and aggregate to *order-level* grain.\n* For orders where tries/events *span across two calendar days* (e.g., activity after midnight), the incremental logic processed relevant source events on *multiple daily runs*.\n* Because we use insert_overwrite on partitions and the partitioning/date derivation didn’t fully align with the incremental filter window, some previously produced order-level rows were *re-inserted*, resulting in duplicate records for the same (order_id, city_id).*Fix*\n\n* The fix ensures that within the rolling incremental window, we *exclude rows that have already been processed and exist in the target*, preventing re-insertion of the same order-level grain and eliminating duplicates going forward.\n\n*Next steps (cleanup)*\n\n# *Full refresh* {{int_matching_blast_rounds}} and {{int_rides_company_order_event}} to remove existing duplicates from these intermediate tables.\n# For {{fact_rides_orders}}: the affected columns are *incorrect*, not just duplicated. So we need to *delete and rebuild* the affected date partitions (we can’t safely “drop duplicates” because neither record is guaranteed to contain the correct values across the impacted columns).\n# *Re-run* fact_rides_orders for the affected dates to backfill correct data.","2026-01-19T15:13:19.468Z"],["3821292","LSS-60542","LSS","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] one thing to add to this - AIK Management would have agreed to our [Bolt Business Terms and Conditions|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ugQ2SMXmyOXXARkNUXXH_UpTBhI9nOXpE6YcIKsieoE/edit?tab=t.0] when signing up for their account. \n\nI wonder if section 2.2 puts us on firmer ground when requesting the LBA?","2026-01-19T15:15:20.499Z"],["3821295","LSS-56585","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Thanks [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1]. [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] will be supporting and will revert by Wednesday. ","2026-01-19T15:15:46.287Z"],["3821299","DSR-3833","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-19T15:16:06.218Z"],["3821300","LSS-61809","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T15:16:06.683Z"],["3821302","PFI-835633","PFI","alexandru.stavarache@bolt.eu","Alexandru Stavarache","[^808ZEXA26017033U_2026-01-19.pdf]","2026-01-19T15:16:22.172Z"],["3821303","LSS-60122","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:46ca1bd4-650e-4217-b42f-78a9deb502a3]hey, thank you - I added the following wording re our termination request - _which the Lessor shall not unreasonably refuse._ \n\nThis would give us protection from the lessor refusing the termination request without any grounds. Otherwise to terminate we will need to sign the respective documents with the lessor so technically we still would not have a unilateral termination right. Please confirm that you accept this from the business side and then we can proceed with the signing.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1QEJDiMvc8AV4R-QSeGrw9qQx05USS6/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1QEJDiMvc8AV4R-QSeGrw9qQx05USS6/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T15:16:32.956Z"],["3821307","LSS-60746","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:615c75e007ac3c0068114285] there is no need to have the disclaimer, as it will look out of place. Perhaps the only piece of advice is to ensure that CS escalates any privacy-related questions from drivers to CSPC (as per Beehive guidance), and then we’ll support them with responses.","2026-01-19T15:17:17.824Z"],["3821310","PFI-819091","PFI","joaomaria.silva@bolt.eu","João Maria Silva","Team! Any news? I really need this.","2026-01-19T15:17:29.631Z"],["3821311","PFI-835100","PFI","audrey.tweed@bolt-outsource.eu","Audrey Tweed","Thank-you for your help!","2026-01-19T15:17:33.671Z"],["3821313","WFM-10040","WFM","tania.lopez@bolt-outsource.eu","Tania Giménez López","Hello! I’m sorry, I wasn’t aware that all the agents already had access to the Safety roles. Thank you very much, there are no issues with this.","2026-01-19T15:17:44.193Z"],["3821314","DSR-3211","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey team - before we deep-dive into this one, let’s clarify with the user whether they still want to go ahead with their request. \n\nOn 23.12.25, the user [said|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/705381632]:\n\n{quote}Once the promo codes will be issued I no longer wish to proceed with the gdpr request I had sent{quote}\n\nOn 30.12.25, CS replied:\n\n{quote}As I mentioned previously, this ride did not meet conditions for the campaign - scheduled ride guarantee. In this case, we are not able to provide compensation of 50 EUR, but we are *sending you 10 EUR to your Bolt balance that will be used for your future rides with Bolt*.{quote}\n\nBased on the above, please message the following to the user:\n\n{quote}Dear [name],\n\nWe are following up on your data subject access request, which we received on [date]. \n\nBased on the data available to us, you indicated on 23 December 2025 that you would no longer wish to proceed with your data protection request once compensation had been applied.\n\nBased on the credit was added to your Bolt balance on 30 December 2025 in connection with this matter, we would like to confirm whether you still wish to proceed with your data subject access request under the GDPR.\n\nPlease let us know how you would like to proceed. \n\nSincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-19T15:18:00.280Z"],["3821319","PRV-616","PRV","joyanne.njau@bolt.eu","Joyanne Njau","*Update:*  \nThe DPIA has been revised based on feedback from privacy legal counsel and the ODPO. The changes are as follows:\n\n* Updated references to supporting assessments to require links (PPRA link; LIA link) instead of names.\n* Simplified wording in Context, Data & Contracts (CDCQ1 simplified; CDCQ4 broadened beyond “processors” for clarity).\n* Aligned personal data categories with PPRA categories and improved wording for data flow questions.\n* Removed the database-combination question (PDPQ8) and related guidance on “pause/consult Privacy Legal.”\n* Strengthened automated processing coverage by clarifying “meaningful human oversight” (PDPQ15) and expanding impacts of solely automated decisions (PDPQ15.1).\n* Added new questions regarding processing scale (approx. volume/# data subjects) and whether processing is one-off or continuous.\n* Reworked purposes/legal basis capture: multiple purposes via dropdown aligned to PPRA; legal basis captured per purpose (ideally auto-populated in Relyance).\n* Moved the consent question into “Why processed” and made it conditional on the selection of the consent legal basis.\n* Expanded retention response options to include Indefinitely and I don’t know.\n* Removed the question about contacting IT to ensure deletion/anonymization (per Privacy Legal feedback).\n\nThe new version of the DPIA can be found [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OMdMzqTjUKEkFanFUK9IBByelRBUOF76Hdp2eV1E2AM/edit?gid=1238824703#gid=1238824703]. This version will be uploaded on Relyance and will remain a live document that can be edited as we continue to use it.\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] ","2026-01-19T15:19:07.448Z"],["3821320","DESIGN-197","DESIGN","maido.parv@bolt.eu","Maido Parv","[~accountid:712020:186ae0de-e4be-463c-8680-879b2f40f45f] Let me know what you need?","2026-01-19T15:19:22.260Z"],["3821326","LSS-59343","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Updated translation can be found in this folder: [https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/11k07F3fDY2-DdSVbRg4A6otPmH7DkxgH|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/11k07F3fDY2-DdSVbRg4A6otPmH7DkxgH|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T15:21:08.953Z"],["3821329","PFI-835634","PFI","joseph.kamange@bolt-outsource.eu","Joseph Kamange","!{6FA579E5-BBD7-4220-8E4A-B0CFB441DC1F}-20260119-152107.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T15:21:41.078Z"],["3821330","LSS-61592","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] \n\nWe are renewing with critical tool for CS Zendesk and I haven’t found any executed legal agreement with them. Previously we relied only on website terms [https://www.zendesk.com/company/agreements-and-terms/zendesk-customer-agreement/|https://www.zendesk.com/company/agreements-and-terms/zendesk-customer-agreement/|smart-link] . Do you recall reviewing Zendesk DPA  [https://www.zendesk.com/company/data-processing-agreement/|https://www.zendesk.com/company/data-processing-agreement/|smart-link] or signing separate DPA with them ? \n\nOrder review WIP here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFpT50we0WS0GPnQX-mXJOBP4D9RrJGP/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFpT50we0WS0GPnQX-mXJOBP4D9RrJGP/edit|smart-link]\n\n* Potentially we want to change governing law to English \n* Make changes to agreement  (incl. DPA) only by mutual agreement of both parties\n* Check if it’s possible to change liability limits in the MSA, currently it’s 12 months fees - 150K USD. Delete loss of data from excluded claims. ","2026-01-19T15:21:59.922Z"],["3821331","DBRE-8101","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Terminated\n\n* {{bolt-ami-proxysql-focal-arm64 20251031-174236}} instance in SQLdb account ($286/mon)\n* {{bolt-ami-proxysql-focal-arm64 20251028-162657}} instance in DB Test account ($286/mon)","2026-01-19T15:22:02.152Z"],["3821333","CLOUDSEC-735","CLOUDSEC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","Asked around. Got a confirmation from david.gardner:\n\n{quote}Hiive is a marketplace where private investors trade shares in private companies. We as a company do not use it and employees cannot use it as they receive options not shares. It will be spam or a scam. Hiive often markets to our employees trying to get them to use the platform to sell shares. Otherwise, it would be a scam trying to get info. It definitely has not come from Bolt - thanks for flagging{quote}","2026-01-19T15:22:12.825Z"],["3821334","PFI-833653","PFI","reinis.levanovics@bolt.eu","Reinis Levanovičs","Hiii thank you for the answer 🤗  you can close the ticket 🌻 ","2026-01-19T15:22:20.038Z"],["3821338","PAW-14996","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @tomekt-bolt\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161144\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 15:23:51 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T15:23:52.076Z"],["3821339","DBRE-8705","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Guys, please don't kill me, but I will need your approval here. :shyyyy:\n\n[@kewei.shang|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5dfb984e9a14250cb69f1697] :please-kitty:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/3871956|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/3871956]","2026-01-19T15:24:10.921Z"],["3821340","PRV-868","PRV","joyanne.njau@bolt.eu","Joyanne Njau","*Update:* \n\nThe assigning of vendors for country specific ROPA’s is underway. Relyance team has completed this for Nigeria only given the external regulator audit happening this quarter. The assigning for the rest of the markets will be done after the uploading of the privacy assessments which is the priority now. \n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] ","2026-01-19T15:24:29.328Z"],["3821341","LSS-61695","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:7257ab62-a7ae-4da0-8457-6957af214bd5] please provide me with the address of the authorized person, thanks.","2026-01-19T15:24:31.000Z"],["3821343","IOTTEAM-323","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","EN_IOT_PWR can’t be toggled [~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] ","2026-01-19T15:24:34.689Z"],["3821344","LSS-61695","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1Oih__QQh0rPIyz6ioRlxTWCs4ajU8uL6|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1Oih__QQh0rPIyz6ioRlxTWCs4ajU8uL6]","2026-01-19T15:24:36.109Z"],["3821345","LSS-61785","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b5de1fd-6c52-410d-afb2-757ecf5f9da4] !\n\nThank you for raising the ticket.\n\nI agree that we should notify the Fleet Owner, but having in mind that we should keep the communication minimal and factual. We should simply inform that the driver is not eligible to operate and that the account is blocked, avoiding sharing detailed reasons, and instruct the fleet to remove them from their roster / not attempt re-onboarding. \n\nHere is my proposed communication:\n\n_“Hi xxxxxx,_\n\n_We are reaching out regarding a driver who was recently registered under your fleet (xxxxxx - add fleet name)._\n\n_Please note that this individual is not permitted to operate on the Bolt platform, and any account(s) associated with them will be blocked/kept blocked in line with our safety and compliance requirements._\n\n_Kindly ensure that this driver is removed from your active roster and is not scheduled to provide services via Bolt going forward. Your cooperation helps ensure platform safety and compliance across all fleet operations._\n\n_If you believe this has been sent in error, you may reply to this email and we will review internally._\n\n_Thank you for your understanding and cooperation,_\n_The Bolt Team”_\n\n\n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T15:25:16.356Z"],["3821346","HS-29135","HS","leonora.lukoviczki@bolt.eu","Leonóra Lukoviczki","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 16.25.12.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T15:25:25.815Z"],["3821350","PIF-3290","PIF",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thanks for the bug!\nNo action needed from you right now.\nWe’ll move it to Clarification and review it then.\nIf we need anything, we’ll reach out.","2026-01-19T15:27:09.585Z"],["3821351","LSS-61648","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi team, checked their request from a privacy perspective. The legal basis they provided (Lietuvos Respublikos Valstybinės kalbos inspekcijos įstatymo 5 str. 1 d. 2 p) gives them the right to request details, including the personal data they asked for: contact details (documents indicating the declared place of residence address, email address, telephone number). I have no issues under privacy law for these to be disclosed.\n\nAdded also [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] for visibility.","2026-01-19T15:27:12.094Z"],["3821352","PRV-951","PRV","joyanne.njau@bolt.eu","Joyanne Njau","*Update:* \nThis task is ongoing. Subrata from Relyance confirms he is actively addressing the existing issue while planning to record additional videos for the remaining features. We are awaiting an ETA from him for task completion.\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] \n","2026-01-19T15:27:29.692Z"],["3821354","LSS-61754","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Support provided in the main ticket. Legal basis is valid, requested data (contact details (documents indicating the declared place of residence address, email address, telephone number)) can be disclosed, added Risk team for visibility.","2026-01-19T15:27:47.534Z"],["3821356","PRV-937","PRV","joyanne.njau@bolt.eu","Joyanne Njau","Looping in [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9], who has taken over this task from Eliise.","2026-01-19T15:28:22.998Z"],["3821357","DSR-3623","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","PDE tool data uploaded to G Drive.\n\nHow to proceed here now? 🤔","2026-01-19T15:28:28.154Z"],["3821361","PC-4924","PC","muhammad.irfan@bolt.eu","Muhammad Irfan","[~accountid:6215e9e7468c2e00716f320c] Currently we don’t have engineering capacity to take it, so need to check with product what we can drop for this task. Once prioritized then we can scope it for implementation. ","2026-01-19T15:29:13.789Z"],["3821362","PFI-833363","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","hi [~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] any updates regarding this case?","2026-01-19T15:29:21.267Z"],["3821365","UXA-2152","UXA","pawel.zelazko@bolt.eu","Paweł Żelazko","I’ve inverted “nosignoutcall” flag in deep link defined in rider backend: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160841|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160841|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T15:31:48.231Z"],["3821368","LSS-59365","LSS","karmen.aherma@bolt.eu","Karmen Aherma","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd],\n\n\nPlease share following information related to Bolt Vietnam audit (if any):\n\n* All meeting minutes and decision documents during the period November - December 2025.\n\nThanks,\n\nKarmen\n\n","2026-01-19T15:33:23.315Z"],["3821369","PFI-835636","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-19T15:33:35.023Z"],["3821370","LSS-60746","LSS","azza.ltifi@bolt.eu","Azza Letifi","Great. Thank you so much [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] for your assistance.\n\nAs a final follow up, please let me know if I am allowed to share this policy with CS and any external partner and what are the next steps required. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-19T15:33:37.156Z"],["3821371","LOC-3813","LOC","nicoleta.pandelea@bolt.eu","Nicoleta-Steluta Pandelea","Hey [~accountid:62472b362e101c006a8f50e6] \nHow are you?\nI wanted to check whether we have the green light to send these ad hocs yet. I’m receiving Jira reminders that the January 15th deadline has passed, and I’d like to make sure I schedule them on time if needed.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-19T15:33:59.673Z"],["3821374","HS-29137","HS","lubos.sitarcik@bolt.eu","Ľuboš Sitarčík","[^Munich-HR_000621.pdf]","2026-01-19T15:34:51.632Z"],["3821375","LSS-28796","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:c6829626-18d0-4d73-9974-74d1569b4bdf] the Swedish Enforcement Authority has informed us that their system cannot register Swedish IBAN and BIC details and that they therefore require the information listed below: \n\n* Name of the bank; \n* Clearing number; and \n* Account number; or alternatively \n* Bankgiro number.\n\nWould you be able to provide this?\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-19T15:34:59.058Z"],["3821376","LSS-61755","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:9bc1ca8e-c2f1-41a2-9476-90ce966c2205] , thanks for submitting your request.\n\nI have reviewed the information you shared and have attached our template data sharing agreement. I have also added comments throughout the document for your review. In particular, I have pre-filled Annex 1 based on the details you provided, but I would appreciate it if you could first check all comments and confirm whether Annex 1 accurately reflects the factual data sharing in scope.\n\n:Google_Drive: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sT3pPAuy6v3h8ks42JNu51G6oRBWkg9L/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sT3pPAuy6v3h8ks42JNu51G6oRBWkg9L/edit|smart-link]  (please don’t share the link to this docuent with Omniasig, and share a word document instead 🙂 )\n\nAs a next step, my recommendation is to align signing of the data sharing agreement with the commercial agreement. Once we receive the commercial offer and move into negotiations, I suggest asking the counterparty to sign our data sharing agreement at the same time. If they push back on this, I can support you with arguments.\n\nOne additional point for internal documentation purposes - could you please confirm how you intend to share the data in practice (for example via API, shared drive, Google Sheet, or another means)?\n\nFor now, it would be great if you could review the document and my comments, and come back with any feedback or confirmations 🙏 ","2026-01-19T15:35:15.940Z"],["3821379","LSS-50863","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi [~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] \n\nI’ve now reviewed the notes from Lachlan’s call with Taavi relating to the agreement. \n\nGiven that some time has passed since the ticket was originally raised, and that both of them are no longer with the company, there are a number of commercial and risk-related items that we should re-align on.\n\nI’ve prepared a summary document here [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CBg6zaYY310hgkCkM5k_BI0aD2e0qwPmJ4GJL1VU0W0/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CBg6zaYY310hgkCkM5k_BI0aD2e0qwPmJ4GJL1VU0W0/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] based on the meeting notes which:\n\n* consolidates the key items that require confirmation or decision,\n* includes the original call notes for reference, and\n* adds a small number of additional questions where clarification would be helpful.\n\nCould you please:\n\n* review the agreement and the items listed in the table,\n* mark each item as *Yes / No*, and/or add comments where changes or alternative proposals are needed, and\n* review the additional questions at the bottom of the table (and feel free to add any further items you think we should consider).\n\nOnce we have alignment on these points, we can proceed with updating the agreement accordingly. Thanks in advance, and let me know if you’d prefer to walk through this together on a call.\n\nBest regards,\nVeera","2026-01-19T15:36:39.778Z"],["3821380","PRV-934","PRV","joyanne.njau@bolt.eu","Joyanne Njau","Looping in [~accountid:712020:3d29a498-3ef1-4867-a3ad-7aeb77a221e9], who has taken over this task from Eliise.","2026-01-19T15:36:40.581Z"],["3821381","DSR-3623","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey [~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] - I am quite concerned about this section of the request:\n\n{quote}This request concerns a security incident that occurred on 6 November 2025, which resulted in an unauthorised change of the phone number associated with my Bolt account and the subsequent suspension of my account.\n\nI expressly state that:\n\n* my original Bolt account registration was completed using the phone number +421 915 990 758\n* I never initiated any change of the phone number,\n* I never approved or confirmed any such change via SMS or any other verification method,\n* no verification SMS was delivered to my original phone number, which I am able to prove by a screenshot.\n\nDespite this, the phone number on my Bolt account was replaced with a number belonging to Mr. Slameda Rianata, a driver from another fleet. This foreign phone number remains linked to my Bolt account to this day, even though I have no contractual or personal relationship with this individual.\n\nI was further informed by the other fleet involved that this situation was confirmed by them in writing as a mistake, not an intentional action on their part.\n\nDespite repeated communication with Bolt’s Slovak customer support, no technical evidence, audit logs, or explanation have been provided as to how this phone number change could have occurred without my knowledge, without my initiation, and without any SMS-based authorisation. The case was marked as “reviewed”, but without transparent clarification of the underlying facts.{quote}\n\n➡️  Has T2/Local Ops been involved in this? Do we have any visibility into this incident? Was it escalated to Privacy at any point?\n\n\n\n* From Admin Panel, I can see that the phone number was changed to *+421949070259*, which is the number the user claims not to recognise, on 13 October 2025:\n\n|5241770514|13 Oct 2025, 16:29:10UTC+03:00|edit|driver_root: 11938007|driver_root: 11938007| |fleet-driver-admin|2a01:c846:1a00:a100:3d7c:d33d:a9b8:5afc|admin-panel: bolt.barbora.laifrova|* *phone* changed from *+421919022715* to *+421949070259*|\n\n* From what I understand, the driver received an email to warn him that a new device logged in his account on 6 November 2025. This checks out with the [information|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8138042?tab=driverDevices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] on Admin.","2026-01-19T15:36:48.314Z"],["3821386","DAEN-1346","DAEN","oleh.mykhash@bolt.eu","Oleh Mykhash","Heads-up on the recent issue from infrastructure side of things and why *_the test failed on attempt 1, but passed on Databricks repair_*:\n\n*What happened*\n• The repair attempt ran {{dbt retry}} with a *different* {{--vars}} window than the original run.\n    ◦ Example: [original run|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/610872075062256/runs/592175767212830?o=3598988355446810] used 2026-01-18 → 2026-01-19, but [repair|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/610872075062256/runs/436336376725472?o=3598988355446810] fell back to job defaults 2024-01-01 → 2024-01-02.\n• Since our models/tests use {{--vars}} to define the interval, the repair run evaluated a different data slice, so the test could “pass” even though the original interval was still broken.\n\n*Root cause*\n• Gap in mudel retry handling under Databricks repair runs: on repair, the resolved job parameters can revert to defaults, and mudel was using the *default* resolved args instead of preserving previous vars.\n\n*Impact / follow-ups*\n• Affects only DAGs/jobs with repair/retry enabled.\n• I’m validating which rides jobs used repair and will share a list of affected runs + coordinate with owners to verify data for those windows.\n\n*Immediate action*\n• Disable repair-run behavior for the affected workflows until the fix is merged and deployed.\n    ◦ [@yuriy.trofymenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:ea34e25e-5aed-4ec5-8c46-0238dbead6e3] please approve this [PR|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9734]\n    ◦ This will *revert dbt retry* for all the DAGs before fix will be merged and tested in mudel\n• Merge fix for mudel","2026-01-19T15:39:39.786Z"],["3821389","LSS-57822","LSS","alijan.dias@bolt.eu","Alijan Keval","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] , its a tricky subject, no stupid questions here!\n\nAligned this should be a split topic, for the time being, this is mostly on fleets as their are the ones with the power of making changes to courier profiles.\n\nReplying directly to your points:\n1. Yes, when a new account is created, we deploy a selfie check during the couriers first login. This is a recent deployment, hence old accounts were not subject to this.\n\n# It would be via Bolt's verification system (but until this is automatic, it would need to be triggered manually by CS)\n# _Are you essentially proposing that each time fleet would like to change Courier details, we trigger a selfie check on the concerned Courier account?_ *Yes* _Why can’t we simply notify the Courier account concerned that there is an attempted phone number change?_ *This is what I intend do do as a second step, as the couriers themselves don’w have the power to make changes to their own profile, and I believe they should have this possibility. Nevertheless, even when the courier requests the change, this should trigger a 2-step verification, by both email and selfie.* _Or would a selfie check be triggered for the account after it’s being transferred on the another individual?_ *Also yes, at this point, we need to trigger a lot of selfie checks to put a stop to the rental market.* _In that case, what’s the process? We suspend the Courier account? Can we suspend the account if it’s a Courier under fleet? What would be the desired result?_ *Yes we can if we see its a fraud situation.*\n\nFor more context, all couriers in PT are under fleet. What we are witnessing is a huge secondary market of account sharing and renting, which we need to stop from both the courier and the fleet side. This is mostly done by a third type of player, which are “bike shops” that rent our accounts. \n\nThe topic is a bit messy in Portugal, feel free to ping me directly or happy o jump on a quick call just to provide more context in case you feel you don’t have the full picture. \n\n","2026-01-19T15:40:17.946Z"],["3821390","LSS-61812","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","[^WFS General Terms and Conditions  03DEC2025 FINAL (1).pdf] _(190 kB)_","2026-01-19T15:40:47.882Z"],["3821392","PFI-835637","PFI","sona.mihokova@bolt-outsource.eu","Soňa Mihoková","[^Transakce_2000024500406896.pdf]","2026-01-19T15:41:11.534Z"],["3821397","DLSP-2021","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","released","2026-01-19T15:43:48.918Z"],["3821398","LSS-61480","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi Susan, \nHope all is well. \nJust checking if you had the chance to review the questions below please? \nI have also rescheduled the HW x Legal meeting to tomorrow, we can discuss it there as well if that works better. \nThank you! ","2026-01-19T15:44:14.903Z"],["3821400","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","This one will fail.","2026-01-19T15:45:29.388Z"],["3821401","LSS-61811","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T15:46:06.802Z"],["3821402","DBRE-8705","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Do i need to change something","2026-01-19T15:46:29.197Z"],["3821404","UKIGFT-101","UKIGFT","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Fixed fee proposal agreed with Howes Percival for preparing and service of the break notices would be  +*£2,135 + VAT.*+ \n\nIn addition, HP recommended for certainty that a process server was employed to effect the service of the notices.  Additional disbursement cost for that is +*£130 + VAT*+ per address. Notices were served at three addresses, therefore total cost for process server is +*£390 + VAT*+. There may be other minor disbursements (still tbc) e.g. for Land Registry checks of +*£7 + VAT.*+\n\nConfirmation from HP on fixed fees is here: [^Bolt Mail - Office lease termination - fee request.pdf] and update on process server costs is here: [^Bolt Mail - Bolt Services UK Limited and Bolt Operations UK Limited Break notices of Premises at Old Street.pdf] ","2026-01-19T15:47:10.941Z"],["3821405","PFI-835639","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T15:47:33.198Z"],["3821406","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Recreated already.","2026-01-19T15:47:34.493Z"],["3821407","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","We need to alter the settings.","2026-01-19T15:47:38.138Z"],["3821408","LSS-60756","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:793bd952-a372-4264-98c5-05f34ecedce8],\n\nPlease find attached the reviewed NDA with some minor comments for you to please share with InComm.\n\nOnce the final version is agreed, you can request InComm to sign the document, and we will with the signature process once you share with us the signed document.\n\nIf InComm prefers that we sign first, we have no problem.   \n\n\n\n[^InComm Europe Mutual NDA (01.01.2025) (2).docx]\n\nPlease let us know if you have any questions.\n\nBest,\n\nAngela","2026-01-19T15:48:02.994Z"],["3821409","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Triggered manually.","2026-01-19T15:48:10.054Z"],["3821410","DBRE-8705","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Ok Thanks much :bowing:","2026-01-19T15:48:22.814Z"],["3821412","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","What happened?","2026-01-19T15:49:53.167Z"],["3821413","XP-3034","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","Current remaining marts/scorecards:\n\n* Geo for user/driver/partner/session/time-slice\n* Rides for user/driver/partner/time-slice/session\n* Micromobility for user\n* Carsharing for user\n\nProgress:\n\n* Geo/Rides/Micromobility in active development\n* Carsharing to follow when Micromobility completed, which is currently close\n* Rides and Geo are SDV-dependent\n** Rides are prioritising SDV metrics\n* Rides appear to be on track:\n** [Large volume of metrics|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hxlz1XslWgbWKpDl6xCXUAH3m5BRDl-jboeEiHmkjwc/edit?gid=0#gid=0]\n** Full time AE on mart creation\n** No blockers in terms of missing core models or metric logic questions\n** Analysts assigned to help with validation\n\nConclusion:\n\n* As of {{2026-01-19}} Teams appear to be on track for approx. end March deadline\n* No need for major re-priotisation of roadmap, however, we should be pro-active in helping with mart/metrics registration and validation, checking in every week and shifting focus whenever required\n\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] ","2026-01-19T15:50:06.676Z"],["3821414","MLC-1378","MLC","robert.pirnuta@bolt.eu","Robert-Mihai Pîrnuță","*Update*: Completed Churn without Debt for the remaining markets: MY, Dubai and DK","2026-01-19T15:50:08.662Z"],["3821415","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Is anyone working on Ti-payment CDC? It's lagging again.\ncc:*@user-U01AH7VKNHY*","2026-01-19T15:50:19.140Z"],["3821416","DBRE-8731","DBRE",null,"Slack","[Shubham Singh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/623194c0442e0e0069ed229c] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768833016429209?thread_ts=1768833016.429209&cid=GFGTF111A|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GFGTF111A/p1768833016429209?thread_ts=1768833016.429209&cid=GFGTF111A|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-19T15:50:20.118Z"],["3821417","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","I rate-limited TTL, but it's still not coming down; we had an unlimited delete_rate_limit\n\n{noformat}| tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit              | 5           {noformat}","2026-01-19T15:50:20.788Z"],["3821418","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","We lost it again. I tried pause, restart , backup, restart, nothing helps . we will need backfill again i believe\ncc [@marat.saddarov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3]","2026-01-19T15:50:21.770Z"],["3821419","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Both time it happened before, I checked CDC logs and couldn’t find anything obvious","2026-01-19T15:50:22.603Z"],["3821420","DBRE-8731","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov",":cryalot:  I guess tomorrow I am summoning PingCap to help research","2026-01-19T15:50:23.447Z"],["3821421","DBRE-8731","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","[@leandro.morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153], please feel free to start new/update old thread regarding the problem","2026-01-19T15:50:24.643Z"],["3821422","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","I am sure its because of TTL\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9EH4JQ83/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_20.31.26.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9EH4JQ83/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_20.31.26.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAF851LU8/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_20.32.01.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAF851LU8/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_20.32.01.png|smart-link]","2026-01-19T15:50:25.302Z"],["3821423","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","We have {{tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit}} unlimited everywhere we should limit it","2026-01-19T15:50:26.288Z"],["3821424","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","TTL Qps came down when i rate limit it","2026-01-19T15:50:26.860Z"],["3821425","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","And one more thing I hate rootly :what-the-hell:","2026-01-19T15:50:27.453Z"],["3821426","DBRE-8731","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","Well, even with TTL, it shouldn't break silently and should be able to continue from last offset","2026-01-19T15:50:28.279Z"],["3821427","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","If you are sure it’s TTL then I would suggest:\n1. open bug with PingCAP\n2. yes, rate limit TTL might be good workaround","2026-01-19T15:50:29.177Z"],["3821428","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","I will open a jira to rate limit TTL in all clusters","2026-01-19T15:50:29.842Z"],["3821429","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","TTL time coincides with the lag as it starts to build up","2026-01-19T15:50:30.409Z"],["3821430","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","The old ones we had broken CDC was because of message size too large [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1766402855124329?thread_ts=1766319703.808659&cid=GMBRX6L8M|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1766402855124329?thread_ts=1766319703.808659&cid=GMBRX6L8M|smart-link]","2026-01-19T15:50:30.947Z"],["3821431","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","I will rebuild the CDC  with current time stamp","2026-01-19T15:50:31.810Z"],["3821432","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","So now we create backfill ourself ?","2026-01-19T15:50:32.325Z"],["3821433","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Yes, but we still need auth from DAP for now","2026-01-19T15:50:32.922Z"],["3821434","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Steps:\n1. Find list of tables in DB schema/CDFC. You can use [this|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-ingestion/ingestion/configs?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22sourceCluster%22%3A%22ti-payments%22%2C%22sourceDatabase%22%3A%22taxify_payment%22%7D%7D] (see screenshot) to find tables.\n2. Check if each table has {{last_update}} or just {{created}}\n    ◦ Run one backfill for tables with {{last_update}} and use predicate like {{last_update >= '2026-01-18 05:00:00' AND last_update < '2026-01-18 06:05:00'}}\n    ◦ Run another backfill for tables with {{created}} and use predicate like {{created >= '2026-01-18 05:00:00' AND created < '2026-01-18 06:05:00'}}\n3. Ask DAP to approve backfill requests \n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9EL2LNDR/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_15.15.53.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9EL2LNDR/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_15.15.53.png|smart-link]","2026-01-19T15:50:33.596Z"],["3821435","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","eg of details: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-ingestion/ingestion/backfills/150116|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/data-platform-ingestion/ingestion/backfills/150116]","2026-01-19T15:50:34.292Z"],["3821436","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Let me know if you need help","2026-01-19T15:50:35.207Z"],["3821437","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Thank you :bowing:","2026-01-19T15:50:35.844Z"],["3821438","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/3871956|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/review-and-approval/requests/view/3871956]","2026-01-19T15:50:36.733Z"],["3821439","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Ah, can’t see (or approve) the details… anyway, ask DAP to approve\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA014FUBB/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_15.23.14.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA014FUBB/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_15.23.14.png|smart-link]","2026-01-19T15:50:37.351Z"],["3821441","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Currently on payment, I've kept rate limit to 10\nSo it means\n10 DELETE statements/sec × 100 rows/statement = 1,000 rows/sec per TiDB node\n\nDoes it look good?\nTTL will be slower, i know, but at least we'll be safe , I can increase the limit WDYT\n\n{noformat}| tidb_ttl_delete_batch_size              | 100         |\n| tidb_ttl_delete_rate_limit              | 10          |{noformat}","2026-01-19T15:50:38.061Z"],["3821442","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","On payment we have 6 TiDB nodes","2026-01-19T15:50:38.693Z"],["3821443","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","This is how it looks before and after\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAFFJS064/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_21.09.14.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AAFFJS064/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_21.09.14.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9M6FF890/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_21.10.01.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9M6FF890/screenshot_2026-01-19_at_21.10.01.png|smart-link]","2026-01-19T15:50:48.654Z"],["3821444","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","I don’t know the “best values” to throttle it to.. it would be the highest we can have without triggering stuck CDC and still being able to keep up with TTL deletion rate (ie,TTL is not so slow as to cause expired rows to pile up)","2026-01-19T15:50:49.290Z"],["3821445","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","True that,\nMaybe we can try turning it up slowly as we gather more data on how it behaves.\nLet [@marat.saddarov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3] be the decision maker .","2026-01-19T15:50:49.960Z"],["3821446","PTWS-2124","PTWS","oana.oprescu-pop@bolt.eu","Oana Oprescu-Pop","Clarification from Liis about 3PL - would it be possible to add them as a sub-category of Agency Staff? or something?\n\n!image-20260119-155030.png|width=499,alt=\"image-20260119-155030.png\"!","2026-01-19T15:51:15.934Z"],["3821447","DBRE-8705","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","CDC was stuck again. I tried to revive but couldn't :smiling_face_with_tear:","2026-01-19T15:51:18.235Z"],["3821449","XP-3041","XP","danil.kazakov@bolt.eu","Danil Kazakov","The plan so far:\n\n[^plan.md]\n\n","2026-01-19T15:52:17.453Z"],["3821453","LSS-61811","LSS","nils.kacars@bolt.eu","Nils Kacars","[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] once you have time, please review and approve all is in order. \nI have requested for clawback Invoice to be made by this Thursday ([FNDP-15943|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/28/FNDP-15943]). \nThank you,","2026-01-19T15:53:28.213Z"],["3821463","LSS-61616","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi all, [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] \n\nJust checking in to see if there are any updates on this.\n\nAs mentioned during the call, we need to provide feedback to our external counsel by tomorrow in order to move forward with next steps.\n\nThanks in advance for your input.\nElisabetta","2026-01-19T15:59:04.486Z"],["3821470","HS-29133","HS","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Please prioritise this as I need the document ASAP 🙏 ","2026-01-19T16:01:55.358Z"],["3821476","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Very good findings [~accountid:5e46575fc8ec310c955b0d4a] \nWe need to solve the 2nd issue with the frame or some jigs.\n\nFYI. [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] [~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] [~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] , as you see on the 2nd line, if you overdo the chain tensioning, the rear wheel will get under angle, and probably the chain will make noise. This was one of the assembly issues in Dynavolt. \n\n[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] My idea was to add some laser markings on the dropouts and anti-rotation washer. This won’t solve the issue completely if the frame isn’t in the correct shape tho. Perhaps jig could solve the issue, but it needs to be adjustable. \n\n!image-20260119-160221.png|width=1044,alt=\"image-20260119-160221.png\"!","2026-01-19T16:05:00.758Z"],["3821479","DSR-3623","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","From a pure DSAR POV:\n\n* Answer letter is good to go in theory. However, I would highly advise that we look into this potential data incident before we re-confirm that the account cannot be unblocked.\n* I am not entirely clear as to what I should review in these two folders:\n** “[SS-DSAR (PDE tool results here also?)|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M0DTxRasJp13JqcTzeUDPmV6CwWYWW9G/view?usp=drive_link]”\n** “[PDE tool results here|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1iB9jNd8W_amdJfHnsj8byMEuqtpKaYg-?usp=drive_link]”\n\n↪️ What input is needed from me here? The driver is essentially asking for an all-data export, so whichever folder contains a full PDE is good to go from my POV.\n\nAgain, before addressing the DSAR in full, let’s review what happened with this driver’s account. Feel free to add me to any chats you start with POCs - please do not let them push you away until we have clarity on whether an investigation has been conducted concerning this case and whether the driver’s claims that he was not at the source of the phone number change, along with the failed selfie verification, have been proven wrong.","2026-01-19T16:06:01.841Z"],["3821485","INT-828","INT","makani.bavya@bolt.eu","Bavya Makani","[~accountid:62a9857bd0132d0068809cdd] please add in any comments here","2026-01-19T16:09:55.065Z"],["3821486","LSS-57939","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] I’ve asked [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] to help you on this one as I’ll be off for vacation a few weeks. Please direct your questions regarding this to her. Thanks! ","2026-01-19T16:10:07.588Z"],["3821488","TAXP-794","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","The Australian Taxation Office published a [Recap of its Pillar Two November information session|https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/business-bulletins-newsroom/recap-of-our-pillar-two-november-information-session] on 9 January 2026.","2026-01-19T16:10:12.582Z"],["3821490","LSS-61586","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] I’ve asked [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] to help you on this one as I’ll be off for vacation a few weeks. Please direct your questions regarding this to her. Thanks! ","2026-01-19T16:10:30.079Z"],["3821491","LSS-59377","LSS","meda.baltramonaityte@bolt.eu","Meda Baltramonaitytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] \n\nFirst of all, thank you for your detailed response and for sharing concrete examples - it’s very helpful.\n\nI’d like to further clarify a few remaining pain points where we would still need your guidance.\n\nStarting with alcohol restrictions: alcohol cannot be restricted at a single-provider level, only per menu editing source. Currently, the alcohol tag is restricted only in Menu Editor, which is where the majority of our partners manage their menus independently.\n\nAdditionally, ensuring compliance on a per-provider basis would be very challenging. When it comes to collecting licenses, we are operating with very lean teams. Even if we asked partners to share their licenses with us, they could still upload alcohol items to their menus without informing us, as there are no effective restrictions preventing this. In fact, partners are already uploading restricted items (such as alcohol or energy drinks) today, often without using the appropriate tags, which are currently disabled for Menu Editor anyway.\n\nOverall, tracking and ensuring that all providers are fully compliant is not something we currently have the capacity to manage.\n\nOur intention is to offer alcohol ordering, especially considering that competitors already do so. However, given the constraints above, moving forward would likely mean a relatively lightweight launch approach: sending a mass communication with setup instructions, enabling it for the LT market, informing couriers, clearly outlining provider and courier responsibilities, and then reacting if issues arise. A more tightly controlled setup would be extremely difficult to enforce.","2026-01-19T16:10:56.244Z"],["3821492","LSS-61778","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] nothing here to be signed, I accidentally marked the ticket “to be signed”. Can this be cancelled?","2026-01-19T16:11:03.666Z"],["3821493","TAXP-1787","TAXP","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","hi [~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68] , are you ok with preparing the notification with the same wording as for [2024|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1grvi59melRMf82UY_i6h1gW77FVmNgld/view?usp=drive_link], just for 2025 or you want to change anything? Local rules have not changed.","2026-01-19T16:11:23.303Z"],["3821495","LSS-61586","LSS","emelie.dufva@bolt.eu","Emelie Dufva","*Signing sub-ticket* above was created by mistake, please disregard it [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] I can’t delete it. ","2026-01-19T16:12:02.507Z"],["3821496","PIF-3290","PIF","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-builder, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-19T16:12:48.799Z"],["3821498","DSR-3255","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - my apologies, I thought CSPC had instructions for LD cases 🤔 \n\nI have prepared the answer letter and reviewed the responsive data. Please send it via the same BH thread as it was received from, the email address is [+veezu@leighday.co.uk+|mailto:veezu@leighday.co.uk]\n\n# Provide the data saved in this [+folder+|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/18O-4NZFU1tjLj6QGZMV3Kh-e93CuHZjh?usp=drive_link].\n# Send the zip files to Leigh Day ([+veezu@leighday.co.uk+|mailto:veezu@leighday.co.uk]- it should be the same Beehive ticket as we have been using on this SD ticket) - the answer letter is in the Gdrive. \n# Monitor the ticket for 7 days and let me know if we receive any follow-ups. If not, the ticket can be closed.\n\nThank you! 🙏","2026-01-19T16:12:58.016Z"],["3821501","LSS-54833","LSS","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","Hello I have the revisions from their legal team here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L0vBWr384YXffHVilwDsyhLz3IQsTaWI/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L0vBWr384YXffHVilwDsyhLz3IQsTaWI/edit|smart-link] \n\nFrom them: \n\n“I have reviewed the Bolt agreement, and it appears only two points remain open:\n\n# Exclusivity: I have provided softened, further limited language which should be acceptable. I am open to proposals on this.\n# Limits of Liability: I have provided explanation for the carve-out of personal data breach, confidentiality breach, and IP infringement and provided a higher cap to address these exclusions.”\n\nAs regards exclusivity - there can be no exclusivity and I am happy to continue to cover this point with them.  But I thought best to capture your thoughts about the limits of liability and go back to them with everything together.  \nThanks for your help [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] \n\n","2026-01-19T16:13:20.440Z"],["3821504","DSR-3255","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","FYI [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab] - adding you for visibility as this is a request from Leigh Day. There’s no immediate action items needed from you on this (Privacy and CSPC are handling the request as we usually do), but it might be worth checking if this driver is a claimant in any current litigation.","2026-01-19T16:14:44.636Z"],["3821506","LSS-58320","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hi [~accountid:638e1e5f9960988ef6c1ec87],\n\nPlease find below the link to the final version of the form in both English and Spanish.\n\nKindly review it and, if you’re happy with it, feel free to proceed with its use. Otherwise, please let us know if you have any comments or suggested changes.\n\nMany thanks!\n\n\n\n[Consent Form|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1RxspRrExbdFeAU4H8-E8dUC4b6G1KhTfM48G0Ou1OnA/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-19T16:15:41.486Z"],["3821513","TAXP-1787","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","[~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] hi, looks good to me! Thank you! ","2026-01-19T16:19:06.592Z"],["3821519","LSS-56736","LSS","roisin.kirk@bolt.eu","Roisin Kirk","Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] Is it possible to get an ETA on this? It’s not super-urgent so fine if next week for example but would like to get this signed and secured.  Thank you ","2026-01-19T16:22:01.408Z"],["3821524","HS-29139","HS","evgenia.moronova@bolt.eu","Evgenia Moronova","[^Brichtova_E001976_ZL_012026.pdf]","2026-01-19T16:24:43.002Z"],["3821529","LSS-61436","LSS","sorina.mihai@bolt.eu","Sorina Mihai","Hey! Any idea when this doc will be signed? 🙂 I got a call from Omega, because they are done with the audit and I have to send their assessment tonight to the licensing authority. Which means we should have the contract signed today or tomorrow at the latest 🙂 \n\nSorina","2026-01-19T16:26:49.237Z"],["3821530","LSS-61515","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9], please could we discuss this ticket before sharing a response to Maria? She needs a response before her meeting with Total on Wednesday?\n\n+*Context*+ (to be applied to Wex or Total)\n\n* *Bolt Offer*: a reduction for drivers for their fuel expense\n* *Issue*: in order to create an “expense card”, drivers need to provide a deposit of the credit limit (usually between 300€ and 500€) - this creates a substantial financial burden for the drivers, and makes the offer less attractive. \n* *Suggested solution from Ops*: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/12qkyvT5ykjqhsxmle8leb3rFwD-97nsSILUQ9iDQ5X4/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/12qkyvT5ykjqhsxmle8leb3rFwD-97nsSILUQ9iDQ5X4/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n** Option 1: Bolt will be the owner of the contract and will work as guarantor for these drivers avoiding the caution. _(Recommended)_\n** Option 2: Each driver is responsible for their contract, Bolt pays the caution for the driver.\n** Option 3: Each driver is responsible for their contract, Bolt pays part of the caution, and the driver pays the remaining portion.\n* *In case of non-payment*:\n** Option 1: Bolt charges the driver directly from their earnings through the app \n** Option 2: Driver pays directly to partner\n*** In case of non-payment\n**** Can Bolt charge the driver directly from their earnings?\n**** Can Bolt block the driver?\n\n\nI had a meeting with Maria last week to discuss this offer, the issue and her suggested approach. I asked her to add more details to the document to help us advise on the risk and the impact of this suggestion. \n\n+*Preliminary thoughts*+\n\n* If the contract were to be with Bolt, and we are responsible in case of non-payment from drivers → *_reclassification risk_*, it could be interpreted as an employee/employer relationship + additional *_contractual friction_*, we would need to have a contract in place with the driver to allow us to recuperate any payment made in their name. \n* If we wish to follow the business in their initiative, the +business should weigh the potential loss of money vs the increase of GMV+ → unlikely to be a strong argument as the pilot will be with Diamond and Platinum drivers that are already top drivers, they won’t drive more, but it would help with platform fidelity and referrals (slow impact). \n* We should discuss with Maria if this pilot is meant as a “limited edition” offer that is meant to jump-start the program before going back to a normal deposit paid by the driver → in this case, we could offer a “no deposit offer” - and Bolt in the shadows becomes guarantor for any non-payments.\n* I thought about any FinReg limitation, but these don’t apply in my opinion because we are not handling or involved in any third-party mandate money (as opposed to the Bolt Car program/\n\nIn light of her document, my suggestion for her meeting on Wednesday would be:\n\n* *Discussion points with Total*:\n** Ask if we can proceed with a bank imprint on drivers, as opposed to a full deposit (responsability remains with drivers, instead of Bolt);\n** Still interested if this is short term pilot, for normal contract after?\n\n\n\nCan we discuss, and do you have any further issues that you would flag?\n\nThank you !","2026-01-19T16:28:19.945Z"],["3821531","PFI-835648","PFI","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","!Changes in VAT Law - GHana.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T16:28:53.454Z"],["3821532","PFI-835648","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-19T16:28:55.515Z"],["3821534","PFI-835649","PFI","wannapat.huang@bolt-outsource.eu","Wannapat Huang","!image-20260119-162021.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-162028.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-162035.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T16:31:24.028Z"],["3821536","LSS-61814","LSS","inorca.rudolph@bolt.eu","Inorca Rudolph","[^04. Abonnement opzeggen-Bijlage_1.pdf (3).pdf] _(269 kB)_\n\n[^H. Sesay 2950 Rechtbank -- Beschikking  002.pdf (2).pdf] _(97 kB)_","2026-01-19T16:34:45.323Z"],["3821537","LSS-61814","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nInorca Rudolph has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T16:34:46.860Z"],["3821538","PFI-835650","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T16:35:06.186Z"],["3821539","PFI-833340","PFI","sofija.politstsuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Sofija Politštšuk","Hello!\nUser let us know that despite this debt, they have no issues with using Bolt Food. The issue occurs only in Bolt app. \n\n","2026-01-19T16:38:14.992Z"],["3821543","PFI-835651","PFI","monica.acevedo@bolt.eu","Mónica Acevedo","!tecnum payment.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T16:43:00.574Z"],["3821546","LSS-61815","LSS","robin.schneider@bolt.eu","Robin Schneider","[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Clement Obazee (1).pdf] _(126 kB)_","2026-01-19T16:43:59.600Z"],["3821550","PFI-835652","PFI","blessing.eriaremhen@bolt-outsource.eu","Blessing Eriaremhen","!{B77E93A4-3233-4086-8D75-28B1C4E3F5E7}-20260119-164708.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T16:47:31.839Z"],["3821551","DSR-3057","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3][~accountid:5dbb027ba766000da47cf09d]  - It seems that that my instructions below were not fully followed:\n\n{quote}# The DSAR that was not handled - Deadline {{2026-01-23}}\n\n* In this [+ticket+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/539053418], the user asked the following:\n** A formal explanation of what exactly was found in your investigation,\n** The process followed in reaching this decision, and\n** Any documentation or records used in concluding this matter.\n* We need to review this request as per our usual Suspension DSAR processes, namely:\n** Follow the *Safety* suspension instructions. In doing so:\n*** Contact the relevant team concerning the block, ask about the HB - the usual process. Of course, the account itself cannot be reinstated as it has been deleted, but the HB could (in theory) be lifted for the driver to create a new account if they wish so.\n*** Extract the relevant data. Here, since we will *already* have shared the data that we hold about the driver in our first answer, what still needs to be sourced is the *Rider safety reports* that led to the HB. Please extract it, redact it (in _Suggestion_ mode for my review) and look for any other relevant tickets about the blocking decision. No need to source the tickets on the driver’s side: those will have been shared already.\n*** If you find any other data that you believe might be relevant, please flag it to me 🙏\n*** Prepare the answer letter as per the usual template, based on your findings.{quote}\n\n🔄 [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] reached out to the POCs and identified two cases: _The_ [+_first case_+ |https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/299824291]_was classified as_ *_high severity_*_, and the_ [+_second_+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/329686332] _as_ *_significant severity_*_. Additionally, there is a_ [+_rating_+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3502199?tab=driverRatings&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] _comment dated 18 November 2023._\n\n➡️ In the [folder|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QkNd4fmFRF8jWazYPXehlqc27kR4QQon] you linked below, there is only one document. Does that document contain all relevant cases? Ideally, we would provide different documents _or_ clearly separate each case - the current format is very confusing for the user (and anyone else looking at it).\n\n➡️ There does not seem to be any *redactions* (properly) done for the extracted tickets. For now, it looks like some of the content was replaced with “X”. *This is not in line with our standards nor regular approach*. Please review the tickets, extract them, and redact them as requested in my instructions. If you are not sure on what/how to redact, do it in _suggestion_ mode for my review. If you need help, please ask [~accountid:603cb85ec58c720071175949] to show you how she usually 1) extracts specific tickets, and 2) redacts information.\n\n➡️ Please keep the tickets in their *original language* - not translated to English. \n\n➡️ Please review the answer letter. Currently, there are dates missing, symbols (e.g. brackets: [ ), as well as instructions (e.g. “CLAUSE NUMBER”) left throughout the draft answer.\n\nOnce the above is done, please re-escalate to me.","2026-01-19T16:47:53.951Z"],["3821552","DELIVERY-91","DELIVERY","bertalan.vad@bolt.eu","Bertalan Vad","26W4: M2 finished last week alongside with topics like location-change-reset and toast-position-interaction-with-recently-viewed-cta, M3 started","2026-01-19T16:51:11.196Z"],["3821553","LSS-60711","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","Thanks [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] The landlord has confirmed that we can use either wet or digital signature depending on our preference.","2026-01-19T16:51:23.019Z"],["3821558","DSR-3351","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Status update: \n\n* asked Radu for a more precise screenshot of the consent, which includes all column names\n* Also enquired whether the driver can be opted out from these communications going forward.\n\n:loading: ","2026-01-19T16:54:39.997Z"],["3821560","LSS-60177","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","Thanks [~accountid:63dba2fb1b13d42998e22e00] [~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] ! As only one invoice is currently overdue (is it overdue by a long time?), do you still want us to look into this further? In that case, could you upload the contract we have with them?","2026-01-19T16:55:34.373Z"],["3821561","RDS-138","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","I spoke to a driver today who suggested showing multiple route options like google maps - faster vs shorter. Or rather his input was: we show him sometime very complicated routes with many twists and turns, small roads, through gas stations etc. Where he would prefer just to go along the main roads sometimes.","2026-01-19T16:56:00.616Z"],["3821562","PFI-835654","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^Factura Bolt.pdf.pdf]\n\n[^op bolt.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-19T16:56:10.758Z"],["3821564","PFI-834554","PFI","luc.nassif@bolt-outsource.eu","Luc Richard Nassif","Hello, please, I apply an investigative suspension on the account. You can proceed with the removal of the definitive suspension.","2026-01-19T16:57:23.133Z"],["3821566","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","*Update*:\n1. {{int_matching_blast_rounds}} and {{int_rides_company_order_event}} are fully refreshed.\n2. The following PR to remove faulty records from fact_rides_order: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15397|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15397]. Can anyone please provide a review on this? I am unsure whether to add  ``{{ and }}hive_metastore` in the script.","2026-01-19T16:58:44.742Z"],["3821567","DELIVERY-1813","DELIVERY","giacomo.giorgianni@bolt.eu","Giacomo Giorgianni","*Reference Slack thread for more info*: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03NX4L2K4G/p1768400617425949|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03NX4L2K4G/p1768400617425949|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T16:58:55.356Z"],["3821571","UKIGFT-101","UKIGFT","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Copies of notices delivered by process server to *landlord, Essex County Council* (with copies to *Aviva Investors Global Services Ltd* and *JLL Limited* (the landlord’s managing agent)) on *Friday 16 January 2026*, in respect of 2F, 3F and 4F of Stylus building.  Postal copies were also sent. \n\n\n\n[^Warwick St, London - Letter to JLL and copy notice - Third Floor.pdf]\n[^Warwick St, London - Letter to JLL and copy notice - Second floor.pdf]\n[^Warwick St, London - Letter to JLL and copy notice - Fourth Floor.pdf]\n[^Fenchurch St, London - Letter to Aviva and copy notice - Third Floor.pdf]\n[^Fenchurch St, London - Letter to Aviva and copy notice - Second Floor.pdf]\n[^Fenchurch St, London - Letter to Aviva and copy notice - Fourth Floor.pdf]\n[^Chelmsford - Break Notice - Third Floor.pdf]\n[^Chelmsford - Break notice - Second Floor.pdf]\n[^Chelmsford - Break notice - Fourth Floor.pdf]\n[^Case Update - JPK_248365.0004.eml]\n[^Case Update - JPK_248365.0004_2.eml]\n[^Case Update - JPK_248365.0004_1.eml]\n[^finalreport_4045942042.pdf]\n[^finalreport_4045921241.pdf]\n[^finalreport_4045453614.pdf]\n[^1612026162027_proof of service - 4th floor.pdf]\n[^1612026161856_proof of service - 3rd floor.pdf]\n[^1612026161733_proof of service - 2nd floor.pdf]\n[^1612026161228_proof of service - 2nd floor.pdf]\n[^1612026161050_proof of service - 3rd floor.pdf]\n[^1612026143428_proof of service - 4th floor.pdf]\n[^1612026143257_proof of service - 3rd floor.pdf]\n[^161202616922_proof of service - 4th floor.pdf]\n[^161202614365_proof of service - 2nd floor.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-19T16:59:35.647Z"],["3821572","DSR-1858","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, thanks for the ping - this one slipped my radar. Could you please de-escalate to T2/Local Ops? The follow-up questions aren’t really Privacy-driver anymore in my opinion.","2026-01-19T16:59:38.710Z"],["3821574","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","*Update*:\n\n# {{int_matching_blast_rounds}} and {{int_rides_company_order_event}} are fully refreshed.\n# The following PR to remove faulty records from fact_rides_order: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15397|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15397|smart-link] .\n\nAction Item:\n\nWaiting for PR review\n\n*Next Steps:*\n\n# Backfill {{fact_rides_order}}for the affected dates.","2026-01-19T17:00:23.759Z"],["3821580","DSR-3295","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, we can share the driver report and the photo attached with it (similar to the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CS/pages/6682379007/CS+Privacy+Compliance+Operational+Playbook#Rider-requests-a-picture-of-the-mess-made-in-vehicle|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CS/pages/6682379007/CS+Privacy+Compliance+Operational+Playbook#Rider-requests-a-picture-of-the-mess-made-in-vehicle|smart-link] , but without de-escalating to T2).\n\nCould you please:\n\n* Extract the driver ticket and redact it as appropriate,\n* Extract the picture shared by the driver,\n* Prepare an answer letter - you can take inspiration from the driver suspension templates","2026-01-19T17:06:11.200Z"],["3821585","SAI-1412","SAI","nosheen.jahan@bolt.eu","Nosheen Jahan","cc: [@nikola.spoustova|https://taxify.slack.com/team/U03ELJQJ2Q3]","2026-01-19T17:09:52.059Z"],["3821586","PFI-835678","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Report can be found in Google Drive folder: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Tv1K2FOxzRg_OjifW99b19A-5sRLyKx8\n\nPlease check the \"reconciliation\" tab for statistics.","2026-01-19T17:11:41.828Z"],["3821587","LSS-58645","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","The partner has been notified to review the shared the document. I will share update during the week. \n\nThanks for the patience. ","2026-01-19T17:13:02.272Z"],["3821588","MARTECH3-1525","MARTECH3","wahyu.herlambang@bolt.eu","Wahyu Herlambang","Progress:\n\nI’ve built:\n\n* {{int_dim_ads_linkedin}}\n* {{ads_bm_metrics__linkedin}}\n\nand updated:\n\n* {{dim_ads}}\n* {{etl_marketing_ads_bm_metrics}}\n\nin [https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3599265223939596?o=3829506390716583#command/6228192695803595|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3599265223939596?o=3829506390716583#command/6228192695803595]\n\nSanity check: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1t45bhnxG7RfhP9nDlzUkmE3vVduXR41D0apAJPp4S5c/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1t45bhnxG7RfhP9nDlzUkmE3vVduXR41D0apAJPp4S5c/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] \n\nNote: 0 discrepancy in impressions, clicks, and spend","2026-01-19T17:13:53.950Z"],["3821591","LSS-58917","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","The partner has been notified to provide additional company details. The document should be ready for final review by the end of the week. \n\nthanks. ","2026-01-19T17:14:23.168Z"],["3821593","LSS-58637","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","We can close the ticket as the partner pulled out of the deal. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-19T17:14:54.801Z"],["3821597","DSR-3349","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, please answer the following:\n\n{quote}Dear [name],\n\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *EDIT: DATE*.\n\nAs communicated in previous correspondences, we confirm that your driver account was permanently deleted on 17 December 2025, following your request. As a result, your account is no longer active, cannot be accessed, and cannot be used to provide services on the Bolt platform. This deletion is effective and not merely formal.\n\nTo be clear, account deletion does not mean that all personal data is immediately erased in every system. Under the applicable data protection law, Bolt is required and entitled to retain limited categories of personal data after account deletion where this is necessary and lawful.\n\nCertain limited data may be retained after account deletion strictly for the purposes set out below, in line with Article 6(1)(c) and 6(1)(f) GDPR:\n\n* Accounting and tax data, retained for up to 10 years after the last trip, where required by law\n* Payment, invoicing and earnings records, for statutory and audit obligations\n* Records related to disputes, complaints, fraud prevention or legal claims, retained only for as long as necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims\n* Regulatory and compliance records, where retention is required by transport, licensing or other applicable laws\n\nThese data are not used to operate an account, are not visible in the app, and are placed under restricted access with appropriate technical and organisational safeguards. The applicable retention periods and legal bases are described in detail in the Global Privacy Notice for Drivers, which applies to former drivers as well as active ones:\n[https://bolt.eu/sv-se/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/|https://bolt.eu/sv-se/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/|smart-link] \n\nThe continued existence of limited retained data for legal or compliance purposes does not mean that your account remains active, reinstatable or usable. It also does not mean that Bolt is processing your data for service provision, marketing, profiling or analytics purposes.\n\nPlease note that Bolt has already provided you with clear confirmations and explanations regarding account deletion and post-deletion data retention as an answer to your previous requests. Repeated requests raising the same points, including via newly created fleet accounts, do not change the legal position or Bolt’s obligations under the applicable data protection framework.\n\nBased on the above, Bolt considers your request to have been fully addressed. We will not engage further on this matter unless you raise materially new facts or identify a specific GDPR right that has not already been exercised and responded to.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.\n\nSincerely,{quote}","2026-01-19T17:18:47.846Z"],["3821599","PFI-835653","PFI","yurii.bilynskyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Yurii Bilynskyi","case closed","2026-01-19T17:19:37.561Z"],["3821601","LSS-61816","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","[^Bolt BOLT LEASE AGREEMENT rev 30-12-2025 (tracked) (1).pdf] _(15.11 MB)_","2026-01-19T17:19:52.965Z"],["3821602","LSS-60176","LSS","karl.laspina@bolt.eu","Karl Laspina","Thanks Catarina! Clear from my side. Feature has been suspended for now.","2026-01-19T17:19:53.631Z"],["3821603","LSS-61669","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:13ae7353-697f-46e7-99dd-8fc938931751] , [~accountid:712020:201fe54a-837d-4edc-aca4-132aa5cf7401] ,\n\nFor clarity purposes, we have made some minor adjustments to the agreement, that you will find in track changes [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FSqUTEP6E9p0lfeLJk9pYGenSHj_dnysJV6LM3cI2zU/edit?usp=sharing]. None of them are material, so we do not foresee any problem for the PY Animal Defense Institution to accept them.\n\n\n\nPlease let us know if you have any comments or questions.\n\nOnce you have the final version of the agreement, you can send it to us again and we will proceed with the signing.\n\nBest,\n\nAngela","2026-01-19T17:22:45.927Z"],["3821606","LSS-61817","LSS","zohra.brahim@bolt.eu","Zohra Brahim","[^image19-01-2026-180637.pdf] _(4.35 MB)_","2026-01-19T17:25:18.088Z"],["3821607","DSR-3275","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC,\n\n* I’ve reviewed and amended the answer letter to include a section on automated-decision making, as the driver asked about it  (/) \n* The responsive data is good to go (/) \n\nPlease go ahead and share the answer and responsive data with the driver.","2026-01-19T17:25:57.838Z"],["3821609","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","Hello [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] \n\nIn [~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] absence, letting you know that we received a reply from the Faro PSP: \n\n\n\n_Exma. Senhora Sofia Cartó,_\n\n \n\n_Na qualidade de instrutora do Inquérito que decorre neste Núcleo de Deontologia e Disciplina da PSP de Faro, e porque se reveste de primordial importância,_\n\n_solicito ainda aos bons ofícios da BOLT_ *_a relação dos dias de em que foram prestadas as viagens referidas._*\n\n \n\n_Antecipadamente grata_\n\n \n\n_Com os melhores cumprimentos,_\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:ab95f96b-73f1-4bb8-a5fd-5178ef3f1339] [~accountid:5b7bea09d08e47445d6fd01e] ","2026-01-19T17:27:20.411Z"],["3821611","DSR-3521","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] , could you please clarify what is needed from me here? There does not seem to be much data nor an answer letter for me to review, and there is also no direct question at me. ","2026-01-19T17:28:25.487Z"],["3821612","L10N-28615","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.790Z"],["3821613","L10N-28616","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.790Z"],["3821614","L10N-28613","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.847Z"],["3821615","L10N-28609","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.873Z"],["3821616","L10N-28608","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.873Z"],["3821617","L10N-28604","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.884Z"],["3821618","L10N-28617","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.890Z"],["3821619","L10N-28607","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.893Z"],["3821620","L10N-28611","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.903Z"],["3821621","L10N-28606","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.902Z"],["3821622","L10N-28603","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:50.936Z"],["3821623","L10N-28618","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:51.027Z"],["3821624","L10N-28612","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:51.061Z"],["3821625","L10N-28610","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:51.143Z"],["3821626","L10N-28605","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:51.182Z"],["3821627","L10N-28614","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-19T17:28:51.214Z"],["3821631","LSS-61817","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T17:31:40.286Z"],["3821632","INT-828","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:712020:dea8d3b8-5acd-466f-bc9c-4f25bcbc0cf6] [~accountid:712020:19830dc9-dbe8-4900-9dbb-62c41b407f4e] I’ve added a few metrics to description and [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dedNH3Qs8AUIjxK5Dlmv0LqJzR8hzbRlKmHEeKgrGwo/edit?gid=1440263319#gid=1440263319]. Also I’ve noticed that not all metrics / drill downs from this file are implemented (from ABC sections, not from “New additions”). I’ll create a separate Jira ticket to address those later in the future. ","2026-01-19T17:34:31.478Z"],["3821634","DSR-3487","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC,\n\n* Please extract the relevant CS tickets, as per the user’s request (currently there are only phone recordings in the GDrive);\n* On the CCTV question, you can leverage the following wording:\nPlease note that drivers using the Bolt platform are independent providers and not Bolt employees. If a driver records, they act as an independent data controller under data protection law and are solely responsible for ensuring that such processing complies with the GDPR and local legislation. Bolt does not provide, install or control any recording devices, and we do not have access to or the ability to provide such content to passengers.\n* There’s no internal note _per se_ that we can share - the ones in the tickets are not to be shared. Usually, we might consider sharing profile comments associated with the request, but there are none in this case.","2026-01-19T17:36:07.116Z"],["3821635","INT-828","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","I’ve also extended AM report fields, let’s check tomorrow with Klavs if that’s enough.","2026-01-19T17:37:34.276Z"],["3821637","LSS-59015","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","Hello team, the lawyer came back with another request after our previous reply: \n\n{quote}_Exmos. Senhores,_\n\n_Os m/ cumprimentos,_\n\n_Acusamos a receção da V/ comunicação, cujo teor não podemos deixar de contestar, por assentar em pressupostos factuais incorretos e numa leitura descontextualizada das comunicações trocadas entre a minha Constituinte e a Bolt._\n\n_Desde logo, importa esclarecer, de forma inequívoca, que não existem quaisquer incongruências nas explicações prestadas pela minha Constituinte._\n\n_A primeira situação que referem infra ocorreu em 17/07, tendo sido devidamente esclarecida à data e ultrapassada, não tendo dado origem a qualquer manutenção de bloqueio ou sanção definitiva._\n\n_A segunda situação, distinta da anterior, ocorreu em 03/08. Relativamente a esta, e ao contrário do que é alegado, a versão dos factos apresentada pela minha Constituinte foi sempre a mesma, traduzindo uma única realidade factual: – o pedido de verificação num primeiro equipamento com câmara avariada; – a subsequente utilização de um segundo telemóvel para concluir a verificação; – a circunstância de tal procedimento ter ocorrido durante uma deslocação entre Porto e Vila Nova de Gaia, o que explica as variações de localização registadas._\n\n_As diferentes formulações utilizadas nas comunicações refletem apenas explicações dadas em momentos distintos, por canais informais e sem assistência jurídica, não consubstanciando versões incompatíveis ou contraditórias, nem muito menos falsas, sendo todas congruentes entre si._\n\n_Importa ainda sublinhar que a minha Constituinte sempre manteve um histórico irrepreensível na plataforma, com avaliações e comentários extremamente positivos, sem qualquer registo prévio de comportamentos fraudulentos, incumprimentos ou violações dos Termos e Condições. Tal circunstância torna a medida aplicada manifestamente desproporcionada e injustificada, sobretudo quando assente em presunções não demonstradas._\n\n_Acresce que a minha Constituinte dispõe de prova testemunhal relevante para o esclarecimento integral da situação, designadamente a Sra. Maria Emília Silva, com o endereço eletrónico_ [_bibica589@msn.com_|http://bibica589@msn.com/] _<_[_mailto:bibica589@msn.com_|http://mailto:bibica589@msn.com/]_> , que já entrou em contacto convosco e que, tal como a minha Constituinte, foi extremamente mal recebida nas vossas instalações pela Sra. Luana, vossa funcionária, circunstância que poderá ser oportunamente confirmada._\n\n_Mais uma vez, a conclusão da Bolt — no sentido de que o registo fotográfico não corresponde à minha Constituinte ou que indicia a intervenção de terceiros — não é acompanhada de qualquer prova objetiva, limitando-se a afirmações genéricas. Nessa medida, e para efeitos de pleno esclarecimento, requer-se expressamente o envio da fotografia submetida aquando da segunda verificação que esteve na origem da suspensão e o histórico completo do registo de GPS associado ao momento da referida verificação, com indicação temporal detalhada._\n\n_Por fim, reitera-se que a aplicação automática e definitiva da sanção máxima — suspensão permanente da conta — sem ponderação concreta dos factos, do histórico da motorista, da existência de prova testemunhal e da inexistência de prova de utilização por terceiros, não se mostra proporcional, nem compatível com os princípios gerais que devem reger a atuação de entidades privadas com impacto direto no exercício de uma atividade profissional._\n\n_Aguardamos, assim, o envio dos elementos solicitados, após o que nos pronunciaremos de forma definitiva._\n\n_Com os melhores cumprimentos,_\n\n_Adriana João Lomba_\n_Advogada_{quote}\n\n\n\nHer message was sent through [*this Beehive Ticket*|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726073659]","2026-01-19T17:38:24.764Z"],["3821638","PAW-14994","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sergey-seleznev\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17218\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-19 17:38:40 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-19T17:38:40.957Z"],["3821639","DAEN-1346","DAEN","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Changes have been applied; I guess we can proceed with backfill.","2026-01-19T17:38:44.201Z"],["3821640","DAEN-1346","DAEN","zafrullah.bhatti@bolt.eu","Zafar Bhatti","Backfilling {{fact_rides_order}} under job:\n\n[https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/573689295413053/runs/204440378297597?focus_task=execute&o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/573689295413053/runs/204440378297597?focus_task=execute&o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-19T17:39:38.732Z"],["3821642","PFI-835714","PFI","adeline.gbandi@bolt-outsource.eu","Adeline Gbandi","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 5.38.48 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T17:40:44.993Z"],["3821643","DSR-3363","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, [~accountid:6001a723d364960139286c95] thanks a lot for the good investigative work and updates on this ticket 🙏 \n\nI have added a line concerning the automated decision-making to the answer letter. Please go ahead with sharing the answer and responsive data with the driver.","2026-01-19T17:40:46.548Z"],["3821644","PFI-835715","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T17:43:09.735Z"],["3821646","BIZ-297","BIZ","thiago.oliveira@bolt.eu","Thiago Ibrahim","Bolt Franchise team is in Dubai meeting with the partner and should have a better update in the coming week.","2026-01-19T17:46:29.156Z"],["3821647","DSR-3547","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC,\n\n* Please make sure that the following plugins are provided to the driver:\nDriver blocks, verifications, driver devices, driver security\n* [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] - since this is a *formal* communication from Bolt to a user, please refrain from using abbreviations (“Oct”) in your answers.\n* !Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 7.44.49 PM.png|width=590,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 7.44.49 PM.png\"!\nI have added a section on automated decision-making to the answer letter.\n\n\n\nOnce the answer letter has been corrected and the data extracted, please share both with the driver.","2026-01-19T17:46:51.224Z"],["3821648","DAEN-1346","DAEN","jens.dobrindt@bolt.eu","Jens Dobrindt","Will other tables (like {{mart_models_spark.mart_rides_order}}) be fixed automatically with the overnight runs or do they require manual backfilling as well?","2026-01-19T17:48:18.567Z"],["3821649","LSS-60176","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Thank you, [~accountid:6320602ec7601c8e4abeda47] !\nIf there are no additional questions/comments, I will close this ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-19T17:49:44.453Z"],["3821654","C2-461","C2","konstantin.karhu@bolt.eu","Konstantin Karhu","Added the possibility of picture upload for every *Fail* reason to Google Form.\nCommunicated to both repair partners in respective channels ([EDC Slack message|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C078MAF8U8J/p1768845257807599], [Ilvestments Slack message|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SXJNJ50Q/p1768845332538809] )","2026-01-19T17:58:50.341Z"],["3821655","L10N-28807","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28804](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28804)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T17:58:58.175Z"],["3821656","L10N-28810","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28804](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28804)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T17:58:59.498Z"],["3821657","L10N-28811","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28804](https://taxify.atlassian.net/brows