ontent owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28804](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28804)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T17:59:07.416Z"],["3821666","L10N-28831","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28804](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28804)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T17:59:07.909Z"],["3821667","L10N-28832","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28804](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28804)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-19T17:59:08.655Z"],["3821674","LSS-61668","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Note - 19.01.2026:\n\nRequested an extension of the deadline directly via email, in order to prevent the application of a fine.","2026-01-19T18:01:49.294Z"],["3821676","LSS-58339","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Hey, \n\nZavki Ruziev has an account, found the comment about the trip which was reported on his profile. The car is also assigned to him, the car documents show, that the owner is Ernestas Paulauskas. The driver is not performing activity since the accident. There were no reports about driver being not the same, but this case reveals us that this was an account sharing event, and from Operational POV I can now see some indications of that after digging.\n\nThe driver is assigned to fleet, but from what I see, the owners of differrent cars vary.\n\nThe car was only added to this fleet, and Ernestas Paulauskas hadn’t had an account in RH. \n\n[~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] do we know anything about the status of Loginesa, and whether this fleet is “private” drivers fleet (accepts drivers with their own rented-found cars) or they have shared ownership with current FO? \n\nThe driver is not performing activity since the accident, he was blocked (account). \nThere were no reports about driver being not the same as in app, but this case reveals us that this was an account sharing event. \n\nI am adding the ticket here as well as it reached us via [ticket.|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/724183849]\n\n","2026-01-19T18:03:26.079Z"],["3821678","HS-29084","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","New task.","2026-01-19T18:06:45.953Z"],["3821679","PFI-835730","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^Comprobante bolt diciembre.pdf]","2026-01-19T18:07:38.259Z"],["3821681","PFI-835518","PFI","tanja.ziros@bolt-outsource.eu","Tanja Žiroš","In this case, it is a user who correctly ordered a ride and the invoice was issued to a business account. The issue is that two information are missing: fiscal codes: ZKI (issuer’s security code) and JIR (unique invoice identifier).  Please let me know if this information should be visible so we can close this case. Thank you in advance! ","2026-01-19T18:10:31.670Z"],["3821688","PFI-835518","PFI","tanja.ziros@bolt-outsource.eu","Tanja Žiroš","Also we have two more cases like this: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726102387|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726102387]\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726332451|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726332451]","2026-01-19T18:17:44.221Z"],["3821689","PFI-835735","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^BOLT PAGO DICIEMBRE 2025 B00PQH30T (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T18:17:47.760Z"],["3821693","RNTL-30188","RNTL","enari.saar@bolt.eu","Enari Saar","{noformat}ffmpeg -v error -i input_file.mkv -f null -{noformat}\n\nThis logs all the errors if there is any. If there are any timestamp errors, converting from mkv to mp4 should fix them.\n\n","2026-01-19T18:19:23.642Z"],["3821698","PFI-835736","PFI","christian.barrios@bolt.eu","Christian Junior Barrios Brassel","!Uniflex_2374450.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T18:22:36.804Z"],["3821699","PFI-833886","PFI","koffi.agoudavi@bolt-outsource.eu","Koffi Escande Marius Agoudavi","Hello Team ,\n\nOn the rider’s account, we can see some rides with the order billing profile set to *Business* and some with a business payment method. But none of these rides show up when searched from the company account. \n\n\n\n","2026-01-19T18:25:54.737Z"],["3821700","WD-22610","WD","lillian.martin@bolt.eu","Lillian Martin","Please note that there is a ticket on the topic from Jizel in parallel 😉 ","2026-01-19T18:26:21.643Z"],["3821701","LSS-61816","LSS","siret.saks@bolt.eu","Siret Saks","Hi Ololade,\n\nIn what currency does the supplier invoice us?\n\nKind regards,\n\nSiret","2026-01-19T18:26:56.769Z"],["3821704","LSS-61818","LSS","pedro.alecrim@bolt.eu","Pedro Alecrim","[^29-12-2025 PE_31_2025.pdf] _(588 kB)_","2026-01-19T18:32:34.046Z"],["3821705","PFI-835742","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 3.31.22 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T18:33:28.888Z"],["3821706","RDS-1246","RDS","chantel.rowe@bolt.eu","Chantel Rowe","[~accountid:5f5b4e09df83ab007d8c9a83] this is pretty much good to go - who do you want to assign it to?","2026-01-19T18:37:28.364Z"],["3821707","PFI-835743","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 3.31.32 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T18:41:02.186Z"],["3821712","LSS-61818","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T18:46:06.188Z"],["3821730","PFI-835749","PFI","jan.dohnal@bolt-outsource.eu","Jan Dohnal","!image-20260119-190856.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260119-190906.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T19:10:03.063Z"],["3821734","LSS-58632","LSS","diego.ramirezgoelz@bolt.eu","Diego Ramirez-Gölz","Have addressed with [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117] in Dec. - waiting for feedback. ","2026-01-19T19:22:38.522Z"],["3821739","PFI-835756","PFI","elvin.hasanov@bolt-outsource.eu","Elvin Hasanov","[^05mk6s15pq1elb.pdf]\n\n[^1610428XO2601090004.pdf]","2026-01-19T19:30:28.899Z"],["3821740","DBRE-7144","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","* Added alerts [https://github.com/bolteu/kubernetes-main/pull/8359|https://github.com/bolteu/kubernetes-main/pull/8359|smart-link] \n* Wrote Runbooks [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/4050223273/TiDB+runbooks#TiDB-Restore-Test-alerts|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/4050223273/TiDB+runbooks#TiDB-Restore-Test-alerts|smart-link] \n* Adjusted Docs [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7389742144/TiDB+Automated+Backup+Restore+Testing|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7389742144/TiDB+Automated+Backup+Restore+Testing|smart-link] ","2026-01-19T19:32:26.873Z"],["3821741","PFI-835759","PFI","monica.acevedo@bolt.eu","Mónica Acevedo","!vilux sa.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T19:35:34.357Z"],["3821743","PFI-835760","PFI","barbora.trstenicova@bolt-outsource.eu","Barbora Trsteničová","!1000006161.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T19:39:03.987Z"],["3821751","PFI-835765","PFI","josephine.anetekhai@bolt-outsource.eu","Josephine Anetekhai","!{86DB492C-EEEE-4E12-92EE-2D53D2F889A5}-20260119-195851.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T19:59:19.132Z"],["3821752","PFI-835769","PFI","gabriela.rios@bolt.eu","Gabriela Rios","[^PAGO BOLT MES DICIEMBRE..pdf.pdf]","2026-01-19T20:00:54.286Z"],["3821755","PFI-835771","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T20:07:07.080Z"],["3821756","PFI-835772","PFI","obozna.oleksandrivna@bolt.eu","Kateryna Obozna","[^Підписана_зі_всіх_сторін_Угода_щодо_виконання_доручення_Лебідь_Тетяна (1).pdf]","2026-01-19T20:08:07.769Z"],["3821758","PFI-835773","PFI","george.ghiveciu@bolt.eu","George-Mihai Ghiveciu","[^PaymentProof2600213045461000 (12).pdf]","2026-01-19T20:14:09.275Z"],["3821759","LSS-61819","LSS","luke.grima@bolt.eu","Luke Grima","[^Bolt Mandat Ta Sekwestru.pdf] _(1.64 MB)_\n\n[^Sequester Order Pt.1 ] _(173 kB)_\n\n!Sequester Pt. 2.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T20:14:40.849Z"],["3821760","LSS-61819","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nLuke Grima has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-19T20:14:41.994Z"],["3821761","CRC-2329","CRC","dmitriy.filippov@bolt.eu","Dmitriy Filippov","[update] Got a feedback from the 1st dry-run, adjusted rules accordingly. Some processes in Payroll team should be adjusted, waiting for them.","2026-01-19T20:15:22.241Z"],["3821762","LSS-61819","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-19T20:16:06.111Z"],["3821764","CRC-2336","CRC","dmitriy.filippov@bolt.eu","Dmitriy Filippov","[update] Waiting for settings change by Deutsche Bank (a crucial field is missing from a statement). They are informed, waiting for a confirmation from their side when it’s fixed.","2026-01-19T20:18:44.359Z"],["3821768","SREC-372","SREC","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","All affected instances have been rebooted. Kernels have been updated successfully. No more critical findings in AWS inspector.","2026-01-19T20:34:40.343Z"],["3821777","PFI-835771","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ → The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see to_execute → it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-19T21:00:47.162Z"],["3821778","PFI-835715","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ → The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see to_execute → it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-19T21:00:47.995Z"],["3821779","PFI-835650","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Adjustments, Compensations*\n* If driver was compensated a while ago in some CS ticket - and this compensation is still not added to driver's balance -> please raise it with Local operations.\n\n*Why?* \nWhen Compensation is created in CS ticket -> it gets added to a csv file. Then local ops take it once a month and submit it into Manual Adjustment tool. They might submit it late, or submitting csv file gets delayed.\n\n\n*Campaign Bonus*\n* If driver did not recevei a bonus for a campaign -> please raise it with campaign team.\n\n*Why?*\nBilling team does not handle campaign setups. So we do not know when, why, how drivers should receive bonuses.\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-19T21:00:48.681Z"],["3821780","WD-22612","WD","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","[^Bolt Poland Sick leaves upload.xlsx]\n\n[^Bolt Services Sick leaves upload.xls]","2026-01-19T21:11:20.799Z"],["3821785","PFI-835784","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-19T21:30:54.314Z"],["3821786","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","It’s done.","2026-01-19T21:33:19.269Z"],["3821793","PFI-834461","PFI","peter.uyokei@bolt-outsource.eu","Peter Uyokei","Hi Team,\n\nCustomer’s account details:\n\n* Moniepoint \n* Okoro Onyebuchi Matthew\n* 7042442168 \n\n","2026-01-19T22:03:42.830Z"],["3821795","PFI-835715","PFI","daniel.oplistil@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniel Oplistil","driver wants earning reports for each month, I can find only invoices for commisions","2026-01-19T22:09:05.963Z"],["3821796","PFI-835794","PFI","joy.abu@bolt-outsource.eu","Joy Abu","!image-20260119-221134.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-19T22:11:56.264Z"],["3821798","PFI-835496","PFI","ricardo.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu","Ricardo Fernandes","Is it possible to confirm that this pre-authorization has been released?","2026-01-19T22:13:27.241Z"],["3821802","WFM-10045","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","[*Request*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601724]\n\n[*UserProfile*|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-user/users/edit/352594?tab=details]","2026-01-19T22:18:52.917Z"],["3821805","WFM-10047","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello [~accountid:712020:a4f6dc7f-ea2b-4b6c-87be-3ca7829f155a] ,\n\nCould you please provide a screenshot of the error appearing in the agent’s screen? After checking the agent’s profile, could see he has all the necessary roles.","2026-01-19T22:21:46.913Z"],["3821811","HS-29014","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Hi [~accountid:712020:740c6298-2781-402d-b09b-daba42f340a2] \n\nI have uploaded the letter to signing. You will receive a copy to your personal email (taken from Workday) once it’s been signed. If you don’t see it in your inbox, I suggest checking the spam folder. Sometimes the letters from Box like to hide there.\n\nLet me know if anything else is needed. I hope your doctor switch goes well!\n\nBest\nAlice, People Ops ","2026-01-19T22:41:30.102Z"],["3821812","PFI-834896","PFI","mykyta.osmalianyi@bolt-outsource.eu","Mykyta Osmalianyi","No changes yet","2026-01-19T22:46:24.330Z"],["3821815","LSS-61480","LSS","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","It's 6:30–7:00 PM here; I'm usually driving home or having dinner then.\n\n\n\n\n*Susan Shao*\n*Sr. Procurement Manager | **Bolt China*\n*susan.shao@bolt.eu <susan.shao@bolt.eu>*\n*(+86) 18662160708*\nblog.bolt.eu\n<https://blog.bolt.eu/?utm_source=email_signature&utm_medium=banner&utm_campaign=email_signature_banner>\n\n[image: Bolt Logo]","2026-01-19T23:16:19.128Z"],["3821816","WFM-10045","WFM","giovanna.novaes@bolt.eu","Giovanna Sochiarelli da Costa Novaes","Hello!\n\nAccess granted. Have a good day!","2026-01-19T23:16:20.272Z"],["3821820","PFI-821627","PFI","barbora.trstenicova@bolt-outsource.eu","Barbora Trsteničová","Please, any new info?","2026-01-19T23:48:58.221Z"],["3821822","PFI-835813","PFI","victor.oradare@bolt-outsource.eu","Victor Oradare","[^Statement_1802853270_20260120010158.pdf]","2026-01-20T00:10:35.866Z"],["3821824","FX-3672","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768868464118919]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3672] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T00:21:21.413Z"],["3821825","PFI-835784","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-20T01:00:43.363Z"],["3821826","PFI-835815","PFI","thitiporn.khumphai@bolt-outsource.eu","Thitiporn Khumphai","!image-20260120-010319.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-010326.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T01:04:25.176Z"],["3821827","HS-29114","HS","dijo.joseph@bolt.eu","Dijo Joseph","Uploading an edited med certificate\n\n[^med cert… edited.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T01:40:26.845Z"],["3821828","PFI-835820","PFI","athitiya.daitooktang@bolt-outsource.eu","Athitiya Daitooktang","!image-20260120-015113.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-015246.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T01:52:53.349Z"],["3821833","SCM-1017","SCM","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","!image-20260120-030020.png|width=381,alt=\"image-20260120-030020.png\"!\n\nSample confirmed from my side. And 20pcs samples were sent to  [~accountid:6130627ef0bf520069526076] ","2026-01-20T03:01:03.497Z"],["3821835","EBIKE1-349","EBIKE1","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","!ed8214547614516584d3e2e2b04a500a.mp4|width=448,alt=\"ed8214547614516584d3e2e2b04a500a.mp4\"!\n\nWe checked EB1..2 frame, and found the latest controller bracket get a little conflict with battery, we need to push the battery into hatch.\n\nAs we don’t want to delay the production, we decided to improve it for next batch, and if needed, we can polished it in warehouse.\n\nWe did assembly test for the whole frame, no other issues, sample confirmed.","2026-01-20T03:19:08.059Z"],["3821837","PFI-835826","PFI","isaac.baraka@bolt-outsource.eu","Isaac Baraka","!screenshot (b1f1a2aa-aa51-49a5-900c-5ce0e307052f).png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T03:36:06.480Z"],["3821838","PFI-835826","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T03:36:08.828Z"],["3821839","SCM-1076","SCM","xiangxue.hu@bolt.eu","Xiangxue Hu","[EB1.2 SIP Doc|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1RVN0AMoNzYi6u5T_DpC4X5Xn8_RJCi0r?usp=sharing]\n\nPlastic parts\n\n||*Parts*||*Status*||*Comments*||\n|EB1-1-3-1-A-R02 Battery compartment plastic 电池仓塑料件|Done| |\n|EB1-1-5-A-R01 Cable divider in the down tube 下管分线器|Done| |\n|EB1-3-2-A-R01&EB1-3-3-A-R00 Front mudguard front part&Front mudguard rear part 前土除|Done| |\n|EB1-7-1-A-R03 Basket plastic 车篮|Done| |\n|EB1-11-4-A-R02 Signal switch housing 转向灯开关外壳|Done| |\n|EB1-17-1-A-R00 Chain cover 链罩|Done| |\n|EB1-18-A-R01 Rear mudguard 后土除|Done| |\n|EB1-7-5-A-R00 Head tube cable cover 头管线束盖|Done| |\n|EB1-8-1-A-R01 Dashboard top plastic| | |\n|EB1-8-2-A-R00 Dashboard left-bottom plastic| | |\n|EB1-8-3-A-R00 Dashboard right-bottom plastic| | |\n\nAluminum parts\n\n||*Parts*||*Status*||*Comments*||\n|EB1-1-1-A-R02 Main frame 车架|Draft| |\n|EB1-2-1-A-R00_Hatch welded subassembly电池仓盖板|Done| |\n|EB1-3-1-A-R03 前叉|Done| |\n|EB1-7-2-A-R02 Basket welded tube 车篮方管|Done| |\n|EB1-8-5-A-R00 Handlebar 把横|Done| |\n|EB1-8-6-A-R04 Stem|Done| |\n|EB1-8-7-A-R02 Stem face plate|Done| |\n|EB1-9-1-A-R03 Seatpost with bracket 坐管|Draft|Modification in verification|\n|EB1-9-5-A-R00 Seatpost clamp sub-assembly 坐管管夹|Draft|Modification in verification|\n\nOthers\n\n|| || || ||\n|EB1-3-5-A-R00 Front hublock cable protector - Lower part 前花鼓锁线保护器|Done| |\n|EB1-17-2-A-R00_Chain cover bracket 链罩支架|Done| |\n|EB1-1-2-A-R01 Kickstand 停车架|Hold on|Modification in verification|\n|EB1-3-4-A-R03 Steering angle limiter pin 止转块| | |","2026-01-20T03:41:38.011Z"],["3821840","LSS-61480","LSS","susan.shao@bolt.eu","Cancan Shao","Hi Veera\n\nSorry for the late reply. Beck is on sabbatical leave starting this week\nand will be back after CNY, so only Konstantin and I will be joining the\nmeeting this and next month I think. Because I'm based in China, there will\nbe a time difference. I'll be available on Thursday and Friday 5:00-5:30\npm, which is your 11:00-11:30am I think. But I'm not sure if the time works\nfor you. Or you can just check our calendars to see if the time works.\nBasically our working time here is  from 9:30am to 5:30pm.\n\nFor the questions, please see my responses below:\n\n   1. *Which suppliers are in scope* (e.g. all current suppliers or a\n   defined subset)? Please list if possible.\n   We will add all the current contracts of these suppliers in the share\n   <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/12D4UmbwNLN_MSxW-yob535v8CoeiqLxjnzEgb7jiCi8/edit?gid=0#gid=0>\n   file\n   <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/12D4UmbwNLN_MSxW-yob535v8CoeiqLxjnzEgb7jiCi8/edit?gid=0#gid=0>\n   .\n   2. *Is the annex intended to be standard or customised per supplier*?\n   It will be a standard annex for all suppliers.\n   3. *How are the commercial mechanics expected to work* (e.g. fixed\n   percentage of free spare parts, tiered approach linked to MOQ)?\n   For the free spare parts percentage and MOQ, you can just leave the\n   numbers there for now, because we are in the process of negotiating with\n   all the direct and indirect suppliers for those items, and it may varies\n   for different suppliers.  We can fill the numbers when we ask the suppliers\n   to sign the annex.\n\n   4. *Are there any logistics or operational requirements to be\nreflected* (e.g.\n   delivery timing, bundling with main orders, reporting or tracking\n   requirements)?\n   Logistics will be binding to the main orders.\n   5. *What is the expected timeline* (e.g. target date for finalising\n   negotiations or implementing the annex)?\n   Basically we hope the annex can be finished before our Chinese New Year\n   , so that all the new orders placed after CNY can use the new contract with\n   this annex. Let's say February 6th, then we have one week for review and\n   revision.\n\n\n\n\nThanks\n*Susan Shao*\n*Sr. Procurement Manager | **Bolt China*\n*susan.shao@bolt.eu <susan.shao@bolt.eu>*\n*(+86) 18662160708*\nblog.bolt.eu\n<https://blog.bolt.eu/?utm_source=email_signature&utm_medium=banner&utm_campaign=email_signature_banner>\n\n[image: Bolt Logo]","2026-01-20T03:42:06.798Z"],["3821841","PFI-835828","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n[^M2309128.TXT] _(0.5 kB)_","2026-01-20T04:01:15.662Z"],["3821842","PFI-835830","PFI","elaf.adam@bolt.eu","Elaf Adam","!pay.png|thumbnail!\n\n!pay1.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T04:02:45.410Z"],["3821843","PFI-835831","PFI","elaf.adam@bolt.eu","Elaf Adam","!add.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T04:06:47.883Z"],["3821844","PFI-835206","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hello team, could you reopen the case and assist please.","2026-01-20T04:10:41.847Z"],["3821846","PFI-835246","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Hi Karan. Thank you so much for your assistance. However I couldnt locate the amount of 478.29 THB lin client payment. Could you please reconfirm if both transaction were imported properly so I can confirm with the client. Thanks","2026-01-20T04:30:21.122Z"],["3821848","MM-947","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Emoji Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements provided; insufficient info for development.|\n|Clarity|🟡|Summary is somewhat clear, but lacks context and details.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting sources.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-20T04:36:44.684Z"],["3821850","HS-28983","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nI sent the letter for signing, once I will receive the scanned copy I will forward it to you and we will post the letter to the address marked on your Workday profile as well.\n\nRegards,\nKadri","2026-01-20T04:56:00.282Z"],["3821863","FDBT-4816","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-20T05:09:37.947Z"],["3821864","PFI-833862","PFI","anastasia.janiashvili@bolt.eu","Anastasia Janiashvili","Hii ❤️ \n\nWe have reported this incident twice already, however we continue to receive the same generic response without any indication that the issue has been properly reviewed or addressed, could you please help us? Or let us know where exactly this should be reported, as this category fits the situation most accurately.","2026-01-20T05:10:39.531Z"],["3821865","PFI-833862","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T05:10:44.366Z"],["3821866","PFI-835845","PFI","al-ameen.nima@bolt-outsource.eu","Al-Ameen Nima","!016014085758BOR07394 (737b6caa-b7e7-4656-a9cf-7593ef9e0536).jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Messenger_creation_197AA064-5B24-4498-B446-5CD93838BCF6.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-050923.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T05:10:53.905Z"],["3821868","PFI-835846","PFI","salome.gabidzashvili@bolt.eu","Salome Gabidzashvili","[^GE_ Payouts 2025 - W4.csv]","2026-01-20T05:11:01.246Z"],["3821869","PFI-835847","PFI","al-ameen.nima@bolt-outsource.eu","Al-Ameen Nima","!image-20260120-051342.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-051353.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-051418.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T05:14:38.946Z"],["3821870","PFI-835853","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T05:24:59.100Z"],["3821872","LSS-61820","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^DE20260119-002 Triasa Iberia - Bolt Drive DE.docx.pdf] _(346 kB)_\n\n[^Nota Registro Mercantil Diciembre 2025.pdf] _(98 kB)_\n\n!PHOTO-2026-01-16-11-53-26 2.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T05:29:05.690Z"],["3821879","LSS-60420","LSS","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","Hi Anett,\n\nticket can be closed, thanks a lot for your support","2026-01-20T05:39:20.638Z"],["3821882","PFI-831610","PFI","paweena.songchaijaroen@bolt-outsource.eu","Paweena Songchaijaroen","Kindly follow up.","2026-01-20T05:47:30.990Z"],["3821884","PFI-833862","PFI","anastasia.janiashvili@bolt.eu","Anastasia Janiashvili","Agent please","2026-01-20T05:51:56.900Z"],["3821920","LSS-61821","LSS","mo.salama@bolt.eu","Mo Salama","[^Bolt_x_Tilstra_Service_Agreement_Michel.docx] _(4.31 MB)_","2026-01-20T06:03:21.354Z"],["3821921","LSS-61821","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMo Salama has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-20T06:03:22.409Z"],["3821923","WFM-10048","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Hello [~accountid:712020:fb3cc377-463c-41f0-8730-d66abe2f0af0],\n\nHave the agents completed the safety trainings? \n\nBest regards!","2026-01-20T06:05:18.813Z"],["3821926","LSS-61790","LSS","yuanhsin.lee@bolt.eu","Carolyn Lee","[^[Shared Fleet] Bolt - Fleet Partnership Agreement Taiwan - (CN trans)_FINAL [MPT Exclusive].docx (1).pdf]\n\nWe have made some edits to the contract, please kindly proceed with this version instead, thank you! \n\n","2026-01-20T06:09:15.761Z"],["3821928","DSR-3521","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], I’ve escalated it as I need your assistance to draft an answer regarding the following:\n\n* *Essential information about the processing* (e.g., purposes, recipients, retention period, lawful basis, etc.)\n* Bolt’s refusal to provide such data would require a *clear and explicit legal justification* and reference to the *specific legal provisions* relied upon.\n* *Detailed explanation* of the *calculation method* used to determine the final fare.\n* *Reassessment of the charge*, considering the *non-malicious and incidental nature* of the address change.","2026-01-20T06:11:18.140Z"],["3821929","WFM-10048","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","IDs: 412207, 502788, 502790, 532634, 532792, 562609\n\nCountry request raised here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541785|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541785]","2026-01-20T06:13:23.637Z"],["3821930","DSR-3835","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T06:16:06.342Z"],["3821932","PFI-835858","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-20T06:17:05.249Z"],["3821933","PFI-835858","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:627cf5040d1e73006f7d2aa9] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T06:17:07.277Z"],["3821935","PFI-835210","PFI","arno.booyzen@bolt.eu","Arno Booyzen","Error on request. New request logged for this fleet company.","2026-01-20T06:19:15.447Z"],["3821936","PFI-835210","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T06:19:19.383Z"],["3821937","FDBT-4817","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-20T06:19:22.502Z"],["3821938","PFI-835210","PFI","arno.booyzen@bolt.eu","Arno Booyzen","Hi [~accountid:627cf5040d1e73006f7d2aa9] , I have logged a new ticket for this request:\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-835858|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-835858|smart-link] .\nI have cancelled this one.","2026-01-20T06:19:25.737Z"],["3821948","DSR-3837","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T06:26:06.752Z"],["3821953","DSR-2905","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi team! Just adding the following user messages:\n\n[~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] \n\n*Message received*\n\n[Ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/712473840] related:\nDespite more than 20 days having passed since I submitted my claim for compensation for the wrongful blocking of my account, and despite my repeated contacts, I have not received a substantive response, only information that the “case is being processed.”\nTherefore, I hereby demand payment of 17,000 PLN as compensation for the damages suffered as a result of the many-month wrongful blocking of my account, which prevented me from performing my work and earning income.\nPlease comply with the above demand or provide a clear position within 7 days of receiving this message. Lack of response within the specified time will be treated as a refusal to resolve the matter amicably and as a basis for taking further formal steps.\n----\n[Ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/698291890] related:\nGood morning,\nthank you for your reply.\nMy compensation claim has been under review for a long time, and my account suspension lasted six months and was caused by Bolt, which resulted in real financial losses on my part.\nTherefore, I request:\n* the current status of the case,\n* an indication of a specific deadline for the conclusion of the proceedings,\n* information about which Bolt department is handling my request.\nDue to the long waiting time, I kindly request a substantive and specific answer, not a general statement about further processing of the case.\nSincerely, Katarzyna Szałowicz","2026-01-20T06:32:26.175Z"],["3821958","LSS-60074","LSS","ina.steinborn@bolt.eu","Ina Steinborn","Hi [~accountid:712020:2449585e-020b-4bbc-ac29-8780f94f6823] !\nCould you confirm if there is a panic button or similar functionality via DTI?\nThanks","2026-01-20T06:35:38.839Z"],["3821959","PFI-835865","PFI","nara.aiamlaoo@bolt-outsource.eu","Nara Aiamlaoo","!image-20260120-063702.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-063714.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T06:38:17.563Z"],["3821960","LSS-61822","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^Chamber Of Commerce - Bulsink Auto's B.V..pdf] _(473 kB)_\n\n[^EE20260120-002 Bulsink Auto's - Bolt Drive EE.docx.pdf] _(348 kB)_\n\n[^Paspoort Nathan.pdf] _(90 kB)_\n\n[^Vies on-the-Web - European Commission (1).pdf] _(62 kB)_","2026-01-20T06:38:44.778Z"],["3821962","DRX-27836","DRX","mariia.nazarenko@bolt.eu","Mariia Nazarenko","We should allow CI account access to GN project: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349965?created=true|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/IIS-349965?created=true]","2026-01-20T06:40:40.613Z"],["3821964","DSR-3839","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T06:41:05.963Z"],["3821968","HS-29131","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Related ticket - [+HS-29114+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/HS-29114]","2026-01-20T06:44:49.786Z"],["3821969","PAW-14999","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161193\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-20 06:45:00 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-20T06:45:00.825Z"],["3821970","HS-29103","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","+Related ticket -+ [+HS-29114+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/HS-29114]","2026-01-20T06:45:04.318Z"],["3821974","DSR-3841","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T06:51:06.515Z"],["3821976","C2-461","C2","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] thanks for pushing this.\n\n\nBesides evaluating the compliance to ADR SOP (5.2.1), I think also any breach of [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sktnprEii3Urxl9nNQSNUr_lgUKa2BBqkwgD7_fXF6A/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sktnprEii3Urxl9nNQSNUr_lgUKa2BBqkwgD7_fXF6A/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] should be reported in a similar manner. ","2026-01-20T06:54:56.502Z"],["3821978","DSR-3843","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T06:56:18.680Z"],["3821980","TA-312","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","Default ones have been confirmed, now to just go over the ones that are being used and inform TA managers + TA team and update documentation.","2026-01-20T06:58:31.332Z"],["3821984","PFI-832448","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Cristina Marcova,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.373Z"],["3821985","PFI-832530","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Jasmina Vaclavkova,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.380Z"],["3821986","PFI-827157","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Montini Hebert Figueiredo Costa De Oliveira Filho,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.405Z"],["3821987","PFI-831414","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Ana Pelivanu,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.440Z"],["3821988","PFI-833093","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Ampikar Ouantai,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.479Z"],["3821989","PFI-832850","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Laura Ernestová,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.500Z"],["3821990","PFI-826390","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Tyler Hamilton Ison,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.650Z"],["3821991","PFI-833222","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Lucian Andrei,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.681Z"],["3821992","PFI-792273","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Natalia Frończuk,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.681Z"],["3821993","PFI-813243","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Nadeem Amar,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.809Z"],["3821994","PFI-735118","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Monica Kartsev,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:25.805Z"],["3821995","PFI-831379","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Febin John,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:27.601Z"],["3821996","PFI-826624","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Borys Sypniewski,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:27.725Z"],["3821997","PFI-831405","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Felicia Ștefania Oprea,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:27.855Z"],["3821998","PFI-832835","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Jasmina Vaclavkova,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:27.916Z"],["3821999","PFI-832819","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Tomás Figueira Calado,\n\nWe haven't heard from you in 5 days. If there's no response in the next 24 hours, we'll go ahead and close this ticket.\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T07:00:28.131Z"],["3822001","TA-282","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","[*Update* |https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0A7KB3V0V9/p1767955867478759]*from Sohail on Friday 9th of Jan:*\n\n_”I’ve created this channel to keep_ *_Quality of Hire (QoH)_* _updates visible and in one place going forward._*_A quick recap:_*\n\n* _TA/PLT proposed the QoH metric and calculation. We discussed, and made hypotheses._\n* _PA ran analysis with different scenarios and proposals. We pitched_ [+_here_+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1360jwD-4Y2tITcK_JPk-FOcBTM74dbXMrlu-hV_rJZ0/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.pkb9zqjp03s7]_._\n* _We aligned together (TA, TM, PT) on the final approach before year-end._\n* _The next step is the implementation of the survey in Workday, so we can start collecting data for analysis._\n\n_Please let's have update visibility about survey implementation if any here. We can capture any questions, blockers, or changes in one transparent place - Thank You”_","2026-01-20T07:00:47.544Z"],["3822015","TA-321","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","[~accountid:712020:a7f24c35-13af-47c1-b146-05c4a36324d4] what would be my due date for this? You have an estimate or I should only start with this in Feb?","2026-01-20T07:01:48.660Z"],["3822016","DSR-3577","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","[~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] Please take a look. Is this something you can handle? 🙂","2026-01-20T07:02:11.647Z"],["3822017","LSS-61633","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] - please assist with this, thanks.  client has signed special terms.  ","2026-01-20T07:02:18.103Z"],["3822019","DSR-3721","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","PDE tool fixed, downloading [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/personal-data-export/exports/1267824?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]","2026-01-20T07:02:38.917Z"],["3822020","LSS-61726","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi team, please assist with this, thanks. ","2026-01-20T07:03:13.730Z"],["3822021","SCM-1017","SCM","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","[~accountid:60b9e4f58cf91900699878ec] Today, I might receive them. ","2026-01-20T07:03:39.586Z"],["3822024","DRAG-713","DRAG","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] Can you please take time to look through the SOP? It is quite short & simple. We’d like to release it ASAP to send as many unusable & safe batteries to repair as we can.","2026-01-20T07:06:16.778Z"],["3822025","PFI-835205","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-20T07:07:09.415Z"],["3822026","PFI-835564","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-20T07:07:12.212Z"],["3822027","PFI-835772","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-20T07:07:14.833Z"],["3822028","PFI-835774","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-20T07:07:17.382Z"],["3822029","DSR-3845","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T07:11:57.837Z"],["3822030","CAMLE-9612","CAMLE","sauban.binusman@bolt.eu","Sauban Bin Usman","Replaced by the following ticket:\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MM-943|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MM-943|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T07:12:43.203Z"],["3822032","OKAI-179","OKAI","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","[~accountid:712020:8d272f38-d046-4ad2-a5b3-a47b219e9fa1] [~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] if needed, we can go to Berlin to analyze the scooters also. ","2026-01-20T07:13:20.750Z"],["3822033","PFI-835163","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank due to a UPI-related issue on the beneficiary side, which usually means the UPI ID is incorrect or the linked bank account is inactive/blocked or not accepting UPI credits. Please ask the partner to verify and correct their UPI ID and ensure the linked account can receive UPI transfers; once fixed, the payout will be retried in the next regular cycle (and for Early Cashout, they can try again after updating the details). \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:13:29.672Z"],["3822034","CSDT-971","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","First PR for changing the logic in dim_support_case_tier_history: [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15388|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15388]","2026-01-20T07:13:34.509Z"],["3822035","PFI-835170","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the bank/payment provider, and they did not share a clear reason; please ask the partner to double‑check their beneficiary details (bank account/UPI ID, name match, IFSC, etc.) and correct them if needed. The payout will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try requesting it again. If the partner still faces issues after verifying details, they may also check with their bank for any account restrictions.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:13:46.557Z"],["3822037","PFI-835881","PFI","roman.polinets@bolt-outsource.eu","Roman Polinets","!image-20260120-071221.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T07:13:52.168Z"],["3822038","PFI-835171","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the bank with a generic UPI error, and they did not share an exact reason. Please inform the partner to verify/update their payout details (UPI ID/account number and IFSC), ensure the account is active and able to receive credits, and if this was an Early Cashout they can try submitting it again after correcting the details. Otherwise, the payout will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:14:06.965Z"],["3822039","LSS-56128","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] The business team raised a question: usually in EE there is a need to present the ASiC-E file container, not just the PDF inside the container. Please confirm whether the below signed document in PDF form is sufficient for a legitimate e-signature, or whether the ASiC-E file is also available.","2026-01-20T07:14:25.702Z"],["3822040","PFI-835193","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout is still pending (last update 2026-01-17) and is being processed; it should appear on the courier’s bank account shortly. As it’s very recent, please allow a bit more time; if it remains pending for over 2–3 business days, it may be due to a compliance review or a provider-side delay, which we’re monitoring. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:14:30.032Z"],["3822041","PFI-835214","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout dated 12 Jan is still in pending status (last update on 12 Jan), which is longer than usual and likely due to an ongoing compliance review or a technical delay on the payment provider’s side. Please inform the partner that we are monitoring pending payouts and respond to any provider requests promptly; no action is needed from their side at the moment. The funds will be processed once the provider releases the payment, and the balance will update accordingly.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:14:45.093Z"],["3822042","PFI-835232","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been pending since 12 Jan, which is longer than usual and likely due to an ongoing compliance review or a temporary issue on the payment provider’s side. We are monitoring such cases and responding to any provider requests; no action is needed from the partner, and the payout will be processed and reflected on the bank account once cleared. P.S. Please note the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase—feel free to share any feedback.","2026-01-20T07:15:02.625Z"],["3822043","PFI-835883","PFI","chidiebere.ukaegbu@bolt-outsource.eu","Chidiebere Ukaegbu","!image-20260120-071437.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T07:15:06.242Z"],["3822045","PFI-835233","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is still in pending status; the last update on 12 Jan shows it was accepted for processing by the bank but has not completed yet. Since it has been pending longer than usual, it may be delayed due to a compliance review or technical issues on the provider’s side—our team is actively monitoring and responding to any requests to move it forward. Please inform the partner that no action is required on their side for now; the payout will post once the review completes. If you have any other questions, please feel free to reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:15:19.317Z"],["3822047","PFI-835236","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was successfully processed on 19 Jan 2026. If the partner claims non‑receipt, please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with them so they can follow up with their bank. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:15:40.198Z"],["3822048","DSR-3847","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T07:16:08.969Z"],["3822049","PFI-835238","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the payment provider, and they did not share an exact rejection reason. It will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, the partner can try to request it again. If the partner recently changed their bank details, please ask them to review and correct the beneficiary details before the next attempt to avoid another failure. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:16:12.385Z"],["3822050","LSS-61492","LSS","brenda.selebwa@bolt.eu","Brenda Selebwa","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1], we will share the addendum for the renewal to 2027 as well, so that they are all signed together.","2026-01-20T07:16:24.456Z"],["3822052","PFI-835265","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still don’t see the funds, advise them to contact their bank and use the proof to trace the transfer.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:16:31.273Z"],["3822054","PFI-835273","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed (state: finished). If the partner still hasn’t received the funds, please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with them so they can contact their beneficiary bank for a trace; note that the proof may not always be available. If you need anything else, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:16:43.907Z"],["3822056","PFI-835283","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout has been pending since 12 Jan, which is longer than usual; such delays are typically due to a compliance review or technical checks on the provider’s side. We’re monitoring all pending transfers and will respond to any provider requests immediately—no action needed from your side for now. If the partner still sees no funds after the payout is marked finished, please share the proof of payout (if available) so their bank can trace it. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:17:05.357Z"],["3822057","PFI-835299","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the beneficiary bank; our system notes the recipient details are valid, but the bank declined the transfer. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed automatically in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again. If the partner needs it sooner or wants more context, advise them to contact their bank to check for any incoming transfer blocks or account restrictions. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:17:22.913Z"],["3822058","PFI-835319","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout is still in pending status (last update 2026-01-13), which is longer than usual. The delay is likely due to a compliance review or a technical issue on the payment provider’s side; we are monitoring it and will respond to any checks to move it forward. Please inform the courier that no action is required from their side right now and the payout will be credited once the review completes.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:17:39.000Z"],["3822059","PFI-835336","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected due to a regulatory/compliance check on the banking side, and the bank did not provide more specific details. Please inform the partner that they can contact their beneficiary bank to check for any restrictions on incoming transfers; we will automatically reprocess this payout in the next regular payout cycle (if it was an Early Cashout, they can try to cash out again). If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:18:02.575Z"],["3822060","PFI-835395","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was rejected by the payment provider, and no specific rejection reason was returned in the log. Please inform the partner that it will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to cash out again. As a precaution, ask the partner to double-check that their bank/beneficiary details in the app are correct and active to prevent repeat failures. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:18:20.721Z"],["3822063","PFI-835413","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed with the account statement date 12.01.2026. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still cannot locate the funds, ask them to contact their bank with the document to trace the transfer. If they believe the payout details were wrong, the proof will show the beneficiary details used so they can verify with their bank. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:18:40.772Z"],["3822066","DRX-28288","DRX","kairi.hennoch@bolt.eu","Kairi Hennoch","Misunderstood the reporting requirement, as only limo plates should be allowed, not all valid car plates","2026-01-20T07:19:06.043Z"],["3822067","SUPX-2329","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Hey, qq - any recent changes in web form that can cause [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04JZ6GCH1V/p1768469399608639?thread_ts=1768469358.404529&cid=C04JZ6GCH1V]? Some [graphs|https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/d/db7fa619-ea34-4677-a2dd-5e65fe788ba7/webform?orgId=1&from=now-30d&to=now] looks a bit susp since Jan 16","2026-01-20T07:19:20.128Z"],["3822068","SUPX-2329","SUPX",null,"Slack","[Christian Kalme|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ae966399abb77267ba68b16] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768832961334709?thread_ts=1768832961.334709&cid=C064CEL9FKP|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1768832961334709?thread_ts=1768832961.334709&cid=C064CEL9FKP|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-20T07:19:21.540Z"],["3822069","SUPX-2329","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Hey, seems some layout issue that allows users to overscroll :sad:\n\nI’ll create a task for it.\n\nRegarding graphs - needs a bit more investigation. From what I can see, it’s seems to be driven by 3 cities - Lagos, Cluj-Napoca and Tallinn. If I filter out those 3 cities, seems to be relatively standard.\n\n[@pranav.dineshkumar|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:33002f0b-c802-4f83-911e-b96c405eae99] can you check the linked graph, it also has some concerns on product level that we could discuss and improve\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA41ZF8SV/screen_recording_2026-01-20_at_09.11.40.mov|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA41ZF8SV/screen_recording_2026-01-20_at_09.11.40.mov|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA42JBL7K/screenshot_2026-01-20_at_09.17.10.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AA42JBL7K/screenshot_2026-01-20_at_09.17.10.png|smart-link]","2026-01-20T07:19:21.906Z"],["3822070","DAEN-1346","DAEN","siddhant.saxena@bolt.eu","Siddhant Saxena","[@yuriy.trofymenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:ea34e25e-5aed-4ec5-8c46-0238dbead6e3] [@silja.mardla|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63dd0f6fa5d0c826306adb04] Can you please share an ETA when the marts will be backfilled with the correct numbers?","2026-01-20T07:19:24.349Z"],["3822071","PFI-835417","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The Early Cashout was sent to the payment provider on 14 Jan 2026 and is still being processed (exported). Given the elapsed time, this may be a provider-side delay or compliance review; we are monitoring it—please ask the partner to check with their beneficiary bank for any pending incoming transfer and allow a bit more time (the status will update once processing completes). \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:19:26.411Z"],["3822072","PFI-835421","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout in question was successfully processed with value date 2025-12-29. If the partner claims non-receipt, please download and share the proof of payout (if available) so they can check with their bank. As the issue raised is about an incorrect W52 payout amount, please route this to the Billing team since payout amounts are calculated by them.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-20T07:19:39.010Z"],["3822073","WAVE-236","WAVE","raimond.koitsalu@bolt.eu","Raimond Koitsalu","Quick one-pager here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/E4FfugE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/E4FfugE|smart-link]  ","2026-01-20T07:19:52.922Z"],["3822074","PFI-835451","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout is in finished state (last update 2026-01-19), so it has been successfully processed. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if they still do not see the funds, ask them to check with their bank using the proof. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:19:59.974Z"],["3822076","PFI-835483","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout has been successfully processed on 2026-01-19. Please inform the partner; if they still haven’t received the funds, download the proof of payout (if available) and share it so they can ask their bank to trace the transfer. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; feedback is welcome.","2026-01-20T07:20:24.783Z"],["3822077","FX-3633","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768893613294229]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3633 is already in the state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T07:20:25.807Z"],["3822078","PFI-835484","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout payout was rejected by the payment provider, and they did not share an exact reason. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if they need it sooner, they can submit a new Early Cashout request. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase—thanks for your patience and any feedback.","2026-01-20T07:20:57.952Z"],["3822080","PFI-835611","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been successfully processed on 2026-01-19. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the courier; if they still cannot see the funds, ask them to contact their (beneficiary) bank for a trace. If you need anything else, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-20T07:21:24.333Z"],["3822081","PFI-835623","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The early cashout requested on 14 January is still in progress — the payout has been exported but not yet completed, and it should be reflected on the partner’s bank account once the provider finishes processing. Since it has remained in this state since 14 January, the delay is likely due to a compliance review or a temporary technical issue on the provider’s side; we are monitoring pending payouts and will handle any checks promptly. Please inform the partner that no action is needed on their side for now and the transfer should arrive soon; if it does not arrive after the next business day, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase; feedback is welcome.","2026-01-20T07:21:58.968Z"],["3822086","PFI-835679","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout has been in Pending status since 2026-01-12; since it’s been more than a few business days, the delay is likely due to an ongoing compliance review or a temporary issue on the payment provider’s side. Please inform the partner that it is still being processed; our team monitors pending payouts and responds to any provider checks promptly—no action is needed from their side right now. The status will update automatically once processed, and the funds should reach the bank shortly after. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase—feedback is welcome.","2026-01-20T07:22:35.525Z"],["3822087","LSS-61165","LSS","emilie.marguerite@bolt.eu","Emilie Marguerite","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742], did you have time to look at our message above ? ","2026-01-20T07:22:35.896Z"],["3822089","HS-29123","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Ahmed! Your employment confirmation letter will be forwarded to you via BoxSign to your personal email.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-20T07:23:21.919Z"],["3822090","PFI-835509","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This payout was exported for processing on 2026-01-12 and is still in progress. Given the longer-than-usual timeline, it’s likely delayed due to a compliance review or technical issues on the provider’s side; we are monitoring and will handle any checks to move it forward. Please inform the partner that the funds should post once processing completes, and they may contact their beneficiary bank to verify any incoming transfer (note: Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase).","2026-01-20T07:23:22.923Z"],["3822092","LSS-61080","LSS","mael.heinrich@bolt.eu","Maël Heinrich","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] & [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] ! Could you kindly look into it and advise about how we could handle such case? Rider is complaining about the handling time. Should we contact the driver, asking about his version of events, and about his RC insurance details / consent to share his contact details to the rider? Thanks!","2026-01-20T07:23:26.195Z"],["3822095","PFI-834274","PFI","frederic.ostbye@bolt.eu","Frederic Løvdal Østbye","Hi. \nThis does not solve the issue. This customer wants an explanation for why we have refunded his customer for November and Desember. He wants to see an individual explanation per refund.","2026-01-20T07:25:40.831Z"],["3822097","WD-22615","WD","kairi.martin@bolt.eu","Kairi Martin","!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 09.13.27.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 09.13.38.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 09.23.26.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T07:26:26.498Z"],["3822098","C2-199","C2","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","already solved under another task, closing this one","2026-01-20T07:26:56.567Z"],["3822099","C2-265","C2","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","no longer relevant","2026-01-20T07:27:13.579Z"],["3822100","DRX-27218","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","✅ Tested on DI.127.0 (195305926) iPhone 14 iOS:18.0 - the issue is not reproducible anymore so closing the ticket\n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-20-2026 09-20-24_1.MP4]","2026-01-20T07:27:29.865Z"],["3822104","DRX-27218","DRX","hardi.hansson@bolt.eu","Hardi Hansson","Tested on DI.127.0 (195305926) iPhone 14 iOS:18.0 - the issue is not reproducible anymore so closing the ticket","2026-01-20T07:28:15.111Z"],["3822108","LSS-61747","LSS","alia.aziz@bolt.eu","Alia Aziz","We received another ticket - [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726403443|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726403443] ","2026-01-20T07:29:19.731Z"],["3822109","WD-22427","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:616ff0d5e79ff6006f3423de] !\n\nAd hoc transaction was created on AHBT-EE003-25-997867 on November 3rd 2025. And you updated the rule on November 28th, 2025. Before update the rule did not consider just DR amount, it was applied to both DR and CR. \n\n!image-20260120-072739.png|width=1426,alt=\"image-20260120-072739.png\"!\n\nSame happened for AHBT-EE003-25-465774 (01/12/2025). Transaction was created before you changed the rule (29/12/2025)\n\n!image-20260120-072904.png|width=1411,alt=\"image-20260120-072904.png\"!","2026-01-20T07:29:40.648Z"],["3822110","LSS-29559","LSS","kristiine.murd@bolt.eu","Kristiine Murd","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] \n\nHere are the requested invoices\n\n[^FA_19_03_2022.PDF]\n[^FA_28_02_2022.PDF]\n[^FA_19_04_2022.PDF]\n[^FA_16_06_2022.PDF]\n[^FA_24_03_2022.PDF]\n\n\nBest wishes\nKristiine","2026-01-20T07:30:10.968Z"],["3822111","HS-28770","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-20T07:30:23.231Z"],["3822112","HS-28690","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:5d5149bc92705e0c1c5e519a],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-20T07:30:23.479Z"],["3822113","HS-28697","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi [~accountId:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb],\n\nThere haven't been any updates to the ticket for *10 days*. Please review this ticket and take the necessary action:\n\n*Update*: If the issue is still ongoing, please provide an update on the current status\n\n*Close*: If the issue has been resolved, please close the ticket.\n\n*Cancel*: If the issue is no longer relevant or has been determined not to be actionable, please add a comment and cancel the ticket.","2026-01-20T07:30:25.736Z"],["3822114","PFI-833340","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi team, \n\nThe customer payments team has escalated the case to the payment engineers to understand where the debt is coming from. \nWill let you know once we have any updates. \n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-20T07:30:53.272Z"],["3822115","PFI-835894","PFI","fisola.kaejaiye@bolt-outsource.eu","Fisola Kaejaiye","!Receipt 3.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T07:31:00.353Z"],["3822117","DSR-3849","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T07:31:08.224Z"],["3822120","HS-29130","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Sent for signing.","2026-01-20T07:31:53.613Z"],["3822121","CL-465","CL","konstantin.peshekhonov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Peshekhonov","Alert should be triggered from first failure or only after 1h or something?","2026-01-20T07:32:16.155Z"],["3822124","HS-29119","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Waiting for Weronika to read the Confluence guide I sent to her via Slack as she reached out to me there.","2026-01-20T07:33:20.998Z"],["3822127","EBIKE1-422","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","They closed the hatch on the 1st Ebike and tested - no issue. They deployed it. ","2026-01-20T07:33:31.693Z"],["3822128","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Jan Stoltman [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768894405225569]*{color}:\nOffer logs as they might expire\n\nLinked files:\n* [Offer logs|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0A99PDM3ST/offer_logs]\n{quote}","2026-01-20T07:33:40.943Z"],["3822129","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768894410067419]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@jan.stoltman>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3673] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T07:33:42.913Z"],["3822130","WD-22485","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:637f26822acfad92d7b13ddb] access added to PRD and Sandbox. Please find *Bolt Cancel Expense Reports* integration. I suggest to do test run in SBX before performing actual run.","2026-01-20T07:34:02.039Z"],["3822131","CRC-1689","CRC","kristiina.taube@bolt.eu","Kristiina Taube","[update] Live countries validated: 87% (0% WoW), #46 (0 WoW) of #53 (0 WoW) (results).\nLive/planned WIP: #0 ( 0 WoW).","2026-01-20T07:34:39.317Z"],["3822133","LSS-61534","LSS","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] ! The tool leaves us without a link etc. after completing \n\n","2026-01-20T07:35:24.569Z"],["3822134","LSS-61694","LSS","marcin.klimkiewicz@bolt.eu","Marcin Klimkiewicz","Hi, can we have this signed today? 🙏 \nWe can’t proceed with customs without it & we are collecting demurage fees now.","2026-01-20T07:35:50.579Z"],["3822141","WD-22230","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:60cb48dc758a5d006a07896b] please find initial instruction and complete your steps to create draft so that expense management team can populate expense lines with expense items. [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IFsK8ZD6Ci4cO3_6Q4KxjuKjgb5uGQQ4pLUVQgpsG8M/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IFsK8ZD6Ci4cO3_6Q4KxjuKjgb5uGQQ4pLUVQgpsG8M/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T07:38:54.316Z"],["3822144","HS-29155","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Shared via Box.","2026-01-20T07:39:13.156Z"],["3822148","PFI-832701","PFI","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Hello, thank you for your help. It appears the local agent managed to generate an Invoice for the user. However, the fine still does not seem to be paid.\n\nI believe this ticket can be closed regardless..\n\nThanks!\n\n","2026-01-20T07:40:30.253Z"],["3822149","DBRE-8599","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Master switch is completed at 2026-01-20 09:22 EET","2026-01-20T07:41:08.755Z"],["3822151","PFI-823507","PFI","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Hello! The Campaigns team redirected us back here with the following answer:\n\nFrom the Campaign’s point of view, I see that bonus amount 10502.76 has been successfully sent out to Fleet 95750: [+https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"public_id\"%3A\"957509-SE1125-5502\"}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22public_id%22%3A%22957509-SE1125-5502%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\n[^8d89a9d0-c86a-43d4-bdf1-adb9d723e6e2.pdf]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 15.58.23.png|width=3004,height=274,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 15.58.23.png\"!\n\n \n\ngeneral records - [+https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter=%7B%22timestamp_from%22[…]%3Afalse%7D&page=%7B%22limit%22%3A100%2C%22offset%22%3A0%7D+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter=%7B%22timestamp_from%22%3A1763416800%2C%22timestamp_to%22%3A1764107999%2C%22from_agent_type%22%3A%22driver%22%2C%22from_agent_id%22%3A8133521%2C%22agent_filter_operator%22%3A%22OR%22%2C%22to_agent_type%22%3A%22driver%22%2C%22to_agent_id%22%3A8133521%2C%22type%22%3A%5B%22bonus%22%2C%22compensation%22%2C%22fleet_compensation%22%5D%2C%22use_handling_timestamp%22%3Atrue%2C%22force_use_timestamp%22%3Afalse%7D&page=%7B%22limit%22%3A100%2C%22offset%22%3A0%7D]\nindividual record - [+https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/27568866594+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/27568866594]\n\nOnce campaigns sent information to Billing in regard to earned bonuses, then Campaigns have unfortunately no further information whether the earned amount was dispatched to the balance of receiver and/or received by the other party (we can only see the Invoice attached above in regard to the sent amount).\n\nI will have to forward you to Billing one more time to verify with the team whether the amount has indeed been dispatched from our side.\n\nI’m sorry I don’t have better news today.","2026-01-20T07:41:26.092Z"],["3822156","PFI-835902","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T07:42:54.403Z"],["3822159","DSR-3191","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], \n\n*The user came back with the following answer:*\n\nSubject: Re: GDPR Information - Objection to Account Suspension – Technical Issue and Request for Re-examination\nDear Bolt Data Protection and Security Team,\nThank you for your response dated 16/12/2025.\nI hereby lodge a formal objection to the continued restriction of my account access.\nI want to make clear that at no time did I attempt to circumvent the identity check or violate your security policies. The problem is technical in nature:\nI cannot open my Bolt account on either my iPhone or my Samsung device. The app can be installed, but access and verification fail due to a technical error — not because of my behaviour.\nTherefore I expressly request the following:\n* A re-examination of my account by a human representative (not a purely automated decision).\n* The option of a manual identity verification, for example:\n* via video identification,\n* by submitting my identity documents, or\n* through in-person verification with a Bolt partner in Germany.\n* A clear explanation of the exact technical issue so that I can resolve it.\nI am willing to fully cooperate with you to re-confirm my identity and meet all required security requirements.\nShould access remain suspended without a transparent justification, I reserve the right to exercise my rights under the GDPR and to contact the competent data protection authority.\nI request a prompt response.\nKind regards,\nShaaban\n\nShould we contact the verification team to provide their input about the above? Thanks!","2026-01-20T07:43:47.821Z"],["3822160","FDBT-4796","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics fails on 2026-01-19 05:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task pl_and_ledger_task failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details. This caused all downstream tasks to get skipped.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 288305418207954, 'task_key': 'pl_and_ledger_task'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_metrics/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-19T05%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=bolt_plus_subscription_revenue.bolt_plus_subscription_revenue&base_date=2026-01-19T05%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-20T07:44:00.010Z"],["3822164","HS-27414","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","Benefits forms were sent out also 1st day email. ","2026-01-20T07:44:53.418Z"],["3822168","HS-29114","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Employer’s certificate sent for signing.","2026-01-20T07:45:13.959Z"],["3822172","LSS-61823","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T07:46:06.304Z"],["3822174","EBIKE1-426","EBIKE1","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Malesia assembly factory doesn’t want to do this rework on the rear mudguard.  \n\nMing said they could try. One issue is that the temperature in the factory is cold, and the paint may not stick well and can come off. [~accountid:5eb363355862510b794e3507] will ask Ming to make one sample and check the result. ","2026-01-20T07:46:23.128Z"],["3822175","HS-26916","HS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","Hi Hélène, have you made any progress?","2026-01-20T07:46:42.044Z"],["3822178","DAEN-1346","DAEN","jens.dobrindt@bolt.eu","Jens Dobrindt","Yes please! I just checked and they have not backfilled yet","2026-01-20T07:47:04.233Z"],["3822179","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","we would be addressing this today :slightly_smiling_face:","2026-01-20T07:47:43.876Z"],["3822181","CL-465","CL","aliaksei.bulhak@bolt.eu","Aliaksei Bulhak","[~accountid:63a2bfff48b367d78a14db98] as initial phase we will trigger alert from first failure to check how often we have cases when not all rates returned by intraday api","2026-01-20T07:48:39.018Z"],["3822182","PFI-835910","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T07:48:58.370Z"],["3822183","BR-4006","BR","arsen.ali@bolt.eu","Arsen Ali","After backfill, notify in [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01A7SKE5C1/p1768894433087519|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01A7SKE5C1/p1768894433087519|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T07:49:19.246Z"],["3822184","PFI-806899","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, no it's not possible. Invoices are issued for the services provided. Issuing a new invoice would only increase the debt of the company. Please, provide company with issued invoices.","2026-01-20T07:49:19.783Z"],["3822185","FX-3611","FX","pavel.grigorev@bolt.eu","Pavel Grigorev","Discussed with [~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] , agreed to move from Epic Duty to Fleet Portal improvements.","2026-01-20T07:49:22.328Z"],["3822186","TAXP-794","TAXP","tyler.ison@bolt.eu","Tyler Hamilton Ison","Lodgment channel: MNE groups lodging via *ATO Online* services for business or Online services for agents should note the 20-entity limit.\n\n[https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/international-tax-for-business/in-detail/multinationals/global-and-domestic-minimum-tax/lodging-paying-and-other-obligations-for-pillar-two|https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/international-tax-for-business/in-detail/multinationals/global-and-domestic-minimum-tax/lodging-paying-and-other-obligations-for-pillar-two|smart-link] \n\n[https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/international-tax-for-business/in-detail/multinationals/global-and-domestic-minimum-tax/transitional-cbc-reporting-safe-harbour|https://www.ato.gov.au/businesses-and-organisations/international-tax-for-business/in-detail/multinationals/global-and-domestic-minimum-tax/transitional-cbc-reporting-safe-harbour|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T07:49:27.712Z"],["3822187","FRAUD-5596","FRAUD","jaroslav.judin@bolt.eu","Jaroslav Judin","Hi,\n\nas I understand this ticket is still viable but some requirements have been changed. \nSuch as: \n\n* store the event from salv on bolt side\n* display it in AuditLog view of admin-panel\n* send alerts to slack\n* can be resolved on Bolt side and the corresponding event is sent back to Salv about the resolution.\n\nis it correct?","2026-01-20T07:49:39.051Z"],["3822190","PFI-833621","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","Hello team,\n\nAny update on this?","2026-01-20T07:50:35.212Z"],["3822191","RDS-951","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] , can you share your perspective here? Are there any plans for the photo feature?","2026-01-20T07:51:05.831Z"],["3822192","DSR-3851","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T07:51:06.898Z"],["3822194","HS-28363","HS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","Hi, please share approved offer letter that has been sent out to the employee.","2026-01-20T07:51:22.719Z"],["3822197","PFI-835913","PFI","martyna.vieraityte@bolt-outsource.eu","Martyna Vieraitytė","!IMG_1279.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T07:51:36.770Z"],["3822204","FX-3612","FX","pavel.grigorev@bolt.eu","Pavel Grigorev","Discussed with [~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] , agreed to move from Epic Duty to Fleet Portal improvements and FX Ready sprint.","2026-01-20T07:53:45.123Z"],["3822207","HS-29040","HS","lauri@bolt.eu","Lauri Lutter","Let’s please regrant him 192 units that start vesting from 01.01.2026. Thank you! ","2026-01-20T07:54:06.593Z"],["3822210","FX-3613","FX","pavel.grigorev@bolt.eu","Pavel Grigorev","Discussed with [~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] , agreed to move from Epic Duty to Fleet Portal improvements and FX Ready sprint.","2026-01-20T07:54:32.215Z"],["3822216","FX-3638","FX","pavel.grigorev@bolt.eu","Pavel Grigorev","Discussed with [~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] , agreed to move from Epic Duty to Fleet Portal improvements and FX Ready sprint.","2026-01-20T07:57:09.379Z"],["3822219","FX-3637","FX","pavel.grigorev@bolt.eu","Pavel Grigorev","Discussed with [~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] , agreed to move from Epic Duty to Fleet Portal improvements and FX Ready sprint.","2026-01-20T07:57:35.794Z"],["3822221","LSS-61488","LSS","emilie.chesse@bolt.eu","Emilie Chesse","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac]  - Worth asking Lisette if this exists elsewhere? I guess the good thing about PT is that we haven’t adopted yet the new Rides T&Cs, which capture Bolt Send - but then if Ops is now considering offering Bolt Send via Couriers, perhaps this wasn’t such a good idea to move away from standalone T&Cs for Bolt Send. Hence why it’s worth getting Lisette’s views, and try to align centrally in case this is being envisaged elsewhere? Thanks!","2026-01-20T07:58:28.281Z"],["3822225","PFI-833625","PFI","sabina.onomiruren@bolt-outsource.eu","Sabina Onomiruren","Hello team,\n\nAny update on this?","2026-01-20T07:58:52.368Z"],["3822227","PFI-835915","PFI","anuoluwapo.oyerinde@bolt-outsource.eu","Anuoluwapo Oyerinde","!image-20260120-073221.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T08:00:04.783Z"],["3822229","RDXENG-4367","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:625fb496efc8a5006a5557e5] In iOS device Safari browser user is able to zoom in the page in general and it appears that pin icons + car icon is rather pixelated. Is there an option to improve this?\n\n!IMG_1803-20260120-074546.PNG|width=273,alt=\"IMG_1803-20260120-074546.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_1804-20260120-075814.PNG|width=276,alt=\"IMG_1804-20260120-075814.PNG\"!","2026-01-20T08:00:07.564Z"],["3822230","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768895995730129]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@divyansh.kumar>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-367] `Check nif reporting issues for fomento spain` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:00:08.450Z"],["3822232","HS-28363","HS","maria-denisa.laslau@bolt.eu","Denisa Laslău","Hello!\nPlease find it attached. Let me know if you need anything else.\n\nDenisa\n\n[^Bolt Mail - Kaur, your offer at Bolt, congrats! (internal offer).pdf] _(157 kB)_","2026-01-20T08:00:12.856Z"],["3822233","PFI-835916","PFI","chaninat.wongrod@bolt-outsource.eu","Chaninat Wongrod","!Messenger_creation_7F0AA84A-F167-4197-8261-45042B0945E6.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!Messenger_creation_88C37C3B-438E-437D-90B3-93A3CE6AD3F5.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T08:00:19.886Z"],["3822234","LSS-56592","LSS","paula.brege@bolt.eu","Paula Breģe","Hi [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] , I noticed that the last document has an error with the signatures. Should we re-sign it? Attaching a screenshot from e-paraksts.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.00.10.png|width=344,height=382,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.00.10.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-20T08:00:32.894Z"],["3822243","XP-3060","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","*Results Update*\n\nAll issues now appear to be resolved - sums match over all {{user/food}} CUPED metrics. Re-running for other dashboards.","2026-01-20T08:02:18.335Z"],["3822248","DSR-3853","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T08:02:40.310Z"],["3822250","DRX-28291","DRX","dmitry.lazarev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Lazarev","Duplicates [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-26555|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-26555|smart-link].","2026-01-20T08:03:00.183Z"],["3822251","WEB-9923","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] \n\n[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] has updated the SEO guideline, and the driver page is good to move to design. \n\nLet me know if you have any questions 🙂 ","2026-01-20T08:03:04.431Z"],["3822256","LSS-56592","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Please assist with re-signing the document. ","2026-01-20T08:03:43.174Z"],["3822258","RDS-1351","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:73f630c1-899f-4b5d-ac71-8a7e5c89eb30] FYI: added prio, feel free to adjust.","2026-01-20T08:03:55.125Z"],["3822260","DRX-26813","DRX","dmitry.lazarev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Lazarev","[~accountid:604aad6403ceda0069bec100] This duplicates an older ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-26556|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-26556|smart-link]; I’ll let you decide which one to keep and which one to close. ","2026-01-20T08:04:04.846Z"],["3822261","WD-22612","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Hi Ewa, please can you provide employee numbers.","2026-01-20T08:04:14.864Z"],["3822263","BDB-1526","BDB","mario.kartezi@bolt.eu","Mario Kartezi","[~accountid:5d289a7c3e09b40c262cfaa9] [Here’s the template|https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1AYlGnybCp93uLRRjVxTextP0V6uRS_rCJOmxtqrRlwE/edit?usp=sharing] with Bolt for Business logos and colours - to use, they can copy/duplicate the deck.","2026-01-20T08:04:30.478Z"],["3822265","RDS-1066","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:73f630c1-899f-4b5d-ac71-8a7e5c89eb30] FYI: added prio, feel free to adjust.","2026-01-20T08:04:43.025Z"],["3822267","FDBT-4819","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-20T08:05:01.942Z"],["3822270","LSS-58345","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","Hi [~accountid:712020:9bc1ca8e-c2f1-41a2-9476-90ce966c2205] , in view of the most recent discussions had on FATII partnership, namely that the operational structure was changed, I have implemented in the [partnership agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14d5_ZNXhgh7EbRoSROdvC1Ot_EjZsOMLLNwrgmrj9ts/edit?tab=t.0] all changes on which we have agreed. Your confirmation is needed!\nHi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] , there is a minor comment inserted by me in our attention at clause 12.2.2, please check it out whenever you have some spare time.\n\nThanks all,\n\nAlex","2026-01-20T08:05:55.094Z"],["3822272","DSR-3801","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Incorrect escalation. Please handle the request based on the [+_KB_+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/56497?country=global&language=en]:\n\n* _If there is rider pushback, please refer them to clause 2.3 in the_ [_Bolt Terms and Conditions_|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/terms-for-riders/]_._\n\nIf the user makes an actual GDPR request, escalate the case to CS Privacy Compliance Tier in Beehive.\n\nThank you ☃️","2026-01-20T08:05:59.538Z"],["3822278","RDS-612","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] thx, I am changing the status to “Development” then. Can I ask you to keep an eye on the progress here? ","2026-01-20T08:07:03.169Z"],["3822282","RDS-849","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] [~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] FYI: added prio, feel free to adjust.","2026-01-20T08:08:02.294Z"],["3822283","MKP-9665","MKP","buin.dylgyrzhapov@bolt.eu","Buin-Dylgyrzhap Dylgyrzhapov","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7404421529/Multi+stop+pricing+v2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7404421529/Multi+stop+pricing+v2|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:08:03.028Z"],["3822287","LSS-59767","LSS","oluwatosin.ogunsanwo@bolt.eu","Oluwatosin Ogunsanwo","Hello [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] \nThey’ve made the change to Section 18 and shared it for signing [here|https://ironcladapp.com/signature?r=f857b6b4-22b3-4a2f-85b2-19740175a9a9&s=fcbd055f-a6ec-41cb-b1aa-f7c32baefda5&utm_source=email&t=IKPdqvqFGiMdCi6ypm6bx&expires=1771427910555&signature=TK4Rj0Y5Dz0OMfNhzNoMjBcD87zVAZIxHV1uoNAyGI0]. Please take a look and let me know if its good to go for signing. Thanks!","2026-01-20T08:08:28.563Z"],["3822292","DSR-2905","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - I have been informed that Local Ops plans on calling the Driver today. I am awaiting an update.","2026-01-20T08:08:42.594Z"],["3822295","SREDESK-7418","SREDESK","daniel.berbece@bolt.eu","Daniel Berbece","I tried also via AA, but got {{throttled_due_monitor}} log\nI see in the pipeline you linked the same happened","2026-01-20T08:09:15.554Z"],["3822296","RDS-612","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] yep, posted again over the weekend, still no reply…\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07GNGJ9V5L/p1768758933589449|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07GNGJ9V5L/p1768758933589449|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:09:29.383Z"],["3822299","PFI-835564","PFI","sylwia.siwek@bolt-outsource.eu","Sylwia Siwek","hi, please help","2026-01-20T08:10:01.270Z"],["3822300","HS-28363","HS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","Thank you, added to WD","2026-01-20T08:10:05.911Z"],["3822301","WEBSD-1489","WEBSD","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] \n\nThanks for the info! \n\nFor the partner logos, you can just send an SVG or high res PNG of the lockup and we'll manage the rest. \n\nAs a heads up, the team aims to support all requests and reviews them based on our current roadmap, capacity, and priorities, which will define the timeline for implementation.","2026-01-20T08:10:08.828Z"],["3822302","RDS-1241","RDS","joel.palgi@bolt.eu","Joel Palgi","{quote}can you validate for me that this is all possible from a back end perspective, the data model supports it?{quote}\n\nSeems possible from simple document data point of view","2026-01-20T08:10:14.796Z"],["3822303","MARTECH3-1437","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","20.01.2026\nFirst version in form of message to users was created, however we are working with Prakhar on Looker dashboard which can lead to change in a way data is exposed, so I’m treating this task as done, while Fina version of documentation is separate task created under: \n\nBelow I’m pasting explanation how explores was exposed initially by me:\n\nI’ve delivered multiple explores that read only pre-calculated data and do not perform any calculations. Because of this, we have a limited number of filter combinations available, but in return we get a single source of truth and avoid heavy computation every time Looker is opened.\nPlease note that this is still in the development/testing phase, so the data is not yet fully complete (I’ll describe what’s currently available below).\nI’d appreciate it if you could spend some time exploring these (not today, of course, but over the next few days when you work) and raise any concerns or feedback you may have. Eventually, we’ll build a dedicated dashboard on top of these explores to make them easier to use.Every explore serves data for a single level of data.\nEvery explore can be filtered by dates. there are daily, weekly, monthly and quaterly timeframes. Please note, that this is not possible to SUM and provide other timeframes. If you pick day, you will get all days data separately for the date range.For instance:\nGlobal level means you can pick only timeframe and timeframe_start_date, and numbers are calculated for the whole company, all countries, all messages etc.Country level means breakdown to countries (and timeframes)\nCountry x message lifecycle stage means breakdown for countries and message lifecycle stages which exist for that country (and timeframes). etc etc.Available explores :\n\n* [+Global+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_global]\n* [+Country+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_country]\n* [+Comm type+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_comm_type]\n* [+Conversion event+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_conversion_event]\n* [+Lifecycle stage+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_lifecycle_stage]\n* [+Country x comm type+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_country_comm_type]\n* [+Country x conversion event+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_country_conversion_event]\n* [+Country x lifecycle stage+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_country_lifecycle_stage]\n* [+Country x lifecycle stage x comm type+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_country_lifecycle_stage_comm_type]\n* [+Journey x channel name+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_journey_channel]\n* [+Message+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_message]\n* [+Message x device (os)+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/marketing_curated/mart_rider_lifecycle_message_performance_message_device]\n\nIn every explore, on the left-hand side, you can pick only dimensions, which are meaningful for that level of data. Also, to avoid seeing duplicates, please always display all dimensions for that level (example -> for country x lifecycle stage level -> always pick timeframe_start_date and country and lifecycle stage as columns + needed metrics).Metrics: there are 3 groups:\nRegular metrics\nUnique user metrics\nTotal metricsRegular metrics are calculated using the formula of DISTINCT event_date, message_id, user_id as described [+here+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7025524983/Lifecycle+mart+models+-+design#Additive].\nUnique users is based on \"old\" formula when we calculate unique users in that window\nTotal is just the count of everything, without any logic for deduplication.How to use timeframe and timeframe_start_date:\nThere are 4 timeframes available: day, week, month and quarter\ntimeframe start date is the first day in that timeframe. If you want to pick October 2025, please use 2025-10-01 as timeframe_start_date.As this is still testing and before final deployment, there is only limited data available. I'm attaching list with available timeframes and timeframe_start_dates which you can pick and cross-validate numbers.\nFor monthly and quarterly data -> this is only for Poland and Estonia (so if you pick global monthly data, it will show numbers only for that two countries). For weeks and days it has all.\n\nweek\t2025-10-27\nweek\t2025-10-20\nweek\t2025-10-13\nweek\t2025-10-06\nweek\t2025-09-29\nweek\t2025-09-22\nweek\t2025-09-15\nquarter\t2025-07-01\nmonth\t2025-10-01\nday\t2025-10-31\nday\t2025-10-30\nday\t2025-10-29\nday\t2025-10-28\nday\t2025-10-27\nday\t2025-10-26\nday\t2025-10-25\nday\t2025-10-24\nday\t2025-10-23\nday\t2025-10-22\nday\t2025-10-21","2026-01-20T08:10:46.287Z"],["3822307","PFI-833616","PFI","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Thank you Kerli,\n\nHere are the adjustment subtype we have created with the not netted manual adjustments types:\n\n1. \n\n|compensation|balance_transfer_compensation|\n\n|fee|balance_transfer_deduction|\n\n\n2. \n\n|compensation|equipment_deposit_compensation|\n\n|fee|equipment_deposit_deduction|\n\n\nWill you assist creating the new subtypes here [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574] ? \n","2026-01-20T08:11:31.593Z"],["3822310","DSR-3585","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey CSPC! \n\nCan you please share the following response with the User?\n\n\n\n{quote}Dear *Ulrik*,\n\n\n\nThank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *8 January 2026*.\n\n\n\nIn your request you asked us the following:\n\n\n\n# Which specific personal data of yours were transmitted to Allianz Versicherung, at what time, for what purpose, on what legal basis, and in what form and content you were presented to Allianz.\n# Whether and on what basis we considered you relevant in relation to the reported incident despite the information you had previously provided.\n# That we cease any further processing and disclosure of your personal data in connection with this incident and correct any incorrect representations made to third parties.\n\n\n\nWe address your questions below.\n\n\n\n*Personal data shared with Allianz Versicherung*\n\n\n\nIn connection with the incident reported on 9 December 2025, we shared the following categories of your personal data with Allianz Versicherung, acting as the motor liability insurer of Bolt Services DE GmbH:\n\n\n\n* Order start date and time;\n* Order end date and time;\n* Your full name;\n* Your date of birth;\n* Your contact details;\n* Your language preferences.\n\n\n\nThe data were transmitted electronically after the incident was reported on 10 December 2025 at 19:30, for the purpose of handling a potential liability claim related to the use of a Bolt e-scooter.\n\n\n\n*Purpose and legal basis of the data sharing*\n\n\n\nThe purpose of the disclosure was to enable the insurer to assess the reported incident and determine whether insurance coverage and further investigation were required.\n\n\n\nThe legal basis for this processing and disclosure is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Bolt has a legitimate interest in investigating reported incidents involving its vehicles and in cooperating with its insurer to manage potential claims and legal obligations. This includes situations where an incident is reported by a third party and requires assessment, even if the case is later closed in the app environment.\n\n\n\n*Presentation of your data and relevance assessment*\n\n\n\nThe personal data were shared in the context of a reported incident involving a Bolt vehicle after your order, to allow the insurer to assess the circumstances and determine next steps under the insurance policy. The transmission of limited identifying and ride related data does not constitute a conclusion of fault or liability.\n\n\n\n*Cessation of processing and correction*\n\n\n\nAt this time, we do not carry out any ongoing processing or further disclosure of your personal data in connection with this incident beyond what is necessary to comply with legal, insurance, or regulatory obligations.\n\n\n\nWe have no indication that incorrect or misleading information about you was provided to Allianz. If any factual inaccuracies are identified, we will take appropriate steps to correct them.\n\n\n\nFor information on how we process personal data more generally, we refer you to our Privacy Notice at [https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders-micromobility/?category=micromobility|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders-micromobility/?category=micromobility|smart-link] , which includes further information about the categories of personal data we process, purposes, recipients, retention criteria, international transfers, and your rights.\n\n\n\n*Your rights*\n\n\n\nIn addition to your right of access, you have the right to request rectification or erasure of your personal data, restriction of processing, or to object to processing, subject to applicable legal requirements. Any such request will be assessed in line with data protection law.\n\n\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response, you have the right to lodge a complaint with your competent data protection supervisory authority and to seek a judicial remedy.\n\n\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-20T08:12:09.455Z"],["3822312","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768896811454839]*{color}:\nHi Kerli,\n\nThanks for approving the ticket, I added the requirements in regards to subtypes naming, will you take it from here <@U03P58BK5FY>?\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:13:44.831Z"],["3822314","HS-26891","HS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","added to WD","2026-01-20T08:14:13.429Z"],["3822315","LSS-61679","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344482|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344482|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:14:26.034Z"],["3822317","RDXENG-4374","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested and OK.* \n\nCar color is sent in {{routeSharing/getOrder}}, displayed and updated when new driver is matched with new car color.\n\n!image-20260120-081425.png|width=316,alt=\"image-20260120-081425.png\"!","2026-01-20T08:14:48.712Z"],["3822318","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Last night was hell :sad_dog:\n\nAlmost all Tikvs were restarted. Received thousands of pagers.\nI didn't find anything like oom or something in the logs, but I found something fatal in all Kvs which were restarted. Immediately after this Fatal message, they were restarted.\nSeems to be a bug to me for the CDC assertion .\n\n{noformat}{\"level\":\"FATAL\",\"message\":\"assertion `left == right` failed\",\n \"location\":\"components/cdc/src/delegate.rs:374\",\n \"thread_name\":\"cdc-0\"}{noformat}\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9RCNJ63C/screenshot_2026-01-20_at_13.39.49.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9RCNJ63C/screenshot_2026-01-20_at_13.39.49.png|smart-link]\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9PC85CMU/tikv-2026-01-20t00-10-10.985.log|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0A9PC85CMU/tikv-2026-01-20t00-10-10.985.log|smart-link]","2026-01-20T08:14:54.226Z"],["3822320","MARTECH3-1440","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","{{2026-01-20}}\n\n[~accountid:712020:5d3eb1bb-0d0e-487e-8912-069bb3f5f2b0]  is helping with finding a good way to expose preaggregated data into dashboard. Next workshop planned: 20/01","2026-01-20T08:15:21.997Z"],["3822321","LSS-61785","LSS","natalia.fronczuk@bolt.eu","Natalia Frończuk","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], thank you, sent it to the Fleet Owner! Will let you know if they come back","2026-01-20T08:15:25.869Z"],["3822322","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Anyone seen that before ?","2026-01-20T08:15:32.446Z"],["3822323","RS-1959","RS","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","[^Document_260120_104212.pdf (2).pdf] _(114 kB)_","2026-01-20T08:16:07.556Z"],["3822324","PFI-835924","PFI","precious.bakare@bolt-outsource.eu","Precious Bakare","!Driver Receipt.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T08:16:07.632Z"],["3822325","LSS-61197","LSS","natalia.fronczuk@bolt.eu","Natalia Frończuk","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac], they haven’t gotten back to us. I think you can close the ticket and if need be I’ll reach out to you again","2026-01-20T08:16:18.125Z"],["3822326","PFI-833211","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, done. Will go live on 01.02","2026-01-20T08:16:57.279Z"],["3822328","DRX-28291","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich"," [~accountid:712020:eb64fa24-b70d-49d6-b62c-e4560e7e1457] [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-28291#:~:text=Preview,.|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-28291#:~:text=Preview,.|smart-link] serves only for safety features [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-26555?focusedCommentId=3592973|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-26555?focusedCommentId=3592973|smart-link] , but we might need to updates other features as well","2026-01-20T08:17:13.659Z"],["3822329","WD-22605","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:620b9b75878c2f00729892b6], we have sent expense report back to user to fill these fields. Then the information will become visible and expense report will go to correct approval flow","2026-01-20T08:17:20.856Z"],["3822332","MARTECH3-891","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","{{2026-01-20}}\n\nI helped last week with fix and adjustements with ingestion of data to Databricks.\n\nWe agreed, that first phase of data availability will be adhoc queries. \n\nAfter adhoc queries show us needs, we will build proper ETL for reporting. \nI’m waiting for requirements to be defined. ","2026-01-20T08:18:22.686Z"],["3822333","CCM-22291","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey [~accountid:634d23c2548f1fe6f0c36d5a]  👋 \n\nThey have been enrolled to the training. ☀️ \n\nWishing you a lovely day!\n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-20T08:18:29.617Z"],["3822335","RISK2-659","RISK2","liisa.aavik@bolt.eu","Liisa Aavik","This project is blocked.","2026-01-20T08:18:31.538Z"],["3822337","LSS-59711","LSS","mirjam.kaasikaaslav@bolt.eu","Mirjam Kaasik-Aaslav","Hey [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] and [~accountid:712020:6ea61242-681c-4fee-9add-2547487ff931] \n\nJust to clarify a bit on the topic on CCTV policy since it seems we got a bit misaligned. This is currently called a “policy” and owned by Privacy but given the subject matter of it and Privacy team being a bit far from the implementation process, we had discussed that it would do better living in an existing Policy (maybe the Access Control Policy for InfoSec ) and/or be condensed down to a procedure.\n\nFrom Physical Security Team, we’d just need input and advice on the existing policy: \n\n* did you [~accountid:712020:6ea61242-681c-4fee-9add-2547487ff931] knew that this policy exists? \n* if you have any oversight over the CCTVs across locations? \n** And if you do, would you need to add anything to the current process?\n\nNow it’s clear that verticals own the CCTV footage and the management of it (that should be captured in the documentation as well [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048]), then I think the existing process can be updated based on vertical needs. [~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] are you responsible from Rentals team for managing and overseeing all location CCTVs?\n\nHope this clarified everything a bit\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:50057dc7-d3c1-4f13-9a33-a34da3415c60] ","2026-01-20T08:18:34.534Z"],["3822340","RISK2-3258","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*19.01. Functionality changed - Accountable Manager can immediately do the assessment now, and if needed, assign the assessment to another user at the top of the page.*","2026-01-20T08:18:52.440Z"],["3822341","RISK2-660","RISK2","liisa.aavik@bolt.eu","Liisa Aavik","Project blocked, deadline deleted.","2026-01-20T08:19:02.481Z"],["3822342","PFI-835930","PFI","oluwatosin.akinbolasere@bolt-outsource.eu","Oluwatosin Akinbolasere","!image-20260120-081632.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260120-081844.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T08:19:39.252Z"],["3822347","LSS-60753","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - yes, it would be a great exercise for you to go through - you don’t need to prioritise over the DSA-work but get it going and we can discuss it together towards the end of next week.","2026-01-20T08:20:15.945Z"],["3822350","PFI-835931","PFI","mercynorah.nyiti@bolt.eu","Mercynorah Nyiti","[^receipt - 2026-01-03T103626.640 (1) (1).pdf]","2026-01-20T08:20:20.965Z"],["3822351","MARTECH3-1424","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","{{2026-01-20}}\nI started development (moving queries to DBT), however Linkedin was defined in the meantime by [~accountid:712020:2c6288c9-f28e-4d20-b26c-875c7bd62e08] so I think I will switch to Linkedin which has higer priority","2026-01-20T08:20:23.874Z"],["3822352","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* cs-d3 downscale: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15462|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15462|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:20:28.105Z"],["3822354","RCE-368","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768897232920489]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@maksim.shashkov>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-368] `Update string context and screenshots in Crowdin` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:20:46.107Z"],["3822356","PFI-835932","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T08:21:17.803Z"],["3822364","CSDA-304","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Hello [~accountid:61f7bc87aab3620070f324ce] !\n\nPlease find December 2025 data attached.\n\nAs we’ve discussed in Slack [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CFN1NTKB5/p1768570515372939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CFN1NTKB5/p1768570515372939|smart-link]  dashboards data for Skip Rate is currently under development.\n\n[^December 2025 Azerbaijan Business Queue Skip Rate.xlsx] ","2026-01-20T08:22:21.543Z"],["3822365","PFI-833717","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T08:22:47.108Z"],["3822366","HS-29138","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi Valentin! \n\nThank You for reaching out. Unfortunately People Operations do not handle leave in France, so unfortunately I can not confirm Your raised topic. \n[~accountid:712020:ad0f28bc-2e04-43b5-8352-a3a48fd3f720] kindly please assist Valentin on this matter. \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-20T08:22:48.007Z"],["3822369","LSS-61533","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] - we don’t currently have any specific documented retention periods for employee records — focus is on User data first this year.\n\nAs for consents, we usually create these on an ad-hoc basis depending on what is required but for repetitive situations, we can definitely work on creating standardised templates this year, think that is a great idea. \n\nCan you add the topic to the Privacy Programme Board as a deprioritised item and we can look at it perhaps in Q2?","2026-01-20T08:23:08.721Z"],["3822375","CNT-341","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","Just an update: the blog has been reviewed and is ready to be published (available as a draft on Strapi), just waiting on the photoshoot. 🙂 ","2026-01-20T08:23:49.682Z"],["3822376","LSS-61827","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","[^Supplier Agreement_Bolt Technology OÜ_OpenAI_16.08.2023 (1).pdf]\n[^Data Processing Agreement_Bolt Technology OÜ_OpenAI_16.08.2023.pdf]\n[^Amendment to the Enterprise Agreement_Bolt Operations OÜ_OpenAI LLC_11.04.2024.pdf]\n\nPlease see current agreement attached.","2026-01-20T08:23:58.033Z"],["3822379","PFI-828440","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\n\n\nAlso checking the customer’s account balance attached, there was no debit in the amount of 980 UAH for the preauthorisation amount, which means that the preauthorisation was never actually made into a real charge and is already reversed.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T08:24:25.843Z"],["3822381","PFI-805526","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Hello \n\n  \n\nSending chargeback report \n\n  \n\nSincerely \n\n *{color:#767171} {color}* \n\n *{color:#767171} *Nino Kabulashvili*{color}*\n{color:#767171} E-Commerce Partners Relationship Senior Manager{color} {color:#767171}| Payments Business |{color}{color:#767171}{color} {color:#767171}Bank of Georgia\n Bank of Georgia: Tbilisi, 29A Gagarini Str., 0160 | E-mail:{color} [{color:#767171} {color}{color:#767171}NKabulashvili@bog.ge{color}{color:#767171}{color}|mailto:NKabulashvili@bog.ge]{color:#767171}\n Phone: (+995 32) 2444 444 (ext. 7492) | Mobile: (+995 555) 444405{color}{color:#767171}{color}{color:#767171}{color}{color:#1F497D}{color}{color:blue}{color}  \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://bankofgeorgia.ge/retail]>{color:blue}{color}!image002.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[https://www.facebook.com/119630781428450]>{color:blue}{color}!image003.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://instagram.com/bankofgeorgia]>{color:blue}{color}!image004.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://www.youtube.com/bankofgeorgiatv]>{color:blue}{color}!image005.png|thumbnail!{color:blue}{color} <[http://www.linkedin.com/company/bank-of-georgia]>{color:#1F497D}{color}\n\n[^Bolt 12-18 January.xlsx] _(11 kB)_","2026-01-20T08:24:41.587Z"],["3822383","RS-1947","RS","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Hello! Just checking if there is any update here, the police agent is quite insistent. \n\n","2026-01-20T08:25:06.241Z"],["3822384","PFI-828454","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T08:25:10.732Z"],["3822385","FDBT-4821","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-20T08:25:17.494Z"],["3822386","CRC-2319","CRC","kenechukwu.nwankwo@bolt.eu","Kenechukwu Nwankwo","[update] Kickstarting this again as launched projects seems to be more stable \n\n* *Fiscal Devices/ Cash Register* — Migrating fleets to new vendor app to kickoff in Q1. We can only switch to the new vendor API when fleet migration is done.\n* *E-invoicing (KSEF)* — We’ll be changing vendors to Fonoa  since Sovos doesn’t seem to be responsive. Initial technical review done and missing some unhappy paths. We’ll check in Jan for updates on these.","2026-01-20T08:25:18.638Z"],["3822387","PFI-835937","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T08:25:20.124Z"],["3822390","RIDE-688","RIDE","fatmakhanim.mammadova@bolt.eu","Fatya Mammadova","[~accountid:712020:6adb952a-b92a-4d70-ad5d-a835963ab6ef] [~accountid:5f1a9692b385da00156b98be]  Could you please add Confluence links that are useful from partners to the document?","2026-01-20T08:25:30.882Z"],["3822392","WEB-8885","WEB","elina.heno@bolt.eu","Elina Liina Heno","Hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \n\n[Here|https://www.figma.com/proto/JHJlg8loTyrsKZhijkizZK/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Brand?page-id=3024%3A10490&node-id=3995-21475&viewport=1010%2C704%2C0.06&t=nCWcIzshdGe1hr1i-1&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=3995%3A21475] is the prototype for the promo codes page. Most primary buttons are interactive and link to the Rides, Food, and Invite a Friend pages. Each promo card is also clickable and opens a bottom sheet with additional details. The bottom sheet can be closed by clicking the X icon or anywhere outside of it.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.","2026-01-20T08:25:38.426Z"],["3822394","RIDE-688","RIDE","fatmakhanim.mammadova@bolt.eu","Fatya Mammadova","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1660cwuvRVPZfjIYb-gIt_880OOUIgwXf70HJRq6PJTM/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1660cwuvRVPZfjIYb-gIt_880OOUIgwXf70HJRq6PJTM/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:25:42.932Z"],["3822395","WEBSD-1450","WEBSD","gabija.dimsaite@bolt.eu","Gabija Dimšaitė","Hey, also attaching vehicle list [article|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VcK1NY0NCgk5R6QEi2rIALy8wpJoY9qCg5Z_Tkj_65o/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.5h920a2e1jch] (both English and Lithuanian) versions - this is the article we enquired about on Slack. \n\n","2026-01-20T08:25:43.072Z"],["3822400","LSS-61829","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[^260119_NDA_Bolt_DB_Draft.docx] _(143 kB)_","2026-01-20T08:26:43.980Z"],["3822403","RDS-850","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] FYI: added prio, feel free to adjust.","2026-01-20T08:27:06.903Z"],["3822411","MARTECH3-1438","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","{{2026-01-20}}\n\nData on dev was reviewed and confirmed by Juan Felipe. I was involved in finding explanations for numbers. \n\nDeployment in progress. \nNext steps: \n\n* Backfill\n* Develop config in experimentation to pull data from marts","2026-01-20T08:28:31.685Z"],["3822414","DELIVERY-45","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: Continue technical scopeout - need to agree on some implementation details.  Similar ETA as last update: app version 106 for employees and 107 for global release. ","2026-01-20T08:29:19.708Z"],["3822416","WFM-10051","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, we have raised market request, kindly add necessary queues. ","2026-01-20T08:29:33.410Z"],["3822418","WFM-10051","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601729|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601729]","2026-01-20T08:29:44.982Z"],["3822419","PFI-830905","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Thanks! I noticed that the previous entity was not VAT liable. We can reissue with the new billing details (SASU NOVTC19), but unfortunately we do not have tooling to change the VAT liability nor amounts on the invoices. If that is acceptable, I will proceed with reissuing. ","2026-01-20T08:29:45.158Z"],["3822421","DRX-28291","DRX","dmitry.lazarev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Lazarev","[~accountid:604aad6403ceda0069bec100], I see Metehan’s comment now, and I disagree with it: I don’t see what makes “Safety” features special, and I’d rather have one ticket for everything.","2026-01-20T08:29:54.856Z"],["3822423","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768897828977879]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3673 successfully transitioned to state 'To Do'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:30:41.354Z"],["3822424","PFI-833813","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T08:30:48.358Z"],["3822426","DSR-3855","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T08:31:06.691Z"],["3822427","MARTECH3-1511","MARTECH3","tomasz.kiapsnia@bolt.eu","Tomasz Kiapśnia","{{2026-01-20}}\n\nI reviewed queries delivered by [~accountid:712020:84ab23ba-018a-41e9-a119-70e7813ad27d] \n\nWaiting for development in dbt","2026-01-20T08:31:21.212Z"],["3822428","LSS-61830","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[^BOLT Operations NDA - Sweatcoin Signed (1).pdf] _(249 kB)_","2026-01-20T08:31:23.567Z"],["3822429","DELIVERY-999","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: All the details are nearly finished. We will full focus on this. The ETA is around 6 weeks from now.","2026-01-20T08:31:24.753Z"],["3822432","RS-1734","RS","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Hello [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c] , my apologies for not responding in October!\nThe data has been now gathered and it still feels excessive. The authorities have already been asked if they can reduce the scope.\n\nPrepared data:\n[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XKzvGdC7vsNPwpEEnsNDl54JAERE2F7efiTxsslebYs/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XKzvGdC7vsNPwpEEnsNDl54JAERE2F7efiTxsslebYs/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] \n\n\nThe response we received when asking for justification:\n\n_The Northern Prefecture sent 2 subpoenas in criminal case no. 25231552037. The subpoenas referred to Penal Code §§ 215 (1), 32 (2). The criminal case has been forwarded to the prosecutor's office. According to Penal Code § 214 (1), pre-trial procedure information may be disclosed only with the permission of the prosecutor's office and to the extent determined by it and under the conditions provided for in subsection 2 of this section._\n\nLatest BH case:\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/658491432|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/658491432]","2026-01-20T08:31:38.009Z"],["3822435","FX-3540","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Pema Couto Matos [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768897915808929]*{color}:\nThat's correct <@U04FV4Z0GQ4> we payback the deposit via the old Viggo Console, which has its advantage as it already takes into account the negative balance the a FO has. When it comes to the payout, the process has not changed and continues being a file that Laura upload to the Jysk bank and it gets approved from someone in Bolt.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09GT7VLPQC/p1758626129437259]\n\nLinked messages:\n[September 23rd, 2025 4:15 AM] laura.decampos: Hi :wave::skin-tone-5:\n\nPlease see the payout slips attached from Viggo Console and let me or <@pema.matos> know if you are missing additional payslips :blush:\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:32:09.070Z"],["3822436","DELIVERY-562","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: We didn’t pick it up yet","2026-01-20T08:32:21.234Z"],["3822437","RDS-851","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8], What is your perspective on that? I see the value in increased clarity for accessibility, but I also feel adding additional labels would be overkill.\n\nI feel that what we should do instead is to make a very clear visual connection between those fields to explain that it is a route. For example, Uber or Google Maps is doing it better than us.\n\n\n\n","2026-01-20T08:32:21.945Z"],["3822438","LSS-61829","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","Timeline: Needs to be signed EOW ","2026-01-20T08:32:31.787Z"],["3822439","HS-28993","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp"," Employee did not consult a doctor about opening a sick leave. They will request personal day instead.","2026-01-20T08:32:39.453Z"],["3822441","PFI-828470","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe are checking with the payment service provider and will revert back here with more information.","2026-01-20T08:32:51.124Z"],["3822443","RDS-852","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] FYI: added prio (IMO very relevant), feel free to adjust.","2026-01-20T08:33:31.229Z"],["3822445","LSS-61751","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hey [~accountid:62134a797580350068337097] - the amendment looks good for signatures. Can you please share the details of the signatory for MasterCard and I will send this ticket forward for signatures. \n\nAlso, regarding termination- Either party may end this Schedule by giving the other party written notice at least fourteen (14) days before the end of the Pilot Phase- so if we extend the pilot by a month and decide to terminate- we need to send a written notice 14 days prior to the Pilot coming to an end. \n\nPlease let me know in case you have any further questions. Thanks. ","2026-01-20T08:33:56.060Z"],["3822448","PFI-835611","PFI","iryna.tkach@bolt-outsource.eu","Iryna Tkach","Hello, [~accountid:5f896b8ee357dd006e937d7b].\n\nClient said the next things:\n\n“My bank saw these receipts!!! They didn't do anything! They declined the payment and didn't accept the good funds! Because of the incorrect tax identification number!!”\n\nHer bank employees said that the transfer operation was rejected. Her bank informs you:\nPrivatBank indicated \"99999\" instead of her correct Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN). Due to the incorrect information, they rejected the money and returned it to the sending bank, our PrivatBank. They also asked her to convey that WE MUST CONTACT PrivatBank regarding the return of these funds, as they are held by PrivatBank!\n\nAnd then, when making a repeat payment to her account, we must instruct our PrivatBank to use the correct TIN, not random nines!\nOnly we, as the bank's clients, can contact t our PrivatBank; they will not provide her with any information.\n\nSo, do you understand the reason of rejecting the payout?\n\nIryna, Bolt","2026-01-20T08:34:21.871Z"],["3822453","DELIVERY-1065","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4:  We paused working working on M2 due to other priorities. We will resume this week M2 and wrap it up asap. Once the M2 will be finished we will revisit plans and estimates.","2026-01-20T08:34:50.343Z"],["3822455","WD-22612","WD","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Heyo, \n\nPESEL numbers are unique and historically I never had to provide employee numbers with this request. \n\nWould you be able to organize it without it, please? 🙏 \n\nThanks a lot in advance!\nEwa","2026-01-20T08:35:13.696Z"],["3822456","HS-29144","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:37cbbb0a-0685-4c67-b916-321d2983dc93], I’ve reached out to you via Slack. Please let me know if you have any further questions. I’m closing this ticket for now. Thank you!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.32.28 AM.png|width=580,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.32.28 AM.png\"!","2026-01-20T08:35:22.618Z"],["3822458","HS-29121","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","All the docs are ready, already reached out on Slack (/) ","2026-01-20T08:35:47.737Z"],["3822459","PFI-835939","PFI","precious.bakare@bolt-outsource.eu","Precious Bakare","!Receipt.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T08:35:49.643Z"],["3822460","DELIVERY-1540","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: Development almost finished (just some analytics missing). We will release it to the users in app version 104.","2026-01-20T08:36:03.831Z"],["3822462","PTWS-2098","PTWS","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hey [~accountid:712020:80f31809-0e9d-4c0f-8939-db5dd3d77922], the reason it’s going to the manager for approving the OTP is because that’s how the Request OTP BP is configured in both Prod and Sandbox (step e):\n\n!image-20260120-083553.png|width=540,alt=\"image-20260120-083553.png\"!\n\nLet’s meet today or tomorrow and discuss! ","2026-01-20T08:36:12.408Z"],["3822464","HS-29149","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Waiting for clarification on last day date","2026-01-20T08:36:15.629Z"],["3822467","BEE-2558","BEE","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","We are rethinking it as part of a dedicated initiative, no need to hold this task.","2026-01-20T08:36:28.949Z"],["3822471","LSS-59904","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^PS Rent Branding Amendment to fleet financing branding agreement (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-20T08:36:43.724Z"],["3822474","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","[@marat.saddarov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3] Is this something already discussed with PingCap or i need to start a thread for this ?","2026-01-20T08:37:13.781Z"],["3822475","DRX-28021","DRX","nyoman.abiwinanda@bolt.eu","Nyoman Abiwinanda","Will wait until PINT team fix new package container size bug: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1768832107220769?thread_ts=1768569171.326739&cid=C049U1GKWQN|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C049U1GKWQN/p1768832107220769?thread_ts=1768569171.326739&cid=C049U1GKWQN|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:37:26.444Z"],["3822476","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768898237128229]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-367 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:37:28.728Z"],["3822478","WFM-10052","WFM","anhelina.babych@bolt.eu","Anhelina Babych","queue was assigned, WFM team please check if anything needs to be adjusted in the assembled ","2026-01-20T08:37:48.688Z"],["3822481","HS-29145","HS","barbara.puss@bolt.eu","Barbara Püss","Dear [~accountid:712020:139873e5-f42f-4b26-92ae-5640b533348c], the FS3 2025 will be available after 15/02/2026.","2026-01-20T08:38:14.017Z"],["3822482","LSS-61694","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:5f9aac6499b42e0069a4f456] ! I understand the case but it is not up to me. it is up to Ahto if he’s present at the office today to sign it. [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please treat it as urgent 🙏  Thank you! 😊 ","2026-01-20T08:38:23.930Z"],["3822484","CRC-2328","CRC","sander.randorg@bolt.eu","Sander Randorg","[update] Two plans for this week: 1) start with mapping the simplest ride-hailing sale with finance controlling; 2) finalize the object discussions on order-based object flows. Trying to work with the resource constraints on controlling and revenue assurance side.","2026-01-20T08:38:35.225Z"],["3822487","WD-22537","WD","anja.marx@bolt.eu","Anja Marx","Good day [~accountid:605ee2ff2f7d900070c2e481] \n\nThanks for supplying the breakdown, it makes sense now.\n\nThe confusion came in, in me not knowing the next months leave is only added on the day of the month you started, (in my case only the 17th) as I have always calculated my added leave from the beginning of the month.\n\nI will keep this in mind for future reference when calculating leave days again.\n\nThanks you for your assistance.\n\nHave a good day.\n\nAnna\n\n","2026-01-20T08:39:37.370Z"],["3822489","DELIVERY-1720","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: We started looking into this and plan to ship this in app version 1.104.","2026-01-20T08:39:45.856Z"],["3822491","RDXENG-4662","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","[~accountid:625fb496efc8a5006a5557e5] Zoom levels are a bit confusing right now in comparison to in-app behaviour. Should user not see the full route?\n\nScreen recording below, tapping on current location button ⬇️ \n\n[^ScreenRecording_01-20-2026 10-34-29_1.MP4]","2026-01-20T08:40:32.153Z"],["3822495","LSS-29559","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","perfect, thank you [~accountid:623c7881562ab90069f8f044] !","2026-01-20T08:40:58.217Z"],["3822497","RDS-853","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] [~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] Quick question: how are we using rating chips? Are there impacting something or are visible somehow?","2026-01-20T08:41:35.850Z"],["3822498","HS-28983","HS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Many thanks! Looking forward to receiving it.","2026-01-20T08:41:40.743Z"],["3822499","RDXENG-4662","RDXENG","juri.noga@bolt.eu","Juri Noga","[~accountid:712020:ef5f49c9-39d4-4c05-820b-dbad89f985a0]  Route coordinates are not included to zoom calculation, I’ll see how to include it.","2026-01-20T08:41:51.521Z"],["3822501","RDXENG-4367","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(x) *Also destination pin appears very detached from the route.* Same order below, webview vs in-app.\n\n!IMG_1810-20260120-084935.PNG|width=199,alt=\"IMG_1810-20260120-084935.PNG\"!\n\n!IMG_1811-20260120-084946.PNG|width=200,alt=\"IMG_1811-20260120-084946.PNG\"!","2026-01-20T08:42:07.375Z"],["3822502","RCE-352","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768898517392659]*{color}:\nCause: lead and driver city are different, causing mismatch in document sets.\nFollow discussion in growth conversion's support channel: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02H52XUKPG/p1768410822034899]\n\nLinked messages:\n[January 14th, 2026 9:13 AM] sandra.figari: Hi team! Our outsourced team escalated these cases to me a few minutes ago where, after accepting the lead and verify the docs, these are not uploaded to the driver’s profile and the following message appears: “. _py_criminal_record_online_check\" \"profile_pic_vr\" \"driver_license_vr\" \"py_drivers_license_back\" \"ncr_vr_. The agent in charge of these leads manually uploaded the documentation after accepting the account.\nWhich would be the cause of it?\nThanks in advance!\n1. [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8506767?tab=profile&amp;filter=%7B%22limit%[…]set%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=America%2FAsuncion|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8506767?tab=profile&amp;filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=America%2FAsuncion]\n2. [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/driver-registration/driverRegistrations/edit/28833263?tab=[…]ffset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/driver-registration/driverRegistrations/edit/28833263?tab=details&amp;filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:42:11.181Z"],["3822504","CRC-2105","CRC","sander.randorg@bolt.eu","Sander Randorg","[update] FDWH to present Billing with latest findings on the reconciliation effort today. The whole last-mile has taken more time than anticipated, forcing us to consider such complexities when timeboxing our next milestone.","2026-01-20T08:42:22.656Z"],["3822505","LSS-59892","LSS","kristjan.okas@bolt.eu","Kristjan Okas","Update: communication went out and the matter was closed. Closing the ticket. ","2026-01-20T08:42:35.008Z"],["3822507","RCE-352","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768898545793019]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-352 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:42:42.804Z"],["3822508","CRC-2107","CRC","sander.randorg@bolt.eu","Sander Randorg","[update] No big updates, work ongoing with commission invoice reconciliations.","2026-01-20T08:42:58.881Z"],["3822513","RDXENG-4367","RDXENG","juri.noga@bolt.eu","Juri Noga","[~accountid:712020:ef5f49c9-39d4-4c05-820b-dbad89f985a0]  Safari has known issues with svg scaling. I’ll see whether I can tweak svg’s so they scale better which should improve stops' icons, not sure about car icon as it’s a complex shape.","2026-01-20T08:43:12.326Z"],["3822515","LSS-61728","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344503|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344503|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:43:19.369Z"],["3822517","SAI-1412","SAI","henadzi.baranau@bolt.eu","Henadzi Baranau","That was result of [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1765792864601739] issue (nodejs common update) when MQ events were duplicated","2026-01-20T08:43:35.715Z"],["3822520","DELIVERY-430","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: Feature enabled for employees, we will continue monitoring. The plan is to enable it to a larger audience next week","2026-01-20T08:43:44.048Z"],["3822521","DRX-28291","DRX","dmitry.lazarev@bolt.eu","Dmitry Lazarev","Or, alternatively, we can convert it to an Epic and have team-specific tasks inside it.","2026-01-20T08:43:54.272Z"],["3822524","PFI-830905","PFI","raphael.perna@bolt.eu","Raphaël Samy Perna","Thank you, [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] .\nWe confirm that we will proceed with whatever is technically possible on your side, the re-issuance of the invoices with the SASU NOVTC19 billing details.\n\n[~accountid:712020:465d1767-e73a-4479-9b0f-095dbe0bbaef] : could you please clearly explain the situation to the driver, especially the VAT point (technical impossibility to change VAT liability and amounts), so that the scope and limitations of the correction are fully understood?\n\nThank you both.","2026-01-20T08:44:21.891Z"],["3822525","WD-22611","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Payment election country updated to Belgium - employee has added banking detils","2026-01-20T08:44:26.837Z"],["3822527","PFI-835941","PFI","chaninat.wongrod@bolt-outsource.eu","Chaninat Wongrod","!Messenger_creation_F27479B8-C9C7-440C-9E16-8156ACAB55EF.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T08:44:48.230Z"],["3822534","LSS-61726","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:f8c30920-765a-42dd-bbe7-058336c97a0c] - We do not electronically stamp documents. Stamps are only available when signing on paper. Does a standard electronic signature without a stamp work for you? We can complete that today; wet signatures take longer.","2026-01-20T08:45:48.232Z"],["3822535","DSR-3191","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - from a GDPR POV, the request has been addressed: there has *already* been a human review of the decision, which happened when CSPC contacted the Verification team (see this [comment|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DSR-3191?focusedCommentId=3765104] in the thread below and the post [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06BQ7T6L4F/p1766131831934799]). This was also communicated to the user in the answer letter sent on 16 January 2025:\n\n{quote}Bolt may use automated processes for the purpose of [detecting and preventing fraud / verifying identification] (and restricting access to accounts, as needed). However, such processes either: (a) rely on relevant exceptions under applicable data protection laws and regulations; (b) do not produce legal or similarly significant effects on individuals; or (c) are subject to human review. For good measure, our specialist team has reviewed the access restriction and determined that it is necessary to maintain the access restriction on your account. As such, we will not be restoring access to your account at this time. We apologise for any inconvenience caused by this decision.{quote}\n\nI suggest you de-escalate to T2/Ops with a summary of the information above. They can close off the case as they deem fit.","2026-01-20T08:45:54.804Z"],["3822537","RS-1960","RS","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Link to the web page [https://www.royalthaipolice.go.th/|https://www.royalthaipolice.go.th/|smart-link] \n\n[^สน.ลาดกระบัง หมายเรียกพยานบุคคล.pdf.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T08:46:08.426Z"],["3822538","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","[@shubham.singh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/623194c0442e0e0069ed229c], can it happen that if an outage happens, only a single table is affected if more are configured for a given feed? Since you’ve requested a backfill for a single table only yesterday and it seems others were affected too?","2026-01-20T08:46:11.459Z"],["3822540","HS-29076","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Waiting for a settlement agreement. ","2026-01-20T08:46:40.526Z"],["3822542","PFI-833647","PFI","kosisochukwu.ochuaka@bolt-outsource.eu","Kosisochukwu Ochuaka","Hello team, please share an update on the issue.  ","2026-01-20T08:47:21.950Z"],["3822543","LSS-61821","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:3628e8e4-2c88-4d47-8c51-14aa1e98735c] , I have reviewed the proposed service agreement for Michel and noticed that its structure differs materially from the two service agreements we have already signed with TPS (Sweta and Clyde).\n\nTo ensure alignment and avoid ambiguity, I would appreciate if you with the help of the counterparty could clarify on the following points:\n\n# *Intended engagement model*\nCan you please confirm whether Michel is intended to be:\n#* (a) an *agency worker employed by TPS* and seconded to Bolt (as with Sweta), or\n#* (b) an *independent interim professional* engaged on a services basis (as with Clyde)?\n# *Employment relationship*\nThe Michel agreement states that the contractor acts as an independent professional and that no employment relationship exists, but it also refers to:\n#* deployment for 8 hours per day / 40 hours per week,\n#* performance under the conditions of the collective labour agreement (cao), and\n#* TPS remaining responsible for the employment relationship and supervision.\nPlease clarify how these elements are intended to operate together in practice.\n# *Use of collective labour agreement (cao)*\nIf Michel is not employed by TPS as an agency worker, could you explain why the agreement refers to the cao for temporary agency workers?\nConversely, if the cao is intended to apply, why does the agreement not follow the same structure as the Sweta agreement (explicit agency employment, phase system, inlenersbeloning, pension, etc.)?\n# *Consistency with existing contracts*\nMichel’s agreement currently appears to sit between the Sweta (agency worker) and Clyde (independent interim) models. Was this intentional, or would you prefer to align Michel’s agreement fully with one of the previously agreed models?\n# *Operational reality*\nFrom a practical standpoint, how do you expect Michel to operate day to day in terms of:\n#* autonomy in how the work is performed,\n#* supervision and instruction, and\n#* integration into Bolt’s organisation?\n\nOnce I understand the intended structure, I am happy to align on the appropriate template so that the agreement accurately reflects the legal and operational reality for all parties.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-20T08:47:31.888Z"],["3822547","PFI-834554","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","I see the hardblock is already removed, I unblocked their recent devices to aid with comms.\nThank you!","2026-01-20T08:47:55.131Z"],["3822549","LSS-61383","LSS","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Good morning [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2], from what I understood the situation is a bit different.\n\nRide price is 10, but Bolt wants to collect money on it so it issues an invoice on behalf of the driver for ride price 10, but on the paid by line it charges an  extra EUr 2, for example, so the total invoiced amount is EUR 12. So currently the paid by line is not necessarily being used to decrease the amount to be paid by customer, but rather to increase it.\n\nLet’s go over this in the meeting planned for this week so we can get to a common position.","2026-01-20T08:48:15.718Z"],["3822550","LSS-61732","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344518|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344518|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:48:50.819Z"],["3822551","DELIVERY-739","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: We plan to enable this soon (1-2 weeks). We need to check for any overlapping (a/b) tests to make sure we don’t affect any outcomes (but it shouldn’t be the case).  ","2026-01-20T08:48:52.866Z"],["3822552","LSS-61743","LSS","kristi.purik@bolt.eu","Kristi Purik","Hi all,\n\nIt is Bolt Operations OÜ","2026-01-20T08:48:54.677Z"],["3822553","WFM-10046","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Agent ID : 352594 ","2026-01-20T08:49:05.710Z"],["3822556","WFM-10046","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, agent \t[rudolfs.upe@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:rudolfs.upe@bolt-outsource.eu] has all the necessary permissions, kindly add the queue.","2026-01-20T08:49:46.613Z"],["3822557","LSS-61726","LSS","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","Hi [~accountid:5f0436f3b545e20015573888]  - yes electronic signature will work as well. Though I know they used to e-stamp too.  But sure signature itself is fine. ","2026-01-20T08:50:03.089Z"],["3822558","DRX-27424","DRX","joonas.niiholm@bolt.eu","Joonas Niiholm","[~accountid:712020:47e6816d-876b-4d46-8a97-5225889a64c8] “its basically what was available in the old screen - can't remember what exactly\nand there's a thread on it which was linked in either that the others catch all RDS”","2026-01-20T08:50:05.636Z"],["3822559","DELIVERY-542","DELIVERY","alex.ovidiunitu@bolt.eu","Ovidiu-Alexandru Nițu","26W4: Feature enabled to 1% of users. However we discovered again a bug which was mitigated, we are continue monitoring and deploy potential fixes","2026-01-20T08:50:21.343Z"],["3822561","RDS-851","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","{quote}I also feel adding additional labels would be overkill. {quote}\n\n[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] can you say more about why? This isn’t just an accessibility issue (although we failed our accessibility audit from Trinidad Wiseman on this with blind users consistently frustrated with the basics of booking a ride) — [usability data on this is clear|https://www.nngroup.com/articles/form-design-placeholders/]: “User testing continually shows that placeholders in form fields often hurt usability more than help it.” \n\nThe inspiration for this ticket was watching my mother try (and fail) to book a ride because she was putting her pickup location into the destination field. There were no field labels, and she had no idea what went where. It was painful to see. She is not disabled, by the way.\n\nI reported this 1.5 years ago 🥲 Original thread for context:\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C019RN6C3Q9/p1721984180517659|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C019RN6C3Q9/p1721984180517659|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:51:06.998Z"],["3822563","DBRE-8705","DBRE","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","And it looks like [this|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CF65PRL0N/p1768897249763399?thread_ts=1768555181.857879&cid=CF65PRL0N] is related.","2026-01-20T08:51:08.682Z"],["3822564","LSS-61775","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344514|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344514|smart-link]  ","2026-01-20T08:51:09.898Z"],["3822566","LSS-61718","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344523|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344523|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:51:33.670Z"],["3822567","LSS-61831","LSS","wojciech.wawro@bolt.eu","Wojciech Wawro","[^Customer Special Terms - Bolt Business (41)_sig.pdf] _(389 kB)_","2026-01-20T08:51:34.110Z"],["3822568","L10N-28843","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source 