his ticket? Did you receive the missing Malta update?","2026-01-20T08:51:54.917Z"],["3822572","L10N-28849","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28841](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28841)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T08:51:55.597Z"],["3822573","L10N-28852","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28841](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28841)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T08:51:59.125Z"],["3822574","L10N-28854","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28841](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28841)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T08:52:00.761Z"],["3822575","L10N-28855","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28841](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28841)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T08:52:00.925Z"],["3822577","L10N-28857","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28841](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28841)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T08:52:02.106Z"],["3822578","FPD-1545","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Looker dashboard for partner data: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/4671?Country=France&Period+Date=12+month+ago+for+12+month&Dynamic+timeframe+selector=Month&City=Paris&Dynamic+City%2FCountry%2FRegion+parameter=City&Active+Partners=>10|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/4671?Country=France&Period+Date=12+month+ago+for+12+month&Dynamic+timeframe+selector=Month&City=Paris&Dynamic+City%2FCountry%2FRegion+parameter=City&Active+Partners=%3E10]\n\nLooking at Paris (image below), values for active partners, churns and activations do not match our data. Also, the condition *Active Partners (t) = Active Partners (t-1) + Partner Activations (t) - Partner Churns (t)* does not hold true.\n\n!image-20260120-084931.png|width=1102,alt=\"image-20260120-084931.png\"!","2026-01-20T08:52:27.105Z"],["3822579","LSS-60553","LSS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] we already received a signed copy from our partner and unfortunately Mahmoud’s signature disappeared from the document - do you know could be the reason for this and confirm it’s valid regardless of lack of Mahmoud’s signature>\n\n[^Copy of Cognizant - template notification and consent PL EN(514274454.1).docx (1) (92de64e8-1de0-4e8f-bae4-3ce2be627e22).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T08:52:35.021Z"],["3822580","LSS-60691","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[~accountid:63d0eccfa197e05f9dadc837] - Kindly share a status update with us - let’s try and get this ticket closed by end of this week. Thanks!","2026-01-20T08:52:39.049Z"],["3822582","RDS-851","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","And let me pull out one quote from that thread as it’s particularly relevant:\n\n{quote}_Just so I’m not misunderstood, I suggest making this change not just because it meets accessibility standards, but because it is the best user experience for_ *_all users_*_. That it helps us stay compliant is fantastic and obviously something we should strive for, but the main reason for this change is just to improve the basic UX._\n\n_The research is pretty settled here:_[https://www.nngroup.com/articles/form-design-placeholders/|https://www.nngroup.com/articles/form-design-placeholders/|smart-link] {quote}","2026-01-20T08:52:53.702Z"],["3822584","TAX2-564","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Hey [~accountid:61419ea149f7bd0068a78d7c] , what are the improvements set for 26Q1?","2026-01-20T08:53:20.459Z"],["3822586","LSS-61827","LSS","kai.vainola@bolt.eu","Kai Vainola","this is not a ticket for Corporate Legal. [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] can you help?","2026-01-20T08:53:43.575Z"],["3822589","RLONE-854","RLONE","anton.berggren@bolt.eu","Anton Berggren","[*Upsell feature in Cancellation Screen*|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09LXATFX8X/p1768558038143389]\n\n* Potential high impact feature related to Driver Acceptance Rate\n* Investigate if (and how) this feature could be tested in Sweden\n** Asked [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02CUF8CFCZ/p1768825816144599?thread_ts=1768554030.659329&cid=C02CUF8CFCZ]","2026-01-20T08:54:07.024Z"],["3822592","LSS-61827","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:6017bc1adc29b4006a7f1030] this was raised by mistake under Corporate Legal but it’s not actually for the Corporate Legal team, but for our HQ legal/internal IT vendor agreement review. \n\nIs it ok if we use this and it gets assigned to [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] (or someone from Maria’s team) or can the request type be changed? \n\nIf not, [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] can raise a new one 🙏  Sorry for the mix up","2026-01-20T08:54:14.499Z"],["3822593","DSR-3521","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] - you can get a headstart on this yourself:\n\n* {color:#006644}*Essential information about the processing:*{color} wording concerning this can be leveraged from the existing templates → all information is in our Privacy Notice. I suggest you use [+DSAR: Access Request template+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/35952?country=global&language=en]\n* {color:#006644}Bolt’s refusal to provide such data would require a {color}{color:#006644}*clear and explicit legal justification*{color}{color:#006644} and reference to the {color}{color:#006644}*specific legal provisions*{color}{color:#006644} relied upon{color}: same as above - we can rely on the second paragraph of the template and add a reference to art 15 GDPR.\n* {color:#006644}*Calculation method*{color}: I’ll look into this, I have drafted something around this question in the past.\n* {color:#006644}*Reassessment of the charge*{color}: not sure why this is being escalated to Privacy/CSPC, this is outside of our scope","2026-01-20T08:54:15.036Z"],["3822594","LSS-59711","LSS","martin.tomberg@bolt.eu","Martin Tomberg","Hej [~accountid:5d0c8f1621a5d30bc4e096a8] \nI was aware about [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/_wEA0|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/_wEA0|smart-link] \nOversight i have only about Offices and some walkins (Total about 120 locations). Access to CCTV only were is Verkada, Tallinn HQ and soon new system Genetec. \n\nRegarding system what is in use in vertical need wider approach. Those systems are in networks what our IT is not controlling. Access to vertical systems is handled in vertical (Dont know by who).\n\nMy thought is decision need to be clear do vertical need to act like office in all levels (IT, Infosec; Risk, P.Security, H&S etc) or not. Do to that it is costly","2026-01-20T08:54:27.869Z"],["3822595","TAX2-563","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Hey [~accountid:712020:dcaeeaea-b979-4efa-93e7-594a518b6eb5] , is there already more information on the work to be carried on this quarter?","2026-01-20T08:54:33.671Z"],["3822598","LSS-60369","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] , [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] - Please provide a status update. It has been a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T08:55:03.684Z"],["3822599","TAX2-564","TAX2","shivam.atri@bolt.eu","Shivam Atri","Hey, the improvements for Q1 are\n\n* Both receivers and senders are able to book. We are also able to tell the driver who to receive the cash from.\n* Receiver and Driver can communicate with each other with a single channel to start with\n* Initiator is able to send the link of the ride to other person for live order tracking.","2026-01-20T08:55:15.166Z"],["3822602","ROPSC-492","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Compliance-related processes reviewed together with local team.\n\nNote from local team:\n”We follow the procedures. The only difference is when we copy a driver ([Driver Copy and Relocation features|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PLBK/pages/4651517493/Driver+Copy+and+Relocation+Features]), we are not using the \"_Copy selected car to car group\".”_","2026-01-20T08:55:27.676Z"],["3822605","RIDE-621","RIDE","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Hey [~accountid:5bbde236ee5d7e7580edbb02] , any updated on the matter? And why is the contract between Bolt Mexico and driver instead of having partner as the contracting party?","2026-01-20T08:55:43.972Z"],["3822606","TAX2-558","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Further waiting for infor from POC.","2026-01-20T08:55:57.861Z"],["3822607","LSS-59925","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - The document is still pending Mehman’s signature. Please provide a status update. It has been over a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T08:56:18.302Z"],["3822610","RCE-369","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768899375167389]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-369] `Add nationality citizenship metadata Argentina to document` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T08:56:27.132Z"],["3822611","LSS-61827","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:6017bc1adc29b4006a7f1030] sure, it should go to HQ support \n\n[~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] I received the ticket and will proceed with the review ","2026-01-20T08:56:42.041Z"],["3822612","DBRE-8705","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Others were not affected; only the lag increased because of the one I requested. The other feeds were fine, and as soon as I rebuilt the broken one, the other feeds' lag went away.","2026-01-20T08:56:42.275Z"],["3822613","LSS-61827","LSS","alex.bucse@bolt.eu","Alex Bucșe","Attached documentation here is existing agreement/DPA executed with OpenAI (amendment was the novation/assignment of the contracts to their European Entity). \n\nWe are finalising the numbers and will ask for order form, but just wanted Legal to have a quick look over existing terms so once Order Form comes in we just have one more look and sign. \n\nCC [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] ","2026-01-20T08:56:44.635Z"],["3822614","PFI-673177","PFI","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Hello and thank you! FO claimed [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/726133276] that they still have not received the payout, neither have any of their drivers. Can you please double-check?","2026-01-20T08:57:01.813Z"],["3822615","TAX2-542","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Hey [~accountid:712020:a0124a71-9df9-4683-aa0c-9dea10fcc90e] , any estimate on when the document Ana mentioned will be ready? What is the status of the project?","2026-01-20T08:57:06.673Z"],["3822617","LSS-59897","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - The document is still pending Oleksandr’s signature. Please provide a status update. It has been over a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T08:57:23.300Z"],["3822618","PFI-833185","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, coupons are invoiced differently based on whether they’re by Users of the Company or not. For more details, please, find here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/4819125137/Invoicing+Flow+for+Business+Coupons|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/4819125137/Invoicing+Flow+for+Business+Coupons|smart-link]. TLDR: coupons used by Employees are invoiced together with Transporation Services and VAT Applies, while those used by the non-Users are invoiced separately and VAT doesn’t apply.\n\nAttached is the aggregation of what went to the invoice. First row: coupons used by non-Users; second row: traditional rides; third row: coupons used by Users of the company aggregated together with Transportation Services Invoice Row. \n\n!image-20260120-085540.png|width=362,alt=\"image-20260120-085540.png\"!\n\nPlease, let me know if explanation suffice or you have any question. On the side topic, I heard that Business Analysts have some nice Lookers with coupons usage, etc.","2026-01-20T08:57:46.694Z"],["3822619","TAX2-537","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","Meeting to talk about the project on 20 January 2026","2026-01-20T08:57:56.620Z"],["3822620","LSS-59893","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - The document is still pending Oleksandr’s and Tetiana’s signatures. Please provide a status update. It has been over a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T08:57:57.894Z"],["3822622","SREC-375","SREC","amin.khoshnood@bolt.eu","Amin Khoshnood","{noformat}cat ~/.aws/config\n\nsso_role_name = ENGSRECloud737418964414{noformat}\n\nIf this is on ENGInfoSecAdmin or ENGInformationSec , please change it to {{ENGCloudSec}}.\n\nThen:\n\n{noformat}aws sso login --profile bolt{noformat}","2026-01-20T08:58:13.201Z"],["3822625","PIF-1693","PIF","sergey.seleznev@bolt.eu","Sergei Seleznev","Now the release freezes are extracted into a separate calendar: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/freeze-schedule/items|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/freeze-schedule/items].\n\nBuilder releases during freezes are blocked by default and require explicit confirmation.\n\nThere are public notifications regarding critical incidents and other critical situations in dev-global, dev-live-incidents, etc.","2026-01-20T08:58:24.915Z"],["3822626","PFI-835621","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, has the Agent Profile been updated, according to: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|smart-link]  ","2026-01-20T08:58:28.284Z"],["3822627","DBRE-8705","DBRE","kewei.shang@bolt.eu","Kewei Shang","[@shubham.singh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/623194c0442e0e0069ed229c], actually what we meant is does the broken feed streams more than 1 table? if so, we need to backfill all the tables included in the broken feed","2026-01-20T08:58:29.929Z"],["3822629","ROPSC-493","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Fleet document sets are now aligned with global standards.\n\nThe only thin that was not configured was “Block if missing” for Profile Pictures. The configuration has now been done. ","2026-01-20T08:58:38.057Z"],["3822630","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Remove cs-db-4 from ProxySQL cluster: [https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139809#nodes|https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139809#nodes]\n* [https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139810#nodes|https://r.db.boltint.net/execution/show/139810#nodes] ( One more run due to discovery discovers the cs-db-4 instance back )\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1768899686304999|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1768899686304999|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T08:58:48.736Z"],["3822632","PFI-835302","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, provide invoice link/invoice number","2026-01-20T08:58:53.260Z"],["3822633","LSS-59841","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - The document is still pending Glib’s and Marchenko’s signatures. Please provide a status update. It has been over a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T08:58:55.215Z"],["3822635","LSS-61430","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nAs mentioned yesterday, could you please remind the team of the following guidance:\n\n* *First suggest a gift card* (this should be done *by phone only*, not in writing).\n* *Do not mention compensation in writing* — not in the invite, nor in the registration form.\n* If the team wants to offer monetary compensation, this should only be discussed *after the driver accepts the invite*, and *strictly over the phone*, never in writing.\n* As flagged in the product RH channel, the focus should remain on the *narrative and purpose* of the session (listening, sharing, contributing).\n* Please also suggest them *avoid saying — even over the phone — things like “we’ll pay you €50 because you can’t drive”* or anything along those lines.\n\nThanks so much!\n\nElisabetta","2026-01-20T08:58:59.439Z"],["3822637","DSR-3811","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","User left new message:\nsir I don’t feel comfortable that anyone any company keep my data when i am not working with thm anymore . I haven’t work even a single day . So i will request by the advocate to responsible government  departments to check with your company  that what data you kept after deleting my account i am not feeling secure and comfortable to keep someone my data Thanks","2026-01-20T08:59:26.592Z"],["3822638","LSS-59815","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - The document is still pending Mykola’s signatures. Please provide a status update. It has been over a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T08:59:26.626Z"],["3822639","PFI-835267","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-20T08:59:28.026Z"],["3822642","LSS-59314","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] , [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] - The document is still pending Rafal’s and Anastasiya’s signatures. Please provide a status update. It has been over a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T09:00:01.419Z"],["3822643","LSS-61600","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344532|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344532|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:00:12.872Z"],["3822644","PFI-833735","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, if the payment is not visible on the company Balance then please, raise it with the Payments team.","2026-01-20T09:00:15.461Z"],["3822646","WD-22616","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] , \nidea is to create a UBSG of [~accountid:712020:c24abb54-ee7f-43ba-bb8e-3ad5ff67df41] and [~accountid:60b2030e25a51300698c52c6] . Assign this group to the Domain Security Policy “*Set Up: Enable Worktags*”.\nTwo of them would receive view and modify access to these 14 items. \n\nPlease check and give your approval in case you agree with me providing the new security access to them. \n\n!image-20260120-085912.png|width=1202,alt=\"image-20260120-085912.png\"!","2026-01-20T09:00:24.552Z"],["3822647","PFI-833735","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T09:00:24.855Z"],["3822649","PFI-833550","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, please, reach out to the payment team for the proof of payments. Invoice for services provided are visible in the Invoices tab of Admin.","2026-01-20T09:00:56.939Z"],["3822650","LSS-58414","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:71a7cd9a-50a4-4498-a9e0-da88ed773162] , [~accountid:712020:03164f2c-f82a-4e8e-9172-2c02cad1e229] - The documents are still pending Moustafa’s signatures. Please provide a status update. It has been a month, so let’s try to close this by the end of the week. If we do not hear from the counterparty, we will cancel the ticket. Thank you!","2026-01-20T09:01:26.425Z"],["3822652","RCE-369","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768899680895789]*{color}:\nHi <@UCVT712UR>\nPlease, make a post in the <#C053YST9V0T|>  channel\nOps can handle your request there\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:02:15.407Z"],["3822656","WD-22606","WD","victoria.covalciuc@bolt.eu","Victoria Covalciuc","Hi Octavian,\n\nthanks so much, I have now figured it out. :)","2026-01-20T09:03:19.279Z"],["3822658","WDFT-3559","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/edit-v2/7425032342?draftShareId=15b01df4-86ac-42e5-843d-c825997f2257|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/edit-v2/7425032342?draftShareId=15b01df4-86ac-42e5-843d-c825997f2257|smart-link] \n\n!image-20260120-090307.png|width=1122,alt=\"image-20260120-090307.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n!image-20260120-090327.png|width=1107,alt=\"image-20260120-090327.png\"!","2026-01-20T09:03:35.942Z"],["3822659","PFI-833434","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, please, raise it with the Local in-house CS Team, if there’re any issues with calculations. Invoices issued are in the Invoices tab: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/789262?tab=invoices|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/789262?tab=invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]; Bank transfers are on the Payments tab: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/789262?tab=payments|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/789262?tab=payments&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22company_id%22%3A789262%7D%7D]; Card Charges are on the Topups tab: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/789262?tab=topups|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/789262?tab=topups&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22business_company_id%22%3A789262%7D%7D]","2026-01-20T09:03:51.686Z"],["3822663","WFM-10050","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Agents IDs: 622385, 622499, 592388, 592389, 592392","2026-01-20T09:04:39.926Z"],["3822687","WD-22612","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","hey! no worries, i can use Pesel no, just wanted to see if you have the employee numbers, it would have been easier to add 😉 ","2026-01-20T09:05:08.890Z"],["3822697","LSS-61609","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] could you please answer this question: The business team raised a question: usually in EE there is a need to present the ASiC-E file container, not just the PDF inside the container. Please confirm whether the below signed document in PDF form is sufficient for a legitimate e-signature, or whether the ASiC-E file is also available? 🙏 ","2026-01-20T09:05:16.777Z"],["3822704","WFM-10050","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, agents have all the necessary roles of CS - Safety, kindly add the queues. ","2026-01-20T09:05:21.119Z"],["3822709","DBRE-8705","DBRE",null,"Slack","This conversation thread has been automatically unsynced from the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1768517045100809|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBRX6L8M/p1768517045100809|smart-link] because [@Leandro Morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] removed the connected work item unfurl on Slack.\n\nFuture replies will no longer sync or update across Slack and Jira.","2026-01-20T09:05:58.180Z"],["3822711","HS-28690","HS","getter.tammeri@bolt.eu","Getter Tammeri","Hi Pedro,\n\nThank you for your patience and reaching out.\n\nI’ve checked up on your vesting in Carta and it seems that there was an issue - i’ve corrected this by now, so please check from your side and confirm before i’ll close this ticket.\n\nKind regards","2026-01-20T09:06:21.387Z"],["3822713","PFI-833286","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Seems like some rounding issues indeed, can we just give 10 cents apologies credits to the Client","2026-01-20T09:06:34.751Z"],["3822714","CNT-348","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","Update: as per our discussion,  the recruitment team is gathering all the facts, after that I’ll take care of the copywriting and request design.","2026-01-20T09:06:49.763Z"],["3822718","PFI-835955","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-20T09:07:00.338Z"],["3822721","PFI-835955","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5cbf158a6fbf5a10040d1d63] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T09:07:02.024Z"],["3822722","DSR-3809","DSR","johannes.varkki@bolt.eu","Johannes Gustav Varkki","Hey [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a]\n\nI changed the user persona in BH and assigned the case in BH to CSPC.\nThis is an Eater request from Zagreb, Croatia.\nAccording to Admin Panel and Bolt website, this is an active market, but for some reason, Beehive thinks it’s an Inactive Market.\n\nThe user has a Privacy question:\n\n* *'What happens with my consents of data sharing after you delete the account?'*\n\nI thought it best to escalate just in case, although I am fairly sure we can just say “the consents will be removed” 😄\n\nPlease confirm how to approach this case. Thank you ☃️\n\n{color:#ff991f}_PS I also talked with Ketter about the issue that inactive market GDPR cases can’t be escalated to CSPC team in Beehive. She will discuss it with Lisanna as well._{color}","2026-01-20T09:07:03.434Z"],["3822724","RDS-1067","RDS","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","Update:\n\nCH: To be launched 1st of Feb 2026, but to be ready from our side this week - already in QA (23rd Jan 2026)\n\nNL: Awaiting input from [~accountid:5b306883ed67e12dd27645e1]  in terms of how we’ll handle the driver and company documents (where there isn’t overlap).","2026-01-20T09:07:24.512Z"],["3822725","LSS-61726","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344536|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344536|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:07:26.491Z"],["3822726","LSS-60746","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] , all open questions have been resolved from my side. So I am leaving the ticket with you, but do let me know in case you have any further questions 🙏 ","2026-01-20T09:07:31.930Z"],["3822727","RDS-1067","RDS","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","Will split this into two for the two markets","2026-01-20T09:07:42.729Z"],["3822728","BB-2284","BB","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Link updated 🙂 [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1-vE_eS-IQ9QCByl3fab1ldwf-LhYeVYwcipzOE7SXtY/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1-vE_eS-IQ9QCByl3fab1ldwf-LhYeVYwcipzOE7SXtY/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link]  \n\n* Row per invoice\n** Column F (*incl. VAT 22% or 24%*) applies to rides with VAT liable drivers\n** Column G (*VAT 0%*) applies to rides with non-VAT liable drivers\n\n\n\nLet me know if any additional questions 🙂 [~accountid:6411726057f0c028e2f4a9b1] ","2026-01-20T09:07:48.702Z"],["3822732","PFI-835362","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Escalated to engineering 🙂 ","2026-01-20T09:08:26.674Z"],["3822734","HS-29120","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2c09d5d-f839-4294-b3c4-98447cbfb8cb], \n\nI am assigning this ticket to you as People Ops doesn’t support time management in Workday. If needed, we can forward this ticket to Workday Tech but maybe you have more insight on why they want to add working hours to August 2025. \n\nIf there is anything that I can support you with regarding this request, let me know. \n\nAll the best, \n\nKerilin ","2026-01-20T09:08:41.374Z"],["3822735","RDS-853","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] right now, we aren’t really using rating chips at all (except internally). Unless a review is flagged for some safety issue, the chips just get added to an endless spreadsheet. It’s a shame. Riders leave feedback — drivers _want_ the feedback — but currently, we don’t close this loop.\n\nIn the future ([soon|https://www.figma.com/design/nEUcpoG7ouxyiApEeaonkz/Driver-Quality?node-id=25602-22597&t=tYLcrLLV8vSdsmIe-1]), we’ll expose these chips to drivers. The idea is to give drivers some idea of why a rider gave a certain rating, and hopefully help the driver improve. This should benefit drivers (higher ratings, more earnings) and the business (more earnings, better supply quality). \n\n!image-20260120-090446.png|width=531,height=432,alt=\"image-20260120-090446.png\"!\n\nIt’s a good idea, and something we should have done years ago, but it has limitations:\n\n* To be very effective, riders must tap on these rating chips. Right now, relatively few riders do. So we need to make this mandatory for ratings <5 like our competitors. Julia has promised to resume discussions on this in ~6 months. \n** This is also important for driver blocks. In many high-risk markets, we cannot block drivers without clear justification, and currently we lack this justification because riders leave low ratings but don’t tap on a chip or leave a comment. As a result, we have millions and millions of these “hollow” ratings that are completely useless to us and to  drivers.\n* Rating chips are still generic. They don’t give specific support or advice. Drivers might be told “cleanliness” is an issue, but it’s not clear if that means the seats are stained, the car has a bad smell, the driver needs a shower, or something else. So the effect of this feedback is limited. For more specific feedback, we need [AI summaries|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A5E8JPG8H/p1768896993435299?thread_ts=1768563254.695659&cid=C0A5E8JPG8H] (which Rishi promised to test in some future phase).\n\nTLDR; rating chips are actually going to be very important in the near future as we’ll finally be surfacing these to drivers. It’s important we refine our list to avoid unnecessary chips, duplicates, or confusing copy.","2026-01-20T09:08:47.335Z"],["3822736","LSS-60691","LSS","dominik.lopuch@bolt.eu","Dominik Lopuch","Hi [~accountid:5f0436f3b545e20015573888] The latest update from yesterday is that due holidays and sickness they did not have this as priority. They should sign it within this week. Thanks","2026-01-20T09:08:52.902Z"],["3822741","PFI-833589","PFI","felicia.oprea@bolt-outsource.eu","Felicia Ștefania Oprea","Hello, \n\nany updates?","2026-01-20T09:09:28.674Z"],["3822743","RDS-419","RDS","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","Update:\n\n* Experiment done, will analyze the two sets of markets with overlapping dates: 15th Dec 2026 - 15th Jan 2026\n* Will check with [~accountid:5e8437c4c8077c0c1f067163] for veritas related metrics/impact","2026-01-20T09:09:45.971Z"],["3822745","LSS-61834","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Support was provided in the main ticket. Process is documented in this policy: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tpEU8RkG8t6w67t_NcnEHTvK5zX4Mst-vRRdSaoftWM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.higxsx47s5ut|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tpEU8RkG8t6w67t_NcnEHTvK5zX4Mst-vRRdSaoftWM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.higxsx47s5ut|smart-link] \n\n+*Summary:*+\n\n* The Rikba category is designed and implemented on the basis of Maltese language proficiency only, not nationality, birthplace, or other protected characteristics, materially reducing discrimination and equal-treatment risk.\n* Eligibility is determined using objective, proportionate verification methods (video assessment, in-person interview, or recognised Maltese A2-level certificate), aligned with the legitimate purpose of improving rider communication and safety.\n* No automated decision-making or profiling is used; eligibility decisions are based on human review of submitted evidence.\n* Personal data processed is strictly limited to what is necessary to verify language proficiency (certificate, short video recording, interview notes, and eligibility outcome).\n* Processing is purpose-limited to onboarding and maintenance of the Rikba category and does not affect a driver’s general access to the Bolt platform or their contractual status.\n* Data storage locations and access are clearly defined (Admin Portal, Beehive tickets, driver profile notes), with access restricted to relevant operational teams.\n* Retention periods are proportionate: videos are deleted one month after validation, certificates and interview notes are retained only for the duration of the driver account or until replaced.\n* Ongoing reassessments are triggered by substantiated complaints or periodic checks and are narrowly scoped to language proficiency.\n* Failure to meet the language standard results only in removal of the Rikba tag, with no automatic sanctions, penalties, or broader account consequences.\n* Driver transparency is handled via CS explanations and escalation of privacy questions to CSPC in line with internal guidance; no standalone or atypical privacy disclaimers are required.\n* Overall, the setup reflects GDPR principles of lawfulness, fairness, data minimisation, purpose limitation, and accountability, and aligns with prior internal and external legal guidance.","2026-01-20T09:10:06.460Z"],["3822746","BIZ-300","BIZ","jake.murphy@bolt.eu","Jake Murphy","Vendor research doc shared with [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] [MVRA-300 Virtual SDRs|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iGkv4rTJlJNzIczyhpoOcVBdqa55P06HOTfTwR8xwN8/edit?usp=sharing] for review and group call to be scheduled to outline any risks / missing information that’s required from each vendor that needs to be suitably answered before moving forward","2026-01-20T09:10:10.990Z"],["3822749","PFI-828500","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThere are no charges on the customer account or any other account that matches this amount and the date provided. After reviewing the bank statement the customer shared, I noticed that there were a reversal of 134 UAH and then a charge of 134 UAH which might be related to an order attempt by the customer that was not completed.  I would suggest the customer checks with their bank why the debit of 134 UAH is stated to have happened on January 2nd while the reversal was made on January 1st.\n\n!Image 20.01.2026 at 11.05.png|width=947,alt=\"Image 20.01.2026 at 11.05.png\"!","2026-01-20T09:10:15.659Z"],["3822751","RDS-263","RDS","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","Update:\n\n* QA to start this week","2026-01-20T09:10:17.676Z"],["3822754","PRF-1860","PRF","opemipo.kehinde@bolt.eu","Opemipo Kehinde","Hey [~accountid:624abfc1f813eb00692c3c5a] please take a look and review these driver ads.","2026-01-20T09:10:42.218Z"],["3822755","DAEN-1301","DAEN","silja.mardla@bolt.eu","Silja Märdla","I am quite sure there’s a hard limit on how far back the fact_rides_search table can be backfilled. \n\nUnfortunately:\n\n* The additional documentation this table has was not linked in the dbt description:\n** [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202086ec9a72d52c498b9eacda73071256c2/pages/5626922397/Core+Fact+Table+fact_rides_search|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202086ec9a72d52c498b9eacda73071256c2/pages/5626922397/Core+Fact+Table+fact_rides_search|smart-link] \n** [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/5631770852/fact_rides_search|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/5631770852/fact_rides_search|smart-link] \n* I did not spot information on this limitation from either document\n\nI do think we probably have that limitation pointed out by Andre somewhere. Try to find it and add to docs. I’m pretty sure it came up with the metrics backfills task you were doing in the autumn. ","2026-01-20T09:10:46.132Z"],["3822756","BZNS-403","BZNS","daria.zaichykova@bolt.eu","Daria Zaichykova","[~accountid:712020:05cbf403-315b-4845-a56c-6718f4ea6dbe] hey Andrea! Any news from the client?","2026-01-20T09:10:50.980Z"],["3822757","RDS-707","RDS","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","Update:\n\n* Technical design to be done by EOW - 23rd Jan 2026","2026-01-20T09:11:06.374Z"],["3822758","HS-28996","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:712020:1a447c27-5947-4ed5-b674-3b465dfa89ac],\n\nPlease check if the currency is now okay. \n\nBest regards,\n\nKerilin ","2026-01-20T09:11:24.981Z"],["3822760","WEBSD-1493","WEBSD","matej.trocil@bolt.eu","Matěj Tročil","*Further context for LT:*\n\nHey, for the LT driver guides, the information in those 6 dropdowns needs to be updated (see screenshot) in both Lithuanian and English.\nThe content in the dropdowns should be replaced with the descriptions provided in the [Google Doc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VcK1NY0NCgk5R6QEi2rIALy8wpJoY9qCg5Z_Tkj_65o/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.q43609j8tljq], so please replace all existing information with the updated text.\nAdditionally, some dropdown titles need to be corrected, as they were previously translated incorrectly. For example, instead of “Pagrindinė kategorija (Vilniuje)“, it should be “„Basic” kategorija (Vilniuje)“, all these titles are visible in the [Google Doc|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VcK1NY0NCgk5R6QEi2rIALy8wpJoY9qCg5Z_Tkj_65o/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.q43609j8tljq] as well.\n\n!image-20260120-091117.png|width=830,height=559,alt=\"image-20260120-091117.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-20T09:11:27.752Z"],["3822761","TAX2-564","TAX2","fernando.souzademan@bolt.eu","Fernando Souza de Man","[~accountid:61419ea149f7bd0068a78d7c] Thanks a lot for the quick reply! Ok, so these improvements have no impact on the tax to be charged on the trip or expansion of Bolt Send to new markets, so I’ll close the tax ticket for this quarter.","2026-01-20T09:11:38.115Z"],["3822762","LSS-61603","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# Draft ODPC response created - [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sS5WKPyXJzzUGmw0Bd3HxmYKVrOeqqy4s9znSNBzxuo/edit?usp=sharing]. It includes a few internal comments from my side to explain the position. To be reviewed by [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \n# DSAR response was finalised from [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] 's side yesterday - to be reviewed by [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] by tomorrow.","2026-01-20T09:11:46.693Z"],["3822763","PFI-834137","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, provide links to invoices","2026-01-20T09:11:57.830Z"],["3822764","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0459EFQ8HJ/p1768339842889929|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0459EFQ8HJ/p1768339842889929|smart-link]","2026-01-20T09:12:06.231Z"],["3822765","RCE-369","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768900326172349]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-369 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:12:16.993Z"],["3822766","BIZ-300","BIZ","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","[~accountid:712020:c28ac319-83e4-4d10-926a-3e90f309e781] thank you!","2026-01-20T09:12:19.941Z"],["3822767","RDS-1318","RDS","afolashakin.ajayi@bolt.eu","Afolashakin Ajayi","Update:\n\n* We’ll prepare a test plan but QA to be done by authentication team","2026-01-20T09:12:29.144Z"],["3822769","WD-22576","WD","lilian.gounden@bolt.eu","Lil Gounden","Access granted, [~accountid:608fb3be0b80a60069c7f299] please approve in WD","2026-01-20T09:12:47.184Z"],["3822771","LSS-59448","LSS","emmanuel.lewis@bolt.eu","Emmanuel Lewis","Hi [~accountid:712020:1f24ce2a-c2f5-4736-ace6-da143abb0cc0],\n\nHappy New Year. I spoke with the potential partner over december and they filled out what they can on the portal. Additionally, they have sent me some additional supporting docs. \n\nPlease let me know if there is anything else outstanding. \n\n\n[^TiAuto Investments CoR39 - Nov 24 (95b59225-ae4e-4310-894d-9024daae0427).pdf]\n[^BIO Confirmation Letter - 4072414974.pdf]\n\n ","2026-01-20T09:13:10.558Z"],["3822773","BZNS-403","BZNS","andrea.attard@bolt.eu","Andrea Attard","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] Not yet - we’re currently chasing the client for an answer and will revert back asap","2026-01-20T09:13:18.988Z"],["3822774","PAW-15004","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-20T09:13:21.177Z"],["3822778","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","Ahh, ok, so it's a known issue. Thanks [@leandro.morgado|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5f5b4e070e396800690aa153] :bowing:\nAny immediate actions from our side?","2026-01-20T09:15:04.094Z"],["3822779","DSR-3811","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hey CSPC,\n\n# Account deletion: has the account been deleted? Can this be confirmed?\nAccounts _can_ be deleted even if HB. Our systems now retain the necessary data.\n# We do not need to send a _detailed_ response on the questions he raises: all information is in our Privacy Notice. The law does not require Controllers to do “individual disclosures” to each data subject - this is what the Privacy Notice is for (/) \nWe can send this kind of wording nonetheless:\n\n{quote}Certain limited data may be retained after account deletion strictly for the purposes set out below, in line with Article 6(1)(c) and 6(1)(f) GDPR:\n\n* *Accounting and tax data*, retained for up to 10 years after the last trip, where required by law\n* *Payment, invoicing and earnings records*, for statutory and audit obligations\n* *Records related to disputes, complaints, fraud prevention or legal claims*, retained only for as long as necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims\n* *Regulatory and compliance records*, where retention is required by transport, licensing or other applicable laws\n\nFor information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Policy at [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|smart-link]  , which includes further information about:\n\n* The categories of personal data we process;\n* The purposes for which we process personal data;\n* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;\n* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;\n* The sources of personal data received from other parties;\n* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and\n* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.{quote}","2026-01-20T09:15:08.232Z"],["3822783","WDFT-3558","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","!image-20260120-091345.png|width=1122,alt=\"image-20260120-091345.png\"!","2026-01-20T09:15:25.004Z"],["3822784","LSS-61801","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] - assigning to you as its not privacy specific, however, not really sure if you are the correct POC. This seems to be fraud related.","2026-01-20T09:15:39.958Z"],["3822788","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","we need to upgrade tidb version to fix it… don’t know of any other workaround","2026-01-20T09:15:58.894Z"],["3822789","WD-22604","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:712020:b74f63f5-ad06-4cbd-9b20-0574e4b815d3], location is reactivated","2026-01-20T09:15:58.938Z"],["3822790","PFI-835932","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued;\n\nThanks for the perfect description of the ticket and providing all the info :)","2026-01-20T09:16:00.371Z"],["3822791","CCM-22292","CCM","alzbeta.zdrazilova@bolt-outsource.eu","Alžběta Zdražilová","!cashback.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T09:16:03.449Z"],["3822792","PFI-806899","PFI","alexandra.pakkonen@bolt.eu","Alexandra Pakkonen","Thank you for an answer, will do.","2026-01-20T09:16:05.260Z"],["3822796","LSS-57900","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Update - followed up with engineers but no progress so far clarifying if any further data is available for new device logins.","2026-01-20T09:16:27.376Z"],["3822798","PAW-13367","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-local-setup, pint-product-local-development-experience, pint-capability-devx\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-20T09:16:44.041Z"],["3822800","PAW-14998","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17226\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-20 09:16:51 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-20T09:16:52.084Z"],["3822801","PAW-14997","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sage386\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/ui-platform-commons/pull/1386\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-20 09:16:59 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-20T09:16:59.585Z"],["3822803","LSS-61616","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Hi [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \n\nThanks for flagging this to our teams and for the context from the discussions with the Brussels Public Prosecutor. \n\nBelow is the initial input to support the approach plan due by end of January.\n\n*1. Scope of data that can be extracted and lawfully disclosed*\n[+Section 3 of Bolt’s Privacy Notice+|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-for-riders-micromobility/?category=micromobility] sets out the full categories of personal data processed in relation to micromobility users (including user account data, ride data, location data, and related operational data).\n\nWhere a *valid and specific legal request* is received in the context of a criminal investigation, and subject to the applicable legal basis, necessity, and proportionality assessment, Bolt can technically extract and disclose relevant data falling within those categories.\n\nImportantly, whether specific data can be disclosed is assessed case by case, and depends on:\n\n* the legal basis invoked;\n* the scope of the request; and\n* the necessity and proportionality of the requested data in relation to the investigation.\n\n# *Data formats*\n\nBolt can currently provide data to law-enforcement authorities in the following formats:\n\n* *.csv* or *.xlsx* for structured/tabular data; and\n* *.jpeg* for images, where applicable.\n\n# *Legal, operational, and technical constraints / prerequisites*\n\nBolt is required under the GDPR and applicable national laws to assess each request before disclosure. In practice, to enable smooth and efficient cooperation and reduce back-and-forth, Bolt expects that requests include:\n\n* a *clear legal basis* obliging or permitting disclosure;\n* a *defined scope*, limited to data necessary for the investigation;\n* an explanation of *how and why* the requested data is relevant to the case.\n\nRequests that are overly broad, insufficiently reasoned, or lacking a clear legal basis may require clarification before data can be disclosed.\n\n*4. Response timelines*\n\n* *Standard requests:* Bolt aims to respond within up to 6 days, depending on complexity and scope.\n* *Urgent requests:* These are prioritised and handled faster (up to 2 days). Precise timelines depend on the nature of the request.\n\nAuthorities can contact Bolt via [a web form|https://bolt.eu/en-lt/privacy/] or email address [+belgium@bolt.eu+|mailto:belgium@bolt.eu]+.+\n\n# *Existing documentation on data sharing*\n\nAs discussed previously, Bolt maintains internal guidance confirming *which legal bases are appropriate* for sharing data with law-enforcement authorities. However, Bolt does *not* maintain a static list of “data that can” or “cannot” be shared. This is deliberate: data disclosure depends on the legal basis, the authority involved, and a proportionality and necessity assessment in each individual case.\n\n*6. October 2024 homicide reference*\nWe located a total of 8 cases from the Public Prosecutor’s Office (either directly or submitted by the Police) in relation to micromobility. The requests all had an official letterhead attachment to make the request and official email domains were used when contacting Bolt. Only one of the requests cited a legal basis, however, CS processed the remaining requests without a legal basis citation due to the exception we have for the Crown Prosecutor to handle these requests as court orders. CS didn’t push back on any of these requests and supported the requestor with several follow-ups as well after initial data was shared.\n\nThe only ticket found with some issues is this one: [+https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/665594322+|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/665594322]. This was an accident report to us, rather than a request for data. CS initially mixed up the request with another one and told the requestor that we’ve already responded. This was fixed the next day and we proceeded with handling the request.\n\n*7. Real-time data sharing during an active ride*\nBolt does *not* provide real-time or continuous access to user or ride data (e.g. via API) to law-enforcement authorities.\nProviding real-time data for all or multiple users on a preventive basis would constitute a *high-risk and likely unlawful disclosure* under EU data protection law, absent a strict legal obligation or licence condition explicitly requiring it.\n\nOur position is that improving *processes, prioritisation, and responsiveness to urgent requests* is a significantly lower-risk and more compliant approach than real-time data sharing.\n\n*8. Centralised overview of Brussels police requests*\nThis is the [+folder+|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/19js5cmZQ9caCm0n5VOl_TXehmXyb_yHH] for all LERs, including Belgium.","2026-01-20T09:17:40.963Z"],["3822805","PFI-835963","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T09:17:59.634Z"],["3822808","DSR-3855","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Rejecting-Wrongly created ","2026-01-20T09:18:14.865Z"],["3822809","PFI-824929","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","{color:#172B4D}Classification: PUBLIC{color}\n   \n\n *From:* Viktoriia GAVRUTENKO <viktoriia.gavrutenko@raiffeisen.ua>  *On Behalf Of*  Rb ACQ RBUA","2026-01-20T09:18:20.715Z"],["3822814","SREC-375","SREC","johannes.kadak@bolt.eu","Johannes Kadak","yep. We use an aws config generator i made that uses engcloudsec as the role","2026-01-20T09:19:06.336Z"],["3822817","PFI-833666","PFI","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Hi again! We still need help here, as (per mentioned in the original message), the proof of payout has already been sent. However, their bank confirmed the sum was not received and the issue is on our end. Can you please look into it further?","2026-01-20T09:19:22.514Z"],["3822820","PFI-822324","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo,\nUnfortunately, we are unable to personalize invoices / invoice templates.\nIf it helps, they may be able to provide a receipt along with the ride invoices, including the drop-off location and license number.","2026-01-20T09:19:50.318Z"],["3822823","WAVE-229","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","+ debug production issue, why latest sentry SDK fails on Android 9","2026-01-20T09:19:58.763Z"],["3822827","SAI-1421","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","!image-20260120-092044.png|width=1286,alt=\"image-20260120-092044.png\"!","2026-01-20T09:20:48.971Z"],["3822829","RDS-177","RDS","jesper.larsen@bolt.eu","Jesper Larsen","[~accountid:712020:d2a0e53f-83a4-4e81-aebd-74db6f57d6fa] Still does not work for me.","2026-01-20T09:21:01.854Z"],["3822830","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] , [~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a] , did you get a chance to review this, please? \n\n[~accountid:624d3e6a45ece00069cdb4e5]  reached out expressing the urgency on this. \n\n\n\n!image-20260120-092057.png|width=918,alt=\"image-20260120-092057.png\"!\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] [~accountid:6239acc09b54ec0068b01a82] ","2026-01-20T09:21:04.576Z"],["3822832","FPD-1408","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Changes have been added to the PR, and have been tested - working as expected ([latest run|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/511904542580533/runs/350312563770951?focus_task=backtesting_consolidate_accuracy&o=2472566184436351]). \nA re-review of the PR has been requested, once it’s approved it’s ready to be merged.","2026-01-20T09:21:50.995Z"],["3822834","CMO-12980","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Add cashback to onboarding.\n\nSeparate Beehive Compensation guide from Compensation in onboarding.","2026-01-20T09:22:16.059Z"],["3822836","WD-22619","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","!image-20260120-092223.png|width=918,alt=\"image-20260120-092223.png\"!","2026-01-20T09:22:26.798Z"],["3822837","WEB-8885","WEB","madli.kaevats@bolt.eu","Madli Kaevats","Hi [~accountid:712020:9c84799a-9aa0-422a-aefb-ff948aabb245] Thanks a lot! The page is looking great! \n\nI’ll share the design for stakeholder review. \n\ncc: [~accountid:712020:f0f7cc2d-5968-45e9-91ec-ea445d725066] ","2026-01-20T09:22:29.312Z"],["3822839","LSS-61793","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ","2026-01-20T09:23:11.898Z"],["3822844","LSS-61533","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Aligned [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] . Created - [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRV-1075|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PRV-1075|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:23:50.325Z"],["3822845","CRC-2178","CRC","shubashini.chandran@bolt.eu","Shuba Chandran","[update]\n\n+*Payments Expansion Update*+\n\n*Customer Payments*\n\n* Network International to be ready Mid March. Still in progress between PO<>NI.\n* Existing [+Checkout.com+|http://checkout.com/] connectivity as backup- it is ready.\n\n*Partner Payments*\n\n* Partner has granted us with UAA access.\n* Testings in progress.\n\nReply","2026-01-20T09:24:03.901Z"],["3822846","PFI-828532","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe were able to find two payments but with the information provided, we can’t say for sure which payment exactly matches the description provided as the first 8 digits of the cards are different. Could you advise the user to provide a bank statement of the transaction, clearly showing the bank name, the date and amount of the charge and if possible the Bolt descriptor [BOLT.EU/X/XXXXXXXXXX|http://BOLT.EU/X/XXXXXXXXXX]? \nHere are the two payments in questions but they might not even be related the real unknown charge.\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3895928163|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3895928163]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3854742577|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3854742577]","2026-01-20T09:24:06.857Z"],["3822848","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768901041328889]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@horia.enache>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3674] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:24:15.061Z"],["3822850","CCM-22292","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey [~accountid:712020:5c171d0c-5baf-4f26-a1e9-b29ef4566bb9]  👋 \n\nYou have both been assigned. 🙂 \n\nBest,\nIrena","2026-01-20T09:24:29.372Z"],["3822851","PFI-828553","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-20T09:24:42.056Z"],["3822852","HS-28911","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hejka, \n\nit’s ready to be collected on my desk. \n\n35th floor, HQ functions, desk 21, nearest to 2.12 meeting room\n\nThanks! \nEwa","2026-01-20T09:24:46.370Z"],["3822855","IOTTEAM-323","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Worked after placing 10K load on the output","2026-01-20T09:25:13.538Z"],["3822859","BP-13457","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on prelive\n\nexclamation icon added (/) \n\n!IMG_0181.PNG|width=362,alt=\"IMG_0181.PNG\"!","2026-01-20T09:25:58.093Z"],["3822860","LSS-60553","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:7ebf1982-dd36-43fb-a386-42b4b1ee6b59] ! As far as I can see there is a valid Mahmoud’s signature in the document attached.\n\nThanks !","2026-01-20T09:26:15.376Z"],["3822862","HS-29165","HS","leila.bahi@bolt.eu","Leila Bahi","!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.23.13.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T09:26:26.734Z"],["3822863","WD-22550","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:62b1977ddcafd965c5ddc33e] ! \n\nI haven got request to create Asset roll forward for 2026. Did I miss something? \n\nand regarding customer invoices - I thought you are handling iy within this ticket.  Correct me if I am wrong, please ","2026-01-20T09:26:29.320Z"],["3822867","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768901206639029]*{color}:\nhey <@U08NZ5XB81G> please use <#C0576CT9MQD|> for these kinds of requests, and separately i think there are Data team contacts supporting Ops?\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:27:28.976Z"],["3822869","BDB-1526","BDB","britt.peet@bolt.eu","Bo Britt Peet","[~accountid:61e52cc538041c00683ed5db] Thank you so much! Will share with teams today.","2026-01-20T09:27:44.387Z"],["3822870","LSS-61460","LSS","joshua.okeleke@bolt.eu","Josh Okeleke","Hey Tom,\n\nI think we're all set on this so you can close the ticket.\n\nThanks again!","2026-01-20T09:28:21.376Z"],["3822871","LSS-56128","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ! I will share the .asice container version shortly","2026-01-20T09:28:30.600Z"],["3822872","PFI-828562","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-20T09:28:35.211Z"],["3822873","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768901308199909]*{color}:\nHi <@U088G9S0Y1H>\n1. We are sending *N0531372A* as a NIF intermediary (not *N0531327A* as stated in your message - this is probably a typo).\n2. The second part (*MARIEM* in your case) is filled in on the Fomento side. We are not sending the *MARIEM* or *BOLT OPERATIONS ÖU* strings.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:28:41.776Z"],["3822875","LSS-60112","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[~accountid:5fa01e19aea468006a8a298e] - Please confirm if standard electronic signature (SpotDraft) works for you?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-20T09:29:10.626Z"],["3822876","PFI-835756","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-20T09:29:24.843Z"],["3822878","WD-22615","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] , \n\nremoving Activity from the Spend Category: Rounding when coming from the invoices in Telema, is this something we can do with the integration? \n","2026-01-20T09:29:44.110Z"],["3822879","WFM-10021","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:a5d31f60-e8a7-4ce6-9f91-7af48161add4]\r\nexcept for karolina.buicenkaite who appears to have karolina.buicen only in Admin - shows inactive\r\nIf you need to reactivate karolina.buicenkaite, please raise an onboarding ticket to IT.","2026-01-20T09:29:48.657Z"],["3822880","FPD-1505","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","PR is approved and I have tested if model training works with the changes (it does - [latest run|https://bolt-incentives.cloud.databricks.com/jobs/38567054453691/runs/489250615663579?o=2472566184436351])\nHowever, even after some testing regarding properly applying adjustments to partner metrics, I’m not confident on pushing these major changes yet. I think it’s good if we can have a specific integration test that verifies if adjustments work as expected to guarantee nothing will break - I’ll take some time later this week to look into this.","2026-01-20T09:30:00.755Z"],["3822881","ROPSC-495","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Suspend drivers that have not done any trips in 2025. These drivers are not eligible for the audit. \n\nRun these drivers via pipeline that declines all their documents, triggering “Block if missing”\n\n[Data of inactive drivers|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1E2TKOddmVgU_0o8bMdb5PLT9yWIKQ9OP9ARzna8fu-8/edit?gid=833371137#gid=833371137]. ","2026-01-20T09:30:01.391Z"],["3822884","LSS-61694","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] ! Yes, I am prioritizing it","2026-01-20T09:30:41.210Z"],["3822888","WFM-10035","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:d68d8892-e046-430d-b677-2436ad1bdae7]","2026-01-20T09:31:36.596Z"],["3822889","LSS-61515","LSS","elisabetta.furfarojerusalmy@bolt.eu","Elisabetta Furfaro Jerusalmy","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] \n\nAs discussed, I’d suggest highlighting to Maria the *significant legal risk* linked to Bolt directly *taking on or paying the fuel deposit* on behalf of drivers.\n\nEven if framed as a pilot, this structure (Bolt as guarantor or financial backer) could be interpreted as *Bolt absorbing a driver’s business expense*, which may:\n\n* Reinforce the perception of a subordination relationship, and\n* Be used to support *reclassification claims* by arguing that Bolt is assuming employer-like responsibilities.\n\nI think we should clearly highlight to Maria that paying instead of drivers the deposit could *materially increase our exposure*.\nIn practice, this could raise reclassification litigation risk *by c. +20–30 percentage points*, *in addition to* creating a *direct financial exposure for Bolt*, since we would ultimately have to absorb the cost in cases of driver non‑payment.\n\nh4. 1. Proposed Alternative: “Fuel Boost Promo – Zero-Deposit Trial”\n\nTo help the business move forward in a legally safer way, we recommend reframing the offer as follows:\n\n* *Total remains the contractual counterparty* – drivers sign directly, Bolt is not involved in the contract or in covering the deposit.\n* *Each month*, Bolt randomly selects *100 Platinum drivers* (or other category) who are eligible for a *30-day “no deposit” fuel card trial*.\n* This is framed as a *limited-time marketing incentive*, not an operational subsidy or standard benefit.\n* The *cost of deposit waivers* could be absorbed by Wex as a commercial promo (in exchange for visibility), or offset by *co-branding, newsletter mentions, or app banners* — *but not by direct financial coverage from Bolt*.\n\nThis keeps Bolt out of the financial chain, reduces risk, and still allows us to test the appeal of fuel incentives among top-tier drivers.\n\nCould you please check with Maria if she sees this as a feasible structure? Ultimately, it’s a Business decision whether to move forward or not — but we should be very clear that the *risk level increases sharply* if we go down the path of funding or guaranteeing driver costs.\n\nThanks,\n\nElisabetta ","2026-01-20T09:31:40.303Z"],["3822893","PFI-817354","PFI","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Hi! Can you please assist here?","2026-01-20T09:32:28.749Z"],["3822895","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Horia Enache [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768901556587229]*{color}:\nthanks <@U09D62DKH9P>, will ask on the above channel.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:32:50.296Z"],["3822896","PAW-15009","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-20T09:32:51.076Z"],["3822900","PFI-830479","PFI","carla.panaite@bolt.eu","Carla Panaite","Thank you! Will you raise this further or do we have to reach out to another department?🙏 ","2026-01-20T09:33:08.940Z"],["3822901","LSS-61730","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344555|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/344555|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:33:23.761Z"],["3822902","LSS-55520","LSS","birgit.tohvrel@bolt.eu","Birgit Tohvrel","Hi [~accountid:5f0ea3c39d9a1200294cef2c], \n\nWith Disainiosakond everything is finalised, so this ticket can be closed. We still have a pending topic with Studio Argus. ","2026-01-20T09:33:28.146Z"],["3822904","LSS-56128","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774], please find this version attached.\n\n [^Vastus Dad Solutions OÜ seisukohtadele (Bolt)(5123103.2).docx (2).asice] ","2026-01-20T09:33:39.411Z"],["3822905","WD-22615","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","# I will confirm with our integration team if it’s possible to do.\n# Change is implemented for the new invoices, older invoices will still stay with the trio mentioned in the screenshot. ","2026-01-20T09:33:41.628Z"],["3822906","LSS-58949","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Thanks a lot [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] \n\nI agree we can accept the wording.","2026-01-20T09:33:43.078Z"],["3822907","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768901617185229]*{color}:\n<@U091U37QE73>, are those fields coming from the company profile?\nJust so the local team could validate it on their own?\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:33:50.323Z"],["3822911","PFI-828591","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThere was no new payment in that amount on the user’s account. I would suggest the user checks with their bank why they are receiving a notification for an old transaction that was completed months ago. The error in the payment logs is not a payment error but the payment is too old for the logs to be fetched.","2026-01-20T09:34:21.068Z"],["3822912","WFM-10025","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","Rides - Vehicle applications' processing rejected as it is internal role. Ops Outsource Private is already assigned to agents","2026-01-20T09:34:23.237Z"],["3822915","DBRE-8731","DBRE","shubham.singh@bolt.eu","Shubham Singh","OKi Noted","2026-01-20T09:34:51.417Z"],["3822917","WD-22571","WD","tauno.tagel@bolt.eu","Tauno Tagel","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] & [~accountid:5e5cecb04befbd0c96cab72a] \n\nIf I’m honest then I don’t fully understand the technical details of your conversation 😄 For example I have no idea how difficult it is to build a new data audit report with different primary BO. That said I just wanted to scout what’s the feasibility of making my request a reality? I’m having a call today with Grace and would be nice to have some kind of status update for her.\n\n\n\nThanks!","2026-01-20T09:35:06.757Z"],["3822919","LSS-61788","LSS","tatsiana.sivukha@bolt.eu","Tatsiana Sivukha","Hi [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] \n\n\n\nPlease review this agreement with Zendesk. The review is needed by the end of this week.","2026-01-20T09:35:27.489Z"],["3822922","WFM-10025","WFM","malgorzata.kolosinska@bolt.eu","Małgorzata Kołosińska","Rides - Vehicle applications' processing rejected as not relevant for the role. rest is approved","2026-01-20T09:35:57.550Z"],["3822924","MM-948","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|The issue lacks detailed requirements, edge cases, and acceptance criteria. Only a brief idea is provided.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The description is somewhat understandable but could be clearer and more structured.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to supporting documentation or references are provided.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is present in the issue.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add functional/non-functional requirements and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the description and break it into sections.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-20T09:36:02.240Z"],["3822929","RDS-1304","RDS","anton.grunichev@bolt.eu","Anton Grunichev","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] affected ~0.8% of users, app hang is when UI got frozen for 1-4 seconds. 4 seconds is an extreme and happens at 10% out of this 0.8%","2026-01-20T09:36:47.822Z"],["3822934","PFI-835966","PFI","daniels.kulcihins@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniels Kulcihins","[^f374900b-a3c0-4093-889f-2247ee387734.pdf]\n\n[^payment - 2026-01-19T170151.655 (1).pdf]","2026-01-20T09:37:16.324Z"],["3822935","PFI-835966","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T09:37:18.703Z"],["3822940","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] ,\n\n\n\nPlease refer this comment: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22550?focusedCommentId=3812658|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WD-22550?focusedCommentId=3812658|smart-link] \n\n\n!image-20260120-093827.png|width=898,alt=\"image-20260120-093827.png\"!\n\nIts a functional setting that we need your advice on .\n\nPlease let me know.\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-20T09:37:48.248Z"],["3822942","PFI-835362","PFI","kaur.kalmu@bolt.eu","Kaur Kalmu","Period changed to 25.03.2024-31.12.2025","2026-01-20T09:38:02.380Z"],["3822945","CCM-22293","CCM","martyna.zdunek@bolt-outsource.eu","Martyna Zdunek","[^OS - Simply Contact - RO Onboarding (1).xlsx]","2026-01-20T09:38:11.576Z"],["3822946","DLSP-2017","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","finalized the vision","2026-01-20T09:38:37.134Z"],["3822948","FDBT-4822","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-20T09:39:31.823Z"],["3822949","PFI-828605","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n[^Refund_Letter_QBSMFXDWJQTT