[User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-20T09:46:09.313Z"],["3822994","LSS-61836","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T09:46:09.484Z"],["3822995","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* cs-db-4 termination: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15464|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15464|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:46:15.868Z"],["3822998","MM-949","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements are provided. The issue lacks sufficient information for a developer to start.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is clear, but without a description, the scope and details are ambiguous.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting information are present.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate is provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description with requirements and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-20T09:46:31.521Z"],["3823002","LSS-61460","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:49ec724a-806f-42f1-86dc-bf9f93671a23] - just for my own visibility, what were the answers to my questions raised last week? I’m conscious that we never had the call to discuss this (apologies from my side - this was due to an unexpected personal event), so I just want to make sure that all the appropriate points were considered before I close the ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-20T09:47:23.682Z"],["3823003","DBRE-8686","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","W4:\n\n* Jan 20:\n** {{cs-d1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{cs-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{cs-d3.sqldb}}:\n*** default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n*** max_binlog_size=250M → default (1024MiB)\n*** innodb_buffer_pool_load_at_startup=OFF → default (ON)\n** {{cs-db-4.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{eu-db-1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{eu-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{eu-db-3.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n* Jan 21:\n** {{na-backup.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{na-db-1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{na-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{na-db-3.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{na-kafka.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{zaf-backup.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{zaf-db-4.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{zaf-db-5.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{zaf-db-6.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n* Jan 22:\n** {{afr-kafka.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n** {{eu-backup.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=4 (default) → 8\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=4 (default) → 8\n** {{fraud-db-1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{fraud-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{fraud-db-3.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{invoicing-backup.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{invoicing-d1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{invoicing-d2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{nig-kafka.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n** {{ru-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{ru-db-3.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{ru-kafka-1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{ukr-kafka.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n** {{was-db-4.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{was-db-5.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{was-db-6.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{was-kafka.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n** {{weu-kafka.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n** {{zaf-kafka.sqldb}}:\n*** innodb_read_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n*** innodb_write_io_threads=8 → 4 (default)\n** Import User Manager manual change: [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5593|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5593]\n** Update MySQL config template: [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5594|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5594]\n* Jan 23:\n** Update MySQL config template – add exception for DELIVERY collation: [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5598|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5598]\n** Debug Grafana file ownership issue on TiDB monitor nodes:\n*** [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1769062279579789|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1769062279579789|smart-link]\n*** Apply changes from [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5596|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5596] (also Jan 26)\n** Debug TI-BILLING VictoriaMetrics migration leftover issue:\n*** [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1769169128558469|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09T8620KLK/p1769169128558469|smart-link]\n*** Review and apply changes from [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5599|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5599] (also Jan 26)\n** Fix Ansible client access to secrets: [https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15522|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/15522]\n** {{central-backup.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{central-db-1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{central-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{central-db-3.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{central-kafka.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{user-backup.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{user-db-1.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{user-db-2.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n** {{user-db-3.sqldb}}: default-character-set=utf8 → utf8mb4\n\nW5:\n\n* Jan 26:\n** Apply changes from\n*** [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5596|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5596]\n*** [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5598|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5598]\n*** [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5599|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5599]\n** Add MySQL {{max_digest_length}}, {{performance_schema_max_digest_length}} and {{performance_schema_max_sql_text_length}} configuration to Ansible:\n*** [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5607|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5607]\n*** Previously managed manually: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1745403415685299?thread_ts=1745402064.316609&cid=CNKLBL33P|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNKLBL33P/p1745403415685299?thread_ts=1745402064.316609&cid=CNKLBL33P|smart-link] \n* Jan 28:\n** Fix hostname on\n*** {{dm-live-dm_master-1.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-1-225}})\n*** {{dm-live-dn_master-2.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-4-141}})\n*** {{dm-order-history-dm_master-1.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-1-46}})\n*** {{dm-order-history-dm_master-2.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-5-20}})\n*** {{dm-order-history-dm_master-3.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-9-49}})\n*** {{dm-order-history-dm_worker-1.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-1-192}})\n*** {{dm-order-history-dm_worker-2.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-5-19}})\n*** {{dm-order-history-dm_worker-3.sqldb}} (was {{ip-172-30-8-158}})","2026-01-20T09:47:29.614Z"],["3823005","PFI-833341","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Invoice sum (sum of invoice rows) don’t include the debt, but includes the amount of services provided. The Balance Box is just a snapshot at the point of invoice issuance; and we can’t reissue it. Please, advise company to view the up-to-date Balance in the Portal.","2026-01-20T09:47:58.597Z"],["3823006","DRX-28020","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Tested the ticket on DI.128.0 (195367345) on iOS 26.2\n\nVerified that App is no more displaying the “Add dashcam” button to the user when there is no vehicle present for the driver\n\nAttaching the screenshot for reference:\n\n!IMG_1028 2.PNG|width=645,alt=\"IMG_1028 2.PNG\"!\n\n\n\nFixed","2026-01-20T09:48:12.096Z"],["3823008","LSS-57822","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Thanks a lot for the answers [~accountid:712020:9cfda827-f644-48a1-9da8-aff3fd427bf9] – this is super helpful.\n\n\n\nI am wondering if you have explored the set up with engineers on the possibilities. I agree that any changes made by fleets on Courier accounts should somehow be confirmed by the Courier. Have you explored the possibility of making any changes to Courier account by Fleet conditional upon Courier acceptance. E.g. that Courier would receive a notification / email that there is a change and get an option to accept / decline?\n\n\n\nThe reason why I’m proposing this instead of selfie verification is that it’ll be difficult to justify the selfie check to be proportionate to the goal. If we think about the point of the selfie check, it’s meant to answer: “Is this the same person?” A profile change confirmation is rather meant to answer “Does this courier agree to this change?”.\n\n\n\nThe goal of this initiative would be that Couriers would be aware and agree to changes made on their accounts. Even for fraud prevention purposes, selfie checks should only be triggered when there’s a strong risk signal. For instance, new device logs in after detail change. Or that there were multiple changes in short amount of time. Such selfie checks would be defensible as proportionate before the regulator.\n\n\n\nTo combat fleet changes on Courier account, I’d propose to come up with some default flow that whenever fleet tries to change email or phone number or name, Courier would receive a notification to accept / decline. This way we could prevent silent account transfers and we’d have minimal friction over necessity of selfie check.\n\n\n\nPlease let me know if I’m misinterpreting something. Happy to discuss further.","2026-01-20T09:48:18.191Z"],["3823009","DRX-28020","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Ticket is tested by [~accountId:628dd714269a9a0068f2a783].","2026-01-20T09:48:31.160Z"],["3823014","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768902528515689]*{color}:\nNo, there is nothing similar to *MARIEM* in company profiles or in the driver profiles.\nFrom company profiles we are sending the reg numbers (the top fields from screens - B87573408 and 61144062B), they are presented correctly.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:49:01.100Z"],["3823015","LSS-56938","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \nI went through the [DSA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/125o395bpmCwcIyETink5Eb72-twZ0SvE/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=116489701835779910985&rtpof=true&sd=true] and overall, it looks solid and broadly aligned with our usual controller-to-controller setup: roles are clearly independent, the data scope is limited, and most of the operational obligations sit with Vodacom as the data importer (purpose limitation, security, DSAR handling, retention, breach notification). The international transfer piece is also covered via SCCs with an Estonian law/regulator anchor.\n\nThe main point I want to flag is the *indemnity*. As currently drafted, Clause 20 reads as a *mutual indemnity*. From what I understand, our usual position in a setup like this is that where Bolt exports the data and the counterparty controls the downstream use and security, the counterparty should stand behind its own downstream data protection failures via a one-way indemnity. Making the indemnity mutual doesn’t really add protection for Bolt (we’re already responsible for our own compliance anyway), but it does increase Bolt’s contractual exposure. Because of that, this feels less like a drafting point and more like a conscious risk decision we should align on.\n\nEverything else in the DSA looks broadly fine to me; this is the only point that seems to materially affect risk allocation.","2026-01-20T09:49:01.334Z"],["3823016","HS-29170","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Confirming with manager the end date ","2026-01-20T09:49:02.119Z"],["3823018","PFI-833277","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued first two invoices; the last one has been refunded in full.","2026-01-20T09:49:35.118Z"],["3823019","CEBF-1701","CEBF","pradeep.yadav@bolt.eu","Pradeep Kumar Yadav","[~accountid:712020:c573470a-712d-474e-a9e6-b0635a9decb9] Please introduce “Type”(picklist on Account Plan Objective) for reporting purpose.\n\nEach Account Plan Objective we create will also populate Type.\n\nLike : \n\n* Target GMV\n* *Target Active Locations* - Yearly\n* *Target Active Locations* - Monthly\n* Target Orders\n* Target AOV\n* % Incentives expected from Partner\n* % Incentives funded by Bolt\n\nMore picklist values will be added in later tickets.\n\nAlso introduce separate picklist to hold Months.","2026-01-20T09:49:39.389Z"],["3823021","SREDESK-7436","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","You should have access to PyPI now. The changes might take a few minutes to propagate however. Let me know if you have any issues.","2026-01-20T09:49:48.768Z"],["3823023","PFI-833241","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","reissued","2026-01-20T09:50:03.627Z"],["3823024","PFI-833653","PFI","reinis.levanovics@bolt.eu","Reinis Levanovičs","As this case keeps going on with Authority, and they are talking about to sue if we don’t provide document with statement were its seen when we received amount and reference token number for ApplePay.  Adding information that we have talked in DM’s, in case if needed for future. \n\nMarten Martinson\n\n  10:21 AM 20.01.2026\n\nHi @reinis.levanovics\n\nI have also checked with ProcessOut and here is some additional information available for us.\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3909863173|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3909863173]\n\nBIN: 43572306\n\nLast 4: 3656\n\nExpiry: 10/2031\n\nCard ID: card_yNxtkLWg1A0doVqUgmCuaG3AC0oIfybj\n\nToken ID: tok_Ct2yRYMYHbTdzsnZdM5K5Rg07m3uBTl1\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3865912139|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3865912139]\n\nBIN: 43572306\n\nLast 4: 1890\n\nExpiry: 10/2031\n\nCard ID: card_dTJJCv82lfildJhTtD0salXDVWQeFjMb\n\nToken ID: tok_CmhGFZQZH22tfbWXzsD1h83sAQ7RO24I\n\nI'm afraid we are not able to provide the bank statement where it shows the payment was received by Bolt. Technically we could provide the daily reports of the transactions received, but these would include amount 250k payments each. \n\n\n*Reinis Levanovičs*  [10:25 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D0AAKM4GGJC/p1768897523122159] 20.01.2026\n\n\nyeah i think he is thinking from the usually company perspective, that company has bank account and we could get bank statement for one payment as PDF document   but i had additional question, in our bank account does the reference\n\n[+BOLT.EU/O/2512031052+|http://bolt.eu/O/2512031052] is this the same as in clients bank account?\n\n*Marten Martinson*  [10:33 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D0AAKM4GGJC/p1768898009642979] 20.01.2026\n\n\nWe don't have a bank account with our payment orchestrator (ProcessOut) or with the payment gateway (CheckOut).\nThey process our payments with the acquirer.\nWe get a report of how many payments were processed. So it's not like a traditional bank statement. Once the payments are processed the funds are sent to our Citi bank account as one payment a day.The reference or the payment descriptors is created by Bolt are included in the payment metadata. This would be available in the reports. However, the authorities will not be able to find any additional information when checking the payment report compared to specific payment data. \n\n*Reinis Levanovičs*  [11:32 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D0AAKM4GGJC/p1768901545191109] 20.01.2026\n\n\nso sorry to write again, but they are saying that in case if we don't provide that document they are going to ask trough court from our bank those statements as in most legal way, but as i understood they can do that, but still i can inform that they will probably get the same answer, right, as we can't provide such document, just wanted to double check\n\n*Marten Martinson*  [11:41 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D0AAKM4GGJC/p1768902085050499] 20.01.2026\n\n\nHey! The tone for this message should be that we want to co-operate with the authorities. If you feel uncertain about the request then I would suggest to open a ticket with the legal/compliance team. You can do it from [+here+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47].\nWe are not able to provide a bank statement where it shows where we received the customers funds. That document they are asking does not exist. \n*Marten Martinson*  [11:44 AM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D0AAKM4GGJC/p1768902277965039] 20.01.2026\n\n\nJust to be sure I checked with ChatGPT about the authorities request.Short answer: *No, you cannot directly identify or extract the user’s underlying card details from an Apple Pay transaction.* However, *limited, indirect payment information is available* and can be used for lawful investigations.\nWhat payment information _is_ available to Bolt / PSPs\nFor an Apple Pay transaction, you can typically access:\n\n* Network token (DAN / DPAN)\n* Card scheme (Visa or Mastercard)\n* Card country\n* Issuer bank (token BIN, not real BIN)\n* Transaction date, amount, merchant details\n* Authorization code\n* ARN (Acquirer Reference Number)\n\nThis data *can identify the transaction*, but *not the person*.What is *not* available\nYou cannot directly obtain:\n\n* Real PAN (card number)\n* Cardholder name\n* Billing address\n* Apple ID or device owner identity\n* Wallet account details\n\nApple deliberately prevents this to preserve user privacy.What authorities can do instead (lawful path)\nIf authorities need to identify the user:\n\n# *Start with Bolt’s transaction records*\n\n\nProvide ARN, timestamps, amounts, tokenized card details\n\n# *Escalate via the card network*\n\n\nVisa / Mastercard can resolve the token → issuing bank\n\n# *Issuing bank identifies the cardholder*\n\n\nOnly the issuer can map the token to a real customer\n\n# *Apple involvement (if required)*\n\n\nApple only responds to *formal legal requests*\nEven then, disclosure is minimal and tightly scoped\nBolt itself *cannot deanonymize* the user from Apple Pay data alone.","2026-01-20T09:50:05.719Z"],["3823026","PFI-835979","PFI","tochi.adimachukwu@bolt-outsource.eu","Tochi Adimachukwu","!{61B5ECCB-41C3-49AA-A4D4-9B02DB898FBB}-20260120-094937.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T09:50:17.127Z"],["3823027","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768902626890549]*{color}:\nI meant the NIF\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:50:40.516Z"],["3823028","LSS-61837","LSS","emmanuel.lewis@bolt.eu","Emmanuel Lewis","[^Bolt x Dekra, Annex_Controller-controller DSA Template (AVAILABLE TO LRP) (1).docx] _(647 kB)_\n\n[^Bolt x Dekra, Partnership Proposal.docx] _(19 kB)_","2026-01-20T09:50:49.492Z"],["3823030","LSS-57383","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi [~accountid:712020:f63df97f-cad1-4718-9bb1-80038488d7e2] following up on how we are handling Drivers complaints {color:#bf2600}*in CA and NZ*{color} in regard to Airwallex services:\n\nPartner Payment Operations currently do not handle such requests due to the different time zone. Local CA and NZ CS Operations team ([~accountid:5f9197f8606d4000694ceed2] for CA and [~accountid:712020:a5562b19-3d5d-4c4f-a083-01aafd36655b] for NZ) are the ones responsible for raising and tracking on AWX though Zendesk (Airwallex portal). If not through Zendesk tickets, they do via a private slack channel shared with Airwallex: #ext-airwallex-bolt-ops. (see the screenshot as example). \n\ncc [~accountid:616ff0d6702bd0006a685f65] [~accountid:712020:1a99e337-a650-4a85-a8ed-f0825a04e850] \n\n\n!image-20260120-093746.png|width=720,alt=\"image-20260120-093746.png\"!\n\nSo, to complement the process describes in Liisa’s comment below, under CA & NZ: Escalate: _within 2 working days after receiving complaint, local CA and NZ (Operations) team must send complaint and all related information to Airwallex though Zendesk (Airwallex portal). If not through Zendesk tickets, they do via a private Slack channel shared with Airwallex: #ext-airwallex-bolt-ops._\n\n[~accountid:712020:a5562b19-3d5d-4c4f-a083-01aafd36655b] and [~accountid:5f9197f8606d4000694ceed2] please let me know if anything of the above is not correct. Thank you. ","2026-01-20T09:51:08.914Z"],["3823031","CCM-22293","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Martyna,\n\nThe agents have been enrolled in the requested onboarding course. \n\nHave a lovely rest of your day.\n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-20T09:51:09.994Z"],["3823032","LSS-61694","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","thanks, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] !!","2026-01-20T09:51:23.848Z"],["3823033","LSS-61688","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Ticket made for audit trail and personal tracking. Responding in the linked ticket.","2026-01-20T09:51:33.865Z"],["3823034","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768902692655099]*{color}:\nWhere is it taken from?\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:51:45.797Z"],["3823035","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768902694351479]*{color}:\nNIF is coming from config as is\n{code}nifOwner: formattedDriverVatNumber as tString,\nnifIntermediary: this.config.bolt_spain_nif as tString,{code}\n\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:51:46.392Z"],["3823036","PFI-828609","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThis is the payment made on the account [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3999259678|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3999259678]. But for some reasons, it was split in two distinct transactions. Kindly advise the user to check with their bank why the payment was split in two. The other 670 CZK transaction proof is a reversal which is the preauthorisation amount reversed on this same payment.","2026-01-20T09:52:07.753Z"],["3823037","PFI-833606","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","reissued","2026-01-20T09:52:08.539Z"],["3823038","LSS-61788","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048] fyi most likely we are not able to make any changes. I already asked Procurement to ask from Zendesk if we can amend some items. Currently waiting for the reply. But it’s an important tool for CS, so even if we can not make any changes we should still highlight the risks.  ","2026-01-20T09:52:11.043Z"],["3823039","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768902723578599]*{color}:\nif config\n{code}        bolt_spain_nif: \"N0531372A\",{code}\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:52:16.566Z"],["3823040","RDS-82","RDS","seidon.pereira@bolt.eu","Seidon Alexis Pereira","List of potential cities for test: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1iuhp3eikmTOdVqajIwKahYhvAui8rQoBCZKY4wvlPUg/edit?gid=2010615086#gid=2010615086|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1iuhp3eikmTOdVqajIwKahYhvAui8rQoBCZKY4wvlPUg/edit?gid=2010615086#gid=2010615086|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:52:18.668Z"],["3823041","LSS-61838","LSS","giulio.delbalzo@bolt.eu","Giulio del Balzo di Caprigliano","[^HF E-bikes Agreement 19.01.26.docx] _(145 kB)_","2026-01-20T09:52:26.632Z"],["3823044","LSS-61837","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nEmmanuel Lewis has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-20T09:52:31.686Z"],["3823046","RDS-877","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] FYI: I added Prio. Feel free to adjust it.","2026-01-20T09:52:35.068Z"],["3823047","LSS-61545","LSS","ewoma.jerryogeme@bolt.eu","Ewoma Jerry-Ogeme","Hello,\n\nPlease what is the status of execution of the document. Thank you","2026-01-20T09:52:35.423Z"],["3823049","PFI-833782","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Can you, please, provide examples of Rides","2026-01-20T09:52:53.498Z"],["3823052","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768902812802389]*{color}:\ncheck with your data teams first, they shouldbe able to support you with reporting? this needs just help in looker vs engineering\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:53:46.344Z"],["3823054","PFI-828642","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nFor cases where refund was issued but can’t be seen on the user’s card or Bolt balance.\n\n* Check where the refund was sent to and if it was successful on the [transaction history page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-balance/trxHistory?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A%2225%22%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22target_account_id%22%3A%2265766018%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] with the correct user ID \n** If Bolt balance refund is successful, there is a green button after the refund “🟢 success”\n** If refund to card, 💳 success\n* Check if the payment method used to make the order is not a business account. In this case, the refund will be sent to the business account balance.\n* Check if the user did not spend their refund on a next order (or orders) for Bolt balance refunds\n* Check if the user did not have a previous debt or previous failed payment that was covered up with the refund\n* If refund was sent to Balance instead of card, check first if payment was made from card. Usually, if card payment fails, card refund also fails. Sometimes refund will be sent to balance in cases payment was charged from balance first as debt and the refund will clear the debt previously created by the balance charge. \n* Check [payment page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/1946767063], to ensure there are no errors on the refund and advise the user to check with their bank if card refund was successfully completed.\n** If there is an error, escalate to Commerce > Ride Hailing/Food/Rentals payments\n* Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.\n{color:#bf2600}For issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.{color}\n\n","2026-01-20T09:54:06.889Z"],["3823055","DPO-148","DPO","quinn.feller@bolt.eu","Quinn Darby Feller","* -Azerbaijani - AZ 🇦🇿-\n* -Bulgarian - BG 🇧🇬-\n* -Czech - CZ 🇨🇿-\n* -English - GH 🇬🇭-\n* -English - KE 🇰🇪-\n* -English - MT 🇲🇹-\n* -Estonian - ET 🇪🇪-\n* -Georgian - KA 🇬🇪-\n* -Greek - EL 🇨🇾-\n* -Latvian - LV 🇱🇻-\n* -Lithuanian - LT 🇱🇹-\n* -Polish - PL 🇵🇱-\n* -Portuguese - PT 🇵🇹-\n* -Romanian - RO 🇷🇴-\n* -Russian - RU 🇷🇺-\n* -Slovak - SK 🇸🇰-\n* -Ukrainian - UK 🇺🇦-","2026-01-20T09:54:21.715Z"],["3823056","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Horia Enache [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768902854119249]*{color}:\nok, will discuss also with data teams\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:54:26.490Z"],["3823058","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Horia Enache [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768902856478129]*{color}:\nmany thanks\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:54:30.224Z"],["3823059","PFI-830905","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please find the invoices reissued.\n\nCommission invoices: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"created_from\"%3A1768863600%2C\"created_to\"%3A1768950000%2C\"system_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing\"%2C\"to_agent_id\"%3A6218100%2C\"to_agent_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing_driver\"}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22created_from%22%3A1768863600%2C%22created_to%22%3A1768950000%2C%22system_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing%22%2C%22to_agent_id%22%3A6218100%2C%22to_agent_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing_driver%22%7D%7D]\n\nRide invoices: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"created_from\"%3A1768863600%2C\"created_to\"%3A1768950000%2C\"system_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing\"%2C\"from_agent_id\"%3A6218100%2C\"from_agent_type\"%3A\"ride_hailing_driver\"}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22created_from%22%3A1768863600%2C%22created_to%22%3A1768950000%2C%22system_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing%22%2C%22from_agent_id%22%3A6218100%2C%22from_agent_type%22%3A%22ride_hailing_driver%22%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\n\n\nLet me know if you have any concerns or questions. Thanks! ","2026-01-20T09:54:33.126Z"],["3823060","FX-3674","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768902866748409]*{color}:\n:pray:\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:54:41.529Z"],["3823061","WFM-10048","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","[~accountid:712020:fb3cc377-463c-41f0-8730-d66abe2f0af0]","2026-01-20T09:54:55.670Z"],["3823066","CAMLE-9827","CAMLE","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","created design doc [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7404912815/Draft+Design+Doc+-+Dynamic+holdout+labels|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7404912815/Draft+Design+Doc+-+Dynamic+holdout+labels|smart-link]  and broke down scope for the tickets aswell","2026-01-20T09:55:36.962Z"],["3823067","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768902959859549]*{color}:\n&gt; formattedDriverVatNumber\nThat's what I'm after: do we really send the *driver's VAT*, or is that variable set to the *company's VAT* (since the driver's fleet has company-based invoicing)?\n{quote}","2026-01-20T09:56:12.387Z"],["3823069","PFI-828651","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T09:56:34.233Z"],["3823070","PAW-15003","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/s3-configless/pull/450\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-20 09:56:35 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-20T09:56:36.045Z"],["3823073","PFI-828654","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T09:57:09.826Z"],["3823078","PFI-834722","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, this appears to be a legitimate user with a good payment history. Please refund the failed payment amount from this [order|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2557041179/261?orderTryId=3431813641] ( EUR 10.50, Refund actor: Bolt ) to bring the balance back to zero. The rule shouldn’t trigger after this.\nThank you!","2026-01-20T09:57:42.678Z"],["3823082","PFI-828655","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T09:57:51.710Z"],["3823086","DRX-28258","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: according to the ticket","2026-01-20T09:58:36.141Z"],["3823087","PAR-137","PAR","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","CAMT.53 mapping is now needed only in EUR: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3731|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAR-3731|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T09:58:39.791Z"],["3823089","LSS-61085","LSS","daniel.severin@bolt.eu","Daniel Severin","Thanks all. From my side, no further insurance input is required.\n\nI am comfortable that the contract and structure are appropriate for the Private Driver / Driver-only category in Ukraine, as outlined previously, and I do not see any insurance-related blockers to proceeding.\n\nThe only remaining points are operational rather than insurance-specific, namely ensuring that compliance with mandatory MTPL is appropriately addressed through the agreed frameworks (e.g. user representations, controls, and ownership within Ops/Product), and that reporting and premium settlement processes are managed as intended.\n\nSubject to that, I I do not think any further actions from my side.\n\nHappy to support separately if questions come up around reporting, claims handling, or invoicing once live.","2026-01-20T09:59:00.320Z"],["3823090","SREDESK-7420","SREDESK","wisutta.maensittirote@bolt.eu","Wisutta Maensittirote","Thank you. [~accountid:712020:782f9535-5dfc-41e5-8bdf-057eef89f6ef] Will this be available soon? As we need to publish a blog by tomorrow. Thanks,","2026-01-20T09:59:01.690Z"],["3823091","PFI-835981","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T09:59:03.159Z"],["3823095","LSS-58345","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] - I have addressed your comment in the document ✅ ","2026-01-20T09:59:46.739Z"],["3823097","WD-22620","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Access granted","2026-01-20T10:00:15.292Z"],["3823098","HS-29026","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-20T10:00:22.239Z"],["3823103","RDS-851","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] Thanks for the context! Just to be clear: I agree that this is a real problem. The question is: what is the best way to solve it? I am not sure if labels are the best way, although I am open to verifying the perspective, if we find the right solution. Still, I would likely change the ticket name to be more solution-agnostic.","2026-01-20T10:00:35.851Z"],["3823104","LSS-61758","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a729743a-fea5-401d-a417-a7025bd4ee5a] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Urban Drive Co-Invest + Kick-Back - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.pdf] ","2026-01-20T10:00:46.430Z"],["3823105","HS-28208","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","needs term decision","2026-01-20T10:00:46.656Z"],["3823106","LSS-61838","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T10:01:35.179Z"],["3823107","LSS-61839","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T10:01:35.226Z"],["3823108","LSS-61837","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T10:01:35.232Z"],["3823109","LSS-61840","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T10:01:35.743Z"],["3823111","PFI-835287","PFI","sofija.danilevica@bolt.eu","Sofija Daņileviča","Updated! New report is available [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eXNZ1ITJKgJMxYn1zHC6-CkVsT35qZy6/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=100545192984689800467&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eXNZ1ITJKgJMxYn1zHC6-CkVsT35qZy6/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=100545192984689800467&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] \n\nFor future requests driver names should be filled in.\n\nBut let me know if any issues!","2026-01-20T10:02:19.385Z"],["3823113","PFI-835986","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T10:02:39.740Z"],["3823114","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768903296418549]*{color}:\nformattedDriverVatNumber is the cleaned *company vat code*\n{code}    private formatDriverVatNumber(vatNumber: string): string | null {\n        // Driver VAT number is expected to have numbers and letters only.\n        const invalidCharactersRegex = /[^0-9a-zA-Z]/g;\n        const normalizedVatNumber = vatNumber.replace(invalidCharactersRegex, \"\");\n\n        return normalizedVatNumber.length === NIF_LENGTH ? normalizedVatNumber : null;\n    }{code}\n\n{quote}","2026-01-20T10:02:48.474Z"],["3823115","RCE-367","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Alisher Matkurbanov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768903356807439]*{color}:\nin these cases - B87573408 and 61144062B\n{quote}","2026-01-20T10:03:08.099Z"],["3823117","LSS-61545","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:63b59fb7d3aeefa40543d2e5] ! It is pending with the Counterparty’s signature\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.03.25.png|width=642,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.03.25.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:03:40.474Z"],["3823118","RF-64","RF","siddhant.saxena@bolt.eu","Siddhant Saxena","I confirmed the exact column mapping on a call with Androus, I will do the reconciliation to see the numbers when I get some time.\n\nImp Note : Androus strongly emphasized that the numbers will never match 100%. At best we should expect 90%.\n\nHe wasn’t in favor of attributing the rest of the cost to all orders fearing it would dilute/bias the actual order level payments. If attribution has to be done, he asked it to be done on our side.","2026-01-20T10:03:48.849Z"],["3823119","LSS-61545","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343322?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/343322?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T10:03:54.537Z"],["3823120","PFI-828663","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nTaking into account the date of the payment and the Bolt descriptor, this is the payment [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4001935525|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4001935525]. This charge must be some extra fees charged by the user’s bank due to the payment being processed by an international acquirer. Kindly advise the user to confirm with their bank.","2026-01-20T10:03:56.712Z"],["3823122","DPM-2115","DPM","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","Closing this ticket. Any new issues appearing will go under [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2212|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DPM-2212|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T10:04:07.056Z"],["3823124","RDXENG-4748","RDXENG","anastasiya.sviatokha@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Sviatokha","Hey *@user-U03J5UATREU*!\n\n[TECH-149000|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/TECH-149000]: CI.216.0: Report from me stating:\n\n{quote}Bottom sheet stuck in loading state after selecting a pickup & dropoff far from my location as a scheduled ride & clicking the “Cancel Scheduled Ride” button to get to the regular ride screen.{quote}\n\nVery niche case, but issue was only resolved once I changed locations, this is happening because the location does not have scheduled rides available & the route isn't allowed as per [this report|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02L9EMP4TE/p1767008549631069], this is consistently reproducible, perhaps the user should be routed back to the screen where they can update pickup after clicking \"Cancel Scheduled Ride\" button to avoid this(?) :big_think:\n\nAdditionally curiously, if you reselect the same route again after manually going to pickup location then a different error is shown (Bolt is not yet available here), example video attached. :eyes:\n\n*STR:*\n• Click \"Schedule\" tile in a city where scheduled rides are available.\n• Select a route that normally isn't allowed (like {{Chloerzyn 556}} to {{Krakon John Paul II Airport (KRK)}}\n• You'll receive an error message that SR is unavailable in this area, click \"Cancel Scheduled Ride\"","2026-01-20T10:04:44.286Z"],["3823125","RDXENG-4748","RDXENG",null,"Slack","[Anastasiya Sviatokha|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d036d01618d7b0bcdf10340] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767343179182259?thread_ts=1767343179.182259&cid=CSFF3R571|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767343179182259?thread_ts=1767343179.182259&cid=CSFF3R571|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-20T10:04:45.299Z"],["3823126","RDXENG-4748","RDXENG","germo.rikk@bolt.eu","Germo Rikk","Hey [@juri.noga|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/625fb496efc8a5006a5557e5] - did you find anything?\n\nIf not [@anastasiya.sviatokha|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d036d01618d7b0bcdf10340] - could you ptal? :prayge:","2026-01-20T10:04:45.780Z"],["3823127","RDXENG-4748","RDXENG",null,"Slack","[Anastasiya Sviatokha|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d036d01618d7b0bcdf10340] unsynced this conversation thread from the Slack thread - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767343179182259|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF3R571/p1767343179182259|smart-link]. Future replies will no longer sync or update across Slack and Jira.","2026-01-20T10:04:53.618Z"],["3823129","WFM-10053","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Country access request : [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601732|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601732]","2026-01-20T10:04:59.344Z"],["3823130","MM-925","MM","david.schryer@bolt.eu","David Schryer","The other task is in our sprint and linked to this.","2026-01-20T10:05:05.857Z"],["3823132","PFI-828692","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-20T10:05:15.886Z"],["3823133","LSS-60939","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] ! The Vincent’s signature has been collected. I am sending the document to Lithuania to collect Benas’.","2026-01-20T10:05:22.171Z"],["3823135","LSS-59365","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:07f1e332-abd8-45eb-a3b9-0dd3708ef2d7] There were none. 🙂 Thank you!","2026-01-20T10:05:54.072Z"],["3823136","DO-5817","DO","maciej.opala@bolt.eu","Maciej Opała","Hi Kristo.\n\nI’ve removed the problematic tables and data according to the error message and started a sync - need to wait to see whether it was effective.","2026-01-20T10:05:57.829Z"],["3823137","LSS-61108","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hei, [~accountid:712020:10daa261-d587-4bee-926d-af5c022abc8e] ! The signature has been collected, I will share the tracking number ASAP.","2026-01-20T10:06:00.976Z"],["3823140","L10N-28859","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28858](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28858)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T10:06:39.832Z"],["3823141","L10N-28861","L10N",null,"Aut