picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28858](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28858)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T10:06:57.093Z"],["3823152","L10N-28884","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-28858](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-28858)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-20T10:06:57.127Z"],["3823154","WD-22621","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:c8f6d6ec-ae4a-4cf3-9078-0632b32a5d28] !\n\nRight now back account details look like this. Should account number and name on Account remain the same? Shouldn’t they change together with IBAN? \n\n!image-20260120-100609.png|width=401,alt=\"image-20260120-100609.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:08:01.299Z"],["3823156","LSS-61694","LSS","marcin.klimkiewicz@bolt.eu","Marcin Klimkiewicz","Thank you 🙂 ","2026-01-20T10:08:35.641Z"],["3823157","PFI-828698","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T10:08:42.176Z"],["3823159","FX-3675","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768903428194899]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@boris.yartsev>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3675] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T10:09:06.200Z"],["3823160","PFI-835990","PFI","bisola.ajayi@bolt-outsource.eu","Bisola Ajayi","[^0ec590cd-156a-48f9-8c97-e65ce4a4ecf7.pdf]","2026-01-20T10:09:11.973Z"],["3823161","PFI-828432","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nCould you advise the user to provide a bank statement showing the debited amount, date and time of the payment, the first 8 and last 4 digits of the debited card and if possible the Bolt descriptor [BOLT.EU/X/XXXXXXXXXX|http://bolt.eu/X/XXXXXXXXXX]? This information will help us locate the unknown transaction.","2026-01-20T10:09:25.838Z"],["3823163","LSS-61460","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","*UPDATE:*\n\n* *Q from Josh* ([Link|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A9AM8ESGP/p1768838966934159]): “_I just want to quickly confirm if Privacy have any preferences on how platform data is shared e.g. sheets, data rooms, API etc. Finmid suggested data room_ [+_DocSend_+|https://www.docsend.com/]_._”\n* *Thoughts*: Provided the medium is secure, then we are ok with it. Ask InfoSec to check if they have previously risk assessed this method, or if they have any preferences.","2026-01-20T10:09:35.472Z"],["3823165","DBRE-7144","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","Work completed for now (list of possible improvements is in the confluence doc)","2026-01-20T10:10:08.173Z"],["3823166","LSS-53138","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:712020:853cbe25-4d18-40c3-8211-69c3936bf72f] Did we get this signed? ","2026-01-20T10:10:11.575Z"],["3823167","RLONE-779","RLONE","renzo.lopez@bolt.eu","Renzo Lopez","[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VVhlh_xOTGlbMZ07hoLvpdrkWchkP_aFcK2f1tKC_V4/edit?gid=2108539543#gid=2108539543|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1VVhlh_xOTGlbMZ07hoLvpdrkWchkP_aFcK2f1tKC_V4/edit?gid=2108539543#gid=2108539543]","2026-01-20T10:10:12.074Z"],["3823168","RLONE-779","RLONE","renzo.lopez@bolt.eu","Renzo Lopez","[~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] done","2026-01-20T10:10:46.329Z"],["3823169","LSS-61108","LSS","lucian.andrei@bolt.eu","Lucian Andrei","Thank you [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]!","2026-01-20T10:10:55.036Z"],["3823173","WD-22590","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","Hello [~accountid:62ea2a72da8620d53392aa71] companies are now removed from Region 5 and added to Region 2","2026-01-20T10:11:30.889Z"],["3823175","DSR-2471","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Re-opening as the deadline to complete DSAR with Slack messages was extended to {{2026-01-29}}.","2026-01-20T10:11:45.723Z"],["3823177","LSS-60074","LSS","sarra.eddahiri@bolt.eu","Sarra Eddahiri","Hi [~accountid:6233300873c8ec00699dc8b6] , could you share what problem you’re trying to solve with a panic button? We currently have the Emergency Assist feature, which already functions as a panic button.","2026-01-20T10:12:57.463Z"],["3823178","LSS-60939","LSS","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","Thanks for the update, [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]!","2026-01-20T10:13:31.796Z"],["3823179","PFI-835993","PFI","erik.semet@bolt-outsource.eu","Erik Šemet","!image-20260120-101201.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T10:13:56.863Z"],["3823180","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] ,\n\nare you sure about it (month of feb we can udate)? because, I think we use the calendar year as the lifespan of our sequence generators, so it would be Jan 2027 next, as the documentation says if I am not wrong it only updates once the lifespan finished?\n\n!image-20260120-101217.png|width=918,alt=\"image-20260120-101217.png\"!\n\n \n\n\n\nIf you think its not the case and next month it will reflect, then we just wait till feb, is there anything we can do to change it earlier?\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-20T10:14:02.898Z"],["3823182","LSS-58768","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e],\n\nThank you for relaying this. Since the file is in PDF format, its difficult to comment or add updates directly. Here are my notes:\n\n*Clause 4.4* - :green: Aligned with the existing wording.\n\n*Clause 6.3* - :yellow_circle: CoachHub’s reply confirms that a reduction in security measures is a real possibility, and it does not agree to remove this wording. To find a pragmatic solution, we suggest accepting this possibility under certain conditions. We propose adding the following:\n\n{quote}_In the event that CoachHub intends to implement an update that would result in a material decrease in the overall protection of Customer Personal Data, CoachHub shall notify Customer in writing at least sixty (60) days in advance of the intended change._\n\n_Any such material decrease shall be subject to Customer’s prior written agreement. If Customer does not agree to the proposed update, Customer shall have the right to terminate the Agreement (or the affected services) with immediate effect, and CoachHub shall refund any prepaid fees on a pro-rata basis for the unused portion of the services._\n\n_This termination right shall apply notwithstanding any contrary termination provisions in the Agreement._{quote}\n\n*Clause 15* - :green: I understand from the comment that CouachHub accepted the proposed higher liability cap by Bolt. We are aligned on this point.","2026-01-20T10:14:24.727Z"],["3823185","FINDATA-4178","FINDATA","ismayil.aghahasanli@bolt.eu","Ismayil Aghahasanli","Update:\n\nAll the mappings moved except -[https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1nWyOvJTQUbCxIRQ0hicrqba5EYtIRM3LOrkIRVZ7B74/edit#gid=0-payment_provider_fees--access|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1nWyOvJTQUbCxIRQ0hicrqba5EYtIRM3LOrkIRVZ7B74/edit#gid=0-payment_provider_fees--access|smart-link]  access denied\n\n(payment_provider_fees).- Finance DWH does not maintain this file\n\n\n\nFivetran access was given based on service account and per file.\n\n\n\n----\n\nMost of the files have been moved to below folder and connected tested.\n\nSome mappings are in Internal - Commerce drive --[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mj7JzxzdithCZYgG_JxtZCGLsVwzVxBE|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mj7JzxzdithCZYgG_JxtZCGLsVwzVxBE|smart-link] \n\nNeed to have temporary manager access to move them to below folder. Asked Dmitri. M to help.\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1uWQ6bC8ozFW3rDE_jmzZDJLm5PxPryaX|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1uWQ6bC8ozFW3rDE_jmzZDJLm5PxPryaX|smart-card]\n\n ","2026-01-20T10:15:51.934Z"],["3823186","WD-22550","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","I updated my lasy message , It can be changed only in Jan 2027.\n\nI think I will make WD case, maybe they can help somehow. what do you think? ","2026-01-20T10:15:52.280Z"],["3823187","LSS-59208","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Update:*\n\n# CoachHub shared the updated DPA - [^Partly clean_CoachHub Data Processing Agreement (Bolt Privacy Team Review 22.12.2025)_CH2026_01_15.pdf] \n# Privacy’s feedback is as follows:\n\n*Clause 4.4* - :green: Aligned with the existing wording.\n\n*Clause 6.3* - :yellow_circle: CoachHub’s reply confirms that a reduction in security measures is a real possibility, and it does not agree to remove this wording. To find a pragmatic solution, we suggest accepting this possibility under certain conditions. We propose adding the following:\n\n{quote}_In the event that CoachHub intends to implement an update that would result in a material decrease in the overall protection of Customer Personal Data, CoachHub shall notify Customer in writing at least sixty (60) days in advance of the intended change._\n\n_Any such material decrease shall be subject to Customer’s prior written agreement. If Customer does not agree to the proposed update, Customer shall have the right to terminate the Agreement (or the affected services) with immediate effect, and CoachHub shall refund any prepaid fees on a pro-rata basis for the unused portion of the services._\n\n_This termination right shall apply notwithstanding any contrary termination provisions in the Agreement._{quote}\n\n*Clause 15* - :green: I understand from the comment that CouachHub accepted the proposed higher liability cap by Bolt. We are aligned on this point.","2026-01-20T10:16:41.022Z"],["3823188","WEB-9914","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","On recent testing, the banner seems stable both during and after deployments.\nWill keep the task open for further observation but if this is not noticed anymore, we can close it after a while","2026-01-20T10:17:03.857Z"],["3823190","SAI-1422","SAI","grzegorz.broton@bolt.eu","Grzegorz Brotoń","!image-20260120-101704.png|width=612,alt=\"image-20260120-101704.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:17:07.546Z"],["3823191","RCE-368","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1768904215271319]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-368 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T10:17:09.490Z"],["3823194","RDS-951","RDS","andreas.palm@bolt.eu","Andreas Palm","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] When we picked up Account Tab 2.0 the profile pic improvement had been descoped/unlinked from AT2.0. Which kinda makes sense because as I understand it’s been one of the longest running topics within Rides and has had some pushback from Identity historically.\n\nOn another note, I would love to improve the whole experience sometime in the future, also the option to upload images from gallery etc, but can’t give anything concrete as of now given other priorities.","2026-01-20T10:17:56.895Z"],["3823195","DELIVERY-1077","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","26W4: Ready for release. Will be part of the 1.103","2026-01-20T10:18:32.399Z"],["3823196","LSS-60939","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","To what I see, Benas if flying to Tallinn next week for GM summit; if you sending it by post - he could  sign it in HQ?\n\n","2026-01-20T10:18:39.028Z"],["3823197","WD-22605","WD","laura.cedazo@bolt.eu","Laura Cedazo","!Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.04.21.png|width=1926,height=1002,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-19 at 13.04.21.png\"!\n\nHi Magnus,\n\nIt seems that from [~accountid:6273c82ed7fd480068d97e5f] side, everything was filled and looked like this, see attachment, so maybe the error must be other? Well lets see now once she sent it to me again.\n\n\n\nThanks\n\n\n\n","2026-01-20T10:18:49.647Z"],["3823198","LSS-46781","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","*Attached:* further Slack message sent to Daniel Severin, chasing for an update.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.18.22 AM.png|width=989,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 10.18.22 AM.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:18:54.433Z"],["3823201","LSS-61843","LSS","aivo.toots@bolt.eu","Aivo Toots","Adding the contract from last year. We are still working on the audit programme document.\n\n[^Consultation services agreement_Bolt Technology_SecTeam_1604.2025.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T10:19:17.679Z"],["3823202","HS-29168","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nThe reference letter will be forwarded to your personal email on your last day (31.01.2026).\n\nKind regards,\n\nKadri","2026-01-20T10:19:22.105Z"],["3823204","WD-22604","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","location inactivated effective from 20.01.2026","2026-01-20T10:19:34.610Z"],["3823206","DELIVERY-1422","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","Should we start an employee test? cc: [~accountid:712020:82be5457-bc4f-4060-a784-a0e5cfa9744d] ","2026-01-20T10:19:55.512Z"],["3823207","WEB-9923","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] could you give [this|https://www.figma.com/design/EA6o5cVzolpDBewnCZ3BOd/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Supply?node-id=2207-60270&t=SVlTrdyBEONv0qkK-1] a quick once over to make sure it aligns with your guidelines? After you give the all clear I’ll develop each section in more detail and expand to cater to country level and city level for each supply funnel.","2026-01-20T10:19:56.801Z"],["3823209","PRF-1860","PRF","r.lonander@bolt.eu","Robin Lönander","For SE 🇸🇪\nNow: “Registrera → dig som Boltförar-partner”\n\nChange to: \n“Registrera dig → som Boltförar-partner” (move the “-->”)\n\n[~accountid:712020:6615e403-65ac-4a5f-8afe-afb4d81cac6c] @jennihalme can you check the assets for NO + FI ?\n[~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] I can not tag Jenni Halme. Can you add her? ","2026-01-20T10:20:07.633Z"],["3823213","WD-22608","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","The problem occured because statutory adjustment book was opened just after this ticket was created. ","2026-01-20T10:20:23.242Z"],["3823214","LSS-60939","LSS","igne.martutaityte@bolt.eu","Ignė Martutaitytė","update: not the next week, but he is flying on the 2nd of Feb\n\n","2026-01-20T10:20:43.514Z"],["3823215","WEB-7729","WEB","elina.heno@bolt.eu","Elina Liina Heno","Hey [~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd] \n\nThe link to the Figma file is [here|https://www.figma.com/design/EA6o5cVzolpDBewnCZ3BOd/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Supply?node-id=2110-25727&t=JKJ1neKdi3IzsX8g-1]\n\nThe link to the prototype is [here|https://www.figma.com/proto/EA6o5cVzolpDBewnCZ3BOd/Bolt-Web-3.0-%E2%80%A2%C2%A0Supply?page-id=1714%3A9121&node-id=2124-20742&viewport=-2872%2C521%2C0.15&t=I1resJTzpLQWRyBr-1&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=2124%3A20742]\n\nThe Drive folder with media is [here|https://drive.google.com/open?id=1QFWQXSZyy-CEFQD7nR56sJMgKGDen9y-&usp=drive_fs]","2026-01-20T10:20:50.087Z"],["3823216","ROPSC-504","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Compliance-related processes reviewed together with local team.\n\nAll processes are aligned with standard global procedures. ","2026-01-20T10:20:52.178Z"],["3823217","LSS-61603","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] \nAs you [asked|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/D095WACR7A8/p1768903108906559], please find:\n1) The ODPC DASR response template [*here*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UD5b1hBKp9gGYQMixLQp6xtfJsNwbRtGFG7kz7Jx8_U/edit?usp=drive_link] \n2) The responsive data for the DSAR [*here*|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/15saksbh5hn7NFchCN2Eb2cChQS6uZxyM?usp=drive_link]\n\nHope it helps 🙂 ","2026-01-20T10:20:58.740Z"],["3823218","WFM-10053","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey, [~accountid:61d593f9e67ea2006bd875f5] \n\nThank you for reaching out!\n\nWe have raised the country request for NL and it is granted, but which verticals agent will support? \n\nLooking forward,","2026-01-20T10:21:06.862Z"],["3823220","RDS-853","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] yep, Uber is giving these badges already…\n\n!image-20260120-102102.png|width=631,height=1110,alt=\"image-20260120-102102.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:21:22.447Z"],["3823221","DELIVERY-1009","DELIVERY","radu.androne@bolt.eu","Radu Androne","26W4\n\n* Defined the retrieval and ingestion flow.\n* Ongoing experimentation on the DS side to assess performance of Redis and Elasticsearch vector DB solutions.\n* Working on the engineering design document.","2026-01-20T10:21:28.448Z"],["3823223","LSS-46781","LSS","sasha.dornan@bolt.eu","Sasha Dornan","Hi [~accountid:62a3287576c0360069f59b72], as mentioned on Slack, we have received a further chaser email from Clyde & Co (attached) regarding the attached invoice.\n\n*Please can you provide an update on settling this invoice which I can then pass on to Clyde & Co?*\n\n[^Bolt Mail - RePayment request - invoice 1110-0391007.pdf]\n[^10726690_1110-0391007_1_2 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T10:21:57.712Z"],["3823226","PRF-1860","PRF","karina.kochanovskaya@bolt.eu","Karina Kochanovskaya","[~accountid:712020:ca818823-efac-45fe-ba7d-a6686a5e08b5] I’m also unable to add Jenni, maybe an access issue","2026-01-20T10:22:14.981Z"],["3823227","LSS-61595","LSS","teresa.yeh@bolt.eu","Teresa Yeh","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] [~accountid:6172754ef485cd006863a3a8] gentle bump!\n\nCould you let me know the expected timeline for this? I need to get back to DBS regarding their query. Appreciate your help!","2026-01-20T10:22:35.788Z"],["3823228","WFM-10055","WFM","tobyas.abithoya@bolt-outsource.eu","Tobyas Abithoya","[^Agents Onboarding.xlsx]","2026-01-20T10:22:57.061Z"],["3823230","DSR-3577","DSR","juan.sanchez@bolt.eu","Juan Martin Sanchez","Hi all,\n\nWe are reviewing this request and will come back to you hopefully soon. \nIn the meantime, could anyone explain where (in which system(s)) the data WD needs access to and which team is the owner of it?\n\n[~accountid:5ac7610ca05a8d1c9884808f] maybe? 🙂 ","2026-01-20T10:23:35.775Z"],["3823231","LSS-60939","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Thanks, [~accountid:61b1d141b0b630006a9698e1] ! I have already bring it to the reception and think it will be dispatched soon. I think we will have a fully executed document by the end of this week than.","2026-01-20T10:23:48.781Z"],["3823233","LSS-61176","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you for sharing [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] - our legal team will review the process and the communications that you have shared. \n\nWe will revert once we have analysed this and confirmed whether we can reactivate a driver or not. \n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] ","2026-01-20T10:23:54.147Z"],["3823234","WFM-10053","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Agent currently has *Beehive CS Agent role,* which is merged Beehive Rides CS Agent & Beehive Delivery CS Agent, therefore granting access permissions to both ride and food users. We need to know what else does [+seger.kuiper@bolt.eu+|mailto:seger.kuiper@bolt.eu] need.","2026-01-20T10:24:33.027Z"],["3823235","LSS-61844","LSS","catalin.jitariu@bolt.eu","Cătălin-Ioan Jitariu","[^Anexa SSM Manpower Staffing_ EN.DOCX] _(160 kB)_\n\n[^Controller-to-Controller - Data Sharing Addendum Manpower Staffing.docx] _(56 kB)_","2026-01-20T10:24:49.389Z"],["3823237","ROPSC-505","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","In general, fleet document sets are aligned with global standards.\n\n\n\nIn CZ, business_entity_transport and bank_account documents are configured as mandatory documents for all drivers, even though only private drivers have to submit these documents. As a result, the compliance rate is low since about 70% of drivers belong to a fleet company and do not need to submit it. ","2026-01-20T10:25:35.994Z"],["3823238","LSS-61802","LSS","marinella.farrugia@bolt.eu","Marinella Farrugia","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] We would appreciate that this is signed by latest today please! 🙏  We are pending installation which needs to go live asap.  Thank you!","2026-01-20T10:25:47.474Z"],["3823239","LSS-61460","LSS","joshua.okeleke@bolt.eu","Josh Okeleke","*Stage 1 Sharing:*\n\n   - Why have we assumed that the data sharing here is “anonymised”? Is\n   this because we are taking specific steps to anonymise the data before we\n   share it, r because of the nature of the data itself?\n   - Are any of the fleets whose information we are sharing here natural\n   persons / sole traders (rather than businesses)?\n   - Is the list of categories of data in Schedule 3 of the agreement\n   (i.e., categories of data being shared as part of Stage 1) complete?\n   - On the understanding that fleets have not yet expressed an interest in\n   any financing options at this stage, are we sharing information about\n   *all* German fleets with the third-party lender, or only certain fleets\n   (if the latter, which ones)?\n\n*Stage 2 Sharing:*\n\n   - Am I correct in understanding that Stage 2 data sharing is not covered\n   in Schedule 3 of the agreement? If so, do we know why not?\n   - How will the fleets be ‘expressing interest’ and ‘consenting’ to data\n   sharing, in practical terms (i.e., what will this look like in practice?\n   Will it be by clicking a link, checking a tickbox, emailing Bolt, or\n   something else)?\n\n*Promoting the Finmid Project:*\n\n   - I see from the agreement that Bolt will be promoting the lender’s\n   financing options to German fleets. Do we know what mediums Bolt will be\n   using to do so? (e.g., will we just be posting this on a general fleet page\n   on the platform, or will we be specifically emailing fleets encouraging\n   them to consider the financing options?)\n\n\nHi Thomas,\n\nNo worries - I hope everything was sorted out!\n\nAnswers:\n\n   -\n*Stage 1: *\n      - Taking steps to anonymise - once the CSP has selected the fleets\n      that fits their internal analysis, we'll get confirmation from\nthe fleet to\n      share their data with the CSP\n      - Yes\n      - No - still in the process, that's what I wanted to clarify with you\n      first before we proceed\n      - Only fleets in specific German cities\n\n\n   - *Stage 2:*\n      - TBD\n      - TBD - it will be based on how we decide to embed finmid. Most\n      likely they'll check a tickbox/link\n\n\n   - *Promoting Finmid:*\n      - All of the above\n\nI've scheduled time later today to close the loop on this. Thanks 🙂\n\nJosh","2026-01-20T10:26:09.745Z"],["3823241","WD-22550","WD","yuvraj.chhikara@bolt.eu","Yuvraj Chhikara","Yes, I think that will help, I don't think Accounting can wait till next year 🧐 \n\n\n\nThank you.\n\n\n\nBest,\n\nYuvi","2026-01-20T10:26:38.924Z"],["3823242","LSS-58949","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Thanks everyone, I will let Cogs know and the agreement should now be ready for signing","2026-01-20T10:27:03.948Z"],["3823243","PFI-835257","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hello Bohdan,\n\nSeems like the user still has a *Hard block* on their profile, meaning that this has not been submitted to the Safety Team for review or that the process is incomplete.\n\nFraud Team does not remove safety *Hard-Blocks* from the profiles, we only help in removing the *device UID blocks* once the investigation has been finalised and the rest of the blocks have been removed.\n\n\nI’ll be closing the ticket now, please let us know once the hard-block has been lifted by pinging me here or creating a new ticket 🙂 ","2026-01-20T10:28:22.859Z"],["3823244","WFM-10042","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:5c75f61c-3531-4b91-8943-2ee3c355f252]!\r\n\r\nRoles requested. Queues will be added as soon as possible.","2026-01-20T10:29:50.368Z"],["3823245","SRED-1042","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","Working fine with already exposed stuff, we have an EPIC to onboard our services to NetBird to provide direct access there.","2026-01-20T10:30:54.959Z"],["3823247","PFI-835965","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-20T10:31:26.778Z"],["3823248","LSS-61844","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T10:31:27.417Z"],["3823249","PFI-835610","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-20T10:31:28.805Z"],["3823250","WEB-9923","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] Looks great, exactly what I was imagining in my head. 😄 I have checked the skeleton and left a few comments with explanations to improve clarity. Thank you very much! \n\nP.S. Please, check also the city-level structure, as well as there will be new sections after “benefits” like:\n\n* Unique city-specific content (let’s start with 5 TOP regions)\n* Local driving or delivery guide (roads, demand, tips)\n\nThanks!","2026-01-20T10:31:30.267Z"],["3823251","PFI-835501","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-20T10:31:31.062Z"],["3823252","PFI-835260","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Done, thanks for letting us know","2026-01-20T10:31:33.294Z"],["3823253","HS-29135","HS","kadri.kivimaa@bolt.eu","Kadri Kivimaa","Hello!\n\nI looked through his contracts and Annexes and he is correct, the start date in Workday was incorrect and has been fixed to his first contractual date with Bolt.\n\nKind regards,\nKadri","2026-01-20T10:32:09.734Z"],["3823260","LSS-61773","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:33:47.332Z"],["3823261","WFM-10042","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello, [~accountid:712020:5c75f61c-3531-4b91-8943-2ee3c355f252]!\r\n\r\nAll changes were applied.\r\n\r\nHave a great day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-20T10:34:23.281Z"],["3823264","LSS-61769","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","Hi [~accountid:712020:176612de-64ab-442f-84ee-ed63bbac2b50] , I recall two previous tickets regarding Box:\n\n#  [LSS-54920: Letter of termination with Box.com|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-54920][*Done*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-54920] . \n# [Renewal with supplier |https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-57505?actionerId=557058%3Af58131cb-b67d-43c7-b30d-6b58d40bd077&sourceType=assign]- We renewed contract till October 31, 2026. Polina Novikova commented last year that “_The plan was to switch the vendor, but we’ve decided to move this to next year, as the team didn’t have enough capacity to handle it this year.“_\n\nJust to be sure we are not terminating this contract or switching vendors, instead we are renewing it, correct? If yes:\n\n* The subscription period in Service Order overlaps with the subscription period of the already signed Service Order (attached), so there is a double-billing risk. Please clarify this and confirm how these two Service Orders should be dealt with to avoid double-billing.\n* New Service Order includes 200,000 Box AI Units per month. Could you please explain what are these?\n\n[^Service Order_Box.com (UK) Ltd._Bolt Operations OÜ_31.10.2025 (1).pdf]\n\nThanks!","2026-01-20T10:34:46.377Z"],["3823265","WD-22605","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:620b9b75878c2f00729892b6] it seems that fields are filled on itemization level:\n\n!image-20260120-103425.png|width=1115,alt=\"image-20260120-103425.png\"!\n\n!image-20260120-103442.png|width=973,alt=\"image-20260120-103442.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:34:51.811Z"],["3823266","LSS-59762","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:35:00.291Z"],["3823267","WD-22616","WD","nataliia.pachkovska@bolt.eu","Nataliia Pachkovska","Hi. In what areas are we using them currently?\n\nSupplier invoices and expense reports? I'm thinking of dependencies. \n\nCan they break something if delete related worktags?","2026-01-20T10:35:04.863Z"],["3823268","LSS-61845","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","[^Bolt orgchart 31.12.24 (1).pdf] _(3.34 MB)_","2026-01-20T10:35:11.759Z"],["3823270","PFI-834910","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe are investigating this issue with the payment service provider and will revert back here once we get an update.","2026-01-20T10:35:30.696Z"],["3823272","LSS-59054","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:35:32.942Z"],["3823273","PFI-834910","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09811Q5N14/p1768905269425179?thread_ts=1768821277.461479&cid=C09811Q5N14|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09811Q5N14/p1768905269425179?thread_ts=1768821277.461479&cid=C09811Q5N14|smart-card]","2026-01-20T10:35:39.406Z"],["3823274","RS-1948","RS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","[~accountid:712020:88708e1d-c334-4279-9692-ef3f2432966b] is correct - we do not employ any of our drivers. We provide intermediary services and enter into contracts with business partners who are responsible for the drivers; hence, these are not employment relationships. Additionally, according to the Beehive messages exchange, the Police are not conducting any investigation; the request is for informational and operational purposes only. In my opinion, we can invoke trade secret protection and do not disclose this information. [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d], please confirm I’m correct and let me know if I should prepare a response.","2026-01-20T10:35:39.751Z"],["3823275","LSS-59351","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:35:50.122Z"],["3823276","LSS-60542","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Thanks for the info [~accountid:633ebe49140ba0bf651e341a] [~accountid:712020:ae4fba9f-a97d-41eb-8fd7-bec2a5bc17d0] .  I will consider and come back to you shortly. ","2026-01-20T10:35:51.594Z"],["3823277","LSS-59052","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:36:08.564Z"],["3823278","ROPSC-507","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Suspend drivers that have not done any trips in 2025 and 2024. These drivers are not eligible for the audit.\n\nRun these drivers via pipeline that declines all their documents, triggering “Block if missing”\n\nAdditionally, document_upload_requested was placed on the profiles due to conditionality on different driver types.\n\n[List of inactive drivers|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SfFw9JD-I34I33_DSUHPnUXhQtaXVIegf_GE9tCQHWU/edit?gid=1382998042#gid=1382998042]","2026-01-20T10:36:34.452Z"],["3823279","LSS-59055","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:36:39.598Z"],["3823280","LSS-61679","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:624196e2f407980070548076], please find the signed contract attached.\n\n[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T10:37:02.598Z"],["3823281","LSS-61677","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:37:13.951Z"],["3823282","LSS-61673","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:38:05.184Z"],["3823284","MLC-303","MLC","suresh.nv@bolt.eu","Suresh NV","Next steps: \n\n* Create master templates based on the new optimizations, and request localizations for the paragraphs that communicate earnings values (currently managed in the CMS tool).\n* Make them live asap as most of the issues have been fixed. \n* Target go live- \n** {{2026-01-27}} - Thailand, Nigeria., \n** {{2026-01-28}} - Estonia, Poland, \n** {{2026-01-29}} - Romania, Azerbaijan, Paraguay. ","2026-01-20T10:38:28.317Z"],["3823285","RDXENG-3087","RDXENG","goutham.perugu@bolt.eu","Goutham Perugu","# It is just a boolean in the Mixpanel event. I tried fetching logs from the user yesterday itself, but it didn’t contain the date when the issue actually happened.\n# So after {{/code/add}}call, {{/code/list/v2}} is made and we are checking if the added code is available in the list or not. Only if it is available, it is marked as selected in local. It is some very old code which is not even migrated to co-routines, so probably no one knows why this logic was added. But what is your suggest? what should be the correct way that should happen for “Add promo code“  flow?","2026-01-20T10:38:34.279Z"],["3823286","LSS-61675","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:38:42.538Z"],["3823287","WD-22616","WD","marko.hulak@bolt.eu","Marko Hulak","Currently I’m using in:\nSuppliers - which goes to supplier invoices\nSpend Category - their ownership\nNewly the expense items from [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] .\n\nTechnically they cannot break anything. Just that all the work we put in defaulting values and setting up the allowed values will disappear. Similar impact like removing a custom validation. ","2026-01-20T10:38:58.994Z"],["3823289","CSDT-976","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","* Notes: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HknFBoL3kYK5l-OzfU7VoeevBlkwCG5MOVlqQmD8zkY/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HknFBoL3kYK5l-OzfU7VoeevBlkwCG5MOVlqQmD8zkY/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n* Diagram: [https://excalidraw.com/|https://excalidraw.com/|smart-link] \n* Notebook: [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832154233?contextId=sql-editor&o=3598988355446810#command/6702239786141398|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/2519319832154233?contextId=sql-editor&o=3598988355446810#command/6702239786141398]\n\n\n\nSteps: \n\n# Check historical data for % of cases that get a repeat contact in 1, 2, 3, 4+ days. Pick one option. \n# Build prototypes for 4 versions of FCR based on the notes and diagram above. Discuss with the team. \n# If aligned, discuss further with Andrei and Andres.","2026-01-20T10:39:21.241Z"],["3823290","LSS-60512","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:712020:33a1a5e8-52cb-4605-9ef3-0b89d57fe7b8] what is the status of this ticket? Did they accept our final agreement? Can we sign it?","2026-01-20T10:39:40.685Z"],["3823291","LSS-61676","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:39:43.460Z"],["3823292","LSS-60553","LSS","wiktoria.lis@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Lis","Sorry! Incorrect file, see the one attached below: \n\n[^Cognizant - template notification and consent PL EN(514274454.1) FINAL (2).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T10:39:52.995Z"],["3823295","LSS-61674","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:40:12.633Z"],["3823296","LSS-61625","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Hi [~accountid:712020:bd27ea39-912c-4d98-9fd7-247ac2e54ec6] ,\n\nYes, please do reach out to the driver to double-check from his side what happened with the package.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-20T10:40:13.109Z"],["3823298","LSS-61670","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:40:34.403Z"],["3823299","PFI-834920","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment was rejected sue to suspected fraud. Could you advise the user to try and use a different payment method or confirm with their bank why the payments are being rejected?","2026-01-20T10:40:35.522Z"],["3823302","BP-13223","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested on Prelive\n\nHopp specific - Canada (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.33.25.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.33.25.png\"!\n\nDifferent Bolt countries checked (sample):\n\nAustria (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.36.54.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.36.54.png\"!\n\nAzerbaijan (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.40.45.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.40.45.png\"!\n\nCroatia (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.47.17.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.47.17.png\"!\n\nGeorgia (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.51.23.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.51.23.png\"!\n\nCyprus (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.55.50.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.55.50.png\"!\n\nCzech (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.58.09.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 11.58.09.png\"!\n\nGhana (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.02.43.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.02.43.png\"!\n\nKenya (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.05.44.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.05.44.png\"!\n\nMexico (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.07.47.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.07.47.png\"!\n\nParaguay (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.12.35.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.12.35.png\"!\n\nSaudi Arabia (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.15.44.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.15.44.png\"!\n\nThailand (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.36.23.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.36.23.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:41:03.505Z"],["3823303","LSS-61672","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] as discussed, looping you in this ticket to investigate. Thank you !","2026-01-20T10:41:01.684Z"],["3823305","PRIV-461","PRIV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Update - result of the review:\n\n\n\n# AMENDMENT NO. 2 TO THE MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT (*allowing the re-use of personal data by Bolt*) - no substantial changes *-* [~accountid:712020:f5c52198-9bb5-40b8-865d-70e96f6ccf5a] *we can sign as agreed previously.*\n\n*Detailed overview - no substantial changes introduced, only cosmetic changes.*\n\nh4. 1. Defined term clean-up: “Master Services Agreement” → “Agreement”\n*Before*\n* Repeated references to *“Master Services Agreement”*\n*After*\n* The agreement is defined once as *“the Agreement”*\n* Used consistently throughout\n*Impact*\n* Pure drafting hygiene.\n* No legal effect, but this is how professional contract sets are normally run.\n----\nh4. 2. Services description narrowed (cosmetic but deliberate)\n*Before*\n* “certain *Embedded Finance services*”\n*After*\n* “certain *services*”\n*Impact*\n* Slightly broader wording.\n* Does *not* change the amendment’s operative clauses, but removes unnecessary specificity from the recital.\n* Sensible if services evolve beyond “Embedded Finance.”\n----\nh4. 3. Clause cross-references updated to match new defined term\nExamples:\n* “Clause 2.3 of the *Master Services Agreement*” → “Clause 2.3 of the *Agreement*”\n* Same throughout Sections 1–3\n*Impact*\n* Mechanical consistency only.\n----\nh4. 4. No change to the actual amendment mechanics\nCritically, *Clause 2.1(a)–(d) is identical*:\n* Controller-to-controller only\n* Processor language disapplied\n* SCC Module 1 / UK IDTA governs transfers\n* Module 4 deleted entirely\n* Customer remains an independent controller with access rights\n*Impact*\n* *Zero change* to data protection allocation, risk, or obligations.\n\n# AWX EEA/UK Amendment [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1c7EassSzgrZcODFRS5A_pmJaddd06jWjv9o5BubXFxs/edit?usp=sharing] - *review in progress* [~accountid:712020:f5c52198-9bb5-40b8-865d-70e96f6ccf5a]. Planning to complete the review by Wednesday EoD. Current AWX feedback is that DPA does not require any updates in light of the expansion.\n\n*Detailed feedback re/ EEA/UK Amendment:*\n\n{quote}_We have reviewed our current DSA in light of our payments solution. With online payments, Bolt can accept payments via different global and local payment methods. The data Airwallex processes for this purpose other than already evidently included in current services provision:_{quote}\n* _Data from payors/payees:_\n** _Identification and contact data Bolt collects during checkout (e.g. name, email, phone, shipping/billing address of the payor/payee)._\n** _Payment data: bank account number, card details, payment method identifiers, wallet tokens, etc._\n** _Transaction data: order IDs, amounts, currencies, timestamps, IP, device/browser fingerprints, etc._\n{quote}_Both the data subjects and types of personal data are already included in the current DSA. They are covered by the following definitions:_{quote}\n* _\"Account Data\" in clause 1.1(ii): \"“Account Data” means contact details; financial data such as the Customer’s or Connected Accounts’ account balance, transaction history, account or other related financial information; payor and payee information (including card number and the payee’s account information); and any other data collected, generated or Processed in connection with the Embedded Finance Solution.\"_\n* _“Payors/Payees” in clause 1.1(xxix): \"“Payors/Payees” means data subjects whose payment data is Processed in connection with transactions conducted via the Embedded Finance Solution.\"_\n{quote}_The processing activities under Exhibit H - Partner Services in Annex A are covered as follows:_{quote}\n* _KYC Information Services: covered via Onboarding Data and Additional Verification Data_\n* _UI Services: for as far as personal data is specifically processed to access the UI, this is covered via Account Data. With the UI itself, all personal data processed to provide services are included and covered by all types of data categorised in the DSA._\n* _Connected Account Support Services: covered via Support Data_\n{quote}_The extension of geographical scope does not have an impact on the current DSA. The SCC's are already part of the DSA and the selected options (e.g. regarding competent supervisory authority) remain sufficient. In conclusion, we don't foresee any necessary changes with the DSA. Please let us know if you disagree._{quote}","2026-01-20T10:41:25.075Z"],["3823309","WEB-9923","WEB","conor.mclaughlin@bolt.eu","Conor McLaughlin","[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] All good! Just sketching this thing out so all of those comments are perfectly clear and I can proceed with more granular propositions. I’ll be in touch 🙂","2026-01-20T10:42:16.743Z"],["3823310","LSS-61439","LSS","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","Hey, fleet said that this has been signed, pls check and let me know. Thanks!","2026-01-20T10:42:34.948Z"],["3823311","LSS-61816","LSS","ololade.olanipekun@bolt.eu","Ololade Olanipekun","Hi [~accountid:5e843508e57b6c0c1e6c703f] \n\nWe currently only have the attached contract with the vendor and the agreement permits payment in naira at the dollar parallel market equivalent rate.","2026-01-20T10:42:52.310Z"],["3823314","PFI-836006","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T10:43:06.917Z"],["3823315","PFI-834946","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T10:43:10.477Z"],["3823316","TAX2-442","TAX2","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","[~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] not yet, it is still pending.","2026-01-20T10:43:15.319Z"],["3823320","RDXENG-4685","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested and OK.*\n\nIcon updated to GPS arrow.","2026-01-20T10:43:53.902Z"],["3823321","PAW-15011","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-20T10:44:04.387Z"],["3823322","PFI-812948","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","I have created the adjustment subtypes and sent communication to local teams' POCs to inform them about the changes. Will close the ticket now.","2026-01-20T10:44:06.086Z"],["3823323","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","* Done\n\n!image-20260120-104404.png|width=958,alt=\"image-20260120-104404.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:44:07.720Z"],["3823325","DBRE-8598","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Done","2026-01-20T10:44:19.238Z"],["3823327","PFI-834953","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n\n\nHello Team!\n\nI completely understand why this might look like a double charge, but I can assure you that the user was only charged once. This is a common part of how card payments are processed. Here's what happens:\n\n# When the user first makes a payment, the bank temporarily ‘reserves' the funds and this is just the bank setting aside the amount for the transaction. The user’s account balance might show less amount but the payment hasn’t actually been taken out by the bank yet.\n# Later, when the payment is fully processed, that reserved amount is now “officially” debited from the user’s account. At that point, some banks send a second notification, which can make it seem like a second charge.\n\n\nI would advise the user to check their final account balance or statement, where they can confirm that only one payment was actually withdrawn. The earlier “pending” amount will either drop off or convert into the final charge.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T10:45:25.203Z"],["3823331","LSS-61847","LSS","aleksandra.kusiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Kusiak","[^formularz_podmiotu (1).pdf] _(100 kB)_\n\n[^formularz_zap (3) (1).pdf] _(49 kB)_","2026-01-20T10:45:42.884Z"],["3823332","LSS-61453","LSS","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","hey, partner said that this has been signed, can you please confirm? thank you","2026-01-20T10:45:57.453Z"],["3823333","PFI-834954","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment has now been completed.","2026-01-20T10:46:16.798Z"],["3823337","PFI-835647","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, I see all invoices have been issued and fiscalized; please, provide more details as to what is the issue","2026-01-20T10:46:57.934Z"],["3823338","PFI-835023","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has now been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-20T10:47:15.635Z"],["3823339","LSS-61730","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:41e1c836-f756-4994-b3dc-d4c2dda9e358] - Please find the signed doc attached.\n\n[^Breeze Social B.V. Trademark consent Bolt.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T10:47:51.263Z"],["3823341","PFI-834970","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nThanks for reaching out! The Customer Payments team doesn't handle promotion or discount codes. For assistance with those, please reach out to the *Campaigns and Incentives team* (technical support). They'll be able to assist you with any questions you have.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-20T10:48:25.573Z"],["3823342","MLC-304","MLC","suresh.nv@bolt.eu","Suresh NV","We will proceed with the launch of V2 in parallel have the following next steps.\n\nNext Steps:\n\n* QA is in progress. The rendering issues and the repeated ‘contact CS’ message appear to be resolved. Infobip has addressed the current issue and optimized the flow; we’ll now test the live optimizations end-to-end.\n** Needs to be tested: \n*** Feedback loop - Optimize the feedback loop to capture “chat closed” as a signal, and log events to ensure we track user intent.\n*** Eyecatcher pop-up (localized): Enable a per-country pop-up across all test markets. Default copy: “_Hi there 👋 Need help? Ask me anything_.”\n* *Message icon:* Update the icon. [+Hugo Horwood+|mailto:hugo.horwood@bolt.eu] to own.\n* *Knowledge base gaps:* Add questions the current flow isn’t answering. [+Viktorija Žuravļova+|mailto:viktorija.zuravlova@bolt.eu] to own.\n* *Comms integration:* Stuck in registration comms, add a content block that deep-links to (or opens) the chatbot. (TBD)","2026-01-20T10:48:28.020Z"],["3823343","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","[@jens.dobrindt|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:1153c9d5-fb49-4e02-ba70-729d45e900dd] [@siddhant.saxena|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:aa41bcd8-b709-4973-a7cd-1ca197d208f6]\n\njust to give you an update, the table that had duplicates had dependencies and those duplicated got copied over to some other places, the PR above removes it. Then we should be able to rerun the pipelines and the data shows up in the marts.\n\nThere may however be 1-2 marts that we would have to clean in the similar way","2026-01-20T10:48:40.547Z"],["3823346","DAEN-1346","DAEN","yuriy.trofymenko@bolt.eu","Yuriy Trofymenko","long-term we have 2 initiatives to mitigate this kind of issues for January and February, one of them close to being published, will keep you posted ofc","2026-01-20T10:49:37.792Z"],["3823347","LSS-61690","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^AMEX Bolt Services UK Limited 2025 (1) (1).pdf]\n\n[~accountid:5da5d5da1e03120c3e010ec6] , there is the one you added yesterday. Currently waiting for Alex Wong’s signatures","2026-01-20T10:49:45.305Z"],["3823348","WFM-10054","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Market access request: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601738|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601738]","2026-01-20T10:50:00.907Z"],["3823349","LSS-61718","LSS","anett.hunt@bolt.eu","Anett Hunt","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d600e3f-d3ca-4f4e-b8af-f6c7510bb923] , please find the signed doc attached.\n\n[^Nova Mobility UG - Kickback - DE_Rides_BoltClub_Berlin (2) (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-20T10:50:37.648Z"],["3823350","PFI-835320","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Natalia, this fraud rule was specifically created to prevent promo abuse by users with multiple existing accounts, where the same promo code could otherwise be reused by simply creating new accounts. In this case, the user has three accounts linked to the same device, which is why the rule is triggering and the promo will not be applied.\n\nSince this is a fairly basic but important prevention rule aimed at limiting campaign abuse, we won’t be making changes or exceptions here 🙂 ","2026-01-20T10:50:42.656Z"],["3823351","WFM-10054","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey WFM team, we raised the market request for South Africa, could you please add necessary queues? ","2026-01-20T10:50:57.154Z"],["3823352","DLVR-341","DLVR","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","+Update after discussion Legal + Tax Product + VAT+\n\n*Business case:* Bolt recharging DineOut campaign costs to restaurants under the +current user flow (i.e. “+[+alt 1+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v0eM1D_AVBAV2xZs3O6VbqHVzyKlp1OOgi2kVgdEp0U/edit?tab=t.0]+”).+ The idea here is to have Bolt pre-fund cashback reward to customers’ Bolt Balance and then recharge the cost as marketing service (with VAT in localised countries or reverse charge in non-localised) to restaurants.\n*Tax approval*: The Cashback option is preferred since it does not “affect” the Partner->Eater tax receipt (i.e. the Partner should not include the discount within the tax base), and the risk of being challenged by tax authorities is lower compared to e.g. using discount option.\n*Legal approval*: Current partner T&Cs cls 6.3 cover cashback option under  launched current user flow “_/…/In addition Bolt may charge the Partner a fee for running a marketing campaign which shall be agreed between the parties.”_\nAs per discussion between Legal-Tax-VAT teams, even though generic, this clause should be sufficient to consider as including the cashback option for DineOut. At the end of the day, marketing campaign can be assimilated to a service, and as such we want to frame the cashback. Thus, agreed not to modify DineOut Partner T&Cs.\n\n*To-do-list for business:*\n\n# *Clear Opt-In:* DineOut Partners should have some sort of opt-in for participating in campaigns where they have to cover the costs, either through:\n## opting-in via email confirmation\n## partner portal where they can tick a box for specific campaign\n# *Clear Terms:* In both cases terms of the campaign must be clearly presented to the partner before it opts-in:\n## duration of the campaign\n## cancellation possibility: available or not. If available under which terms\n## cost division and percentage: cost-shared vs partner covered campaign + what %/sums will be covered by partner/Bolt\n## any restrictions on applicability: e.g. available to specific user groups, applicable only for DineOut\n## disclaimer that partner has read the campaign terms, understand them and agree to them + that Bolt cannot guarantee any specific business outcome or performance with this campaign\n# *Guidance for Partners*: if it is confusing for the partners how the recharge takes place or how is it displayed, then this should be described under FAQ section for DineOut, under specific guidance shared with partners or somewhere in Partner Portal or email where Partner opts-in to the campaign","2026-01-20T10:51:09.693Z"],["3823353","ROPSC-496","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Prepare the audit tool for the market and run all drivers though the tool.\n\n[+Data of active drivers+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1E2TKOddmVgU_0o8bMdb5PLT9yWIKQ9OP9ARzna8fu-8/edit?gid=1435314065#gid=1435314065]","2026-01-20T10:51:11.539Z"],["3823356","ROPSC-497","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","All active drivers (3 554 total) have been processed through the automated audit tool.\nOverall, *9.6% (340 drivers)* were flagged. As a result, these 340 drivers will need to go through a manual audit.","2026-01-20T10:52:32.091Z"],["3823358","LSS-61848","LSS","juan.alvarez@bolt.eu","Juan Álvarez","[^MOD_CONTRATO.doc] _(102 kB)_","2026-01-20T10:52:34.488Z"],["3823359","IOTTEAM-324","IOTTEAM","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","{{I (35727) BDI: millig=-352,516,-770 mdegs=-1114,-46,701 celsius=24 }}\n{{I (35728) BDI: command done; err: 0; ret: 0; (imu_read)}}","2026-01-20T10:52:49.123Z"],["3823360","LSS-61838","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d5390cd-af56-43c8-9d12-f431b20183ba] and [~accountid:712020:03164f2c-f82a-4e8e-9172-2c02cad1e229] We will do our best to review the agreement. Please note, however, that the agreement is approximately 40 pages long, which means that reviewing it within the current timeframe requires us to deprioritise other work and focus exclusively on this contract.\n\nFor future matters, we would appreciate either receiving agreements earlier or managing counterparty expectations so that we are given at least 4 working days to complete a proper review.\n\nAt this stage, please also confirm whether all commercial terms are acceptable and whether, from an operational and product perspective, we are able to meet all of the requirements set out in the agreement.","2026-01-20T10:52:59.241Z"],["3823361","PFI-836019","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T10:53:04.083Z"],["3823367","WEB-9923","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:63c11ab62a526608c5506c05] Thank you! I will be here to support anytime! ","2026-01-20T10:53:39.740Z"],["3823372","ROPSC-508","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Prepare the audit tool for the market and run all drivers though the tool.\n\n[+Data of active drivers+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SfFw9JD-I34I33_DSUHPnUXhQtaXVIegf_GE9tCQHWU/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-20T10:54:04.474Z"],["3823373","PFI-836020","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-20T10:54:09.457Z"],["3823374","BDMCD-70","BDMCD","mercedes.ramirezmolina@bolt.eu","Mercedes Ramírez Molina","Court date 21.02.2026 got cancelled. The defendant withdrew the objection to the payment order, the court hearing was cancelled, and the claim is now final and enforceable.","2026-01-20T10:54:46.604Z"],["3823375","LSS-55158","LSS","miroslava.gorejova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Gorejova","cc [~accountid:712020:68e3fab1-1f89-4afb-b02b-42fffee9a8c4] ","2026-01-20T10:54:56.706Z"],["3823376","PFI-835539","PFI","julija.gorskova@bolt-outsource.eu","Julija Gorskova","Hi, we still need an assistance. \n\n","2026-01-20T10:55:02.765Z"],["3823379","PFI-835565","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Serhii, we weren’t initially rejecting any of these attempts. We only started rejecting once they passed a rate limiter threshold for single number attempts. Meaning the issue was that we allowed to send the OTP, but for some reason, either the user did not receive the OTP, or there were other issues in the login flow.\nAs you can see from the screenshot below, we allowed the OTP for the most recent attempt. If there’s still an issue, I’d recommend reaching out to Comms or Tech support.\nThanks!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.52.56.png|width=1021,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 12.52.56.png\"!","2026-01-20T10:55:49.073Z"],["3823380","ROPSC-509","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Overall, *14%*  were flagged. As a result, these drivers will need to go through a manual audit.\n\n[Audit tool results|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tu0vII72JOeKWUiHEdlqEmNiFTL4slyhRsU5vsS4mq8/edit?gid=0#gid=0]","2026-01-20T10:55:49.232Z"],["3823384","PFI-834137","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","Hi [~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f], \n\nThanks for your follow up. \n\nAs requested please find link bellow: \n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/765345?tab=invoices&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-invoicing/businessCompanies/edit/765345?tab=invoices&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]\n\nLet me know if you need additional info.","2026-01-20T10:56:21.781Z"],["3823387","LSS-61850","LSS","ariana.nikolaou@bolt.eu","Ariana Nikolaou","[^Larnaca International Airport - License and Service Agreement.pdf] _(582 kB)_","2026-01-20T10:56:48.204Z"],["3823388","LSS-61838","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] the agreement can be found [HERE|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1k-LZ5KzYOxfqO1VK0kSZcRMWDiNDDdSe/edit] ","2026-01-20T10:56:54.064Z"],["3823391","LSS-61403","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:6052892160d39e006f72f166] - in which case, no further comments from my side 🙂 ","2026-01-20T10:57:13.017Z"],["3823394","PFI-835539","PFI","julija.gorskova@bolt-outsource.eu","Julija Gorskova","Driver also contacted the bank, and they confirmed that the sum is returned to Bolt ","2026-01-20T10:57:36.511Z"],["3823395","PFI-835575","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey, duplicate case. Since it’s the same number and same issue as in your ticket here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/378/PFI-835565|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/378/PFI-835565|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T10:57:37.600Z"],["3823400","TAX2-561","TAX2","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","+Update - On B2G central model adjustment+\n\nRecap the B2G Central model alignment meeting we had on Tuesday (13 January):\n\n* *Billing* - according to Billing, the (billing) setup for two models (principal and agency) simultaneously would work only if the driver account switching is built for B2G purposes;\n** since driver account switching is not that favourable from Product side, the Product is currently exploring other workable options (i) to ensure consumer-facing business is ring-fenced ad (ii) to ensure Billing works for both models simultaneously for both B2G and B2C purposes\n* *Tax* - alignment on the Central Model reached.\n* *Co-payment option* - in some tenders the co-payment option will be used where the passenger and the government are to pay for the transportation service together\n** Legal to come up with a separate slide on the structure\n** alignment to be reached on the possible co-payment solutions as well (there may possibly be issues with finreg.","2026-01-20T10:59:00.373Z"],["3823401","LSS-28796","LSS","brita.lubi@bolt.eu","Brita Lubi","Hi! Details below as received from treasury team:\n\n* Name of the bank: CITIBANK N.A\n** Branch Name: CITIBANK EUROPE PLC, SWEDEN BRANCH\n* Clearing number: 9040\n* Account number: 90401415076\n* Bankgiro number: 5901-7988\n\n","2026-01-20T10:59:47.211Z"],["3823402","TAX2-596","TAX2","victor.garces@bolt.eu","Víctor Garcés","+Update+ \n\nSince B2G operating model has been agreed on a global level, as next step it will be reviewed by local counsel for Sweden - WIP.","2026-01-20T10:59:48.286Z"],["3823403","PFI-834137","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","The invoices aren’t issued since the VAT code is missing in the Agent Profile. Please, update the VAT code, based on the: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7069859934/Portugal+Fiscalisation+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7069859934/Portugal+Fiscalisation+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|smart-link] ","2026-01-20T11:00:19.399Z"],["3823404","DMC-735","DMC","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:621f66f84160640069c66ff4] as discussed in the call, this will be covered by allowing PIM users to select multiple stores at a time by selecting a city they belong to. Adding a 3rd “column” to the stores listed is a bit too much for such a UI element as a dropdown picker (we already have provider name and provider ID there)","2026-01-20T11:00:19.594Z"],["3823405","WD-22567","WD","kristiina.vaik@bolt.eu","Kristiina Vaik","Hi [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] ,\nThank you! Actually this validation is mainly needed for intercompany invoices, as we are not allowed to submit IC invoices without attachments. At the moment, when we receive these invoices, it often takes quite a lot of time to follow up with the invoice creator to request the missing attachments :pleading_face: .","2026-01-20T11:00:21.304Z"],["3823408","LSS-60899","LSS","jacqueline.tiessi@bolt.eu","Jacqueline Tiessi","Hello [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742] ,\n\nThanks for sharing this, the proposed structure makes sense from an operational standpoint and looks feasible to enable as described.\n\nI do have one question to clarify the edge case around prevention drivers:\n_If a driver in the prevention segment has already served a block and then accumulates 3+ warnings again, how would you suggest we proceed?_\n\nIn this case, should we apply another 3-day block, or do you have a more coercive approach in mind for handling repeat offenders at this stage?\n\n","2026-01-20T11:00:31.733Z"],["3823411","SOBB-1030","SOBB","lucas.santossilva@bolt.eu","Lucas Oliveira dos Santos Silva","(flag) Flag added \n\nNo access in Sales Cloud for Slack settings to proceed with the debug. [~accountid:712020:b996cecd-aad9-4981-9528-5e20041886f2] created a case and we are following it.","2026-01-20T11:01:02.739Z"],["3823412","PFI-834316","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-20T11:01:04.070Z"],["3823413","LSS-61848","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-20T11:01:06.809Z"],["3823415","PFI-834315","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-20T11:01:33.969Z"],["3823416","WFM-10047","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey [~accountid:712020:a4f6dc7f-ea2b-4b6c-87be-3ca7829f155a] , could you please update us what kind of access error does your agent receive? Apparently [+afonso.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:afonso.fernandes@bolt-outsource.eu] already has *Outsourced CS - PT Invoice role* which grants him to access to edit user invoice.","2026-01-20T11:01:36.048Z"],["3823417","SRED-506","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, all clusters switched to separate SG from redises.","2026-01-20T11:01:40.008Z"],["3823419","RDS-898","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] FYI: I added Prio. Feel free to adjust it.","2026-01-20T11:02:01.213Z"],["3823425","HS-29114","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","Hi Dijo,\n\nI requested the Health Insurance Fund to open a sick leave for you for the period 02.01.2026-18.01.2026. Once the sick leave is visible in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee], then I will approve your requests in Workday as well.\n\nKind regards,\nAike-Maris","2026-01-20T11:02:22.340Z"],["3823426","DPM-2289","DPM","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","[~accountid:621f66f84160640069c66ff4] High makes sense to me 👍  Highest doesn’t (cc [~accountid:712020:ddfe83d1-e2c1-4238-8459-1dfffb836745] ) as this is still only applicable to a minority of menus","2026-01-20T11:02:34.080Z"],["3823428","FX-3583","FX","jana.lutus@bolt.eu","Jana Lutus","[~accountid:712020:a29a1eb0-406b-4e1d-be6f-0bc875cbd442] each activity metric is the sum of durations of all suitable events (on-ride, waiting,  break and/or offline). For example for on-ride activity, we summarise all finished orders that happen during the selected time range. If there’s an event that’s started a day before the requested time range and continued within it, we include the part that happened during the time range into the calculations. \n\nThe only issue I was able to identify is that if an event stated *more than a day* before the requested time range and continued into the first day, it wouldn’t get included in the calculations, and the last event of the day would be stretched to cover for blindspots. However, I doubt this happens often, and the effect of this is likely too small to account for the huge discrepancy we see on the screenshots. \n\nThe more realistic explanation is the difference in data we get from the orders team vs what the driver portal gets. According to [~accountid:712020:30ff8030-613c-48f8-a402-a48bd2c25e5f], there’s a lot of variability when it comes to what can be fetched, such as whether scheduled rides are included, what counts as start and end times (moment when rider requested vs moment when driver accepted), etc. And the orders team doesn’t have a single unified way to provide this information.  \n\nAs a side note, it also seems we don’t even have consistency for the online hours we display within FOP: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3517|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3517|smart-link] 😔 ","2026-01-20T11:02:44.186Z"],["3823429","WFM-10021","WFM","nikita.bogomazovs@bolt-outsource.eu","Nikita Bogomazovs","Thank you! ","2026-01-20T11:02:44.661Z"],["3823430","ROPSC-510","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","[CZ manual audit and working sheet.|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yLqTouZMxYzqoGrja0Ehmbv0RN1keNuxXmAYhPWYxw0/edit?gid=959184512#gid=959184512]\n\nDrivers are going through the manual review twice. The drivers that failed and had already a suspension on their profile, were suspended right away by declining the failed document which triggered “Block if missing”. The ones that were marked as failed, are being reviewed once again. If the drivers still fail, an expiry date is being (15 days of grace period) added to trigger automated comms to upload new valid document and eventually trigger suspension. ","2026-01-20T11:02:53.748Z"],["3823436","CSXBS-51","CSXBS","mafalda.vaz@bolt.eu","Mafalda Vaz","[~accountid:712020:6b69a264-7ea3-44f2-8afc-3ec18f946f92] ","2026-01-20T11:03:07.618Z"],["3823438","PFI-833730","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment matched !","2026-01-20T11:03:17.790Z"],["3823439","C2-462","C2","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","h1. Capacity/ESR test\n\n# Test without balancing \n# Test after balancing\n\nh2. Test flow\n\n# Charge battery to 100% SoC\n## Option A. Charge with regular charger and take into consideration the actual pack voltage for the capacity\n## *Option B*. Charge with power supply and low current to charger the battery to max. Charging to 4.1V per cell.\n# Load the battery\n#* with pulses on each 10% SOC\n#* 19A for 10 seconds\n#* else 0.2C discharging\n# Measure cell group voltages\n#* Periodic sampling 1 second\n#* Measure voltage (faster sampling during pulse)\n#** Before pulse\n#** End of pulse\n#** After pulse\n# Calculate\n## ESR for each cell group on each 10% SOC\n## Capacity\n\nh1. Batteries for testing\n\n* Older C1 cell error batteries, Techsum and TWS\n* Balance voltages to cell voltage delta < 10mV\n* 10 pcs","2026-01-20T11:03:28.322Z"],["3823440","LSS-51490","LSS","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","[~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] just to confirm per my Slack chat yesterday, the DPIA is for our DPO rep as standard visibility to comply with their legal obligations (i.e., the person performing functions that the ODPO would normally be responsible for). DPO rep’s letter is a notification that *would only*: \n\n* Reference that a DPIA has been conducted for this specific processing activity; and \n* include details of that processing activity (from the DPIA as drafted) to show that benefits/risk mitigation have been considered.\n\nLet me know if this is an issue or how you wish to proceed. ","2026-01-20T11:03:29.091Z"],["3823443","PFI-836025","PFI","lucian.andrei@bolt.eu","Lucian Andrei","[^op bolt (5).pdf]","2026-01-20T11:03:58.940Z"],["3823444","CSXRT-204","CSXRT","mari-liis.pork@bolt.eu","Mari-Liis Põrk","They will implement a No Go zone in Liverpool that will be active only on weekends (9PM - 5AM) via a schedule. It will cover a large portion of the city centre.\n\nSuggestion - alert/pop-up to the user 5-10 minutes before the zone is active to avoid the ride auto-finishing mid-ride. Product involved to see possibility. [Slack|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CLARAF0S0/p1768911111015459?thread_ts=1768840261.479339&cid=CLARAF0S0]\n\nPossible process change necessary/info to the agents either via CS OPS or BH article/FAQ?","2026-01-20T11:04:01.271Z"],["3823448","CNT-377","CNT","amal.bahar@bolt.eu","Amal Bahar","[~accountid:61cac1b0326554006c9b5945] got product to review the content as well. 1 fdbk standing out: want to avoid using exclusive subscriber-only “discounts”, as it was recently decided that member discounts may be lower than generic offers for non-members :smiling_face_with_tear: . So I striked from the above desc as well. \nNeed your expertise: do you suggest we say exclusive subscriber-only ‘perks' (indicating benefits above/ creating excitement) OR remove exclusive subscriber-only 'perks’ all together? \n--\nOnce this is applied, we can lock the content. And I’ll take a final look before handing it LCM, thanks so much!","2026-01-20T11:05:05.824Z"],["3823453","WEBSD-1475","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c] 👋 \n\nI was thinking the same.\n\n[~accountid:712020:c7bffa72-768e-4809-ac1d-628c7bb93ccd]  maybe this is something you can check with [~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] . \n\n[~accountid:712020:341b8095-1e4f-44ea-ad93-e6b03a07da4c]  Just a small piece of advice: To check with Legal to ensure these documents are approved for whichever path we choose. To make sure we have all in order before implementation. \n\nIf you have the approval already then I guess [~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f]  maybe you can help us here to comment your idea.","2026-01-20T11:05:50.611Z"],["3823455","PFI-835858","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, will go live on 01.02","2026-01-20T11:06:20.999Z"],["3823456","BIZ-292","BIZ","teresa.rodrigues@bolt.eu","Teresa Cipriano Rodrigues","RH team postpones the Italy lunch. It is now planned for Q2","2026-01-20T11:06:22.298Z"],["3823458","WFM-10057","WFM","toyosi.olusesi@bolt-outsource.eu","Toyosi Olusesi","*Role: Outsource CS - Micromobility*\n\n*Market*: global markets supporting micromobility","2026-01-20T11:06:31.627Z"],["3823459","PFI-833625","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-20T11:06:32.004Z"],["3823463","DLSP-1994","DLSP","konstantin.konashenkov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Konashenkov","[~accountid:712020:e9e1dc43-86eb-4bae-af6e-e24db5f48519]  confirmed [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A45PMAZ0X/p1768907152949269?thread_ts=1768907056.056739&cid=C0A45PMAZ0X], that application status isn’t needed","2026-01-20T11:06:54.025Z"],["3823466","LSS-61539","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Hi, after a few discussions, it seems we still need to proceed with the Cancellation Letter. Please re-open the ticket.","2026-01-20T11:07:12.507Z"],["3823471","PFI-835646","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Miranisa, the promo code is being blocked because the monthly combined campaign coverage for their device has exceeded the allowed threshold. This rule is designed to prevent campaign power users and users who create multiple accounts with the same device, to repeatedly abuse the same promotion.\n\nGiven that this is a core safeguard for basic campaign abuse prevention, from a risk perspective, it’s in our best interest to keep this rule unchanged.","2026-01-20T11:07:50.022Z"],["3823476","DMC-728","DMC","kirill.krechetnikov@bolt.eu","Kirill Krechetnikov","I don’t reproduce it. Neither in the option groups selector, nor when using the search on the product listing page. Trying with my test region 4002 on prelive. It seems that there are some specific conditions that trigger this situation. [~accountid:60950a25539c14006ae92e40] I think we need to help engineers further by discovering these conditions","2026-01-20T11:08:13.304Z"],["3823478","RDS-851","RDS","dashiell.stanford@bolt.eu","Dash Stanford","[~accountid:712020:6b7effe8-70c7-4436-a9a0-e4b027cf915f] makes sense! Updated 🙂 ","2026-01-20T11:08:17.160Z"],["3823480","PFI-830721","PFI","julija.gorskova@bolt-outsource.eu","Julija Gorskova","hey, are there any apdates?","2026-01-20T11:09:15.720Z"],["3823481","RDS-957","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] FYI: I added Prio. Feel free to adjust it.","2026-01-20T11:09:16.103Z"],["3823482","SREDESK-7432","SREDESK","mehran.eftekhari@bolt.eu","Shahriar Eftekhari","Created index in Valkey. Check if it works for you and let me know so I can merge the PR and close the ticket.","2026-01-20T11:09:44.223Z"],["3823484","LSS-60553","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:7ebf1982-dd36-43fb-a386-42b4b1ee6b59] , there is no Mahmoud’s signature for real. I wll collect it again.","2026-01-20T11:09:59.590Z"],["3823486","LEG-1133","LEG","ana.abenza@bolt.eu","Ana Abenza","[~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] Thanks Michael, makese sense. We currently run the Mystery Shopping surveys and share feedback with fleets but dont enforce KPIs of the back of it. I wonder if a half-way solution would be to add some wording to the contracts explaining we would run Mystery Shopping surveys and share feedback with them and that there is an expectation to work together on improvements - without linking them to KPIS? - what do u think?","2026-01-20T11:10:08.501Z"],["3823488","PFI-835321","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, access has been requested. In general, on our end, the configuration is the same for all partner markets, they’re supposed to have the invoice issuer setup.","2026-01-20T11:10:22.438Z"],["3823489","DAEN-1368","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","Working on the audit report [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Svf4muDnhvYA2XTfmQQnCBthMgj-n18OUQBagYj2feE/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.dit3ukm4zlcp]","2026-01-20T11:10:22.697Z"],["3823492","DBRE-8731","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","Btw, i'm not sure PingCap told issue is getting fixed, it was rather \"we changed everything, so it might work as a fix\", so after upgrade we can retry, but very gently. In any case, i'd add more cases into open ticket (if any), cause i can push it based on the fact that each such case is an incident for us.","2026-01-20T11:10:43.425Z"],["3823493","RDS-905","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] do you remember what the negative comments were about?","2026-01-20T11:10:43.531Z"],["3823494","LSS-61504","LSS","monicah.mumina@bolt-outsource.eu","Monicah Mumina","Update","2026-01-20T11:10:44.078Z"],["3823497","BIZ-258","BIZ","ana.abenza@bolt.eu","Ana Abenza","Hi all, i’ll close this ticket so we align with the MVRA process, though we are still refining a few points on this","2026-01-20T11:10:52.712Z"],["3823498","RDS-905","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:5e0f0e7f0242870e996ebba8] FYI: I added Prio. Feel free to adjust it.","2026-01-20T11:11:00.400Z"],["3823499","PFI-835366","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\nPlease create a new ticket for the correct team! https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T11:11:03.216Z"],["3823501","PFI-835677","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Pimlapas, checked the orders/riders, and everything looks legitimate. You may compensate for the lost bonus.\nThank you!","2026-01-20T11:11:05.905Z"],["3823502","WEB-9703","WEB","vishal.kapoor@bolt.eu","Vishal Kapoor","Jenkins pipeline - [https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/PL/job/autocode-baca-autocode/351/|https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/PL/job/autocode-baca-autocode/351/]\n\nAutomated PR - [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161236|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/161236|smart-link] \n\nOverall looks good, when trying to find why it didnt create for rider rating page found out that it made a comment - Note in the pipeline that there were no urls found for rider ratings email, which turns out to be correct","2026-01-20T11:11:14.668Z"],["3823504","DAEN-1346","DAEN","mangesh.khairnar@bolt.eu","Mangesh Khairnar","Deleted problematic records, let’s rerun the pipelines now. [@zafrullah.bhatti|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:5a6af830-067b-4540-b6fc-bcc5f15ba576]","2026-01-20T11:11:18.824Z"],["3823506","LSS-60062","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] Is there anything else you need on this?  If not, I will close the ticket. Thanks.","2026-01-20T11:12:00.800Z"],["3823507","PAW-15013","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-20T11:12:02.172Z"],["3823509","HWMISC-768","HWMISC","klemet-gustav.tamm@bolt.eu","Klemet-Gustav Tamm","Only tracking file from EE is missing, will be marked done once we get it.","2026-01-20T11:12:22.367Z"],["3823510","RDS-935","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] [~accountid:712020:648af4f5-f134-458a-b3aa-9320408d346e] Do we know how many rides end with giving the rating and how many users ignore it?","2026-01-20T11:12:47.887Z"],["3823511","LSS-60512","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","hi Jola, agreement is signed. Ticket can be closed. Thanks!","2026-01-20T11:12:49.480Z"],["3823513","WEB-8659","WEB","vishal.kapoor@bolt.eu","Vishal Kapoor","Deployed on prelive","2026-01-20T11:13:18.722Z"],["3823520","PFI-817354","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-20T11:14:29.287Z"],["3823521","HS-29177","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Data change task is with PP-s","2026-01-20T11:14:32.413Z"],["3823522","DPO-150","DPO","mengel.paula@bolt.eu","Paula Maria Mengel","[+CONT-101522+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/13/CONT-101522] translations ticket","2026-01-20T11:14:36.509Z"],["3823523","LSS-61724","LSS","nina.paragoso@bolt.eu","Nina Paragoso","Hi, any update here?","2026-01-20T11:14:41.398Z"],["3823524","LSS-61213","LSS","nina.paragoso@bolt.eu","Nina Paragoso","Hi, any update here?","2026-01-20T11:14:46.938Z"],["3823526","RDS-948","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] I wonder how many users are affected by that? Any idea who may know it?","2026-01-20T11:15:38.494Z"],["3823527","ROPSC-515","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Compliance-related processes reviewed together with local team. The processes mostly aligned with standard operating procedures. Discrepancies can be found [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1RGfH-wz4VeJiY9H1Pl1seDWspdCq_VegjsqGHk-pmY8/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.gd2wj3oy2uml]. ","2026-01-20T11:16:08.738Z"],["3823530","WFM-10022","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","Hello, [~accountid:712020:647d9435-b4ad-4729-aebd-e4f4f0044a62]  seems like adding WW-SHIFT canceled out the segment: WW-SHIFT_NIGHT. This segment is used during 22:00-06:00 LT time. Agents who have WW-SHIFT_NIGHT are affected during 22:00-00:00 LT time. However, after 00:00 until 06:00 their adherence is visible with WW-SHIFT_NIGHT segment.\n\nWW-SHIFT_NIGHT should be the same as WW-SHIFT - reflected as a productive event with trackable adherence as agents are solving tickets during that time.\n\nI am adding agents, who have this segment but the adherence is not visible in Assembled. I am also adding a few screenshots of how the adherence currently looks like.\n\n|Affected Agent Bolt Email|Date when affected|\n|[aldas.palubinskas@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:aldas.palubinskas@bolt-outsource.eu]|19th|\n|[mindaugas.posecnas@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:mindaugas.posecnas@bolt-outsource.eu]|16th, 18th|\n|[lorenas.raicevas@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:lorenas.raicevas@bolt-outsource.eu]|17th|\n|[rosvaldas.panumis@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:rosvaldas.panumis@bolt-outsource.eu]|17th, 18th, 19th|\n|[gintare.kirkliauskaite@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:gintare.kirkliauskaite@bolt-outsource.eu]|17th|\n\n!First half of agent adherence with WW-NIGHT-SHIFT added from 2200-0400.png|width=1043,height=302,alt=\"First half of agent adherence with WW-NIGHT-SHIFT added from 2200-0400.png\"!\n\n!Second half of agent adherence with WW-NIGHT-SHIFTadded from 2200-0400.png|width=737,height=313,alt=\"Second half of agent adherence with WW-NIGHT-SHIFTadded from 2200-0400.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-20T11:16:51.368Z"],["3823532","PFI-835212","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Payment not found. Please confirm with the partner if the payment has bounced back from their bank. If already checked, add a comment here and we’ll investigate further.","2026-01-20T11:17:25.945Z"],["3823533","RDS-951","RDS","adrian.dampc@bolt.eu","Adrian Dampc","[~accountid:712020:2791559d-8cee-435c-95ba-4a8c95b36b65] sure, makes sense. I wonder, as this is a non-critical issue with low adoption, is it better to keep it broken or disable it until we do it right? wdyt?","2026-01-20T11:17:36.867Z"],["3823534","ROPSC-513","ROPSC","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","Fleet document sets are aligned with global standards","2026-01-20T11:17:52.615Z"],["3823536","PFI-833425","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, thank you\n\nIntermediary BB Invoice issuer is ready","2026-01-20T11:17:58.273Z"],["3823537","RDXENG-4435","RDXENG","evamaria.pedosk@bolt.eu","Eva-Maria Pedosk","(/) *Tested and OK.*\n\nCar icon moves according to drivers location.","2026-01-20T11:18:28.748Z"],["3823538","WFM-10057","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541796|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541796]\n","2026-01-20T11:18:42.802Z"],["3823539","RS-1962","RS","tomislav.lukacevic@bolt.eu","Tomislav Lukačević","!Slika zaslona 2026-01-20 u 12.15.51.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Slika zaslona 2026-01-20 u 12.15.55.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T11:18:59.970Z"],["3823541","PFI-835700","PFI","karl.kutsar@bolt.eu","Karl Kristjan Kutsar","Hey Natalia, thanks for reaching out.\nYes, the reasoning you outlined is correct. The device was blocked because it logged into multiple different accounts within a short time frame, which is considered highly suspicious behaviour. This can indicate potential fraud or account takeover attempts, which is why the Identity controls were applied.\n\n_Is there any way for the rider to use the app normally?_ \nThey can do so with a single account. When multiple accounts are used from the same device, protective measures like this are expected to trigger.\n\nAs a next step, please ask the user to explain why multiple accounts were created and why they were registered under different names. If we can confirm a valid and legitimate reason for this behaviour, we can review the case and consider unblocking the device.\n\nI’ll be closing the ticket now. Let us know once you have the user’s explanation by either pinging me in this ticket, or creating a new one.\nThanks!","2026-01-20T11:19:52.637Z"],["3823542","PFI-836031","PFI","sonja.djemrovski@bolt-outsource.eu","Sonja Djemrovski","!Screenshot_20260120_073937_Bolt Courier.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T11:20:03.241Z"],["3823543","PFI-836031","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-20T11:20:06.029Z"],["3823545","LSS-59587","LSS","svenkristjan.bormann@bolt.eu","Sven-Kristjan Bormann","[~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] User asked yesterday for an update.","2026-01-20T11:20:10.540Z"],["3823549","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768908028810479]*{color}:\nHey <@U01FRLQSQ15> from what I can find in logs, the possible reason is that order and offer were created on 13 January but the taxi tag was added to the car on 14 January according to [Audit Log|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs/view/5708911676] reference. Can it be the reason tags didi not match?\n{quote}","2026-01-20T11:20:43.610Z"],["3823553","WFM-10057","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Hey, [~accountid:63e39f9928cddcc707749ab1] ,\nWe have raised the role request, and now it’s pending approval. If approved, it may take around 10-15 minutes for changes to take effect. \nMeanwhile, can you clarify, do these agents work on *02 MM_Global_English*?\nLooking forward,","2026-01-20T11:21:11.283Z"],["3823554","LSS-61818","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63b62e9-e039-44cb-8feb-1a5c42b0eb41] ,\n\nCan you provide me the requested list, please? (vehicles and license plates registered under Fleet NoiteCitadina Lda, NIF 514716355). \n\nThank you!\n","2026-01-20T11:21:27.126Z"],["3823556","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","For this specific CDC error:\n {{\"level\":\"FATAL\",\"caller\":\"<http://lib.rs:479|lib.rs:479>\",\"message\":\"assertion }}left == right``\nThere is a bug fix in 8.5.4","2026-01-20T11:21:31.374Z"],["3823558","WFM-10057","WFM","kamran.hasilov@bolt.eu","Kamran Hasilov","Mind you, [+dorcas.irabor@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:dorcas.irabor@bolt-outsource.eu] , [+imemesit.sifon@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:imemesit.sifon@bolt-outsource.eu] , [+esther.otitolaiye@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:esther.otitolaiye@bolt-outsource.eu] have already *Outsource CS - Micromobility* roles assigned.","2026-01-20T11:21:49.556Z"],["3823560","PFI-833361","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature