r/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T11:22:00.494Z"],["3823564","DBRE-8731","DBRE","leandro.morgado@bolt.eu","Leandro Ricardo Rodrigues Morgado","This ^^ was not what caused CDC stuck.. it was cause of TiKV restart","2026-01-20T11:22:07.746Z"],["3823566","LSS-58632","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello,\n\nplease find attached two files of PoA issued for [~accountid:712020:4a020e03-91ec-4656-9308-5b9b6428f675] .\n\n+*The signing process for both files:*+\n\n* wet ink\n* [~accountid:5b18f5574bec0e53fdb555d5] signature\n\nplease [~accountid:712020:4a020e03-91ec-4656-9308-5b9b6428f675] let us know if you need the original versions of each PoA physically at your local office (Czech) or the scan of PoA would be sufficient.\n\nCZ: [^PoA GM Bolt Drive_CZ.docx.pdf] \n\nSK: [^PoA GM Bolt Drive_SK.docx.pdf] \n\nBest, Jola","2026-01-20T11:22:38.162Z"],["3823568","FIN2-550","FIN2","katarina.saage@bolt.eu","Katarina Elisabeth Saage","hi [~accountid:60b5deeb5fa6f1006f994b75], cc: [~accountid:62567ec6a872710069210b83] . \n\nIs there anything to be done for the Rides launch in Italy from the Treasury end? If not, I’d mark this as complete or update it to a more specific task to be completed. \n\nPS: launching as a cross-border, centralised. See Commerce setup here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7323158468/Italy+Rides+2026|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/7323158468/Italy+Rides+2026|smart-link] \n\nThanks!","2026-01-20T11:23:00.214Z"],["3823569","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768908168176489]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3673 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T11:23:00.838Z"],["3823571","LSS-60756","LSS","alexandre.lancastre@bolt.eu","Alexandre Lancastre","\n\n[^InComm Europe Mutual NDA - BOLT OPERATIONS OÜ CLEAN.doc]\n\nBuenos dias Angela,\n\nMuchas gracias por compartirlo.\n\nEl cliente ya lo firmó, podemos firmarlo también?\n\nGracias y un saludo,\n\nAlexandre Lancastre","2026-01-20T11:23:04.389Z"],["3823572","PFI-829646","PFI","natalia.fronczuk@bolt.eu","Natalia Frończuk","Hi Team, can this be looked into?","2026-01-20T11:23:11.984Z"],["3823573","FX-3670","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768908183420319]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3670 successfully transitioned to state 'Progress'.\n{quote}","2026-01-20T11:23:15.203Z"],["3823574","CMO-12980","CMO","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Cashback in Delivery rollout and following reporting in Feb","2026-01-20T11:23:18.014Z"],["3823575","CMO-13001","CMO","nigel.janssen@bolt.eu","Nigel Janssen","Change [document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hczs2P1RFaofTuSJ5bg8-U7-ZORsdWVShxSLLoOwZ6s/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-20T11:23:30.246Z"],["3823577","LSS-60512","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","can you please upload here the signed agreement? cc: [~accountid:712020:783602a6-282a-4f15-930c-066bdff8e5c5] ","2026-01-20T11:23:53.804Z"],["3823579","PFI-833286","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Have reached out to Local Ops, to understand if this can be done. Will bet back to you once I know more. Thank you!","2026-01-20T11:24:03.593Z"],["3823582","RDXENG-3087","RDXENG","mykhailo.pohoda@bolt.eu","Mykhailo Pohoda","I think we initially aimed at {{/code/add}} to be self-sufficient and to not required any follow-up calls (so it’s actually returns same “campaign” object as {{/code/list/v2}}). Maybe you can just rely on successful {{/code/add}} result? The only edge case I think you’d miss is “user adds a code, but they have other preferred code”, which is probably not the common, especially when user tries to add code while having active ride search.\nAim of that change would be to j*ust reduce chance of user seeing error when adding cod*e, since we’re already fixed original issue with backend fix (which I think should stay there, as it potentially covers for other edge cases).\n\nOr we don’t do anything now, and just hope that we’ll rework whole incentives interaction sometime later 😄 ","2026-01-20T11:24:26.959Z"],["3823584","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Jan Stoltman [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1768908315392309]*{color}:\n:melting_face: That's absolutely correct, thanks! I was looking at changes instead of owned by \n\n<@U09B111L8G1> that's the cause :smile:\n{quote}","2026-01-20T11:25:29.337Z"],["3823585","SRED-1083","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done","2026-01-20T11:25:38.814Z"],["3823587","PFI-832990","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo [~accountid:712020:62bdec5c-99dd-4eb7-9b0a-8a99dca351fb] could you please check whether you have access to this [page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-fiscalization/fiscalization/agents?tz=Europe%2FLondon&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D] to perform the batch action? \nIf not, please lmk whether the PL team has had any training and permissions on how to use this fiscalisation → Agents view.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.25.48.png|width=542,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.25.48.png\"!","2026-01-20T11:26:06.305Z"],["3823588","DMC-728","DMC","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:62b2cf2c99eafa602d88ec9e] I tried to do the same with your test provider, I was still able to reproduce:\n\n!linking_OG.mp4|width=766,alt=\"linking_OG.mp4\"!","2026-01-20T11:26:07.296Z"],["3823591","PFI-836035","PFI","esther.ndubuisi@bolt-outsource.eu","Esther Ndubuisi","!IMG_3443.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-20T11:26:23.789Z"],["3823593","PFI-805738","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Hey we do not process refunds in AZ market , please ask the partner to go the dispute route ! and then we can do the following !","2026-01-20T11:26:34.435Z"],["3823599","BDB-1547","BDB","henno.luts@bolt.eu","Henno Luts","Hopp version is here: [https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/l9fl3lud78hc0w06mfa2p/Hopp-Polite-Project.mp4?rlkey=mhan8job9jkug1wq45a3di7rp&dl=0|https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/l9fl3lud78hc0w06mfa2p/Hopp-Polite-Project.mp4?rlkey=mhan8job9jkug1wq45a3di7rp&dl=0]","2026-01-20T11:27:10.384Z"],["3823600","WD-22625","WD","saloni.dhawan@bolt.eu","Saloni Dhawan","[^account_details_proof_eur.pdf]","2026-01-20T11:27:23.380Z"],["3823602","PFI-807879","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Hey the bank transfer has reflected on their account and if they still would want a return , please reach out customer payments they process refunds related to cards !","2026-01-20T11:27:42.324Z"],["3823604","SREDESK-7440","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Hello! Seems that the automation that should have granted you this access is broken. I’ve created a ticket to IT so they could sort it out, after which you should have your access. I’ll let you know when it’s fixed.","2026-01-20T11:28:01.710Z"],["3823605","SREDESK-7438","SREDESK","arnold.kell@bolt.eu","Arnold Kell","Hello! Seems that the automation that should have granted you this access is broken. I’ve created a ticket to IT so they could sort it out, after which you should have your access. I’ll let you know when it’s fixed.","2026-01-20T11:28:17.252Z"],["3823607","LSS-61441","LSS","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","Hey, partner says that this has been signed, pls confirm. ","2026-01-20T11:28:25.725Z"],["3823613","PFI-835968","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T11:29:03.451Z"],["3823614","PFI-835966","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T11:29:10.767Z"],["3823616","PFI-836019","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! \n\n- [Partner Payments] Business made payment, but didn't reflect: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/306\n- [Customer Payments] Business had issues with their credit card: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/303\n\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/304\n\n[Billing] - Business invoicing and balance issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/59/create/305\n\n[Billing/Tax Tech]- Business invoice has not been reported (Fiscalized) : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-20T11:29:19.142Z"],["3823618","PC-4720","PC","pavel.melnikau@bolt.eu","Pavel Melnikau","After doublecheck, the information was enough - we can display proper value based on business_line","2026-01-20T11:29:24.499Z"],["3823619","LSS-61769","LSS","aire.vaigu@bolt.eu","Aire Vaigu","Hi! \n\nYes, we are renewing the contract with Box and changing the subscription type (from Enterprise to Enterprise Advanced).  Answers to your questions: \n\n\n# This new Service Order is set up as a contract re-start which means it will negate our old contract and create a new one with Box. We’ll receive credit for any future-facing payments that Bolt has already made against ourcurrent subscription. (In our case there is unlikely to be a large credit as we pay monthly, but whatever credit there is will be applied to our next payment)\n\n# AI units are how Box measures AI usage. For this renewal, the main goal is to start using Box’s AI features for document handling, specifically automatic metadata tagging. This would allow us to run audits, such as NC/NS clause checks, with AI support instead of doing them manually. Based on the volume of documents we plan to tag with metadata, we’ve estimated a need for 200,000 AI units.\n\nHope this helps! \n\n","2026-01-20T11:29:29.571Z"],["3823620","PC-4686","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-4720 has been resolved","2026-01-20T11:29:35.432Z"],["3823622","WD-22605","WD","laura.cedazo@bolt.eu","Laura Cedazo","Thanks Magnus!\n\n\n\nNot a clue about what you are referring to 😄 , but [~accountid:6273c82ed7fd480068d97e5f] is in the ticket, so good if you can guide her on how to do it correctly 🙌 ","2026-01-20T11:30:10.357Z"],["3823625","HS-29119","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","WD task is with PP-s","2026-01-20T11:30:40.955Z"],["3823626","CAMLE-9852","CAMLE","davit.khechoyan@bolt.eu","Davit Khechoyan","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/campaign/riderCodes?filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"userId\"%3A35361175}}&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&userId=35361175|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/campaign/riderCodes?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22userId%22%3A35361175%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn&userId=35361175]","2026-01-20T11:30:46.598Z"],["3823628","HS-29172","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-20T11:30:51.997Z"],["3823629","FIN2-550","FIN2","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","Yes no actions needed, marked as done","2026-01-20T11:30:58.806Z"],["3823630","PFI-836020","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Please, put this code under the Invoice Comment field if Customer wants it to be visible on the invoice;","2026-01-20T11:31:11.066Z"],["3823631","PAW-15019","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-20T11:31:11.405Z"],["3823632","PAW-15018","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-20T11:31:12.741Z"],["3823635","PC-4769","PC","alexey.efimov@bolt.eu","Alexey Efimov","Seems fix with {{use_balance: false}} works well. Closing issue.","2026-01-20T11:31:21.765Z"],["3823637","PC-4054","PC",null,"Automation for Jira","The linked issue - PC-4769 has been resolved","2026-01-20T11:31:31.139Z"],["3823644","WEBSD-1428","WEBSD","marit.ausmees@bolt.eu","Marit Ausmees","Hi, [~accountid:62b2cf3033a882e2be49d95a] Thanks! I am trying to set up the tags, but I have some questions on how to do it:\n\n* Should I use the same Meta Pixel code as last time, or do I need to create a whole new pixel now? Do I just use the same HTML text that we had previously, or should I get a new one?\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.24.40.png|width=723,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.24.40.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.24.08.png|width=754,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.24.08.png\"!\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.23.55.png|width=754,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.23.55.png\"!\n* The same for event tags - where do I get the HTML text? Can I just use the same text that we had last time and just change the name inside?\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.27.21.png|width=778,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.27.21.png\"!\n\n* Is there a way for me to see what each step means in real life without having to sign up myself? I can see how many steps we have but not what they actually mean.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.29.33.png|width=296,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-20 at 13.29.33.png\"!\n\nSorry for the trouble. I’m just not sure what I need to do :smiling_face_with_tear: \n\nThank you!!!","2026-01-20T11:32:48.212Z"],["3823647","RS-1906","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Thank you! I’ll make the necessary adjustments","2026-01-20T11:33:57.627Z"],["3823649","PFI-832990","PFI","anna.klimek@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Klimek","Hi [~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574], I do have access to the page. Could you please assist or send instructions how to successfully use it? Thank you","2026-01-20T11:34:07.379Z"],["3823652","BDRIV-16","BDRIV","aydin.zengin@bolt.eu","Aydın Zengin","Hi [~accountid:624b3bdf8678e900705d9004] [~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] \nI made this task for battery size research. Feel free to edit the description. ","2026-01-20T11:34:43.246Z"],["3823653","PFI-835647","PFI","ines.caetano@bolt-outsource.eu","Inês Caetano","Hello, thank you for letting me know. At the time they weren’t but they are now, you can close this. : )","2026-01-20T11:34:46.480Z"],["3823655","DBRE-8731","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","is this bug being fixed in 8.5.5?","2026-01-20T11:35:05.021Z"],["3823656","MLC-3442","MLC","suresh.nv@bolt.eu","Suresh NV","\n\nProduct Screens: [https://www.figma.com/board/IpkI6CawJbDtxkm206uG5P/Bolt-Flow---Learnings---Research?node-id=35-14505&t=Zs51qg1dwu4wEjqC-0|https://www.figma.com/board/IpkI6CawJbDtxkm206uG5P/Bolt-Flow---Learnings---Research?node-id=35-14505&t=